COLLDATA("mujamkabir","en",[[1,"Abu Bakr As-Siddiq, his name is Abdullah bin Uthman bin Amer bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah. He witnessed the Battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . The mother of Abu Bakr, the mother of goodness, Salma bint Sakhr bin Amer bin Amr bin Kaab bin Saad bin Taim bin Murrah bin Kaab bin Luay bin Ghalib bin Fehr bin Malik. The mother of the mother of goodness, Dilaaf, she is Ummamah bint Ubaid bin An-Naqid Al-Khuzaiyyi. The grandmother of Abu Bakr, Umm Abu Quhafa, Aminah bint Abdul Uzza bin Huthan bin Awf bin Ubaid bin Uwaid bin Adi bin Kaab."],[2,"The mother of Abu Bakr ؓ was called Umm al-Khayr bt. Sakhr b. Amir. Abu Bakr died and both his parents inherited from him; they had both embraced Islam. Abu Bakr's mother died before his father."],[3,"It is also said: Atiq b. Uthman. He was named Atiq because of the beauty of his face."],[4,"Abu Bakr ؓ was named Atiq because of the beauty of his face. His name was Abdullah b. Uthman."],[5,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Atiq from the Fire."],[6,"Abdullah. I said, \"But people say Atiq.\" She said, \"Abu Quhafa had three sons, and he named one Atiq, one Mu'aytiq, and one Mu'taq.\""],[7,"Abu Bakr's name was Abdullah b. Uthman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Atiq from the Fire."],[8,"I heard Abdullah b. al-Zubayr say, \"Abu Bakr's ؓ name was Abdullah b. Uthman.\""],[9,"I entered upon Aisha, the Mother of the Believers ؓ, and she said, \"Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to him, 'You are Atiq from the Fire.' From that day on he was called Atiq.\""],[10,"\"That Abu Bakr passed by the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Whoever wants to see a person freed from Hellfire, should look at this (referring to himself).'\" She said, and his name given by his family is Abdullah ibn Uthman.\""],[11,"We do not know of four generations who met the Prophet ﷺ, along with their sons, except these four: Abu Quhafa, Abu Bakr, Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, and Abu Atiq b. Abd al-Rahman. Abu Atiq's name was Muhammad ؓ."],[12,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"After me there will be twelve caliphs. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq will remain after me only a short time. The owner of a turning millstone will live praiseworthily and die as a martyr.\" It was said, \"Who is he, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Umar b. al-Khattab\" ؓ. Then he turned to Uthman and said, \"And you: the people will ask you to take off a shirt that Allah ﷻ has clothed you with. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you take it off you will not enter Paradise until the camel passes through the eye of the needle.\""],[13,"From Safina, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The caliphate is thirty years, then it will be kingship.\" He said, \"Abu Bakr held it for two years, Umar for ten, Uthman for twelve, and Ali for six\" ؓ."],[14,"I heard Ali ؓ swear: By Allah, Allah sent down the name of Abu Bakr from heaven as al-Siddiq."],[15,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he was taken on the Night Journey, \"I want to go out to the Quraysh and inform them.\" So he informed them, but they rejected him and Abu Bakr confirmed him (believed him), so he was called \"As-Siddiq\" that day."],[16,"Three men of Quraysh had the brightest faces, the best character, and the firmest modesty. If they told you something, they would not lie to you; and if you told them something, they would not accuse you of lying: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ."],[17,"Abu Bakr ؓ dyed his hair with henna and katam."],[18,"Abu Bakr ؓ dyed his beard with henna and katam, while Umar ؓ dyed his hair with henna alone."],[20,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to dye his hair with henna and katam, and Umar ؓ used to dye his hair with henna."],[21,"She saw a man passing by while she was in her howdah and said, \"I have never seen a man more resembling Abu Bakr than this one.\" It was said to her, \"Describe Abu Bakr for us.\" She said, \"He was a fair-skinned, slender man with light hair on his temples, slightly stooped; his waist-wrapper would not stay up and would slip from his hips; he had a lean face, deep-set eyes, a prominent forehead, and thin forearms. This is his description.\""],[22,"I saw Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, while he was the caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with a reddish beard, deep red in color."],[23,"Abu Bakr ؓ used to dye his hair with henna."],[24,"I saw Abu Bakr ؓ during the campaign of Dhat al-Salasil, and his beard was like the flame of the arfaj plant, on a white camel of his, light and slender."],[25,"Muawiyah ؓ said, \"I entered with my father upon Abu Bakr ؓ, and I saw Asma standing at his head, fair-skinned. I saw Abu Bakr ؓ as fair-skinned and slender. He mounted me and my father on two horses, then we were presented to him and he granted us rewards.\""],[26,"The Prophet ﷺ died at the age of sixty-three."],[27,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[28,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ mentioned their birth dates in my presence, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was older than Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was sixty-three, and Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three, two and a half years after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[29,"I was with Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan ؓ and I heard him say: \"The Prophet ﷺ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three, and 'Umar ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three.\" Abu Ishaq said: Mu'awiya ؓ also said: \"This [age] for me is fifty-seven, then he lived about twenty years.\""],[31,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[32,"Abu Bakr was taken when he was sixty-three."],[34,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[35,"Abu Bakr ؓ died when he was sixty-three years old, and Abu Bakr ruled for two years. He was buried at night, and 'Umar ؓ prayed over him."],[36,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old, and Abu Bakr ؓ was at the same age."],[37,"When Abu Bakr ؓ intended to appoint 'Umar as his successor, he sent for him and called him. He came to him and he said: \"I am calling you to a matter that is exhausting for the one who undertakes it. So fear Allah, O 'Umar, through obedience to Him, and obey Him through fear of Him, for the God-fearing is secure and protected. Then indeed the affair is presented [as a test]; none deserves it except the one who acts upon it. Whoever commands the truth but acts upon falsehood, and commands the right but acts upon the wrong, his hope is about to be cut off and his deeds to be nullified. If you are given authority over them, then if you are able to keep your hand dry from their blood, to keep your stomach empty of their wealth, and to keep your tongue from their honors, then do so. And there is no power except with Allah.\""],[38,"When Abu Bakr was on his deathbed, he said, \"Oh Aisha, look at the container from which we used to drink its milk, and the slaughter tool from which we used to slaughter animals, and the garment that we used to wear. We used to benefit from these things when we were in the service of the Muslims. So when I die, return them to Umar.\" When Abu Bakr passed away, I sent them to Umar, and Umar said, \"May Allah be pleased with you, Abu Bakr. You have really exhausted those who came after you.\""],[39,"In the sermon of Abu Bakr ؓ it was said: \"Do you not know that you go out in the morning and return in the evening for a fixed term? Whoever is able to have his term expire while he is in the work of Allah ﷻ, let him do so. You will never attain that except with Allah ﷻ. Indeed some people have made their terms for other than Him, so Allah has forbidden you to be like them: {And be not like those who forgot Allah, so He made them forget} [Quran 59:19]. Where are those of your brothers whom you knew? They have sent forth what they sent forth in the days of their predecessors, and they have fallen therein into misery or felicity. Where are the first tyrants who built cities and surrounded them with walls? They have become beneath rocks and wells. This is the Book of Allah ﷻ; its wonders never cease. So enjoin one another to follow it for a day of darkness, and illuminate yourselves with its light and its clarity. Indeed Allah ﷻ praised Zakariyya and his household, saying: {They used to hasten to good deeds and supplicate Us in hope and fear, and they were humbly submissive to Us} [Quran 21:90]. There is no good in a saying by which the face of Allah is not intended, no good in wealth that is not spent in the path of Allah, no good in one whose ignorance overcomes his forbearance, and no good in one who fears the blame of a blamer for the sake of Allah.\""],[40,"Abu Bakr ؓ died on Tuesday night and was buried at night."],[41,"I heard my grandfather say: \"Abu Bakr ؓ died while he had a touch of consumption, and he ruled for two and a half years.\""],[42,"Abu Bakr ؓ was appointed as successor on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. Abu Bakr ؓ died in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year thirteen, and his age on the day he died, as 'A'isha ؓ mentioned, was the age of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which is sixty-three."],[43,"I entered upon Abu Bakr ؓ to visit him during the illness in which he died. I greeted him and asked him how he was and he sat up straight. I said, \"By the praise of God, you are recovering.\" He said, \"Indeed, as you see, I am in pain, and you have made a distraction for me along with my pain. I made a covenant for you after me and chose for you the best of you in my own judgment, so every one of you has his nose swollen at that, hoping that the matter will be his. And I saw that the world has turned towards you, and it has not yet turned, and it is coming. You will adorn your houses with silk curtains and brocade cushions, and you will feel pain from lying on coarse wool as if one of you is on the thorns of Saʿdan. By God, if one of you were to come forward and have his neck struck without hadd punishment, it would be better for him than to roam in the flood of the world.\" Then he said, \"Indeed, I regret nothing except three things I did that I wish I had not done, three things I did not do that I wish I had done, and three things I wish I had asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about. As for the three things I wish I had not done: I wish I had not uncovered the house of Fatimah and left it, and had not closed the war upon myself. I wish that on the day of the Saqifah of Banu Saʿidah I had thrown the matter upon the neck of one of the two men, Abu ʿUbaydah or ʿUmar, so that he would have been the Commander of the Believers and I would have been a minister. And I wish that when I dispatched Khalid b. al-Walid to the people of apostasy, I had stayed at Dhu al-Qassah, so if the Muslims prevailed, they prevailed, and if not, I would have been a support or a reinforcement. As for the things I wish I had done: I wish that on the day al-Ashʿath was brought to me as a prisoner I had struck his neck, for it seems to me that he will be an evil frame around him. I wish that on the day al-Fuja'ah al-Sulami was brought to me, I had not burned him but had killed him quickly or released him successfully. And I wish that when I dispatched Khalid b. al-Walid to Syria, I had dispatched ʿUmar to Iraq, so that I would have stretched out both my hands, right and left, in the way of God ﷻ. As for the three things I wish I had asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about: I wish I had asked him to whom this matter belongs, so that its people would not dispute it. I wish I had asked him whether the Ansar have a share in this matter. And I wish I had asked him about the paternal aunt and the brother's daughter, for I have a need in my heart concerning them.\""],[44,"Ali and al-Abbas brought a dispute before Abu Bakr ؓ concerning the inheritance of the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"I will not transfer it from the place where the Messenger of God ﷺ put it.\""],[45,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning the Ansar: \"Accept from their doers of good and overlook their doers of evil.\""],[46,"\"That the Messenger of God ﷺ consulted concerning the matter of war.\" Stick to that."],[47,"I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ say: I said, \"O Messenger of God, do we act upon a matter already decreed or upon a matter newly initiated?\" He said, \"Rather upon a matter already decreed.\" I said, \"Then what is the point of action, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Everyone is facilitated for what he was created for.\""],[48,"Al-Shifa' bt. Abd Allah, who was among the first emigrant women, informed me that Labid b. Rabi'ah and Adi b. Hatim came to Madinah and went to the mosque. They found Amr b. al-As and said, \"O Ibn al-As, seek permission for us to see the Commander of the Believers.\" He said, \"By God, you two have hit upon his name: he is the commander and we are the believers.\" Amr went in to Umar and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers.\" Umar said to him, \"What is this?\" He said, \"You are the commander and we are the believers.\" And the title has been used from that day on."],[49,"\"I was reciting poetry to him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, and I did not recognize his Companions until a man came who was broad between the shoulders and bald.\" It was said to me, \"Be quiet! Be quiet!\" I said, \"Alas, who is this for whom I must be quiet in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ?\" It was said to me, \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[50,"The people of Madinah went out for a gathering of theirs, and there I saw a bald man, left-handed but using his right, who towered above the people by a forearm's length, wearing a coarse loincloth and a striped cloak, saying: \"O people, emigrate and do not abandon, and let none of you throw a stone or stick at a rabbit and then eat it; let spears, lances, and arrows be of service to you.\" I said, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\""],[51,"\"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was bald, severely bald.\""],[52,"That he will expel us from our land."],[53,"\"When Umar b. al-Khattab got angry, he would twist his mustache and blow.\""],[54,"\"Umar ؓ would take hold of his ear, meaning his own ear, then leap onto the horse.\""],[55,"Umar ؓ was offered by a freedwoman of his that he dye his beard. He said, “Do you want to extinguish my light as so-and-so extinguished his light?”"],[56,"I heard Abu 'Amir Sulaym b. 'Amir say, “I saw Umar not changing anything of his beard.”"],[57,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection,” and I will not change my gray hair."],[58,"I was in Madinah when there was a dark brown man, left-handed on one side and right-handed on the other, huge; when he appeared before the people it was as if he were on a mount. Then it was Umar ؓ."],[59,"I saw Umar ؓ as a huge man, as if he were one of the men of Banu Sadus."],[60,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Jibril ﷺ said to me: Let Islam weep over the death of Umar ؓ.”"],[61,"When Umar ؓ was struck, I heard a voice: “Let him weep for Islam who would weep; they have nearly perished. The covenant has not arrived, and the world has turned its back, and its good has turned away; those who believed in the promise have grown weary of it.”"],[62,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ held authority for ten years, then he died."],[63,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ died when he was sixty-six years old."],[64,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ died when he was sixty-three."],[65,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, Abu Bakr ؓ was taken when he was sixty-three years old, and Umar was taken when he was sixty-three years old."],[66,"Umar ؓ was killed when he was sixty-one years old."],[67,"Umar ؓ died at the beginning of fifty-five."],[68,"Umar ؓ passed away when he was fifty-five years old."],[69,"Umar ؓ died when he was fifty-five years old."],[70,"And he said: \"Gray hair came to me quickly from the side of my maternal uncles, Banu al-Mughira.\""],[71,"Umar ؓ was buried on Wednesday, when four nights remained of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year twenty-three."],[72,"Umar was appointed in the month of Rajab in the thirteenth year and he was killed in the month of Dhul-Hijjah in the twenty-third year. He remained alive for three days after being stabbed, then he died in the end of Dhul-Hijjah. Suhaib led the funeral prayer for him, and his son Abdullah ibn Umar washed his body and shrouded him in five garments. He was buried next to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . Umar was stabbed on Wednesday, the ninth day of the remaining days of Dhul-Hijjah. Some people say he died on that day, and his age on the day he died was what I have heard from Malik ibn Anas, who mentioned that the Prophet's ﷺ age when he died was sixty-three. Some people say it was fifty-nine, and others say it was fifty-three. Some people say it was forty-five, and his caliphate lasted for ten years, four months, and some days."],[73,"The Commander of the Faithful, Umar ؓ, was killed at the return of the pilgrims, and that was in the year twenty-three."],[74,"He was fifty-eight years old."],[75,"Umar died in the year twenty-three, and his caliphate lasted ten years."],[76,"He was accused of practicing sorcery, and it was Abu Lu'lu'a, the servant of Al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, who stabbed him. He was a Zoroastrian."],[77,"Umar was stabbed. They sent for a physician, and a man from the Ansar came and gave him milk to drink. The milk came out white from the stab wound below the navel. The physician said to him: \"Make your will, for I do not think you will live until evening.\" He said: \"He has told me the truth.\""],[78,"I witnessed the death of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ, and the sun was eclipsed on that day."],[79,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"May one of us sleep while he is in a state of major ritual impurity?\" He said: \"Yes, and he should perform ablution as he does for prayer.\""],[80,"The Prophet ﷺ heard me saying: \"By my father,\" and he said: \"Allah ﷻ forbids you to swear by your fathers.\""],[81,"He said: O people, do not judge based on opinion in matters of religion. Indeed, you have seen me opposing the orders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with my own opinion as an effort. By Allah, that has not diverted me from the truth. This happened on the day of Abu Jandal, when the message was between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people of Makkah. He said: \"Write in the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\" They said: \"Do you see that we have believed you in what you say?\" However, you write in your own name, so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will be satisfied. I refused until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do you see that I am satisfied and you refuse?\" I said: \"I am satisfied.\""],[82,"I said to Abī, \"Who is the man who freed you from the polytheists on the day they beat you?\" He said, \"That was al-ʿĀṣ b. Wāʾil al-Sahmī.\""],[83,"ʿUmar ؓ went out to pray for rain and took al-ʿAbbās with him to pray for rain, saying, \"O Allah, we used to seek intercession with You through our Prophet ﷺ when we suffered drought during the time of our Prophet ﷺ , and now we seek intercession with You through the uncle of our Prophet ﷺ, so accept it from him.\""],[84,"I heard ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say on the pulpit, \"Gold for gold is ribā unless equal for equal, with no increase; whatever exceeds that is ribā.\" Ibn ʿUmar said, \"If you are in doubt, ask Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī about that.\" So he went and asked Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, and he told him that he had heard that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn ʿAbbās was told what Ibn ʿUmar and Abū Saʿīd had said, so he sought forgiveness and said, \"This is an opinion I held.\""],[85,"\"Are you satisfied with your father?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So we gathered before the Commander of the Faithful, and Saʿd said to him, \"I urinated, performed ablution, wiped over my leather socks, and then prayed.\" He said, \"You have done well and followed the Sunnah.\" He said, \"But your son ʿAbdullāh criticized me for that.\" He said, \"O Saʿd, you are older and more knowledgeable than him.\""],[86,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The price of a singing slave-girl is unlawful, her singing is forbidden, looking at her is forbidden, her price is like the price of a dog, and the price of a dog is unlawful. Whoever's flesh grows on unlawful gain, the Fire is more fitting for him.\""],[87,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to marry one of his women, he would come to her from behind the veil and say to her, \"O my daughter, so-and-so has proposed to you. If you dislike him, say no, for no one should be ashamed to say no. And if you accept, then your silence is consent.\""],[88,"Allah ﷻ to His Prophet ﷺ”"],[89,"He is also called Abū ʿAbdullāh. The mother of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān is Arwā bt. Kurayz b. Rabīʿa b. Ḥabīb b. ʿAbd Shams. Arwā's mother is Umm Ḥakīm al-Bayḍāʾ bt. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umm Ḥakīm's mother is Fāṭima bt. ʿAmr b. ʿĀʾidh b. ʿImrān b. Makhzūm, who is the paternal grandmother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[90,"\"The mother of ʿUthmān ؓ, Arwā bt. Kurayz, accepted Islam.\""],[91,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ on Friday on the pulpit wearing a thick ʿAdanī lower garment worth four or five dirhams and a Kufan dyed cloak, of sturdy build, with a long beard and a handsome face.\""],[92,"\"On Friday, Uthman used to lean on a walking stick. He was the most beautiful of people and he wore two yellow garments, an undergarment and a cloak, until he would reach the pulpit and sit on it.\""],[93,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ, and I have never seen any male or female with a more beautiful face than his.\""],[94,"\"I saw ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ with a white beard.\""],[95,"I saw Uthman b. Affan ؓ with a yellow beard."],[96,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Uthman ؓ with a dish containing meat. I entered upon him while Ruqayyah was sitting, and I never saw two people more beautiful than them ؓ. I found myself looking once at Ruqayyah and once at Uthman. When I returned, the Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"Did you enter upon them?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Did you see a couple more beautiful than them?\" I said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah, I kept looking once at Ruqayyah and once at Uthman.\" Abu al-Qasim, may Allah have mercy on him, said, \"This was before the revelation of the verse of hijab.\""],[97,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon his daughter while she was washing Uthman's ؓ head and said, \"O my dear daughter, be kind to Abu Abd Allah, for he is the closest of my Companions to me in character.\""],[98,"I entered upon Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and wife of Uthman ؓ, with a comb in her hand. She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me a little while ago after I combed his hair. He said, 'How do you find Abu Abd Allah?' I said, 'Well.' He said, 'Honor him, for he is among the closest of my Companions to me in character.'\""],[99,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ was killed in the middle of the days of tashriq."],[100,"I heard Zubayr ibn Bakkar say, \"Uthman ibn Affan was killed on Friday, in the eighteenth day of Dhu al-Hijjah, in the year thirty-six, after 'Asr prayer. He was eighty-two years old at that time and was fasting.\""],[101,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[102,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[103,"Uthman was killed when he was ninety or eighty-eight years old."],[104,"Uthman ؓ was killed in the year thirty-five."],[105,"The caliphate of Uthman ؓ was twelve years."],[106,"The shura was held, and the people agreed upon Uthman ؓ with three nights remaining in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year twenty-three. Then Uthman ؓ was killed on Friday, eighteen nights having passed in Dhu al-Hijjah, at the completion of the year thirty-five. He was eighty-eight years old. He used to dye his beard yellow, and the reign of Uthman ؓ was twelve years."],[107,"Uthman ؓ was killed when he was ninety or eighty-eight years old."],[108,"I heard Malik say: Uthman ؓ was killed, and he lay cast aside on the rubbish heap of the Banu Fulān for three days. Then twelve men came to him, among them my grandfather Malik b. Abi Amir, Huwaytib b. Abd al-Uzza, Hakim b. Hizam, Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, and Aisha bt. Uthman, with a lamp inside a small box. They carried him on a door, and his head kept knocking against the door: tap, tap. Then they brought him to al-Baqi`, and they differed about praying over him, so Hakim b. Hizam or Huwaytib b. Abd al-Uzza prayed over him — Abd al-Rahman was unsure. Then they wanted to bury him, but a man from the Banu Mazin stood up and said: By Allah, if you bury him with the Muslims, I will tell the people. So they carried him until they brought him to the orchard of Kawkab. When they lowered him into his grave, Aisha bt. Uthman cried out, and Ibn al-Zubayr said to her: Be quiet, for by Allah, if you do it again, I will strike the part where your eyes are. When they had buried him and leveled the earth over him, Ibn al-Zubayr said to her: Cry now, as much as you want. Malik said: Before that, Uthman b. Affan ؓ used to pass by the orchard of Kawkab and say: A righteous man will surely be buried here. Abu al-Qasim said: al-hushsh means the garden."],[109,"When evening came, I said: If you leave your companion until morning, they will mutilate him, so take him to Baqi al-Gharqad, and make it possible for us in the middle of the night. Then we carried him, and a blackness came over us from behind, and we feared them until we almost dispersed from around him. Then a caller called out: Do not be afraid; stand firm, for we have come to witness him with you. Ibn Hubaysh used to say: They were, by Allah, the angels."],[110,"O Commander of the Faithful, what do you say about Uthman? The two men hastened to answer and said: Why do you ask? About a man who disbelieved in Allah after his faith and acted as a hypocrite? The man said to them: I am not asking you two, and I did not come to you two. Ali said to him: \"I do not say what they say.\" They both said to him: Then why did we kill him? He said: He was put in authority over you and ruled badly in his final days, and you became distressed and behaved badly in your distress. By Allah, I hope that I and Uthman will be as Allah ﷻ said: {And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts; they will be brothers, on couches facing one another}."],[111,"Ali ؓ addressed the people and said: O people, by Allah, if no one enters the Fire except those who killed Uthman, I will not enter it; and if no one enters Paradise except those who killed Uthman, I will not enter it. When he came down, it was said to him: You have spoken a word that has divided your companions against you. So he addressed them and said: \"O people, indeed Allah ﷻ caused Uthman to be killed, and I am with him.\" Hammad said: And Habib b. al-Shahid narrated to us from Muhammad b. Sirin: A Qurayshi expression that has two meanings. Abu al-Qasim said: It is as if he meant, \"Allah, exalted is He, caused him to be killed, and I too will be killed with him ؓ.\""],[112,"Ali ؓ addressed them, but they interrupted his sermon. He said: I was only weakened the day Uthman ؓ was killed. And he struck for them a parable: the parable of three bulls and a lion who met in a thicket — a black one, a red one, and a white one. Whenever the lion wanted one of them, they gathered together against him and resisted him. So the lion said to the black one and the red one: The one who disgraces us in our thicket and exposes us is this white one. Let me eat him, so that your color will match mine and my color will match yours. The lion attacked him, and it was not long before he killed him. Then he said to the black one: The one who disgraces us and exposes us in our thicket is this red one. Let me eat him, so that my color will match yours and your color will match mine. He attacked him and killed him. Then he said to the black one: I will eat you. He said: Let me cry out three cries. So he cried out: Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was eaten the day the white one was eaten. Indeed, I was only weakened the day Uthman was killed."],[113,"\"By Allah, you have killed him while he was one who fasted much and prayed much.\" Al-Ashtar went and informed Ammar ؓ, so Ammar came to Masruq and said: By Allah, Ammar will be flogged, Abu Dharr will be exiled, and the protected pasture will be guarded, and you say, 'You have killed him while he was one who fasted much and prayed much.' Masruq said to him: \"By Allah, you have not done one of two things: you have not been punished as you have been punished, nor have you been patient, and patience is better for the patient.\" It was as if he had thrust a stone into his mouth. He said: And al-Shabi said: \"No woman of Hamdan has given birth to one like Masruq.\""],[114,"We gathered in the house of Makhrama after Uthman ؓ was killed, wanting to pledge allegiance. Abu Jahm b. Hudhayfa said: Whoever of you we give allegiance to, we will not stand in the way of retaliation. Ammar b. Yasir said: Not for the blood of Uthman. Abu Jahm said: O son of Sumayya, by Allah, retaliation will be taken from you for the lashes you were given, but no retaliation will be taken for the blood of Uthman ؓ. So they departed that day without pledging allegiance."],[115,"Waththab, who was one of those whom Uthman ؓ had freed and who used to stand before Uthman, informed me: Uthman sent me and I summoned al-Ashtar for him. Ibn Awn said: I think he said: I placed a cushion for the Commander of the Faithful, and he had a cushion. He said: \"O Ashtar, what do the people want from me?\" He said: Three things, one of which is unavoidable. He said: \"What are they?\" He said: They give you the choice between handing over their affair to them, saying, 'This is your affair, so choose for it whom you will,' and between exacting retribution from yourself. If you refuse these two, then the people will fight you. He said: \"Is one of them unavoidable?\" He said: One of them is unavoidable. He said: \"As for handing over their affair to them, I would never remove a garment with which I have been clothed.\" He said: And al-Hasan said: By Allah, to be brought forward and have my neck struck is dearer to me than to remove the affair of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ from one another. Ibn Awn said: This is more like the words of Uthman. As for exacting retribution from myself, by Allah, I know that my two companions before me were punished, and my body cannot withstand retaliation. As for killing me, by Allah, if you kill me, you will never love one another after me, and you will never fight an enemy together after me. Then al-Ashtar stood up and left. We waited and said: Perhaps the people... Then a man came who looked like a wolf, peered in from a door, and then went back. Then Muhammad b. Abi Bakr came with thirteen men and reached Uthman ؓ. He grabbed his beard and said with it, and said with it, until I heard the chattering of his teeth, and said: What did Muawiya avail you? What did Ibn Amir avail you? What did your letters avail you? He said: \"Let go of my beard, O son of my brother. Let go of my beard, O son of my brother.\" He said: I saw him summon a man from the group with his eye, and the man went to him with a small spear and struck him with it on his head. I said: Then what? He said: Then they all attacked him, by Allah, until they killed him."],[116,"Muhammad said: O Kab, do you not find this ship of ours in the Torah, how it sails? He said: \"No, but I find in it a man, the most wretched of the young men of Quraysh, who leaps into the turmoil as a donkey leaps. Do not be that one.\" Ibn Sirin said: They claimed that it was indeed him."],[117,"A man of the Ansar entered upon Uthman, and he said: Go back, O son of my brother, for you are not my killer. He said: How do you know that? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day, and he chewed a date for you and blessed you.\" Then another man of the Ansar entered upon him, and he said: Go back, O son of my brother, for you are not my killer. He said: How do you know that? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day, and he chewed a date for you and blessed you.\" Then Muhammad b. Abi Bakr entered upon him, and he said: You are my killer. He said: How do you know, O Nathal? He said: Because \"you were brought to the Prophet ﷺ on your seventh day so that he might chew a date for you and bless you, but you defecated on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So he leaped onto his chest and grabbed his beard, saying: If you do that, it would be hard for your father that you upset him. Then he struck him in the throat with small spears that were in his hand."],[118,"It was the first hand that wrote the Mufassal."],[119,"\"A righteous ruler who is not deterred from the cause of Allah by the blame of any blamer.\" He said: Then what? He said: \"Then after you there will be a caliph whom a sinful faction will kill.\" He said: Then what? He said: \"Then there will be the tribulation.\""],[120,"to collapse"],[121,"had the people not sought the blood of Uthman, they would have been stoned from the sky"],[122,"I heard al-Hasan say: “The corrupt Muhammad b. Abi Bakr was seized in a ravine among the ravines of Egypt, then put inside a donkey’s belly and burned.”"],[123,"\"I sought refuge with my Lord for ten days. Indeed, I am the fourth among four in Islam. I have not intended or desired anything, nor have I ever placed my right hand on my private parts since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Every Friday that has passed since I embraced Islam, I have freed a slave in it, except that if I did not have one, then I would continue to do so afterwards. I have never committed adultery, neither during the period of ignorance nor after embracing Islam.\""],[124,"As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, Uthman is occupied with Your need and the need of Your Messenger,” so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him his arrow."],[125,"Uthman b. Affan stayed behind in Madinah with his wife, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was ill, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him his arrow. He said: And my reward, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “And your reward.”"],[126,"And Talhah ؓ was washing one side of his head, so he did not answer her. So she put her hands into the sleeve of her garment and brought out her breasts and said: I ask you by what I carried you and nursed you: do it. So he got up, twisted the side of his hair until he tied it while it was washed, then went out until he came to Ali ؓ while he was sitting beside his house. Talhah ؓ, with his mother and the mother of Abdullah b. Rafi’, said: If only you would ease this man’s siege, for it has become severe. He said: He tapped with a cup in his hand three times, then raised his head and said: “By Allah, I do not love anything of this that you dislike.” He said: And Abu Khalifah recited to us, saying: Al-Abbas b. al-Faraj al-Riyashi recited to us for Layla al-Akhyaliyyah."],[128,"“Welcome to those who speak justly, and by prayer, welcome and family.”"],[129,"The wife of Uthman ؓ said when they surrounded him intending to kill him: “If you kill him or spare him, he used to keep the whole night alive in a single rak’ah, gathering the Quran in it.”"],[130,"I heard al-Hasan say: I reached the time of Uthman ؓ when I was then near puberty, and I heard him delivering a sermon, and I witnessed him saying: “O people, what do you hold against me?” He said: And there was no day but they would share in some good. He would say: “O people, come in the morning for your gifts,” so they would come and take them in full. Then it would be said: “O Muslims, come in the morning for your clothing,” so fine robes would be brought and divided among them. Al-Hasan said: “The enemy is repelled, gifts are flowing, harmony is good, and good is abundant. No believer on earth fears another believer. Whomever he meets, from whatever tribe he is, he is his brother, his friend, and his supporter. The tribulation is that someone draws a sword against him.”"],[131,"“To fall from the sky and be torn apart would be dearer to me than to have shared in the blood of Uthman ؓ.”"],[132,"And who is the man? I said: From the people of Basra. She said: From which people of Basra? I said: From Bakr b. Wa’il. She said: From which Bakr b. Wa’il? I said: From Banu Qays b. Tha’labah. She said: Are you from the household of so-and-so? I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, for what reason was Uthman, the Commander of the Believers ؓ, killed? She said: “By Allah, he was killed unjustly. May Allah curse his killers. May Allah exact retribution for him from Ibn Abi Bakr. May Allah drive humiliation into the eyes of Banu Tamim in his house. May Allah shed the blood of Banu Budayl upon error. May Allah send to al-Ashtar an arrow from His arrows.” For by Allah, there was no man among those people but her supplication struck him."],[133,"The majority of the riders who marched against Uthman went mad."],[134,"Why do I see that you have kept away from the Commander of the Faithful, Uthman ؓ? Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ said: Shall I tell him that I did not stay behind from Badr? Uthman ؓ was informed of that, so he said: As for his saying that I did not stay behind from Badr, I was nursing Ruqayya bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until she died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted me a share, and whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share to has indeed attended."],[135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The caliphate after me in my community is thirty years. He said: So we calculated and found Abu Bakr two years, Umar ten, Uthman twelve, and Ali six ؓ."],[136,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, they claim that you said, 'A people will disbelieve after their faith.' He said, 'Yes, and you are not among them.' Abu al-Darda died before the killing of Uthman ؓ."],[137,"Uthman, possessor of the two lights, was killed wrongfully."],[138,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, you got his name right; Umar, a horn of iron; Uthman, possessor of the two lights, you got his name right, killed wrongfully, he was given two portions of reward."],[139,"From its highest, one with above."],[140,"I heard Abdullah say when allegiance was given to Uthman: We did not hold back from its highest, one with above."],[141,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There will be after me twelve caliphs: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who will not remain except a little; and the companion of the millstone of the Arab abode, who will live praiseworthy and be killed as a martyr. A man said: Who is he, O Messenger of Allah? He said, 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' Then he turned to Uthman and said, 'And you, the people will ask you to take off a shirt with which Allah has clothed you. By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you take it off, you will not enter Paradise until the camel enters the eye of the needle.'"],[142,"Uthman ؓ went out as an emigrant to the land of Abyssinia, and with him was Ruqayya bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. News of them was withheld from the Prophet ﷺ, and he would go out looking for news of them. A woman came and told him. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Uthman is the first to emigrate to Allah with his family after Lot.'"],[143,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent Uthman to the people of Makkah and then his companions pledged the pledge of al-Ridwan, he pledged for Uthman with one of his hands on the other. The people said: Congratulations to Abu Abdullah, he will circumambulate the House in safety. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'If he stayed such and such, he would not circumambulate until I circumambulate.'"],[144,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ, while delivering a sermon on the pulpit: I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Nothing prevented me from telling you except concern for you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A night of guard duty in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights in which its night is spent in prayer and its day is spent in fasting.'"],[145,"Uthman ؓ adjured the people one day and said: Do you know that the Prophet ﷺ climbed Uhud, and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ and I, and Uhud trembled, and upon it were Muhammad the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ؓ? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be still, Uhud, for upon you are none but a Prophet, a Siddiq, and two martyrs.\""],[146,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Anything that exceeds the shade of a house, a crust of bread, and a garment that covers a man's private parts\"—or he said, \"the private parts of the son of Adam\"—\"and anything that exceeds that, the son of Adam has no right to it.\""],[147,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays the later Isha in congregation, it is as if he prayed the whole night; and whoever prays the morning prayer in congregation, it is as if he prayed the whole day.\""],[148,"I heard Uthman ؓ—and he narrated little from the Messenger of God ﷺ—say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs wudu as he has been commanded and prays as he has been commanded, his sins depart him as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[149,"Abu Talib's name was Abd Manaf b. Abd al-Muttalib; Abd al-Muttalib's name was Shaybah b. Hashim; Hashim's name was Amr b. Abd Manaf b. Qusayy; and Qusayy's name was Zayd."],[150,"It is said that she was the first Hashimite woman to give birth to a Hashimite. She embraced Islam, emigrated to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah, died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ buried her. Her mother was Fatimah bt. Harim b. Rawahah b. Hujr b. Abd Mu'arrid b. Amir b. Lu'ayy."],[151,"\"O Amr, look at the Commander of the Believers for me.\" He said: \"I did not see that he had dyed his beard; he had a large head.\""],[152,"\"I saw Ali ؓ with a white head and beard, wearing a lower garment and a cloak.\""],[153,"\"I saw Ali ؓ on the pulpit with a white head and beard.\""],[154,"I went out with my father to the Friday prayer when I was a boy. When Ali ؓ came out and ascended the pulpit, my father said to me: \"Get up, O Amr, and look at the Commander of the Believers.\" He said: \"I got up, and there he was standing on the pulpit, white of beard and head, wearing a lower garment and a cloak, no shirt on him.\" He said: \"I did not see him sit on the pulpit until he descended from it.\" We said to Abu Ishaq: \"Did he perform qunut?\" He said: \"No.\""],[155,"When Ali ؓ married Fatimah ؓ, she said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"You have married me to a bleary-eyed man with a big belly.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have married you to him, and he is the first of my companions in submission, the most knowledgeable of them, and the greatest of them in forbearance.\""],[156,"\"I saw Ali ؓ on the pulpit, white of beard, which had filled what was between his shoulders.\" Yahya b. Sa'id added in his narration: \"on his head there were small hairs.\""],[157,"It is said, \"Ali ibn Abi Talib was a stout and robust man, with broad shoulders, long beard, bald head, big belly, thick eyebrows, and white hair and beard.\""],[158,"I asked Abu Ishaq, \"Are you older than al-Sha'bi?\" He said to me, \"Al-Sha'bi is older than me by a year or two.\" He said: And Abu Ishaq saw Ali ؓ and used to describe him to us as \"large-bellied, bald-headed.\" Shu'ba said, \"Abu Ishaq was older than Abu al-Bakhtari, but Abu al-Bakhtari did not meet Ali and did not see him.\""],[159,"I mentioned to Ibn Mas'ud the saying of Ali ؓ, and he said, \"Do you not see his head? It is like a basin, and around it is only a rim.\""],[160,"\"I saw Ali ؓ as fat, with thinning hair, as if on his side was the hide of a sheep.\""],[161,"\"Ali b. Abi Talib accepted Islam when he was eight years old.\""],[162,"\"The first to believe was Ali b. Abi Talib, when he was fifteen or sixteen years old.\""],[163,"\"Ali b. Abi Talib was killed on Friday, the seventeenth of the month of Ramadan, in the year forty.\""],[164,"\"Ali ؓ died when he was sixty-three years old.\""],[165,"\"Ali died when he was fifty-eight.\""],[166,"When Abd al-Rahman b. Muljam struck Ali ؓ and he was carried to his house, visitors came to him. He praised God (glorified and exalted be He) and extolled Him, and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said: Every person will meet what he flees from in his flight, and the appointed term drives the soul, and flight from its calamities does not avail. How many days have I pursued, examining their hidden depths about the secret of this matter, but God (glorified and exalted be He) willed only to conceal it. Alas, it is hidden knowledge. As for my testament to you: fear God (glorified and exalted be He) and associate nothing with Him, and do not neglect the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ. Uphold these two pillars, and you will be free of blame as long as they are not dispersed. Each person will be burdened according to his effort, and the ignorant will be shown leniency by a merciful Lord, a sound religion, and a knowledgeable Imam. We were among winds and the scattering of branches, under the shade of a cloud whose center has vanished, and a captive neighbor will drive it away, bringing days in succession, then it fell. After him you will be left with a hollow corpse, still after motion, silent after speech. Indeed, that is a greater admonition for those who reflect than the speech of the eloquent. Your caller is a caller on the watch for the meeting. Tomorrow you will see my days, and my secrets will be revealed. God (glorified and exalted be He) will not show me favor unless I draw near to Him through piety, so that He forgives excess. Peace be upon you until the day of inevitability. If I remain, I am the guardian of my own blood; if I perish, then annihilation is my appointed time. Forgiveness for me is a means of nearness to God, and for you it is a good deed, so forgive, may God forgive us and you. {Do you not love that God should forgive you? And God is Forgiving, Merciful.} Then he said:"],[168,"\"Its most wretched one will not be held back. By the One in whose hand is my soul, this will surely be dyed from this,\" and he recited these two lines of poetry."],[169,"He said, \"Did anything bring you here other than this?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, {That is a nation which has passed away. It will have what it earned, and you will have what you earned, and you will not be asked about what they used to do.}"],[170,"\"Ali ؓ was killed in the year forty.\""],[171,"Ali was killed in the year forty, and his caliphate was five years and six months."],[172,"He visited Ali ؓ during an illness he was suffering from. I said to him, \"We feared for you, O Abu al-Hasan, in this illness of yours.\" He said, \"But by Allah, I did not fear for myself from it, because I heard the truthful, the believed one ﷺ say: 'You will be struck with a blow here and a blow here'—and he pointed to his temples—'and its blood will flow until it dyes your beard, and the one who strikes it will be its most wretched, just as the hamstringer of the she-camel was the most wretched of Thamud.'\""],[173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed the banner to Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ when he was twenty years old."],[174,"I married Fatimah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, arrange my marriage?\" He said, \"Do you have anything to give her?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Where is your Hutama armor?\" I said, \"With me.\" He said, \"Give it to her.\""],[175,"Ali used to say during the life of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , that Allah says, \"If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?\" By Allah, we will not turn back on our heels after Allah has guided us. And by Allah, if he dies or is killed, I will surely fight for what he fought for until I die. And by Allah, I am his brother, his guardian, his cousin, and his inheritor. So, who is more entitled to him than me?"],[176,"\"Shall I not inform you of the good of this nation after its Prophet ﷺ ?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Abu Bakr.\" Then he said, \"Shall I not inform you of the good of this nation after Abu Bakr?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Umar, and if I wanted, I would inform you about the third.\""],[177,"He was sitting on the pulpit and mentioned Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and said: \"The best of this nation after its Prophet ﷺ is Abu Bakr, and the second is Umar. And if I wished to mention the third, I would mention him.\""],[178,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Exalted, for three qualities for my nation, and He granted me two and withheld one. I said, 'O Lord, do not destroy my nation by hunger.' He said, 'This is granted.' I said, 'O Lord, do not set over them an enemy from other than them'—meaning the people of polytheism—'and make them need him.' He said, 'That is granted to you.' I said, 'O Lord, do not make their might between themselves,' and He withheld this one from me.\""],[179,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said, 'O people of the gathering, lower your gazes until Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ passes.' So she passes, and upon her are two green cloaks, ؓ.\""],[180,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah curse Suhayl three times, for he used to tithe the people in the land, so Allah transformed him into a meteor.\""],[181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: \"Allah becomes angry for your anger and pleased for your pleasure.\""],[182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Use ithmid, for it grows the hair, removes the speck, and clears the vision.\""],[183,"\"I do not know but that we set out as pilgrims, proclaiming the Hajj, and neither the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor Umar ؓ exited the state of ihram until they circumambulated the House on the Day of Sacrifice and between al-Safa and al-Marwa.\""],[184,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to observe continuous fasting from pre-dawn to pre-dawn.\""],[185,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Whoever frees a Muslim or believing slave, God will shield, for every limb of that slave, a limb of his from the Fire.\""],[186,"Because he was in the lands of Hadramawt, where ʿAmr b. Nāhiḍ al-Ḥimyarī was killed. Then he fled to Makkah and became an ally of Ḥarb b. Umayya. The Ḥaḍramī’s name was ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmmār b. Rabīʿa b. Akbar b. ʿAwf b. Mālik b. ʿUwayf b. Khazraj b. Iyād b. al-Ṣadaf b. Ḥaḍramawt b. Qaḥṭān b. Kinda. Al-Ṣaʿba was the sister of al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī, and her mother was ʿĀtika bt. Wahb b. ʿAbd b. Quṣayy b. Kilāb b. Murra b. Kaʿb."],[187,"\"Umm Ṭalḥa bt. ʿUbayd Allāh accepted Islam.\""],[188,"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAmr b. Kaʿb b. Saʿd b. Taym b. Murra. He was in Syria, then he arrived and spoke to the Messenger of God ﷺ about his share, so he assigned him his share. He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And your reward,\" meaning on the day of Badr."],[189,"\"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh is given the kunya Abū Muḥammad ؓ\""],[190,"\"Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh ؓ was fair-skinned with a reddish tinge, of medium height, closer to short, broad-chested, wide-shouldered; when he turned, he turned his whole body; he had large feet.\""],[191,"\"I saw the hand of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh paralyzed; he had shielded the Messenger of God ﷺ with it on the day of Uḥud.\""],[192,"\"The finger of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh ؓ was paralyzed.\""],[193,"Sufyān, and his family used to say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Fayyāḍ.\""],[194,"Ṭalḥa visited me one day and I noticed heaviness in him. I said, \"What is the matter with you? Has something from us upset you, so that we may make amends?\" He said, \"No, and what a good wife of a Muslim man you are. But wealth has accumulated with me, and I do not know what to do with it.\" She said, \"What distresses you about it? Call your people and divide it among them.\" He said, \"O boy, bring my people to me.\" I then asked the treasurer how much he had distributed. He said, \"Four hundred thousand.\""],[195,"\"The daily income of Ṭalḥa b. ʿUbayd Allāh was one thousand complete.\""],[196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me on the day of Uhud Talhah al-Khayr, and in the expedition of Dhu al-‘Ushayrah Talhah al-Fayyad, and on the day of Hunayn Talhah al-Jud. Abu al-Qasim said: with both sīn and shīn; with sīn it is from ‘usrah (difficulty), and with shīn it is a place."],[197,"Talhah slaughtered a camel and dug a well on the day of Dhu Qarad, and he fed them and gave them to drink. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Talhah al-Fayyad!” So he was called Talhah al-Fayyad."],[198,"Al-Waqidi said: “He was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada of the year thirty-six.”"],[199,"“Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah ؓ was killed on the Day of the Camel in Jumada of the year thirty-six, and his age was fifty-two or fifty-four years. Al-Zubayr was older than him, and he was given the kunyah Abu Muhammad.”"],[200,"\"That he died.\""],[201,"From his face and his beard while he was asking for mercy for him and saying, “Would that I had died twenty years before this day.”"],[202,"I heard ‘Ali ؓ on the Day of the Camel say to his son Hasan: “O Hasan, I wish I had died twenty years ago.”"],[203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[204,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, part of humility before Allah is contentment with a lowly seat in gatherings of honor.”"],[205,"I heard the Messenger of Allah say: “One who marries among his own people is like one who plants fresh pasture in his own land.”"],[206,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There has never been prophethood except that after it came killing and crucifixion.”"],[207,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Amr b. al-‘As is among the righteous of Quraysh.”"],[208,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O ‘Amr, you are indeed a man of sound judgment in Islam.”"],[209,"“Should I lead you in prayer, are you pleased with my prayer?” They said, “Yes, and who would dislike that, O disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Any man who leads a people in prayer while they dislike him, his prayer will not pass beyond his ears.’”"],[210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is granted a favor should mention it. Whoever mentions it has thanked it, and whoever conceals it has denied it.”"],[211,"The mount and perfume of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were in my charge. A man came to him asking for one of them, and he said: “That is up to Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah.” The man came to me and informed me, but I refused him. He returned to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he replied to him with the same thing. He came to me and informed me, but I refused him. He went back to the Prophet ﷺ and said the same thing, then returned to me. I said to myself: He would not have sent him to me unless he wanted his need to be fulfilled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was hardly ever asked for something without doing it. I said: That I should take charge of the Prophet’s own saddle is dearer to me than that I should take charge of his mount. So I handed it over to him. The Prophet ﷺ then intended to travel and ordered that a mount be saddled for him. He came to me and said: Which of the two saddles was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: The one from Ta’if. So he saddled it for him, then brought it close to him. When it bolted with him, it stumbled, and he said: “Who saddled this?” They said: So-and-so. He said: “Return it to Talhah.” So it was returned to me. Talhah said: By Allah, I did not deceive anyone in Islam except him, so that the saddle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come back to me."],[212,"On the day of Uhud, I placed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my back until he stood upright and was on the rock, shielded from the polytheists. He said: “Like this,” and gestured with his hand behind my back, “this is Jibril ﷺ . He has informed me that he will not see you on the Day of Resurrection in any terror except that he will rescue you from it.”"],[213,"On the day of Uhud, an arrow struck me and I said: “Hiss!” He said: “If you had said: In the name of Allah, the angels would have flown with you while the people were looking at you.”"],[214,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he would say: “Whoever would like to look at a martyr walking on the face of the earth, let him look at Talhah b. ‘Ubayd Allah.”"],[215,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he would say: “My predecessor in this world and my predecessor in the Hereafter.”"],[216,"When the Prophet ﷺ returned from Uhud, he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, and then recited this verse: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah” — the entire verse. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these? I approached wearing two green garments, and he said: “O questioner, this is one of them.”"],[217,"On the day of Uhud the Prophet ﷺ named me Talhah al-Khayr (Talhah of Goodness), on the day of the expedition of Dhat al-‘Ushayrah Talhah al-Fayyad (Talhah the Generous), and on the day of Hunayn Talhah al-Jud (Talhah of Bounty)."],[218,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was among a group of his companions, holding a quince in his hand, turning it over. When I sat down beside him, he rolled it toward me and said: “Take it, Abu Muhammad, for it strengthens the heart, purifies the soul, and removes the heaviness of the chest.”"],[219,"From ‘Urwah, regarding those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza: al-Zubayr b. al-‘Awwam b. Khuwaylid b. Asad."],[220,"Al-Zubayr was given the kunyah Abu Abdullah."],[221,"When it was the battle of Yarmuk, they said to al-Zubayr, O Abu Abdullah."],[222,"I heard Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Urwah b. al-Zubayr say: Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was fair-skinned, tall, with a trimmed beard, light on the sides."],[223,"Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ was tall; his feet would touch the ground when he mounted a riding beast. He had much hair, and sometimes I would grasp the hair on his shoulders."],[224,"Ibn Umar heard a man say, 'I am the son of the disciple of the Prophet ﷺ.' Ibn Umar said, 'If you are from the family of al-Zubayr, then yes; otherwise, no.'"],[225,"The first to draw a sword in the path of Allah was al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam."],[226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of the Trench, 'Who will bring us news of Banu Qurayzah?' He called them a second time, then a third time, and al-Zubayr volunteered. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.'"],[227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.'"],[228,"I covered him, so I covered him. It occurred to me to glance at him, and I saw him mutilated with swords. I said, 'By Allah, I have seen marks on you that I have never seen on anyone else.' He said, 'And you have seen that?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'By Allah, there is no wound among them except that it was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in the path of Allah, may He be exalted.'"],[229,"Gabriel ﷺ descended on the day of Badr in the appearance of al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, wearing a yellow turban."],[230,"On the day of Badr, there were two horsemen with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam on a horse on the right flank, and al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad on a horse on the left flank."],[231,"That I entrust it to him: al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, for he is a pillar among the pillars of the religion."],[232,"Do you hear what he says to me? Zubayr struck him until he fell."],[233,"Abdullah said to him, \"Will you make my mother a target for your oath?\" So he rushed upon him and freed her from him, and she became separated from him. He said, \"I was a boy who sometimes grabbed the hair on Zubayr's shoulders.\""],[234,"\"O my sons, do not marry your daughters except to suitable matches.\" They said, \"O our father, who are the suitable matches?\" He said, \"The descendants of Zubayr b. al-Awwam.\""],[235,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say, \"Zubayr was killed at the age of sixty-four, and he was killed in the year thirty-six.\""],[236,"\"Zubayr embraced Islam at the age of sixteen and was killed at the age of sixty-something.\""],[238,"Zubayr b. al-Awwam embraced Islam at the age of eight, and he emigrated at the age of eighteen. Zubayr's uncle would hang Zubayr in a mat and smoke him with fire, saying, \"Return to disbelief,\" and Zubayr would say, \"I will never disbelieve.\""],[239,"\"When Umar ؓ was killed, Zubayr erased his name from the register.\""],[240,"The killer of Zubayr approached Zubayr, and Zubayr turned to face him. He said, \"I remind you of Allah,\" and Zubayr refrained from him until he did that several times. Then Zubayr said, \"May Allah fight him—he reminds by Allah ﷻ yet forgets Him.\""],[241,"On the Day of the Camel, Ali ؓ saw heads being severed. He took al-Hasan ؓ by the hand and placed it on his belly, then said, \"O my son, what good is there after this?\""],[242,"I was sitting with Ali ؓ when the head of Zubayr ؓ was brought. Ali ؓ said, \"Give news of Hellfire to the killer of the son of Safiyyah. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Zubayr.'\""],[243,"About a military expedition that the Messenger of God ﷺ undertook, and he was killed at the age of sixty-something, and he was from al-Basra, at about a barid away."],[244,"Al-Zubayr was killed in the year thirty-six. Ibn Jurmuz killed him, and with him were al-Nu'man b. Zimam and Abu al-Madrahi, two men from Banu Tamim. He was killed in Wadi al-Siba' and buried there."],[245,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, Uthman, al-Miqdam b. al-Aswad, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and Muti' b. al-Aswad made their wills to al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam."],[246,"Ali, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas were of the same age."],[247,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A single suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.\""],[248,"\"On the day of Uhud, it was as if I was seeing servants on her thighs encouraging people.\""],[250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in the morning prayer in the mosque of Madinah. When he finished, he said: \"Which of you will follow me to the delegation of the jinn tonight?\" The people fell silent, and none of them spoke. He said that three times. Then he passed by me walking, took me by the hand, and I walked with him until all the mountains of Madinah receded from us, and we were led to a flat land. There were tall men, as if they were spears, having tucked their garments between their legs. When I saw them, a severe trembling seized me until my legs could not hold me from fear. When we drew near to them, the Messenger of God ﷺ drew a line with the big toe of his foot on the ground and said to me: \"Sit in the middle of it.\" When I sat down, everything I felt of apprehension left me. The Prophet ﷺ went between me and them and recited the Qur'an in a raised voice until dawn broke. Then he came back, passed by me, and said: \"Follow.\" I walked with him, and we went a short distance. Then he said to me: \"Look back and see if you can see anyone where those had been.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I see many dark shapes.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ lowered his head to the ground, strung a bone with dung, threw it at them, and said: \"Those were rightly guided from the delegation of a people—they are the delegation of Nasibin. They asked me for provision, so I made for them every bone and dung.\" Al-Zubayr said: \"So it is not permissible for anyone ever to clean oneself with bone or dung.\""],[251,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. Abd Awf b. Abd al-Harith b. Zuhrah b. Kilab."],[252,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ was called Abd al-Ka'bah in the pre-Islamic era, so the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Abd al-Rahman."],[253,"My name was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of God ﷺ named me Abd al-Rahman."],[254,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. Abd Awf b. Abd al-Harith b. Zuhrah, whose kunya is Abu Muhammad, was present at Badr."],[255,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr, concerning those who were present at Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ from the Banu Zuhrah b. Kilab b. Murrah: Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. al-Harith b. Zuhrah."],[256,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik, from Hisham b. Urwah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ, “How did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in touching the corner?”—meaning the Black Stone. Abd al-Rahman said, “I touched it and left off.” The Messenger of God said, “You have done correctly.”"],[257,"A companion of mine [said]: The Commander of the Faithful did not give you a good ruling until he asked the man. Umar ؓ heard part of his speech, so Umar struck him with the whip as a beating. Then he turned to me to strike me, so I said, “O Commander of the Faithful, I did not say anything; he said it.” So he left me. He said: Then he said, “You wanted to kill what is sacred and transgress the fatwa.” Then he said, “In a person there are ten traits: nine good and one evil. That evil one corrupts it.” Then he said, “Beware of the company of young men.”"],[259,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ used to wear a shirt of karabisi cloth reaching to the middle of his calf, and his cloak would strike his buttocks."],[260,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf had lost his two front teeth, was gap-toothed, left-handed, and lame. He was injured at Uhud, so his teeth were broken, and he received twenty wounds or more, some of which affected his leg, so he became lame."],[262,"While Aisha ؓ was in her house, she heard a sound from which Madinah trembled. She said, “What is this?” They said, “A caravan has arrived for Abd al-Rahman b. Awf from Syria, consisting of seven hundred camels.” Aisha ؓ said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘I saw Abd al-Rahman b. Awf entering Paradise crawling.’” This reached Abd al-Rahman, so he came to her and asked her about what had reached him, and she told him. He said, “I call you to witness that it, with its loads, its saddle-frames, and its saddle-cloths, is for the sake of God.”"],[263,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf gave half his wealth in charity during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ—four thousand. Then he gave forty thousand [dirhams]. Then he gave forty thousand dinars. Then he equipped five hundred horses in the path of God. Then he equipped one thousand five hundred camels in the path of God. Most of his wealth came from trade."],[264,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “If the plague breaks out in a land and you are in it, do not leave it, fleeing from it. If it breaks out in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it.” Abu al-Qasim said: Thus it was narrated by Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid b. Tamim and Sufyan b. Husayn, and Ibn Abi Dhiʾb differed from them."],[265,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “This pain, or this illness, is a punishment with which those before you were punished. So if it is in a land where you are not, do not go down upon it; and if it is in a land where you are, do not leave fleeing from it.” He said: Then ‘Umar ؓ turned the people back that year."],[266,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[267,"Al-Qa‘nabī narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from ‘Abd al-Ḥamīd b. ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Zayd b. al-Khaṭṭāb, from ‘Abd Allāh b. al-Ḥārith b. Nawfal, from ‘Abd Allāh b. ‘Abbās, from ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. ‘Awf ؓ, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[268,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of this epidemic in a town, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs while you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[269,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs in a land while you are there, fleeing from it must not make you leave.”"],[270,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear of it in a land, do not advance upon it; and if it occurs while you are there, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This epidemic is a punishment with which Allah destroyed some nations, and some of it remains on the earth, coming at times and going at times. So if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave it; and if you hear of it in a land, do not go there.”"],[272,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “This pain, or sickness, is a punishment with which some nations before you were punished; then it remained afterwards on the earth, going one time and coming another. So whoever hears of it in a land, they should not advance upon it, and whoever is in a land where it occurs, fleeing from it must not make him leave.” And the wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Layth."],[273,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “It is a punishment that befell those before you, or a torment that befell those before you. So if you hear of it in a town, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a town, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This epidemic is something with which the nations before you were punished, and there remains on the earth a remnant of it. It occurs at times and goes at times. So if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land where you are not, do not enter upon it.”"],[275,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “It is a defilement that befell those before you. So if you hear of it in a town, do not enter it upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a town, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear of it in a land, do not enter upon it; and if it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave fleeing from it.”"],[277,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, 'Which part of the night is best for hearing (prayers)?' He said, 'The last part of the night. Then prayer is accepted until you pray the dawn. Then there is no prayer until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands as a spear. Then there is no prayer until the sun declines. Then prayer is accepted until the sun is a spear-length or two spear-lengths high. Then there is no prayer until the sun sets.'"],[278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ missed a man from his companions. He said, 'Where were you? For I did not see you. Did you not attend the prayer?' He said, 'Yes, but I came when the people had already settled, and I disliked stepping over people's necks.' He said, 'You did well.'"],[279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The official, when he is appointed and takes what is right and gives what is right, is like the one striving in the way of God until he returns to his home.'"],[280,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The midday prayer is from the night prayer.' So I asked Abd al-Rahman b. Humayd about the midday. He said, 'When the sun declines.'"],[281,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf ؓ heard a man from Banu Hashim saying, 'I am the closest of people to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said, 'Another is closer to him than you, but you have his lineage.'"],[282,"Umama bt. Abi al-As became critically ill. Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ saying to him, 'My daughter is critically ill.' He sent to his daughter, 'To God belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He leaves.' She became critically ill a second time, and she sent to him, 'My daughter is critically ill.' He sent to his daughter, 'To God belongs what He takes, and to Him belongs what He leaves.' Then it was the third time, and the Prophet ﷺ came to her. She brought the child out to him, and her soul was rattling in her chest. With the Prophet ﷺ were some of his companions. His eyes shed tears until he grasped his beard. He noticed them while they were looking at him, and he said, 'What is with you that you look?' They said, 'O Messenger of God, we saw you become tender.' He said, 'It is a mercy that God ﷻ places wherever He wills. And God will have mercy tomorrow on the merciful among His servants.'"],[283,"Sleep was cast upon us on the day of Uhud."],[284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'A little understanding is better than much worship, and the best of your deeds are the easiest.'"],[285,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Gently, O Talha, for he witnessed Badr as you did. And the best of you is the best to his clients.'"],[286,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Satan, may God curse him, said, \"The owner of wealth will never be safe from me through one of three things: I will come to him with them morning and evening – his taking wealth without its right, spending it without its right, and making it beloved to him so that he withholds it from its right.\"'"],[287,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, who am I?' He said, 'Sa'd b. Malik b. Uhayb b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhra. Whoever says otherwise, upon him is the curse of God.'"],[288,"To Saʿd: \"Thus is the thought concerning you, O Abū Isḥāq.\""],[289,"Saʿd said: O Messenger of God, who am I? He said: \"You are Saʿd b. Mālik b. Ahyab b. ʿAbd Manāf b. Zuhrah, so whoever says otherwise, upon him is the curse of God.\""],[290,"The mother of Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ was Ḥamnāh bt. Abī Sufyān b. Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams b. ʿAbd Manāf, and her mother was the daughter of Abī Sarḥ b. Ḥabīb b. Jadhīmah b. Naṣr b. Mālik b. Ḥasal b. ʿĀmir b. Luʾayy b. Ghālib."],[291,"\"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ had curly hair, a hairy body, was tall, dark-skinned, and flat-nosed.\""],[292,"\"My father was a short, stout, thick-set man with a large head and coarse fingers, and he had witnessed Badr.\""],[293,"\"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ used to dye his hair black.\""],[294,"\"Saʿd used to dye his hair black.\""],[295,"\"On the day of Badr, I, ʿAmmār, and Saʿd shared in the spoils. Saʿd got two captives, while I and ʿAmmār got nothing.\""],[296,"I heard Saʿd say: \"No one embraced Islam except on the day I embraced it, and indeed I remained for seven days while I was one-third of Islam.\""],[297,"\"Saʿd was the last of the Emigrants to die ؓ.\""],[298,"My father said: \"He died at the age of eighty-three, and he died ten miles from Madinah, and was carried on the shoulders of men to Madinah. Marwān was the governor of it at that time. He embraced Islam when he was nineteen years old.\""],[299,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Saʿd died while Marwān was governor of Madinah, and he prayed over him. He died in the year fifty-five.\""],[300,"Sa'd died in al-ʿAqīq, in his palace, ten miles from Madinah, and was carried on the shoulders of men to Madinah. It is said that he died when he was seventy-some years old."],[301,"He said, “I embraced Islam when I was nineteen years old, and he died in the year fifty-five.”"],[302,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ died in the time of Muʿāwiyah ؓ after his first Hajj, when he was eighty-three years old."],[303,"Saʿd was the last of the Muhājirūn to die ؓ."],[304,"Ibn Masʿūd had a claim of money against Saʿd ؓ. Ibn Masʿūd said, “Pay the money that you owe.” Saʿd said, “Woe to you! What is between me and your money?” He said, “Pay the money that you owe.” Saʿd said, “By Allah, I see that you will meet evil from me. Are you anything but Ibn Masʿūd, a slave of the Banū Hudhayl?” He said, “Yes, by Allah, I am Ibn Masʿūd and you are Ibn Ḥamnah.” Hāshim b. ʿUtbah said to them, “You are both companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. People look to you.” Saʿd threw down a stick that was in his hand, then raised his hands and said, “O Allah, Lord of the heavens...” ʿAbdullāh said to him, “Say words, and do not curse.” So he fell silent. Then Saʿd said, “By Allah, were it not for fear of Allah, I would call upon you with a supplication that would not miss you.”"],[305,"While Saʿd was walking, he passed by a man who was reviling ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, and al-Zubayr. Saʿd said to him, “You are reviling people for whom Allah has already decreed what He has decreed. By Allah, you must stop reviling them, or I will supplicate Allah ﷻ against you.” The man said, “You frighten me as if you were a prophet.” Saʿd said, “O Allah, this man reviles people for whom You have already decreed what You have decreed, so make him an example today.” Then a Bactrian camel came, the people made way for it, and it trampled him. I saw the people following Saʿd, saying, “May Allah answer your supplication, O Abū Isḥāq.”"],[306,"The people of Kufa complained about Saʿd to ʿUmar ؓ. He sent men to ask about him in Kufa. They did not come to any mosque of the people of Kufa except that they praised him and spoke well of him, until they came to a mosque of the Banū ʿAbs. A man called Abū Saʿdah stood up and said, “Since you have asked us, he does not lead raiding parties, he does not judge fairly, and he does not distribute equally.” Saʿd said, “O Allah, if he is lying, blind him, prolong his poverty, and expose him to trials.” ʿAbd al-Malik said, “I saw him accosting slave women in the streets. When they asked him, ‘How are you, Abū Saʿdah?’ he would say, ‘Old, blind, poor, and afflicted. The supplication of Saʿd has overtaken me.’” Abū al-Qāsim said, “Abū Saʿdah is the grandfather of Abū Bakr b. Abī Shaybah.”"],[307,"She was called Zīrā, and she was wearing a new shirt. The wind uncovered her, so ʿUmar ؓ struck her with a whip. Saʿd came to stop him, and he struck him with the whip. Saʿd went to supplicate against ʿUmar, but ʿUmar handed him the whip and said, “Take retribution.” So he forgave ʿUmar ؓ."],[310,"To his son when death came to him: “O my son, you will never meet anyone more sincere to you than I am. When you want to pray, perform your ablution well, then pray a prayer such that you do not think you will pray after it. Beware of greed, for it is present poverty. And cling to despair [of what people have], for that is wealth. Beware of doing or saying anything for which you would have to apologize. Do what seems right to you.”"],[311,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ: “No one embraced Islam on the day I did, and I remained for seven days while I was a third of Islam.”"],[312,"I heard Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas say: \"Indeed, I am the first Muslim man to shoot an arrow in the cause of God, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[313,"The Prophet ﷺ combined his parents for him. He said: \"A man from the polytheists had incited the Muslims, so the Prophet ﷺ said to Sa'd: 'Shoot, may my father and mother be your ransom.'\" He said: \"So I drew a blunt arrow and struck his side. He fell, and his private parts were exposed, and the Prophet ﷺ laughed until I saw his molars.\""],[314,"\"Shroud me in it, for in it I faced the polytheists on the day of Badr, and I was keeping it for this.\""],[315,"\"When my father prayed in the mosque, he was brief but completed the bowing and prostration; when he prayed at home, he prolonged the bowing, prostration, and prayer.\" I said: \"O father, when you pray in the mosque you are brief, but when you are alone at home you lengthen it.\" He said: \"O my son, we are leaders who are followed.\""],[316,"On the day of Badr, I was shooting before the Prophet ﷺ. I placed the arrow on the bowstring and said: 'O God, make their feet slip, terrify their hearts, and do to them such and such.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O God, answer Sa'd.'"],[317,"\"You disobeyed me concerning this arbitration.\" A dark-complexioned youth stood up to him and said: \"By God, you did not forbid us; rather, you commanded us and destroyed us. When something you disliked happened, you absolved yourself and saddled us with your sin.\" 'Ali ؓ said to him: \"What have you to do with this speech? May God disfigure you! By God, there was a community and you were insignificant in it. When the strife appeared, you emerged in it like the horns of a goat.\" Then he turned to the people and said: \"For God is the standing of Sa'd b. Malik and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar. By God, if it was a sin, it is small and forgiven; and if it was a good deed, it is great and appreciated.\""],[318,"When 'Umar ؓ was wounded, he began advising the people of the council: \"If Sa'd is chosen, then that is it; otherwise let the one appointed seek his help, for I did not remove him out of incapacity or betrayal.\""],[319,"He said: \"Sit here for the people.\" Sa'd apologized to him and swore that he had not spoken the word that had reached the Commander of the Faithful."],[320,"\"I will not fight until you bring me a sword with two eyes, a tongue, and lips that recognizes the believer from the disbeliever, for I have struggled while knowing jihad.\""],[321,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas approached. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"This is my maternal uncle; let a man show me his uncle.\""],[322,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Killing a Muslim is disbelief, insulting him is wickedness, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days.\""],[323,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.\""],[324,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My father used to maintain ties of kinship, and he was, and he was—so where is he?\" He said, \"In the Fire.\" It was as if the bedouin was hurt by that, so he said, \"O Messenger of God, then where is your father?\" He said, \"Wherever you pass by the grave of a disbeliever, give him tidings of the Fire.\" The bedouin later accepted Islam, and he said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ tasked me with a burden; I never passed by the grave of a disbeliever except that I gave him tidings of the Fire.\""],[325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever desires humiliation for Quraysh, God will humiliate him.\""],[326,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.\""],[327,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, part of happiness is a righteous wife, a good dwelling, and a good mount. And indeed, part of misery is a bad wife, a bad dwelling, and a bad mount.\""],[328,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"It is a punishment that afflicted those before you. If it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and if it occurs in a land, do not enter it.\""],[329,"Three verses from the Book of God (Mighty and Sublime) were revealed concerning me. When the prohibition of wine was revealed, I had been drinking with a man; I opposed him and he opposed me, and I became rowdy with him and wounded him. Then God (Exalted is He) revealed, {O you who believe, wine and gambling...} up to His saying {So will you desist?} And there was revealed concerning me, {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents. His mother carried him with hardship} to the end of the verse. And there was revealed, {O you who believe, when you consult the Messenger in private, give charity before your private consultation.} So I offered a barley grain, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"You are indeed frugal.\" Then the other was revealed, {Are you afraid to give charities before your private consultation?} the entire verse."],[330,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa.\""],[331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.\""],[332,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Rabah b. 'Abd Allah b. Qurt b. Razah b. 'Adi b. Ka'b; his kunya is Abu al-A'war, and his mother is Fatimah bt. Na'jah b. Umayyah b. Khuwaylid, from Khuza'ah."],[333,"Sa'id b. Zayd was tall, dark-skinned, and hairy."],[334,"I heard Abu Hafs Amr b. Ali say: Sa'id b. Zayd was dark-skinned, tall, and very hairy."],[335,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl arrived from Syria after the Messenger of God ﷺ had returned from Badr. He spoke to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he allotted him his share. He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God, as they claim?\" He said, \"And your reward.\""],[336,"Sa'id b. Zayd arrived from Syria after the Prophet ﷺ had arrived from Badr. He spoke to the Prophet ﷺ about his share, so he said to him, \"Your share.\" He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And your reward.\""],[337,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl died in the year fifty-one, or in the seventies, and was buried in Madinah. He died at al-Aqiq, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas and Ibn Umar went down into his grave. His kunya was Abu al-A'war."],[338,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas washed Sa'id b. Zayd at al-Sajara."],[339,"She stole my land and incorporated it into her land. Sa'id said, \"I would not steal from her after I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever steals a span of land will be collared with it down to the seven earths.'\" She said, \"I will not dispute with you after this.\" Sa'id said, \"O God, if she is lying, take away her sight and kill her in her land.\" Her sight was taken away, and she fell into a pit in her land and died."],[340,"I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr saying, \"Sa'id ibn Zaid died in the year fifty-one in Medina.\""],[341,"I did not wash from the washing of Sa'id; I washed only because of the heat."],[342,"A man from Syria said, \"What is holding you back?\" He said, \"Until Sa'id b. Zayd comes and gives allegiance, for he is the most noble of the people of the land. When he gives allegiance to the people, the people give allegiance.\""],[343,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There will be after me trials, and in them there will be, and there will be.\" We said, \"If we live to see that, we will perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for my Companions.\""],[345,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the trials, so we said, \"O Messenger of God, will everyone tried in them perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for you.\""],[346,"He mentioned a tribulation — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — like patches of dark night. He said, \"People will go in it in the quickest going.\" It was said, \"Will all of them perish?\" He said, \"The killing will be enough for them.\""],[347,"Indeed, the one you seek will appear in your land. He turned back saying: \"At Your service, truly, truly, in worship and servitude. I seek piety, not the transient. Is an emigrant like one who said: I seek refuge in what Ibrahim sought refuge, while he was standing? I disown for You, O God, a submissive, compelled one. Whatever You burden me with, I will bear.\" Then he fell down and prostrated to the Kaaba. He said: Zayd b. Amr passed by the Prophet ﷺ and Zayd b. Haritha while they were eating from a traveling provision of theirs. They invited him, so he said, \"O son of my brother, I do not eat from what is slaughtered on the stone altars.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ was not seen eating from what is slaughtered on the stone altars from that day until he was sent as a prophet. He said: Sa'id b. Zayd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Zayd was as you saw, or as you have heard. Pray for forgiveness for him.\" He said, \"Yes,\" so he prayed for forgiveness for him, \"for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone.\""],[348,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced Hasan and said: “O Allah, I have loved him, so love him.”"],[349,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[350,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in defense of his property until he is killed is a martyr.”"],[351,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[352,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever unjustly diminishes even a handspan of the earth, Allah will encircle him on the Day of Judgment from seven earths.\""],[353,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on Hira. It shook, so he struck it with his foot and said: “Be still, Hira, for upon you is none but a prophet, a siddiq, or a martyr.” And these people were with him: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and myself—meaning himself."],[354,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Among the worst forms of usury is a man’s attack on the honor of a Muslim without right. Indeed this womb-relationship is a branch of the Most Merciful; whoever severs it, Allah forbids him Paradise.”"],[355,"Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah—he is Amir b. Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah b. Hilal b. Uhayb b. Dabbah b. al-Harith b. Fihr—left no descendants. The mother of Abu Ubaydah was Umm Ghanm bt. Jabir b. Abd b. al-Ala b. Amir b. Umayrah b. Wadi'ah b. al-Harith b. Fihr."],[356,"“Abu Ubayd Amir b. Abd Allah b. al-Jarrah.”"],[357,"The father of Abu Ubaydah kept confronting Abu Ubaydah on the Day of Badr, but Abu Ubaydah kept avoiding him. When he persisted, Abu Ubaydah headed for him and killed him. Then Allah ﷻ revealed about him, when he killed his father, this verse: {You will not find a people who believe in Allah and the Last Day} to the end of the verse."],[358,"Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah was present at Badr from the Banu al-Harith b. Fihr."],[359,"He got ahead of him. Indeed I saw the two forelocks of Abu Ubaydah bobbing as he galloped behind him on an Arabian horse."],[360,"It is said that Mu'adh b. Jabal prayed over him."],[361,"Its matter concerning al-Harith himself, and he feared for it when he saw it. Abu Ubaydah swore to him by Allah that he would not love to have in exchange for it red camels."],[362,"Syria was under two commanders: Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Yazid b. Abi Sufyan. Abu Ubaydah died and appointed as his successor his maternal uncle Iyad b. Ghanm, one of the Banu al-Harith b. Fihr, and Umar ؓ confirmed him. Then Iyad died, and he appointed in his place Sa'id b. 'Amir b. Judhaym. Then Sa'id b. 'Amir died, and he appointed in his place 'Umayr b. Sa'd."],[363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among the prayers, there is no prayer more excellent than the Fajr prayer on Friday in congregation, and I do not think anyone among you who attends it but will be forgiven.\""],[364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, this matter (Islam) began as mercy and prophethood, then it will become mercy and caliphate, then it will become a cruel monarchy, then it will become tyrannical rule, and finally corruption on the earth. They will make silk, sex trade, and alcohol permissible, and they will be provided sustenance based on that, and they will be victorious until they meet Allah.\""],[365,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, entrust me to a man of good teaching. He entrusted me to Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, then said: I have entrusted you to a man who will teach you well and discipline you. I went to Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah while he and Bashir b. Sa'd, Abu al-Nu'man b. Bashir, were conversing. When they saw me, they fell silent. I said: O Abu Ubaydah, by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not tell me this. He said: You came while we were speaking of a hadith we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so sit until we tell you. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Among you is prophethood, then there will be a caliphate upon the pattern of prophethood, then there will be kingship and tyranny.\""],[366,"I passed by the mosque and found Ali and al-Abbas ؓ sitting. They said: O Usama, ask permission for us to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali and al-Abbas are at the door wanting to enter upon you. He said: \"Do you know what brought them?\" I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what brought them. He said: \"But I know what brought them. Give them permission.\" They entered upon him, and Ali said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you which of your family is most beloved to you? He said: \"Fatimah daughter of Muhammad\" ﷺ. Ali said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I am not asking you about your family. He said: \"The most beloved of my family to me is the one whom Allah has blessed and whom I have blessed: Usama.\" He said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Then you.\" Al-Abbas said: You have made your uncle the last of them? He said: \"Ali preceded you in the Hijrah.\""],[367,"Usama went to a palm tree, tapped it, and extracted its heart, then fed it to his mother. They said to him: What led you to do this when you see the palm tree has reached a thousand? He said: \"My mother asked me for it, and she does not ask me for anything I am able to give but that I give it to her.\""],[368,"Usama b. Zayd was called to the command until he died. They said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him, then did not remove him until he died."],[369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Usama is the most beloved of people to me.\""],[370,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr regarding his lineage: Usama b. Zayd b. Harithah b. Sharahil b. Ka'b b. Abd al-Uzza b. Yazid b. Imri al-Qays, the Kalbi, and Allah and His Messenger ﷺ blessed him."],[371,"I heard our elders say: The inscription on the ring of Usama b. Zayd was 'the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[372,"\"I saw people among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapping their lower garments midway up their shins. He mentioned Ibn Umar, Zayd b. Arqam, Usama b. Zayd, and al-Bara b. Azib ؓ.\""],[373,"The Prophet ﷺ clothed him with a Coptic garment from what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted him. I clothed my wife with it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is the matter with you that you do not wear the Coptic garment?\" I said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: \"Tell her to put a lining under it, for I fear it may reveal the outline of her bones.\""],[374,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, I descended and the people descended to Madinah. I entered upon him while he had become silent and was not speaking. He began raising his hand to the sky and lowering it upon me, and I knew that he was supplicating for me."],[375,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ja'far: \"Your physical form is like my physical form, and you are from me, and you, O 'Ali, are from me and the father of my child.\""],[377,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Jam' (Muzdalifah), he prayed Maghrib and 'Isha there."],[378,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military expedition to Al-Hurqu'at.\""],[379,"He informed him (the Prophet), saying, \"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Indeed, I have divorced and remembered the hadith.'\""],[380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, this plague is a punishment,\" then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[381,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, this plague is a punishment,\" then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[382,"He informed him: \"I rode with the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey, on a packsaddle, on a velvet cloth,\" then he mentioned the hadith in full."],[383,"He departed with the Prophet ﷺ on the evening of 'Arafah. He went to a narrow pass, made his mount kneel, relieved himself, then came and performed ablution while Usamah poured water for him. He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the prayer?' He said: 'The prayer place is ahead of you.'"],[384,"Gloom entered upon the Prophet ﷺ. I said: 'What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Jibril ﷺ promised me that he would come to me, but he has not come to me for three days.' He said: And there was a dog. Usamah said: I put my hand on my head and shouted. He said: 'What is the matter with you, O Usamah?' I said: 'A dog.' So the Prophet ﷺ ordered it and it was killed. Then Jibril came to him and said: 'What is the matter with you that you did not come to me? When you promise me, you do not break it.' He said: 'We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images.'"],[385,"The Messenger of Allah said, \"Is there anyone eager for Paradise? By the Lord of the Kabah, it is a radiant light, a [breezes] of sweet fragrances, a steady flowing river, a lovely and beautiful spouse in an everlasting garden and an abode of joy.\""],[386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions used to accept pardon from the polytheists and the People of the Book as Allah, Mighty and Sublime, commanded them, and they were patient in the face of harm. Allah, Mighty and Sublime, said: 'You will surely hear from those who were given the Scripture before you and from those who associate others with Allah much abuse' [Quran 3:186]. The Prophet ﷺ used to interpret the command of pardon as Allah had commanded him until Allah gave permission concerning them. When the Prophet ﷺ raided Badr and Allah killed those He killed of the disbelievers among the leaders of Quraysh, Ibn Ubayy and those with him among the polytheists said: 'This is a matter that has taken hold. So pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam.' And they became Muslims."],[387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to visit 'Abdullah b. Ubayy during the illness in which he died, and I was with him. He recognized death in him and said: 'I used to forbid you from loving the Jews.' He said: 'As'ad b. Zurarah died, so what?' When he died, his son 'Abdullah came to him and said: 'Abdullah has died, so give me your shirt to shroud him in it.' He removed his shirt and clothed him with it."],[388,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim, nor does a Muslim inherit from a disbeliever, and the people of two religions do not inherit from each other.'"],[389,"I thrust a spear into a man while he was saying 'There is no god but Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said to Usamah: 'What will you do with \"There is no god but Allah\" on the Day of Resurrection?' He repeated that several times until I wished that I had not become Muslim before that moment."],[390,"I sought permission for some people from among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and he granted them permission. There he was, with his head covered with a striped Yemeni cloak of his. He uncovered his head and then said: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[391,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to al-Huraqat.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[392,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “A man will be brought” and then he mentioned the hadith."],[393,"That he “saw the Prophet ﷺ enter the House” — the hadith."],[394,"\"The Prophet wiped over the Khuff and the Khimar.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 101)"],[395,"“The daughters of the Prophet ﷺ were sent” — the hadith."],[396,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Indeed Allah, exalted be He, does not love the obscene and the one who acts obscenely.”"],[397,"From Usama: “The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to raid the people of Ibna’ in the morning and to burn.”"],[398,"A man arrived from one of the rural areas and was afflicted with pain, so he returned. The Prophet ﷺ said: “I hope that its mountain pass will not appear to us,” meaning the mountain pass of Madinah."],[399,"Indeed, I do not say to a man, “You are the best of people,” after I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection” — the hadith."],[400,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This plague is a punishment and torment with which those before you were punished. So if it is in a land, do not leave it, and if it falls in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it.”"],[401,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, Allah does not like obscenity and vulgarity.\""],[402,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed Allah, exalted be He, hates the obscene and foul-mouthed.”"],[403,"That the Prophet ﷺ “entered the House and walked until he reached its middle, drew near to the wall, and entered between Usama and Bilal” — the hadith."],[404,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House and saw images. He called for water and began wiping them out, saying, “May Allah fight a people who depict what they do not create.”"],[405,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zhuhr in the intense heat."],[406,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Deeds are presented to Allah (mighty and sublime be He) on Monday and Thursday, and Allah forgives except whatever is between two people bearing mutual hatred or one who severs family ties.”"],[407,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"All of them are from this Ummah.\""],[408,"The Prophet ﷺ said during his final illness: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[409,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim.” Ma‘mar, Sufyan b. Husayn, and Salih b. Kaysan added in their narration that the Prophet ﷺ said, “And did ‘Aqil leave us any house?”"],[410,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, where will we stay tomorrow?” He said, “And did ‘Aqil leave us any house or property? Our place is at Khayf of Banu Kinanah where Quraysh swore an oath upon disbelief.”"],[411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued riding in his usual manner after departing from Jam‘."],[412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[414,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[415,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I have not left behind any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have not left among people any trial more harmful to men than women.”"],[417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have not left behind me any trial more harmful to men than women.\""],[418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I stood at the gate of Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I saw that the people of hard work were held back from entering, except for those who were from the people of hell, as they were ordered to be taken to the fire.\""],[419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever abandons three Friday prayers without an excuse is written among the hypocrites.\""],[420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had Umm Salamah with him when Jibril ﷺ came and spoke as was decreed. When he stood up, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Umm Salamah, who is this?\" She said: \"Dihyah.\" She said: \"By Allah, I did not think he was anyone but Dihyah until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon about the news of Jibril ﷺ.\" Mu'tamir said: My father said to Abu 'Uthman: \"From whom did you hear it?\" He said: \"From Usamah.\""],[421,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When a believer is praised to his face, faith grows in his heart.\""],[422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The most grateful of people to Allah are the most grateful of them to people.\""],[423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of Hamal, he and Bilal, and Bilal came out to them and informed them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks.\""],[425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[426,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[428,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[429,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in credit sales (nasi'ah).\""],[430,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in the deferred sale (nasīʾa).”"],[431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale.”"],[432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale or in a delay (naẓira).”"],[433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt.”"],[434,"He narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt.”"],[435,"“It is lawful with an increase or decrease if it is hand to hand.” Abu Salih said: I asked Abu Saʿid al-Khudri about that, and he said: “It is unlawful except equal for equal.” So I informed Abu Saʿid of what Ibn Abbas said, and I informed Ibn Abbas of what Abu Saʿid al-Khudri said. They met while I was with them. Abu Saʿid al-Khudri began and said: Ibn Abbas, what is this fatwa you give to people about selling gold for silver? You command them to buy it with an increase or a decrease, hand to hand. Ibn Abbas said: I have not accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ longer than you, and this is Zayd b. Arqam and al-Baraʾ b. ʿAzib; they say: We heard the Prophet ﷺ…"],[436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is in the deferred sale.”"],[437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Riba is only in the deferred sale.”"],[438,"I heard Usama b. Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in debt,” or he said, “in the deferred sale.”"],[439,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no riba in a hand-to-hand transaction; riba is only in debt.”"],[440,"He said to Ibn Abbas ؓ: Did you accompany the Prophet ﷺ longer than I did? I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Gold for gold, equal for equal, and silver for silver, equal for equal.” Ibn Abbas said: Usama narrated to me that that was a deferred sale."],[441,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no riba except in the deferred sale.”"],[442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in deferred payment.\""],[443,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[444,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[445,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no riba in what is hand to hand.\""],[446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Riba is only in deferred payment.\""],[447,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is no riba except in deferred payment.\""],[448,"\"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah.\""],[449,"\"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah.\""],[450,"He was with Abu al-Minhal, saying: A partner of mine in Kufah sold dirhams for dirhams with a difference between them. I said: I do not think this is permissible. He said: I sold them in the market and no one found fault with me for that. So I went to al-Bara' b. 'Azib and asked him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while our trade was like this, and he said: \"Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm in it; whatever is deferred, there is no good in it.\" And I went to Zayd b. Arqam, for he was a greater trader than me. I went to him and mentioned that to him, and he said: Al-Bara' spoke the truth. Al-Humaydi said: \"This is abrogated; it is not to be acted upon.\""],[451,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri met Ibn 'Abbas and testified concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Gold for gold and silver for silver, like for like. Whoever increases has committed riba.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"I repent to Allah ﷻ from what I used to give as a legal opinion.\" Then he retracted."],[452,"\"I see no harm in what is hand to hand.\" Then I came to Makkah the following year, and he had \"forbidden it.\""],[453,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: O Allah, I repent to You from exchange; this is only my opinion, and here is Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating it from the Prophet ﷺ."],[454,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and I turn to Him in repentance from sarf.\""],[455,"Abu Sa'id said to Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah have mercy on him: \"Repent to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\" He said: \"I seek forgiveness from Allah and I turn to Him in repentance.\" He said: \"Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold for gold and silver for silver, and said: 'Indeed I fear for you riba?'\" I said to 'Atiyyah: \"What is riba?\" He said: \"Increase and surplus between them.\""],[456,"O people, there is no harm in sarf as long as it is hand to hand; riba is only in nasi'ah. So a word spread among the people of the east and the west until when the season ended, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri entered upon him and said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, have you consumed riba and fed it to others?\" He said: \"Did I do that?\" He said: \"Yes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba. Silver for silver, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba. Barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, like for like; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba.'\" Until when the next year came, Ibn 'Abbas came and I came with him. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O people, last year I spoke a word from my own opinion, and I seek forgiveness from Allah for it and turn to Him in repentance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Gold for gold, weight for weight, like for like, its ore and its minted; whoever increases or asks for increase has committed riba.'\" And he repeated to them these six types."],[457,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When zina and riba appear in a town, they have made lawful for themselves the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not appoint the death of a servant in a land except that He has made for him a need therein.\""],[459,"That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his mount did not lift its foot at a run until he came to Jam'.\""],[460,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ at 'Arafat and greeted him. The birds were on the heads of his companions. The Bedouins came to him from here and there: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in such and such? Is there any harm upon us in such and such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O servants of Allah, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from a Muslim man wrongfully; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said: \"Seek treatment, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He placed for it a cure, except old age.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best of what people have been given?\" He said: \"People have not been given anything better than good character.\""],[461,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when Bedouins came to him, many people from here and there. The people fell silent, no one speaking but them. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in such and such?\" Regarding things from people's affairs that are not objectionable. He said: \"O servants of Allah, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from a man wrongfully; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any harm upon us in seeking treatment?\" He said: \"Seek treatment, O servants of Allah, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not place a disease except that He placed for it a cure, except old age.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best of what a person is given?\" He said: \"Good character.\""],[462,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when the Bedouins came and asked him, \"What is the best thing that people are given?\" He said, \"Good character.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?\" He said, \"Yes, you should seek medical treatment, for indeed Allah ﷻ has not created any illness except that he has also created its cure, except for one illness.\" They asked, \"What is it?\" He said, \"Old age.\""],[463,"\"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ , and the Bedouins came to him saying, 'We are facing difficulty in such and such matter, we are facing difficulty in such and such matter, is there any harm in it?' He said, 'O servants of Allah, Allah has removed all difficulty except for the one who borrows from someone and intends to repay him back. That person is the one who faces difficulty and destruction.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?' He said, 'Yes, seek medical treatment. Indeed, Allah has not revealed a disease except that He has also revealed its cure, except for one disease.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a person can be given?' He said, 'Good manners.'\""],[465,"I attended the Prophet ﷺ and he was asked which actions are the best. He said, \"Having good character.\""],[466,"“I saw the Bedouins asking the Prophet ﷺ: ‘Is there any harm in such and such, is there any harm in such and such?’ He said to them: ‘O slaves of Allah! Allah has only made harm in that which transgresses the honor of one’s brother. That is what is sinful.’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! Is there any sin if we do not seek treatment?’ He said: ‘Seek treatment, O slaves of Allah! For Allah does not create any disease but He also creates with it the cure, except for old age.’ They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing that a person may be given?’ He said: ‘Good manners.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3436)"],[467,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what is the most excellent of what a Muslim is given?\" He said: \"Good character.\""],[468,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ as if birds were on our heads; none of us was speaking. Then people came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about such and such; give us a ruling about such and such.\" He said: \"O people, Allah has removed harm, except for one who borrows from his brother a loan; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed. Should we seek treatment, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Yes, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down for it a cure, except one disease.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and what is it?\" He said: \"Old age.\" They said: \"Then who is the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah?\" He said: \"The best of them in character.\""],[469,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ as a pilgrim, and the people would come to him. A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did sa'i before tawaf\" or \"I delayed something.\" He said to them: \"No harm, except upon a man who borrows from the honor of a Muslim man while he is wronging; that is the one who is in harm and is destroyed.\""],[470,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who shaved before slaughtering. He said: \"No harm; let him shave.\""],[471,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when some people came to him and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you seek medical treatment?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed, Allah ﷻ has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure.\""],[472,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked during his Hajj: What is the best thing people have been given? He said, \"Good character.\""],[473,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while people were asking him, and someone said, \"I shaved before sacrificing,\" and another said, \"I did this and that before Fajr.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no harm, there is no harm.\""],[474,"The Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him if there was any difficulty in something for them. The Prophet replied, \"Allah has only placed difficulty on a man who borrows from his brother's wealth. That is what causes difficulty and destruction.\" He also said, \"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down a cure for it, except for one disease, old age.\""],[475,"The Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which people are best?\" He said, \"Those with the best character.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said, \"Yes, seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure.\""],[476,"The Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such? Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" He said, \"There is no sin. Allah has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from the honor of his brother; that is the sin.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment?\" He said, \"Seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure, except old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a human being has been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[477,"Some Bedouin people came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing swords, and they crowded around him asking him questions. We feared for the Prophet ﷺ, so we drew near to them. He said: I heard them saying, \"Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such? Is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O people, Allah has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from the honor of his Muslim brother; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment for such-and-such? Should we seek treatment for such-and-such?\" He said, \"Seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a remedy, except old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a Muslim servant has been given in this world?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[478,"A Bedouin said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is best for a Muslim man?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[479,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when some Bedouin people came to him asking him from his right and from his left, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" twice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ has removed the sin except for one who borrows from a Muslim man wrongfully\" or he said \"with wrong.\" \"That is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we seek treatment for such-and-such?\" twice. He said, \"Yes, seek treatment, for Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure, except for one disease: old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing people have been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[480,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the Bedouins came from all directions, until they surrounded him, and the people became silent. They called out, \"O Messenger of Allah, can you cure?\" He replied, \"Yes, indeed Allah has not created any disease except that He has also created its cure, except for one disease.\" They asked, \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Old age.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing that can be given to a person?\" He replied, \"Good manners.\" They called out, \"O Messenger of Allah, we face difficulties in various matters. What should be done about that?\" He said, \"O servants of Allah, Allah has not created any difficulty except for those who borrow from others, for that is what causes difficulty and loss.\""],[481,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Hajj saying, \"Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then your nearest.\" Then some people came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Banu Yarbu' have killed some of us.\" He said, \"No soul bears the sin of another.\" Then a man asked him about forgetting to throw the pebbles. He said, \"Throw, and there is no sin.\" Then another man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I forgot the circumambulation.\" He said, \"Circumambulate, and there is no sin.\" Then another came who had shaved before slaughtering. He said, \"Slaughter, and there is no sin.\" He said: They did not ask him about anything that day but that he said, \"No sin, no sin.\" Then he said, \"Allah ﷻ has removed the sin except for a man who borrows from a Muslim; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" And he said, \"Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a remedy, except old age.\""],[482,"When the Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ, we took advantage of their roughness to ask him questions. They came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon us in such-and-such?\" He said, \"There is no sin. The sin has been removed from the servants of Allah, except for one who borrows from the honor of his brother wrongfully; that is the one who has sinned and is ruined.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing a human being has been given?\" He said, \"Good character.\" This is how Wahb b. Isma'il narrated it from Muhammad b. Qays, and he erred in it. The correct version is from Usamah b. Sharik."],[483,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and his companions we as if they birds were perched on their heads (i.e. they were still and attentive)."],[484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Any man who goes out to divide my community, strike his neck.\" This is how Zayd b. 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib narrated it from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah from Usamah, but the correct version is from 'Arfajah. Likewise, Muhammad b. Bishr narrated it from Mujalid."],[485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever divides my community while they are united, strike his head, whoever he may be.\""],[486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah's hand is with the community. If anyone deviates from it, Satan snatches him as a wolf snatches a sheep from the flock.\""],[487,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, \"My Companions were weighed last night. Abu Bakr ؓ was weighed, then 'Umar ؓ was weighed, then 'Uthman ؓ was weighed.\" This is how Yazid b. Harun narrated it. Sa'dawayh narrated it from 'Abd al-A'la b. Abi al-Masawir from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah from Qutbah b. Malik from 'Arfajah."],[488,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"In the black seed there is healing for every disease except death.\""],[489,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and nights; and for the resident, one day and night.\""],[490,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one enters Paradise by his deeds.\" We said, \"Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, not even me, unless Allah ﷻ envelops me in mercy from Him.\" And he placed his hand on his head."],[491,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is none of you but with him is a devil.\" We said, \"And with you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And with me, except that Allah ﷻ helped me against him, so he submitted.\""],[492,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral bier was brought near to him so that he could pray over it. He turned and saw a woman approaching, and he said, \"Turn her back.\" So they turned her back repeatedly until she disappeared. When he saw that she had disappeared, he said the takbir over it."],[493,"We prayed Isha in Basra and were rained upon. Then I came and sought to open [the door]. My father Usamah said to me: \"I saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we were rained upon, and the sky did not wet the bottoms of our sandals. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: 'Pray in your dwellings.'\""],[494,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a rainy day, and he ordered a caller who called out: \"The prayer is in the dwellings.\""],[495,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we set out to Hunayn when seventeen nights of Ramadan had passed. It coincided with a Friday, a rainy day. The Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called out among the people: \"The prayer is in the dwellings.\""],[496,"I witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a light rain—meaning a drizzle—fell upon us. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out: \"Whoever wishes to pray in his dwelling, let him pray.\""],[497,"I went out one rainy night to the mosque. When I returned and sought to open [the door], my father said to me: \"I saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah, and a rain fell upon us that did not wet the bottoms of our sandals. Then the caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pray in your dwellings.'\""],[498,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a rainy Friday. He ordered a caller who called out: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[499,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"If a nation among the nations testifies, and they are forty or more, Allah accepts their testimony—or he said: He confirms their testimony.\""],[500,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There is no man over whom one hundred pray except that he is forgiven.\""],[501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fast from one brightness to the next.\""],[502,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement.\""],[503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzlement.\""],[504,"A man freed a share of a slave, so the Prophet ﷺ allowed his emancipation and said: \"Allah has no partner.\""],[505,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the skins of beasts of prey.\" Yazid b. Harun added: \"to be used as floor coverings.\""],[506,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[507,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[508,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade that the skins of beasts of prey be used as floor coverings.\""],[509,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I complain to you about whispers that I feel in my chest. When I am in prayer, I do not know whether to finish my prayer in a sitting position (after two units) or in a prostrating position (after one unit).\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you experience this, raise your right index finger and stab it in your left thigh and say, 'In the name of Allah,' for it is the weapon of the Satan.\""],[510,"From his father, who had accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: There were two women, one of whom struck the other with a tent pole, killing her and what was in her womb. The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the blood money for the woman was to be paid, and for the fetus a ghurra, a male or female slave, or a horse, or two camels, or such and such from sheep. A man from the clan of the killer said: \"How can we pay blood money, O Messenger of Allah, for one who did not eat, drink, or cry out? Such a one should be disregarded.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Are you a rhymester?\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the inheritance of the woman belonged to her husband and her child, and that the blood money was upon the male relatives of the killer."],[511,"It is said that Haml ibn Malik had two wives, one of them was Hudhayyah and the other was 'Amirayah. Hudhayyah struck the stomach of 'Amirayah with a thin stick or a whip, causing her to miscarry a dead fetus. Hudhayyah then went to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ with her brother, 'Imran ibn 'Uwaymir, and they told him the story. The Prophet said, \"Leave it,\" and 'Imran said, \"O Prophet of Allah, should the one who has not eaten, drunk, or shouted be blamed? She committed such an act.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Leave the wrath of the Bedouins to me, in return there will be a slave or a servant, or five hundred sheep, or a horse, or twenty camels.\" 'Imran said, \"O Prophet of Allah, she has two sons who are the leaders of the community and it is more appropriate for them to be compensated by their mother.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have more right to make a decision regarding your sister than her children do.\" 'Imran said, \"I have nothing to decide on.\" The Prophet said, \"O Haml ibn Malik, who was at that time responsible for such charity, being the husband of both wives and the father of the killed fetus, take from the charity under your supervision twenty and one hundred sheep.\" And so he did."],[513,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when our camel stumbled. I said: \"May the devil perish!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not say 'May the devil perish,' for he then grows until he becomes like a house and says: 'By my power.' Say: 'In the name of Allah,' for he then becomes like a fly.\""],[514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Delay the evening prayer, and you will increase in clemency.\""],[515,"The angels descended on the day of Badr wearing turbans, and on that day al-Zubayr had a yellow turban."],[516,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “Allah does not thank one who does not thank people.”"],[517,"He prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr with the Prophet ﷺ, and he prayed near him, so he prayed two light rak'ahs, and I heard him say, “O Allah, Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, Israfil, and Muhammad, I seek refuge in You from the Fire,” three times."],[518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the owner of the plot that was added to the Mosque of Madinah, and its owner was a man from the Ansar. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “You will have for it a house in Paradise.” He said: Then 'Uthman came and said to him, “You will have for it ten thousand,” and he bought it from him. Then 'Uthman ؓ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, buy from me the plot that I bought from the Ansari.” So he bought it from him for a house in Paradise. 'Uthman said, “I bought it for ten thousand dirhams.” The Prophet ﷺ placed a brick, then he called Abu Bakr ؓ and he placed a brick, then he called 'Umar ؓ and he placed a brick, then 'Uthman ؓ came and placed a brick, then he said to the people, “Place [bricks],” and they placed them."],[519,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say, “The name of Abu al-Malih is 'Amir b. Usama.”"],[520,"He was called Asram. He was among the group who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He brought him an Abyssinian slave boy of his whom he had purchased in that region and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I bought this one and I would like you to name him and supplicate for blessing for him.” He said, “What is your name?” He said: He said, “Asram.” He said, “Rather, you are Zur'ah.” He said, “What do you want for him?” He said, “I want him as a shepherd.” He said, “Then he is 'Asim.” And the Prophet ﷺ closed his hand."],[521,"From 'Urwah: Among those who witnessed Badr was Ubayy b. Ka'b b. Qays b. 'Ubayd b. Zayd b. Mu'awiya b. 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[522,"I saw Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ with white hair and beard; he did not dye them."],[523,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “May knowledge be pleasant for you, Abu al-Mundhir.”"],[524,"Ubayy had some harshness in his character."],[525,"The companions of judicial authority among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were six: 'Umar, 'Ali, 'Abd Allah, Ubayy, Zayd, and Abu Musa."],[526,"Ubayy b. Ka'b ؓ, whose kunya was Abu al-Mundhir, died in Madinah in the year twenty-two, though one says in the year thirty, during the caliphate of 'Uthman ؓ."],[527,"Ibn Numayr, and some of them say, “during the caliphate of Uthman ؓ.”"],[528,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of the son of Adam has been set as a parable for this world. Consider what comes out of the son of Adam, even if he seasons it and salts it, he knows what it becomes.”"],[529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see a man expressing grief with the grief of Jahiliyyah, then rebuke him and do not use kunyah.”"],[530,"The last verse revealed to the Prophet ﷺ was {There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves} to the end of the verse."],[531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever wishes that a building be raised for him and that his rank be elevated, let him pardon those who wrong him, and give to those who deprive him, and maintain ties with those who cut him off.”"],[532,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at the watering place of Banu Ghifar and said, “O Muhammad, Allah ﷻ commands you to teach your community the Quran in one mode.” Then he said, “In two modes,” until he reached seven modes. So whoever recites any one of them, it is as he said."],[533,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say concerning {And He bound them to the word of God-consciousness}, “There is no god but Allah.”"],[534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes to reveal a mountain of gold, for which nine-tenths of them will fight.”"],[535,"The verdict that water (bath) is necessary when there is emission given by the people (in the early days of Islam) was due to the concession granted by the Messenger of Allah in the beginning of Islam. He then commanded to take a bath (in such a case). Abu Dawud said : By Abu Ghassan is meant Muhammad b. mutarrif. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 215)"],[536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abu al-Mundhir, I have been commanded to present the Quran to you.” Ubayy said, “In Allah I have believed, at your hand I have submitted, and from you I have learned.” He said, so the Prophet ﷺ repeated the statement, “O Messenger of Allah, and I was mentioned there?” He said, “Yes, by your name and lineage in the highest assembly.” He said, “Then recite, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[537,"He said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of fever?” He said, “Good deeds continue to flow for its bearer as long as a foot twitches or a vein throbs.” Ubayy said, “O Allah, I ask You for a fever that does not prevent me from going out in Your path, nor from going out to Your House, nor to the mosque of Your Prophet.” He said, and from then on Ubayy was never without fever."],[538,"He had a store of dates that was decreasing, so he guarded it one night and found an animal resembling a young man who had reached puberty. He greeted it and it returned the greeting. He said, “Are you a jinn or a human?” It said, “No, rather a jinn.” He said, “Then give me your hand.” It gave him its hand, and its hand was like a dog’s paw and its hair was like a dog’s hair. He said, “This is how the jinn are created.” It said, “The jinn know that there is no man among them stronger than me.” He said, “Then what brought you here?” It said, “It reached us that you love charity, so we came to get some of your food.” He said, “Then what protects us from you?” It said, “This verse in Surat al-Baqarah: {Allah—there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer}. Whoever says it in the evening is protected from us until morning, and whoever says it in the morning is protected from us until evening.” When morning came, he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, “The evil one told the truth.”"],[539,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “If a human being had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of a human being except dust. Then Allah ﷻ turns in mercy to those who repent.”"],[540,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He recited {You have reached from my presence} with tashdid (doubling)."],[541,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, \"Whoever attains his parents or one of them and then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him.\""],[542,"From Ibn 'Umarah al-Ansari, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed in his house facing both qiblahs. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may I wipe over the leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes, for a day.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and two days?\" He said, \"Yes, and three.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and three?\" He said, \"Yes, and as long as you wish.\""],[543,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in his house. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, may I wipe over the leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"For a day?\" He said, \"Yes, and two days.\" He said: I said, \"And three, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes, and as much as appears to you.\""],[544,"From 'Urwah concerning those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge: Usayd b. Hudayr b. Simak b. 'Ubayd b. Rafi' b. Imri' al-Qays b. Zayd b. 'Abd al-Ashhal, and he was a naqib (leader)."],[545,"\"Usayd b. Hudayr died, whose kunyah was Abu Yahya, in the year twenty, and 'Umar ؓ carried him between the two posts of the bier until he placed him in al-Baqi' and prayed over him.\""],[546,"\"Usayd b. Hudayr died in the year twenty, in Sha'ban.\""],[547,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal: Usayd b. Hudayr, and he was a naqib (leader)."],[548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will see after me selfishness (atharah).\" They said, \"What do you command us?\" He said, \"Be patient until you meet me at the Hawd (basin).\""],[550,"From his mother Fatimah bt. Husayn ؓ, from 'A'ishah ؓ, that she said: Usayd b. Hudayr was among the most virtuous of people, and he used to say: If I could always be as I am in any one of three states, I would be of the people of Paradise, and I have no doubt about that: when I recite the Qur'an, or when I listen to it being recited, and when I hear a sermon of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when I attend a funeral. And I have never attended a funeral but that I told myself nothing except what is done to it and what it is becoming."],[551,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that if you find it with a man who is not suspected, then if its master wishes he may take it for the price, and if he wishes he may pursue its thief. Then Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman ؓ ruled accordingly after him. Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah sent to Marwan: You are not the one to pass judgment against me, nor is Usayd, in what I have been entrusted with. Rather, I pass judgment upon you two, so carry out what I have commanded you. So Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter to me, and I said: By God, I will never rule by it."],[552,"While he was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he had jest in him, he was telling people things to make them laugh. The Messenger of God ﷺ poked him in his side, so he said: Let me get even with you. He said: Get even. He said: You are wearing a shirt and I am not wearing a shirt. So the Messenger of God ﷺ lifted his shirt, and he embraced him and began kissing his flank, saying: I only wanted this, O Messenger of God."],[553,"A man was making people laugh in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ pointed with his finger at his side. He said: You have killed me, O Messenger of God. He said: Retaliate. He said: You are wearing a shirt and I was not wearing a shirt. So the Messenger of God ﷺ lifted his shirt until his flank showed, and he embraced him and began kissing his flank, saying: May my father and mother be your ransom; this is what I wanted."],[554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution with the meat of camels.\""],[555,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Pray in sheep pens, and do not perform wudu' from their milk, and do not pray at camel resting places, and perform wudu' from their milk.'"],[557,"\"He was reading Surah Al-Baqarah while his horse was tied.\""],[559,"When something like a cloud covered me, in which there were things like lamps, while a woman was sleeping beside me and she was pregnant, and a horse was tied in the house, I feared that the horse would bolt and the woman would be startled and miscarry her child. So I stopped my prayer, and I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ in the morning, and he said: 'Recite it, O Usayd, for that was an angel who listened to the Qur'an.'"],[560,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, last night I was reciting Surat al-Kahf when something came and covered my mouth. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'That was the Sakinah; it came to listen to the Qur'an.'"],[561,"I was praying on a moonlit night, and I had tied up my horse, and it moved suddenly, and I was startled. Then it moved again, and I raised my head, and there was a canopy that had covered me, and it had come between me and the moon, and I was startled, so I entered the house. In the morning I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Those were the angels; they came to listen to your recitation of the Qur'an at the end of the night: Surat al-Baqarah.' And Usayd had a beautiful voice."],[562,"He said: O Messenger of God, while I was reciting Surat al-Baqarah, I heard a thud behind me, and I thought my horse had been set loose. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Recite it, O Abu 'Atik.' He said: I turned around, and there were lamps hanging between heaven and earth, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was saying: 'Recite it, O Abu 'Atik.' He said: O Messenger of God, I could not continue. He said: 'Those were the angels who descended for the recitation of Surat al-Baqarah. Indeed, if you had continued, you would have seen wonders.'"],[564,"The people of two households from my people came to me and said: Speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ for us, that he may distribute to us from these dates. So I went to him and spoke to him, and he said: 'Yes, we will distribute to each household a half, and if God gives us more, we will give them more.' I said: May God reward you well on our behalf. He said: 'And you, may God reward you well on my behalf, O company of the Ansar, for you are, as far as I know, chaste and patient. Indeed, you will meet after me preference being given to others, so be patient until you meet me.'"],[565,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of God ﷺ considered Rafi' b. Khadij too young. His uncle Zuhayr, may God have mercy on him, said to him: O Messenger of God, he is a man who can shoot. So the Messenger of God ﷺ allowed him. Then an arrow struck him in his throat, and his uncle brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My brother's son has been struck by an arrow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If you wish, we will remove it, and if you wish, we will leave it; for if he dies while it is in him, he dies as a martyr.'"],[566,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A prayer in the mosque of Quba' is like an 'umrah.'"],[567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leasing land."],[568,"From 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those killed on the Day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar from Banu Sa'idah: Usayd b. Yarbu'."],[569,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of al-Yamamah among the Ansar from Banu Sa'idah: Usayd b. Yarbu'."],[570,"And in it [i.e., that year], Abu 'Amrah al-Mazini died in the year thirty-seven."],[571,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition he undertook. The people suffered severe hunger, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to slaughter some of their riding camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was about to grant them permission for that, when 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"Consider, O Messenger of Allah, if we slaughter our riding camels and then meet our enemy tomorrow while we are hungry and on foot?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you think, O 'Umar?\" He said: \"Call the people to bring the remnants of their provisions, then supplicate to Allah for us for blessing in them, for Allah ﷻ will surely suffice us through your supplication, if Allah wills.\" He said: \"It was as if a covering had been upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was removed.\" So he called for a cloth and ordered it to be spread. Then he called the people to bring the remnants of their provisions. They came with what they had; some people brought a large bowl of food or a handful, and some brought something like an egg. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered it to be placed on that cloth. Then he supplicated for blessing in it and spoke as Allah willed him to speak. Then he called out in the army, and they came. Then he ordered them, and they ate and were satisfied, and they filled their vessels and their provision bags. Then he called for a small water skin and placed it in front of him. Then he called for water and poured it into it. Then he spat into it and spoke as Allah willed him to speak. Then he inserted his little finger into it. I swear by Allah, I saw the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gushing forth springs of water. Then he ordered the people, and they drank and gave water to their mounts and filled their water skins and their water vessels. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars appeared. Then he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. No one meets Allah with these two on the Day of Resurrection except that he enters Paradise, no matter what he has done.\""],[572,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who believe in you but have not seen you, and affirm you but have not seen you? What will they have?\" He said: \"Blessedness be to them, twice. Those are of us, those are with us.\""],[573,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr among the Ansar: Abu Salit Usayr b. 'Amr."],[574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys, and the cooking pots were boiling, so we overturned them."],[575,"The people suffered severe hunger during the Battle of Khaybar, so they went to their donkeys in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and slaughtered them, then threw the meat into cooking pots. While they were boiling, the prohibition of them came down upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prohibition of the donkeys you are cooking has come down,\" so the pots were overturned."],[576,"The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against eating the flesh of donkeys came to us while the cooking pots were boiling with them, so we overturned them."],[577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs the full ritual bath on Friday, and goes early and arrives early, and draws near to the imam and listens attentively, he will have for every step he takes the reward of fasting for a year and standing in prayer for a year, and that is easy for Allah.\""],[578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs the full ritual bath and goes early and arrives early, then sits close to the imam and listens and remains silent, he will have for every step he takes the reward of a year's fasting and standing in prayer.\""],[579,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ that he said on Friday: “Whoever bathes and washes himself, comes early, draws near and listens, for every step he takes from his house to the mosque he will have the reward of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[580,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then goes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, and does not engage in idle talk, a year’s deeds will be written for him.” Ibn Jabir said: I narrated this hadith to Yahya b. al-Harith al-Dhimari, and he said: I heard Abu al-Ash‘ath narrate it from Aws b. Aws from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he said: “For every step he will have the deeds of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.” Ibn Jabir said: “Yahya remembered and I forgot.” Al-Walid said: I mentioned that to Abu ‘Amr al-Awza‘i, and he said: “The hadith is established that for every step he will have the deeds of a year.”"],[581,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then comes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, draws near and listens, and does not engage in idle talk, for every step he takes he will have the deeds of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself, goes early and arrives early, walks and does not ride, draws near to the imam, and does not engage in idle talk, he will have the reward of a year of fasting and standing in prayer.”"],[583,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ he said: “When Friday comes, and one of you washes his head and bathes, then goes early and arrives early, draws near, listens, and remains silent, for every step he takes he will have a year of fasting and a year of standing in prayer.”"],[584,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever bathes and washes himself on Friday, then goes early or leaves or arrives early, then draws near, remains silent, and listens, for the measure of every step he takes he will have like the reward of standing in prayer for a year and fasting for a year.”"],[585,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the best of your days is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it the trumpet will be blown, and on it the blast will occur. So increase your prayers upon me on it, for your prayers are presented to me.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our prayers be presented to you when you have decayed? He said: He says: “You have become worn out.” He said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.”"],[586,"\"Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, 'Jesus, son of Mary, will descend near the white minaret to the east of Damascus.'\""],[587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever lies about his Prophet, or about his own eyes, or about his parents will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[588,"I heard Aws b. Aws al-Thaqafi say: I came to the Prophet ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif. He said: I was at the lower part of the qiblah, in which there was no one except the Prophet ﷺ sleeping, when a man came to him and whispered to him. Then he said: “Go and kill him.” Then he said: “Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me, except by its right.”"],[589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while we were in a tent in the mosque of Madinah. He took hold of something from the tent, and a man came to him and whispered something that could not be known what he said. Then he said: “Go and tell them to kill him.” Then he said: “Perhaps he testifies that there is no god but Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Go and tell them to release him, for I have been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they say it, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me, except by a rightful matter, and their reckoning is with Allah ﷻ.”"],[590,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ while his hair was disheveled and I was listening. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Go to them and say to them, 'Kill him.' Then, he called him back after he had left and said, 'Perhaps he will say, 'There is no god but Allah.' \" The man said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Tell them to release him, for I have been commanded to fight against people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, their blood and wealth become inviolable to me, except for its right, and their account is with Allah.\""],[591,"He informed him, saying: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was narrating to us and reminding us, when a man came to him and whispered to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Go and kill him.” When the man turned away, he called him and said: “Does he testify that there is no god but Allah?” He said: Yes. He said: “Take him and let him go, for I have only been commanded to fight the people until they say there is no god but Allah. When they do that, their blood and their wealth become forbidden to me by its right, and their reckoning is with Allah.”"],[592,"“We stayed with the Prophet ﷺ for half a month. I saw him turn to his right and I saw him turn to his left, and I saw his sandals had two straps.”"],[593,"I stayed with the Prophet ﷺ for half a month and saw him praying while wearing two unlined sandals, and I saw him spit to his right and to his left."],[594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: While I was sitting, Jibril ﷺ came to me and carried me and entered me into the Garden of my Lord ﷻ. While I was sitting, an apple was placed in my hand, and the apple split into two halves, and out of it came a maiden the like of whose beauty I had never seen and the like of whose loveliness I had never seen. She was glorifying Allah with a glorification the like of which the first and the last had never heard. I said, 'Who are you, O maiden?' She said, 'I am from the hūr al-ʿīn. Allah ﷻ created me from the light of His Throne.' I said, 'For whom are you?' She said, 'For the wronged caliph, ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ.'"],[595,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a delegation of Thaqīf, and we were lodged with him in a tent of his. Our brothers from the allies lodged with al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us after the evening prayer and talk to us, and most of his talk was complaining about the Quraysh. He would say, 'It is not equal: we were in Makkah despised and oppressed, but when we came to Madinah, the war was alternately for us and against us.' One night he was late in coming to us and stayed away long, so we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you have been late.' He said, 'A portion of the Qur'an came upon me, and I disliked to go out until I had completed it.' We asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divide the Qur'an into portions?' They said, 'He divided it into threes, fives, sevens, nines, elevens, thirteens, and the portion of the Mufaṣṣal.'"],[596,"\"We arrived at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us every night and tell us stories. One night, he came to us later than usual, so we asked him, \"What's the matter with you?\" He replied, \"I received a portion of the Quran, and I wanted to finish it before I leave.\""],[597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man's recitation of the Qur'an without looking at the mushaf is a thousand degrees, and his recitation in the mushaf is multiplied over that up to two thousand degrees.'"],[598,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and asked for water to be poured over his hands three times. Shuʿbah said: He was an Arab man, so I said to him, 'What does istawkaf mean?' He said, 'He washed his hands three times.'"],[599,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come to a water outlet, meaning a purification place, and perform ablution and wipe over his feet."],[600,"He would say, 'Hand me my sandals,' and he would put them on and pray in his sandals. He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.'"],[601,"I saw my father wiping over the sandals. I said, 'Do you wipe over them?' He said, 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ do it.'"],[602,"We passed by some water of the Bedouins, and my father stood and urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his sandals. I said, 'Will you not take them off?' He said, 'I will not add to what I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[603,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his sandals.\""],[604,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his sandals, then stand for prayer."],[605,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in his sandals."],[606,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in his sandals."],[607,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me, and with him was Abu Bakr ؓ, at Khadawat between al-Juhfah and Harsha, both of them on a single camel, heading to al-Madinah. Ibn al-Rida' mounted them on a stud camel of his, and he sent with them a servant of his called Mas'ud. He said to him: \"Take them by the hidden passes of the roads which you know, and do not leave them until they have fulfilled their need from you and from your camel.\" So he took them through Thaniyyat al-Zamha', then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Kubah, then he brought them to Ahya', then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then he brought them from the mountain pass of Dhat Kasht, then he took them through al-Mudlajah, then he took them through al-'Ishalah, then he took them through Thaniyyat al-Murrah, then he brought them into al-Madinah, and they had fulfilled their need from him and from his camel. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mas'ud back to his master Aws b. 'Abd Allah. He was negligent, not branding the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to tell Aws to brand them on their necks with the mark of a horse's fetter.\" Sakhr b. Malik said: \"And it is, by Allah, our brand today. The fetter of a horse, as I see it, is two rings and a line drawn between them.\""],[608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Hadathan during the days of Tashriq, and they called out: \"None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.\""],[609,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Give Zakat al-Fitr as a sa' of food.\" Our food that day was wheat, dates, and raisins. This is the wording of Zayd b. Akhzam. Sha'tham said: \"Our food that day was dates, raisins, and dried curd.\""],[610,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Asram b. Fihr b. Ghanm b. 'Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Aws b. al-Samit and his brother 'Ubadah."],[611,"From Ibn Shihab, concerning the naming of whoever witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu Awf ibn al-Khazraj, or Aws ibn al-Samit."],[612,"One day he came in to me and spoke to me about something while he was somewhat irritable about it, so I answered him back. He said: \"You are to me like the back of my mother.\" Then he went out and sat in the gathering of his people. Then he returned to me and wanted me for himself, but I refused him. He struggled with me and I struggled with him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said: \"No, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach it until Allah judges between me and you with His judgment.\" So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining to him of what I had suffered from him. He said: \"Your husband and your cousin? Fear Allah.\" And Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah has indeed heard the statement of the woman who pleads with you concerning her husband} up to the mention of the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Tell him to free a slave.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no slave to free.\" He said: \"Then let him fast two consecutive months.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he is not capable of fasting.\" He said: \"Then let him feed sixty poor people.\" She said: \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he has nothing to feed them with.\" He said: \"We will help him with a basket of dates.\" A basket holds thirty sa's. I said: \"And I will help him with another basket.\" He said: \"You have done well. Tell him to give it in charity.\""],[613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When it is the day of Fitr, the angels stand at the gates of the roads and call out: 'Go forth, O assembly of Muslims, to a Generous Lord who bestows good and then rewards abundantly for it. You were commanded to pray at night and you prayed; you were commanded to fast during the day and you fasted; you obeyed your Lord, so receive your prizes.' When they have prayed, a caller announces: 'Indeed your Lord has forgiven you, so return rightly guided to your mounts.' It is the day of prizes, and that day is called in heaven the Day of Prizes.\""],[614,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When it is the morning of Fitr, the angels stand at the mouths of the roads and call out: 'O assembly of Muslims, go forth to a Merciful Lord who bestows good and rewards abundantly for it. You were commanded to fast during the day and you fasted; you obeyed your Lord, so receive your prizes.' When they have prayed the Eid prayer, a caller from heaven announces: 'Return to your homes rightly guided; I have forgiven all your sins.' That day is called in heaven the Day of Prizes.\""],[615,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever walks with an oppressor to help him, knowing that he is an oppressor, has left Islam.\""],[616,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever drinks wine, flog him. If he repeats—he said it three times—on the fourth, kill him.\""],[617,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah: Aws b. Mu'adh b. Aws al-Ansari.\""],[618,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Aws b. Mu'adh b. Aws, no offspring for him."],[619,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who witnessed al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar, and who witnessed Badr: Aws b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir, a Badri."],[620,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed Badr: Aws b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir, who had no surviving offspring."],[621,"From Urwah regarding naming those of the Ansar who were martyred on the day of Uhud, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. al-Mundhir."],[622,"About Ibn Shihab's account of the names of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr among the Ansar, then from the Banu Auf bin Al-Khazraj, Aws bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Khauliy."],[623,"\"Those who descended into the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were al-Fadl, Qutham, Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Aws b. Khawli.\""],[624,"Ali b. Abi Talib, al-Fadl and Qutham the two sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended into the burial niche of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Abu Layla Aws b. Khawli said to Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, \"I adjure you by Allah and by our share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So Ali ؓ said, \"Descend,\" and he descended."],[625,"When the Prophet ﷺ became gravely ill, and Aishah and Hafsah were with him, Ali ؓ entered. When he saw him, he raised his head and said, \"Draw near to me.\" So he leaned against him and remained with him until he ﷺ passed away. When he died, Ali ؓ rose and locked the door. Al-Abbas ؓ came with the Banu Abd al-Muttalib and stood at the door. Ali ؓ began to say, \"May my father be ransomed for you, pure in life and pure in death.\" A sweet fragrance spread that they had never smelled the like of before. Ali ؓ said, \"Let al-Fadl b. Abbas enter to me.\" The Ansar said, \"We adjure you by Allah concerning our share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So they brought in a man from among them called Aws b. Khawli, carrying a water jar in one of his hands. They heard a voice in the house: \"Do not strip the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; wash him as he is in his shirt.\" So Ali ؓ washed him, inserting his hand beneath the shirt while al-Fadl held the cloth away from him, and the Ansari poured the water. On Ali's ؓ hand there was a cloth, and he inserted his hand."],[626,"It is said: Sulaym Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Daws. Muhammad b. Ishaq mentioned him among those who witnessed Badr."],[627,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. Yazid b. Asram."],[628,"From Ibn Shihab regarding naming those of the Ansar who witnessed al-Aqabah, then from the Banu al-Najjar: Aws b. Thabit."],[629,"From Urwah regarding naming those of Quraysh who were killed at Ajnadayn, then from the Banu Abd Shams b. Abd Manaf: Aban b. Sa'id b. al-As."],[630,"\"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ abolished every blood claim that existed in the time of ignorance.\""],[631,"From Aban al-Muharibi, who was one of the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Abd al-Qays, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no servant who says in the morning, 'Praise belongs to Allah, my Lord; I associate nothing with Him, and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' except that he remains forgiven of his sins until evening. And if he says it in the evening, he passes the night forgiven of his sins until morning.\""],[632,"Madaan had a dispute with a man over some land, and they brought the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. He ruled that one of them should take an oath. The other said, \"Will he take away my land?\" He said, \"If he swears by Allah falsely,\" Ibn Awn said, \"he said something severe.\""],[633,"A man from Kindah and a man from Hadramawt brought a dispute before the Prophet ﷺ concerning a piece of land in Yemen. The Hadrami said, 'O Messenger of God, it is my land; this man's father usurped it from me.' He said to the Kindi, 'What do you say?' He said, 'I say it is my land, in my possession; I inherited it from my father.' He said to the Hadrami, 'Do you have any proof?' He said, 'No, but let him swear, O Messenger of God, by the One besides whom there is no god, that he does not know it is my land which his father usurped.' The Kindi prepared to take the oath, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'No man seizes property but that he will meet God ﷻ on the Day of Resurrection with it as a leper.' So the Kindi returned it."],[634,"A man of the Hadramis disputed with a man of ours called al-Hafshish before the Prophet ﷺ concerning a piece of land belonging to the latter. The Prophet ﷺ said to the Hadrami, 'Bring your witnesses to prove your right; otherwise, he will swear to you.' He said, 'My land is too great a matter for him not to swear concerning it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The oath of a Muslim stands behind what is greater than that.' He went to swear, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'If he swears falsely, God ﷻ will admit him to the Fire.' Al-Ash'ath went and informed him, and he said, 'Make peace between me and him.' So he made peace between them."],[635,"I once bought my oath for seventy thousand, because I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever seizes the right of a Muslim by an oath will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him.'"],[636,"In this verse, it was revealed to me that I had a piece of land in the possession of my paternal uncle. So, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"Do you want me to arbitrate or shall I uphold his oath?\" I said, \"If he has taken an oath, then you should arbitrate, O Messenger of Allah.\" So, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes an oath, while he is still a sinner and uses it to wrongfully take the wealth of a Muslim, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\" So, Allah revealed the verse: \"Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their [own] oaths for a small price...\" until the end of the verse."],[637,"This verse was revealed concerning me. I had a dispute with a man before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...}"],[638,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever swears a patient oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim will meet God while He is angry with him.' Then al-Ash'ath entered and said, 'What did Abu 'Abd al-Rahman tell you?' We said, 'Such and such.' He said, 'It was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over some land of ours. I brought the case to the Prophet ﷺ, but I had no proof. He said, \"Shall I make him swear?\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, then he will swear.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever swears an oath to seize thereby the property of a person while he is lying in it will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him.\" And the verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...} to the end of the verse."],[639,"This verse was revealed concerning me. There was a dispute between me and a man over some property or land. I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, 'Do you have proof?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Then your opponent will be made to swear.' I said, 'Then he will swear.' So this verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...} to the end of the verse."],[640,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Whoever swears a patient oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim will meet God ﷻ while He is angry with him, whether He pardons him or punishes him.'"],[641,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ in a group from Kindah, and they did not consider me the best of them. I said, 'O Messenger of God, we claim that you are one of us.' He said, 'No, we are Banu al-Nadr b. Kinanah; we do not follow our mother nor disown our father.' Al-Ash'ath b. Qays said, 'O Prophet of God, I will not hear anyone deny that Quraysh is from Kinanah except that I will flog him.'"],[642,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ among the delegation of Kindah. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you have any children?' He said, 'None except a newborn who was born when I set out to you. I would wish that in his place the people had been filled.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not say that, for in them is joy for the eyes and reward when they die. And if you say that, they are indeed a cause of cowardice, grief, and stinginess.'"],[643,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'A child was born to me from the daughter of Jamd b. Wali'ah al-Kindi. I wished that in his place we had a bowl of tharid.' He said, 'Indeed, children are a cause of stinginess, cowardice, and grief.'"],[644,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The most grateful of you to God ﷻ is the most grateful of you to people.'"],[645,"And he said: 'By God, I have not disbelieved; rather, this man married me to his sister. If we were in our own land, we would have had a wedding feast other than this. O people of Madinah, slaughter and eat; and O owners of camels, come and take its equivalent.'"],[646,"I had a debt owed to me by a man from Kindah, and I used to frequent him before dawn. The Fajr prayer overtook me in the mosque of al-Ash'ath, so I prayed. When the imam said the salam, he placed before every person a fine garment, a pair of sandals, and five hundred dirhams. I said, 'I am not one of the people of the mosque.' He said, 'Even if you are not one of the people of the mosque?' I said, 'What is this?' They said, 'Al-Ash'ath b. Qays has arrived from Makkah.'\""],[647,"\"What do you have to do with him, O Ash'ath? By Allah, if you were to wrestle with the servant of Thaqif, the little hairs of your buttocks would stand on end.\" It was said to him, \"O Commander of the Believers, and who is the servant of Thaqif?\" He said, \"A young man who will rule over them; he will not leave any household of the Arabs but he will bring them humiliation.\" It was said, \"How long will he reign?\" He said, \"Twenty years, if he reaches that.\""],[648,"Muhammad b. Sallam said: Nobility is only counted from a short time before the Prophet ﷺ to the era of the Prophet ﷺ and continued in Islam. The house of Yemen that is in the courtyard near the honor, in Kindah, is al-Ash'ath b. Qays; its horseman among the Banu Zubayd is 'Amr b. Ma'dikarib; and its poet Imru' al-Qays, from Kindah; there is no disagreement about this."],[649,"\"Have you prevented me because of these two, O Commander of the Believers? You know that their companion came to us and filled us with lies,\" meaning 'Ali. Ibn 'Abbas said, \"Do you think I will insult you because of Ibn Abi Talib?\" He said, \"No Arab better than me has been insulted.\" Ibn 'Abbas said, \"The servant of Mahrah killed your grandfather and stabbed your father in the buttocks.\" He said, \"Do you not hear what he says to me, O Commander of the Believers?\" He said, \"You began it.\""],[650,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Hamzah."],[651,"I asked Anas b. Malik, saying, 'O Abu Hamzah...'"],[652,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a kunya when I was a young boy.\" He said, \"And he gave me a kunya because of a herb I used to gather.\""],[653,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik with a white head and beard; he dyed his head with henna.\""],[654,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ dyeing with henna.\""],[655,"\"Anas b. Malik used to dye his beard yellow with wars.\""],[656,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ dyeing with red.\""],[657,"And he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me.\""],[658,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, “O you with two ears.”"],[659,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to me, “O you with two ears.”"],[660,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ touching his forearms with perfume made from whiteness that was on him."],[661,"I saw Anas b. Malik wearing a dark-colored silk-blend jubba, a dark silk-blend cloak, and a black turban with a hanging end behind him, dyeing with yellow."],[662,"I saw on Anas b. Malik a yellow silk-blend garment."],[663,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ with his sons carrying him around the House on their arms, and they had fastened his teeth with gold."],[664,"He saw Abu Saʿid al-Khudri, Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah, ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ, Abu Usayd al-Badri, Rafiʿ b. Khadij, and Anas b. Malik ؓ trimming their moustaches closely like shaving and letting their beards grow, and plucking their armpits."],[665,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ leaning on a staff with a silver ferrule on its top."],[666,"I accompanied my grandfather Anas b. Malik for thirty years and never saw him drink nabidh at all."],[667,"Anas' wine was sweet, causing the lips to stick together."],[668,"I saw Anas b. Malik ؓ drinking tila' (reduced grape juice)."],[669,"Anas b. Malik had a servant who prepared fine delicate dishes for him, cooked two kinds of food, baked white bread for him, and kneaded it with clarified butter."],[670,"When Anas b. Malik completed the Quran, he would gather his family and children and supplicate for them."],[671,"He resolved to fast before his death for a year, so he broke it and fed a poor person each day."],[672,"\"I performed Hajj with Anas b. Malik, and I saw him stop saying the talbiyah when he descended from the mountain pass when he saw the houses of Makkah.\""],[673,"Anas used to hasten breaking the fast and not wait for the call to prayer."],[674,"And we heard him reciting: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\"."],[675,"Anas used to sit and a bed was laid for him to sit on. He would hold his son between his hands and play with him. One day, he came out while we were playing and said, \"O my sons! How bad what you throw is!\" Then he took something and threw it, and it did not miss the target."],[676,"We approached with Anas from Kufah until when we were at Uthth, morning came while the ground was mud and water, and he prayed the prescribed prayer on his mount. Then he said, \"I never prayed the prescribed prayer on my mount before today.\""],[677,"I went out with Anas to the land of Baythaq Sirin until when we were at the Tigris, the noon prayer arrived, \"and he led us sitting on a mat in the boat while the boat was pulling us along strongly.\""],[678,"He stayed with Anas in Naysabur for two years, and he used to pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."],[679,"\"He saw Anas b. Malik going between Safa and Marwah on a donkey.\""],[680,"that the imam should pray."],[681,"about his sons the slaughtered camel."],[682,"\"Anas used to wipe over the socks.\""],[683,"from his side, and open the gates of heaven for his soul, and replace for him a home better than his home."],[684,"\"I saw Anas b. Malik prostrating on his turban.\""],[685,"\"That Anas had loudly pronounced during noon or afternoon prayer and did not prostrate.\""],[686,"\"I saw Anas ibn Malik volunteering to travel.\""],[687,"That I should die on my bed — by Allah, that will never be. Allah has tried me, and I have killed a hundred of the polytheists, some of whom I killed alone and some of whom I shared in killing.\""],[688,"Anas said to him: \"Remember Allah, my brother.\" So he sat up straight and said: \"O Anas, do you think I would die on my bed when I have killed a hundred polytheists in single combat, besides those whose killing I shared in?\""],[689,"\"I stayed with Anas b. Malik for two months and he never performed qunut in the dawn prayer.\""],[690,"and on his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[691,"\"I gave Anas b. Malik walking medicine.\""],[692,"\"Anas b. Malik used to pass by us, and we were women, but he did not greet us.\""],[693,"\"This is a place where permission is not sought.\""],[694,"\"He was a governor over Naysabur, and a dihqan brought him khabis in a silver vessel, but he disliked it and returned it to him. Then he transferred it and came again with it, and he ate it.\""],[695,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — we heard it from him, but we would not lie to one another.\""],[696,"Anas ؓ said to us: \"Bind knowledge with writing.\""],[697,"that he would not leave it night or day, so Anas made peace among them for every day and night at six."],[698,"to bathe at midday and at nightfall.\""],[699,"I entered the house of Abu Talhah while he had locked the door on Umm Sulaym and was beating her, and she is the mother of Anas. I called out from behind the door, \"What do you want with this old woman that you beat her?\" She called out to me from behind the door and said, \"You call me an old woman? May Allah weaken your support.\""],[700,"Al-Hajjaj: It is you I mean; may Allah make your hearing deaf. Anas ؓ sought return (said: \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return\"), then went out from him and said, \"Had I not remembered my children and feared for them, I would have spoken to him in my place with words after which he would never respond to me again.\""],[701,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Medina when I was ten years old, and he passed away when I was twenty years old.\""],[702,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[703,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[704,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years.\""],[705,"\"I served the Prophet ﷺ for seven years.\""],[706,"Umm Sulaym: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for Anas. He said, \"O Allah, increase his wealth and children and bless him in it.\" Anas said, \"I have indeed buried from my loins, apart from my grandchildren, one hundred and twenty-five, and my land yields fruit twice a year, and there is nothing in the town that yields fruit twice other than it.\""],[707,"A'ishah: \"What knowledge do Abu Sa'id and Anas have of the hadiths of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They were only two young boys.\""],[708,"\"I had a lock of hair, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pull it and take hold of it.\""],[709,"I heard Anas b. Malik say, \"I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was eight years old.\" Yazid said, \"This shaykh Hammad b. Salamah directed me to this.\""],[710,"I washed Anas b. Malik, and when I reached his private area, I said to his sons, \"You are more entitled to wash his private area. Here, you wash it.\" The one who washed it put a cloth on his hand, and over it was a garment. Then he washed the private area from beneath the garment."],[711,"\"Anas b. Malik died, and in his embalming perfume was placed a small amount of sukk or musk containing sweat of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[712,"The last of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to die in Kufa was Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, and in Basra Anas b. Malik."],[713,"Anas b. Malik died in the year ninety-three."],[714,"In the year ninety."],[715,"Muwarriq al-Ijli said: \"Today half of knowledge has gone.\" It was said: \"And how is that, O Abu al-Mu'tamir?\" He said: \"When a man of the people of whims differed with us about a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would say to him, 'Come to someone who heard it from him.'\""],[716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do good throughout your entire life, and expose yourselves to the breezes of Allah's mercy, for Allah has breezes of His mercy with which He touches whom He wills of His servants. And ask Allah to conceal your faults and to secure your fears.\""],[717,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appoint as miqat for the people of the garrison towns al-Aqiq, for the people of Basra Dhat Irq, for the people of Madinah Dhul-Hulayfah, and for the people of Sham al-Juhfah."],[718,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"An Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj with me.\""],[719,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.\""],[720,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are three things that if a person possesses, he has tasted the sweetness of faith: to love nothing more than Allah, to love being thrown into the fire more than turning back on his religion, and to love for the sake of Allah and to hate for the sake of Allah.\""],[721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in a house, and each one of us moved back from his seat so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might sit next to him. He stood at the door and said: \"The leaders are from Quraysh, and they have a right, and I have a right over them as long as they do three things: if they judge, they are just; if they make a covenant, they fulfill it; and if they are asked for mercy, they show mercy. Whoever of them does not do that, upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.\""],[722,"The Prophet ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still completing it."],[723,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would stand up immediately upon giving the greeting of peace. Then I prayed with Abu Bakr ؓ, and when he gave the greeting of peace, he would spring up as if he were rising from a hot stone."],[724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Helpers, and he made brothers of Sa'd b. al-Rabi' and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. Sa'd said to him: \"I have wealth, so it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them you like, and I will divorce her, and when her waiting period is over, marry her.\" He said: \"I have no need of your wealth or your family; show me the market.\" So he went, then returned with dates and dried curd, having profited. He came to the Prophet ﷺ with traces of yellow perfume on him, and the Prophet said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I have married a woman from the Helpers.\" He said: \"What did you give her as a dowry?\" He said: \"The weight of a date stone of gold, or a date stone of gold.\" He said: \"Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep.\""],[725,"I attended a wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that had no bread and no meat. I said: What was it then, O Abu Hamza? He said: Barley porridge and dates."],[726,"A bird was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he placed it before him and said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You to eat with me. Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ came and knocked on the door. I said: Who is it? He said: I am Ali. I said: The Prophet ﷺ is occupied. So he went back. He came three times, each time coming back like that. Then he struck the door with his foot and entered. The Prophet ﷺ said: What kept you? He said: I came three times, and each time it was said: The Prophet ﷺ is occupied. The Prophet ﷺ said: What made you do that? I said: I wanted it to be a man from my people."],[727,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and put his eye to a gap in a hut. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and aimed at him with a stick or an iron tool to pierce his eye with it. When the Bedouin saw the Prophet ﷺ, he withdrew. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: Indeed, had you remained, I would have pierced your eye."],[728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Madinah will shake three times, and every hypocrite and disbeliever will leave it."],[729,"There is no ruqya except for the evil eye, or a fever, or blood that does not stop."],[730,"The most beloved fragrance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was faghiya."],[731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the children of the children of the Ansar, and the daughters-in-law and the neighbors."],[732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not enter upon women, even if they are daughters-in-law. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what about the brother-in-law? He said: The brother-in-law is death."],[733,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered the pots on the day of Khaybar to be overturned because of donkey meat."],[734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The Quran is a richness with no poverty after it, and there is no richness without it."],[735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' silently, and Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ did the same."],[736,"\"O Messenger of Allah! Can I go out with you for battle?\" Umm Salamah said. He replied, \"O Umm Salamah, it is not required for women to engage in warfare.\" She responded, \"But I will take care of the wounded, treat the sick, and provide water.\" He said, \"Indeed, that would be excellent.\""],[737,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Four things are not attained except with wonder: patience, which is the first form of worship; humility; remembrance of Allah; and having little."],[738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prayer of one sitting is equivalent to half the prayer of one standing.\""],[739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was sent and the Hour are like these two.\""],[740,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: \"Jibril ﷺ took out his entrails in a golden basin and washed them, then packed them with wisdom and light, or wisdom and knowledge.\""],[741,"Zainab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ passed away, so we went out with him and saw Rasul Allah ﷺ extremely saddened and distressed. We did not speak to him until we reached the grave. He had not finished burying her yet, so Rasul Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat around him. He sighed and looked up at the sky for a moment, then he finished burying her. Rasul Allah ﷺ descended into the grave, and I saw him becoming even more sorrowful. Then he finished and came out, and I saw him relieved and smiling ﷺ . We said, \"O Rasul Allah, we saw you deeply saddened and distressed, and we could not speak to you, but then we saw you relieved and smiling. Why is that?\" He said, \"I remembered the narrowness, darkness, and weakness of the grave, and it caused me difficulty because of Zainab. So I supplicated to Allah to ease her burden, and He did. He made her grave narrow, and only jinn and humans can hear its constriction.\""],[742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the call to prayer is given in a town, Allah grants it safety from His punishment on that day.\""],[743,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday between the afternoon prayer and the setting of the sun, and it is about this much,\" indicating a handful."],[744,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My father died without performing Hajj. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"What if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would that settle it for him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community.\""],[746,"Fatimah ؓ brought a piece of bread to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"What is this?\" She said: \"A loaf I baked, and I was not comfortable until I brought you this piece.\" He said: \"This is the first food that has entered your father's mouth in three days.\""],[747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He does not believe in me who goes to bed full while his neighbor next to him is hungry, and he knows it.\""],[748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Hour will not come until people vie with one another in building mosques.\""],[749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him before his death.\""],[750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A servant may, through good character, reach the highest ranks of the Hereafter and the noblest stations, even though he is weak in worship; and through bad character he may reach the lowest level of Hell.\""],[751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a woman performs ghusl after her menstruation, she should undo her hair and wash it with marshmallow and potash. And when she performs ghusl after janabah, she should pour water over her head and wring it.\""],[752,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom.\""],[753,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command giving gifts as a means of connection between people, and he would say: \"If people were to embrace submission, they would exchange gifts without hunger.\""],[754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Jibril ﷺ comes to me in the form of Dihyah al-Kalbi.\" Anas said: \"Dihyah was a handsome, fair-skinned man.\""],[755,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate: \"O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\""],[756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you.\""],[757,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"Set prices for us, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the rise and fall of your prices is in the hand of Allah, may He be exalted. I hope to meet Allah, may He be exalted, while none of you has a grievance against me concerning wealth or blood.\""],[758,"I arrived to the Prophet ﷺ from a journey, and the Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Have lunch.\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Shall I inform you about the traveler? Indeed, Allah has relieved him of fasting and half of the prayer.\""],[759,"He arrived in Madinah and entered upon the Prophet ﷺ for a need of his, and found the Prophet ﷺ eating. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Come close.\" The man said: \"I am fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of fasting and half of the prayer, and likewise the pregnant and the nursing woman.\""],[760,"Abu Qilabah said to me: \"He is alive, so meet him and hear the hadith from him.\" Ayyub said: \"I met al-Amiri, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out cavalry, and they raided the camels of a neighbor of ours and took them away. So he set out regarding that—either my father said, or my paternal uncle, or he said a close relative of his—and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. He said: I came to him while he was eating, and he said: 'Come to lunch.' I said: 'I am fasting.' He said: 'Come, and I will tell you about that. Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, has relieved the traveler of fasting and half of the prayer, and likewise the pregnant woman'—or he said 'the nursing woman.' And he ordered the camels, and they were returned. And whenever he narrated this hadith, he would lament and say: 'Would that I had eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[761,"Cavalry belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided us, so I went to him while he was eating. He said: \"Sit and eat from this food of ours.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am fasting.\" He said: \"Sit, and I will tell you about prayer and fasting. Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of half—or half of the prayer—and has relieved the traveler, the sick, and the pregnant woman of fasting.\" By Allah, he said all of them or one of them. So I reproached myself for not having eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[762,"Cavalry belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raided us, so I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was eating. He said: \"Sit and eat from our food.\" I said: \"I am fasting.\" He said: \"Sit, and I will tell you about prayer and fasting. Indeed, Allah has relieved the traveler of half the prayer, and has relieved the traveler and the nursing woman of fasting.\" So I reproached myself for not having eaten from the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[763,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Come.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Come, let me tell you: Allah has relieved the traveler of the fast and half of the prayer.\""],[764,"His paternal aunt, al-Rubayyiʿ bt. al-Nadr, slapped a girl and broke her tooth. They offered them compensation, but they refused; they sought pardon, but they refused. So they came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered them to exact retaliation. Her brother Anas b. al-Nadr came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will the tooth of al-Rubayyiʿ be broken? No, by the One who sent you with the truth, her tooth shall not be broken.\" He said, \"O Anas, the Book of Allah prescribes retaliation.\" The people then pardoned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Among Allah's servants are those who, if they swore by Allah, He would fulfill their oath.\""],[768,"Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah narrated to him that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar. He mentioned the hadith—its completion is to be written in the chapter of Sīn, under Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah; and in the chapter of Zāy, under Zayd b. Rāfiʿ, the story of stoning."],[769,"The first thing that called me to Islam was that we were a group of Arabs, and then affliction struck us. I carried my mother"],[770,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who were killed on the day of the Bridge of al-Madaʾin from the Ansar, from the Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu Zaʿuraʾ: Unays b. ʿAtīk b. ʿĀmir."],[771,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in naming those who were killed on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from the Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then from Banu Zaʿuraʾ: Aws b. ʿAtīk b. ʿĀmir."],[772,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from the Banu ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Najjār, then from the Banu Qays b. ʿUbayd b. Zayd b. Muʿāwiyah b. ʿAmr b. Mālik: Unays b. Muʿādh b. Qays."],[773,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from the Banu Zurayq: Unays b. Qatādah."],[774,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws: Unays b. Qatādah."],[775,"His freed slave used to seek permission for him—meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[776,"From 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[777,"From Ibn Shihāb, concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Anasah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[778,"From Iyās b. 'Abd al-Muzanī, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of water.\""],[782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not strike the female servants of Allah.\" So they stopped striking them. Then 'Umar came and said: \"By Allah, the women have become defiant toward their husbands.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they strike them. Then many women came to the family of Muhammad ﷺ, and when morning came he said: \"Seventy women came to the family of Muhammad last night, all of them complaining of the beating. By Allah, I do not think those are among the best of you.\""],[799,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Nabit: Iyas b. Aws."],[800,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim b. 'Awf: Iyas b. Wadhqah."],[808,"“He had a ringworm on his face – meaning qawba' – and I disliked his nose.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and wiped his face, and on that day it was not touched and there was no trace of it."],[809,"Ahmar b. Jaz', a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to us. He said: “We used to seek shelter for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from what kept his hand away from his sides when he prostrated.”"],[810,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and gave him the oath of allegiance, and he said, “Whoever gets to something that no Muslim has gotten to before, it is his.” So the people went out racing and drawing lines."],[811,"He informed him that his father al-Aswad attended the Prophet ﷺ while the people were giving him the oath of allegiance at Qarn Masqalah. He said: Qarn Masqalah is next to the houses of Abu Thumamah, and it is what faces the house of Ibn 'Amir and what is behind it toward the house of Ibn Samurah and its surroundings. Al-Aswad said: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ taking the oath of allegiance from the people. Men, women, young, and old came to him and gave him the oath of allegiance on Islam and the shahadah.” I said: And what is the shahadah? Muhammad b. al-Aswad informed me, he said: “On the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.”"],[812,"“The Prophet ﷺ ordered him to renew the boundary markers of the Haram in the year of the conquest.”"],[813,"He brought some fat camels to Madinah at a time of drought and barrenness of the land. When the people of Madinah saw them, they marveled at their fatness. I mentioned that to the Messenger ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for them, and they were brought to him. He went out to them and looked at them and said, “Why did you bring these camels of yours?” He said, “I wanted a servant for them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who has a servant?” Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ said, “I have one, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Bring her.” So Uthman brought her. When Aswad saw her, he said, “I want one like her.” He said, “You have her, so take her.” So Aswad took her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received his camels. Then Aswad said, “O Messenger of Allah, give me advice.” He said, “Do you control your tongue?” He said, “What do I control if I do not control it?” He said, “Do you control your hand?” He said, “What do I control if I do not control my hand?” He said, “Do not say with your tongue anything but good, and do not extend your hand to anything but good.”"],[814,"I said: O Messenger of God, give me advice. He said: \"Do you control your hand?\" I said: What do I control if I do not control my hand? He said: \"Do you control your tongue?\" He said: Then what do I control if I do not control my tongue? He said: \"Do not extend your hand except toward good, and do not say with your tongue except what is right.\""],[815,"I was reciting poetry to him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, and I did not recognize his companions until a man came who was broad between the shoulders, bald. It was said to me: Be quiet, be quiet. I said: O my bereavement! Who is this for whom I should be quiet in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ? It was said: He is Umar b. al-Khattab. By God, I knew thereafter that it would have been easy for him, had he heard me, not to speak to me until he took hold of my foot and dragged me to al-Baqi."],[816,"I was a poet and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, shall I recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Exalted is He? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask me for more."],[817,"\"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask him for more than that."],[818,"O Prophet of God, shall I let you hear praises with which I praised my Lord? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise, or there is nothing more beloved to Him than praise from God, Exalted is He.\""],[819,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have praised my Lord with praises. He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask him to recite."],[820,"O Messenger of God, shall I recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Exalted is He? He said: \"Indeed, your Lord loves praise.\" And he did not ask me for more."],[821,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I praised you with praises. He said: \"Indeed, God, Exalted is He, loves to be praised.\" And he did not ask him to recite."],[822,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a military expedition and it was reported to him that they killed the children of the polytheists. When the Prophet ﷺ received this news, he said, \"What is the matter with people who reach the point of killing the children of the polytheists?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah! And he mentioned a statement after that.\" He ﷺ said, \"Isn't it your best among you the children of the polytheists? By the One in Whose Hand my soul is, no newborn is born but upon the natural disposition until his parents make him Jewish or Christian.\""],[823,"When they killed the offspring, the Prophet ﷺ was informed about it. He said, \"Are not the best of you those who are born to the polytheists? Every newborn is born on the fitrah (natural inclination towards Islam) until his parents make him a Jew, a Christian, or a Magian.\""],[824,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Every child is born upon Fitrah (innate goodness), until his language expresses something else. His parents raise him as a Jew or a Christian.\""],[825,"\"I participated in a battle alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he achieved victory over our enemies. Some people started killing infants, and when the Prophet ﷺ was informed about this, he said, 'What has happened to people that they have gone so far as to kill children?' Then a man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, they are the sons of the idolaters.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'The best among you are the children of the idolaters. Do not kill children, for every child is born on the natural disposition (fitrah) until his tongue expresses it. His parents make him Jewish or Christian'.\""],[826,"\"We went on a campaign with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and killing continued until they killed the offspring. When the Prophet ﷺ was informed of that, he said, 'What is the matter with people who have killed the offspring?' A man said, 'Are they not the children of the polytheists?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Are not the best of you those who were born from the polytheists, and then their parents made them Jews, Christians, or Magians?' (This is the wording of the hadith narrated by Al-Muqaddimiy)\""],[827,"About Aswad ibn Sari'a, they fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and encountered the enemy, killing them until they reached the women and children. They asked the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Every child is born on Al-Fitrah (the natural inclination towards monotheism), and it is his parents who convert him to Judaism or Christianity.\""],[828,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sent a detachment and they killed the children. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , asked them, \"What is the matter with the children?\" They replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, are they not from their fathers?\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Are not the best of you those who are born to polytheists? Indeed, every newborn child is born on the natural inclination (fitrah) until their tongue expresses it.\""],[829,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, every child is born upon the Fitrah (natural inclination), and it is only his parents who turn him into a Jew or a Christian or a Magian.\""],[830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and they encountered the enemy and engaged in fighting until they reached the children. When the expedition returned, they informed the Prophet ﷺ about what happened. He asked them, \"Didn't they tire you?\" They replied, \"They were the children of the polytheists.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Are not the best among you those who are born to polytheists?\" Then he called for a crier and announced, \"Indeed, every newborn is born on the fitrah (natural inclination towards monotheism).\""],[831,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ hastened in killing until it reached killing children. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Every newborn is born upon the fitrah, until his parents make him a Jew or a Christian.\""],[832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No one loves praise more than God, Exalted is He, and no one makes more excuses than God, Exalted is He.\""],[833,"When Uthman b. Maz'un died, the Muslims feared for him. When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, he said: \"He has been joined to our righteous predecessor, Uthman b. Maz'un.\""],[834,"It was said: O Messenger of God, who is in Paradise? He said: \"The prophet is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, and the newborn is in Paradise.\""],[835,"A captive was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “I repent to God, but I do not repent to Muhammad.” He said, “He has acknowledged the truth for its people.”"],[836,"A captive was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “O God, I repent to You, but I do not repent to Muhammad.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “He has acknowledged the truth for its people.”"],[837,"On the Day of Resurrection, there will be four types of people who will present their excuses. The first is a deaf person who cannot hear, and he will say, \"O Lord, I came and the children threw me with stones.\" The second is a foolish person who lacks understanding, and he will say, \"Certainly Islam came, but I did not comprehend.\" The third is an old person who will say, \"Indeed, Islam came, but my mind failed to grasp it.\" And the fourth is a person who died during the interval between the messengers, and he will say, \"O Lord, Your messenger did not come to me, nor did he take their covenants, so that I may follow them.\" Then a messenger will be sent to them, instructing them to enter the Fire. But by the One in Whose hand is my soul, if they enter it, it will be a cool and peaceful place for them."],[838,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I praised God with one praise and I praised you with one praise.” He said, “Bring it, and begin with praise of God.”"],[840,"I came to the Prophet of God ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of God, I composed poetry in which I praised God ﷻ and praised you.” He said, “As for what you praised God with, bring it; and as for what you praised me with, leave it.” So I began to recite, and a tall, aquiline-nosed man entered, and he said to me, “Stop.” When he left, he said, “Go on.” So I resumed reciting, and before long he returned, and he said to me, “Stop.” When he left, he said, “Go on.” I said, “Who is this who entered, O Prophet of God, that you said ‘Stop,’ and when he left you said ‘Go on’?” He said, “This is Umar b. al-Khattab, and he has nothing to do with falsehood.”"],[841,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those from the Ansar who witnessed Badr, then from the Khazraj, from Banu Salama: Aswad b. Zayd b. Tha'laba b. Ghanm."],[842,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Hunayn: Ayman b. Ubayd."],[843,"Sa'd said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, “I saw Ayman while he was fleeing from the fighting,” and I recognized dislike in the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Sa'd said, “I said, ‘I have not seen a speech farther from every good.’” Then after that they were on the verge of fighting, and Sa'd said, “I saw Ayman, the most obstinate of the people, and that pleased the Prophet ﷺ.” He said: And Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said to Ayman, “I have been told that you do not stand between the two ranks out of cowardice.” He said, “I hope to stand in a station that God and His Messenger love.” Umar said, “You are worthy to do that.”"],[844,"Ayman was in charge of the Prophet's ﷺ ablution water and his sandals, and he would hand him what he needed."],[845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The minimum for which the thief's hand is cut off is the price of a shield.” He said: It used to be valued at a dinar."],[846,"Hands were cut off in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ for the price of a shield."],[848,"“No. My father and my uncle witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they enjoined upon me not to fight anyone who testifies that there is no god but God. So if you bring me proof of immunity from the Fire, I will fight with you.” He said, “Go, for we have no need of you.” Ayman said, “...”"],[849,"From 'Urwah, concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Qarabūs b. Ghanm b. Sālim: Umayyah b. Lawdhān b. Sālim b. Thābit b. Hazzāl b. 'Amr b. Qarabūs b. Ghanm."],[850,"In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end. So I asked him about that and he said, \"My grandfather, Umayyah ibn Makhshiyya, narrated to me that he was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ . There was a man who used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ but he would not mention the name of Allah before eating. Then, when he was in the last morsel, he would say, 'In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'The devil was eating with him until he mentioned the name of Allah at the beginning and at the end, and then the devil vomited out everything he had eaten.'\""],[851,"From his paternal uncle, Umayyah b. Makhshiyy, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting while a man was eating. The man did not pronounce Allah's name until only one morsel of his food remained. He said, \"In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and then said, \"The devil kept eating with you, and when you mentioned Allah's name, he vomited what was in his belly.\""],[852,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ sent him as a spy to Quraysh. I came to the wood of Khubayb while I was wary of being seen. I climbed upon it and untied him, and he fell to the ground. I left him not far away, then I turned around and could not see the wood of Khubayb—it was as if the earth had swallowed it. No trace of Khubayb has been mentioned until now.\""],[853,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek victory through the poor among the Muhājirūn.\""],[854,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek victory through the poor among the Muhājirūn.\""],[855,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek victory and help through the poor among the Muslims.\""],[856,"\"Umayyah b. 'Abd Allāh b. Khālid b. Usayd led us in prayer in Khurasan, and he recited these two sūrahs: 'Indeed, we seek Your help and Your forgiveness.'\" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth."],[857,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he granted me al-Ghamīm, stipulating for me and for the wayfarer the first watering. He granted Sā'idah, a man from among us, a well in the desert called al-Ja'ūniyyah—a well in which water is stored, and it is not sweet water. And he granted Iyās b. Qatādah al-'Anazī al-Jābiyah, which is on this side of al-Yamāmah. We had all come to him together, and he wrote for each one of us that grant on leather."],[858,"\"Do not shroud me in a sewn garment.\" So when he died and was washed, they sent to me, saying, \"Send the shroud.\" I sent them the shroud. They said, \"A shirt?\" I said, \"My father forbade me to shroud him in a sewn shirt.\" So I sent to the fuller—my father had a shirt with the fuller. It was brought and put on him, and he was taken away. I locked my door and followed him. When I returned, the shirt was in the house. I sent to those who had washed my father and asked, \"Did you shroud him in a shirt?\" They said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Is this it?\" They said, \"Yes.\""],[859,"\"Will you not come out and help me against these people?\" He said, \"Yes, if you wish. O girl, hand me the sword.\" She handed him the sword, and he placed it in his lap. Then he drew part of it and said, \"My close friend and your cousin ﷺ commanded me, when there is fighting between two tribes of the Muslims, to make a sword of wood.\" He drew part of it while it was in his lap and said, \"If you wish, I will go out with you with this.\" He said, \"I have no need of you.\""],[860,"My close friend—meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—advised me, saying: \"There will be tribulation and division. When that happens, break your sword and make a sword of wood.\" And when he became gravely ill, he commanded his family to shroud him but not to put a shirt on him. We put a shirt on him, and in the morning the shirt was on the clothes rack."],[861,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When you see two men of my community fighting over wealth, then prepare a sword of wood.\""],[862,"When Ali ؓ came to Basra, he came to us at the house and said, 'Is Abu Muslim here?' We said, 'Yes.' He came out to him, and Ali said to him, 'Will you not help us in this matter?' He said, 'Yes. O slave girl, bring me that sword.' She brought his sword, and he unsheathed it, and it was a sword of wood. Abu Muslim said to him, 'Your cousin, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, enjoined upon me that if there is a trial among the Muslims, I should take a sword of wood.' Ali turned away angry and said, 'We have no need of you or your sword.' Yazid b. Zuray' said: Yunus b. Ubayd narrated this hadith to me from this shaykh before I met him."],[863,"That Ali ؓ came to her father, stood at the door, asked permission to enter, and said, 'O Abu Muslim, what prevents you from striving in this matter and taking your share of it?' He said, 'What prevents me from that is a covenant which my close friend and your cousin ﷺ made with me: \"He commanded me that if tribulation occurs, I should take a sword of wood.\" Here it is with me, so if you wish, I will fight with it.'"],[864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see differences among my companions. If you live to that day, make your sword from palm branches.' He said: So I made my sword from palm branches. Then Ali ؓ came to me, grasped the two side-posts of the door, then gave the greeting of peace and said, 'O Uhban, will you not come out?' I said, 'By my father and mother, O Abu al-Hasan, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me' or 'commanded me' or 'enjoined me' or 'instructed me' – Ibn Zahdam was uncertain – and he said: 'O Uhban, if you remain after me, you will see differences among my companions. If you live to that day, make your sword from palm branches.' So I brought out my sword to him, and Ali ؓ turned away."],[865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on the day of Ashura and said, 'Go to your people and command them to fast this day.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not think I will reach them until they have eaten.' He said, 'Command whoever among them has eaten to fast the rest of his day.'"],[866,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ placing his hand, I think, on his thigh, pointing with his finger during the tashahhud."],[867,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turn away from his left side toward his house when he gave the greeting of peace."],[868,"We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so is swift in fighting.' He said, 'He is in the Fire.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so, with his worship, effort, and gentle manner, is in the Fire, then where are we?' He said, 'That is the humility of hypocrisy, and he is in the Fire.' He said: We used to watch him in battle: no horseman or foot soldier passed by him but he would leap upon him, and his wounds multiplied. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has been martyred.' He said, 'He is in the Fire.' When the pain of his wounds became severe, he took his sword, placed it between his breasts, and leaned on it until it came out through his back. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man may perform the deeds of the people of Paradise, yet he is among the people of the Fire, and a man may perform the deeds of the people of the Fire, yet he is among the people of Paradise. Wretchedness or happiness overtakes him at the departure of his soul, and he is sealed with it.'"],[869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath.'"],[870,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have purchased a slave, so pray to Allah for blessing for him and name him.' He said, 'What is your name?' He said, 'Asram.' He said, 'Rather, you are Zur'ah.' He said, 'What do you want him to be?' He said, 'A farmer.' He said, 'Then he is Asim.'"],[871,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ and saddle his mount. One night he said to me, 'O Asla', get up and saddle the mount.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been afflicted by major ritual impurity.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him with the verse of tayammum. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum.' He said: So I got up and performed tayammum, then saddled the mount for him. He traveled until he passed by some water and said to me, 'O Asla', touch – or 'touch this' – your skin.' He said: My father showed me how to perform tayammum just as his father showed him: 'One strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.'"],[872,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, 'O Asla', get up and show me how such-and-such is done.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been afflicted by major ritual impurity.' He remained silent for a while until Jibril ﷺ came to him with tayammum using earth. He said, 'Get up, O Asla', and perform tayammum.' He said: Then he showed me, Asla', how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him tayammum. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the earth with both palms, then shook them off, then wiped his face with them until they passed over his beard, then returned them to the earth and wiped the earth with his palms, rubbing one with the other, then shook them off, then wiped his forearms, both their outer and inner sides."],[873,"I was saddling the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was afflicted by major ritual impurity on a cold night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to depart, and I disliked saddling his camel while I was in a state of major ritual impurity, and I feared that if I bathed with cold water I would die or become ill. So I ordered a man from the Ansar to saddle it, and I placed stones and heated water with them, then bathed. Then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. He said, 'O Asla', why do I see that your saddle has changed?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not saddle it; a man from the Ansar saddled it.' He said, 'Why?' I said, 'I was afflicted by major ritual impurity, and I feared the cold for myself, so I ordered him to saddle it. I placed stones and heated water with them, and bathed with it.' Then Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated} until {Indeed, Allah is ever Pardoning and Forgiving}."],[874,"He called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from behind the chambers, saying, “O Muhammad, my praise is an adornment and my blame is a disgrace.” He said, “That is Allah, exalted be He.”"],[875,"He informed him that al-Agharr, a man from Muzaynah who had companionship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, had several wasqs of dates owed by a man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf. He went back and forth to him several times. He said, “So I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ with me.” He said, “Everyone we met greeted us with salam, so Abu Bakr ؓ said, ‘Do I not see people greeting you first, so the reward is theirs? So greet them first, and the reward will be yours.’”"],[876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ordered a portion of dates for me from a man among the Ansar, but he delayed paying me. So I spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Go early with him, O Abu Bakr, and take his dates for him.” Abu Bakr ؓ promised to meet me at the mosque after we prayed the dawn prayer. I found him where he had promised, and we set off. Whenever a man saw Abu Bakr from afar, he greeted him. Abu Bakr said, “Do you not see what reward the people earn because of you? Let no one beat you to the greeting.” So whenever a man appeared, we hurried to greet him before he greeted us.”"],[877,"From al-Agharr, one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited Surah al-Rum."],[878,"He narrated to us from al-Agharr, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that he heard the Prophet say, “Indeed I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times a day.”"],[879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O people, repent to your Lord, for by Allah, I repent to my Lord one hundred times a day.”"],[881,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “O people, repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day.”"],[882,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “O people, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for I seek forgiveness and repent to Him one hundred times a day, or every day, or more than once.”"],[883,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, so that I seek forgiveness one hundred times a day.”"],[884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, and I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times every day.”"],[885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed a covering comes over my heart, and I seek Allah’s forgiveness one hundred times.”"],[887,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have woken up and have not performed the Witr prayer.\" The Prophet replied, \"Verily, Witr is performed at night.\" The man persisted and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have woken up and have not performed the Witr prayer.\" The Prophet said, \"Then, perform the Witr prayer.\""],[888,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from Banu Sa'idah: As'ad b. Harithah b. Lawdhan."],[889,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: As'ad b. Zayd b. al-Fakih b. Zayd b. Khalda b. Amir b. Ajlan."],[890,"In the year one, Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah died; the quinsy seized him while the mosque was being built."],[891,"As'ad b. Zurarah was one of the Naqibs on the night of al-Aqabah."],[892,"Abu Umamah was afflicted with a pain that the people of Madinah call quinsy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I shall strive or excuse myself concerning Abu Umamah.\" He said, \"So he cauterized him with his own hand, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'An evil death for the Jews. They will say: Why did he not protect his companion? I possess no power for him or for myself from Allah.'\""],[893,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah, and he was a Naqib."],[894,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ relates that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to al-Dahhak b. Qays to give inheritance to the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi from the blood money of her husband."],[895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever wishes for Allah to shade him on the day when there is no shade except His shade, then let him ease the difficulty of someone in hardship, or help someone in need.\""],[896,"\"O my son, the happiest person who ever joined us in the city before the Prophet's arrival was during the defeat of a group from the Banu Bayadha tribe in the valleys of Naki'in. I asked, 'How many of you were there then?' He said, 'We were forty men.'\""],[897,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: As'ad b. Salamah."],[898,"I heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Nu'mayr say, \"Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf died in the year one hundred.\""],[899,"The first person to pray al-Duha was a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ known as Abu al-Zawa'id."],[900,"I was tending sheep at al-Qa' in Namira, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alight there. He established the prayer and prayed with his companions, and I prayed with them. It was as if I could see the whiteness beneath the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was prostrating."],[901,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraysh, then from Banu Makhzum b. Nuqta b. Murra b. Ka'b: al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam. The name of Abu al-Arqam was Abd Manaf, and he was called Abu Khindif b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Makhzum."],[902,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam."],[903,"From his grandfather al-Arqam, who was a Badri. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took shelter in his house near al-Safa until forty men had become Muslims, the last of them to accept Islam being Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ. When they reached forty, they went out to the polytheists. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to bid him farewell, intending to go to Jerusalem. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Where do you intend to go?\" I said, \"I intend to go to Jerusalem.\" He said, \"What takes you there? Is it for trade?\" I said, \"No, but I wish to pray there.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers there.\""],[904,"On the authority of his father al-Arqam, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who steps over people’s necks on Friday and separates them is like one dragging his own intestines into the Fire.”"],[905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr: “Put aside whatever spoils you have taken.”"],[906,"“Aslam, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died after the killing of ʿUthmān ؓ in the year thirty-five.”"],[907,"The name of Abū Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was Aslam."],[922,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the call to prayer in the ear of al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ when they were born, and he commanded it. The wording is that of al-Himmani."],[923,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us, Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub b. Muhammad b. Tahla' narrated to us from Abu al-Rijal from Salim b. 'Abd Allah from Abu Rafi', who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to kill dogs. I went out killing every dog I met until I came to al-'Asiyya. There was a dog around a house. I moved toward it to kill it, and a woman from the house called out to me: 'What do you want?' I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to kill dogs.' She said: 'Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that I am a woman whose sight has gone, and it alerts me to those who approach and drives away wild beasts from me.' So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said: 'Go back and kill it.' So I went back and killed it."],[924,"A book fell into my hands containing the opening supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he would say: 'I have turned my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With that I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. Glory be to You and praise. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. No partner has You. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins except You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.' Then he would recite."],[925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever washes a dead body and conceals its faults, forty major sins will be forgiven for him. Whoever digs a grave for his brother until he buries him, it is as if he has given him a dwelling until he is resurrected.'"],[956,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, who said: \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ being brought a shoulder, and he ate it, then prayed without touching a drop of water.\""],[957,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the middle of the night to supplicate at al-Baqi', and Abu Rafi' was with him. He supplicated as Allah willed, then turned back and passed by a grave. He said, \"Uff, uff, uff.\" Abu Rafi' said to him, \"O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. No one is with you except me, so did you say 'uff' because of me?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but I said 'uff' because of the occupant of this grave who was asked about me and doubted me.\""],[958,"Manbudh, a man from the family of Abu Rafi', narrated to me, from al-Fadl b. Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', who said: When the Prophet ﷺ prayed 'Asr, he would sometimes go to Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal and converse with them, and sometimes he would converse until Maghrib prayer. While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Maghrib prayer and he was hurrying, we passed by al-Baqi'. He said, \"Uff, uff, for you.\" I thought he meant me, so he said to me, \"Walk. What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, have I done something?\" He said, \"What is that?\" I said, \"You said 'uff' because of me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but this is the grave of so-and-so. I sent him as a collector for Banu So-and-so, and he stole a coat of mail. Now he has been made to wear the like of it from the Fire.\""],[959,"He informed him that he came with a letter from Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Islam was cast into my heart. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will never return to them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I do not break a covenant, nor do I detain messengers. But return, and if what is in your heart now remains, then come back.\" So I returned to them, then came back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accepted Islam."],[960,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kept handing me, you would continue handing me.\""],[961,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed it to him. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kept handing me, you would continue handing me.\""],[962,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Fa'id, the mawla of Ubayd Allah b. Ali b. Abi Rafi', narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Ali, from his grandfather, who said: \"I cooked the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ate from it, then prayed 'Isha' and did not perform wudu'.\""],[963,"I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered a sheep with a wooden peg.\" He said, \"Eat it.\""],[964,"While the Prophet ﷺ was walking in Baqi' al-Gharqad and I was walking behind him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May you not be guided, may you not be guided,\" three times. Abu Rafi' said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is wrong with me?\" He said, \"It is not you I mean. I mean the occupant of this grave. He is asked about me and claims that he does not know me.\" And there was a grave upon which water had been sprinkled when its occupant was buried."],[965,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to roast a sheep for him. I roasted it for him. He said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said, \"Hand me the foreleg.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how many forelegs does it have?\" He said, \"If you had remained silent, you would have found it as long as I called you.\""],[966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us and we had cooked mutton with us. He said, \"O Abu Rafi', give me the forearm.\" So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said, \"Give me the forearm.\" So I handed it to him and he ate it. Then he said, \"Give me the forearm.\" So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, does the mutton have anything other than two forearms?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you had remained silent, I would have continued to eat forearms as long as I wished.\""],[967,"Some people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us from this community that you commanded to be killed?\" meaning dogs. Then Allah, Mighty and Sublime, revealed: {They ask you what is lawful for them} the verse."],[968,"Gabriel came asking permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He gave him permission, but he delayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his cloak and stood up to him while he was standing at the door. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We have given permission.\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\" Then they found a puppy in one of their houses. Abu Rafi' said: So he commanded me when morning came, and I did not leave in Madinah any dog except that I killed it. Then there was a woman far away who had a dog that barked at her. I felt compassion for her and left it, then came back. He commanded me, so I returned to the dog and killed it. The people said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is lawful for us from this community that you commanded to be killed?\" Then Allah, Mighty and Sublime, revealed: {They ask you what is lawful for them. Say: Lawful for you are good things}"],[969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went around to all his wives in one night, performing a complete ghusl after each of them. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why not make it a single ghusl?\" He said, \"This is purer and better.\""],[970,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Baqi' al-Gharqad, walking behind him, he suddenly said, 'You are not guided, you are not guided.' Abu Rafi' said: I turned around but saw no one. I said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the matter with me?' He said, 'I do not mean you; rather I mean the occupant of this grave. He is being asked about me and he claims that he does not know me.' Then there was a grave that had been sprinkled with water when its occupant was buried."],[971,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, with people around him: 'Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch when a command of mine comes to him, saying: We do not find it in the Book of God, so we act upon it [only if it is there].'"],[972,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent.'"],[973,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; and Bishr b. Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us; and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us; they said: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Maysarah narrated to us; he said: I heard 'Amr b. al-Sharid say: Al-Miswar b. Makhramah took me by the hand and said, 'Come with us to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas.' So I went out with him, his hand on one of my shoulders. Then Abu Rafi' came and said to al-Miswar, 'Will you not command this one' – meaning Sa'd – 'to buy from me my two houses that are in his dwelling?' Sa'd said, 'No, by God, I will not give you more than four hundred dinars,' either in installments or deferred. Abu Rafi' said, 'By God, I would sell them for five hundred dinars in cash, and were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent,\" I would not sell to you.' The wording is that of al-Humaydi."],[974,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The neighbor has more right to his property that is adjacent.'"],[975,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'He roasted some meat for the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[976,"\"I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he ordered me to prepare its stomach for him. He ate from it, then he stood up and performed prayer without performing ablution.\""],[977,"\"I testify that I used to cook the sheep's belly for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he would eat from it and then pray without performing ablution.\""],[978,"'The Prophet ﷺ ate from the meat of a sheep and did not perform ablution.'"],[979,"'The Messenger of God ﷺ ate meat, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[980,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'I roasted the belly of a sheep for the Prophet ﷺ, and he ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution.'"],[981,"\"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he passed by a pot where some of his family members were cooking meat. Some of them handed him a shoulder from it, and he ate it while standing. Then he performed the prayer without performing ablution.\""],[982,"'A sheep was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I roasted some of it. He ate from it, then stood and prayed without touching water.'"],[983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to al-'Abbas: 'O uncle, shall I not maintain ties with you? Shall I not gift you? Shall I not benefit you?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Pray, O uncle, four rak'ahs. In each rak'ah recite the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation, say: Allahu akbar, wal-hamdu lillah, wa subhan Allah, wa la ilaha illa Allah – fifteen times before you bow. Then bow and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. Then stand up. That is seventy-five in each rak'ah and three hundred in four rak'ahs. Even if your sins were like the foam of the sea, God would forgive you.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, who can say it every day?' He said, 'If you cannot pray it in a day, then pray it in a week.' Until he said, 'Pray it in a month.' Until he said, 'Pray it in a year.'"],[984,"From Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Baqi' and said, 'Uff, uff, uff,' with no one with him except me. That alarmed me, so I said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom.' He said, 'The occupant of this grave – I appointed him over Banu so-and-so, and he betrayed a cloak. I was shown it upon him, blazing.'"],[985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited a guest, but he did not find anything suitable at the Prophet's ﷺ house. So he sent a message to a Jewish man, saying to him \"Muhammad ﷺ asked you to lend him some dates until the month of Rajab.\" The man replied, \"Only if you give me something as collateral.\" So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, \"By Allah, I am trustworthy in the heavens and trustworthy on earth. If he lent me or sold me something, I would fulfill my obligation to him.\" When I left him, the following verse was revealed to me, until the end of the verse, as a consolation to him regarding worldly matters: \"And do not extend your eyes toward that by which We have given enjoyment to [some] categories of them\" (Quran 20:131)."],[986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from praying with his hair tied back."],[987,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was in prostration, and I had unkempt hair. He straightened it and advised me against doing that.\""],[988,"A shaykh from the people of Ta'if, whose kunya was Abu Sa'id, narrated to me from Abu Rafi' that he saw al-Husayn b. Ali prostrating with his hair tied back, and Abu Rafi' said, 'I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"None of you should ever pray while he has tied back his hair.\"'"],[989,"He saw Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, pass by Husayn b. Ali while Husayn was praying standing and had pinned his braid at the nape of his neck. Abu Rafi' untied it, and al-Husayn turned around angrily. Abu Rafi' said, 'Attend to your prayer and do not be angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"That is the devil's share\" – meaning the devil's seat, that is, the place where his braid was pinned.'"],[990,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Ali to Yemen and tied a banner for him. When he set off, he said, 'O Abu Rafi', catch up with him and do not leave him; let him stop and not turn around until I come to him.' He came to him and enjoined upon him several things, then said, 'O Ali, if Allah guides one man through your hands, it is better for you than all that the sun has risen upon.'"],[991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali ؓ, 'There will be an affair between you and A'ishah ؓ.' He said, 'Me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Me, from among my companions?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then I am the most wretched of them.' He said, 'No, but when that happens, return her to her place of safety.'"],[992,"Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, be one who raises dust and pours down [abundantly].'"],[993,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ at Mina speaking to the people, saying to them, 'Face the sandals.'"],[994,"We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits indecencies; should I report his matter to the ruler? He said, 'I killed ninety-nine polytheists in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it would not please me to kill the like of them in number if I had [instead] unveiled the private affair of a Muslim.'"],[995,"The Prophet ﷺ came to them in the company of the Muhajirun, and a man asked him, 'Which verse in the Quran is greatest?' The Prophet ﷺ said, '{Allah – there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence. Neither drowsiness overtakes Him nor sleep.}'"],[996,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he placed him in charge of the captives of Qurayzah. He would look at the private part of a boy; if he saw that pubic hair had grown, he struck his neck, and whoever had not grown pubic hair he took and placed among the spoils of the Muslims."],[997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Asad b. Kurz, you will not enter Paradise by your deeds, but by the mercy of Allah.' I said, 'Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Not even I, unless Allah encompasses me or covers me with mercy from Him.'"],[998,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Indeed, illness removes sins just as leaves fall off a tree.'"],[999,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a drinker while he was at Khaybar, and he threw dust in his face. Then he ordered his companions, and they struck him with their sandals and with whatever was in their hands, until he said to them, “Lift him,” so they lifted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and that was his Sunnah. Then Abu Bakr lashed forty for wine, then Umar ؓ lashed forty in the beginning of his rule, then he lashed eighty at the end of his caliphate. Then Uthman ؓ lashed the prescribed punishment of forty, then Mu'awiyah ؓ eighty."],[1000,"That his father al-Firasi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, shall I ask?” He said, “No, but if you must ask, then ask the righteous.”"],[1001,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr, a client of Abu Bakr ؓ."],[1002,"About the naming of those who witnessed the Battle of Badr, Bilal, the slave of Abu Bakr, was mentioned.\""],[1003,"It is said that he was the contemporary of Abu Bakr ؓ in Damascus during the plague and was buried near Bab al-Saghir, and his kunya is Abu Abdullah, in the year seventeen or eighteen. He was among those born in al-Sarat. It is also said that Bilal was given the kunya Abu Amr."],[1004,"“Abu Bakr ؓ freed seven of those who were tortured for the sake of Allah, among them Bilal and Amir b. Fuhayrah.”"],[1005,"“...from my evil deeds and excuse me for my faults.”"],[1006,"Bilal said to Abu Bakr when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, ؓ: “If you bought me for yourself, then keep me; but if you freed me for Allah, then let me work for Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[1007,"Bilal came to Umar ؓ while he was in Syria, and the commanders of the armies were sitting around him. He said, “O Umar!” He said, “Here I am, Umar.” Bilal said, “You are between Allah and these people, and there is no one between you and Allah. So look to your right, to your left, in front of you, and behind you. These people around you eat nothing but the flesh of birds.” He said, “You have spoken the truth. By Allah, I will not rise from this seat of mine until you guarantee for every Muslim man his food and his share of oil and vinegar.” They said, “This is up to you, O Commander of the Faithful, for Allah has expanded our provision and increased the good.”"],[1008,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “I heard a soft sound in front of me when I entered Paradise, so I said, 'Who is this?' They said, 'Bilal.'” He informed him, and he said, “How do you precede me to Paradise?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I never perform ablution except that I pray, and I never pray except that I pray two rak'ahs after the ablution.”"],[1009,"From their forefathers they said: Bilal came to Abu Bakr ؓ and said, “O successor of the Messenger of Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The best deed of a believer is jihad in the path of Allah,' and I want to bind myself in the path of Allah until I die.” Abu Bakr said, “I adjure you by Allah, O Bilal, and by my sanctity and my right: my age has become advanced, my strength has weakened, and my term has drawn near.” So Bilal stayed with him. When Abu Bakr ؓ died, Umar came and said to him something similar to what Abu Bakr said, but Bilal refused. Umar ؓ said, “Then to whom, O Bilal?” He said, “To Sa'd, for he called the adhan at Quba during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” So Umar assigned the adhan to Sa'd and his descendants."],[1010,"I passed by Bilal while he was sitting at the time of the morning prayer. I said, “What keeps you, O Abu Abdullah?” He said, “I am waiting for the sun to rise.”"],[1011,"Umar said, “Abu Bakr is our master, and he freed our master,” meaning Bilal."],[1014,"I had dates of low quality, so I purchased with them from the market better dates for half their measure. I presented them to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “I have not seen today dates better than these. Where did you get these, O Bilal?” He said: I told him what I had done. He said: “Go and return them to their owner, take your dates, sell them for wheat or barley, then buy these dates with that, then bring them to me.” He said: I did so. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Dates for dates, equal for equal; wheat for wheat, equal for equal; barley for barley, equal for equal; salt for salt, equal for equal; gold for gold, equal for equal, weight for weight; silver for silver, equal for equal, weight for weight. Whatever is in excess is ribā.”"],[1015,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1018,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I had some dates. He said: “What is this?” I said: We stored it for our winter. He said: “Do you not fear that you will see a vapor for it in Hell?”"],[1065,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the head covering (khimār).\""],[1072,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The best deed of a believer is striving in the path of Allah.\""],[1075,"'We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and they slept until the sun rose. He ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer, then they prayed the two rak'ahs of dawn, then they prayed the morning prayer.'"],[1076,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, people engage in business and pursue their livelihoods, but we are unable to do so.\" He said, \"Don't you want the muadhin (caller to prayer) to have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection?\""],[1082,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and over the turban.'"],[1083,"'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1084,"'The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and the turban.'"],[1085,"'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and over the turban.'"],[1086,"'The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1087,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the khuffs."],[1088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the iqamah for Fajr, and he forbade me from calling the iqamah for Isha."],[1089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the iqamah for Fajr, and he forbade me from calling the iqamah for Isha."],[1090,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. When you see that, hasten to prayer.”"],[1091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs and the head covering."],[1092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs and the head covering."],[1093,"I had some dates belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I found better dates than them, a sa‘ for two sa‘s, so I bought them and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “What is this?” I said, “I took a sa‘ for two sa‘s.” He said, “Return our dates to us.”"],[1094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Feed us, O Bilal, some dates.” So I scooped handfuls for him. He said, “Give us more, O Bilal.” I added three more and said, “Nothing remains except a little I had stored for the Prophet ﷺ.” He said, “Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear poverty from the Owner of the Throne.”"],[1095,"He heard ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf ask Bilal how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his khuffs. Bilal said: “He went to relieve himself, then called for a vessel of water with a small bucket, washed his face and hands, then wiped over his khuffs and over his head covering as a substitute for the turban.”"],[1096,"A shaykh from Banu Taym, whose kunya is Abu ‘Abd Allah, told me, from Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, who said: I was with ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf when Bilal passed by. They asked him about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “He would relieve himself, then come and perform ablution, and wipe over the head covering and the muqs.”"],[1098,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-fourth.”"],[1099,"“Wipe over the head coverings and the muq,” tracing it back to the Prophet ﷺ."],[1100,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Wipe over the turban and the leather socks.'"],[1101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1102,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Wipe over the leather socks and the leather socks.'"],[1103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1104,"He and a man from Quraysh were performing ablution from the water container of the mosque, and they disputed about wiping over the leather socks. Bilal said: 'The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1105,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1106,"Bilal, the freed slave of Abu Bakr ؓ, reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he came from relieving himself on the day of the Battle of Tabuk and called for water for ablution and wiped over the leather socks."],[1107,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the turban."],[1108,"That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the turban and the leather socks."],[1109,"Bilal wiped over his leather socks, and it was said to him: 'What is this?' He said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks and the turban.' Ma'mar did not mention Abu Idris in his hadith, and likewise Yahya b. Abi Ishaq narrated it from Abu Qilabah."],[1110,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1111,"He was sitting in Damascus on a cold day performing ablution when Bilal, the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, passed by him. He said: 'O Bilal, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution?' He said: 'He would wipe over the leather socks and the turban.'"],[1112,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[1113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban."],[1115,"I met Bilal, the muezzin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said: O Bilal, tell me how was the expenditure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: He had nothing. I was the one who took charge of that for him from the time Allah, may He be exalted, sent him until he passed away. When a Muslim man came to him and he saw him unclothed, he would order me concerning him, and I would go and borrow and buy a cloak, clothe him and feed him. This continued until a man from the polytheists came in my way and said: O Bilal, I have ample means, so do not borrow from anyone except me. So I did that. Then one day I performed ablution and then stood to call the adhan for prayer, and there was the polytheist approaching with a group of merchants. When he saw me, he said: O Abyssinian! I said: At your service. He scowled at me and said harsh words to me. He said: Do you know how much time is between you and the month? I said: It is near. He said: It is only four days, and I will seize you for what you owe me, for I did not give you what I gave you out of respect for you or for your companion; rather, I gave it to you to make you my slave, and I will return you to herding sheep as you were before. Then something took hold of my soul as it takes hold of people's souls. I departed, then called the adhan for prayer, until when I had prayed the evening prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his family. I asked permission to enter upon him, and he gave me permission. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheist from whom I used to borrow said such-and-such to me. You do not have anything to pay on my behalf, and I do not have anything, and he will disgrace me. So permit me to flee to some of those Arab tribes that have accepted Islam until Allah provides His Messenger ﷺ with something to settle my debt. So I went out until I reached my dwelling. I placed my sword, my provision bag, my shield, and my sandals at my head, and I faced the horizon with my face. Whenever I slept for a while I would wake up, and when I saw that night was still upon me I would sleep until the first column of dawn broke. Then I wanted to depart, and there was a man running and calling: O Bilal, answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So I went until I came to him, and there were four mounted camels with their loads upon them. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Rejoice, for Allah has brought you the means to settle your debt.\" I praised Allah, may He be exalted, and he said: \"Did you not pass by the four mounted camels?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"You have their necks and what is on them—clothing and food—as a gift sent to me by the chief of Fadak. Take them and pay your debt.\" I did so. I unloaded their burdens, then hobbled them, then went to give the call for the dawn prayer, until when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed, I went out to al-Baqi' and put my fingers in my ears and called out: Whoever has a debt owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him come forward. I kept selling and paying until no debt remained owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on earth, until there remained in my hand two uqiyyahs or one and a half uqiyyahs. Then I went to the mosque, and most of the day had passed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting alone in the mosque. I greeted him, and he said to me: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: Allah has settled everything that was owed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and nothing remains. He said: \"Is there any surplus?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"See that you relieve me of it, for I will not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of it.\" No one came to us until evening. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed the evening prayer, he called me and said: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: It is with me; no one came to us. He spent the night in the mosque until morning, and remained the second day until near the end of the day, when two riders came. I went with them and fed them and clothed them, until when he had prayed the evening prayer, he called me and said: \"What happened with what you had?\" I said: Allah has relieved you of it, O Messenger of Allah. He said takbir and praised Allah, may He be exalted, out of fear that death might overtake him while he still had that. Then I followed him until he came to his wives, and he greeted each wife one by one until he reached his sleeping place. That is what you asked me about."],[1117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not give the call to prayer until you see the dawn like this,\" and he gestured with his hand and then opened it."],[1118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.\""],[1119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Bilal, announce among the people: Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah' before his death by a year, or a month, or a week, or a day, or an hour, will enter Paradise.\" Bilal said: \"Then they will rely on that.\" He said: \"Even if they rely on it.\""],[1120,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Do not precede me in saying Amin.\""],[1121,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Do not precede me in saying Amin.\""],[1122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every act of kindness is charity.\""],[1123,"Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani died in the year sixty, and his age was eighty years."],[1125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, «A man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath without realizing how far it will reach, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the Day of Resurrection. And a man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure without realizing how far it will reach, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1127,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, «A man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure without thinking it will reach what it has reached, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath without thinking it will reach what it has reached, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1128,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. (H) And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik reported to us. (H) And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Abi al-Hakam narrated to us: Malik b. Anas reported to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr b. 'Alqama, from his father, from Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, «A man may utter a word that earns God's pleasure, not thinking it would reach what it has reached, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word that incurs God's wrath, not thinking it would reach what it has reached, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.» Abu al-Qasim said: \"Malik and Muhammad b. 'Ajlan omitted 'Alqama b. Waqqas, the grandfather of Muhammad b. 'Amr, from the chain, and Hammad b. Salama narrated it, and the people differed with him in this.\""],[1129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man may speak a word that angers Allah without realizing its severity, so Allah writes His anger against him until the day they meet. And indeed, a man may speak a word that pleases Allah without realizing its significance, so Allah writes His satisfaction with him until the day they meet.\""],[1130,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, «A man may utter a word of goodness without knowing how far it will reach, and God will record His pleasure for him for it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word of evil without knowing how far it will reach, and God will record His wrath against him for it until the day he meets Him.»"],[1131,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad b. 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Bilal b. al-Harith, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said, «The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.»"],[1132,"I said, 'O Messenger of God, is the termination of Hajj for 'Umrah specific to us or for all people generally?' He said, «Rather, it is specific to us.»"],[1133,"«The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath along with a witness.»"],[1134,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ granted him all of al-'Aqiq as a fief.»"],[1135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him this piece of land and wrote for him: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, gave Bilal b. al-Harith: He gave him the minerals of al-Qabilah, its lowland and its highland, Ghashayah, Dhat al-Nusub, and wherever cultivation is suitable from Quds, if he is truthful.” Muawiyah wrote [it]."],[1136,"When the Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far away."],[1137,"We accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on some of his journeys, and he went out to relieve himself. Whenever he went out to relieve himself, he would go far away. I came to him with water for purification, and he set off. I heard some men arguing and making noise by him, like nothing I had ever heard before. He came and said, \"Bilal.\" I said, \"Bilal.\" He asked, \"Do you have water?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have done well.\" So he took it from me and performed ablution. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard some men arguing and making noise near you. I have never heard anyone speak like them before.\" He said, \"The Muslim and non-Muslim jinn disputed with me, asking me to accommodate them. So I accommodated the Muslim jinn in the lowlands and the non-Muslim jinn in the mountains.\" Abdullah ibn Kathir said, \"I asked Kathir, 'What are the lowlands and mountains?' He said, 'The lowlands are the villages and the mountains are the places between the mountains and the seas.' Kathir said, 'We have never seen anyone afflicted with the lowlands except that they were safe, and we have never seen anyone afflicted with the mountains except that they were barely safe.'\""],[1138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A Ramadan in Madinah is better than a thousand Ramadans elsewhere, and a Friday in Madinah is better than a thousand Fridays elsewhere.”"],[1139,"Abu Musa: “And Buraydah b. Husayb is called Abu Abd Allah.”"],[1140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Buraydah, there will be expeditions. You must join the expedition of Khurasan, then you must go to the city of Marw, for no harm will befall its people because Dhu al-Qarnayn built it.”"],[1141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now visit them, for they remind of the Hereafter. I had forbidden you [to use] gourds, but now make nabidh in any vessel and avoid every intoxicant. I had forbidden you to eat the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, but now eat, store, and keep provisions.”"],[1142,"A group of the Ansar said to Ali ؓ: “Fatimah is with you.” So he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him. He said: “What is the need of the son of Abu Talib?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have thought of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Welcome and family!” He added nothing more. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ went out to that group of Ansar who were waiting for him. They said: “What happened?” He said: “I don't know, except that he said to me: ‘Welcome and family!’” They said: “One of the two from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is enough for you. He gave you family and welcome.” Then later, after he married him, he said: “O Ali, a bridegroom must have a walimah.” Sa'd said: “I have a ram.” And a group of the Ansar collected for him measures of corn. On the wedding night he said: “Do not do anything until you meet me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, performed ablution with it, then poured it over Ali and said: “O Allah, bless them and bless their union.”"],[1143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who judges unjustly while knowing it—that one is in the Fire. A judge who judges while not knowing and thereby destroys people's rights—that one is in the Fire. And a judge who judges with truth—that one is in Paradise.”"],[1144,"We prayed Zuhr behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he finished his prayer, he turned to us angrily and called out in a voice that made the women in their chambers hear: “O assembly of those who have submitted but faith has not entered their hearts! Do not disparage Muslims, do not seek their faults. For whoever seeks the fault of his Muslim brother, Allah will expose his own faults and reveal his private matters even if he is in the innermost part of his house.”"],[1145,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who judges unjustly while knowing it—he is in the Fire. A judge who judges unjustly while not knowing it—he is in the Fire. And a judge who judges with truth while knowing it—he is in Paradise.” Abu al-Qasim said: Abd Allah b. Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, disagreed with the people about this man. He said Abbad, and al-Mutayyan, Muhammad b. Uthman b. Abi Shaybah, al-Tirmidhi and others narrated from him, saying Ubadah b. Ziyad."],[1146,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the market, he would say: “O Allah, I ask You for the good of this market and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of what is in it. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from incurring a false oath or a losing deal in it.”"],[1147,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A stone the size of seven pregnant camels will be thrown into Hell and it will fall for seventy autumns without reaching its bottom.”"],[1148,"While the Prophet ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he came upon a man turning over on the burning ground, on his back and on his belly, saying, “O soul, sleep at night and vanity by day, and you hope to enter Paradise?” When the man had finished his own prayer, he came over to us and said, “Here is your brother for you.” We said, “Supplicate Allah for us, may Allah have mercy on you.” He said, “O Allah, unite their affair upon guidance.” We said, “More.” He said, “O Allah, make piety their provision.” We said, “More.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “Give them more. O Allah, grant him success.” He said, “O Allah, make Paradise their final abode.”"],[1149,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he gestured to us with his hand to sit down."],[1150,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black, and his standard was white."],[1151,"Al-Samad is the One who has no hollow."],[1152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade naming a dog Kalb or Kulayb."],[1153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The inviolability of the wives of the mujahidun over those who stay behind is like that of their mothers. Whoever among those who stay behind is left in charge of any mujahid's family and betrays him regarding them will be brought to a halt for him on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to him: ‘This one betrayed you regarding your family, so take from his deeds whatever you wish.’”"],[1154,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr."],[1155,"Ibn Umar and I were presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr, and we were deemed too young, but we were present at Uhud."],[1156,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr."],[1157,"Ibn Umar and I were deemed too young on the day of Badr, so we did not witness it."],[1158,"We were sitting waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Eid al-Adha. He came, greeted the people, and said, “The first rite of this day of yours is the prayer.” He then went forward and prayed two rak'ahs with the people, then said the salam, then faced the people, and then was given a bow or a staff. He leaned on it, praised Allah Almighty, extolled Him, commanded them, and forbade them."],[1159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he entered the morning and the evening: “We have entered the morning and the dominion belongs to Allah, and praise belongs to Allah. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. O Allah, we ask You for the good of this day and the good of what comes after it, and we seek refuge in You from the evil of this day and the evil of what comes after it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the evil of pride, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the Fire.”"],[1160,"A man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about loneliness, so he said: \"Say: Glory be to the King, the Holy, Lord of the angels and the Spirit. You have clothed the heavens and the earth with might and dominion.\" The man said it, and Allah ﷻ removed the loneliness from him."],[1161,"Al-Bara' b. 'Azib said to me: \"Shall I not teach you a supplication that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me?\" He said: \"When you see people competing for gold and silver, supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in the matter and I ask You for determination upon guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessings and patience in Your trials and excellence in worshiping You and contentment with Your decree. I ask You for a sound heart and a truthful tongue, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.\""],[1162,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man: \"What is your name?\" He said: \"Nu'm.\" He said: \"Rather you are 'Abd Allah.\""],[1163,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night for wiping over the leather socks.\""],[1164,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fast upon seeing it, and break your fast upon seeing it. If it is obscured to you, then complete thirty.\" And he said with his hand: \"The month is like this and like this,\" meaning twenty-nine."],[1165,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, the earnings of a cupper, the payment of a soothsayer, and the stud fee of a stallion.\" And al-Bara' had a he-goat that anyone who wanted would bring to it for breeding, without preventing anyone, and he would not accept a fee for the stallion."],[1166,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we came to a well with little water. Sulayman said: \"Al-dhamma means little water.\" He said: \"Six of us went down, I being the sixth, or seven, I being the seventh, to draw water.\" Sulayman said: \"Al-maha are those who draw water.\" He said: \"We lowered a bucket while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the edge of the well. We filled it halfway, or nearly two-thirds, or about that. Then I raised it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Bara' said: \"I searched my vessel to see if I could find anything to put in my throat, but I found nothing.\" He said: \"Then I raised it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he dipped his hand into it and said whatever Allah willed him to say. The bucket was returned to the well with the water in it. I saw one of us brought out with a garment for fear of drowning. Then it overflowed,\" or he said \"it gushed,\" and the wording is from the hadith of al-Muqri'."],[1167,"Anas said to him: \"O my brother,\" so he sat up and said: \"O Anas, do you think I will die on my bed when I have killed one hundred of the polytheists in single combat, besides those I participated in killing?\""],[1168,"\"O my brother, Allah has taught you what is better for you than that.\" He said: \"Yes.\" Al-Bara' said to him: \"Do you fear that I will die on my bed? By Allah, that will not be a trial from Allah to me, for I have killed one hundred of the polytheists whom I killed alone, and among them those I shared in killing.\""],[1169,"To Abu Talha: \"We used not to give a fifth of the spoils, but the spoils of al-Bara' have reached a great amount of wealth, so I think we should give a fifth of it.\""],[1170,"\"A tall man with a white sword in his hand.\" He said: \"Al-Bara' was a short man. Al-Bara' struck his legs with the sword, and it seemed to miss him, and he fell on his back.\" He said: \"I took his sword and sheathed my own, and I struck only once until it broke, so I threw it away and took my sword.\""],[1171,"While Anas b. Malik and his brother al-Bara' b. Malik were at a fortress of the enemy's fortresses, the enemy was throwing hooks attached to heated chains that would catch a person and lift him up to them. One of those hooks caught Anas b. Malik, and they lifted him until he was raised off the ground. His brother al-Bara' b. Malik came, and it was said: \"Catch up to your brother!\" He was fighting among the people, so he came running until he leaped onto the wall, then he grabbed the chain with his hand while it was being turned. He kept pulling them while his hands were smoking until he cut the rope. Then he looked at his hands, and the bones were showing; the flesh on them had gone. And Allah ﷻ saved Anas b. Malik by that."],[1172,"From ʿUrwa: “Regarding the naming of the Companions of al-ʿAqaba who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Salima b. Yazid b. Jusham: al-Bara' b. Maʿrur b. Sakhr b. Khansa', and he was a naqib (leader), and he was the first to bequeath a third of his wealth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approved it.”"],[1173,"From Ibn Shihab: “Among those who attended al-ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Salima: al-Bara' b. Maʿrur. He was the first to bequeath a third of his wealth and to face the Kaʿba while he was in his own land, and he was a naqib (leader).”"],[1174,"That al-Bara' b. Maʿrur “bequeathed a third of his wealth to the Prophet ﷺ to dispose of as he wished, but the Prophet ﷺ returned it to his children.”"],[1175,"That the Prophet ﷺ proposed to the wife of al-Bara' b. Maʿrur, and she said: “I stipulated to my husband that I would not marry after him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is not appropriate.”"],[1176,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered into an alliance on the day of al-Hudaybiya with Khuzaʿa and wrote to them and to Budayl b. Warqa' and the leaders of Banu ʿAmr: “Peace be upon you. I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not harbored ill intentions toward you nor neglected your side. The most honored people of Tihama to me are you and those of the Mutayyabin who follow you. I have secured for those of you who emigrate the same as I have secured for myself, even if he emigrates in his own land without residing in Makkah. You shall not fear from me nor be made to fear.” This or similar."],[1177,"And he said: “O my son, this is the letter of the Prophet ﷺ, so follow its instructions. You will remain in good as long as it is among you. In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Budayl b. Warqa', Busr, and the leaders of Banu ʿAmr. I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I have not harbored ill intentions toward you nor neglected your side. The most honored of my people from Tihama to me are you, and the closest of them to me in kinship, and those of the Mutayyabin who follow you. I have secured for those of you who emigrate the same as I have secured for myself, even if he emigrates in his own land without residing in Makkah except as a pilgrim for ʿumra or hajj. I have not placed any burden upon you since I made peace, and you shall not fear from me nor be confined. To proceed: ʿAlqama b. ʿUlatha and the two sons of Hawdha have embraced Islam and pledged allegiance and emigrated on behalf of those who followed them from ʿIkrima, and he secured for those of you who followed them the same as he secured for himself. And some of you are from some others forever in the sacred and non-sacred territory.” Abu Muhammad said: My father narrated to me: “I heard our elders say: This is the handwriting of ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ.”"],[1178,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “ordered Budayl to detain the captives and the spoils at al-Jiʿrana until he came to him, so they were detained.”"],[1180,"That he heard his father Busr say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday.” He said: “If one of you finds nothing but to chew the bark of a tree, he should not fast that day.” And ʿAbdullah b. Busr said: “If you doubt, ask my sister.” So Khalid b. Maʿdan went to her and asked her about what ʿAbdullah had mentioned, and she narrated that to him."],[1181,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them riding a mule that we used to call a Syrian donkey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions entered upon them. My mother stood and placed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a velvet cloth over a mat in the house, preferring it for him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on it, I pressed down the mat. ʿAbdullah b. Busr said: My father Busr brought them dates to occupy them with, and he ordered my mother, so she prepared for them a dish of crushed wheat. ʿAbdullah said: I was the servant between my father and mother, and my father was the one standing over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions. When my mother finished the crushed wheat, I came carrying it until I placed it before them, and they ate. Then he gave them a drink of fadikh (a beverage made from dates), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank and gave to the one on his right. Then I took the cup until what was in it was finished, so I filled it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Give it to the one to whom the cup came.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the food, he supplicated for us and said: “O Allah, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless their provision.” And we continued to recognize from Allah ﷻ abundance in provision."],[1182,"That the Prophet ﷺ spat one day on his palm and placed his finger on it, then said: “O son of Adam, Allah ﷻ says: You will never frustrate Me, for I created you from something like this. Then when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments, and the earth resounded from your heavy tread. Then you gathered and withheld until when it reached the collarbones, you said, 'Should I give charity?' But how, when it is the time of charity?”"],[1183,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended his hand and spat into it, then looked at it and said: “Allah says: How will you frustrate Me, O son of Adam, when I created you from something like this, then I fashioned you and proportioned you, and you walked between two garments, and the earth resounded from your heavy tread? Then you gathered and withheld until when it reached the collarbones, you said, 'Should I give charity now?' But how, when it is the time of charity?”"],[1184,"That he said on the pulpit when he flogged the two men who had stolen from the people's spoils: “Nothing prevented me from cutting off their hands except that Busr b. Arta'a found a man stealing during a military expedition, so he flogged him and did not cut off his hand, and he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from amputation during a military expedition.'”"],[1185,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O Allah, make my final outcome good in all matters, and protect me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.”"],[1186,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O Allah, make my final outcome good in all matters, and protect me from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.” And he said: “Whoever makes this his supplication will die before affliction befalls him.”"],[1187,"He used to supplicate: “O Allah, make our final outcome good in all matters, and protect us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.”"],[1188,"From 'Urwah: “In naming the companions of al-'Aqabah who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah b. Yazid b. Jusham: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, and he was present at Badr.”"],[1189,"From Ibn Shihab: “Among those who were present at al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, and he is the one who ate with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the sheep that was poisoned on the day of Khaybar.”"],[1190,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who were present at Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Ubayd b. 'Adi: Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.”"],[1191,"A Jewish woman gave the Prophet ﷺ a roasted sheep as a gift. He ate from it, then said: “It has informed me that it is poisoned.” Bishr b. al-Bara' died from it. He sent for her and said: “What prompted you to do what you did?” She said: “I wanted to know if you were a prophet, it would not harm you, and if you were a king, I would relieve the people of you.” So he ordered her and she was killed."],[1192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is your chief, O Banu 'Ubayd?” They said: “Al-Jadd b. Qays, although he has some miserliness.” He said: “What disease is worse than miserliness? Rather, your chief is Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur.”"],[1193,"When Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, granted victory at Khaybar to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he killed those he killed among them, Zaynab bt. al-Harith the Jewess, the daughter of Marhab's brother, gave him a roasted sheep as a gift, and she put poison in it, adding more to the shoulder and foreleg, because she was told that those were the parts of the sheep most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and with him was Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'rur, the brother of Banu Salimah, she presented it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he took the shoulder and foreleg and bit into them, and Bishr took another bone and bit into it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swallowed his mouthful, Bishr swallowed what was in his mouth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Raise your hands, for the shoulder of the sheep tells me that treachery has been intended in it.” Bishr b. al-Bara' said: “By the One who honored you, I found that in the morsel I ate; if I did not spit it out, it was only because I disliked spoiling your food. When you ate what was in your mouth, I did not prefer my own life over yours, and I hoped that I had not swallowed it while it contained treachery.” Bishr did not rise from his place until his color turned like a black cloak, and pain lingered in him until he could not move except when moved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained alive for three years after that, until the illness in which he died."],[1194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us during the days of tashriq and said: “These are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only a believing soul will enter Paradise, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1196,"“The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.”"],[1198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on the days of Tashriq and said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer, and these days are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1199,"The Prophet ﷺ delivered a sermon to us on the days of Tashriq and said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the days of Mina and said, \"Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them.\""],[1201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking, the days of Mina.\""],[1202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to announce on the days of Tashriq, \"Indeed, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1203,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to announce on the days of Tashriq, \"None will enter Paradise except a believer; indeed, these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him, so he announced at Mina during the days of Tashriq, \"None will enter Paradise except a submitting soul, and these are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1205,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Constantinople will surely be conquered, and excellent is its commander, and excellent is that army!\" Then Maslama b. 'Abd al-Malik called me and asked me about this hadith, so I narrated it to him, and he campaigned that year."],[1206,"From Bishr b. 'Isma, a Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Azd are from me and I am from them; I am angry for them when they are angry, and pleased for them when they are pleased.\" Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him, said, \"He only said that about Quraysh.\" Bishr said, \"Would I then lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? If I were to lie about him, I would have made it for my own people.\""],[1207,"Abu Ma'shar al-Bara' narrated to us: al-Nawwar bt. 'Umar narrated to me, she said: Fatima bt. Muslim narrated to me, she said: Khalifa b. Bishr narrated to me from his father Bishr that when he embraced Islam, the Prophet ﷺ returned to him his wealth and his children. Then the Prophet ﷺ met him and saw him and his son Talq tied together with a rope. He said, \"What is this, O Bishr?\" He said, \"I swore that if Allah returned my wealth and my children to me, I would perform the pilgrimage to the House of Allah tied together.\" So the Prophet ﷺ took the rope and cut it, and said to them, \"Perform the pilgrimage, for this is from Satan.\""],[1209,"From 'Urwa, \"In the naming of the Aqaba participants from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. Sa'd, and he witnessed Badr.\""],[1210,"From 'Urwa, \"Among those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Zayd b. Malik b. Tha'laba b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. Sa'd b. Tha'laba b. Jilas.\""],[1211,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"Regarding the naming of the participants of the ʿAqaba pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Bashīr b. Saʿd Abū al-Nuʿmān.\""],[1212,"From Bashīr b. Saʿd, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The position of the believer to the believer is like the position of the head to the body: whenever the body complains, the head complains for it; and whenever the head complains, the rest of the body complains.\""],[1214,"From his father, who had companionship with the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this vegetable—meaning garlic—let him not approach our mosque.\""],[1215,"When the Muhājirūn arrived in Madinah, they found the water unpleasant. A man from Banū Ghifār had a spring called Rūmah, and he would sell a waterskin of it for a mudd. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Sell it to me for a spring in Paradise.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have nothing besides it for myself and my dependents; I cannot do that.\" This reached ʿUthmān ؓ, so he bought it for thirty-five thousand dirhams. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, will you give me the like of what you gave him—a spring in Paradise—if I buy it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I have bought it and made it for the Muslims.\""],[1216,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever delivers a speech seeking nothing but ostentation and reputation, God ﷻ will make him stand in a position of ostentation and reputation.\""],[1217,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever delivers a speech seeking nothing but ostentation and reputation, God ﷻ will make him stand in a position of ostentation and reputation.\""],[1218,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"A fire is about to emerge that will illuminate the necks of camels in Buṣrā, moving at the pace of a slow camel: it will travel by day and halt by night. It will go forth in the morning and return in the evening. It will be said: 'The fire has set out, O people, so set out!' The fire will say: 'O people, take your midday rest!' It will return, saying: 'O people, return!' Whoever it overtakes, it will consume.\""],[1219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ—his name in the pre-Islamic era was Zaḥm, and when he migrated the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Bashīr—said: While I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said to me: \"O Ibn al-Khaṣāṣiyyah, what have you come to resent about God?\" He said: \"I have not come to resent anything about God; all good has been done to me.\" He said: Then he came upon the graves of the Muslims and said: \"These attained much good\"—he said it three times. Then he came upon the graves of the polytheists and said: \"These missed much good\"—he said it three times. Then a glance occurred from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and there was a man walking on the graves wearing two sandals. The Prophet ﷺ called out to him: \"O owner of the two sandals, remove your sandals!\" The man looked and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he removed his sandals and threw them away. The wording is that of Muslim's hadith."],[1220,"And he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from this. He said: \"Only the Christians do that. Rather, my fasting is as God ﷻ commanded; then complete the fast until night, and when night comes, break the fast.\""],[1221,"He asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"Should I fast on Friday and not speak to anyone that day?\" He said: \"Do not fast on Friday except as part of days of which it is the last. As for not speaking to anyone, by my life, to speak and command good and forbid evil is better than to remain silent.\""],[1222,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him. He stipulated for me: \"You must testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger, perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, give zakāh, perform the pilgrimage to the House, and strive in the path of God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, as for two of them, I cannot bear them: zakāh—for by God, I have only ten camels that are the means of transport for my family and their baggage—and jihād—for they claim that whoever flees has incurred wrath from God, and I fear that if fighting confronts me, my soul will be frightened and I will hate death.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew his hand and shook it, then said: \"No charity and no jihād—will you enter Paradise?\" So I pledged allegiance to him on all of them."],[1224,"The Prophet ﷺ said, relating from his Lord, Exalted is He: \"Fasting is a shield with which My servant shields himself from the Fire. Fasting is for Me, and I reward it: he leaves his food and his desire for My sake. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person is sweeter to God ﷻ on the Day of Resurrection than the scent of musk.\""],[1226,"There was an uprising among Banu Mu'awiyah. The Prophet ﷺ went to reconcile between them. He turned to a grave and said, “You did not know.” It was said to him, so he said, “Indeed this one is being asked about me,” and he said, “I do not know.”"],[1227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of Dhu Qar: “This is the first day on which the Arabs obtained justice from the Persians.”"],[1228,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those killed on the Day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Bashir b. 'Abd Allah.”"],[1229,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and became Muslims, and we asked him to waive the 'atamah for us. He said, “The 'atamah prayer.” We said, “We are occupied with milking our camels.” He said, “You will, if Allah wills, milk and pray.”"],[1230,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Buhayr b. al-Haytham.”"],[1231,"The Prophet ﷺ used to use the siwak horizontally, drink by sipping, and breathe three times, and he would say, “It is more wholesome, more palatable, and more healing.”"],[1232,"I married a virgin woman in her chamber, and I found her pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said, “As for the child, he is a slave for you. When she gives birth, flog her one hundred lashes, and she has the dower because of what he made lawful from her private part.”"],[1233,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Tarif b. al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, their ally."],[1234,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, from Banu Sa'idah b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj: Basbas al-Juhani, an ally of theirs.”"],[1235,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar b. al-Najjar: Bujayr b. Bujayr, an ally of theirs.”"],[1236,"Narrated Abu Huraira: \"The first person who saddled a ride in the mosque was Tamim al-Dari.\""],[1237,"“Tamim al-Dari bought a cloak for one thousand and used to pray in it.”"],[1238,"Tamim al-Dari asked 'Umar for permission to tell stories. He refused to grant him permission. Then he asked him again, and he refused to grant him permission. Then he asked him again, and he said, “If you wish,” and he gestured with his hand, meaning slaughter."],[1239,"A man of the people of Makkah said to me, 'This is the standing place of your brother Tamim al-Dari. I saw him stand in prayer one night until morning, or nearly until morning, reciting a verse from the Book of Allah ﷻ, then bowing, prostrating, and weeping: {Or do those who commit evil deeds think that We will make them like those who believe and do righteous deeds, equal in their life and their death? Evil is what they judge.}'"],[1240,"Tamim al-Dari kept repeating this verse until morning: {Or do those who commit evil deeds think...}"],[1241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever recites one hundred verses in a night, the devout obedience of a night is recorded for him.'"],[1242,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Whoever recites ten verses in a night, a qintar is recorded for him, and the qintar is better than this world and all it contains. On the Day of Resurrection, your Lord ﷻ will say: \"Recite and ascend; for every verse there is a degree,\" until he reaches the last verse he has with him. Your Lord ﷻ will say to the servant: \"Take hold.\" The servant will say, gesturing with his hand: \"My Lord, You know best.\" He will say: \"With this one, eternity; with this one, bliss.\"'"],[1243,"I entered upon Tamim al-Dari while he was governor of Jerusalem and he was cleaning barley for his horse. I said, 'O governor, is there no one to take care of this for you?' He said, 'No, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever cleans barley for his horse and then carries it until he hangs it on the horse, Allah records for every barley grain a good deed.\"'"],[1244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing the servant is brought to account for is the prayer; then the rest of the deeds.'"],[1245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing the servant is brought to account for is the prayer; then the rest of the deeds.'"],[1246,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The Friday prayer is obligatory except upon a woman, a child, a sick person, a slave, or a traveler.'"],[1247,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The right of the husband over the wife is that she not forsake his bed, that she keep his oath, that she obey his command, that she not leave except with his permission, and that she not admit into his presence anyone he dislikes.'"],[1248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every ambiguous matter is forbidden; there is no ambiguity in the religion.'"],[1249,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel.' It was asked, 'To whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'To Allah, to His Book, to the leaders of the believers, and to their common folk.'"],[1250,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: 'Religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel; religion is sincere counsel.' They said, 'To whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims and the believers, and to their common folk.'"],[1251,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. I said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common folk.\""],[1253,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the believers, and to their common folk.\""],[1254,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, religion is sincere counsel\" — three times. They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His angels, to His Messenger, to the leaders of the believers, or the Muslims, and to their common folk.\""],[1255,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel, religion is sincere counsel.\" They said, \"To whom, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To God, to His Messenger, to His Book, to the leaders of the believers, and to the believers generally.\""],[1256,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the good city, al-Madinah, and any of its mountain passes are guarded by an angel with an unsheathed sword. The Dajjal will never enter it.\" Abu Kurayb 'Uthman b. Zayd also said it."],[1257,"I heard the caller of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , calling for the congregational prayer. I left with a group of Ansar women until we reached the mosque. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , prayed the Dhuhr prayer with us, then he ascended the pulpit and faced us with a smiling face. Then he said, \"By Allah, I did not gather you out of desire or fear except for a story that Tamim ad-Dari told me. He came to me, embraced Islam, and pledged his allegiance. He informed me that he rode with thirty men from Lakhm and Juzam, who were two tribes from the Arab tribes of Yemen. They encountered the sea and were captured by the waves for a month. Then the waves cast them near the sunset to an island from the islands of the sea. There they encountered a creature that resembled neither its face nor its back. We asked, \"What are you, O creature?\" It spoke to us by the permission of Allah with a swift and fluent tongue, saying, \"I am Al-Jassasah.\" We asked, \"And what is Al-Jassasah?\" It said, \"You should go to that monastery in the farthest part of the island. There is a man who is eagerly awaiting news from you.\" So we went to the monastery and found the greatest man we had ever seen, with a beautiful physique. His eyes were wiped as if they had kohl on them, and his hands were tied to his neck. His feet were tied with shackles. We said to him, \"Who are you, O man?\" He replied, \"You should know that I am Al-Masih ad-Dajjal (the Anti-Christ). It will soon be announced for me to emerge, and as soon as I exit, I will step on every land of Arabia except Makkah and Madinah. Whenever I intend to approach them, an angel with a drawn sword prevents me from doing so.\" Abu Al-Ashhab said, \"Amir said, Fatimah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , raising his hands until his armpits were visible. Then he said, 'Shall I not inform you of the mystery of this matter?' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Shall I not inform you of its location?' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Rather, it is in Yemen.' He repeated it three times. Then he said, 'Rather, it is towards ash-Sham (Syria).' Then he fell unconscious for a while. Then he woke up and said, 'Rather, it is in Iraq. Rather, it is in Iraq. Rather, it is in Iraq.' He will emerge from a village called Asbahān, from a village named Rastqabath. He will emerge with seventy thousand people, and they will have banners with them, and there will be two"],[1259,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, a man who accepts Islam at my hands and then dies?\" He said, \"You have the most right among the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1260,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the Sunnah regarding a man from the people of disbelief who accepts Islam at the hands of a man from the Muslims?\" He said, \"He is the closest of the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1261,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, a man from the polytheists who accepts Islam at the hands of a man from the Muslims?\" He said, \"He is the closest of the people to his living and his dying.\""],[1262,"He used to give the Prophet ﷺ a container of wine every year. When the year in which it was forbidden came, he gave him a container, and the Prophet ﷺ smiled and said, \"It has been forbidden.\" He said, \"Shall I sell it?\" He said, \"Its buying and its price are unlawful.\""],[1263,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"There are people who cut off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep.\" He said, \"Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead.\""],[1264,"They said, \"O Messenger of God, there are people who cut off the humps of camels and the tails of sheep while they are alive.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is carrion.\""],[1265,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, One, Single, Eternal, who has not taken a consort or a child, and there is none equal to Him, ten times, God will record for him forty thousand good deeds.\""],[1266,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to grant me land in Syria before it was conquered, and he gave it to me. Then Umar conquered it in his time, so I went to him and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me land from such-and-such to such-and-such.' So Umar ؓ made one third of it for the wayfarer, one third for its development, and one third for us."],[1267,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"This religion will continue to prevail until it reaches the houses of mud and houses of camel hair, until Allah makes Islam triumph and humiliates the disbelievers.\" Tameem said, \"I have witnessed that in my family, those who embraced Islam found goodness, honor, and prestige, while those who remained steadfast on disbelief suffered humiliation, servitude, and taxation.\""],[1268,"Tamim al-Dari reported—or I was informed about him—that Tamim al-Dari prayed two rak'ahs after Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ had prohibited prayer after Asr. So Umar came to him and struck him with the whip. Tamim gestured to him to sit while he was still in prayer, and Umar sat until Tamim finished. Then he said to Umar, 'Why did you strike me?' He said, 'Because you prayed these two rak'ahs, and I have prohibited them.' He said, 'Indeed I prayed them with one better than you—with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Umar ؓ said, 'It is not you, O group, that I fear for, but I fear that after you there will come a people who pray between Asr and Maghrib until they pass the hour in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited praying, just as they join between Zuhr and Asr. Then they will say: We saw so-and-so and so-and-so praying after Asr.'"],[1269,"Abu Rifa'ah used to heat water for his companions and say, 'Make your ablution excellent with this, for I will make mine excellent with this,' then he would perform ablution with cold water."],[1270,"It is the path of Abu Rifa'ah: I take it, and I strive in work after him with great striving."],[1271,"Abu Rifa'ah al-Adawi: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a stranger has come asking about his religion; he does not know what his religion is.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and left his sermon, then a chair was brought whose legs I thought were iron. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed it and began teaching me from what Allah had taught him. Then he returned to his sermon and completed it."],[1272,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution. He began by washing his face and forearms, then rinsed his mouth and inhaled water into his nostrils, then wiped his head."],[1273,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe with water over his beard and his feet."],[1274,"Abu al-Hasan al-Mazini: 'The grandfather of Amr b. Yahya, whose name was Tamim b. Amr. Ali b. Abi Talib appointed him over Madinah when he went to Iraq, when Sahl b. Hunayf went to him.'"],[1275,"From Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Khudrah b. Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Tamim b. Yu'ar b. Qays b. Adiy."],[1276,"From Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Tamim b. Yu'ar b. Qays b. Adiy b. Umayyah."],[1277,"From Urwah: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Tamim, the mawla of Banu Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws b. Harithah.'"],[1278,"From Ibn Shihab: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Tamim, the mawla of Banu Ghanm b. al-Salam b. Malik b. al-Aws.'"],[1279,"From ʿUrwa: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Anṣār: Tamīm, the freedman of Khirāsh b. al-Ṣimma.”"],[1280,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Anṣār, then from the Khazraj, then from Banū Salama: Tamīm, the freedman of Khirāsh b. al-Ṣimma.”"],[1281,"From ʿUrwa, in naming those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Ajnādayn, then from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm b. Huṣayṣ: Tamīm b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays."],[1282,"From Ibn Shihāb, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Ajnādayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: Tamīm b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays."],[1283,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he used to feed me and measure out for me a mudd, and I would set it aside and eat with the people until it became food. He said: And al-Talib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: You fed me a mudd on such-and-such a day, and I collected it until today. He said: “So the Prophet ﷺ borrowed it from him, and he had from him what he used to measure out for him before that.”"],[1284,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Hospitality is a binding right for three days; whatever is after that is charity.”"],[1285,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, seek forgiveness for me. He said: “When permission is given to you – or until permission is given to you.” He said: So he waited as long as God willed, then he called him and wiped his hand over his face and said: “O God, forgive al-Talib and have mercy on him,” three times."],[1286,"“I accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and I did not hear any prohibition regarding the small creatures of the earth.”"],[1287,"“A man manumitted a portion of a slave he owned, and the Prophet ﷺ did not make him liable for the remainder.”"],[1288,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do I see you coming to me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would have made the siwāk obligatory upon them just as prayer has been made obligatory upon them.”"],[1289,"From Abū ʿAlī al-Ṣayqal, the freedman of Banū Asad, from Jaʿfar b. Tammām b. ʿAbbās, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do you enter upon me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would command them to use the siwāk at every purification.”"],[1290,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Why do you enter upon me with yellow teeth? Use the siwāk. Were it not that I would make things difficult for my community, I would command them to use the siwāk at every prayer.”"],[1291,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say during his march to Khaybar to 'Amir b. al-Akwa'—and al-Akwa's name was Sinan—\"Take for us some of your songs.\" So he dismounted and recited rajaz poetry for the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1292,"\"Urwa narrated that the person who was killed on the day of Yamama from the Ansar, and then from the Banu Harith bin Khazraj, was Thabit bin Qais bin Shammass.\""],[1293,"\"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas was martyred on that day, in the year twelve.\""],[1294,"\"O God, I declare myself innocent before You of what these people have brought, and I apologize for what these people have done.\" Then he was killed. He had a coat of mail that was stolen. A man saw him in a dream, and he said, \"My coat of mail is in a pot under the brazier in such-and-such a place,\" and he charged him with some instructions. They sought the coat of mail and found it, and they carried out the instructions."],[1295,"\"Thabit b. Qays was the orator of the Ansar.\""],[1296,"The Prophet ﷺ missed Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas. A man said, \"I know his news, O Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He went to him and found him in his house with his head bowed, weeping. He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has been missing you.\" He said, \"I raised my voice above the voice of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so my deeds are nullified and I am among the people of the Fire.\" The man came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Go back to him and tell him that he is not of the people of the Fire and that he is of the people of the Garden.\""],[1297,"Thabit came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God forbade us to be praised for what we have not done, and I am a man who loves praise; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice; and He forbade us arrogance, and I am a man who loves beauty.\" He said, \"O Thabit, would you not like to live praised and be killed as a martyr?\" So he was killed on the day of al-Yamama."],[1298,"He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of God, by God, I fear that I have been destroyed.' He said, 'By what?' I said, 'God forbade a man to be praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; God forbade arrogance, and I find myself loving arrogance; and God forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' So he lived praised and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima.\""],[1299,"He said, \"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"By what?\" He said, \"God forbids us to be praised for what we have not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I am a man who loves beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O Thabit b. Qays, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\""],[1300,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said to him, \"Why?\" He said, \"God forbade a man to love to be praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I find myself loving beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" So he lived praised and was killed on the day of Musaylima."],[1301,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God, the Exalted, forbade us praise—that we be praised for what we have not done—and I love praise; He forbade us arrogance, and I love beauty; and He forbade us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am a man with a loud voice.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" So he lived praised and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima the Liar."],[1302,"\"O Messenger of God, I fear that I have been destroyed.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"God prevents a man from being praised for what he has not done, and I find myself loving praise; He forbids arrogance, and I find myself loving beauty; and God forbids us to raise our voices above your voice, and I am loud-voiced.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Thabit, do you not want to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\""],[1303,"When this verse was revealed: \"{Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet}\" (Q 49:2), Thabit sat in the road weeping. 'Asim b. 'Adi passed by him and said, \"What makes you weep, O Thabit?\" He said, \"I have a loud voice, and I fear that this verse was revealed concerning me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"O my son, would you not be pleased to live praised, be killed as a martyr, and enter the Garden?\" He said, \"I am content with the good tidings of God and His Messenger. I will never raise my voice above the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Then it was revealed: \"{Indeed, those who lower their voices}\" (Q 49:3), the verse."],[1304,"Pride was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke sternly about it, saying, “Indeed, Allah does not love any arrogant boaster.” A man among the people said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I wash my clothes and their whiteness pleases me, and the strap of my sandal and the thong of my whip please me.” He said, “That is not pride. Pride is only to reject the truth and to scorn people.”"],[1305,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he recited this verse: “Indeed, Allah does not love any arrogant boaster.” He mentioned pride and magnified it, and Thabit b. Qays wept. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him, “What makes you weep?” He replied, “O Prophet of Allah, I love beauty, so much so that I would be pleased if the strap of my sandal were fine.” He said, “Then you are one of the people of Paradise. Pride is not that you make your mount and your saddle fine; rather pride is one who rejects the truth and despises people.”"],[1306,"I came to the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer. When the Prophet ﷺ said the salutation, he turned to me while I was praying. The Prophet ﷺ kept looking at me as I prayed. When I finished, he said, “Did you not pray with us?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then what is this prayer?” I replied, “O Messenger of Allah, the two rak‘ahs of Fajr. I left my house and had not prayed them.” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not find fault with me for that.”"],[1307,"I heard my father say when the following verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Indeed, Allah does not like everyone self-deluded and boastful\" (Quran 57:23), the difficulty intensified for Thabit. He closed the door and started crying. He was informed about the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ, who sent for him and asked him about the hardship he was going through. Thabit explained that he was a man who loved beauty and being from a black-skinned people, he was feeling dejected. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You are not one of them. Instead, you will live well, die well, and Allah will admit you into Paradise.\" When Allah revealed the verse, \"O you who have believed, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet or be loud to him in speech\" (Quran 49:2), Thabit started practicing it. He informed the Prophet ﷺ, who sent for him and told him that he had been too loud and that he was concerned his deeds might go to waste. The Prophet ﷺ assured him, \"You are not one of them. Instead, you will live well, die well, and Allah will admit you into Paradise.\" When Abu Bakr mobilized the Muslims against the apostates of Al-Riddah, the Battle of Yamama, and Musaylima the Liar, Thabit bin Qais joined the campaign. They faced Musaylima and the Banu Hanifa three times, and the Muslims were defeated each time. Thabit said, \"O Saeed, my servant of Abu Hudhaifa, this is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" They dug a trench for themselves and fought until they were both killed. I dreamt of a Muslim man, Thabit bin Qais, who said, \"Yesterday, after I was killed, a Muslim man passed by me and took a beautiful shield from me. He has his tent in the furthest part of the camp, and there is a horse tied in front of it, with a saddle placed on the horse's back.\" Thabit asked Saeed to inform Khalid bin Walid and ask him to collect the shield and inform the Caliph, Abu Bakr, about his debt, his share of the money, and the enslaved person who served him. He advised him not to say it was a dream. Saeed went to Khalid bin Walid and described the shield as Thabit had mentioned. He also went to Abu Bakr and informed him about what was said. After the death of Abu Bakr, his testament became known, and we do not know of anyone whose testament was carried out after their death except Thabit bin Qais bin Shammash."],[1308,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you.”"],[1309,"We fight the enemy facing them, and how evil is what you have accustomed your peers to. By Allah, this is not how we used to fight alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[1317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever accuses a believing man or woman of disbelief is like killing him. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A servant has no vow in what he does not possess.”"],[1318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no vow concerning what one does not possess, and cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said, and whoever says to a believer, ‘O disbeliever,’ it is like killing him.”"],[1319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1320,"He informed him that he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under the tree, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess.”"],[1321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter.”"],[1323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. A man is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess.”"],[1324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam is as he said. The son of Adam is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not possess. Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever curses a believer is like killing him, and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief is like killing him.”"],[1325,"The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely and deliberately is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something, Allah will punish him with it in the fire of Hell.”"],[1326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no oath in disobedience to Allah, nor concerning what the son of Adam does not possess. Whoever curses a Muslim is like killing him. Whoever calls a Muslim a disbeliever has indeed disbelieved. Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam falsely and deliberately is as he said. Whoever kills himself with something by which he dies is in the Fire.”"],[1327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cursing a believer is like killing him, and whoever declares a Muslim a disbeliever, one of them incurs it.” Abu al-Qasim said: “This Abu Abdullah is called Khalid al-Hadhdha’, and Khalid has two kunyas: Abu Munazil and Abu Abdullah.”"],[1328,"A man made a vow during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to slaughter a camel at Buwana. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I vowed to slaughter at Buwana.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Was there any idol among the idols of the Jahiliyyah worshipped there?” He said, “No.” He said, “Was there any festival among their festivals held there?” He said, “No.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fulfill your vow, for there is no fulfillment of a vow in disobedience to Allah, nor in severing ties of kinship, nor concerning what the son of Adam does not possess.”"],[1329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping."],[1330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping."],[1331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, wearing a cloak wrapped around him, placing his hand on it to protect himself from the cold of the pebbles."],[1332,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Thabit b. Aqram b. Tha'labah b. Adiyy b. al-Ajlan."],[1333,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Ajlan: Thabit b. Aqram."],[1334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition before the Umrah to Najd, whose commander was Thabit b. Aqram. Thabit b. Aqram was killed in it."],[1335,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Adiyy b. Malik b. al-Najjar b. Aws: Thabit b. al-Mundhir b. Haram b. Amr b. Zayd Manat b. Adiyy b. Amr."],[1336,"From Urwah: Among the names of those who were killed on the day of al-Yamamah from the Muslims, then from the Ansar, then from Banu Malik b. Taym Allah: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man b. Khansa'."],[1337,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamamah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man."],[1338,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. Khalid b. al-Nu'man b. Khansa'."],[1339,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the Bridge of al-Mada'in with Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas from the Ansar, then from Banu Amr b. Mabdhul: Thabit b. Atik."],[1340,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the names of those killed on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar: Thabit b. Atik."],[1341,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the Bridge from the Ansar, then from Banu Amr b. Mabdhul: Thabit b. Atik."],[1342,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended the 'Aqaba pledge from the Ansar: Thabit b. Ajda'."],[1343,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salama, then from Banu Haram: Thabit b. Tha'laba b. Zayd b. al-Harith b. Haram."],[1344,"He was called al-Jidh'.\""],[1345,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"Concerning the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar: Thabit b. al-Jidh'.\""],[1346,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit b. Hazzal b. 'Amr."],[1347,"From Ibn Shihab concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Balhubla: Thabit b. Rabi'a."],[1348,"From Ibn Shihab: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Thabit b. 'Amr b. Zayd b. 'Adi.\""],[1349,"From Ibn Shihab: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Adi b. al-Najjar: Thabit b. Hassan b. 'Amr; he had no descendants.\""],[1350,"A lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"A nation that was transformed—and Allah knows best.\""],[1352,"A man from Banu Fazarah brought the Prophet ﷺ some lizards he had hunted. He began turning one of them over in front of him, and the Prophet said: \"A nation that was transformed.\" And the best of my knowledge is that he said: \"I do not know what happened to it, and I do not know—perhaps this is one of them.\""],[1353,"A roasted lizard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ took a stick and began counting its toes, then said: \"A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I do not know which beasts they are.\" So he did not eat from it, nor did he forbid it."],[1354,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people caught some lizards, roasted them, and ate them. I caught one of them, roasted it, then brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He took a palm branch and began counting its toes with it, then said: \"A nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth, and I think it may be that.\" I said: \"The people have roasted them and eaten them.\" He neither ate nor forbade."],[1355,"The Jews used to say that if a small child of theirs died, they would say he is a truthful one (siddiq). That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: \"The Jews have lied. There is no soul that Allah creates in its mother's womb except that it is either wretched or blessed.\" So Allah ﷻ then revealed this verse: {He is most knowing of you when He produced you from the earth and when you were fetuses in the wombs of your mothers} – the entire verse."],[1356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted on the day of Khaybar to Sahla bt. 'Asim b. 'Adi and to a daughter of hers who was born."],[1357,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Thabit b. 'Amr b. Zayd b. 'Adi b. Sawwad b. 'Usaymah, or 'Usayyah, an ally of theirs from Ashja'."],[1358,"We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar, and the people plundered them. The Prophet ﷺ came while their cooking pots were boiling. He said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"Plunder, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Overturn them, for plunder is not permissible.\" So they overturned what remained in them."],[1359,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass by cooking pots containing meat of sheep they had plundered. He ordered them to be overturned and said: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\""],[1360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plunder."],[1361,"We captured sheep on the day of Khaybar and plundered them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came while their cooking pots were boiling. They said: \"It is plunder.\" He said: \"Overturn the cooking pots, for plunder is not permissible.\""],[1362,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me captive when I was a young man, and I heard him ﷺ forbidding plunder and ordering that the cooking pots of domestic donkey meat be overturned."],[1363,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"We do not eat plunder, for it is not permissible.\" I said to Simak: \"What is this plunder that the Prophet ﷺ forbade?\" He said: \"Tha'labah said: It is sheep they plundered on the day of Khaybar before it was distributed. So the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Overturn the cooking pots.'\""],[1364,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\" A group plundered sheep, and they informed him. So the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Overturn the cooking pots and what is in them.\""],[1365,"We captured sheep belonging to the enemy and plundered them. We set up our cooking pots, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by the cooking pots and ordered them to be overturned. Then he said: \"Verily plunder is not permissible.\""],[1366,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and I heard him forbidding plunder and ordering that the cooking pots be overturned."],[1368,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God (mighty and majestic is He) will say to the scholars on the Day of Resurrection, when He sits on His throne to judge His servants: 'I did not place My knowledge and My wisdom among you except that I intend to forgive you for what is in you, and I do not care.'"],[1369,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, plunder is not permissible.\""],[1370,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever withholds the right of a person by making a false oath, a black spot will be written on his heart. And as long as that spot remains on his heart, it will not be changed by anything till the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1371,"A man from Banu Tha'labah b. Yarbu' came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, and he was saying: \"The upper hand is the giving hand. Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then your nearest, then your nearest.\" A man from the Ansar stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, these Banu Tha'labah b. Yarbu' struck so-and-so in the pre-Islamic period.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ shouted: \"No soul shall bear the burden of another.\""],[1375,"The Jews are disbelievers who did not believe in Muhammad, and none followed him except our evil ones. Even if they were among our best, they would not have abandoned their religion of their forefathers. So Allah revealed concerning them from His saying, \"They are not equal to the people of the Book\" to His saying \"from the righteous.\""],[1376,"That the Prophet ﷺ stood as a preacher and commanded the zakat al-fitr for the young and the old, the free and the slave: one sa' of dates or one sa' of barley for each individual, or for each head, and one sa' of wheat between two."],[1377,"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us in the hadith of Ibn Abi Rafi': \"Tha'labah b. Qayzi b. Sakhr b. Salamah, a Badri.\""],[1386,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from Banu Salim, then from Banu Haram: Tha'labah, the one called al-Jidh'.\""],[1403,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are performing deeds that are not recognized, and soon the unmarried man will return to his family, either happy or distressed.”"],[1404,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man who was cupping during Ramadan while he was lending money to another man, and he said: “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.”"],[1405,"I heard Thawban say: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade “wearing gold rings, al-qassi garments, dyed garments of yellow, and animal-skin mats.”"],[1406,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now visit them, and make your visit to them a prayer for them and a request of forgiveness for them. I had forbidden you to eat the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, but now eat from them and store some. I had forbidden you from that which is fermented in gourds, green jars, and pitch-covered vessels, but now ferment in them and make use of them.”"],[1407,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Three things with which no deed benefits: associating partners with God, disobedience to parents, and fleeing from the battlefield.”"],[1408,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Compeller, Exalted is He, will come on the Day of Resurrection, place His foot on the bridge, and say: 'By My might and majesty, no wrongdoer shall pass Me.' Then He will render justice to the creation, some from others, to the extent that He will even render justice for the hornless sheep against the horned one by a butt that it butted.\""],[1409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping performed, gave the cupper his wage, and said: \"Feed it to the water-carrying camel.\""],[1410,"Forty men from the Companions gathered to discuss fate and predestination. Among them were Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them. Then the trustworthy spirit, Jibril ﷺ , descended and said, \"O Muhammad, go out to your nation, for they have innovated.\" So he went out to them in a moment in which he had never gone out before, and they denied this from him. He came out with a reddish complexion, and his cheeks seemed as if they were sprinkled with sour pomegranate. They hurriedly approached the Messenger of Allah with their hearts throbbing, their palms trembling, and their arms shivering. They said, \"Seek forgiveness for us from Allah and His Messenger.\" The Prophet, ﷺ , replied, \"I am closer to you. If you were about to force me to divulge information, then indeed, the trustworthy spirit came to me and said, 'Go out to your nation, O Muhammad, for they have fabricated falsehood.'\""],[1411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Banu al-Abbas will have two banners; its highest is disbelief and its center is misguidance. If you reach it, do not go astray.\""],[1412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was shown Banu Marwan taking turns on my pulpit, and that grieved me. And I saw Banu al-Abbas taking turns on my pulpit, and that pleased me.\""],[1413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do I have to do with Banu al-Abbas? They led my Ummah astray, shed its blood, and clothed it in black garments. May Allah clothe them in garments of fire.\""],[1414,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When my Companions are mentioned, refrain; when the stars are mentioned, refrain; when divine decree is mentioned, refrain.\""],[1415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He had struck his sister at the beginning of the night while she was reciting: \"Read in the name of your Lord who created\" (Quran 96:1) until I thought he had killed her. Then he got up before dawn and heard her voice reciting: \"Read in the name of your Lord who created.\" He said: \"By Allah, this is not poetry or muttering.\" So he went until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Bilal at the door. He pushed the door. Bilal said: \"Who is this?\" He said: \"Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said: \"Until I ask permission for you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Bilal said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Umar is at the door.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If Allah wills good for Umar, He will admit him into the religion.\" Then he said to Bilal: \"Open.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his upper arms, shook him, and said: \"What do you want, and what have you come for?\" Umar said to him: \"Present to me what you call to.\" He said: \"You testify that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" Umar embraced Islam on the spot, and he said: \"Go out.\""],[1416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the millstone of Islam is turning.\" He was asked: \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Present my hadith to the Book. Whatever agrees with it is from me, and I said it.\""],[1417,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Allah has pardoned my Ummah for three things: mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do.\""],[1418,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"There will be peoples from my Ummah whose jurists engage in complex questions. Those are the worst of my Ummah.\""],[1419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is forbidden by suckling is forbidden by lineage.\""],[1420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who will guarantee me that he will not ask people for anything, and I will guarantee him Paradise?\" Thawban said: \"I will.\" And Thawban never asked anyone for anything after that."],[1422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will guarantee me one quality, and I will guarantee him Paradise?” I said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Do not ask people for anything.” He (the narrator) said: “Indeed, Thawban’s whip would fall while he was on his camel, and a man would go to hand it to him, but he would make his camel kneel and take his whip himself.”"],[1423,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and said: “We are traveling by night, so let no weak or unruly (mount) enter with us.” A man set off on a difficult she-camel, and it threw him, and his thigh was broken, and he died. The Prophet ﷺ ordered the funeral prayer over him, then ordered Bilal, who called out three times: “Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient person.”"],[1424,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “My cistern is between Aden and Oman. Its water is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey, and those who come to it most are the poor among the Emigrants.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the poor among the Emigrants? He said: “Those with disheveled hair and soiled clothes, who do not marry women who are inaccessible, for whom the doors of the great are not opened, who give the right that is upon them and are not given what is due to them.”"],[1425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things do not break the fast: cupping, vomiting, and nocturnal emission, but the fasting person should not vomit deliberately.”"],[1426,"I heard Thawban ؓ say: The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man among his companions who had a ring of copper on his hand, and he said: “What is this?” He said: For the pain of the vein (wāhina). He said: “Remove it from you.”"],[1427,"He narrated to us from the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ vomit, and he broke his fast.”"],[1428,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.”"],[1429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Nothing repels fate except supplication, and nothing increases lifespan except righteousness. Indeed, a man is deprived of provision because of a sin he commits.”"],[1430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, my cistern is between Aden and Oman. Its cups are as numerous as the stars, and its water is whiter than snow and sweeter than honey. The first to come to it are the poor among the Emigrants.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: “Those with disheveled hair and soiled clothes, who do not marry inaccessible women, for whom the doors of the great are not opened, who give what is upon them and are not given what is due to them.”"],[1431,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that among the best of your deeds is prayer and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 278)"],[1432,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person remains in the khurfa of Paradise.” It was said: What is the khurfa of Paradise? He said: “Its picked fruit.”"],[1433,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person remains in the khurfa of Paradise until he returns.”"],[1434,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.”"],[1436,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “When a man plucks (a fruit) from Paradise, another grows in its place.”"],[1437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you is afflicted (by it), fever is a piece of the fire of Hell, so let him extinguish it from himself with cold running water, facing the flow of the water, and let him say after dawn before sunrise: ‘O Allah, confirm Your Messenger and heal Your servant.’ Let him immerse himself in it three times. If he is not cured in five (days), then in seven; and if he is not cured in seven, then in nine, for it will hardly exceed nine by Allah’s permission.”"],[1438,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six (days) of Shawwal, that is the fasting of a year.”"],[1439,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The nations are about to call one another against you,” and he mentioned the hadith."],[1440,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled, the last person of his household he would bid farewell to was Fatimah, and when he returned, the first person he would visit was her. He said: He arrived from a military expedition or journey of his, and behold, Fatimah had hung a cloth on her door and adorned al-Hasan and al-Husayn with two silver bracelets. He turned back. She thought he turned back only because of what he saw, so she removed the curtain and removed the bracelets from the two boys and cut them off, then gave them to the two boys. They came to the Prophet ﷺ crying, and he said, “O Thawban, take these two and go with them to a household in Madinah” – I think he said – “who are needy, for these are my household, and I dislike that they consume their good things in their worldly life.” Then he said, “O Thawban, buy for Fatimah a necklace of ‘asab (beads) and two bracelets of ivory.”"],[1441,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever you see reciting poetry in the mosque, say to him, ‘May Allah break your mouth,’ three times; and whoever you see announcing a lost item in the mosque, say to him, ‘May you not find it,’ three times; and whoever you see buying and selling in the mosque, say to him, ‘May Allah not make your trade profitable.’” Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed us."],[1442,"I heard Ma‘n b. Yazid say, “I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled in my favor, delivered a sermon on my behalf, and married me; and I and my grandfather pledged allegiance to him.”"],[1443,"And among those killed on the day of Khaybar from Quraysh, then from Banu ‘Abd Manaf, was Thaqif b. ‘Amr, an ally of theirs from Banu Asad b. Jazimah."],[1444,"“The Prophet ﷺ sent Ja‘far to Mu’tah in Jumada of the year eight.”"],[1445,"“Ja‘far b. Abi Talib wore a ring on his right hand.”"],[1446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the companions of Mu’tah from the pulpit, one by one: he began with Zayd b. Harithah, then Ja‘far b. Abi Talib, then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah, may Allah have mercy on them. He said, “Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the banner, and he is a sword among the swords of Allah.”"],[1447,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of Zaid and his companions before receiving the news, and his eyes were filled with tears."],[1448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army and appointed Zayd b. Harithah over them, saying, “If he is killed or martyred, your commander is Ja‘far b. Abi Talib; and if he is killed or martyred, your commander is ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah.” They set out and met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Ja‘far b. Abi Talib took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the banner, and Allah ﷻ granted victory through him. Their news reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he came out, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: “To proceed: your brothers met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Ja‘far took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then ‘Abd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah granted victory through him.” Then he gave the family of Ja‘far three days before coming to them. Then he came to them and said, “Do not weep for him after today.” Then he said, “Bring me the sons of my brother.” We were brought to him as if we were chicks. He said, “Call the barber for me,” and ordered him, and he shaved our heads. Then he said, “As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib; and as for ‘Awn, he resembles my physical appearance and character.” Then he took my hand and raised it, saying, “O Allah, be a successor for Ja‘far in his family, and bless ‘Abd Allah in the transaction of his right hand.” He said it three times. Then our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?”"],[1449,"From his sorrel horse, then he fought the people until he was killed."],[1450,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Zayd b. Harithah as commander during the expedition of Mu'tah and said, \"If Zayd is killed, then Ja'far; and if Ja'far is killed, then 'Abd Allah b. Rawahah.\" 'Abd Allah said, \"I was with them in that expedition, and we sought Ja'far and found that he had received something over ninety wounds between stabs and shots.\""],[1451,"\"We missed Ja'far b. Abi Talib, so we searched for him and found him among the slain. We found in him more than ninety wounds between sword strikes, spear stabs, and arrow shots, and we found that all of them were in the front of his body.\""],[1452,"He informed him that he stood over Ja'far that day while he was slain. He said, \"I counted in him fifty wounds between stabs and strikes, none of which was in his back.\""],[1453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I entered Paradise last night and looked around in it, and there was Ja'far flying with the angels.\""],[1454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib as an angel flying in Paradise, possessing two wings with which he flies wherever he wishes, the leading feathers of his wings dyed with blood.\""],[1455,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was shown them in a dream and saw Ja'far as an angel with two wings stained with blood, and Zayd opposite him on the couch.\""],[1456,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after conquering Khaybar, it was said to him, \"Ja'far has arrived from the Negus.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I do not know which of the two makes me happier: the arrival of Ja'far or the conquest of Khaybar.\" Then he kissed him between his eyes."],[1457,"When Ja'far came from the emigration to Abyssinia, the Prophet ﷺ met him, embraced him, kissed him between his eyes, and said, \"I do not know which of the two makes me more joyful: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja'far.\""],[1458,"\"When the death of Ja'far came, we recognized grief in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them something that preoccupy them.\""],[1460,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shown in a dream the companions of Mu'tah, and he saw Ja'far as an angel with two wings stained with blood, meaning dyed.\""],[1461,"Peace be upon you, O son of the one with two wings."],[1462,"Ja'far b. Abi Talib was killed on the day of Mu'tah in al-Balqa'."],[1463,"I used to ask 'Ali ؓ for something and he would refuse me, so I would say, 'By the right of Ja'far,' and when I said, 'By the right of Ja'far,' he gave it to me."],[1464,"Ja'far used to love the poor, sitting with them, talking to them and they talking to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call him Abu al-Masakin (the father of the poor)."],[1465,"And he said, \"What do you say?\" So we said, \"Indeed, our people worship idols, and indeed Allah has sent a Messenger to us, so we believed in him and affirmed him.\" So Najashi said to them, \"Are they your slaves?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then they are free from any debt from you?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"So leave them alone.\" So we left his presence. 'Amr bin Al-Aas said, \"Indeed, these people say about 'Isa (Jesus) what you do not say.\" He said, \"If they do not say about 'Isa what I say, I will not leave them in my land for a moment of the day.\" He said, \"So he sent for us, and his invitation was tougher on us than the first. So he said, \"What does your companion say about 'Isa ibn Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary)?\" So we said, \"He says he is the Spirit of Allah and His word, which He bestowed upon the Virgin Mary.\" He said, \"So he sent for them and said, \"Summon this priest and this monk.\" So people from among them came to him, and he said, \"What do you say about 'Isa ibn Maryam?\" They said, \"You know best.\" He said, \"So what do you say?\" Najashi took something from the ground, and said, \"This is what 'Isa says. He does not exceed what these people say.\" Then he said to them, \"Does anyone harm you?\" They said, \"Yes.\" So he commanded a caller to announce, \"Whoever harms any of them will be granted an allowance of four dirhams.\" Then he said, \"Is this enough for you?\" They said, \"No.\" So he doubled it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated to Al-Madinah and appeared there, we said to Najashi, \"Indeed, our companion has left for Al-Madinah and has appeared there, and he emigrated and killed those whom we informed you about, and we wanted to join him.\" So he provided us with what we needed and said, \"Inform your companion of what I have done for you, and this is my Messenger with you, and I testify that there is no god but Allah, and that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" So tell him to seek forgiveness for me.\" Ja'far said, \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, performed ablution, then he prayed three times, 'O Allah, forgive Najashi.' And the Muslims said, 'Ameen.' Ja'far said, \"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , 'Leave now and inform your companion about what you have seen of the Prophet ﷺ .' And the wording is that of the hadith of Muhammad bin Adam.\""],[1466,"A messenger was sent among us whose tongue, truthfulness, and fidelity we knew. He called us to worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, and to abandon what our people and others besides them worshipped besides Him. He commanded us to do what is right and forbade us from what is wrong, and commanded us to pray, fast, give charity, and maintain family ties. He called us to what we knew, and he recited to us a revelation that came from Allah, which nothing else resembles. We believed him, had faith in him, and knew that what he brought was the truth from Allah. At that point our people parted from us, harmed us, and overpowered us. When they had reached with us what we detested and we were unable to defend ourselves against them, we went out to your land and chose you over anyone else. Al-Najashi said, 'Go, for you are sayūm (secure) in my land. Whoever insults you will pay a fine.'"],[1467,"They mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.' Then he gestured with his hand as if pouring with both of them over his head."],[1468,"Washing from janabah was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.'"],[1469,"We learned from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ how to perform the ritual purification after sexual impurity (janabah). The Prophet ﷺ said, \"As for me, I pour water on my head three times and then I wash my head to purify it from janabah.\""],[1470,"We learned about performing the ritual of washing after sexual impurity from the Prophet Muhammad (PBUH). One of us asked, \"What should we do?\" The Prophet (PBUH) answered, \"As for me, I take a handful of water and pour it on my head, and then I pour water on the rest of my body.\""],[1471,"From Jubayr b. Mut'im that they mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times,' and he gestured with both of his hands."],[1472,"We argued about washing in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour three handfuls of water over my head.'"],[1473,"They argued in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about washing from janabah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for me, I pour water over my head three times.'"],[1474,"Washing was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'As for me, it suffices me to pour over my head three times a handful of water from janabah.'"],[1475,"We mentioned washing from janabah in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'As for me, I perform wudu' as I do for prayer, then I take a handful of water three times and pour it over my head, then I wash.'"],[1476,"Washing from major ritual impurity was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"As for me, I pour water over my head three times.\""],[1477,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A Qurashi has the strength of two men from other than Quraysh.\" A questioner asked Ibn Shihab what he meant by that, and he said, \"Soundness of judgment.\""],[1478,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1479,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, who said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1480,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the ransom of the people of Badr, and I heard him recite in the Maghrib prayer: \"By the Mount, and a Book inscribed\" (Q 52:1-2)."],[1481,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, and Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, and Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, and Muad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, and Musaddad said: They said, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Muhammad ibn Jubair ibn Mut'im from his father that he heard the Prophet saw reciting in al-Maghrib \"At-Tur\". And the wording is for al-Humaidi."],[1482,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer."],[1483,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting al-Tur(surah lii) in the sunset prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 811)"],[1484,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the Maghrib prayer: 'By the Mount, and a Book inscribed' (Q 52:1-2).\""],[1485,"It is mentioned in the Fida' of the captives of Badr that I happened to coincide with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer and the Surah at-Tur that is written in a parchment spread out. He then took me from his recitation with such pain. This was the first thing I heard about the matter of Islam."],[1486,"\"Hushaim, and I think I have only heard it from Al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubair ibn Mut'im, from his father Jubair ibn Mut'im, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to speak to him about the prisoners of Badr. I met him while he was praying Maghrib or Isha with his companions. I heard him say or recite, and his voice came from the mosque, 'Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur. There is none who can avert it.' It was as if my heart was torn apart.\""],[1487,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1488,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite al-Tur in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[1489,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying with his companions the Isha or Maghrib prayer, and I heard him reciting, his voice coming out of the mosque: \"Indeed, the punishment of your Lord will occur; of it there is no repeller\" (Q 52:7-8), and it was as if my heart was cracked open."],[1490,"\"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding the captives of Badr, and he led the people in the Maghrib prayer and recited al-Tur in it.\""],[1491,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding the captives of Badr, \"If al-Mut'im b. 'Adi were alive and spoke to me about these foul ones, I would have left them for him.\""],[1492,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If Mut'im b. 'Adiyy were alive and then spoke to me concerning these foul ones—or concerning these captives—I would have released them,” meaning the captives of Badr."],[1493,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak to him about the captives of Badr, and he said: “If he had come to us regarding them, we would have granted his intercession,” meaning his father al-Mut'im b. 'Adiyy. Hushaym said: “He had a favor owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[1494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If he had come to me concerning these foul ones, I would have granted his intercession,” meaning al-Mut'im b. 'Adiyy. At that, Jubayr accepted Islam."],[1495,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the ransom of the people of Badr. When I spoke to him, he said: “If Mut'im b. 'Adiyy were with me and then spoke to me concerning these, I would have released them for him.” Mut'im b. 'Adiyy had a favor owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1496,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1497,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1498,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.” Sufyan said: “Its explanation is one who severs ties of kinship,” and the wording is that of al-Humaydi."],[1499,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1500,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.” Baqiyyah added in his narration: “ties of kinship.”"],[1502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who severs kinship ties will enter Paradise.”"],[1504,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ: “The one who severs ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[1505,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who severs ties will not enter Paradise.”"],[1584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no alliance (ḥilf) in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the time of ignorance, Islam only increases it in strength.”"],[1589,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I will surely know you, O Banū 'Abd Manāf, if you prevent any circumambulator who goes around this House at any hour of night or day.\""],[1594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A prayer in my mosque exceeds a prayer in other mosques by a thousand prayers, except the Sacred Mosque.\""],[1595,"I was with Quraysh at their encampment below 'Arafah, and I lost a donkey, so I went looking for it among the people who were at 'Arafah, and I found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Arafah."],[1598,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In his naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Jubayr b. Khalid b. Makhlad b. Iyas.\""],[1599,"In the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': \"In the naming of those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ: Jubayr b. Hubab b. al-Mundhir.\""],[1600,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those Muslims killed on the day of al-Yamamah, then from Banu Quraysh: Jubayr b. Malik, who is Ibn Buhaynah, and he is from Banu Nawfal b. 'Abd Manaf.\""],[1653,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The prescribed punishment of the sorcerer is a strike with the sword.”"],[1657,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he sent a group and appointed Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah or Ubaydah as their leader. When he went to depart, Subabah (the wife of Abu Ubaydah) wept and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . She sat down and he sent Abdullah bin Jahsh in his place and wrote a letter to him, instructing him not to read the letter until he reached a certain place. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not force anyone from your companions to travel with you.\" When he read the letter, he reconsidered and said, \"We listen and obey Allah and His Messenger.\" He informed them of the news and read the letter to them. Two men returned and the rest continued on. They met Ibn al-Hadrami and killed him without realizing that it was Rajab or Jumada [lunar months] (the sacred months). The disbelievers then said to the Muslims, \"You killed in the sacred month.\" Allah revealed the verse, \"They ask you about the sacred month - about fighting therein. Say, 'Fighting therein is great [sin], but averting [people] from the way of Allah and disbelief in Him and [preventing access to] al-Masjid al-Haram and the expulsion of its people therefrom are greater [evil] in the sight of Allah. And fitnah is greater than killing.' And they will continue to fight you until they turn you back from your religion if they are able. And whoever of you reverts from his religion [to disbelief] and dies while he is a disbeliever - for those, their deeds have become worthless in this world and the Hereafter. And those are the companions of the Fire, they will abide therein eternally\" (Quran 2:217). Some of them said, \"If they had not encountered us, they would not be burdened with sin.\" Allah revealed, \"Indeed, those who have believed and those who have emigrated and fought in the cause of Allah - those expect the mercy of Allah. And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful\" (Quran 2:218)."],[1669,"I witnessed Safwan and Jundub and his companions while he was advising them, and they said to him: Have you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I heard him say: 'Whoever lets others hear of his deed, God will let others hear of him on the Day of Resurrection.' And I think he said: 'And whoever makes a breach, God will make things hard for him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of God ﷻ, so let not God demand of you anything from His protection. For whoever He demands of anything from His protection, He will catch him and cast him into the fire of Hell.'"],[1673,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ five [days] before his death saying: 'I had among you brothers and friends, and I declare myself free to God from having any intimate friend among you. If I were to take an intimate friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend. Indeed, my Lord ﷻ has taken me as an intimate friend just as He took Abraham as an intimate friend. Indeed, those before you used to take the graves of their prophets and righteous ones as places of worship, so do not take graves as places of worship, for I forbid you from that.'"],[1710,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a bringer of good news from his expedition came to him and informed him of the victory that Allah had granted his expedition and the conquest that Allah had opened for them. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, while we were pursuing the people, whom Allah Almighty had defeated, I caught up with a man with my sword. When he felt that the sword was about to strike him, he ran and said, ‘I am a Muslim, I am a Muslim.’” He said: “Did you kill him?” He replied: “O Messenger of Allah, he only sought protection.” He said: “Why did you not split open his heart to see whether he was truthful or lying?” He said: “If I had split open his heart, how would I know? Is his heart anything but a piece of flesh?” He said: “Neither do you know what is in his heart, nor did you believe his tongue.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me.” He said: “I will not ask forgiveness for you.” He said: Then that man died and they buried him, but in the morning he was on the surface of the earth. Then they buried him again, and in the morning he was on the surface of the earth, three times. When they saw that, they were ashamed and humiliated by what had happened to him, so they carried him and threw him into one of those mountain passes."],[1711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “After me there will be trials like patches of dark night. A man will wake up a believer and become a disbeliever by evening, and a disbeliever by evening and wake up a believer.” A man among the Muslims said: “What should we do then, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Enter your houses and keep your remembrance.” A man said: “What if someone enters the house of one of us?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let him hold back his hand and be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the servant of Allah who kills. For a man may be in the group of Islam yet devour his brother’s wealth, shed his blood, disobey his Lord, and disbelieve in his Creator, and the Fire becomes due for him.”"],[1712,"A magician was performing before al-Walid b. 'Uqbah; he would take a sword and slaughter himself and do such-and-such, and it would not harm him. Jundub then rose to the sword, took it, and struck his neck. Then he recited: \"Will you then come to magic while you see plainly?\""],[1713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Ghalib b. 'Abd Allah al-Kalbi, of the Kalb of 'Awf b. Layth, on a raiding party in which I was among them. He ordered him to attack Banu al-Mulawwih at al-Kadid. He said: We set out, and when we were at Qudayd we met al-Harith b. Barsa' al-Laythi and captured him. He said: I have only come to become Muslim; I set out intending to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: We said: If you are a Muslim, a night's tethering will not harm you, and if you are otherwise, we will secure you. So we tied him up, then left behind one of our small black men who was with us. We said to him: If he struggles with you, cut off his head. Then we came to al-Kadid at sunset, and we were on one side of the valley. My companions sent me as a lookout for them to a hill overlooking the settlement. He said: I climbed it, and when I was on its top and looked at the people, I lay flat. By Allah, I was on it looking when a man came out of his tent and said to his wife: By Allah, I see a black shape that I did not see at the beginning of the day. Look in your vessels, lest the dogs have dragged off some of them. She looked and said: By Allah, I do not miss anything from my vessels. He said: Give me my bow. She gave him a bow and two arrows with it. He said: He shot an arrow, and by Allah, it did not miss my side. He said: I pulled it out and remained still. He said: Then he shot the other and placed it in my shoulder. I pulled it out and remained still. He said to his wife: If it were something that moves, it would have moved by now; my two arrows have struck it. When morning comes, look for them and take them, lest the dogs ruin them. He said: Then he entered. When the people's animals had returned from their camels and sheep, and they had milked them and were at ease and settled, we launched the raid upon them. We killed and captured the sheep. Then we drove them away, and the cry of the people went out among their tribe, and a host came. They came in pursuit of us until we passed by Ibn al-Barsa', and we took him with us along with our companion whom we had left behind. He said: The people caught up with us until we saw them, and between us and them was nothing but the valley, with us facing one side and them on the other side in pursuit of us. Then Allah brought from where He willed what we had never seen before—rain such that no one could cross it. I saw them standing, looking at us while we drove the camels, and no man among them could reach us. When we had gone up with them, I will never forget the words of a poet among the Muslims as he drove them from behind them."],[1714,"When we were at al-Ghamim, news came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Quraysh that they had sent Khalid b. al-Walid with a troop of cavalry to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked meeting him, and he was merciful toward them. He said: \"Who is a man who will turn us away from the road?\" I said: I, may my father be your ransom. So he took them on a road that had rough stony ground, hillocks, and an 'uqab (steep pass). The land leveled out for us until he brought him down at al-Hudaybiyah, which was a dry well. He tilted into it an arrow, or his arrow, from his quiver, then spat into it, then supplicated, and its springs gushed forth until I say, or we say: If we wished, we could scoop water with our hands."],[1715,"From 'Urwah, in \"the naming of those who were martyred among the Muslims on the Day of Ajnadayn: Jundub b. Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams.\""],[1716,"From Ibn Shihab, in \"the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Ajnadayn: Jundub b. 'Amr Humamah al-Dawsi, ally of Banu Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams.\""],[1717,"From 'Urwah, in \"the naming of the participants of the 'Aqabah pledge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar: Jabir b. 'Abd Allah b. Haram b. Ka'b b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salamah.\""],[1718,"From Ibn Shihab, \"in the naming of those who witnessed the 'Aqabah pledge with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar: Jabir b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr.\""],[1719,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year seventy-eight, and his age was eighty-five, and he was given the kunyah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.\""],[1720,"\"I saw on his bier a striped cloak, and Aban b. 'Uthman, who was governor of Madinah, prayed over him. Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died at the age of ninety-four, and he was given the kunyah Abu 'Abd Allah, and he had lost his sight, may Allah have mercy on him.\""],[1721,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah perished in the year seventy-four.\""],[1722,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year seventy-nine.\""],[1723,"\"Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year sixty.\""],[1724,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr saying, 'Jabir b. 'Abd Allah died in the year ninety-eight, having lost his sight.'"],[1725,"The sons of Jabir swore by Allah, and he went out, and al-Hajjaj plunged into the pit until he finished it."],[1726,"We came to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah after his sight had become weak."],[1727,"I saw Jabir b. 'Abd Allah dyeing with yellow, and he attended al-'Aqabah."],[1728,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqabah. Jabir said, 'My maternal uncle brought me out, and I could not throw a stone.'"],[1737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am Ahmad, I am Muhammad, I am al-Hashir before whom people will be gathered, and I am al-Mahi through whom Allah erases disbelief. On the Day of Resurrection the banner of praise will be with me, and I will be the leader of the messengers and the holder of their intercession.\""],[1738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no place in the seven heavens, neither a foot's span, a hand-span, nor a palm, except that there is an angel standing, bowing, or prostrating. On the Day of Resurrection they will all say: 'Glory be to You, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped, but we have not associated anything with You.'\""],[1739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the people under protection are wronged, the state becomes the state of the enemy. When adultery becomes widespread, captivity increases. When sodomy becomes widespread, Allah ﷻ withdraws His hand from creation and does not care in which valley they perish.\""],[1740,"My ears heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah while there was silver in Bilal's garment, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing it to the people. A man said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, be just.\" He said: \"Woe to you! Who will be just if I am not just? You would surely be a loser if I were not just.\" Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"Let me kill this hypocrite, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah forbid that people should say that I kill my companions. This man and his companions recite the Qur'an but it does not pass their throats; they pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through its target.\""],[1741,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Mu'adh, I am sending you to a people of the Book. If you are asked about the milky way in the sky, say: It is the saliva of a serpent beneath the Throne.\""],[1742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah wills evil for a servant, He makes him flourish in mud and clay until he builds.\""],[1743,"On the day of the battle of al-Ta'if, the Prophet ﷺ stood with Ali ؓ for a long time during the day. Abu Bakr ؓ said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, your private conversation with Ali has been long today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I did not confide in him; rather Allah confided in him.\""],[1744,"My maternal uncle Jadd b. Qays carried me among seventy riders who came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with his uncle al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib and said: \"O uncle, take the oath from your maternal nephews.\" The seventy said: \"O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish.\" He said: \"As for what I ask you for my Lord, that you worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. As for what I ask for myself, that you protect me from what you protect yourselves from.\""],[1745,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was black."],[1746,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the sea: \"Its water is purifying and its dead animals are lawful.\""],[1747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on an expedition, and we had no food except a leather bag of dates. He appointed Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah over us, and he would give each of us a handful of dates, until we ran out, and he would give us one date at a time. Then the sea cast up a creature and we ate from it. Abu Ubaydah ordered its rib and it was bent, then he ordered a man who mounted a camel, and the rider passed on the camel."],[1748,"Dates and unripe dates are wine."],[1749,"From 'Urwah: \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Jubayr b. Iyas b. Khalid b. Makhlad b. Zurayq.\""],[1750,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Dinar b. al-Najjar: Jabir b. Khalid b. ʿAbd al-Ashhal, who has no descendants."],[1751,"From ʿUrwa, regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Riʾab b. Nuʿman b. Sinan."],[1752,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then Banu ʿUbayd b. ʿAdi: Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Ziyad b. Nuʿman."],[1753,"Ibn Ishaq: When Allah, exalted is He, wished to make His religion prevail, to honor His Prophet ﷺ, and to fulfill His promise, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went forth in the season in which the group from the Ansar met him. They were, as they claim, six, among them Jabir b. ʿAbd Allah b. Riʾab."],[1754,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Jibril passed by me while I was praying, and he smiled at me, so I smiled back at him."],[1755,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Khadija: Jibril came to me and said, “Give Khadija glad tidings of a house of reeds in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[1756,"And Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Haysha said."],[1757,"From Ibn Shihab: Among the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Muʿawiya b. Malik b. ʿAwf: Jabr b. ʿAtik b. al-Harith."],[1758,"Jabir b. ʿAtik died in the year sixty-one; his age was seventy-one."],[1759,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say: “Part of jealousy is loved by Allah and part of it is hated by Allah. The jealousy Allah loves is jealousy in suspicion; the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy without suspicion. And part of pride is loved by Allah and part of it is hated by Allah. The pride Allah loves is a man’s pride in himself at the time of charity and fighting; the pride Allah hates is his pride in wrongdoing and immorality.”"],[1760,"And his father was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Of jealousy, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates; and of pride, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates. As for the jealousy that Allah loves, it is jealousy in suspicion; and the jealousy that Allah hates is jealousy without suspicion. And the pride that Allah loves is a man’s showing off of himself for Allah at the time of battle; and the pride that Allah hates is pride in wrongdoing or in wickedness.”"],[1761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Of jealousy, there is what Allah loves and of it what Allah hates. As for what Allah loves of jealousy, it is jealousy in suspicion; and as for the jealousy that Allah hates, it is jealousy without suspicion. And as for the pride that Allah loves, it is a man’s showing off of himself at the time of battle; and as for the pride that Allah hates, it is a man’s showing off in wrongdoing and wickedness.”"],[1765,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever goes out as a fighter in the path of Allah,” then he joined his three fingers, then said: “And where are the fighters? For if he falls from his mount and dies, then his reward has fallen upon Allah; or if he dies a natural death, then his reward has fallen upon Allah; and whoever is killed instantly has certainly deserved the final abode.”"],[1766,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jābir b. ʿAtīk, from ʿAtīk b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAtīk—and he is the grandfather of ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh, the father of his mother—that he informed him that Jābir b. ʿAtīk informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit ʿAbd Allāh b. Thābit and found him overcome. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to him, but he did not answer. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return,” and he said, “We have been overcome for you, O Abū al-Rabīʿ.” The women shouted and wept, and Ibn ʿAtīk began to hush them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave them; for when it becomes due, let no weepers weep.” They said, “And what is the due, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “When he dies.” His daughter said, “By Allah, I had hoped that you would be a martyr, for you had completed your equipment.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah ﷻ has indeed placed his reward upon his intention. And what do you count as martyrdom?” They said, “Being killed in the path of Allah.” He said, “Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the path of Allah: the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one with a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies by fire is a martyr, the one who dies under a collapsed building is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr.”"],[1767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him during his illness, and someone said, “We had certainly hoped that his death would be a killing in the path of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In that case, the martyrs of my nation would indeed be few. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the one with a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one who dies by fire is a martyr, and the one with pleurisy is a martyr.”"],[1768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked in the mosque of Banū Muʿāwiya for three things, and he was given two and denied one. He asked Him that He should not destroy his nation by famine, and that He should not give an enemy dominance over them, and he was given these. And he asked Him that He should not put their misfortune among themselves, and he was denied that."],[1769,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by his oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him and made the Fire due for him.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something little?” He said, “Even if it is a toothstick.”"],[1770,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever unjustly takes the wealth of a Muslim by his right hand, Allah has forbidden Paradise for him.\" They asked, \"Even if it is a small amount, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Even if it is a twig of a miswak tree.\""],[1772,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Everything that is not part of the remembrance of Allah ﷻ is either frivolity or heedlessness, except four qualities: a man’s walking between the two targets, his training of his horse, his playing with his family, and learning swimming.”"],[1773,"I met the Prophet ﷺ among his Companions in the market, and I asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah where he was heading. They said, “He is marking out a mosque for your people.” So I returned, and there were my people standing. I said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out a mosque for us and fixed a piece of wood in the qiblah, standing it in it.”"],[1774,"I went to the market and met the Prophet ﷺ among his Companions. I asked them where he was heading, and they said, “He is marking out a mosque for your people.” So I returned and found my people standing. I said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out a mosque for us with his foot and fixed a piece of wood in the qiblah, fixing it in it.”"],[1776,"I sat with the Messenger of God ﷺ more than a hundred times."],[1777,"Jabir b. Samurah died, and Amr b. Hurayth prayed over him."],[1778,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: This religion will continue to be strong till the time of twelve caliphs. The people then uttered: Allah is more great and uproared. He then silently a word which I could not understand. So I said to my father: What did he say, father ? He said: All of them will belong to Quraish. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4280)"],[1779,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Islam will remain mighty until twelve caliphs.”"],[1781,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “This community will have twelve upright leaders; those who abandon them will not harm them.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ whispered a word I did not hear. I said to my father: What was the word the Prophet ﷺ whispered? He said: “All of them from Quraysh.”"],[1782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon one day, and I heard him say, \"This religion will always be strong, preventing anyone who opposes it, until twelve will rule it, all of them from Quraysh.\" Then the people became confused and started discussing, and I did not understand what he meant by \"all of them\". So I asked my father, \"Oh my father, what did he mean by 'all of them'?\" He said, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[1783,"I have heard the Prophet ﷺ saying in the Farewell Pilgrimage, \"This matter will always remain apparent to anyone who seeks it, unaffected by any opposing or deviant individuals, until there have been twelve Caliphs from the Quraysh.\""],[1784,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I heard him say, \"The matter of this nation will remain apparent until there are twelve (caliphs).\" And he said a word that I did not hear, and my father was closer to him in the gathering than me. So I asked, \"What did he say?\" He said, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[1785,"I went to the Prophet with my father, and the Messenger of Allah said, \"This nation will remain upright in its affair until there are twelve caliphs.\" Then he said a whispered word, and I asked my father what he said. He said, \"All of them will be from Quraish.\""],[1786,"I came with my father to the mosque and the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon. I heard him say, \"There will be twelve successors after me.\" Then he lowered his voice and I couldn't catch what he was saying. So, I asked my father, \"What was he saying?\" He replied, \"All of them will be from the Quraysh tribe.\""],[1787,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage, \"The affairs of this Ummah will continue to be stable for those who adhere to it, until there are twelve leaders among you.\" Then he said something I did not hear, so I asked my father, who was closer to him than me, what did he say? He said he said, \"All of them will be from Quraish.\""],[1788,"We heard Jabir b. Samurah say: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said: “This affair will continue standing until twelve amirs have passed.” He said: And he shortened a word I did not hear. He said: When the Prophet ﷺ fell silent, I said to my father Samurah: What was the word he shortened? He said: “All of them from Quraysh.”"],[1789,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When God ﷻ bestows a favor on a servant, let him begin with himself and his household.”"],[1790,"Regarding a hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God gives any of you good, let him begin with himself and his family.”"],[1791,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on a Friday evening, the day he stoned Maiz al-Aslami, say: “A band of Muslims will conquer the White House.” I said: Kisra? He said: “Kisra.”"],[1792,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will extract the treasure of the White One, Kisra and the family of Kisra.”"],[1793,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the one who precedes you to the Pool.”"],[1794,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I am your predecessor at the Lake-Fount, and some of you will be brought in front of me till I will see them and then they will be taken away from me and I will say, 'O Lord, my companions!' It will be said, 'You do not know what they did after you had left.' (Using translation from Bukhārī 6576)"],[1795,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"The religion will continue to be established until there are twelve caliphs from the Quraysh, then there will emerge liars before the Hour.\""],[1796,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The religion will continue to stand until the Day of Judgment, or until there are twelve caliphs, all of them from the Quraysh.'\""],[1797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows behind me as the angels form rows before their Lord?” They said: How do the angels form rows before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1798,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to us and said: “Will you not form rows as the angels form rows before their Lord?” They said: O Messenger of God, how do the angels form rows before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?” He said: “They complete the foremost rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not form rows as the angels who are in the presence of their Lord form rows?” They said, “And how do the angels who are in the presence of their Lord form rows?” He said: “They establish the first rows and stand close together in the row.”"],[1801,"Why do you stand in rows as the angels do in the presence of their Lord? We asked: how do the angles stand in rows in the presence of their Lord? He replied: they make the first row complete and keep close together in the row. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 661)"],[1803,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gestured to us to sit, so we sat. Then he said: “What prevents you from forming rows as the angels form rows in the presence of the Most Merciful?” They said, “And how do they form rows, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “They complete the first rows and align themselves in the rows in a compact manner.”"],[1804,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them while they were raising their eyes, and he said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1806,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Some people will surely stop raising their eyes to the sky during prayer, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[1807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The people who lift their eyes towards the sky in Prayer should avoid it or they would lose their eyesight. (Using translation from Muslim 428)"],[1808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Certain people should stop casting their gazes around during prayer or else their sight will not be returned to them.\""],[1809,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque and saw them raising their hands. He said: “What is the matter with them, raising their hands as if they were the tails of restive horses? Be still during the prayer.”"],[1828,"I entered with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat with him, and he said, \"Islam will continue to be apparent until there are twelve princes or caliphs, all of them from Quraysh.\""],[1868,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, may I pray in the garment in which I have intercourse?” He said: “Yes, unless you see something on it, in which case wash it.”"],[1869,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “This matter (Islam) will remain prevail, and no one who opposes it will harm it.”"],[1976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It suffices one of you, when he finishes his prayer, to place his hand on his thigh and greet his brother on his right: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,' and on his left the like of that.\""],[1977,"I sat with the Prophet ﷺ more than a hundred times in the mosque; his companions would sit reciting poetry to one another, and sometimes they would discuss matters of the pre-Islamic era, and the Prophet ﷺ would smile with them."],[1980,"«When the Prophet ﷺ returned from the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdah, a horse was brought to him unsaddled, and he mounted it while we walked around him.»"],[1988,"«I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deliver a sermon except standing on Friday. He would deliver a sermon, then sit, then stand and deliver a sermon. He used to deliver two sermons with a sitting between them.»"],[2001,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah, \"Did you mention poetry in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes, we used to mention poems in his presence and laugh, and he would smile.\""],[2026,"The Prophet ﷺ would not go out on the day of Fitr until he had eaten seven dates."],[2035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose to pray Fajr and then leaned with his hand."],[2036,"Ma'iz, a short man wearing a waist-wrapper, was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining on a cushion. When he was brought, he turned aside from the cushion and spoke with him. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned red, and he knew that he had angered him. So he gestured with his hand: “Stone him.” Then he sent a man after him and spoke with him briefly. Then he said, “Take him away and stone him.” The people rose, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: “Now then, whenever we set out in the way of Allah, one of them stays behind and bleats like a billy goat, giving one of them something. Indeed, if Allah gives me power over any of them, I will make an example of him.”"],[2037,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come out for the funeral of Thabit b. al-Dahdah while he was on a white-faced horse with white feet, wearing nothing on it, and the people were with him around him. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted, then sat until it was finished, then stood and mounted his horse, then departed riding."],[2038,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver his sermons on the pulpit while sitting and someone denied it, and Jabir said: \"I bear witness that he used to deliver his sermons while standing, then he would sit and then stand again and deliver the sermon of the hereafter.\" He said, \"So I said, 'How were his sermons?' He said, 'He would advise the people and recite verses from the Book of Allah, and it would be concise. His prayer timings were in accordance with the rising and setting of the sun and the sky and the morning prayer and the noon prayer, except for the morning prayer and the noon prayer when Bilal would recite the call to prayer when the sun was declining, and sometimes the call to prayer would be delayed a little and sometimes he would hasten it. As for the call to prayer, it should not be delayed and the Asr prayer should be offered close to the time that you normally offer it, and the Maghrib prayer close to the time that you normally offer it, and the evening prayer should be delayed a little from your prayer timings.'\""],[2039,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray prayers similar to your prayer. He would pray Zuhr when the sun declined, and in the Fajr prayer he would recite Qāf wa-l-Qur'ān al-Majīd, Yā Sīn, and the like."],[2043,"I saw the seal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was by his shoulder like a pigeon's egg."],[2044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling animals for animals on credit."],[2045,"I heard Jabir b. Samurah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointing with his finger while in prayer. When he said the taslim, I heard him say: “O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know.”"],[2046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This nation will remain upright, and its affairs will be apparent against its enemies until twelve caliphs pass from them, all of them from Quraysh.\" When he returned home, Quraysh came to him and asked, \"And then what will happen?\" He said, \"Then there will be turmoil.\""],[2055,"I entered with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"Indeed, this matter will not pass and it will not come to an end until twelve Caliphs have passed.\" Then he said something that I did not understand. I asked my father, \"What did he say?\" He said, \"All of them are from the Quraysh.\""],[2057,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"There will be twelve leaders after me.\" Then he spoke softly, and I asked the one next to me, and he said, \"All of them are from Quraysh.\""],[2059,"I was in the assembly of the Prophet ﷺ with Samurah and Abu Umamah, and he said: \"Obscenity and indecency have nothing to do with Islam in any way. Indeed, the best people in Islam are those who are best in character.\""],[2060,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: \"Twelve custodians from Quraysh; the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them.\" He said: Then I turned around, and there was 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ and my father among the people, and they confirmed the hadith for me just as I had heard it."],[2061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated. May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated. May God curse whoever returns to a Bedouin life after having migrated, except during a period of tribulation, for Bedouin life is better than remaining in the midst of tribulation.\""],[2062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Will you not form rows just as the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, how do the angels form rows in the presence of their Lord?\" He said: \"They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row.\""],[2063,"I went to the market and encountered the Prophet ﷺ among his companions. I asked them where he was heading, and they said: \"He is going to mark out a mosque for your people.\" So I returned and found my people standing. I said: \"What is the matter with you?\" They said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ marked out a mosque for us with his foot, and he set up a piece of wood in the qiblah that he had planted there.\""],[2072,"I saw cut squash before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: What do you do with this? He said: \"We use it to increase our food.\""],[2078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take fresh water for the head.\""],[2115,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks the world through the work of the Hereafter, his face will be blackened, his remembrance will be effaced, and his name will be registered in the Fire.”"],[2116,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a captive who had been among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They had captured him while he was still a polytheist, but then he embraced Islam. They brought that captive to the Prophet ﷺ, who gave him two garments as a gift, one made of fine linen and the other made of coarse wool. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go to Aisha, and she will give you from the fine garments that she has, two garments.\" He entered upon Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and said, \"May Allah bless you, choose for me two garments from these fine garments that you have, as the Prophet ﷺ has given me two garments from them.\" She replied, \"May I extend the garment for you like I see others?\" He said, \"Take this one and take this one.\" At that time, Arab women did not cover their faces."],[2123,"“ʿAbdullah b. Rawaha estimated for the people of Khaybar for one year only, then he was struck down on the Day of Muʾta. Then Jabir b. Sakhr b. Khansaʾ—the Messenger of God ﷺ used to send him after Ibn Rawaha, and he would estimate for them.”"],[2138,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ while food was in front of him, so Jarhad brought his left hand near to eat, and his right hand was injured. He said: “Eat with the right.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is injured. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ blew on it, and he did not complain about it until he died."],[2139,"That he came with a group of his people wanting to accept Islam. They attended the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the salam, he said: “Let every man take the hand of his companion.” None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was big and tall, so no one could be preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I finished it until he had milked seven goats for me, and I finished them. Then I was brought a cooked dish in a pot, and I finished it. Umm Ayman said: May Allah starve whoever starves the Messenger of Allah this night. He said: “Enough, O Umm Ayman. He has eaten his provision, and our provision is with Allah.” When morning came, they went out and gathered with his companions, and each man told what had been brought to him. Jahjah said: Seven goats were milked for me, and I finished them, and a cooked dish in a pot, and I finished it. Then they prayed the Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Let every man take the hand of his companion.” None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and me. I was big and tall, so no one could be preferred over me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to his house and milked a goat for me, and I drank my fill and was satisfied. Umm Ayman said: O Messenger of Allah, is this not our guest? He said: “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tonight he ate in the intestine of a believer, and before that he ate in the intestine of a disbeliever. A disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while a believer eats in one intestine.”"],[2140,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta’if: Julayhah b. ‘Abd Allah b. Muharib b. Nashib b. Sa‘d b. Layth."],[2141,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended the expedition to Tabuk, he said to Jadd b. Qays, \"Would you like (to fight) the fair-skinned women (lit. daughters of the yellow ones)?\" He said, \"Permit me to stay behind and do not tempt me.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: \"And among them is he who says, 'Permit me and do not tempt me'\" (Qur'an 9:49)."],[2142,"We met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Friday, and he asked us who we were. We said, \"We are the Banu 'Abd Manaf.\" He said, \"You are the Banu 'Abd Allah (servants of Allah).\""],[2145,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Mounts are not to be ridden except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Mosque of Jerusalem (Bayt al-Maqdis).\""],[2146,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The livers of camels are only to be driven to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No journeys are to be undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of the Messenger, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2148,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No mounts are to be ridden except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and the farthest mosque (al-Masjid al-Aqsa).\""],[2149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"I am riding out to the Jews. Whoever goes with me among you should not initiate the greeting of peace to them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\" So when we came to them, they greeted us, and we said, \"And upon you.\""],[2150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are going tomorrow to the Jews. When you meet them and they greet you, say, 'And upon you.'\" So we met them and they greeted us, and we said, \"And upon you.\""],[2151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am proceeding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of peace with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[2152,"From Abu Basra al-Ghifari ؓ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the 'Asr prayer one day at al-Mukhammas, then departed and said: \"This prayer was presented to those before you, but they neglected it and abandoned it. Whoever of you prays it will have its reward doubled twice, and there is no prayer after it until the witness (the star) rises.\" Al-Layth said: \"I heard it from Khayr b. Nu'aym with this chain.\""],[2153,"That he heard Abu Basrah al-Ghifari say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the ‘Asr prayer at al-Mukhammas, a valley among some of their valleys, then he said, “This prayer was presented to those before you, but they neglected it. Behold, whoever prays it, his reward is doubled, and there is no prayer after it until you see the witness” — and that is the star."],[2154,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ informed me that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Indeed, Allah has added a prayer for you, so pray it between the 'Isha prayer and the Witr prayer. Indeed, it is the Witr prayer.\" And know that he is Abu Basrah al-Ghifari."],[2155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has added to you a prayer, so preserve it, and He has made its time from the period between Isha and Fajr, and it is Witr.\""],[2156,"I boarded a ship from al-Fustat with Abu Basrah, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ. Then he brought his lunch near, and said to me, “Come closer.” I said, “Aren’t we in the houses?” Abu Basrah said, “Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”"],[2157,"That he traveled with Abu Basrah al-Ghifari in Ramadan. When they departed from al-Fustat, he called for food while we could still see al-Fustat. I said to him, “Will you eat while, if we wanted to look at al-Fustat, we could see it?” He said, “Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions?” Then he broke his fast."],[2158,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I asked my Lord for four things, and He gave me three and withheld one. I asked Him that my Ummah not unite upon misguidance, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not destroy them with years of famine as He destroyed the nations before them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not let an enemy from other than themselves overcome them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him that He not make them into factions, nor let them taste one another’s violence, but He withheld it from me.”"],[2159,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of his expeditions, and I was riding an emaciated, weak mare of mine, so I was at the rear of the people. He caught up with me and said, “Walk on, O owner of the horse.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, she is emaciated and weak.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised a whip he had with him and struck her with it, and said, “O Allah, bless him in her.” He said: I saw myself holding her head back so that she would not outrun the people. He said: And I sold one of her foals for twelve thousand."],[2160,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group from the Azd on Friday, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited us to a meal that was before him. We said, “We are fasting.” He said, “Did you fast yesterday?” We said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” We said, “No.” He said, “Then break your fast.” Then he said, “Do not fast on Friday alone.”"],[2162,"From Junadah al-Azdi, that they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being a group of eight men, he being the eighth of them, on Friday. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food and said to one man, “Eat.” He said, “I am fasting.” He said to another, “Eat.” He said, “I am fasting,” until he had asked them all. Then he said, “Did you fast yesterday?” They said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” They said, “No.” So he ordered them to break their fast."],[2163,"That they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, eight men, he being the eighth of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought food near to them on a Friday, and he said, “Eat.” They said, “We are fasting.” He said, “Did you fast yesterday?” They said, “No.” He said, “Will you fast tomorrow?” They said, “No.” He said, “Then break your fast.”"],[2164,"That Junadah al-Azdi led a people in prayer. When he stood for the prayer, he turned to his right and said, “Do you approve?” They said, “Yes.” Then he did the same on his left, then said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever leads a people while they dislike him, his prayer does not go beyond his collarbone.’”"],[2165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things are from the deeds of the people of ignorance that the people of Islam will not abandon: seeking rain from the stars, reviling lineage, and wailing over the dead.”"],[2166,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with camels that I had branded on their noses. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Junadah, did you find no limb to brand except on the face? Indeed, ahead of you is retribution.” He said, “I leave the matter to you, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Bring me something that has no brand on it.” So I brought him a two-year-old male camel and a three-year-old female camel. I placed the branding iron on the neck, but he kept saying, “Move it back, move it back,” until it reached the thigh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Brand with the blessing of Allah.” So I branded them on their thighs. Their zakah was two three-year-old females, and they were ninety."],[2167,"From Jurmuz al-Hujaymi, he said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said, “I advise you not to be a curser.”"],[2168,"He heard Jurmuz al-Hujaymi say: I said, 'O Messenger of God, advise me.' He said, 'I advise you not to be a curser.'"],[2170,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'They brought a man to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This man wanted to kill you.\" He said to him, \"Do not be afraid, do not be afraid. If you had intended that, you would not have been given power over me.\"'"],[2171,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had a dream, so he sent for him. He came and narrated it to him. He had a large belly. He said, pointing with his finger at his belly, 'If this were in something other than this, it would be better for you.'"],[2172,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with a large belly. He said, pointing with his finger at his belly, 'If this were in something other than this, it would be better for you.'"],[2173,"It was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that there was a freed slave of the Bani Abd al-Muttalib who prayed all night and did not sleep, fasted continuously without breaking his fast. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"As for me, I pray and sleep, fast and break my fast. For every deed, there is a span (of time), and for every span (of time), there is an interval. Whoever follows the interval according to the Sunnah, is guided, and whoever goes beyond that, is astray.\""],[2174,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the later ones are the worst.'"],[2175,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'The best of people are my generation, then the one that follows it, then the later ones are the worst.'"],[2176,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me from three things: wearing a gold ring, wearing qassi cloth, and using a saddle cloth."],[2177,"A group from Kindah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'You are from us,' claiming him. He said, 'We do not trace our lineage through our mothers, nor do we disown our fathers. We are the children of al-Nadr b. Kinanah.'"],[2178,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'From whom are you, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'We are the Banu al-Nadr b. Kinanah. We do not trace our lineage through our mothers, nor do we disown our fathers.'"],[2179,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, send my brother Zayd with me.' He said, 'That is up to him. If he goes with you, I will not prevent him.' Zayd said, 'No, by God, O Messenger of God, I will never prefer anyone over you.' He said, 'I saw that my brother's opinion was better than mine.'"],[2181,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he did not go on a military expedition, would give his weapon to Ali or Usamah ؓ."],[2182,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'When you retire to your bed, recite \"Say, O disbelievers\" until you finish it, for it is a declaration of freedom from polytheism.'"],[2183,"From Jabalah b. al-Azraq, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed beside a wall with many stones, a Zuhr or 'Asr prayer. When he sat in the two rak'ahs, a scorpion came out and stung him, and he fainted. The people treated him with incantations. When he regained consciousness, he said, “Allah healed me, not your incantation.”"],[2184,"And in the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': “In naming those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ , Jabalah b. 'Amr, and from Banu Bayadah, a Badri.”"],[2185,"And in the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi': “In his naming of those who were present with 'Ali b. Abi Talib: Jabalah from Banu Bayadah, a Badri.”"],[2186,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have a desert area in which I pray. Command me a night to go down to the mosque to pray in it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Go down on the night of the twenty-third.”"],[2187,"I recited aloud behind the Prophet ﷺ. When he finished, he said, “O Jahr, let your Lord hear, but do not let me hear.”"],[2188,"The Prophet ﷺ wrote him a letter, and he patched his bucket with it. His daughter said to him, “You took the letter of the master of the Arabs and patched your bucket with it!” So he fled, taking every little and much that was his, then later came as a Muslim. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Look for whatever of your belongings you find before the division of shares, and take it.”"],[2189,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to consult him about jihad. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do you have parents?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Stay with them, for Paradise is under their feet.”"],[2190,"From Jidar, a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Our enemy met us, and he stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “O people, you have woken up among green, yellow, and red, and in the baggage is what is in them. When you meet your enemy, advance, advance! For there is no one who charges in the path of Allah but two of the wide-eyed houris hasten to him. When he is martyred, the first drop that falls from his blood, Allah ﷻ expiates every sin from him, and the two wipe the dust from his face, saying, ‘We are for you,’ and he says, ‘I am for you both.’”"],[2191,"I heard Junayd b. Sab' say, “I fought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of the day as an disbeliever, and I fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim.” And it was revealed about us: {And had it not been for believing men and believing women} [Qur'an 48:25]. He said, “We were nine persons: seven men and two women.”"],[2192,"“Abu 'Abd Allah, meaning Jarir, went early to al-Kunasah to buy a mount from there.”"],[2193,"I said to Jarir, “O Abu 'Amr.”"],[2194,"“I saw Jarir dyeing his beard yellow.”"],[2195,"I saw Jarir dyeing [his hair] with saffron and turmeric."],[2196,"I saw Jarir b. 'Abdullah dyeing his head and beard with black."],[2197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will appear before you the best of a blessed people, upon whom is the touch of an angel.\" Then Jarir b. 'Abdullah appeared."],[2198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Jareer is from us, the people of the household, both in appearance and lineage.” He repeated it three times."],[2199,"Jarir ؓ dueled Mihran and killed him. His belt was valued at thirty thousand, and whoever dueled a man and killed him had the right to his spoils. They wrote to 'Umar ؓ, so 'Umar said: \"This is not among the spoils that are given; it is neither from weapons nor from horses.\" He did not grant it to him as a special reward and made it part of the general booty."],[2200,"When 'Umar ؓ led the people in prayer, something (i.e., wind) came out from a man, so he said: \"I firmly resolve that the one who did this must perform ablution and repeat his prayer.\" Jarir said: \"Would you also firmly resolve that everyone who heard it must perform ablution and repeat the prayer?\" He said: \"What an excellent thing you have said, may Allah reward you with good,\" and he ordered them to do that."],[2201,"I was a doorkeeper at the door of Jarir b. 'Abdullah. He would go out and mount a mule of his, and he would carry his servant behind him."],[2202,"Indeed a man clothes himself while he is naked—meaning thin clothes."],[2203,"Jarir and al-Ash'ath b. Qays met at a funeral, and al-Ash'ath gave precedence to Jarir, so he led the funeral prayer over it."],[2204,"Jarir, 'Adi b. Hatim, and Hanzalah the scribe left Kufah for Qarqisiya, and they said: \"We will not stay in a city where 'Uthman ؓ is reviled.\""],[2205,"I accompanied Jarir, and he would serve me.\" He was older than Anas. Jarir said: \"I saw the Ansar doing something for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, such that I would not see any one of them except that I honored him."],[2206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled me since I embraced Islam, nor did he ever see me except that he smiled."],[2207,"I heard Jarir b. 'Abdullah say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw me except that he smiled in my face.\""],[2208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never veiled me since I embraced Islam, nor did he ever see me except that he smiled in my face."],[2209,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ never screened me since I became Muslim, and never saw me but that he smiled.”"],[2210,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ never screened me since I became Muslim, and never saw me but that he smiled.”"],[2211,"Jarir said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2212,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see the moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2213,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was looking at the moon on the night of the full moon, and he said: “Indeed you will be presented before your Lord and you will see Him just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting.}"],[2214,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and he looked at the moon on the night of the fourteenth and said: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited this verse: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.}"],[2216,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will see your Lord as you see the moon, you will not be harmed by seeing Him.\""],[2219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed you will see your Lord, not being harmed in seeing Him, just as you look at the night of the full moon.”"],[2220,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: “Indeed you will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection clearly (ʿiyānan) just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset, then do so.” Then he recited: {And glorify the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting.} Abu al-Qasim said: In this hadith there is an additional wording, namely his saying “clearly (ʿiyānan),” which Abu Shihab alone narrated, and he is a careful memorizer of the trustworthy Muslims."],[2221,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the fourteenth of a month, and he said: “Do you see this moon? Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this moon, not being harmed in seeing Him. So whoever of you is able, let him never be overcome in respect of a prayer before sunrise and before sunset.”"],[2222,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night, and our eyes were raised and we began looking at the moon on the night of the full moon. He said: “Indeed you are looking at your Lord just as you look at this, not being harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome in respect of two prayers, then do so: a prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.”"],[2223,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said to us: “Indeed you will see your Lord just as you see this, not being harmed in seeing Him.”"],[2224,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the moon rose. He said: “You will certainly look at your Lord, not being harmed in seeing Him, just as you look at the moon.”"],[2225,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2226,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2227,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God will not show mercy to one who does not show mercy to people.”"],[2228,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2229,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, God will not show mercy to him.”"],[2244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of the idols of Jahiliyyah remains except Dhul-Khalasah.\""],[2245,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man from the best of Dhū Yumn will enter upon you through the door; on his face is the touch of an angel.\" Then Jarir entered."],[2246,"I was in Yemen with Dhū Kalāʿ and Dhū ʿAmr. I came to inform them about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Dhū ʿAmr said: \"O Jarir, if your companion is as you describe, his term has already come three days ago.\" Then a man was raised up for us, and we said: \"What is the news?\" They said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has passed away, and Abu Bakr ؓ has been appointed as his successor, and the people are righteous.\" Then we returned, and they said: \"Convey peace to your companion.\" Then Dhū ʿAmr said: \"O Jarir, you will remain righteous as long as when a leader dies, another leader stands up. But when it becomes swords, you will become kings, pleased with the pleasure of kings and angry with the anger of kings.\""],[2251,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a military expedition to Khathʿam. Some of them sought protection by prostrating, but killing was hastened upon them. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he ordered half of the blood money for them and said, “I am free from every Muslim who resides among the polytheists.” They said, “O Messenger of God, why?” He said, “Their fires should not be visible to each other.”"],[2259,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He raised his gaze to the sky and said, “Glory be to God! What trials are being sent down upon them, like the sending of rain?”"],[2262,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The one who transgresses in charity is like the one who withholds it.”"],[2268,"When the ayah, \"Your Lord would never destroy the towns unjustly while their people were reformers,\" was revealed, he said: \"That is, their people treat one another justly.\""],[2269,"\"We used to wipe (over leather socks) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" We said: \"Before the revelation of al-Ma'idah or after its revelation?\" He said: \"I only became Muslim after the revelation of al-Ma'idah.\""],[2278,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2279,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us on the night of the full moon and looked at the moon, then said, “You will see your Lord on the Day of Resurrection just as you see this moon, and you will suffer no hardship in seeing Him.”"],[2282,"The Prophet ﷺ said to the owner of a right, “Take your right in a manner that is either full or less than full.”"],[2300,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he urged the people to give charity until that was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then a man from the Ansar came with a piece of gold and threw it to the Prophet ﷺ, and joy was seen in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “Whoever establishes a good sunnah in Islam that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the like of the reward of those who act upon it, without any of their rewards being diminished. And whoever establishes an evil sunnah in Islam that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the like of the burden of those who act upon it, without any of their burdens being diminished.”"],[2303,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, stretch out your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you, and set the conditions upon me, for you know the conditions better than I.\" He said, \"I pledge allegiance to you on the basis that you do not associate anything with God, that you establish prayer, give zakah, give sincere counsel to the Muslim, and separate from the polytheist.\""],[2304,"I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, and he stipulated for me to worship God, not associating anything with Him, and to give sincere counsel to every Muslim."],[2340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah only has mercy on the merciful among His servants.\""],[2344,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When a slave runs away, no prayer is accepted from him, and if he dies, he dies as a disbeliever.\" Then a slave of Jarir ran away, so he seized him and struck his neck. Abu al-Qasim said: \"Its meaning is that he disbelieved and joined the abode of war.\""],[2349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The charity collector should not return from you except while he is pleased.\""],[2355,"That there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan."],[2377,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, does not show mercy to the one who does not show mercy to people.\""],[2386,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over leather socks. He said: ‘Three days for the traveler and a day and a night for the resident.’"],[2443,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The freed ones of Quraysh, the freed ones of Thaqif, the Muhajirun, and the Ansar are allies of one another.\""],[2444,"I heard Jarir b. 'Abd Allah, who was our commander, say: \"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then I returned, and he called me and said: 'I will not accept from you until you pledge allegiance with sincerity to every Muslim.' So I pledged allegiance to him.\""],[2459,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ took our pledge upon hearing and obedience and sincere counsel for every Muslim, so I pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2460,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon hearing and obedience and sincere counsel for every Muslim.”"],[2461,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[2462,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven.”"],[2463,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not forgive will not be forgiven, and whoever does not repent will not be granted repentance.”"],[2464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy, and whoever does not repent will not be granted repentance.”"],[2465,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Allah does not forgive one who does not forgive, and Allah does not show mercy to one who does not show mercy.”"],[2466,"Abu Sa'id, the servant of Banu Hashim, narrated to us and Ahmad bin Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us and Bishr bin Adam narrated to us and Ya'qub bin Ishaq al-Hadrami said they both narrated to us and Zaidah narrated to me from Ziyad bin Ilaqa from Jarir who said, \"A scholar told me in Yemen that if your companion was a prophet, then he has died.\" He said, \"So the Prophet ﷺ died on Monday.\""],[2467,"I heard Jarir b. Abdullah say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw me except that he smiled.”"],[2468,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Any slave who runs away has indeed absolved himself of the covenant of protection.”"],[2469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a slave runs away, Allah’s covenant of protection is absolved from him.” He did not mention al-Mughirah b. Shubayl."],[2470,"When I approached Madinah, I made my mount kneel, then I untied my bag and put on my fine clothes and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. I greeted the Prophet ﷺ, and the people stared at me. I said to the one sitting next to me: “O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention anything about me?” He said: “Yes, he mentioned you with the best of mentions. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, he digressed in his sermon and said: ‘There will enter upon you from this mountain pass or from this gate one of the best of those with blessing; indeed, on his face is the mark of an angel.’” He said: “So I praised Allah for what He had bestowed upon me.”"],[2471,"“I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he stipulated sincerity to every Muslim.”"],[2472,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2473,"“The Prophet ﷺ passed by some women and greeted them.”"],[2474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[2475,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2476,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2477,"“I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wiped over his leather socks after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed.”"],[2478,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.\""],[2479,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2481,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “Whoever does not show mercy to people will not be shown mercy by God.”"],[2482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.\""],[2483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah wrote in the Mother of the Book before He created the heavens and the earth: 'I am the Compassionate, the Merciful. I created the womb and derived for it a name from My names. So whoever maintains it, I will maintain him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him.'\""],[2484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not show mercy to those on the earth will not be shown mercy by the One in the heaven.\""],[2485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon to the people one day and said: \"There has come to you the best of a blessed man, on whose face is the touch of an angel,\" meaning me."],[2486,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Fasting three days of every month is equivalent to fasting for a lifetime: the days of the full moon, the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.\""],[2488,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah.\""],[2489,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heaven will show mercy to you.\""],[2490,"\"I embraced Islam only after the revelation of the Table Spread (Surah al-Ma'idah), and I only saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his feet after I embraced Islam.\""],[2491,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.”"],[2492,"We witnessed the season during the pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , and it was the Farewell Pilgrimage. We reached a place called Ghadir Khumm, and the call for prayer was made. The immigrants and the supporters gathered and the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , stood in our midst and said, \"O people, what do you bear witness to?\" They said, \"We bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\" He said, \"Then what else?\" They said, \"And that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.\" He said, \"Then who is your guardian?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger are our guardians.\" He said, \"Who is your guardian?\" Then he struck Ali on his shoulder, and he stood him up, then he pulled his arm and said, \"Whoever I am his guardian, then Ali is his guardian. O Allah, be a friend to the one who loves him and an enemy to the one who hates him.\" O Allah, I cannot find anyone on earth after the two righteous servants whom I entrust with this matter except for You, so decide in it with the best.\" Bashir said, \"I asked, who are these two righteous servants?\" He said, \"I do not know.\""],[2493,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. The Prophet ﷺ walked away and performed ablution, then he wiped over his socks.\""],[2494,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over the leather socks.” It was said to him after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed, so he said: “Did I embrace Islam only after Surah al-Ma’idah was revealed?”"],[2495,"“I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon Islam, and he held back his hand so that he could stipulate upon me sincerity (nush) toward every Muslim.”"],[2496,"That some people from ‘Uraynah raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “so the Prophet ﷺ ordered that their hands and feet be cut off and that their eyes be branded with heated iron.”"],[2497,"That when he offered a commodity for sale, he would point out its defects and then give the buyer the choice, saying: “If you wish, take it, and if you wish, leave it.” It was said to him: “May Allah have mercy on you; if you do this, your sale will not go through.” He said: “We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon sincerity (nush) toward the people of Islam.”"],[2498,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.”"],[2499,"“I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the revelation of al-Ma’idah, and I saw him wiping over the leather socks.”"],[2500,"I heard my grandfather, Abu Qirsafah, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: The beginning of my Islam was that I was an orphan between my mother and my maternal aunt. I inclined more toward my maternal aunt, and I used to tend some little sheep of mine. My maternal aunt would often say to me: “O my son, do not pass by this man”—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—“lest he lead you astray and misguide you.” I would go out until I reached the pasture, leave my little sheep, then go to the Prophet ﷺ and remain with him listening to him. Then I would return with my sheep lean and with dry udders. My maternal aunt said to me: “What is wrong with your sheep? Their udders are dry.” I said: “I do not know.” Then I returned to him on the second day, and he did as he had done the first day, except that I heard him say: “O people, emigrate and hold fast to Islam, for emigration does not cease as long as jihad continues.” Then I returned with my sheep as I had returned the first day. Then I returned to him on the third day, and I remained with the Prophet ﷺ listening to him until I embraced Islam, pledged allegiance to him, and shook his hand. I complained to him about my maternal aunt and about my sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Bring me the sheep.” I brought them to him, and he wiped their backs and their udders and prayed for blessing in them, and they became full of fat and milk. When I entered upon my maternal aunt with them, she said: “O my son, graze them like this.” I said: “O aunt, I did not graze them except where I used to graze every day, but I will tell you my story.” I told her the story and that I had gone to the Prophet ﷺ, and I told her about his conduct and his words. Then my mother and my maternal aunt said: “Take us to him.” So I, my mother, and my maternal aunt went, and they embraced Islam and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but they did not shake hands. This is how Abu Qirsafah’s Islam and his emigration to the Prophet ﷺ came about. Ziyad said: “Abu Qirsafah used to live in the land of Tihamah.”"],[2501,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do you have any offspring?” I said: “I have a brother.” He said: “Then bring him.” I was gentle with my brother, and he was a young boy, until he came with me. When he drew near to the Prophet ﷺ, he fled, so I caught him and held his hands and feet together, then brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ accepted his pledge of allegiance. His name was Misam, so the Prophet ﷺ said to me: “What is his name, O Abu Qirsafah?” I said: “His name is Misam.” He said: “Rather, his name is Muslim.” So I said: “Muslim is with you, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[2502,"That he “saw the Prophet ﷺ lying on his back, placing one of his legs over the other.”"],[2503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Narrate from me what you hear, and it is not lawful for a man to lie about me. Whoever lies about me and says about me other than what I said, a house will be built for him in Hell in which he will dwell.”"],[2504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ghifar—may Allah forgive them—and Aslam—may Allah keep them safe.”"],[2505,"I heard Abū Qirṣāfah say: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ — myself, my mother, and my maternal aunt — and we returned from his presence departing, my mother and my maternal aunt said to me, “O my son, we have not seen anyone like this man, more handsome of face, nor cleaner of garment, nor gentler of speech; and we saw as if light were emanating from his mouth.”"],[2506,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever loves a people, God will resurrect him in their group.”"],[2507,"The Messenger of God ﷺ clothed me in a burnoose and said, “Wear it.”"],[2508,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Build mosques and remove rubbish from them, for whoever builds a mosque for God, God builds for him a house in Paradise.” A man said, “O Messenger of God, and these mosques that are built along the road?” He said, “Yes, and removing rubbish from them is the dowry of the wide-eyed houris.”"],[2509,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “O God, do not disgrace me on the day of battle, nor disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2510,"The Byzantines took captive a son of Abū Qirṣāfah. Whenever the time of each prayer came, Abū Qirṣāfah would climb the wall of Ascalon and call out, “O so-and-so, the prayer!” and he would hear him while he was in the land of the Byzantines."],[2511,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and heard him say, 'O Allah, do not disgrace me on the Day of Resurrection, nor on the Day of Judgment.'"],[2512,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: “Al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī is given the kunyah Abū Muḥammad.”"],[2513,"Umm al-Faḍl came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I saw a part of your body in me.” He said, “You have seen well. Fāṭimah will give birth to a boy, and you will suckle him with the milk of Qutham.” He said: She came carrying him to the Prophet ﷺ and placed him in his lap, and he urinated, so she slapped him with her hand. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You have hurt my son, may God have mercy on you.” She said, “Give me your waist-wrapper so that we may wash it.” He said, “Only the urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled.”"],[2514,"And he (referring to the Prophet ﷺ) said, \"There is no one like Ali, not even similar to him.\" He (referring to Ali) was present with him, and he started laughing. All agreed."],[2516,"“Indeed he used to resemble the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[2517,"That he “saw al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ, his hair striking his shoulders.”"],[2518,"ʿUbādah, the client of al-Ḥasan, though he is in fact the client of al-Ḥusayn."],[2519,"“I saw al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ dyeing with black.”"],[2520,"«I saw al-Hasan b. Ali dyeing with henna and katam.»"],[2521,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to dye with black.»"],[2522,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to dye with black.»"],[2523,"That he «saw al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ dyed black on a horse with a long tail.»"],[2524,"«I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ as young men, and they did not dye.»"],[2525,"«I saw on al-Hasan's head a tuft of hair, and indeed I saw al-Hasan pulling it until he brought it close.»"],[2526,"That he said: «Al-Hasan used to wear a ring on his left hand.»"],[2527,"«Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to wear a ring on his left hand.»"],[2528,"I said: O Messenger of God, I saw in a dream as if a limb of your limbs was in my house, or she said: in my room. He said: «Fatimah will give birth to a boy, if God wills, and you will nurse him.» She said: So Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and he handed him to her, and she nursed him with the milk of Qutham b. al-Abbas. She said: I brought him one day to the Prophet ﷺ, and he urinated on his chest, so I pushed him on his back. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Gently, may God have mercy on you; you have hurt my son.» I said: Give me your waist-wrapper so I can wash it. He said: «No, pour water on it, for water is poured on the urine of a boy, and the urine of a girl is washed.»"],[2529,"I was among those who attended Fatimah ؓ when labor struck her, among some women. The Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: «How is she?» I said: She is exhausted, O Messenger of God. He said: «When she gives birth, do not do anything with the child before me.» She said: So she gave birth, and they anointed him and wrapped him in a yellow cloth. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said: «What has she done?» I said: She has given birth to a boy, and I anointed him and wrapped him in a cloth. He said: «You disobeyed me.» She said: I seek refuge in God from disobeying God and from the anger of His Messenger. He said: «Bring him to me.» I brought him to him, and he threw away the yellow cloth and wrapped him in a white cloth, and he spat in his mouth and fed him with his saliva. Ali ؓ came, and he said: «What have you named him, O Ali?» He said: I named him Jafar, O Messenger of God. He said: «No, but Hasan, and after him Husayn, and you are Abu Hasan al-Khayr.»"],[2530,"«The one who resembled the Messenger of God ﷺ the most was al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ.»"],[2531,"«I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him.»"],[2532,"We discussed the resemblance of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"If you want to look at someone resembling the Prophet ﷺ, then look at al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ.\""],[2533,"Abū Juḥayfah said to me: \"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2534,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2535,"I said to Abū Juḥayfah: \"Did you see the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes, and the person who most resembled him was al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ.\""],[2536,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī resembled him.\""],[2537,"Al-Haytham b. ʿAdī, and he was contradicted."],[2538,"\"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2539,"\"Saʿd and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2540,"\"Saʿd and al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died after ten years had passed of Muʿāwiyah's rule ؓ.\""],[2541,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī ؓ died when he was forty-seven.\""],[2542,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died in the year forty-eight.\""],[2543,"\"Al-Hasan b. ʿAlī died in the year forty-nine, and Saʿīd b. al-ʿĀṣ prayed over him. His death was in Madinah, and his age was forty-six or forty-seven. He was called Abū Muḥammad.\""],[2544,"\"The turmoil lasted for five years for Al-Hasan ibn Ali, and from that, four months. And the group was with Muawiyah for forty years.\""],[2545,"In it died al-Hasan b. Ali and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas in the year fifty-eight."],[2546,"Muʿawiyah said to him: When it is so, stand and speak, and inform the people that you have surrendered this matter to me. Perhaps Sufyan said: Inform the people of this matter which you have left to me. So he stood and delivered a speech from the pulpit. He praised Allah and extolled Him—al-Shaʿbi said: while I was listening—then he said: To proceed: the most prudent prudence is piety, and the most foolish folly is wickedness. This matter over which I and Muʿawiyah differed: either it was a right of mine which I relinquished to Muʿawiyah, desiring the well-being of this community and the sparing of their blood, or it was a right belonging to a man more entitled to it than me, and so I did that. And I do not know; perhaps it is a trial for you and an enjoyment for a time."],[2547,"That Ali ؓ would return before the Day of Resurrection. He laughed and said: Glory be to Allah! If we knew that, we would not have married off his wives nor cast lots for his inheritance."],[2548,"One of them, and I think it was Hanafiyyah: a small provision from a departing beloved."],[2549,"A small provision from a departing beloved."],[2550,"By Allah, I will marry you off, and I know that you are prone to attachment, prone to divorce, and flattering, except that you are the noblest of the Arabs in house and the noblest in lineage."],[2551,"Al-Hasan b. Ali married a woman and sent her one hundred slave girls, with each slave girl a thousand dirhams."],[2552,"I used to play with al-Hasan and al-Husayn using toy horses. When they won against me, they would ride on me, and when I won against them, they would say: Would you ride on a part of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"],[2553,"I asked Ata, \"Should I carry water from Zamzam?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried it, and so did Hasan and Husayn.\""],[2554,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"gave his approval for Hasan and Husain.\""],[2555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2556,"On behalf of al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ."],[2557,"That Hasan and Husayn had ʿaqiqah performed for them."],[2558,"From Abu Saʿid al-Khudri ؓ, he said: Ali ؓ said: As for Hasan, Husayn, and Muhassin, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named them, performed ʿaqiqah for them, shaved their heads, gave charity equal to the weight of it, and ordered that they be circumcised, and they were circumcised."],[2559,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2560,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2561,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿaqīqah on behalf of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ»"],[2562,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the heads of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, the two sons of ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ, to be shaved on their seventh day, so they were shaved, and he gave its weight in silver as charity, and he did not find an animal to slaughter.»"],[2563,"When Fāṭimah ؓ gave birth to Ḥasan, she said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not perform ʿaqīqah on behalf of my son? He said: No, but shave his head and give in charity the weight of his hair in silver — or he said silver — to the poor. Then when she gave birth to Ḥusayn ؓ, she did the same for him. Mūsā b. Dāwūd said in his narration: to the awfāḍ and the poor. Abū al-Qāsim said: “Al-awfāḍ are the poor, and al-awqāṣ are the amounts between the two obligatory shares.”"],[2564,"That she perform ʿaqīqah for him with a great ram. So she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Do not perform ʿaqīqah for him with anything, but shave the hair of his head then give in charity its weight in silver in the way of Allah or to the awfāḍ.” Then she gave birth to al-Ḥusayn ؓ in the following year and did the same for him."],[2565,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ call the iqāmah for prayer in the ear of al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī when Fāṭimah ؓ gave birth to him»"],[2566,"«The Prophet ﷺ called the iqāmah for prayer in the ears of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn when they were born and ordered it.»"],[2567,"«Raise your garment so that I may kiss where I saw the Prophet ﷺ kiss.» So he raised it from his belly and placed his hand on his navel."],[2568,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced Ḥasan, then said: «O Allah, I have loved him, so love him.»"],[2569,"I heard al-Barāʾ b. ʿĀzib say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī on his shoulder, and he was saying: «O Allah, I love him, so love him.»"],[2570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī ؓ: «O Allah, I have loved him, so love him and love those who love him.»"],[2571,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ carrying al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ on his shoulder, saying: “O God, I love Hasan, so love him.”"],[2572,"The Prophet ﷺ would take Hasan and embrace him, saying: “O God, this is my son, so love him and love whoever loves him.”"],[2573,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we were invited to a meal, and there was al-Husayn ؓ playing in the road. The Prophet ﷺ hurried ahead of the people, then spread out his hands, and Husayn began running this way and that, making him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one of his hands on his chin and the other between his head and ears, then embraced and kissed him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Husayn is from me and I am from him. May God love whoever loves him. Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are two grandsons among the grandsons.”"],[2574,"Hasan and Husayn came walking towards the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . When one of them arrived, he placed his hand on his neck. Then the other came and placed his other hand on his neck. He kissed this one, then kissed the other one. Then he said, \"O Allah, I love them, so love them, O people. Indeed, children are a source of stinginess and cowardice.\""],[2575,"While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering a sermon, al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ climbed up to him, and the Prophet ﷺ embraced him and said: “This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God ﷻ will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2576,"From Ya'la b. Murra al-'Amiri that they went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to a meal to which they had been invited, and there was Husayn ؓ playing with some boys. He came to meet the Messenger of God ﷺ, who spread out his hand, and the boy began to flee this way and that while the Messenger of God ﷺ made him laugh until he caught him. He placed one of his hands on his neck and the other on the crown of his head, then embraced and kissed him. Then he said: “Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May God love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a grandson among the grandsons.”"],[2577,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the pulpit with al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ beside him, looking at the Messenger of God ﷺ once, and the Messenger of God ﷺ looking at him once, saying: “This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2578,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying, and al-Hasan would come, being a small child. Whenever the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, he would jump onto his neck and back, and the Prophet ﷺ would raise his head gently so as not to drop him. They said: “O Messenger of God, you do something with this boy that we have not seen you do with anyone.” He said: “He is my sweet basil in this world. This son of mine is a master, and perhaps God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2579,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ with al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ, saying: “This son of mine is a master, and God will bring about reconciliation at his hands between two great factions of the Muslims.”"],[2580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said of al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: “This son of mine is a master, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of my community.”"],[2581,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed one day with Hasan and Husayn present. When he prostrated, al-Hasan came and jumped onto his back, and whenever he raised his head he would move him aside, fearing he might fall. When he finished, he took him by the hand and seated him in his lap and kissed him, and said: “This son of mine is a master, and he is my sweet basil in this world, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two great factions of the Muslims.”"],[2582,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said of al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ: “This son of mine is a master, and I hope that God will bring about reconciliation through him between two factions of my community.”"],[2583,"And upon you, my master. It was said to him: “Do you say ‘my master’?” He replied: “I bear witness that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘He is a master.’”"],[2584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My son—meaning al-Hasan—is a chief, and through him Allah will surely reconcile two factions of the Muslims.”"],[2585,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2587,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah ؓ: “By Allah, there is no prophet but that the prophets’ children were born to others, not to me. Indeed, your two sons are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, except for the two cousins, Yahya and Isa.”"],[2591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An angel from heaven who had never visited me asked Allah ﷻ permission to visit me, and he gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2592,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2593,"The Messenger ﷺ said: “This is an angel from among the angels who asked his Lord’s permission to greet me and visit me. He had never descended to the earth before. He gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2595,"We saw joy in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, so we said: “O Messenger of Allah, we have seen signs of joy in your face.” He said: “How could I not be joyful when Jibril ﷺ came to me and gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.”"],[2596,"I spent the night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I saw a figure with him. He said to me: “O Hudhayfah, did you see?” I said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “This is an angel who has not descended to me since I was sent. He came to me tonight and gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise.”"],[2597,"Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri ؓ narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the chiefs of the youths of the people of Paradise, except for the two cousins, Isa son of Maryam and Yahya son of Zakariyya.”"],[2598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2600,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2603,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hasan and Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise.”"],[2604,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.”"],[2605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the two masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. O Allah, I love them, so love them.”"],[2606,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and al-Husayn: “I am at peace with those with whom you are at peace, and at war with those with whom you are at war.”"],[2607,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a house in which were Fatimah, Ali, Hasan, and Husayn ؓ, and said: “I am at war with those with whom you are at war, and at peace with those with whom you are at peace.”"],[2608,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Ali, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and Fatimah ؓ and said: “I am at war with those who fight you, and at peace with those who make peace with you.”"],[2609,"Ali ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited us and spent the night with us while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up to a water skin of ours and began squeezing it into a cup. Then he came to give him water and handed it to al-Hasan, but al-Husayn reached out to drink, so he stopped him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if he is the more beloved of the two to you. He said: “He asked for water first.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and these two—and I think he said: and this sleeping one, meaning Ali—on the Day of Resurrection will be in one place.”"],[2610,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “I, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn are gathered together—and whoever loves us on the Day of Resurrection—we will eat and drink until the servants are separated.” This reached a man among the people, so he asked about it, and I informed him. He said, “What about the presentation and the reckoning?” I said to him, “How was it for the companion of Ya-Sin in that regard when he was admitted to Paradise immediately?”"],[2611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali ؓ: “The first four to enter Paradise will be I, you, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, with our descendants behind our backs, our wives behind our descendants, and our Shi'ah to our right and to our left.”"],[2612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah guarded her chastity, and Allah (Mighty and Sublime) admitted her and her offspring to Paradise because she guarded her chastity.”"],[2613,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit addressing the people. Al-Hasan b. 'Ali ؓ came out with a rag around his neck dragging it, and he tripped on it and fell on his face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit heading for him. When the people saw him, they took the child and brought him to him, so he carried him and said: “May Allah curse Satan. Verily a child is a trial. By Allah, I did not know that I had descended from the pulpit until he was brought to me.”"],[2614,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lying on his back in one of his rooms, al-Hasan came toddling until he sat on the Prophet's ﷺ chest, then urinated on his chest. I came to remove him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke and said: “Woe to you, O Anas! Leave my son and the fruit of my heart, for whoever harms this one has harmed me, and whoever harms me has harmed Allah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, pouring it, and said: “Water is poured over a boy's urine, and a girl's urine is washed.”"],[2615,"Why should I not consider it a calamity, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: “This one is from me, and Husayn is from 'Ali.”"],[2616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The prophets will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection on mounts so that they may arrive at the gathering place on that day. Salih will be sent on his she-camel, I will be sent on al-Buraq, and my two sons, al-Hasan and al-Husayn, will be sent on two she-camels from the she-camels of Paradise.”"],[2617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah (Mighty and Sublime) placed the progeny of every prophet in his loins, and Allah, Exalted is He, placed my progeny in the loins of 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ.”"],[2618,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every child of a female, their 'asabah (paternal kin) are from their father, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their 'asabah and I am their father.”"],[2619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every child of a mother affiliates with a paternal group, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and I am their 'asabah.”"],[2620,"He said: “O 'Ali, the days, months, and years only increase you in blindness regarding your affair. By Allah, if you do it, there will certainly be—there will certainly be matters whose number is known.” Then he went off dragging his garment. 'Ali said to al-'Abbas: “By Allah, that from him is not sincere advice, but rather 'Umar's whip has brought him out to what you see. By Allah, it is not desire for you, O 'Aqil, but 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Every tie and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.’” So 'Umar ؓ laughed and said: “Woe to 'Aqil, a fool and an idiot.”"],[2621,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every tie and lineage on the Day of Resurrection will be severed except my tie and my lineage.”"],[2622,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"On the Day of Resurrection every bond and lineage will be severed except my bond and my lineage.\""],[2623,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns. Whoever fights against us in the last days is as if he fought alongside the Dajjal.\""],[2624,"I saw Abu Dharr holding the two doorposts of the Ka'bah while saying: \"Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr al-Ghifari. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Noah among the people of Noah: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it perishes; and like the gate of Hittah among the Children of Israel.'\""],[2625,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my household is the likeness of Noah's ark: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns.\""],[2626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Love God for the blessings He bestows upon you, love me for the love of God, and love my household for love of me.\""],[2627,"\"Place the family of Muhammad ﷺ in the position of the head to the body, and of the eyes to the head; for the body is only guided by the head, and the head is only guided by the eyes.\""],[2628,"\"When {Say, I do not ask you for this message any payment except loving kinship} They said, O Messenger of Allah, who are your close relatives that we are obligated to love them? He said, 'Ali, Fatimah, and their children.'\""],[2629,"The Prophet ﷺ used to take me and Al-Hussein, and one of us would sit on his right thigh and the other on his left thigh, and he would say, \"O Allah, I love them, so love them.\""],[2630,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to al-Husayn b. Ali: \"Whoever loves this one has loved me.\""],[2631,"The Prophet ﷺ was praying while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were on his back. People tried to separate them, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave them alone, by my father and mother. Whoever loves me, let him love these two.\""],[2632,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.\""],[2633,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me\" - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2634,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me\" - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2635,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.\""],[2636,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: \"Whoever loves them loves me, and whoever hates them hates me.\""],[2637,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever loves me has loved them\"—meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."],[2638,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"O God, I love them, so love them and hate whoever hates them.\""],[2639,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood at Fatimah's house and greeted, and al-Hasan or al-Husayn came out to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Climb up, may your father be your ransom, you are a little bug's eye.\" He took hold of his two fingers, and he climbed onto his shoulder. Then the other one—al-Hasan or al-Husayn—came out with one of his eyes raised, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Welcome! Climb up, may your father be your ransom, you are the little bug's eye.\" He took hold of his two fingers, and he settled onto his other shoulder. The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of the backs of their necks until he placed their mouths on his mouth, then said: \"O God, I love them, so love them and love whoever loves them.\""],[2640,"These two ears of mine heard and these two eyes of mine saw the Messenger of God ﷺ holding by both his hands al-Hasan or al-Husayn, with his feet on the feet of the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he said: \"Huzuqqah, huzuqqah, climb up, little bug's eye.\" The boy would climb until he placed his feet on the chest of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he said to him: \"Open.\" He said: Then he kissed him. Then he said: \"O God, love him, for I love him.\""],[2641,"“Whoever loves me and loves these two and their father and their mother will be with me at my level on the Day of Resurrection.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 576)"],[2642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said concerning al-Hasan and al-Husayn: \"Whoever loves them, I love him; and whoever I love, God loves him; and whoever God loves, He admits him to the Gardens of Bliss. And whoever hates them or transgresses against them, I hate him; and whoever I hate, God hates him; and whoever God hates, He admits him to the punishment of Hell, and for him is an abiding punishment.\""],[2643,"From Ishaq b. Abi Habibah, the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, from Abu Hurayrah, that Marwan b. al-Hakam came to Abu Hurayrah during his final illness and said: \"O Abu Hurayrah, I have not found fault with you in anything since we have been companions except in your love for al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\" Abu Hurayrah stirred and sat up and said: \"I bear witness that we went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when we were on part of the road, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the sound of al-Hasan and al-Husayn crying while they were with their mother. He hastened his pace until he reached them, and I heard him say to her: 'What is the matter with my two sons?' She said: 'Thirst.' The Messenger of God ﷺ turned back to a water skin seeking water in it—water that day was in pools, and the people were seeking water. He called out: 'Does any of you have water with him?' Not one remained but that he turned his hand to his hook, seeking water in a water skin, and not one of them found a drop. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Hand me one of them.' She handed him one from beneath the curtain, and I saw the whiteness of her forearms when she handed him. He took him and pressed him to his chest while he was crying and would not be quiet. He stuck out his tongue for him, and he began to suck it until he calmed down or became still, and I no longer heard him crying. The other one kept crying and would not be quiet. He said: 'Hand me the other one.' She handed him to him, and he did the same with him, so they both became quiet, and I heard no sound from them. Then he said: 'Move on.' We dispersed right and left away from the women's litters until we met him on the main road. So should I not love these two when I have seen this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\""],[2644,"Al-Husayn came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying, and he clung to the neck of the Prophet ﷺ. He stood up with him and took hold of his hand, and he did not cease holding it until he bowed."],[2645,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ parting the thighs of Al-Hussein and kissing his little private area.\""],[2646,"While we were praying the night prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, whenever he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ would jump on his back. When he wanted to bow, he would take them by the hand gently and place them on the ground. When he returned, they returned, until he finished his prayer and turned away, placing them on his thighs. Abu Hurayrah said: I went to him and said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I take them away?\" He said: \"No.\" Then a lightning flash flashed, and he said: \"Go to your mother.\" They kept walking in its light until they entered."],[2647,"Al-Husayn ؓ was with the Prophet ﷺ, and he loved him intensely. He said: \"I am going to my mother.\" I said: \"I will go with him.\" Then a lightning flash came from the sky, and he walked in its light until he arrived."],[2648,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was walking on all fours, with al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ on his back, and he was saying: \"What an excellent camel is your camel, and what excellent riders are you two.\""],[2649,"This verse was revealed in my house: {God only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.} She was sitting at the door, and I said: \"O Messenger of God, am I not from the People of the House?\" He said: \"You are towards good.\""],[2650,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , brought together Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and then he brought them under his cloak. Then he said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household.\" Umm Salamah said, \"I said, O Messenger of Allah, include me with them.\" He said, \"Indeed, you are among my family.\""],[2651,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah, “Bring me your husband and his two sons.” So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast a Fadakī cloak over them, then placed his hand upon them and said, “O Allah, these are the family of Muḥammad ﷺ, so make Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muḥammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.” Umm Salamah said, “I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hand and said, ‘You are upon good.’”"],[2652,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fāṭimah, “Bring me your husband and your two sons.” So she brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cast a cloak over them, then said, “O Allah, these are the family of Muḥammad, so make Your prayers and blessings upon the family of Muḥammad as You made them upon Ibrāhīm. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[2653,"I heard Umm Salamah saying, \"Fatimah came, carrying a tray with food in it, and she placed it between his hands. He then asked her, 'Where is your cousin?' She said, 'He is at home.' He said, 'Go and call him, and bring me my two grandsons.' So she came with her two sons, each of them holding the hand of the other, and Ali walking behind them, until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He made them sit in his chamber, with Ali on his right and Fatimah on his left.\" Umm Salamah said, \"I took off my cloak, which was our mattress at home, and in which there was a piece of pig's meat. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Pray to Allah for your husband and your two sons, Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn.' So she called upon Allah for them, and they all ate from that piece of pig's meat.\" Umm Salamah said, \"And I was praying in that chamber when this verse was revealed: 'Allah only desires to keep away the uncleanness from you, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification.' Then the Prophet ﷺ took the edge of the cloak and covered them with it, and then he extended his right hand out from beneath it, pointing it towards the sky, and said, 'O Allah! These are the people of my household and my close ones, so keep away impurity from them and purify them with a thorough purification.' Umm Salamah said, 'I entered my head into the chamber and said, 'O Messenger of Allah! Am I not included with you?' He said, 'You shall have a good outcome twice.'\""],[2654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ embraced ʿAlī and Fāṭimah with one hand and Ḥasan and Ḥusayn with the other, wrapped over them a black cloak that was upon him, and kissed ʿAlī and kissed Fāṭimah ؓ. Then he said, “O Allah, to You, not to the Fire—I and my household.” Umm Salamah said, “I said, ‘And I?’ He said, ‘And you.’”"],[2655,"Fatimah brought a dish to her father while he was at the house of Umm Salamah. She said, \"Mother, go and call my son and your nephew.\" They came and he covered them with a garment and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household and my protection. Remove impurity from them and cleanse them thoroughly.\" Umm Salamah said, \"And am I included with them, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You are the wife of the Prophet ﷺ , and you have a good status.\""],[2656,"Regarding what they insulted me about, I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a certain day when Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn came. He threw his cloak over them and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household. O Allah, remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.\" So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about me?\" He said, \"And you.\" He said, \"By Allah, it is indeed the most steadfast action in myself.\""],[2657,"Fāṭimah went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling him until he came. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ḥasan and Ḥusayn and seated each one of them on his thigh, drew Fāṭimah near to his lap, then wrapped his garment over them while I was leaning back. Then he said, {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.} Then he said, “These are my family.” Wāthilah said, “I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, and am I of your family?’ He said, ‘And you are of my family.’” Wāthilah said, “It is indeed the most hope I have.”"],[2658,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months when he went out from the morning prayer, he would say, \"O family of the house, the prayer. Allah desires only to remove from you all impurity, O people of the house, and to purify you with thorough purification.\""],[2659,"I heard Abu Al-Hamra'a saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming to the door of Fatimah for six months, saying, \"Indeed, Allah wants to remove impurity from you, O people of the household, and purify you with a thorough purification.\""],[2660,"This verse was revealed: {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity} O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly—regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn ؓ."],[2661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Exalted is He, divided creation into two divisions and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {And the companions of the right} and {the companions of the left}. I am of the companions of the right and I am of the best of the companions of the right. Then He made the two divisions into houses and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {And the companions of the right—what are the companions of the right? And the companions of the left—what are the companions of the left? And the foremost—the foremost.} I am of the best of the foremost. Then He made the houses into tribes and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {peoples and tribes}. I am the most God-fearing of the children of Ādam and the most honorable of them before Allah, may He be glorified, and no boast. Then He made the tribes into houses and placed me in the best of them; that is His saying, {Allah only intends to remove from you impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.}”"],[2662,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his illness in which he was taken, and Fāṭimah ؓ was at his head. She wept until her voice rose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to her and said, “My beloved Fāṭimah, what makes you weep?” She said, “I fear loss after you.” He said, “O my beloved, do you not know that Allah, may He be glorified, looked upon the earth one look and chose your father from it, and sent him with His message? Then He looked another look and chose your husband from it, and revealed to me that I should marry you to him. O Fāṭimah, we are a household to whom Allah has given seven qualities not given to anyone before us, nor given to anyone after us: I am the seal of the prophets and the most honorable of the prophets before Allah and the most beloved of creation to Allah, may He be glorified, and I am your father. My successor is the best of successors and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is your husband. Our martyr is the best of martyrs and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is your paternal uncle Ḥamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he is the uncle of your father and the uncle of your husband. Among us is one who has two green wings, flying in Paradise with the angels wherever he wishes, and he is the cousin of your father and the brother of your husband. Among us are the two grandsons of this community, and they are your two sons, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, and they are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise. Their father, by the One who sent me with the truth, is better than them. O Fāṭimah, by the One who sent me with the truth, from them is the Mahdī of this community when the world becomes chaos and confusion, tribulations appear, ways are cut off, and they raid one another, no elder shows mercy to a child and no child honors an elder. Then Allah, may He be glorified, will send from them at that time one who conquers the fortresses of misguidance and sealed hearts, who will uphold the religion at the end of time as I upheld it at the beginning of time, and will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with oppression. O Fāṭimah, do not grieve and do not weep, for Allah, may He be glorified, is more merciful and more compassionate to you than I, because of your place with me and your position in my heart. Allah married you to your husband, and he is the noblest of your household in lineage, the most generous of them in standing, the most merciful of them to the people, the most just of them in equity, and the most discerning of them in judgment. I asked my Lord, may He be glorified, that you be the first of my household to join me.” ʿAlī ؓ said, “When the Prophet ﷺ was taken, Fāṭimah ؓ remained after him only seventy-five days until Allah joined her to him ﷺ.”"],[2664,"We were around the Prophet ﷺ when Umm Ayman came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn have gone astray.” He said, “That was at the rising of the day,” meaning the height of the day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Arise and seek my two sons.” He said, “Each man took the direction he faced, and I took the direction of the Prophet ﷺ. He did not stop until he came to the foot of a mountain, and there were al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn ؓ, each one clinging to his companion, and a serpent standing on its tail, from its mouth coming something like fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastened to it, and it turned addressing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then slithered and entered among some rocks. Then he came to the two of them, separated them, wiped their faces, and said, ‘May my father and mother be your ransom, how honored you are before Allah.’ Then he carried one of them on his right shoulder and the other on his left shoulder. I said, ‘Blessed are you two, what an excellent mount is your mount.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘And what excellent riders are they, and their father is better than them.’”"],[2665,"\"Narrated by Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'O people, I am leaving behind among you two things, if you hold onto them, you will never go astray after me: the Book of Allah, which is a stretched rope between the heaven and the earth, and my family, the people of my household. Indeed, they will not part ways until they meet me at the Pond of Kawthar.'\""],[2666,"It is as if I have been called and I answered. I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah, a rope stretched between heaven and earth, and my progeny, my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool. So consider carefully how you succeed me in them."],[2667,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his pilgrimage on the day of ʿArafah while he was on his she-camel al-Qaṣwāʾ, and he delivered a sermon. I heard him saying, “O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household.”"],[2668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the pool, whose width is between Ṣanʿāʾ and Buṣrā, containing as many golden and silver goblets as the number of stars. So consider carefully how you succeed me in the two weighty things.” A man stood and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two weighty things?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The greater is the Book of Allah, a rope one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end in your hands. Hold fast to it, and you will never cease nor go astray. The lesser is my progeny. They will never separate until they return to me at the pool, and I asked that for them from my Lord. So do not go ahead of them and perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you.”"],[2669,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the ʿaṣr prayer, and when he was in the fourth rakʿah, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn came and climbed onto the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said salām, he placed them in front of him, and al-Ḥusayn came forward. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried al-Ḥasan on his right shoulder and al-Ḥusayn on his left shoulder, then said, “O people, shall I tell you of the best of people in grandfather and grandmother? Shall I tell you of the best of people in paternal uncle and paternal aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in maternal uncle and maternal aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in father and mother? They are al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn. Their grandfather is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their grandmother is Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid, their mother is Fāṭimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their father is ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ, their paternal uncle is Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib, their paternal aunt is Umm Hāniʾ bt. Abī Ṭālib, their maternal uncle is al-Qāsim b. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, their maternal aunts are Zaynab, Ruqayyah, and Umm Kulthūm, daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Their grandfather is in Paradise, their father is in Paradise, their paternal uncle is in Paradise, their paternal aunt is in Paradise, their maternal aunts are in Paradise, they are in Paradise, and whoever loves them is in Paradise.”"],[2670,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O people, I am a forerunner for you, and you will come to me at the Pond, a pond as wide as the distance between Sana'a and Busra, in which there are as many silver cups as the number of stars. I will ask you when you come to me about the two weighty things, so consider how you will succeed me in them. The greater tie is the Book of God ﷻ, a tie one end of which is in God's hand and the other in your hands, so hold fast to it and do not go astray and do not alter it. And my progeny, the people of my house, for the Gentle, the All-Aware has informed me that they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond.”"],[2671,"“The pen has been lifted and the pages have dried, and matters are decreed in a book that has already passed.”"],[2672,"Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ used to practice coitus interruptus with her, and she was his concubine."],[2673,"“Put down the knife, say the name of God, and eat.”"],[2674,"“I saw Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn ؓ circumambulate after Asr and pray two rak'ahs.”"],[2675,"He asked his son al-Hasan ibn ʿAlī about certain matters of manly virtue (murū’ah). He said: “My son, what is soundness (sadād)?” He replied: “Father, soundness is repelling wrongdoing with what is right.” He said: “Then what is nobility (sharaf)?” He replied: “Doing good to one’s clan, bearing burdensome liabilities, being in harmony with one’s brothers, and safeguarding the neighbors.” He said: “Then what is murū’ah?” He replied: “Chastity and setting one’s wealth aright.” He said: “Then what is meticulousness (diqqah)?” He replied: “Looking into small matters and preventing what is insignificant.” He said: “Then what is blameworthiness (lawm)?” He replied: “A man’s guarding himself while exposing his wife.” He said: “Then what is generosity (samāḥah)?” He replied: “Giving in hardship and in ease.” He said: “Then what is miserliness (shuḥḥ)?” He replied: “To regard what you have spent as loss.” He said: “Then what is brotherhood (ikhā’)?” He replied: “Sharing and consoling in hardship and in prosperity.” He said: “Then what is cowardice (jubn)?” He replied: “Boldness against a friend and shrinking from an enemy.” He said: “Then what is booty (ghanīmah)?” He replied: “Desiring piety and renouncing the world—this is the cool (easy) gain.” He said: “Then what is forbearance (ḥilm)?” He replied: “Suppressing anger and mastering oneself.” He said: “Then what is wealth (ghinā)?” He replied: “The soul’s contentment with what God Most High has allotted it, even if little; wealth is only the wealth of the soul.” He said: “Then what is poverty (faqr)?” He replied: “The soul’s avid craving in everything.” He said: “Then what is strength (manaʿah)?” He replied: “Great severity in battle and contending with the mighty among people.” He said: “Then what is humiliation (dhull)?” He replied: “Panic when truly tested.” He said: “Then what is ineptness (ʿiyy)?” He replied: “Fidgeting with the beard and much spitting when speaking.” He said: “Then what is audacity (jur’ah)?” He replied: “Keeping pace with one’s peers.” He said: “Then what is affectation/burdening oneself (kulfah)?” He replied: “Your speaking about what does not concern you.” He said: “Then what is glory (majd)?” He replied: “To give despite liability, and to pardon despite offense.” He said: “Then what is intellect (ʿaql)?” He replied: “Preserving in the heart whatever you have taken in.” He said: “Then what is stupidity/rashness (kharq)?” He replied: “Opposing your leader and raising your voice against him.” He said: “Then what is good praise?” He replied: “Doing what is beautiful and leaving what is ugly.” He said: “Then what is prudence/resolve (ḥazm)?” He replied: “Long deliberation and gentleness with those in authority.” He said: “Then what is foolishness (safah)?” He replied: “Following baseness and keeping company with the errant.” He said: “Then what is heedlessness (ghaflah)?” He replied: “Your leaving the mosque and your obeying the corrupter.” He said: “Then what is deprivation (ḥirmān)?” He replied: “Your leaving your share when it has been offered to you.” He said: “Then what is the corrupter (mufsid)?” He replied: “The fool with his wealth, the one who is careless about his honor.” Then ʿAlī said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘No poverty is harsher than ignorance; no wealth is more beneficial than intellect; no loneliness is more desolate than self-admiration; no support is more fitting than consultation; no intellect is like sound planning; no lineage is like good character; no piety is like restraint; no worship is like reflection; and no faith is like modesty and patience. The bane of speech is lying; the bane of knowledge is forgetfulness; the bane of forbearance is foolishness; the bane of worship is slackening; the bane of elegance is insolence; the bane of courage is transgression; the bane of generosity is reminding others of one’s favors; the bane of beauty is arrogance; and the bane of lineage is boastfulness.’ My son, never belittle any man you ever see: if he is better than you, then consider him your father; if he is like you, then he is your brother; and if he is younger than you, then consider him your son.” Abū al-Qāsim said: “No one narrated this ḥadīth from Shuʿbah except Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh Abū Rajā’ al-Ḥabaṭī; it was uniquely reported by ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Zayyāt. And it is not narrated from ʿAlī except with this chain of transmission.”"],[2676,"“They are two sufficing (prayers) beyond which there is nothing else.”"],[2677,"“O God, make his death be solitary, for killing is an expiation.”"],[2678,"I went out with Al-Hassan and a servant who had some henna on her nails. Suddenly, pangs of pain from a toothache struck him. He said, \"Oh servant, bring the powdered medicine,\" so she poured water in it and threw the books in the water. None of them opened or reacted to it, and he did not look at it. So, I asked, \"Oh Abu Muhammad, whose books are these?\" He said, \"They are from the people of Iraq, who do not return to the truth nor abstain from falsehood. I am not afraid of them for myself, but I fear them for that.\" And he pointed towards Al-Hussein.\""],[2679,"Take me out to the open desert so that I may look at the dominion of the heavens, meaning the signs. When he was taken out, he said: “O God, I seek reward from You for my soul, for it is the dearest of souls to me.” And it was part of what God did for him that he sought reward for his soul."],[2680,"I heard Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr say: “Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ died at the age of forty-seven.”"],[2681,"That he poisoned him."],[2682,"I heard Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Numayr say: “Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ died in the year forty-nine, in the month of Rabi al-Awwal.”"],[2683,"“Al-Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ died in the year forty-nine, and Sa'id b. al-As prayed over him. His death was in Madinah, and his age was forty-six or forty-seven.”"],[2684,"to bury him with the Prophet ﷺ, but he feared that Banu Umayyah would prevent him. So when they brought him to the mosque, Banu Umayyah stood up, and 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far stood up and said: \"I heard him say: 'If they prevent you, then bury me with my mother.'\""],[2685,"\"I will not ascend or speak until you grant me that if I speak truth, you will affirm me, and if I speak falsehood, you will refute me.\" So they granted him that, and he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: \"By Allah, O 'Amr, and you, O Mughirah, you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah cursed the driver and the rider' — one of them being so-and-so?\" They said: \"O Allah, yes, indeed.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, O Mu'awiyah, and O Mughirah, do you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed 'Amr with a curse for every rhyme he uttered?\" They said: \"O Allah, indeed.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, O 'Amr, and you, O Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, do you both know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the people of this one?\" They said: \"Indeed.\" Al-Hasan said: \"I praise Allah that you have fallen among those who dissociated from this one.\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[2686,"Mu'awiyah ؓ: \"Do not say that, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into his mouth, and whoever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into his mouth is not inarticulate.\" Then al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ said: \"As for you, O 'Amr, two men disputed over you, so consider which of them is your father. And as for you, O Abu al-A'war, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed Ri'l, Dhakwan, and 'Amr b. Sufyan.\""],[2701,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: \"I was walking with him one day when he passed by a pile of charity dates. I found a date and threw it into my mouth, and he took it out with my saliva. Some of the people said: 'What harm would it have been, O Messenger of Allah, if you had left it?' He said: 'We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us.'\""],[2702,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with her two sons, and he gave her three dates. She gave each of her two sons one date, and they ate their two dates, then they began looking at their mother. She split her date into two halves between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has shown her mercy because of her mercy to her two sons.\""],[2711,"Yesterday a man departed from you whom the earlier ones did not surpass in knowledge, nor will the later ones overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on expeditions and give him the banner; Jibril was on his right and Mika'il on his left, and he would not return until Allah ﷻ granted him victory."],[2712,"O people, tonight a man has passed away among you whom the earlier ones did not surpass, nor will the later ones overtake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send him on expeditions, and Jibril would flank him on his right and Mika'il on his left. He would not turn back until victory was granted to them. He left nothing except seven hundred dirhams with which he intended to buy a servant. He passed away on the night on which Isa b. Maryam was raised—the night of the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."],[2713,"We are a people who do not marry off our women until we consult them, so go to her. So I went to her and mentioned Yazid to her. She said, 'By Allah, that will not happen until your companion behaves among us as Pharaoh behaved among the Children of Israel, slaughtering their sons and sparing their women.' I returned to al-Hasan and said, 'You sent me to a splitting piece of creation who calls the Commander of the Believers Pharaoh.' He said, 'O Muawiya, beware of hating us, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hates us or envies us except that on the Day of Resurrection he will be increased with whips of fire.\"'"],[2714,"A man called Muawiya—meaning Ibn Hudayj—reviled Ali ؓ with a foul insult in Muawiya's presence. Do you know him? He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'When you see him, bring him to me.' He said, 'He saw him at the house of Amr b. Hurayth, and he pointed him out to him.' He said, 'Are you Muawiya b. Hudayj?' He remained silent and did not answer him three times. Then he said, 'You are the one who reviled Ali in the presence of the son of the liver-eater. Indeed, if you reach the Pond—and I do not think you will reach it—you will find him with his sleeves rolled up and his arms bared, driving the disbelievers and hypocrites away from the Pond of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as stray camels are driven away from their owner. This is the saying of the truthful one, the one who was believed, Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[2715,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'War is deception.'"],[2716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wherever you are, send blessings upon me, for your blessings reach me.'"],[2717,"It was said, “O Messenger of God, a group of people come to a house and one of them asks permission—does that suffice for all of them?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “And one man of the group responds—does that suffice for the whole group?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “A group passes by and one of them gives the greeting of peace—does that suffice for all of them?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “And one man of the group returns the greeting—does that suffice for the whole group?” He said, “Yes.”"],[2718,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Among the things that bring about forgiveness is bringing joy to your Muslim brother.”"],[2719,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The one who is cheated is neither praiseworthy nor rewarded.”"],[2720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites the Verse of the Throne after the prescribed prayer is in the protection of God until the next prayer.”"],[2721,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed while men and women were walking in front of him, with no barrier, on the side facing the Black Stone."],[2722,"A man from the people of Madinah, whose kunya is Abu Abd Allah, narrated to me: Abd Allah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ , who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Palm trees and trees are a blessing upon their owners and upon their descendants after them, if they are thankful to God.”"],[2723,"Ammar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Nakha‘i narrated to us, from Abd Allah b. Hasan b. Hasan, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever offers a sacrifice, his soul being pleased with it, seeking reward for his sacrificial animal, it will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[2724,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ascended the pulpit on the day of the expedition of Tabuk, praised God and extolled Him, then said, “O people, by God, I do not command you except with what God has commanded you, nor do I forbid you except from what God has forbidden you. So be moderate in seeking; for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, one of you is sought by his provision just as he is sought by his appointed term. If any of it becomes difficult for you, then seek it through obedience to God, exalted is He.”"],[2725,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Among the things that obligate forgiveness is your bringing joy to your Muslim brother.”"],[2726,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution, he would leave extra water until he let it flow over the place of his prostration."],[2727,"I was between al-Hasan and al-Husayn while Marwan was exchanging insults with them. Al-Hasan kept trying to silence al-Husayn, but Marwan said, “A cursed household!” Al-Hasan became angry and said, “You said, ‘A cursed household’? By God, God has cursed you on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ while you were still in your father’s loins.”"],[2728,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: I climbed with him to the room where charity (dates) was stored. I took a date and chewed it. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Spit it out; charity is not lawful for us.”"],[2729,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Fatimah's house, and she handed him a cooked shoulder of a sheep. He ate it, then stood to pray. She took hold of his clothes and said, \"Will you not perform ablution, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"From what, my dear daughter?\" She said, \"You have eaten from that which the fire has touched.\" He said, \"The purest of your food is that which the fire has touched.\""],[2730,"One of them said, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not stand?\" The other said, \"Yes, then he sat.\""],[2731,"Al-Hasan said, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ not stand for the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess that passed by him?\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Yes, and he sat.\""],[2732,"The one standing said to the one sitting, \"Did the Prophet ﷺ not stand?\" He said, \"Yes, then he sat.\""],[2733,"That a funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ and he stood?\" He said, \"Yes, and he has sat.\""],[2734,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed stood and sat?\""],[2735,"If you were to look between Jabars and Jabalq, you would not find a man whose grandfather is a prophet other than me and my brother. I think you should unite behind Mu'awiyah. {And I do not know; perhaps it is a trial for you and enjoyment for a time.} Ma'mar said: Jabars and Jabalq are the east and the west."],[2736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Anas, go and summon for me the master of the Arabs,\" meaning Ali. Aisha ؓ said, \"Are you not the master of the Arabs?\" He said, \"I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.\" When Ali ؓ came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for the Ansar, and they came to him. He said to them: \"O assembly of Ansar, shall I not direct you to something which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after it?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"This is Ali, so love him with my love and honor him for my honor, for Jibril ﷺ commanded me with what I have told you from Allah ﷻ.\""],[2737,"I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: \"Whoever regularly goes to the mosque gains a brother obtained for Allah ﷻ, novel knowledge, a word that calls him to guidance, a word that turns him away from ruin, and he abandons sins out of modesty or fear, and a blessing or awaited mercy.\""],[2738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The gift for the fasting person is perfume and incense.\""],[2739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did both: he entered ihram when his mount stood him upright, and he entered ihram while he was at al-Bayda', on the ground, before his mount stood him upright.\""],[2740,"They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the saying of Allah ﷻ {Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet}?\" He said, \"This is from what is hidden, and had you not asked me about it, I would not have informed you. Indeed, Allah ﷻ appointed two angels over me. I am not mentioned before a Muslim servant who sends blessings upon me except that those two angels say, 'May Allah forgive you,' and Allah and His angels say in response to those two angels, 'Amin.' And no one sends blessings upon me except that those two angels say, 'May Allah forgive you,' and Allah and His angels say in response to those two angels, 'Amin.'\""],[2741,"Do not rebuke me, may God have mercy on you, for the Messenger of God ﷺ was shown the Umayyads mounting his pulpit, one man after another, and that grieved him. Then this verse was revealed: {Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar} — a river in Paradise — and it was revealed: {Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree. And what can make you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months} — the Umayyads will possess it. Al-Qasim said: 'We calculated that, and it was exactly one thousand, neither more nor less.'"],[2742,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot and naked.' A woman said, 'O Messenger of God, how will we see one another?' He said, 'The eyes that Day will be staring.' He raised his gaze to the sky, and she said, 'O Messenger of God, ask God to cover my nakedness.' He said, 'O God, cover her nakedness.'"],[2743,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to wear the best of what we find, to perfume ourselves with the best of what we find, and to slaughter as sacrifices the fattest of what we find: a cow on behalf of seven, a camel on behalf of ten, and to proclaim the takbir aloud, with tranquility and dignity upon us."],[2744,"He said to her, 'Do you show gloating over the killing of Ali? Go, for you are divorced thrice.' She veiled herself with a cloak of hers and sat in a corner of the house, saying, 'By God, I did not intend what you thought.' She remained until her waiting period ended, then moved away from him. He sent her the remainder of her dower that he owed and a gift of ten thousand. When the messenger came to her with that, she said, 'A small provision from a departing beloved.' When the messenger returned to al-Hasan and told him what she said, al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ wept and said, 'Were it not that I heard my grandfather the Messenger of God ﷺ — or heard my father narrating from my grandfather — that he said: \"If a man divorces his wife thrice at the times of purity or divorces her thrice without specification, she is not lawful to him until she marries another husband,\" I would have taken her back.'"],[2745,"Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan performed Hajj, and with him performed Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj, who was among the people most abusive of Ali. He passed through Madinah in the mosque of the Messenger ﷺ while al-Hasan b. Ali was sitting with a group of his companions. It was said to him, 'This is Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj, the abuser of Ali ؓ.' He said, 'Bring the man to me.' The messenger came to him and said, 'Answer.' He said, 'Who?' He said, 'Al-Hasan b. Ali is calling you.' He came to him and greeted him. Al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ said to him, 'Are you Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj?' He said, 'Yes.' He repeated it three times. Then al-Hasan said to him, 'The abuser of Ali?' He seemed ashamed. Al-Hasan ؓ said to him, 'By God, if you reach the pool — and I do not think you will reach it — you will find him with his garment girded up his shin, driving away the hypocrites as a stray camel is driven away. This is the saying of the truthful one, the one who is believed ﷺ, and he who fabricates has failed.'"],[2746,"I heard al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ say: 'I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream clinging to the Throne. I saw Abu Bakr ؓ holding the waist of the Prophet ﷺ. I saw Umar ؓ holding the waist of Abu Bakr ؓ. I saw Uthman ؓ holding the waist of Umar ؓ. And I saw blood pouring from the sky to the earth.' Al-Hasan narrated this hadith while a group of Shi'ah were with him. They said, 'And what did you see of Ali?' Al-Hasan said, 'There was no one I would have loved more to see holding the waist of the Prophet ﷺ than Ali, but it was a dream I saw.'"],[2747,"Ali ؓ said to him, 'How have you become this morning, O son of the Messenger of God?' He said, 'By God's praise, I have become cured.' Ali said, 'So it is, God willing.' Then al-Hasan ؓ said, 'Support me.' Ali ؓ leaned him against his chest. He said, 'I heard my grandfather the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"In Paradise there is a tree called the Tree of Trial. On the Day of Resurrection the people of trial will be brought, and no record will be raised for them, nor will a scale be set up for them; their reward will be poured upon them in abundance.\"' And he recited: {Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account.}"],[2748,"When Al-Hasan ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) became the leader after Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was killed, while he was leading the people in prayer, a man attacked him and stabbed him in the thigh with a dagger. He was bedridden because of it for months. Then he stood on the pulpit to deliver a sermon and said: \"O people of Iraq, fear Allah concerning us, for we are your leaders and your guests. We are the family of the house about whom Allah Almighty said: {Allah only desires to remove defilement from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly}.\" He continued speaking that day until no one in the mosque was seen except that they were weeping."],[2749,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever receives a gift while a group of people are sitting with him, they are his partners in it.'"],[2750,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Feed food and speak good words.'"],[2751,"'Lift your garment so that I may kiss where I saw the Prophet ﷺ kiss.' He lifted it from his belly and placed his hand on his navel."],[2753,"Between al-Hasan and al-Husayn there was only one purity period."],[2754,"O Abu Abd Allah, I saw you on the hands of the Messenger of God ﷺ with them stained with blood when you were brought to him at birth, and he delighted in you and wrapped you in a cloth. He spat into your mouth and spoke words I do not know. Fatimah ؓ had raced ahead of him in cutting the navel cord of al-Hasan ؓ, and he said, 'Do not race me in that.'"],[2755,"Whoever would like to look at the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his neck to his face, let him look at al-Hasan b. Ali; and whoever would like to look at the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his neck to his ankle in physique and complexion, let him look at al-Husayn b. Ali."],[2756,"Whoever would like to look at the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ from his head to his neck, let him look at al-Hasan; and whoever would like to look at what is below his neck, let him look at al-Husayn. They divided it between themselves."],[2757,"Al-Hasan was the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from the chest upward. Then he mentioned something similar."],[2758,"The person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his head to his chest was al-Hasan."],[2759,"Al-Hasan was the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from the head to the chest."],[2760,"When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Hasan.' When al-Husayn was born, we named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Bring me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Husayn.' When the third was born, I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and said, 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, he is Muhassin.' Then he said, 'I have named them with the names of the sons of Aaron: Shabar, Shubayr, and Mushabbir.'"],[2761,"When al-Hasan was born, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: “Show me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: I named him Harb [which means ʿwarʿ]. He said: ʿRather he is Hasan.” When al-Husain was born, he said: ʿShow me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: I named him Harb, He said: ʿRather he is Husain.” When the third one was born, the Prophet ﷺ said: ʿShow me my son; what did you name him?ʿ I said: Harb, He said: “Rather. he is Muhassin.” Then he said: “I have named them after the fashion of the sons of Haroon, Shabbar and Shabeer and Mushabbir.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 953)"],[2762,"I wanted to have the kunya Abu Harb. When al-Hasan was born, I named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said, 'He is al-Hasan.'"],[2763,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'No, name him Hasan.' Then al-Husayn was born, and I named him Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Rather, name him Husayn.' Then another was born, and I named him Harb. He ﷺ said, 'What have you named him?' I said, 'Harb.' He said, 'Name him Muhassin.'"],[2764,"Ali ؓ said: I was a man who loved war. When al-Hasan was born, I wanted to name him Harb, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Hasan. When al-Husayn was born, I wanted to name him Harb, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named him al-Husayn, and he ﷺ said, 'I have named these two sons of mine after the two sons of Aaron: Shabar and Shubayr.'"],[2765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I have named them—meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn—after the two sons of Aaron: Shabar and Shubayr.'"],[2766,"Al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye his hair with wasima (a dark dye)."],[2767,"He named his eldest son Hamza and named Husayn Ja'far after his uncle, but the Messenger of God ﷺ named them Hasan and Husayn."],[2768,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ dying [their hair] with henna and katam."],[2769,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ dying [their hair] with black."],[2770,"Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed on the day of Ashura in the year sixty-one, and he was fifty-eight years old, and he used to dye [his hair] with henna and katam."],[2771,"Ali was killed when he was fifty-two, and at that same age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed, and at that same age Ali b. al-Husayn died, and at that same age Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Husayn died."],[2772,"I heard al-Mahdi ask Ja'far, \"How old was Ali when he was killed?\" He said, \"Fifty-eight, and at that same age al-Husayn b. Ali was killed.\""],[2773,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing [his hair] with black."],[2774,"I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ, the two sons of Fatimah ؓ, dyeing [their hair] with black, and al-Husayn used to leave the tuft under the lip."],[2775,"I entered upon Al-Husayn ibn Ali, and he had dyed himself with black."],[2776,"Al-Husayn b. Ali used to dye [his hair] with black."],[2777,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali dyeing [his hair] with black."],[2778,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ used to dye [his hair] with black."],[2779,"From Umar b. Ata b. Abi al-Khuwar and Ubayd Allah b. Abi Yazid, they said: \"We saw al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ dyeing [his hair] with wasmah.\""],[2780,"\"No.\" I said, \"Then should I let it hang below the two ankles?\" He said, \"What is below the two ankles is in the Fire.\""],[2781,"I saw on al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ upright khazz socks, and I saw them riding trade horses."],[2782,"I saw on al-Husayn b. Ali a red khazz cloak."],[2783,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali with a khazz turban on him, his hair emerging from beneath the turban."],[2784,"I entered upon al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ and he had a khazz garment on."],[2785,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ used to wear a ring on his left hand."],[2786,"I saw on al-Husayn on the day he was killed a sindus yalmaq."],[2788,"Ali ؓ said: \"Shall I not tell you about my own special self and my household?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"As for Hasan, he is a man of large bowls and a table, a youth among the youths. If the two loops of the girth meet, he will not avail you in war more than a sparrow's snare. As for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of amusement, shade, and falsehood. Let not the two sons of Abbas deceive you. As for me and Husayn, I and Husayn are of you and you are of us. By Allah, I fear that these people will be given power over you because of their uprightness in their land and your corruption in yours, their discharging the trust and your betrayal, their obedience to their leader and your disobedience to him, their unity upon their falsehood and your division over your truth, until their rule lasts long, until they leave no sacred thing of Allah but they make it lawful, and no town dweller or desert dweller remains but their oppression enters upon him, and until one of you becomes a follower of them, and until one of you's support from them is like the slave's support from his master: when he is present he obeys him, and when he is absent he reviles him, and until the wealthiest of you in it is the one with the best opinion of Allah. If Allah brings you well-being, accept it; if you are tested, be patient, for the outcome belongs to the God-fearing.\""],[2789,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ and they mentioned his household. Ali ؓ said: \"As for al-Hasan, he will not avail you in war more than a sparrow's snare. As for Abdullah b. Jafar, he is a man of shade and a table. As for Husayn, he is of you and you are of him.\""],[2790,"Muawiyah died in the month of Rajab, after four nights had passed. Yazid was appointed as his successor for two years. In the year 61, Husayn ibn Ali and his companions were killed, for ten nights, starting from the first day of Muharram, until the day of Ashura. Abbas ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib and his mother Umm al-Banin Amiriyya, Ja'far ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Uthman ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, Abu Bakr ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, and his mother Layla bint Mas'ud Nahshalyya, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib (the eldest), and his mother Layla Thaqafiyya, Abdullah ibn al-Husayn and his mother Rabbab bint Imru' al-Qays Kalbiyya, Abu Bakr ibn al-Husayn, Qasim ibn al-Hasan, Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib, Ja'far ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, Muslim ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, Sulaiman, a servant of Husayn, and Abdullah, the infant of Husayn, were all killed. Husayn himself was killed at the age of 58."],[2791,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed when he was fifty-eight years old."],[2792,"Indeed, with him were killed seventeen of those who had moved in the womb of Fatimah ؓ."],[2794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Husayn b. Ali ؓ will be killed at the head of sixty [years] from my emigration.”"],[2795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Husayn will be killed when grey hair overtakes him.” Abu al-Qasim said: al-qatir means white hair."],[2797,"“Ali ؓ was killed while he was fifty-eight years old, al-Husayn ؓ was killed while he was fifty-eight years old, and Ali b. al-Husayn died while he was fifty-eight years old.”"],[2798,"He traveled with Ali ؓ, and when he came parallel to Nineveh, he said: “Patience, Abu Abd Allah, patience by the bank of the Euphrates.” I said: “And what is that?” He said: “I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while his eyes were overflowing [with tears], so I said: ‘Has someone angered you, O Messenger of Allah? Why do I see your eyes overflowing?’ He said: ‘Jibril ﷺ had just left me and informed me that my ummah will kill al-Husayn, my son.’ Then he said: ‘Would you like me to show you some of his soil?’ I said: ‘Yes.’ So he stretched out his hand and grasped [some], and when I saw it, I could not control my eyes from overflowing.”"],[2799,"He said: “What is the name of this land?” It was said: “Karbala.” Then he said: “The Prophet ﷺ spoke the truth: ‘It is the land of distress and affliction.’”"],[2800,"The angel of rain sought permission from his Lord, exalted and glorified, to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and He granted him permission. So he came to him while he was in the house of Umm Salama. He said: “O Umm Salama, guard the door for us; let no one enter upon us.” While they were at the door, al-Husayn came and opened the door, and he began jumping on the Prophet’s ﷺ back while the Prophet ﷺ embraced him and kissed him. The angel said to him: “Do you love him, O Muhammad?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Indeed, your ummah will kill him, and if you wish, I can show you some of the soil of the place where he will be killed.” He said: “So he grasped a handful from the place where he will be killed and brought him red soil, and Umm Salama took it and placed it in her garment.” Thabit said: “We used to say that it is Karbala.”"],[2801,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while revelation was descending upon him, and he climbed onto the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was prostrate and played on his back. Jibril said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Do you love him, O Muhammad?” He said: “O Jibril, why would I not love my son?” He said: “Indeed, your ummah will kill him after you.” Then Jibril ﷺ stretched out his hand and brought him white soil and said: “In this land your son will be killed, O Muhammad, and its name is al-Taff.” When Jibril ﷺ left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with the soil in his hand, weeping, and said: “O A’isha, Jibril ﷺ informed me that al-Husayn, my son, will be killed in the land of al-Taff and that my ummah will be tested after me.” Then he went out to his companions, among them Ali, Abu Bakr, Umar, Hudhayfa, Ammar, and Abu Dharr ؓ, while he was weeping. They said: “What makes you weep, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Jibril informed me that my son al-Husayn will be killed after me in the land of al-Taff, and he brought me this soil and informed me that his resting place is in it.”"],[2802,"that al-Husayn b. Ali entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Aishah, shall I not tell you something astonishing? A moment ago an angel entered upon me who had never entered upon me before, and he said: This son of mine will be killed. He also said: If you wish, I will show you the soil in which he will be killed. The angel then reached out with his hand and showed me red soil.\""],[2804,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ were playing in front of the Prophet ﷺ in my house when Jibril ﷺ descended and said: “O Muhammad, your ummah will kill this son of yours after you,” and he gestured with his hand toward al-Husayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept and clasped him to his chest. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This soil is a trust with you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smelled it and said: “Woe, distress and affliction!” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Umm Salama, when this soil turns into blood, know that my son has been killed.” He said: Umm Salama placed it in a glass bottle, then she began to look at it every day and say: “The day you turn into blood will be a great day.”"],[2805,"She said: “They killed him – may Allah, exalted and glorified, kill them! They deceived and humiliated him – may Allah curse them!”"],[2806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day in my house and said: “Let no one enter upon me.” So I waited, and al-Husayn ؓ entered. I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping, so I looked and saw Husayn in his lap while the Prophet ﷺ was wiping his forehead and weeping. I said: “By Allah, I did not know when he entered.” He said: “Jibril ﷺ was with us in the house and said: ‘Do you love him?’ I said: ‘As for in this world, yes.’ He said: ‘Your ummah will kill this one in a land called Karbala.’ Then Jibril ﷺ took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet ﷺ. When Husayn was surrounded at the time he was killed, he said: ‘What is the name of this land?’ They said: ‘Karbala.’ He said: ‘Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: the land of distress and affliction.’”"],[2807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Sit by the door and no one should enter upon me.\" So I stood by the door when Al-Hussein came, and I went to fetch him, but the young boy went in before me and entered upon his grandfather. I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, may Allah sacrifice me for you, you ordered me that no one should enter upon you, and yet your son has come and I went to fetch him, but the young boy entered before me.\" When a long time passed, I looked out of the door and found you turning something in your hands and tears flowing, with the child on your chest. You said, \"Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my ummah will kill him, and he brought me the soil on which he will be killed. It is this soil that I am turning in my hands.\""],[2808,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down one day and woke up distressed, with red soil in his hand, turning it over. I said: “What is this soil, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Jibril ﷺ informed me that this one – meaning al-Husayn – will be killed in the land of Iraq. I said to Jibril ﷺ : ‘Show me the soil of the land in which he will be killed.’ So this is its soil.”"],[2809,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in what the sleeper sees at midday, disheveled, dusty, with a glass bottle in his hand containing blood. I said: “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is this?” He said: “The blood of al-Husayn and his companions. I have been collecting it since today.” That day was counted, and it was found that he had been killed on that day."],[2810,"I accompanied Ali ؓ until he reached Kufa. He ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled God, then said, “How will you be when the descendants of your Prophet settle among you?” They replied, “In that case, we shall strive for God’s sake concerning them in an excellent manner.” He said, “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they will surely settle among you, and you will surely go out against them and kill them.” Then he turned away saying,"],[2811,"“Al-Husayn will certainly be killed, and I know the very soil in which he will be slain, near the two rivers.”"],[2812,"I was with Ali ؓ at the two rivers of Karbala. He passed by a tree beneath which was gazelle dung. He took a handful of it, smelled it, then said, “From this ridge will be gathered seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[2813,"I was with Ali ؓ when he came to Karbala and said, “Martyrs will be killed in this place, whose like are no martyrs except the martyrs of Badr.” I said, “This is one of his lies,” while there was the leg of a dead donkey. I told my servant, “Take this donkey’s leg and peg it into his seat and conceal it.” Time passed, and when al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, I set out with some companions of mine, and there was the body of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ upon the leg of that donkey, with his companions lying slain around him."],[2814,"We used to hear that a son of a Prophet would be killed at Karbala. Whenever I entered it, I would spur my horse until I passed beyond it. But when al-Husayn was killed, after that I began to travel at my own pace.”"],[2815,"The passage translates to: \"Hajjaj said to him, 'Indeed, the two of you will never meet in one place.'\""],[2816,"that I might pass by the Prophet ﷺ and he would look at my face.”"],[2817,"I heard Abu Raja al-Utaridi say: Do not revile Ali or the people of this house, for a neighbor of ours from Balhujaym said, “Do you not see this sinner al-Husayn b. Ali? May God kill him.” So God struck him with two stars in his eyes, and God obliterated his sight."],[2818,"\"To keep that a secret.\""],[2819,"When the head of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad and his companions were brought and placed in the open square, I came to them while they were saying, “It has come, it has come.” And behold, a snake came, weaving through the heads until it entered the nostril of Ubayd Allah. It stayed for a little while, then came out and went away. Then they said again, “It has come,” and it did that two or three times."],[2820,"It was as if men descended from heaven with spears, pursuing the killers of al-Husayn ؓ . It was not long before al-Mukhtar came down and killed them.”"],[2821,"“When al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, no stone was lifted in Jerusalem but that fresh blood was found beneath it.”"],[2822,"from blood ؓ ”"],[2823,"“Al-Husayn b. Ali was killed while I was then a young girl, and the sky remained for days like a clot of blood.”"],[2824,"\"When al-Husayn was killed, the sky turned red.\" I said, \"What is it you are saying?\" He replied, \"Indeed, the liar is a hypocrite. The sky turned red when he was killed.\""],[2825,"It is she."],[2826,"\"When al-Husayn ؓ was killed, we remained for seven days; when we prayed the afternoon prayer we looked at the sun on the edges of the walls as if it were dyed yellow sheets, and we looked at the stars striking one another.\""],[2827,"\"There was no redness in the sky until al-Husayn was killed.\""],[2828,"A man threw (something) at al-Husayn while he was drinking, and his jaw was paralyzed, so he said, \"May Allah not quench your thirst.\" He said, \"So he drank until it overflowed.\""],[2829,"\"What you see of the matter has indeed come down. The world has changed and become disfigured; its goodness has turned away and continued until nothing remains of it except like the dregs in a vessel, except a despicable livelihood like a barren pasture. Do you not see that truth is not acted upon and falsehood is not forbidden? Let the believer long for the meeting with Allah. Indeed, I see death as nothing but happiness and life with the wrongdoers as nothing but weariness.\" And al-Husayn ؓ was killed on the Day of Ashura in the year sixty-one at al-Taff in Karbala. He was wearing a dark green khazz cloak, dyed with black, and he was fifty-six years old."],[2830,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave allegiance to al-Hasan, al-Husayn, 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas, and 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far ؓ while they were young and had not reached puberty.\" He said, \"He did not accept the allegiance of any minor except from among us.\""],[2831,"\"Al-Husayn ؓ performed the pilgrimage twenty-five times on foot.\""],[2832,"\"The body of al-Husayn was similar to the body of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2833,"Husayn had indeed set out toward Kufa, and your time has been tested with him among all times, and your city among all cities, and you have been tested with him among all governors. At that point, he will either be freed or return to being a slave as slaves are enslaved. Then 'Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad killed him and sent his head to him. When it was placed before him, he recited the verse of al-Husayn b. al-Humam."],[2834,"The Prophet ﷺ came out of 'A'ishah's house ؓ and passed by Fatimah's house, and he heard Husayn crying ؓ, so he said, \"Do you not know that his crying hurts me?\""],[2836,"“O Allah, drive him into the Fire.” The mount bolted with him, and his foot caught in the stirrup. He said: By Allah, nothing of him remained on it except his foot."],[2837,"“No; that is the garment of one upon whom humiliation has been struck.” So he took a garment and tore it and put it beneath his clothes. Then when he was killed, they stripped him."],[2838,"Ali ؓ passed by Ka'b and said, “A man from the children of this man will be killed among a band whose horses’ sweat will not dry before they arrive at Muhammad ﷺ.” Then Hasan ؓ passed by, and they said, “This one, O Abu Ishaq?” He said, “No.” Then Husayn passed by, and they said, “This one?” He said, “Yes.”"],[2839,"Sinan b. Anas."],[2841,"Sufyan: “And who doubts this?”"],[2842,"When we mentioned Husayn and those who were killed with him ؓ, Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya said, “Seventeen youths were killed with him, all of whom had stirred in the womb of Fatima ؓ.”"],[2843,"I said, “No stone was lifted at the Holy House except that fresh blood was found beneath it.” Abd al-Malik said, “You and I are paired in this hadith.”"],[2844,"“As for one of them, his penis grew long until he would wrap it around, and as for the other, he would face the waterskin with his mouth until he came to its end.” Sufyan said, “I saw the child of one of them as if he had a defect and as if he was mad.”"],[2845,"“I saw the wars (dye) that was taken from Husayn’s camp become like ashes.”"],[2846,"“That this should disparage me or you, I would have clasped my hand in your head.” He said: But what he replied to me was: “That I should be killed at such-and-such a place is dearer to me than that the sanctity of Allah and His Messenger should be violated through me.” He said: That is what consoled me about him."],[2847,"“And the people of that house were afflicted with defect, madness, leprosy, illness, and poverty.”"],[2848,"Amr b. Bukayr b. Bakkar al-Qanabi narrated to us, Mujashi b. Amr narrated to us, both said: Abdullah b. Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu Qabil: Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As narrated to me that Muadh b. Jabal informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a changed complexion and said: \"I am Muhammad. I was given the openings of speech and its closings, so obey me as long as I am among you. When I am taken away, then hold fast to the Book of Allah, glorified and exalted be He. Make lawful its lawful, and forbid its forbidden. It has come to you with the spirit and the ease, a Book from Allah that has preceded. Tribulations will come to you like patches of the dark night. Whenever messengers go, messengers come. Prophethood was succeeded and became kingship. May Allah have mercy on one who takes it by its right and leaves it as he entered it. Hold back, O Muadh, and count.\" He said: When I reached five, he said: \"Yazid. Allah will not bless Yazid.\" Then the eyes of the Prophet ﷺ shed tears, then he said: \"Husayn was announced to me as killed, and I was brought his soil, and I was informed of his killer. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, he is not killed among a people who do not defend him except that Allah will cause discord between their chests and hearts, give their wicked ones power over them, and clothe them in sects.\" Then he said: \"Alas for the offspring of the family of Muhammad ﷺ from a successor appointed, a luxurious one who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold back, O Muadh.\" When I reached ten, he said: \"Al-Walid is the name of a Pharaoh, a destroyer of the laws of Islam. Before him is a man from a household; Allah will draw his sword and there will be no sheath for it. The people differed and were thus,\" and he interlaced his fingers, then said: \"After one hundred and twenty, there will be swift death and rapid killing. In that will be their destruction. Woe to them from a man of the descendants of al-Abbas.\""],[2849,"\"I heard the jinn mourning over Husayn ibn Ali.\""],[2850,"I was in Khuza'ah when they brought something from the inheritance of al-Husayn. It was said to them: 'Shall we slaughter or sell and divide?' He said: 'Slaughter.' He said: 'He sat on a large bowl, and when it was placed, it boiled with fire.'"],[2851,"When al-Husayn ؓ was killed, a camel from his army was plundered. When it was cooked, it was blood, so they overturned it."],[2852,"Crying of the jinn over al-Husayn b. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ was heard."],[2853,"The plasterers narrated to me: They said: 'When we went out at night to the cemetery at the place where al-Husayn ؓ was killed, we heard the jinn wailing over him and saying.'"],[2854,"I heard the jinn wailing over al-Husayn ؓ."],[2855,"I heard the jinn wailing over al-Husayn."],[2856,"I have heard the wailing of the jinn since the Prophet ﷺ passed away, except tonight. I do not think my son except that he has been killed, meaning al-Husayn ؓ. She said to her slave girl: 'Go out and ask.' She was informed that he had been killed, and there was a female jinn wailing."],[2857,"The first humiliation that entered upon the Arabs was the killing of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ and the claim of Ziyad."],[2858,"Al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed while he had a large debt, so Ali b. Husayn sold such-and-such a spring and such-and-such a spring for it."],[2859,"Al-Husayn ordered a caller, and he called out: 'Let no man with a debt accompany us.' A man said: 'My wife guaranteed my debt.' Husayn ؓ said: 'And what is the guarantee of a woman?'"],[2860,"When al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ was killed, they cut off his head and sat at the first halt drinking nabidh, greeting each other with the head. Then a pen of iron came out from a wall and wrote in a line of blood."],[2863,"\"The head of al-Husayn ؓ was the first head carried in Islam.\""],[2864,"\"I entered upon Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad and there was the head of al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ before him on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon al-Mukhtar, and there was the head of Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr, and there was the head of al-Mukhtar on a shield. By Allah, I did not remain but a little while until I entered upon Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, and there was the head of Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr on a shield.\""],[2865,"When the head of al-Husayn b. Ali was brought to Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad, he began poking it with a stick in his hand and saying, \"Indeed he had beautiful teeth.\" I said, \"By Allah, I will displease you: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing the place where your stick is, from his mouth.\""],[2866,"I was with Ibn Ziyad when the head of al-Husayn was brought, and he began saying, poking with a stick in his nose, \"I have not seen anything as beautiful as this.\" I said, \"Indeed, he was among the most similar of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[2867,"\"Whoever loves us for the sake of this world, then the lover of this world is loved by both the righteous and the wicked. Whoever loves us for the sake of Allah, we and he will be on the Day of Resurrection like these two,\" and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."],[2868,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ has three sanctities. Whoever preserves them, Allah will preserve for him the affairs of his religion and his world; and whoever does not preserve them, Allah will not preserve anything for him: the sanctity of Islam, my sanctity, and the sanctity of my kinship.\""],[2869,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"I have been given al-Kawthar.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is al-Kawthar?\" He said, \"A river in Paradise whose width and length are between the east and the west. No one drinks from it and remains thirsty, and no one performs ablution from it and becomes disheveled. No person who violates my protection or kills the people of my household will drink from it.\""],[2870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Six I have cursed, and every prophet is answered: the one who adds to the Book of Allah ﷻ, the one who denies the decree of Allah, the one who makes lawful what Allah has forbidden, the one who makes lawful from my kindred what Allah has made forbidden, and the one who abandons the Sunnah.\""],[2871,"About the blood of a mosquito, while they have killed the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"They are my two fragrant flowers in this world.\""],[2872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The miser is he before whom I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me.\""],[2873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Part of the excellence of a person’s Islam is his leaving alone what does not concern him.”"],[2874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever I am mentioned in his presence and he errs in sending blessings upon me has missed the path of Paradise.”"],[2875,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Observing Iʿtikāf (seclusion for worship) for ten days in Ramadan is like performing two Hajj pilgrimages and two Umrah pilgrimages.\""],[2876,"Love us with the love of Islam, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not raise me above my due, for Allah, Exalted is He, took me as a servant before He took me as a messenger.”"],[2877,"I heard my father say: Three days before the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Gabriel ﷺ descended upon him and said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you as an honor for you, a distinction for you, and specifically for you, to ask you what He knows better than you. He says: How do you find yourself? The Prophet ﷺ said: “I find myself, O Gabriel, distressed, and I find myself, O Gabriel, grieved.” He said: Then on the third day, Gabriel ﷺ descended, and the Angel of Death (peace be upon them) descended, and with them descended an angel in the air called Isma'il, over seventy thousand angels, and there was not an angel among them except that he was over seventy thousand angels, with Gabriel ﷺ accompanying them. Then he said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you as an honor for you, a distinction for you, and specifically for you, to ask you what He knows better than you. He says: How do you find yourself? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I find myself, O Gabriel, distressed, and I find myself, O Gabriel, grieved.” He said: Then the Angel of Death ﷺ asked permission at the door. Gabriel ﷺ said: O Muhammad, this is the Angel of Death asking permission to enter upon you. He has never asked permission from any human before you, nor will he ask permission from any human after you. He said: Give him permission. So Gabriel ﷺ gave him permission, and he came forward until he stood before him. He said: O Muhammad, Allah, Majestic is He, sent me to you and commanded me to obey you in whatever you command me. If you command me to take your soul, I will take it, and if you dislike it, I will leave it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Will you do so, O Angel of Death?” He said: Yes, and with that I have been commanded, to obey you in whatever you command me. Then Gabriel ﷺ said to him: Allah, Majestic is He, has longed to meet you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Proceed with what you have been commanded.” Gabriel said to him: This is the last time I will set foot on the earth; my need was only in this world. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and condolences came, someone came whose voice they heard but whose person they did not see. He said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Every soul will taste death. In Allah there is consolation for every affliction, a replacement for every loss, and a compensation for everything missed. So in Allah put your trust, and on Him place your hope, for the truly afflicted is the one deprived of reward. And peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah."],[2878,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his death gave three instructions: he instructed that the army of Usama be sent out, and that no one but the people of his religion should live with him in Madinah.” Muhammad said: And I forgot the third."],[2879,"Come to lunch. I said: I have already had lunch, O son of the Messenger of Allah. He said to me: It is endive. I said: O son of the Messenger of Allah, what is in endive? He said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no leaf among the leaves of endive except that upon it is a drop from the water of Paradise.”"],[2880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The beggar has a right, even if he comes on a horse.”"],[2881,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Khalid b. Ilyas narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Uthman, from Fatima bt. al-Husayn, from Husayn b. Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah loves noble matters and their heights, and He dislikes their lowly ones.”"],[2882,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever is afflicted by a calamity and says when he remembers it: “Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return,” Allah will renew for him the reward of it, the like of what it was on the day it afflicted him."],[2883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not disturb birds in their nests, for the night is a protection for them.”"],[2884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prolong looking at lepers.”"],[2893,"I heard al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever wears a garment of fame (to stand out), Allah will turn away from him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[2895,"That the Prophet ﷺ hid the word 'smoke' (dukhan) for Ibn Sayyad and asked him what he had hidden for him. He said: 'Dukh.' He said, 'Be gone! You will never exceed your station.' When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'What did he say?' Some of them said, 'Dukh,' and others said, 'Rather he said, Zukh.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'You have differed while I am still among you, so you will differ even more after me.'"],[2898,"A woman from the wives of al-Husayn prepared food in some of his land, and he ate. Then the food was cleared away, and a client (mawla) of his came, and he called for the food. He said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, I do not want it. He said: Why? He said: We ate a short while ago at the house of 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abbas. Al-Husayn said: Indeed, his father was the leader of Quraysh. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, feed the food and speak kindly.'"],[2899,"It is the Sunnah. He says: The gray hair—I have not outlived it?” And Sa'id was governor of Madinah at that time."],[2900,"I saw al-Husayn b. Ali ؓ put Sa'id b. al-'As forward for the funeral prayer of al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ."],[2901,"'Abd al-Muttalib married Halah bt. Uhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah."],[2902,"From 'Urwah regarding the naming of those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib."],[2903,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf."],[2904,"'Abd al-Muttalib: I went out to Yemen on one of the two journeys of ilaf, and I stayed with a man from the Jews. A man from the people of the monasteries saw me and asked about my lineage, so I traced my lineage for him. He said, 'Do you permit me to look at some part of you?' I said, 'Yes, as long as it is not private.' He opened one of my nostrils and looked, then looked in the other, and said, 'I bear witness that in one of your hands is kingship and in the other prophethood, and we find that in the Banu Zuhrah. How is that?' I said, 'I do not know.' He said, 'Do you have a sha'ah?' I said, 'What is a sha'ah?' He said, 'A wife.' I said, 'Not today.' He said, 'When you return, marry among the Banu Zuhrah.' 'Abd al-Muttalib returned and married Halah bt. Wuhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and she bore him Hamzah and Safiyyah. He married his son 'Abd Allah to Aminah bt. Wahb. The Quraysh said, 'Abd al-Muttalib has outdone his son.' She bore him the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So Hamzah ؓ was the brother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ through suckling—Thuwaybah, the freedwoman of Abu Lahab, suckled both of them—and he was older than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[2905,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'Shall I point out to you the most beautiful young woman of Quraysh?' He said, 'Who is she?' He said, 'The daughter of Hamzah.' He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2906,"Ali ؓ said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like the daughter of your paternal uncle, the most beautiful young woman in Quraysh? He said, 'Do you not know that Hamzah is my brother through suckling?'"],[2907,"I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he might marry her. He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2908,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you seeking wives among Quraysh and leaving us aside?' He said, 'Do you have someone?' I said, 'Yes, the daughter of Hamzah.' He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[2909,"The Prophet ﷺ was offered the daughter of Hamzah, and he said, 'She is not lawful for me; she is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and whatever is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling.'"],[2910,"The Prophet ﷺ was offered the daughter of Hamzah, and he said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and Allah ﷻ forbids through suckling what He forbids through lineage.'"],[2911,"I heard Umm Salamah say: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the daughter of Hamzah?' Or it was said, 'Will you not propose to the daughter of Hamzah?' He said, \"Hamzah is my brother through suckling.\""],[2912,"Yes, by Allah, people saw him. He came forward until he reached that gathering at al-Safa and al-Marwah, and there they were sitting with Abu Jahl among them. He leaned on his bow and said, \"I have shot such and such and done such and such.\" Then he gathered his hand with the bow and struck with it between the ears of Abu Jahl, breaking its end. Then he said, \"Take this from the bow, and another from the sword. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and that he has come with the truth from Allah.\" They said, \"O Abu 'Umarah, he has insulted our gods. If it had been you, and you are better than him, we would not have accepted this from you. And you, O Abu 'Umarah, are not one who speaks obscenely.\""],[2913,"Abu Jahl confronted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Safa and harmed him. Hamzah ؓ was a hunter and a man of game, and that day he was out hunting. When he returned, his wife, who had seen what Abu Jahl had done to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said to him, \"O Abu 'Umarah, if only you had seen what Abu Jahl did to your nephew.\" Hamzah became angry and went off just as he was, before entering his house, with his bow hanging from his neck, until he entered the mosque and found Abu Jahl in one of the gatherings of Quraysh. He did not speak to him until he struck his head with his bow and wounded him. Some men of Quraysh stood up to Hamzah to restrain him from Abu Jahl. Hamzah said, \"My religion is the religion of Muhammad. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, I will not turn away from that, so prevent me from it if you are truthful.\" When Hamzah accepted Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Muslims were strengthened by him, and some of their affairs became established. Quraysh feared him, and they knew that Hamzah ؓ would protect him."],[2914,"\"O Messenger of Allah, you established brotherhood between me and Hamzah.\""],[2915,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib and Zayd b. Harithah, and Hamzah ؓ was martyred on the day of Uhud.\""],[2916,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on Friday after praying the Friday prayer, and by morning he was at the mountain pass of Uhud. They met on Saturday in the middle of Shawwal in the year three.\""],[2917,"\"Uhud was in Shawwal in the year three.\""],[2918,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the emigrants: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib."],[2919,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stripped Hamzah, he wept, and when he saw his mutilated form, he sobbed.\""],[2920,"\"Hamzah was struck down on the day of Uhud.\""],[2921,"\"Hamzah was struck down on the day of Uhud.\""],[2922,"When Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, Safiyyah came looking for him, not knowing what had happened to him. She met Ali and al-Zubayr. Ali said to al-Zubayr, \"Mention it to your mother,\" and al-Zubayr said to Ali, \"You mention it to your paternal aunt.\" She said, \"What has happened to Hamzah?\" They indicated to her that they did not know. Then the Prophet ﷺ came and said, \"I fear for her mind.\" He placed his hand on her chest and supplicated for her. She sought Allah's reward and wept. Then he came and stood over him, and he had been mutilated. He said, \"Were it not for the grief of women, I would have left him until he is gathered from the crops of birds and bellies of beasts.\" Then he ordered the slain, and he began praying over them. He would place nine and Hamzah, and pronounce seven takbirs over them. Then they would be lifted and Hamzah left. Then he would bring nine and pronounce seven takbirs over them, until he finished with them."],[2923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray over the martyrs of Uhud, nine with Hamzah as their tenth, until he finished with them."],[2924,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ looked at Hamzah, who had been killed and mutilated, and saw a sight more painful and more frightening to his heart than any he had ever seen. He said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, for you were one who maintained ties of kinship and did much good. Were it not for the grief of those after you, it would please me to leave you until you come forth from various groups.\" Then, while standing in his place, he swore, \"By Allah, I will mutilate seventy of them in your place.\" Then the Qur'an was revealed while he was still standing in his place, not having moved: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you are patient, it is better for the patient} until the surah was completed. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ atoned for his oath and refrained from what he had intended."],[2925,"On the day of Uhud, sixty-four of the Ansar were killed and six of the Muhajirun, among them Hamzah ؓ. They mutilated their dead. The Ansar said, \"If we ever defeat them one day, we will surpass them.\" When it was the day of the conquest of Makkah, a man whose identity is unknown called out, \"No Quraysh after today.\" Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you are patient, it is better for the patient.} The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Refrain from the people.\""],[2926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Hamzah after Uhud, and he had been mutilated. He said, \"Were it not that Safiyyah would feel distress, I would have left him until scavengers ate him, until he is gathered from their bellies.\" Then he called for a striped cloak. When it was extended over his head, his feet showed; and when it was extended over his feet, his head showed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Extend it over his head.\" The cloth was scarce and the slain were many. One, two, or three men would be shrouded in a single cloth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask which of them knew more Qur'an and would place him toward the qiblah. So they buried them, and he did not pray over them."],[2927,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated that Muhammad bin Salih Al-Tammar narrated from Yazid bin Zaid, from Abu Usaid Al-Sa'idi, who said: \"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the grave of Hamza bin Abd al-Muttalib. They began dragging thorns on his face, causing his feet to be exposed. Then they dragged them on his feet, causing his face to be exposed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Place it on his face and place it on his feet with this tree.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head and saw his companions crying. He said, 'Indeed, a time will come upon people when they will go out to the outskirts and the cities will be better for them if they knew. No one will endure its hardships and difficulties except that I will be his intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[2928,"I saw Hamzah, and we found no cloth to shroud him in except a burdah. When we covered his feet with it, his head was exposed; and when we covered his head with it, his feet were exposed. So we covered his head and placed idhkhir (a fragrant grass) over his feet."],[2929,"Hamzah had a striped cloak. When his head was covered with it, his feet showed; and when his feet were covered, his head showed. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that his head be covered, and a tree branch and stones were placed over his feet."],[2930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ shrouded Hamzah in a single cloth. Jabir said, \"That cloth was a striped cloak.\""],[2931,"The Prophet ﷺ returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their dead. He said, \"But Hamzah has no weepers.\" So the women of the Ansar came and wept over Hamzah in his presence. He woke up while they were weeping and said, \"Woe to them! They are still here until now. Tell them to go back and not weep over any dead after today.\""],[2932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Last night I entered Paradise and looked around, and there was Hamzah reclining on a couch.\""],[2933,"When Hamzah and his companions were struck down on the day of Uhud, they said, \"Would that those behind us knew what reward Allah has given us, so that it would be a reward for them.\" Allah, exalted is He, said, \"I will inform them.\" So Allah, blessed and exalted is He, revealed: {And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead} – the verse."],[2934,"About his killing of Hamzah, may Allah have mercy on him, how did he kill him? We went toward him, and a man met us as we were asking about him. He said, \"He is a man overcome by this wine. If you find him sober, you will find an Arab man who will tell you whatever you want of his story; but if you find him otherwise, leave him.\" So we came to him and found him in his courtyard. He looked at Ubaydullah b. Adi and said, \"Son of Adi b. al-Khiyar?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I have not seen you since your mother al-Sa'diyyah handed you to me in your swaddling. It was only when your feet glimmered that I recognized you.\" He said, \"I said to him, 'We have come to you to tell us about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him.'\" He said, \"I was a slave of Jubayr b. Mut'im. His uncle Tu'aymah b. Adi was killed on the day of Badr. He said, 'If you kill Muhammad's uncle in return for my uncle, you are free.' So I went out on the day of Uhud among the people with my spear. My only concern was to be freed. I made Hamzah my target. I headed for him, but Sabba' b. Abd al-Uzza got ahead of me toward him.\" He said, \"I withdrew from him while he was cutting down people with his sword like a dark gray camel. When Sabba' got ahead of me toward him, Hamzah said, 'Come here, O son of the cutter of clitorises.'\" He said, \"He approached him and struck him, but it was as if he missed him. I hid behind something and shook my spear until I was satisfied with it, then I thrust it and it struck his groin.\" He said, \"He tried to rise but was overcome. I withdrew and returned to the people, then to Makkah, and I was freed. When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, I went out to al-Ta'if and stayed there. When the people of al-Ta'if agreed to make peace with the Prophet ﷺ, the paths became unclear to me. I began thinking about where to go. While I was in my worry, a man met me and said, 'Why do I see you like this?' I said, 'This man – I have done to his uncle what I did, and I see these people have agreed to make peace with him, so I do not know where to go.' He said, 'By Allah, he does not kill anyone who comes to him and bears witness to his testimony.' So I went out as I was. By Allah, I was not aware until I stood before his head in Madinah. He raised his head and looked at me and said, 'Wahshi?' I said, 'Wahshi,' and I bore witness to his testimony. He said, 'Woe to you, tell me about your killing of Hamzah, how you killed him.' So I told him, by Allah, just as I have told you two. He said, 'Woe to you, hide your face from me.' So I avoided him until Allah, exalted is He, took him. When Abu Bakr ؓ sent the army to al-Yamamah, I went out with the people. I made Musaylimah my target. I charged at him along with a man from the Ansar, and with me was my spear with which I had killed Hamzah. He said, 'I hurled the spear at him, and the Ansari charged at him. Your Lord knows best which of us killed him. If I killed him, then I have killed the best of people and the worst of people.'"],[2935,"And there were killed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud among the Muslims, then from Banu Hashim, Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. Wahshi, the freed slave of 'Utbah b. Ghazwan, killed him."],[2938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in a dream the kind of thing a sleeping person sees. He said: \"I saw as if I was riding behind a ram, and as if the blade of my sword broke. I interpreted it that I would kill the ram of the people, and I interpreted the blade of my sword as the killing of a man from my kin.\" Then Hamzah was killed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed Talhah, who was the standard-bearer."],[2939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is written with Allah in the seventh heaven: Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger.\""],[2940,"Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib used to fight in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with two swords, saying: \"I am the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger.\""],[2941,"I heard Abu Dharr say: I swear by Allah, this verse was revealed: {These are two adversaries who disputed concerning their Lord} about these six: Hamzah, 'Ubaydah, 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, and 'Utbah, Shaybah the two sons of Rabi'ah, and al-Walid b. 'Utbah. They had challenged each other to single combat on the day of Badr."],[2942,"That did not escape the notice of the Prophet ﷺ."],[2943,"Mu'awiyah said to him: \"O Hawdhah, did you witness Badr?\" He said: \"Yes, O Commander of the Faithful, against me, not for me.\" He said: \"How old were you then?\" He said: \"On that day I was a sturdy, compact youth, like a solid boulder. It is as if I am looking at them when they lined up against us in a long row, and it is as if I am looking at the gleam of their swords like the rays of the sun through the gaps in the clouds. I did not regain my senses until the vanguard of the people overwhelmed us, at their head 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ, a mighty lion, striking ferociously, saying: 'You will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah; you will never eat dates in the belly of Makkah.' Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib followed him, with a white feather on his chest by which he was marked, as if he were a camel trampling dry grass. I was terrified of the two of them, and the two of them turned upon Hanzalah,\" meaning Mu'awiyah's brother. Mu'awiyah ؓ said: \"Away from you, and no ingratitude to Allah. You have gone on. I wish I knew when you rested, O Hawdhah.\" He said: \"By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, I did not rest until I looked at the hills of Arthad and said: I wish I knew what happened to Hanzalah.\" Mu'awiyah said: \"By your mentioning Hanzalah, you are like the rich man remembering his poor brother, for he hardly mentions him except drowsy or half-asleep.\""],[2944,"That is the one who did to us what he did."],[2947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib one day and did not find him, so he asked his wife 'Inabah, who was from Banu al-Najjar. She said: He went out just now, may my father be your ransom, heading toward you. I think he missed you in one of the alleys of Banu al-Najjar. Will you not enter, O Messenger of Allah? So he entered, and she served him some hais, and he ate from it. She said: O Messenger of Allah, may it be wholesome and pleasant for you. You have come while I intended to come to you to congratulate you and wish you well. Abu 'Umarah told me that you were given a river in Paradise called al-Kawthar. He said: \"Yes, and its expanse is of ruby, coral, chrysolite, and pearl.\" She said: I would love for you to describe your pool to me with a description I can hear from you. He said: \"It is the distance between Aylah and San'a'. In it are pitchers like the number of the stars, and the dearest of those who come to it to me are your people, O daughter of Qahd,\" meaning the Ansar."],[3046,"The Prophet ﷺ would bring near two horned rams and slaughter one of them, saying, 'O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' And he brought the other near and said, 'O Allah, this is on behalf of my Ummah, for whoever bears witness to You of Your Oneness and bears witness to me of conveying the message.'"],[3047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten things before the Hour: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Hijaz of the Arabs, Ya'juj and Ma'juj, a wind that will sweep them and cast them into the sea, the rising of the sun from its west, the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, and the descent of 'Isa son of Maryam.'"],[3052,"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah died in the year thirty. His kunyah was Abu Muhammad. His age was sixty-five. Ibn 'Affan prayed over him in Madinah."],[3081,"I went out to Yemen and bought a hulla of Dhu Yazan, then I gifted it to the Prophet ﷺ during the truce that was between him and Quraysh. He said, 'I do not accept the gift of a polytheist,' and returned it. So I sold it, and he bought it and wore it. Then he came out to his companions wearing it, and I never saw anything on anyone more beautiful than it on him ﷺ. I could not help saying—"],[3082,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ and pressed him, so he said, 'How strange is your request, O Hakim! Indeed this wealth is lush and sweet, and it is, along with that, only the filth of people's hands. Indeed Allah's hand is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the recipient, and the lowest of hands is the hand of the recipient.'"],[3105,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated. If they are truthful and clear, they are blessed, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out.\""],[3107,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best charity is that given from sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support.\""],[3108,"A vessel containing milk was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. On his right was a man from the desert dwellers and on his left a man from his companions who was older than him. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his need of drinking, he said, \"O young man, this is for you. Will you permit me to give it to him?\" He said, \"It is for me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I will never give my share of your leftover to anyone.\" The Prophet ﷺ handed it to him and he drank."],[3109,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was among his companions, he said to them, \"Do you hear what I hear?\" They said, \"We do not hear anything.\" He said, \"I hear the creaking of the sky, and it is not blamed for creaking. There is not a handspan in it except that upon it is an angel prostrating or standing.\""],[3110,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting. He said, \"Fast three days of every month.\" I said, \"I am able to do more,\" until he debated with me. Then he said, \"Fast three days of the month.\" I said, \"I am able to do more,\" until he debated with me. Then he said, \"Fast the fast of David: fast one day and break the fast one day.\""],[3111,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him, and he said: \"Whoever asks people and is given will be like one who eats but what he eats does not benefit him. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and the best charity is what is given from surplus wealth. Begin with those whom you support.\" Hakim said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, by the One who honored you, I will never take anything from anyone ever again.\""],[3112,"Muhammad ﷺ was the most beloved man to me among the people in the pre-Islamic era. When he was made a prophet ﷺ and went out to Madinah, Hakim attended the fair while he was a disbeliever and found a suit belonging to Dhu Yazan being sold. He bought it to give as a gift to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He brought it to him in Madinah and wanted him to accept it as a gift, but he refused, saying: \"We do not accept anything from the polytheists. However, if you wish, I will take it from you for its price.\" So I gave it to him when he refused the gift, and he wore it. I saw him wearing it on the pulpit, and I never saw anything more beautiful than him on that day. Then he gave it to Usama b. Zayd. Hakim saw it on Usama and said: \"O Usama, are you wearing the suit of Dhu Yazan?\" He said: \"Yes, by God, I am better than Dhu Yazan and my father is better than his father.\" Hakim said: \"So I went to the people of Makkah to amaze them with Usama's statement.\""],[3115,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered and took a handful of pebbles, faced us with it, threw it at us, and said: \"May the faces be ugly!\" So we were defeated, and God ﷻ revealed: {You did not throw when you threw, but God threw}."],[3116,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Which charity is best?\" He said: \"Begin with those whom you support, and charity is given from surplus wealth.\""],[3117,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that retaliation be carried out in mosques, that poems be recited in them, or that legal punishments be carried out in them.\""],[3118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Legal punishments are not carried out in mosques, nor is retaliation carried out in them.\""],[3121,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him to buy a sacrificial animal for him for a dinar. He bought it, then sold it for two dinars. He bought a sheep for a dinar and brought back a dinar. \"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for blessing for him and ordered him to give the dinar as charity.\""],[3135,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no bad omen, and good fortune may be in the house and the woman.”"],[3151,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys.\" He said, 'Al-Hakam b. Amr al-Ghifari used to say among us, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the sea refused that' — meaning Ibn Abbas ؓ — and he recited: {Say, I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden} to the end of the verse."],[3155,"When the Prophet ﷺ died and Abu Bakr was made caliph, it was said to him about al-Hakam b. Abi al-As. He said, 'I would not loosen a knot that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied.'"],[3159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever takes a handspan of the Muslims' path, he will come carrying it from seven earths.'"],[3184,"Al-Hajjaj b. ‘Ilat gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ his sword Dhu al-Fiqar, and Dihya al-Kalbi gifted him his gray mule."],[3208,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banu Sahm: Hajjaj b. al-Harith."],[3227,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, an ally of theirs."],[3276,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: 'Hakim b. Hizam is Abu Khalid.'"],[3361,"From ʿUrwah concerning the naming of those Muslims who were killed on the Day of al-Yamāmah, then from Quraysh, then from Banū Makhzūm: Ḥakīm b. Ḥazn b. Abī Wahb b. ʿAmr b. ʿĀʾidh."],[3362,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab, regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Ajnadayn from Quraysh, then from Banu Sahm: Hajjaj b. al-Harith b. Qays."],[3370,"From Urwah, in naming those who were killed on the Day of Bi'r Ma'unah among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: al-Hakam b. Kaysan al-Makhzumi."],[3459,"From Ibn Shihab regarding the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Harithah b. Zayd b. Abi Zuhayr b. Imri' al-Qays."],[3474,"From Ibn Shihāb regarding the naming of those among the Anṣār who were martyred on the day of Uḥud from the Banū al-Nabīt: al-Ḥārith b. Aws b. Rāfiʿ."],[3530,"I fought the Prophet ﷺ at the beginning of the day as an unbeliever, and I fought with him at the end of the day as a Muslim. We were three men and nine women, and concerning us was revealed {Were it not for believing men and believing women}."],[3531,"Ibn Numayr—and people say Nusayba—and her sister, the two daughters of Kaʿb b. ʿAmr; her husband Zayd b. ʿĀṣim; and her two sons, ʿAbdallāh b. Zayd and Ḥabīb b. Zayd, the one whom Musaylima seized."],[3532,"And it is said, “Rather, it was revealed about Khārija b. Zayd b. Abī Zuhayr, the brother of the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj.”"],[3533,"His father brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ while his eyes were whitened and he could not see anything with them. He asked him, “What happened to him?” He said, “I was driving a camel of mine and my leg fell on snake eggs, so my sight was afflicted.” The Messenger of God ﷺ blew into his eye, and he regained his sight. I saw him passing thread through a needle while he was eighty years old and his eyes were still whitened."],[3539,"Ḥuṣayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “What do you think of a man who maintained family ties and hosted guests and died before you?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “My father and your father are in the Fire.” Not twenty nights passed before he died as an idolater."],[3541,"When Ṭalḥa b. al-Barāʾ met the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “O Messenger of God, command me to do whatever you love, and I will not disobey any command of yours.” The Prophet ﷺ marveled at that, for he was a youth, and said to him at that point, “Go and kill your father.” He turned and went out to do it, but the Prophet called him back and said, “Come back, for I was not sent to sever family ties.” After that Ṭalḥa fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him in winter during cold and clouds. When he departed, he said to his family, “I think Ṭalḥa is about to die, so inform me when it happens so that I may be present and pray over him; and hasten him.” But the Prophet ﷺ had not yet reached the Banū Sālim b. ʿAwf when he died, and night fell over him. Among what Ṭalḥa had said was: “Bury me and join me to my Lord ﷻ, and do not call the Messenger of God ﷺ, for I fear for him from the Jews lest he be harmed because of me.” The Prophet ﷺ was informed when morning came, and he came and stood at his grave. The people lined up with him, then he raised his hands and said, “O God, meet Ṭalḥa while You smile at him.”"],[3544,"From his father regarding the naming of those who attended [battles] with ʿAlī ؓ: al-Ḥārith b. al-Nuʿmān, a Badrī."],[3549,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is nothing in the hāmah, and the evil eye is real, and the truest of birds is the fa'l.\""],[3550,"Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by on the day of Siffin, leaning on Al-Ashtar. Then, Habis, who was known to be a devout worshiper, also passed by. Al-Ashtar said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, Habis is with them. By Allah, my last account of him was that he was a believer.\" Ali replied, \"Today, he is indeed a believer.\""],[3551,"Habis b. Sa'd al-Ta'i entered the mosque in the pre-dawn while he had met the Prophet ﷺ, and some people were praying in the front of the mosque. He said, \"The ostentatious ones, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, frighten them! Whoever frightens them has obeyed God and His Messenger.\" Then he said, \"The angels pray in the pre-dawn in the front of the mosque.\""],[3552,"I passed by one day, and the Messenger of God ﷺ called me, so I came to him, and he said: \"Say often: 'There is no power and no strength except with God,' for it is one of the treasures of Paradise.\""],[3553,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit on Friday saying: \"We have ordered for the women wars and needles. As for the wars, it came to them from Yemen; and as for the needles, they were taken from some of the people of the covenant from the jizyah that they owe.\" I said to al-Rabi', or it was said to him, or al-Rabi' b. Harb heard him: Yes."],[3554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed during his Hajj, while we were with him, by a man who had finished his Hajj, and said to him: \"Has your Hajj been accepted for you?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Start the work anew.\""],[3555,"I came to Madinah with merchandise to sell, and I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “I will give you twenty sāʿs of dates if you guide these companions of mine to the road to Khaybar.” I did so. When the Messenger of God ﷺ reached Khaybar and conquered it, I came and he gave me the twenty. Then I embraced Islam."],[3557,"ʿAlī ؓ proposed to the Messenger of God ﷺ for Fāṭimah ؓ. He said, “She is yours, on condition that you treat her well as a companion.”"],[3558,"Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ proposed to Fāṭimah ؓ. The Prophet ﷺ said, “She is yours, O ʿAlī.”"],[3559,"The Prophet of God ﷺ delivered a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said, “O people, what land is this?” They said, “A sacred land.” He said, “What month is this?” They said, “A sacred month.” He said, “What day is this?” They said, “A sacred day.” He said, “Indeed, your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, like this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours. Let those present convey to those absent. Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[3560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon on the day of Khaybar. “He forbade them to sell a share of the spoils before it was divided, to have intercourse with pregnant captives until they gave birth, and to sell fruit until its ripeness was evident and it was safe from blight.” Duḥaym added in his report: “And he permitted them three things that he had forbidden them: he permitted them the meat of sacrificial animals, visiting graves, and leather containers.”"],[3561,"A man asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, should I make one-third of my prayers for you?\" He said, \"Yes, if you wish.\" The man asked, \"What if I make two-thirds of my prayers for you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The man then asked, \"And if I dedicate all of my prayers to you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In that case, Allah will suffice you in all matters of your worldly life and the Hereafter that concern you.\""],[3562,"From Ḥayyān b. Buḥḥ al-Ṣudāʾī, a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: He said, “My people disbelieved. I was told that the Prophet ﷺ was preparing an army against them, so I went to him and said, ‘My people are upon Islam.’ He said, ‘Is that so?’ I said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘So I followed him that night until morning, and I announced the prayer. When morning came, he gave me a vessel and I performed ablution from it. The Prophet ﷺ placed his fingers in the vessel, and springs gushed forth. He said, ‘Whoever among you wishes to perform ablution, let him do so.’ So I performed ablution and prayed, and he appointed me over them and gave me their charity.”"],[3563,"I heard Ḥayyān, the grandfather of Ibn Abjar al-Akbar, say, “Leave off medicine as long as your body can bear the illness.”"],[3564,"From the belly of a woman, her clothes, until he treated her.”"],[3565,"The owner of this house, Ḥarīz or Abū Ḥarīz, told me: “When I reached the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, I placed my hands on the cushion of his saddle and found it to be from the skin of a wool-bearing sheep.”"],[3566,"Hassan b. Thabit died in the year fifty-four."],[3567,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to place a pulpit for Hassan b. Thabit in the mosque, upon which he would recite poetry. She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, support him with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends Your Prophet.”"],[3568,"The Prophet ﷺ placed a pulpit for Hassan, upon which he recited satire against the polytheists."],[3570,"Al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam ؓ passed by a gathering of the Prophet's ﷺ Companions while Hassan b. Thabit was reciting his poetry to them, and they were not attentive to what they heard from him. Al-Zubayr sat with them and said: “Why do I see you not listening to the poetry of Ibn al-Furay'a? He used to present it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would listen well, generously reward him, and not be distracted from him by anything.” Hassan said:"],[3571,"He said to him: “I adjure you by God, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Respond on my behalf, may God support you with the Holy Spirit?’” He said: “O God, yes.”"],[3572,"Hassan recited poetry in the mosque, and Umar ؓ passed by him and glanced at him, saying: “In the mosque? In the mosque?” Hassan said: “By God, I recited in it to one better than you.” Umar feared that he meant the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he let him be and left him."],[3574,"I used to recite in it to one better than you. Umar ؓ turned away, fearing that he would say the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: “I adjure you by God, do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘O Hassan, respond on behalf of the Messenger of God. O God, support him with the Holy Spirit’?” He said: “Yes.”"],[3575,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Hassan, \"Lampoon them (i.e. the pagans) and Gabriel is with you.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3213)"],[3576,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “Satirize them—or ‘satirize them’—meaning the polytheists, for Gabriel is with you.”"],[3577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Hassan, \"Verily, the Holy Spirit is with you as long as you befriend them.\" He means the polytheists."],[3578,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves."],[3579,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves."],[3580,"We, the Ansar, had a need to present to the governor, and what we sought from him was a difficult matter. We went to him with men from Quraysh and others, and they spoke to him and mentioned the bequest of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning us. He mentioned the difficulty of the matter, so the people excused him and left, while Ibn Abbas kept pressing him, and by God, he found no alternative but to fulfill our need. We went out until we entered the mosque, and there the people were in circles. Hassan said: I laughed as I listened to them. For by God, he was the most deserving of it; it is the remnant of prophethood and the inheritance of Ahmad ﷺ, the refinement of his roots and the extraction of the likeness of his character. The people said: “Speak well, O Hassan.” Ibn Abbas said: “They are right.” Then Hassan began to praise Ibn Abbas ؓ and said:"],[3581,"His mother went as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to you as a delegate so that you may supplicate for this son of mine, that God may place blessing for him in it and make him abundant and good. So he performed ablution, and from the leftover water of his ablution he wiped his face, and said: “O God, bless her in him and make him abundant and good.”"],[3582,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Ta’if, and he saw men among his companions who had dyed their beards red and dyed their beards yellow, so he said: “Welcome to those who dyed yellow and those who dyed red.”"],[3583,"His wife said: Now you will be sold on account of his debt. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Who is the one responsible for the estate of al-Hubab?” His brother Abu al-Yasar Ka‘b b. ‘Amr said: I am. The Prophet ﷺ called him and said: “Do not sell her; set her free. When you hear of slaves that have come to me, come to me and I will compensate you.” They did so. Then they differed among themselves after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some said: An umm walad is owned as a slave; were it not for that, the Prophet ﷺ would not have compensated them. Others said: She is free; the Prophet ﷺ had set her free."],[3584,"“I am its little trimmed stump and its propped-up little palm—Hubab b. al-Mundhir.”"],[3585,"He spent the night dragging a rope on his back for two saa‘s of dates. He turned back with one of them to his family, who benefited from it, and he brought the other to draw near to God Almighty. He brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Scatter it among the charity.” The hypocrites said about him and mocked him: “This man had no need to draw near to God with a saa‘ of dates.” Then God Almighty sent down: {Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities, and those who find nothing but their effort} to the end of the two verses."],[3586,"He was called Humam, and that was in the pre-Islamic era. My uncle came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and spoke to him about his son. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Receive back your son as much as you are able.” So he went and took his son and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The boy’s master also came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ offered him two slave boys and said: “Take one of them and leave the man his son.” So he took a slave boy and left him his son."],[3587,"His grandfather came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: “What is your name?” He said: Hazn. He wanted to change his name, but he said: “I would not change a name my father gave me.” Sa‘id said: That ruggedness has remained among us until now."],[3588,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Trench while he was taking the people’s pledge for emigration. He said: O Messenger of God, accept the pledge of this one for emigration. He said: “And who is this?” He said: My cousin Hawt b. Yazid, or Yazid b. Hawt. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I will not accept your pledge. The people emigrate to you, but you do not emigrate to them.”"],[3590,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed a man over a military expedition. When he set out and then returned to him, he said to him: “How did you find command?” He said: I was like one of the people; when I rode, they rode, and when I dismounted, they dismounted. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The holder of authority stands at the gate of hardship, except for the one whom God Almighty protects.” The man said: By God, I will never work for you or for anyone else again. The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars showed."],[3592,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Mecca, migrating to Madinah, he was accompanied by Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr's servant Amir b. Fuhayrah, and their guide Abdullah b. Urayqit. They passed by the two tents of Umm Mabad al-Khuzaiyyah. She was a strong woman who would sit in front of her tent and provide water and food to travelers. They asked her for some meat and dates to purchase, but found nothing with her as the people were facing a severe famine. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed a sheep in the corner of the tent and asked, \"What is this sheep, O Umm Mabad?\" She replied, \"This sheep has been left behind by weakness.\" He asked, \"Does it have any milk?\" She replied, \"It is too weak for that.\" He ﷺ asked, “Would you allow me to milk it?” She replied, \"Yes, may my parents be sacrificed for you, if you see any milk in it, then milk it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for the sheep, put his hand on its udder, and invoked the name of Allah. Suddenly, milk started flowing abundantly. He ﷺ called for a large container which could satisfy the thirst of many people. He milked it until it filled the container, then gave her to drink until she was satisfied, and then he gave to his companions to drink until they were satisfied. Finally, he ﷺ drank. Then he repeated the milking to fill the container again, leaving it with her. Shortly after they left, Umm Mabad's husband, Abu Mabad, returned driving some lean goats whose udders were dry. When he saw the milk, he was astonished and asked, \"From where did you get this milk, O Umm Mabad, as the sheep is dry and there's no milking goat in the house?\" She replied, \"No, by Allah, a blessed man passed by us.\" He asked, \"Describe him to me, O Umm Mabad.\" She replied, \"I saw a man of radiant appearance, with a bright face, beautiful in form. Neither too thin nor deficient in physique. He was handsome and well-proportioned, with large dark eyes, long eyelashes, and a deep, slightly hoarse voice. His neck was well-defined, and his beard was thick. His eyebrows were long and arched, and if he remained silent, he was enveloped in dignity, but when he spoke, he was adorned with grace and majesty. From a distance, he was the most beautiful of people, and up close, he was the most pleasant and delightful. His speech was sweet, distinct, neither too brief nor excessive, as if his words were strung pearls flowing down. He was neither too tall to intimidate nor too short to be disregarded, but perfectly proportioned, like a branch between two other branches, the most striking and noble of the three. He was surrounded by companions who were attentive to him. When he spoke, they listened intently, and when he commanded, they hastened to fulfill his command. He was well-attended, always surrounded by people, yet never frowning nor disregarded.” Abu Mabad said, \"By Allah, he is the companion of Quraysh whom we were informed about. I have decided to accompany him, and if I find a way to do so, I will surely do it.\" Later, there was a loud voice in Mecca heard from the sky, saying..."],[3593,"He mentioned seventy of the Ansar. When night fell upon them, they would retire to a teacher in Madinah and spend the night studying the Quran. When morning came, those who had strength would gather firewood and fetch fresh water, and those who had means would get a sheep and prepare it. It would be hanging by a stone of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the morning. When Khubayb was killed, the Messenger of God ﷺ sent them out, and among them was my maternal uncle Haram. They came to a clan of Banu Sulaym. Haram said to their commander: Shall I tell these people that we are not after them, so that they leave us alone? He said: So he went to them and told them that. A man among them met him with a spear and thrust it through him. When Haram felt the touch of the spear in his belly, he said: God is greatest! I have won, by the Lord of the Ka‘bah. They were delayed against them, and no one survived to bring news. I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ grieve over an expedition as he grieved over them. Anas said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ every time he prayed the dawn prayer raise his hands supplicating against them.” After that, Abu Talhah came to me and said: Would you like to confront the killer of Haram? I said: What is the matter with him? May God do to him and do. Abu Talhah said: Do not do that, for he has accepted Islam."],[3594,"Some people from the tribe of Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him to send with them people who can teach them the Quran. So he sent with them seventy men from the Ansar, among them Harām ibn Milhān, the uncle of Anas. However, they betrayed them and killed them.Harām was the first to be stabbed with a spear, and blood was flowing from him. He grabbed it, raised it towards the sky, and said, \"I have won by the Lord of the Kāʿbah.\" Then the Quran was revealed regarding them, \"Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.\""],[3595,"“I saw Hashraj, a man whom the Prophet ﷺ took and placed in his lap, wiped his head, and supplicated for him.”"],[3596,"\"I was holding the halter of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ she-camel during the middle of the days of Tashriq in the Farewell Pilgrimage.\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[3597,"He is called Humamah, one of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. He went out as a warrior to Isfahan during the caliphate of Umar ؓ, and Isfahan was conquered. Humamah said, \"O Allah, Humamah claims that he loves to meet You. If he is truthful, then decree for him upon it with sincerity, and if he is lying, then decree for him upon it even if he dislikes it.\" Then he was seized by a stomach illness and died in Isfahan. Abu Musa said, \"O people, by Allah, we have not heard in what we have heard from your Prophet ﷺ and what our knowledge has reached except that Humamah is a martyr.\""],[3598,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr: \"Among those who witnessed Badr was Khabbab b. al-Aratt b. Khuwaylid b. Sa'd b. Jadhima b. Ka'b b. Sa'd.\""],[3599,"\"Khabbab b. al-Aratt was a freed slave of Banu Zuhrah. He witnessed Badr and was given the kunya Abu Abdullah. He died in the year thirty-seven, when Ali ؓ returned from Siffin to Kufa, and he was the first of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to be buried in Kufa. Khabbab's Islam was in Makkah.\""],[3600,"I heard Kurdus say: \"Khabbab embraced Islam as the sixth of six; he was one-sixth of Islam.\""],[3601,"\"It is not with me, but upon you is the one who took it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Upon you is Abu Abdullah Khabbab b. al-Aratt.\""],[3602,"\"In this chest there are eighty thousand, for which no purse-string was tied and no beggar was turned away. I wish it were such-and-such\" — either he said, \"dung\" or something else."],[3603,"Khabbab returned with remnants of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . They said, \"Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, your brothers will come before you tomorrow.\" So he cried and then said, \"Indeed, those [companion] have already gone with their rewards, and I fear that my recompense for those actions will be what we have been given after them.\""],[3604,"\"...that he be buried among the people of Kufa.\""],[3632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Kaaba, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists and they had exhausted us. I said, 'Won't you supplicate for us?' He said, 'Among those before you, a man would be seized and combed with iron down to his flesh and bones, and that would not turn him away from his religion.'"],[3638,"He said, \"I will not repay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad ﷺ.\" I said, \"No, by Allah, I will not disbelieve in him until you die and are resurrected.\" He said, \"When I am resurrected, I will have wealth and children, and I will repay you your due.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down: {Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses} the verse."],[3656,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Let none of you wish for death; (if not for the prohibition,) I would have wished for it.\""],[3657,"We entered upon Khabbab, and he had cauterized his stomach seven times. He said, \"Had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Let none of you wish for death,' I would have wished for it.\""],[3658,"\"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I did not own a dirham, and now here are forty thousand (dirhams) set aside.\""],[3659,"\"I saw myself with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I did not own a dirham, and today in one corner of my house there are forty thousand dirhams.\""],[3660,"We entered upon Khabbab while a wall was being built in his house. He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A believer is rewarded for his spending, except for what he puts into the dust (i.e., building on earth).'\""],[3661,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about hunger, but he did not show any signs of discontent.\""],[3662,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying on the scorching hot ground, but he did not relieve us (of that hardship).\""],[3663,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying on the scorching hot ground, but he did not relieve us (of that hardship).\""],[3664,"\"That our rewards go (to us) along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and whatever worldly things we obtained after him.\""],[3665,"Hamzah was shrouded in a burdah (striped cloak) such that when his head was covered, his feet would show, and when his feet were covered, his head would show."],[3666,"I saw Hamzah and we could not find any cloth to shroud him in except a burdah. When we covered his feet with it, his head showed, and when we covered his head with it, his feet showed. So we covered his head and placed idhkhir (a kind of grass) over his feet."],[3667,"We entered upon Khabbab, then his shroud was brought. When he saw it, he wept and said: 'But Hamzah had no shroud found for him except a burdah. When it was put over his head, it shrank away from his feet, and when it was put over his feet, it shrank away from his head, until it was stretched over his head and idhkhir was placed over his feet.'"],[3668,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3669,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3670,"I said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3671,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the sun-baked ground, but he did not respond to our complaint."],[3672,"We said to Khabbab: How did you know the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3673,"We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'Yes.' We said: How did you know that? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3674,"We said to Khabbab: How did you know the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'"],[3675,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Let none of you wish for death; for had it not been so, I would have wished for it.'"],[3676,"On the day of 'Ashura', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O people, whoever among you wants to fast this day, let him fast it. Whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast. And whoever has eaten, let him fast the rest of his day.'"],[3677,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Ashura: \"O people, whoever of you has eaten, let him not eat for the rest of his day, and whoever of you intended to fast, let him fast it.\""],[3678,"In His saying, \"And do not turn away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon, seeking His countenance\". It was narrated that the Prophet ﷺ used to sit with Bilal, 'Ammaar bin Yaasir, Sohayb, and Khabbaab ibn Al-Aratt (may Allah be pleased with them), in the company of some weak believers. When they saw those around the Prophet ﷺ , they demeaned them, so they went to him and spoke in this manner, \"We would like for you to establish a separate gathering for us, where the Arabs can recognize our importance. When Arab delegations come to visit you, we feel ashamed to be seen sitting with these slaves. Or when we come to you, have them leave, and when we leave, let them sit if you wish.\" He said, \"Yes.\" They said, \"Then write for us a treaty.\" He called for a parchment in order to write for them, and he called 'Ali to write. While we were sitting in a corner, with him, Angel Gabriel descended upon him, and he recited the verse, \"And do not turn away those who call upon their Lord morning and afternoon\". Then, he mentioned Al-Aqra' Ibn Habis and his companion and said, \"And thus We made some of them as a trial for others to say, “Are these the ones upon whom Allahhas bestowed favor among us?” Is not Allah most knowing of the grateful?\" Then, he mentioned him and said, \"And when those come to you who believe in Our verses, say, 'Peace be upon you; your Lord has decreed upon Himself mercy'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the parchment, called us, and approached us while saying, \"Peace be upon you,\" until we sat down with our knees touching his knees."],[3679,"He was brought his shroud, and white fine Egyptian linen was spread over him. He wept. They said, \"What makes you weep, O Abu Abdullah, when you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"I remembered Mus'ab b. Umayr, who did not hasten to enjoy any of its good things. He was shrouded in a burdah, and nothing was found to shroud him in it. When we covered his head with it, his feet stuck out, and when we covered his feet, his head stuck out, until we placed idhkhir and plants of the earth over him.\""],[3680,"Some people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Khabbab. They said, \"Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, you will come to Muhammad ﷺ at the Hawd.\" He said, \"How can I, with this?\" and he pointed to the upper part of his house and its lower part. The Prophet ﷺ had said: \"What suffices any of you in this world is like the provision of a rider.\""],[3681,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When you fast, use the tooth-stick in the morning, but do not use it in the evening; for there is no fasting person whose lips become dry in the evening except that it becomes light between his eyes on the Day of Resurrection.\" 'Ali did not trace it back to the Prophet."],[3682,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. We were afflicted with thirst, and we had no water with us. A she-camel belonging to one of us knelt down, and between her legs there was something like a water-skin, so we drank from her milk.\""],[3683,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint,\" meaning regarding the midday prayer."],[3684,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3685,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not grant us relief.\""],[3686,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the severity of the ground's heat, and he did not heed our complaint. He said, \"When the sun declines, then pray.\""],[3687,"\"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of the ground, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3688,"Who among us complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the heat of the hot season, but he did not complain and said, \"When the sun sets, then pray\"?"],[3689,"\"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the intense heat on our foreheads and palms, and he did not heed our complaint.\""],[3690,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the Children of Israel were destroyed, they told stories.\""],[3691,"I entered upon Khabbab and saw in his house uncovered dirhams. I said, “What is this?” He said, “I sold my such-and-such estate, and I have spent it. I do not see anyone more entitled to it than myself.”"],[3692,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Horses are of three kinds: a horse for the Most Merciful, a horse for man, and a horse for Satan. The horse of the Most Merciful is that which is kept for the cause of God and upon which the enemies of God, may He be exalted, are fought. The horse of man is that which is used for breeding and for carrying loads. The horse of Satan is that which is staked for gambling and wagered upon.”"],[3693,"From the Prophet of God ﷺ that he never went to his bed without reciting “Say: O disbelievers” until he completed it."],[3694,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me on an errand. I said, “O Messenger of God, you are sending me far away while I am anxious about you.” He said, “What has your anxiety about me reached?” I said, “I wake in the morning and do not think you will reach the evening, and I reach the evening and do not think you will reach the morning.” He said, “O Khabbab, [there are] five things: if you do them, you will see me, and if you do not do them, you will not see me.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what are they?” He said, “Worship God, associating nothing with Him, even if you are cut up and burned, and believe in divine decree.” I said, “O Messenger of God, what is belief in divine decree?” He said, “Know that what befalls you could not have missed you, and that what misses you could not have befallen you. Do not drink wine, for its sin knocks against other sins just as its tree clings to trees. Be dutiful to your parents, even if they command you to leave this world. And hold fast to the rope of the community, for God’s hand is upon the community. O Khabbab, if you see me on the Day of Resurrection, you will not be separated from me.”"],[3695,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O God, cover my faults, calm my fears, and settle my debt.”"],[3696,"“Khuzaymah b. Thabit fought on the Day of Siffin until he was killed.”"],[3697,"Zayd b. Thabit said: When we wrote the mushafs, I missed a verse that I used to hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I found it with Khuzaymah b. Thabit al-Ansari: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to God; among them are those who have fulfilled their vow, and among them are those who await, and they have not changed in the least.” He said, “Khuzaymah used to be called Dhu al-Shahadatayn.”"],[3728,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Allah is not shy of the truth. Do not come to women in their rears.”"],[3729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah forbids you to come to women in their rears.”"],[3730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this plague is a defilement and a remnant of a punishment with which some people were punished. If it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if it occurs in a land while you are not in it, do not enter it.”"],[3731,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this ailment is a defilement and a remnant of a punishment with which people before you were punished. If it is in a land, do not enter it; and if it is in a land while you are in it, do not approach it” — meaning the plague."],[3732,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3736,"From Khuzaymah b. Thabit: A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks. He said: “For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night.” And if we had asked for more, he would have made it five."],[3737,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Wiping over the leather socks is for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3738,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night.”"],[3739,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about wiping over the leather socks. He said: “For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night.” And if the questioner had pressed his question, he would have increased it."],[3740,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Wipe over the leather socks for three days.\" And if we had asked for more, he would have increased for us."],[3741,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set a time limit for the traveler to wipe three days, and for the resident a day and a night. And if we had asked for more, he would have increased for us. Abu al-Qasim said: \"Abu al-Ahwas omitted 'Amr b. Maymun from the chain.\""],[3742,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ directed us to wipe three times; and if we had asked for more, he would have granted us more.\""],[3743,"An Arab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about ablution. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Three for the traveler and one for the resident.\" If the Arab had insisted, the Prophet ﷺ would have allowed him to wipe over his socks."],[3744,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The traveler wipes for three days.\" Shu'bah said: \"I think he said: 'and their nights.'\""],[3745,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks, he said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights.\""],[3746,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Regarding wiping over the leather socks, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3747,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set three days for the traveler and one day for the resident."],[3748,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3749,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The traveler wipes over the leather socks for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.\""],[3750,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3751,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3752,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.\""],[3753,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said regarding wiping over the leather socks: \"For the traveler, three days and their nights.\""],[3754,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding wiping: “For the traveler, three days, and one day for the resident.”"],[3755,"I asked ʿAʿishah ؓ about wiping over the khuff (leather slippers) and she said: Ask ʿAli ؓ . I asked him and he said: Three days and nights - i.e., for the traveller - and one day and night for one who is not travelling (Using translation from Aḥmad 780)"],[3756,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks, he said: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3757,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler wipes for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3758,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “For the traveler, three days, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3760,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to wipe: for the resident, a day and a night, and for the traveler, three.”"],[3761,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3762,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3763,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Wiping over the leather socks: for the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3764,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night, without removing them.”"],[3765,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3766,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wiping over the leather socks is for three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.”"],[3767,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.”"],[3769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also said: “The traveler [may wipe over his leather socks] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3770,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3771,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three [days], and the resident for one day, wiping over the leather socks.”"],[3772,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler wipes over his leather socks for three days, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3773,"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding wiping over the leather socks: “A day and a night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler.”"],[3774,"From the Prophet ﷺ [regarding] wiping over the leather socks: “For the traveler, three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night.” ʿAbd Allāh said: My father said this is a mistake. Abū al-Qāsim said: Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal meant that he considered the ḥadīth of Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jadalī, to be a mistake, and the correct [version] from the ḥadīth of Manṣūr is the ḥadīth of ʿAmr b. Maymūn."],[3775,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3776,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding wiping over the leather socks: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days, and the resident for a day and a night.”"],[3777,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The traveler [may wipe] for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night, wiping over his leather socks when he put them on while his feet were pure.”"],[3778,"There were men among us who, when they came from defecation, would wash away the traces of feces. Then this verse was revealed concerning them: {In it are men who love to purify themselves}."],[3779,"A woman was stoned during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and the people said, “Her deeds have been nullified.” That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “It is an expiation for her sins, and she will be resurrected [in a state] besides that.”"],[3780,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, [what about] the rabbit?” He said: “I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.” I said, “But I will not leave it unless you forbid it.” He said: “It menstruates,” or he said, “It bleeds.” I said, “Then what about the hyena?” He said: “And who would eat the hyena?”"],[3781,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to ask you about some things, about the creeping creatures of the earth. What do you say about the dabb (spiny-tailed lizard)? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it.” I said: Then I will eat what you have not forbidden. And why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “An ummah (nation) among the nations was lost, and I saw a creation that disturbed me.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the rabbit? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it.” He said: Then I will eat what you have not forbidden. And why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “I was informed that it menstruates.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the hyena? He said: “And who would eat the hyena?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the fox? He said: “And who would eat the fox?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the wolf? He said: “And would anyone with any good in him eat the wolf?”"],[3782,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the creeping creatures of the earth, and he said: “Ask about whatever you wish.” So I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about the dabb (spiny-tailed lizard)? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it. I was told that an ummah (nation) from the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth.” I said: I will not leave anything that you have not forbidden without eating it. He said: I said: And the rabbit? He said: “I do not eat it and I do not forbid it. I was informed that it menstruates.” I said: I will not leave anything that you have not forbidden without eating it. I said: And the fox? He said: “Does anyone eat the fox?” I said: And the hyena? He said: “Does anyone eat the hyena?” I said: And the wolf? He said: “Does anyone with any good in him eat the wolf?”"],[3783,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, and he mentioned Khalid b. al-Walid: An excellent servant of Allah and brother of the clan, and a sword among the swords of Allah."],[3784,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he announced the death of the people of Mu'tah, said: “Then a sword among the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and Allah granted victory through him.”"],[3785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the death of the people of Mu'tah from the pulpit, then said: “Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the standard, and he is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Glorified.”"],[3786,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah, Mighty and Glorified, which Allah has poured upon the disbelievers.”"],[3787,"“And a Yemeni plate of mine held firm in my hand.”"],[3788,"Khuraym b. Aws: “No one was more hostile to the Arabs than Hurmuz. When we had finished with Musaylimah and his companions, we proceeded toward the area of Basrah, and Hurmuz met us at Kazimah with a huge gathering. Khalid went out to meet him and called for single combat. Hurmuz came out against him, and Khalid killed him, and he wrote about that to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ, who granted him his spoils. The qalansuwah (cap) of Hurmuz was worth one hundred thousand dirhams. The Persians, when a man was honored among them, would make a cap worth one hundred thousand dirhams.”"],[3789,"“Look for it,” so they found it, and it was an old worn cap. Khalid said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ‘umrah and shaved his head, and the people rushed to get the sides of his hair. I beat them to his forelock hair, and I placed it in this cap. I have never witnessed a battle with it with me except that I was granted victory.”"],[3790,"“O assembly of Quraysh, Allah, Exalted, has not given your faces any superiority over our faces except what Allah favored His Prophet ﷺ with.” Then Khalid said: “Let him retaliate.” The man said to his nephew: “Slap him.” But when he raised his hand, he said: “Leave it for Allah, Mighty and Glorified.”"],[3791,"“...from our hands while you are humiliated, for with me are people who love killing in the path of Allah as a Persian loves wine. And peace be upon those who follow guidance.”"],[3792,"I heard Qays b. Abi Hazim say: “Khalid b. al-Walid led the people in prayer wearing a garment wrapped around him.”"],[3793,"When Khalid b. al-Walid came to al-Hirah, he said, \"Bring me the poison.\" So it was brought to him, and he placed it in his palm and then said, \"In the name of Allah,\" and swallowed it, and it did not harm him."],[3794,"\"In the name of Allah,\" and he swallowed it down."],[3795,"\"Enough, for what is between us has not reached the level of our religion.\""],[3796,"\"Your disbelief, not your glorification: indeed I have seen that Allah has humiliated you.\""],[3797,"\"I sought death but it was not decreed for me except to die on my bed. There is no deed I hope in more than 'there is no god but Allah,' and I am shielded by it.\" Then he said, \"When I die, look at my weapons and my horse and make them provisions in the path of Allah.\""],[3798,"\"Yes, by Allah, He is sought for help in that.\""],[3807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Maymunah, and she brought him a cooked dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) with dates. Maymunah said, “Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he eats.” When he was informed of it, he held back his hand from it. They said, “Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “No, but I find it distasteful.” Khalid b. al-Walid pulled it over and ate it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ watched him."],[3809,"Al-Qa'nabi and Ibrahim b. Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: 'Amr b. Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu Najih narrated to me from Khalid b. Hakim b. Hizam, who said: Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah took hold of a man from the people of the earth over something, and Khalid b. al-Walid spoke to him about it. It was said to him, “Did you anger the commander?” He said, “I did not intend to anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were most severe in punishing people in this world.’”"],[3819,"'Ammar insulted me during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, were it not for you, the son of Sumayyah would not have insulted me.” He said, “Gently, O Khalid. Whoever insults 'Ammar, Allah insults him, and whoever belittles 'Ammar, Allah belittles him.”"],[3822,"“...that we teach our children archery and the Qurʾān.”"],[3823,"He complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: “I feel terror at night.” He said: “Shall I not teach you words that Jibrīl ﷺ taught me? He claimed that an ʿifrīt of the jinn was scheming against me.” He said: “I seek refuge in the perfect words of God, which neither a righteous nor a wicked person can surpass, from the evil of what descends from heaven and what ascends in it, from the evil of what He has scattered in the earth and what emerges from it, from the evil of the trials of the night and the trials of the day, and from the evil of the night visitors and day visitors, except a visitor who comes with good, O Merciful.”"],[3824,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Shall I not teach you words that, if you say them, you will sleep? Say: O God, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they lead astray, be for me a neighbour against the evil of all jinn and humans, that any of them may assault me or harm me. Mighty is Your protection, exalted is Your praise, and there is no god but You.”"],[3825,"From Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ashʿarī ؓ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man who did not complete his bowing, pecking in his prostration while he was praying. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If this man died in this state of his, he would die on other than the religion of Muḥammad ﷺ.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The example of one who does not complete his bowing and pecks in his prostration is like a hungry person who eats one or two dates, which do not avail him anything.” Abū Ṣāliḥ said: I said to Abū ʿAbd Allāh: “Who told you this from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said: “The commanders of the armies: ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, Khālid b. al-Walīd, and Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasana heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[3826,"“...and al-Hind, in our hearts at that time, was al-Baṣra, while I disliked that.” He said: A man stood and said: “O Abū Sulaymān, fear God ﷻ, for tribulations have appeared.” He said: “Is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb alive? It will only be after him, and the people at Dhī Billiyān—and Dhī Billiyān is at such-and-such a place. A man will look and reflect whether he can find a place that has not been struck by the like of what struck his own place, of tribulation and evil, and he will not find it.” He said: “And those are the days that the Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned: ‘Before the Hour there will be days of harj.’ We seek refuge with God that those days should overtake us and you.”"],[3843,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If anyone were to escape the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped it.\""],[3844,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Measure your food, and you will be blessed in it.\""],[3845,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image.\""],[3858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper, and whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day should not enter the bathhouse.\""],[3859,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought food, he would eat some of it and then send it to us. We were brought food that he had not eaten from at all. I said to the woman, \"Do not be hasty.\" I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"This herb—I dislike its smell.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"I dislike what you dislike, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[3860,"I never prayed behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him when he finished his prayer saying: \"O Allah, forgive me all my errors and sins. O Allah, revive me, restore me, provide for me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to their righteousness and none turns away any of their evil except You.\""],[3883,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Ibrahim ﷺ . He said: 'O Jibril, who is this with you?' He said: 'Muhammad.' He greeted me and welcomed me, and said: 'Command your ummah to plant abundantly in Paradise, for its soil is good and vast.' I said: 'What is the planting of Paradise?' He said: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah).'\""],[3884,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to me: 'Shall I not teach you a word that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me?' I said: 'Yes, uncle.' He said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, he said: \"Shall I not teach you, Abu Ayyub, a word from the treasure of Paradise?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\" He said: \"Increase in saying: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah).\"'"],[3885,"He said to me: 'Shall I not command you with what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me? To increase in saying: La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no power and no strength except with Allah), for it is among the treasures of Paradise.'"],[3905,"I asked Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, “How were sacrifices among you in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said, “In the time of the Prophet ﷺ, a man would sacrifice a sheep on behalf of himself and his household, and they would eat from it and feed others from it; then people began to vie with one another, and it became as you see.”"],[3906,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to face the qiblah while defecating or urinating. When we came to Syria, we found their latrines were built facing the qiblah, so we would turn aside and seek Allah’s forgiveness, exalted be He."],[3907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Abū Ayyūb, shall I not guide you to a charity that Allah and His Messenger love? You reconcile between people when they hate one another and become corrupt.”"],[3959,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: “Do not sever relations, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of God, brothers. The separation of believers is three [days]; if the two do not speak, God turns away from them until they speak.”"],[3965,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ washing his head while in iḥrām.”"],[3971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was lodged on the lower floor, and Abu Ayyub went up to the upper floor. When evening came and night fell, Abu Ayyub kept thinking that he was above the roof of the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the Prophet was below him, and that he was between him and the revelation. So Abu Ayyub could not sleep, fearing that dust might fall on him or that he might move and disturb him. When morning came, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not sleep a wink last night, neither I nor Umm Ayyub.' He said, 'Why is that, O Abu Ayyub?' He said, 'I remembered that I am above the roof of a house while you are below me, and I move and dust falls on you and my movement disturbs you, and I am between you and the revelation.' He said, 'Do not do that, O Abu Ayyub. Shall I not teach you some words? If you say them in the morning ten times and in the evening ten times, you will be given ten good deeds for them, ten evil deeds will be wiped away from you, you will be raised ten degrees, and on the Day of Resurrection they will be for you like the reward of ten freed slaves. You say: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise, and He has no partner.'\""],[3972,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me and be brief.' He said, 'When you stand for your prayer, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell. Do not speak a word for which you will have to apologize. And renounce hope for what people possess.'"],[3974,"The Prophet said: \"The five daily prayers, from one Friday to the next, and fulfilling the trust are all expiation for whatever (sins) come between them.\" I said: \"What is fulfilling the trust?\" He said: Having a bath to cleanse oneself from sexual impurity, for under every hair there is the state of sexual impurity.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 598)"],[3975,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while al-Hasan and al-Husayn ؓ were playing in front of him and in his lap. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you love them?' He said, 'How could I not love them? They are my two fragrant flowers of this world whom I smell.'"],[3982,"A man may have from his wife anything except intercourse, meaning while she is menstruating. He said, 'They may spend the night under one cover,' meaning the menstruating woman, if there is a cloth over the private part."],[3984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not weep over the religion when its people are put in charge of it, but weep over it when other than its people are put in charge of it.\""],[4014,"“Will you not listen to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought of good?” They said, “And how much good has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought?” He said: “Who can recite a third of the Qur’an in a night?” We feared it, so we remained silent. He repeated it to us three times, then said: “Whoever recites Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad, it is as if it equals a third of the Qur’an.”"],[4024,"I saw Abū Ayyūb remove his leather socks, and people looked at him. He said: “Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over them, but ablution has been made beloved to me.”"],[4030,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever dies without associating anything with God will enter Paradise.”"],[4031,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, \"Did you not know that Allah looked at the people of the earth and chose your father, so He sent him as a prophet? Then He looked again and chose your husband, so I received revelation and married him, and took him as my successor?\""],[4033,"The Prophet ﷺ was going between Safa and Marwa when a feather fell onto his beard. Abu Ayyub hastened to him and removed it from his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “May God keep away from you what you dislike.”"],[4034,"We came to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari while he was feeding horses of his in Sa'naba. We asked him: O Abu Ayyub, you fought the polytheists with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and now you have come to fight the Muslims? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to fight three groups: the oath-breakers, the deviators, and the renegades. I have fought the oath-breakers and fought the deviators, and I shall fight, if God wills, the renegades at the passes, the paths, and the Nahrawan areas. And I do not know who they are."],[4035,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The angel has a station with me that none of you has, and I dislike that he should find any odor from me.”"],[4038,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ when a group of riders from the Ansar came wearing turbans and said: Peace be upon you, O our master. Ali ؓ said: I am your master, and are you Arab people? They said: Yes, we heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever has me as his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.” And this is Abu Ayyub among us. Abu Ayyub uncovered his face from the turban and said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever has me as his master, Ali is his master. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.”"],[4039,"He brought the Messenger of God ﷺ a beef broth containing garlic, and the Messenger of God ﷺ detected the smell of garlic and said: “Take it away.” He said: Why, O Messenger of God? Is it forbidden? He said: “No, but Gabriel is conversing with me.”"],[4060,"An Arab came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I love horses. Are there horses in Paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"When you enter Paradise, you will be brought a horse made of ruby with wings. You will be carried on it and you will fly in Paradise wherever you wish.\""],[4061,"Whenever our food was ready, we would send for Abu Ayyub and the people of his ship. Abu Ayyub came and said, \"You invited me while I was fasting, but it was my duty to answer you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'A Muslim has six obligatory rights over his fellow Muslim. Whoever abandons one of them has abandoned an obligatory right owed to his brother: to answer him when he calls him, to greet him when he meets him, to respond to his sneeze, to visit him when he falls ill, to follow his funeral procession when he dies, and to give him sincere counsel when he seeks his advice.'\" My father said: There was among us a man who was a joker, and a man was in charge of our expenses. The joker would say to the one in charge of the food, \"May God reward you with good and righteousness.\" When he repeated that many times, the man began to get angry and insult him. The joker said, \"O Abu Ayyub, what do you think of a man who, when I say to him, 'May God reward you with good and righteousness,' gets angry and insults me?\" Abu Ayyub said, \"We used to say: Whoever good does not reform, evil will reform.\" So it was turned around for him. When the man came, the joker said to him, \"May God reward you with evil and hardship.\" The man laughed and was pleased, and he said, \"You never abandon your nonsense in any state.\" The joker said, \"May God reward Abu Ayyub with good and righteousness, for he told me.\""],[4067,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate or drank, he said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has given food and drink and made it easy to swallow, and provided an exit for it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3851)"],[4068,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"My community will remain in good—or upon the natural disposition—as long as they do not delay the Maghrib prayer until the stars become dense.\""],[4069,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed this prayer—meaning the 'Asr—was made obligatory upon those before you, but they neglected it. So whoever among you today guards it will be given its reward twice, and there is no prayer after it until the witness appears, meaning the star.\""],[4070,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Four are from the practices of the Messengers: modesty, applying perfume, marriage, and the tooth-stick.\""],[4071,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the news of the sky. He said, 'You ask me about the news of the sky while you leave your nails like the claws of birds, in which filth and dirt accumulate.'"],[4075,"I prepared for the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr enough food for the two of them, and I brought it to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Go and invite thirty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' That was hard for me. I said, 'I have nothing to add.' It was as if I pretended not to hear. He said, 'Go and invite thirty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' So I invited them and they came. He said, 'Eat.' They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said, 'Go and invite sixty of the notables of the Ansar for me.' Abu Ayyub said, 'By Allah, I am more generous with sixty than with thirty.' He said, 'So I invited them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stay.\" They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said, \"Go and invite ninety of the Ansar for me.\" He said, 'I am more generous with ninety and sixty than with thirty.' He said, 'So I invited them. They ate until they were satisfied. Then they bore witness that he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. One hundred and eighty men, all of them from the Ansar, ate from that food of mine.'"],[4076,"The Ansar cast lots for their dwellings to see which of them would host the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The lot fell to Abu Ayyub, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed at his house. When food was given as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would eat some of it, then send it to us."],[4077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten things: whoever says them at the end of his prayers, when he has prayed, \"There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things,\" Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, raises him ten degrees, and they are equivalent to ten slaves, and they are a protection for him from Satan until evening. And whoever says them in the evening, the same applies until morning.'"],[4078,"He said, while he was in the land of the Romans: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever says in the morning: \"There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things,\" ten times, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and they are equivalent to ten slaves, and Allah protects him from Satan. And whoever says it in the evening, the same applies.'"],[4079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever meets the enemy and remains patient until he is killed or prevails will not be tried in his grave.'"],[4104,"Khālid—then he perished."],[4107,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, the people most severe in punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those most severe in punishment in this world.” Then he said, “Go and let them go.”"],[4108,"I saw Khalid b. al-Hawari, a man from Abyssinia among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. He came to his family, and when he finished, death came upon him, so he said: “Wash me with two washings: one washing for janāba and one washing for death.”"],[4109,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever receives good from his brother without asking or expecting it, let him accept it and not reject it, for it is only provision that Allah has driven to him.”"],[4110,"From his father, “regarding the naming” of those who witnessed with ʿAlī from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Khālid b. Abī Dujāna ؓ."],[4112,"That he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the eastern part of Thaqīf while he was standing on a bow or a staff when he came to them seeking victory. He said: “I heard him reciting ‘By the sky and the night comer’ until he completed it.” He said: “I memorized it in the Jāhiliyya while I was a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam. They said, ‘What did you hear from this man?’ So I recited it to them, and those of Quraysh who were with them said, ‘We know our companion better. If we knew that what he says is true, we would have followed him.’”"],[4114,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has given you at your death one-third of your wealth as an increase in your deeds.”"],[4115,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Saḥbal b. Muḥammad b. Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us (ḥ), and al-Ḥusayn al-Tustarī narrated to us, ʿAmr b. Hishām Abū Umayya al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from Saḥbal b. Muḥammad al-Madanī from Khālid b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥarmala al-Mudlijī who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at ʿUsfān, and a man said, “Would you like some of the noblest women and the best camels of Banū Mudlij?” Among the people was a man from Banū Mudlij, and that was recognized on his face. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of people is the one who defends his people as long as he does not sin.”"],[4119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sows a crop and a bird or a passerby eats from it, it will be charity for him.”"],[4122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: Allah the Exalted has given you an extra prayer which is better for you then the red camels (i.e. high breed camels). This is the witr which Allah has appointed for you between the night prayer and the daybreak. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1418)"],[4123,"And it is said: Rather, it was revealed about Kharija b. Zayd Abu Zuhayr, the brother of Balharith b. al-Khazraj."],[4124,"I heard a clamor, and I turned away, and there he was moving. He said: \"The most excellent of the people is their middle one: 'Abd Allah 'Umar, Commander of the Faithful, strong in body, strong in the command of God ﷻ. 'Uthman b. 'Affan, Commander of the Faithful, the chaste, the self-restrained, who pardons many sins. Two nights came and four remained. The people differed and had no order. O people, turn to your leader, listen to him, and obey. This is the Messenger of God ﷺ and Ibn Rawaha.\" Then he said: \"What happened to Zayd b. Kharija?\"—meaning his father—then he said: \"I took concubines wrongfully.\" Then the voice became faint."],[4125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest, while I was at his camel's side: \"No bequest to an heir. God ﷻ has given every possessor of a right his right. For the fornicator is the stone. Whoever claims descent from other than his father or takes as patrons other than his masters, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all people. God will accept from him neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4126,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Khawwat b. Jubayr is given the kunya Abu Salih.\""],[4127,"From his father: \"In the naming of those who were present with 'Ali ؓ: Khawwat b. Jubayr, a Badri from Banu Haritha. He turned back from the road, so the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted him a share.\""],[4128,"Khawwat b. Jubayr b. al-Nu'man b. Umayya b. al-Bark—and the name of al-Bark is Imru' al-Qays b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. 'Awf—the Messenger of God ﷺ allotted him on the Day of Badr his share and his reward."],[4129,"Khawwat b. Jubayr died in the year forty, and his age was seventy-four."],[4130,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Numayr say: \"Khawwat b. Jubayr died in the year forty.\""],[4131,"We encamped with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Marr al-Zahran. He said: I came out of my tent, and there I saw some women conversing. They pleased me, so I returned, took out my bag, and from it took out a fine garment and put it on. Then I came and sat with them. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out of his dome and said: \"Abu 'Abd Allah, what makes you sit with them?\" When I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, I was awed and confused. I said: \"O Messenger of God, a camel of mine has strayed, and I am looking for a hobble for it.\" He went on, and I followed him. He threw his cloak to me and entered the arak trees. It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his back against the greenness of the arak. He relieved himself, performed ablution, and came back while water was flowing from his beard onto his chest—or he said dripping from his beard onto his chest. He said: \"Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of your camel?\" Then we set off, and he would not catch up with me on the journey except to say: \"Peace be upon you, Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of that camel?\" When I saw that, I hurried to Madinah and avoided the mosque and sitting with the Prophet ﷺ. When that went on for a long time, I looked for a time when the mosque was empty, so I went to the mosque and stood praying. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out suddenly from one of his rooms and prayed two brief rak'as. I prolonged my prayer hoping he would leave and let me be. He said: \"Prolong as much as you wish, Abu 'Abd Allah, for I will not stand until you finish.\" I said to myself: By God, I will apologize to the Messenger of God ﷺ and clear his heart. When he said: \"Peace be upon you, Abu 'Abd Allah, what happened to the straying of that camel?\" I said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth, that camel has not strayed since I became a Muslim.\" He said: \"May God have mercy on you\" three times. Then he did not return to any of what had been."],[4132,"A man died and left a bequest to me. Among what he bequeathed were the mother of his child and a free woman. There occurred between the mother of the child and the woman some talk, and the woman said to her: \"You wretched one, tomorrow you will be taken by your ear and sold in the market.\" I mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"She will not be sold.\""],[4133,"I fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ visited me. When I recovered, he said: \"There is no sick person who falls ill except that he vows something and intends something good. So fulfill for God what you promised Him.\""],[4134,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large amounts, a small amount of it is unlawful.\""],[4135,"I was praying when a man behind me said: \"Make it light, for we have a need for you.\" I turned and there was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4136,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are of six kinds. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies as a Muslim, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and whoever dies as a disbeliever, the Fire becomes obligatory for him. Like for like: a servant intends a good deed, so a good deed is recorded for him; and he intends an evil deed but is not requited except with the like of it. The servant does a good deed, so ten are recorded for him. And the servant spends an expenditure in the path of God, so it is multiplied for him seven hundred times. And people are of four kinds: one given abundance in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; one given scarcity in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and scarcity in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[4137,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are of six kinds. Among them is one given abundance in this world and in the Hereafter; among them is one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; among them is one given restriction in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; and among them is one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies not associating anything with God enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating something with God enters the Fire. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him; and whoever does it, an evil deed is recorded against him. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is recorded for him; and if he does it, ten times are recorded for him. And an expenditure in the path of God, exalted is He, is seven hundred times.\""],[4138,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are six. The people are: one given abundance in this world and the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; one given restriction in this world and abundance in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. The deeds are: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times, and seven hundred times. The two that make obligatory: whoever dies as a Muslim or a believer not associating anything with God, Paradise becomes obligatory for him; and whoever dies as a disbeliever, the Fire becomes obligatory for him. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, but God knows that he has made his heart aware of it and was eager for it, a good deed is recorded for him and nothing is multiplied. Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not recorded against him; and whoever does it, one is recorded against him and nothing is multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, it is for him ten times the like of it; and whoever spends an expenditure in the path of God, it is for him seven hundred times.\""],[4140,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"People are of four kinds, and deeds are six. [Among people are:] one given abundance in this world and the Hereafter; one given abundance in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; one given restriction in this world and restriction in the Hereafter; and one given abundance in the Hereafter and restriction in this world. The deeds are six: two that make obligatory, like for like, ten times its like, and seven hundred times. Whoever dies as a Muslim or a believer not associating anything with God enters Paradise; and whoever dies as a disbeliever enters the Fire. Whoever intends a good deed until his heart is aware of it, a good deed is recorded for him and it is not multiplied. Whoever does an evil deed, one evil deed is recorded against him and it is not multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, ten times its like are recorded for him; and whoever spends an expenditure in the path of God, seven hundred times are recorded for him.\""],[4141,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What a man you would be were it not for two traits in you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, what are they?\" He said: \"You let your lower garment hang low and you let your hair grow long.\" I said: \"No doubt I will not go back.\" He said: \"So he cut his hair and raised his lower garment.\""],[4142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man: letting the lower garment hang low and letting the hair grow long.\""],[4143,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Excellent is the young man Khuraym, if only he would take from his hair and shorten his lower garment.\""],[4144,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"O Khuraym b. Fātik, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man.\" He said: \"What are they, may my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God? Is one enough for me?\" He said: \"Letting your hair grow long and letting your lower garment hang low.\" So Khuraym went off and cut his hair and shortened his lower garment."],[4146,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Excellent is the young man Khuraym, if only he would shorten from his hair and raise from his lower garment.\" Khuraym said: \"My hair will not pass my ears and my lower garment will not pass my ankles.\""],[4147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the morning prayer, and when he finished, he said while standing: \"False testimony has equated with associating partners with God\" three times, then he recited this verse: {And avoid the word of falsehood, being upright for God, not associating partners with Him}."],[4148,"From Khuraym b. Fātik al-Asadī, a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The people of Syria are God's whip on His earth; He takes vengeance through them upon whomever He wills of His servants. It is forbidden for their hypocrites to prevail over their believers, and they will die only in grief and sorrow.”"],[4149,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There will be a tribulation in which the one sleeping is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one striving, and the one striving is better than the one riding.”"],[4154,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood in one of the prayers, and when he raised his head from bowing he said: “O God, curse Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God and His Messenger. Ghifār—may God forgive them—and Aslam—may God grant them peace.”"],[4157,"He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said during a prayer: “O God, curse Banū Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God. Ghifār—may God forgive them—and Aslam—may God grant them peace.”"],[4158,"The Prophet ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer. When he raised his head from the last rakʿa he said: “God curse Liḥyān, Riʿl, Dhakwān, and ʿUṣayya who disobeyed God and His Messenger. Aslam—may God grant them peace—and Ghifār—may God forgive them.” Then he fell down in prostration. When he finished the prayer he turned his face to the people and said: “O people, it was not I who said this; rather God, exalted be He, said it.”"],[4159,"Khafāf b. Īmāʾ: The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, then raised his head and said: “Ghifār—may God forgive them—Aslam—may God grant them peace—and ʿUṣayya disobeyed God and His Messenger. O God, curse Banū Liḥyān, Riʿl, and Dhakwān.” Then he went down into prostration. Khafāf said: On account of that, the curse of the disbelievers was made to fall."],[4160,"The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed—ḥ—and ʿUbayd b. Ghannām narrated to us: Abū Bakr b. Abī Shayba narrated to us—ḥ—and al-Ḥusayn b. Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUthmān b. Abī Shayba narrated to us: They both said: Muḥammad b. Bishr narrated to us: Muḥammad b. ʿAmr narrated to us: Khālid b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥarmala narrated to us, from al-Ḥārith b. Khafāf b. Īmāʾ, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, then raised his head and said: “Ghifār—may God forgive them—Aslam—may God grant them peace—and ʿUṣayya disobeyed God and His Messenger. O God, curse Banū Liḥyān. O God, curse Riʿl and Dhakwān. God is greatest.” Then he fell down in prostration."],[4161,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he sat at the end of his prayer, would point with his index finger. The polytheists used to say that he was casting a spell with it—they lied—but it is tawḥīd."],[4162,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with my son, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not commit a crime against him, and he will not commit a crime against you.”"],[4163,"On the authority of his father: “In naming those who witnessed with ‘Ali ؓ from the Ansar: Khalifa b. ‘Adi from Banu Bayada, a Badri.”"],[4164,"On the authority of ‘Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi‘, the two sons of Yazid b. Jariya, they said: “Khidam married off his daughter, while she was unwilling, to a man, and she was a thayyib. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, so he annulled her marriage.”"],[4165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be trials in which the one sleeping is better than the one awake, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening. Lo, whoever it comes upon, let him strike his sword against the rock until it breaks, then lie down until it clears from what it cleared.”"],[4166,"On the authority of Kharasha b. al-Haritha, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Let none of you witness a person killed in retaliation, for perhaps he may be killed unjustly, and wrath will descend upon them and afflict him along with them.”"],[4167,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said the salam after three rak‘ahs in the ‘Asr prayer, then entered. A man called al-Khirbaq, who had long arms, stood up to him and said, “Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of God?” He came out angry, dragging his cloak, and said, “He spoke the truth?” They said, “Yes.” So he stood and prayed that rak‘ah."],[4168,"“Abu Salama al-Sulami stayed with us, and we hosted him for two months.”"],[4169,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if he has harm that hurts him.”"],[4170,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if he may suffer harm from him that hurts him.”"],[4171,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his patron who takes charge of him, even if there may be harm in it that hurts him.”"],[4173,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, while the Prophet ﷺ looked at the Angel of Death ﷺ at the head of a man from the Ansar: “O Angel of Death, be gentle with my companion, for he is a believer.” The Angel of Death ﷺ said: “Be of good heart and cool of eye, and know that I am gentle with every believer. And know, O Muhammad, that I seize the soul of the son of Adam, and when a crier from his family cries out, I stand in the house with his soul and say, ‘What is this crier? By God, we have not wronged him, nor have we preceded his term, nor have we hastened his decree. We have no sin in seizing him. If you are content with what God has done, you will be rewarded; but if you grieve and are displeased, you will sin and be burdened. You have no claim against us, and we still have a return to you, and then another return, so beware. There is no household, O Muhammad, of hair or clay, land or sea, plain or mountain, but I examine them every day and night, until I know their young and old better than they know themselves. By God, O Muhammad, if I wanted to seize the soul of a mosquito, I could not do so until God Himself permits its seizure.’” Ja‘far said: “It has reached me that he examines them only at the times of prayer. When he looks at the time of death, whoever was diligent in the prayers, the angel draws near to him, drives away Satan from him, and prompts him with ‘There is no god but God; Muhammad is the Messenger of God.’ And that is the tremendous state.”"],[4174,"“The Prophet ﷺ commanded the cutting of bells.”"],[4175,"He narrated to me that a traveling group from Mudar passed by and in it was a bell, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “The angels do not approach a traveling group in which there is a bell.”"],[4176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a detachment as spies for him and appointed over them 'Asim b. Thabit, who was the grandfather of 'Asim b. 'Umar. They set out until when they were in part of the way between 'Usfan and Makkah and stopped at a place, they were reported to a tribe of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. They pursued them with nearly a hundred archers, tracking their traces until they reached a stopping place where they found a date-stone from dates they had taken as provision from the dates of Madinah. They said, 'This is from the dates of Yathrib,' and followed their traces until they caught up with them. When 'Asim b. Thabit and his companions sensed them, they took refuge on a hillock. The people came and surrounded them and said, 'You have a covenant and a pledge that if you come down to us, we will not kill any man of you.' 'Asim b. Thabit said, 'As for me, I will not descend under the protection of an unbeliever. O Allah, inform Your Messenger about us.' So they fought them, and they shot them until they killed 'Asim among seven men. Khubayb b. 'Adi and Zayd b. Dathina remained until they sold them in Makkah. Banu al-Harith b. 'Amir b. Nawfal bought Khubayb, and al-Harith had been killed on the day of Badr. He remained with them as a prisoner until they resolved to kill him. He borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Harith, and she lent it to him to shave his pubic hair. She said: 'I became heedless of a little child of mine, who crawled to him until he reached him. He took him and placed him on his thigh. When she saw him, she became terrified with a fright that he recognized in her, while the razor was in his hand. He said, \"Do you fear that I will kill him? I would not do that, if Allah wills.\"' She used to say, 'I have not seen a prisoner better than Khubayb. I saw him eating from a bunch of grapes, and there was no fruit in Makkah that day, while he was bound in iron. It was nothing but provision that Allah provided him.' Then they took him out of the sanctuary to kill him. He said, 'Let me pray two rak'ahs.' So he prayed two rak'ahs, then said, 'Were it not that you would think that what is in me is fear of death, I would have increased.' He was the first to institute the two rak'ahs at the time of killing. Then he said, 'O Allah, count them by number,' then he said..."],[4178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me alone as a spy to Quraysh. He said: I came to the wood of Khubayb while I was wary of being seen, and I climbed up it and untied Khubayb. He fell to the ground, and I withdrew not far. Then Khubayb seemed as if the earth had swallowed him, and Khubayb has not been seen until now. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba said: Ja'far b. 'Awn had narrated from Ja'far b. 'Amr b. Umayya, from his father, from his grandfather."],[4179,"The Prophet ﷺ went out seeking a face, so I and another man from my people went with him. We said, \"We dislike that our people witness something that we do not witness with them.\" He asked, \"Have you both embraced Islam?\" We replied, \"No.\" He said, \"Then we do not seek assistance from pagans.\" We both embraced Islam and witnessed with him. Afterward, a man from the pagans struck me on my shoulder, so I killed him. Then I married his daughter, and she used to say, \"May you never be deprived of a man who wears this turban!\", and I used to reply, \"May you never be deprived of a man who made your father hasten towards Hell.\""],[4180,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and a man from my people, before we had embraced Islam, and we said: 'We feel ashamed that our people should witness a scene that we do not witness with them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Have you embraced Islam?' We said: 'No.' He said: 'I do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists.' So we embraced Islam and witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[4181,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I do not seek help from a polytheist.”"],[4182,"“By Allah, today I have seen a matter that I did not think I would see: a people who turned away from the guidance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions.” He said that about those who fasted, then he said at that: “O Allah, take me to You.”"],[4183,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to Caesar, the ruler of the Romans, with a letter. I said, 'Ask permission for the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' It was told to Caesar, 'There is a man at the door who claims that he is the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They were alarmed at that. He said, 'Let him enter.' So he admitted me to him, and with him were his patricians. I gave him the letter, and it was read to him. In it was: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Caesar, the ruler of the Romans.' A nephew of his, ruddy, blue-eyed, and lank-haired, snorted and said, 'Do not read the letter today. He began with himself and wrote \"ruler of the Romans\" and did not write \"king of the Romans.\"' He said: The letter was read until they finished, then he ordered them and they left his presence. Then he sent for me, so I entered upon him. He asked me and I informed him. He sent for the bishop, and he entered upon him; he was the one in charge of their affairs, and they acted according to his opinion and his word. When he read the letter, the bishop said, 'By Allah, he is the one whom Moses and Jesus gave us glad tidings of, the one we have been waiting for.' Caesar said, 'What do you command me?' He said, 'As for me, I believe in him and follow him.' Caesar said, 'I know that it is so, but I cannot do it. If I do, my kingdom will be gone and the Romans will kill me.'"],[4184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took some fine Egyptian linen (qibati) and gave me a qibtiyyah garment, saying: \"Tear it into two pieces and cut one of them into a shirt, and give the other to your wife to cover her head with.\" When I turned away, he said: \"Tell your wife to put under that torn piece another cloth so that it does not describe her.\""],[4185,"“A woolen jubba and two leather socks were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he wore them until they were worn out, and he did not ask about them whether they had been properly slaughtered or not.”"],[4186,"Mu'awiya ؓ sent to Daghfal and asked him about Arabic, about the genealogies of people, and about the stars, and he found him a scholar. He said, 'O Daghfal, from where did you memorize this?' He said, 'I memorized this with an inquiring tongue and a comprehending heart, and the bane of knowledge is forgetfulness.' He said, 'Then go with Yazid and teach him Arabic, the genealogies of Quraysh, and the stars.'"],[4187,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five years.”"],[4188,"The Christians were required to fast the month of Ramadan. A king ruled over them and fell ill, so he said, 'If Allah heals him, he will increase by ten.' Then another king ruled after him and ate meat, and it caused him pain, so he said, 'If Allah heals him, he will increase by eight days.' Then another king ruled after him and said, 'We will not leave any of these days but we will complete them and make our fasting in the spring.' So he did, and it became fifty days."],[4189,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land and we drink a beverage to gain strength from it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Does it intoxicate?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then do not approach it.\" Then he repeated the question to him, and he ﷺ said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Do not approach it.\" He said: They will not be able to abstain from it. He said: \"Whoever does not abstain from it, then kill him.\""],[4190,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, a drink made from this wheat that we use to gain strength for our work and against the cold of our land. He said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then avoid it.\" Then I came to him from in front of him and said the same thing to him. He said: \"Does it intoxicate?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then avoid it.\" I said: The people will not leave it. He said: \"If they do not leave it, then kill them.\""],[4191,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a cold land, intensely cold, where we make a drink from wheat. Is drinking it lawful? He said: \"Does it intoxicate you?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then it is khamr.\""],[4192,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as four hundred riders asking him for food. He said: \"O Umar, go and feed them and give them.\" Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I have only a few measures of dates, which my family subsists on. Abu Bakr ؓ said: Hear and obey. Umar ؓ said: Hearing and obedience. Umar went until he came to an upper room, took out a key from his waistband, opened it, and said to the people: Enter. They entered, and I was the last of the people to enter, so I delayed. Then I turned and found the like of a weaned camel of dates."],[4196,"That a dirham came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I have come to ask you for a ruling about going on military expeditions. He said: \"Do you have a mother?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Then stay with her.\""],[4197,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a sacrificial camel with him and said: \"If any of it becomes defective and you fear it will die, then slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it. Do not eat from it yourself, nor anyone of your traveling companions, and distribute it.\""],[4198,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send sacrificial camels with him and then say: \"If any of it becomes defective and you fear it will die, then slaughter it, then dip its sandal in its blood, then strike its side with it. Do not eat from it yourself, nor anyone of your traveling companions, and distribute it.\" The wording is from the hadith of Yazid b. Zuray', and Khalid b. al-Harith said: Dhu'ayb b. Qabisa."],[4199,"That when the Prophet ﷺ was dying, Safiyya said: O Messenger of Allah, every woman among your wives has family to whom she can turn, and you have expelled my family. If something happens, to whom should I turn? He said: \"To Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ.\""],[4200,"That the delegation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Umm Zubayb and took her carpet. Zubayb caught up with the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, the delegation took my mother's carpet. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Return his mother's carpet to him.\" So he took from the one who took his mother's carpet a measure of barley, his sword, and his belt. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and wiped Zubayb's head with it, then said: \"May Allah bless you, O boy, and bless your mother.\" Musa b. Harun said: The carpet (zirbiyya) is a covering heavier than a ziliyya. Allah ﷻ said: {And rich carpets spread out} (Q 88:16), meaning spread out."],[4201,"O Prophet of Allah, I want a freed slave from the descendants of Ishmael ﷺ, deliberately. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Wait until the spoil from al-Anbar comes tomorrow.\" The spoil from al-Anbar came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take from among them four young boys, fair and handsome, whose heads are not hidden.\" Ata' b. Khalid said: I took my grandfather Rudayh, I took my paternal cousin Samura, I took my paternal cousin Rakhya, and I took my maternal uncle Zabib. Then the Prophet ﷺ raised his hand and wiped their heads with it and blessed them, then said: \"These, O Aisha, are from the descendants of Ishmael, deliberately.\""],[4202,"Something was entrusted to me for the Banu Hashim, so I came to Abu Ja'far in Madinah. He sent me to a woman among them, a daughter of Ali, a very old woman. He said: The mawla of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Tahman or Dhakwan narrated to me, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sadaqah is not lawful for me nor for my household. The mawla of a people is one of them.\""],[4203,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended the Second pledge at al-Aqaba from the Ansar, then from the Banu Zurayq: Dhakwan b. Abd Qays b. Khalda.\""],[4204,"From Urwa: \"In the naming of those who attended al-ʿAqaba from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays b. Khalada. He had left Madinah for Makkah as an emigrant to Allah, and he witnessed Badr.\""],[4205,"From Urwa: \"In the naming of those who were martyred with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uḥud, from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays.\""],[4206,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud, from the Anṣār, then from Banū Zurayq: Dhakwān b. ʿAbd Qays.\""],[4207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be four armies, so upon you is Syria, for Allah, Exalted is He, has guaranteed Syria for me.\""],[4208,"ʿAmmār: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, three of us, all of us were aḍbaṭ.\" It was said to Abū Shayba: \"What is al-aḍbaṭ?\" He said: \"The one who works with both his hands: Dhū al-Shimālayn, ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb, and Abū Laylā.\""],[4209,"From his father Muṭīr, and Muṭayr was present, confirming his statement. He said: \"How did I inform you?\" He said: \"O father, you informed me that Dhū al-Yadayn met you at Dhū Khashab and told you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in one of the two evening prayers, which was ʿAṣr, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then gave the salutation. The swift among the people left, saying, 'The prayer has been shortened.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, may Allah have mercy on them both, followed him. Then Dhū al-Yadayn caught up with him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget?' He said, 'The prayer has not been shortened, nor did I forget.' Then he turned to Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ and said, 'What is Dhū al-Yadayn saying?' They said, 'He has spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and the people came back, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then gave the salutation, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[4211,"I was with al-Ḥasan when a man passed by him and spoke to him. He said: Dhū al-Yadayn said: \"O assembly of the Anṣār, did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you to be patient until you meet him?\""],[4212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This affair was in Ḥimyar, then Allah took it from them and put it in Quraysh.\""],[4213,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a raid. They traveled at night for a while, then they stopped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said: \"O Dhū Makhmar.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.\" He took hold of the head of my she-camel and said: \"Sit here and do not be a lukaʿ tonight.\" So I took hold of the she-camel's head, but my eyes overcame me and I slept. The she-camel slipped away and went off, and I did not wake up except with the heat of the sun. The Prophet ﷺ came to me and said: \"O Dhū Makhmar.\" I said: \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.\" He said: \"By Allah, last night you were a lukaʿ as I said.\" So we moved away from that place, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us. When he finished the prayer, he supplicated that the she-camel be brought back, and a whirlwind came driving her. The next day, when dawn broke, he ordered Bilāl, so he gave the call to prayer, then he ordered him, so he gave the iqāmah, then he prayed with us. When he finished the prayer, he said: \"This is our prayer from yesterday.\" Then he started the prayer of that day afresh.\""],[4214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will make peace with the Byzantines, a secure peace, until you and they raid a common enemy, and you will be victorious. Then you will encamp in a meadow with hills.\""],[4215,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will soon make peace with the Byzantines, a secure peace. Then you and they will raid a common enemy, and you will be victorious, take spoils, and be safe. Then you will depart until you encamp in a meadow with hills. A man from among the Christians will raise a cross and say, 'The cross has prevailed.' A Muslim man will become angry, rise to it, and smash it. At that point, the Byzantines will act treacherously and gather for the great battle.\""],[4216,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will make peace with the Byzantines for ten years, a secure peace. They will fulfill two years and break the treaty in the third, or fulfill four and break it in the fifth. Then an army of you will encamp in their city, and you and they will raid an enemy behind you and behind them. You will fight that enemy and Allah will grant you victory, and you will depart with the reward and spoils you have gained. Then you will encamp in a meadow with hills. One of your men will say, 'Allah has prevailed,' and one of their men will say, 'The cross has prevailed,' and they will go back and forth over it. The Muslims will become angry, and their cross will be not far from them. That Muslim will rise to their cross and smash it, and they will come out against the breaker of their cross and strike his neck. Then that band of Muslims will rise to their weapons, and the Byzantines will rise to their weapons, and they will kill that band of Muslims, who will be martyred. Then they will go to their king and say, 'We have spared you the might and strength of the Arabs, so what are we waiting for?' He will gather for you an army the size of a woman's pregnancy, and then they will come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.\""],[4219,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ looked upon the people of Madinah when it was a wide, gravelly plain before it was built up, with no clod of earth or soft grassy place in it, and He said: 'O people of Yathrib, I lay upon you three conditions and will drive to you fruits of every kind: do not disobey, do not become exorbitant in prices, and do not wax arrogant. If you do any of that, I will leave you like a slaughtered camel that no one prevents from being eaten.'\""],[4220,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"Do we act in a matter newly begun or in a matter already decreed?\" He said: \"Rather in a matter already decreed.\" He said: \"Then what is the point of action?\" He said: \"Act, for each is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[4221,"That he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do we act in a matter newly begun or in a matter already decreed?\" He said: \"No, rather in a matter already decreed.\" He said: \"Then what is the point of action?\" He said: \"Act, for each is facilitated toward what he was created for.\""],[4222,"That he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if we are tested with remaining after you, what do you command us?\" He said: \"You must keep to the House of the Holy, perhaps Allah will provide you with offspring who go there in the morning and return in the evening.\""],[4223,"We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if we are tested after you with remaining, where do you command us?\" He said: \"You must keep to the House of the Holy, for perhaps offspring will arise for you who go to that mosque in the morning and return in the evening.\""],[4224,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, commanding the people and forbidding them, then he said: \"Have I conveyed?\" They said: \"O Allah, yes.\" He said: \"O Allah, bear witness.\" Then he said: \"Take the stipend as long as it is fresh. But when Quraysh violently wrest the kingship among themselves and the stipend becomes bribery for your religion, then leave it.\""],[4225,"I saw Rafi' b. Khadij dyeing with yellow."],[4226,"He went out on the day of Uhud, and the Prophet ﷺ intended to send him back, but he insisted on going. His uncle said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, my nephew insists on going, and he is young.\" So he allowed him to go. He was then struck by an arrow in his chest or neck. He came to his uncle, the Prophet ﷺ , and said, \"My son has been struck by an arrow.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If you leave it in him, he will die as a martyr.\" Abdullah bin Hussein said, \"His wife told me that she used to see him showering and moving in his chest.\""],[4227,"\"That Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj was hit by an arrow alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud or the day of Khaybar. ʿUmar doubted it, so he went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, remove the arrow.' He ﷺ replied, 'O Rāfiʿ, if you want, I will remove the arrow along with its barbs. And if you want, I will remove the arrow and leave the barbs, and I will testify for you on the Day of Judgment that you are a martyr.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed the arrow and left the barbs, and Rāfiʿ lived with them until the time of the Caliphate of Muʿāwiyah. Then the wound burst open, and he died after ʿAṣr prayer. Ibn ʿUmar came, and it was said to him, 'O Abā ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Rāfiʿ b. Khadīj has died.' He showed mercy and said, 'A person like Rāfiʿ should not be buried without informing the villages around Madīnah.' So when we carried his funeral, Ibn ʿUmar came and sat by the head of the grave. A woman from our party shouted, 'What does this crazy woman want, harming the old man?' Ibn ʿUmar replied, 'Surely, she should not harm the sheikh, for he does not deserve Allah's punishment.'\""],[4228,"I came with my paternal uncle to the Prophet ﷺ when he was heading to Badr. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I wish to go out with you.\" He began to take hold of my hand and say: \"I consider you too young, and I do not know what you will do when you meet the enemy.\" I said: \"Do I know how to shoot whoever shoots?\" So he sent me back."],[4229,"Indeed Rafi' b. Khadij is an old man who has no strength to endure the punishment of Allah."],[4230,"Rafi' b. Khadij died in the year seventy-three in Madinah."],[4231,"And in it Rafi' b. Khadij died at the beginning of this year, and Ibn Umar, may Allah have mercy on him, attended his funeral, meaning the year seventy-three, and Rafi' was eighty-six on the day he died."],[4232,"Rafi' b. Khadij died in the year seventy-four, at its beginning."],[4233,"I heard Rafi' b. Khadeej say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping (muzara'ah).\""],[4234,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prohibited it, and we abandoned it because of his statement.\""],[4235,"\"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ prohibited it.\""],[4236,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited it.\""],[4237,"Rafi' b. Khadeej: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us.\""],[4238,"Ibn 'Umar: \"Rafi' b. Khadeej certainly deprived us of the benefit of our land.\""],[4239,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prohibited leasing land.\""],[4240,"We did not see any harm in leasing land until Rafi' b. Khadeej narrated to us: \"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited leasing land.\""],[4259,"“The Prophet forbade the hire and purchase of non-Arabs.”"],[4357,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a matter that was lenient for us, but in the command of the Messenger of God ﷺ there is blessing and right guidance.” They said: What is that? He said: “Ḥaql.” I said to Usayd: What is ḥaql? He said: “Leasing land.” I said: How did they lease it? He said: “For quarters and for a portion of the harvest.”"],[4360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muḥāqalah, muzābanah, and munābadhah; he forbade a man saying to another man, \"Buy this for cash and buy it on credit,\" until he buys it and takes possession of it; and he forbade a deferred [payment] for a deferred [payment] and a debt for a debt."],[4363,"On the Day of the Trench, there was no fortress more fortified than the fortress of Banū Ḥārith, so the Prophet ﷺ placed the women, the boys, and the children in it and said, \"If anyone comes near you, flash your swords at them.\" Then a man from Banū Thaʿlabah b. Saʿd, called Bujdān, one of Banū Jaḥḥāsh, came to them on a horse until he reached the base of the fortress, then he began saying to the women, \"Come down to me; it is better for you.\" So they brandished the swords, and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw him. A group of people rushed to the fortress, among them a man from Banū Ḥārithah called Ẓuhayr b. Rāfiʿ, and he said, \"O Bujdān, come out!\" So he came out to him, and his horse charged at him and killed him, and he took his head and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[4402,"I came with al-Khatmi to the Prophet ﷺ when he was intending to go to Badr and said: 'O Messenger of God, I want to go out with you.' He began to clench his hand and said: 'I consider you too young, and I do not know what you will do when you meet the people.' I said: 'Do you know that I can shoot whoever shoots?' So he sent me back, and I did not witness Badr."],[4403,"He said to him: O my father, we have rented our land to so-and-so for two hundred dirhams. He said: My son, leave that aside, for Allah will provide you with a crop other than it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade renting out land."],[4404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The love that is inherited among the people of Islam.\""],[4413,"and from Rafi bin Khadij, the two of them said - :\"Abdullah bin Sahl bin Zaid and Muhayysah bin Mas'ud went out until when they reached Khaibar, they went their separate ways. Then Muhayysah found 'Abdullah bin Sahl slain, so he buried him. Then he came to the Mesenger of Allah, along with Huwayysah bin Mas'ud and 'Abdur-Rahman bin Sahl, who was the youngest of them, 'Abdur-Rahman started to speak before his two companions, but the Messenger of Allah said to him: \"Let the clear speak first.\" So he fell silent and his two companions spoke, then he spoke with them. They told the Messenger of Allah about the killing of 'Abdullah bin Sahl, and he said to them: \"Will you swear fifty oaths, then you will receive compensation, or be entitled to retaliate?\" They said: \"How can we swear an oath when we did not witness what happened?\" he said: \"Then can the Jews swear fifty oaths declaring their innocence?\" They said: \"How can we accept the oath of a disbelieving people?\" When the Messenger of Allah saw that, he paid the blood money (himself). (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4712)"],[4416,"Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of Banu Tamim, narrated to me from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Rafi' b. Khadij: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tie a thread on his ring to remind himself.\""],[4419,"Rijal b. Ghanmawayh had such an astonishing amount of humility, constancy in reciting the Quran, and goodness in what the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that it was a wonder. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while Rijal was sitting with us among a group. He said, «One of this group is in the Fire.» Rafiʿ said: I looked at the people, and there were Abu Hurayra al-Dawsi, Abu Arwa al-Dawsi, al-Tufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsi, and Rijal b. Ghanmawayh. I began to look and wonder, saying, \"Who is this wretched one?\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, Banu Hanifa apostatized and asked what Rijal b. Ghanmawayh had done. They said, \"He was tried. He is the one who testified to Musaylima against the Messenger of God ﷺ that he made him a partner in his affair after him.\" I said, \"What the Messenger of God ﷺ said is true.\" And Rijal was heard saying, \"Two rams butted heads; the more beloved of them to us is our ram.\""],[4420,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of Badr, «By Him in whose hand is my soul, if a newborn were born in the understanding of the people of religion for forty years, acting in complete obedience to God and avoiding all sins until he is returned to the most abject age or returned to knowing nothing after having knowledge, none of you would reach what they have reached this night.» And he said, «The angels who witnessed Badr have excellence over those who stayed behind among them.»"],[4428,"He cultivated a piece of land, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was watering it. He asked, «Whose is the crop and whose is the land?» He replied, \"My crop by my own hand and labor is from one half, and the land of Banu So-and-so is the other half.\" He said, «You have dealt in usury; return the land to its people and take your expenses.»"],[4429,"The Prophet ﷺ said: «People are a faction, and my Companions are a faction.» Zayd b. Thabit and Rafiʿ b. Khadij said: \"He has spoken the truth,\" while they were with Marwan b. al-Hakam."],[4430,"The Prophet ﷺ would not rise from a gathering until he said: «Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.» Then he would say: «It is an expiation for whatever occurred in the gathering.»"],[4433,"Rafi‘ b. Khadij said, “Our Prophet ﷺ forbade us—or the Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade—leasing land.”"],[4434,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on our mounts cloths with red threads, wide. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do I not see that red has overcome you?” He said, so we rose quickly at the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until some of our camels bolted. We took the cloths and pulled them off them."],[4435,"O you who are speaking, I see that you have spoken at length in Makkah and mentioned some of its virtue. What you omitted of its virtue is greater. But you did not mention Madinah, and I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Madinah is better than Makkah.”"],[4456,"And it is said: Rafi' b. Zayd."],[4457,"A slave belonged to Banu Sa'id, and they freed him except one of them. He came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his intercession with the man, and he spoke to him about him, so the man gave his share to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ freed him. He used to say: I am the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and his name was Rafi' Abu al-Bahi."],[4460,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr — then from Banū al-Najjār: Rāfiʿ b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād.”"],[4461,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr — then from Banū al-Aws, then from Banū ʿAmr b. ʿAwf, then from Banū Umayyah b. Zayd: Rāfiʿ b. ʿUnjudah.”"],[4546,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar: Rifa'ah b. Aws b. Za'ur b. 'Abd al-Ashhal.\""],[4549,"\"This verse was revealed concerning ten people, I being one of them.\" {And We have conveyed to them the Word} to the end of the verse."],[4564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “Ask me about whatever you wish.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?” He said, “Your father is so-and-so, the one to whom you are attributed.” Another man asked him, “Am I in Paradise?” He said, “In Paradise.” Another said, “Am I in Paradise?” He said, “In the Fire.” Umar ؓ stood up and said, “We are content with Allah as Lord.”"],[4566,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period at the market of Dhu al-Majaz saying, “O people, say there is no god but Allah and you will prosper.” He kept repeating it many times while people were lined up around him following him, and behind him was a cross-eyed man with two long locks of hair and a bright face, saying, “He is a renegade, a liar,” twice. I asked, “Who is this?” They said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4567,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going around among the people at Mina in their encampments before he emigrated to Madinah, saying, “O people, Allah ﷻ commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a man saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I asked, “Who is this man?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4568,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhu al-Majaz following the people, calling them to Allah in their encampments.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man saying, “Do not let this one tempt you away from the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4569,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhu al-Majaz following the people in their encampments, calling them to Allah ﷻ.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man saying, “O people, do not let this one deceive you away from your religion and the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4570,"He heard Rabi'ah b. 'Abbad al-Dili say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ going around among the people at Mina in their encampments before he emigrated to Madinah, saying, “O people, Allah has commanded you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a cross-eyed man with a bright face and two long locks of hair, saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I asked about him and it was said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4571,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the market of Dhu al-Majaz before he emigrated, going around among the people saying, “O people, Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.” Behind him was a man saying, “O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.” I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4572,"I saw Abu Lahab at 'Ukaz following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was saying, “O people, this one has gone astray, so do not let him lead you astray from the noble deeds of your forefathers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fleeing from him while he followed him."],[4573,"I was with my father, a young man, looking at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ following the tribes, and behind him was a cross-eyed man with a bright face and a full head of hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would stop at a tribe and say, “O Banu So-and-so, I am the Messenger of Allah to you, commanding you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and to believe me and protect me until I convey what Allah has sent me with.” When he finished his speech, the other man behind him would say, “O Banu So-and-so, this one wants you to cast off al-Lat and al-'Uzza and your allies from the tribe of Banu Malik b. Uqaysh, in favor of the innovation and misguidance he has brought. Do not listen to him and do not follow him.” I said to my father, “Who is this?” He said, “This is his uncle Abu Lahab.”"],[4574,"I saw Abu Lahab at 'Ukaz following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was saying, “O people, this one has gone astray, so do not let him lead you astray from the noble deeds of your forefathers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was hastening away with Abu Lahab on his tracks, and we were following them. It is as if I am looking at him: cross-eyed, with two long locks of hair, the fairest and most handsome of people."],[4575,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing in a place before he was sent as a Prophet, then I saw him after he was sent standing in that same place at 'Arafat.\""],[4576,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ standing with the polytheists at 'Arafat, then I saw him after he was sent standing at his station there, so I knew that God had guided him to that.\""],[4577,"A man from Banu Layth came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I implore you\"—he said it three times—then on the fourth he implored him with a eulogy for him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If any poet excels, you have excelled.\""],[4578,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Persist in invoking 'O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.'\""],[4579,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud among the Ansar, then from Banu Mu'awiyah b. 'Awf: Rabi'ah b. al-Fadl b. Habib b. Zayd b. Tamim.\""],[4580,"He heard Rabi'ah al-Jurashi say that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Remain upright, and excellent it is if you remain upright; maintain ablution, for the best of your deeds is prayer; and be wary of the earth, for it is your mother, and there is no one who acts upon it with good or evil but that it will report it.\""],[4581,"He heard Rabi'ah al-Jurashi say that the Prophet of God ﷺ was approached and it was said to him, \"Let your eye sleep, let your ear hear, and let your heart comprehend.\" He said, \"So my eye slept, my ear heard, and my heart comprehended.\" He said, it was said to him: \"A master built a house and prepared a banquet and sent an inviter. Whoever answers the inviter enters the house and eats from the banquet and the master is pleased with him. Whoever does not answer the inviter does not enter the house, does not attain the banquet, and the master is angry with him. The master is God, the inviter is Muhammad ﷺ, and the banquet is Paradise.\""],[4583,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the allies of Banu 'Abd Shams b. 'Abd Manaf: Rabi'ah b. Aktham from Banu Asad b. Khuzaymah.\""],[4584,"On the authority of Ibn Shihab, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Banu 'Abd Shams: Rabi'ah b. Aktham, an ally of theirs from Banu Asad.\""],[4585,"On the authority of 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those Muslims who were martyred on the day of Uhud, then from Quraysh: Rabi'ah b. Aktham, ally of Banu 'Abd Shams from Banu Asad.\""],[4586,"Rabi'ah b. Ruwa' al-'Ansi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him having supper, so he invited him to supper and he ate. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?\" Rabi'ah said, \"I testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said, \"Out of desire or fear?\" Rabi'ah said, \"As for desire, by God, it is not in your hand; as for fear, by God, I am in a land that your armies and cavalry do not reach us, but I was made to fear and so I feared, and I was told to believe and so I believed.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What an orator from 'Ans!\" He stayed, coming and going to the Prophet ﷺ, then came to bid him farewell. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"If you sense any danger, flee to the people of the town.\" He left, sensed danger, and fled to a town where he died."],[4587,"Rabi'ah b. Umayyah b. Khalaf al-Jumahi was the one who called out on the day of 'Arafah beneath the chest of the Messenger of God's ﷺ she-camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Call out\"—and he had a loud voice—\"O people, do you know which month this is?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, the sacred month.\" He said, \"Indeed God has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you until you meet your Lord, like the sanctity of this month of yours.\" Then he said, \"Call out: Do you know which land this is?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, the sacred land.\" He said, \"Indeed your blood and your wealth are sacred to you until the day you meet Him, like the sanctity of this land of yours.\" Then he said, \"Call out: Which day is this?\" He called out and they said, \"Yes, this is a sacred day, and this is the day of the greater pilgrimage.\" He said, \"Indeed God, exalted be He, has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you until the day you meet Him, like the sanctity of this day of yours.\""],[4588,"I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered for us two small flocks of camels and said, “Command your household to trim their nails so that they do not injure the udders of their livestock with them when they milk.”"],[4589,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr: Rāfiʿ b. Jaʿdabah.”"],[4590,"From Ibn Shihab: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Bilhubla: Rabi' b. Iyas.”"],[4591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited the son of Jabar al-Ansari's brother, and his family began weeping over him. Jabar said to them, “Do not annoy the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave them; let them weep as long as he is alive, and when death occurs, let them be silent.” Some of them said, “We never thought that your death would be on your bed until you were killed in the path of Allah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is martyrdom only in being killed in the path of Allah? The martyrs of my community would then be few. Indeed, plague and pestilence are martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, the woman who dies in childbirth with a child in her womb is martyrdom, burning is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, demolition is martyrdom, and pleurisy is martyrdom.”"],[4592,"He heard Rabi' b. Ziyad say: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, he saw a young man from Quraysh traveling apart. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is that not so-and-so?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Call him.” He came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “What is the matter with you that you have turned aside from the road?” He said, “I disliked the dust.” He said, “Do not turn aside from it, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is the perfume of Paradise.”"],[4593,"From his father: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed with 'Ali ؓ from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Rib'i b. 'Amr, a Badri.”"],[4594,"From his father: “Regarding the naming of those who witnessed with 'Ali ؓ: Rib'i b. Rafi', from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, a Badri.”"],[4595,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended the ‘Aqabah: Rafi‘ b. Malik al-Zuraqi.”"],[4596,"He divorced his wife irrevocably, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him. He said to him, “What did you intend?” He said, “One.” He said, “By Allah?” He said, “By Allah.” He said, “It is what you intended.”"],[4597,"He divorced his wife irrevocably, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned it to him. He said to him, “What did you intend by it?” He said, “One.” He said, “By Allah, did you intend by it only one?” He said, “By Allah, I intended by it only one.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “It is one.”"],[4598,"I met a man in Makkah from the people of 'Asqalan called Abu al-Hasan, and he narrated to me from Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. 'Ali, from Ibn Rukanah, from his father, that Rukanah wrestled with the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ threw him. Rukanah said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The difference between us and the polytheists is the turbans over the caps.”"],[4599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Blessed is one who is humble without deficiency, humbles himself without poverty, spends wealth he has gathered without disobedience, shows mercy to the poor and needy, and associates with people of understanding and wisdom. Blessed is one who humbles himself, makes his earning good, improves his inner self, and keeps his evil away from people. Blessed is one who acts upon his knowledge, spends the surplus of his wealth, and withholds the surplus of his speech.”"],[4600,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Blessed is he who humbles himself without deficiency and lowers himself in his own soul without destitution, and spends wealth he gathered without disobedience, and shows mercy to the people of humility and poverty, and mixes with the people of understanding and wisdom. Blessed is he whose earnings are pure, whose inner self is sound, whose outward conduct is honorable, and who keeps his evil away from people. Blessed is he who acts upon knowledge, spends the surplus of his wealth, and withholds the surplus of his speech.\""],[4601,"He informed him that he went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition he undertook, in which Khalid b. al-Walid was in command of the vanguard. Rabah and the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a woman who had been killed, one of those the vanguard had struck. They stopped at her, looking at her and marveling at her form, until the Messenger of God ﷺ caught up with them on a she-camel of his. They parted to make way for the woman. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he looked into the faces of the people and said to one of them: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid. He must not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4604,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, with Khalid b. al-Walid in command of the people's vanguard. There was a woman killed on the road, and they were marveling at her form; the vanguard had struck her. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and stood over her, then said to a man: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and say: He must not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4605,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition when the people were gathered around a woman who had been killed. He said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he said: \"Who is in command of the vanguard?\" They said: \"Khalid b. al-Walid.\" He sent a man to him and said: \"Command Khalid not to kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4606,"He informed him that he went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a military expedition, and the vanguard was under Khalid b. al-Walid. Rabah and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ passed by a slain woman whom the vanguard had killed. They gathered around her, looking at her and at her form, and marveling at her, until the Messenger of God ﷺ came and they parted. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at her and said: \"This woman was not one to fight.\" Then he looked into the faces of the people and said to one of them: \"Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and say: Do not kill any child or hired servant.\""],[4607,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he had given every three of us a camel, with two riding it and one driving it in the deserts, while we led it in the mountains. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me while I was walking, and said to me: \"I see you, O Rabah, walking.\" I said: \"I have just dismounted, and these two companions of mine have ridden.\" He went on and passed by my two companions, and they made their camel kneel and dismounted from it. When I caught up, they said: \"Ride the front of this camel, and remain on it until we return, and my companion and I will take turns.\" I said: \"Why?\" They said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You have a righteous companion, so be good to him.'\""],[4608,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"What has been born to you?\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, what could be born to me? Either a boy or a girl.\" He said: \"Whom will he resemble?\" He said: \"What could he resemble? Either his mother or his father.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Hush! Do not say that. When the drop settles in the womb, God ﷻ brings before it every lineage between it and Adam. Have you not read this verse in the Book of God ﷻ: 'In whatever form He willed, He assembled you'?\""],[4609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Egypt will be conquered, so seek the best of its pasture, but do not make it a dwelling, for the people with the shortest lifespans will be driven to it.\""],[4610,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a servant boy named Rabah.\""],[4611,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a servant boy named Rabah.\""],[4612,"From Urwa: \"In naming those killed on the day of al-Yamama from the Ansar: Rabah, the freedman of Banu Jahjaba.\""],[4613,"From Ibn Shihab in naming \"those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamama from the Ansar, then from the Aws, then from Banu Amr b. Awf: Rabah, the freedman of Banu Jahjaba.\""],[4614,"When Islam appeared, and we had a well at al-Danina, we feared that those around us would overpower us over it. He said: So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: He wrote for me a document: \"From Muhammad the Messenger of God ﷺ. To proceed: they have their well, if he was truthful.\" He said: We never brought a case regarding it to any of the judges of Madinah except that they judged in our favor. He said: In the Prophet's ﷺ document it was such-and-such, and he claimed that it was such-and-such, this was the Prophet's ﷺ document."],[4615,"I met a number of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, among those who were truthful was Ruqad b. Rabi'a. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ took from us from sheep: from a hundred, one ewe; and if they increased, then two ewes.\""],[4616,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man came to him with a plate on which were dates. He said to him: \"What is this? A gift or charity?\" The man said: Charity. He said: \"Present it to the people.\" He said: Hasan was in front of him, playing in the dirt. The boy took a date and put it in his mouth. The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed him, inserted his finger into the boy's mouth, extracted the date, then threw it away, and said: \"We, the family of Muhammad, do not eat charity.\""],[4617,"That he was with his grandfather when he went to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a boy, and found him with his buttons undone."],[4618,"From his father, who was from the people of Hajar and was a jurist, that he set out to the Messenger of God ﷺ in a delegation with some alms, and brought them to him. He forbade them from nabidh in these vessels, so they returned to their land, which is the land of Tihama, a hot land. They found it unhealthy, so they returned to him the second year with their alms. They said: O Messenger of God, you forbade us from these vessels, so we left them, and that was hard on us. He said: \"Go and drink whatever you wish, but do not drink what is tied in a skin that leads to sin.\""],[4619,"That the Prophet ﷺ wrote him a document on red leather, and he patched his bucket with it. The Messenger of God ﷺ was informed, and the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a raiding party. They did not leave him any grazing livestock, nor any going out to pasture, nor family, nor property, except that they took it. He escaped naked on a horse and came to his daughter, who was married among Banu Hilal. The people's sitting place was in the courtyard of her door. He entered upon her from behind the houses. She said: What is wrong with you? He said: Every evil has befallen your father; no grazing livestock, nor any going out to pasture, nor family, nor property was left to him except that it was taken. I said: She had been called to Islam, and she had already become Muslim. He said: So she threw a garment over him, and he went out. He said: Where is your husband? She said: In the camp. He came to him wearing a garment that, if his head was covered with it, his buttocks were exposed; and if his buttocks were covered, his head was exposed. He said: What do I see with you? He said: Every evil has befallen me. He repeated to him the same words he had said to his daughter. He said: I want Muhammad before he divides my property. He said: Take my riding camel. He said: I have no need of it, but give me the young camel. So he took it and went to the Prophet ﷺ. He came to him at the dawn prayer while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, he said: Stretch out your hands, I will pledge allegiance to you. The Messenger of God ﷺ stretched out his hand, but when he wanted to strike it, the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew it. He did that several times, then he turned to him and said: \"Who are you?\" He said: Ri'ya al-Suhaymi. The Prophet ﷺ took him by his upper arm and lifted him off the ground, then said: \"Here is Ri'ya al-Suhaymi; I wrote him a document and he patched his bucket with it.\" Ri'ya said: My property and my son? He said: \"As for your property, it is too late; it has already been divided. As for your son and your family, whoever you find among them.\" He said: He went away, then returned, and there was his son, who had been recognized. He came back to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: This is my son. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Bilal, go out with him; if he claims that he is his son, then hand him over to him.\" So he went out with him, and he said: This is my son, so he handed him over to him. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: He claimed that he was his son, and I did not see either of them shed a tear for the other. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is the harshness of the Bedouins.\""],[4620,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote him a document, and he patched his bucket with it. A raiding party of the Messenger of God ﷺ passed by him and drove away some camels of his, so he became Muslim. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"As for what you find of your property intact before it is divided, you have the most right to it.\""],[4621,"From 'Urwa: 'In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Mu'awiya b. al-Harith: Ruqaym b. Thabit b. Tha'laba.'"],[4622,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: 'In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of al-Ta'if from the Ansar, then from the Aws: Ruqaym b. Thabit b. Tha'laba b. Zayd b. Lawdhan b. Mu'awiya.'"],[4623,"From Ibn Shihab: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Bayada: Rukhayla b. Tha'laba b. Khalda.'"],[4624,"Some of them said to others: 'Kingship was among us, the people of Syria, and it is being transferred to the Hijaz; we are not pleased with that.'"],[4625,"From 'Urwa: 'In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraysh, from Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b: Zayd b. al-Khattab.'"],[4626,"It is said: Abū Thawr.”"],[4629,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade the killing of jinn.\""],[4631,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest of Makkah toward the graveyards. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down by a grave, and we saw him as if he were conversing privately. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up wiping tears from his eyes. ʿUmar, may God have mercy on him, met him—he was the first of us—and said: “With my father and mother as ransom for you, what makes you weep?” He said: “I asked my Lord, exalted be He, for permission to visit my mother’s grave. She was a mother, and she had a right over me that I ask forgiveness for her, but He forbade me.” Then he gestured to us to sit, so we sat. He said: “I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so whoever of you wishes to visit, let him visit. I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, so eat and store whatever you wish. I had forbidden you from certain vessels, and I have commanded you concerning vessels, so soak [in them], for vessels do not make anything lawful or unlawful, and avoid every intoxicant.”"],[4632,"From ʿUrwa: “Concerning the naming of those who witnessed Badr: Zayd b. Ḥāritha b. Sharāḥīl b. Kaʿb b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā b. Yazīd b. Imriʾ al-Qays al-Kalbī, upon whom God and His Messenger bestowed favor.”"],[4633,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws, then from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, then from Banu Umayyah b. Zayd: Abu Lubabah Bashir b. 'Abd al-Mundhir.\""],[4635,"Zayd b. Ḥāritha embraced Islam after ʿAlī ؓ and was the first to embrace Islam after him."],[4636,"The first to embrace Islam was Zayd b. Ḥāritha."],[4637,"From ʿUrwah: “In the naming of those from the Anṣār who attended Badr: Rāfiʿ b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād b. Zayd b. Thaʿlabah.”"],[4638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Muʾta in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year eight. He appointed Zayd b. Ḥāritha as commander and said to them: \"If Zayd is struck down, then Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib is over the people; and if Jaʿfar is struck down, then ʿAbdullāh b. Rawāḥa is over the people.\""],[4639,"Then the people went on until, when they were at the borders of al-Balqāʾ, the hosts of Heraclius met them. The Muslims withdrew to a village called Muʾta, and the people met there. The Muslims arrayed themselves and placed on their right wing a man from Banū ʿUdhra called Quṭba b. Qatāda, and on their left wing a man from the Anṣār called ʿAbāya b. Mālik. Then the people met, and Zayd b. Ḥāritha fought with the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he was pierced by the spears of the people."],[4640,"Jibrīl ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ at the first of what was revealed to him and taught him the ablution and the prayer. When he finished, the Prophet ﷺ took some water in his hand and sprinkled his private part with it."],[4641,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you made a bond of brotherhood between me and Ḥamza b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.\""],[4642,"O Messenger of Allah, you made a bond of brotherhood between me and Ḥamza."],[4643,"Ḥamza, the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was the brother of Zayd b. Ḥāritha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a bond of brotherhood between them."],[4644,"Zayd b. Ḥāritha said regarding the daughter of Ḥamza: \"She is the daughter of my brother; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a bond of brotherhood between me and her father.\""],[4645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give glad tidings to those who walk in the darkness to the mosques of a radiant light on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, with me riding behind him, to one of the stone altars. We slaughtered a sheep for him, then we cooked it in a fire pit. When it was done, we took it out into our traveling provision bag. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted his she-camel, with me riding behind him. When we reached the upper part of Makkah, he met Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl. One of them greeted the other with the greeting of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Why do I see that your people have come to dislike and hate you?\" He said: \"By Allah, that from them is not because of any wrong I did to them, except that I see them in error. So I went out seeking this religion until I came to the Jewish scholars of Khaybar. I found them worshiping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said: By Allah, this is not the religion I am seeking. So I went out until I came to the Jewish scholars of Syria. I found them worshiping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said: By Allah, this is not the religion I went out seeking. A rabbi among the Jewish scholars of Syria said: You are asking about a religion we know of no one who worships Allah by it except a certain person in the Peninsula. So I went out until I came to him and told him what I had gone out for. He said to me: Everyone you have seen is in error. You are asking about the religion of Allah and His angels. A prophet has appeared in your land, or is about to appear. Return, believe in him, and follow him. So I returned, and I have not tested any prophet since.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his she-camel kneel and placed the provision bag before him. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"A sheep we slaughtered for such-and-such a stone altar.\" Zayd b. ʿAmr said: \"We do not eat anything slaughtered for other than Allah.\" Then we parted. He said: Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl died before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent as a prophet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation unto himself.\""],[4648,"I circumambulated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and I touched one of the idols. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Do not touch it.\" I said: I will go back until I see what he says. Then I touched it. He said: \"Were you not forbidden from this?\" He said: By the One who honored him with the Book, he did not touch any idol among them until Allah honored him and sent down the Book upon him."],[4649,"I was a young boy during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let us go to a person whose situation we have seen.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went walking, and his companions with him, until they entered between two walls in a long alley. They stopped at a small door at the far end of the alley and entered a house. They saw no one in the house except a single woman, and there was a large water skin full of water. They said: We see a water skin but we do not see its carrier. Speak to the woman. She pointed to a velvet cloth in a corner of the house and said: Look under the velvet cloth. They uncovered it, and under it was a man. He raised his head, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Ugly is the face.\" He said: O Muhammad, why do you use obscene language against me? The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"I have hidden something for you. Tell me what it is?\" And he said to his companions: Indeed I have hidden for him Surat al-Dukhan. He said: \"Dukh.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Be off! What Allah wills happens.\" Then he left."],[4650,"\"I gave a horse of mine in charity. Then I saw its filly being sold in the market, and I wanted to buy it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about it.\""],[4651,"He had given a horse in the way of Allah. Then later he found it being sold in the market, tied up and emaciated. He bargained for it, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: I had given a horse in the way of Allah, and I found it being sold in the market for a small price, emaciated and tied up, and I recognized its sweat. Should I buy it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade him to buy it."],[4652,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about the time of the dawn prayer. He said: \"Pray it with us today and tomorrow.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at Qāʿ Nimrah from al-Juhfah, he prayed it when the first light of dawn appeared. Then when he was at Dhū Ṭuwā, he delayed it until the people said: \"Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away? If only we had prayed.\" He then prayed just before sunrise. Then he turned to the people and said: \"What did you say?\" They said: \"If only we had prayed.\" He said: \"If you had done so, punishment would have befallen you.\" Then he called the questioner and said: \"Its time is between my two prayers.\""],[4654,"On the authority of 'Urwah: \"In naming the companions of al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Rifa'ah b. Rafi' b. Malik b. 'Ajlan b. 'Amr b. Zurayq. He was a naqib and had witnessed Badr.\""],[4655,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who attended the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Hubla: Rifa'ah b. 'Amr, and he attended Badr.\""],[4711,"I entered the mosque and I recognized in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hunger, so I asked Umm Sulaym, “Do you have anything?” She gestured with her two hands and said, “I have something.” I said, “Prepare it, knead it,” and I sent Anas and said, “Go to him, whisper in his ear, and invite him.” When Anas returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This is a man who has brought you good. With what thing did your father send you to invite us?” Anas said, “Yes.” So I met him, and he said, “Get up, in the name of Allah.” Anas turned and ran quickly until he came to Abu Talhah and said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he has come to you among the people.” Abu Talhah said, “So I met him at the door, at the rest of the step, and I said, ‘What have you done to us, O Messenger of Allah? I only recognized hunger in your face, so I prepared something for you to eat.’ He said, ‘Enter and rejoice.’ He entered, and their dish was brought, and he began to smooth it with his hand, then he said, ‘Is there any—’ as if he meant condiment. They brought him their small butter-skin, containing something or not containing it, and he gestured with his hand, and ghee poured from it. Then he said, ‘Admit to me ten at a time, ten at a time.’” He said, “And they were about a hundred. They entered and ate until they were full. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the leftover that remained, ‘Eat, you and your dependents.’ So they ate and were full.”"],[4715,"From Abū Ṭalḥah, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he entered upon Sahl while he was ill, and beneath Sahl was a coverlet containing figures. Sahl said, “Remove from beneath me this coverlet.” Abū Ṭalḥah said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding images: ‘The angels do not enter it, except what is embroidery in a cloth, for there is no harm in it.’” Sahl said, “Even so, remove it.”"],[4716,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate pieces of dried curd, then performed ablution because of it.”"],[4717,"Yaḥyā b. Sulaym b. Zayd, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me that he heard Ismāʿīl b. Bashīr, the freed slave of Banū Maghālah, saying: I heard Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Ṭalḥah b. Sahl al-Anṣārī, the two Anṣārīs, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no person who forsakes a Muslim in a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated, except that Allah forsakes him in a place where he loves His help. And there is no one who helps a Muslim in a place where his honor is diminished and his sanctity is violated, except that Allah helps him in a place where he loves His help.”"],[4768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'My Companions are a group, and the people are a group.' Zayd b. Thābit and Rāfi' b. Khadīj said: He has spoken the truth."],[4769,"I heard Zayd b. Thābit say: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he became heavy because of it, and his forehead poured sweat like pearls, even in the cold. The wording is that of 'Uqba b. Mukram."],[4784,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah remains in the servant’s need as long as he remains in his brother’s need.”"],[4788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Zayd, give the zakah of your head along with the people, even if you find nothing but a saʿ of wheat.”"],[4813,"He said in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ: \"Authority is an evil thing.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Authority is a good thing for the one who takes it by its right and fulfills it, and authority is an evil thing for the one who takes it without its right, and it will be a regret for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4857,"A man from the Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a piece of land between two mountains, so he wrote it for him. Then he embraced Islam, and then went to his people and said to them: Embrace Islam, for I have come to you from a man who gives like one who does not fear poverty."],[4858,"Zayd b. Thabit said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge except in three cases: for the head wound reaching the brain, the bone-breaking wound, and the flesh-exposing wound. For the head wound reaching the brain, thirty-three; for the bone-breaking wound, fifteen; and for the flesh-exposing wound, five. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged concerning the eye of an animal at a quarter of its price.”"],[4861,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There was no emigrant between Uthman and Ruqayya and Lot\" — meaning that they were the first to emigrate to the land of Abyssinia."],[4862,"Someone related to us a hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"And what shall I tell you? I was his neighbor. When revelation descended, he would send for me, and I would write down the revelation. When we mentioned the Hereafter, he would mention it with us; when we mentioned this world, he would mention it with us; and when we mentioned food, he would mention it with us.\" So all of this I relate to you from him."],[4865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? [It is] 'There is no might nor power except with God.'\" Abu Nu'aym did not mention Kharijah."],[4876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ partitioned off a room and used to pray in it. His companions noticed him and would pray following his prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best prayer is a man's prayer in his house, except the prescribed prayer.”"],[4877,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If you hear of a plague in a land, do not enter it. If it occurs while you are in a land, do not leave it.”"],[4886,"“The verse intensifying the killing of a soul, which is in Surat al-Nisa’, came down after the one in al-Furqan by six months.” His saying: {And whoever does that will meet a penalty}."],[4887,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi’b narrated to us, from ‘Uqbah b. ‘Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad b. ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Thawban, from Zayd b. Thabit, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.”"],[4888,"“That ‘Ali consummated marriage with Fatimah ؓ before he allotted her anything.”"],[4895,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lengthen the recitation and move his lips.”"],[4896,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not dispute about the Qur’an, for disputing about it is disbelief.”"],[4897,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If this is your affair, then do not compel her.”"],[4903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am leaving among you after me the two weighty things: the Book of God, exalted be He, and my kindred, the people of my house. They will never separate until they come to me at the pool.”"],[4904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God have mercy on a person who hears my statement and conveys it, for many a bearer of understanding is not a jurist, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one more learned than himself.”"],[4910,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Things come to me that I dislike being read. Can you learn Syriac?\" I said, \"Yes.\" \"So I learned it in seventeen [days].\" Abu al-Qasim said: \"This is how Abu Bakr b. Ayyash narrated it from Adi b. Thabit, thus differing from the companions of al-A'mash in the chain. If he preserved it, it is strange from the hadith of Adi b. Thabit; otherwise, the hadith is as the people narrated from al-A'mash, from Thabit b. Ubayd.\""],[4911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Every weak, humble person; if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Shall I not tell you about the people of the Fire?\" He said: \"Every harsh, coarse, arrogant person.\""],[4915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while we were with him: \"Blessed is Syria (al-Sham).\" We said, \"What about it, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The Most Merciful spreads His mercy over it.\""],[4916,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-four portions, up to his prayer [being] twenty-five.\""],[4917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever makes a claim against his brother without evidence, the defendant is more entitled to take the oath.\" The wording is that of Ali b. Bahr."],[4918,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited sharecropping (mukhabarah).\" I said, \"What is mukhabarah?\" He said: \"That you take land in return for a half, a third, or a quarter [of its produce].\""],[4919,"\"Do you not feel shy before one from whom the angels feel shy?\" We said, \"What is that?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Uthman passed by me while an angel from among the angels was with me, and he said: \"A martyr whom his people will kill; we feel shy before him.\" Badr said: \"So a band of people turned away from him.\"\""],[4937,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the ruqbā for the one to whom he granted ruqbā and the ‘umrā for the one to whom he granted ‘umrā.”"],[4938,"From ‘Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Jusham b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj: Zayd b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.”"],[4939,"From ‘Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Jazrah b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and they are Banu al-Hubullayy: Zayd b. al-Marsi.”"],[4946,"A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Convey peace to him and say: Were we not in a state of consecration, we would not have returned it.\""],[4951,"The Prophet ﷺ stopped at al-Juhfa, then turned to the people, praised and extolled Allah, and said: \"I find that no prophet lives beyond half the age of the one before him, and I am about to be summoned and will answer. So what will you say?\" They said: \"You have counseled well.\" He said: \"Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that Paradise is true, and the Fire is true, and that resurrection after death is true?\" They said: \"We testify.\" He said, raising his hands and placing them on his chest: \"And I testify with you.\" Then he said: \"Do you not hear?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I will go ahead of you to the Pond, and you will come to me at the Pond. Its width is as far as the distance between San'a' and Busra; in it are goblets of silver numbering the stars. So watch how you succeed me in the two weighty things!\" A caller asked: \"What are the two weighty things, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"The Book of Allah, one end in the hand of Allah, Mighty and Exalted, and one end in your hands, so hold fast to it and you will not go astray; and the other is my offspring. The Subtle, the Aware has informed me that they will never separate until they come to me at the Pond. I asked that for them from my Lord. So do not precede them or you will perish, and do not fall short of them or you will perish, and do not teach them, for they are more knowledgeable than you.\" Then he took 'Ali ؓ by the hand and said: \"He whose affairs I have more right to than his own self, 'Ali is his guardian. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[4964,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicate and raise his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits."],[4965,"Ali adjured the people in the Rahbah: 'Whoever heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say what he said to him?' Sixteen men stood up and testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.' Zayd b. Arqam said: 'I was among those who concealed it, so my sight was taken away, and Ali ؓ had supplicated against those who concealed it.'"],[4969,"Ali ؓ was in Yemen when three men came to him disputing about a child, each claiming it was his son. He was alone with two of them and said, 'Would you be content to give the child to this one?' They said, 'No.' Then he was alone with two of them and said to them the like of that, and they said, 'No.' He said, 'I see you are obstinate partners, so I will draw lots among you.' He drew lots among them and made the child belong to the one whom the lot struck, and he charged him two-thirds of the blood money for the remaining two."],[5019,"On the authority of al-Bara’ and Zayd b. Arqam, they said: The Prophet ﷺ came while we were exchanging money. He said: “There is no harm in it hand to hand, but deferred payment is disliked.”"],[5020,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of God and my family (ʿitrah)?” He said: Yes."],[5040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Ali, shall I not teach you a supplication that, if you call upon with it, even if you had sins as numerous as the number of atoms, they would be forgiven for you, although you are forgiven? Say: O God, there is no god but You, the Wise, the Generous. Blessed are You, glory be to You, Lord of the Mighty Throne.”"],[5044,"We were in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , when we were in prayer, if one of us wanted something, he would speak to him and continue walking until this verse was revealed, \"And stand before Allah, devoutly obedient\" (Quran 2:238), so we were commanded to remain silent."],[5045,"I was sitting in the gathering of the Banu al-Arqam when a man from Murad came riding on his mount until he stopped at the gathering and greeted. He said: Is Zayd among the people? They said: Yes, this is Zayd. He said: I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god, O Zayd, did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say to Ali: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy”? He said: Yes. Then the man turned away from him."],[5046,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a sermon on the day of Ghadir and said: “Am I not more entitled to the believers than their own selves?” They said: Yes. Then he took hold of Ali’s ؓ hand and said: “Whoever’s mawla I am, Ali is his mawla. O God, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy.”"],[5047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever wants to live my life, die my death, and reside in the eternal paradise that my Lord has promised me, should take 'Ali ibn Abi Talib as their leader. For he will not lead you astray and will not admit you into misguidance.\""],[5052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How can I be at ease while the companion of the horn has placed the horn in his mouth, waiting for when he is commanded, and then he will blow into it?” They said: What should we say? He said: “Say: Sufficient for us is God, and He is the best Disposer of affairs.”"],[5057,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah ﷻ is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately deviate; He guides him toward good as long as he intends nothing else.”"],[5058,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “‘Abd Allah b. Mas’ud taught me a surah, Zayd taught it to me, and my father taught it to me, and their recitations differed. Whose recitation should I adopt?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, while ‘Ali ؓ was beside him. ‘Ali ؓ said: “Let each person recite as he was taught; each is good and beautiful.”"],[5059,"“It is the night of the seventeenth, the night of the Quran’s revelation, and the day the two armies met.”"],[5060,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “If a man promises his brother, intending to keep it, but does not come to the appointment, there is no sin upon him.”"],[5061,"“I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said the takbir five times.” I will not abandon them for anyone after him."],[5062,"I heard ‘Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul say: {Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse.} I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. Ibn Ubayy came to him and swore that he had not said it. Then the companions of the Prophet ﷺ came to me and blamed me. I went to my home and slept in a dejected state. The Prophet ﷺ sent for me, and I came to him—or he said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ—and he said: “Allah has confirmed you and excused you.” And he recited these two verses: {They are the ones who say, ‘Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah’} until he completed the two verses."],[5063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his father or mother, it suffices him and them.”"],[5068,"He said: “Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, senility, the torment of the grave, and the trial of the Dajjal. O Allah, grant my soul its piety; You are the best to purify it, You are its guardian and master. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from a heart that is not humble, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not heard.” Or he said: “a call that is not answered.”"],[5077,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali on the day of Ghadir Khumm: \"O Allah, whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\""],[5086,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, the sons of the sons of the Ansar, the women of the Ansar, the women of the sons of the Ansar, and the women of the sons of the sons of the Ansar.”"],[5098,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What an excellent man Bilal is, and the muezzins will be the longest of people in necks.\""],[5099,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What an excellent person Bilal is, and none follows him except a believer, and he is the master of the muezzins, and the muezzins will be the longest of people in necks on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5100,"Ilyas ibn AbuRamlah ash-Shami said: I witnessed Mu'awiyah ibn AbuSufyan asking Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you offer along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Friday and 'Id prayers synchronised on the same day? He said: Yes. He asked: How did he do? He replied: He offered the 'Id prayer, then granted concession to offer the Friday prayer, and said: If anyone wants to offer it, he may offer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1070)"],[5103,"Some people from the Arabs came and said: \"Let us go to this man. If he is a prophet, then we will be the happiest of people with him, and if he is a king, we will live under his protection.\" So I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him what they had said. Then they came to the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ and began calling out, \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad!\" He said: Then God, may He be exalted, sent down: {Indeed, those who call you from behind the rooms, most of them do not understand}. The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of my ear and said: \"God has confirmed your words, O Zayd.\""],[5108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to plant trees, so we stood up what was under them and sprinkled them with water. Then he addressed us and said, \"By Allah, there is nothing that will happen until the Hour comes, but we have been informed about it on that day.\" Then he said, \"O people, who is more worthy of you than yourselves?\" We said, \"Allah and His Messenger are more worthy of us than ourselves.\" He said, \"So whoever I am his guardian, 'Ali is his guardian.\" Then he took his hand and said, \"O Allah, be a protector to those who protect him and be an enemy to those who show enmity to him.\""],[5109,"\"The Prophet ﷺ forbade gourds, pitch-covered vessels, and hollowed-out stumps.\""],[5125,"And I said while I was in prayer: 'Glory be to God, glory be to God.' Then he said: 'Be silent, be silent.' (He said): 'Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' This was in the first book. 'Abu Bakr al-Siddiq has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth — weak in his body, strong in the cause of God.' This was in the first book. 'Umar b. al-Khattab has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth — strong in his body, strong in the cause of God.' This was in the first book. 'Uthman b. Affan has spoken truth, spoken truth, spoken truth.' 'Two have passed and four remain, and the protected zones have been permitted — the well of Aris. And what is the well of Aris? Peace be upon you, 'Abd Allah b. Rawaha. Have you sensed Kharija and Sa'd with me?' Sharik said: 'They are his father and his brother.'"],[5126,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque of Madinah, and he began to say: 'Where is so-and-so, son of so-and-so?' He did not cease to notice their absence and send for them until they had gathered before him. Then he said: 'I am going to tell you a hadith, so memorize it, understand it, and relate it to those after you: God has chosen a creation from His creation.' Then he recited this verse: {God chooses from the angels messengers and from the people} 'a creation whom He will admit to Paradise. I am chosen from among you; whoever I wish to choose, I choose, and I make brotherhood among you just as God made brotherhood among the angels. Rise, O Abu Bakr.' He rose and knelt before him. He said: 'You have a hand with me that God will reward you for. If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken you as a close friend. You are to me like my shirt to my body.' And he moved his shirt with his hand. Then he said: 'Come close, O 'Umar.' He came close. He said: 'You were harsh in your opposition to us, Abu Hafs. I called upon God to strengthen the religion through you or through Abu Jahl, and God did that through you. You are the more beloved of the two to me, and you will be with me in Paradise, the third of three of this ummah.' Then he stepped aside and made him a brother with Abu Bakr. Then he called 'Uthman and said: 'Come close, O 'Uthman. Come close, O 'Uthman.' He kept drawing near until he touched his knee to the knee of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he looked at him, then looked at the sky and said: 'Glory be to God, the Magnificent' three times. Then he looked at 'Uthman, and his buttons were undone, so the Messenger of God ﷺ buttoned them with his hand. Then he said: 'Gather the two ends of your cloak over your chest, for you will have an affair among the people of heaven. You are among those who will come to me at the cistern with his jugular veins gushing blood, and I will say: Who did this to you? You will say: So-and-so and so-and-so. That is the speech of Gabriel ﷺ , when he called from heaven: Verily 'Uthman is trustworthy over every one who is forsaken.' Then he called 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and said: 'Come close, O trusted one of God, the trusted one in heaven. God will give you power over your wealth with truth. Verily you have a supplication with me, and I have delayed it.' He said: 'Choose for me, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'You have burdened me, O 'Abd al-Rahman, with a trust. May God increase your wealth.' He said: And he began to move his hand. Then he stepped aside and made him a brother with 'Uthman. Then Talha and al-Zubayr entered, and he said: 'Come close to me.' They came close. He said: 'You two are my disciples, like the disciples of Jesus son of Mary ﷺ .' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he called Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas and 'Ammar b. Yasir and said: 'O 'Ammar, you will be killed by the rebellious faction.' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he called 'Uwaymir Abu al-Darda' and Salman al-Farisi and said: 'O Salman, you are from us, the People of the House. God has given you the first knowledge and the last knowledge, the first book and the last book.' Then he said: 'Shall I direct you, O Abu al-Darda'?' He said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'That you rescue them, they would rescue you; if you leave them, they will not leave you; if you flee from them, they will catch you. So lend them your honor for the day of your poverty.' Then he made brotherhood between them. Then he looked at the faces of his companions and said: 'Rejoice and be comforted, for you are the first to come to me at the cistern, and you will be in the highest chambers.' Then he looked at 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar and said: 'Praise be to God who guides from misguidance.' Then 'Ali said: 'O Messenger of God, my spirit has departed and my back has broken when I saw you do what you did with your companions other than me. If it is from displeasure with me, then to you belongs the right to be pleased and honor.' He said: 'By the One who sent me with the truth, I did not delay you except for myself. You are to me in the position of Aaron to Moses, and you are my heir.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, what do I inherit from you?' He said: 'What the prophets inherited.' He said: 'And what did the prophets inherit before you?' He said: 'The Book of God and the sunnah of their prophet. And you will be with me in my palace in Paradise, with Fatimah my daughter, and my companion.' Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited the verse: {Brothers on couches, facing one another} 'the beloved friends in God, looking at each other.'"],[5130,"“The Prophet ﷺ deemed some people too young on the day of Uhud: among them Zayd b. Jariya — meaning himself — al-Bara' b. 'Azib, Sa'd b. Khaythama, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, and Jabir b. 'Abd Allah.”"],[5134,"From his father: “In naming those who witnessed with 'Ali: Zayd b. Aslam, from the Ansar, a Badri.”"],[5135,"“And among those killed on the day of Hunayn from the Muslims, from Quraysh, then from Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Zayd b. Rabi'a.”"],[5136,"From 'Urwa: “In naming those killed on the day of al-Yamama from the Muslims: Zayd b. Ruqaysh, an ally of Banu Umayya.”"],[5137,"From ʿUrwa: “In the naming of those who were killed on the Day of the Bridge, the Bridge of al-Madāʾin, with Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Najjār: Zayd b. Surāqa b. Kaʿb.”"],[5138,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj: Zayd b. al-Muzayyan.”"],[5139,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū ʿAwf b. al-Khazraj, from Balḥublā: Zayd b. Wadīʿa b. ʿAmr b. Qays.”"],[5140,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of al-Yamāma from Quraysh, then from Banū Zuhra: Zayd b. Usayd b. Jāriya.”"],[5224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, his previous sins will be forgiven.\""],[5241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not leave anything for another thing among the prayers until he used the toothstick."],[5244,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade plundering and mutilation."],[5259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not make your houses graves, and pray in them.\""],[5260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever shelters a stray, he remains a stray as long as he doesn't identify it.\""],[5262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out intending Makkah until when he was in part of Wadi al-Rawha, the people found a wounded wild donkey. They mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Leave it until its owner comes.\" Al-Bahzi, who was its owner, came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this donkey is yours to deal with.\" He ordered Abu Bakr to distribute it among the traveling groups, and they were in ihram. Then we passed on until when we were at al-Uthaya, there was a gazelle standing in the shade with an arrow in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man to stand by it until he informed the people about it."],[5272,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge be taken away while we recite the Qur’an, teach it to our sons, our women, and our slaves?” He said: “By Allah, I used to consider you, O Ziyad, among the jurists of the Muslims. Do you not know that the Torah and the Gospel were sent down to the Jews and the Christians, so what did it benefit them when they did not act upon it?”"],[5273,"He came to Madinah with a camel of his loaded with food, and the Prophet ﷺ met him and said: “O Bedouin, what are you carrying?” I said: “I am preparing wheat.” He said to me: “What do you want?” I said: “I want to sell it.” Then he wiped my head and said: “Be fair in trading with the Bedouin.”"],[5274,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Saʿida b. Kaʿb b. al-Khazraj: Ziyad b. ʿAmr al-Juhani, an ally of theirs.”"],[5275,"From Abu al-Yasar b. ʿAmr and Ziyad b. al-Fard that they both heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to ʿAmmar: “The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[5284,"From Qabisah b. Mukhariq al-Hilali and Zuhayr b. Amr, they said: When this verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: {And warn your closest kindred}, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ went to a pile of rocks on a mountain and climbed to the top of it, on a rock, then said: 'O Banu Abd Manaf, I am a warner to you. My likeness and yours is like a man who saw the enemy and went to alert his family, fearing that they would reach his family before him, so he began shouting: \"O morning! O morning! You have been attacked! You have been attacked!\"'"],[5285,"He was called Ma'ruf; if his name was not Zuhayr b. Uthman, I do not know what it was. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The walimah on the first day is a right, the second is a kindness, and the third is showing off and ostentation.'"],[5286,"A woman from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a son of hers who had died, and it was as if the people had rebuked her. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah, two of my children have died since I entered Islam, besides this one.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah, you have shielded yourself from the Fire with a strong shielding.'"],[5287,"A man of shabby appearance came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Do you have wealth?' He said: 'Yes, of all kinds of wealth.' He said: 'Then let it be seen on you, for Allah ﷻ loves to see the traces of His blessing on His servant in a good way, and He does not love misery or feigning misery.' Zuhayr b. Mu'awiyah al-Jushami: he is not included in the authentic collections."],[5288,"Uthman b. Affan ؓ and Zuhayr b. Umayyah came and asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and they praised me in his presence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I know him better than you two; he was my partner in the Jahiliyyah.'"],[5293,"Her grandfather al-Zari' set out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and took with him a son of his, or a son of his sister, who was insane. My grandfather said: When we arrived in Madinah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have with me a son of mine, or a son of my sister, who is insane; I have brought him to you so that you may supplicate to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for him. He said: 'Bring him to me.' So I went with him to the Prophet while he was still on the riding camel, and I untied him, removed his travel clothes, and dressed him in two fine garments. I took him by the hand until I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Bring him close to me, and place his back facing me.' He then took hold of the gathers of his garment from its top and bottom and began striking his back until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, while saying: 'Come out, enemy of Allah! Come out, enemy of Allah!' Then he began looking with the gaze of a healthy person, not his previous gaze. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then seated him in front of him, called for water, wiped his face, and supplicated for him. After the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, there was none in the delegation who surpassed him."],[5294,"Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ: 'The Prophet ﷺ wrote to al-Dahhak b. Sufyan instructing him to give inheritance to the wife of Ashaym al-Dibabi from the blood-money of her husband.'"],[5295,"From the Prophet ﷺ: {Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, all things We created with predestination.} He said: 'It was revealed concerning some people of my community in the last days who deny the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[5401,"From ʿUrwah in the list of those who attended al-ʿAqabah from the Ansar, then from Banū ʿAdiyy b. ʿAmr b. Mālik b. al-Najjār b. Aws: Abū Ṭalḥah, whose name is Zayd b. Sahl b. al-Aswad b. Ḥarām b. ʿAmr b. Zayd Manāt b. ʿAdiyy b. ʿAmr b. Mālik."],[5402,"From Ibn Shihāb in the list of those who attended al-ʿAqabah from the Ansar: Abū Ṭalḥah Zayd b. Sahl from Banū al-Najjār, and he attended Badr."],[5471,"From 'Urwa: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Zayd b. Aslam b. Tha'laba b. 'Adi b. al-'Ajlan.”"],[5491,"'Uthman: “Which of the people should I have write?” They said, “Zayd b. Thabit.”"],[5521,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from al-Aws, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Zayd b. Aslam b. Tha'laba.”"],[5582,"Sahl b. Hunayf: \"O people, be suspicious of your own opinion, for by God, we never took hold of their legs for any matter that cut us off except that it led us smoothly to a matter we recognized, except this matter of yours, for it only increases in hardship and confusion. If only you had seen me on the day of Abu Jandal — had I found helpers against the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would have objected.\""],[5591,"Sahl b. Hunayf used to say, \"I have never seen anyone like the one who did not question his own judgment: We set out with the Messenger of God ﷺ as pilgrims, and when we arrived in Makkah, he ordered us to turn it into an Umrah.\""],[5614,"From his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathmah, they both said: Habibah bt. Sahl was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, and he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, I see him, and were it not for fear of God ﷻ, I would spit in his face.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Will you return to him his garden that he gave you as a dowry?' She said: 'Yes.' So he sent for him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated them. That was the first khul' in Islam."],[5615,"Turn to what you have turned to, O Abu Hazim. Shall I not tell you from my father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'That I pray the morning prayer and then sit in a gathering remembering God ﷻ until the sun rises is dearer to me than racing fine horses in the path of God ﷻ.'"],[5619,"From Ibn Shihab: “In naming those who witnessed the ʿAqaba from the Ansar, then from Banu Bayada: Ziyad b. Labid, and he witnessed Badr.”"],[5620,"From Ibn Shihāb: “In the naming of those who were killed on the day of Ajnādayn from Quraysh, then from Banū Sahm: Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith b. Qays.”"],[5621,"From ʿUrwa: “In the naming of those who witnessed al-ʿAqaba from the Anṣār, then from Banū Bayāḍa: Zayd b. Labīd.”"],[5623,"About Ibn Shihab, \"Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar and then from the Banu Harith bin Al-Khazraj, Sa'd bin Ar-Rabi'.\""],[5624,"From ʿUrwa: In naming those who were martyred on the day of al-Yamāma among the Anṣār, then from Banū Sāʿida, Saʿd b. Ḥāritha b. Lūdhān b. ʿAbd Wudd."],[5625,"\"About Urwah, in regards to the identification of the person who witnessed the pledge of allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , at Al-Aqaba, from the Ansar, and then from the Banu Najjar, Sahl ibn Atik.\" (Note: The translation may not be exact as the passage provided does not have context)"],[5633,"That he married seventy women, who either died or he divorced, and he saw nothing wrong with that."],[5634,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should brandish a sword at his brother, for Satan may seize his hand and cause him to fall into a pit of the pits of Hell.”"],[5714,"He was in a gathering in which were his father, Abu Hurayrah, Abu Usayd, and Abu Humayd, and they discussed the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they mentioned that he gave the greeting of peace to his right and to his left."],[5717,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “There is no one reciting the talbiyah except that what is to his right and left of stones and trees recites the talbiyah.”"],[5736,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Every people has a forerunner, and I am your forerunner at the Pond. Whoever comes to me at the Pond and drinks will never thirst, and whoever never thirsts will enter Paradise.\""],[5752,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will see the people of the chambers above them just as you see the brilliant star passing across the horizon, east and west, because of the superiority that exists among them.”"],[5777,"“I saw someone better than me wipe over them.”"],[5810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I will precede you to the Basin. Whoever comes to me will drink, and whoever drinks will never thirst. Indeed, some people will come to me whom I will recognize, but then they will be prevented from reaching me.\""],[5816,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Dhū al-Ḥulayfah and there was a dead sheep with its leg raised. He said: “Do you consider this sheep insignificant to its owners?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this sheep is to its owners. If the world weighed as much as a mosquito’s wing in the sight of Allah, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it.”"],[5835,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to eat watermelon with fresh dates.”"],[5838,"And with his chain: I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ when his front tooth was broken, his face was wounded, and his helmet was crushed on his head. I surely know who washed the blood from his face, who carried water to him, and what was placed on his wound until the blood stopped. Fatimah bt. Muhammad, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, was washing the blood from his face, and ʿAlī ؓ was carrying water to her in a shield. When she had washed the blood from her father’s face, she burned a mat until it became ash, then took some of that ash and placed it on his face until the blood stopped. Then he said that day: “God’s anger has intensified against a people who wounded the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then he paused for a while, then said: “O God, forgive my people, for they do not know.”"],[5839,"“Abū Usayd married and invited the Prophet ﷺ to his wedding feast. His wife served us and gave us nabīdh to drink that she had soaked overnight, and she served it to him.”"],[5840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Everything has a summit, and the summit of the Qurʾān is Sūrat al-Baqarah. Whoever recites it in his house at night, no devil will enter it for three nights, and whoever recites it in his house by day, no devil will enter it for three days.”"],[5841,"“The midday nap during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ was after the Friday prayer.”"],[5849,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour were sent like these two.\""],[5893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The space of a whip in Paradise is better than the world and everything in it.”"],[5897,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “If the world weighed as much as a mosquito’s wing in God’s sight, He would not give a disbeliever any of it.”"],[5900,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A man came to him and confessed in his presence that he had committed adultery with a woman whom he named. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for the woman and asked her about that, but she denied having committed adultery, so he flogged him the prescribed punishment and left her.'"],[5918,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The intention of a believer is better than his action, and the action of a hypocrite is better than his intention, and each acts according to his intention. When a believer performs an action, a light is kindled in his heart.”"],[5919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will certainly follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until even if they entered a lizard’s hole you would follow them.” We said: O Messenger of God, the Jews and the Christians? He said: “Who else but the Jews and the Christians?”"],[5920,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There has been no heresy except that it was preceded by denial of destiny.”"],[5931,"The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed heartily, so they said, “O Messenger of God, we have seen you laugh a laugh the like of which we have not seen you laugh.” He said, “Because of a people who will be brought to Paradise in iron chains.”"],[5932,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Some people open the door to good and close the door to evil, and some people open the door to evil and close the door to good. Glad tidings to those in whose hands Allah places they keys to good, and woe to those in whose hands Allah places the keys to evil.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 237)"],[5953,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Clapping is only for women, and glorification (tasbih) is for men.\""],[5956,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they hasten to break the fast.\""],[5957,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The station of one of you in the path of God is better than the world and all that is in it.\""],[5958,"There was a conflict among the Ansar, and the Prophet ﷺ came to them to make peace between them. The Prophet ﷺ came while Abu Bakr ؓ was leading the people in prayer, and he prayed behind Abu Bakr ؓ."],[5977,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and he was describing Paradise until he reached it, then he said, \"In it is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.\" Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds to call upon their Lord in fear and hope, and they spend out of what We have provided them} up to His saying {as a reward for what they used to do}."],[5978,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"A morning or an evening spent in the path of God is better than the world and all that it contains.\""],[5983,"He said: There was an old woman who used to cook on Friday the roots of chard and throw on it grains of barley. When we finished the Friday prayer, we would enter and eat."],[5986,"\"Shall I not tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever is in the mosque waiting for the prayer is in prayer.'\""],[5992,"“We used to take a midday nap after Friday prayer.”"],[5995,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us while some of us were teaching others. He said: “Praise be to God. The Book is one, and among you are the red and the black. Recite the Qur'an, recite the Qur'an, recite it before there come people who will pronounce it perfectly, as an arrow is made straight, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They seek its reward in haste and do not defer it.”"],[5996,"“I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ raise his hands at all in supplication, whether on the pulpit or elsewhere. But I saw him do this” – and he pointed with his index finger and bent the middle finger against the thumb."],[5997,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us one day while we were reciting. He said, “Praise be to God. The Book of God is one, and among you are the white and among you are the black. Recite it before people recite it who will straighten it as an arrow is straightened. One of them will hasten his reward and not delay it.”"],[5998,"Two men differed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ about the mosque founded on piety. One said it was the mosque of Madinah, and the other said it was the mosque of Quba. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “It is this mosque of mine.”"],[5999,"“If I were to give you water from the well of Buda‘ah, you would dislike it, but by God, I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ water from it with my own hand.”"],[6000,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever has roots in Madinah, let him hold fast to them, and whoever does not have roots there, let him establish roots there. There will come upon people a time when one who has no roots there will be like one leaving it, passing through to elsewhere.”"],[6007,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ, Suhayl ibn Bayda’ was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Suhayl ibn Bayda’,” and raised his voice twice or three times. Each time Suhayl answered him, so that the people heard the voice of the Messenger of God ﷺ and knew that he meant them. Those in front sat down, and those behind caught up, until when they had gathered, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God, God forbids him from the Fire and makes Paradise obligatory for him.”"],[6008,"From Ibn Shihab, “In the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Najjar: Suhayl ibn Rafi‘ ibn Abi ‘Amr. He and his brother had the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ as a date-drying ground.”"],[6011,"I heard al-Hasan say: The nobles of Quraysh gathered at the door of Umar ؓ, among them al-Harith b. Hisham, Abu Sufyan b. Harb, and Suhail b. Amr. Meanwhile, those slaves and freedmen from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ [were also present]. His permission came out, and he gave permission to Bilal, Suhaib, and their like, and left the others. Abu Sufyan said: 'I have never seen [anything] like today; he gave permission to these slaves and left us sitting at his door without granting us permission.' Suhail b. Amr, who was a wise man, said: 'O people, by God, I see what is in your faces. If you are angry, then be angry with yourselves. The people were called and you were called; they hastened and you delayed. By God, what they preceded you to of virtue is more severely missed by you than this door of yours over which you competed.' Al-Hasan said: 'God does not make a servant who hastens to Him like a servant who delays from Him.'"],[6034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever says: 'O Allah, I call You to witness, and I call to witness Your angels and the bearers of Your Throne, and I call to witness whoever is in the heavens and the earth that You are Allah; there is no god but You, alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger' — whoever says it once, Allah frees one-third of him from the Fire; whoever says it twice, Allah frees two-thirds of him from the Fire; and whoever says it three times, Allah frees all of him from the Fire."],[6035,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, every prophet has a wasi (legatee/trustee); who is your wasi? He was silent. Later he saw me and said: \"O Salman.\" I hastened to him and said: At your service. He said: \"Do you know who Musa's wasi was?\" I said: Yes, Yusha' b. Nun. He said: \"Why?\" I said: Because he was the most knowledgeable of them. He said: \"My wasi, the keeper of my secret, the best of those I leave after me, who fulfills my promise and pays my debt, is 'Ali b. Abi Talib.\" Abu al-Qasim said: His saying \"my wasi\" means he entrusted him with his family, not with the caliphate; and his saying \"the best of those I leave after me\" means from his household ﷺ."],[6041,"I entered upon Salman and saw his house was worn and shabby. Someone remarked to him about that, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined me that your provision in this world should be like the provision of a rider.\""],[6048,"He said: I was a man from the people of Jayy, the city of Isfahan. While I was thus, Allah cast into my heart concern about the truth of the heavens and the earth. I went to a man who would not speak to people out of scrupulousness and asked him, 'Which religion is best?' He said, 'What do you have to do with this talk? Do you want a religion other than your father's religion?' I said, 'No, but I would like to know who is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, and which religion is best.' He said, 'I do not know anyone upon this except a monk in Mosul.' So I went to him and stayed with him. He was straitened in worldly provisions; he would fast by day and stand in prayer by night. I worshipped as he worshipped, and I remained with him for three years. Then he died. I said, 'To whom do you entrust me?' He said, 'I do not know anyone among the people of the east upon what I am upon. You should go to a monk beyond the Jazirah, and convey my greetings to him.' So I went to him, conveyed his greetings, and told him that he had died. I remained with him for another three years. Then he died. I said, 'Where do you command me to go?' He said, 'I do not know anyone on earth upon what I am upon except a monk in Amorium, an old man. I do not know whether you will reach him or not.' So I went to him and stayed with him. He was a man with ample provision. When death came to him, I said, 'Where do you command me to go?' He said, 'I do not know anyone on earth upon what I am upon. But if you live to see a time when a man is heard of who comes forth from the house of Ibrahim ﷺ — and I do not think you will live to see him, though I had hoped to — then if you can be with him, do so, for he is upon the religion. Its signs are that his people will say he is a sorcerer, a madman, a soothsayer; that he eats gifts but does not eat charity; and that at the cartilage of his shoulders there is the seal of prophethood.' While I was thus, a caravan came from the direction of Madinah. I said, 'Who are you?' They said, 'We are from the people of Madinah. We are merchants who live by our trade. But a man has come forth from the house of Ibrahim ﷺ and came to us. His people fight him, and we fear that he may come between us and our trade. But he has taken possession of Madinah.' I said, 'What do they say about him?' They said, 'They say he is a sorcerer, a madman, a soothsayer.' I said, 'This is the sign. Direct me to your companion.' I went to him and said, 'Will you carry me to Madinah?' He said, 'What will you give me?' I said, 'I have nothing to give you except that I will be your slave.' So he carried me. When I arrived, he put me among his palm trees. I would water them as a camel waters, until my back and chest became calloused from that. I found no one who understood my speech until an old Persian woman came to water. I spoke to her, and she understood my speech. I said to her, 'Where is the man who has come forth? Direct me to him.' She said, 'He will pass by you in the morning when he prays the dawn prayer at the beginning of the day.' I went out and gathered dates. When morning came, I approached and brought the dates near to him. He said, 'What is this? Is it charity or a gift?' I gestured that it was charity. He said, 'Take it to these,' and his companions were with him. They ate, but he did not eat. I said, 'This is one sign.' The next day, I came with dates. He said, 'What is this?' I said, 'This is a gift.' He ate and called his companions, and they ate. Then he saw me trying to look at the seal. He recognized that, so he threw off his cloak. I began to turn him around and embrace him. He said, 'What is the matter with you?' He asked me, so I told him my story. He said, 'You stipulated to them that you are a slave. Purchase your freedom from them.' So the Prophet ﷺ purchased him on the condition that he bring them one hundred palm trees and forty uqiyahs of gold; then he would be free. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Plant.' So he planted. Then he said, 'Go and throw the bucket into the well. Then do not raise it until it rises, for when it is full, it will rise. Then sprinkle [the water] at their roots.' He did so, and the palms grew the fastest of growth. He said, 'Glory be to Allah! We have never seen the like of this slave. This slave has great importance.' People gathered around him. The Prophet ﷺ gave him gold nuggets, and in it were forty uqiyahs."],[6049,"He said to him: 'Shall I not urge you toward what you are upon?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Ribat (guarding the frontier) for one day in the path of Allah is better than fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever dies as a murabit in the path of Allah, his deeds continue to be recorded for him, and he is protected from the trial of the grave.'"],[6058,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"When the heart of a believer trembles in the path of God, his sins fall away as the branches of a date-palm tree fall away.\""],[6081,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever loves al-Hasan and al-Husayn, I love him; whoever I love, God loves him; and whoever hates them, I hate him; and whoever I hate, God hates him.\""],[6119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Islam began as something strange and will return to being strange.”"],[6120,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ is too shy, when a servant raises his hands to Him, to return them empty, with nothing in them.”"],[6121,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about locusts, so he said: “That is the most numerous of God's armies; I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.”"],[6124,"Salman led us in a prayer, then he went to a branch of a dry tree and shook it, and its leaves fell. Then he said, “Do you know why I did this?” They said, “No.” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in a prayer, then he went to a branch of a dry tree and shook it, and its leaves fell. Then he said, ‘When a servant performs ablution and does it well, then prays and does it well, his sins fall away just as the leaves of this tree fall away.’” The wording is that of the hadith of Abdan."],[6125,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “On the Day of Resurrection, a man will come with so many good deeds that he thinks they will save him. Then another man will keep coming—someone he had wronged with an injustice—and it will be taken from his good deeds and given to the wronged one, until no good deed remains for him. Then someone else will come seeking recompense from him while he has no good deed left, so it will be taken from the sins of the wronged one and placed upon his own sins.”"],[6126,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You must observe the night prayer, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, a means of drawing near to God, the Exalted, an atonement for evil deeds, a deterrent from sin, and a repeller of disease from the body.”"],[6129,"Salman ؓ said: Hudhayfa used to narrate things that the Messenger of God ﷺ said in his anger to certain people. I said, “O Hudhayfa, either you stop, or I will write to Umar about you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am one of the children of Adam; any servant of my community whom I have cursed or insulted without just cause, I will make it a blessing upon him.”"],[6130,"“Your superiority over the rest of the Messenger of God ﷺ—meaning the Arabs—is that we do not marry your women.”"],[6139,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks and the head-covering."],[6142,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When speech proliferates, action is stowed away, tongues come together, hearts come to hate one another, and every relative severs his ties of kinship—then God curses them, makes them deaf, and blinds their sight.”"],[6143,"I asked Salmān al-Fārisī about the tashahhud. He said: “I will teach you as the Messenger of God ﷺ taught me. The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me the tashahhud word by word: ‘Greetings are for God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God's mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon God's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His messenger.’”"],[6144,"I set out when I came to al-Madāʾin, and there was a man wearing worn-out clothes, holding a red hide and rubbing it. I turned, and he looked at me and gestured with his hand: “Stay where you are, servant of God.” I stood still and asked those who were with me: “Who is this man?” They said: “This is Salmān.” He entered his house, put on white clothes, then came back, took my hand, shook it, and asked me about myself. I said: “Abū ʿAbd Allah, you have not seen me before, nor have I seen you, nor did you know me.” He said: “Indeed, by the One in whose hand is my soul, my spirit recognized your spirit when I saw you. Are you not al-Ḥārith b. ʿAmīra?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Spirits are assembled troops. Those among them that recognize one another in God become close, and those that do not recognize one another in God differ.’”"],[6145,"I was walking with Salmān along the bank of the Tigris. He said: “Brother of Banū ʿAbs, go down and drink.” I drank. Then he said: “Drink.” I drank. He said: “Has your drinking decreased the Tigris?” I said: “How could it possibly decrease?” He said: “Knowledge is like that: it is taken from, and it does not decrease.” Then he said: “Mount.” We passed by piles of wheat and barley, and he said: “Do you see this? It was opened for us and withheld from the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ. Was that good for us and bad for them, or bad for us and good for them?” I said: “I do not know.” He said: “But I know: it was bad for us and good for them. The Messenger of God ﷺ never ate his fill for three consecutive days until he joined God, Exalted is He.”"],[6146,"The first of this Ummah to embrace Islam was Ali ibn Abi Talib."],[6147,"Salman: “It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ: {That is because among them are priests and monks}.”"],[6153,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Four things are from the deeds of the living that continue for the dead: a man who leaves behind righteous offspring who supplicate for him, and their supplication follows him; a man who gives a perpetual charity after him, and he has its reward as long as it continues after him; and a man who teaches knowledge that is acted upon after him, and he has the like of the reward of those who act upon it without any decrease in the reward of those who act upon it.”"],[6154,"When death came to him, they noticed some anxiety in him, so they said: “What makes you anxious, O Abu ʿAbd Allah, when you have a precedence in good? You witnessed great conquests with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: “It grieves me that our beloved Muhammad ﷺ, when he parted from us, made a covenant with us, saying: ‘Let the provision of one of you be like that of a rider.’ That is what has grieved me.” So Salman's wealth was gathered and its value was fifteen dirhams."],[6155,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The most hungry of people on the Day of Resurrection will be those who were most full in this world. O Salman, this world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.”"],[6156,"And from Salman, they both said: The Messenger of God ﷺ took ʿAli ؓ by the hand and said: “This is the first to believe in me, and he is the first to shake my hand on the Day of Resurrection. This is the greatest ṣiddīq, and this is the Fārūq of this community, by whom truth is distinguished from falsehood. This is the leader of the believers, and wealth is the leader of the wrongdoer.”"],[6157,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to visit a man from the Ansar. When he entered upon him, he placed his hand on his forehead and said: “How do you find yourself?” But he gave no reply. It was said: “O Messenger of God, he is too distracted by pain to answer you.” He said: “Leave me alone with him.” So the women left his presence and left the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hand, and the sick man gestured: put your hand back where it was. Then he called out: “O so-and-so, what do you feel?” He said: “I feel good. Two persons have come to me, one black and one white.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Which of them is closer to you?” He said: “The black one.” He said: “Good is little and evil is much.” He said: “Then give me the benefit of a supplication from you, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O God, forgive the much and increase the little.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What do you see?” He said: “Good, may my father and mother be your ransom. The good is growing, and I see the evil fading away. The black one has withdrawn from me.” He said: “Which of your deeds was most in control of you?” He said: “I used to give water to drink.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Listen, O Salman, do you find anything objectionable in me?” He said: “Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom. I have seen you in many situations, but I have never seen you in a state like today.” He said: “I know well what he is meeting: there is no vein in him but it is experiencing death on its own.”"],[6158,"Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays.” They left the Messenger of God ﷺ feeling heavy-hearted. I met them and said: “Why do I see you two heavy-hearted?” They said: “Because of a hadith we heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: ‘Among the traits of a hypocrite are: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays.’” He said: “Did you not ask him about it?” They said: “We were in awe of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I said: “But I will ask him.” So I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Abu Bakr and ʿUmar met me, and they were heavy-hearted.” Then I mentioned what they had said. He said: “I did tell them that, but I did not place it where they placed it. Rather, a hypocrite is one who speaks while telling himself that he is lying, promises while telling himself that he will break it, and is entrusted while telling himself that he will betray.”"],[6159,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us from putting ourselves to hardship for a guest by providing what we do not have."],[6162,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"No man performs the major ablution on Friday, purifies himself with whatever purification he can, anoints himself with some of his oil, or touches some perfume from his house, then goes out, and does not separate between two people, then prays what is decreed for him, then remains silent when the imam speaks, except that he is forgiven what is between that Friday and the next.\""],[6202,"On the authority of Jabir b. Abdullah and Salamah b. al-Akwa', a man from Aslam among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that they both said: We were on a military expedition when the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ says: \"Enjoy yourselves.\"'"],[6218,"We visited with the Messenger of God ﷺ a man who was feverish. I said, “O Messenger of God, I have never seen anything hotter than him.” He said, “Shall I not tell you of something hotter on the Day of Resurrection? Those two men, the two riders coming forward,” referring to two men from his companions at that time."],[6226,"“I gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ among those who gave allegiance under the tree.”"],[6234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered among the sacrificial camels in the year of Hudaybiyyah a camel that had belonged to Abu Jahl at the Battle of Badr, with a silver ring in its nose.\" Abdullah said: \"My father narrated it from him long ago, then later abandoned it.\""],[6235,"God forbid that I would do so without the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Go out to the desert, O Aslam, and smell the winds and dwell in the mountain passes.\" They said: \"We fear that this will change our status as emigrants.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You are emigrants wherever you are.\""],[6243,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and entered the mosque. He said: \"Catch him, for he is a spy.\" I caught him, being swift, and killed him, and the Prophet ﷺ gave me his belongings as a reward."],[6244,"Amir b. al-Akwa fought a duel with a man, struck him and killed him, but the sword struck Amir's leg. He began to say: \"I have killed myself,\" and he died. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"He will have two rewards.\""],[6245,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not leave camels untethered; tie them securely, for the devils suckle them.\""],[6272,"In Ramadan during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whoever wished fasted and whoever wished broke his fast and fed a poor person as ransom, until this verse was revealed: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it}."],[6329,"A young man came and stood before the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said at the top of his voice: O Messenger of God, what do you think of someone who did not leave any evil deed except that he did it, nor any sin except that he committed it, nor any arrow that was raised for him except that he seized it with his right hand, and someone whose sins, if distributed among the people of Madinah, would overwhelm them? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Have you become a Muslim?\" Or \"Are you a Muslim?\" He said: As for me, I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: \"Go, for God has replaced your evil deeds with good deeds.\" He said: O Messenger of God, and my treacheries and my immoralities? He said: \"And your treacheries and your immoralities,\" three times. Then the young man turned away saying: God is greater. I kept hearing him say takbir until he disappeared from me or was hidden from me."],[6331,"From his two paternal uncles Yaʿlā and Salama, the two sons of Umayya, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabūk, and with us was a companion of ours from the people of Makkah. He fought a man, and the man bit his forearm, so he pulled it out of his mouth, and his two front teeth fell out. He went to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him for compensation. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"One of you goes to his brother and bites him like a stallion bites, or as a stallion bites, then comes to ask for compensation? There is no right for it.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ nullified it."],[6332,"He came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he and a group from his household and his children. They asked permission to enter upon him, and they entered. He said: \"Who are these?\" It was said to him: This is the delegation of ʿAnaza. He said: \"Excellent, excellent, excellent! What a good tribe ʿAnaza is: wronged but helped. Welcome to the people of Shuʿayb and the in-laws of Moses. Ask, O Salama, about your need.\" He said: I have come to ask you about what you have made obligatory upon me regarding camels, sheep, and goats. So he informed him. Then he sat near him. Then he asked his permission to leave, and he said to him: \"Leave.\" No sooner had he stood up than he said: \"O God, provide ʿAnaza with sufficiency, not bare sustenance and not extravagance.\""],[6344,"He was called Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfa. Just as the Prophet ﷺ adopted Zayd, Abu Hudhayfa married Salim — while considering him his son — to his niece, Fatima bt. al-Walid b. Utba. She was among the first Muhajirat and was then one of the most virtuous unmarried women of Quraysh. When God ﷻ revealed what He revealed concerning that — 'Call them by their fathers' — each of those adopted persons was called to his father; if his father was unknown, he was returned to his patron. Then Sahla bt. Suhayl, the wife of Abu Hudhayfa, who was from Banu Amir b. Luayy, came and said, 'O Messenger of God, we used to consider Salim a son. He used to enter upon me while I was in a loose garment, and we had only one house. What do you think?' He said to her, 'Suckle him, and you will become forbidden to him.'"],[6345,"He was with Abu Bakr ؓ on a rooftop in Ramadan while he was praying. He came to him and said, 'Will you not eat, O Caliph of the Messenger of God?' He gestured with his hand, and he did that twice. When it was the third time, he said, 'Bring me your food.' He ate, prayed two rak'ahs, then entered the mosque and the prayer was established."],[6348,"His father Salim came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was a young boy. 'The Messenger ﷺ invoked blessing upon him and prayed for him, and he performed ablution from the leftover water of his ablution.' That day he had a forelock, and he had reached or nearly reached puberty."],[6356,"I sought the Prophet ﷺ but did not find him. I sat down and saw a group of five or six men, and a man was reconciling between them regarding wounds that had occurred. He made peace between them on the basis of sheep. When the people stood up, a man said: O Messenger of Allah. When I heard that, I said: Upon you be peace, O Messenger of Allah, three times. He said to me three times: \"Upon you be peace is the greeting of the dead.\""],[6367,"We were among the delegation that came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He pitched two tents for us near the house of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. Bilal used to come to us with our iftar, so we would say, 'O Bilal, has the Messenger of God ﷺ broken his fast?' He would say, 'Yes, I did not come to you until the Messenger of God ﷺ had broken his fast.' Then he would put it down and eat, and we would eat. And Bilal used to come to us with our suhur."],[6368,"Our delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they accepted Islam in the middle of Ramadan. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered them, and they fasted with him for what they faced, but he did not order them to make up what they had missed."],[6369,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'It is enough of a betrayal that you tell your brother something he believes from you while you are lying to him.'"],[6387,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition, and we were afflicted with severe thirst. We complained of that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Is there any leftover water in a waterskin?\" A man brought him leftover water in a waterskin. The Prophet ﷺ dug a pit in the ground, placed a leather mat over it, put his palm on the ground, then said to the owner of the waterskin, \"Pour the water onto my palm and mention the name of God.\" He did so. Abu Layla said, \"I saw water springing from between the fingers of the Messenger of God ﷺ until the people drank and all were given water.\""],[6388,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I shall give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God and His Messenger love.\" Then he called Ali and gave it to him."],[6392,"From his brother Isa or al-Hakam or both of them, from Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever sees a snake and does not kill it for fear of its retaliation is not one of us.\""],[6396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing house snakes. He said, \"When you see any of them in your dwellings, say: We adjure you by the covenant which Noah took upon you, and we adjure you by the covenant which Sulayman b. Dawud took upon you. If they return, then kill them.\""],[6397,"He passed by the Prophet ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ was praying a voluntary prayer, and he came across a verse mentioning the Fire, so he said, \"Woe to the people of the Fire! I seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the Fire.\""],[6398,"When the Prophet ﷺ came seeking support at al-Ta'if and entered upon her, she ordered a drink of sawiq for him and he drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O Ruqayqa, do not worship their taghut and do not pray to it.\" I said, \"Then they will kill me.\" He said, \"When they say that to you, say: My Lord is the Lord of this taghut. And when you pray, turn your back to it.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left them. The daughter of Ruqayqa said: My two brothers Sufyan and Wahb, the sons of Qays b. Aban, informed me. They said: When Thaqif embraced Islam, we went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, \"What happened to your mother?\" We said, \"She died in the state in which you left her.\" He said, \"Then your mother has indeed embraced Islam.\""],[6402,"\"I ate hubara meat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6403,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Ali came and sought permission. He lightly knocked on the door and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Safinah, open the door for him.\""],[6404,"From Safinah, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a bird, and he said, \"O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird.\" Then Ali ؓ came, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, be his ally.\""],[6432,"We set out intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ, and Wa'il b. Hujr was with us. An enemy of his seized him. The people were reluctant to take an oath, so I swore that he was my brother, and they released him. Then we came to the Prophet ﷺ and I informed him. He said, \"You have spoken the truth. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim.\""],[6438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best property of a man is a well-trained mare or a productive palm grove.\""],[6449,"\"I came to the Prophet, ﷺ , and he ordered me to give them an instruction. He said, 'When you return to your home, tell them to beautify their actions and order them to trim their nails. And they should not harm the udders of their livestock when milking them.'\""],[6456,"The Prophet ﷺ heard two men while they were exchanging insults, one of them getting angry, and his anger intensified. The Prophet ﷺ said, “I know a word which, if he said it, Satan would leave him.” So the man came to him and he said, “Say: I seek refuge in God from Satan.”"],[6458,"We came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to him, “By our fathers and mothers, O Messenger of God, we hear a hadith from you but we are unable to transmit it exactly as we heard it.” He said, “If you do not make lawful what is unlawful and do not make unlawful what is lawful, and you get the meaning right, then there is no harm.”"],[6462,"The Prophet ﷺ came upon a dead young she-camel and said, “What harm would it have been to the owners of this if they had benefited from its hide?”"],[6463,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, the expedition of al-Muraysiʿ, and our battle cry was: “O Victorious One, kill, kill!”"],[6476,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out on the migration, he was accompanied by Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), Amir ibn Fuhayrah, the servant of Abu Bakr, and 'Abdullah bin Uraiqit, who was guiding them on the way. When they passed by the tent of Umm Ma'bad al-Khuza'iyyah, she did not recognize him. He said to her, \"O Umm Ma'bad, do you have any milk?\" She replied, \"No, by Allah, the sheep are too weak.\" He then said, \"What about this sheep I see in the corner of the tent?\" She replied, \"It is a sheep that has been left behind by the flock because it is too weak.\" He asked, \"Will you allow me to milk her?\" She said, \"By Allah, no male has touched her; still, go ahead and try.\" He then stroked her back and her udder, prayed, and asked for a large bowl. He milked it until it was full and then gave his companions a drink, all drinking until satisfied. Then he milked her again, filling another bowl, which he left with her, and set off. When Umm Ma'bad's husband came home in the evening, he asked her, \"O Umm Ma'bad, what is this milk? There is no milking sheep in the house, and the flock is too weak.\" She replied, \"By Allah, a man who appeared to be blessed, with a handsome face, bright eyes, and a lovely voice passed by. His presence was calm when he spoke and dignified when silent. His words were well-arranged, and he was the best-looking and most handsome of his companions, surrounded by men who listened to his commands and followed his instructions promptly. When he forbade something, they adhered to his prohibition.\" The husband said, \"This is the description of the companion of Quraysh. If I saw him, I would follow him and strive to do so.\" They did not know in Mecca where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had headed until they heard someone calling out on Mount Abu Qubais."],[6477,"From ʿUrwah: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uḥud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Anṣār, then from Banū al-Nabt: Salīṭ b. Thābit b. Waqsh.”"],[6522,"The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ saw a cloud and said: “O Messenger of God, we hoped that this cloud would rain on us.” He said: “It has been commanded to rain on Balīl”—meaning a valley called Balīl."],[6523,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The balance is in God’s hand: He raises some peoples and lowers others. And the heart of the son of Adam is between two of the fingers of the Most Merciful: if He wills, He causes it to deviate; and if He wills, He keeps it upright.”"],[6524,"From Sabrah b. Abī Fākih, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Satan sits in wait for the son of Adam on all his paths. He sits for him on the path of Islam and says: ‘Will you submit and leave your religion and the religion of your forefathers?’ Then he sits for him on the path of emigration and says: ‘Will you emigrate and leave your birthplace, so that you will be like a horse on a long tether?’ Then he sits for him on the path of jihad and says: ‘Will you fight, so that you will be killed, your wife will be remarried, and your wealth will be divided?’ The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Whoever does that, God has guaranteed him Paradise.’”"],[6525,"That his father came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked: “What are your children’s names?” He said: “ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā, Sabrah, and al-Ḥārith.” He said: “Do not name him ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā,” and he named him ʿAbd God. Then he said: “The best of names are ʿAbd God and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” And he supplicated for him and for his children, and they have remained in honor to this day. Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥajjāj b. al-Minhāl said: Khaythamah b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is one of them."],[6552,"Is our ʿUmrah for this year of ours or for ever and ever? The Messenger of God ﷺ interlaced his fingers, one over the other, and said, 'The ʿUmrah has been merged into the Hajj—twice. No, rather, for ever and ever.'"],[6553,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ during his illness and said, 'What do you think about a stray animal that comes to the watering trough of my camels—is there any reward for me if I give it water?' He said, 'Yes, in every warm liver there is a reward.'"],[6562,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us at al-Batha' and said: \"The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6563,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered ihram for both Hajj and 'Umrah together, and I heard him say: \"The 'Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6569,"He informed him that when the Messenger of God ﷺ left Makkah as an emigrant to Madinah, Quraysh offered a hundred she-camels to whoever brought him back. While I was sitting in the assembly of my people, a man came and said: By God, I have just seen three riders pass by me; I think it is Muhammad ﷺ. He said: I gestured to him to be quiet: they are only the sons of so-and-so seeking a stray animal of theirs. I stayed for a little while, then I got up, entered, and ordered that my horse be led to the bottom of the valley. I took out my weapons from behind my room, then took the divining arrows with which I sought omens and put on my armor. Then I brought out my divining arrows and drew omens, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. He said: I had been hoping to bring him back and take the hundred she-camels. So I mounted and followed his tracks. While my horse was galloping with me, it stumbled and I fell off. I took out my divining arrows and drew omens with them, and the arrow I disliked came out: that I would not harm him. But I refused anything except to follow him. I mounted my horse, and when the group appeared to me and I looked at them, my horse stumbled with me and its forelegs sank into the ground, and I fell off. It pulled out its forelegs and there followed them smoke like a staff. Then I knew that he had been protected from me and that he would prevail. So I called out to them: Wait for me, for by God I will not harm you, and nothing you dislike will come from me. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What do you want? I said: Write for me a document that will be a sign between me and you. He said: Write for him, O Abu Bakr. He said: So he wrote a document for me, then threw it to me. He said: I returned and kept silent, and did not mention anything of what had happened until God ﷻ granted His Messenger ﷺ victory over Makkah and he had finished with Hunayn. Then I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ to meet him, with the document he had written for me. While I was making for him, I entered among a battalion of the Ansar's battalions, and they began prodding me with their spears, saying: Away with you, away with you, until I drew near to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was on his she-camel. I looked at his shin in the stirrup as if it were a palm pith. I raised my hand with the document and said: O Messenger of God, this is your document. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A day of fulfillment and kindness. So I became a Muslim, and I brought him the sadaqah of my wealth."],[6570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed tamattu', and we performed tamattu' with him. It was said: O Messenger of God, is it for us or for ever? He said: For ever."],[6571,"I heard my father say: Suraqah b. Malik b. Ju'shum came from the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us such-and-such. A man said, as if mocking: Did he not teach you how to defecate? He said: Indeed, by the One who sent him with the truth, he commanded us to lean on the left foot and set up the right."],[6575,"From Ibn Shihab: In naming those who were martyred with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Khaybar among the Ansar, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Murrah b. Suraqah b. Hubab. Thus said Ibn Shihab."],[6581,"Two men passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was sitting and reminding. He said: Sit, for you are upon good. When the Messenger of God ﷺ got up and his companions dispersed from him, the two stood and said: O Messenger of God, you said to us: Sit, for you are upon good. Is that for us specifically or for the people generally? He said: No servant seeks knowledge except that it is an expiation for what came before."],[6587,"He used to say, \"Drink from the water dispenser of al-Abbas, for it is from the Sunnah.\""],[6588,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There is no ablution except from wind or sound.\""],[6605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whatever afflicts the crop of any of you from straying animals or birds, Allah records for him a reward for it.”"],[6606,"It is also said that he died in the year eighty-two."],[6652,"A woman entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “O ʿĀʾishah, do you know this one?” She said, “Yes.” Then she sang to her, and he said, “Satan has blown into her nostrils.”"],[6653,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bring out Abdullah b. Hanzalah from beneath the curtains of the Kaaba and kill him. Then he said, “No Qurayshi will be executed patiently after this.”"],[6657,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man behind him turning pebbles while he was in prayer and said, “Who turned the pebbles?” A man said, “I did.” He said, “That is your share of your prayer.”"],[6658,"I heard al-Sa'ib b. Yazid say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited a protective charm over me with the Opening of the Book, with a light spitting.”"],[6659,"The middle of al-Sa'ib's head was black while the rest of his head and his beard were white. I said to him, “O my master, by Allah I have never seen the like of this head of yours: this is white and this is black.” He said, “Shall I not inform you, O my son?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “I was with some boys playing when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me. I presented myself to him and greeted him. He said, ‘And upon you. Who are you?’ I said, ‘I am al-Sa'ib b. Yazid, the brother of al-Namir b. Qasit.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped my head and said, ‘May Allah bless you.’ He said, ‘By Allah, it will never turn white,’ or he said, ‘it will remain like this forever.’”"],[6660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed Hasan. Al-Aqra' b. Habis said to him, “I have ten children and have never kissed any of them.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah will not have mercy on one who does not have mercy on people.”"],[6661,"Go to that old man and say to him: My uncle Isa b. Talhah says to you: Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? So I went to him and he said, “Yes, I saw him ﷺ, and I entered upon him with some boys who were with me. We found him eating dates from a basket, and with him were some people from his companions. He took a handful of those dates for us and wiped our heads.”"],[6678,"He came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon on the pulpit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Have you prayed?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Pray two rak'ahs and keep them brief.\""],[6679,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Perform ablution from the meat of camels, but do not perform ablution from the meat of sheep. Pray in the sheep pens, but do not pray in the camels' resting places.\""],[6680,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ at the stones of oil, and he was muffled with his hands, supplicating.\""],[6683,"\"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by a witness and an oath.\""],[6684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is afflicted with a calamity, let him remember his calamity in me, for it is the greatest of calamities to him.\""],[6685,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat or the hollow of the neck?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6686,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat or the hollow of the neck?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6687,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, is slaughtering only in the throat?\" He said: \"If you were to stab it in its thigh, it would suffice you.\""],[6688,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the 'atirah and he deemed it good."],[6689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while my father was dying, and he spat on him from his head to his feet, and it was as if I were looking at the specks of saliva on his body."],[6690,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am the son of the 'Awatik.\""],[6691,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and I heard from his mouth to my ear. We carried wheat from al-Balqa' to Madinah and sold it, and we wanted to buy dates of Madinah, but they prevented us. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said to those who prevented us: \"Does it not suffice you that this food is cheap while these dates they are carrying are expensive? Leave them so they may carry it.\" Simuwayh was from al-Balqa', a Christian deacon who embraced Islam, and his Islam became good. He lived one hundred and twenty years."],[6692,"He was with al-Zinba' b. Salama al-Judhami, who became angry with him, so he castrated him and mutilated him. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke harshly to al-Zinba' and freed him from him. He said, \"Enjoin me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"I enjoin [you to be good to] every Muslim.\""],[6693,"I was in a district of Makkah, and a Muslim man came while I was among my sheep. I said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah.\" I said, \"Welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah and greetings. What do you want?\" He said, \"I want the zakat of your sheep.\" He said, \"So I brought him a ewe that had just given birth. When he looked at it, he said, 'Our due is not in this.' I said, 'Then in what is your due?' He said, 'In the thaniyyah and the jadha'ah that is fleshy.'\""],[6694,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases. The adhan is: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah. And the iqamah is in pairs."],[6695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhan and said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah. Then he would go back and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah."],[6696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the adhan of nineteen phrases and the iqamah of seventeen phrases."],[6697,"He was an orphan in the care of Abu Mahdhurah, who equipped him for Syria. He said: I said to Abu Mahdhurah, \"I am going to Syria, and I fear that I will be asked about your adhan.\" So he informed me that Abu Mahdhurah told him: He said: I went out with a group, and we were on part of the road when the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called to prayer in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We heard the voice of the mu'adhdhin while we were near him, and we shouted, imitating him, so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ might hear the voice. He sent for us, and we stood before him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Which of you is the one whose voice I heard raised?\" The people all pointed to me, and they were truthful. He sent them all away and detained me. He said, \"Get up and call the adhan for prayer.\" I got up, and nothing was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and what he commanded me. I stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he himself dictated the adhan to me. He said: Say: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah.\" Then he said to me, \"Go back and extend your voice, and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah.\" Then he called me when I had finished the adhan and gave me a purse containing some silver. Then he placed his hand on the forelock of Abu Mahdhurah, then passed it over his face from the front, then over his liver, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the purse of Abu Mahdhurah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah bless you and bless upon you.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, command me to call the adhan in Makkah.\" He said, \"I have already done so.\" Every feeling of dislike in my heart toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ vanished, and all of it turned into love for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to 'Attab b. Asid, the governor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and called the adhan for prayer with him by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dictated the adhan to me word by word: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah; Hayya 'ala al-salah, Hayya 'ala al-salah; Hayya 'ala al-falah, Hayya 'ala al-falah; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah.\""],[6700,"Abu Mahdhurah said: I went out with ten youths with the Prophet ﷺ to Hunayn, and they were the most hateful people to us. They called the adhan, and we stood mocking them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Bring me these youths.\" Then he said, \"Call the adhan.\" They called the adhan, and I was the last of them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes, this is the one whose voice I heard. Go and call the adhan for the people of Makkah, and tell 'Attab b. Asid that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to call the adhan for the people of Makkah.\" He wiped his forelock and said: Say: \"Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah twice; then go back and say: Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah, Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah twice; Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah, Ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah twice; Hayya 'ala al-salah twice; Hayya 'ala al-falah twice; Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illa Allah. And when you call the adhan for the first prayer of the morning, say: Al-salahu khayrun mina al-nawm, al-salahu khayrun mina al-nawm. And when you pronounce the iqamah, say twice: Qad qamat al-salah. Did you hear?\" Abu Mahdhurah did not cut his forelock or comb it because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had wiped over it. Abu al-Qasim 'Uthman, from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith, is 'Uthman b. al-Sa'ib, the mawla of Banu Jumah."],[6701,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me the Sunnah of the call to prayer. He wiped the front of his head and said: You say: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, raising your voice with it. Then you say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, lowering your voice with it. Then you raise your voice with the testimony, then you say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to success, Hasten to success. If it is the dawn prayer, you say: Prayer is better than sleep, Prayer is better than sleep. Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is no deity except Allah."],[6702,"Tell me about your father's call to prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He would begin and say the takbir, then say: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Hasten to the prayer, Hasten to the prayer, once each. Then he would return, saying: I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, until he came to the end of the call to prayer: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is no deity except Allah."],[6703,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the water supply to the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib and the custody of the Ka'bah to the Banu 'Abd al-Dar, and made the call to prayer for us and our clients.\""],[6704,"I used to give the call to prayer for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the dawn prayer, and when I said in the first call to prayer, 'Hasten to success,' I would say: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep."],[6705,"I heard Abu Mahdhura saying: I was a young boy, and I gave the call to prayer before the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. When I reached 'Hasten to the prayer, hasten to success,' the Prophet ﷺ said to me: Add to it: Prayer is better than sleep."],[6706,"I asked Abu Mahdhura: How did you give the call to prayer for the Prophet ﷺ? What did you make the end of your call to prayer? He said: I used to say the phrases of the call to prayer twice and the phrases of the iqamah twice, and I made the end of my call to prayer: there is no deity except Allah."],[6707,"\"The final words of the Adhan are: 'Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar; La ilaha illallah (Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, there is none worthy of worship except Allah.)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 649)"],[6708,"\"There is no deity except Allah, and Allah is the Greatest.\""],[6709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The muezzins are the trustees of the Muslims over their breaking the fast and their pre-dawn meal.\""],[6710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"When you give the call to prayer for Maghrib, let it descend with the sun, descending quickly.\""],[6711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"At sunset, watch for it with the sun.\""],[6712,"Abu Mahdhura had a forelock at the front of his head; when he sat, he would let it down and it would reach the ground. They said to him: Why don't you shave it? He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped it with his hand, and I will not shave it until I die.\" So he did not shave it until he died."],[6713,"I saw Abu Mahdhura and he had hair, so I said to him: Why don't you cut your hair? He said: \"I would not cut hair that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed his hand over.\""],[6714,"When I came to Abu Mahdhura, he would ask me about a certain man, and when I came to that man, he would ask me about Abu Mahdhura. So I said to Abu Mahdhura: When I come to you, you ask me about so-and-so, and when I come to him, he asks me about you. He said: I, Abu Hurayrah, and so-and-so were in a house, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'The last of you to die will be in the Fire.' Then Abu Hurayrah died, then Abu Mahdhura died, then the man died."],[6716,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, then said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so? Indeed, your companion is being held at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owes.”"],[6717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the prayers, then said, “Who is here from the clan of so-and-so? Indeed, your companion has been detained from Paradise because of a debt he owed. So either ransom him from the punishment of Allah or surrender him [to it].”"],[6718,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is there anyone here from Banu al-Najjar?” He called out three times and no one answered him. Then a man answered him, so he said, “Did you hear my call?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, so-and-so who died among you has been detained from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, ransom him, and if you wish, surrender him to the punishment of Allah.”"],[6719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, and when he finished, he said, “Is there anyone here from Banu al-Najjar?” He called out three times, and a man answered him on the third. He said, “Did you hear my call?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, your companion so-and-so has been detained from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, ransom him from the punishment of Allah, and if you wish, surrender him.”"],[6720,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the people and said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so?” The people remained silent, and whenever he began something with them they would remain silent. Then he said, “Is there anyone here from Banu so-and-so?” A man from the people said, “This is so-and-so.” He said, “Indeed, your companion is being held short of Paradise because of his debt.” A man from the people said, “His debt is upon me.”"],[6721,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral. When he finished, he said, “Is there anyone here from the family of so-and-so?” He said, “No one stood up until he said it three times. Then a man stood up and said, ‘I, O Messenger of Allah.’ The Prophet ﷺ said to him, ‘What prevented you from standing up on the first two times? Indeed, I did not call you by name except for good. Indeed, so-and-so died as a man held captive by his debt.’ He said, ‘I saw his family and those who were grieving over his affair.’ He said, ‘They paid off what he owed until nothing remained against him.’”"],[6723,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever narrates a hadith from me while he thinks it is false is one of the liars.”"],[6724,"“From the Prophet ﷺ that he addressed the people and forbade [drinking from] gourds and vessels smeared with pitch.”"],[6725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wear these white garments and shroud your dead in them, for they are purer and better.”"],[6726,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Wear white, for indeed it is very pure and cleaner, and shroud your dead in it.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2810)"],[6727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Wear white garments, for they are better and purer, and shroud your dead in them.”"],[6728,"“The best of your garments are those which are white, so shroud your dead in them, and wear them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1472)"],[6729,"“A woman died in her postpartum bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed over her and stood at her middle.”"],[6730,"“The Prophet ﷺ prayed over a woman and stood at her middle.”"],[6731,"“A woman died in childbirth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over her and stood at her middle.”"],[6732,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Asking is like a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it.”"],[6733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Asking is only scratches with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that he asks a man of authority or in a matter from which he finds no alternative.”"],[6734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “These askings are like a scratching with which one of you scrapes his face, except that a man asks a man of authority or a matter from which he has no alternative.”"],[6735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “These askings are like a scratching with which a man scrapes his face, except that he asks a man of authority or in a matter from which he finds no alternative.”"],[6736,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks a man of authority or in a matter from which there is no alternative.”"],[6737,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face. So whoever wishes may keep his face, and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks a man of authority or in a matter from which there is no alternative.”"],[6738,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “These askings are only a scratching with which a man scrapes his face.”"],[6739,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ‘ids: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6740,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ‘ids: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to “recite in the Friday prayer: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the narration of the Overwhelming?’”"],[6742,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6743,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” in the first, and in the second “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6744,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two Eids: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” in the first, and in the second “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6745,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the Friday prayer: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[6746,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from splitting a leather strap between his fingers."],[6747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loses an item and finds it in the possession of a particular man, he has more right to it, and the buyer returns to the seller for the price.”"],[6748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two months do not complete sixty days.”"],[6749,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Two months do not complete sixty days.”"],[6750,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best thing by which you treat yourselves is cupping.\""],[6751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a barber and had him shaved with a razor and a blade. An Arab man from the tribe of Banu Fazara saw this and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why do you let him cut your flesh?\" He ﷺ said, \"Do you not know the benefit and the best thing you can use for treatment?\""],[6752,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he called a cupper and ordered him to cup him. He brought out his cupping horns and applied them to him, then made an incision with the tip of a blade and let the blood flow into a vessel he had. A man from Banu Fazara entered upon him and said, “What is this, O Messenger of Allah? Why do you allow this one to cut your skin?” He said, “This is cupping.” He said, “It is the best treatment people use.”"],[6754,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon, interrupting his sermon. He turned to him, and he was to his right, and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about lizards?” He said, “A community of the Children of Israel was transformed. Allah knows best into which animals it was transformed.”"],[6755,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “What do you say about lizards?” He said, “A community of the Children of Israel was transformed. Allah knows best which animals were transformed.”"],[6757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most beloved speech to Allah, Exalted is He, is four: ‘There is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, Glory be to Allah, and Praise be to Allah.’ It does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[6758,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The most beloved speech to Allah ﷻ is: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. It does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[6759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not name your boy Yasar, nor Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, for you will say, 'Is he there?' and he will not be, so it will be said, 'No.' They are only four, so do not add to them.”"],[6760,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not name your slave Rabah, nor Najih, nor Aflah, nor Yasar.”"],[6761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from naming our slaves with four names: Nafi', Aflah, Rabah, and Yasar."],[6762,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in prayer during a solar eclipse, and no voice was heard from him.”"],[6763,"One of us said to his companion: “Come with us, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will surely speak to us today about the solar eclipse, concerning his Ummah.” We reached the mosque and found it filled to capacity. That coincided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming out. He came forward and prayed with the people while we were behind him. He stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed with us for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated with us for the longest prostration, and we heard no voice from him. Then in the second rak'ah he did the same, and the clearing of the sun coincided with the sitting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He then finished, praised Allah, extolled Him, bore witness that there is no god but Allah, and bore witness that he is His servant and Messenger. Then he said: “O people, I am only a human messenger. I remind you by Allah: if you know that I have fallen short in conveying any of the messages of my Lord, then tell me, for I have conveyed the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed. And if I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then why do you not tell me?” They said: “We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.” Then he said: “To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and this moon, or the disappearance of stars from their rising places, is due to the death of great men of the earth. They have lied. But they are signs among the signs of Allah by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. I was shown while standing in prayer what you will encounter in this world and the Hereafter. The Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Tahya, an old man of the Ansar who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him and affirms him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and denies him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. The believers will be besieged in Bayt al-Maqdis with a severe siege and pressed with severe pressure.” Al-Aswad b. Qays said: “And I think he said: 'Isa b. Maryam ﷺ will appear among them, and Allah will defeat him and his armies, until the base of a wall and the branch of a tree will call out to the believer, saying: 'Here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him.' That will not happen until you see matters of your own affair growing grave in your souls, until you ask among yourselves: 'Did your Prophet mention anything of this?' And until mountains move from their places. Then upon that comes the seizing, the seizing.'” Ibn al-Mubarak said: “i.e., death.”"],[6764,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “While I and a boy from the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the sun rose and was in the eye of the beholder about a spear or two spears from the horizon, then darkened until it became like a colocynth. One of us said to his companion: 'Come with us to the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ, for by Allah, he will surely speak to us today about the matter of this sun regarding his Ummah.' We went to the mosque and met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he came out to the people. He came forward and prayed. He stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed with us for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated with us for the longest prostration he ever prostrated with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he stood and led us in another rak'ah like it. Then he sat, and his sitting coincided with the clearing of the sun. He said the taslim and turned around, praised Allah and extolled Him. Then he said: 'O people, I remind you by Allah: if you know that I have conveyed the message of my Lord, then tell me. And if you know that I have fallen short in conveying anything of the message of my Lord, then tell me.' They said: 'We bear witness that you have conveyed the message of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.' Then he said: 'To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon and the disappearance of stars from their rising places is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth. They have lied. But they are only signs of Allah by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. By Allah, I saw what you will encounter in the affairs of your world and your Hereafter from the time I stood to pray. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Yahya, an old man of the Ansar who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him and affirms him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and fights him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. He will drive the people to Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be besieged with a severe siege.'” He said: “And I think he said: 'Isa b. Maryam will appear among them and kill him and his armies, until the stone or the base of a wall will call out: O Muslim, or O believer, here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him. That will not happen until you see great matters whose gravity grows in your souls, and you ask among yourselves: Did your Prophet ﷺ mention anything of them to you?' Then he said: 'Immediately after that comes the seizing.'”"],[6765,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “While I and a boy from the Ansar were shooting at two targets of ours in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the sun was about two or three spears' length in the eye of the beholders from the horizon, it darkened until it became like a colocynth. One of us said to his companion: 'Come with us to the mosque, for by Allah, the matter of this sun will surely cause the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak to his Ummah.' We went to the mosque and found it packed, that is, full. We met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he came out to the people. He came forward and stood with us for the longest standing he ever stood with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he bowed for the longest bowing he ever bowed with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then he prostrated for the longest prostration he ever prostrated with us in prayer, and we heard no voice from him. Then in the second rak'ah he did the same, and the clearing of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak'ah. He said the taslim, then praised Allah and extolled Him, and bore witness that there is no god but He and that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: 'O people, I am only a human messenger. I adjure you by Allah: if you know that I have fallen short in conveying any of the messages of my Lord, then tell me—so that I may convey the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed. And if you know that I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then why do you not tell me?' The people stood and said: 'We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your Ummah, and fulfilled what was upon you.' Then they fell silent. Then he said: 'To proceed: some men claim that the eclipse of this sun and the eclipse of this moon and the disappearance of these stars from their rising places is due to the death of great men of the people of the earth. They have lied. But they are only signs among the signs of Allah ﷻ by which He causes His servants to take heed, to see who among them will turn in repentance. By Allah, I saw from the time I stood to pray what you will encounter in the affairs of your world and your Hereafter. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, with his left eye effaced, resembling the eye of Abu Tahya, an old man of the Ansar at that time who lived between him and the room of Aisha. Whenever he emerges, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him, affirms him, and follows him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and denies him, he will not be punished for any deed he did before. He will appear over all the earth except the Haram and Bayt al-Maqdis. He will besiege the Muslims in Bayt al-Maqdis, and they will be pressed with severe pressure. Then Allah will destroy him and his armies, until the base of a wall and the root of a tree will say: O believer, or O Muslim, here is a disbeliever, come and kill him. That will not happen until you see great matters whose gravity grows in your souls, then you ask among yourselves: Did your Prophet ﷺ mention anything of them to you? And until mountains move from their places. Then immediately after that comes the seizing.' He closed his fingers and gestured right and left. Then I attended a sermon of Samura in which he mentioned this hadith, and he did not advance a word or delay it from its place.”"],[6766,"“The Prophet ﷺ ruled in favor of the neighbor.”"],[6767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house and the land than anyone else.”"],[6768,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house than anyone else.”"],[6769,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the right of preemption of the house.”"],[6770,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6771,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of the neighbor.”"],[6772,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6773,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The neighbor of the house has more right to the house.”"],[6774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6777,"“Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him, and whoever mutilates (his slave) we will mutilate him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2663)"],[6778,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6780,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him.”"],[6781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we will mutilate him; and whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him.”"],[6885,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Dajjal will appear. His left eye is blind, with a thick growth over it. He will heal the born-blind and the leper, bring the dead to life, and say to people: ‘I am your lord.’ Whoever says, ‘You are my lord’ has been tried; and whoever says, ‘My Lord is God’ and remains on that until he dies will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal, and there will be no trial upon him. He will remain on earth as long as God wills, then Jesus son of Mary will come from the west, affirming Muhammad ﷺ, and will kill the Dajjal. Indeed, it is the coming of the Hour.”"],[6901,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from cutting a leather strap between his two fingers."],[6902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every boy is held in pledge for his aqiqah, to be slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, his head shaved, and he is named.”"],[6907,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The neighbor of a house has the greater right to its preemption.”"],[6908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pause twice: when he entered the prayer, and when he finished the recitation. Imran b. Husayn rejected that, so they wrote about it to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, and he wrote back to them that Samurah spoke the truth."],[6909,"A man manumitted six slaves of his at the time of death while he had no property other than them, so the Prophet ﷺ cast lots among them and freed two and kept four enslaved."],[6910,"The Prophet ﷺ used to forbid mutilation and urge giving charity."],[6926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that an animal be tied up and shot, and that its flesh be eaten if it was tied up and shot."],[6930,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People have not given charity anything like knowledge that is spread.\""],[6931,"\"O Messenger of God, I saw as if a bucket was lowered from the sky. Abu Bakr ؓ came and took hold of its rope, and drank a weak drink. Then Umar ؓ came and took hold of its rope until he was filled. Then Uthman ؓ came and took hold of its rope and drank until he was filled. Then Ali ؓ came and took hold of its rope, but it slipped from him and spilled on him.\""],[6932,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid mutilation and urge charity.\""],[6933,"\"A bowl of tharid was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and placed before the people, and they took turns with it from early morning until noon; people would get up and others would sit down.\" A man said to Samurah, \"Was it replenished?\" Samurah said, \"From what thing are you amazed? It was not replenished except from here,\" and he gestured with his hand toward the sky."],[6936,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among them are those whom the Fire will take up to their ankles, and among them are those whom it will take up to their waist, and among them are those whom it will take up to their collarbone.\""],[6937,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[6943,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Adhere to these white garments; let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them.\" Ibn 'Ulayyah did not mention Abu al-Muhallab."],[6944,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it the next day at its time.\""],[6959,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the children of the polytheists, and he said: \"They are the servants of the people of Paradise.\""],[7031,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: 'Do not go out to meet the caravans before they reach their market.'"],[7032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'Do not sell on behalf of the Bedouins, even if one of you is his brother or his father or his mother.'"],[7033,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Whoever sells land or a house, the neighbor of the land or the neighbor of the house has more right to buy it if he meets its price.”"],[7034,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “If a woman is married off and two different men wish to marry her, both of them guardians, the one with the most right among the two suitors is the first of them. And in a sale, if two men purchase the same item, the one with the most right to it is the first of them.”"],[7035,"The Prophet ﷺ used to forbid shighar (exchange marriage) with women."],[7037,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking his ruling about eating lizard. He said: “I neither command nor forbid anyone regarding it, except that we, the family of Muhammad, do not eat it.”"],[7038,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us one night, while we were encamped at a pit, from eating the meat of domestic donkeys, and he ordered us to use the meat we had with us, so we threw it away."],[7039,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “By God, it would not please me to have Mount Uhud all in gold and then bequeath it.”"],[7040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “One of you on the day he dies has three companions: among them one who withholds from him what he asks—that is his wealth; among them a companion who goes with him until he enters the grave but gives him nothing and does not accompany him after that—those are his relatives; and among them a companion who says, ‘By God, I am going with you wherever you go, and I will never part from you’—that is his deeds, whether they be good or evil.”"],[7041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say to us: “You will be gathered to Jerusalem, then you will assemble on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7042,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid any of us from cutting a leather strap between two fingers,” saying: “In that there are two eyes.”"],[7043,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “When a man disputes with another and one of them calls his companion to the Messenger to judge between them, whoever refuses to come has no right.”"],[7044,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the believing men and believing women, and for the Muslim men and Muslim women, every Friday.”"],[7045,"When we were caught by rain while traveling and the call to prayer was made, the Messenger of God ﷺ, out of dislike that he should cause us hardship, would order the muezzin to say: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[7046,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: \"Indeed, I get angry with you and excuse you, then I supplicate to Allah between me and Him, 'O Allah, do not punish them, curse them, or be angry with them. Rather, make them a source of blessing, mercy, forgiveness, and prayer for them, for they are my people and I am their well-wisher.\""],[7047,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “The false messiah (al-Masīḥ al-Dajjāl) is blind in the left eye, upon which there is a thick white film. He will heal the blind from birth and the leper, bring the dead to life, and say: ‘I am your Lord.’ Whoever takes refuge in God and says: ‘My Lord is God,’ then refuses that until he dies, no punishment or trial will be upon him. But whoever says: ‘You are my Lord,’ has been tried.” And the Prophet ﷺ said: “The false messiah will remain on earth for as long as God wills, then Jesus son of Mary ﷺ will come from the east, confirming Muhammad ﷺ and following his religion, then he will kill the false messiah.”"],[7048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Before the Hour comes, you will see things you will find gravely objectionable, and you will say: ‘We are destroyed. Were we told of this?’ When you see that, remember God Almighty and know that they are the beginnings of the Hour.” He even said: “You will see mountains move before the time of the Cry.” And he used to tell us: “The Hour will not come until the stone points out a Jew who is hiding: a Muslim man will be chasing him, and he will look ahead and hide, then the stone will say: ‘O servant of God, this is the one you seek.’”"],[7049,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “In this world there is no regret except in three cases: a man who had irrigation and a water-drawing camel with which he watered his land. When his land’s thirst became severe and its fruits emerged, his camel died, and he feels regret for the camel that he had trained to draw water, since he will not find its like, and he feels regret for the fruit of his land, lest it spoil before he can contrive a plan for it. And a man who had a swift horse and met a gathering of disbelievers. When they drew near to one another, the enemies of God fled, and the man raced ahead on his horse. But when he was about to catch up, his horse broke down and left him standing beside it, so he feels regret for his horse, since he will not find its like, and he feels regret for the victory that had been within his reach. And a man who has a wife whose appearance and religion please him, and she gives birth to a boy but dies in childbirth. He feels regret for his wife, thinking he will never find her like, and he feels regret for her child, fearing that he will perish neglected before he can find a wet-nurse for him.” He said: “And this last is the greatest of those regrets.”"],[7050,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to order the Emigrants and the Helpers to be in the front rows, and he would say: “They are more knowledgeable about the prayer than the Bedouins and the foolish. Those behind them follow them, and I do not like the Bedouins to be in front of them, not knowing how to pray.”"],[7051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a tree standing on a single trunk; the width of its trunk is a journey of seventy years.”"],[7052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to tell us: “The name of the believing man in the [earlier] books is al-karm (generosity), because of what God has honored him with over creation. But you call the wall of grapevines al-karm, whereas its name is al-ḥafr (the trench), and it is the man who is al-karm.”"],[7053,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Al-Firdaws is the middle hill of Paradise, the highest and most beautiful of it.”"],[7054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “I do not find any kind of beast of which a single one is better than a hundred of its fellows, except the man who finds [another] man: he is better than a hundred men.”"],[7055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Whoever mortgages land for a debt he owes, he shall repay from its produce what remains after its expenses, and he shall repay that from that time what he owes, after accounting for the owner’s work and expenses with justice.”"],[7056,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us on the day he arrived at the Hijr of Thamud, at a well near the side of the city, from drinking from it or watering with it, and he forbade us from entering their dwellings. And he informed us that the young of the she-camel ascended a mountain that I heard people call Kinanah, and that its track is clearly visible on its slope."],[7057,"When the Prophet ﷺ went on a military expedition or a journey and then returned to Madinah, he would say: “Returning to our Lord, praising our Lord, worshipping our Lord.”"],[7058,"A man once said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: When the confederates come, forbid the people of Madinah from irrigating the palm trees. He replied: “If I were to make things forbidden for you, you would be ruined. Indeed, the prohibitions of the prophets are things mountains cannot bear.”"],[7059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of extremism and haughtiness, for many of the Children of Israel went to extremes, to the point that a short woman would make two wooden clogs, stuff them, then put her feet into them. Then she would go with a tall woman, and when they walked together, she would be equal to her or even taller.”"],[7060,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, he would say: “O Allah, send down upon our land its adornment. O Allah, send down upon our land its tranquility.”"],[7061,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: Banu Ghifar and Aslam were a great trial for many people, who said, ‘If there were any good in them, Allah would not have made them the first to accept it.’ But Ghifar—may Allah forgive it—and Aslam—may Allah grant it peace."],[7062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “One of you will soon wish to look at me even once, giving all his family and wealth for it.”"],[7063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “Soon you will be among the people like salt in food; food is only good with salt.”"],[7064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should kill a captive of his companion once he has taken him.”"],[7065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “There is none among you but that I am holding onto his waist-wrapper to keep him from falling into the Fire.”"],[7066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to us: “Whoever of you is killed while steadfast, advancing, and being killed in the cause of Allah—he is in Paradise.”"],[7067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the battle cry of the Emigrants ‘O Banu Abd al-Rahman,’ the battle cry of the Khazraj ‘O Banu Abd Allah,’ and the battle cry of the Aws ‘O Banu Ubayd Allah.’ And he named our horses ‘the horses of Allah’ when we were alarmed.”"],[7068,"When we were alarmed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command us to come together, remain steadfast, and be calm, and when we fought."],[7069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “Indeed my Ummah is a community, seventy thousand of them will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[7070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"I would enter this room, only fearing that there may be wealth in it that I have not spent before I die.\""],[7071,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “We are people of the desert and livestock. Do we need to perform ablution after eating camel meat and drinking its milk?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “Do we need to perform ablution after eating sheep meat and drinking its milk?” He said: “No.”"],[7072,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us for one of the two daytime prayers, Zuhr or Asr, carrying al-Hasan or al-Husayn. He came forward and placed him by his right foot, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated and lengthened the prostration. I raised my head from among the people and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating while the boy was riding on his back. I returned to prostration. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, people said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you prostrated in this prayer a prostration you never used to do. Was it something you were commanded to do, or was revelation coming to you?” He said: “None of that. But my son climbed on me, and I disliked to rush him until he finished his need.”"],[7073,"A man from the Bedouins came to the Prophet ﷺ, believed in him and followed him, and said: “I will emigrate with you.” The Prophet ﷺ instructed his Companions to look after him. When it was the battle of Khaybar – or he said Hunayn – the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired some spoils and distributed them, and allotted a share for him. He gave his Companions what he had allotted for him, and the man was tending their riding animals. When he came, they handed it to him. He said: “What is this?” They said: “A share the Prophet ﷺ allotted for you.” He took it and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muhammad, what is this?” He said: “A share I allotted for you.” He said: “It is not for this that I followed you. I followed you so that I may be shot here,” and he pointed to his throat with an arrow, “and die and enter Paradise.” He ﷺ said: “If you are truthful to Allah, He will be truthful to you.” They waited a little, then they went out to fight the enemy. He was brought back carried, having been struck by an arrow where he had pointed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Is it he?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “He was truthful to Allah, so He was truthful to him.” Then the Prophet ﷺ shrouded him in the Prophet’s own jubbah, then brought him forward and prayed over him. Among what was heard of his prayer over him was: “O Allah, this is Your servant who went out as an emigrant in Your path and was killed as a martyr, and I am a witness for him.”"],[7074,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him for emigration, then fell ill. He ﷺ said: “What is the matter with you, O Shaddad?” I said: “I am ill, O Messenger of Allah. If I could drink from the water of Batha, I would recover.” He said: “What prevents you?” I said: “My emigration.” He said: “Go, for you are an emigrant wherever you are.”"],[7075,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took his hand, and it was softer than silk and cooler than snow."],[7106,"“The wise man is the one who takes account of himself and strives for that which is after death. And the helpless man is the one who follows his own whims then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4260)"],[7107,"I said, “O Messenger of God, how were you taken on the Night Journey?” He said, “I prayed the evening prayer with my companions in Makkah, delaying it. Then Jibrīl ﷺ came to me with a white riding beast, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule. He said, ‘Mount.’ It was difficult for me, so he turned it by its ear, then mounted me upon it. It set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. We came to a land with palm trees. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. Then we mounted. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God knows best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Yathrib; you prayed in Ṭībah.’ Then it set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. We came to a white land. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. Then we mounted. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God knows best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Madyan; you prayed at the tree of Mūsā.’ Then it set off moving swiftly with us; its hooves landed wherever its gaze reached. Then we reached a land whose palaces appeared to us. He said, ‘Dismount.’ I dismounted. Then he said, ‘Pray.’ I prayed. He said, ‘Do you know where you prayed?’ I said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You prayed in Bayt Laḥm, where ʿĪsā the Messiah, son of Maryam ﷺ , was born.’ Then he took me until we entered the city from its Yemeni gate. He came to the qiblah of the mosque and tied his mount. We entered the mosque through a gate where the sun inclines. I prayed in the mosque as much as God willed. I was overcome by the most intense thirst I had ever experienced. Then two vessels were brought to me, in one of them milk and in the other honey. They were both sent to me. I balanced between them, then God ﷻ guided me, and I took the milk and drank until it struck my forehead. Before me was an old man leaning on a cushion of his. He said, ‘Your companion has taken the natural disposition; indeed he is guided.’ Then he took me until we came to the valley that is in the city, and behold, Hell was uncovered like carpets. We said, ‘O Messenger of God, how did you find it?’ He said, ‘Like hot bathwater.’ Then he returned with me, and we passed by a caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such a place. They had lost a camel of theirs, and so-and-so had gathered them. I greeted them, and some of them said, ‘This is the voice of Muhammad ﷺ.’ Then I came to my companions before dawn in Makkah. Abu Bakr ؓ came to me and said, ‘O Messenger of God, where were you tonight? I looked for you in your place.’ He said, ‘Do you know that I went to the Aqsa Mosque tonight?’ He said, ‘O Messenger of God, it is a month’s journey; describe it to me.’ Then its image was opened for me, as if I were looking at it. They did not ask me about anything except that I informed them of it. Abu Bakr ؓ said, ‘I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God.’ The polytheists said, ‘Look at Ibn Abī Kabshah, claiming that he came to the Aqsa Mosque tonight.’ He said, ‘Among the signs of what I tell you is that I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such a place, led by a gray camel with a black saddlecloth and two black sacks.’ When that day came, the people looked out, and around midday the caravan came led by that same camel described by the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[7120,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “There will come upon you leaders who will delay the prayer beyond its proper times, so pray the prayer at its proper time and make your prayer with them a voluntary one.”"],[7121,"More than one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, among them Shaddad b. Aws and Thawban, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The pen is lifted from the minor until he grows up, from the sleeping person until he wakes, from the insane until he regains his senses, and from the feeble-minded imbecile.”"],[7122,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When people hoard dinars and dirhams, hoard these words: O God, I ask You for steadfastness in the affair and determination upon right guidance, and I ask You for gratitude for Your blessing and excellence in worshipping You, and I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know, and I seek Your forgiveness for what You know.”"],[7123,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O people, indeed this world is a passing enjoyment, from which the righteous and the wicked both eat, and indeed the Hereafter is a true promise, in which a Mighty King will judge, by which He will establish the truth and nullify falsehood. O people, be people of the Hereafter, and do not be people of this world, for every child follows its mother.”"],[7131,"He would hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a matter involving hardship, then he would go out to his desert land, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would later grant a concession in it, and the concession would be preserved from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in that matter. Abu Dharr would not hear it, so Abu Dharr would adhere to the first command that he had heard before that.”"],[7136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you leave your heirs wealthy, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people. You will not spend any expense seeking the Face of Allah except that you will be rewarded for it, even what you place in your wife’s mouth.”"],[7149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.'"],[7150,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: There is no servant who, when he enters upon morning and when he enters upon evening, says: O Allah, You are my Lord. There is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I acknowledge Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive my sins, for none forgives them but You - if he dies that day, he will enter Paradise, and if he dies that night, he will enter Paradise."],[7151,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning leadership and he said: The first part of leadership is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment from Allah on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who shows mercy and acts justly. And he said, moving his hand like this and like this regarding wealth, then he fell silent for as long as Allah willed, then he said: 'How can there be justice when it comes to relatives?'"],[7152,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not inform you of the chief of seeking forgiveness?' They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'O Allah, there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge to You Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge to You my sins, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. No one says it when evening falls and then dies that night except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and no one says it when morning comes and then death comes to him except that Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"],[7153,"‘The cupper and the one for whom cupping is done both break their fast.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1679)"],[7176,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up after two rakʿahs of prayer and did not sit until he finished his prayer; then he prostrated twice, then he said the salām.”"],[7180,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a wen on my palm and said: O Prophet of God, this wen has harmed me; it comes between me and the grip of the sword when I wish to grasp it, and between me and the rein of the mount. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Come close to me.” So I came close to him. He said: “Open your hand.” So I opened it. Then he said: “Close it.” So I closed it. He said: “Come close to me.” So I came close to him. He said: “Open it.” So I opened it. He then blew on my palm, placed his hand on the wen, and kept rubbing it with his palm until he lifted his hand, and I could see no trace of it."],[7181,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had finished with the people of Badr, bringing a colt of my mare called al-Qarḥāʾ. I said: O Muhammad, I have brought you the colt of al-Qarḥāʾ so that you may take it. He said: “I have no need for it, but if you wish, I can give you in exchange for it the select coats of mail from Badr.” I said: I would not exchange it today for anything else. He said: “I have no need for it.” Then he said: “O Dhū al-Jawshan, will you not become a Muslim, so that you may be among the first of this affair?” I said: No. He said: “Why?” I said: I have seen your people making light of you. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said in his narration: making a game of you. He said: “How did the news of their defeats at Badr reach you?” I said: It has reached me. He said: “Would it surprise you?” I said: Yes — only if you gain mastery over the Kaʿbah and settle in it. He said: “Perhaps, if you live, you will see that.” Then he said: “O Bilāl, take the man's saddlebag and provision him with some ʿajwah dates.” When I turned to leave, he said: “Indeed, he is among the best horsemen of Banū ʿĀmir.” By God, I was still with my family at al-Fawr when a rider approached. I said: From where? He said: From Makkah. I said: What have the people done? He said: By God, Muhammad ﷺ has gained mastery over it and settled in it. I said: May my mother be bereft of me! By God, if I had become a Muslim on that day and then asked him for al-Ḥīrah, he would have granted it to me as a fief. Abu Muslim said: Musaddad said: It has reached me from Ibn al-Mubārak that he said: His name was Shuraḥbīl, and he was called Dhū al-Jawshan only because he was prominent in the chest."],[7184,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter Paradise by his deeds.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy and grace from Him.”"],[7185,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “None of you will enter Paradise by his deeds.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy.”"],[7186,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is not one among you whom his deeds will cause to enter Paradise.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, unless God envelops me in mercy from Him.”"],[7187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is none of you but has a devil.” They said: Not even you, O Messenger of God? He said: “Not even I, except that God helped me against it, so it submitted.”"],[7188,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no one but has a devil.” They said: And you? He said: “And me, except that God helped me against it.”"],[7189,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever commits adultery, faith departs from him; whoever drinks wine without being forced or compelled, faith departs from him; and whoever plunders a spoil that people keep looking at, faith departs from him — but if he repents, God will turn to him.”"],[7190,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, teach me a supplication for protection with which I may seek refuge. He took my hand and said: Say: I seek refuge in You from the evil of my self, from the evil of my hearing, from the evil of my sight, from the evil of my tongue, from the evil of my heart, and from my manī. Then he said to me: “Memorize it.” Saʿd said: Manī is his semen."],[7191,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: Four people will torment the inhabitants of the Fire on top of the torment they already have; they run between the ḥamīm and the jaḥīm, calling out with woe and destruction. The inhabitants of the Fire say to one another: What is the matter with these ones? They have tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He said: One is a man with a chest of embers locked upon him; one is a man dragging his intestines; one is a man whose mouth flows with pus and blood; and one is a man eating his own flesh. It will be said to the one with the chest: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He will say: The distant one died while people's wealth was on his neck, and we find no settlement or repayment for it. Then it will be said to the one dragging his intestines: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. It will be said: The distant one did not care if urine got on him and did not wash it. Then it will be said to the one whose mouth flows with pus and blood: What is the matter with the distant one? He has tormented us on top of the torment we already have. He will say: The distant one used to eat the flesh of people."],[7192,"Umar (said): “A man came who would testify only to truth.” He said: “I saw an ugly sight and a dazzling display.” He said: “So Umar flogged them the prescribed punishment.”"],[7193,"He went early to the mosque and sat by one of the rooms of the Prophet ﷺ. He heard his voice, and he said: “Abu Yahya?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Enter.” He entered, and the Prophet ﷺ was having lunch. He said: “Come to lunch.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I intend to fast.” He said: “And I intend to fast. Our muezzin has weak eyesight; he called the adhan before dawn.”"],[7194,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir on the days of tashriq from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until he left Mina.”"],[7195,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir on the days of tashriq until he left Mina, saying the takbir after every prayer.”"],[7196,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Salm b. Abi al-Dhayyal, from Abu Sinan, a man from the people of Madinah who heard Jabir b. Abd Allah narrate from Shihab, a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who used to reside in Egypt, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever conceals the private shame of a believer, it is as if he has brought a dead person back to life.”"],[7197,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had placed his hand on his thigh, pointing with his index finger and saying: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.”"],[7198,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Umm Mildam (fever) eats the flesh and drinks the blood; its cold and its heat are from Hell.”"],[7199,"He heard Anas b. Malik, Shu'ayb b. Amr, and Najiyah b. Amr say: “We saw the Prophet ﷺ dye (his hair).”"],[7200,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Tell me about a man who committed all sins, leaving none of them, and along with that he did not leave any need or desire but that he fulfilled it. Is there any repentance for him?” He said: “Have you embraced Islam?” He said: “As for me, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that you are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Yes, do good deeds and abandon evil deeds, and Allah will turn them all into good deeds for you.” He said: “And my treacheries and my immoralities?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Allah is greatest,” and he kept saying the takbir until he disappeared."],[7201,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is not ashamed of what he said or what was said to him, then he is not of sound maturity; his mother bore him without purity.”"],[7202,"The Prophet ﷺ seated me behind him and said: “Do you not recite to me something of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Go on.” So I recited to him one hundred verses, or one hundred rhyming lines; every time I came to a verse or a rhyming line, he said: “Go on.”"],[7203,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “Do you have with you anything of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Go on.” So I recited a verse to him, and he kept saying: “Go on.” I recited a verse to him, and he kept saying: “Go on,” and I kept reciting to him until I had recited one hundred verses."],[7204,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Do you have any poetry with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then recite something to me.\" So I recited one verse, then I stopped. He said, \"Go on.\" So I recited one verse, then I stopped. He said, \"Go on.\" So I recited one verse, until I had recited one hundred verses, then I stopped and he was silent."],[7205,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had let his lower garment hang down, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Raise your lower garment.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of God, I am bow-legged; my knees knock together.\" He said, \"Raise your lower garment, for all of God's creation is beautiful.\" After that, the man was not seen except with his lower garment reaching halfway down his shins."],[7206,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man letting his lower garment hang down, so he hurried towards him or hastened towards him and said, \"Raise your lower garment and fear God.\" The man said, \"I have bow legs; my knees knock together.\" He said, \"All of God's creation is beautiful.\" He said, \"After that, the man was not seen except with his lower garment reaching halfway down his shins or hitting the middle of his shins.\" Asad b. Musa did not mention in his hadith the uncertainty about 'Amr b. al-Sharid and Ya'qub b. 'Asim."],[7207,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was sitting like this, leaning on the back of his hand behind his back, and said, \"This is the sitting posture of those upon whom is [God's] wrath.\""],[7208,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man who had sat down and leaned on his left hand, and he said, \"This is the sitting posture of those upon whom is [God's] wrath.\""],[7209,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"If one of you drinks [intoxicants], flog him. If he repeats, flog him. Then if he repeats, flog him. Then if he repeats a fourth time, kill him.\""],[7210,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever kills a sparrow in vain, it will cry out to God on the Day of Resurrection, saying, 'O Lord, this servant of Yours killed me in vain and did not kill me for any benefit.'\""],[7212,"A leper came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, so I went to him and mentioned him. He said, \"Go to him and inform him that I have accepted his pledge, so let him return.\""],[7213,"\"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks.\""],[7214,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Delay by a wealthy person makes his honor and punishment permissible.\""],[7215,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Delay by a wealthy person makes his honor and punishment permissible.\" Sufyan said, \"Makes his honor permissible means that one may complain about him, and his punishment means his imprisonment. The correct reading is Wabar b. Abi Dulaylah, with a damma on the dal. Al-Nu'man b. 'Abd al-Salam narrated it from Sufyan and said, \"'Amr, from Wabar b. Abi Dalilah,\" with a fatha on the dal."],[7216,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking about something concerning camels. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Slaughter the fat one, ride the thin one, milk on the day of watering, and enter Paradise in peace.\""],[7217,"A woman was stoned during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we finished with her, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'We have stoned this wicked woman.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The stoning is an expiation for what she did.'"],[7218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him.'"],[7219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him.' I said to 'Umar, 'What is al-saqab?' He said, 'Neighborliness.'"],[7220,"The Prophet ﷺ would grant preemption in a well, a house, and a walled garden before it was divided."],[7221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The neighbor has more right to what is adjacent to him, as long as he is in greater need of it.'"],[7222,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my mother bequeathed that a slave be freed on her behalf, and I have a black female servant.' He said, 'Call her.' She came, and he said, 'Who is your Lord?' She said, 'Allah.' He said, 'Who am I?' She said, 'The Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Then free her, for she is a believer.'"],[7223,"Al-Sharid came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I vowed that if Allah granted you victory over Makkah, I would pray in Jerusalem.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Pray here,' three times."],[7224,"While al-Sharid was walking between Mina and the mountain pass during the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he performed, he said: I heard the sound of a camel behind me, so I turned and it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He recognized me and said, 'Al-Sharid?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Shall I carry you behind me, O Sharid?' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, though I am not tired or exhausted, but I seek blessing in riding with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'O Sharid, do you have any of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt?' I said, 'I am the best of people in narrating it.' He said, 'Recite.' So I recited, and whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was silent, I stopped, and whenever he said, 'Continue,' I recited until it went on for a long time. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah has knowledge of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt.'"],[7225,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb died, may Allah have mercy on him, nine years into the rule of 'Uthman ؓ, and Abu Sufyan b. Harb had lost his sight."],[7226,"In that year Abu Sufyan Sakhr b. Harb died, and he was eighty-eight years old, meaning in the year thirty-one."],[7227,"Umayyah said to me, 'O Abu Sufyan, shall we go ahead of the caravan and talk?' I said, 'Yes.' So we did, and he said to me, 'O Abu Sufyan, what about 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah?' I said, 'What about 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah?' He said, 'Noble on both sides, who avoids injustices and forbidden things?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And an elder of high rank?' I said, 'And an elder of high rank.' He said, 'Age and rank have diminished him.' I said to him, 'You lie; he only increases in honor as he increases in age.' He said, 'O Abu Sufyan, this is a word I have not heard anyone say to me since I became a Christian. Do not be hasty with me until I tell you.' I said, 'Proceed.' He said, 'I used to find in my books a prophet who would be sent from this region of ours, and I thought—rather I did not doubt—that I was him. But when I studied with the people of knowledge, he was from Banu 'Abd Manaf. I looked among Banu 'Abd Manaf and found no one suitable for this matter except 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah. When you told me his age, I knew it was not him, since he had passed forty and had not received revelation.' Abu Sufyan said: Time passed, and revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I set out with a group of Quraysh to Yemen for trade and passed by Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt. I said to him, as if mocking, 'O Umayyah, the prophet you were waiting for has emerged.' He said, 'Indeed, it is true, so follow him.' I said, 'What prevents you from following him?' He said, 'Nothing prevents me from following him except shyness before the women of Thaqif. I used to tell them that I was him, and then they would see me following a young man from Banu 'Abd Manaf.' Then Umayyah said, 'And it is as if, O Abu Sufyan, if I oppose him, I will be tied up as a kid is tied until you are brought to him and he judges in your case as he wishes.'"],[7228,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with twelve thousand, comprising the Muhajirun, the Ansar, Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, and Banu Sulaym, and they led the horses until they encamped at Marr al-Zahran, and Quraysh did not know about them. They sent Abu Sufyan and Hakim b. Hizam to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Secure for us a guarantee of protection from him, or give him notice of war.' Abu Sufyan b. Harb and Hakim b. Hizam went out and met Budayl b. Warqa', so they took him as a companion. When they were at al-Arak, near Makkah, and that was at nightfall, they saw the tents and the army and heard the neighing of the horses, and that alarmed and frightened them. They said, 'These are Banu Ka'b whom war has stirred up.' Budayl said, 'These are more than Banu Ka'b; their gathering has not reached this extent. Would Hawazin seek pasture in our land? By Allah, we do not recognize this either; this is like the pilgrimage of the people.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent cavalry ahead to seize scouts, and Khuza'ah was on the road, not letting anyone pass. When Abu Sufyan and his companions entered the Muslim camp, the cavalry seized them under cover of night and brought them fearing execution. 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ went to Abu Sufyan and struck his neck, and the people grabbed him and took him out to bring him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The guards prevented him from reaching the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he feared being killed. Al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ had been his close friend in the pre-Islamic era, so Abu Sufyan called at the top of his voice, 'Will you take me to 'Abbas?' He came to him and defended him, and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hand him over to him. He went among the people in his place, and 'Abbas rode with him under cover of night and moved through the army camp until they all saw him. 'Umar ؓ had said to Abu Sufyan when he struck his neck, 'By Allah, you will not approach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until you die.' So he sought help from 'Abbas and said, 'I am going to be killed.' 'Abbas protected him from the people so they would not seize him. When he saw the size of the army and their obedience, he said, 'I have never seen a gathering of people like tonight.' 'Abbas saved him from their hands and said, 'You will be killed if you do not submit and bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' He kept trying to say what 'Abbas commanded him, but his tongue would not obey. So he spent the night with 'Abbas. As for Hakim b. Hizam and Budayl b. Warqa', they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and accepted Islam, and he began asking them about the people of Makkah. When the call to the dawn prayer was made, the people stirred, and Abu Sufyan was startled and said, 'O 'Abbas, what do they want?' He said, 'They are the Muslims preparing to attend the Prophet ﷺ.' 'Abbas took him out, and when Abu Sufyan saw them passing to the prayer, bowing and prostrating in their prayer, whenever they prostrated he said, 'O 'Abbas, does he not command them to do anything but they do it?' 'Abbas said, 'If he forbade them food and drink, they would obey him.' He said, 'O 'Abbas, then speak to him about your people; does he have any pardon for them?' So 'Abbas took Abu Sufyan and brought him before the Prophet ﷺ. 'Abbas said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Sufyan.' Abu Sufyan said, 'O Muhammad, I sought help from my god and sought help from your God. By Allah, I have never met you but you prevailed over me. If my god had been right and your God false, I would have prevailed over you.' Then he bore witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. 'Abbas said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I would like you to permit me to go to your people and warn them of what has come and call them to Allah and His Messenger.' He permitted him. 'Abbas said, 'How should I speak to them, O Messenger of Allah? Make clear to me a guarantee of safety that they can rely on.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Say to them: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and bears witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and withholds his hand, he is safe. Whoever sits at the Ka'bah and lays down his weapon, he is safe. Whoever locks his door upon himself, he is safe.'"],[7231,"We came as a delegation to Muʿāwiyah ؓ, and among us was Abū Hurayrah ؓ. One of us would prepare food one day and invite the other, and the other would prepare food another day and invite this one. I said, “O Abū Hurayrah, today is my day.” He came before the food was ready, so I said, “O Abū Hurayrah, tell us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ until our food is ready.” He said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest, and he said, ‘O Abū Hurayrah, call the Anṣār for me.’ I called them, and they came hurrying. He said, ‘Do you see the riffraff of the people?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘When you meet them tomorrow, mow them down completely, then your appointment is at al-Ṣafā.’” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Khālid b. al-Walīd over one of the two flanks and al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām over the other flank ؓ, and he appointed Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ over the infantry in the middle of the valley. When the people came, we met them, and no one advanced but that they struck him down. Victory was granted to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came and climbed al-Ṣafā, and the Anṣār came and surrounded al-Ṣafā. Abū Sufyān came and said, ‘O Messenger of God, the green of Quraysh has been made lawful. There is no Quraysh after today.’ He said, ‘Whoever locks his door is safe, and whoever throws down his weapon is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.’”"],[7232,"That when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest, Abū Sufyān came and said, “O Messenger of God, Quraysh has been made lawful. There is no Quraysh after today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever locks his door is safe, and whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe.” Then he mentioned something similar to the ḥadīth of Ḥammād b. Salamah."],[7233,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Abū Sufyān is close to you, so beware of him.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Submit, O Abū Sufyān.” He said, “O Messenger of God, my people, my people.” He said, “As for your people, whoever locks his door is safe.” He said, “Grant me something.” He said, “Whoever enters your house is safe.”"],[7234,"I set out during the truce that was between us and the Messenger of God ﷺ. While I was in Syria, a letter from the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought to Heraclius. Diḥyah al-Kalbī had brought it and handed it to the governor of Buṣrā, who handed it to Heraclius. Heraclius said, “Is there here a man from the people of this man who claims to be a prophet?” They said, “Yes.” So I was summoned along with a group of Quraysh, and we entered upon Heraclius. He seated us before him and said, “Which of you is closest in kinship to this man who claims to be a prophet?” Abū Sufyān said, “I said, ‘I am.’” So they seated me before him and seated my companions behind me. Then he called for his interpreter and said, “Tell them that I am going to ask about this man who claims to be a prophet. If he lies to me, then call him a liar.” Abū Sufyān said, “By God, were it not that lying would be reported of me, I would have lied.” Then he said to his interpreter, “Ask him how is his lineage among you?” I said, “He is among us of noble lineage.” He said, “Was any of his fathers a king?” I said, “No.” He said, “Did you ever accuse him of lying before he said what he said?” I said, “No.” He said, “Who follows him, the nobles of the people or their weak ones?” I said, “Rather their weak ones.” He said, “Are they increasing or decreasing?” I said, “Rather they are increasing.” He said, “Does anyone of them apostatize from his religion after entering it out of displeasure with it?” I said, “No.” He said, “Have you fought him?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “How was your fighting against him?” I said, “War between us and him alternates; he strikes us and we strike him.” He said, “Does he betray?” I said, “No, and we are with him in a truce, not knowing what he will do during it.” He said, “By God, I was not able to insert anything else into a word besides this.” He said, “Has anyone said this saying before him?” I said, “No.” He said to his interpreter, “Tell him: I asked you about his lineage, and you claimed that he is among you of noble lineage, and so are messengers sent among the noblest of their people. I asked you whether any of his fathers was a king, and you claimed not, so I said, had any of his fathers been a king, I would have said he is a man seeking the kingdom of his fathers. I asked you about his followers, whether they are their weak ones or their nobles, and you said rather their weak ones, and they are the followers of the messengers. I asked you whether you accused him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed not, so I knew that he would not refrain from lying against people and then go and lie against God. I asked you whether anyone of them apostatizes from his religion after entering it out of displeasure with it, and you claimed not, and so is faith when it mingles with the joy of hearts. I asked you whether they increase or decrease, and you claimed that they increase, and so is faith until it is complete. I asked you whether you fought him, and you claimed that you fought him, and war between you and him alternates; he gains from you and you gain from him, and so are messengers tested, then the outcome is theirs. I asked you whether he betrays, and you claimed that he does not betray, and so messengers do not betray. I asked you whether anyone said this saying before him, and you claimed not, so I said, had anyone said this saying before him, I would have said a man following a saying said before him.” Then he said, “What does he command you?” I said, “He commands us to prayer, zakāh, maintaining ties, and chastity.” He said, “If what you say about him is true, he is a prophet. I knew that he was to emerge, but I did not think he would be from among you. If I knew I could reach him, I would love to meet him, and if I were with him, I would wash his feet. His dominion will surely reach what is beneath my feet.” Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and read it. In it was: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Arīsiyyīn. And {O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you} until His saying {that we are Muslims}.” When he finished reading the letter, voices rose around him and clamor increased, and we were ordered to leave. When we left, I said to my companions, “The affair of Ibn Abī Kabshah has become great. The king of the Banū al-Aṣfar fears him.” I remained convinced that the affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ would prevail until God brought Islam to me. Al-Zuhrī said: Heraclius summoned the nobles of the Romans and gathered them in a hall of his. He said, “O assembly of Romans, will you accept success and right guidance forever and that your kingdom remain firm?” They bolted like wild asses to the doors, but found them locked. Then he called them back: “I only tested your steadfastness in your religion. I have seen from you what pleases me.” So they prostrated to him and were pleased with him."],[7235,"Abu Sufyan bin Harb informed me that Heraclius had sent a messenger to him while he had been accompanying a caravan from Quraish. They were merchants doing business in Sham (Syria, Palestine, Lebanon and Jordan), at the time when Messenger of Allah ﷺ had truce with Abu Sufyan and Quraish infidels. So Abu Sufyan and his companions went to Heraclius at Ilya (Jerusalem). Heraclius called them in the court and he had all the senior Roman dignitaries around him. He called for his translator who, translating Heraclius's question said to them, \"Who amongst you is closely related to that man who claims to be a Prophet?\" Abu Sufyan replied, \"I am the nearest relative to him (amongst the group).\" Heraclius said, \"Bring him (Abu Sufyan) close to me and make his companions stand behind him.\" Abu Sufyan added, Heraclius told his translator to tell my companions that he wanted to put some questions to me regarding that man (The Prophet) and that if I told a lie they (my companions) should contradict me.\" Abu Sufyan added, \"By Allah! Had I not been afraid of my companions labeling me a liar, I would not have spoken the truth about the Prophet. The first question he asked me about him was: 'What is his family status amongst you?' I replied, 'He belongs to a good (noble) family amongst us.' Heraclius further asked, 'Has anybody amongst you ever claimed the same (i.e. to be a Prophet) before him?' I replied, 'No.' He said, 'Was anybody amongst his ancestors a king?' I replied, 'No.' Heraclius asked, 'Do the nobles or the poor follow him?' I replied, 'It is the poor who follow him.' He said, 'Are his followers increasing decreasing (day by day)?' I replied, 'They are increasing.' He then asked, 'Does anybody amongst those who embrace his religion become displeased and renounce the religion afterwards?' I replied, 'No.' Heraclius said, 'Have you ever accused him of telling lies before his claim (to be a Prophet)?' I replied, 'No. ' Heraclius said, 'Does he break his promises?' I replied, 'No. We are at truce with him but we do not know what he will do in it.' I could not find opportunity to say anything against him except that. Heraclius asked, 'Have you ever had a war with him?' I replied, 'Yes.' Then he said, 'What was the outcome of the battles?' I replied, 'Sometimes he was victorious and sometimes we.' Heraclius said, 'What does he order you to do?' I said, 'He tells us to worship Allah and Allah alone and not to worship anything along with Him, and to renounce all that our ancestors had said. He orders us to pray, to speak the truth, to be chaste and to keep good relations with our Kith and kin.' Heraclius asked the translator to convey to me the following, I asked you about his family and your reply was that he belonged to a very noble family. In fact all the Apostles come from noble families amongst their respective peoples. I questioned you whether anybody else amongst you claimed such a thing, your reply was in the negative. If the answer had been in the affirmative, I would have thought that this man was following the previous man's statement. Then I asked you whether anyone of his ancestors was a king. Your reply was in the negative, and if it had been in the affirmative, I would have thought that this man wanted to take back his ancestral kingdom. I further asked whether he was ever accused of telling lies before he said what he said, and your reply was in the negative. So I wondered how a person who does not tell a lie about others could ever tell a lie about Allah. I, then asked you whether the rich people followed him or the poor. You replied that it was the poor who followed him. And in fact all the Apostle have been followed by this very class of people. Then I asked you whether his followers were increasing or decreasing. You replied that they were increasing, and in fact this is the way of true faith, till it is complete in all respects. I further asked you whether there was anybody, who, after embracing his religion, became displeased and discarded his religion. Your reply was in the negative, and in fact this is (the sign of) true faith, when its delight enters the hearts and mixes with them completely. I asked you whether he had ever betrayed. You replied in the negative and likewise the Apostles never betray. Then I asked you what he ordered you to do. You replied that he ordered you to worship Allah and Allah alone and not to worship any thing along with Him and forbade you to worship idols and ordered you to pray, to speak the truth and to be chaste. If what you have said is true, he will very soon occupy this place underneath my feet and I knew it (from the scriptures) that he was going to appear but I did not know that he would be from you, and if I could reach him definitely, I would go immediately to meet him and if I were with him, I would certainly wash his feet.' Heraclius then asked for the letter addressed by Allah's Apostle which was delivered by Dihya to the Governor of Busra, who forwarded it to Heraclius to read. The contents of the letter were as follows: \"In the name of Allah the Beneficent, the Merciful (This letter is) from Muhammad the slave of Allah and His Apostle to Heraclius the ruler of Byzantine. Peace be upon him, who follows the right path. Furthermore I invite you to Islam, and if you become a Muslim you will be safe, and Allah will double your reward, and if you reject this invitation of Islam you will be committing a sin of Arisiyin (tillers, farmers i.e. your people). And (Allah's Statement:) 'O people of the scripture! Come to a word common to you and us that we worship none but Allah and that we associate nothing in worship with Him, and that none of us shall take others as Lords beside Allah. Then, if they turn away, say: Bear witness that we are Muslims (those who have surrendered to Allah).' (3:64). Abu Sufyan then added, \"When Heraclius had finished his speech and had read the letter, there was a great hue and cry in the Royal Court. So we were turned out of the court. I told my companions that the question of Ibn-Abi-Kabsha) (the Prophet ﷺ Muhammad) has become so prominent that even the King of Bani Al-Asfar (Byzantine) is afraid of him. Then I started to become sure that he (the Prophet) would be the conqueror in the near future till I embraced Islam (i.e. Allah guided me to it).\" The sub narrator adds, \"Ibn An-Natur was the Governor of llya' (Jerusalem) and Heraclius was the head of the Christians of Sham. Ibn An-Natur narrates that once while Heraclius was visiting ilya' (Jerusalem), he got up in the morning with a sad mood. Some of his priests asked him why he was in that mood? Heraclius was a foreteller and an astrologer. He replied, 'At night when I looked at the stars, I saw that the leader of those who practice circumcision had appeared (become the conqueror). Who are they who practice circumcision?' The people replied, 'Except the Jews nobody practices circumcision, so you should not be afraid of them (Jews). 'Just Issue orders to kill every Jew present in the country.' While they were discussing it, a messenger sent by the king of Ghassan to convey the news of Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Heraclius was brought in. Having heard the news, he (Heraclius) ordered the people to go and see whether the messenger of Ghassan was circumcised. The people, after seeing him, told Heraclius that he was circumcised. Heraclius then asked him about the Arabs. The messenger replied, 'Arabs also practice circumcision.' (After hearing that) Heraclius remarked that sovereignty of the 'Arabs had appeared. Heraclius then wrote a letter to his friend in Rome who was as good as Heraclius in knowledge. Heraclius then left for Homs. (a town in Syrian and stayed there till he received the reply of his letter from his friend who agreed with him in his opinion about the emergence of the Prophet ﷺ and the fact that he was a Prophet. On that Heraclius invited all the heads of the Byzantines to assemble in his palace at Homs. When they assembled, he ordered that all the doors of his palace be closed. Then he came out and said, 'O Byzantines! If success is your desire and if you seek right guidance and want your empire to remain then give a pledge of allegiance to this Prophet (i.e. embrace Islam).' (On hearing the views of Heraclius) the people ran towards the gates of the palace like onagers but found the doors closed. Heraclius realized their hatred towards Islam and when he lost the hope of their embracing Islam, he ordered that they should be brought back in audience. (When they returned) he said, 'What already said was just to test the strength of your conviction and I have seen it.' The people prostrated before him and became pleased with him, and this was the end of Heraclius's story (in connection with his faith). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7)"],[7236,"We were a trading people, and the war between us and the Messenger of God had confined us until our wealth was destroyed. When the truce was made between us and the Messenger of God ﷺ, we felt secure in our wealth. I set out with a group of Quraysh heading to Syria, where our trade was. I arrived there when Heraclius had defeated those Persians who had opposed him and expelled them from it, and his great cross was recovered for him, which they had seized. When he learned of that and that his cross had been retrieved, and Ḥimṣ was his residence, he left it on foot, thanking God for what had been restored to him, to pray in Jerusalem. Carpets were spread for him on the road and aromatic plants were thrown on them. When he reached Īliyāʾ and completed his prayer there, with his patricians and bishops of the Romans, the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ was brought to him with Diḥyah b. Khalīfah al-Kalbī: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the Messenger of God, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the peasants.” Muḥammad b. Isḥāq said: Ibn Shihāb said: The bishop of the Christians narrated to me, saying, “I lived to see him in the time of ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān, and he claimed that he witnessed that affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the affair of Heraclius and understood it.” He said: When the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived with Diḥyah, he took it and placed it between his thighs and his side. Then he wrote to a man in Rome who read Hebrew, mentioning his affair, describing his situation, and the news of what he brought. The man of Rome wrote back to him that he is the prophet we have been awaiting, no doubt about it, so follow him and believe him. Heraclius ordered the patricians of the Romans to be gathered in the hall of his kingdom, and he ordered the hall to be locked upon them. Then he looked down upon them from an upper room, fearing them for himself, and said, “O assembly of Romans, I have gathered you for a matter. A letter from this man has come to me calling me to his religion. By God, he is the man we have been awaiting and whom we find in our book. Come, let us follow him and believe him, and our world and our hereafter will be safe for us.” They snorted with one snort, then rushed to the doors of the hall to leave, but found them locked against them. He said, “Bring them back to me,” fearing them for himself. They were brought back, and he said, “O assembly of Romans, I only said this statement to you to see how firm you are in your religion in this matter that has occurred. I have seen from you what pleases me.” So they prostrated to him and were pleased with him. He ordered the doors of the hall to be opened for them, and they departed."],[7237,"That he was in Syria with men of Quraysh who had come as merchants, during the truce between the Messenger of God ﷺ and the disbelievers of Quraysh. Abū Sufyān said: The messenger of Caesar came and took me and my companions until we arrived at Īliyāʾ. We entered upon him, and he was seated in his royal court wearing the crown, with the nobles of the Romans around him. He said to his interpreter, “Ask them which of them is closest in kinship to this man who claims to be a prophet.” Abū Sufyān said, “I said, ‘I am the closest of them to him in kinship.’” He said, “What is the relationship between you and him?” I said, “He is my cousin.” Abū Sufyān said, “There was no one from Banū ʿAbd Manāf in the caravan that day except me.” Caesar said, “Bring him near me.” Then he ordered my companions, and they were placed behind my back at my shoulders. Then Caesar said to his interpreter, “Tell his companions: I am going to ask this man about the man who claims to be a prophet. If he lies, then call him a liar.” Abū Sufyān said, “Were it not for the shame that my companions would report lying about me, I would have lied about him when he asked me. But I was ashamed that they would report lying, so I told the truth.” Then Caesar said to his interpreter, “Ask him how is this man’s lineage among you?” I said, “He is among us of noble lineage.” He said, “Has anyone among you ever said this saying?” I said, “No.” He said, “Did you accuse him of lying before he said what he said?” I said, “No.” He said, “Was any of his fathers a king?” I said, “No.” He said, “Do the nobles of the people follow him or their weak ones?” I said, “Rather their weak ones.” He said, “Are they increasing or decreasing?” I said, “Rather increasing.” He said, “Does anyone of them apostatize out of displeasure with his religion after entering it?” I said, “No.” He said, “Does he betray?” I said, “We are with him in a truce now, and we fear that.” Abū Sufyān said, “I was not able to insert into any word anything by which I could disparage him, except that I feared it would be reported of me.” He said, “Have you fought him and has he fought you?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “How is his war and your war?” I said, “It has been alternating, sometimes favoring us and sometimes favoring him.” He said, “What does he command you?” I said, “He commands us to worship God alone and not associate anything with Him, and he forbids us to worship what our fathers worshipped. He commands us to prayer, charity, chastity, fulfilling covenants, and returning trusts.” He said to his interpreter when I said that, “Tell him: I asked you about his lineage among you, and you claimed that he is among you of noble lineage, and so messengers are sent among the nobility of their people. I asked you whether anyone said this saying before him, and you said no, so I said, had anyone of you said this saying, I would have said he is a man following the saying of one who said it before him. I asked you whether you accused him of lying before he said what he said, and you claimed not, so I knew that he would not refrain from lying against people and then lie against God. I asked you whether any of his fathers was a king, and you claimed not, so I said, had any of his fathers been a king, I would have said he is a man seeking the kingdom of his fathers. I asked you whether the nobles of the people follow him or their weak ones, and you claimed that their weak ones are his followers, and so are the followers of messengers. I asked you whether they increase or decrease, and you claimed that they increase, and so is faith. I asked you whether anyone of them apostatizes out of displeasure with his religion after entering it, and you claimed not, and so is faith when it mingles with the joy of hearts; no one dislikes it. I asked you whether he betrays, and you claimed not, and so messengers do not betray. I asked you whether you fought him and he fought you, and you claimed that he has done that and that your war and his war alternates, sometimes favoring you and sometimes favoring him, and so are messengers, then the outcome is theirs. I asked you what he commands you, and you claimed that he commands you to worship God alone and not associate anything with Him, and he forbids you from what your fathers worshipped, and he commands you to prayer, charity, chastity, and returning trusts. He is a prophet. I knew that he was to emerge, but I did not think he would be from among you. If what I said is true, he will soon possess the place of these two feet of mine. By God, if I hoped to reach him, I would endure meeting him and wash his feet.” Abū Sufyān said: Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and ordered it to be read. In it was: “In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muḥammad, the servant of God and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the great one of the Romans. Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: I call you with the call of Islam. Submit, and you will be safe. Submit, and God will give you your reward twice. If you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Arīsiyyīn. And {O People of the Book, come to a word common between us and you: that we worship none but God and associate nothing with Him, and that none of us takes others as lords besides God. If they turn away, then say: Bear witness that we are Muslims}.” Abū Sufyān said: When he finished his speech, the voices of those around him from the nobles of the Romans rose, and their clamor increased. I do not know what they were saying. He ordered us to leave. When I left with my companions and was alone, I said, “The affair of Ibn Abī Kabshah has become great. This king of the Banū al-Aṣfar fears him.” Abū Sufyān said: By God, I remained humbled and convinced that his affair would prevail until God brought Islam to me, though I was reluctant."],[7239,"Caesar, in his kingdom, his power, and his presence, what did he say? It means that his saying was \"If I had known that he was him, I would have walked to him, kissed his head, and washed his feet.\" Abu Sufyan and his presence, his forehead was sweating with the anxiety of the letter that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to him. Abu Sufyan said, \"So, I remained desired by Muhammad ﷺ until I embraced Islam and in his message, he said: 'O people of the Book, come to a word that is just between us and you, that we worship none but Allah, and that we do not associate anything with Him, and that none of us shall take others as lords besides Allah. But if they turn away, then say: 'Bear witness that we are Muslims'.\" \"It is He who has sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth, that He may make it prevail over all religions, even if the disbelievers hate it.\" \"Fight against those who do not believe in Allah, nor in the Last Day, nor forbid what Allah and His Messenger have forbidden, and do not adhere to the religion of truth from among those who were given the Scripture, until they give the jizyah willingly while they are humbled.\""],[7240,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “O God, bless my community in its early morning.” And when he sent out a raiding party, he would send it at the beginning of the day. Ṣakhr was a merchant, and he would send his servants at the beginning of the day, so his wealth increased."],[7242,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O God, bless my community in its early morning.”"],[7243,"From Ṣakhr, who lived to see the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not revile the dead, for you will hurt the living.”"],[7244,"I took the paternal aunt of al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and al-Mughīrah came and asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for his aunt. He said, “O Ṣakhr, when people embrace Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so return her to them.” So I returned her to him. He said: And the Prophet ﷺ had given me wealth for Banū Sulaym, and they embraced Islam and came to the Prophet ﷺ asking for the wealth. The Prophet of God ﷺ called me and said, “O Ṣakhr, when people embrace Islam, they secure their wealth and their blood, so return it to them.” So I returned it to them."],[7246,"The Prophet ﷺ saw his father standing in the sun while he was delivering a sermon, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to move, or ordered that he be moved, and he was moved."],[7247,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby appearance, so he said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth. Allah has given me camels, cattle, and sheep.\" He said, \"Whoever has wealth, let it be seen on him.\""],[7248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"After one hundred years, no child will be born for whom Allah has any need.\""],[7249,"I met the Prophet ﷺ between Arafah and Muzdalifah, so I took hold of the halter of his she-camel and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what will bring me near Paradise and keep me far from the Fire?\" He said, \"By Allah, if you have been brief in asking, you have indeed made it great and lengthy. Establish the prescribed prayers, pay the obligatory zakat, perform Hajj to the House, and whatever you would love people to do to you, do it to them; and whatever you would hate people to do to you, leave people alone from it. Let go of the halter of the she-camel.\" Ibrahim b. al-Hajjaj said: \"And Sakhr b. al-Qa'qa' al-Bahili said it.\""],[7250,"Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to your people, Banu Sa'd, and I began presenting Islam to them and calling them to it? I said, 'Indeed, he calls to good and commands it. Indeed, he calls to good and commands it.' So I conveyed that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Allah, bind [good] for al-Ahnaf.' And al-Ahnaf used to say: 'There is nothing among my deeds that I hope for more than this.'\""],[7251,"Suhayb b. Sinan, whose kunya was Abu Yahya, died in Madinah in Shawwal of the year thirty-eight. He was among the captives of Mosul, taken captive by the Byzantines."],[7252,"When Umar ؓ was stabbed, he ordered Suhayb, the freedman of Banu Jud'an, to lead the people in prayer."],[7253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The forerunners are four: I am the forerunner of the Arabs, Suhayb is the forerunner of the Byzantines, Salman is the forerunner of Persia, and Bilal is the forerunner of Abyssinia.\""],[7254,"In his saying {And among the people is he who sells himself} it was revealed about Suhaib ibn Sinan and Abu Dharr, and that the one who met Suhaib on the way to the city was Qunfudh ibn Umayr ibn Jud'an."],[7255,"Suhayb ransomed himself from his people with his wealth, then he set out as an emigrant, and they caught up with him on the road, so he brought out for them what remained of his wealth."],[7256,"Ibn Umar [said]: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Banu Amr b. Awf to pray in it, and Suhayb entered with him. Then some men from the Ansar entered upon him greeting him. Abdullah said: So I asked Suhayb, \"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond when someone greeted him during prayer?\" He said, \"He would gesture with his hand.\""],[7257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the mosque of Quba and was praying, and people began entering and greeting him. When Suhayb came out, I asked him, \"How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond to them?\" He said, \"With his hand, like this,\" and he gestured with it."],[7258,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, so I greeted him, and he responded to me with a gesture."],[7259,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal came to Syria, he saw the Jews prostrating to their rabbis and scholars, and he saw the Christians prostrating to their bishops. When he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he prostrated to him. He said, \"What is this, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"I came to Syria and saw the Jews prostrating to their scholars and rabbis, and I saw the Christians prostrating to their priests and monks. I asked, 'What is this?' They said, 'The greeting of the prophets.'\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"They lied about their prophets, just as they distorted their book. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[7260,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"He who declares lawful its forbidden things has not believed in the Qur'an.\""],[7261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I was shown the abode of your emigration, a land of salt marshes between two lava tracts; either it is Hajar or it is Yathrib.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ departed for Madinah, and Abu Bakr ؓ departed with him. I had intended to go out with him, but some young men of Quraysh prevented me. That night I kept standing and did not sit. They said, \"God has distracted him from you with his stomach,\" but I was not ill. They slept, so I went out. Some people from them caught up with me after I had traveled, wanting to bring me back. I said to them, \"Would you like me to give you some ounces of gold and two bracelets of mine in Makkah, and you let me go and give me your word?\" They did so. I followed them to Makkah and said, \"Dig under the threshold of the door, for beneath it are the ounces. Go to such-and-such a woman with such-and-such a sign and take the two ornaments.\" I left until I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ at Quba before he moved from it. When he saw me, he said, \"O Abu Yahya, did the bargain profit?\" three times. I said, \"O Messenger of God, no one has preceded me to you, and nothing informed you except Gabriel ﷺ.\""],[7262,"Umar ؓ said, \"What is wrong with him—may he have no father—he calls the people against me?\" He said, \"He is only calling a servant of his named Yahnas.\" He said, \"O Suhayb, there is nothing in you that I find fault with except three traits; were it not for them, I would not place anyone ahead of you.\" He said, \"What are they?\" He replied, \"You are a fault-finder.\" He said, \"Will he tell me about them?\" He said, \"You will not ask me about anything but I will inform you of it.\" He said, \"And you will not inform me of anything but I will believe you.\" He said, \"I see you squander your wealth, you take a kunya with the name of a prophet—Abu Yahya—and you claim Arab lineage while your tongue is non-Arab.\" He said, \"As for my squandering my wealth, I spend it only in its proper right. As for my kunya, the Messenger of God ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya; shall I abandon it because of your words? And as for my claiming Arab lineage, the Byzantines captured me when I was young, and I do not remember my family. Even if I had emerged from a piece of dung, I would trace my lineage to it.\""],[7263,"David, the prophet of God ﷺ, when he finished his prayer, would say, \"O God, set right for me my religion, which You have made the protection of my affair; and set right for me my worldly life, in which You have placed my livelihood. O God, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. None can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can avail against You his fortune.\" Ka'b al-Ahbar said: Suhayb informed me that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to conclude his prayer with this supplication."],[7264,"Ka'b swore by God who parted the sea for Moses that Suhayb narrated to him that the Messenger of God ﷺ never saw a town he intended to enter but that he said when he saw it, \"O God, Lord of the seven heavens and what they overshadow, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people.\""],[7265,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to supplicate, saying, \"O God, You are not a god whom we have newly invented, nor a Lord whom we have originated, nor was there for us before You any god to whom we could flee and abandon You, nor did anyone help You in creating us so that we would associate him with You. Blessed are You, and exalted.\" Ka'b said, \"Thus did David, the prophet of God ﷺ, use to supplicate.\""],[7266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever gives a woman a dowry while resolving not to fulfill it to her will meet God ﷻ as an adulterer, and whoever takes on a debt while resolving not to repay it will meet God as a thief.\""],[7268,"\"I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ before revelation came to him.\""],[7269,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while there were dates and bread in front of him. He said, \"Draw near and eat.\" I began eating from the dates. He said, \"Do you eat dates while you have an eye inflammation?\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, I suck them from the other side.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled."],[7270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man’s prayer in congregation equals twenty-five times his prayer alone.”"],[7271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You should use cupping on the jugular area of the back of the head, for it is a cure for seventy-two diseases and five ailments: insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, and toothache.”"],[7272,"Abu Bakr ؓ passed by a captive of his to seek protection for him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while Suhayb was sitting in the mosque. He said to Abu Bakr, “Who is this with you?” He said, “A captive of mine from the polytheists; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has granted him protection.” Suhayb said, “There was a place for the sword on this one’s neck.” Abu Bakr ؓ became angry. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said, “Why do I see you angry?” He said, “I passed by this captive of mine in front of Suhayb, and he said, ‘There was a place for the sword on this one’s neck.’” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Perhaps you harmed him.” He said, “No, by Allah.” He said, “If you had harmed him, you would have harmed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[7273,"That the polytheists, when they circled around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and approached the cave and retreated, Wahshi said: Neither Suhayb (was wounded), nor Suhayb should (stay) by me. So when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to leave, he sent Abu Bakr twice or three times to Suhayb, and he found him praying. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, I found him praying, so I disliked interrupting his prayer. Abu Bakr said: You were right. So they both left during the night. And when it was morning, he continued until he came to Umm Rumân, the wife of Abu Bakr, and she said: Shouldn't I see you here (with your brother)? They have left (and they) have left something for you from their provisions. Suhayb said: So I left until I entered upon my wife, Umm 'Umar, and I took my sword, my provisions, and my bow, until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Al-Madinah, and I found him (with) Abu Bakr sitting. So when Abu Bakr saw me, he stood up and gave me the glad tidings of the verse that was revealed about me, and he held my hand. So I mentioned some complaints to him, and he apologized and granted me a blessing. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Abu Yahya has made a profit.\""],[7274,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never witnessed any scene except that I was present; he never pledged allegiance except that I was present; he never dispatched a raiding party except that I was present; he never went on any expedition, from the first of the time to its last, except that I was in it on his right or his left. Whenever they feared what was before them, I was in front of them; whenever they feared what was behind them, I was behind them. I never placed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between me and the enemy until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away.”"],[7275,"He said to him, “O Suhayb, you have adopted a kunya though you have no son, and you claim Arab lineage though you are a man from the Byzantines.” He said, “O Commander of the Faithful, as for your saying that I have adopted a kunya though I have no son, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya. As for your saying that I claim Arab lineage though I am a man from the Byzantines, I am a man from the tribe of al-Namir b. Qasit; I was taken captive from Mosul after I had been a boy who knew my family and lineage.”"],[7276,"From the Prophet ﷺ that one day he said to Ali ؓ, “Who is the most wretched of the early peoples?” He said, “The one who hamstrung the she-camel, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “You have spoken the truth. Then who is the most wretched of the later peoples?” He said, “I have no knowledge, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The one who will strike you on this,” and the Prophet ﷺ pointed with his hand to the crown of his head. Ali ؓ used to say to the people of Iraq, “By Allah, I wish that the most wretched of you would be sent and would dye this,” meaning his beard, “from this,” and he placed his hand on the front of his head. The wording is that of the hadith of Suwayd b. Sa’id; al-Hadrami said in his version, “and he pointed with his hand to the crown of his head.”"],[7277,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a donkey brays, seek refuge in Allah from Satan the accursed.”"],[7278,"When water, then wine, then milk were presented to the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , he took the milk and said to him, Jibril, \"You have chosen the fitrah (natural disposition). With it, every living creature is punished. If you had taken the wine, you would have gone astray and your nation would have also gone astray. And he pointed to the valley known as Hellfire. So I looked into it and saw that it was blazing."],[7279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, a caller will call out: ‘O people of Paradise, you have a promise with Allah that He intends to fulfill for you.’ They will say, ‘What is it? Has He not made our scales heavy, whitened our faces, admitted us to Paradise, and saved us from the Fire?’ He said: ‘Then the veil will be lifted, and they will look at Him. By the One in whose hand is my soul, He has not given them anything dearer to them than looking at Him.’”"],[7281,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I am amazed at Allah’s decree for the Muslim; it is all good. If ease befalls him and he is grateful, Allah ﷻ rewards him; and if hardship befalls him and he is patient, Allah ﷻ rewards him.” Hammad added in it: “And every decree that Allah ﷻ decrees for the Muslim is good.”"],[7282,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one of the night prayers. When he finished, he turned to us with a smiling face and said, “Will you not ask me why I laughed?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “I am amazed at Allah’s decree for the Muslim servant. Indeed, everything Allah decrees for him is good, and no one has all of Allah’s decrees be good for him except the Muslim servant.”"],[7283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to move his lips with something during the days of Hunayn when he prayed the dawn prayer. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, you keep moving your lips with something after the dawn prayer, and you did not used to do that.” He said, “A prophet before us was impressed by the large number of his community and said, ‘These will not last,’ I think he said something, so Allah ﷻ revealed to him: ‘The best of your community is between one of three: either I send death upon them, or the enemy, or famine.’ He presented that to them, and they said, ‘As for famine, we have no strength for it, and we have no strength for the enemy, but death.’ So seventy thousand of them died in three days. Today I say: O Allah, by You I strive, by You I attack, by You I fight.”"],[7285,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Among those before you there was a king who had a sorcerer. When the sorcerer grew old, he said to the king, \"I have become old, so send me a boy whom I can teach sorcery.\" He sent him a boy, and he taught him sorcery. Between the king and the sorcerer there was a monk. The boy heard his words, and he was impressed by his manner and speech. Whenever he went to the sorcerer, he sat with the monk, and when he went to the sorcerer, he beat him, saying, \"What kept you?\" When he returned to his family, he sat with the monk, and when he went to his family, they said, \"What is keeping you?\" and they beat him. He complained about that to the monk, who said, \"When the sorcerer wants to beat you, say, 'My family kept me,' and when your family wants to beat you, say, 'The sorcerer kept me.'\" He said, \"While that was the case, one day he came upon a great beast that had blocked the people from passing. He said, 'Today I will know whether the affair of the sorcerer is dearer to God or the affair of the monk.' He took a stone and said, 'In the name of God. O God, if the affair of the monk is dearer to You and more excellent, then kill this beast.' He threw it and killed it, and the people went on. This reached the monk, who said, 'My son, you are more excellent than I, and you will be tested. If you are tested, do not point to me.' The boy used to heal the blind from birth and the leper and these diseases. The king had a close companion who went blind. He heard about the boy and came to him with many gifts, saying, 'Heal me, and you shall have all that is here.' The boy said, 'I do not heal anyone; only God ﷻ heals. If you believe in God, He will heal you.' So he believed in Him, and the boy called upon God ﷻ, and he was cured. The blind man was seized and continually tortured until he pointed to the boy. The king said to him, 'Do you have a lord other than me?' He said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is God.' He kept at him until he pointed to the monk. He seized him with torture and said, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He ordered a saw, and it was placed on the top of his head, and they split him. He said to the blind man, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He placed the saw on the top of his head until its two halves fell to the ground. It was said to the boy, 'Recant your religion.' He refused. He sent him with a group to a mountain and said, 'Climb such-and-such mountain with him, and when you reach its summit, if he recants his religion, then fine; otherwise, push him down.' He said, 'They took him to the mountain, and when he reached its summit, he said, \"O God, suffice me against them however You will.\" The mountain shook them, and they all perished. The boy came and entered upon the king, who said, 'What happened to your companions?' He said, 'God ﷻ sufficed me against them.' He sent them with a group in a ship, saying, 'Take him to the sea, and when you are in the middle of the sea, if he recants, then fine; otherwise, drown him.' They took him, and when they were in deep water, he said, \"O God, suffice me against them however You will.\" They all drowned. The boy came, and the king said, 'What happened to your companions?' He said, 'God ﷻ sufficed me against them.' Then the boy said to the king, 'You will not kill me until you do what I command you. If you do it, you will kill me.' He said, 'What is it?' He said, 'Gather the people on a single open plain, then take an arrow from your quiver and say, \"In the name of God, the Lord of the boy,\" then shoot me. If you do that, you will kill me.' He did so, placed the arrow, and said, 'In the name of God, the Lord of the boy.' The arrow struck his temple. The boy placed his hand on the spot of the arrow and died. The people said, 'We believe in the Lord of the boy' three times. It was said to the king, 'Do you see what you were wary of? By God, it has befallen you; all the people have believed.' He ordered the mouths of the streets to be dug, and trenches were dug in them. He said, 'Whoever recants his religion, then fine; otherwise, throw him into them.'"],[7286,"I prepared food for the Messenger of God ﷺ and came to him while he was sitting among a group of people. I stood facing him and gestured to him, and he gestured to me, 'And these?' I said, 'No.' So I remained silent and stood in my place. When he looked at me, I gestured to him, and he said, 'And these?' I said, 'No.' He did that twice or three times. Then I said, 'Yes, and these,' though it was only a little food I had prepared for him. He came, and they came with him, and they ate. I think he said, 'And some of it remained.'"],[7287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The superiority of a man's prayer in his home over his prayer where people can see him is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary prayer.'"],[7288,"'By God, I do not know which of the two calamities is greater: the death of my father or the killing of Uthman.'"],[7289,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'With whom did you stay, Abu Wahb?' He said, 'I stayed with Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib.' He said, 'You stayed with the Qurayshite who has the greatest love for Quraysh.'"],[7290,"It was said to Safwan, 'Whoever does not emigrate has perished.' So he called for his mount, rode it, and came to Madinah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'What has brought you, Abu Wahb?' He said, 'I have heard that there is no religion for one who has no emigration.' He said, 'Return to the valleys of Makkah.' So he returned and entered the mosque, and he placed his cloak under his head as a pillow. A man came and stole it, and he was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'O Messenger of God, this man stole my cloak.' The Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be punished by cutting. He said, 'O Messenger of God, my cloak did not reach the value for which a man's hand is cut; I have given it to him as charity.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Why not before you brought him to me?'"],[7291,"Safwan b. Umayyah came to Madinah and slept in the mosque, placing a khamisah of his under his head. A thief came and stole it. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that his hand be cut. He said, 'O Messenger of God, it is his.' He said, 'Why not before you brought him to me?'"],[7292,"Safwan ibn Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and there was a garment under his head. A man came and took it from under his head while he was sleeping. Safwan woke up and followed him, and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned the matter to him. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that the man be punished. Safwan said to the Prophet ﷺ , \"I had not reached the point of wanting it to be severed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Why didn't you come to me before bringing him?\""],[7293,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague is martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, and a woman who dies in childbirth is martyrdom.'"],[7294,"From Safwan b. Umayyah, raised to the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague, the woman who dies in childbirth, and drowning are martyrdom.'"],[7295,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'The plague, drowning, burning, and the woman who dies in childbirth are martyrdom for my nation.'"],[7296,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Eat meat by tearing it with your teeth, for it is tastier, more wholesome, and more agreeable.'"],[7297,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “It is more appetizing, more wholesome, more pleasant, and more wholesome.”"],[7298,"Safwan b. Umayyah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was cutting meat off the bone, so he said, “O Safwan.” I said, “At your service.” He said, “Bring the meat close to your mouth, for it is more pleasant and more wholesome.”"],[7299,"A thief came to him while he was sleeping and stole his waist-wrapper from beneath him. He woke up, seized him, and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have made it lawful for him.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me? When a case reaches the ruler concerning any of the prescribed punishments, he must carry it out.”"],[7300,"I was sleeping in the mosque on a cloak of mine worth thirty dirhams. A man came to me and snatched it from me. The man was caught and brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that his hand be cut off. I went to him and said, “Will you cut off his hand for thirty dirhams? It is his.” He said, “Why was this not before you brought him to me?”"],[7301,"A thief came to his father while he was sleeping and stole his waist-wrapper from under his head. He woke up, seized him, and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have made it lawful for him.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me? When a case reaches the ruler concerning any of Allah’s prescribed punishments, he must carry it out.”"],[7302,"A man stole a cloak, and he brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have pardoned him.” He said, “If only this had been before you brought him to me, O Abu Wahb.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had his hand cut off."],[7303,"I slept in the mosque, and my waist-wrapper was stolen from beneath me. I caught the thief and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ordered that his hand be cut off. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is his.” He said, “Why not before you brought him to me?”"],[7304,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed some iron armor from me on the day of Hunayn. I said, “Is it guaranteed, O Muhammad?” He said, “Guaranteed.” He said: Then some of it was lost. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “If you wish, we will compensate you for it.” He said, “No, I desire Islam more than that.”"],[7305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me gifts on the day of Hunayn, while he was the most hated of people to me, and he kept giving to me until he became the most beloved of people to me."],[7306,"When it was said to me, “Whoever does not emigrate is destroyed,” I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said, “Return, Abu Wahb, to the valleys of Makkah.”"],[7307,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Amr b. Qurrah came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, misery has been decreed for me, and I see that I have no provision except from my tambourine with my hand. Will you permit me to sing without obscenity?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I do not permit you, nor honor. You have lied, O enemy of Allah! Allah has provided you with lawful, good sustenance, but you chose what Allah has forbidden of His provision over what He has made lawful of His lawful sustenance. If I had warned you before, I would have done so. Get away from me and repent to Allah. Indeed, if you obtain anything after this warning, I will strike you a painful blow, shave your head as a disgrace, banish you from your family, and make your spoils lawful plunder for the youths of Madinah.” Amr got up, bearing evil and disgrace that only Allah knows. When he turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said, “These are the disobedient ones. Whoever among them dies without repentance, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection as he was, effeminate, naked, not covering himself from the people even with a thread; whenever he stands, he falls down.”"],[7308,"«I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on one of his journeys. He prayed Isha, then slept until, when it was around the middle of the night, he rose and recited these verses from the end of Surah Al Imran until he completed the surah. Then he performed ablution, used the siwak, and prayed two rak'ahs—I do not know whether his standing, bowing, or prostration was longer.» Then he said: «Then he woke and recited the verses again, then used the siwak, performed ablution, and did the same as before. Then he prayed the same as the first time. Then he continued praying two rak'ahs at a time, sleeping and then waking as he did the first time, until he had prayed eleven rak'ahs.»"],[7309,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: «Verily, when the sun rises, Satan accompanies it; when it becomes high, he leaves it; when it nears its zenith, he accompanies it; when it declines, he leaves it; when it nears its setting, he accompanies it; and when it sets, he leaves it.» So he prohibited prayer at those times."],[7310,"We set out as pilgrims. When we were at al-Arj, we came upon a snake writhing, and before long it died. A man among us took out a cloth from his 'ubayyah and wrapped it, and dug a trench for it in the ground. Then we arrived in Makkah, and while we were in the Sacred Mosque, a person stood before us and said: 'Which of you is the companion of Amr b. Jabir?' We said: 'We do not know him.' He said: 'Which of you is the companion of the jinni?' They said: 'This one.' He said: 'Indeed he was the last of the nine believers who came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to listen to the Quran.'"],[7311,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to announce: «Do not make nabidh in earthenware jars.»"],[7312,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was reclining in the mosque on a cloak of his, and I said to him: 'O Messenger of God, I have come seeking knowledge.' He said: «Welcome to the seeker of knowledge. The seeker of knowledge—the angels cover him and shade him with their wings, then they climb one upon another until they reach the lowest heaven, out of love for what he seeks. What have you come to seek?» He said: Safwan said: 'O Messenger of God, we do not cease traveling between Makkah and Madinah, so give us a ruling about wiping over the leather socks.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: «Three days for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.»"],[7313,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey, a man came and said: 'O Muhammad.' They said: 'Lower your voice.' He said: 'O Messenger of God, a man loves a people but has not seen them.' He said: «A person is with those whom he loves.» Then he asked him about wiping over the leather socks, and he said: «Three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident. He does not remove them for urine, sleep, or defecation, only for major impurity.» Then he asked him about repentance, and he said: «For repentance there is a gate in the west, a journey of seventy years—or forty years—that remains open until some of the signs of your Lord come: the sun's rising from its west.»"],[7314,"Indeed, no one does what you have done except that the angels lower their wings for him, pleased with what he does. I said: 'I came early to ask you about wiping over the leather socks.' He said: 'I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Should I wipe over the leather socks, O Messenger of God?' He said: «Yes, three for the traveler—he does not remove them due to defecation, urine, or sleep—and a day for the resident.»"],[7360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ has opened a gate from the west, its extent being seventy years, for repentance; He will not close it until the sun rises from its west. And no man goes out seeking knowledge except that the angels lay down their wings for him, pleased with what he does.” At that the Arabs said, “O Prophet of Allah, has not Allah given a servant a single trait that is better?” He said, “Good character.” Then they said to him, “Shall we seek medical treatment?” He said, “Do you not know that the One who sent down the disease sent down the cure – or no disease has been sent down except that He sent down a cure for it, except one disease.” They said, “O Prophet of Allah, what is it?” He said, “Old age.” Then he said, “For the traveler, three days to wipe over his leather socks; and for the resident, one day and one night.”"],[7361,"\"A Jew said to his companion: 'Let us go to this Prophet.' His companion said to him: 'Do not say Prophet; if he hears you, he will become big-headed.' So they came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and asked him about nine clear signs. He said to them: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill any soul whom Allah has forbidden you to kill, except by right, do not speak falsely about an innocent man before a ruler, do not engage in magic, do not consume Riba (usury), do not slander chaste women, and do not flee on the day of the march (to battle). And for you Jews especially, do not break the Sabbath.' They kissed his hands and feet and said: 'We bear witness that you are a Prophet.' He said: 'What is keeping you from following me?' They said: 'Dawud prayed that there would always be a Prophet among his descendants, and we are afraid that if we follow you, the Jews will kill us.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4078)"],[7362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military expedition and said: “Raid in the name of Allah, in the path of Allah. Do not steal from the spoils, do not act treacherously, and do not kill a child. And for the traveler, three days and their nights; and for the resident, one day and one night to wipe over the leather socks.”"],[7363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urged the seeking of knowledge before its disappearance. A man said, “How will it disappear when we have learned it and taught it to our children?” He became angry and said, “Are not the Torah and the Gospel in the hands of the People of the Book? Does that avail them anything?”"],[7364,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Delay the midday prayer until it cools down, for intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell.”"],[7365,"My father Safwan migrated to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam. The Prophet ﷺ extended his hand to him and wiped over it. Safwan said to him, “I love you, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “A person is with the one he loves.”"],[7366,"He went to his sheep and hunted two rabbits, then slaughtered them with a piece of white flint. He brought them to the Prophet ﷺ and presented them. He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered them with a piece of white flint.” He said, “Eat both of them.”"],[7371,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “O Suhar b. Abbas, make your drink good and give your neighbor to drink.”"],[7372,"He had a connection, Sila b. al-Harith al-Ghifari, and he is one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"By Allah, we did not abandon the covenant of our Prophet, nor did we sever our ties of kinship until you and your companions stood among us.\""],[7375,"From Shuqran, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"I saw him, meaning the Prophet ﷺ, heading on the day of Khaybar on a donkey, praying while gesturing.\""],[7431,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever introduces satire against Islam, cut off his tongue.” Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal said, meaning that he satirized Islam."],[7470,"A man died during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and no shroud was found for him. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Look inside his waist wrapper.\" A dinar or two dinars were found. He said: \"Two cauterizations. Pray over your companion.\" A man said: \"I will pay it, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he prayed over him."],[7514,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks after he had urinated."],[7515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Love is from Allah and reputation is in the heaven. When Allah loves a servant, He says: ‘O Gabriel, your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him.’ Then Gabriel calls out in the heaven: ‘Your Lord loves so-and-so, so love him.’ Then love is sent down for him upon the people of the earth.”"],[7584,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called for his leather socks to put them on. He put on one of them, then a crow came and carried off the other, then dropped it, and a snake came out of it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day should not put on his leather socks until he shakes them out.\""],[7594,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Gabriel kept instructing me about the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"],[7595,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: Mary asked her Lord for meat without blood, and He fed her locusts. She said, “O God, give him life without nursing and make him grow without satiation.”"],[7596,"The Prophet ﷺ came during the Farewell Pilgrimage on a she-camel until he stopped in the middle of the people on the Day of 'Arafah and said: \"Which day is this?\" They said: The Day of 'Arafah, the sacred day. He said: \"Then which month?\" They said: In the sacred month. He said: \"Then which land is this?\" They said: The sacred land. He said: \"Indeed your wealth, your honors, and your blood are sacred to you as this day of yours in this month of yours in this land of yours. Indeed every prophet's supplication has passed except my supplication, for I have stored it with my Lord until the Day of Resurrection. Now then, the prophets are vying in numbers, so do not disgrace me, for I will be waiting for you at the Basin.\""],[7600,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no servant who dies and leaves behind gold and silver but he will be branded with it.\""],[7601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The borrowed item is to be returned, the gift is to be given back, and whoever finds a she-camel whose udder has been tied up, it is not lawful for him to untie it until he returns it.\""],[7602,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By the intercession of a single man who is not a prophet, the like of the two tribes, or one of the two tribes, Rabi'ah and Mudar, will certainly enter Paradise.\""],[7603,"That he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among the best of people are the kings, the kings of Himyar, Sufyan, al-Sakun, and al-Ash'ariyyin.\""],[7604,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a commander, he said: \"Shorten the sermon and reduce the speech.\""],[7608,"From the hadith of 'Amr al-Hadrami from the people of Homs, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon one day, and most of his sermon was mention of the Dajjal, warning us against him, telling us about him until he finished his sermon. Among what he said to us that day: \"Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not sent a prophet except that he warned his nation, and I am the last of the prophets and you are the last of the nations, and he will certainly come out among you. If he comes out while I am among you, then I am the advocate for every Muslim, and if he comes out among you after me, then each person is the advocate for himself, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is my successor over every Muslim. He will come out from a gap between Iraq and the Levant, spreading corruption right and left. O servants of Allah, remain steadfast, for he will begin by saying: I am a prophet, and there is no prophet after me. Indeed, written between his eyes is 'disbeliever', which every believer will read. Whoever of you meets him should spit in his face and recite the opening verses of Surah of the Companions of the Cave. He will be given power over one soul from the children of Adam, so he will kill it and then bring it back to life, and he will not go beyond that, nor will he be given power over any soul other than it. Among his trials is that with him are a Paradise and a Fire, but his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire. Whoever is tested with his fire should close his eyes and seek help from Allah, and it will be coolness and peace, just as the fire was coolness and peace for Ibrahim. His days are forty days: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and the rest of the days like ordinary days. The last of his days is like a mirage: a man reaches the gate of the city in the morning, and he walks before he reaches its other gate.\" They said: How should we pray, O Messenger of Allah, in those short days? He said: \"Estimate them as you estimate the long days.\""],[7610,"The Prophet ﷺ would say to his companions: \"If one of you has performed ablution, then he eats food, he should perform ablution again, unless it is camel milk. When you drink it, rinse your mouths with water.\""],[7612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A borrowed item is to be returned.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about a covenant with Allah?\" He said, \"A covenant with Allah is most worthy of being fulfilled.\""],[7613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Whoever prays Fajr in a mosque in congregation, then remains until he performs the Duha glorification, will have the reward of a complete Hajj and Umrah, with his Hajj and Umrah accepted.\""],[7614,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A person gets what he intends, and bears what he earns, and a person is with the one he loves. Whoever dies at the end of the road is from its people.\""],[7617,"I heard an elderly man called Abu Abdullah Marih narrate that he heard Abu Umamah narrate that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I do not fear for my Ummah hunger that kills them, nor an enemy that destroys them, but I fear for my Ummah misleading leaders. If they obey them, they will tempt them, and if they disobey them, they will kill them.\""],[7618,"I heard Abu Umamah say: A man died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and they could not find a shroud for him. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we could not find a shroud for him.\" He said, \"Look in his waist-wrapper.\" They found two dinars. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Two brands. Pray over your companion.\""],[7625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah loves that His concessions be accepted, just as the servant loves the forgiveness of his Lord.\""],[7626,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent out a commander, he would say: \"Shorten the sermon and reduce the speech, for some speech is sorcery.\""],[7683,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The gates of heaven are opened and the supplication of the Muslim is answered at the establishment of prayer, at the descent of rain, at the advance of the ranks, and at the sight of the Kaʿbah.”"],[7684,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no Muslim who is in charge of ten or more people but he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand shackled to his neck; his righteousness will release it or his sin will bind it. Its beginning is blame, its middle is regret, and its end is the punishment of the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7685,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when he was asked: “Will the people of Paradise have marital relations?” He said: “Yes, with a male organ that does not tire and desire that does not cease, thrust after thrust.”"],[7686,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not fast on Saturday except for an obligatory fast, and if you find nothing but the bark of a tree, then break your fast with it.”"],[7720,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Good character is part of faith, and the best of you in faith are the best of you in character.”"],[7733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.”"],[7741,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, did not make permissible anything in tribulation that He had forbidden before that. What is the matter with one of you that he comes to his brother and greets him, then later comes and kills him?”"],[7744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, a group of people will stand up, filling the horizon, their light like the sun. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it (i.e., wonder if it refers to him). Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then another group will stand up, filling what is between the horizons, their light like the moon on the night of the full moon. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it. Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then another group will stand up, filling what is between the horizons, their light like a star in the sky. It will be said: 'The unlettered Prophet.' Every prophet will feel for it. Then it will be said: 'Muhammad and his community.' Then he will take two scoops and say: 'This is for you, O Muhammad, and this is from me for you, O Muhammad.' Then the Balance will be set up and the reckoning will begin.\""],[7750,"I witnessed the Prophet's ﷺ sermon in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said many good and beautiful things, and among what he said was: \"Whoever from the People of the two Books (Jews and Christians) becomes Muslim, he will have his reward twice, and he will have the same as what is due to us, and upon him the same as what is due from us. And whoever from the polytheists becomes Muslim, he will have his reward, and he will have the same as what is due to us, and upon him the same as what is due from us.\""],[7758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he praises Allah for it, except that that praise is better than that blessing, even if it were great.”"],[7759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever is terrified by the night to endure it, is stingy with wealth to spend it, and is cowardly before the enemy to fight him, let him frequently say: Glory be to Allah and with His praise. For it is more beloved to Allah than a mountain of gold and silver spent in the path of Allah, Exalted and Glorified."],[7760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah’s chosen land is al-Sham, and in it are His chosen ones from His creation and His servants. A throng from my nation will certainly enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.”"],[7764,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is overwhelmed by the night such that he struggles through it, or is miserly with wealth such that he withholds spending it, or is cowardly before the enemy such that he fears fighting him, let him say abundantly: ‘Glory be to God and with His praise,’ for it is more beloved to God than a mountain of gold that he spends in the path of God ﷻ.”"],[7765,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no hāmah, no ṣafar, no contagion, and two months do not complete thirty days.”"],[7766,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever says in the morning three times: ‘O God, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I have entered upon the morning upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from my evil deeds and seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,’ then if he dies on that day he will enter Paradise. And if he says in the evening three times: ‘O God, to You belongs praise; there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I believe in You, sincerely devoting my religion to You. I have entered upon the evening upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I repent to You from my evil deeds and seek Your forgiveness for my sins which none forgives but You,’ then if he dies on that night he will enter Paradise. He said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ used to swear an oath that he would not swear about anything else, saying: “By God, no servant says it in the morning three times and then dies on that day but that he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening three times then dies on that night but that he will enter Paradise.”"],[7825,"from the Prophet ﷺ that he said, \"Indeed, Allah has forbidden the teaching of female singers, the buying and selling of them, and the consumption of their earnings.\""],[7867,"A foul-tongued woman, known for that, came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ while he had some dried meat before him that he was eating. He took a piece of dried meat with sinew and put it in his mouth, chewing it sometimes on one side and sometimes on the other. The woman said, \"O Prophet of Allah, will you not feed me?\" He said, \"Of course.\" He handed her some of what was before him, but she said, \"No, only the piece in your mouth.\" So he took it out and gave it to her. She took it, put it in her mouth, and kept chewing it until she swallowed it. After that, the foulness and sharpness of tongue that she had were no longer known of her."],[7868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever invites you, respond to him.\""],[7889,"The greatest name of God, when invoked, answers in three Surahs from the Quran: Al-Baqarah, Al-Imran, and Taha."],[7890,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever supplicates with these supplications after every prescribed prayer, my intercession will be permitted for him on the Day of Resurrection: ‘O God, grant Muhammad the wasilah, and place his love among the chosen, his rank among the worlds, and the remembrance of his abode among those brought near.’”"],[7893,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said, “Whoever wipes the head of an orphan, for every hair he will have a good deed.”"],[7938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Pray.” Then he said: “Will not anyone give charity to this man by praying with him?” A man stood and prayed with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And this is a congregation.”"],[7939,"She was called Umm Hashim. She seated him behind the curtain with an inkpot and a pen, and sent to Abu Umamah asking him about a hadith he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about ablution. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever rises to perform ablution and washes his hands, sins depart from his hands. When he rinses his mouth, sins depart from his mouth. When he sniffs water into his nose and blows it out, they depart from his nose. Thus it continues until he washes his feet. If he goes out to an obligatory prayer, it is like an accepted Hajj. If he goes out to a voluntary prayer, it is like an accepted Umrah.”"],[7942,"A slave lowered himself from the fortress of al-Ta’if and came. His master came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, return my slave to me.” He said: “If a slave accepts Islam before his master, he is not returned to him. If the master accepts Islam, then the slave accepts Islam, the slave is handed over to him.”"],[7943,"I witnessed Abu Umaymah while he was in the throes of death. He said, \"If I die, then treat me as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to treat our deceased. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When one of your brethren dies, and you have leveled the earth over his grave, let one of you stand at the head of his grave, and say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So.' For verily, he hears him but does not respond. Then let him say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So.' For verily, he sits up straight. Then let him say, 'O So-and-So, son of So-and-So,' for verily, he says, 'Guide us, may Allah have mercy on you, but you do not perceive.' Then let him say, 'Remember what you used to say in the world: testimony that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that you were pleased with Allah as your Lord, with Islam as your religion, with Muhammad as your Prophet, and with the Quran as your Imam. For verily, Munkar and Nakir will come to him, and one of them will take his hand and say, 'Come with us, where we shall seat ourselves with one who has been taught his argument.' Then Allah shall be his advocate against them.' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what if his mother doesn't know him?' He said, 'Then he will be attributed to Hawwa, O son of Hawwa.'\""],[7944,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When a servant stands in prayer, the gates of Paradise are opened for him, the veils between him and his Lord are lifted, and the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise face him, as long as he does not blow his nose or spit.”"],[7945,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fasts on Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside.”"],[7951,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “Praise be to God as many as what God has created; praise be to God as many as what His Book has enumerated; praise be to God as many as every thing; praise be to God for every thing; glory be to God for every thing; and glory be to God as many as every thing.”"],[7952,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it.”"],[7953,"While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting, a woman came with her children, carrying some of them while others walked. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she did not ask him for anything that day except that he gave it to her. Then she departed walking. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “They are bearers, mothers, and merciful to their children. Were it not for what they do with their husbands, their praying women would enter Paradise.”"],[7956,"I entered the mosque of Hims, and there was Abu Umama delousing himself in it and burying the lice in it. I sat with him, and he glorified God three times, said God is greater three times, and praised God three times. Then he said: “They are light on the tongue, heavy in the balance, and they ascend to the Most Merciful.” I said: “O Abu Umama, I am from the desert people, and the alms collectors used to transgress against us.” He said: “Alms are a right, and its collectors are in the Fire. The saying of the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘Whether he falls short or transgresses, bring the wealth as a delegation and do not hide any of it, lest you corrupt what you hide. When you see them, do not revile them, but seek refuge in God from their evil.’”"],[7959,"Abu Umamah narrated to me in a hadith he raised to the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “No Muslim performs ablution, washing his hands, rinsing his mouth, and performing ablution as he has been commanded, except that Allah removes from him the sins he committed that day — what his mouth uttered, what his hand touched, and what he walked toward — so that the sins trickle down from his extremities. Then when he walks to the mosque, one foot records a good deed and the other erases a bad deed.”"],[7960,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The bath on Friday pulls out sins from the roots of the hair, a thorough pulling out.”"],[7961,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Some people from my Ummah will spend their nights indulging in food, amusement, and play, and then they will wake up in the morning transformed into monkeys and pigs.\""],[7962,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years. His prayer every day was ten rak'ahs: two rak'ahs of Fajr, two before Zuhr, two after Maghrib, and two after Isha."],[7965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ favored me over the prophets — or he said: my ummah over the nations — with four things: He sent me to all people; He made the whole earth a means of purification and a mosque for me and my ummah, so wherever a man of my ummah is overtaken by the prayer, his mosque and his purification are right there; I was aided with terror (cast into the hearts of the enemy) for a month’s journey; and the spoils of war were made lawful for me.”"],[7971,"From the Prophet ﷺ: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the husband over the wife?” He said: “If a woman were to go out of her house and then return to find her husband afflicted with severe leprosy, his nose constantly dripping, and she were to lick it with her tongue, she would not have fulfilled his right. A woman may not go out of her husband’s house except with his permission, nor may she give from his house except with his permission.”"],[7979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter, and the first of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise will be the people of goodness.\""],[7991,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the morning or the evening, he would supplicate with these words: “O God, You are more worthy of being remembered and more worthy of giving. You are the King, no partner is with You. You are the One, nothing perishes except Your face. You are not obeyed except by Your permission, and You are not disobeyed except by Your knowledge. When You are obeyed You give thanks, and when You are disobeyed You forgive. You are the nearest witness and the closest guardian. You intervened before the frontiers, You seized the forelocks, You recorded the traces, and You copied the appointed times. The hearts are disclosed to You, and the secret with You is open. The lawful is what You have made lawful, the unlawful is what You have made unlawful, the religion is what You have legislated, the command is what You have decreed, the creation is Your creation, and the servant is Your servant. You are God, the Clement, the Merciful. I ask You by the light of Your face, by which the heavens and the earth shine, by every right that is Yours, and by the right of those who ask You, that You accept me in this morning or in this evening and that You protect me from the Fire by Your power.”"],[7994,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever peeps at a people through a qatarah (small hole), and his eye is gouged out, it is wasted.” Hafs said, “The qatarah is the small window.”"],[7995,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “No Muslim attends a prescribed prayer, performs ablution well, then prays well, except that God forgives by it the sins between it and the prayer that was before it.”"],[8050,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When Allah created the intellect, He said to it, 'Come forward,' and it came forward. Then He said to it, 'Turn back,' and it turned back. He said, 'By My might, I have not created a creation more wondrous to Me than you. By you I give, and by you is reward, and upon you is punishment.'\""],[8051,"The Prophet ﷺ laughed and then said, \"I wonder about people who are being dragged to Paradise in chains while they dislike it.\""],[8052,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Allah has those freed from the Fire at every breaking of the fast.\""],[8053,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Allah has, at every breaking of the fast, those freed from the Fire.\""],[8054,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Three people's prayer does not go beyond their heads: a runaway slave, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and an imam who leads a people while they dislike him.\""],[8055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Spitting in the mosque is a bad deed, and burying it is a good deed.\""],[8056,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever spits in the mosque and does not bury it, it is a bad deed, and if he buries it, it is a good deed.\""],[8058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it.\""],[8059,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he spoke, would speak three times so that he could be understood."],[8060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives, \"Do not make this boy cry,\" meaning Husayn. He said, \"It was the day of Umm Salamah, so Jibril ﷺ descended and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the inner chamber and said to Umm Salamah, 'Do not let anyone enter upon me.' Husayn ؓ came, and when he saw the Prophet ﷺ in the house, he wanted to enter, so Umm Salamah took him and held him in her lap, and began to soothe him and calm him. When he intensified in crying, she let him go, so he entered until he sat in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. Jibril ﷺ said, 'Your nation will kill this son of yours.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'They will kill him while they are believers in me?' He said, 'Yes, they will kill him.' Then Jibril took some soil and said, 'At such and such a place.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, embracing Husayn, distressed and troubled, so Umm Salamah thought that he was angry at the boy's entering upon him. She said, 'O Prophet of Allah, may I be your ransom, you told us not to make this boy cry, and you commanded me not to let anyone enter upon you, but he came, so I let him go.' He did not answer her. He went out to his companions while they were sitting and said to them, 'My nation will kill this one.' Among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar ؓ, and they were the boldest of the people toward him, so they said, 'O Prophet of Allah, they will kill him while they are believers?' He said, 'Yes, and this is his soil,' and he showed it to them.\""],[8061,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The imam is a guarantor, and the mu'adhdhin is entrusted.\""],[8062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Three people whose prayer does not go beyond their ears until they return: the runaway slave, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and the imam of a people who dislike him."],[8063,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Bahilah. I came to them while they were having a meal. They welcomed me and honored me and said, \"Come and eat.\" I said, \"I have come to forbid you from this food, and I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I have come to you so that you may believe in him.\" They disbelieved me and rebuked me, so I left while I was hungry and thirsty, having suffered severe hardship. I slept and was brought in my sleep a drink of milk, which I drank and quenched my thirst, and my stomach became full. The people said, \"A man from the best and noblest of you came to you, and you rejected him. Go to him and feed him of food and drink whatever he desires.\" They brought me food, but I said, \"I have no need of your food and drink, for Allah has fed me and given me drink.\" So look at the state I am in. They looked and so they believed in me and in what I brought from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8064,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Give me a servant.\" He said to him, \"There are three in the house; choose one of them.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you choose for me.\" He said, \"Take this boy, for I saw him praying since we left, for a while, and do not beat him, for we have been forbidden from beating the people of prayer.\""],[8065,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog.\""],[8066,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels sit at the doors of the mosques on Friday and write down the first, the second, and the third. When the imam comes out, the scrolls are raised.\""],[8067,"He said: \"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"The speech of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Quran, and he increased in remembrance, shortened the sermon, and lengthened the prayer. He did not disdain or feel too proud to go with the poor and the weak until he fulfilled their need.\""],[8068,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Abu Dharr a slave and said, \"Feed him from what you eat and clothe him from what you wear.\" Abu Dharr had a garment, so he tore it into two halves, wrapping himself in one half and giving the other half to the slave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Why do I see your garment like this?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you said: Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Should I free him?\" He said, \"May Allah reward you, O Abu Dharr.\""],[8069,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at midday, for at that time Hell is stoked.\""],[8070,"From the Prophet ﷺ, or from the brother of Abu Umamah, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not pray at sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at sunset, for it sets between the two horns of a devil, and every disbeliever prostrates to it. Do not pray at midday, for at that time Hell is stoked.\""],[8071,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"He forbade prayer when the horn of the devil rises or sets.\""],[8072,"Abu Umamah asked the Prophet ﷺ: \"At what time is prayer disliked?\" He said, \"From the time you pray the dawn prayer until the sun rises a spear's length, and from the time the sun turns yellow until it sets.\""],[8073,"From Abu Umamah and his brother, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a people performing ablution and said, \"Woe to the heels from the Fire.\""],[8074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people performing ablution, and on the heel of one of them there was a spot the size of a dirham that the water did not reach. He said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the things I fear most for my ummah in its latter time are the stars, the denial of divine decree, and the injustice of rulers.”"],[8078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people performing ablution, and on their feet there remained a spot the size of a dirham that the water did not reach. So he said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8079,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he saw a man perform ablution for prayer, leaving a spot the size of a fingernail unwashed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to complete the ablution, then said: “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[8080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some people, and on the heel of one of them there was a spot like a dirham or the size of a fingernail that the water did not reach. He began saying: “Woe to the heels from the Fire” twice."],[8081,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “My Lord came to me in the most beautiful form and said: ‘O Muhammad.’ I said: ‘At Your service, gladly.’ He said: ‘About what does the highest assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘I do not know.’ So He placed His hand between my chest and I came to know in that moment all that He asked me about concerning the affairs of this world and the Hereafter. He said: ‘About what does the highest assembly dispute?’ I said: ‘About degrees and expiations. As for degrees, they are performing ablution thoroughly in severe cold, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous one.’ He said: ‘You have spoken truth. Whoever does that lives in good and dies in good, and his sins are removed as on the day his mother gave birth to him. As for expiations, they are feeding others, spreading peace, kind speech, and praying while people sleep.’ Then he said: ‘O Allah, I ask You for good deeds, abandonment of evil deeds, love for the poor, forgiveness, and that You accept my repentance. If You intend a trial for a people, deliver me from it without being afflicted.’”"],[8082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Learn the Qur’an, for it will intercede for its companions on the Day of Resurrection. Learn Surat al-Baqarah and Al ‘Imran. Learn the two radiant ones, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection like two clouds or two canopies, or like two flocks of birds in rows, arguing in defense of their companion. And learn Surat al-Baqarah, for learning it is a blessing, abandoning it is a regret, and the idle cannot master it.” He meant by the idle the magicians."],[8083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to learn the Qur’an and urged us to it, saying: “The Qur’an will come to its people on the Day of Resurrection when they are most in need of it. It will say to the Muslim: ‘Do you recognize me?’ He will say: ‘Who are you?’ It will say: ‘I am the one whom you used to love and hate to part with, the one who would draw you near and bring you close.’ He will say: ‘Perhaps you are the Qur’an.’ Then he will be brought before his Lord, may He be exalted, and he will be given sovereignty in his right hand and eternity in his left, tranquility will be placed on his head, and upon his parents will be spread two robes the likes of which the world cannot weigh. They will say: ‘For what have we been clothed with this when our deeds did not merit it?’ It will be said: ‘This is because your child took up the Qur’an.’”"],[8084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I and the sponsor of an orphan will be in Paradise like these two.”"],[8085,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"],[8086,"The Prophet ﷺ came out while I was sitting moving my lips, so he said, “What are you moving your lips for?” I said, “I am remembering Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Shall I not tell you something that, if you say it and then persist night and day, you would not reach it?” I said, “Yes, please.” He said, “Say: All praise is due to Allah, as many as His Book has enumerated; and all praise is due to Allah, as many as what is in His Book; and all praise is due to Allah, as many as His creation has enumerated; and all praise is due to Allah for what is in His creation; and all praise is due to Allah, filling His heavens and His earth; and all praise is due to Allah, the number of all things; and all praise is due to Allah, filling all things. And glorify Him similarly, and magnify Him similarly.”"],[8087,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “No household over whom a faddān (a yoke of oxen) arrives but they are humiliated.”"],[8088,"\"Be upright and well, if you persist in uprightness. No one can maintain their ablution except a believer.\""],[8089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Give glad tidings to those who walk in the dark to the mosques of pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection, when people will be terrified but they will not be terrified.”"],[8091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me, or by a man milking, and said, “Leave the milk that remains in the udder (dawāʿī al-laban).” This is how Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Sinān, and the companions of al-Aʿmash disagreed with him, narrating it from al-Aʿmash, from Yaʿqūb b. Buḥayr."],[8092,"We gave a milch camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I milked it for him. When I took hold of it to exhaust the milk, he said, “Do not do that; leave the milk that remains in the udder.”"],[8093,"My family sent me with a milch camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, having given it to him as a gift. He said to me, “Milk it and leave the remaining milk in the udder,” and he supplicated for me."],[8094,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a she-camel as a gift. He said to me, “Get up and milk it.” So I got up and milked it. When I went to exhaust the milk, he said, “Leave the remaining milk in the udder.”"],[8095,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with the offspring of my camels. He said, “Milk it,” so I said, “Shall I exhaust the milk?” He said, “Do not exhaust it; leave the milk that remains in the udder.”"],[8098,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There will not cease to be a guardian (wālī) from Quraysh.”"],[8099,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of a dark night, tribulations like patches of smoke. In them a man's heart will die just as his body dies. In them a man will wake up as a believer and end the day as a disbeliever, and he will end the day as a believer and wake up as a disbeliever. In them some people will sell their morals and their religion for a paltry gain of this world.\" And indeed Yazid b. Mu'awiya has died, and you are our brothers and our full brothers, so do not precede us with anything until we choose for ourselves."],[8100,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"When a man comes to a people and they say, 'Welcome, welcome to him until the day he meets his Lord,' and when a man comes to a people and they say, 'Barren, barren for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[8101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Trim and do not exhaust, for it is more radiant for the face and more favorable with the husband.\""],[8102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Dahhak, what is your food?\" I said, \"Meat and milk.\" He said, \"Then what does it become?\" I said, \"Then it becomes what you know.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ has made what comes out of the son of Adam a parable for this world.\""],[8103,"\"I do not consider the blood money to belong to anyone but the male relatives, because they pay on his behalf. Does any of you have anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that?\" Dahhak b. Sufyan al-Kilabi, whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed over the Bedouins, said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me to give an inheritance to the wife of Ashim al-Dibabi from the blood money of her husband.\" 'Umar ؓ adopted that."],[8104,"\"Enter your dome so that I may inform you.\" He entered, and the [Prophet] came to him and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me that a woman from Ashyam Al-Dibabiy is to inherit from her husband’s mind.\""],[8105,"I do not know anything for you, then we call upon the people that anyone who has knowledge from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let him stand up. Then Dhahhak bin Sufyan al-Kilabi stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to me that I should inherit the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi from the blood money of her husband.\" So Umar inherited her."],[8106,"“The blood money is for the near male relatives from the father's side and the wife does not inherit anything from the blood money of her husband,” until Ad-Dahhak bin Sufyan wrote to him, and told him that the Prophet ﷺ ruled that the wife of Ashyam bin Dibabi should inherit from the blood money of her husband. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2642)"],[8107,"\"Ashim al-Dibabi had been killed by mistake.\""],[8108,"From 'Urwa, in naming those who attended the 'Aqaba pledge to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from the Banu Tha'laba b. 'Ubayd: al-Dahhak b. Haritha b. Zayd b. Tha'laba, and he \"witnessed Badr.\""],[8109,"When the Prophet ﷺ marched to Khaybar, he placed 'Ali ؓ in command of his vanguard and said: \"Whoever enters the palm grove is safe.\" When the Prophet ﷺ said that, 'Ali ؓ proclaimed it. The Prophet ﷺ looked at Jibril ﷺ and smiled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What makes you smile?\" He said: \"I love him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali: \"Jibril says he loves you.\" He said: \"It has reached me that Jibril loves me.\" He said: \"Yes, and one better than Jibril: Allah the Exalted.\""],[8111,"It is said to him: Dimam. He was in Yemen, and he used to treat people possessed by spirits. He came to Makkah and heard them saying about Muhammad ﷺ: a sorcerer, a soothsayer, and a madman. So he said: \"If I go to this man, perhaps Allah will heal him through my hands.\" He met him and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah heals through my hands, and I treat these spirits.\" He said: \"Praise be to Allah, we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said: \"Repeat it to me.\" He repeated it to him three times. He said: \"I have heard the speech of soothsayers, the speech of sorcerers, and the poets, and I have never heard anything like these words. It has reached the depth of the sea. Stretch out your hand, I pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.\" He stretched out his hand and pledged allegiance to him upon Islam and upon my people. So he pledged allegiance to him upon his people."],[8112,"Dimam b. Tha'laba came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Shall I not perform ruqya on you, O Muhammad?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Praise be to God; we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of our souls and the misdeeds of our actions. Whomever God guides, there is none to misguide him; and whomever He misguides, there is none to guide him. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\" Dimam said, \"I have read the scriptures — the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms — but I have never heard the like of this speech. Repeat them to me.\" So he repeated them to him. Then he said, \"Repeat them to me,\" and he repeated them to him. Then it was mentioned that he embraced Islam."],[8113,"Banu Sa'd b. Bakr sent Dimam b. Tha'laba to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He came to him, made his camel kneel at the door of the mosque, then hobbled it, then entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was sitting in the mosque. Dimam was a man with thick hair and two locks, until he stood over the Messenger of God ﷺ and his Companions and said, \"Which of you is of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said, \"Muhammad?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"O son of 'Abd al-Muttalib, I am going to question you and be harsh in my questioning, so do not take it personally.\" He said, \"I will not take it personally; ask about whatever comes to you.\" He said, \"I adjure you by God, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those after you: Has God commanded you to command us to worship God alone, not associating anything with Him, and to cast off these rivals that our fathers used to worship besides Him?\" He said, \"O God, yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by God, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those after you: Has God commanded you to command us to perform these five prayers?\" He said, \"O God, yes.\" Then he began mentioning the obligations of Islam one by one: zakat, fasting, Hajj, and all the laws of Islam, adjuring him at each obligation as he had adjured him in the previous one. When he finished, he said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. I will fulfill these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me, not adding to it or diminishing it.\" Then he turned away toward his camel. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If the one with the two locks is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8114,"A man from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had been nursed among them. He said, \"O son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said, \"I have answered you.\" He said, \"I am the envoy of my people and their messenger, and I am going to question you, and my questioning will be intense, and I will adjure you, and my adjuration will be intense, so do not be angry with me.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Tell me: Who created the heavens and the earth, Paradise and Hell?\" He said, \"God, may He be exalted.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Him: Is it He who sent you with what came to us of your letter and your messengers came to us, that we should bear witness that there is no god but God and that we should abandon al-Lat and al-'Uzza?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I adjure you by Him: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should pray five prayers every day and night. I adjure you by Him: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should fast one month every year. I adjure you: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Your letter came to us and your messengers came to us, that we should perform Hajj to it in Dhul-Hijjah. I adjure you: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"These are five, and I will not add to them.\" When he turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, if he does what he said, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8115,"A bedouin from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Peace be upon you, O boy of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"And peace be upon you.\" He said, \"I am a man from your maternal uncles, from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, and I am the messenger of my people to you and their envoy. I am going to question you, so my questioning will be intense, and I will adjure you, so my adjuration will be intense.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go ahead, O brother of Banu Sa'd.\" He said, \"Who created you, and who created those before you, and who is the Creator of those after you?\" He said, \"God.\" He said, \"I adjure you by that: Is it He who sent you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Tell me: Who created the seven heavens and the seven earths, and made provision flow between them?\" He said, \"God.\" He said, \"I adjure you by that: Is it He who sent you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should pray night and day five prayers at their times. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that we should fast the month of Ramadan. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"We have found in your book, and your messengers commanded us, that you should take from the surplus of our wealth and put it among our poor. I adjure you by that: Is it He who commanded you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"As for the fifth, I am not asking about it, and I have no need of it\" — meaning obscene acts. Then he said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I will act upon these and whoever obeys me among my people.\" Then he turned back. The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then said, \"If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise.\""],[8117,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Husayn b. 'Abd Allah b. Dumayra narrated to us from his father from his grandfather that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, marry me to so-and-so.\" He said, \"What do you have to give her as her dower?\" He said, \"I have nothing.\" He said, \"Whose is this ring?\" He said, \"Mine.\" He said, \"Then give it to her.\" And he married him to her. And he married another man on the basis of Surat al-Baqarah when he had nothing."],[8118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young and does not recognize the right of our elders. And he is not one of us who deceives us. And a believer is not a believer until he loves for the believers what he loves for himself.\""],[8119,"From Damura b. Tha'laba al-Bahzi, a Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"He used to charge into the enemy's camp until he broke through the ranks, then return until he stood back in his place.\""],[8120,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"Pray to God for martyrdom for me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O God, I make the blood of Ibn Tha'laba forbidden to the polytheists and disbelievers.\" He said, \"I used to charge into the thick of the people, and the Prophet ﷺ would appear to me behind them.\" They said, \"O Ibn Tha'laba, you charge and attack the people.\" He said, \"The Prophet ﷺ appears to me behind them, so I charge at them until I stand beside him. Then he appears to me at my companions, so I charge until I am with my companions.\" He said, \"And he lived for a long time after that.\""],[8121,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People will remain in good as long as they do not envy one another.\""],[8122,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing two fine Yemeni garments. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do you think these two garments of yours will admit you to Paradise?\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, if you seek forgiveness for me, I will not sit down until I take them off.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O God, forgive Damura b. Tha'laba.\" He went off quickly until he took them off."],[8123,"Umm al-Harir, when a man of the Arabs died, it weighed heavily on her. It was said to her, \"Umm al-Harir, why do we see that when a man of the Arabs dies, it weighs heavily on you?\" She said, \"I heard my master say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Among the signs of the approach of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs.'\" Muhammad b. Abi Razin said, \"Her master was Talha b. Malik.\""],[8124,"When a man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and had no acquaintance in Madinah with whom to stay, he stayed with the people of the Suffah. I had companions there, and we used to receive from the Messenger of God ﷺ each day, between every two of us, two mudds of dates. While the Messenger of God ﷺ was in one of the prayers, a caller from among his Companions called out, \"O Messenger of God, the dates have burned our stomachs and our guts are on fire.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he stood up, praised God, and extolled Him, then mentioned what he and his people had endured of hardship. He said, \"I and my two companions spent more than ten days with no food except wild berries, until we came to our brothers among the Ansar, and they shared their food with us. The bulk of their food was dates. By the One besides whom there is no god, if I could find bread and meat for you, I would feed you. Perhaps you will live to see a time — or whoever among you lives to see it — when people will wear garments like the covering of the Ka'bah, and bowls of food will be brought to you morning and evening.\""],[8126,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I desire to wage jihad in the path of God.\" He said, \"Is your mother alive?\" I said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Stay close to her feet, for there is Paradise.\""],[8127,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Extend your hand.\" He said, \"Even if I command you to sever ties with your mother?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then I returned to him and said, 'Extend your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you.' He said, 'Upon what?' I said, 'Upon Islam.' He said, 'Even if I command you to sever ties with your mother?' I said, 'No.' Then I returned to him a third time. He had a mother and was one of the most dutiful of people to her. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'O Talha, there is no severing of kinship ties in our religion, but I wished that there be no doubt in your faith.' So he embraced Islam and his Islam was excellent. Then he fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ visited him and found him unconscious. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I think Talha will pass away tonight. If he regains consciousness, send for me.' Talha regained consciousness in the middle of the night and said, 'Did the Messenger of God ﷺ visit me?' They said, 'Yes,' and told him what he had said. He said, 'Do not send for him at this hour, lest an animal sting him or something befall him. But in the morning, convey my greetings to him and tell him to ask forgiveness for me.' Then he passed away. After the Prophet ﷺ prayed the dawn prayer, he asked about him, and they informed him of his death and what he had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ raised his hands and said, 'O God, meet him while he smiles at You and You smile at him.'"],[8175,"A delegation of Qays came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said: \"Begin with the Ahmasiyyin before the Qaysiyyin. O God, bless the Ahmasiyyin and their men.\""],[8176,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, in our land we have grapes that we press and drink from.' He said: 'No.' I repeated it and he said: 'No.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, we seek healing with it.' He said: 'That is not a cure, but it is a disease.'"],[8179,"On the authority of a brother of 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from her mother's side, from Banu Daws, he said: I saw in a dream that I met a group of Jews, so I asked them and they asked me. I said: 'You are a people, were it not that you say 'Uzayr is the son of God.' They said: 'And you, you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' Then I met their counterparts among the Christians, so I asked them and they asked me. I said: 'You are a people, were it not that you say the Messiah is the son of God.' They said: 'And you, you are a people, were it not that you say: What God wills and Muhammad wills.' So I told the Messenger of God ﷺ about it. He said: 'Did you tell anyone about it before me?' I said: 'Yes, O Prophet of God.' Then the Prophet of God ﷺ stood on the pulpit and said: 'Your brother saw a dream and has told you what he saw. What prevented me from forbidding you from that was shyness. So when you speak, say: What God wills alone.'"],[8183,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions arrived and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8184,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ faced the qibla and raised his hands. The people said, \"Daws is ruined.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8185,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8186,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God against them.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8187,"Ṭufayl b. ʿAmr al-Dawsī and his companions arrived and said, \"O Messenger of God, Daws has disobeyed and refused, so pray to God.\" It was said, \"Daws is ruined.\" He said, \"O God, guide Daws and bring them.\""],[8189,"That the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sent Tufayl ibn Amr and another person to Daws. They came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to destroy Daws.\" He said, \"O Allah, guide Daws and bring them to us.\""],[8190,"He hosted the Messenger of God ﷺ among a group of people. They spent the night at his place, and the Messenger of God ﷺ came out at night and found him lying on his stomach. He nudged him with his foot and woke him, then said, \"Do not lie like this, for it is the lying posture of the people of the Fire.\""],[8191,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave instructions, and one man went with another man, and one man went with two men, until I was left as the fifth of five. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Go.\" We went with him to ʿĀʾisha ؓ, and he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought hashīsha and we ate. Then she brought ḥaysa like a small bird and we ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, give us something to drink.\" She brought a small cup of milk and we drank. Then he said, \"If you wish, you may stay the night; and if you wish, go to the mosque.\" We said, \"We will go to the mosque.\" While I was lying on my stomach, a man moved me with his foot and said, \"This is a lying posture that God hates.\" I looked and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8193,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would look at the common people and say, \"So-and-so, take so-and-so and host him.\" He continued until I remained with the Messenger of God ﷺ as the fifth of five. He said to us, \"Go to the house.\" We went with him and entered the house of ʿĀʾisha ؓ—that was before the veil was imposed on them. He said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought hashīsha and we ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, feed us.\" She brought ḥaysa like a small bird and they ate. Then he said, \"O ʿĀʾisha, give us something to drink.\" She brought a bowl with ḍiyāḥ and they drank. Then he said to us, \"If you wish, stay here; and if you wish, go to the mosque.\" We said, \"No, rather we will go to the mosque,\" and we disliked burdening the Messenger of God ﷺ. I slept in the mosque, and while I was lying on my stomach, a man came to me and moved me with his foot and said, \"Turn over like this, for it is a sleeping posture that God Almighty hates.\" I looked and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8194,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque while I was sleeping on my stomach. He moved me with his foot and said, \"This is a sleeping posture that God hates.\" I raised my head and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[8195,"While I was lying down in the mosque, a man nudged me with his foot, saying, “[Lie] like this, for this is a posture that Allah ﷻ hates.” I raised my head and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O so-and-so, take this one with you; O so-and-so, take this one with you.” I remained the fourth of four. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “Go.” We set out until we came to the house of 'A'ishah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O 'A'ishah, feed us.” She brought some herbs, and we ate. Then he said, “O 'A'ishah, feed us.” She brought some hais the size of a small bird. Then he said, “O 'A'ishah, give us something to drink.” She brought a small cup of milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, “If you wish, stay the night here, or if you wish, go to the mosque.” We said, “Rather, we will go to the mosque.” While I was sleeping on my stomach before dawn, a man pushed me with his foot and said, “[Lie] like this, for this is a posture that Allah ﷻ hates.” I raised my head and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8197,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who performs ablution and then lowers his hand and touches his penis, or should I sprinkle water on it?” He said, “It is a part of you.”"],[8198,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am in prayer and I touch my penis with my hand.” He said, “It is a piece of you.”"],[8199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you desires his wife, let him come to her even if she is at the oven.”"],[8200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Fajr is not the white light that rises vertically, but rather the red glow that spreads horizontally.”"],[8202,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. If it is cloudy for you, then complete the count as thirty.”"],[8203,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was laying the foundations of the mosque of Madinah. I began carrying stones as they were carrying. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You people of al-Yamamah are the most skilled at mixing clay, so mix the clay for us.” I mixed the clay for them, and they carried it."],[8204,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say, “When a man calls his wife to his need, she should respond, even if she is at the oven.”"],[8205,"We set out, six of us, as a delegation to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: five from Banu Hanifah and the sixth a man from Banu Dab'ah b. Rabi'ah. We came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, prayed with him, and told him that in our land there was a church of ours. We asked him for some of the leftover water of his purification. He called for water, performed ablution with it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a water skin. He said, “Take this water, and when you reach your town, demolish your church, then sprinkle its place with the water, and take that place as a mosque.” We said, “O Prophet of Allah, the town is far and the water will dry up.” He said, “Then add water to it, for that will only increase its goodness.” We set out with it until we reached our town and did as he commanded. That day a monk from Tayyi' saw us, and when we called the adhan for prayer, the monk said, “A call of truth.” Then he fled, and we never saw him again."],[8206,"I built the mosque of Madinah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would say, “Let the Yamami handle the clay, for he is the best of you at kneading it.”"],[8207,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man, as if he were a Bedouin, asked him, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about a man who touches his private part after performing ablution?” He said, “Is it anything but a piece of flesh from you or a morsel?”"],[8208,"“A scorpion stung me while I was with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and he recited ruqyah over me.”"],[8209,"“O Prophet of Allah, what do you think about praying in a single garment?” So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ untied his lower garment, folded his cloak over it, wrapped himself in both, and led us in prayer. When he finished his prayer, he said, “Does every one of you find two garments?”"],[8210,"“When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ gave the salam in prayer, we would see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek.”"],[8211,"Qays ibn Talq said: Talq ibn Ali visited us on a certain day during Ramadan. He remained with us till evening and broke fast with us. He then stood up and led us in the witr prayer. He then went to his mosque and led them in prayer. When the witr remained, he put forward another man and said: Lead your companions in the witr prayer, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There are no two witrs during one night. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1439)"],[8212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A woman must not refuse her husband, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle.”"],[8213,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think: if one of us touches his private part, should he perform ablution?” He said, “No, it is only a piece of flesh from you.”"],[8214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A believer is not one whose neighbor is not safe from his harmful actions.”"],[8215,"From his father Talq b. Ali, who was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[8216,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever touches his private part must perform ablution.” This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub b. Utbah except by Hammad b. Muhammad, and Hammad b. Muhammad also narrated the other hadith. Both are authentic according to me. It seems likely that he heard the first hadith from the Prophet ﷺ before this one, then heard this one later. Thus it agrees with the hadith of Busrah, Umm Habibah, Abu Hurayrah, Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, and others who narrated from the Prophet ﷺ the command to perform ablution from touching the private part. So he heard both the abrogated and the abrogating."],[8217,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment?” He remained silent until the time of Asr prayer arrived, then he matched his lower garment with his outer sheet, wrapped himself in them like this, and led the Asr prayer. When he finished, he said, “Where is the one who asked about praying in a single garment?” The man said, “O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Does every one of the people find two garments?”"],[8218,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions while they were building the mosque. When I saw their work, I began skillfully handling the shovel and mixed the clay with it. It was as if he was pleased with my handling of the shovel and their work. He said, “Leave the Hanafi and the clay, for he is the most skilled of you with clay.” The wording is from the hadith of Asim b. Ali."],[8219,"He witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man asked him about a man praying in a single garment, but he said nothing. When the prayer was called, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ matched his two garments and prayed in them."],[8220,"We sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the delegation of Abd al-Qays came. He said, \"Why have your complexions turned yellow, your bellies grown large, and your veins become prominent?\" They said, \"Our leader came to you and asked you about a drink that suited us, and you forbade him from it. We were in a land that was unhealthy and feverish.\" He said, \"Then drink whatever seems good to you.\""],[8221,"He was brought in, so we entered. I served him tharid, meat, and nabidh. He ate and drank, and he pressed me, so I ate and drank with him, though I was afraid of the dawn. Then he said, \"My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Eat and drink, and do not let the spreading, rising light alarm you. Eat and drink until the red glow appears before you,'\" and he gestured with his hand."],[8222,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he forbade us to start fasting a day before Ramadan until we see the crescent or complete the count, and we should not break the fast until we see it or complete the count."],[8223,"We sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Mukhtar b. Abd al-Qays came and said, \"O Prophet of Allah, what do you think about a drink we make from our fruits?\" The Prophet ﷺ turned away from him until he asked him three times. Then he stood and led us in prayer. When he finished the prayer, he said, \"Who is the one asking about the intoxicant? You ask me: do not drink it and do not give it to your Muslim brother. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no man ever drinks it seeking to become intoxicated but that Allah will give him wine to drink on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8224,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to us, \"Soon there will come a people who recite the Qur'an but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes through the game. Blessed is the one who kills them, and blessed is the one whom they kill.\" Then he turned to me and said, \"Indeed, they will emerge in your land, O Tihami, fighting between the rivers.\" I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, it has no rivers.\" He said, \"Indeed, it will.\""],[8225,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his back in his bowing and prostration.\""],[8226,"\"I was mixing clay in Madinah when a scorpion stung me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and recited an incantation over me until I recovered.\""],[8227,"\"A scorpion stung Talq in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ recited a ruqyah over him and wiped him with his hand.\""],[8228,"From Urwah, in the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Zuhayr b. Rafi."],[8229,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who attended al-Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah b. al-Harith: Zuhayr b. Rafi."],[8230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us something that was beneficial to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said, \"What do you do with your cultivated fields?\" I said, \"We lease them for a quarter and an eighth.\" He said, \"Do not do that. Either cultivate them or keep them.\" I said, \"We hear and obey.\""],[8231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us something that was convenient for us. I said, \"What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said is true.\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you do with your cultivated fields?' We said, 'We lease them for a quarter, a third, and loads of straw and barley.' He said, 'Do not do that. Cultivate them or give them to be cultivated.'\""],[8232,"From ʿUrwah, regarding naming those who made the first emigration to the land of Abyssinia: Abū Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Asad, and with him was his wife Umm Salamah. She gave birth in the land of Abyssinia to ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah."],[8270,"The Messenger of God ﷺ seated me with him at a meal and said to me: “Mention the name of God, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you.”"],[8291,"Abu Quhafa was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, his head and beard like thaghama. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Take him to some of his women to change it.\" He said, \"So they took him and dyed it red.\""],[8298,"By Allah, I did not marry her when I married her out of desire for wealth or children, but I wanted her to tell me about ʿUmar’s night. So he asked her: How was ʿUmar’s prayer at night? She said: He would pray ʿatamah, then he would order us to place a basin of water at his head and cover it. He would wake during the night, put his hand in the water, wipe his face and hands, then remember Allah Almighty as much as he willed. Then he would wake again several times until he came to the hour in which he would stand for his prayer. Ibn Buraydah said to him: Who told you this? He said: The daughter of ʿUthmān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ told me. He said: Trustworthy, by Allah."],[8301,"The last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon me was: “When you lead people in prayer, lighten the prayer for them.”"],[8309,"When the north wind blew strongly, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have sent.'"],[8312,"The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon me was that I make the prayer light for the people."],[8317,"He informed him that the last thing upon which the Messenger of God ﷺ parted from him was: 'Make the prayer light for the people.'"],[8318,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to place the mosque of al-Ṭāʾif where their idol had been."],[8333,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who drinks it and the one who sells it,\" meaning wine."],[8349,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “Fasting is a shield with which the servant shields himself from the Fire.”"],[8350,"That he gave him wealth to trade with, the profit to be shared between them. He gave him twenty thousand dirhams, and with it he bought wine. Then he brought it to al-Ubulla, and ʿUthman went out to him and did not leave a single jar or anything else but smashed it. ʿUthman said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “cursed wine, its drinker, its buyer, its seller, its presser, and its carrier.”"],[8351,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, the torment of the grave, the trial of life, and the trial of death.”"],[8352,"That he used to prefer fasting while traveling, saying: “It was a concession.”"],[8353,"“Breaking the fast while traveling is a concession.”"],[8354,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: “The gates of heaven are opened halfway through the night, and a caller calls out: Is there any supplicant, that he may be answered? Is there any asker, that he may be given? Is there any distressed person, that he may be relieved? No Muslim remains supplicating with a supplication but Allah answers him, except an adulteress who goes about with her private parts or a tax collector.”"],[8355,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to the Muslims, \"There are three Egypt's: one at the meeting point of the two seas, one in the Nile Delta, and one in Sham (Syria). The Muslims will be terrified by three terrifying events: the emergence of the Dajjal (Antichrist) in the East, which will be defeated by the first Egypt (meeting point of the two seas) with an army of seventy thousand, accompanied by a group of Jews and women. The people of Egypt will be divided into three groups: one group will stay in Egypt and say, 'We will defend ourselves,' one group will join the Bedouins, and one group will join the second Egypt (in the Nile Delta). Then the Dajjal will proceed to Sham, while its people take refuge in the mountain pass of Afiq. They will send a detachment to confront him, but they will be defeated. They will face severe famine and hardships, to the extent that one of them will burn his bow and eat it. While they are in that state, a caller from the sky will announce, 'O people, here comes your help!' They will say, 'This is the voice of a well-fed person.' Then Jesus the son of Mary ﷺ will descend while leading the Fajr prayer, and the people will say to him, 'O Spirit of Allah, come forward and lead us in prayer.' He will reply, 'You are all leaders of Muhammad's nation, some of you leading others. So, you should come forward and lead the prayer.' The leader will then perform the prayer, and Jesus will take his weaponry and head towards the Dajjal. When the Dajjal sees Jesus, he will dissolve like salt in water, and Jesus will place his spear in the ground between the two horns of the Dajjal and kill him. The companions of the Dajjal will be defeated, and there will not be a single one among them without being killed. Even the trees and rocks will say, 'O believer, there is a disbeliever behind me, so kill him!'\""],[8356,"That ʿUthman b. Abi al-ʿAs came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some people of Thaqif. They entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: “Guard our goods, or our mounts, for us.” He said: “On condition that when you leave, you wait for me until I come out from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him for a copy of the Qur'an that he had, and he gave it to me. He appointed me over them and made me their imam, though I was the youngest of them.”"],[8357,"“The Islam of ʿAmr b. al-ʿAs, Khalid b. al-Walid, and ʿUthman b. Talha took place with the Negus, and they came to Madinah in Safar of the year eight of the Hijrah.”"],[8358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUthmān b. Ṭalḥah on the day of conquest: “Bring me the key of the Kaʿbah.” He was slow in bringing it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood waiting for him until sweat like pearls dripped from him, and he said: “What is delaying him?” A man hastened to him, while the woman who had the key—and it was thought that he said Umm ʿUthmān—said: “If he takes it from you, he will never give it back to you.” ʿUthmān kept after her until she gave him the key, and he went with it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He opened the door, then entered the House, then came out with the people with him and sat by the drinking place. ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ said to him: “O Messenger of Allah, if we have been given prophethood, and we have been given the siqāyah, and we have been given the ḥijābah, no people have a greater share than us.” He said: It was as if the Prophet ﷺ disliked his statement. Then he called ʿUthmān b. Ṭalḥah and handed the key to him and said: “Keep it hidden.” ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: I narrated this to Ibn ʿUyaynah, and he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me—I think from Ibn Abī Mulaykah—that the Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī that day when he spoke to him about the key: “I have only given you what you bear as a burden, and I have not given you what you will be burdened by.” He means: I gave you the siqāyah because you incur expense in it, and I did not give you the House—that is, they take from its gift. This is the statement of ʿAbd al-Razzāq."],[8359,"I asked ʿUthmān: Why did the Prophet ﷺ send for you after he came out of the Kaʿbah? He said: He said to me: “I saw the two horns of the ram and forgot to command you to cover them, for nothing should be in the House that distracts a person praying.”"],[8360,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying behind the middle pillar of the House, two rakʿahs. And in the House—or he said the Kaʿbah—there were three pillars."],[8361,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in the House."],[8362,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever steps over people’s necks on Friday after the imam has come out, or separates between two people, is like one who drags his intestines into the Fire.”"],[8363,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār: ʿUthmān b. ʿAmr b. Rifāʿah b. al-Ḥārith b. Sawwād."],[8364,"Mūsā b. ʿAwn b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd dictated to me the lineage of ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd: ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. Kāhil b. Ḥabīb b. Tāmir b. Makhzūm b. Ṣāhilah b. Kāhil b. al-Ḥārith b. Tamīm b. Saʿd b. Hudhayl b. Mudrikah b. Ilyās b. Muḍar b. Nizār."],[8365,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. al-Ḥārith b. Shamkh b. Makhzūm b. Ṣāhilah b. al-Ḥārith b. Tamīm b. Hudhayl b. Mudrikah b. Ilyās b. Muḍar b. Nizār b. Maʿd b. ʿAdnān, an ally of Banū Zuhrah, witnessed Badr."],[8366,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. al-Ḥārith b. Shamkh b. Makhzūm b. Kāhil b. al-Ḥārith b. Saʿd b. Hudhayl, from the allies of Banū Zuhrah."],[8367,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd died; he was nicknamed Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and he was some sixty-odd years old, in the year thirty-two in Madinah. He bequeathed to al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām, who prayed over him, and he was buried in al-Baqīʿ."],[8368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ nicknamed him Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, though no child was born to him."],[8369,"I saw myself as the sixth of six when there was no Muslim on the face of the earth other than us."],[8370,"Ibn Mas'ud used to wash his head, then leave his hair behind his ears."],[8371,"\"I saw Abdullah Ibn Masood throwing stones.\""],[8372,"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud ؓ had two braids and bore the mark of the people of the Jahiliyyah, and he had thin shins."],[8373,"We used to go to Abdullah b. 'Amr and talk to him, Ibn Numair said: One day we made a mention of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, whereupon he said: You have made mention of a person whom I love more than anything else. I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Learn Qur'an from four persons: Ibn Umm 'Abd (i. e. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud) he started from him-then Mu'adh b. Jabal and Ubayya b. Ka'b, then Salim the ally of Abu Hudhaifa. (Using translation from Muslim 2464a)"],[8374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek the Qur'an from four: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal, 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Khudhayfah.\""],[8375,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Take the Qur'an from four: from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud\"—and he began with him—\"and from Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah.\""],[8376,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by with Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and they passed by 'Abdullah while he was praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ibn Umm 'Abd, ask, and you will be given.\" 'Umar ؓ said: \"Abu Bakr and I raced, and we never raced to any good but that he beat me to it, so he gave him the good news.\" 'Abdullah said: \"I do not know except that among my supplications, which I can hardly leave off in my prayer, is: O Allah, I ask You for bliss that never ends, coolness of eyes that never perishes, and the companionship of Muhammad ﷺ in the highest garden of eternity.\""],[8377,"The Prophet ﷺ went out with Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ. Abu Bakr ؓ had invited them, so they went out from his house to the mosque, the mosque of Madinah. 'Abdullah was standing in it, praying and reciting. Then he sat down, recited the testimony of faith, praised Allah as He deserves, with the best praise a man can offer, and sent blessings upon His Prophet ﷺ. Then he earnestly supplicated, while the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr ؓ said: \"Who is this, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"This is 'Abdullah, the son of Umm 'Abd. Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm 'Abd recited.\" Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ hastened to him, and Abu Bakr ؓ beat him. 'Umar mentioned that Abu Bakr beat him. 'Umar said: \"He was always first in good deeds.\""],[8378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited Abu Bakr and 'Umar, and they had supper with him. When they finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out between Abu Bakr and 'Umar and came upon Ibn Mas'ud while he was standing praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\""],[8379,"'Abdullah was asked: \"What was it you supplicated for on the night when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to you: 'Ask, and you will be given'?\" He said: \"O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that never ends, and the companionship of Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest degree of eternity.\""],[8380,"The Prophet ﷺ came to him between Abu Bakr and 'Umar while 'Abdullah was praying. He began reciting Surat al-Nisa', and he recited it in full. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.\" Then he sat down and supplicated, and the Prophet ﷺ kept saying: \"Ask, and you will be given. Ask, and you will be given.\" Among what he asked was: \"O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that never ends, and the companionship of Your Prophet ﷺ in the garden of eternity.\" 'Umar went to 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud to give him the good news and found Abu Bakr ؓ already leaving, having beaten him to it. He said: \"If you did, you were indeed always first in good deeds.\""],[8381,"While he was reciting in the mosque, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ passed by as he was supplicating. The Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and 'Umar ؓ had gone out. When they drew parallel to him, the Prophet ﷺ heard his supplication but did not recognize him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr ؓ went back to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \"What was the supplication you were making?\" He said: \"I praised and glorified Allah, then I said: O Allah, there is no god but You. Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, Your messengers are true, the prophets are true, and Muhammad ﷺ is true.\""],[8382,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Sharik b. 'Abdullah b. Abi Namir, from 'Awn b. 'Abdullah b. 'Utbah, from his father, who said: While Ibn Mas'ud was in the mosque supplicating, the Prophet ﷺ passed by with Abu Bakr. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew parallel to him, he heard his supplication, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recognize him. He said: \"Who is this? Ask, and you will be given.\" Abu Bakr went back to 'Abdullah and said: \"What was the supplication you were making?\" He said: \"I praised and glorified Allah, then I said: O Allah, there is no god but You. Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Your Book is true, the prophets are true, Muhammad ﷺ is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and Your messengers are true.\""],[8383,"A man came to 'Umar ؓ and said: \"I have come to you from a man who dictates the masahif from memory.\" He said: 'Umar was alarmed and said: \"Woe to you! Watch what you say,\" and he became angry. The man said: \"I have come to you only with the truth.\" 'Umar said: \"Who is he?\" He said: \"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud.\" 'Umar said: \"I know no one more entitled to that than him. I will tell you about 'Abdullah. We stayed up one night in a house with Abu Bakr ؓ for some need of the Prophet ﷺ. Then we went out, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking between me and Abu Bakr. When we reached the mosque, there was a man reciting. The Prophet ﷺ stood to listen to him. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it is late,' but he nudged me with his hand, saying: 'Be quiet.' He recited, bowed, prostrated, sat down supplicating and seeking forgiveness. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Ask, and you will be given.' Then he said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.' So my companion and I knew that it was 'Abdullah. When morning came, I went to him to give him the good news, but he said: 'Abu Bakr beat you to it.' And I never raced him to any good but that he beat me to it.\""],[8384,"ʿWhoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd.ʿ Umar bin al-Khattab narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said... a similar report, in which he said: crisp or fresh. (Using translation from Aḥmad 35)"],[8385,"O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind in Iraq a man dictating the codices from memory. ʿUmar ؓ became angry until his face reddened. ʿUmar said to him repeatedly, “Do you know what you are saying?” He said, “I only inform you of the truth.” ʿUmar ؓ said, “Who is he?” He said, “Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” He said, “He became calm until the anger left him, then he said: There is no one on the face of the earth more deserving of that than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed up one night in the house of Abu Bakr ؓ for some need until it became dark, then he returned walking between me and Abu Bakr until we reached the mosque, and there was a man from the Emigrants praying. He stood listening to his recitation. I and my companion did not know who he was. He said: When he had stood for a while, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Emigrants is praying; if you would return, for it has become dark.” He said: He poked me, and the Prophet ﷺ kept listening to his recitation. He said: He bowed and prostrated, then sat supplicating, and the Prophet ﷺ began saying, “Ask, you shall be given; ask, you shall be given.” Neither I nor my companion knew who he was until we heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite as Ibn Umm ʿAbd recites.” He said: “That is when I and my companion learned who he was.” He said: “I went early to ʿAbdullah to give him the good news, and he said: Abu Bakr has preceded you. By Allah, I never vied with Abu Bakr for any good except that he preceded me.”"],[8386,"Abu Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ gave him the good news that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Masʿud.”"],[8387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while I was with him and Abu Bakr, near Ibn Masʿud while he was reciting. He stood listening to his recitation. Then ʿAbdullah bowed and prostrated, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran as it was revealed, let him recite from Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” He said: I went early to Ibn Masʿud to give him the good news of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. When I knocked on the door, he heard my voice and said, “What brings you?” I said, “I came to give you glad tidings of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.” He said, “Abu Bakr has preceded you.” I said, “If he did, he is indeed foremost in good deeds. We never raced to any good except that Abu Bakr preceded me to it.”"],[8388,"O Commander of the Faithful, I left behind in Kufa a man dictating the codices from memory. ʿUmar became angry until his face swelled, then said, “Who is he?” He said, “ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud.” So he said, “May your father be for Allah’s sake, and who is more deserving of that than him? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever is pleased to recite the Quran fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.’”"],[8389,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, and be guided by the guidance of ʿAmmar, and hold fast to the covenant of ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud.”"],[8390,"ʿAbdullah addressed us when the codices were being torn, and the mosque was full of the people of Badr. He said, “The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ know that I am the most knowledgeable among them concerning the Book of Allah.” Shaqiq said: Then I saw that he felt ashamed of what he said, so he said, “But I am not the best of them. If I knew a man more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would go to him.” Shaqiq said: “When ʿAbdullah finished his sermon, I sat in the circles to listen to what they said, and I heard no one disapproving of that.”"],[8391,"When Uthman commanded regarding the copies of the Quran as he was commanded, Abdullah stood up and praised Allah. Then he said, \"O people, surely Allah says, 'And whoever commits a sin only earns it against himself. And Allah is ever Knowing and Wise.' So commit transgression with the copies of the Quran upon the recitation of the one whom I command to recite it upon the recitation of Zaid bin Thabit. By He in whose hands is my soul, I have taken from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs. And Zaid bin Thabit has two things, he plays with the boys, and by He in whose hands is my soul, if I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, I would come to him.\""],[8392,"“By Allah, no surah of the Quran was revealed except that I know where it was revealed, and no verse of it was revealed except that I know concerning what it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would go to him.”"],[8393,"“By the One besides whom there is no god, no surah of the Quran was revealed except that I know where it was revealed, and no verse, and I know concerning whom it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would ride to him.”"],[8394,"“There is no verse in the Book of Allah except that I know where it was revealed and concerning whom it was revealed. If I knew anyone more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than me, whom camels could reach, I would journey to him.”"],[8395,"\"And there is none worthy of worship except Him. There is no surah (chapter) in the Book of Allah except that I know where it was revealed and there is no verse except that I know what it was revealed about.\""],[8396,"It was asked of Abdullah, \"Read according to the recitation of Zaid.\" He said, \"Should I abandon my recitation for the recitation of Zaid? I have read seventy Surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was a young boy and he had two twisted hairs.\""],[8397,"“...that he should embezzle a codex, let him do so, for whoever embezzles something will come with what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8398,"\"I have read seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and Zaid ibn Thabit has two scrolls in the Book.\""],[8399,"Abdullah said, \"I have read from the Prophet ﷺ seventy surahs,\" and Zaid bin Thabit, with a small bird, plays with the children."],[8400,"On whose reading am I ordered to read? \"I have read seventy surahs to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" And indeed, Zaid bin Thabit is a companion of the wolves who plays with the boys."],[8401,"“Do I not see you praying when the Book of Allah has been ordered and then torn apart? So I prayed hastily, and I was not detained. I entered the house and was not detained. I climbed up and was not detained. Then I found al-Ashʿari, Hudhayfah, and Ibn Masʿud disputing, with Hudhayfah saying to Ibn Masʿud, ‘Hand over this codex to them.’ He said, ‘No, by Allah, I will not hand it over to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it more than seventy times, and then I should hand it over to them? By Allah, I will not hand it over to them.’”"],[8402,"He heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ood say, \"I have received from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy Surahs.\" I memorized them before Zaid ibn Thabit, who had a stutter, had mastered them and was playing with the boys."],[8403,"\"Wondrous it is for people to abandon my recitation and prefer the recitation of Zaid ibn Thabit, even though I have received seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Zaid ibn Thabit is a young man with a lisp.\""],[8404,"\"Abdullah ibn Mas'ood said, 'I have read seventy-two surahs from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ .' And indeed, Zaid ibn Thabit had two notebooks.\""],[8405,"I have taken seventy chapters from the Prophet ﷺ in which no one disputes with me."],[8406,"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs."],[8407,"\"I have read seventy-two surahs during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. And Zaid ibn Thabit had two helpers who used to play with the children.\""],[8408,"\"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy surahs. And indeed, Zaid bin Thabit is a disbeliever in Allah as he did not believe in it.\""],[8409,"I have read seventy surahs from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I completed the recitation of the Quran with the best of people, Ali ibn Abi Talib."],[8410,"He said to him: O my brother, we have a gathering, so come to us. I went to him in his gathering and learned from him seventy surahs. ʿAbd Allah said to me, “I took them from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Jibril ﷺ brought them down from the Lord of the worlds, Exalted is He.”"],[8411,"I have read from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seventy Surahs."],[8412,"That the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “Your permission with me is that you may raise the veil and hear my secret conversation until I forbid you.” Al-Hasan said: al-siwad means secret talk."],[8413,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your permission with me is that you may uncover the curtain.”"],[8414,"“ʿAbd Allah ؓ was the keeper of the cushion, the siwak, and the sandals.”"],[8415,"I used to pick a siwak for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the arak tree. The wind would bend him over, and there was thinness in his legs, so the people laughed. The Prophet ﷺ said, “What are you laughing at from the thinness of his legs? By the One in whose hand is my soul, they are heavier in the Balance than Uhud.”"],[8416,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, the legs of Ibn Masʿud on the Day of Resurrection will be stronger and greater than Uhud.”"],[8417,"While he was walking behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his companions or some of them nudged him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, ʿAbd Allah in the Scales on the Day of Resurrection is heavier than Uhud,” as if they were amazed at his lightness."],[8418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr ؓ came to me after he had fled from the polytheists, while I was tending sheep belonging to Ibn Abi Muʿayt at Jiyad. He said, “O boy, do you have any milk to give us?” I said, “I am entrusted and I am not going to give you milk.” He said, “Do you have a young she-goat that no male has mounted?” I said, “Yes.” I brought it to him, and he wiped the udder, and the udder filled with milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought him a hollowed rock, and he milked and drank and gave drink, and he gave Abu Bakr ؓ to drink and gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink,” and it shrank."],[8419,"I was among the sheep of ʿUqbah b. Abi Muʿayt when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said, “O boy, do you have any milk?” I said, “Yes, but I am entrusted.” He said, “Then bring me a ewe that no male has mounted.” I brought him a young she-goat or a yearling, and he began wiping the udder and supplicating until it let down milk. Abu Bakr ؓ brought a rock, and he milked into it, then he handed it to Abu Bakr and he drank, then the Prophet ﷺ drank after him. Then he said to the udder, “Shrink by Allah's permission,” and it shrank and returned to what it had been."],[8420,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was herding sheep for Uqbah. He wiped my head and said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, for you are a diligent teacher.\""],[8421,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I am pleased for my community with what Ibn Umm ʿAbd was pleased with for it.”"],[8422,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Recite.” So he began Surat al-Nisaʾ until when he reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” (Q 4:41)—the verse—his eyes shed tears, and he said, “It is enough for us.”"],[8423,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Recite.” He said: I said, “O Messenger of God, should I recite to you when it was revealed to you?” He said, “Yes.” So I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ until I reached this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” He said, “Enough for you now.” I turned to him and his eyes were flowing with tears."],[8425,"He recited to the Prophet ﷺ until he came to this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ wept, and he said in the hadith, “Whoever would like to recite the Qurʾan as fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.”"],[8426,"The Prophet ﷺ asked me to recite Surat al-Nisaʾ while he was on the pulpit, so I recited it until when I reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” the eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ filled with tears, and he said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Qurʾan as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.”"],[8427,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Recite the Qurʾan to me.” Ibn Masʿud said, “O Messenger of God, should I recite the Qurʾan to you when it was revealed to you?” He said, “I would love to hear it from someone other than myself.” So he recited to him until he reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” and the eyes of the Messenger of God ﷺ filled with tears, and he said, “Whoever is pleased to recite the Qurʾan as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm ʿAbd.” This is how it was narrated by ʿAmr b. Marzuq and the companions of Shuʿbah, and Sulayman b. Harb connected it."],[8429,"Ibn Masʿud said: I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when I came to this verse, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” his eyes overflowed."],[8430,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered me to recite to him while he was on the pulpit. I recited Surat al-Nisaʾ to him until when I reached, “So how will it be when We bring from every community a witness and bring you as a witness against these?” the Messenger of God ﷺ pressed me, so I looked at him and his eyes were shedding tears, shedding tears."],[8431,"ʿAbd Allah struck Abu Jahl but did nothing. He said, “A little shepherd boy of yesterday?” He said, “That is him.” So he took his sword and struck him until he killed him."],[8432,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr and said, “I have killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, did you kill him?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” Joy overwhelmed him, and he said, “Show me him.” So I went with him until I stood with him at his head, and he said, “Praise be to God who has disgraced you. This is the Pharaoh of this community. Drag him to the well.” He said: I had struck him with my sword but it did not cut him, so I took his sword and struck him with it until I killed him. The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me his sword as booty."],[8433,"I reached Abu Jahl while he was thrown down, wearing his helmet, with a good sword, and with me a bad sword. I began to poke his head with my sword, remembering how he used to poke my head in Makkah, until his hand weakened. I took his sword, and he raised his head and said, “On whose side was the defeat—for us or against us? Are you not our little shepherd boy in Makkah?” I killed him. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” He made me swear three times, then he stood and went with me to them and supplicated against them."],[8434,"When God defeated the polytheists on the day of Badr, I passed by and saw Abu Jahl thrown down with his leg struck. I said, “O enemy of God, O Abu Jahl, God has disgraced the other.” He said, and I did not fear him at that time, “Get away from a man whom his own people have killed.” So I struck him with a useless sword of mine, but it availed me nothing until his sword fell from his hand. I took it and struck him until he became cold. Then I came running to the Messenger of God ﷺ, hurrying faster than any creature of God, until I reached him and said, “O Messenger of God, God has killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” He said, “How?” So I told him how the story went and how I found him. He said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity?” I said, “By the God besides whom there is no deity, I killed him.” He said “Allahu Akbar,” then said, “Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise and aided His servant.” Then he set out until he came to him and said, “This is the Pharaoh of this community.”"],[8435,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, God Almighty has killed Abu Jahl.” He said, “Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and exalted His religion.”"],[8436,"I brought the head of Abu Jahl to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “This is the head of Abu Jahl.” He said, “By God, besides whom there is no god?”—and this was how he used to swear—so I said, “By God, besides whom there is no god, this is indeed the head of Abu Jahl.” He then said, “This is the Pharaoh of this nation.”"],[8437,"I came upon Abu Jahl at the Battle of Badr lying slain, and I said, “O enemy of God, God has disgraced you.” He said, “And how has God disgraced me by a man whom you killed while I had my sword with me?” I began striking him with my sword but it would not cut him, while he had a good sword of his own. Then I struck his hand, and the sword fell from his grip, so I took it. Then I uncovered the helmet from his head and struck his neck. After that I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him, and he said, “By God, besides whom there is no god?” I said, “By God, besides whom there is no god.” He said, “Go and verify.” So I went, hastening like a bird, then returned, hastening like a bird, laughing, and told him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Then go and show me.” So I went with him and showed him. When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood over him, he said, “This is the Pharaoh of this nation.” Thus it was narrated by Zayd b. Abi Unaysa from Abu Ishaq from ʿAmr b. Maymun, and Abu Wakiʿ concurred with him."],[8438,"I arrived at Abu Jahl on the day of Badr while he was dying, so I struck him with a sword that I had with me. His sword then slipped from his hand, so I took it and killed him. Then I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a hot day, as if I were carrying the Earth, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see that Allah killed Abu Jahl?\" He said, \"Allah?\" I said, \"Yes, Allah, until he swore to me three times.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Go and show me.\" So I went to him, and when he looked at him, he said, \"This man was the Pharaoh of this nation.\""],[8439,"At the Battle of Badr I was pushed toward Abu Jahl, and I had been seated. I took his sword and struck his head with it. He said, “Our little shepherd in Makkah.” I struck him with his sword until he became cold. Then I came to the Prophet and said, “O Messenger of God, I have killed Abu Jahl.” ʿAqil, who was a captive with the Prophet ﷺ, said, “You lie; you did not kill him.” I said, “Rather you are the liar and the sinner, O enemy of God. By God, I have killed him.” He said, “What is his distinguishing mark?” I said, “On his thigh there is a ring like the ring of a hobbled camel.” He said, “You have spoken the truth.”"],[8440,"We were sitting with ʿUmar when ʿAbdullah came, and those seated nearly equaled him in height because of his shortness. ʿUmar laughed when he saw him. He began speaking with ʿUmar and joking with him while standing before him, then he turned away. ʿUmar followed him with his gaze until he disappeared, then said, “A little vessel filled with understanding.”"],[8441,"ʿUmar wrote to the people of Kufa: “I have sent ʿAmmar as commander and ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud as teacher and minister. They are among the noble ones of the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, from the people of Badr and Uhud. Follow them and listen to their words. I have preferred you over myself by sending ʿAbdullah to you.”"],[8442,"“May God have mercy on Ibn Masʿud. He was indeed a jurist, but I will give him the share of a maternal brother on account of his mother, then divide the property between them.”"],[8443,"Hudhayfa said: “The person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ in manner, bearing, moderation, and address from the time he leaves his house until he returns—though I do not know what he does with his family—is ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud. By God, the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad know that ʿAbdullah is among the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8444,"“The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Umm ʿAbd is the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8445,"“The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that Ibn Masʿud is among the closest of them to God in nearness on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8447,"“I have not seen a man more resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ in bearing, manner, and conduct from the time he leaves his house until he returns to it than this one”—meaning ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud. “And the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ know that he is among the closest of them in nearness to God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8448,"I was sitting with Hudhayfah when Ibn Mas'ud and Abu Musa passed by. Hudhayfah did not want to ignore them, so he said, \"The person who most resembles the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he leaves his house until he returns to his family is Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and Allah knows best what he does.\""],[8449,"Hudhayfah said: \"Indeed, the closest of people in guidance, manner, judgment, and preaching to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the time he leaves his house until he returns – and I do not know what he does with his family – is ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud. By Allah, the fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ surely know that Ibn Masʿud is among the closest of them in means (wasilah).\""],[8450,"\"Tell us of a man close in conduct, guidance, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"I do not know of anyone closer in guidance, conduct, and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the wall of his house conceals him than Ibn Umm ʿAbd.\""],[8451,"We were with Hudhayfah opposite the house of ʿAbd Allah, and he said: \"I do not know of anyone more similar in manner and conduct to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the occupant of this house, from the time he leaves until he enters his home. When he is concealed, then Allah knows best. The fortunate ones among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ certainly knew that he is among the closest of them in means (wasilah) to Allah on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8452,"\"Shall I not tell you of the closest of people in resemblance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in guidance, manner, and conduct?\" We said: \"Yes, indeed.\" He said: \"ʿAbd Allah.\""],[8453,"\"Whoever wishes to look at the most similar of people in guidance, conduct, and bearing to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he leaves his home until he returns, let him look at ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8454,"\"And indeed, the one of you two most similar in guidance and manner to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8455,"I was sitting with Hudhayfah and Abu Musa al-Ashʿari, and one of them said to his companion: \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say such-and-such a hadith?\" He said: \"No.\" The other said to him: \"Then did you hear it?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then the occupant of this house claims that he heard it.\" Abu Musa said: \"If he did, he used to enter when we were screened, and witness when we were absent.\" Sulayman al-Aʿmash said: \"He means ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud.\""],[8456,"Ibrahim said: ʿAbd Allah came to Abu Musa and conversed with him. When the prayer became due and the iqamah was called, Abu Musa stepped back. ʿAbd Allah said to him: \"You indeed know that it is part of the Sunnah for the owner of the house to lead.\" Abu Musa refused until a freedman of one of them went forward."],[8457,"We were in the house of Abu Musa with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they were looking into a mushaf. ʿAbd Allah stood up, and Abu Masʿud said: \"I do not know of anyone left after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more knowledgeable of what Allah, Exalted is He, revealed than this standing one.\" Abu Musa said: \"Since you have said that, he used to witness when we were absent and be granted permission when we were screened.\""],[8458,"\"I do not see any man more knowledgeable of what was revealed upon Muhammad ﷺ than ʿAbd Allah.\" Abu Musa said: \"If that is said, then indeed he used to hear when no one was heard, and enter when no one was allowed to enter.\""],[8459,"Abu Masʿud said: \"No, by Allah, I do not know of anyone left by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah than this standing one.\""],[8460,"That he heard Abu Musa say: \"My brother and I arrived from Yemen, and we stayed for some time, thinking that ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud was from the household of the Prophet ﷺ, because of his frequent entering upon the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[8461,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and I considered Ibn Masʿud to be from the household.\""],[8462,"\"My wife's milk was retained in her breast, so I began to suck it and then spit it out. Some of it then entered my stomach.\" He said: \"She has become forbidden to you.\" So he went to ʿAbdullah. Abu ʿAtiyyah said: So he stood, and we stood with him. He said: \"Suckle from the breast of this one, for suckling is only what grows the flesh and the blood.\" Then Abu Musa said: \"Do not ask me about anything as long as this learned man is among you.\""],[8463,"That his wife's breast became swollen, so he began to suck it and spit it out, and some of it entered his stomach. He said: \"I do not think she is suitable for him.\" So he went to Ibn Masʿud and asked him about that. He said: \"She has not become forbidden to you. Only that suckling which grows the flesh and strengthens the bone becomes prohibited, and there is no suckling after weaning.\" So it was said to Abu Musa, and he said: \"Do not ask us about anything as long as this learned man remains among us, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[8464,"From ʿAbdullah, regarding {Fear Allah as He should be feared}: He said: \"That He is obeyed and not disobeyed, remembered and not forgotten, thanked and not denied.\""],[8465,"In his saying \"Fear Allah as He should be feared,\" he said, \"That He is obeyed and not disobeyed, and that He is thanked and not ungrateful, and that He is remembered and not forgotten.\""],[8466,"From Murrah, regarding His saying {and gave wealth despite love for it}: He said: Ibn Masʿud said: \"That you give it while you are healthy and miserly, hopeful of life and fearful of poverty.\""],[8467,"From ʿAbdullah: \"The major sins are those between the beginning of Surat al-Nisaʾ and the beginning of its thirtieth verse.\""],[8468,"ʿAbdullah said: \"How excellent are the two detested things: death and poverty. By Allah, indeed wealth and poverty—I do not care with which of them I am tested. If it is wealth, indeed in it there is compassion; and if it is poverty, indeed in it there is patience.\""],[8469,"ʿAbdullah told us one day: \"Indeed, sickness does not have any reward written for the one who suffers it.\" That grieved us and weighed heavily upon us. Then he said: \"But Allah ﷻ expiates sins through it.\""],[8470,"ʿAbdullah said: \"Shall I warn you against excess in speech? It is enough for one of you to say only what achieves his need.\""],[8471,"\"That I remember Allah from morning until evening is more beloved to me than that I raid upon thoroughbred horses from morning until evening.\""],[8472,"ʿAbdullah said: \"Indeed I know households that the Dajjal will frighten.\" They said: \"Who, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman?\" He said: \"The houses of the people of Kufah.\""],[8473,"“Do not mention him excessively, for when the matter is decreed in heaven, it is quicker to descend to the earth that it appear on people's tongues.” He said: “Indeed, how will you be when the people are secure and you are fearful? And how will you be when the people are in shade and you are in the sun?”"],[8474,"ʿAbdullāh said: “If he were to wake up in Bābil, some of them would wake up complaining to him of sore feet from the speed.”"],[8475,"“Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him; whoever seeks to be heard of, Allah will make him heard of; whoever acts arrogantly out of pride, Allah will abase him; and whoever humbles himself out of humility, Allah will raise him. People are either given ample provision in this world but constrained in the Hereafter, constrained in this world but given ample provision in the Hereafter, constrained in both this world and the Hereafter, or given ample provision in both this world and the Hereafter. And there is one who finds rest and one from whom rest is found.” We said: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what is the one who finds rest and the one from whom rest is found?” He said: “As for the one who finds rest, he is the believer; when he dies, he finds rest. As for the one from whom rest is found, he is the one who wrongs people and backbites them.”"],[8476,"I examined the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ and found that their knowledge ended with six: ʿUmar, ʿAlī, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, Abū al-Dardāʾ, and Zayd b. Thābit. Then I examined the six and found that their knowledge ended with ʿAlī and ʿAbdullāh."],[8477,"Indeed, knowledge and faith are in their place; whoever seeks them will find them. He said that three times. And seek knowledge from four: ʿUwaymir Abū al-Dardāʾ, Salmān al-Fārisī, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, and ʿAbdullāh b. Salām."],[8478,"“None remained with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uḥud except four, one of them being ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd.”"],[8479,"I heard ʿAlī say: The Prophet ﷺ ordered Ibn Masʿūd to climb a tree and bring him something from it. His Companions looked at the thinness of his legs and laughed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What makes you laugh? The leg of ʿAbdullāh in the Scale is heavier than Uḥud.”"],[8480,"I climbed a small arāk tree to pick some of its fruit, and my companions began to marvel at my lightness. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What do you marvel at? By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is heavier in the Scale on the Day of Resurrection than Uḥud.”"],[8481,"It is only two things: guidance and speech. The best speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad ﷺ. Beware of newly invented matters and innovations, for the worst of affairs are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is misguidance. Do not let the time span grow long for you, lest your hearts harden. Hope: what is coming is near. Indeed, what is far is what is not coming. Indeed, the wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who is admonished by others. The worst of mounts are the mounts of falsehood. Indeed, lying is not proper in seriousness or jest. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. It will be said of the truthful one: he spoke truth and was righteous; and it will be said of the liar: he lied and acted wickedly."],[8484,"It is only two things: guidance and speech. The most truthful speech is the speech of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad ﷺ. The worst of affairs are their newly invented ones, and every newly invented matter is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance, and every misguidance is in the Fire."],[8485,"He used to come every Thursday and stand, not sitting, and say: Do not put the people to trial, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need. He would say: They are two: the best guidance is the guidance of Muḥammad, the most truthful speech is the Book of Allah, and the worst of affairs are their newly invented ones. Every newly invented matter is misguidance. The wretched is the one who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is the one who is admonished by others. Indeed, let not the time span grow long for you, nor let hope divert you, for all that is coming is near, and only what is not coming is far. Among the worst of people is the one who prolongs the day out of fear of the night. Killing a believer is disbelief and insulting him is wickedness. It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. Indeed, the worst of mounts is falsehood. Lying is not proper in seriousness or jest, nor for a man to promise his child something and not fulfill it. Indeed, lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire; and truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. It will be said of the truthful one: he spoke truth and was righteous; and it will be said of the liar: he lied and acted wickedly."],[8487,"'Indeed, the truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and the worst of matters are their innovations. Indeed, what you are promised is surely coming, and you are not able to escape. Indeed far is only what is not coming. Beware, hold fast to truthfulness, for it leads to Paradise. A man keeps being truthful until he is recorded with God as a true friend, and righteousness becomes firm in his heart, and wickedness does not have in his heart even the space of a needle to settle therein. Beware, and beware of lying, for it leads to the Fire. A man keeps lying until he is recorded with God as a liar, and wickedness settles in his heart until there is not in his heart the space of a needle for it to settle therein.'"],[8488,"'Lying is not appropriate in jest or seriousness, nor may one of you promise his child something and then not fulfill it for him.'"],[8489,"Abd Allah said: 'Lying is not appropriate in seriousness or jest.'"],[8490,"She was called Buraydah. We said: 'O Buraydah, tell Abu Wa'il to narrate to us.' She said: 'O Abu Wa'il, narrate to the people what you heard from Abd Allah.' He said: 'I heard Abd Allah say: O people, you will be gathered on a single plain where the caller will make you hear and your sight will penetrate you. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb' — he said, and I think he added — 'and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8491,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8492,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8493,"'The wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who was fortunate in his mother's womb.'"],[8494,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud used to address us every Thursday, saying: 'Indeed, the truest speech is the Book of God, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and every innovation is a heresy, and every heresy is misguidance, and the worst of matters are their innovations. Indeed, you will be gathered on a single plain where your sight will penetrate you and the caller will make you hear. Indeed, the wretched is he who was wretched in his mother's womb, and the fortunate is he who is admonished by others.'"],[8495,"'O people, hold fast to truthfulness, for it brings near to righteousness, and righteousness brings near to Paradise. Beware of lying, for it brings near to wickedness, and wickedness brings near to the Fire. It is said of the truthful one: He was truthful and righteous, and of the liar: He lied and was wicked. Indeed, the angel has an inclination and the devil has an inclination. The angel's inclination is an admonition to good, and the devil's inclination is an admonition to evil. Whoever finds the angel's inclination, let him praise God, and whoever finds the devil's inclination, let him seek refuge from that, for God (may He be exalted) says: {Satan promises you poverty and commands you} until the end of the verse. He said: Indeed, God (may He be exalted) laughs at two men: a man who rises from his bed, his blanket, and his cover in a cold night, performs ablution, then stands for prayer. God says to His angels: What made My servant do what he did? They say: Our Lord, hope for what is with You and fear of what is with You. He says: I have given him what he hoped for and secured him from what he feared. And a man who was in a group, knew what he would gain from fleeing and knew what he would have with God, so he fought until he was killed. He says to the angels: What made My servant do what he did? They say: Our Lord, hope for what is with You and fear of what is with You. He says: I call you to witness that I have given him what he hoped for and secured him from what he feared — or a similar phrase.'"],[8496,"Abd Allah b. Masʿud said: “None of you is but a guest and a loaned item. The guest is departing, and the loan is to be returned to its owner.”"],[8497,"Abd Allah said: “Knowledge is not from abundant hadith; rather, knowledge is from fear (of Allah).”"],[8498,"That I be ashes."],[8499,"Ibn Masʿud instructed his son Abu ʿUbaydah with three statements: “O my son, I instruct you to fear Allah, let your house suffice you, weep over your sin, and hold back your tongue.”"],[8500,"A man said to Abd Allah: “Instruct me with comprehensive, beneficial words.” Abd Allah said to him: “Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him. Remain with the Quran wherever it goes. Whoever brings you truth, accept it from him even if he is far away, and whoever brings you falsehood, reject it even if he is a beloved close one.”"],[8501,"That I see a man idle, neither engaged in work for this world nor the Hereafter.”"],[8502,"That I see a man idle, neither engaged in work for this world nor the Hereafter.”"],[8503,"“Whoever emigrates seeking something shall have what he sought.” He said, “A man emigrated to marry a woman called Umm Qays, and he was known as the emigrant of Umm Qays.”"],[8504,"\"A man should not say, 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence, and I repent to Him three times, except that his sins will be forgiven, even if he flees from crawling.'\""],[8505,"Indeed, the mountain calls out to the mountain by its name: “O so-and-so, did anyone pass by you today who remembered Allah?” When it says yes, it rejoices. ʿAwn said: “They listen to evil and do not listen to good, yet they are better at hearing good.” And he recited: {And they say, “The Most Merciful has taken a son.” You have done an atrocious thing. The heavens almost rupture therefrom, and the earth splits open, and the mountains collapse in devastation that they ascribe to the Most Merciful a son. And it is not appropriate for the Most Merciful that He should take a son.}"],[8506,"Abd Allah said: “Whoever his prayer does not enjoin him to what is right and forbid him from what is wrong, he only increases in distance from Allah.”"],[8507,"Abd Allah said: “Patience is half of faith, and certainty is faith.”"],[8508,"While I was with Abd Allah, I saw a crowd; it stirred and then settled. He said: “Beware of the clamor of the market, for it is the clamor of Satan.”"],[8509,"Abd Allah said: “Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires. Whoever peers through the veil will fall upon what lies behind it.”"],[8510,"ʿAbd Allah (said): “The people with the most sins on the Day of Resurrection will be those who most indulge in falsehood.”"],[8511,"“Yaʿqub delayed his sons until the pre-dawn time.”"],[8512,"And knowledge."],[8513,"Ibn Masʿud (said): “Beware of ‘Do you think?’ and ‘Do you think?’, for those before you were destroyed only by ‘Do you think?’ and ‘Do you think?’. Do not compare anything with anything, lest a foot slip after it was firm. When one of you is asked about what he does not know, let him say, ‘I do not know,’ for that is a third of knowledge.”"],[8514,"ʿAbd Allah (said): “There is no year but that the one after it is worse than it, and no year is better than another year, and no community is better than another community. Rather, it is the passing away of your best ones and your scholars, and people will come who judge matters by their own opinions, and Islam will be demolished and broken.”"],[8515,"“The righteous depart one after another, and there remain people of doubt who do not recognize good and do not reject evil.”"],[8516,"When he sat down, he used to say: “You are in the passage of the night, with diminished lifespans and recorded deeds. Death comes suddenly. Whoever sows good is likely to reap desire, and whoever sows evil is likely to reap regret. Every sower is such that a slow one does not miss his share, and a greedy one does not attain what was not decreed for him. Whoever is given good, it is Allah who gave it; whoever is protected from evil, it is Allah who protected him. The God-fearing are masters, the jurists are leaders, and their company is an increase.”"],[8517,"\"Do not fight against this night, for you will not be able to endure it. And if one of you becomes sleepy, let him go to his bed, for it is surrendered to him.\""],[8518,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty.”"],[8519,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty.”"],[8520,"“Yusuf and his mother were given two-thirds of all beauty—the beauty of people in the face, whiteness, and other than that. When a woman came to him, he would cover his face for fear that she would be tempted.”"],[8521,"That he should report everything he hears.”"],[8522,"“When you invite a man, then you have given him permission.”"],[8523,"The most painful thing in a believer is obscenity."],[8524,"The most base of a believer's character traits is obscenity."],[8525,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"A man may go out with his religion and return with nothing of it. He comes to a man who possesses no benefit or harm for him or for himself, and swears to him by Allah, 'You have lied and committed sin,' and then he returns without having obtained anything of his need, and he has made Allah angry with him.\""],[8527,"He said: \"He is ruined who does not enjoin good and forbid evil.\" He said: \"Rather, he is ruined whose heart does not know the good and whose heart does not reject the evil.\""],[8529,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"Whoever desires the Hereafter harms his worldly life, and whoever desires the worldly life harms his Hereafter.\" And he commanded them to harm the perishable for the sake of the enduring. And he said: \"You are in a time in which its scholars are many and its orators are few, and its givers are many and its beggars are few. So lengthen the prayer and shorten the sermon. And indeed some eloquence is magic. And after you will come a time in which its orators are many, its scholars are few, its beggars are many, and its givers are few.\""],[8530,"\"You are in a time in which the prayer is long and the sermon is short, and its scholars are many and its orators are few. And a time will come upon you in which the prayer is short and the sermon is long, its orators are many and its scholars are few. They will delay the ʿIsha prayer until the rising of the dead (i.e., very late). Whoever of you reaches that should pray the prayer at its proper time and make it with them as a supererogatory prayer. You are in a time in which a man is envied for the abundance of his wealth and the abundance of his dependents. And a time will come upon you in which a man is envied for the fewness of his dependents and the lightness of his burden. I do not leave behind in my family anyone dearer to me than their death, nor any household among the beetles. And indeed I love them as they love your families.\""],[8531,"ʿAbd Allah saw some children of his offspring playing in front of him, and he said: \"These are less important to me than their number of beetles.\""],[8532,"\"False testimony is equal to associating partners with Allah.\" And he recited: {And avoid false speech}."],[8533,"that He finds him with his face in the dust."],[8534,"\"Indeed charity falls into the hand of Allah before it falls into the hand of the beggar.\" Then ʿAbd Allah recited: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants} until the end of the verse."],[8535,"A man brought his nephew to ʿAbd Allah while he was drunk, and said: \"I found this one drunk.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Shake him, rinse his mouth, and smell his breath.\" He said: So he was shaken, his mouth was rinsed, and his breath was smelled, and the smell of wine was found on him. So ʿAbd Allah ordered him to prison, then released him the next day. Then he ordered a whip whose end was beaten until it became a light switch. Then he said to the flogger: \"Flog and draw back your hand, and give every limb its due.\" So he flogged him with a flogging that was not severe, and he was in a cloak and trousers, or a shirt and trousers. Then he said: \"By Allah, how bad is the guardian of the tribe! I did not discipline and improve the discipline, nor did I cover the disgrace.\" He said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, he is my nephew; I feel for him the same anguish I feel for my own son.\" ʿAbd Allah said: \"Indeed Allah Almighty loves pardon, but it is not appropriate for a guardian to be brought a prescribed punishment and not carry it out.\""],[8536,"Abdullah said, \"If any of you is afflicted with a punishment, do not curse him, rather ask Allah to forgive him and have mercy on him.\""],[8537,"When you see your brother commit a sin, do not be helpers of Satan against him by saying, 'O Allah, disgrace him! O Allah, curse him!' Rather, ask Allah for pardon. For we, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, would not say anything about anyone until we knew upon what he would die. If he was sealed with good, we knew that he had attained good; and if he was sealed with evil, we feared for him because of his deeds."],[8538,"That I be provided with a whip in the path of Allah is dearer to me than that I perform Hajj after Hajj."],[8539,"Abdullah had permitted exchange (al-sarf) and permitted a man to marry a woman, then she died before he consummated the marriage, and to marry her mother. Then he came to Madinah and it was as if he met Umar, so he retracted. He then went to the money-changers and forbade them from that."],[8540,"Abdullah used to permit a dirham for two dirhams and a dinar for two dinars. Then he returned to Madinah and went to Umar, Ali, and the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and they forbade him from that. When he returned, I saw him going around among the money-changers saying, 'Woe to you, O people! Do not consume usury, and do not buy a dirham for two dirhams, nor a dinar for two dinars.'"],[8541,"About his saying."],[8542,"He informed him that she is not lawful for him. When he returned to Kufa, he said to the man, 'She is forbidden to you,' so he separated from her."],[8543,"Abdullah said, 'When you meet the wicked man, meet him with a frowning face.'"],[8544,"That you should change it, so frown in his face."],[8545,"Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, looked into the hearts of His servants and found the heart of Muhammad ﷺ to be the best of the hearts of His servants, so He chose him for Himself and singled him out—or he said: He sent him with His message. Then He looked into the hearts of His servants after his heart and found the hearts of his companions to be the best of the hearts of His servants, so He made them the ministers of His Prophet ﷺ, fighting for His religion."],[8546,"Allah, may He be exalted, looked into the hearts of His servants and chose Muhammad ﷺ, so He sent him with His message and selected him with His knowledge. Then He looked into the hearts of the people and chose his companions, so He made them the ministers of His Prophet ﷺ and the supporters of His religion. Whatever the believers deem good is good in the sight of Allah, and whatever the believers deem ugly is ugly in the sight of Allah."],[8547,"Abdullah heard a man say, 'Where are those who abstain from this world and desire the Hereafter?' Abdullah said, 'Those are the people of al-Jabiyah. Five hundred Muslims stipulated that they would not return until they were killed.' So they shaved their heads, met the enemy, and were killed, except one who informed about them."],[8548,"The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people: those who do not recognize good and do not reject evil. They will copulate like beasts in the road. A woman will pass by a man in the road, and he will approach her and satisfy his need with her, then return to his companions and laugh to them and they laugh to him, like the foul, wormy dates that are not good to eat."],[8549,"The Hour will not be established except upon the worst of people, upon a people who do not enjoin good and do not forbid evil; they will copulate like donkeys copulate. A man will take a woman by the hand, be alone with her, and fulfill his need from her; then he will return laughing to them and they will laugh to him, like the putrid discarded dates that are not eaten."],[8550,"That a man says to his brother, 'Fear Allah,' and he replies, 'Mind yourself; you are commanding me?'"],[8551,"It is enough of a sin for a man that when it is said to him, 'Fear Allah,' he becomes angry."],[8552,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and from their elders. When knowledge comes from their young ones, that is when they perish."],[8553,"I heard Ibn Mas'ud say: People will remain righteous and cohesive as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and from their elders. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish."],[8554,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from their elders and those of their predecessors. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish. This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd b. Wahb, and Zayd b. Hibban concurred with him."],[8555,"People will remain in good as long as knowledge comes to them from the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ and their elders. When it comes to them from their young ones, they perish."],[8556,"Indeed Allah ﷻ looked into the hearts of the servants and found the heart of Muhammad ﷺ to be the best of hearts of the servants.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of 'Asim."],[8557,"“When you send peace and blessings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then do it well, for you do not know, that may be shown to him.” They said to him: “Teach us.” He said: “Say: ‘Allahumma aj’al salataka wa rahmataka wa barakatika ‘ala sayyidil-mursalin wa imamil-muttaqin wa khatamin- nabiyyin, Muhammad ‘abdika wa Rasulika imamil-khayri (wa qa’idil- khair), wa Rasulir-Rahmah. Allahummab’athhu maqaman mahmudan yaghbituhu bihil-awwaluna wal-akhirun. Allahumma salli ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama sallayta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim; Allahumma barik ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim, innaka Hamidum Majid (O Allah, send Your grace, honour, mercy and blessings upon the leader of the Messengers, the imam of the pious and the seal of the Prophets, Muhammad, Your slave and Messenger, the Imam of the good (and the leader) of the good, and the Messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a station of praise and glory that will be the envy of the first and the last. O Allah, send Your grace, honour and mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your grace, honour and mercy upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 906)"],[8558,"“When you send peace and blessings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then do it well, for you do not know, that may be shown to him.” They said to him: “Teach us.” He said: “Say: ‘Allahumma aj’al salataka wa rahmataka wa barakatika ‘ala sayyidil-mursalin wa imamil-muttaqin wa khatamin- nabiyyin, Muhammad ‘abdika wa Rasulika imamil-khayri (wa qa’idil- khair), wa Rasulir-Rahmah. Allahummab’athhu maqaman mahmudan yaghbituhu bihil-awwaluna wal-akhirun. Allahumma salli ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama sallayta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim; Allahumma barik ‘ala Muhammadin wa ‘ala ali Muhammadin kama barakta ‘ala Ibrahim wa ‘ala ali Ibrahim, innaka Hamidum Majid (O Allah, send Your grace, honour, mercy and blessings upon the leader of the Messengers, the imam of the pious and the seal of the Prophets, Muhammad, Your slave and Messenger, the Imam of the good (and the leader) of the good, and the Messenger of mercy. O Allah, raise him to a station of praise and glory that will be the envy of the first and the last. O Allah, send Your grace, honour and mercy upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent Your grace, honour and mercy upon Ibrahim, You are indeed Praiseworthy, Most Glorious. O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Most Glorious).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 906)"],[8559,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. By my life, I do not think any of you has not taken a mosque in his house. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen us, and none would stay behind from them except a known hypocrite or one whose hypocrisy was recognized. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he is stood in the row. No man purifies himself and does it well, then takes a step intending to go to a mosque from the mosques, except Allah writes for him a good deed because of it, raises him a degree because of it, and removes from him a sin because of it—so much so that we used to take short steps."],[8560,"Whoever would like to meet Allah as a Muslim servant, let him guard these five prayers where the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. By my life, if every one of you prayed in his house as the one who stays in his house prays, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen us, and none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I have seen us, and indeed a man would be supported between two men until he is brought into the row. No Muslim servant performs ablution and does it well, intending to go to a congregational mosque and pray in it, and takes a step except Allah raises him a degree because of it or removes from him a sin because of it—so much so that we used to take short steps.\" And the wording is that of the hadith of Hajjaj."],[8561,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them in congregation, for they are among the ways of guidance. Indeed Allah ﷻ has obligated for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he is brought and stood in the row. A time came upon us when none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. Indeed we used to take short steps between them."],[8562,"Whoever would like to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard the prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you prayed in your houses as this one who stays behind prays in his house, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. A time came upon us when none would stay behind from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was clear. I have seen a man being supported between two men until he stands in the row."],[8563,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah has prescribed for your Prophet the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. By my life, if you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prays in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. A time came upon us when none stayed away from them except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I saw a man being supported between two men until he was stood in the row. No man purifies himself and perfects his purification, then heads to one of the mosques to pray in it, and takes a step except that Allah records for him a good deed by it, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a sin by it, until we used to take short steps."],[8564,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. By my life, if you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prays in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known."],[8566,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for His Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays behind prayed in his home, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. No man purifies himself and perfects the purification, then heads to one of these mosques except that Allah records for him for every step he takes a good deed, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a bad deed by it. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, and a man would be supported between two men until he was stood in the row."],[8567,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. I think there is no one among you except he has a mosque in which he prays. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. No Muslim servant performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then proceeds to prayer except that Allah records for him for every step a good deed, raises him a degree by it, and removes from him a sin by it."],[8568,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers when the call is given for them, for they are among the ways of guidance.\" Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of al-Mas'udi."],[8569,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers when the call is given for them, for Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. Each man among you has a mosque in his house. If you abandoned your mosques, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, you would go astray."],[8570,"Whoever wants to meet Allah tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these prescribed prayers where the call is given for them, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. If you were to pray in your homes as this one who stays away from it prays, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, and if you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, you would go astray. I saw us when none stayed away from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I saw a man among us being supported between two men until he was stood in the row. No Muslim servant performs ablution in his house, perfects the ablution, then heads to a mosque, comes to it, lifting a foot and placing a foot, except that Allah records for him by it ten good deeds, erases from him ten bad deeds, and raises for him by it ten degrees, until we used to take short steps."],[8571,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known or a sick person, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8572,"From prayer except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known, and the sick person would walk between two men to come to prayer."],[8573,"Adhere to the five prayers in the mosque, for they are from the matter of guidance and the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ."],[8574,"He should meet Allah as a Muslim servant; so let him perform the prayers wherever the call is made for them, for they are the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ. Indeed, if every man prayed in his house, you would abandon the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, and if you abandoned the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, you would go astray. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among us, and the prayer would not be commenced until the rows were made straight—or when our rows were made straight—whereas today the prayer is commenced and then one of them calls out, 'O slave girl, bring me water for ablution,' and he bares his forearms. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among us, and we used to speak that when a man performed ablution in his house and then went out to prayer, he would not lift a foot except that a degree was raised for him thereby, and he would not place the other except that Allah removed a sin from him thereby. So we used to take short steps."],[8575,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except that he spoke one day and the words 'The Messenger of Allah said' slipped from his tongue, and distress overcame him until I saw sweat rolling down him. He said, 'If Allah wills—either above this, or close to this, or below this.'"],[8576,"He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' and when he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' trembling overcame him and he would say, 'Like this, or something like this, or close to this, or whatever Allah wills.'"],[8577,"Abdullah would go a year without narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then one day he narrated while we were with him and said, 'Like this, or close to this.'"],[8578,"I sat with Abdullah for a year and did not hear him narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then one day he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then his face changed, then he said, 'Like this, or above this, or below this.'"],[8579,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one hadith, and he sweated, then said, 'This, or like this, or similar to this.'"],[8580,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—until one evening he said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' then he lowered his head. He raised his head and I saw that the buttons of his shirt were undone, his jugular veins had swollen, and his eyes had filled with tears. He said, 'Or above that, or below that, or close to that, or similar to that.'"],[8581,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then his face changed, then he said, 'Like this, or close to this.'"],[8582,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'Like that, or similar.' He was not seen narrating after this hadith ever again."],[8583,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,' then trembling seized me, and he said, 'Like this, or similar to this.'"],[8584,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said' more than once. He said: I looked at him while he was leaning on a staff, and I saw the staff shaking."],[8585,"'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and his clothes trembled. He said, 'This, or like it, or similar to this.'"],[8586,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would change color and his complexion would alter, and he would say, “This or something close to this.”"],[8587,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, except a hadith I heard him narrate; then he shuddered like the shuddering of a palm branch, then he said, “This or something like it.”"],[8588,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ ever, except once; and indeed I saw him shudder like the shuddering of a palm branch, then he said, “Close to this or something like this.”"],[8589,"Abdullah stayed for a year without saying \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.\" And when he said \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,\" he was struck by a thunderbolt and his face changed, and he said, \"It is like this or like that or like this.\""],[8590,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ; and when he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ,” he said, “This or something like this, or close to this,” and indeed he was trembling."],[8591,"I left a people in the mosque saying, “Whoever glorifies such and such will have such and such.” He said, “Stand, O ‘Alqama.” When he saw them, he said, “O ‘Alqama, divert the people’s eyes from me.” When he heard them and what they were saying, he said, “Indeed you are clinging to the tail of misguidance, or indeed you are more guided than the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.”"],[8592,"A storyteller who sits at night and tells the people, “Say such and such,” was mentioned to Ibn Masʿūd. He said, “When you see him, inform me.” He said, so they informed him, and ʿAbdullāh came veiled and said, “Whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd. Do you know that you are more guided than Muḥammad ﷺ and his companions, or indeed you are clinging to the tail of misguidance?”"],[8593,"A people would sit from sunset to nightfall glorifying, saying, “Say such and such, and say such and such.” ʿAbdullāh said, “If they sit, notify me.” When they sat, they came to him, and he set out, entered with them and sat wearing a burnoose. They began their glorification, and ʿAbdullāh uncovered the burnoose from his head and said, “I am ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd.” The people fell silent. He said, “You have brought a dark innovation, or you have surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” A man from Banū Tamīm said, “We have not brought a dark innovation, nor have we surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” ʿAmr b. ʿUtba b. Farqad said, “I seek forgiveness from God, O Ibn Masʿūd, and I repent to Him.” So he ordered them to disperse. He said: And Ibn Masʿūd saw two circles in the mosque of Kufa, so he stood between them and said, “Which of you was before its companion?” One of them said, “We were.” He said to the other, “Arise and go to it,” and he made them one."],[8594,"He said to the boy, “Go and see whether these were sitting before or those.” He came and said, “These.” He said, “The mosque only needs one innovator, for those before you perished only through mutual hatred.”"],[8596,"He informed him, “When they sit, notify me.” When they sat, he notified him, and ʿAbdullāh came wearing a burnoose until he entered upon them, uncovered the burnoose from his head, then said, “I am the son of Umm ʿAbd. By God, you have brought a dark innovation, or you have surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ in knowledge.” Muʿaḍḍad, who was an eloquent man, said, “By God, we have not brought a dark innovation, nor have we surpassed the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.” ʿAbdullāh said, “If you follow the people, they have preceded you with a clear precedence; and if you deviate right and left, you have gone astray with a far misguidance.”"],[8597,"“Do not weary the people, lest they weary of the remembrance.”"],[8598,"“O warner, do not drive the people to despair.”"],[8599,"Abū Mūsā said, “What has brought you at this hour?” He said, “No, by God, except that I saw a matter that alarmed me, and indeed it is good, and indeed it alarmed me, and indeed it is good: a people sitting in the mosque and a man saying to them, ‘Glorify such and such, praise such and such.’” He said, so ʿAbdullāh set out, and we set out with him until he came to them and said, “How quickly you have gone astray, while the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ are alive, his wives are young, and his garments and vessels have not changed. Count your evil deeds, for I guarantee from God that He will count your good deeds.”"],[8600,"Abdullah stood by me while I was narrating stories in the mosque and said: O Amr, you have indeed introduced an innovation of misguidance. Are you more guided than Muhammad ﷺ and his companions? I saw them disperse from me until I saw my place with no one in it."],[8601,"Are you more guided or the companions of Muhammad ﷺ? Indeed you are clinging to a fringe of misguidance."],[8602,"They mentioned to him a man who narrates stories, so he came among the people and I heard him say: \"Glory be to Allah, such and such.\" When he heard that, he stood up and said: \"Do you not hear?\" When they looked at him, he said: \"Indeed you are more guided than Muhammad ﷺ and his companions. Indeed you are clinging to a fringe of misguidance.\""],[8603,"When people fall into evil, say: I have no example in evil."],[8604,"When people fall into trial and they say: Go out, you have an example in the people, then say: I have no example in evil."],[8605,"That he should learn something from it, let him do so, for the smallest of houses in good is the one in which there is nothing of the Book of Allah. Indeed the house in which there is nothing of the Book of Allah is like the ruin of a house that has no one to inhabit it, and indeed Satan leaves the house in which Surah al-Baqarah is heard."],[8606,"Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for Satan does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited."],[8607,"\"Every thing has a peak and the peak of the Quran is Surah Al-Baqarah, and every thing has a core and the core of the Quran is the detailed explanation. Indeed, the devils flee from the house in which Surah Al-Baqarah is recited. And even the smallest houses have an inside that does not contain anything from the Book of Allah.\""],[8608,"Abdullah used to say: \"The smallest of houses is the one in which there is no Book of Allah, and indeed the house in which there is no Book of Allah is ruined like the ruin of a house that has no one to inhabit it.\""],[8609,"Indeed this Quran is the banquet of Allah, so learn from His banquet what you can. Indeed this Quran is the rope of Allah which He commanded, and it is the clear light and the beneficial healing, a protection for the one who holds fast to it and a salvation for the one who clings to it. It does not go crooked so that it would need to be straightened, and it does not deviate so that it would need to be corrected. Its wonders do not cease, and it does not wear out from repetition. Recite it, for indeed Allah ﷻ will reward you for every letter of it with ten good deeds. I do not say to you that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter."],[8610,"Whoever recites the Quran, for every letter of a verse he has ten good deeds, and I do not say Alif Lam Mim is ten, but Alif, Lam, and Mim are thirty good deeds."],[8611,"Learn the Quran and recite it, for you will be rewarded for it with a good deed for every letter of it. Indeed I do not say Alif Lam Mim is a good deed, but Alif, Lam, and Mim are thirty good deeds. That is because Allah ﷻ says: {Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times its like}."],[8612,"Learn the Quran and recite it, you will be rewarded for every letter with ten good deeds. Indeed I do not say Alif Lam Mim, but I say Alif, Lam, and Mim."],[8613,"A man died, so the angels of punishment came to him and sat by his head. They said, \"You have no way to escape from us. He used to recite Surah Al-Mulk.\" Then they sat by his feet and said the same. Finally, they sat by his abdomen and said, \"You have no way to escape from us. Indeed, he has passed away while Surah Al-Mulk was with him.\" Thus, he was given the name \"Al-Mani'ah\" (the Preventer)."],[8614,"A man is approached in his grave. His feet are approached, and they say: \"You have no way over what is before us; he used to recite Surat al-Mulk upon us.\" Then his torso is approached, and it says: \"You have no way over me; he had contained Surat al-Mulk within me.\" Then he is approached from his head, and it says: \"You have no way over what is before me; he used to recite Surat al-Mulk within me.\" Abdullah said: \"It is the preventer, preventing the punishment of the grave. And in the Torah it is: Surat al-Mulk—whoever recites it in a night has done much and good.\""],[8618,"Abdullah said: \"The Quran is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, and an advocate whose testimony is believed. Whoever makes it his guide, it leads him to Paradise; whoever puts it behind him, it drives him to the Fire.\""],[8619,"\"Whoever loves the Quran and is pleased with it, he is upon good.\""],[8620,"\"Whoever loves to know that he loves Allah and His Messenger, let him look: if he loves the Qur'an, then he loves Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[8621,"You heard Abdullah, and I confirm you—or I narrate and you confirm me. He said: I heard Abdullah say: The most comprehensive verse in the Quran for good and evil is a verse in Surat al-Nahl: {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrongdoing, and oppression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.} He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: I heard Abdullah say: The greatest verse in the Quran in bringing joy is a verse in Surat al-Ghuraf: {Say, O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair} of the mercy of Allah. Indeed Allah forgives all sins, if He wills. He said: You have spoken the truth."],[8622,"Masruq said to Shutayr: These people have turned to us only for us to narrate to them. Either you narrate and I confirm you, or I narrate and you confirm me. Masruq said: Narrate, and I will confirm you. Shutayr said: Abdullah b. Mas'ud narrated to us that the greatest verse in the Book of Allah is {Allah—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. He narrated to us that Abdullah said: The most comprehensive verse in the Book of Allah is {Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. And he narrated to us that the most or greatest verse in the Book of Allah in bringing joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair} of the mercy of Allah to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth. And he narrated to us that the verse in the Book of Allah conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect} to the end of the verse. Masruq said: You have spoken the truth."],[8623,"We sat in the mosque, and the people surged toward the two of them. One of them said to his companion: They only stood up to us so that we narrate to them. Either I narrate to them and you confirm me, or you narrate and I confirm you. One of them said: I heard Abdullah say: \"The greatest verse in the Quran is the Verse of the Throne.\" The other said: You have spoken the truth. The other said: I heard Abdullah say: The most comprehensive verse in the Quran is {Indeed Allah commands justice and excellence}. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: And I heard him say: The verse in the Quran conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out}. He said: You have spoken the truth. The other said: And I heard him say: The greatest verse in the Quran in bringing joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves}. He said: You have spoken the truth."],[8624,"Masruq said: I do not think these people sat with us except to hear good from us. Either you narrate from Abdullah and I confirm you, or I narrate from Abdullah and you confirm me. He said: Narrate to us, Abu 'A'ishah. Masruq said: I heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say: \"The two eyes commit adultery, the two feet commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the private part confirms or denies that.\" He said: Yes, and I have also heard it. He said: Have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the most comprehensive verse in the Quran regarding lawful and unlawful, command and prohibition is {Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality} to the end of the verse? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. He said: Have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the verse in the Quran conveying the greatest reliance is {And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect}? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. He said: And have you heard Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that the verse in the Quran bringing the greatest joy is {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah} to the end of the verse? He said: Yes. He said: And I have also heard it. The wording is from the hadith of Hammad b. Zayd."],[8626,"He used to recite a verse to a man and then say: \"It is better than what the sun has risen upon, or better than anything on the earth,\" until he would say that concerning the entire Quran."],[8627,"\"Whoever desires the good of the first and the last, let him stir the Quran, for in it is the good of the first and the last.\""],[8628,"Abdullah said, \"Whoever seeks knowledge should start with the Quran, for it is the best of all things, both in the beginning and in the end.\""],[8629,"\"Whoever desires knowledge, let him stir the Quran, for in it is the knowledge of the first and the last.\""],[8630,"For every letter there is a limit, and for every limit there is a point of ascent."],[8631,"Indeed, there is not a single letter of the Qur'an except that it has a limit, and for every limit there is a point of ascent."],[8632,"Whoever recites 'Say: He is Allah, the One' it is as if he has recited a third of the Qur'an."],[8633,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'The parable of one who recites the Qur'an but does not act upon it is like a fragrant herb whose scent is pleasant but has no taste. The parable of one who acts upon the Qur'an but does not recite it is like a date whose taste is pleasant but has no fragrance. The parable of one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it is like a citron whose taste is pleasant and whose fragrance is pleasant. The parable of one who does not recite the Qur'an nor act upon it is like a colocynth whose taste is bitter and whose smell is bitter.'"],[8634,"Whoever recites Surah al-Baqarah in a night has done much and has done well."],[8635,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'Whoever recites three verses from Surah al-Baqarah in a night has done much and has done well.'"],[8636,"ʿAbd Allah said: 'Whoever recites ten verses from Surah al-Baqarah in a house, no devil will enter that house that night until morning: four verses from its beginning, the Verse of the Throne, two verses after it, and its closing verses.'"],[8637,"He used to recite: {And all will come to Him in humility} (Q27:87)."],[8638,"I recited the Qur'an to ʿAbd Allah and he did not correct me except for two letters. I recited: {And all will come to Him in humility} (Q27:87). He said: {And all will come to Him in humility}. And I recited: {Until, when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied} (Q12:110). He said: {And thought that they had been lied to}."],[8639,"He used to recite: {This is nothing but the tales of the ancients} (Q68:15), saying: 'Something they fabricated.'"],[8640,"Ibn Masood used to recite the Quran to a man. The man recited the verse \"Verily, the sadaqat (charity) are only for the poor and the needy\" incorrectly. So Ibn Masood said, \"This is not how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to me. He recited it as 'Verily, the sadaqat are only for the poor and the needy'.\" And he elongated it."],[8641,"He recited: (Wherever He directs him, he brings only good)."],[8642,"That you worship none but Him.'"],[8643,"I heard the Quran reciters and I found their recitations close to one another, so recite as you have been taught, and beware of being overly meticulous and of disagreement, for it is only like one of you saying, 'Come here' and 'Come on.'"],[8644,"ʿAbdullah [said]: Do not say {hīt} [i.e., do not alter the reading]. We have already asked about that, and I prefer to recite as I was taught."],[8645,"He used to recite {majrāhā wa-mursāhā}."],[8646,"It is permitted to recite some of it [one variant] in place of some [another variant], but the error is to attach to it something that is not part of it."],[8647,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar, for it is Arabic."],[8648,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar."],[8649,"Inflect the Quran according to Arabic grammar, for it is Arabic, and there will come a people who will master it but they are not the best of you."],[8650,"Keep looking at the mushaf continuously."],[8651,"Keep reviewing the mushafs, for it slips away from men's chests more quickly than camels break free from their tethers."],[8652,"He recited it as {bal ʿajibtu wa-yaskharūn}."],[8653,"He used to recite it as \"al-Ḥayy al-Qayyām\"."],[8654,"He used to recite {ḥattā yalija al-jamalu fī sammi al-khiyāṭi} [until the camel goes through the eye of the needle], saying, \"It means the male camel.\""],[8656,"Abdullah said: \"When one of you asks his companion how he recites such-and-such a verse, let him ask him about what comes before it.\""],[8657,"Abdullah said: \"When one of you asks his brother about a verse, he should not say, 'Such-and-such,' for that is not upon him, but he should recite what comes before it, then let him come between him and his need.\""],[8658,"I recited to Abdullah and he was pleased with my voice, so he said: \"Recite in a measured tone, may my father and mother be your ransom.\""],[8659,"Ibn Masʿud said: \"Keep looking at the mushaf, and if you differ over a ya or a ta, make it ya; treat the Quran as masculine.\""],[8660,"He said: \"When you dispute over a ya or a ta, make it ya and treat the Quran as masculine, for it is masculine.\""],[8661,"He said: \"This Quran will surely be snatched away from among you.\" I said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, how can it be snatched away when we have fixed it in our mushafs?\" He said: \"It will be taken away by night, and nothing of it will remain in the heart of any servant or in any mushaf, and people will wake up poor like beasts.\" Then Abdullah recited: \"And if We willed, We could surely take away that which We have revealed to you, then you would find no guardian for you against Us.\""],[8662,"Abdullah said: \"The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing that will remain is prayer, and a people will surely pray who have no faith.\""],[8663,"And the Quran will surely be snatched away from among you.\" They said: \"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, are we not reciting the Quran and have we not fixed it in our mushafs?\" He said: \"The Quran will be taken away by night and removed from the hearts of men, so that nothing of it will remain on the earth.\""],[8664,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8665,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8666,"He said: \"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is a rajaz reciter.\""],[8668,"\"Whoever recites the Quran in less than three days is negligent.\""],[8669,"\"He used to read the Quran on Fridays and he used to read it three times in Ramadan.\""],[8670,"Abdullah said: \"The Quran is not to be recited in less than three days. Recite it in seven, and let a man keep to his portion every day and night.\""],[8673,"Ibn Masʿūd used to recite the Qur’an in three [days], and he would only take a little help from the daytime."],[8674,"ʿAbdullāh used to recite the Qur’an every three [days], and he rarely took from it during the daytime."],[8675,"Our companions ʿAlqamah, al-Aswad, and al-Rabīʿ b. Khuthaym."],[8677,"Abū Isḥāq was asked, and it was said to him: “Do you remember from al-Aswad that ʿAbdullāh said: ‘When you recite a sūrah whose end is a prostration, then if you wish, bow, for the rakʿah is from the prostration; and if you wish, prostrate, then recite a sūrah after it?’” He said: “Yes.”"],[8678,"“When the prostration is the seal of the sūrah, then if you wish, bow; and if you wish, prostrate.”"],[8680,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd: “It is only the repentance of a prophet that is mentioned, so he would not prostrate in it,” meaning Ṣād."],[8681,"ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād."],[8682,"And he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8683,"He would not prostrate in Ṣād, and he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8684,"ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād."],[8685,"From al-Shaʿbī: They both said: ʿAbdullāh would not prostrate in Ṣād, and he said: “It is only the repentance of a prophet.”"],[8686,"“Recite,” and he would prompt him while he was reciting."],[8687,"“Read,” and he began reading, and he began prompting him."],[8688,"Ibrahim: “ʿAbd Allah went aside to relieve himself, then a man asked him to open (the recitation), and he prompted him before touching water.”"],[8689,"“On Ibn Masʿud’s ring there was a tree, or something, between two flies.”"],[8690,"“Whoever recites five verses in a night will never be recorded that night among the heedless; whoever recites one hundred verses will be recorded among the devout; whoever recites three hundred will have a qintar recorded for him; and whoever recites seven hundred will succeed.”"],[8691,"ʿAbd Allah would prostrate in “When the sky is split open.”"],[8692,"I prostrated with ʿUmar and with ʿAbd Allah in “When the sky is split open.” Al-Aswad said, “As for one of them, I have no doubt about it.”"],[8693,"I saw ʿAbd Allah and ʿUmar, or one of them, prostrate in “When the sky is split open.”"],[8694,"“ʿAbd Allah would prostrate in (Surah) al-Najm and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created.’”"],[8695,"ʿAbd Allah: “Whoever recites Surah al-Aʿraf, or al-Najm, or ‘When the sky is split open,’ or the Children of Israel, or ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes to bow at the end of any of them, he may bow, and the prostration of bowing suffices him; and if he prostrates, let him add another surah to it.”"],[8696,"“Whoever recites al-Aʿraf, al-Najm, and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes to bow at the end of any of them, he may bow, and the prostration of bowing suffices him; and if he prostrates, let him add another surah to it.”"],[8697,"“Whoever recites al-Aʿraf, al-Najm, and ‘Read in the name of your Lord who created,’ then if he wishes he may bow with it and it suffices him; and if he wishes he may prostrate, then stand and recite the surah and bow and prostrate.”"],[8698,"When Ibn Masʿud recited al-Najm to the people, he prostrated with it; and when he recited it in prayer, he bowed with it and prostrated."],[8699,"There is nothing upon him regarding smiling in the prayer."],[8700,"Abdullah b. Masʿud used to prostrate in the first verse of Ḥā Mīm Tanzīl from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."],[8701,"Abdullah said: Indeed, the prayers are the good deeds and an expiation for what is between the first to the afternoon prayer is the afternoon prayer, and an expiation for what is between the afternoon prayer to the sunset prayer is the sunset prayer, and an expiation for what is between the sunset to the night prayer is the night prayer, then the Muslim retires to his bed with no sin upon him as long as he avoids major sins. Then he recited: {Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds}."],[8702,"Abdullah b. Masʿud said: You burn until when they pray the dawn prayer, they are washed; then you burn until when they pray the noon prayer, they are washed; you burn until when they pray the afternoon prayer, they are washed; until he counted all the prayers like this."],[8703,"Indeed, these prayers are the true expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided."],[8704,"The prayers are expiations for what is between them, as long as major sins are avoided."],[8705,"We used to recite to Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī while he was walking. When we came to a prostration verse, he said Allahu Akbar and we said Allahu Akbar, and he prostrated and we prostrated, gesturing. He would raise his head and say, 'Peace be upon you,' and we would say, 'And upon you be peace.' Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān claimed that Abdullah used to do that with them."],[8706,"Whoever among you recites the Quran, let him learn the obligatory shares of inheritance, for if a bedouin meets him and says, 'O Muhājir, do you recite the Quran?' and he says, 'Yes,' then the bedouin says, 'And I recite,' then the bedouin says, 'Do you assign the shares, O Muhājir?' If he says, 'Yes,' he says, 'An addition and good.' But if he says, 'I do not know it well,' he says, 'Then what is your superiority over me, O Muhājir?'"],[8707,"Abdullah said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, there is nothing on the face of the earth more in need of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8708,"Abdullah said: By Allah, besides whom there is no god, there is nothing on the back of the earth more in need of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8709,"Abdullah said: There is nothing on the earth more deserving of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8710,"I heard Abdullah b. Masʿud say: There is nothing more deserving of lengthy imprisonment than a tongue."],[8711,"“Sin is what scratches the hearts; whatever scratches the heart of any of you, let him leave it.”"],[8712,"“Whatever is from a glance, the devil has a share of desire in it, and sin is what scratches the hearts.”"],[8713,"ʿAbd Allah: “Beware of the whisperings of the chests.”"],[8714,"“Whoever lets others hear of his deeds, Allah will expose him; whoever shows off, Allah will expose him on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever humbles himself before Allah out of humility, Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8715,"“Go forth as a scholar or a learner, and do not go forth between that; if you do not, then love the scholars and do not hate them.”"],[8716,"ʿAbd Allah counseled his son ʿAbd al-Rahman, saying: “I counsel you to be mindful of Allah, let your house suffice you, weep over your sin, and control your tongue.”"],[8717,"“A man who hoards will be cauterized; a dirham will touch another dirham and no dinar another dinar; his skin will be expanded until every dinar and dirham is placed separately on it.”"],[8718,"“Accustom yourselves to good, for good comes by habit, and guard your intentions in prayer.”"],[8719,"“Whoever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.”"],[8720,"“Whoever desires the Hereafter harms his worldly life, and whoever desires the world harms his Hereafter, so He commanded them to harm the perishable for the everlasting.”"],[8721,"I was at Shuraf, and ʿAbd Allah stopped with us. My family sent me to him with some things, and some slave boys of ours who were with the camels came from a journey of four nights with a bird. I took it to him. When I took it to him, he asked me, “From where did you bring me this bird?” I said, “Some slave boys of ours who were with the camels brought it from a journey of four nights.” ʿAbd Allah said, “I wish that I were where it was hunted, not speaking to any human about anything, and no one speaking to me until I meet Allah.”"],[8722,"By Allah, other than whom there is no god, there is no living soul but that death is better for it: if it is righteous, for Allah ﷻ says, “And what is with Allah is better for the righteous,” and if it is wicked, for Allah ﷻ says, “And let not those who disbelieve think that Our granting them respite is better for themselves; We only grant them respite that they may increase in sin.”"],[8723,"O people, learn! Whoever knows, let him act."],[8724,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “A people will come who drink knowledge as one drinks.”"],[8725,"“You have spoken the truth, by the One besides whom there is no god.”"],[8726,"\"Abdullah said, 'I do not know any of you who has the endurance of a camel in the darkness of the night and the heat of the day.'\""],[8727,"\"Do not imitate the religion of anyone among you, for if he believes, he will believe, and if he disbelieves, he will disbelieve. If you are to follow anyone, follow the one who has passed away, for the living are not safe from trials.\""],[8728,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “None of you should be an immaʿa (one who blindly follows others).” They said, “What is an immaʿa, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “He says, ‘I am only with the people: if they are guided, I am guided; and if they go astray, I go astray.’ Indeed, let each of you resolve in himself that even if the people disbelieve, he will not disbelieve.”"],[8729,"“In the Age of Ignorance we used to call the immaʿa the one who comes to food without being invited. Indeed, the immaʿa among you is the one who makes his religion a mount for others.”"],[8730,"“In the Age of Ignorance we used to call the immaʿa a man who is invited to food and another man follows him. Today it is the one who makes his religion a mount for people. And we used to call slander sorcery; today it is ‘it was said and he said.’”"],[8731,"“You pray more and strive more than the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ, yet they were better than you.” They said, “Why is that, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “Because they were more abstinent from this world and more desirous of the Hereafter.”"],[8733,"\"Follow and do not innovate, for you have been sufficed with every innovation of misguidance.\""],[8734,"“The whole earth will be fire on the Day of Resurrection, and Paradise will be beyond it. They will see its maidens with swelling breasts and its goblets. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of ʿAbd Allāh, a man will sweat so profusely that his sweat will flow over the earth up to his own height, then it will rise until it reaches his nose, while the reckoning has not touched him.” They said, “Why is that?” He said, “Because of what he sees people suffering.”"],[8735,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “By the One besides whom there is no god, no servant thinks well of Allah except that He gives him what he thought, and that is because all good is in His hand.”"],[8736,"ʿAbd Allāh said to his wife: “Is today better or yesterday?” She said, “I do not know.” He said, “But I know: yesterday is better than today, and today is better than tomorrow, and so on until the Hour comes.”"],[8737,"ʿAbd Allāh came out to us one day while he was weak. We said, “What is the matter with you?” He said, “The pure part of this world is gone, and nothing remains but its dregs. Today death is a gift for every Muslim.”"],[8738,"“The pure part of this world is gone, and nothing remains but its dregs. Today death is a gift for every Muslim.”"],[8739,"The likeness of this world is that of a water-hole (thaghab).\" We said, \"What is a thaghab?\" He said, \"A pool whose clear water has gone and whose dregs remain. So death is a gift for every believer.\""],[8740,"The people of affliction will wish on the Day of Resurrection, when they behold the reward, that their skins had been cut with scissors."],[8741,"that their bodies had been cut with scissors.\""],[8742,"The disbeliever will be bridled with his sweat on the Day of Resurrection, because of the length of that day, until he says, \"My Lord, relieve me, even if it be to the Fire.\""],[8743,"that he should ask, let him begin with praising and extolling Allah as He deserves, then let him invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then let him ask afterwards, for that is more likely to succeed.\""],[8744,"When a man mounts a riding beast and does not remember Allah, Satan rides behind him and says to him, \"Sing.\" If he is not good at it, he says to him, \"Wish.\""],[8745,"The Satan of a believer meets the Satan of a disbeliever. The Satan of the believer appears pale, dusty, and emaciated, so the Satan of the disbeliever says, \"What is the matter with you? Woe to you, you are ruined.\" The Satan of the believer says, \"No, by Allah, I cannot get at him with anything. When he eats, he mentions the name of Allah; when he drinks, he mentions the name of Allah; and when he enters his house, he mentions the name of Allah.\" The other one says, \"But I eat from his food, drink from his drink, and sleep on his bed.\" So this one is fat and that one is emaciated."],[8746,"Abdullah, the major sins are associating partners with Allah, despairing of Allah's relief, despondency of Allah's mercy, and feeling secure from Allah's plan."],[8747,"that he said: The greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, feeling secure from Allah's plan, despondency of Allah's mercy, and despairing of Allah's relief."],[8748,"The greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, despairing of Allah's relief, despondency of Allah's mercy, and feeling secure from Allah's plan."],[8749,"Go to your mother and tell her to dress you in a shirt other than this one.\""],[8750,"We were with Abdullah when a son of his came wearing a silk shirt. He said, \"Who clothed you in this?\" He said, \"My mother.\" He said, \"So he tore it.\" He said, \"Tell your mother to clothe you in something other than this.\""],[8751,"He said: “A man will never find the taste of faith until he believes in divine decree and knows that he will die and that he will be resurrected.”"],[8752,"That he will die and then be resurrected after death.”"],[8753,"Three qualities: whoever has them will find the sweetness of faith—abandoning disputation in what is true, avoiding lying in jest, and knowing that what befalls him could not have missed him and what misses him could not have befallen him."],[8754,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Did they say, ‘We are the people of Paradise’?”"],[8755,"A man said in the presence of ʿAbd Allāh, “I am a believer.” ʿAbd Allāh said, “Say, ‘I am in Paradise,’ but we believe in God, His angels, and His messengers.”"],[8756,"“I adjure by God any one who has severed ties of kinship to leave us, for we wish to call upon our Lord while the gates of heaven are closed to the one who severs ties of kinship.”"],[8757,"“When a man among the Children of Israel committed a sin, he would wake to find written on his door, ‘You have committed such-and-such a sin, and its expiation is such-and-such a deed,’ so perhaps he would be eager to make it known.” Ibn Masʿūd said, “I would not love that God ﷻ gave us that in place of this verse: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks God’s forgiveness will find God Forgiving, Merciful}.”"],[8758,"A man passed by another man while he was prostrating and stepped on his neck. He said, “You step on my neck while I am prostrating? By God, God will never forgive you, ever.” God said, “Do you swear by Me? Indeed, I have forgiven him.”"],[8759,"“Indeed, the likeness of the belittled (minor) sins is like the likeness of a group of travelers who camped in a barren land. With them was food that could not be cooked except with fire. So they scattered: one came bringing dung, another came bringing a bone, and another came bringing a stick, until they gathered from that enough with which to cook their food. Likewise is the one who commits the belittled sins: he tells a lie, and commits a sin, and gathers from that what may cause God to cast him on his face into the Fire of Hell.”"],[8760,"He said: We asked permission to enter upon ʿAbd Allāh after the dawn prayer, and he gave us permission, casting a velvet cloak over his wife and saying, “I disliked keeping you waiting.”"],[8761,"Two men at whom God laughs: a man upon a horse among the finest horses of his companions; when they meet the enemy, they flee, but he remains firm—if he is killed, he is killed as a martyr, so God laughs at him. And a man who rises in the night when no one knows of him, performs ablution thoroughly, prays for Muḥammad ﷺ, praises God, and begins the recitation—God laughs at him, saying, ‘Look at My servant; no one sees him but Me.’"],[8762,"Three things I swear by, and a fourth—if I swore by it, I would be truthful: God will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes God as his protector in this world but that God entrusts him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no man loves a people but that he will come with them. The fourth, which if I swore by it I would be truthful: God does not conceal a servant in this world but that God will conceal him in the Hereafter."],[8763,"ʿAbd Allāh said: Three things I swear by, and a fourth—if I swore by it, I would hope not to sin and would be truthful: God will not make one who has a share in submission like one who has no share; no Muslim servant takes God as his protector but that God will entrust him to another on the Day of Resurrection; and no man loves a people but that God will resurrect him with them. The shares of Islam are three: prayer, alms, and fasting. The fourth, if I swore by it, I would hope not to sin: God does not conceal a servant in this world but that God will conceal him in the Hereafter."],[8764,"I went with a man to ʿAbdullāh, and found him standing in prayer while two men had flanked him. When he said the salutation, they asked him about a verse. He said to one of them, \"Who taught you to recite?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" He said to the other, \"Who taught you to recite?\" He said, \"Abū Ḥakīm\"—or he said \"Abū ʿAmrah.\" He said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then he wept until his tears soaked the pebbles. Then he said, \"ʿUmar ؓ was a strong fortress for Islam: people entered Islam and did not leave it. When ʿUmar was struck, the fortress was breached.\""],[8765,"And the other said, \"ʿUmar taught it to me.\" When ʿUmar was mentioned, ʿAbdullāh wept while standing, wiped his eyes, and shook his hand over the pebbles. Then he said, \"It is clearer than the road of al-Saylaḥīn.\" Then he said, \"Recite it as ʿUmar taught you. Any household of the Muslims that was not entered by grief for ʿUmar on the day he was struck is a household of evil. ʿUmar was the most God-fearing of us and the best reciter of the Book of Allah among us.\""],[8766,"Two men disputed about a verse. While we were in that state, ʿAbdullāh approached from the direction of his in-laws. They went to him, and I went with them. They said, \"We have disputed about a verse.\" ʿAbdullāh said to one of them, \"Recite.\" He recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"Abū ʿAmrah Maʿqil b. Muqarrin.\" Then he said to the other, \"Recite it.\" He recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" His eyes brought forth four [streams of tears], and he wept until I saw him take some of his tears in his palm and gesture with it like this. I saw two marks in the pebbles from ʿAbdullāh's tears. Then ʿAbdullāh said, \"I do not think any household of the Muslims that was not entered by grief for ʿUmar on the day he was struck is anything but a household of evil. ʿUmar was the most knowledgeable of us about Allah, the best reciter of the Book of Allah among us, and the most understanding of the religion of Allah among us. Recite it as ʿUmar taught you, for by Allah it is clearer than the road of al-Saylaḥīn.\""],[8767,"Two men came to ʿAbdullāh while we were with him. One said, \"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, how should we recite this verse?\" ʿAbdullāh recited it to him. The man said, \"Abū Ḥakīm taught it to me in such-and-such a way.\" The other recited, and ʿAbdullāh said, \"Who taught it to you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar.\" ʿAbdullāh said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then ʿAbdullāh wept until I saw his tears flowing down onto the pebbles. Then he said, \"ʿUmar was a strong fortress over Islam: people entered it and did not leave. The fortress has now become breached, so people leave it and do not enter.\""],[8768,"Abū Ḥakīm al-Muzanī taught me. He asked the other to recite, then said, \"Who taught you?\" He said, \"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb taught me.\" ʿAbdullāh wept until his tears dyed the pebbles. Then he said, \"Recite as ʿUmar taught you.\" Then he traced a circle with his hand and said, \"ʿUmar was a strong fortress for Islam: people entered through it and did not leave it. When ʿUmar died, the fortress was breached, so people leave it and do not enter.\""],[8769,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"ʿUmar's acceptance of Islam was a conquest, his emigration was a victory, and his rule was a mercy. By Allah, we were not able to pray at the Kaʿbah openly until ʿUmar accepted Islam.\""],[8770,"From Qatādah and Ḥammād, who said: I heard them saying—he heard the two of them saying—that Ibn Masʿūd used to say, \"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was a strong fortress for Islam: one entered Islam and did not leave it. When ʿUmar died, a breach was made in the fortress, so one leaves it and does not enter it. When he took a path, we found it easy. When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar. He was the dividing line between increase and decrease. By Allah, I wish I could serve someone like him until I die.\""],[8771,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"By Allah, I think that if ʿUmar's knowledge were placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of the rest of the living people of the earth were placed in the other pan, ʿUmar's knowledge ؓ would outweigh it.\" Sulaymān said: I mentioned that, and he said, \"ʿAbdullāh said something even better than that. He said, 'I think ʿUmar went away with nine-tenths of knowledge.'\""],[8772,"ʿUmar's knowledge was placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of the people of the earth in the other pan, his knowledge would outweigh their knowledge.\" Wakīʿ said: al-Aʿmash said: I found that objectionable, so I went to Ibrāhīm and mentioned it to him. He said, \"What do you find objectionable in that? By Allah, ʿAbdullāh said something even better than that. He said, 'I think nine-tenths of knowledge went away on the day ʿUmar ؓ went away.'\""],[8773,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"I think nine-tenths of knowledge was raised with ʿUmar on the day he died. I think that if ʿUmar's knowledge were placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of those after him in the other, ʿUmar's knowledge ؓ would outweigh it.\""],[8774,"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. Where is he? He said, \"He is in Paradise.\" He said, \"Abū Bakr passed away. Where is he?\" He said, \"That is al-Awwāh; with every good he is sought.\" He said, \"ʿUmar passed away. Where is he?\" He said, \"When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar.\""],[8775,"ʿAbdullāh said, \"When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with ʿUmar.\""],[8776,"When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar. His acceptance of Islam was a victory, and his rule was a conquest. By God, I know of nothing on the earth except that it felt the loss of ʿUmar—even the thorny trees. By God, I reckon that between his eyes there is an angel who guides him and directs him aright. By God, I reckon that Satan is afraid of him, lest he introduce something new into Islam and ʿUmar refute him. By God, if I knew of a dog that loved ʿUmar, I would love it."],[8777,"I loved ʿUmar so much that I feared God, and if I knew that a dog loved ʿUmar, I would love it. I wish I had been a servant to ʿUmar ؓ . Everything felt his loss, even the thorny trees. His migration was a victory, and his authority was a mercy."],[8778,"If ʿUmar loved a dog, that dog would be the most beloved of dogs to me."],[8779,"ʿAbdullāh said: “I feared God in my love for ʿUmar ؓ .”"],[8780,"ʿAbdullāh said: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar.”"],[8781,"ʿAbdullāh used to say: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar. I wish I were a servant to someone like ʿUmar until I die.”"],[8782,"ʿAbdullāh said: “When the righteous are mentioned, then hail to ʿUmar.”"],[8783,"ʿAbdullāh said: “ʿUmar’s acceptance of Islam was a conquest, and his rule was a mercy. By God, we were not able to pray at the House until ʿUmar accepted Islam. When ʿUmar accepted Islam, he confronted them until they called us, and we prayed.”"],[8784,"“We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8785,"I heard Ibn Masʿūd say: “We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8786,"“We have remained mighty since ʿUmar ؓ accepted Islam.”"],[8787,"ʿAbdullāh said: Satan met a man from among the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ and wrestled with him. The Muslim threw him down and pressed his thumb. He said: “Let me go and I will teach you a verse that none of us hears except that he turns away.” So he released him, but he refused to teach him. He returned and wrestled with him again, and the Muslim threw him down and pressed his thumb. He said: “Tell me it.” But he refused to teach him. When he returned the third time, he said: “The verse in Sūrat al-Baqarah: {Allāh—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining} to its end.” It was said to ʿAbdullāh: “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who was that man?” He said: “Who could it be except ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ ?”"],[8788,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"I think that Satan flees from Umar's perception.\""],[8789,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud met a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , who was struggling with a jinn. The man was able to overpower the jinn, and the jinn asked the man to let him go. The man agreed on the condition that the jinn teach him something beneficial if he overpowered him for a third time. The man overpowered the jinn again, and the jinn said, \"I see you as weak and thin, like the offspring of a dog. That is how you and the jinn are.\" The man replied, \"No, by Allah, I am not one of them. Rather, let me overpower you for the third time, and if I do, you must teach me something beneficial.\" The man overpowered the jinn again, and then he asked the jinn to teach him. The man asked, \"Can you recite the Ayat al-Kursi?\" The jinn replied, \"Yes.\" The man said, \"You will not recite it inside a house, but the Shaytan will leave the house with a noise like that of a donkey. It will not enter the house until morning.\" A man from the people asked, \"O Abu Abdullah! Who is that man from the companions of Muhammad ﷺ ?\" Abdullah ibn Mas'ud frowned and approached him, saying, \"Who could it be but Umar?\""],[8790,"That tranquility speaks upon the tongue of Umar.\""],[8792,"The most perceptive of people are three: the companion of Musa who said, {O my father, hire him. Indeed, the best you can hire is the strong and the trustworthy}. He said, \"What did you see of his strength?\" She said, \"He came to the well with a rock over it that so-and-so many could not lift, and he lifted it.\" He said, \"What did you see of his trustworthiness?\" She said, \"I was walking in front of him and he put me behind him.\" And the companion of Yusuf when he said, {Make his stay comfortable; perhaps he will benefit us or we will take him as a son}. And Abu Bakr when he appointed Umar as successor."],[8794,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"I think that between Umar's eyes there is an angel guiding him.\""],[8795,"And as if an angel between his eyes was guiding him.\""],[8796,"That between his eyes there was an angel guiding him.\""],[8797,"\"Umar disliked praying after the afternoon prayer, and I dislike what Umar disliked.\""],[8798,"We, the companions of Muhammad, gathered and appointed the best of us, one with superiority."],[8799,"From the best of us, one with superiority, so we pledged allegiance to him; so pledge allegiance to the Commander of the Believers, Uthman b. Affan.\""],[8801,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"It would not please me to shoot Uthman with an arrow that missed him—I think he said—intending to kill him, even if I had the like of Uhud in gold.\""],[8803,"ʿAbd Allah came announcing Umar's death and Uthman's appointment as successor. ʿAbd Allah said, \"By God, we did not fall short regarding our highest one, the one with superiority.\""],[8804,"From its highest—that is above.”"],[8805,"When ʿUthmān ؓ was appointed caliph, ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said, “We have placed in authority the best of those who remain, and we have not been remiss.”"],[8806,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said, “We have placed in authority the best of those who remain, and we have not been remiss.”"],[8807,"That he announced the death of ʿUmar, and weeping choked him once or twice. Then he said, “ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was a strong fortress for Islam, into which people entered and from which they did not leave. The fortress has now crumbled.” Then he announced his death, and then said, “And ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān was appointed caliph, and we have not been remiss concerning the best of it—that is above.”"],[8808,"That his soul be taken, and his taking is the departure of his people. And you must hold to knowledge, for one of you does not know when he will need what he has. And you must hold to knowledge, and beware of excessive precision and going too deep. And you must hold to the old, for a people will come who recite the Book of Allah and cast it behind their backs.”"],[8809,"“O people, learn, for one of you does not know when he will be in need of it.” Then a man came to him and said, “O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, what do you think of a man who recites the Quran in reverse order?” He said, “That is one whose heart is reversed.” Then a muṣḥaf was brought to him that had been adorned and gilded, and ʿAbdullāh said, “The best adornment of a muṣḥaf is its recitation in truth.”"],[8810,"That he used to say, “O Allah, if You have written me among the people of wretchedness, then erase me and establish me among the people of felicity.”"],[8811,"That Ibn Masʿūd would sometimes quote a line of poetry from the events of the Arabs."],[8812,"I heard ʿAbdullāh say, “There is no word I can speak to a person of authority by which I can ward off from myself two lashes of the whip but that I would speak it.”"],[8813,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “A man may relate a hadith, and someone whose intellect cannot reach the understanding of that hadith hears it, and it becomes a trial for him.”"],[8814,"There were two towns, one righteous and the other wicked. A man left the wicked town intending to go to the righteous town, and death came to him wherever Allah willed. The angel and the devil disputed over him. The devil said, “By Allah, he never disobeyed me.” The angel said, “He had set out intending repentance.” It was decided between them that they should see to which of the two towns he was closer. They found him closer to the righteous town by a span, so he was forgiven. Maʿmar said, “And I heard someone say, ‘Allah brought the righteous town closer to him.’”"],[8815,"“One who forbids what is lawful is like one who permits what is unlawful.”"],[8816,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd say: 'The one who forbids the lawful is like the one who makes the unlawful lawful.'"],[8817,"'I do not leave behind me anything dearer to me than camels I give water to.'"],[8818,"'Allah, Mighty and Exalted, will question every guardian about what He entrusted to him: did he establish Allah's command among them or did he neglect it? Even a man will be questioned about his own household.'"],[8819,"that it would burst upon us, so if you sent someone to dam it... ʿAbd Allah said: 'We will not dam it. By Allah, a time will come upon people when, if they sought a basin of water, you would not find it. Every water will return to its source, and the water and the Muslims will be in Syria.'"],[8820,"The Euphrates River extended during the time of Abdullah, and the people disliked that. Abdullah said, \"Do not dislike it, for there will soon come a time when people will search for a cup of water and will not find it, as all water will return to its source, and the remainder of the water will be with the believers in Sham.\""],[8821,"'When the year thirty-five comes, a great event will occur. If they perish, then it is fitting; if they survive, then perhaps. And when the year seventy comes, you will see what you disapprove of.'"],[8822,"'It is as if I see the Turks coming to you on horses with cropped ears until they tether them at the bank of the Euphrates.'"],[8823,"that a man should love his brother, loving him only for the sake of Allah, and in it..."],[8824,"'...from idolatry.'"],[8825,"'Amulets, incantations, and love charms are idolatry, or a portion of idolatry.'"],[8826,"He saw on the neck of a woman of his household a leather strap containing amulets. He pulled it firmly until he cut the strap and said: 'The family of ʿAbd Allah is indeed free of need from idolatry.' Then he said: 'Love charms, amulets, and incantations are indeed idolatry.' A woman said: 'One of us gets a headache and seeks a ruqya. When she seeks a ruqya, it is thought to have helped her.' ʿAbd Allah said: 'Satan comes to one of you and inserts into her head. When she seeks a ruqya, he withdraws; when she does not, he pricks. If one of you were to call for water and sprinkle it on her head and face, then say, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,\" then recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" \"Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak,\" and \"Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind,\" that would benefit her, if Allah wills.'"],[8827,"'The marrow of the leg of a woman of the houris will be seen through the flesh and bone and from beneath seventy garments, just as red wine is seen in a white glass.'"],[8828,"'Sudden death is a relief for the believer and a regret for the disbeliever.'"],[8829,"Indeed, the soul of the believer comes out as a sweat, and indeed the soul of the disbeliever comes out through the sides of his mouth like the breath of a donkey comes out."],[8830,"O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter, I ask You for the good of it and the good of what is in it, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it."],[8831,"ʿAbdullāh used to fast little. That was mentioned to him, so he said, “When I fast, I become too weak to recite, and reciting the Qur’an is more beloved to me.”"],[8832,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.” If he fasted, he fasted three days of the month."],[8833,"ʿAbdullāh used to fast little, so we said to him, “You fast little.” He said, “When I fast, I become too weak for prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.”"],[8834,"“Prayer is more beloved to me than fasting,” and he used not to pray the ḍuḥā (forenoon prayer)."],[8835,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting.”"],[8836,"I heard al-Shaʿbī say, “ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd used not to pray the ḍuḥā, and he would pray between ẓuhr and ʿaṣr along with a long portion of the night.”"],[8837,"The matter of those two days."],[8838,"…about prayer, and prayer is more beloved to me than fasting. If he fasted, he fasted three days of the month.”"],[8839,"I used to go to Ibn Masʿūd for a year, “and I never saw him fasting on any day at all except in Ramadan, and he used to drink strong nabīdh from a green jar.”"],[8840,"I used to go to Ibn Masʿūd for a year, “and I did not see him praying the ḍuḥā, nor did I see him fasting voluntarily except on the day of ʿĀshūrā’.”"],[8842,"We were with ʿAbd Allah when a drink was brought to him. He said, \"Pass it to the people.\" They said, \"We are fasting.\" He said, \"But I am not fasting.\" So he drank, then recited: {They fear a day in which the hearts and eyes will turn about}."],[8843,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud saying: \"The righteous depart one after another, and there remain people of doubt who do not recognize what is good and do not reject what is evil.\""],[8844,"\"Allah ﷻ divided good and made it into ten parts, placing nine parts in Syria and the remainder in the rest of the earth. And He divided evil and made it into ten parts, placing one part of it in Syria and the remainder in the rest of the earth.\""],[8845,"\"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. And death comes before meeting Allah.\""],[8846,"\"When one of you seeks a need, let him seek it privately; for he will only have what has been decreed for him. And let none of you go to his companion and praise him, thereby breaking his back.\""],[8847,"We were sitting with ʿAbd Allah when the people mentioned a man and spoke of his character. ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do you think that if you cut off his head you could restore it?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"His hand?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"His leg?\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"You will never be able to change his character until you change his physical creation. The drop of semen settles in the womb for forty nights, then descends as blood, then becomes a clot, then becomes a lump of flesh. Then the angel is sent to it and writes down its provision, its character, and whether it is wretched or blessed.\""],[8848,"The people said, \"Is there no one to restrain him?\" ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do you think that if his head were cut off you could make a head for him? Or if his hands were cut off you could make a hand for him? Or if his leg were cut off you could make a leg for him?\" They said, \"No.\" ʿAbd Allah said, \"When the drop of semen falls into the woman, it remains for forty days, then descends as blood, then becomes a clot, then becomes a lump of flesh like that. Then Allah sends the angel and says, 'Write down his term, his deeds, his provision, his effect, and whether he is wretched or blessed.' You will never be able to change his character until you change his physical creation.\""],[8849,"Indeed, your Lord—Exalted is He—has neither night nor day; the light of the heavens and the earth is from the light of His Face. And the measure of each day of your days with Him is twelve hours. So your deeds from yesterday are presented to Him at the beginning of today’s day, and He looks into them for three hours; then He sees in them what He dislikes, and that angers Him. The first to know of His غضب (wrath) are the Bearers of the Throne; they praise Him, and it weighs heavily upon them. Then the Bearers of the Throne, the curtains/canopies of the Throne, the angels brought near, and the rest of the angels glorify Him. Then Jibrīl ﷺ blows the horn, and nothing remains except that it hears its sound, and they glorify the Most Merciful—Exalted is He—for three hours, until the Most Merciful is filled with mercy; that makes six hours. Then the wombs are brought, and He looks into them for three hours. That is His saying in His Book: “He is the One who shapes you in the wombs however He wills,” and: “He grants to whom He wills females, and He grants to whom He wills males; or He couples them—males and females—and He makes whom He wills barren. Indeed, He is Knowing, Powerful.” That makes nine hours. Then provision is brought, and He looks into it for three hours—His saying in His Book: “He expands provision for whom He wills and restricts it,” and: “Every day He is upon a matter.” He said: This is from your affair and the affair of your Lord."],[8850,"ʿAbd Allah used to say: \"Servants are in a state of ease under Allah's ﷻ covering as long as they maintain worship and do not shed forbidden blood.\""],[8851,"I said to ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAziz, \"Ibn Masʿud used to say: 'There will be ambiguous matters. Whoever among those absent from them approves of them is like one who witnessed them, and whoever among those who witness them detests them is like one who was absent from them.'\" This pleased him."],[8852,"When ʿAbd Allah left his house he would say, \"In the name of Allah, I rely upon Allah. There is no power and no strength except with Allah.\" Muhammad b. Kaʿb al-Qurazi said: This is in the Quran: {Embark therein: in the name of Allah} and He said: Upon Allah we rely."],[8853,"ʿAbd Allah said, \"Do not swear by the swearing of Satan, that one of you says, 'By the might of Allah.' Rather, say as Allah said: Allah, Lord of might.\""],[8854,"\"If you were a hypocrite, you would not fear that.\""],[8855,"When Uqbah's death came to Abdullah, he wept. It was said to him: 'You weep?' He said: 'He was my brother in lineage and my companion with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Along with that, I would not love that I was before him — that he die and I seek reward for him is dearer to me than that I die and he seek reward for me.'"],[8856,"Ibn Mas'ud used to say: 'O Beginner with no beginning before You, O Everlasting with no end to You, O Living, Reviver of the dead, You are the One standing over every soul with what it has earned.'"],[8857,"Abdullah said: 'Whoever has a handsome appearance, is in a position that does not disgrace him, and is granted ample provision, then is humble — he is among the pure ones of Allah.'"],[8858,"O Allah, I ask You for the good of it and the good of its people, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people."],[8859,"against wrongdoing, and a man who recognized the truth with his heart."],[8860,"Ibn Mas'ud said: 'Guarantee for me intentional killing, and I will guarantee for you accidental killing.'"],[8861,"Abdullah passed by me while I was selling some of my goods and swearing about them. He began to raise my head with something in his hand and said: 'Do not swear, for an oath profits the goods but erases blessing.'"],[8862,"His Lord will meet with him privately just as one of you meets with the moon on the night of the full moon. He will say: 'Son of Adam, what deceived you concerning Me? Son of Adam, what deceived you concerning Me? Son of Adam, what did you answer the messengers? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you do with what you knew?'"],[8863,"By Allah, there is none among you except that Allah will meet with him privately on the Day of Resurrection just as one of you meets with the moon on the night of the full moon. He will say: 'What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What deceived you concerning Me, son of Adam? What did you do with what you knew? Son of Adam, what did you answer the messengers?'"],[8864,"He said: 'Enter.' We said: 'We will wait a little; perhaps some of the people of the house have a need.' He began to glorify Allah, then said: 'You thought the family of Abdullah to be heedless.' Then he said: 'O slave girl, see whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' Then he said to her a second time: 'See whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'No.' Then he said to her a third time: 'See whether the sun has risen.' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Praise be to Allah who granted us this day and pardoned our slips in it.' And I think he said: 'And did not punish us with the Fire.'"],[8865,"To swear by Allah falsely is dearer to me than to swear by other than Him truthfully."],[8866,"The height of Musa ﷺ was twelve cubits, his staff was twelve cubits, and his leap was twelve; he struck Uj ibn Unuq and struck nothing but his ankle."],[8867,"That he should come to him and greet him »"],[8868,"«The souls of the martyrs are inside green birds that roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, then they take shelter in lanterns hanging from the Throne»"],[8869,"«Whoever of you comes seeking a fatwa, let him sit until we give it to him. Whoever of you comes as a litigant, let him keep hold of his opponent until we judge between them. And whoever of you comes to inform us of a shameful act that God has concealed, let him conceal himself with God’s concealment and entrust it privately to the One who possesses its forgiveness, for we do not possess its forgiveness and would impose a legal penalty on him; and with their dung»"],[8870,"ʿAbd Allah was brought an udder, and a man withdrew, saying, “I have forbidden it.” ʿAbd Allah said: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things God has made lawful for you} Eat and offer expiation."],[8871,"ʿAbd Allah was brought an udder, and he began eating from it. He said to the people, “Come close.” The people came close, but a man among them withdrew. ʿAbd Allah said, «What is the matter with you?» He replied, “I have forbidden the udder.” He said, “This is from the steps of Satan. Come close, eat, and expiate your oath.” Then he recited: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things God has made lawful for you}"],[8872,"«Every trait a believer may be folded upon except treachery and lying»"],[8873,"“My brother is ill; he complains of his stomach, and wine has been prescribed for him. Should I give it to him to drink?” ʿAbd Allah said, “Glory be to God! God has not placed healing in filth. Healing is only in two things: honey is a healing for people, and the Qurʾan is a healing for what is in the chests.”"],[8874,"People set out early in two ways: a seller of his own soul, so he destroys it, and a redeemer of it, so he sets it free. Charity is a proof, fasting is a shield, prayer is a light, tranquility is a gain, and abandoning it is a loss."],[8875,"«Souls are troops that have been marshaled. Those among them that recognize one another come together, and those that reject one another differ»"],[8876,"«Indeed God supports the religion through the sinful man»"],[8877,"Women are only a private part. A woman goes out of her house while there is no harm in her, but Satan looks up at her and says, ‘You will not pass by anyone but that you please him.’ And a woman puts on her clothes and it is said, ‘Where do you intend to go?’ She says, ‘I am visiting a sick person, or attending a funeral, or praying in a mosque.’ No woman has worshiped her Lord like worshiping Him in her house."],[8878,"«When you are three on a journey, appoint one of you as your leader, and let no two of you converse privately apart from their companion»"],[8879,"Abd Allah [said]: \"That is Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq, the sacrifice of Allah, son of Ibrahim, the friend of Allah.\""],[8880,"I heard Abd Allah supplicate with this supplication: \"O Allah, I ask You by Your abundant blessing which You bestowed upon me, and by Your trial which You tested me with, and by Your grace which You granted me, that You admit me to Paradise. O Allah, admit me to Paradise by Your grace, Your favor, and Your mercy.\""],[8881,"Abd Allah recited: {Except him who has taken a covenant with the Most Merciful} (19:87). He said: Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'Whoever has a covenant with Me, let him stand.' They said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, teach us.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, I covenant with You in this worldly life that if You entrust me to myself, You bring me near evil and distance me from good. I trust only in Your mercy, so make it for me a covenant with You that You fulfill to me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break the promise.' He said: Zakariyya Abu Yahya added in it from al-Qasim: 'Fearful, seeking refuge, seeking forgiveness, desirous of You.'"],[8882,"\"Assess people by their close companions.\""],[8883,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud [said]: \"O people, a time has come upon us when we do not judge and we are not there. Indeed, Allah has brought us to what you see. So whoever of you is presented with a judgment after today, let him judge in it according to what is in the Book of Allah. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, let him judge in it according to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge in it, let him judge according to what the righteous judged. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not judge in it, and the righteous did not judge in it, let him exercise his judgment. Let none of you say: 'I fear' or 'I think.' Indeed, the lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are doubtful matters. So leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.\""],[8884,"Abd Allah [said]: \"If a matter confronts you that is unavoidable, look at what is in the Book of Allah and judge by it. If you are unable, then by what the Messenger ﷺ judged. If you are unable, then by what the righteous judged. If you are unable, then head toward it and do not be remiss. If you are unable, then acknowledge and do not be ashamed.\""],[8885,"\"Illness does not earn reward; reward is only for deeds, but Allah expiates sins by it.\""],[8886,"\"The one who gives legal verdicts to people in everything they ask him about is insane.\""],[8887,"Al-Hawdi said in his narration: \"in everything they ask him about.\""],[8888,"Abd Allah b. Mas'ud [said]: \"What an excellent assembly is the assembly in which wisdom spreads.\""],[8889,"That a man becomes poor in knowledge he once had, or remains among people who do not know.\""],[8890,"Abd Allah [said]: \"Sufficient as knowledge is fear of Allah, and sufficient as ignorance is being deceived regarding Allah.\""],[8891,"ʿAbd Allah: When a commander is appointed, he will have two inner circles from his own people: one inner circle that commands him to obey Allah, and one inner circle that commands him to disobey. He is with whichever of the two he obeys."],[8892,"ʿAbd Allah: Do not hasten to praise people or to blame them. For perhaps you see something from your brother today that pleases you, and perhaps it will displease you tomorrow. And perhaps you see something from him today that displeases you, and perhaps it will please you tomorrow. People find fault, but Allah alone forgives sins on the Day of Resurrection. Allah is more merciful to His servant on the day he meets Him than a mother who spread out for him on the ground, then touched him: if there was a thorn, she would be struck by it before him; and if there was a sting, she would be struck by it before him."],[8893,"ʿAbd Allah: I think that a man does not forget knowledge that he once knew except because of a sin that he commits."],[8894,"ʿAbd Allah: Let none of you say: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from tribulation,' for there is none among you who is not surrounded by tribulation. But whoever seeks refuge, let him seek refuge from its difficult entanglements. For Allah, may He be exalted, says: 'Your wealth and your children are but a trial' [Q 64:15]."],[8895,"ʿAbd Allah: Let none of you say: 'I am a sarurah.' For a Muslim is not a sarurah. And let none of you say: 'I am a hajj performer,' for the hajj performer is the one in ihram. But let him say: 'I intend to go to Makkah.'"],[8896,"There is no prescribed punishment except for two: a man who is disowned from his father, or who slanders a chaste woman."],[8898,"ʿAbd Allah: There is no prescribed punishment except for two: that he slanders a chaste woman, or a man is disowned from his father."],[8900,"ʿAbd Allah: Repentance is offered to the son of Adam as long as one of three things has not occurred: as long as the sun has not risen from its west, or the beast has not emerged, or Yaʾjuj and Maʾjuj have not come out."],[8901,"It was said to ʿAbd Allah: 'Allah the Exalted mentions prayer often in the Qurʾān: \"Those who are constant in their prayer\" [Q 70:23], \"And those who are mindful of their prayer\" [Q 70:34].' ʿAbd Allah said: 'That refers to its proper times.' They said: 'O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, we thought it meant abandoning it.' ʿAbd Allah said: 'Abandoning it is disbelief.'"],[8902,"Whoever abandons prayer has disbelieved."],[8903,"It was said to ʿAbd Allah: 'Allah the Exalted mentions prayer often: \"Those who are constant in their prayer\" [Q 70:23], \"And those who are mindful of their prayer\" [Q 70:34].' ʿAbd Allah said: 'That refers to its prescribed times.' We said: 'We thought it meant abandoning it.' He said: 'Abandoning it is disbelief.'"],[8904,"Whoever does not pray has no religion."],[8905,"“Whoever does not pray has no religion.”"],[8906,"That ʿAbd Allah went out for the dawn prayer after some people had leaned their backs against the qiblah side of the mosque, and he said: “Move back like this from the faces of the angels.”"],[8907,"That he saw some people leaning their backs against the qiblah between the dawn call to prayer and the iqamah, and he said: “Do not come between the angels and their prayer.”"],[8908,"Abdullah came at dawn and found a group of people with their backs facing the qibla. He said, \"Delay your prayers to avoid standing between the angels and the qibla, for it is the prayer of the angels.\""],[8910,"“As much as you are able to, O servants of Allah.”"],[8911,"ʿAbd Allah: “The two months are fifty-nine days.”"],[8912,"ʿAbd Allah arrived after Saʿd had built the palace and had made a mosque among the date-palm growers; he used to go out to it for the prayers. When ʿAbd Allah was put in charge of the treasury, someone made a breach in the treasury and the man was caught. ʿAbd Allah wrote to ʿUmar, and ʿUmar wrote back: “Do not cut off his hand, but move the mosque and put the treasury on the side facing the qiblah, for there is always someone in the mosque praying.” So ʿAbd Allah moved it and drew this plan. The palace that Saʿd had built was a shadhara, and when the imam stood upon it, ʿAbd Allah ordered it demolished until the imam’s standing place was level with the people."],[8913,"That ʿAbd Allah lent some money to maternal uncles of his from Banu Saʿd. When their stipends were distributed, they chose for him their property, and when it was brought to him, ʿAbd Allah said: “This is better than our money that we gave you, so gather your stipends and give us from its goods.”"],[8914,"ʿAbd Allah: “By the One besides whom there is no god, Allah apportioned this fayʾ upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ before Persia and Rome were conquered.”"],[8915,"ʿAbd Allah: “Four things have been finished: creation, character, provision, and the appointed term.”"],[8916,"Four things have been finished: creation, character, provision, and the appointed term. None of us can earn anything on behalf of another."],[8917,"ʿAbd Allah had a Christian scribe. ʿAbd Allah entered the palace and the Christian returned, so ʿAbd Allah followed him with the greeting of salam."],[8918,"Some people from among the polytheists walked with ʿAbd Allāh, and when he reached the gate of the palace he greeted them."],[8919,"ʿUmar (?) said: I passed by one of the mosques of Banū Ḥanīfah and heard them reciting something God had not sent down: the grinders grinding, the kneaders kneading, the bakers baking, the morsel-eaters eating morsels. He said: So Ibn Masʿūd put Ibn al-Nawwāḥah forward as their leader and killed him, and found the rest to be many, and said: “I will not slaughter them today for the devil. Send them to Syria so that God may grant them repentance or the plague may destroy them.”"],[8920,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Were it not that you are a messenger, I would strike your neck.” So today you are not a messenger. Then he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb, and he struck his neck in the market. Then he said: “Whoever wants to look at Ibn al-Nawwāḥah killed in the market.”"],[8921,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"If it were not for the fact that you are a messenger, I would have killed you.\" As for today, O Harashah, you are not a messenger. Stand up and strike his neck. So he got up and struck his neck."],[8922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn al-Nawwaha, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Do you bear witness that Musaylimah is the Messenger of Allah?\" The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"If it was not for the fact that you are a messenger, I would have killed you.\""],[8923,"ʿAbd Allāh was approached and it was said to him: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, there are people here reciting the recitation of Musaylimah. ʿAbd Allāh sent him back, and he stayed as long as God willed him to stay. Then he came to him and said: By the One by whom I swear, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I have left them now in a house, and that muṣḥaf is indeed with them. So he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb, and he set out with the people with him, and said: “Bring them.” When they were brought, ʿAbd Allāh said: “What is this after the spread of Islam?” They said: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, we ask God's forgiveness and repent to Him, and we bear witness that Musaylimah is the liar who fabricated against God and His Messenger. He said: So ʿAbd Allāh asked them to repent and sent them to Syria, and they were nearly eighty men. Ibn al-Nawwāḥah refused to repent, so he ordered Qaraẓah b. Kaʿb concerning him, and he took him out to the market and struck his neck, and ordered him to take his head and throw it into his mother's lap. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh said: I met an old man among them later in Syria, and he said: May God have mercy on your father. By God, if he had killed us that day, we would all have entered the Fire."],[8924,"The first to spread the Quran among the companions of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was Abdullah ibn Masood. The first to build a mosque for prayer was Ammar ibn Yasir. The first to give the call to prayer was Bilal. The first to ride his horse in the way of Allah was Al-Miqdad ibn Al-Aswad. The first Muslim to throw a spear in the way of Allah was Saad. The first Muslim to be martyred on the day of Badr was Mahja, the servant of Umar ibn Khattab. The first group of people who pledged allegiance to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were the people of Juhayna. And the first to give voluntary charity from their own selves were the sons of Uthra ibn Saad."],[8925,"I stood next to Abdullah during the afternoon or evening, and I heard him reciting."],[8926,"\"It is as if I am looking at him while he is prostrating and he leaned on his elbows, to the point that I almost saw the whiteness of his armpits.\""],[8927,"I entered the mosque and said: I will pray at every pillar. Then I came to ʿAbd Allāh while he was sitting and his companions were with him, and they were talking about me (?). He said: “If he knew that his Lord is at the first pillar, he would not leave it until he finished his prayer.”"],[8928,"That God ﷻ is at the nearest pillar, he would not pass it until he finished his prayer.”"],[8929,"“If I were to tread on a live coal, it would be dearer to me than to tread on the grave of a Muslim.”"],[8930,"“The wedding feast on the first day is a duty, on the second is a virtue, and on the third is showing off and reputation. Whoever seeks to be heard, God will make him heard.”"],[8931,"There was an argument between a man from among the companions of ʿAbd Allāh and his wife. She said: Your food and the food of your family is nothing but from the milk of my ewe. So he swore that he would not eat anything from its milk. Then a guest came to them, and she prepared food for him with the milk of her ewe. The man said: You know that I do not eat it. The woman said: By God, if you do not eat, I will not eat. The guest said: By God, if you two do not eat, I will not eat. So they spent the night without dinner. The talk reached ʿAbd Allāh, and the man came to ʿAbd Allāh. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “What came between you and your family?” He said: There was no divorce, no ẓihār, and no īlāʾ. Then he told him the story. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “I adjure you, when you return to your family, that the first thing you do is eat from the milk of this ewe. And I think it would be better for yourself to expiate for your oath.”"],[8932,"I heard Abdullah bin Mas'ood saying, \"Indeed, Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for death.\""],[8933,"“Then adhere to the community of the people.”"],[8934,"“O people, fear God, and you must adhere to obedience and the community, for they are the rope of God which He commanded. What you dislike in obedience and the community is better than what you love in division. God did not create anything of this world but that He made for it an end point at which it stops, and then it decreases until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, the bonds of Islam have been established, and it is about to decrease and retreat until the Day of Resurrection. The sign of that is that you sever your ties of kinship, and that poverty becomes widespread, so that the rich fears nothing but poverty, and the poor finds no one who shows compassion to him, and the beggar stands between the two Friday prayers and nothing falls into his hand. While the people are like that, the earth will low a lowing like the lowing of a cow; every people will think that it lowed from their courtyard. Then there will be a return, and it will low a second time with pieces of its liver.” It was said to him: And what are pieces of its liver? He said: “Like these pillars, of gold and silver. From that day gold and silver will not benefit until the Day of Resurrection, and he will find no one to accept the charity of his wealth.”"],[8935,"He said: “O people, upon you is obedience and the community, for they are the rope of Allah which He commanded. Indeed, what you dislike in obedience and the community is better than what you love in division. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has not created a thing except that He made for it a limit at which it stops. Indeed, Islam has advanced and has stability. It is about to reach its limit, then it will recede and decrease until the Day of Resurrection. The sign of that is that poverty will increase, ties of kinship will be severed so that the poor will not find anyone to return to him, until the rich will think that what he has is not enough for him, and until a man will complain to his brother and his cousin and they will not give him anything, and until the beggar will walk between the two Fridays with nothing placed in his hand. Then, when that happens, the earth will bellow a bellowing: the people of every tract will think that it bellowed in their tract. Then it will calm upon them as long as Allah wills. Then the earth will surprise them vomiting the pieces of its liver.” It was said: “O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, what are the pieces of its liver?” He said: “Pillars of gold and silver. From that day, neither gold nor silver will be of benefit until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8936,"“Adhere to this community, for it is the rope of Allah which He commanded. Indeed, what you dislike in the community is better than what you love in division. Indeed, Allah has never created a thing except that He made for it an end. Indeed, this religion has been completed, and it is going to decrease. The sign of that is that kinship ties will be severed, wealth will be taken without its right, blood will be shed, a relative will complain to his relatives and they will not give him anything, and the beggar will go around between the two Fridays with nothing placed in his hand. While they are like that, the earth will bellow like the bellowing of a cow, then it will throw out the pieces of its liver. After that, neither gold nor silver will be of benefit.”"],[8937,"“Whoever establishes the prayer but does not give zakah, there is no prayer for him.”"],[8938,"ʿAbd Allah entered upon him while he had set up goods in his house. ʿAbd Allah said: “Conceal the furnishings of your house, for the people are about to be people of the pack-saddle.”"],[8939,"Abdullah said, \"Indeed, a believer is amiable, and there is no good in someone who is not amiable and is not befriended.\""],[8940,"ʿAbd Allah used to seek refuge from four things, saying: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that makes me tyrannical, from poverty that makes me forget, from desire that destroys me, and from deeds that grieve me.”"],[8941,"ʿAbd Allah used to say: “Beware of the difficult modes of speech.”"],[8942,"ʿAbd Allah said to his companions when they came to him: “Do you sit together?” They said: “We do not abandon that.” He said: “Do you visit one another?” They said: “Yes, O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman. Indeed, a man among us misses his brother, so he walks seeking him to the farthest end of Kufa until he meets him.” He said: “You will remain in good as long as you do that.”"],[8943,"“Do not eat from cheese except what the Muslims and the People of the Book have made.”"],[8944,"“When ʿAbd Allah stood in prayer, he lowered his voice, his hand, and his gaze.”"],[8945,"ʿAbd Allah did not give a sermon in Kufa except that I attended it. I heard him one day when he was asked about a man who divorces eight times and similar things. He said: “It is as it is said.” Then he said: “Indeed, Allah ﷻ sent down His Book and clarified its clarification. Whoever comes to the matter from its proper direction, it is clarified for him. Whoever opposes, then by Allah, we cannot endure all your opposition.”"],[8946,"And he said: “Fasting three days of every month.”"],[8947,"“Fasting three days of every month removes the rancor of the chest.”"],[8948,"Abdullah used to say after the rukuʿ: “O Allah, to You belongs all praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever else You will. O You worthy of praise and glory. There is none to withhold what You give and none to give what You withhold, and no possessor of riches can benefit from You his riches.”"],[8949,"“The distance between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years.”"],[8950,"That he said: “Between the lowest heaven and the one above it is a journey of five hundred years, and between each heaven is a journey of five hundred years, and between the seventh heaven and the Footstool (Kursi) is a journey of five hundred years, and between the Footstool and the water is a journey of five hundred years, and the Throne is above the water, and Allah ﷻ is above the Throne, and He knows what you are upon.”"],[8951,"The sun rises from the depths of hell between two devil horns, and it does not rise in the sky as a cinder unless a gate from the gates of fire is opened. When the heat intensifies, all of its gates are opened."],[8952,"Abdullah saw a man with some dirhams and said: “What will you do with them?” He replied: “I will buy some clarified butter with them.” He said: “Give them to your wife to place under her mattress, then buy meat with a dirham every day.”"],[8953,"“Indeed Allah ﷻ has distributed your characters among you just as He has distributed your provisions among you. And indeed Allah gives wealth to those He loves and those He does not love, but He does not give faith except to those He loves. So if Allah loves a servant, He grants him faith. So whoever is not guaranteed to spend his wealth, and fears the enemy to fight him, and fears the night to endure it, let him increase in saying: There is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah.”"],[8954,"Abdullah said: “Do you know how Islam diminishes?” They said: “As the dye of a garment fades, as a mount loses weight, and as a dirham becomes worn from long use.” He said: “That is part of it, but more than that is the death or departure of the scholars.”"],[8955,"The Bridge (Sirat) will be placed across the surface of Hell, like the edge of a sharpened sword, slippery and treacherous. Upon it will be hooks of fire by which people will be snatched. Some will be held back and fall into it, and some will be thrown down. Among them are those who will pass like lightning and will not be caught, and that one will be saved. Then like the wind and will not be caught, and that one will be saved. Then like the galloping of a horse, then like the running of a man, then like the quick walking of a man, then like the walking of a man, until the last of them will be a man whom the Fire has scorched and has met with evil in it, until Allah admits him to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy. Then it will be said to him: ‘Wish and ask.’ He will say: ‘O Lord, are You mocking me while You are the Lord of Might?’ Then it will be said to him: ‘Wish and ask.’ He said: Until when his wishes are exhausted, He will say: ‘You shall have what you asked for and the like of it along with it.’ He said: And Abu Salih narrated to me from Abu Hurayrah who said: ‘And ten times the like of it along with it.’”"],[8956,"A man from Bajilah came to Abdullah and said: “I have married a virgin slave girl, and I fear that she may dislike me.” Abdullah said: “Indeed affection is from Allah, and dislike is from Satan, so that he may make hateful to him what Allah has made lawful for him. So when you enter upon her, tell her to pray two rakʿahs behind you.” Al-Aʿmash said: I mentioned this to Ibrahim, and he said: Abdullah said: “And say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me. O Allah, provide me from them and provide them from me. O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in good, and separate us when You separate us to good.”"],[8957,"“I have married a woman and I fear dislike.” He said: “When you bring her, pray two rakʿahs and say: O Allah, bless me in my family and bless them in me. O Allah, join us together as long as You join us in good, and separate us when You separate us to good.”"],[8958,"That he says: “Indeed Allah has commanded such and such and forbidden such and such,” and Allah ﷻ will say to him: “You have lied,” or he says: “Indeed Allah has forbidden such and such and made lawful such and such,” and Allah will say to him: “You have lied.”"],[8959,"“The example of one who persists in prayer is like one who knocks at a door. Whoever persists in knocking at the door, it is likely to be opened for him.”"],[8960,"Abdullah said: “As long as you are in prayer, you are knocking at the door of the King. Whoever knocks often at the door of the King, it is likely to be opened for him.”"],[8961,"\"The virtue of night prayer over day prayer is like the virtue of secret charity over public charity.\""],[8962,"ʿAbdullah: \"The virtue of night prayer over day prayer is like the virtue of secret charity over public charity.\""],[8963,"ʿAbdullah: \"The master of months is Ramadan, and the master of days is Friday.\""],[8964,"ʿAbdullah recited this verse: {On the day the earth will be changed to a different earth, and the heavens, and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Subduer.} He said: \"An earth will be brought like an ingot of silver, on which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed. The first matter judged among people on it will be regarding blood.\""],[8965,"\"Al-awwāh means the merciful.\""],[8966,"On the authority of ʿAbdullah regarding His saying: {Indeed Abraham was compassionate (awwāh), forbearing.} He said: \"Al-awwāh means the merciful.\""],[8967,"\"It means the one who supplicates much.\""],[8968,"\"O Abu Abdurrahman, what is lamentation?\" said Ar-Raheem. He replied, \"What is extravagant?\" He said, \"What is wasteful expenditure.\" He then asked, \"What is aid?\" He replied, \"What do people cooperate with each other in, meaning the difficulties.\""],[8969,"\"Spending wealth in an unlawful way,\" and he asked him about al-awwāh; he said: \"The merciful.\""],[8970,"To ʿAbdullah: \"Whom should we ask if we do not ask you?\" So ʿAbdullah felt compassion for him and said: \"What is al-awwāh?\" He said: \"The merciful.\" He said: \"What is al-ummah?\" He said: \"The one who knows good.\" He said: \"What is al-qānit?\" He said: \"The obedient.\" He said: \"What is al-māʿūn?\" He said: \"What people share among themselves.\" He said: \"What is al-tabdhīr?\" He said: \"Spending wealth in something other than its rightful due.\""],[8971,"\"Spending in something other than what is right.\""],[8972,"\"It is spending in something other than what is right.\""],[8973,"We, the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, used to say that al-māʿūn is the bucket, the cooking pot, and the axe, which are indispensable to them."],[8974,"In his saying, \"Al-Ma'un\", he said: \"the axe, the pot, and the bucket.\""],[8975,"Regarding His saying {and withhold the small kindnesses}, he said: \"It is wealth whose right is not given.\" I said: \"Ibn Masʿūd says: 'It is the good things people exchange among themselves.'\" He said: \"That is what I am telling you.\""],[8976,"\"Every good deed is charity. At the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to consider the small kindness to be lending the bucket and the cooking pot and the like of that.\""],[8977,"\"We used to consider the small kindness to be the axe, the cooking pot, and the bucket.\""],[8978,"Regarding His saying {Indeed the hypocrites are in the lowest depths of the Fire}, he said: \"Coffins of iron that close over them.\""],[8979,"Regarding His saying {a dwelling place and a repository}, he said: \"The dwelling is the womb and the repository is the earth in which one dies.\""],[8980,"ʿAbdullāh said: \"Its repository is in this world and its dwelling is in the womb.\""],[8981,"In his statement, \"and from the cattle as pack animals and bedding,\" he said, \"The pack animals are what are carried by camels, and the bedding refers to the young ones.\""],[8982,"In his saying, \"Do they wait except for the angels to come to them, or for your Lord to come, or for some signs of your Lord to come on the day when some signs of your Lord come? On that day, belief will not benefit a soul that did not believe before.\" He said, \"The rising of the sun with the moon from its setting place is like the meeting of two companions.\""],[8983,"In His statement {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord will come, no soul's faith will benefit it}, He said, \"The rising of the sun from its west.\""],[8984,"\"Spending on what is not its right.\""],[8985,"Regarding His saying {then there is no sin upon them if they lay aside their garments, not displaying adornment}, he said: \"The outer garment.\""],[8986,"About this verse: {And do not think those who have been killed in the way of Allah} up to {they are provided for}, he said: \"The souls of the martyrs are with Allah ﷻ like green birds with lanterns hanging from the Throne, roaming in Paradise wherever they wish.\" He said: Then your Lord looked over them and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Our Lord, are we not roaming in Paradise wherever we wish?\" He said: Then He looked over them a second time and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Our Lord, are we not roaming in Paradise wherever we wish?\" Then He looked over them a third time and asked: \"Do you desire anything that I might increase you?\" They said: \"Restore our souls to our bodies so that we may fight in Your way and be killed once again.\" He said: \"So He fell silent regarding them.\""],[8989,"Regarding His saying {its fuel is people and stones}, he said: \"Stones of sulfur that Allah ﷻ keeps with Himself however He wills and as He wills.\""],[8990,"Regarding His saying {and say 'ḥiṭṭah'}, he said: They said 'ḥinṭah,' a red grain with a hair-like awn in it. That is His saying {But those who wronged changed the saying to other than what was said to them}."],[8991,"Regarding His saying {But whoever hastens on in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, then there is no sin upon him}, he said: \"He is forgiven.\""],[8992,"These verses were sent down from the end of al-Baqarah: {The Messenger believes} from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[8993,"The verse after it abrogated it: {To it belongs what it earns, and upon it is what it acquires}."],[8994,"Indeed this path is attended; devils attend it, saying: 'O servants of God, this is the way, so hold fast to the rope of God, for the straight path is the Book of God.'"],[8995,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying {And hold fast to the rope of God all together}: ʿAbdullāh said, 'The Qurʾan.'"],[8996,"'The rope of God ﷻ is the congregation.'"],[8997,"In his statement, \"Those who remember Allah while standing, sitting, and lying on their sides,\" he said, \"If you are unable to pray standing, then sitting, and if not, then lying down.\""],[8998,"ʿAbdullāh said: In the Book of God there are two verses; no servant commits a sin then recites them and seeks God's forgiveness except that God forgives him: {And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember God and seek forgiveness for their sins—and who forgives sins except God?} and His saying {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself, then seeks God's forgiveness, will find God Forgiving, Merciful}."],[8999,"From ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd regarding His saying {And married women, except what your right hands possess}: ʿAlī said, 'The polytheist women, when they are taken captive, become lawful for him.' Ibn Masʿūd said, 'The polytheist women and the Muslim women.'"],[9000,"In his saying \"And the one on his side\" he said, \"The woman.\""],[9001,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying {And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment}: he said, 'The day of Badr,' and {the greater punishment, that they might return}: he said, 'Those of them who remain, that they might repent and return.'"],[9002,"Indeed it is written in the Torah for those whose sides forsake their beds: what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has conceived; and indeed it is in the Qurʾan: {No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for the eyes}."],[9003,"'Indeed the dung beetle is tormented in its burrow because of the sins of the children of Adam.' Then he recited: {If God were to take people to task for what they have earned, He would not leave upon its back any creature}."],[9004,"In His saying, \"And the angels lined up in rows\" He said, \"The angels.\" In His saying, \"And those who drive away with a firm command\" He said, \"The angels.\" In His saying, \"And those who recite the remembrance\" He said, \"The angels.\" He said, \"The angels.\""],[9005,"\"Indeed, in the seven heavens, there is not a single space the width of a handspan except that it has an angel's forehead or feet standing [in worship]. Then, He recited, 'Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an and indeed, We will be its guardian.'\""],[9006,"That he said: {Entrust her to me}."],[9007,"Regarding His saying {Our Lord, You have caused us to die twice and given us life twice}: he said, 'It is like the one in al-Baqarah: {You were dead, then He gave you life, then He will cause you to die, then He will give you life, then to Him you will be returned}.'"],[9009,"We were sitting in the mosque when a man entered narrating to us: He said, “On the Day of Resurrection a smoke will come and seize the hearing of the hypocrites, and it will seize the believers like a cold.” So we entered upon ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd and narrated it to him while he was reclining. He sat up and said, “O people, whoever knows something, let him speak it; and whoever does not know, let him say, ‘Allāh knows best,’ for it is part of a man’s knowledge to say about what he does not know, ‘Allāh knows best.’ Allāh said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of those who pretend} (38:86). I shall narrate to you about the smoke: when Quraysh became obstinate and delayed in accepting Islam, the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ supplicated against them, saying, ‘O Allāh, help me against them with seven years like the seven years of Yūsuf.’ Then a famine struck them until everything was destroyed, until they ate carrion and bones, until a man would see between him and the sky something like smoke. That is His saying: {So watch for the Day when the sky will bring a visible smoke, covering the people; this is a painful punishment. Our Lord, remove from us the punishment; indeed we are believers} (44:10–12). It was removed from them, but they returned to their disbelief, so He seized them on the Day of Badr. That is His saying: {The Day We shall seize with the greatest seizure; indeed We shall take retribution} (44:16). He said, ‘The greatest seizure is the Day of Badr.’”"],[9012,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd [said]: “Five have passed: the smoke, the moon, the Byzantines, the seizure, and the unavoidable punishment.”"],[9013,"Regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “That is Jibrīl ﷺ in a green silk robe that filled what is between the heaven and the earth.”"],[9014,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He saw a green silk canopy that blocked the horizon.”"],[9015,"Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, they said: Shuʿbah informed us, from Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He saw a green silk canopy that blocked the horizon of the sky.”"],[9016,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “A green silk canopy from Paradise that blocked the horizon.”"],[9017,"In his saying, \"{Indeed, he (Muhammad) saw of the greatest signs of his Lord],\" he said, \"Muhammad ﷺ saw Gabriel in his true form, with six hundred wings, and not one wing but it filled the space between the east and the west.\""],[9018,"From ʿAbd Allāh regarding His saying: {He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest} (53:18), he said, “He has six hundred wings.”"],[9019,"In his statement \"{§By the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary}\" he said, \"The reward of Paradise includes palaces of silk and brocade.\""],[9020,"“A righteous dream is one of seventy parts of prophethood. The poisonous wind from which the jinn were created is one of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam. This fire of yours is one of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam.”"],[9021,"“Coral is the red bead.”"],[9022,"From ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd regarding His saying: {O you who believe, do not take as allies a people with whom Allāh is angry; they have despaired of the Hereafter} (60:13): “They do not believe in it and will not be rewarded. This is the disbeliever when he dies and sees his reward and looks upon it.”"],[9023,"Regarding this verse: {And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his own soul — it is those who will be successful} (59:9). “I am a man who has not been able to prevent anything from coming out of me, and I feared that this verse might have afflicted me.” ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd said, “You have mentioned miserliness, and what an evil thing miserliness is. As for what Allāh mentioned, it is not as you said. That is when you deliberately take the wealth of another or the wealth of your brother and consume it.”"],[9024,"In his statement \"حُسُومًا,\" he said \"مُتَتَابِعَاتٌ.\""],[9025,"Regarding His saying: {Its seal is musk} (83:26), he said, “It is not a seal with which it is sealed, but rather its mixture is musk. Have you not seen a woman among your women say, ‘Its mixture is of such-and-such perfume’?”"],[9026,"From ʿAbd Allah [regarding] {the receding stars, the running [stars]} (Q 81:15–16): “What are they, O ʿAmr?” He said: I said, “Cattle.” He said, “And that is what I think.”"],[9027,"From ʿAbd Allah [regarding] {And recite to them the story of him to whom We gave Our signs} (Q 7:175): “He is Balʿam, and it is also said Balʿām.”"],[9028,"“The sky.”"],[9029,"I said, “As for the reward, we have come to know it. So what is the ghanīmah?” He said, “Forty dirhams from every person.”"],[9030,"ʿAbd Allah: “Indeed, before the Hour there will be the harj.” Abu al-Aḥwaṣ said: al-harj is killing."],[9031,"“The price for which Yūsuf was bought was twenty dirhams. And his family, when he sent for them while they were in Egypt, were ninety-three people: their men were prophets and their women were ṣiddīqāt. By God, they did not leave with Mūsā until they numbered six hundred and seventy thousand.”"],[9032,"ʿAbd Allah: “Indeed, among the women there are five verses [or signs] for which I would not trade the world and all it contains. And I have come to know that when the scholars come across them, they recognize them: {If you avoid the major sins that you are forbidden, We will expiate your evil deeds and admit you to a noble entrance} (Q 4:31); and His saying {Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] the weight of an atom; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward} (Q 4:40); and {Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners should be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills} (Q 4:48); and {If only they had, when they wronged themselves, come to you and asked Allah’s forgiveness, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Accepting of repentance, Merciful} (Q 4:64); and {Whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks Allah’s forgiveness will find Allah Forgiving, Merciful} (Q 4:110).”"],[9033,"Abdullah replied, \"Indeed, in the Qur'an there are two verses that if a servant commits a sin and then recites them and seeks forgiveness from Allah, he will be forgiven.\" They asked him about these verses, but he did not inform them. Alqamah and Al-Aswad said to each other, \"Let us go with him.\" So they went to the house, took the Mushaf (book), and started reciting Surah Al-Baqarah. They said, \"We did not see them.\" Then they continued reciting until they reached the verse, \"And whoever does evil or wrongs himself but then seeks forgiveness from Allah, he will find Allah forgiving and merciful.\" They said, \"This is one.\" Then they continued reciting Surah Al-Imran until they reached the verse, \"And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins - and who can forgive sins except Allah? And [who] do not persist in what they have done while they know.\" They said, \"This is the other.\" Then they closed the book and went to Abdullah and asked, \"Are these the two verses?\" He replied, \"Yes.\""],[9034,"ʿAbd Allah: “A man will continue to be in spaciousness in his religion as long as he does not shed unlawful blood. When he sheds unlawful blood, modesty is stripped from him.”"],[9035,"In His saying \"upon yourselves be it\" He ﷻ said, \"This is not the time for it, so say it if it is accepted from you. But if it is rejected from you, then it is upon yourselves. It will not harm you if someone goes astray.\""],[9036,"In his saying {On the day of Furqan, the day the two groups met}, he said, \"It was on the seventeenth night of Ramadan.\""],[9037,"Seek the night of Al-Qadr in the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first nights of Ramadan, during the pre-dawn of the day of Badr, the day of the great distinction, the day the two groups met. It cannot occur except in an odd-numbered night."],[9038,"ʿAbd Allah: “Test the hypocrites by three things: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he makes a covenant he betrays it. And Allah sent down confirmation of that in His Book: {And among them are those who made a covenant with Allah: if He gives us from His bounty} (Q 9:75) to the end of the verse.”"],[9039,"“The Qur’an and honey are two cures.”"],[9040,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {Those whom they call upon seek the means of nearness to their Lord} (Q 17:57): “There were people who used to worship them. Then those who had been worshipping them accepted Islam, while those who had been worshipped did not know. So Allah ﷻ rebuked them for that,” and he said: {Those whom they call upon seek the means of nearness to their Lord} (Q 17:57)."],[9041,"In His saying \"And whoever desires other than Islam as a religion - never will it be accepted from him, and he, in the Hereafter, will be among the losers\" (Quran 3:85), Allah warns against deviation and wrongdoing. He declares that those who plan or intend to commit a sin, but have not executed it, will not be held accountable until they actually commit the sin. Likewise, those who plan or intend to commit a sin and execute it only in private will not be punished by death until they are given a taste of painful punishment by Allah."],[9042,"\"Allah [God] ﷻ [may He be exalted] [has created] men [who are] not distracted by trade or selling [from] the remembrance of Allah.\""],[9043,"“Allah sends the wind, and it carries the water, and a cloud passes and lets it down as a milch camel lets down its milk, then it rains.”"],[9044,"“I do not analogize anything with anything. No foot slips after it has been firmly planted.”"],[9045,"From Salama b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak, that ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud ؓ melted silver from the public treasury, then sent word to the people of the mosque and said: “Whoever wants to look at molten metal, let him look at this.”"],[9046,"He entered the public treasury and called for the scraps that were in it. He lit a fire under them until they melted, then said: “Where is the one asking about al-muhl (molten metal)? This is al-muhl.”"],[9047,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding {And there is none of you but will pass over it}: “Passing over it means the sirat (bridge).”"],[9048,"That Marwan said regarding {And We gave him his family and the like of them with them}: “He received a family other than his own.” Ibn Masʿud said: “Rather, he received his own family themselves and the like of them with them.”"],[9049,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding {And Dhū al-Nūn, when he went away in anger}: “He was a slave who fled from his master.”"],[9050,"When those who will remain in the Fire forever are left, they will be placed in coffins of Fire containing nails of Fire. He said that two or three times. They will see no one in the Fire being punished besides them. Then ʿAbd Allah recited: {For them therein is sighing, and they therein will not hear.}"],[9051,"“They are the akhtān (sons-in-law / in-laws).”"],[9052,"“Al-hafada are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[9053,"“They are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[9054,"ʿAbd Allah said to me: “Do you know what hafada are?” I said, “Yes, they are a man’s helpers from his children and his children’s children.” He said, “No, they are the aṣhār (in-laws).”"],[9055,"I used to hold the mushaf for ʿAbd Allah. When he came to this verse: {And He has made for you from your spouses sons and hafada}, ʿAbd Allah said to me: “Do you know what al-hafada are?” I said, “A man’s servants.” He said, “No, they are the akhtān (in-laws).”"],[9056,"In his saying \"{He had sons and daughters},\" he said \"The sisters are the daughters of the paternal uncle.\""],[9057,"God ﷻ indeed supports the religion with the wicked man."],[9058,"{The devouts}[Quran 9:112] – “the fasting ones.”"],[9059,"From ʿAbdullah regarding {And how many a prophet there was with whom fought many devoted men}[Quran 3:146]. He said, “Thousands.”"],[9060,"“The path of good and evil.”"],[9061,"\"That disbelief.\""],[9062,"“The unlawful is bribery in religion.”"],[9063,"“Bribery in judgment is disbelief, and among the people it is unlawful.”"],[9064,"“That is disbelief.”"],[9065,"From ʿAbdullah regarding their saying {Our Lord, whoever brought this upon us, increase for him a double punishment in the Fire}[Quran 38:61]. He said, “Vipers and snakes.”"],[9066,"In his saying \"{زِدْنَاهُمْ عَذَابًا فَوْقَ الْعَذَابِ}\", he said, \"Increase their punishment with the extension of their fangs, like the long palm tree.\""],[9067,"Regarding His saying {We increased them with punishment over punishment}[Quran 16:88]. He said, “Scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees.”"],[9069,"Regarding the saying of the Blessed and Exalted {Then they will meet deviation}[Quran 19:59]. He said, “A valley in Hell.”"],[9070,"“A river in Hell.”"],[9071,"“Al-Ghayy is a river in Hell into which those who followed lusts are thrown.”"],[9072,"A valley in Jahannam of pus."],[9073,"A river in Jahannam and a valley in Jahannam."],[9074,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they will soon meet ghayyā}: \"A valley in Jahannam, deep-bottomed, foul in food.\""],[9075,"It is a river in the Fire; it has a ghayy."],[9076,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they will soon meet ghayyā}: \"A river in Jahannam called Ghayy.\""],[9077,"Wayl is a valley in Jahannam of pus."],[9078,"From ʿAbd Allah: {and not to display their adornment except what is apparent of it}—he said: \"Clothing.\""],[9079,"From ʿAbd Allah: {and not to display their adornment except what is apparent of it}—he said: \"Adornment is the earring, the armlet, the anklet, and the necklace.\""],[9080,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {and not to display their adornment}: \"Adornment is the bracelet, the armlet, the anklet, the ring, the earring, and the necklace; and what is apparent of it is clothing and the outer wrap.\""],[9081,"From ʿAbd Allah: {they put their hands into their mouths}—he said: \"They bit them.\""],[9082,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {they put their hands into their mouths}: \"They bit their fingers in rage.\""],[9083,"From Abdullah with regards to his statement \"And there is none of you except that he will come to it,\" he said, \"The path.\""],[9084,"From ʿAbd Allah, regarding His saying {the Fire will scorch their faces while they are grimacing therein}: \"Have you not seen the heads, singed, with their teeth showing and their lips shriveled?\""],[9085,"About this verse: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “He will be collared with a bald-headed serpent that pecks at his head.”"],[9086,"Whoever has wealth and does not pay its zakat, on the Day of Resurrection it will be made into a collar for him — a bald-headed serpent that pecks at his head, saying: “I am your wealth with which you were miserly. {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection}.”"],[9087,"His wealth will come as a huge serpent that pecks at his head, saying: “I am your wealth with which you were miserly,” and he will be collared with it."],[9088,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Sublime: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “He will be collared with a bald-headed serpent with two fangs that pecks at his head, and he will say: ‘What have I to do with you?’ It will say: ‘I am your wealth with which you were miserly.’”"],[9089,"About His saying: {They will be collared with what they were miserly with on the Day of Resurrection} — he said: “A serpent that bites his jaw.”"],[9090,"\"Allah says, 'Establish the prayer at the decline of the sun.'\""],[9091,"The sun’s dulūk is its setting. The Arabs say, when the sun has set, idhā dalakat al-shams: the sun has declined and departed."],[9092,"“Its dulūk is its setting.”"],[9093,"“The sun’s dulūk is its setting.”"],[9094,"ʿAbdullāh prayed Maghrib and when he finished we kept turning around. He said: “Why are you turning around?” We said: “We think the sun is still risen.” He said: “This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer.” Then he recited: {Establish the prayer at the sun’s dulūk until the darkness of the night} — so this is the sun’s dulūk and this is the darkness of the night."],[9095,"ʿAbdullāh prayed one day and a man kept looking to see whether the sun had set. ʿAbdullāh said: “What are you looking at? This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer. Allah, Mighty and Sublime, says: {Establish the prayer at the sun’s dulūk until the darkness of the night} — so this is the sun’s dulūk and this is the darkness of the night.”"],[9096,"We were with Abdullah when he finished and he said, \"By the One besides whom there is no deity, this is the time for this prayer to be performed wherever the sun sets.\""],[9097,"“This, by Allah besides whom there is no god, is where the sun has declined and the time of prayer has arrived.”"],[9098,"“The sun’s dulūk is its setting.”"],[9099,"The sun's declining is when it sets."],[9102,"Abdullah used to say: The two guards from the angels of Allah meet – the guard of the night and the guard of the day – at the rising of dawn. And recite if you wish: {And the Qur'an of dawn – indeed, the Qur'an of dawn is ever witnessed}."],[9103,"We were with Abdullah on the road to Makkah. When the sun set, he said: \"This is the darkness of the night.\" Then the call to prayer was given. Then he said: \"This, by Allah besides whom there is no deity, is the time of this prayer.\""],[9104,"The later evening prayer."],[9105,"The later evening prayer."],[9106,"From Abdullah regarding {Indeed, for him is a narrow livelihood}: He said: \"The punishment of the grave.\""],[9107,"Abdullah used to say: When I narrate to you a hadith, I bring you its confirmation from the Book of Allah. Indeed, when a Muslim servant says: 'Praise be to Allah, glory be to Allah, there is no deity but Allah, Allah is greatest, and blessed is Allah,' an angel takes hold of them and places them beneath his wing. Then he ascends with them and does not pass by any assembly of angels except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them until he brings them before the face of the Most Merciful, Exalted is He. Then Abdullah recited: {To Him ascends the good word, and righteous action raises it}."],[9108,"\"When Abdullah informs you of a narration, I confirm it to you. Indeed, when a Muslim servant dies, he is made to sit in his grave and it is said to him, 'Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet?' Allah will make him firm and he will say, 'My Lord is Allah, my religion is Islam, and my Prophet is Muhammad ﷺ .' Then his grave will be expanded for him and illuminated, and it will be opened for him. Then Abdullah recited, 'Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in worldly life and in the Hereafter. And Allah sends astray the wrongdoers.'\""],[9109,"He said: 'Write.' He says: 'O Lord, what should I write?' He says: 'Write whether he is wretched or blessed, male or female, his provision, his trace, and his term.' Then Allah, mighty and sublime is He, reveals to him whatever He wills, and the angel writes. Then Abdullah recited: {Indeed, We created man from a mixed drop to test him}. He said: And Abdullah said: \"The mixed (amshaj) are the veins.\""],[9110,"From Abdullah, he recited this verse: {But you prefer the worldly life}. Then he said: \"Do you know by what thing the worldly life began? For what thing did it prefer the worldly life? The world was hastened for us, and we were given its pleasure and its splendor, while the Hereafter was hidden from us and withheld from us. So we answered the immediate and abandoned the delayed.\""],[9111,"I saw Abdullah scratching out the two protective surahs and saying: \"Why do you add what is not in it?\""],[9112,"He used to scratch out the two protective surahs from his mushaf and say: \"Indeed, they have mixed into it what is not in it.\""],[9113,"He used to scratch out the two protective surahs from the mushaf, saying: \"They are not from the Book of Allah.\""],[9114,"He used to say: Do not mix into the Quran what is not in it. They are only two surahs of seeking refuge with which the Prophet ﷺ sought refuge: “Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak” and “Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind.” And ʿAbdullah used to erase them from the mushaf."],[9115,"He used to scratch out the two muʿawwidhatayn from the mushafs and say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only commanded that refuge be sought by means of them, and he did not use to recite them.”"],[9116,"ʿAbdullah said to him: “It was not proper for it to take hold of you. Atone for your oath and speak of it.” He said: Take the urine of camels that eat arak, meaning that eat arak, and cook it until it thickens, then drink it. And take arak leaves, pound them, and sprinkle them on it. He said: He did so and was cured."],[9117,"ʿAbdullah said: “The people of the lowest part are rulers over the people of its highest part.”"],[9118,"“Guard your children with regard to prayer, and accustom them to good, for good is a habit.”"],[9119,"“Accustom yourselves to good, for good comes only by habit.”"],[9120,"“Indeed your wealth is mine, but I have left it for you.”"],[9121,"“That I equip a whip in the path of Allah is more beloved to me than a Hajj after the Hajj of Islam.”"],[9122,"“The millstone of Islam will turn upon the head of thirty-five, then a great event will occur. If their destruction is in it, then it is likely; otherwise it will be delayed from them for seventy years. Whoever reaches that will see what he disapproves of.” Thus Abu al-Ahwas narrated it as mawquf, and Masruq, ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAbdullah, and al-Baraʾ b. Najiyah raised it."],[9123,"“A man may speak a word to make his companions laugh, and he does not return to his family with anything from it; he falls by it farther than from heaven to earth.”"],[9124,"That he wanted to bequeath more than one-third, so they permitted him. Then they retracted it after he died. ʿAbdullah was asked about that, and he said: “That is the objectionable thing; it is not permissible.”"],[9125,"From ʿAbdullah concerning a man who makes a bequest and the heirs approve, then they retract. ʿAbdullah said: “That is the objectionable thing; it is not permissible.”"],[9126,"Indeed, Allah ﷻ has not sent down any disease except that He has sent down with it a cure. So adhere to the milk of cows, for they graze upon every kind of tree."],[9127,"Abdullah said, \"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for one disease, the old age. So you should take the milk of cows, as it comes from the entire tree.\""],[9128,"Abdullah used to not consistently observe any act of worship except for performing the Witr prayer before the rak'ah."],[9129,"Abdullah used to not perform the morning prayer regularly, and when he did, he would perform the Witr prayer before the last unit."],[9130,"From two men among the companions of ʿAbd Allah that they used to bring their heads close to ʿAbd Allah in order to hear what he said in his prostration. One of them said: I heard him say, “Glory be to You, there is no god besides You.” The other said: I heard him say, “Glory be to You, there is no Lord besides You.”"],[9131,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say, “The one who is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[9132,"ʿAbd Allah said, “Hasten to the Friday prayers, for Allah ﷻ appears to the people of Paradise every Friday on a hill of camphor, and they will be close to Him according to how quickly they hastened to the Friday prayer. Allah ﷻ will bring about for them something of honor that they had not seen before. Then they will return to their families and narrate to them what Allah has brought about for them.” He said: Then ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque, and there were two men on Friday who had preceded him. So ʿAbd Allah said, “Two men, and I am the third, if Allah wills to bless the third.”"],[9133,"ʿAbd Allah said, “A Muslim man does not mock any state of the world he wakes up in or spends the evening in, without there being distress in his soul.”"],[9134,"\"It is better for one of you to bite on a live coal until it cools down or to hold on to it until it cools down than to say something that Allah has decreed, 'I wish it had not happened'.\""],[9135,"If only ten nights remained of my appointed term, I would love for a woman not to part from me during them."],[9136,"ʿAbd Allah said, “The one who raises his head before the imam raises his head is not safe from his head turning into the head of a dog. And let people who raise their eyes to the sky desist, or their eyesight will be snatched away.”"],[9137,"That he raise his head in prayer before the imam, lest his head turn into the head of a dog. And let people who raise their eyes in prayer desist, or their eyesight will not return to them."],[9138,"ʿAbd Allah said, “A man is not safe, if he raises his head before the imam, from his head turning into the head of a dog. Let people who raise their eyes to the sky desist, or their eyesight will not return to them.”"],[9139,"“ʿAbd Allah was one of the most generous of people in white garment and one of the best of people in fragrance.”"],[9140,"“ʿAbd Allah was pleased by perfume.”"],[9141,"ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque on Friday wearing clean, beautiful white clothes. He looked at a place where there was space and sat down, not stepping over anyone. He said: The imam came out, and there were two men talking. So he took some pebbles and threw them at them. They looked at him and fell silent. When the imam descended, he said, “Did you not know that you are in prayer?”"],[9142,"that he should take a stipend for it, while the keeper of their spoils...\""],[9143,"ʿAbd Allāh said: \"We are more entitled to it.\" He then sat conversing for a while, then rose and departed. ʿAlqamah went off, and when he reached the bearers of the coffers, he sent after him and summoned him back. He said: \"Are you in need?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Take the wealth.\" When he took it, ʿAbd Allāh said: \"That I should lend wealth twice is dearer to me than that I should give it once in charity.\""],[9144,"“Eat you and your companions a third, send to our Bedouin a third, and give a third in charity.”"],[9145,"“When one of you errs in his prayer, let him strive for what is correct within himself, then complete it accordingly, then prostrate two prostrations after the salutation while seated.”"],[9146,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Whoever doubts or errs in his prayer, let him strive, then prostrate two prostrations.”"],[9147,"Ibn Masʿūd used to say after “Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God”: “Peace be upon us from our Lord.”"],[9148,"About nabīdh? He said: “I do not drink except in something stoppered.” His son said: “Did not Ibn Masʿūd used to drink among you from the green jar?” He said: “Indeed.”"],[9149,"He heard Abdullah bin Mas'ud saying, \"How do you react when you see a group of people or when a group with dirty faces comes to you?\""],[9150,"“This is not the misleading trial, but rather this is a horn of the Devil.”"],[9152,"He said to him: “Rise and enter Paradise.” He turned to him frowning and said: “Have you left me anything?” He said: “Yes, for you is the like of what the sun has risen upon or set upon.”"],[9153,"“Do I not see you, a young man, reciting these two sūrahs in this prayer, while you are young?”"],[9154,"A man came to ʿAbd Allāh perfumed with ḥanūṭ. When he saw him and detected the scent of the perfume, he said: “O God, I seek refuge in You from his evil.” He said: Then he came to him and mentioned to him that he had had intercourse with his wife’s slave-girl. He said: “Apply the legal punishment to me.” He said: “Ask God’s forgiveness and repent to Him, and conceal it upon yourself; and if you are able to free her, then free her.”"],[9155,"ʿAbd Allāh used to pronounce the takbīr when he finished the recitation, then when he finished the qunūt he pronounced the takbīr and bowed."],[9156,"until the shadow of every thing becomes its like,” and he asked him about the time of ʿAsr, and he said, “Pray it while the sun is white and alive,” and he asked about the time of Maghrib, and he said, “When the sun has set.”"],[9157,"ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, “I warm myself with her in winter and cool myself with her in summer.”"],[9158,"Ibn Masʿud “would warm himself with his wife in winter while he was junub and had already performed ghusl, and he would cool himself with her in summer while they were in that state.”"],[9159,"A paternal cousin of his made ilaʾ from his wife for ten days, then he went out and returned after four months had passed, and he had intercourse with his wife. Then he met a man who reminded him of his oath, so he came to Ibn Masʿud and asked him. He made him swear by Allah, “I did not know,” then he sent for his wife and made her swear by Allah ﷻ, “I did not know,” then he ordered him, and he proposed to her on his own behalf."],[9160,"About a man who made a vow and did not name anything, he said, “He frees a slave.”"],[9161,"A young girl was brought to ʿAbd Allah who had stolen and had not yet menstruated, and he did not cut off her hand."],[9162,"ʿAbd Allah: Whoever swears an oath and then says, “If Allah wills,” has made an exception."],[9163,"ʿAbd Allah bought a slave girl from his wife – or from one of his wives – and he stipulated a condition for her, and she stipulated her service. ʿUmar ؓ said, “None of your property is that in which someone else has a stipulation of service.”"],[9164,"ʿAbd Allah said the takbir when he began the prayer, and he said, “Like this,” and Misʿar raised his hands above his chest."],[9165,"ʿAbd Allah stood up in the two rakʿahs and did not sit."],[9166,"My paternal uncle married me to his slave girl, and she bore me children, and now he wants to enslave them. He said, “He has no right to that.”"],[9167,"“He has no right to that.”"],[9168,"“ʿAbd Allāh continued proclaiming the talbiyah until he threw the pebble.”"],[9169,"That he heard ʿAbd Allāh say, while he was bowing: “There is no might and no power except with Allāh.”"],[9170,"ʿAbd Allāh said to a man: “When you ask your Lord for good, do not ask while there is a stone in your hand.”"],[9171,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Enter the morning anointed with oil, fasting.”"],[9172,"That she intended to combine an ʿumrah with her Hajj. She asked ʿAbd Allāh, and he said: “I find these to be only the months of Hajj. Allāh, exalted is He, said: {well-known months}.”"],[9173,"His statement refers to washing the two feet in His saying: {and your feet up to the ankles}."],[9174,"“A man must certainly rub between his fingers in ablution, or the Fire will certainly rub between them.”"],[9175,"“A man must certainly rub between his fingers with purification, or the Fire will certainly rub between them.”"],[9176,"That he said: “Rub between the five fingers, lest Allāh fill them with Fire.”"],[9177,"He said to me: “Cut it off,” while laughing: “Where will you isolate it from yourself? It is only a piece of you.”"],[9178,"“Is it anything but like the tip of your nose?”"],[9179,"“I do not care whether I touched it or the tip of my nose.”"],[9180,"He said: “I do not care whether I touch it or my knee.”"],[9181,"One of them said: “I do not care whether I touch my penis or the tip of my nose,” another said, “my ear,” another said, “my thigh,” and another said, “my knee.”"],[9182,"Ibn Masʿūd prayed while on his stomach there were rumen contents and blood from a slaughtered camel he had slaughtered, and he did not perform ablution."],[9183,"Ibn Masʿūd slaughtered a camel and became smeared with its blood and rumen contents, then the prayer was called, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."],[9184,"Regarding the hide of a dead animal, its tanning is its purification."],[9185,"That I perform ablution from an evil word is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from good food."],[9186,"That I perform ablution from an evil word is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from a good morsel."],[9187,"I perform ablution from an evil word: that is more beloved to me than that I perform ablution from good food."],[9188,"ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd, and al-Shaʿbī said regarding a man who sleeps while sitting: “He does not have to perform ablution.”"],[9189,"A man performs ablution on account of intimate touching, touching with his hand, and kissing when he kisses his wife. He used to say regarding this verse: “or you have touched women” — it is groping."],[9190,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd said: “Kissing is one of the forms of touching, and from it ablution is required.”"],[9191,"“Touching (mulāmasa) is whatever falls short of intercourse.”"],[9192,"That a man touches his wife's body with desire, there is wudu' required for it."],[9193,"Indeed, Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and takes hold of a hair from his backside, so he thinks that he has broken wind. He should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9194,"he hears a sound."],[9195,"Indeed, Satan surrounds a man during prayer to cut off his prayer from him. When he is unable, he blows in his backside to make him think that he has broken wind. So if he feels any of that, he should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9196,"he hears a sound or finds a smell."],[9197,"that he washed the tips of his fingers and rinsed his mouth, then prayed."],[9198,"We were brought a bowl from the house of Ibn Mas'ud containing bread and meat, and we ate while Ibn Mas'ud was with us. He rinsed his mouth and washed his fingers before Maghrib."],[9199,"We were brought a bowl and we ate while 'Abdullah was with us. Then 'Abdullah rinsed his mouth and washed his fingers, then we set off to the Maghrib prayer."],[9200,"Wudu' is only from what comes out, not from what goes in; and fasting is from what goes in, not from what comes out."],[9201,"That 'Abdullah used to wear his leather socks at Fajr prayer and would not remove them until he retired to his bed."],[9202,"That he used to wipe over the socks and the sandals."],[9203,"'Abdullah made the wiping three days for the traveler and one day for the resident."],[9204,"I traveled with Abdullah b. Masud for three days to Madinah, and he did not remove his leather socks."],[9205,"I traveled with Abdullah to Madinah, and he did not remove his leather socks for three days and their nights. Sulayman said: I narrated this hadith of Shaqiq to Ibrahim, and he said: Abu Ubaydah narrated to me from Amr b. al-Harith this hadith."],[9206,"I traveled with Abdullah b. Masud, and he used to wipe over his leather socks for three [days]."],[9207,"For the traveler [is] three days to wipe over the leather socks, and for the resident, a day and a night. And I traveled with Abdullah, and he remained for three days wiping over the leather socks."],[9208,"For the traveler [is] three days and their nights, and for the resident, a day and a night."],[9209,"The traveler wipes over the leather socks for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night."],[9210,"The traveler wipes for three days and their nights, and the resident for a day and a night."],[9211,"A man had smallpox, so Ibn Masud ordered that dust be brought near in a basin or a bowl, and he wiped himself with the dust."],[9212,"If I were in a state of major ritual impurity and then did not find water for a month, I would not pray. Sufyan said: This is not to be acted upon."],[9213,"That he does not perform the major ablution."],[9214,"From Aishah, they said: When the two circumcised parts meet, the major ablution becomes obligatory. Masruq said: She was the most knowledgeable of them regarding that."],[9215,"Sufyan said: And the majority hold that the major ablution is obligatory."],[9216,"As for me, when I reach that point with the woman, I perform ghusl."],[9217,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say: “Any person in a state of janābah who washes with khiṭmī has done what is sufficient.”"],[9218,"If he washes his head while in a state of janābah with khiṭmī, he has done what is sufficient, and it does not harm him not to pour water over it."],[9219,"When one of you washes his head while in a state of janābah with khiṭmī and then performs ghusl after that, let him wash his head with water if he wishes."],[9220,"Ibn Masʿūd used to wash his head with khiṭmī while in a state of janābah, then perform ghusl, and he would not wash his head [with water]."],[9221,"If a person in a state of janābah washes his head with khiṭmī, that suffices him from washing it with water."],[9222,"What I strove to catch first was the opening takbīr at the beginning of the prayer."],[9223,"I strove to catch the beginning of the prayer."],[9224,"Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī led them in prayer and took off his sandals. ʿAbd Allah said to him: “Why did you take off your sandals? Are you in the sacred valley?”"],[9225,"Abū Mūsā said to him: “Go forward, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, for you are older in age and more learned.” He said: “No, rather you go forward, for we came to you in your home and your mosque.” So Abū Mūsā went forward and took off his sandals. When he had prayed, he said: “What did you intend by taking them off? Are you in the sacred valley of Ṭuwā? I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in leather socks and sandals.”"],[9226,"And he would not prostrate except on the ground."],[9227,"He used to stand on the burdī and prostrate on the ground. We said: “What is the burdī?” He said: “The mat.”"],[9228,"Ibn Masʿud performed prayer over (i.e., wiped over) a leather sock."],[9229,"Ibn Masʿud used to patrol the mosque and would not leave any darkness (person) in it except he would remove him, except a man praying."],[9230,"on his right, and he was not in prayer.”"],[9231,"from this.”"],[9232,"nor your Quran reciters."],[9234,"The prohibition of prayer is the takbir and its release is the taslim. When you have said the salam and a need hastens you, then depart before he turns his face back."],[9235,"He prayed with his companions in his house without an iqamah and said, “The iqamah of the townsman is sufficient.”"],[9236,"Sufyan said, “The iqamah of the town was sufficient for them.”"],[9237,"Abdullah bin Mas'ood saw a man raising his hands to the sky, supplicating while in his prayer. So, Abdullah bin Mas'ood said, \"What does he know? Perhaps his sight may be dazzled before it returns to him.\""],[9238,"When the prayer has been made obligatory, do not leave it for something else."],[9239,"when the sun had declined."],[9240,"ʿAbdullah prayed when the sun had declined. I said to Sulayman, “Zuhr?” He said, “Yes.” Then ʿAbdullah said, “This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the appointed time of this prayer.”"],[9241,"ʿAbdullah used to pray Zuhr while the grasshoppers were leaping in the heat of the sun-baked ground."],[9242,"Ibn Masʿūd used to delay the ʿAṣr prayer."],[9243,"The sun rises between the two horns of a devil. It does not rise even a spear’s length before a gate of the gates of Hell is opened for it. When the day reaches its midpoint, the gates of Hell are opened for it.” He said: So ʿAbdullāh used to forbid us from two prayers during these two times: when it rises until it has risen, and at midday."],[9244,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd used to brighten the dawn prayer (perform it a bit late when light appeared)."],[9245,"ʿAbdullāh used to say: “Be brief in prayer, for behind you are the elderly, the weak, and those with needs.” We would pray behind our imam while wearing our clothes, and he would recite a surah from the miʾīn (the long surahs of about a hundred verses), then we would go to ʿAbdullāh and find him still in prayer."],[9246,"Allah the Exalted said: {until the darkness of the night, and the recitation of dawn. Indeed, the recitation of dawn is ever witnessed}."],[9247,"Someone who saw Ibn Masʿūd told me: He prayed Fajr, then sat and did not stand for any prayer until the call for Ẓuhr was made. Then he stood and prayed four (rakʿahs)."],[9248,"None of you should pray with an open gap between him and the qiblah — meaning an opening."],[9249,"Do not pray while there is an open gap between you and the qiblah."],[9250,"...that no one should pass in front of him while he is praying, let him do (what he can to prevent it); for the one passing in front of the praying person has a lesser reward than the one he passes in front of."],[9251,"...that no one should pass in front of him, let him do (what he can); for the one passing in front of the praying person has a lesser reward than the one he passes in front of."],[9252,"...that no one should cause someone to pass in front of him while he is praying, let him do (what he can); for the one passing in front of the praying person is less (in reward) than the one he passes in front of."],[9253,"...that someone should pass in front of you while you are praying, do not let him; for he throws away half of his prayer."],[9254,"that he should prostrate while saying in his prostration, “Labbayka wa saʿdayka (Here I am at Your service, and blessed are You).”"],[9255,"\"Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who take their place in the first rows (of prayer), meaning the advanced row.\""],[9256,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “Do not form rows between the columns, and do not follow a group as your imam while they are conversing.”"],[9257,"ʿAbdullāh said, “Do not follow as your imam a people who are disputing, and do not pray between the columns.”"],[9258,"I heard Ibn Masʿūd saying, “Do not form rows between the pillars, and do not pray while there are people passing in front of you.”"],[9259,"\"I hated praying between the pillars, single or double.\""],[9260,"Ibn Masʿūd used to say the takbīr every time he lowered and raised."],[9261,"Ibn Masʿūd used to raise his hands at the first instance, then did not raise them after that."],[9262,"ʿAbdullāh did not raise his hands in any part of the prayer except in the first takbīrah."],[9263,"When he entered the prayer, he raised his hands, then did not raise them after that."],[9264,"From Ibn Masʿūd ؓ: When they began the prayer, they used to say, “Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You,” before the recitation."],[9265,"He used to say, “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his arrogance, and his poetry.”"],[9266,"His whisper means Satan, his sneezing means madness, his snorting means arrogance, and his breath means poetry."],[9267,"\"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud did not pronounce aloud 'Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Rahim' (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) nor 'A'udhu billahi min ash-Shaytan ir-Rajim' (I seek refuge in Allah from Satan, the accursed) nor 'Ameen'.\""],[9268,"Ibn Masʿūd used to begin his prayer with {All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds}."],[9269,"Ibn Masʿūd used to recite in the first two rakʿahs of the noon and afternoon prayers the Opening of the Book and a surah in each rakʿah, and in the last two rakʿahs the Opening of the Book."],[9270,"Ibn Masʿūd led them in the ʿIshāʾ prayer and recited forty verses of al-Anfāl, then in the second rakʿah he recited a sūrah from the Mufaṣṣal."],[9271,"Ibn Masʿūd led us in the ʿIshāʾ prayer. He began with Sūrat al-Anfāl until when he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, he bowed. Then in the second rakʿah he recited two sūrahs from the Mufaṣṣal."],[9272,"ʿAbdullāh recited in the later ʿIshāʾ in the first rakʿah {They ask you about the spoils of war} until he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, then he bowed. Then in the second he recited a sūrah from the Mufaṣṣal? He said: Yes."],[9273,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd led us in the later ʿIshāʾ prayer. He began al-Anfāl and recited until when he reached {How excellent a protector and how excellent a helper}, he bowed. Then he stood and in the second rakʿah recited a sūrah."],[9274,"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, should I recite behind the imam? He said: “Listen attentively to the Qurʾān, for in the prayer there is enough preoccupation, and the imam will suffice you for that.”"],[9275,"That he should be an imam who does not recite.”"],[9276,"Ibn Masʿūd would not recite behind the imam,” and Ibrāhīm used to follow that."],[9277,"“When the imam falters, do not correct him, for that is speech.”"],[9278,"He said, \"It is a statement.\""],[9279,"Alqamah and Al-Aswad said: \"We prayed behind Abdullah, and when he went into the bowing position, he placed his hands on his knees and struck our hands.\" So we did the same."],[9280,"Ibn Masʿūd bowed and placed his hands together, putting them between his knees.”"],[9281,"ʿAbdullāh would place his hands together when bowing, putting his hands between his knees and spreading his forearms on his thighs.”"],[9282,"ʿAbdullāh would say in his bowing: My Lord, forgive me.”"],[9283,"To say in his bowing and prostration, \"Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika, la ilaha ghairuka.\""],[9284,"Abū al-Aswad said: ʿAbd Allāh used to say in his prostration: “Glory be to You; there is no lord other than You.” Shaddād said: He used to say: “Glory be to You; there is no god other than You.”"],[9285,"“I entered the mosque and found ʿAbd Allāh praying. He bowed, and I began [reciting] Sūrat al-Aʿrāf and finished it before he prostrated.”"],[9286,"When [the imam] says: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” then let the one behind him say: “Our Lord, to You belongs praise.”"],[9287,"When [the imam] says: “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” then let the one behind him say: “Our Lord, to You belongs praise.”"],[9288,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate resting on his hip or lying on his side, for if he perfects the prostration, all his bones prostrate.”"],[9289,"“When one of you prostrates, let him not prostrate lying on his side or resting on his hip, for if he perfects the prostration, every limb of his prostrates.”"],[9290,"“He rises on the balls of his feet in the first and second rakʿah.”"],[9291,"“ʿAbd Allāh used to rise on the balls of his feet.”"],[9292,"That Ibn Mas'ood used to do it."],[9293,"“ʿAbd Allāh, when he said takbīr upon raising his head from the prostration, would stand up with it.”"],[9294,"ʿAbd Allāh said to him: “Do not tie back [your hair], for your hair prostrates, and for every hair you have a reward.” He said: “I only tied it back so that it would not get dusty.” He said: “If it gets dusty, that is better for you.”"],[9295,"ʿAbd Allāh passed by a man prostrating who had tied back his hair. He undid his tied hair and let it loose, then waited until he finished praying. ʿAbd Allāh said: “Indeed your hair prostrates with you, so do not tie it back, for for every hair of it you have a reward.” The man said: “I feared it would get dusty.” ʿAbd Allāh said: “If it gets dusty, that is better for you.”"],[9297,"“ʿAbd Allāh would not turn around in prayer. If his need was to his right, he would turn away to his right, and if his need was to his left, he would turn away to his left.”"],[9298,"He used to say: 'When the imam has said the salam, then depart wherever your need takes you, to the right or to the left, and do not turn around like the turning around of a donkey.'"],[9299,"on his right.'"],[9300,"'When the imam has said the salam, then let him stand or turn away from his place.' I said: Is it sufficient for him to turn away from his place while facing the qiblah? He said: 'The turning away is to go west or east, according to more than one.'"],[9301,"that he 'when he had said the salam, he would get up from his place or turn away to the east or to the west.'"],[9302,"'When the imam has said the salam and a man has a need, he should not wait for him, once he has said the salam, to turn his face toward him, for the ending of the prayer is the salam.' And ʿAbdullah, when he had said the salam, would not delay in getting up or moving from his place and turning his face toward them."],[9303,"'When you are behind the imam, do not bow until he bows, and do not prostrate until he prostrates, and do not raise your head before him. Then when the imam has finished and has not gotten up or turned away, and you have a need, go and leave him, for your prayer is complete.'"],[9304,"From Abu Khalid, one of the companions of ʿAbdullah: A man came to ʿAbdullah and said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, so-and-so recites the Quran while bowing, and he recites while prostrating. ʿAbdullah said: 'Indeed, there are men who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. When it enters the heart and becomes firmly rooted in it, then it benefits.'"],[9305,"as if it were a thrown garment."],[9306,"'Make the prayer settled.' Mansur was asked what he meant by that, and he said: 'That one should be still in his prayer when he bows and when he prostrates.'"],[9307,"ʿAbdullah: 'Be settled in the prayer,' meaning: be still and at ease."],[9308,"\"God continues to look favorably upon His servant with His face as long as he does not turn away or speak.\""],[9309,"'As for this man, he has deviated from the Sunnah. If he had alternated between the two, it would have been more beloved to me.'"],[9312,"'Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught the prayer.'"],[9313,"\"Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught [the prayer].\""],[9314,"He informed him from ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud that they both said, \"Whoever does not catch the rakʿah should not count the prostration.\""],[9315,"\"Whoever misses the bowing should not count the prostration.\""],[9316,"I and ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque while the people were bowing, so we bowed, then we walked until we joined the people. They raised their heads and we raised [ours] with them. When we finished the prayer, I stood up to make up [what I missed], but ʿAbd Allah spoke to me and said, \"You have completed the prayer.\""],[9317,"I and Ibn Masʿud entered the mosque while the imam was bowing, so we bowed, then we moved on until we stood in line with the row. When the imam finished, I stood up to make up [the prayer], but he said, \"You caught it.\""],[9318,"And he said, \"Indeed you caught it.\""],[9319,"\"... that you bow before reaching the row.\""],[9320,"\"When one of you bows and then walks to the row before they raise their heads, he counts it; but if they raise their heads before he reaches the row, he does not count it.\""],[9321,"\"You have caught it, if Allah wills.\""],[9322,"ʿAbd Allah entered the mosque and [someone] entered with him. The imam bowed, so we bowed before we reached the row, then we reached the row when the imam said 'Samʿa Allahu li-man hamidah.' When the imam said the taslim, ʿAbd Allah's companion stood up to make up [the prayer], but ʿAbd Allah grabbed his garment and said, \"Sit down, for you have caught the prayer.\""],[9323,"\"Is not the prayer the most worthy thing I hasten to?\""],[9324,"\"When a man doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he prayed three or two [rakʿahs], he should base it on the more certain of the two, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[9325,"He said: 'He should seek the most correct course and prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness.'"],[9326,"That ʿAbd Allah used to say regarding forgetfulness: He should seek the correct course and prostrate two prostrations while seated after the taslim."],[9327,"Forgetfulness is when one stands where one should sit, or sits where one should stand, or says the salam after two rakʿahs. Then he should complete his prayer and prostrate two prostrations while seated, reciting the tashahhud in them."],[9328,"When you stand or sit or say the salam, then prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then recite the tashahhud, then say the salam."],[9329,"I am amazed at these two men. As for the one who lets his lower garment hang down, Allah will not look at him; and as for the other, Allah will not accept his prayer."],[9330,"Yes. As for this one, Allah will not look at him, meaning the one who lets his lower garment hang down; and as for this one, Allah will not accept from him, meaning the one who does not complete his bowing or his prostration."],[9331,"That he saw a bedouin praying with his lower garment hanging down, and he said: 'The one who lets his lower garment hang down in prayer is not in a state of what is lawful or unlawful with Allah ﷻ.'"],[9332,"He should make what he catches with the imam the end of his prayer."],[9333,"Each has done well, and we will do as Masruq did."],[9334,"Both are good, and I will do as the one who recited in the two rakʿahs did."],[9335,"That Jundub and Masruq caught one rakʿah of the Maghrib prayer. When the imam said the salam, they stood to make up the remaining rakʿahs. Jundub stood in the second rakʿah, while Masruq sat in both of them. They mentioned this to Ibn Masʿud, and he said: 'Both of you have done well, and I will do as Masruq did.'"],[9336,"Jundub and Masruq prayed Maghrib in a mosque, having caught only one rakʿah with the imam. They stood to make up the rest. Masruq sat in the second rakʿah, and Jundub stood in the first rakʿah of the make-up. They came to ʿAbd Allah and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Both of you have done well, and do as Masruq did.'"],[9337,"Masruq and Jundab reached the imam after they had missed a rakʿah. Masruq did not recite, while Jundab recited. They mentioned that to ʿAbd Allah, and he said: \"Neither of you has fallen short in the matter, but the correct course is what Masruq did.\""],[9338,"Prayer has an appointed time, like the appointed time of Hajj."],[9339,"Straighten your rows, for Satan passes through them like small pebbles, or like the young of pebbles."],[9340,"Do not bow before the imam, do not rise before him, do not prostrate before him, and do not raise [your head] before him."],[9341,"The imam is appointed only to be followed. When he bows, bow; when he rises, rise. Do not get ahead of him when he bows, nor when he rises, nor when he prostrates. If you are concerned about catching up with what he has preceded you in, then he prostrates before you and rises before you, so you will catch up with that."],[9342,"We perform Hajj to the House of our Lord and settle debts, and he is like the sandgrouse swooping down. ʿAbd Allah said: \"We have not heard of this in the latter religion; this is nothing but fabrication.\" Then ʿAbd Allah left."],[9343,"He turned towards the north and then prayed with them."],[9344,"ʿAbd Allah prayed with ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad. One stood on his right and the other on his left, then he stood between them."],[9345,"Ibn Masʿud prayed with him and with al-Aswad, and he stood between them."],[9347,"ʿAbd Allah said: \"When they are three, let them all stand in a row. When they are more than that, let one of them go forward.\""],[9348,"Ibn Masʿud came while the imam was praying the morning prayer, and he prayed two rakʿahs facing a pillar, and he had not yet prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr."],[9350,"The prayer was called, and ʿAbd Allah went to the mosque and prayed two rakʿahs, then he entered the mosque."],[9351,"Ibn Masʿud used to say: \"Attach your needs to the obligatory prayer.\""],[9352,"I heard the recitation of ʿAbd Allah in one of the two daytime prayers."],[9353,"I prayed beside ʿAbd Allah, and I did not realize he was reciting anything until I heard him say, “My Lord, increase me in knowledge” (Q 20:114), so I knew he was in Sūrat Ṭā Hā."],[9354,"For one of you to sit on two embers would be better for him than to sit cross-legged in prayer."],[9355,"\"Because for a man to sit on two cushions is better for him than to sit cross-legged during prayer.\" Abdul Razzaq said, \"If he prays standing, then he should not sit in a cross-legged position during the tashahhud (a part of the prayer) and if he prays sitting, then he should sit cross-legged.\""],[9356,"About a sick person, when he prays, he said: “If he cannot reach the ground, let him gesture; and let him make his prostration lower than his bowing.”"],[9357,"“Gesture, and let your bowing be higher than your prostration.”"],[9358,"ʿAlqama and al-Aswad entered upon ʿAbd Allah and said, “Al-Aswad’s mother has been bedridden, and he props up a palm-frond fan stick for her to pray on. What do you think?” He said, “I think Satan presents the stick to her; she should prostrate on the ground if she can, and if not, she should gesture.”"],[9359,"I said to ʿAlqama, “How was ʿAbd Allah’s recitation?” He said, “The people of the house could hear his voice.”"],[9360,"He made himself hear."],[9361,"He made his ears hear."],[9364,"We asked ʿAlqama, “How was ʿAbd Allah’s recitation at night, when he used to stay overnight with him?” He said, “He would make the household of his brother ʿUtba hear him, while they were in a room in front of him.”"],[9365,"He narrated to us, so we asked him, “How did ʿAbd Allah use to recite?” He said, “He would make the household of ʿUtba hear him, while they were in a room in front of him.”"],[9366,"\"He used to perform Tahajjud (night prayer) when there was still time left in the night, just as he used to perform the Maghrib prayer before the nightfall.\""],[9367,"He would make those around him hear, but he did not raise his voice, until there remained of the pre-dawn darkness only about the interval between the call to prayer for Maghrib and finishing it; then he performed Witr."],[9368,"Abdullah used to perform the Sunnah prayer after returning from the Maghrib prayer when a portion of the night remained."],[9369,"\"The Witr is the prayer between the two regular prayers.\""],[9370,"Abdullah: \"Al-Witr is the prayer between the two obligatory prayers.\""],[9371,"Abdullah said, \"Al-Witr is the prayer that is performed between Isha prayer and Fajr prayer.\""],[9372,"\"The period between the two prayers is considered to be a voluntary prayer, and specifically the period between the Isha (Night) prayer and the Fajr (Dawn) prayer.\""],[9374,"\"The Witr is the prayer performed between the two prayers.\""],[9375,"I bear witness that Abdullah ibn Mas'ood, indeed I heard him calling out with it as a call: \"Witr is the prayer that is between the two prayers, the last prayer of the night which you call Al Atamah, and the prayer of Fajr, when do you pray Witr, it is good.\""],[9376,"Ibn Mas'ood used to perform the night prayer after Fajr, and my father used to perform the night prayer before Fajr."],[9377,"\"The Fajr prayer was called and I was performing Witr.\""],[9378,"\"To call the iqamah for Fajr prayer while I was still in my nightly recitation, having not yet performed Witr.\""],[9379,"\"O Abu Abdurrahman, is there a prayer after the adhan (call to prayer)?\" He said, \"Yes, and after the iqama (call to commence prayer).\""],[9380,"\"That Abdullah used to perform the voluntary prayers of night (Tahajjud) in sets of three.\""],[9381,"\"Abdullah used to perform the voluntary night prayer in sets of three, and then he would end with one additional unit.\""],[9382,"Ibn Mas'ud said: \"The night prayer is like the day prayer, (meaning they both hold equal importance and reward) and the Maghrib prayer should be performed three times (meaning one should perform three units of prayer for Maghrib).\""],[9383,"\"The Witr prayer is three, like the Witr of the daytime prayer.\""],[9384,"\"Witr is three units of prayer, similar to the prayer of Maghrib.\""],[9385,"\"A rak'ah cannot be divided.\""],[9386,"Abdullah replied, \"Yes, but three are better.\" Saad then said, \"I can't add anything more to it.\" This made Abdullah angry, and Saad said, \"Are you angry with me for praying one additional unit of prayer while you inherit three grandmothers? Won't you also leave a share for Hawwa, the wife of Adam?\" Yahya informed me about this from Thawri."],[9387,"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman stayed up conversing at al-Walid b. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt's, then left his company and stood talking until they saw the first glimmers of dawn. Then each of them performed Witr with one rak'ah."],[9388,"Abdullah used to recite \"Qul Huwallahu Ahad\" in the last Rak'ah of Witr, then he would raise his hands and make supplication before the Rak'ah."],[9389,"Ibnu Mas'ud used to observe voluntary night prayers throughout the year."],[9390,"From more than one of the companions of 'Abdullah that Ibn Mas'ud used to say, \"When one of you performs Witr, then sleeps, then wakes, let him break his Witr and pray an additional rak'ah, then perform Witr after that.\""],[9391,"\"That Ibn Mas'ud would not perform qunut in Fajr prayer.\""],[9392,"\"That Ibn Mas'ud would not perform qunut in the morning prayer.\""],[9393,"Abdullah used to not pray the Fajr prayer regularly, but when he did, he would pray the Witr prayer before the Rak'ah."],[9394,"\"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud did not perform qunut in the morning prayer.\""],[9395,"He used to offer voluntary prayers before the bowing (rak'ahs) in a prayer, but he did not offer voluntary prayers before the morning prayer."],[9396,"Regarding the prayer on the day of Eid, the Fajr prayer was called, so Ibn Mas'ud stood behind a pillar and prayed two rak'ahs, then joined them."],[9397,"\"That the morning prayer be performed.\""],[9398,"That he \"disliked speaking after praying the two rak'ahs before Fajr.\""],[9399,"\"To speak after Fajr except with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[9400,"\"To hear anyone speaking in it from the break of dawn until sunrise.\""],[9401,"that you should keep silent.”"],[9402,"that you two should keep silent.”"],[9403,"“Ibn Masʿud disliked speaking after praying the two rakʿahs of Fajr.”"],[9404,"“ʿAbd Allah’s prayer during the day was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Fajr. He did not pray before ʿAsr or after it.”"],[9405,"ʿAbd Allah’s voluntary prayer, which he would not abandon, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Subh."],[9406,"“ʿAbd Allah’s voluntary prayer, from which he did not diminish, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before the morning prayer.”"],[9407,"“ʿAbd Allah’s prayer, which he would not leave, was four rakʿahs before Zuhr, two after it, two after Maghrib, two after ʿIsha, and two before Fajr.”"],[9408,"he used to say: “When the sun declined, he would stand and pray four rakʿahs, reciting in them two surahs from the Miʾin (the long surahs). When the muʾadhdhins called one another, he would tighten his garment and then go out to the prayer.”"],[9409,"ʿAbd Allah [said]: “Nothing equals the night prayer among the daytime prayers except four rakʿahs before Zuhr, and their virtue over the daytime prayer is like the virtue of congregational prayer over praying alone.”"],[9410,"that his father “did not pray the Duha prayer.”"],[9411,"“I never came to him at any hour except that I found him standing in prayer between Maghrib and ʿIsha” — meaning ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud."],[9412,"“It is an hour of heedlessness.”"],[9413,"ʿAbd Allah: “Yes, the hour of heedlessness,” meaning the prayer between Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[9414,"“Drowsiness during fighting is security from Allah, and drowsiness during prayer is from Satan.”"],[9415,"ʿAbd Allah: “Drowsiness during prayer is from Satan, and drowsiness during fighting is security from Allah.”"],[9416,"“Yawning and sneezing during prayer are from Satan.”"],[9417,"“Prayer is not shortened except in Hajj or Jihad.”"],[9418,"He said, \"Do not decrease from your prayers in your homes, nor take part in your affairs, nor travel in the valleys of the lowlands for your needs, and then say that you are travelers, for a traveler is only one who travels from horizon to horizon.\""],[9419,"He said: “Do not be deluded by your trades and your gatherings, and travel to the villages of the Sawad, and say, ‘We are a people on a journey.’ The traveler is only one from horizon to horizon.”"],[9420,"“Do not be deluded by your Sawad, for the gathering place of any of you and his family is one thing, unless he chooses otherwise.”"],[9422,"“Whoever prays four rakʿahs while traveling must repeat the prayer.”"],[9423,"About a man who lies on his side at the two rakʿahs of Duha? He said: “What is the matter with one of you that he rolls around like the rolling of a donkey?”"],[9424,"“Do you burden people with what Allah has not burdened them? They see you praying and then consider that obligatory upon them. If you must do it, then in the houses.”"],[9425,"When ʿAbd Allah stood, we would sit after him and help people with the recitation. Then when we stood, we prayed. That reached him, so we entered upon him and he said: “Do you burden people with what they are not burdened? They see you and think it is a Sunnah. If you must do it, then in your houses.” Sulayman said: ʿAmr b. Murrah also narrated to us from Abu ʿUbaydah from ʿAbd Allah."],[9426,"That I prostrate, so I disobeyed, and to me is the Fire."],[9427,"A man, while he was irrigating a field of his, saw a cloud raining. He heard a voice in it saying, 'Irrigate the land of So-and-so.' He followed the voice until he reached the land that was named. He asked its owner, 'What is your practice regarding it?' He said, 'I return one-third [of its produce to the land], I give one-third in charity, and I reserve one-third for my family.'"],[9429,"\"May Allah curse the women who tattoo, those who have themselves tattooed, those who file their teeth for the sake of beauty, altering Allah's creation.\" This reached a woman of Banu Asad called Umm Ya'qub. She said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I heard that you cursed such and such.' He said, 'Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed and who are mentioned in the Book of Allah?' She said, 'Indeed I read what is between the two covers, but I do not find it.' He said, 'If you were a reader, you would have found it. Have you not read, \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it\"?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it.' She said, 'I think your family does some of that.' He said, 'Go and look.' She entered and did not see anything of what she sought. 'Abd Allah said, 'If she was like that, she would not have been intimate with us.' Al-Dabari said: We said to Abu Bakr, 'What is al-namisa?' He said, 'The one who plucks her hair.'"],[9430,"\"The Messenger of Allah cursed, so a woman from the Banu Asad said to him, 'I think he is cursing your family.' He said, 'Go and look.' So she went and then came back and said, 'I did not see anything in them (i.e., his family), and I did not see him (i.e., the curse) in the Quran.' Abdullah said to her, 'Indeed, yes, the Messenger of Allah said that.'\""],[9431,"Something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or you find it in the Book of Allah? He said, 'Rather, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I find it in the Book of Allah.' She said, 'By Allah, I have read what is between the two covers of the mushaf, and I did not find it.' He said, 'Do you not find in it, \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it\"?' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'By Allah, I think the one in your house does it.' He said, 'Then I have not kept the advice of my brother Shu'ayb.' He said, 'I adjure you by Allah: enter upon her and look at her hair.' She entered and looked at a bald woman and saw nothing in her hair. She came out and said, 'I found nothing.' He said, 'Then I have not kept the advice of Shu'ayb.'"],[9432,"\"May Allah curse the women who file their teeth, pluck their eyebrows, tattoo themselves, altering Allah's creation.\" A woman of Banu Asad called Umm al-Mustawrid came to him and said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I heard that you cursed the women who file their teeth, pluck their eyebrows, and tattoo themselves.' He said, 'Should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed, and it is in the Book of Allah?' She said, 'I have read what is between the two covers, and I did not find it in it.' He said, 'If you have read what is between the two covers, indeed it is in the Book of Allah: \"And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it.\"' She said, 'By Allah, I think your family does it.' He said, 'Enter and look. If they do it, they will not spend a night with me.' She entered and looked, then came out saying, 'I saw nothing. I saw nothing.'"],[9433,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said, \"May the one who connects (= tribal affiliations) be cursed, as well as the tattooer, the fortune-teller, and those who pluck their facial hairs.\" This statement was said by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ."],[9434,"\"By Him besides whom there is no god, a woman never prays a prayer better for her than a prayer she prays in her house, except in the Sacred Mosque or the Mosque of the Messenger, except for an old woman in her manqalayha.\""],[9435,"\"A woman does not pray in any place that is better for her than her house, except in the Sacred Mosque or the Mosque of the Prophet ﷺ, except a woman who goes out in her manqalayha,\" meaning her khuffs."],[9436,"I heard the Lord of this house swearing an oath and going far in the oath: \"There is no prayer place for a woman better for her than her house, except in Hajj or 'Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of marriage, for she is in her manqalayha.\" I said, \"What is her manqalayha?\" He said, \"An old woman whose steps have become short.\""],[9437,"'Abd Allah swore an oath and went far in the oath: \"There is no prayer place for a woman better than her house, except in Hajj or 'Umrah, except a woman who has despaired of marriage, for she is in her manqalayha.\""],[9438,"He saw Ibn Mas'ud driving women out of the mosque on Friday and saying, \"Go out to your houses; that is better for you.\""],[9439,"\"I saw Ibn Mas'ud driving women out of the mosque on Friday.\""],[9440,"He used to drive women out of the mosque on Friday and say, \"Pray in your houses.\""],[9441,"That she sits in the depth of her house worshipping her Lord. One of them says, 'I will go to my family,' and the Shaytan seeks to make her look attractive until she says, 'No one saw me except that I pleased him.'"],[9442,"Women are but ʿawrah. Indeed, a woman leaves her house while there is nothing wrong with her, and Satan seeks to raise himself up for her, saying: “You will not pass by anyone but that you will charm him.” And indeed, a woman puts on her clothes, and it is said: “Where do you intend to go?” She replies: “I am visiting a sick person, attending a funeral, or praying in a mosque.” But a woman has not worshipped her Lord with anything like worshipping Him in her home."],[9443,"Indeed, a woman is ʿawrah. When she leaves her house, Satan raises himself up for her, and she says: “No one sees me but that I charm him.” The closest she is to Allah is when she is in the innermost part of her home."],[9444,"“A woman’s prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her chamber, and her prayer in her chamber is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer anywhere else.” Then he said: “Indeed, when a woman goes out, Satan raises himself up for her.”"],[9445,"“A woman’s prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her courtyard is better than her prayer outside it.”"],[9446,"“Two wooden dancers (i.e., two clogs or stilts).”"],[9447,"“A woman of the Children of Israel used to wear two wooden clogs and stand upon them to set a tryst with her lover, so menstruation was imposed upon them.” And ʿAbd Allah (i.e., Ibn Masʿūd) used to say: “Keep them back where Allah has kept them back.”"],[9448,"“Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” When he finished, he said: “It used to be said: among the signs of the Hour are that a man will greet another man only because he knows him, that mosques will be taken as thoroughfares, that women and horses will become expensive and then become cheap and will not become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection, and that a man and a woman will trade together.”"],[9449,"“That mosques be taken as thoroughfares.”"],[9450,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Among the signs of the Hour are that a man will pass through the length and breadth of the mosque without praying two rakʿahs in it.” This is how Mansūr narrated it, and Qatādah connected it."],[9451,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Allah and His Messenger ﷺ have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Among the signs of the Hour are that a man will pass through the mosque without praying two rakʿahs in it, that a man will not greet anyone except one he knows, and that a young boy will make an old man cool (i.e., will relieve him or act as his superior).’”"],[9452,"“Peace be upon you, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” He laughed and said: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The Hour will not come until greeting is only upon acquaintance; indeed this man recognized me from among you and greeted me, and until mosques are taken as thoroughfares so that no prostration is made to Allah in them, and until a young boy sends an old man as a messenger between the two horizons, and until a merchant travels between the two horizons and finds no profit.’”"],[9453,"The prayer was commenced in the mosque, and we came walking with ʿAbd Allah. When the people bowed, ʿAbd Allah bowed and we bowed with him while we were walking. A man passed in front of him and said: “Peace be upon you, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.” ʿAbd Allah said while bowing: “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” When he finished, some of the people asked him: “Why did you say, when the man greeted you, ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth’?” He replied: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Among the signs of the Hour are when greeting is upon acquaintance.’”"],[9454,"ʿAbdullah used to say: “Perform this prayer well and shorten these sermons.”"],[9455,"“Lengthy prayer and short sermon are an indication of a man’s understanding.”"],[9456,"“Lengthy prayer and short sermon are an indication of a man’s understanding.”"],[9457,"“There will be rulers over you who kill the prayer. Whoever of you reaches that should pray it at its proper time and make his prayer with them a supererogatory prayer.”"],[9458,"“You are in a time whose preachers are few and scholars many; they make the prayer long and the sermon short. There will come upon you a time whose preachers are many and scholars few; they make the sermon long and delay the prayer until it is said: ‘This is the glow of the dead.’” I said to him: “What is the glow of the dead?” He said: “When the sun turns very yellow. Whoever of you reaches that should pray the prayer at its proper time; if he is detained, let him pray with them and make his prayer alone the obligatory one and his prayer with them voluntary.”"],[9459,"“There will be rulers who abandon practices like this. If you abandon them, they will make them like this. If you abandon them, they will bring the great calamity.”"],[9460,"“Do not be a tax collector, nor a headman, nor a policeman, nor a courier, and pray the prayer at its appointed time.”"],[9461,"“ʿAbdullah would pray with them when they delayed it a little, and he held that they bore the sin of that.”"],[9462,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “None of that was done, and Allah and His Messenger ﷺ did not command us to wait for you with our prayer while you are attending to your need.”"],[9463,"That he hears the muezzin say: “Allah is most great, Allah is most great; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,” and he does not say the like of what he says, and that he wipes his face before finishing his prayer, and that he urinates standing, and that he prays when there is nothing between him and the qiblah to screen him."],[9464,"From al-Musayyab, who traced the hadith back to ʿAbdullah, who said: “Four things are from coarseness: that a man hears the muezzin say ‘Allah is most great’ and does not say it, and hears the testimony of faith and does not say it, and wipes dust from his forehead while praying, and prays in open ground with no screen between him and the qiblah.”"],[9465,"And that you hear the muezzin and do not say what he says."],[9466,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah said to him: Perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray. He saw that ʿAbd Allah did not understand the gravity of what he had done. He then repeated: O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah said to him: «Perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray.» He remained silent, and when those with him had departed, he said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose. ʿAbd Allah took hold of his finger and pressed it, then said: «It was only said to you so that you would understand: perform wuḍūʾ as well as you used to perform wuḍūʾ and pray as well as you used to pray.»"],[9468,"«Does every one of you find two garments? He may pray in a single garment.»"],[9469,"«Ibn Masʿūd and ʿĀʾishah used to offer voluntary prayers while traveling before the prayer and after it.»"],[9470,"He said to Ibn Masʿūd: Are you not amazed at people between your house and the house of Abū Mūsā who claim that they are observing iʿtikāf? He said: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong.»"],[9471,"\"Do not be surprised by the people between your house and the house of Abu Musa who claim that they are in seclusion,\" Ibn Mas'ood said. \"Perhaps they have succeeded and you have failed, or they have remembered and you have forgotten.\" He said, \"As for me, I have learned that seclusion is only in the congregational mosque.\""],[9472,"He said: Shall I not amaze you at people observing iʿtikāf between your house and the house of al-Ashʿarī? ʿAbd Allah said: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong.» Ḥudhayfah said: I do not care whether I observe iʿtikāf in it or in this market of yours. Iʿtikāf is only in these three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Aqsa Mosque. Those who observed iʿtikāf and whom Ḥudhayfah criticized were in the great mosque of Kufa."],[9473,"Ḥudhayfah said to ʿAbd Allah: There are people observing iʿtikāf between your house and the house of Abū Mūsā. Will you not forbid them? ʿAbd Allah said to him: «Perhaps they are right and you are wrong, and they have remembered while you have forgotten.» Ḥudhayfah said: There is no iʿtikāf except in these three mosques: the Mosque of Madinah, the Mosque of Makkah, and the Mosque of Iliya."],[9474,"A man observed iʿtikāf in a tent of his, and people pelted him with pebbles. The man sent for ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd, and ʿAbd Allah came, «drove the people away, and deemed that commendable.»"],[9475,"Abdullah ibn Mas'ud used to make nine takbirs for both Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr, starting by making four takbirs, then reciting Quran, then making one takbir and performing the bowing position (Ruk'u), then standing back up for the second unit of prayer and starting by reciting Quran, then making four takbirs and performing the bowing position with one of them."],[9476,"This is the festival of the Muslims, so how is the prayer? They said: Ask Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. So he asked him, and he said: «He stands and says takbīr four times, then recites the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah from the mufaṣṣal, then says takbīr and bows; that makes five. Then he stands and recites the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah from the mufaṣṣal, then says takbīr four times and bows at the last of them; that makes nine in the two festival prayers.» None of them objected to that."],[9477,"Al-Walīd said: The festival has arrived, so what should I do? Ibn Masʿūd said: «Say Allāhu akbar, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate to Allah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate to Allah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate; then say takbīr and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah; then say takbīr and bow and prostrate. Then stand and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and supplicate; then say takbīr, praise Allah, extol Him, invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and bow and prostrate.» Ḥudhayfah and Abū Mūsā said: He is correct."],[9478,"About the takbīr in prayer on the day of Fiṭr and Aḍḥā. One said: Ask this one, and the other said: Ask this one, until Ḥudhayfah said to him: Ask this one, meaning ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿūd. So he asked him, and Ibn Masʿūd said: «He says takbīr four times, then recites, then says takbīr and bows, then says takbīr in the second, then recites, then says takbīr four times after the recitation.»"],[9479,"«Ibn Masʿūd used to say takbīr nine times in the two festival prayers: four before the recitation, then he would say takbīr and bow; and in the second he would recite, and when he finished he would say takbīr four times, then bow.»"],[9480,"He «used to say takbīr nine times on Aḍḥā and Fiṭr: he would stand and say takbīr four times, then recite, then say one takbīr and bow with it, then stand and recite and say four takbīrs, bowing with one.»"],[9481,"He used to say the takbir in the first (rakʿah) five times: with the takbir of the rakʿah and the takbir of commencement, and in the other four times, with the takbir of the rakʿah."],[9482,"Al-Ashʿari said: Ask ʿAbd Allah, for he is the most learned and the earliest of us. So he asked him, and he said: You begin with four, and you finish with four, and you say one takbir, then you add three to it, then you say takbir and bow. When you raise from the prostration, you recite, then you say four takbirs, then you bow."],[9483,"The takbir in the two ʿIds is four, like the prayer over the deceased."],[9484,"Indeed between every two takbirs there is the measure of a word."],[9485,"They both would make anyone they saw praying before the imam's departure on the ʿId sit down."],[9486,"About the prayer before the imam's departure."],[9487,"That anyone should pray before the imam."],[9488,"\"About the prayer on the day of Eid before the Imam's departure.\""],[9489,"Ibn Masʿud would not pray before it (the ʿId prayer) and would pray after it four rakʿahs."],[9490,"Ibn Masʿud would pray after it four rakʿahs or eight, and he would not pray before it."],[9491,"Ibn Masʿud would pray four (rakʿahs) after the two ʿIds."],[9492,"He would pray four (rakʿahs) after the two ʿIds."],[9493,"ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud said: Whoever misses the ʿId, let him pray four (rakʿahs)."],[9494,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: \"Whoever misses the Eid prayer should pray four rak'ahs.\""],[9495,"He used to say the takbir from the dawn prayer on the Day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice."],[9496,"A mudd of wheat or a sa' of dates or barley."],[9497,"I performed ghusl with Ibn Mas'ud on the Day of Arafah under the arak tree."],[9498,"Abdullah used to say: \"The takbir during the days of Tashriq is after the dawn prayer from the Day of Arafah until after the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice.\""],[9499,"He used to say the takbir in the dawn prayer on the Day of Arafah and stop after the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice, saying takbir when he prayed the afternoon prayer.\" He said: And he used to say: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illa Allah, wa Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, wa lillahi al-hamd."],[9500,"Abdullah: \"If I had recited it as 'fas'a' (walk briskly), I would have walked briskly until my cloak fell off. And he used to recite it 'famdu' (proceed).\""],[9501,"In the words of Ibn Mas'ood, \"Proceed to the remembrance of Allah, which is like His saying: 'Indeed, your efforts are diverse.'”"],[9502,"He asked Ubayy b. Ka'b, while the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon, about a verse from the Book of Allah. Ubayy turned away from him and did not reply. When he finished his prayer, he said: \"You did not perform the Friday prayer properly.\" So Ibn Mas'ud asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Ubayy spoke the truth.\""],[9503,"Abdullah said to him: \"What you asked about is your share of the Friday prayer.\""],[9504,"To say to your companion 'Be quiet' when the imam has come out for the Friday prayer."],[9505,"I prayed with Zirr and he led me, but we missed the Friday prayer. I asked Ibrahim, and he said: \"Abdullah did that with 'Alqamah and al-Aswad.\" Sufyan said: \"Sometimes I and al-A'mash did it.\""],[9506,"Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Friday prayer should add another to it, and whoever misses the two rak'ahs should pray four."],[9507,"Whoever catches the rakʿah has caught Jumuʿah, and whoever does not catch the rakʿah should pray four."],[9508,"Whoever catches the two rakʿahs or one of them has caught Jumuʿah, and whoever misses the two rakʿahs should pray four? He said: \"Yes.\""],[9509,"Whoever catches the khutbah, then Jumuʿah is two rakʿahs, and whoever does not catch it should pray four, and whoever does not catch the rakʿah should not rely on the prostration until he catches the rakʿah."],[9510,"\"Whoever misses the last rakʿah should pray four.\" Maʿmar said: Qatādah said: He prays four. It was said to Qatādah that Ibn Masʿūd came while they were sitting at the end of the prayer, and he said to his companions: \"Sit, you have caught it, if Allah wills.\" Qatādah said: \"He only means: 'You have caught the reward.'\""],[9511,"that we should pray four rakʿahs after Jumuʿah, until we heard the statement of ʿAlī: \"Pray six.\" Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \"So we pray six.\" ʿAṭāʾ said: \"Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān prays two rakʿahs then four.\""],[9512,"that we should pray four before Jumuʿah and four after it, until ʿAlī ؓ came and ordered us to pray two rakʿahs after it, then four."],[9513,"that we should pray four before Jumuʿah and four after it, until ʿAlī came and ordered us to pray two rakʿahs after it, then four."],[9514,"\"Make it six.\""],[9515,"\"Ibn Masʿūd prayed on the day of Jumuʿah, after the imam had said the salām, four rakʿahs.\""],[9516,"Abū Isḥāq: \"ʿAlī used to pray six rakʿahs after Jumuʿah.\""],[9517,"\"Ibn Masʿūd used to pray four after Jumuʿah.\""],[9518,"\"We used to pray Jumuʿah with ʿAbd Allah, then return and take a siesta.\""],[9519,"We used to gather with Ibn Masʿūd, then we would return and take a midday nap."],[9520,"I saw ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd patrolling the mosque at night. He would remove anyone he saw in it as a dark figure, except a man standing in prayer."],[9521,"\"Your imam should come forward.\" We said, \"Our imam is not here.\" He said, \"Let one of you come forward.\" So a man came forward and stood on a bench in the qiblah of the mosque, and ʿAbd Allāh forbade him."],[9522,"that he lead them from an elevated place.\""],[9523,"ʿAbd Allāh said, \"The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing to remain is prayer. There will surely be people who pray yet have no religion.\""],[9524,"Fasting is from the sighting of the crescent to its sighting; if it is obscured from you, then thirty days."],[9525,"I came to Abdullah bin Masood and said, \"Some people in the neighborhood and some of our neighbors are fasting today.\" He asked, \"Did they see the crescent?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"Because it is more beloved to me to break my fast for a day in Ramadan and then make it up, than to fast for a day in Sha'ban.\""],[9526,"\"You had been in a state of major ritual impurity, so prayer was not lawful for you. Then you performed ghusl, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you, so fast.\""],[9527,"He came to the mosque of the neighborhood after they had prayed Fajr and said to them—that was in Ramadan—\"I had intercourse with my wife, then sleep overcame me, and I entered the morning without having performed ghusl. What do you think?\" The people said to him, \"We think you have broken your fast.\" So he went to ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd and said to them, \"I have come to one who is better than you or more knowledgeable.\" He said, \"Breaking the fast is only from food and drink, so complete your fast.\""],[9528,"\"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, I was in a state of major ritual impurity and did not perform ghusl until morning.\" ʿAbd Allāh said, \"You had been in a state of major ritual impurity, so prayer was not lawful for you. Then you performed ghusl, so prayer became lawful for you, and fasting became lawful for you.\" That was in Ramadan."],[9529,"\"If I had intercourse with a woman at night, then deliberately left the ghusl until morning, it would not prevent me from fasting. I only had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9530,"\"If I had intercourse with a woman at night, then deliberately left the ghusl until morning, that would not prevent me from fasting, because I only had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9531,"\"If I had intercourse with my wife at the beginning of the night, then entered the morning in a state of major ritual impurity, I would still fast, because I had intercourse with her while she was lawful to me.\""],[9532,"If I were in a state of major ritual impurity and stayed for a month not finding water, I would not pray until I found water."],[9533,"Sufyān: This is not to be taken."],[9534,"Ibn Masʿūd would fondle his wife in the middle of the day while he was fasting."],[9535,"Ibn Masʿūd: Whoever breaks his fast on a day in Ramadan without a dispensation will meet Allah with that, even if he fasts the entire age; if He wills He will forgive him, and if He wills He will punish him."],[9537,"Fasting is only from what enters, and not from what exits; and ablution is from what exits, and not from what enters."],[9538,"We had the predawn meal with ʿAbd Allāh, then we went out and the prayer was called."],[9539,"If food or drink is offered to one of you while he is fasting, he should say: I am fasting."],[9540,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd: Seek the Night of Decree on the night of the seventeenth, the morning of Badr, or the twenty-first night, or the twenty-third."],[9541,"May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He knew that it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from the people so that they would not rely on it. By the One who sent down the Book to Muḥammad ﷺ, it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. We observed and memorized it. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception. I said to Zirr: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises on that morning like a basin, with no rays."],[9542,"May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. By Allah, he knew that it is in Ramadan, but he disliked that they should rely on it, or he loved that they should not rely on it. By Allah, it is indeed in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night—he swore without making an exception. He said: I said: O Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. Ḥammād said: I said to ʿĀṣim: What is the sign? He said: The sun rises on the morning after that night without rays, like a basin, until it rises high."],[9543,"Tell me about the Night of Decree, for ʿAbd Allāh says: Whoever stands in prayer the whole year will attain it. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He knows that it is in Ramadan, but he concealed it from the people so that they would not rely on it. By Allah, it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: Abū al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us. We counted and memorized that it is indeed it. ʿĀṣim said: I said to Zirr: What is that sign? He said: The sun rises white like a basin, with no rays, until it rises high. He said: I observed it many times like that."],[9544,"It is in Ramadan, and it is the twenty-seventh night. I said: How did you know that? He said: By the sign that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us. We counted and memorized. By Allah, it is indeed it, without exception."],[9545,"\"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh.\" I said, \"O Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that?\" He said, \"By the verse about which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, so I memorized it and counted it. By the One who sent down the Book upon Muhammad, it is the night of the twenty-seventh.\""],[9546,"\"Narrate to me, for I used to love meeting you, and I did not come except to meet you. So narrate to me about the Night of Decree, for Ibn Masʿud says: 'Whoever stands the whole year in prayer will attain it or reach it.' Ubayy said: 'He knew that it is in Ramadan, but he loved to keep it hidden from you. It is the night of the twenty-seventh, based on the verse about which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, so we memorized it and learned it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would continue it until dawn, and when it was one day before or one day after, he would ascend and look at the sun and say: \"The sun rises on its morning without rays until it rises high.\"'\","],[9547,"Ubayy said, \"May Allah have mercy on Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman. He knew that it is in the month of Ramadan on the night of the twenty-seventh, but he loved that they not rely on it.\""],[9548,"\"Whoever stands the entire month of Ramadan in prayer will attain it.\" He said, \"Then I came to Madinah and mentioned that to Ubayy. He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I know which night it is - the night that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to stand in prayer.' He said, 'So I asked him about it, and he said: \"The night of the twenty-seventh.\"' Abda said, 'So when the month was thirty days, we stood three nights after it, and when it was twenty-nine, we stood two nights after it.'\""],[9549,"\"Abdullah used to lead us in prayer during the month of Ramadan and would leave while it was still night.\""],[9550,"That he said, \"For twenty-five camels, a bint makhad; if not available, then a male ibn labun?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[9551,"\"You have no stipend from me. Your stipend is only from your fay' and your jizya, and charity is for its people.\" When they kept coming back to him, he brought the keys to ʿUthman and threw them, saying, \"I am not a treasurer.\""],[9552,"\"When they reach the age of maturity, inform them about the obligation of paying Zakat. If they wish, guide them to fulfill it, and if they wish to leave it, then let them.\""],[9553,"He said to him, \"You owe zakat of such-and-such for a year.\""],[9554,"\"He used to give us the stipend, then take its zakat.\""],[9555,"\"In my care are orphans, so shall I give it to them?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[9556,"\"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, is there zakat on my jewelry?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"I have a nephew who is an orphan, so shall I put it for them?\" He said, \"Put it for them.\""],[9557,"\"Whoever earns lawfully, withholding zakat corrupts it, and whoever earns unlawfully, zakat does not purify it.\""],[9558,"“When one of you follows a funeral, let him take hold of all sides of the bier, for that is from the Sunnah; then afterwards let him volunteer or leave off.” And the wording is that of the hadith of Abū Nuʿaym."],[9559,"“That you carry by the four sides of the bier, then volunteer or leave off.”"],[9560,"“That you take hold of the four sides of the bier, then volunteer afterwards or leave off.”"],[9563,"“Indeed your companion is impure, so perform ghusl from it; otherwise, wudu suffices you.”"],[9564,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “No recitation or speech has been prescribed for us over the funeral. Say takbir as the imam says takbir, and increase in the best of speech.”"],[9565,"“To tread on a live coal is more beloved to me than to tread on the grave of a Muslim man.”"],[9566,"“No recitation or speech has been prescribed for us in the funeral prayer. Say takbir as the imam says takbir, and increase in good speech.”"],[9567,"ʿAbd Allāh said: “Do not buy fish in water, for it is uncertainty.”"],[9568,"“Riba is seventy-some odd doors.”"],[9569,"“A transaction within two transactions is riba.”"],[9570,"“Pure, without intercourse.”"],[9571,"“(She must be) pure without intercourse. If he wishes to divorce her according to the Sunnah three times, he divorces her once in a period of purity, then she must observe a menstrual period after the final divorce.”"],[9572,"“That he divorce according to the Sunnah as Allah ﷻ commanded him: let him divorce her when she is pure without intercourse.”"],[9573,"Abd Allah b. Masʿud said regarding {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at their prescribed periods}: “The divorce at the prescribed period is that you divorce her when she is pure, then leave her until she completes her waiting period, or take her back if you wish.” Shuʿbah said: The people of Kufa say: “without intercourse.”"],[9574,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {divorce them at their prescribed periods}: He said: “Whoever intends the divorce that is truly a divorce should give her time, so that when the woman becomes pure from menses he divorces her while pure without intercourse.”"],[9575,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding His saying {divorce them at their prescribed periods}: He said: Whoever intends the divorce that is truly a divorce should give the woman time until she becomes pure without intercourse. He says to her: “Observe your waiting period.” If he regrets it and his soul follows her, he calls two men to witness her return; otherwise he leaves her until her waiting period ends. He should not divorce her three times while she is pregnant, for Allah would cause him to regret it, and he would have to spend on her during her pregnancy and breastfeeding.”"],[9576,"O Commander of the Believers, my husband divorced me, and my bleeding ceased for three menstrual periods. Then he came to me after I had placed my water (for ghusl), closed my door, and taken off my clothes, and said: “I have taken you back, I have taken you back.” Umar said to Ibn Masʿud: “What do you think about her?” He said: “I think she is his wife as long as prayer has not become lawful for her.” Umar said: “And I think that too.”"],[9577,"The woman said: “Indeed, what happened from you did not make me report the matter as it really was.” Umar said: “Tell me.” She said: “He divorced me, then left me until I was in the last of three menstrual periods and my bleeding stopped. I prepared my ghusl, closed my door, and took off my clothes. Then he knocked on the door and said: ‘I have taken you back, I have taken you back.’ So I left my ghusl and put on my clothes.” Umar said: “What do you say about her, O Ibn Umm ʿAbd?” I said: “I see that he has more right to her as long as prayer has not become lawful for her.” Umar said: “What a good opinion you have, and I think that too.”"],[9579,"Uthman sent to my father asking him about her. My father said: “How can a hypocrite give a fatwa?” Uthman said: “We seek refuge in Allah from your being a hypocrite, and we seek refuge in Allah from calling you a hypocrite. We seek refuge in Allah that such a thing should exist in Islam, then he should die without clarifying it.” He said: “I think he has more right to her until she performs ghusl after the third menses and prayer becomes lawful for her.” I do not know but that Uthman adopted that."],[9580,"A man divorced his wife once. She menstruated three times. When she sat down to perform ghusl, her husband came and took her back. She said: “You have no right to that.” They went to Ibn Masʿud, and he made her swear by Allah, besides whom there is no god, that he had taken her back after prayer had become lawful for her. She did not swear, so he returned her to him."],[9581,"If she has been entered upon, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."],[9582,"From ʿAbd Allah regarding a man who divorces his wife three times before consummating the marriage. He said: “ʿAbd Allah considered her in the position of one with whom the marriage has been consummated.”"],[9583,"That the menstruation had ceased from her but that was not clear, she should wait a year; if she does not menstruate during it, she observes the waiting period after the year of three months. If she menstruates during the three months, she observes the waiting period by menstruation. If she menstruates but her menstruation is not completed after she has observed those three months following the year, he said: “Do not hasten against her until you know whether her menstruation is completed or not.”"],[9584,"Yes, so he married her and she bore him a child. Then he came to Umar and asked him, and he said: “Separate between them.” He said: She has borne him a child. He said: “Even if she bears ten, separate between them.”"],[9585,"Concerning the woman gifted (in marriage): “If they accept her, it is one (divorce), and she is more entitled to herself; if they do not accept her, it is nothing.”"],[9586,"\"If they accept it, then it is a clear one.\""],[9587,"A man says to his wife: “Your affair is in your hand,” or “Seek success in your affair,” or he gifts her to her family and they accept it: it is one irrevocable divorce."],[9588,"\"Allah ﷻ has clearly explained divorce, so whoever divorces as Allah ﷻ has commanded, it has been made clear to him. And whoever took upon himself the clothing of someone else, we made it his clothing, and Allah is not burdening you with what you say upon yourselves.\" He said, \"And we see the statement of Ibn Sirin as an expression that I do not remember well, as he said, 'If he had the women of the people of the earth, then he said, 'All of them have gone away.'\""],[9589,"“It is as you said.” Then a man came to him and said: I divorced my wife the number of the stars. He said: “Did you say it once?” He said: Yes. He said: “Do you want her to be separated from you?” He said: Yes. He said: Then Abdullah mentioned at that point the women of the people of the earth with something I do not remember. Then Abdullah said: “Allah has made clear to you how divorce is. Whoever divorces as Allah commanded him, it has been made clear to him. Whoever confuses, we assign to him his confusion. By Allah, you will not confuse yourselves and we will bear it for you. It is as you say.”"],[9590,"I divorced my wife ninety-nine times, and I asked and was told that she has become separated from me. Ibn Mas'ud said: “They loved that separation be made between you and her.” He said: What do you say, may Allah have mercy on you? He thought that he would grant him a concession. He said: “Three separate her from you, and the rest of them are aggression.”"],[9591,"I divorced my wife ninety times, and I have a child from her, and some people want to separate me and my family. Abdullah said: “Three are sufficient for you, and the rest of them are aggression.”"],[9592,"“Concerning the prohibited (utterance), it is an oath that he expiates.”"],[9593,"“Concerning the prohibited (utterance), the expiation of an oath.”"],[9594,"Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: “Concerning the prohibited (utterance), the expiation of an oath.”"],[9595,"That you touch them, and he did not say: When you divorce the believing women then you marry them."],[9596,"God has indeed made clear. Whoever approaches the matter from its proper aspect, it has been made clear to him; and whoever opposes, then by God, we cannot oppose you."],[9597,"If four months have passed, it is īlāʾ."],[9598,"And he said: When four months have passed, then acknowledge one pronouncement of divorce."],[9599,"ʿAlī, Ibn Masʿūd and Ibn ʿAbbās said: When the four months have passed, it is one pronouncement of divorce and she is more entitled to herself. Qatādah said: ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd said: She observes the waiting period of a divorced woman."],[9600,"She has become irrevocably separated from you, so propose to her on her own behalf. So he proposed to her on her own behalf and gave her a riṭl of silver as a bridal gift."],[9601,"This verse which is in the shorter Sūrat al-Nisāʾ, {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden}, was revealed after the one in al-Baqarah, {And those of you who die and leave behind wives}, the verse. He said: And it reached him that ʿAlī said: It is the later of the two terms. And he said that."],[9602,"Whoever wishes, I will invoke mutual cursing with him: The verse {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden} was not revealed except after the verse of the woman whose husband died, {And those of you who die and leave behind wives, they shall wait concerning themselves four months and ten days}."],[9603,"The shorter Sūrat al-Nisāʾ was revealed after four months and ten days."],[9604,"The waiting period of a divorced woman is from the time she is divorced, and of a woman whose husband has died from the time he dies. And whoever wishes, I will swear with him that the shorter sūrah was revealed after al-Baqarah."],[9605,"The shorter sūrah was revealed after the longer one, meaning al-Nisāʾ."],[9606,"{...that they deliver their burden} after the one in al-Baqarah {And those of you who die and leave behind wives, they shall wait concerning themselves}."],[9607,"ʿAbd Allāh said: Do you think that if four months and ten days pass and she has not delivered her burden? They said: Until she delivers. Then ʿAbd Allāh said: So you impose hardship on her and do not give her the concession. The verse of the shorter sūrah was revealed after the longer one: {And for those who are pregnant, their term is that they deliver their burden}. When she delivers her burden, the waiting period has ended."],[9608,"\"But his paternal uncle did not say this.\" He said: \"So I met Malik b. ʿAmir al-Hamdani and asked him, and he began to recall the hadith of Subayʿah. I said: 'I am not asking you about that. Did you hear Ibn Masʿud say anything about it?' He said: 'Yes. They mentioned that in his presence, and he said: \"What do you say if she gives birth before the end of four months and ten days?\" We said: \"She must wait until the four months and ten days have passed.\" He said: \"And what do you say if the four months and ten days pass before she gives birth?\" We said: \"Until she gives birth.\" He said: \"You impose the strict ruling upon her but do not grant her the concession. The shorter Surah al-Nisaʾ was revealed after the longer one: {And those who are pregnant}\" '\""],[9609,"\"There was between me and my wife what occurs between people. She said: 'If the authority you have over my affair were in my hand, you would know what I would do.' He said: 'Then the authority I have over your affair is in your hand.' She said: 'Then you are divorced three times.' He said: 'I consider it one, and you are more entitled to take her back.' And I will meet the Commander of the Believers ʿUmar. So he met him and related the story to him. He said: 'May God do to the men, may God do to the men! They take what God placed in their hands and put it into the hands of women. May dust fill her mouth! What did you say?' He said: 'I said: \"I consider it one, and he is more entitled to her.\"' He said: 'And I think that. If you had thought otherwise, I would have considered that you were wrong.'\" Mansur said: \"I said to Ibrahim: 'But Ibn ʿAbbas used to say: May God cause her star to err; if she had said, \"I have divorced myself.\"' Ibrahim said: 'They are the same.'\""],[9610,"\"There was between me and my wife some words. She said: 'If the authority over my affair were in my hand, you would know what I would do.' I said: 'Then I call you to witness that the authority you have over your affair, which I possess, is in your hand.' She said: 'Then you are divorced three times.' Ibn Masʿud said: 'So it is one, and you are more entitled to her. And I will ask the Commander of the Believers about that.' So he rode and met ʿUmar and related the story to him. He said: 'May stones fill her mouth! May God do to the men and do—they take what God placed in their hands regarding the affair of women and place it in their hands. What do you think?' I said: 'I consider it one, and he is more entitled to her.' He said: 'Yes, what you have considered is good. Had you considered otherwise, you would have been wrong.'\""],[9611,"ʿUmar: \"And I think that.\""],[9612,"\"If she decides something, then she has no authority.\""],[9613,"\"If she chooses her husband, it is nothing; and if she chooses herself, then it is one.\""],[9614,"ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud: \"If she chooses herself, then it is one; and if she chooses her husband, then it is nothing.\""],[9615,"That ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud said regarding \"your affair is in your hand\": \"If she chooses herself, then it is one, and he is more entitled to her; and if she chooses her husband, then it is nothing.\""],[9616,"ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿud: \"If she chooses her husband, there is no harm; and if she chooses herself, then it is one, and he has the right of return over her.\""],[9617,"\"It is three.\""],[9618,"\"They gather during the day, then each one of them returns to her house at night.\""],[9620,"ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud: \"If he slanders her after having divorced her while he has the right of return over her, he invokes the liʿan against her; and if he slanders her after having divorced her with a final divorce, he does not invoke the liʿan against her.\""],[9621,"The two who invoke curses upon one another will never come together."],[9622,"The entire inheritance of the child of a woman who has invoked curses belongs to his mother."],[9623,"From 'Ali and Ibn Mas'ud, they said: \"The paternal relatives of the child of a woman who has invoked curses are the paternal relatives of his mother.\""],[9624,"\"If Allah took a covenant for a soul in the loins of a man and then poured it upon a rock, He would bring it out from that rock. So if you wish, complete it; and if you wish, do not practice coitus interruptus.\""],[9625,"Regarding coitus interruptus: \"It is the hidden female infant buried alive.\""],[9626,"\"Ibn Mas'ud disliked combining two sisters in the possession of one's right hand.\""],[9628,"\"And I dislike that your slave woman be a polytheist.\""],[9629,"We disagreed about the recitation of this letter: {And He knows what you do} or do you do? So I came to Ibn Mas'ud to ask him about that. While I was with him, a man came to him and said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, a man committed adultery with his wife, then they repented and made amends.\" So 'Abdullah recited this verse: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds, and He knows what you do}."],[9630,"\"They are fornicators as long as they are together.\" It was said to Ibn Mas'ud: \"What if they repent?\" He said: {And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds}. Ibn Mas'ud kept repeating it until I said: \"Indeed, he sees no harm in it.\""],[9631,"About misdeeds} the verse"],[9633,"that he said, “They are two fornicators as long as they are together.”"],[9634,"Ibn Mas'ud and Aisha both said, \"They will continue to be adulterers as long as they continue to meet.\""],[9635,"\"Ibn Mas'ud disliked a slave woman and her mother.\""],[9636,"“Half the punishment will be upon her, but she will not receive half the concession.”"],[9637,"“The slave woman is to be confirmed free of pregnancy by one menstrual period.”"],[9638,"“Divorce and the waiting period pertain to the woman.”"],[9639,"“Divorce pertains to men, and the waiting period pertains to women.”"],[9640,"“If she is freed while married to a slave and does not know that she has the option, or is not given the choice until her husband is freed or until he dies or she dies, they inherit from one another.”"],[9641,"Ibn Masʿūd said, “The likeness of the one who frees his concubine and then marries her is like the likeness of the one who offers his camel as a sacrificial animal and then rides it.”"],[9642,"“Selling her is her divorce.”"],[9644,"“If you must do it, then place it in the share of her child.”"],[9645,"Omar, we definitely find this to be true. I don't desire anything, and yet I am told that I only go to the daughters of so-and-so to look at them. At this point, Abdullah bin Mas'ood said to him, \"Didn't you know that Ibrahim complained to Allah about the nature of Sarah's womb? It was said to him, 'She was created from a rib, so wear her according to what she had in her, as long as it does not bring disgrace upon her in her religion.'\" Upon hearing this, Omar said, \"Indeed, Allah has filled your heart with much knowledge.\""],[9646,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd said concerning a virgin who fornicates with a virgin, “They are each to be flogged one hundred lashes and banished for a year.”"],[9647,"Ibn Masʿūd said concerning a man who has intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, “If he forced her, she is freed and he is fined her equivalent; and if she willingly obeyed him, he keeps her and is fined her equivalent.”"],[9648,"Then we will stone you if you have been married before. They said, 'He only came to his wife's slave woman.' ʿAbd Allah said, 'If you forced her, then set her free and give your wife a slave woman in her place.' He said, 'By Allah, I forced her and struck her.' He did not stone him, and he ordered that he be flogged below the prescribed punishment."],[9650,"It is not lawful for this slave woman to be stripped, stretched out, shackled, or fettered."],[9651,"Her embracing Islam is her marital chastity."],[9652,"ʿAbd Allah: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you} Set free a slave."],[9653,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I swore that I would not sleep on my bed for a year. ʿAbd Allah recited this verse: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things that Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors.} Expiate your oath and sleep on your bed. He said, 'I am wealthy.' He said, 'Set free a slave.'"],[9654,"Umar said to Ibn Masʿud, 'What are these people saying?' He said, 'I did that.' He said, 'Did you see that?' He said, 'Yes.' They said, 'We came to summon him, and there he was asking him.'"],[9655,"On the servants of Allah, as much as you are able."],[9656,"From ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud regarding a virgin who is coerced: A virgin is entitled to the equivalent of the dower of one of her women, and a previously married woman is entitled to the equivalent dower of someone like her."],[9657,"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said regarding a slave woman who is forced: \"If she was a virgin, then one-tenth of her price, and if she was previously married, then half of one-tenth of her price.\""],[9658,"From Ali and Ibn Mas'ud: they said: \"A small or large amount of suckling makes marriage unlawful.\""],[9659,"Ali and Ibn Mas'ud said regarding suckling: \"A small or large amount of it makes marriage unlawful.\""],[9660,"Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: \"A woman given three divorces is entitled to lodging and maintenance.\""],[9661,"\"Like the departure of people who leave at dawn after the Fajr prayer.\""],[9662,"\"You and your companions eat one-third, give one-third as charity, and send one-third to the family of my brother Utbah.\" It was said to Sufyan: \"Is it voluntary?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[9663,"You hear Allah say: {The Hajj is in months well-known}. I do not consider these except to be the months of Hajj."],[9664,"\"The impotent man is given a year's delay; if he consummates with her, then fine, otherwise they are separated.\""],[9665,"\"The impotent man is given a year's delay.\""],[9666,"\"The engagement will be postponed for a year, if they agree to it. Otherwise, they will be separated and she will get the alimony.\""],[9667,"\"Whoever divorces in jest or marries in jest, it is valid.\""],[9668,"He used to say: \"The sexual intercourse of her master does not make her lawful for her husband until she marries another husband.\""],[9669,"Allah ﷻ has prohibited twelve women, and I dislike twelve: the slave woman and her mother; the two sisters being combined; the slave woman when your father has had intercourse with her; the slave woman when your son has had intercourse with her; the slave woman when she commits adultery; the slave woman in the waiting period of another; the slave woman who has a husband; your slave woman who is a polytheist; your paternal aunt and maternal aunt through suckling."],[9670,"He gave him nabīdh to drink from a green jar. Abu Wāʾil said: “I have seen that jar.”"],[9671,"“I used to prepare nabīdh for ʿAbdullāh in a green jar while he watched it, and he would drink from it.”"],[9672,"\"A man from the people said, 'Has it really been revealed like this?' So Abdullah said, 'Woe to you! I have indeed recited it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said to me, \"You have done well.\"' While he was talking, he smelled the odor of alcohol from him. So Abdullah said, 'Do you drink alcohol and deny the Quran? I will not stand until you are lashed with the punishment.'\""],[9673,"A man said, “It was not revealed like that.” I drew close to him and detected the smell of wine from him. I said, “Do you deny the truth and drink impurity? By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it like this. I will not leave you until I impose the prescribed punishment on you.” So he imposed the prescribed punishment on him."],[9674,"ʿAbdullāh said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, would not place your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9676,"One of us fell ill, and suk r was prescribed for him. We came to ʿAbdullāh and asked him. He said: “Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has not placed your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9677,"Ibn Masʿūd said: “Do not give your children [nabīdh] to drink. They were born upon the fiṭrah. Would you give them to drink what is not lawful for them? Their sin is upon the one who gave it to them to drink, for Allah, Mighty and Exalted, has not placed your healing in what He has forbidden you.”"],[9678,"“Those who fall from mountaintops, are eaten by wild beasts, or drown in the seas are martyrs in the sight of Allah.”"],[9679,"About a man who manumitted his slave at death while he had no other wealth and owed a debt, he said: “He should work to earn his value.”"],[9680,"“A slave girl of mine nursed a son of mine, and I want to sell her.” Ibn Masʿūd detested that and said: “Would that the one to whom I sell her were called the mother of my child.”"],[9681,"From its owner: “If its owner comes, he is given the choice: if he chooses the reward, it is his; if he chooses his property, his property is his.” Ibn Masʿūd said: “Thus do with lost property.” The wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq."],[9682,"“Those are the two times: withholding during life and squandering at death.”"],[9683,"“That one of you should die leaving neither kin nor relatives. What prevents him, when that is the case, from placing his wealth among the poor or the needy?”"],[9684,"My uncle bequeathed his estate to me, and this is part of his estate. May I buy it? He said: \"No, and do not borrow anything from their wealth.\""],[9685,"O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, shall I buy this horse? He said: \"What is the matter with it?\" He said: Its owner bequeathed it to me. He said: \"Do not buy it, and do not borrow anything from his wealth.\""],[9686,"Quasi-intentional killing is with a stone, a stick, a whip, a push, or a throw, and everything with which you deliberately strike someone; in it there is aggravation in the blood money. And mistake is when you throw something and miss with it."],[9687,"Quasi-intentional killing is with a stone and a stick."],[9688,"From ʿAli and Ibn Masʿud, they said: \"Aggravation in quasi-intentional killing; one is not killed for it.\""],[9689,"Quasi-intentional killing is twenty-five hiqqahs, twenty-five jadhaʿahs, twenty-five bint makhads, and twenty-five bint labuns."],[9690,"“The blood money of one who killed by mistake is twenty Hiqqah (three-year-old she camels), twenty Jadha'ah (four year old she camels), twenty Bint Makhad (one year old she camel), twenty Bint Labun (two year old she camels), and twenty Bani Makhad (one year old she camels).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2631)"],[9691,"Ibn Masʿud: \"For every pair of organs, the full blood money is due, and for every single organ, the full blood money is due.\""],[9692,"The two eyes are equal, the two testicles are equal, the fingers are equal, the teeth are equal, the two hands are equal, and the two feet are equal."],[9693,"Regarding a man and a woman: \"They are equal up to five camels.\" He said: And ʿAli said: \"Half of everything.\""],[9694,"Regarding a man from whom retaliation is taken and then he dies. He said: \"Upon the one who exacted retaliation is his blood money, then the blood money for his wound is deducted from it.\""],[9695,"ʿUmar said to Ibn Masʿud, while he was beside him: \"What do you say?\" Ibn Masʿud said: \"I say to him: He has been secured from execution.\" He said: Then he struck his shoulder and said: \"A vessel filled with knowledge.\""],[9696,"When death comes, it wipes out everything."],[9697,"Ibn Masʿūd [said]: \"The people of faith are the most restrained in killing.\""],[9698,"And ʿAlī also said it."],[9699,"He said: \"For every covenanted person, Magian or otherwise, the blood-money is payable in full.\""],[9700,"\"A slave of mine stole a cloak from another slave of mine. Is his hand to be amputated?\" He said: \"No. Your property, one part of it from another.\""],[9701,"Regarding spying: \"If it becomes clear to us\"—meaning, \"we shall enforce the punishment upon him.\""],[9702,"\"The hand is not to be amputated except for a dinar or ten dirhams.\""],[9703,"ʿAbd Allāh [said]: \"The hand is not to be amputated except for a dinar or ten dirhams.\""],[9704,"\"The shroud is to be taken from the entire estate.\""],[9705,"ʿAbd Allāh [said]: \"Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever.\" Al-Masʿūdī did not say it on the authority of his father."],[9706,"\"Whoever kills a snake or a scorpion has killed a disbeliever.\" Isrāʾīl did not trace it back to the Prophet, but Sharīk did trace it back."],[9707,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Kill snakes, for whoever fears their retaliation is not of me.\""],[9708,"A Muslim has six duties of kindness toward another Muslim: he greets him with salām when he meets him, answers him when he invites him, says \"May God have mercy on you\" when he sneezes, attends his funeral when he dies, gives him sincere counsel in his absence, and loves for him what he loves for himself. Abū Jaʿfar al-Farrāʾ did not trace it back to the Prophet, but Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī did trace it back."],[9709,"A time will come upon people when a man will come to a grave and say, “Would that I were in the place of its occupant.” It is not out of love for meeting Allah, but because of the affliction he sees."],[9710,"A time will certainly come upon you when a man will pass by a grave and say, “Would that I were in the place of this one,” while he has no love for meeting Allah, but because of the severity of the affliction he sees. It was said, “What is best at that time?” He said, “A sturdy horse and a weapon with which a man can go wherever he goes.”"],[9711,"“For a camel smeared with tar to crowd against me is more beloved to me than for a perfumed woman to crowd against me.”"],[9712,"“For a man to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry.”"],[9713,"Abdullah: “Strip the Quran bare, and do not mix with it what is not part of it.”"],[9714,"“The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing you will lose of your religion is prayer.”"],[9715,"“The trumpet is like a horn into which it is blown.”"],[9716,"Abdullah: “Mix with people and keep away from them.”"],[9717,"“Mix with people and be sincere with them regarding what they desire, but as for your religion, do not let them touch it.”"],[9718,"There was a man who had wealth and never did any good with it. When death came to him, he said to his family, “When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind.” So that was done to him. Then Allah gathered him and said, “What made you do what you did?” He said, “Out of fear of You.” So Allah’s mercy reached him."],[9719,"Abdullah: “Do not ask the People of the Book about anything, for they will never guide you when they have already led themselves astray. Either they will tell you something true and you will disbelieve them, or something false and you will believe them.”"],[9720,"“Then your Prophet ﷺ will stand as the fourth of four.” Shuʿba said, “I only heard this in this hadith.”"],[9722,"\"Allah ﷻ will punish a people from among the people of faith, then remove them through the intercession of the intercessors.\" Then he said: \"These are those whom the intercession of the intercessors will not benefit.\""],[9724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: People will stand before the Lord of the Worlds for forty years, their eyes fixed, awaiting the decisive judgment, until sweat engulfs them from the severity of the distress. Then Allah ﷻ will descend, and the nations will kneel, and He will call out: O people, are you not content with your Lord who created you and commanded you to worship Him, then you turned away from Him and denied His favor, that He leaves you and what you turned to? Every person will turn to what he turned to. Then a caller will call out: Whoever used to turn to something, let him stick to it. He said: Then those who turned to a stone, or a piece of wood, or a riding animal will depart. Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Zayd b. Abi Unaysa."],[9725,"We conversed one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the talk kept us up. When morning came, we went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: The prophets were presented to me with their followers from their nations. There was a prophet ﷺ with a small group from his nation, and a prophet with no one. Allah has informed you about the people of Lot, for He said: {Is there not among you a man of right judgment?} He said: Until Moses b. Imran ﷺ passed by with those with him from the Children of Israel. I said: My Lord, where is my nation? He said: Look to your right. I looked and there were the hills, the hills of Makkah, filled with the faces of men. He said: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? I said: I am pleased, my Lord. He said: Look to your left. I looked and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. He said: Are you pleased, O Muhammad? I said: I am pleased, my Lord. He said: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan al-Asadi came and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me one of them. He said: \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Then another man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me one of them. He said: \"ʿUkkasha has preceded you to it.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"If you can, may my father and mother be your ransom, be among the seventy thousand, then be so. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the hills. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I have seen many people crowding together.\" Then he said: \"I hope that those who follow me from my nation will be a quarter of Paradise.\" The people said takbir. Then he said: \"I hope that they will be half of the people of Paradise.\" The people said takbir. Then he recited this verse: {A multitude of those from among the first, and a few from those of later times.} They discussed among themselves who these seventy thousand were. Some said: People born in Islam and died upon it. Then the matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"They are those who do not seek ruqyah, do not practice tiyarah, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[9726,"We spoke at length one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we went to him in the morning. He said: The prophets were presented to me with their nations. A prophet ﷺ would pass by with a small group, a prophet with a band, a prophet with a few, and a prophet with no one. Until Moses ﷺ passed by me with a large throng from the Children of Israel, and they impressed me. I said: Who are these? It was said: This is your brother Moses, and with him are the Children of Israel. I said: Where is my nation? It was said: Look to your right. I looked and the hills were filled with the faces of men. Then it was said to me: Look to your left. I looked and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. It was said to me: Are you pleased? I said: I am pleased, O Lord, I am pleased, O Lord. It was said to me: Indeed with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom. If you can be among the seventy thousand, then do so. If you fall short, then be among the people of the hills. If you fall short, then be among the people of the horizon. For I have seen people crowding together.\" Then ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan al-Asadi stood and said: Supplicate for me, O Messenger of Allah, that He make me among the seventy. So he supplicated for him. Then another man stood and said: Supplicate to Allah, O Messenger of Allah, that He make me among them. He said: \"ʿUkkasha has preceded you to it.\" He said: Then we discussed among ourselves who these seventy thousand were: People born in Islam until they died upon it. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not practice tiyarah, and upon their Lord they rely.\""],[9731,"By Allah, I am not more grieved over these two if they died than my grief over these two birds if they fell dead. Indeed I find for them what a parent finds for his child. But I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Hour will not be established until every tribe is ruled by its hypocrites.\" That is why I desired that we die before that time."],[9732,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The feet of the son of Adam will not move on the Day of Resurrection from before his Lord until he is asked about five things: his life, in what he spent it; his youth, in what he wore it away; his wealth, from where he earned it and on what he spent it; and what he did with what he knew."],[9733,"That this verse was revealed with Allah reproaching them except for four years: {And do not be like those who were given the Scripture before, and a long period passed over them, so their hearts hardened; and many of them are defiantly disobedient.}"],[9734,"The day seemed long to me, so I tried to remember whom I could talk to. He said: He began to narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I narrated to him. Then he started to narrate to me and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be a fitnah in which the one lying down is better than the one reclining, the one reclining is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one galloping. Its slain are all in the Fire.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, when will that be? He said: \"That will be in the days of al-harj.\" I said: When are the days of al-harj? He said: \"When a man does not trust his companion.\" I said: What do you command me to do if I live to see that time? He said: \"Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he enters my house? He said: \"Then enter your room.\" I said: What do you think if he enters my room? He said: \"Then enter your mosque and do like this,\" and he grasped his right hand on his wrist, \"and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that.\""],[9735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The last person to enter Paradise will walk on the bridge and will walk one step and then kneel. The fire will surround him, and when he surpasses it, he will turn towards it and say, 'Blessed is He who saved me from you. He has given me something that He has not given to anyone among the earlier and later people.' A tree will be raised for him, and he will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to this tree so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything other than this?' He will say, 'Yes, my Lord, but I will not ask You for anything other than this.' Allah will excuse him because He will see something that he cannot bear, and he will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to it so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Then a tree will be raised for him at the gate of Paradise, which is better than the first one. He will say, 'O Lord, bring me closer to this tree so that I may take shade under its shade and drink from its water.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, did you not make a covenant with Me that you would not ask Me for anything other than this?' He will say, 'Yes, my Lord, but I will not ask You for anything other than this.' Allah will excuse him because He will see something that he cannot bear, and He will bring him closer to it. He will then hear the voices of the people of Paradise, and he will say, 'O Lord, admit me to it.' Allah will say, 'O son of Adam, would it please you if I were to give you the entire world and a similar world along with it?' He will say, 'Are You making fun of me, though You are the Lord of all the worlds?' The Messenger of Allah laughed and then said, 'Do you not ask me why I laughed?' The person asked, 'Why did you laugh, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'I laughed at the laughter of the Lord of the worlds when He said, 'Do you make fun of Me, though You are the Lord of all the worlds?' He said, 'No, I am not making fun of you, but I can do whatever I will.'\""],[9736,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The deeds of the children of Adam are presented every Monday and every Thursday. He has mercy on those who show mercy and forgives those who seek forgiveness, then He leaves the people of rancor with their rancor.\""],[9737,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A time will surely come upon the people when you will envy a man for a light burden as you envy him today for abundant wealth and children, until one of you passes by the grave of his brother and rolls upon it as an animal rolls in its pasture, saying: Would that I were in his place. It is not out of longing for Allah nor for righteous deeds he has sent ahead, but only because of the affliction that befalls him."],[9738,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When a servant prays but does not complete his prayer—its humility and its bowing—and frequently turns around, it is not accepted from him. And whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, even if he is honorable in the sight of Allah.\""],[9739,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\""],[9740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A person is with the one he loves.”"],[9741,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was a witness over them as long as I was among them.”"],[9742,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to pray at the eclipse of the sun and the moon. And when you see that it has afflicted them, then hasten to prayer; for if it is the one you fear, it will occur while you are not heedless, and if it is not, you will have attained good and earned it."],[9743,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying and greeted him, and he gestured to me."],[9744,"From Abu Rafiʿ, the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, from ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, that the Prophet of God ﷺ said: “There was no prophet but he had disciples who guided by his guidance and followed his way. Then after them came successors who say what they do not do and do what you disapprove of. Whoever strives against them with his hand is a believer, whoever strives against them with his tongue is a believer, and whoever strives against them with his heart is a believer. Beyond that there is not even a mustard seed’s weight of faith.”"],[9745,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever has a need and brings it to people, his poverty will not be relieved; but if he brings it to God, may He be exalted, God will soon grant him sufficiency, either a delayed reward or immediate wealth.”"],[9747,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The Hour has drawn near, and they only increase in distance from it.”"],[9748,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Treat yourselves with cow’s milk, for I hope that God will place healing in it, for it grazes on trees.”"],[9749,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who, when he hears the call to prayer, says the takbir and bears witness that there is no god but God and bears witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, then says: ‘O God, give Muhammad the wasilah and the excellence, and place him in the highest rank, and in the chosen ones his love, and in those brought near his remembrance,’ but that intercession will be assured for him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[9750,"I heard Ibn Masʿud say: “When the Messenger of God ﷺ became angry, his cheeks would turn red.”"],[9751,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “God, may He be exalted, is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.”"],[9752,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, I think he was ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud, that the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to delay the noon prayer until cooler, for intense heat is from the blast of Hell."],[9753,"We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying in the midday heat, but he did not complain to us."],[9754,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When one of you fears the ruler, let him say: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, be a protector for me from the evil of so-and-so son of so-and-so—meaning the one he fears—and from the evil of the jinn and mankind and their followers, lest any of them transgress against me. Mighty is Your protection, and exalted is Your praise, and there is no god besides You."],[9755,"A rooster crowed in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and a man said: O Allah, curse him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not curse it and do not revile it, for it calls to prayer.\""],[9756,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The one who remembers Allah among the heedless is like the one who stands firm among those who flee.\""],[9757,"It was revealed concerning a group of Arabs who used to worship a group of jinn. The jinn accepted Islam, but the group of Arabs were unaware of it, regarding His saying: {Those whom they call upon seek means of access to their Lord}."],[9758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no believing servant from whose eyes tears flow, even if it were the size of a fly's head, out of fear of Allah, except that Allah will forbid him from the Fire.\""],[9759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The closest of people to me on the Day of Resurrection will be the one who sends the most blessings upon me.\""],[9760,"From ʿAbdullah, I do not know but that he raised it [to the Prophet]: \"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt, and she may not stipulate the divorce of her sister in order to empty what is in her plate.\""],[9761,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most virtuous? He said: \"Prayer at its appointed time.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Kindness to parents.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"That people are safe from your tongue.\" Then he fell silent, and if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9763,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which deeds are most virtuous. He said: \"Prayer at its proper time.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Then kindness to parents.\" I said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Jihad in the path of Allah.\" Then he fell silent, and if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9764,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? Or: Which deed is most beloved to Allah? He said: \"Prayer at its proper time.\" I said: Then which? He said: \"Kindness to parents.\" I said: Then which? He said: \"Then jihad in the path of Allah.\" And if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[9765,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ which deeds are most virtuous, and he said: \"Prayer at its proper time, then jihad in the path of Allah.\""],[9766,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time, then dutifulness to parents, then jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9767,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which deed is best?” He said, “The prayer at the beginning of its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.” It was said, “Then which?” He said, “Dutifulness to parents.” It was said, “Then which?” He said, “Jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9769,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its appointed time.” I said, “Then which?” He said, “Dutifulness to parents.” I said, “Then which?” He said, “Jihad in the cause of Allah.” Then he fell silent with me, and if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9770,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿUmayr, that Ibn Masʿud said: “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “Establishing the prayer at its time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.”"],[9771,"You asked me about what I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “The prayer at its proper time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9772,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.”"],[9773,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ was asked, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time.”"],[9774,"The prescribed prayer at its time and dutifulness to parents."],[9775,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayers at their times, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And the wording is from the hadith of Maʿmar, and the others are similar."],[9776,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “The prayer at its proper time, dutifulness to parents, and jihad in the cause of Allah.” And if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."],[9777,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ‘Which deeds are best?’ He said: ‘That you perform the prayer at its proper times.’ He said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ He said: ‘Then what?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ And if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me. The wording is that of the hadith of Ibrahim b. Tahman, and the others are similar to it."],[9779,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ‘Which deeds are best?’ He said: ‘Prayer at its time.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Struggle (jihad) in the path of Allah.’ By Allah, if I had asked him for more, he would have increased for me. I said: ‘Then which sin is greatest in the sight of Allah?’ He said: ‘That you set up a rival to Allah, while He created you.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘That you kill your child for fear that he will eat with you.’ I said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘That you commit adultery with your neighbor’s wife.’ It was not long before Allah sent down the confirmation of it: ‘And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery. And whoever does that will meet a penalty.’ Yazid b. Mu‘awiyah transmitted it well, while Hammad b. Salamah did not transmit it well."],[9781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, ‘Which deed is best?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents and prayer at its time.’ Za’idah traced it back to the Prophet, while Shu‘bah and Hammad b. Salamah stopped it at the companion."],[9782,"‘The prayers at their times.’"],[9783,"‘O Abu ‘Abd al-Rahman, which of the degrees of Islam is best?’ He said: ‘Prayer.’ He said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Zakat.’ He said: ‘Then which?’ He said: ‘Kindness to parents.’ He said: ‘Then with whom is a person (to be)?’ He said: ‘I think he said: ‘With the one he loves.’’"],[9784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us and then increased in his prayer or decreased. Mansur said, ‘It is Ibrahim who forgot, whether from ‘Alqamah or ‘Alqamah from ‘Abdullah b. Mas‘ud.’ ‘Abdullah said: ‘When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer and turned his face toward us, we said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?’ He said, ‘No.’ Then what he had done was mentioned to him, so he bent his leg, faced the qiblah, and prostrated twice. Then he turned away and said, ‘If something new had occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you. But I am a human being like you; I forget as you forget. So if I forget, remind me. And if any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek what is right, complete it upon that, then say the salam and prostrate twice.’’"],[9785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us a prayer in which he added or subtracted. When he finished his prayer, we said, ‘Has something been added to the prayer?’ He said, ‘What is that?’ We said, ‘You prayed with us such and such.’ So he turned, bent his legs, and prostrated twice. Then he turned his face toward us and said, ‘I am only a human being like you. So if I forget, remind me. And if any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek the right course, complete it, then prostrate twice.’"],[9786,"The Prophet ﷺ said: ‘If any of you doubts his prayer, let him seek what he thinks is right, complete it, then prostrate twice.’"],[9787,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted something. When he finished, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'If something had occurred, I would have informed you. I am only a human being; I forget just as you forget. So whoever among you prays and adds or omits something, let him seek what is correct, complete it, and prostrate twice for forgetfulness.'"],[9791,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and either he added or omitted something. Ibrahim said: 'By Allah, that came only from me.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'No.' We told him what he had done. He said: 'When a man adds or omits something, he should prostrate twice.' He then prostrated twice."],[9792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If one of you doubts in the obligatory prayer, let him seek what is correct, then prostrate twice for forgetfulness.'"],[9793,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If one of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what is correct and prostrate twice for forgetfulness while sitting.'"],[9794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted something. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' We said: 'You prayed such-and-such.' He then faced the qiblah, prostrated twice, and then said the salam."],[9795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the 'Asr prayer and rose in the fourth rak'ah without sitting until he prayed a fifth with us. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you prayed five with us.' He then faced the qiblah, said the takbir, and prostrated twice."],[9796,"'Alqamah prayed the 'Asr prayer with five rak'ahs. When he said the salam, we said: 'You prayed five.' He said to a man from al-Nakha' called Ibrahim b. Suwayd: 'Is that so, O one-eyed?' He said: 'Yes.' He then prostrated with us twice while standing, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam. Then he said: ''Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the 'Asr prayer with five rak'ahs. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' We said: 'You prayed five.' He said to a man called Dhu al-Shimalayn: 'Is that so, O Dhu al-Yadayn?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He then prostrated with us twice while sitting, then recited the tashahhud, then said the salam. Then he said: 'O people, I am only a human being like you; I forget just as you forget. So if I forget, remind me. And if one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know whether he added or omitted something, let him seek what is correct in that, complete it, and prostrate twice. For if anything were added to your prayer, I would have informed you.'"],[9797,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr or 'Asr. When he finished his prayer, it was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' He then faced the qiblah and prostrated twice. Then he said: 'I am only a human being; I forget just as you forget. So if one of you errs in his prayer, let him prostrate twice.'"],[9798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He said: 'What is that?' They said: 'You prayed five.' He then prostrated twice."],[9799,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed five rak'ahs and prostrated twice."],[9800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rak'ahs. They said to him: 'O Prophet of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?' He then said the salam and prostrated twice for forgetfulness."],[9802,"He led the people in five rak'ahs. When he finished, they said: 'You prayed five rak'ahs.' 'Alqamah said: 'Do you say that, O one-eyed?' meaning Ibrahim. He said: 'Yes.' 'Alqamah then prostrated twice for forgetfulness, then recited the tashahhud and said the salam. Then he turned to them and informed them from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud from the Prophet ﷺ that he did that."],[9803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five rakʿahs with them. When he said the salam, he was told about that, so he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice while seated."],[9804,"ʿAlqamah led us in Zuhr prayer with five rakʿahs. When he finished, they said to him, “You prayed five.” He said, “I did not.” Then he said, “Is that so, O one-eyed man?” He said, “I said, ‘Yes.’” So he turned and prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said the salam. Then he mentioned from ʿAbdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prayed five rakʿahs and saw them whispering to one another. He said, “What is the matter with you?” They said, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “And what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” He said, “No, but I forgot.” So he turned and prostrated twice."],[9805,"ʿAlqamah led us in prayer with five rakʿahs. He was told, so he said, “I did not.” I said, “Yes, you did.” He said, “And you, O one-eyed man?” I said, “Yes.” So he prostrated twice, then narrated to us from ʿAbdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prayed five rakʿahs, and the people whispered to one another, saying, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No.” They told him, so he bent his leg and prostrated twice, then said, “I am only a human being; I forget as you forget.”"],[9806,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he did something similar."],[9807,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr or ʿAsr with five rakʿahs, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “These two prostrations are for whoever of you thinks that he added or omitted something.”"],[9810,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five rakʿahs and then prostrated twice."],[9811,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he prayed five rakʿahs. When he finished, it was said, “O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No, and what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” He said, “I am only a human being like you; I remember as you remember and forget as you forget.” Then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."],[9812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in Zuhr or ʿAsr prayer with five rakʿahs. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “No, and what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” So he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice, then said, “These two prostrations are for whoever of you thinks that he added or omitted something.”"],[9813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer, then entered [his house]. Some of the people said to others, “Has something been added to the prayer?” He said, “And what is that?” They said, “You prayed five.” So he took him by the hand and went out to the mosque, where there was a circle in which Abu Bakr and Umar were present. He said, “Is what Dhu al-Yadayn says true?” They said, “Yes, O Prophet of Allah.” So he faced the qiblah and prostrated twice."],[9814,"ʿAbdullah: “Rather, you have recited quickly, like the recitation of poetry and the scattering of bad dates. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite pairs of similar surahs in one rakʿah.” Then he mentioned ten rakʿahs with twenty surahs, according to the arrangement of ʿAbdullah, the last of them being “When the sun is wrapped up [in darkness]” (al-Takwir) and al-Dukhan."],[9815,"Give every surah its due share of bowing and prostration, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recite twenty surahs in ten rakʿahs."],[9816,"Reciting quickly like the recitation of poetry? Recite as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: two surahs from the Mufassal in one rakʿah."],[9817,"I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine, two surahs in a rakʿah."],[9818,"Rapid recitation like the rapid recitation of poetry? Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the analogous surahs, two surahs, twenty surahs."],[9819,"I recited the mufassal last night in a single rakʿah. He said, 'Scattered [recitation] like scattering poor dates, and rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair together, two surahs in a rakʿah.' The wording is that of the hadith of Abu ʿUbayd."],[9820,"ʿAbd Allah [said]: I certainly knew the analogous surahs with which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray: al-Dhariyat and al-Tur, and Iqtarabat and al-Najm, and al-Rahman and al-Waqiʿah, and Nun and al-Haqqah, and al-Muzzammil and La Uqsimu bi-Yawm al-Qiyamah, and Hal Ata ʿala al-Insan and al-Mursalat, and ʿAmma Yatasaʾalun and al-Naziʿat, and ʿAbasa and Waylun li-l-Mutaffifin, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat and Ha Mim al-Dukhan."],[9822,"I recited the mufassal tonight in a single rakʿah. ʿAbd Allah said, 'Rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in a single rakʿah,' and he mentioned twenty surahs from the beginning of the mufassal, pairing two surahs [in each rakʿah]."],[9823,"I certainly know the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in a single rakʿah. Then ʿAbd Allah stood, took ʿAlqamah by the hand, and ʿAlqamah came out to us. We said to him, 'Did he tell you the analogous surahs?' He said, 'He said the first twenty of the mufassal, among them a surah from the Al Ha Mim family: al-Dukhan, and its counterpart ʿAmma Yatasaʾalun.'"],[9824,"I certainly memorize the paired surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: eighteen from the mufassal and two surahs from the Al Ha Mim family."],[9825,"I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair together, two surahs in a rakʿah."],[9826,"Rapid like the rapid recitation of poetry? I certainly knew the analogous surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pair: twenty surahs in ten rakʿahs."],[9828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a man who left behind his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister. He assigned to the daughter one half, to the son's daughter one sixth, and what remained to the sister."],[9830,"To the daughter one half and to the sister one half, and he did not assign anything to the son's daughter. He said, 'Ask Ibn Masʿud, for he will agree with me.' So they asked Ibn Masʿud and informed him of al-Ashʿari's statement. He said, 'Then I have gone astray and I am not among the rightly guided. I judge among you by the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"To the daughter one half, to the son's daughter one sixth, and to the sister one third.\"' This reached al-Ashʿari, and he said, 'Do not ask me about anything as long as this learned man is among you.'"],[9831,"Then I have gone astray and I am not among the rightly guided, but I judge concerning it by the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"To the daughter one half, to the son's daughter a share to complete the two thirds, and what remains to the full sister.\""],[9833,"From a man who died leaving his daughter, his son's daughter, and his full sister. He said: 'To the daughter belongs half, and whatever remains goes to the full sister.' He said to us: 'Ibn Masʿūd will surely say the same as I said.' So they asked Ibn Masʿūd, then they told him what Abū Mūsā had said. He said: 'How could I say what he said when I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"To the daughter belongs half, to the son's daughter one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and whatever remains goes to the full sister.\"'"],[9834,"I would then have gone astray and I am not of the rightly guided. But I will judge in it as the Prophet ﷺ judged in it: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth to complete two-thirds, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9835,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9836,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a sister: 'To the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth, and whatever remains goes to the sister.'"],[9837,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who is tattooed, the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who has them joined, the one who consumes ribā and the one who enables it, and the one who makes a woman lawful (for her previous husband) and the one for whom it is done."],[9838,"He said: 'I had a slave, so I freed him and made him a sāʾibah for the sake of God.' ʿAbd Allāh said to him: 'The people of Islam do not set slaves free as sāʾibah; only the people of the Jāhiliyyah used to do that. You are the patron of his favor and the most entitled of people to his inheritance. If you feel uneasy about anything, show it to us and we will place it in the public treasury.'"],[9839,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ, delaying the latter to the end of its time and performing the former at the beginning of its time."],[9840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine the two prayers while traveling."],[9841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You are the most similar of nations to the Children of Israel. You will surely follow their way closely, step by step, until there is nothing among them but there will be something like it among you, to the point that if one of them were to pass by a woman, one of them would stand with her and have intercourse, then return to his companions laughing to them and they would laugh back to him.'"],[9842,"That he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[9843,"They used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ. One of them said: 'Peace be upon God.' He said: 'Who said \"Peace be upon God\"? Indeed God is al-Salām (the Source of Peace), but say: \"Greetings, prayers, and good things are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\"'"],[9844,"When we sat (in prayer), we used to say: 'Peace be upon God, peace be upon Jibrīl.' The Prophet ﷺ heard us and said: 'Indeed God is al-Salām (the Source of Peace). So when one of you sits in prayer, let him say: \"Greetings, prayers, and good things are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God.\"'"],[9845,"When we sat down in the prayer, we used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon us from our Lord; peace be upon Jibril and Mika'il; peace be upon so-and-so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam (the Source of Peace). When you sit in the prayer, say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. When he says that, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens or on the earth. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.' Then he chooses whatever words he wishes."],[9847,"From Hammad, Mansur, Husayn, al-A'mash, and Abu Hashim, from Abu Wa'il and Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad and Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, who said: We did not know what to say in the prayer; we used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon Mika'il.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud and said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam. When you sit after two rak'ahs, say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin.' Abu Wa'il said in the hadith of 'Abdullah from the Prophet ﷺ: 'When you say it, it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and the earth.' Abu Ishaq said in the hadith of 'Abdullah: 'When you say it, it reaches every angel brought near, or every prophet sent, or every righteous servant. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9849,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ heard that and said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9852,"They used to say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon the Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9853,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril and Mika'il and every angel whose name we know.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught us: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu. When you say this, every angel, every prophet, and every righteous servant is included in your words.'"],[9854,"The Prophet ﷺ turned to them and taught them the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9855,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon so-and-so; peace be upon so-and-so,' naming those from the angels and prophets whom we knew. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught us the tashahhud, and we used to learn it as one of us would learn a surah from the Qur'an. He said: 'Say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9857,"We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people would say, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril; peace be upon Mika'il; peace be upon the angels brought near.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not say, \"Peace be upon Allah,\" for Allah is as-Salam.' Then he taught them the tashahhud and said: 'Say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9859,"We used to say in the prayer, 'Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibril,' until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9861,"'Abdullah said: We used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and say, 'Peace be upon Allah.' He said, 'Indeed, Allah is as-Salam. Rather say: At-tahiyyatu lillahi was-salawatu wat-tayyibatu; as-salamu 'alayka ayyuhan-nabiyyu wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuhu; as-salamu 'alayna wa 'ala 'ibadillahis-salihin. Ash-hadu an la ilaha illallah wa ash-hadu anna Muhammadan 'abduhu wa rasuluhu.'"],[9863,"From Mansur, Sulayman, Hammad, Abu Hashim, and Mughira, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, who said: We used to say in the prayer: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'Allah Himself is Peace. But say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9865,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to teach us the Tashahhud and the Khutbah, just as he would teach us a Surah from the Quran, beginning with \"All greetings, prayers, and good words belong to Allah\" until his saying, \"His servant and Messenger.\""],[9866,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9867,"We, when we sat, used to say: 'Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il, peace be upon the angels.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us words which, if we say them, we greet every angel in the heaven and every righteous servant on the earth: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9868,"The translation of the passage into English is: \"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , taught us to recite the Tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and good acts are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' \""],[9870,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer just as he taught us a surah from the Qur'an: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9871,"We did not know what to say in every rak'ah; we glorified, magnified, and praised our Lord. Muhammad ﷺ was given the openings of good and its endings—or he said: its comprehensive words. He said to us: 'When you sit after every two rak'ahs, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then let him choose of supplication what pleases him most and supplicate with it.'\""],[9872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud in prayer: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' The wording is that of the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Ishaq, and the others are similar."],[9873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said] to us: 'When you sit after every two rak'ahs, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he chooses of supplication what pleases him most.'\""],[9874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Qur'an: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9876,"We did not know what to say in every two rak'ahs of prayer except that we magnified, glorified, and praised our Lord. Muhammad ﷺ was given the openings of good and its endings. He said: 'When you sit for the tashahhud, say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9877,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: 'All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud and said: 'Say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: 'Say: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.'\""],[9881,"The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran, and he would say: “Learn it, for there is no prayer without the tashahhud.”"],[9882,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and taught me the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9883,"He heard him say: ʿAlqama took me by the hand, ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud took ʿAlqama by the hand, and the Prophet ﷺ took Ibn Masʿud by the hand, and he taught him the tashahhud in prayer: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9887,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9889,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the tashahhud in prayer. He said: We used to memorize it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as we would memorize the letters of the Quran, the waws and the alifs. He said: When he sat on his left hip, he said: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” Then he would supplicate to his Lord, then he would say the salam and depart."],[9892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: When one of you sits in his prayer, let him say: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9893,"We used to say in prayer: “Peace be upon our Lord.” It was said to us: Say: “Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah,” for when you say that, you greet everyone in the heavens and the earth."],[9894,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran.”"],[9895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us a surah from the Quran: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9896,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. O Allah, bless Muhammad and his household as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless us with them. O Allah, bless Muhammad and his household as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, bless us with them. The prayers of Allah and the prayers of the believers upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, ﷺ and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\""],[9897,"The Prophet ﷺ taught them the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[9898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud: “All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.” Al-Ajlaḥ raised it, but Ḥammād b. Salama did not raise it."],[9899,"O Allah, I ask You for all that is good, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the good that Your righteous servants have asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants have sought refuge. O Allah, our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire."],[9900,"I heard ʿAbdullah say: When one of you sits in prayer, let him say the greetings — and he mentioned the tashahhud — then he said: Let him say: O Allah, I ask You for all that is good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know. O Allah, I ask You for the best of what Your righteous servants have asked You for, and I seek refuge in You from the evil from which Your righteous servants have sought refuge. Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire. Our Lord, we believe, so forgive us our sins and expiate our evil deeds, and cause us to die with the righteous. Our Lord, grant us what You have promised us through Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection; indeed You do not break the promise."],[9902,"It was recited in his presence, or he recited it: {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} Then ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient. They said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} Then ʿAbdullah said: Do you know what the nation is? The one who teaches people good, and the devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger."],[9903,"ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif, and he was not of the polytheists. Farwah, a man from Ashjaʿ, said: You forgot — indeed it is Ibrahim. He said: Who forgot? We used to liken Muʿadh to Ibrahim. He was asked about the nation and said: A teacher of good. And he was asked about the devoutly obedient and said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9904,"Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif. It was said to him: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif.} He said: Did you hear me mention Ibrahim? Then he said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah, a hanif. He said: We used to liken Muʿadh to Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[9905,"ʿAbdullah said: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient. Farwah said: It is a mistake; {Indeed Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient.} He said: We used to liken him to him. He was asked about the nation and said: A teacher of good. And he was asked about the devoutly obedient and said: Obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9906,"The nation is the one who teaches people good, and the devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger. And such was Muʿadh b. Jabal: he used to teach good and was obedient to Allah and His Messenger."],[9907,"A man said: O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, we do not see you narrating to us anything you do not know. Allah ﷻ says {Indeed Ibrahim} but you say: Indeed Muʿadh. He said: They keep hearing truth from me and rejecting it. The devoutly obedient is the one who obeys Allah, and Muʿadh was like that."],[9909,"On the authority of ʿAbdullah: Indeed Muʿadh was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah. Do you know what the nation is? It is the one who teaches people good."],[9910,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself and told Ibn Masʿud to bring him three stones. He came with two stones and a piece of dung. He threw away the dung and said: “This is filth; bring me a stone.”"],[9911,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the jinn, and he said to me: “Find me three stones.” I found him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, and said: “This is filth.”"],[9912,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and he wanted to fulfill his need, so he said, \"Bring me three stones.\" I looked for them and found two stones, but I didn't find the third stone. So, I found a small piece of dung and brought it to him. He said, \"Didn't you know that it is impure?\""],[9913,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to relieve himself and said: “Bring me three stones with which to clean myself.” I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and threw away the dung, saying: “It is filth.”"],[9914,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ so he could relieve himself. He ordered me to bring him three stones. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and discarded the dung, saying: “This is filth.”"],[9915,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered me to bring him three stones. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He took the two stones and discarded the dung, saying: “It is filth.”"],[9916,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring me three stones.” He performed ablution without touching water. I brought him two stones and a piece of dung. He said: “Throw away the dung, for it is filth.”"],[9917,"The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself and said: “Bring me something with which to clean myself, but do not bring me anything that is a barrier or dung.” I did so, then he performed ablution and prayed."],[9918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set off for his need and said, \"Bring me something and do not bring me a bone or a reed.\" So I did, and he performed ablution and then prayed."],[9919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me three stones.” I brought him two stones and the dung of a donkey. He took the two stones and cast away the dung, saying: “It is impure.”"],[9920,"He made ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with nabīdh, so he performed ablution and said: “A drink that is purifying.”"],[9921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: “I have been commanded to recite to your brethren among the jinn. Let a man from you stand with me, and let no man stand who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride.” I stood with him and took a water-skin containing nabīdh and went with him. When he went out, he drew a line for me and said: “Do not step out of it, for if you step out, you will not see me nor I you until the Day of Resurrection.” Then he went and disappeared from me until I could not see him. When dawn broke, he came back and said to me: “I see you standing?” I said, “I have not sat down.” He said: “It would not have harmed you if you had.” I said, “I feared I might step out of it.” He said: “Indeed, if you had stepped out, you would not have seen me nor I you until the Day of Resurrection. Do you have water for ablution?” I said, “No.” He said, “What is this water-skin?” I said, “It contains nabīdh.” He said, “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution and began the prayer. When he finished the prayer, two men from the jinn came to him and asked him for provisions. He said, “Did I not command provisions for you and your people with what is good for you?” They said, “Yes, but we wanted some of us to witness the prayer with you.” He said, “Which people are you from?” They said, “From the people of Naṣībīn.” He said, “These two have succeeded and their people have succeeded,” and he commanded for them dung and bones as food and meat. The Prophet ﷺ forbade cleaning oneself with bone or dung."],[9922,"On the night of the jinn, two of them stayed behind and said, “We will witness the dawn prayer with you, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you have water?” I said, “I have no water, but I have a water-skin containing nabīdh.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “A good date and purifying water,” and he performed ablution. Isrāʾīl said in his version: Then he prayed the morning prayer."],[9923,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the night of the jinn: “What is in your water-skin?” He said, “Nabīdh.” He said, “A good date and purifying water.”"],[9924,"ʿAbd al-Wārith Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaqarī narrated to us, from Sharīk, from Abū Fizāra, from Abū Zayd, from ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought water for ablution on the night of the jinn. I said, “I have nothing but nabīdh in a water-skin.” He said, “A good date and purifying water,” and he performed ablution with it."],[9925,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was among a group of his companions, he said: “Let a man from among you stand with me, but let no man stand with me in whose heart is an atom’s weight of deceit.” So I stood with him and took the water-skin, which I thought contained only water. I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we were in upper Makkah, and I saw dark shapes gathered together. He drew a line for me and then said: “Stand here until I come to you.” I stood while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to them, and I saw them rushing toward him. The Messenger of Allah stayed away for a long part of the night, then came to me at dawn and said: “Have you been standing all this time, O Ibn Masʿud?” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, did you not tell me to stand until I come to you?” Then he said to me: “Do you have any water for ablution?” I said: “Yes.” I opened the water-skin and found it was nabīdh. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I took it thinking it was only water, but it turned out to be nabīdh.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution with it. When he stood to pray, two figures from among them came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we would like you to lead us in our prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lined them up behind him and then prayed with us. When he finished, I said to him: “Who are these, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “These are jinn of Nasībīn; they asked me for provision, so I gave them the refuse as provision. Whatever dung they find becomes barley for them, and whatever bone they find becomes meat for them.” At that point the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade using dung and bone for istinja."],[9926,"On the night of the jinn, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you have something for purification?” I said: “Nothing but nabīdh in a water-skin.” He said: “A good date and purifying water.” Then he performed ablution."],[9927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out before the Hijrah to the outskirts of Makkah. He drew a line for me and said: “Do not do anything until I come to you.” Then he said: “Let nothing you see alarm or frighten you.” He went forward a little and sat down, and there were black men like the men of the Zutt. They were as Allah Almighty said: {They almost crowded upon him}. I wanted to get up and defend him as much as I could, but then I remembered the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed still. Then they dispersed from him, and I heard them saying: “O Messenger of Allah, our route is long and we are leaving, so give us provision.” He said: “You may have the dung and any bone you come upon—there is meat for you on it, and any dung you come upon is dates for you.” When they left, I said: “Who are these?” He said: “These are jinn of Nusaybīn.”"],[9928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me to accompany him on the night of the jinn. I went with him until we reached upper Makkah. He drew a line for me and said: “Do not leave.” Then he went off into the mountains. I saw men descending upon him from the mountain tops until they came between me and him. I drew my sword and said: “I will strike until I rescue the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then I remembered his words: “Do not leave until I come to you.” I remained like that until dawn came. The Prophet ﷺ came while I was standing. He said: “Have you been in this state all along?” I said: “If you had stayed a month, I would not have left until you came to me.” Then I told him what I had intended to do. He said: “If you had left, neither I nor you would have met until the Day of Resurrection.” Then he intertwined his fingers with mine and said: “I was promised that the jinn and mankind would believe in me. As for mankind, they have believed in me; and as for the jinn, you have seen.” He said: “I think my appointed time has drawn near.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Abu Bakr as successor?” He turned away from me, and I saw that he did not agree. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Umar as successor?” He turned away from me, and I saw that he did not agree. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not appoint Ali as successor?” He said: “That one—by the One besides whom there is no god—if you pledge allegiance to him and obey him, he will admit you all into Paradise, completely.”"],[9929,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on the night of the delegation of jinn. He sighed, so I said: “What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Abu Bakr.” He remained silent for a while, then moved on. Then he sighed again, so I said: “What is the matter with you, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Then appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Umar.” He remained silent for a while, then moved on. Then he sighed again, so I said: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “My soul has been announced to me as departing, O Ibn Masʿud.” I said: “Then appoint a successor.” He said: “Who?” I said: “Ali b. Abi Talib.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they obey him, they will all enter Paradise, completely.”"],[9930,"I was not with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but I wish I were with him. (Using translation from Muslim 450d)"],[9931,"The Prophet ﷺ removed his sandals while praying, so those behind him removed their sandals. He said: “What made you remove your sandals?” They said: “We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours.” He said: “Jibril ﷺ informed me that there was something unclean on one of them, so I removed them for that reason. Do not remove your sandals.”"],[9932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform qunūt except for one month; he did not perform qunūt before it or after it."],[9933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt for thirty days, supplicating, then he abandoned it."],[9934,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his houses on his left. When he finished the prayer, he would go to his houses on his left."],[9935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the Burāq and he mounted it with Jibril, may Allah bless them both. They traveled, and whenever he came to a mountain, his legs would rise, and when he descended, his hands would rise, until they reached a land that was dark and stinking, then a land that was spacious and fragrant. I said: “O Jibril, we were traveling in a dark, stinking land, then to a spacious, fragrant land.” He said: “That is the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.” Then I came upon a man standing in prayer. He said: “Who is this with you, O Jibril?” I said: “Your brother Muhammad.” He welcomed him and prayed for blessing. He said: “Ask for ease for your ummah.” I said: “Who is this, O Jibril?” He said: “Your brother Musa.” I said: “Was his voice and his complaining to his Lord like that?” He said: “Yes, that was known of him and his intensity.” Then we traveled on, and I saw lamps and light. I said: “Who is this, O Jibril?” He said: “This is the tree of your father Ibrahim.” I said: “Shall I approach it?” He said: “Yes.” So we approached it, and he prayed for blessing for me and welcomed me. Then we went on to Bayt al-Maqdis, and I tied the animal to the ring to which the prophets tie their animals. Then I entered the mosque, and the prophets were gathered for me—those whom Allah named in His Book and those He did not name. I prayed with them, except for the possessors of the cow: Isa, Musa, and Ibrahim, may Allah bless them and grant them peace."],[9936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If hardship were in a hole, ease would enter upon it until it brought it out.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Indeed, with hardship comes ease}."],[9937,"Announcing death is from the affairs of the Jāhiliyyah."],[9938,"I used to see the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said the salam to his right and to his left."],[9939,"\"We were not commanded to fast on Ashura except before Ramadan was revealed, so when Ramadan was revealed we were not commanded or forbidden from it.\""],[9940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I had resolved to order Bilal to call the prayer, then go to people who hear the call but do not respond, and burn their houses down upon them.\""],[9941,"Regarding the Sunnah of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[9942,"No concession was given for abandoning the congregation except for one who is afraid or ill."],[9943,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Hasan and Husain passed by, and they were young children. He said, \"Bring me my two sons, I seek refuge for them with the same protection that Ibrahim sought for his two sons, Ismail and Ishaq.\" He said, \"I seek refuge for you both in the perfect words of Allah, from every evil eye, harmful thing, and Satan.\""],[9944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is the equal of his father.\""],[9945,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no forgetfulness in the prayer of fear.\""],[9946,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When the two parties to a sale disagree about the sale, they should rescind the sale.\""],[9947,"We used to eat with the Prophet ﷺ and would hear the glorification of the food."],[9948,"\"Yes, we used to fast it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before the month of Ramadan was made obligatory. When the month of Ramadan was made obligatory, it abrogated it.\" Then he said, \"Sit down,\" so I sat and ate."],[9949,"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet ﷺ while traveling, and with Abu Bakr and Umar."],[9950,"When the Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit, we would face him."],[9951,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that a man be named Harith, or Walid, or Hakam, or Abu al-Hakam, or Aflah, or Najih, or Yasar. And he said: “The most beloved of names to God ﷻ is that by which one is rendered a servant (of Him).”"],[9952,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seeking the lawful is an obligation after the obligatory.”"],[9953,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed qunut for thirty nights, supplicating against the tribes of Banu Sulaym, Riʿl, Dhakwan, and ʿUsayya, who had disobeyed God and His Messenger."],[9954,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would sleep in his prostration, and his sleep was not recognized except by his breathing; then he would rise for his prayer."],[9955,"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[9956,"I saw the moon split into two, with Hiraʾ between them."],[9957,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us, when one of us sneezed, to say ‘yarhamuka Allah’ to him."],[9958,"Tell us when the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer? He said, \"When a portion of the night remains after the previous prayers until the Maghrib prayer, he was asked about his recitation, and he said, 'He used to recite aloud for the people of the household.'\""],[9959,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard seed of pride, and no one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a grain of mustard seed of faith.”"],[9961,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: “And whoever does that will meet a penalty.”"],[9962,"I asked Abdullah b. Masud: Did the Prophet ﷺ deliver the sermon standing or sitting? He said: Do you not recite: “And they left you standing”?"],[9963,"On the day of Badr, Saʿd fought the fighting of both a horseman and an infantryman."],[9964,"Whoever goes to a diviner or a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[9965,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Looking at the face of ʿAlī is an act of worship.”"],[9966,"from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever is generous with his family on the day of Ashura will remain in abundance throughout the rest of his year.\""],[9967,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every prophet has a special group among his companions, and my special group among my companions are Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ.”"],[9968,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the moon split, and one part went behind the mountain. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bear witness, bear witness.”"],[9969,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not clean yourselves after defecation with dung or bones, for they are the provision of your brothers among the jinn.”"],[9970,"The Jews said: “Are not your brothers who died the ones who used to drink it?” Then God ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten} (Qur'an 5:93). The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It was said to me, 'You are one of them.'”"],[9971,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us the istikhārah (prayer for guidance). He said: “When one of you wants to do something, let him say: 'O God, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek ability by Your power, and I ask You of Your great bounty. For You know and I do not know, and You have power and I have no power, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If this matter which I intend is good for my religion and for the outcome of my affairs, then make it easy for me. And if something else is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be.' He says that, then he resolves.”"],[9972,"“The fourth of four—and what is the fourth of four? It is not far from God. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'People will sit with God on the Day of Resurrection according to their going early to the Friday prayers: the first, then the second, then the third, then the fourth.'” Then he said: “The fourth of four—and what is the fourth of four? It is not far from God.”"],[9973,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The closest a servant is to God is when he is prostrating.”"],[9974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The soul of a believer comes out as sweat, while the soul of a disbeliever flows out as the soul of a donkey. A believer may commit a sin, and it is intensified for him at death so that he may be expiated by it. And a disbeliever may do a good deed, and it is made easy for him at death so that he may be rewarded for it.”"],[9976,"The two sons of Mulaykah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, our mother used to honor the husband, show affection to the child,” and he mentioned the guest, “except that she buried a daughter alive in the Jahiliyyah.” He said, “Your mother is in the Fire.” They turned away, and evil could be seen in their faces. He ordered that they be brought back, and joy could be seen in their faces hoping that something had happened. He said, “My mother is with your mother.” A man from the hypocrites said, “What does this avail his mother while we tread on his heels?” A man from the Ansar—and I have never seen a man who asked more questions than him—said, “O Messenger of God, has your Lord promised concerning her or both of them?” He said, “Do you think it is from something?” He said, “I have not asked my Lord, and indeed I will stand at the Praised Station on the Day of Resurrection.” The Ansari said, “And what is that Praised Station?” He said, “That is when you are brought barefoot and naked, and the first to be clothed will be Ibrahim ﷺ , who will say, ‘Clothe my friend.’ Then two white garments will be brought, and he will put them on, then sit facing the Throne. Then my clothing will be brought, and I will put it on, and I will stand at his right in a station that no one other than me will stand; the first and the last will envy me for it. And my river Kawthar will be opened to the Pool.” A man from the hypocrites said, “For it, no water ever flowed over pebbles or pebbles but it had a quality or pebbles.” He said, “O Messenger of God, what quality and pebbles?” He said, “Its quality is musk and its pebbles are pearls.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard like today: water that flows over quality or pebbles but it has vegetation.” The Ansari said, “O Messenger of God, does it have vegetation?” He said, “Yes, rods of gold.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard like today; for no rod grows but it leaves and has fruit.” The Ansari said, “Does it have fruit?” He said, “Yes, colors of jewels, and its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst again, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after it.” This hadith was also narrated by al-Saʿiq b. Hazn from ʿAli b. al-Hakam, and he differed from Saʿid b. Zayd in its chain."],[9978,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, “You and your wealth belong to your father.”"],[9979,"The Prophet ﷺ clasped his hands together."],[9980,"“We did not fast twenty-nine days with the Messenger of God ﷺ more often than we fasted thirty.”"],[9981,"“Traits that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do and people have abandoned, one of them is the imam’s salam in the funeral prayer like his salam in the prayer.”"],[9982,"“Add more of this for us, may my father and mother be your ransom; for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘A beautiful voice is an adornment of the Quran.’”"],[9983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about whispering, and he said, “That is pure faith.”"],[9984,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[9985,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “A cow is for seven and a camel is for seven in the sacrificial animals.”"],[9986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O young people, marry, for it is the best way to guard one's chastity and lower one's gaze. Whoever is not able to marry, then he should observe fasting, for it will be a shield for him.\""],[9987,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me to begin the day of my fast with oiled and combed hair, and not to begin the day of your fast frowning. And answer the invitation of whoever invites you from the Muslims as long as they do not display musical instruments; if they display musical instruments, then do not answer them. And pray over whoever dies from the people of our qiblah, even if he was killed crucified or stoned; for if you meet God with the like of the earth’s fill of sins, it is better for you than to affirm martyrdom for anyone from the people of the qiblah.”"],[9988,"“Do you know which charity is best?” They said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The best charity is a grant: to grant a dirham or the back of a mount.”"],[9989,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Indeed God ﷻ loves that His dispensations be accepted, just as He loves that His obligatory duties be fulfilled.”"],[9990,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a group of Banu Hashim approached. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them, his face reddened and his eyes welled up. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing something in your face that we dislike.” He said, “We are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world, and my household will face trials and expulsion after me.”"],[9991,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say Takbeer (Allahu Akbar) during every lifting and lowering, and would greet (say salaam) to his right and left until the whiteness of his face could be seen from both sides."],[9992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"All of creation are the family of Allah, and the dearest of them to Allah are those who benefit His family the most.\""],[9993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever dies and has a male or female child is granted peace or does not grant peace, is pleased or is not pleased, will have no reward except Paradise.\""],[9995,"Abdullah stood at al-Safa next to a crevice in it and said, “Here, by the One besides whom there is no god, stood the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down.”"],[9996,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever buys a sheep that has been left unmilked, if he is pleased with it, he keeps it; otherwise he returns it along with a saa‘ of dates.”"],[9997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not go out to meet the trade caravans.”"],[9998,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Injury caused by a beast is without liability, and [injury caused by falling into] a well is without liability, and [injury caused by] a grazing animal is without liability, and on buried treasure the fifth is due.”"],[9999,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a naked woman approached. This distressed the Prophet ﷺ and he closed his eyes. A man from the group stood up, threw a garment over her, and held her close. Some of his companions said, “O Messenger of Allah, I think she is his wife.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you think her jealous? Allah ﷻ has decreed jealousy for women and jihad for men. Whoever among them bears it patiently with faith and seeking reward will have the like of the reward of the martyrs.”"],[10000,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Let those of maturity and wisdom stand closest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them. Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Beware of the commotion of the marketplaces.”"],[10001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes twist the forelock of his horse with his hand."],[10002,"From Ibrahim, and ‘Umarah had gone out to Makkah, so I hired a donkey and brought him to al-Qadisiyyah. He narrated to me from Ibrahim, from ‘Alqamah, from Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have young men from his household pass by him and his complexion would change because of that. One day some young men from his household passed by him and his complexion changed because of that. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing from you what distresses us: young men from your household pass by you and your complexion changes because of that.” He said, “These members of my household: Allah has chosen the Hereafter for them and has not chosen this world for them.”"],[10003,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no retaliation except with the sword.”"],[10004,"Five signs have passed and five remain. Among them: the splitting of the moon, which we have seen; the smoke has passed; the great seizure has passed; the barren day has passed; and the inevitable punishment has passed."],[10005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “My description is Ahmad, the one who relies on Allah; he is neither harsh nor coarse. He repays a good deed with a good deed and does not repay an evil deed in kind. His birthplace is Makkah, his migration is to Taybah, and his nation is the praisers. They tie their lower garments at their waists and wash their limbs. Their gospels are in their breasts. They line up for prayer as they line up for battle. Their sacrifice by which they draw near to Me is their blood. They are monks by night and lions by day.”"],[10006,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Every act of kindness is charity, whether the giver is rich or poor.”"],[10007,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “You will not be an ascetic until you are humble.”"],[10008,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The soul of a believer comes out like sweat, and I do not love a death like the death of a donkey.” It was said: “What is the death of a donkey?” He said: “The soul of a disbeliever comes out from the corners of his mouth.”"],[10009,"A ruqya for fever was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: “Present it to me.” They presented it: “In the name of Allah, a cleft, a horned, a salty, a sea, Qifta.” He said: “These are covenants which Sulayman b. Dawud ﷺ took upon the vermin, and I see no harm in it.”"],[10010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on three days: the day before the Day of Tarwiyah, the day of Fitr, and the day of Adha."],[10011,"From the Prophet ﷺ that when he sought guidance in a matter he wanted to undertake, he would say: “O Allah, I seek Your guidance through Your knowledge, and I seek Your ability through Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty; for You have power and I have none, and You know and I know not, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if this affair is good for me in my religion, and good for me in my livelihood, and good for me in what I seek good through, then decree it for me in well-being and make it easy, then bless me in it. And if other than that is better for me, then decree for me what is good wherever it may be.”"],[10012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded fighting the breakers of allegiance, the wrongdoers, and the renegades."],[10013,"Ali commanded fighting the breakers of allegiance, the wrongdoers, and the renegades."],[10014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Faith is Yemeni, and Mudar is at the tails of camels.”"],[10015,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wine is cursed, and its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one who has it pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the consumer of its price.”"],[10016,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed riba (usury), the one who consumes it, the one who pays it, its scribe, and its two witnesses if they know, and the woman who joins hair extensions and the one who asks for it, the one who asks for tattooing, the woman who plucks eyebrows and the one who asks for it, and he forbade wailing."],[10017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of people are my generation, then the second, then the third. Then there will come a people in whom there is no good.”"],[10018,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The woman who buries her daughter alive and the girl buried alive will both be in the Fire.”"],[10019,"That he should read the scroll of Muhammad ﷺ that bore his seal, let him read: “Say, come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden you” up to His saying, “so that you may become righteous”."],[10020,"From ʿAbdullāh regarding His saying, “O you who believe, do not consume one another’s wealth wrongfully, unless it be trade by mutual consent among you” – he said, “It is definitive; it has not been abrogated.”"],[10021,"While we were with the Prophet ﷺ, we heard a caller calling out: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Upon the natural disposition.” Then he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allāh.” He said, “He has brought it out of the Fire.” So we hurried to him and found a shepherd among his sheep, and prayer time had arrived, so he called it out."],[10022,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, he heard a caller saying: Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Upon the natural disposition.” Then he said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allāh.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He has come out of the Fire.”"],[10024,"When Ibrāhīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, the sun was eclipsed. The people said, “It was eclipsed because of the death of Ibrāhīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah, may the blessings of Allah be upon them both.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The sun and the moon do not eclipse because of anyone’s death or life. When you see that, pray until it clears.”"],[10025,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “No one who has an atom’s weight of pride will enter Paradise, and no one who has an atom’s weight of faith will enter the Fire.”"],[10026,"Ṭalḥah said: I recited to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb; Yaḥyā b. Waththāb recited to ʿAlqamah b. Qays; ʿAlqamah b. Qays recited to ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd; and ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Māliki yawmi al-dīn” with alif, and “ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim” with kasrah."],[10027,"O Muhammad, you will ascend one heaven after another."],[10028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “This dinar and this dirham destroyed those before you, and I do not think they will do anything but destroy you.”"],[10029,"I said to al-Aʿmash, “From whom did you recite ‘wal-rujza fahjur’?” He said, “I recited to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb; Yaḥyā recited to ʿAlqamah; ʿAlqamah recited to ʿAbdullāh; and ʿAbdullāh recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10030,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, “When people differ, Ibn Sumayyah will be with the truth.”"],[10032,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"You will certainly see after me favoritism and matters you will disapprove of.\" We said, \"What do you command us?\" He said, \"Give them their due and ask Allah for your due.\""],[10033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[10034,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: A man will come holding another man by the hand and say, \"O Lord, this one killed me.\" Allah ﷻ will say, \"Why did you kill him?\" He will say, \"So that glory might be Yours.\" He will say, \"It is indeed Mine.\" He said: And a man will come holding another man by the hand and say, \"O Lord, this one killed me.\" Allah will say, \"Why did you kill this one?\" He will say, \"I killed him so that glory might be for so-and-so.\" He will say, \"It is not his. Bear your sin.\""],[10035,"People from Kufa came to him, and he greeted them with salam and enjoined them to fear Allah, and not to differ about the Quran or dispute over it, for it does not differ, nor does it fall away, nor does it change through much repetition. Do you not see that the law of Islam in it is one—its prescribed punishments, its recitation, and Allah's command in it? If one of the two readings commanded something and the other prohibited it, that would be difference, but it combines all of that. I hope that there has come to be among you of understanding and knowledge the best of what is among people. If I knew anyone whom camels could reach who knew better than I what Allah revealed to Muhammad ﷺ, I would seek him out until I added his knowledge to my knowledge. I know that the Quran used to be presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ once every year, and it was presented to him twice in the year he passed away. Whenever I recited the Quran to him, he told me I was doing well. So whoever recites according to my recitation, let him not abandon it out of aversion to it; for whoever denies a single letter of it denies all of it."],[10036,"From Ibn Mas'ud, tracing it to the Prophet ﷺ: \"The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the bad breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk.\""],[10037,"Allah ﷻ said: \"Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: a joy when he breaks his fast and a joy when he meets his Lord. And the bad breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk.\""],[10038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the tashahhud for a need: \"Indeed, all praise is due to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead; and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\""],[10039,"Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the sermon for a need: \"All praise is due to Allah; we praise Him and seek His help. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead; and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. 'O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word' (to the end of the verse). 'O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims.' 'O people, fear your Lord who created you' to the end of the verse. To proceed.\""],[10040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, Islam began as something strange, so glad tidings to the strangers.\""],[10041,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No prayer is heavier upon the hypocrites than the Isha and Fajr prayers. If they knew the merit in them, they would come to them even crawling.\""],[10042,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A man will be bridled by his sweat on the Day of Resurrection and will say, 'My Lord, relieve me even if it is to the Fire.'\""],[10043,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and say: \"My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[10044,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal ata 'ala al-insan."],[10045,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: There was a man who was praying, and when he prostrated, another man came and stepped on his neck. So the one underneath said, “By Allah, he will never be forgiven!” Allah ﷻ said: “My servant swore by Me that I would not forgive My servant. Indeed, I have forgiven him.”"],[10046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two fasts, two prayers, two garments, two foods, two marriages, and two sales. As for the two days, they are the day of Fitr and the day of Adha. As for the two prayers, they are a prayer after Fajr until the sun rises, and a prayer after Asr until the sun sets. As for the two garments, they are wrapping oneself in a single garment with nothing between one's private parts and the sky; that is called al-summa. As for the two foods, they are eating with one's left hand while one's right hand is sound, and eating while reclining. As for the two sales, they are a man saying, “You sell for me and I will sell for you.” As for the two marriages, they are marrying a prostitute, and marrying a woman along with her maternal aunt or paternal aunt."],[10047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ask Allah of His bounty, for Allah ﷻ loves to be asked. And the best of worship is awaiting relief.”"],[10048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[10049,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Quran was revealed in seven dialects.”"],[10050,"Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ, “What has made you gray, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Hud and al-Waqiah.”"],[10051,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man stood up and accidentally stepped on another man's foot. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Make space.\" The man asked, \"What does 'make space' mean, O Messenger of Allah? Did I eat my brother's flesh?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Indeed, you have eaten your brother's flesh.\""],[10052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The food of one person is enough for two, and the food of two is enough for four.”"],[10053,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[10054,"“We have been commanded to establish prayer and give zakat. Whoever does not give zakat has no prayer.”"],[10055,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate with these words: “O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and self-sufficiency.”"],[10056,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people.”"],[10057,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man's prayer in congregation surpasses his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees, each like his prayer in his house.”"],[10058,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “The prayer of a congregation exceeds the prayer of a man alone by twenty-five prayers.”"],[10061,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five degrees.”"],[10062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds a man’s prayer alone by twenty-some prayers.”"],[10063,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A man’s prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-some degrees.”"],[10064,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[10065,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but he is my brother and companion. God has taken your companion as an intimate friend.”"],[10066,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: \"If I were to take a close friend, I would have chosen Abu Bakr as my close friend. However, your close friend is Allah.\""],[10067,"The reading of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was known in the afternoon and the evening by the movement of his beard."],[10068,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he has killed a polytheist man whose blood has become lawful.”"],[10069,"We asked the Messenger of God ﷺ whether apes and pigs are from the lineage of the Jews. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, may He be exalted, has never cursed a people and then transformed them so that they had descendants until He destroyed them. Rather, this was a creation that existed, and when God, may He be exalted, became angry with the Jews, He transformed them and made them like them.”"],[10070,"\"He does not like the wide/uncrowded space of the two arms with blood; for it has a killer in the sight of God who does not die. And it does not please you that a person earns money from forbidden (illegitimate) means, so if he spends from it, it will not be accepted from him, and if he withholds it, it will not be blessed for him. And if he dies and leaves it, it will become his provision for the fire.\""],[10071,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, the disbeliever will be called to account on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he says, ‘O Lord, grant me relief, even if it is to the Fire.’”"],[10072,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever swears a solemn oath deliberately to seize the property of a Muslim unjustly will meet God on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him.” Then he recited, “Indeed, those who purchase a small price with the covenant of God and their oaths…” [Al ʿImran 3:77]. Yazid b. Ibrahim traced it back to the Prophet, but Hammad b. Zayd did not trace it back."],[10073,"“Whoever swears a solemn oath, deliberately committing a sin in it, in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim, will meet God while He is angry with him.”"],[10074,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The woman is ʿawrah, and when she goes out, the Shayṭān seeks to tempt her, and she is closest to God when she is in the depths of her house.\""],[10075,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: 'Alif-Lām-Mīm, the sending down of the Book' (Sūrat al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man' (Sūrat al-Insān)."],[10076,"When the Prophet ﷺ began the prayer, he would say: 'Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You; blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god besides You.'"],[10077,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever is moderate will not be in need.'"],[10078,"\"I swear by nine that the Ibn Sayyad is the Dajjal is more beloved to me than swearing by one, and I swear by nine that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was martyred is more beloved to me than swearing by one that he was not martyred because Allah made him a prophet and took him as a martyr.\""],[10079,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. When he finished his prayer, he said: 'Indeed, God ﷻ brings about for His Prophet whatever He wills, and one of the things He has brought about for him is that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[10080,"We used to talk during the prayer; some of us would greet others, and one of us would gesture to his companion about a need. One day I came while the Prophet ﷺ was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what had newly occurred. When he finished, he said: 'Indeed, God ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[10081,"Ibn Masʿūd ؓ said: 'We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to us. But when I came from the land of Abyssinia, I greeted him and he did not respond to us. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what would come after. Then I waited for him, and when he finished his prayer, I mentioned that to him. He said: \"Indeed, God brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has decreed—or he said: He has brought about—that you should not talk during the prayer.\""],[10082,"We used to talk during the prayer; some of us would greet others, and one of us would gesture to his companion about a need. One day I came while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying and greeted him, but he did not respond to me. I was seized by thoughts of what had happened before and what had newly occurred. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'Indeed, God brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not talk during the prayer.'"],[10083,"People used to return the greeting to one another during the prayer, until Ibn Masʿūd ؓ greeted the Prophet ﷺ and he did not respond to him. He sat down sad, imagining that something had been revealed concerning him. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, Ibn Masʿūd mentioned that to him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is enough occupation, and the prayer suffices as an occupation.'"],[10084,"That he had gone out to the land of Abyssinia, and the people used to greet one another during the prayer. When ʿAbdullāh returned, he greeted the Prophet ﷺ and he did not respond. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said: 'I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger. I greeted you and you did not respond to me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[10085,"We used to greet the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in prayer, and he would respond to us. But when we returned from the Negus, we greeted him and he did not respond to us. We said: 'O Messenger of God, we used to greet you during the prayer and you would respond to us.' He said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[10086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, in the prayer there is occupation.'"],[10087,"He used to send greetings upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would respond to him with greetings. Then, he sent greetings upon him while he was praying, but he did not respond to him. Abdullah thought this was due to a reason from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . When he finished, Abdullah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I used to send greetings upon you while you were praying and you would respond to me, but today I sent greetings upon you and you did not respond to me. I thought there might be a reason for that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but we were forbidden from speaking during prayer except with the Quran and remembrance.\""],[10088,"We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ during the prayer, and he would respond to us. Then one day I greeted him and he did not respond to me. I asked him about that, and he said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills.\""],[10089,"We used to speak during the prayer, some of us greeting others. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ brings about in His command whatever He wills, and He has now brought about that you should not speak during the prayer.\""],[10090,"I went out for a need while some of us were greeting one another during the prayer. Then I returned and greeted, but he did not respond to me, and he said: \"Indeed, in the prayer there is enough occupation.\""],[10091,"Abdullah [Ibn Masud] said: While I was concealed behind the curtains of the Ka'bah, three persons came: a Thaqafi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts. They conversed among themselves. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears what we say?\" Another said, \"If we raise our voices, He hears; and if we lower them, He does not hear.\" The third said, \"If He hears when we raise our voices, then He hears when we lower them.\" I went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight, or your skins; but you thought that Allah does not know much of what you do} up to His saying {among the losers}. This is how Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it, and Abu Mu'awiyah and the companions of al-A'mash differed from him."],[10093,"Abdullah [Ibn Masud] said: I was concealing myself behind the curtains of the Ka'bah. Three persons came, with much fat on their bellies and little understanding in their hearts: a Qurayshi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Thaqafis, or a Thaqafi and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis. They spoke words I did not understand. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears our words?\" Another said, \"If we raise our voices, He hears them; if we do not raise them, He does not hear them.\" The third said, \"If He hears anything from it, He hears all of it.\" I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight} – the verse."],[10095,"I was concealing myself behind the curtain of the Ka'bah, and in the mosque there was a man from Thaqif and his two brothers-in-law, who were Qurayshis. He said, \"Do you think Allah hears our murmur?\" One of the two said, \"He hears when we raise our voices.\" The other said, \"If He hears when we raise our voices, He will surely hear when we lower them.\" Ibn Mas'ud said: I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of their words, and Allah ﷻ sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves, lest your hearing should testify against you, or your sight, or your skins} to the end of the verse. And al-Mas'udi differed from them."],[10097,"Three persons sat at the gate of the Ka'bah: two Qurayshis and a Thaqafi, or two Thaqafis and a Qurayshi. Some of them whispered to others about a matter. One of them said, \"Do you think Allah hears what we say?\" Another said, \"As for what we say aloud, He hears it.\" The third said, \"If He hears what we say aloud, then He hears what we whisper.\" Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down: {And you were not covering yourselves} – the verse."],[10099,"Abdullah [Ibn Mas'ud] said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs; and with Umar two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you. Would that my share of four rak'ahs were two accepted rak'ahs."],[10100,"Abdullah [Ibn Mas'ud] said: I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you. Would that I had, for four rak'ahs, two accepted rak'ahs."],[10101,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs. Then the paths diverged with you."],[10102,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs. This is how the companions of al-A'mash narrated it, and Shu'bah differed from them."],[10103,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prayed at Mina two rak'ahs; with Abu Bakr, and he prayed two rak'ahs; and with Umar, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Would that my share were two accepted rak'ahs. And Qays b. al-Rabi' differed from them."],[10104,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar at Mina two rak'ahs, and Muhammad b. Ubaydillah al-Arzami contradicted them."],[10105,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs, and Isra'il contradicted them."],[10106,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, and with Umar two rak'ahs."],[10107,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} descended upon him. He said: I was receiving it from his mouth while it was still fresh, and his mouth was indeed moist, when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it,\" but it eluded us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10108,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave at Mina when a snake sprang upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" We rushed toward it, but it outran us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10109,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of a snake in the Haram."],[10110,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of a snake in Mina.\""],[10111,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when a snake came out. He said, \"Kill it,\" but it outran us, and he said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10112,"Abdullah said: The Mursalat was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were in a cave, and he taught it to me. I am indeed reciting it close to what he taught me, and I do not know with which of its two endings it ends: {When it is said to them, 'Bow down,' they do not bow} or {Then in what statement after it will they believe?}"],[10113,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} descended upon him. I took it from his mouth, and his mouth was indeed moist with it, and I do not know with which of the two it is ended: {Then in what statement after it will they believe?} or {When it is said to them, 'Bow down,' they do not bow}. He said: And a snake escaped him into a hole, so he said, \"You were protected from its evil and it was protected from your evil.\""],[10114,"It was sent down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the snake. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the night of the snake? He said: I was with him when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seek it.\" We sought it, but it eluded us until it entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your evil and protected you from its evil.\""],[10115,"From Abdullah: We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when {By those sent forth in succession} was sent down upon him. We were indeed receiving it from his mouth while it was fresh, when a snake came out upon us. We rushed to kill it, but it slipped away. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil and you were protected from its evil.\""],[10116,"While we were in the mosque of al-Khayf on the night of Arafah, we heard the sound of a snake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" It entered a crack of a hole, so he brought a palm frond and lit a fire in it, then we emptied part of the hole but did not find it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave it, for Allah has protected it from your evil and protected you from its evil.\""],[10117,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at Mina when al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and suddenly there was a snake. They sought it, but it eluded them. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have been protected from its evil just as it was protected from your evil.\""],[10118,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when al-Mursalat was revealed to him, and we were receiving it from his mouth when a snake came out upon us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Kill it.\" We rushed toward it, but it entered its hole. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It was protected from your evil just as you were protected from its evil.\""],[10120,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, nor should he see it as a right upon himself to turn away only from his right side. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10121,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, seeing only that it is a right upon him to turn away only from his right side. Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10122,"None of you should make for Satan any share of himself, seeing only that it is a right upon him to turn away from his right side. Indeed, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10123,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left. And this is how the companions of al-A'mash narrated it, but al-Hajjaj b. Arta'ah differed from them."],[10124,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often turning away from his left."],[10125,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever is capable of marriage should get married; otherwise, let them fast, for fasting will be a shield for them.\""],[10127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O young men, whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it is more effective in lowering the gaze and guarding chastity. And whoever cannot, then upon him is fasting, for it is a shield for him.\""],[10129,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever among you can afford to get married, let him do so, and whoever cannot afford it should fast, for it will be a restraint (Wija) for him.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2241)"],[10130,"We complained to the Prophet ﷺ about being single, so he said, \"Marry, and if you are unable to, then observe fasting, as it will be a restraint for you.\""],[10132,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to give the greeting to his right and to his left: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.'"],[10133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10134,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeting with salam, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and from the other side the like of that."],[10135,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to greet with salam to his right, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10136,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he used to greet with salam to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his face could be seen or appear. I have not forgotten, among what I have forgotten: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10138,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , that he used to give salutations with his left-hand."],[10139,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah' and to his left the like of that, until his cheek appeared to them."],[10140,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us from Hajjaj from al-Shaʿbi and Abu al-Duha from Masruq from ʿAbdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left, turning the side of his face toward them."],[10141,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and his left hand until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, saying 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah'.\""],[10142,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen."],[10143,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and left hand until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen, saying \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.\""],[10144,"Whatever I have forgotten, I have not forgotten the salam of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer: to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10145,"The Prophet ﷺ used to greet with salam to his right and to his left."],[10146,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to greet with his right hand and left hand."],[10147,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeting with salam to his right and to his left, saying: 'al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah, al-salam ʿalaykum wa rahmat Allah.'"],[10148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer. When he finished, we said: 'O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer?' He said: 'No. I am only a human like you. When I forget, remind me.' He then faced the qiblah with them and said takbir, and they said takbir. Then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then he said takbir and prostrated, and they prostrated. Then he greeted with salam to his right and to his left."],[10149,"It is as if I am looking at the whiteness of the cheeks of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he gave the salam to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,” and to his left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.”"],[10150,"I prayed with ʿAli and ʿAbdullah, and I saw them give the salam to their right and to their left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.” He claimed that they both prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave the salam to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” and to his left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah,” until the whiteness of his cheek was seen from both sides."],[10151,"It was said to Abdullah, \"A man in Makkah greets with two greetings, so how should he respond?\" He said, \"How should he attach them?\""],[10152,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform two salutations (i.e., the act of greeting by saying 'As-Salamu Alaikum').\""],[10153,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give the salam to his right and to his left.”"],[10154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fortify your wealth with zakat, treat your sick with charity, and prepare for affliction with supplication.”"],[10155,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any man whom Allah has given knowledge and he conceals it, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[10157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks for something while he is self-sufficient regarding it, it will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches on his face.”"],[10158,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever gives a loan twice, he will have the like of the reward of one of them had he given it as charity.”"],[10159,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought captives, and he began to give each household as a whole, and he disliked separating them.”"],[10160,"\"We used to perform ablution with the water of a leper's basin.\""],[10161,"«Seek it on the night of the seventeenth, for it is the morning of the Day of Furqan, the day the two hosts met.»"],[10162,"«The duration of the noon prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in summer was three feet to five feet, and in winter five feet to seven feet.»"],[10163,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: «Allah does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from stolen spoils; and begin with those you support.»"],[10164,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: «There will be rulers who kill the prayer and strangle it to the point of the death rattle; indeed it is the prayer of one worse than a donkey, and the prayer of one who finds no alternative. Whoever of you reaches that time, let him perform the prayer at its proper time, and make your prayer with them a supererogatory one.»"],[10165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade anyone from monopolizing from the children of Adam."],[10166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The world will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name.»"],[10167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was detained one night with one of his wives, and he did not come to us for the later evening prayer until the night had passed. Then he came to us, and among us were those praying and those lying down. He gave us glad tidings and said: «Indeed no one from the People of the Book performs this prayer.» Then it was revealed: {They are not all alike; among the People of the Book is an upright community who recite the verses of Allah during the hours of the night while they prostrate.}"],[10168,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «People must have a leadership, whether righteous or wicked. As for the righteous one, it is just in distribution and your spoils are divided among you equally. As for the wicked one, the believer is tested therein; and a wicked leadership is better than harj.» It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is harj?\" He said: «Killing and lying.»"],[10169,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about these two suras, and he said: «It was said to me and I said, so say as I said.»"],[10170,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ praising Nakhaʿ until I wished I were a man from Nakhaʿ."],[10171,"From Abdullah b. Masud, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: «The world will not pass away until Allah sends a man from my household whose name matches my name and whose father's name matches my father's name.»"],[10172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The Hour will not come until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name, and he will fill the earth with justice and fairness as it was filled with injustice and oppression.»"],[10173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «The nights and days will not pass away until a man from my household rules, whose name matches my name.»"],[10174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If there remained of this world but one night, a man from the household of the Prophet ﷺ would still rule during it.”"],[10175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name.”"],[10176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The world will not come to an end until a man from my family, whose name matches my name, becomes the ruler of the Arabs.\" And this wording is from the hadith of Musaddad."],[10177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The days and nights will not pass until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name. He will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with tyranny and oppression.”"],[10178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household assumes authority. He will fill the earth with fairness and justice as it was filled with oppression and tyranny. His name matches my name.”"],[10179,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household assumes authority whose name matches my name.”"],[10180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If only one day of this world remained, Allah would lengthen that day until He sends in it a man from me — or from my family, my household — whose name matches my name and whose father’s name matches my father’s name.”"],[10181,"\"For me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The world will not pass away, nor will the days end, until a man from my family controls the Arabs, and his name matches mine.'\""],[10182,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If only one night of this world remained, Allah would lengthen that night until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name and whose father’s name matches my father’s name. He will fill it with fairness and justice as it was filled with oppression and tyranny.”"],[10183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world will not come to an end until a man from my household rules whose name matches my name. He will fill the earth with fairness and justice as it was filled with tyranny and oppression.”"],[10185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The days and nights will not pass until a man from my household rules.”"],[10186,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A man from my family will come forth whose name matches my name and whose character matches my character. He will fill it with justice and fairness as it was filled with oppression and tyranny.\""],[10187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The days and nights will not pass—even if only one day remains of this world—until Allah sends a man from my ummah whose name matches my name.\""],[10188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Keep reviewing the Qur'an, for it is more prone to escape from the hearts of men than a camel from its hobbles. None of you should say, 'I forgot such-and-such a verse,' but rather he was made to forget.\""],[10189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth is the fasting of the entire age and its breaking of the fast.\""],[10190,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to fast on Mondays and Thursdays.\""],[10191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever deceives us is not of us; scheming and deceiving are in the Fire.\""],[10192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat the pre-dawn meal, for there is blessing in the pre-dawn meal.\""],[10193,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"The woman who buries her daughter alive and the girl who is buried alive are in the Fire.\""],[10194,"The companions of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr were three hundred."],[10195,"About prayer at sunrise and at sunset.\""],[10196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \"What is richness?\" He said, \"Despairing of what is in people's hands.\""],[10197,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There are no two Muslims who have two children of theirs die between them except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.\""],[10198,"\"The first to shoot an arrow in the path of Allah was Sa'd.\""],[10199,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"As for me, I prostrate on seven bones and I do not tie back hair or a garment.\""],[10200,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Abu Bakr, verily I saw myself last night at a well drawing water. You came and drew water, and you were weak, and may Allah forgive you. Then 'Umar came and it turned into a large bucket, and the people struck at the watering trough.\""],[10201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Marry virgins, for they have sweeter mouths, more productive wombs, and are more content with little.\""],[10202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say: He is Allah, the One (Qur'an 112) equals one-third of the Qur'an.\""],[10203,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When three are gathered, let not two converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that will grieve him.\""],[10204,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A woman must not describe another woman to her husband as if he were looking at her.\""],[10205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him.\""],[10206,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"],[10207,"\"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn: 'Say: O disbelievers' (Qur'an 109) and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Qur'an 112).\""],[10208,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rak'ahs after sunset: 'Say: O disbelievers' (Qur'an 109) and 'Say: He is Allah, the One' (Qur'an 112).\""],[10209,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"A caller is sent at the time of every prayer and says: O children of Adam, arise and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves. So they arise, purify themselves, and their sins fall from their eyes. They pray, and they are forgiven for what is between the two prayers. Then they kindle again in between. When the first prayer comes, he calls: O children of Adam, arise and extinguish what you have kindled upon yourselves. So they arise, purify themselves, pray, and they are forgiven for what is between the two prayers. When the afternoon prayer comes, the same, and when the sunset prayer comes, the same, and when the night prayer comes, the same. Then they sleep, having been forgiven.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"So one travels in the night for good and one travels in the night for evil.\""],[10211,"\"We used to call it in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ 'the protector', and in the Book of Allah it is a surah; whoever recites it every night has indeed done much and good.\""],[10212,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is as if I am looking at Musa in this valley, in ihram, between two Qatwani cloaks.”"],[10213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ took Ibrahim as a close friend, and your companion is the close friend of Allah, and Muhammad ﷺ is the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he recited: {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station}."],[10214,"On the day of Badr, when they brought the captives, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Abu Bakr and said: “What do you think about these?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are your people. If you kill them, they will enter the Fire. If you take ransom from them, then whoever accepts Islam will be a support for us, and whoever refuses we will take his ransom.” He said: “What do you think, O Umar?” He said: “I think you should present them and strike their necks. These are the leaders of disbelief and the commanders of disbelief. By Allah, they were not satisfied until they expelled us, and they were the first of the Arabs to raid us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abu Bakr, your likeness is that of Ibrahim ﷺ when he said: {Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me—indeed You are Forgiving and Merciful}. As for you, O Umar, your likeness is that of Nuh when he said: {My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any inhabitant from among the disbelievers}.”"],[10215,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the captives and said: “What do you think?” Umar said: “O Messenger of Allah, they belied you and expelled you; strike their necks.” Abdullah b. Rawahah said: “O Messenger of Allah, you are in a valley with much firewood; set it ablaze and throw them into it.” Al-Abbas said: “May Allah sever your kinship.” Abu Bakr said: “O Messenger of Allah, they are your kin, your root, and your people. Overlook them; Allah will save them from the Fire through you.” He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and some said the opinion was what Abu Bakr said, and others said the opinion was what Umar said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: “What do you say about these two men? Their likeness is that of brothers they had before them. Nuh said: {My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any inhabitant from among the disbelievers}. Musa said: {Our Lord, obliterate their wealth}. Isa said: {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise}. Ibrahim said: {Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me—indeed You are Forgiving and Merciful}. Allah hardens the hearts of men in it until they are harder than stones, and He softens the hearts of men in it until they are softer than softness. You are in need, and none of them will depart except with ransom or a blow to the neck.” Abdullah said: I said: “Except Suhayl b. Bayda'.” Abdullah said: I had heard him mention Islam, so he fell silent. I kept looking at the sky, waiting for stones to fall on me. I said: I put the words before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he said: “Except Suhayl b. Bayda'.”"],[10218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would find a man's shoulder leaning away from his companion's shoulder and would straighten it, saying: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.”"],[10219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform the night prayer, O People of the Quran.\" An Arab man asked, \"What does the Prophet ﷺ say?\" He replied, \"You are not one of its people.\""],[10220,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite the Night Prayer, O people of the Quran.\""],[10221,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the Children of Israel acted in disobedience, their reciters and scholars forbade them from what they were doing, but they disobeyed them. Then they mixed with them in their livelihoods, and Allah struck their hearts one upon another, then He cursed them on the tongue of Dawud and Isa son of Maryam.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat up, having been reclining, and said: “No, by the One in whose hand is my soul, until you bend them to the truth completely.”"],[10222,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “When the Children of Israel took to acts of disobedience, their scholars forbade them, but they did not desist. Then they sat with them and associated with them, so Allah struck their hearts one upon another.” Then he said: {Those who disbelieved among the Children of Israel were cursed}—the verse."],[10224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, you must enjoin good and forbid evil, and you must seize the hand of the wrongdoer and bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will strike your hearts one upon another and curse you as He cursed them.”"],[10225,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people before you, when one of them committed a sin, the one who forbade him would forbid him as a mere excuse. Then the next day, he would sit with him, eat with him, and drink with him, as if he had not seen him commit the sin yesterday. When Allah saw that from them, He struck their hearts one upon another, then He cursed them on the tongue of their Prophet Dawud and Isa son of Maryam. That was because they disobeyed and transgressed. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you must enjoin good and forbid evil, and you must seize the hands of the wrongdoer and bend him to the truth completely, or Allah will strike your hearts one upon another, then He will curse you as He cursed them.” Khalaf said: “ta'tirunahu” means “you subdue him.”"],[10226,"They were made to appear few in our eyes on the day of Badr, until I said to my companion beside me: “How many do you think they are? Do you think they are seventy?” He said: “I think they are a hundred.” Then we captured a man from them and asked him, and he said: “We were a thousand.”"],[10227,"We heard a singer singing a song that had a stronger melody than Muhammad's ﷺ melody on the day of Badr when he said, \"O Allah, I sing to you what you promised me. O Allah, if you destroy this group, they will not be worshiped.\" Then he turned around as if his face was the moon, and said, \"It's as if I'm watching the people's wrestling match at night.\""],[10229,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , performed the prayer of fear (Salat al-Khawf), so he arranged them in rows, facing the enemy, row after row. He prayed one rak'ah with them, then the row that followed him stayed behind, and they stood in the position of those who were facing the enemy. Those people advanced and prayed behind him one rak'ah, then he said the salutation to them. Then those who were behind him stood up and prayed one rak'ah, then those people advanced and stood in the position of those people, and they prayed one rak'ah.\""],[10230,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Quran was revealed in seven modes. Whoever recites according to one of them should not turn to another out of aversion to it.”"],[10231,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a donkey named Ufayr.”"],[10232,"Some people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Our companion is ill; shall we cauterize him?' He remained silent for a while, then said: 'If you wish, cauterize him; and if you wish, treat him with heated stones.'"],[10233,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from fraud.'"],[10234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heaven will show mercy to you.'"],[10235,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Who is the noblest of people?' He said, 'Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq, Allah's sacrifice.'"],[10236,"\"The Prophet ﷺ married Aisha when she was six years old, and consummated the marriage when she was nine years old, and he passed away when she was eighteen years old.\""],[10237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to instruct us, when we began the prayer, to say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. Blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god but You.'"],[10238,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The one who repents from sin is like one who has no sin.'"],[10239,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to his bed, he would say: 'O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants.'"],[10240,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we were delayed from the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha prayers. That was difficult for us, so we said, 'We are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in the path of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he called the iqama for prayer, and we prayed with each prayer's iqama. Then he said: 'There is no group on earth remembering Allah other than you.'"],[10241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat during the two rak'ahs as if on hot stones."],[10242,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he was in the two rak'ahs, was as if on hot stones. I would say, 'Until he stands,' and he would say, 'Until he stands.'"],[10243,"And Abdullah said, \"O Aba Yazid, if the Messenger of Allah saw you, he would love you. And whenever I see you, I am reminded of the sincere worshippers.\""],[10244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever builds beyond what suffices him will be burdened to carry it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[10245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated in Surat al-Najm, he and the polytheists all together."],[10246,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree, and he said, \"Which of you remembers al-Sahbawat?\" ʿAbdullah said, \"I do, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, when the moon rose, and that was the night of the twenty-seventh.\""],[10247,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Be truly modest before God.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, we are indeed modest, and praise be to God.\" He said, \"It is not that. But whoever is truly modest before God must guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it holds, and remember death and decay. Whoever desires the Hereafter abandons the adornment of this world. Whoever does that has been truly modest before God.\""],[10248,"The Messenger of God ﷺ wrote to al-Mundhir b. Sawa: \"Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat, that one is a Muslim, having the protection of God and the protection of the Messenger ﷺ.\""],[10249,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If one of you points a spear at a man, and its tip is at the hollow of his throat, and he says, 'There is no god but God,' then let him lift the spear away from him.\""],[10250,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a military expedition, and they were killed. They said, \"When you meet your people, convey to them from us that we met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.\""],[10251,"\"Beware of testimonies; if you must, then testify for an expedition the Messenger of God ﷺ sent out, who were killed, and it was revealed about them: 'Convey from us to our people that we met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and made us pleased.'\""],[10252,"God Almighty sent His Prophet ﷺ to cause a man to enter Paradise. He entered a synagogue and found Jews reading the Torah. When they came to the description of the Prophet ﷺ, they stopped. In a corner there was a sick man. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Why did you stop?\" The sick man said, \"They came to the description of a prophet and stopped.\" The sick man came crawling until he took the Torah and read it until he reached the description of the Prophet ﷺ and his community, then said, \"This is your description and the description of your community. I bear witness that there is no god but God and that you are the Messenger of God.\" Then he died. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Attend to your brother.\""],[10253,"\"We did not have a festival except at the beginning of the day, and I saw us praying the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the shade of al-Hatim.\""],[10254,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade slapping the cheeks and tearing the garments."],[10255,"ʿAbdullah: \"You have been commanded with four things: establishing prayer, giving zakah, performing Hajj and ʿUmrah to the House; Hajj is the greater Hajj and ʿUmrah is the lesser Hajj.\""],[10256,"You have been commanded in the Book of God with four things: establishing prayer, giving zakah, Hajj, and ʿUmrah to the House.\" He did not mention Ibn Masʿud."],[10257,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Bilal, and he had a heap of dates. He said, \"What is this, O Bilal?\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, it is for you and your guests.\" He said, \"Do you not fear that it will have a vapor from the Fire? Spend, O Bilal, and do not fear diminution from the Owner of the Throne.\""],[10258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not return after me to being disbelievers, striking one another's necks.\""],[10259,"Your Prophet ﷺ, when he was bowing or prostrating, would say: \"Glory be to You and praise. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\""],[10260,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The two eyes commit adultery, the two hands commit adultery, and the two feet commit adultery.\""],[10261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I had forbidden you from nabidh in certain vessels. Indeed, no vessel makes anything unlawful. Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[10262,"The passage translates to: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah has commanded me to marry Fatimah to Ali.'\""],[10263,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers.\""],[10264,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes an oath on a false matter, let him use it to take away the wealth of a Muslim and meet Allah while He is angry with him.\""],[10265,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Abusing a Muslim is Fusuq (an evil doing) and killing him is Kufr (disbelief).\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 48)"],[10266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for that, and the tattooer and the one who asks for tattooing."],[10267,"We were sitting with Abdullah bin Mas'ood when a man asked him, \"O Abu Abdullah, did you ask your prophet ﷺ how many caliphs would this ummah have?\" Ibn Mas'ood replied, \"No one has asked me about it since I arrived in Iraq before you did. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, 'The caliphs of the Children of Israel were twelve in number.'\" The wording is from a narration by Hujjaj."],[10268,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The mill of Islam will turn for five and thirty years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; if they survive, they will remain for seventy years.\""],[10269,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ looked at the slain on the day of Badr, he said to Abu Bakr: \"If Abu Talib were alive, he would know that our swords have taken hold of the chiefs.\" And that is why Abu Talib says:"],[10270,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No judge judges between people except that he will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with an angel holding him by the back of his neck until he is made to stand over Hell. Then he will raise his head to the sky; if God says, 'Throw him,' then his fall will be for forty autumns.\""],[10271,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, strengthen Islam with 'Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.\" Then God made the supplication of His Messenger for 'Umar b. al-Khattab come true, and through him He built Islam and destroyed idols."],[10272,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[10273,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, fighting him is disbelief, and the sanctity of his property is like the sanctity of his blood.\""],[10274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to like to supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."],[10275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: He is Allah, the One (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad) is one third of the Qur’an.”"],[10276,"I heard ʿAbd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “Ammā baʿd (to proceed).”"],[10277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over the people of the well and said: “O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, do they hear?” He said: “You are not more able to hear what I say than they are, but today they cannot answer.”"],[10278,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the light of the moon on the night of the full moon. The second group will be like the color of the most beautiful shining star in the sky. Each man among them will have two wives from the ḥūr al-ʿīn, each wife wearing seventy robes. The marrow of their shins will be visible from behind their flesh and robes, just as red drink is seen in a white glass.”"],[10279,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek refuge from five things: cowardice, miserliness, bad old age, the trial of the chest, and the punishment of the grave."],[10280,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying: {On the Day the earth will be changed to another earth} (Qur’an 14:48), he said: “A white earth, as if it is silver, in which no unlawful blood has been shed and no sin has been committed.”"],[10281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The houses of Allah on earth are the mosques, and it is incumbent upon Allah to honor the one who visits Him in them.”"],[10282,"He said: “The best of you is the one who learns the Qur’an and teaches it.”"],[10283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us: When one of you sneezes, let him say: “Al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds).” When he says that, let those near him say: “Yarḥamuka Allah (May Allah have mercy on you).” When they say that, let him say: “Yaghfiru Allahu lī wa lakum (May Allah forgive me and you).”"],[10284,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in an upper room that was like a bathhouse, and he was sleeping on a mat that had left marks on his side. I wept. He said: “What makes you weep, O ʿAbd Allah?” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, Kisrā and Caesar walk on silk, brocade, and fine silk, while you sleep on this mat that has left marks on your side.” He said: “Do not weep, O ʿAbd Allah, for they have this world and we have the Hereafter. What have I to do with this world? My likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who stops under a tree, then moves on and leaves it.”"],[10285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever makes his heart drink the love of this world will cleave to three things from it: misery whose weariness never ends, greed whose wealth is never attained, and hope whose end is never reached. This world is both pursuing and pursued. Whoever pursues the world, the Hereafter pursues him until death comes and seizes him. Whoever pursues the Hereafter, the world pursues him until he receives his provision from it in full.”"],[10286,"No people of prophethood were ever destroyed until fornication and usury appeared among them."],[10287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A camel [slaughtered] on the Day of Sacrifice is for ten.\""],[10288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No disease has been placed on earth except that a cure for it has been provided. It is known to those who know and unknown to those who do not know.\""],[10289,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Food for one day is a right, food for two days is a sunnah, and food for the third day is showing off. Whoever seeks to be heard, God will make him heard.\""],[10290,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The expiation for a gathering is for the servant to say: 'Glory be to You, O God, and praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.'\""],[10291,"A man from the People of the Book came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, God places the heavens on one finger, the mountains on one finger, the trees on one finger, and the water and the earth on one finger, then says: 'I am the King.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed until his molars showed, then recited: {They did not estimate God with His true estimation}."],[10293,"A scholar from among the Jewish rabbis came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"On the Day of Resurrection, God will place the heavens on this, the creatures on this, the mountains on this, and the earth on this.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and recited: {They did not estimate God with His true estimation} up to His saying: {from what they associate with Him}."],[10294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best of this community is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimonies and whose testimonies precede their oaths.\""],[10295,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"Which people are best?\" He said: \"My generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people where the testimony of one of them will precede his oath and his oath will precede his testimony.\""],[10296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The last person to exit the Fire and enter Paradise is a man who will be pushed into Paradise. He will think that it is already full, so he will say, 'O Allah! It is already full!' It will be said to him, 'Enter, for you have ten times the world or ten times what the world contains.' He will say, 'Are You laughing at me though You are the King?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars became visible.\""],[10297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Have you not seen the last person to enter Paradise and the last person to exit Hell? A man who has been touched by the flames of Hell will pass by his Lord and say, 'O Lord, take me out of this fire and put me under the shade of a tree.' When his soul leaves his body, he will look at the tree of Paradise and say, 'O Lord, let me enter Paradise.' But there will be no deeds for him to rise with, so he will depart, crawling until he reaches them. However, he will not find a place for himself there and will return to his Lord, saying, 'O Lord, I did not find a place for myself there.' The Lord will say, 'Go, for you have the equivalent of the whole world and ten times its size.' The man will say, 'Are you making fun of me when You are my Lord?' At this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars and incisors appeared.\""],[10298,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and I brought him water. He said, \"Who ordered you to do this?\" I said, \"No one ordered me.\" He said, \"You have done well; rejoice in Paradise.\" Then Ali came and he gave him glad tidings of Paradise."],[10299,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you.\" Then Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ entered, greeted, and ascended."],[10300,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will appear before you.\" Then Abu Bakr appeared, then Umar ؓ."],[10301,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in a garden and said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Abu Bakr entered. Then he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Umar entered. Then he said, \"A man from the people of Paradise will enter.\" Then Ali ؓ entered."],[10302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom, and some eloquence is magic.\""],[10303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.\""],[10304,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Keep refreshing your knowledge of the Qur'an, for it slips away from men's chests more readily than camels escape to their homelands.\""],[10305,"When the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" he would say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will. You are worthy of praise and glory.\""],[10306,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. The people said, \"Stop for us to rest,\" so he said, \"Who will wake us?\" I said, \"I will guard you and wake you.\" Then I slept and they slept, and we did not wake up except by the heat of the sun on our heads. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the last of us, so he got up, performed ablution along with the people, prayed two rak'ahs, then prayed the dawn prayer."],[10307,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"How will you be when a quarter of the people of Paradise is yours, while the rest of mankind has three-quarters?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"How will you be when a third is yours?\" They said, \"That is more.\" He said, \"How will you be when half is yours?\" They said, \"That is more.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will be one hundred and twenty rows, of which you are eighty rows.\""],[10308,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. The people fled from him, and I remained with him along with eighty of the Muhajirun and Ansar. We retreated on our feet about eighty steps, but we did not turn our backs to them. They are the ones upon whom Allah sent down tranquility. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept moving forward on his mule. His mule swerved, so he leaned off the saddle, and I rushed toward him and said, \"Lift yourself up, may Allah raise you.\" He said, \"Hand me a handful of dust.\" He threw it in their faces, and their eyes filled with dust. He said, \"Where are the Muhajirun and the Ansar?\" I said, \"They are near.\" He said, \"Call them.\" So I called them, and they came with their swords in their right hands, like shooting stars, and the polytheists turned their backs and fled."],[10309,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No Muslim is ever afflicted with any worry, grief, or distress, and says: 'Allahumma inni 'abduka, wa ibn 'abdika, wa ibn amatika, nasīyatī bi-yadika, mādin fiyya hukmuka, 'adlun fiyya qadā'uka, as'aluka bi kulli ismin huwa laka sammayta bihi nafsaka, aw anzaltahu fi kitabika, aw 'allamtahu ahadan min khalqika, awi ista'tharta bihi fi 'ilmil-ghaybi 'indaka an taj'alal-Qur'āna rabī'a qalbi, wa nūra basari, wa jalā'a huznī wa dhahāba hammi', Illa adhhaba Allahu hamahu wa abadala hu makan huznih farahan.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn these words?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Yes, whoever hears them should learn them.\""],[10310,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let your house be sufficient for you, weep over the remembrance of your sin, and control your tongue.\""],[10311,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets to mention the name of Allah at the beginning of his meal should say when he remembers: 'In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end.' For he starts a new meal and the evil one is prevented from partaking of it.\""],[10312,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Kill all snakes. Whoever leaves them out of fear of their revenge is not of me.\""],[10313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The millstone of Islam will turn at the head of thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; and if they remain, they will remain for seventy years.\""],[10315,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place his right hand over his left hand in prayer.\""],[10316,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought captives, he would give the members of a household all together, out of dislike of separating them.\""],[10317,"ʿAbdullah [b. Masʿūd ؓ ] said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by, and the people began saying, \"This is the Messenger of Allah.\" A Jew said, \"If he is the Messenger of Allah, I will ask him about something, and if he is a prophet, he will know it.\" He said, \"O Abu al-Qāsim, tell me: is a human being created from the man's semen or from the woman's semen?\" He replied, \"The man's semen is white and thick; from it come the bones and the nerves. The woman's semen is yellow and thin; from it come the blood and the flesh.\""],[10318,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer beyond its times and introduce innovations.\" He [Ibn Masʿūd] said, \"What should I do if I live to see them?\" He replied, \"You ask me, O son of Umm ʿAbd, what you should do? There is no obedience to one who disobeys Allah.\""],[10319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the glance is a poisoned arrow from among the arrows of Iblīs. Whoever abandons it out of fear of Me, I will replace it for him with faith whose sweetness he will find in his heart.\""],[10320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I saw Ibrāhīm ﷺ on the night I was taken on the Night Journey. He said, 'O Muhammad, convey greetings from me to your community, and tell them that Paradise has good soil and sweet water, and that it is a plain, and its plants are: Subḥān Allāh (Glory be to Allah), al-Ḥamdu lillāh (Praise be to Allah), Lā ilāha illā Allāh (There is no god but Allah), Allāhu akbar (Allah is Greatest), and Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh (There is no might or power except with Allah).'\""],[10321,"\"There were two men from Juhaynah who jointly owned a slave, and one of them freed him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he made him liable for it. He had a small flock of nearly one hundred sheep, so he sold them and paid his companion.\""],[10322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When two parties to a transaction differ, and the commodity is still present, then the word is the word of the seller, or they may return it.\""],[10323,"\"I have not lied since I became Muslim except for one lie. I was saddling the mount for the Prophet ﷺ when a man from the people of al-Ṭāʾif came and asked me, 'Which saddle is most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' I said, 'The Ṭāʾifī turned-down one,' but he disliked it. When it was brought to him, he said, 'Who saddled this?' They said, 'Your saddle-maker.' He said, 'Tell Ibn Umm ʿAbd to saddle it.' So the saddle was returned to me.\""],[10324,"That it was in the handwriting of his father ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, written with his own hand, and in it ʿAbdullāh said: “By Allah, besides Whom there is no deity, I have not seen anyone harsher against the overly scrupulous than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10325,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Verily the overly scrupulous are destroyed.”"],[10326,"ʿAbdullāh said: “It is only a day we used to fast before Ramaḍān.”"],[10327,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The Children of Israel appointed a successor over themselves, and he stood praying in the moonlight above Bayt al-Maqdis. He mentioned things he had done, then he lowered himself by a rope, and in the morning the rope was hanging from the mosque while he had gone. He set off until he came to a people on the seashore, and he found them making bricks. He asked them, ‘How much do you charge for these bricks?’ They told him, so he made bricks with them and ate from the work of his own hands. When prayer time came, he purified himself and prayed. That worker reported him to their village chief, saying, ‘Among us is a man who does such and such.’ So he sent for him, but he refused to come to him. Then he came riding on his mount, and when he saw him he fled. He pursued him and overtook him and said, ‘Wait, let me speak a word to you.’ He stood until he spoke to him and told him that he had been a king and that he had fled from fear of his sin. He said, ‘I will join you in that.’ So they both worshipped Allah and asked Allah to cause them to die together, and they both died.” ʿAbdullāh said: “If I were at the sands of Egypt, I would show you their graves,” describing it as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did."],[10328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has servants whom He withholds from being killed; He lengthens their lives in excellence of deeds, gives them good provision, keeps them alive in well-being, and takes their souls in well-being upon their beds, and He grants them the stations of martyrs.”"],[10329,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered the state of iḥrām when his mount set off with him."],[10330,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he passed by an anthill that had been burned with fire. He said: “It is not appropriate for anyone to punish with the punishment of Allah.”"],[10332,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a small bird fluttering over the heads of his Companions and said: “Who has disturbed this one?” A man from the Anṣār said: “I took its eggs, or its chicks.” So he ordered him to return them."],[10334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When the two parties to a sale disagree, the word is that of the seller.”"],[10335,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"No one is more jealous than Allah, because He has forbidden indecencies. And no one loves praise more than Allah, because He has praised Himself. And no one loves excuses more than Allah, because He accepts excuses from His creation. And no one loves praise more than Allah, because He praises Himself.\""],[10336,"The Prophet ﷺ went hungry, so he sent a message to his wives to bring him some food, but none of them had any. He then said, \"O Allah, I ask you for your bounty and mercy, for no one possesses them except you.\" He was then given a praying sheep and he said, \"This is from the bounty of Allah, and we are awaiting His mercy.\""],[10337,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Insulting a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.”"],[10338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform the dawn prayer when it is bright, for that is greater for the reward.”"],[10339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The excellence of the night prayer over the day prayer is like the excellence of secret charity over open charity.”"],[10340,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Our Lord marvels at two men: a man who rises from his bed and cover, leaving his beloved and family for his prayer. Allah ﷻ says to His angels, 'Look at My servant; he rose from his bed and cover, leaving his beloved and family for his prayer, out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me.' And a man who goes out to fight in the cause of Allah and flees, then knows the consequence of fleeing and the reward of returning, so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah, the Exalted, says to His angels, 'Look at My servant; he returned out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me until his blood was shed.'"],[10341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If it were said to the people of the Fire, 'You will remain in the Fire for the number of every pebble in the world,' they would rejoice. And if it were said to the people of Paradise, 'You will remain in Paradise for the number of every pebble in the world,' they would grieve. But eternity has been decreed for them."],[10342,"He said: Won't you come near, O Abu Muhammad, for the midday meal? He said: Did you fast this day? He said: 'We used to fast this day before Ramadan was revealed. When Ramadan was revealed, we fasted it and abandoned what was other than it.'"],[10343,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'Allah will gather the nations on the Day of Resurrection, then He will descend from His Throne to His Footstool, and His Footstool encompasses the heavens and the earth.'"],[10344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments: a San'ani striped cloak and two Hibara striped cloaks."],[10345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Two types of people are insatiable and never satisfied: the seeker of knowledge and the seeker of this world."],[10346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone, for the first to seize the dominion of my community and what Allah has granted them will be the Banu Qantura'.'"],[10347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will always be forty men of my community whose hearts are like the heart of Abraham; Allah repels harm from the people of the earth through them. They are called al-Abdal.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They did not attain this through prayer, fasting, or charity.' They said: O Messenger of Allah, how did they attain it? He said: 'Through generosity and sincere counsel to the Muslims.'"],[10348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, al-Salam (peace) is one of the names of Allah which He placed on earth, so spread it among yourselves. When a man greets a group and they respond, he has a degree of superiority over them because he reminded them. If they do not respond, then one better and purer than them responds to him.'"],[10350,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The Fire has been kindled and Paradise has been brought near. O people of the rooms! If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.'"],[10351,"From the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"Indeed, after you there will come a time of patience for those who adhere to it, their reward will be equivalent to that of fifty martyrs.\" So, 'Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, from us or from them?\" He said, \"From among you.\""],[10352,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a horse that he rode at a flowing pace, and it pleased him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This horse of mine is indeed a sea.'"],[10353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something which, if you do it, you will love one another? Spread peace among yourselves.'"],[10354,"The first thing I learned of the affair of the Messenger of God ﷺ: I came to Makkah with some uncles of mine, and we were directed to al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. We reached him while he was sitting at Zamzam, so we sat with him. While we were with him, a man approached from the gate of al-Safa, white with a redness over him, having thick, curly hair reaching halfway down his ears, aquiline-nosed, with a slight projection at the bridge, bright front teeth, dark wide eyes, a full beard, a thin line of hair from chest to navel, rough hands and feet, wearing two white garments, as though he were the moon on the night of the full moon. Walking on his right was a beardless youth of handsome face, near puberty or having reached it, and behind them came a woman who had covered her beauty until he made for the Black Stone and touched it, then the youth touched it, then the woman touched it. Then he circumambulated the House seven times, with the youth and the woman circumambulating with him. Then he touched the corner, raised his hands and said takbir, and the youth stood at his right and raised his hands, and the woman stood behind them, raised her hands and said takbir. He prolonged the qunut, then bowed and prolonged the bowing, then raised his head from bowing and performed qunut while standing, then prostrated, and the youth and the woman prostrated with him, doing as he did and following him. He said: We saw something we did not recognize in Makkah, so we found it strange. We turned to al-Abbas and said: O Abu al-Fadl, this religion we did not know among you—has something new occurred? He said: Yes, by God. Do you not know this one? We said: No. He said: This is my nephew, Muhammad b. Abd Allah, and the youth is Ali b. Abi Talib, and the woman is Khadija bt. Khuwaylid. By God, there is no one on the face of the earth who worships God by this religion except these three."],[10355,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; my community from them are eighty rows.”"],[10356,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days.”"],[10357,"Aisha had an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma'il. Captives from Bal'anbar arrived, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to free from among them, and he said: “Whoever has an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma'il, let him not free anyone from Himyar.” Ali b. 'Abis said: I said to Isma'il b. Abi Khalid: What was Himyar? He said: He is greater than Isma'il."],[10358,"They said: O Messenger of God, you have forgotten? He said: “Why should I not forget when the groove of one of you is between his nail and his fingertips?”"],[10359,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I am your forerunner at the Pool, and I will vie with the nations by you, so do not fight one another after me.”"],[10360,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When the appointed term of one of you is in a land, he is brought to it for a need.”"],[10361,"“We have been commanded to fulfill an oath.”"],[10362,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and then the nearest, then the next nearest.”"],[10363,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Perform Hajj and 'Umrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sin as the bellows removes impurity from iron and gold and silver, and Hajj Al-Mabrur brings no less a reward than Paradise.''' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2631)"],[10364,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The slain person will come, grasping his killer, while his veins gush blood before the Possessor of Might, and he will say: O Lord, ask this one why he killed me. Then He will say: Why did you kill him? If he says: I killed him so that glory would be for so-and-so, He will say: It is God's.”"],[10365,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The Emigrants, the Helpers, the freed ones of Quraysh, and the freed ones of Thaqif—some of them are allies of others in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[10366,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am your forerunner at the Pool.”"],[10367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies while setting up a rival to Allah, Allah will place him in the Fire.”"],[10368,"To wash your hands until they are clean, then enter your right hand into the container and pour with your right hand onto your left hand to wash your private parts until they are clean. Then hit the wall and the ground with your left hand and rub them, then pour water onto them with your right hand to wash them. Then perform ablution for prayer."],[10369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every good deed is charity.”"],[10370,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Among the worst of people are those whom the Hour overtakes while they are still alive, and those who take graves as places of prostration.”"],[10371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, and there were some women of the Ansar in it. He admonished them and reminded them, and said: “There is no woman among you who loses three of her children but that she will enter Paradise.” One of the women said: “Is it not [also] for those who lose two, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “And for those who lose two.”"],[10372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How bad it is for one of you to say, ‘I forgot a verse, such-and-such,’ but rather he was made to forget. Keep reviewing the Quran, for it is wild and flees more swiftly from the chests of men than camels from their hobbles.”"],[10373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies setting up a rival to Allah will enter the Fire. And the five prescribed prayers are expiations for what occurs between them, as long as major sins are avoided.”"],[10374,"“Instruct your dying ones to say: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ for the soul of the believer comes out like sweat, while the soul of the disbeliever comes out from the side of his mouth like the breath of a donkey.”"],[10375,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Keep reviewing the Quran, for it flees more swiftly from the chests of men than cattle from their hobbles.”"],[10376,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman must not have skin-to-skin contact with another woman, for she will describe her to her husband or to a man as if he is looking at her.”"],[10377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you are three,” and he mentioned something similar, and he added to it: “Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[10378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the prayer of seeking guidance: “O Allah, I ask You to choose for me by Your knowledge and to decree for me by Your power, and I ask You of Your bounty, for You are able and I am not able, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah, if You know that this matter is good for me in my religion and good for me in my livelihood and good for me in what I seek good through, then decree it for me in well-being, make it easy for me, and bless it for me. And if You know that something other than it is better for me, then decree for me the good wherever it may be.”"],[10379,"The Prophet ﷺ only forbade the meat of domesticated donkeys because they were used for work."],[10380,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I saw Jibril ﷺ , and he had six hundred wings.\""],[10381,"\"The most beloved of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the best of you in character, and the most hateful of you to me on the Day of Resurrection are the boastful and the arrogant.\" I said to Ibn Bahdalah, \"What are the arrogant?\" He replied, \"The proud.\""],[10382,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The first thing to be judged between people on the Day of Resurrection is bloodshed, and the first thing for which a servant will be called to account is prayer.\""],[10383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us these words: \"O Allah, reconcile our hearts and bring harmony between us, guide us to the paths of peace, deliver us from darkness to light, keep us away from immoralities, both apparent and hidden. O Allah, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our spouses, and our offspring, and turn to us in mercy. Indeed, You are the Ever-Relenting, the Merciful. Make us grateful for Your blessings, praising You for them, and proclaiming them, and complete them upon us.\""],[10384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah while there were three hundred and sixty idols around the House. He began striking them with a stick he had, saying: \"Truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is bound to vanish. Truth has come, and falsehood can neither originate nor repeat.\""],[10385,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Hell will be brought, led by seventy thousand reins; with each rein, seventy thousand angels pulling it.\""],[10386,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one is killed unjustly without a share of the sin falling upon the son of Adam.\" This is how Sulayman al-Taymi narrated it from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah b. Murrah, from Shaqiq; but others narrated from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah b. Murrah, from Masruq."],[10387,"'Abdullah said: \"Indeed, I am informed of where you are, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except the dislike of boring you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to space out his admonitions to us over the days, fearing we would become weary.\""],[10389,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with people who honor the extravagant and belittle the worshipers, and who act according to the Qur'an when it aligns with their desires and abandon it when it contradicts their desires? At that point, they believe in some things and disbelieve in others. They strive for what can be attained without effort, without taking into account predestined fate, appointed time, and allotted sustenance. And they do not strive for what cannot be attained except through effort, hoping for a fully rewarded return, a deserving effort, and a trade that does not perish.\""],[10390,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, how can I know when I have done well and when I have done wrong?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"When you hear your neighbors saying, 'You have done well,' then you have done well; and when you hear them saying, 'You have done wrong,' then you have done wrong.\""],[10391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer, and he either added to it or omitted from it. Some of them asked him, \"Has something new occurred in the prayer?\" He replied, \"Nothing new has occurred in it. Had something new occurred, I would have told you; but I am a human being and I forget. So when I forget, remind me.\" He then completed what remained of his prayer, performed two prostrations of forgetfulness, and said, \"When one of you prays and does not know whether he has added or omitted, let him strive to determine what is correct, then let him prostrate twice while sitting.\""],[10392,"\"He said about reading behind the imam, listen to the recitation as you have been commanded; for in prayer, there is fulfillment and that imam will suffice you.\""],[10393,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"How bad it is for a man or a woman to say, 'I forgot such-and-such a Surah' or 'such-and-such a verse.' Rather, he was made to forget.\""],[10394,"From Ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the Prophet ﷺ saying: 'Let none of you say: I forgot such-and-such a verse, for he did not forget; rather, he was made to forget.'"],[10395,"I entered upon Ibn Mas'ud on the day of 'Ashura' while he was eating fresh dates. He said: 'This is the day of 'Ashura', a day we were commanded to fast before Ramadan was revealed.'"],[10396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim.'"],[10397,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, the drop of semen remains in the womb for forty days, then it becomes a clinging clot for a similar period, then it becomes a lump of flesh for a similar period. Then God sends the angel with four words, and he writes its provision, its lifespan, and whether it is wretched or blessed.'"],[10398,"'None is more jealous than God; that is why He forbade immorality, both open and secret.'"],[10399,"O daughter of the Messenger of God, did the Messenger of God ﷺ leave with you anything that you could gift me? She said: 'O servant girl, bring that leaf.' She searched for it but could not find it. She said: 'Woe to you, search for it; for it is equal in my sight to Hasan and Husayn.' She searched for it, and behold, she had swept it away with her sweepings. In it was written: Muhammad ﷺ said: 'He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his harm. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. God loves the modest, forbearing, chaste, self-restrained one, and He hates the obscene, foul-mouthed, persistent beggar. Indeed, modesty is part of faith, and faith is in Paradise, while obscenity is from vulgarity, and vulgarity is in the Fire.'"],[10400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When one of you approaches his wife, let him cover himself, and let them not strip completely like two donkeys.'"],[10401,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Accept the invitation, do not reject the gift, and do not strike the people'—or 'the Muslims.'"],[10402,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever God wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.'"],[10403,"O tongue, speak good and you will gain, and be silent from evil and you will be safe, before you regret. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Most of the sins of the son of Adam are from his tongue.'"],[10404,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever has a daughter and disciplines her well, teaches her well, and gives her generously from the blessings of God that He has bestowed upon him, she will be a protection and a shield for him from the Fire.'"],[10405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When my companions are mentioned, remain silent. And when the stars are mentioned, remain silent. And when fate is mentioned, remain silent.\""],[10406,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Keep revising the Qurʾān, for it escapes from the hearts of men more quickly than camels escape from their hobbles. How bad it is for any of you to say, \"I forgot such-and-such a verse,\" when in fact he was made to forget.'"],[10407,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The Qurʾān is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted and a disputant whose argument is confirmed. Whoever places it before him, it leads him to Paradise; whoever places it behind him, it drives him to the Fire.'"],[10408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Among the signs of the Hour's approach is the swelling of the new moons.'"],[10409,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'In the last days there will be people who sit in the mosques in circles, their focus being this world. Do not sit with them, for God has no need of them.'"],[10410,"\"I came to Kufa for trade and I stayed near Al-A'mash. When it was night, I intended to descend, but he stood up and performed Tahajjud prayer. I passed by him reciting this verse: 'Allah bears witness that there is no deity except Him, and [so do] the angels and those of knowledge - [that He is] maintaining [creation] in justice. There is no deity except Him, the Exalted in Might, the Wise. Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.' Then Al-A'mash said, 'I bear witness to what Allah has borne witness to, and I entrust this testimony to Allah, and it is in His custody: 'Indeed, the religion in the sight of Allah is Islam.' He repeated it several times. I said, 'Indeed, I heard something in it,' so I went to him the next morning and bid him farewell. Then I said, 'O Abu Muhammad, I heard you reciting this verse repeatedly.' He said, 'So, you did not understand its meaning?' I said, 'I have been with you for a month and you have not informed me.' He said, 'By Allah, I will inform you of its meaning after a year.' So, I stayed for a year, and I was at his door. When the year passed, I said, 'O Abu Muhammad, the year has passed.' He said, 'Abu Wa'il informed me from Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The one who brings this verse with its companion on the Day of Resurrection, Allah will say: My servant fulfilled his covenant, and I am more entitled to fulfill the covenant. Bring My servant into Paradise.'\""],[10411,"'The straight path upon which the Messenger of God ﷺ left us.'"],[10412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah than these ten days.\" It was said, \"Not even Jihad in the cause of Allah?\" He said, \"Not even Jihad in the cause of Allah.\""],[10413,"that we prostrate on seven bones and that we do not gather up our hair or our garment."],[10414,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abū Bakr as an intimate friend.'"],[10415,"'We used to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ and we did not perform ablution from wherever our feet trod.'"],[10416,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The dead are tormented in their graves, so much so that even the beasts hear their cries.'"],[10417,"'A Muslim man may do good in the last third of his life at the time of his death, and God will thereby render his zakat complete.'"],[10418,"From ʿAbdullāh, who attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ: 'People are of two kinds: a scholar and a learner, and there is no good in anyone else.'"],[10419,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said regarding His saying, \"He will pay them their rewards in full and give them more from His bounty\": 'Their rewards: He will admit them to Paradise; and He will give them more from His bounty: intercession for those for whom intercession is due, who did good to them in this world.'"],[10420,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.”"],[10421,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a rider came and made his camel kneel by the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I have come to you from a journey of nine days; I have exhausted my body, stayed awake through my nights, and gone thirsty through my days to ask you about two traits that keep me awake. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “What is your name?” He said: I am Zayd al-Khayl. He said: “Rather, you are Zayd al-Khayr.” He said: I ask you about God's sign regarding one whom He wills good for and His sign regarding one whom He does not will good for. I love good and its people and those who act upon it, and if I act upon it I am certain of its reward, and if I miss anything of it I long for it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “God's sign regarding one whom He wills good for and His sign regarding one whom He does not will good for is: if He willed good for you in the Hereafter, He would prepare you for it, then He would not care in which valley you go.”"],[10422,"'Abdullah: divorce is in a period of purity without intercourse."],[10423,"The eighteen men from the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ who were killed on the day of Badr: God placed their souls in Paradise in green birds that roam freely in Paradise. He said: While they were like that, your Lord looked upon them with a glance and said: “O My servants, what do you desire?” They said: “Our Lord, there is nothing above this.” He said: “O My servants, what do you desire?” They said on the fourth time: “Return our souls to our bodies so that we may be killed as we were killed.”"],[10424,"He said to his family: If you follow what I command you, I will hand over my wealth to you; otherwise I will not. They said: We will follow what you command us. He said: When I die, burn me with fire, then crush my bones thoroughly, and when you see a day of strong wind, climb to the top of a mountain and scatter me in the wind. He said: They did it. 'Abdullah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: He fell into God's hand, and He said to him: “What carried you to do what you did?” He said: “Fear of You.” He said: “I have forgiven you.”"],[10425,"A Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: How excellent a community is your community, were it not that they associate equals. He said: “How do they associate equals?” He said: They say, “What God wills and you will.” He said: “He is saying something. Say: What God wills, then you will.”"],[10426,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I want to go out to Bahrayn for trade. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Pray two rak'ahs.”"],[10427,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Were the religion suspended from the Pleiades, men from the sons of Persia would reach it.”"],[10428,"“Indeed, before the Hour there will be days of turmoil in which knowledge will be lifted and ignorance will descend.”"],[10429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to place his hands between his knees in prayer."],[10430,"He sent to his brothers among the people of Kufa and ordered them to gather so that he could bid them farewell. They gathered in the portico of the mosque. He came to them, greeted them, and ordered them not to dispute about the Qur'an. He informed them that whoever rejects anything of it has rejected all of it. He told them that they used to dispute about it in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ and that they used to recite to him, and he would tell all of them that they were excellent. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “Tongues do not differ over it, nor does it wear out from much repetition. That is because the law of Islam in it is one: its prescribed punishments and its obligations. If one of the two readings commanded something the other forbade, the obligations and prescribed punishments would differ in it.” And he mentioned a word: “If I knew that anyone had more knowledge than me of what was sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ, whom camels could reach, I would go to him until I joined his knowledge to my knowledge. I read seventy suras from the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Qur'an was presented to him every year, and I would present it to him and he would tell me that I was excellent, until the year in which he was taken, when it was presented to him twice, then I recited to him. I will not abandon it out of aversion to it.”"],[10431,"«I saw the Prophet ﷺ apply kohl to the eye of ʿAlī ؓ with his saliva.»"],[10432,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ used to breathe three breaths into the vessel, pronouncing the Name of God at each breath and expressing gratitude at the last of them.»"],[10433,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «Among people are keys to the remembrance of God—when they are seen, God is remembered.»"],[10434,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the words of God ﷻ, {For God is his protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous believers}: He said, “The righteous believers are Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ.”"],[10435,"ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd: This verse was revealed—{Those who purchase a small price with God’s covenant and their oaths}—nothing abrogated it. So any man who seizes the property of a Muslim by his oath is among the people of this verse."],[10436,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «Paradise has eight gates: seven closed and one open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction.»"],[10437,"I performed Hajj with Ibn Masʿud , and saw him doing Rami of the big Jamra (Jamrat-ul-Aqaba) with seven small pebbles, keeping the Kaʿba on his left side and Mina on his right. He then said, \"This is the place where the one on whom Surat-al-Baqara was revealed (i.e. Messenger of Allah ﷺ ) stood.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1749)"],[10438,"Here, I saw the one upon whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed, responding."],[10439,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I did everything with her except intercourse,” meaning with a woman. Then God ﷻ revealed: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds.}"],[10440,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: «The believer is not a slanderer, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor indecent.»"],[10442,"From al-tabaqqur.\""],[10443,"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade a gold ring or a gold circle."],[10444,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold rings.\""],[10445,"That Abu Bakr went out, and nothing brought him out but hunger, and that Umar went out, and nothing brought him out but hunger, and that the Prophet ﷺ came out to them, and they told him that nothing had brought them out but hunger. He said, \"Come with us to the house of a man from the Ansar called Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan.\" When he was not at home—he had gone to fetch water—the woman welcomed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his two companions and spread something for them, and they sat on it. The Prophet ﷺ asked her, \"Where has Abu al-Haytham gone?\" She said, \"He has gone to fetch fresh water for us.\" He did not wait long before he came with a water-skin containing water and hung it up. He wanted to slaughter a sheep for them, but it was as if the Prophet ﷺ disliked that for them. So he slaughtered a young she-goat for them. Then he went off and came with clusters of dates. They ate of that meat, unripe dates, and ripe dates, and drank from the water. One of the two—either Abu Bakr or Umar—said, \"This is part of the bliss about which we will be asked.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The believer is not reproached for anything he obtains in this world; only the disbeliever is reproached.\""],[10446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are a man who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, or a man who leads people astray without knowledge, or an image-maker who makes images.\""],[10447,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud: \"They have diminished it, may Allah diminish them. By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for ten years and he never diminished it by even one.\""],[10448,"\"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ that he used to say in the sermon of necessity, 'Praise be to Allah, we seek His help and ask for His forgiveness. We seek refuge in Allah from the evil within ourselves. Whoever Allah guides, there is no one who can lead him astray, and whoever He leads astray, there is no guide for him. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. Whoever obeys Allah and His messenger has been guided, and whoever disobeys them harms only themselves. Allah will not be harmed by anyone.'\""],[10449,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Beware of the sins that are considered insignificant, for they gather against a man until they destroy him. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave an example for them: like a man in a desolate land who was preparing food for a group. One man began bringing a stick and another man began bringing a stick until they gathered a great heap and lit a fire, and cooked what was in it.\""],[10450,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Bathing on Friday is sunnah.\""],[10451,"\"That it be for me is dearer than what the sun has risen upon.\" He stood before the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr and said: \"We do not say to you as the people of Musa said, 'So go, you and your Lord'\" - the verse - \"but we will fight on your right and on your left.\" And I saw the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, its features beaming."],[10452,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Indeed, incantations, amulets, and love charms are shirk.\""],[10453,"A man said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, this is the camel we used to hear about.\" He said: \"Then where is the she-camel with the blaze?\""],[10454,"I was sitting with 'Abdullah and Hudhayfah when a woman and a man passed by them on a camel, their faces turned away. One of them said to his companion: \"This is the one we used to talk about.\" He said: \"No, with that one there is the she-camel with the blaze.\""],[10455,"Some people came to the Prophet of God ﷺ with their companion and said: \"O Prophet of God, our companion here has been ruined by shyness.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed, shyness is part of the laws of Islam, and obscenity is from a person's baseness.\""],[10456,"My father had stopped praying with us. I said: \"What is the matter with you that you have stopped praying with us?\" He said: \"You make it too light.\" I said: \"What about the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: 'Among you are the old, the weak, and those with needs'?\" He said: \"I heard 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud say that.\" Then he prayed three times as much as you pray."],[10457,"\"About the private parts of women.\""],[10458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People among the Muslims who were punished in the Fire will certainly enter Paradise by God's mercy and the intercession of the intercessors.\""],[10459,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ was not imagined by anyone who saw him.\""],[10460,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, God ﷻ has not made anything sacred except that He knew someone among you would come to know of it. Verily, I am holding you by your waists to keep you from tumbling into the Fire as moths and flies tumble.\""],[10461,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no man who is among a people who disobey God while they are more numerous and stronger than him, then they flatter regarding his affair, except that God punishes them.\""],[10462,"Intercession will continue for people as they are coming out of the Fire, until even Iblis, the most deceitful, will stretch his neck hoping that it may reach him."],[10463,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Do not ever seek to please anyone by displeasing Allah, and do not praise anyone for a favor that is from Allah, and do not blame anyone for what Allah has not given you. For the provision of Allah is not brought to you by the greed of a greedy person, nor is it repelled from you by the dislike of one who dislikes it. And indeed Allah, exalted is He, in His justice and fairness placed ease and joy in contentment and certainty, and placed worry and grief in displeasure.\""],[10464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of the Fire with the most severe punishment on the Day of Resurrection are one who killed a prophet or was killed by a prophet, a tyrannical imam, and these image-makers.\""],[10465,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which wrongdoing is greatest? He said: \"A cubit of land that a believer diminishes from his brother's right, not a single pebble of it except that he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first of this ummah are its best, and the last of them are its worst, differing and divided. So whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, then let his death come to him while he treats people as he would love to be treated.\""],[10467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the riding beast of one of you runs loose in a desert land, let him call: 'O servants of Allah, restrain it for me! O servants of Allah, restrain it for me! For indeed Allah has in the earth someone present who will restrain it for you.'\""],[10468,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no night talk except for one who is praying or for a traveler.\""],[10469,"A group of the nobles of Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while some Muslims, including Suhayb and Khabbab, were with him. They said: \"O Muhammad, are these the ones Allah has favored from among us? If you were to drive these away, we would follow you.\" Then Allah, glorified and exalted, revealed: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face} up to His saying: {Is not Allah most knowing of the thankful?}"],[10470,"\"Eat, for this is a day that used to be fasted before Ramadan was revealed; then Ramadan was revealed and this day was abandoned.\""],[10471,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"There is none among you but has been assigned a companion from the jinn.\" It was asked, \"Even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Even me. However, Allah has helped me against him, so he has embraced Islam and does not command me except with good.\""],[10474,"Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Dhuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha; so it was said to him (why), and he said: \"I did it so that my ummah may not be in hardship.\""],[10475,"He said to me: \"Come closer,\" so he brought me close until he seated me on his carpet, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Parents will have a debt owed to them by their child, and on the Day of Resurrection they will cling to him and he will say: I am your child; then they would wish, or they will desire, that he had been more than that.\""],[10476,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Being killed in the cause of Allah expiates all sins\" or he said \"everything except the trust. And the trust is in prayer, the trust is in fasting, and the trust is in speech; but the most severe of that is deposits.\" Sharik said: ʿAyyash al-ʿAmiri narrated to me from Zadhan from ʿAbdullah from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[10477,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) has angels on the earth who roam about, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10478,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) has angels who roam about on the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10479,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, God has angels who roam about on the earth, conveying to me the greetings of peace from my community.”"],[10481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Dreams are glad tidings from Allah, and they are part of Prophet-hood, seventy parts of it. Verily, this fire of yours [in the light of the sun] is one of seventy parts of the heat of Hell.\" And he also said, \"Whoever goes to the mosque and waits for the prayer, he is considered to be in prayer as long as he does not commit any impurity. And whoever observes prayer after the prayer, he is considered to be in prayer as long as he does not commit any impurity.\""],[10482,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one will enter the Fire who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, and no one will enter Paradise who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride.” A man said: “O Messenger of God, I like my garment to be clean, my head to be oiled, my sandal strap to be new”—and he mentioned things, until he mentioned the whip's loop—“is that from pride, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No, that is beauty. Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) is beautiful and loves beauty. But pride is to disregard the truth and look down on people.”"],[10483,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he allotted dwellings, and he allotted to Ibn Masʿūd among those he allotted. His companions said to him: “O Messenger of God, turn him away from us.” He said: “Why then did God send me? Indeed, God (Mighty and Sublime) does not sanctify a community that does not give its weak ones their right.”"],[10484,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the Day of Conquest, and around the Kaʿbah there were three hundred and sixty idols. He began piercing them and saying: “The truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed, falsehood is ever vanishing.”"],[10485,"He heard ʿAbd Allāh b. Masʿūd say: “I did not fast with the Messenger of God ﷺ twenty-nine days more often than I fasted with him thirty.”"],[10486,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever commits a sin and then regrets it, that is its expiation.”"],[10487,"“Indeed, usury, even if it becomes abundant, its outcome leads to scarcity.”"],[10488,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Riba does not become widespread except that its outcome leads to scarcity.”"],[10489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A true, righteous dream is one of seventy-six parts of prophethood.”"],[10490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is sufficient for a person, when he sees an evil that he is unable to change, that Allah knows that he disapproves of it.”"],[10491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A servant may be born a believer, live as a believer, and die a disbeliever; and a servant may be born a disbeliever, live as a disbeliever, and die a believer. A servant may act for a period of his life with felicity, then what is written for him overtakes him and he dies wretched; and a servant may act for a period of his life with wretchedness, then what is written for him overtakes him and he dies happy.”"],[10492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created Yahya b. Zakariyya in his mother’s womb a believer, and created Pharaoh in his mother’s womb a disbeliever.”"],[10493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There are no two Muslims except that between them is a veil from Allah. When one of them says to his companion something offensive, he tears his veil, and when he says, ‘O disbeliever,’ then one of them has disbelieved.”"],[10494,"I used to greet the Prophet ﷺ and he would return my greeting, but I greeted him and he did not return it. I said: I used to greet you and you would return my greeting, but I greeted you and you did not return it. He said: “Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings about whatever He wills in His command.”"],[10495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed your companion is the Khalil of Allah,” meaning himself ﷺ."],[10496,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he did not see Jibril in his true form except twice. He said: As for one time, he asked him to show himself in his true form, so he showed himself to him, and he came filling the horizon. As for the second, he was with him when he ascended, regarding His saying: “Then he drew near and came down, and was at a distance of two bow lengths or nearer, and He revealed to His servant what He revealed” [53:8–10]. When Jibril sensed his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, he returned to his form, and that is His saying: “And he certainly saw him in another descent at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, near which is the Garden of Refuge… He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord” [53:13–18]. He said: “The creation of Jibril.”"],[10497,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will guard us tonight?” Abdullah said: I said, “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will sleep.” Then he repeated: “Who will guard us tonight?” I said, “I will,” until he repeated it three times, and I said, “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then you.” So I guarded them until near dawn, when the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ overtook me, “You will sleep,” and I slept. Nothing woke us except the heat of the sun on our backs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and performed ablution as he used to do and prayed the two rak‘ahs of Fajr, then led us in the Fajr prayer. When he finished, he said: “If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had willed that you not sleep through it, you would not have slept, but He willed it to be—or he said, it will be—for those after you. So this is for anyone who sleeps or forgets.” Then the Prophet’s she-camel and the people’s camels scattered. The people went out searching for them and brought back their camels except the Prophet’s she-camel. Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Take this direction.” I took the direction he indicated and found its halter tangled around a tree. By Allah, nothing could have untied it except a hand. He said: I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I found its halter tangled around a tree, nothing could have untied it except a hand. He said: And upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was revealed: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [48:1]."],[10498,"I heard Abdullah b. Mas‘ud say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram from al-Hudaybiyyah. We traveled at night and stopped in soft sandy ground. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who will guard us?” Bilal said: “I will.” He said: “Then you will sleep.” He said: They slept until the sun rose, and so-and-so and so-and-so woke up, among them Umar, but the Prophet ﷺ did not wake. Someone said: “Dismount,” and the Prophet ﷺ woke up and said: “Do as you used to do.” When they did, he said: “Thus is it for anyone among you who sleeps or forgets.”"],[10499,"“With us on the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept through the Fajr prayer until the sun rose, there were two camel-drivers.”"],[10500,"From the Prophet ﷺ: When he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he would say, “O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling whatever is between them and filling whatever You will after that—Lord of praise and Lord of majesty and glory. There is none to withhold what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him not against You.”"],[10502,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no faith for him who has no trustworthiness, and there is no religion for him who has no covenant. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the religion of a servant will not be correct until his tongue is correct, and his tongue will not be correct until his heart is correct. And he will not enter Paradise who does not feel secure from his neighbor's harms.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the harms?\" He said, \"His cheating and his oppression. And whatever man acquires wealth from unlawful sources and then he spends from it, it will not be blessed for him, and if he gives charity, it will not be accepted from him. And what remains will only increase him in the Fire. Verily, the impure does not remove the impure, but rather the pure removes the impure.\""],[10503,"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? He replied, \"Like the flowing water, yes.\""],[10504,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by his companions one day and said to them, “Do you know what your Lord, Mighty and Sublime, is saying?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said it three times. He said, “By My might and My majesty, no servant performs it at its proper time except that I enter him into Paradise, and whoever performs it other than at its proper time, if I will I have mercy on him, and if I will I punish him.”"],[10505,"“From which people is the man?” I said, “A man from the people of Basra.” He said, “From which tribe?” I said, “From this clan of Banu Saʿd.” He said to me, “O Saʿdi, I will narrate to you a hadith about you which I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, shall I not guide you to a people of great wealth and great strength, from whom you may take abundant property—or he said, much property?’ He said, ‘Who are they?’ He said, ‘They are this clan of Banu Saʿd from the people of the sands.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Indeed Banu Saʿd have a great share with Allah.’ Ask, O Saʿdi.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, is there any knowledge by which the Hour is known?” He was reclining, and he sat up straight and said, “O Saʿdi, you have asked me about something I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, is there any knowledge by which the Hour is known?’ He said to me, ‘O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed the Hour has signs, and indeed the Hour has portents. Indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the child becomes a source of anger, and that the rain becomes scorching heat, and that the wicked overflow in abundance. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the liar is believed and the truthful is rejected. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the treacherous is entrusted and the trustworthy is betrayed. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that close relatives sever ties and wombs are cut off. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that every tribe is ruled by its hypocrites and every market by its wicked. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mosques are adorned and hearts are ruined. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that a believer in his tribe is more humiliated than a stray sheep. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that men suffice with men and women with women. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that mosques become crowded and pulpits are raised. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that the ruins of the world are built up and its inhabited places are ruined. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that musical instruments appear and wine is drunk. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is the drinking of wine. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour are the police, the slanderers, and the backbiters. O Ibn Masʿūd, indeed among the signs and portents of the Hour is that children born of fornication become many.’” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, while they are Muslims?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, while the Qur’an is among them?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, how can that be?” He said, “A time will come upon people when a man divorces his wife, then denies her divorce and remains upon her private part, so the two of them are fornicators as long as they remain.”"],[10506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Souls are troops assembled together; those that recognized one another came together, and those that disavowed one another differed.”"],[10507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Let not the call of Bilal prevent any of you from his pre-dawn meal, for he only calls the adhan so that your sleeper may wake, and your standing one may return, and the dawn appears like this.”"],[10508,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever drags his garments out of pride, Allah will not look at him, neither in what is lawful nor in what is unlawful.” This Ismaʿil is Ibn Abi Khalid, and Allah knows best."],[10509,"A man kissed a woman and then went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have done such and such.\" So Allah revealed the verse, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove the evil deeds.\" The man asked, \"Is it for me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"No, it is for my Ummah (nation).\""],[10510,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about a man who performs ghusl from janabah and water misses part of his body. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “He should wash that place, then pray.”"],[10511,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Shall I not inform you of those for whom the Fire is forbidden?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Every gentle, soft, near, and easy person.”"],[10512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When one of you is invited to a meal, let him respond. If he is not fasting, let him eat, and if he is fasting, let him supplicate for blessing.”"],[10513,"I argued with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me, so I came to ʿImran b. al-Husayn al-Khuzaʿi, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said, “O Abu Nujayd, I argued with the Qadariyyah and they cornered me. Is there a hadith you can narrate to me, perhaps Allah will benefit me by it?” He said, “Perhaps if I narrate a hadith to you, you will cover your ears as if you did not hear it.” I said, “I came only for that.” He said, “If Allah were to punish the people of the heavens and the people of the earth, He would punish them and He would not be unjust; and if He were to admit them into His mercy, His mercy would be more expansive for them than their sins. It is as Allah, Mighty and Sublime, said: {He punishes whom He wills and forgives whom He wills}. Whoever is punished, it is the truth; and whoever is shown mercy, it is the truth. If the mountains were gold or silver for one of you and he spent them in the path of Allah, then did not believe in qadar, its good and its evil, that would not benefit him.” Then I came to ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud and asked him. ʿAbd Allah said to Ubayy b. Kaʿb, “O Abu al-Mundhir, narrate to him.” Ubayy said, “O Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥman, narrate to him.” So Ibn Masʿud narrated the like of the hadith of ʿImran b. Husayn from the Prophet ﷺ, and upon his family, with abundant, good, blessed peace."],[10514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I hope that Allah will brighten our faces with a boy,” and she gave birth to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas."],[10515,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: When the Prophet ﷺ and his family were in the mountain pass, my father came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, I think Umm al-Fadl has conceived.” He said, “Perhaps Allah will delight our eyes from her with a boy.” I was brought to the Prophet ﷺ while I was in my swaddling cloth, and he chewed and gave me from his mouth. Mujahid said, “We do not know anyone who was given tahnik with the saliva of prophethood other than him.”"],[10516,"I was born three years before the Hijrah, while the Prophet ﷺ was still alive, and I was thirteen years old."],[10517,"Abdullah ibn Abbas died in the year seventy-eight."],[10518,"I heard Abu Nuʿaym say, \"Ibn ʿAbbas died in the year sixty-eight.\""],[10519,"Ibn ʿAbbas was tall, tinged with yellowness, corpulent, handsome, with a beautiful face, and he had two braids."],[10520,"I saw Ibn ʿAbbas and he had a jumma (hair reaching the shoulders)."],[10521,"I saw Ibn ʿAbbas during the days of Mina with long hair, wearing a waist-wrapper that had some trailing, and over it a yellow cloak."],[10522,"I witnessed Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya when Ibn ʿAbbas died in al-Taʾif. He said the takbir over him four times, took him from the qibla side when he placed him in the grave, and set up a tent over him for three days."],[10523,"I witnessed the death of Ibn ʿAbbas in al-Taʾif. Muhammad b. al-Hanafiyya took charge of him, said the takbir over him four times, placed him in the grave from the side of his feet, and set up a tent over him."],[10524,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when I was ten years old."],[10525,"\"I recited the muhkam (i.e., the mufassal) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" and he was then twelve years old."],[10526,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I had recited the muhkam of the Qurʾan.\" Shuʿba said: I asked Abu Bishr, \"What is the muhkam?\" He said, \"The mufassal.\""],[10527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was fifteen years old, and I had been circumcised."],[10528,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while I was still a young boy.\""],[10529,"While I was passing by, and the Prophet ﷺ was in the Hijr, he said, \"O Umm al-Fadl.\" I said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"You are pregnant with a boy.\" She said, \"How, when Quraysh have sworn that women will not give birth?\" He said, \"It is as I tell you. When you give birth to him, bring him to me.\" When she gave birth to him, she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he named him ʿAbd Allah, and he fed him from his saliva. Then he said, \"Take him away, and you will surely find him to be clever.\" She said: I went to al-ʿAbbas and told him, and he dressed and then came to the Prophet ﷺ. He was a handsome man, tall in stature. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he stood up to him, kissed him between the eyes, then seated him on his right, and then said, \"This is my uncle, so whoever wishes may boast of his uncle to him.\" Al-ʿAbbas said some words: \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Why should I not say it, when you are my uncle and the remnant of my forefathers, and the uncle is a father?\""],[10530,"Ibn ʿAbbas died in al-Taʾif, and I attended his funeral. A white bird came, the like of which had not been seen, and entered his bier, then was not seen leaving it. When he was buried, this verse was recited at the edge of the grave, and we did not know who recited it: \"O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing, and enter among My servants and enter My Paradise.\""],[10531,"It is said to be a crane [ghurnūq] until it entered into the interior of the bier and was not seen."],[10532,"It is said to be a crane [ghurnūq], then it entered into the bier and was not seen after that."],[10533,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and with the Prophet ﷺ there was a man confiding privately with him, and he seemed to be turning away from my father. So we left him, and my father said, “Did you not see your cousin seeming to turn away from me?” I said, “O my father, there was a man with him confiding privately with him.” He said, “Was there anyone with him?” I said, “Yes.” So we went back, and he said, “O Messenger of God, I said to ʿAbd Allāh such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such. Was there anyone with you?” He said, “Yes. Did you see him, O ʿAbd Allāh?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “That was Gabriel ﷺ ; he is the one who occupied me from you.”"],[10534,"The Messenger of God ﷺ placed his hand on the head of ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās and said, “O God, grant him wisdom and teach him interpretation.” He placed his hand on his chest, and ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās felt its coolness in his back. Then he said, “O God, fill his interior with judgment and knowledge.” So he never felt uneasy in himself about asking anyone among the people, and he remained the ḥabr (learned man) of this community until God took him to Himself."],[10535,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was wearing white clothes, and he was confiding privately with Diḥya b. Khalīfa al-Kalbī, who was Gabriel ﷺ , and I did not know. I did not greet them. Gabriel said, “O Muḥammad, who is this?” He said, “This is my cousin, this is Ibn ʿAbbās.” He said, “How intensely white his clothes are! Indeed, his descendants will prevail after him. If he had greeted us, we would have returned his greeting.” When I returned, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, “O Ibn ʿAbbās, what prevented you from greeting?” I said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, I saw you confiding privately with Diḥya b. Khalīfa, and I disliked interrupting your private conversation.” He said, “And you saw him?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, your sight will go and will be restored to you at your death.” ʿIkrima said: When Ibn ʿAbbās died and was placed on his bier, a bird of intense radiance came and entered into his shrouds. They wanted to unfold his shrouds, but ʿIkrima said, “What are you doing? This is the glad tidings of the Messenger of God ﷺ that he told him.” When he was placed in his grave, he was met with words that were heard by those at the edge of his grave: {O tranquil soul, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing, and enter among My servants and enter My garden}."],[10536,"I was in the house of Maymūna bt. al-Ḥārith, and I placed ablution water for the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Who placed this?” Maymūna said, “ʿAbd Allāh placed it.” He said, “O God, teach him interpretation and give him understanding in religion.”"],[10537,"The Prophet ﷺ embraced me and said, “O God, teach him wisdom.”"],[10540,"And he said: 'If any prophethood remained among them, he would inform me of what I ask them about.' So he wrote to him asking about the galaxy, the rainbow, and the place the sun had not touched except for one hour. When the letter and messenger reached Mu'awiya, he said: 'This is something I never thought I would be asked about until this day of mine. Who is this for?' It was said: 'Ibn Abbas.' So Mu'awiya folded up Heraclius' letter and sent it to Ibn Abbas. Ibn Abbas wrote back to him: 'The rainbow is a safeguard for the people of the earth from drowning. The galaxy is the gate of the sky through which it will split open. As for the place the sun had not touched except for one hour of the day, it is the sea that was parted for the Children of Israel.'"],[10541,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to a man: 'Come, let us learn from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask them, for they are many.' He said: 'How strange, by God, O Ibn Abbas! Do you think people will need you when among the people are those you see from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' So I left that and devoted myself to asking and seeking out the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I heard of a man who had a hadith he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would go to him and find him taking a midday nap. I would use my cloak as a pillow at his door while the wind blew dust onto my face until he came out to me. When he saw me he would say: 'O cousin of the Messenger of Allah, what is the matter?' I would say: 'A hadith has reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I wanted to hear it from you.' He would say: 'Why did you not send for me so that I could come to you?' I would say: 'I was more deserving of coming to you.' Then that man would see me when the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away and people needed me, and he would say: 'You were more deserving than me.'"],[10542,"I sat with seventy or eighty individuals from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Not one of them differed with Ibn Abbas and then met him except that he said: 'The saying is as you said' or 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[10543,"The man is not lying, but rather disagreeing. Ibn Abbas said, \"So what do you say about what happened in yourself?\" And the man said to him, \"May Allah tell you, He says, 'So there will be no blood relations among them on that day, nor will they ask about one another.'\" And he said in another verse, \"And some of them will come to others questioning.\" And he said in another verse, \"They do not conceal from Allah anything.\" And he said in another verse, \"And Allah is our Lord, we have not associated anything with Him.\" They have concealed in this verse and in His saying, \"He constructed the heavens and extended its scope and perfected it and created the night and formed the light and spread the earth.\" So He mentioned in this verse the creation of the heavens before the creation of the earth, then He said in this other verse, \"Do you deny the One who created the earth in two days and make for Him equals? That is the Lord of the worlds. And He placed on it firmly set mountains over its surface and blessed it and determined therein its [creatures'] sustenance in four days without distinction - for [the information] of those who ask. Then He directed Himself to the heaven while it was smoke and said to it and to the earth, 'Come into being, willingly or by compulsion.' They said, 'We have come willingly.'\" So He mentioned in this verse the creation of the earth before the creation of the heavens, \"And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\" \"And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\" \"And Allah is Hearing and Seeing.\" And it is as if it was then that Ibn Abbas said, \"Tell me what is in yourself.\" The questioner said, \"If you inform me about this, it is enough for me.\" And Ibn Abbas said, \"His saying, 'So there will be no blood relations among them on that day, nor will they ask about one another.' This is in the first blowing of the trumpet, the statues will be blown off and those in the heavens and on the earth except whoever Allah wills.\" \"So there will be no blood relations among them at that time, nor will they ask about one another. Then when it is in the second blowing of the trumpet, they will rise.\" \"So as for His saying, 'And Allah is our"],[10544,"Abu Salih al-Harrani narrated to us in the year two hundred and twenty-three, saying: Hayyan b. Ubayd Allah b. Zuhayr al-Misri, Abu Zuhayr, narrated to us sixty years ago, saying: I asked al-Dahhak b. Muzahim about His saying: {No disaster strikes upon the earth or among yourselves except that it is in a register before We bring it into being; indeed that, for God, is easy}, and about His saying: {Indeed We were copying what you used to do}, and about His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}. He said: Ibn Abbas said: God, exalted is He, created the Throne and settled upon it. Then He created the Pen and commanded it to flow by His permission, and He magnified the Pen to the extent of what is between heaven and earth. The Pen said: 'With what, O Lord, shall I flow?' He said: 'With what I am creating, whether in My creation of a drop, a plant, a soul, or a trace—meaning by that deed, provision, or term.' So the Pen flowed with what is to be until the Day of Resurrection, and God recorded it in the hidden Book with Him beneath the Throne. As for His saying: {Indeed We were copying what you used to do}, God entrusted angels who copy from that Book every year in Ramadan on the Night of Decree what will occur on earth from one event until the like of it in the coming year. They compare it with the guardian angels over the servants every Thursday evening, and they find what the guardians have raised to match what is in their Book, with no addition or subtraction. As for His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}, God created for everything what suits it from His creation and what benefits it from His provision. He created the camel with a form that is not suitable for anything from His creation other than it among the animals. Likewise is every thing from His creatures. He created for the beasts of the land and its birds from provision what benefits them on land, and He created for the beasts of the sea and its birds from provision what benefits them in the sea. That is His saying: {Indeed, all things We created with qadar}."],[10545,"Do you find the five prayers in the Book of God? He said: 'Yes.' He recited to him: {So glory be to God when you reach the evening} — that is Maghrib; {and when you reach the morning} — that is Subh; {and in the afternoon} — that is Asr; {and when you reach midday} — he said: that is Zuhr; {and after the Isha prayer} — he said: that is the Isha prayer."],[10547,"When the Haruriyya seceded and were in a separate abode on their own, I said to Ali: 'O Commander of the Faithful, delay the prayer a little so that perhaps I may go to these people and speak with them.' He said: 'I fear them for you.' I said: 'Not at all, if God wills.' So I put on the best Yemeni garment I could, then entered upon them while they were resting during midday. I entered upon a people more intense in worship than any I had ever seen. Their hands were like the calloused knees of camels, and their faces were marked from the traces of prostration. I entered and they said: 'Welcome, O Ibn Abbas. What brings you?' I said: 'I have come to tell you about the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Revelation came down while they were more knowledgeable of its interpretation.' Some of them said: 'Do not speak to him,' while others said: 'We will certainly speak with him.' I said: 'Tell me what you hold against the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his son-in-law, the first to believe in him, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who were with him?' They said: 'We hold three things against him.' I said: 'What are they?' They said: 'The first is that he appointed men as arbiters in the religion of God, while God has said: {Judgment belongs to none but God}.' I said: 'And what else?' They said: 'He fought but did not take captives or war spoils. If they were disbelievers, their wealth would be lawful to him; and if they were believers, their blood would be forbidden to him.' I said: 'And what else?' They said: 'He erased his own title as Commander of the Faithful. If he is not the Commander of the Faithful, then he is the commander of the disbelievers.' I said: 'Tell me, if I recite to you from the clear Book of God and narrate to you from the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ that which you cannot deny, will you return?' They said: 'Yes.' I said: 'As for your saying that he appointed men as arbiters in the religion of God, God says: {O you who believe, do not kill game while you are in the state of ihram} up to His saying: {two just men among you shall judge it}. And He said about a woman and her husband: {And if you fear a breach between them, send an arbitrator from his people and an arbitrator from her people}. I adjure you by God: is the judgment of men in the sparing of their blood and their lives and the rectification of their relations more worthy, or in a rabbit whose value is a quarter of a dirham?' They said: 'O God, in the sparing of their blood and the rectification of their relations.' He said: 'Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' 'As for your saying that he fought but did not take captives or war spoils: would you take your mother captive and make lawful from her what you make lawful from other women? If you claim she is not your mother, then you have disbelieved and left Islam. God, exalted is He, says: {The Prophet is closer to the believers than their own selves, and his wives are their mothers}. So you are wavering between two errors. Choose whichever you wish. Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' 'As for your saying that he erased his own title as Commander of the Faithful: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Quraysh on the day of Hudaybiyya to write a document between him and them. He said: \"Write: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has agreed upon.\" They said: \"By God, if we knew that you were the Messenger of God, we would not have turned you away from the House nor fought you. But write: Muhammad b. Abd Allah.\" He said: \"By God, I am indeed the Messenger of God even if you deny me. Write, O Ali, Muhammad b. Abd Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was superior to Ali. Have I answered this one?' They said: 'O God, yes.' Then twenty thousand of them returned, and four thousand remained and were killed."],[10548,"If you fear that he may overpower you, then say: 'God is greater, God is greater than all His creation. God is mightier than what I fear and am wary of. I seek refuge in God, besides whom there is no deity, the Holder of the seven heavens lest they fall upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of Your servant so-and-so and his soldiers and followers from jinn and mankind. O my God, be for me a protector from their evil. Great is Your praise, mighty is Your protection, blessed is Your name, and there is no deity other than You.' Three times."],[10549,"Ibn Abbas used to say: 'O Allah, I ask You by the light of Your Face, by which the heavens and the earth are illuminated, that You place me in Your fortress, Your protection, Your refuge, and under Your care.'"],[10551,"I saw on Ibn Abbas's bed—or in Ibn Abbas's gathering—a cushion of silk."],[10552,"Salamah b. Nubayt al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk b. Muzāḥim narrated to us, saying: Ibn ʿAbbās passed by a storyteller and kicked him with his foot, saying: “Do you know the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “And what is the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “You do not know the abrogating from the abrogated?” He said: “No.” He said: “You have perished and caused others to perish.”"],[10553,"The young man asked you if he can kiss while he is fasting, and you said no. Then he asked you if he can be kissed while he is fasting, and you said yes. So how can it be permissible for him to do what is forbidden for me, while we are on the same religion? Ibn Abbas said to him, \"The veins of the testicles are connected to the nose. When the nose smells something, the male reproductive organ moves, and when it moves, it calls for something bigger. And the elder one is in control of his desires, while the other person has lost his vision and has a woman behind him.\" It was said to Ibn Abbas, \"O Ibn Abbas, there is a woman behind you.\" He said, \"Woe to you! What a bad company you have!\""],[10554,"That with me there was a man from the people of qadar (fatalism/denial of divine decree), so I struck his head. They said: “And why that?” He said: “Because Allah created a preserved tablet of a white pearl; its covers are of red ruby, its pen is light, its writing is light, and its width is what is between heaven and earth. He looks into it every day three hundred and sixty looks; with each look He creates, gives life, honours, humiliates, and does whatever He wills.”"],[10555,"When Allah ﷻ sent Mūsā ﷺ and revealed to him the Torah, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” So Mūsā ﷺ desisted. Then when Allah ﷻ sent ʿUzayr and revealed to him the Torah after He had raised it from the Children of Israel, until some said that he was the son of Allah, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” But his soul refused until he asked again, saying: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” But his soul refused until he asked again. He said: “Can you tie up a bundle of the sun?” He said: “No.” He said: “Can you bring a measure of wind?” He said: “No.” He said: “Can you bring a mithqāl of light?” He said: “No. Can you bring a qīrāṭ of light?” He said: “No.” He said: “Thus you are not able to do what you asked about. I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked. Indeed, I will not make your punishment except that I erase your name from the prophets, so you will not be mentioned among them.” So He erased his name from the prophets, and he is not mentioned among them, though he is a prophet. Then when Allah sent ʿĪsā ﷺ , and he saw his station with his Lord, and He taught him the Book, the wisdom, the Torah, and the Gospel, and he healed the blind and the leper, and raised the dead, and informed them of what they ate and what they stored in their houses, he said: “O Allah, You are a great Lord. If You willed to be obeyed, You would be obeyed; and if You willed not to be disobeyed, You would not be disobeyed. Yet You love to be obeyed, and in that You are disobeyed. So how is this, O Lord?” Then Allah revealed to him: “I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked. And you are My servant, My messenger, and My word which I cast to Maryam, and a spirit from Me. I created you from dust, then said to you ‘Be,’ and you were. If you do not desist, I will surely do to you as I did to your companion before you. I am not asked about what I do, but they will be asked.” So ʿĪsā ﷺ gathered his followers and said: “Divine decree is the secret of Allah, so do not burden yourselves with it.”"],[10556,"“I found that the most correct of people concerning it in speech is the most ignorant of them of it, and the weakest of them concerning it in speech is the most knowledgeable of them of it. And I found the one who looks into it like one who looks into the rays of the sun: the more he increases his looking into it, the more his sight increases in bewilderment.”"],[10557,"“The mosques are the houses of Allah on earth, shining for the inhabitants of heaven just as the stars of heaven shine for the inhabitants of the earth.”"],[10558,"May Allah bless you, I said to Pharaoh, and may he bless you too, and Pharaoh has died."],[10559,"\"Whenever a year comes to mankind, they introduce innovations in it and abandon the traditions until innovations thrive and traditions die.\""],[10560,"That there is not on earth a pomegranate that is pollinated except with a grain from the grains of Paradise, and perhaps it is this one.”"],[10561,"“Whoever wears yellow sandals will remain in happiness as long as he wears them.”"],[10562,"I will tell you a discourse that is neither secret nor open. When there happened concerning this man what happened—meaning ʿUthmān—I said to ʿAlī: “Withdraw; for if you were in a hole, you would be sought until you are brought out.” But he disobeyed me. By Allah, Muʿāwiyah will surely rule over you, and that is because Allah ﷻ says: {And whoever is killed unjustly, We have given his heir authority, so let him not exceed in killing; indeed he is helped}. And the Quraysh will surely make you follow the way of Persia and Rome, and the Christians, the Jews, and the Magians will surely wish for you. So whoever among you then holds to what he knows will be saved, and whoever leaves it—and you will leave it—you will be like a generation among the generations that perished.”"],[10563,"That he was in the house of Maymūnah, and he placed water for the Prophet ﷺ's purification. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who placed it?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “I did.” So he struck me on my shoulder and said: “O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation.”"],[10564,"“I saw Jibrīl twice, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me for wisdom twice.”"],[10565,"ʿUmar used to ask me along with the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf said to him: “You ask him?” He said: “He is from where you know.” So he asked them about {When the help of Allah comes and the victory}. I said: “It is only the appointed term of the Prophet ﷺ.” And he recited the surah to its end up to {He is ever accepting of repentance}. ʿUmar said: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[10566,"ʿUmar used to admit me with the elders of Badr. Some of them said: “Why do you admit this youth with us, when we have sons like him?” He said: “He is among those you know.” He said: One day he called them and called me, and I did not see him call me that day except to show them from me. He said: “What do you say about {When the help of Allah comes and the victory, and you see the people entering the religion of Allah in multitudes}”—until he finished the surah. Some of them said: “He commanded us to praise Allah and seek His forgiveness when we are helped and victory is granted to us.” Others said: “We do not know,” and some said nothing. Then he said to me: “O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you say the same?” I said: “No.” He said: “Then what do you say?” I said: “It is the appointed term of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah taught him: when the help of Allah comes and the victory—the conquest of Makkah—that is the sign of your term, so glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever accepting of repentance.” ʿUmar said: “I know nothing from it except what you know.”"],[10567,"From Qatada and 'Asim, that they heard 'Ikrima say: Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab summoned the companions of Muhammad ﷺ and asked them about Laylat al-Qadr, and they agreed that it is in the last ten nights. Ibn 'Abbas said: I said to 'Umar, 'Indeed I know, and I think, which night it is.' 'Umar said, 'And which night is it?' I said, 'The seventh that passes or the seventh that remains of the last ten.' 'Umar said, 'And from where did you know that?' Ibn 'Abbas said: I said, 'Allah created seven heavens and seven earths and seven days, and the month revolves in seven, and He created man from seven, and he eats from seven, and he prostrates on seven, and the circumambulation of the House is seven, and the stoning of the jamarat is seven—for things he mentioned.' 'Umar said, 'You have perceived a matter we did not perceive.' Qatada used to add on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas regarding his saying 'and he eats from seven': he said, 'It is the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {And We caused to grow therein grain, and grapes, and green fodder} [Quran 80:27-28], to the end of the verse.'"],[10568,"Al-'Abbas said to me: 'O my son, the Commander of the Believers is summoning you, bringing you near, and consulting you along with the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So preserve from me three traits: be wary—let him never test a lie on you; do not reveal a secret of his; and do not backbite anyone in his presence.' 'Amir said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Each one of these is better than ten thousand.'"],[10569,"On the evening of 'Arafah he would recite Surat al-Baqarah and Surat Al 'Imran, then explain them verse by verse. He was a copious, resourceful, far-reaching [scholar].\""],[10570,"That all the people know of it what I know of it, and indeed I hear of a judge among the judges of the Muslims who is just in his judgment and I rejoice for him, though perhaps I will never bring a case before him; and indeed I hear of rain that has fallen on a land of the Muslims and I rejoice, though I have no livestock there."],[10572,"Ibn 'Abbas said to him: 'O Commander of the Believers, may Allah reward you well. Rejoice, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated that Allah would strengthen the religion through you while the people were in disagreement. When you accepted Islam, your Islam became a source of honor, and Allah brought Islam, the Messenger of Allah, and his companions to prominence through you. You migrated to Madinah, and your migration was a conquest. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while he was pleased with you.'"],[10573,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Makkah: 'How good you are, and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that your people expelled me from you, I would not dwell in any other than you.'"],[10574,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal, and that it is a sunnah. He said: They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood. He did perform ramal, but it is not a sunnah. Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived while the polytheists were on the mountain of Qu'ayqi'an, and it reached him that they were saying that he and his companions were weak, so he commanded them to perform ramal to show them that they had strength."],[10576,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Your people claim that the Prophet ﷺ performed ramal around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood; it is not a sunnah.'"],[10577,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ramal around the House, and that it is a sunnah. He said: They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood. I said, 'What have they spoken truth about, and what falsehood?' He said, 'They spoke truth that he performed ramal, and falsehood that it is not a sunnah. Quraysh said, \"Leave Muhammad and his companions from al-Hudaybiyyah until they die the death of maggots.\" When they made a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he would come the following year and stay in Makkah three days, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came the following year while the polytheists were on the side of Qu'ayqi'an. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Perform ramal around the House,\" and it is not a sunnah.' I said, 'Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwah on a camel, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth and spoken falsehood.' I said, 'What have they spoken truth about, and what falsehood?' He said, 'They spoke truth that he performed tawaf on a camel, and falsehood that it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have people pushed away from him, nor would they be struck away from him, so he performed tawaf on a camel so that they could hear his words and see his place, and their hands would not reach him.' I said, 'Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed sa'i between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and that it is a sunnah.' He said, 'They have spoken truth. When Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded with the rites, Satan confronted him at the place of sa'i, and he raced with him, and Ibrahim ﷺ outran him. Then Jibril ﷺ took him to Jamrat al-'Aqabah, and Satan confronted him, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he confronted him at the middle jamrah, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he laid him down on his forehead, and Isma'il had a white shirt on. He said to him, \"O my father, it is not a shirt, so shroud me in it.\" Ibrahim ﷺ turned around, and there was a white, big-eyed, horned ram, so he slaughtered it. Then Jibril ﷺ took him to the farthest jamrah, and Satan confronted him, so he threw seven pebbles at him until he went away. Then he took him to Mina and said, \"This is al-Mash'ar al-Haram.\" Then he took him to 'Arafah.' Ibn 'Abbas said, 'Do you know why it is called 'Arafah?' I said, 'Why is it called 'Arafah?' He said, 'Jibril ﷺ said, \"Have you come to know?\" He said, \"Yes.\"' Then Ibn 'Abbas said, 'Do you know how the talbiyah was?' I said, 'And how was the talbiyah?' He said, 'When Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded to proclaim the pilgrimage to the people, the mountains lowered their heads for him, and the towns were raised for him, so he proclaimed to the people.'"],[10578,"That when the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah, he said: 'The people have claimed that you have perished from weakness and hunger, so perform ramal when you enter and when you touch [the corner] for three circuits.' So they did. The people of Makkah said, 'We do not see the people except as strong, yet you claimed that they had perished from weakness.'"],[10579,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah and performed tawaf around the House on foot."],[10580,"Ibn ʿAbbas [said]: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to touch [in tawaf] anything except the Yamani Corner. Muʿawiya ؓ said: Nothing of the House is forsaken."],[10581,"He said: I could hear their words. Muʿawiya began to touch the two corners of the Black Stone, so Ibn ʿAbbas said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not used to touch these two corners. Muʿawiya said: Leave me alone, O Ibn ʿAbbas; for nothing of it is forsaken."],[10582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Makkah: “How good you are and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have dwelt in other than you.”"],[10583,"Muʿawiya and Ibn ʿAbbas performed Hajj. Muʿawiya began to touch all the corners, so Ibn ʿAbbas said: I only saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch these two corners."],[10584,"He narrated to him that he heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: “I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ touch other than the two Yamani corners.”"],[10585,"Muʿawiya performed Hajj and did not come to any corner of the House except that he touched it. Ibn ʿAbbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used only to touch the Yamani Corner and the Black Stone. Muʿawiya said: Nothing of the corners of the House is forsaken."],[10586,"I heard him say: “We used to call it Shabbaʿa—meaning Zamzam—and we used to find it an excellent aid for the family.”"],[10588,"The people herded sheep and slaughtered them, then they started cooking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and ordered for the pots to be overturned and said, \"Do not partake in plundering.\""],[10589,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any believer who frees a believer, Allah will ransom by every limb of him a limb of him from the Fire.” This is how al-Nadr narrated it from Muhammad b. Abi Humayd from ʿAmra bt. ʿUbayd Allah b. al-ʿAbbas, and Abu ʿAmir al-ʿAqadi disagreed with him, saying: from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas."],[10590,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever frees a believer in this world, Allah will ransom by every limb of him a limb from the Fire.”"],[10595,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the courtyard of his house in Makkah, ʿUthman b. Mazʿun passed by him and smiled broadly at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Do not sit.” He said, “Indeed I will.” So the Messenger of Allah sat facing him. While he was speaking with him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky, looked at the sky for a while, then began lowering his gaze until he fixed it on the ground to his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from his companion ʿUthman toward where he had fixed his gaze, and began nodding his head as if he were trying to understand what was being said to him. Ibn Mazʿun was watching. When he had accomplished what he needed and understood what was being said to him, the Messenger of Allah raised his gaze until it disappeared into the sky. Then he returned to ʿUthman in his original sitting posture and said, “O Muhammad, what was it that I was sitting with you for? I have never seen you do what you did this morning.” He said, “Did you notice that?” ʿUthman said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A messenger from Allah ﷺ came to me.” “While you were sitting?” He said, “Yes.” “What did he say to you?” He said, “{Indeed Allah commands justice, excellence, and giving to relatives, and forbids immorality, wrong, and oppression. He admonishes you so that you may take heed.}” ʿUthman said, “That was when faith became firmly established in my heart, and I loved Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[10596,"From ʿAli b. Abi Hamalah and al-Awzaʿi, they said: ʿAli b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbbas used to prostrate a thousand times every day."],[10597,"I spent the night at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ’s. He went to the mosque and led the people in the last ʿisha prayer until no one remained in the mosque except him. Then he passed by me and said, “Who is this?” I said, “ʿAbdullah.” He said, “What is it?” I said, “Al-ʿAbbas ordered me to spend the night with you tonight.” He said, “Then come along.” When he left, he entered and said, “Spread a bed for ʿAbdullah.” I was brought a cushion of coarse cloth. Al-ʿAbbas had instructed me, “Do not sleep until you have memorized his prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed, raised his head to the sky, and said, “Glory be to the King, the Most Holy,” three times. Then he recited this verse from the end of Surah Al ʿImran until he completed it: {Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth...}. Then he got up, cleaned his teeth with a siwak, performed ablution, entered his prayer place, and prayed two rakʿahs that were neither short nor long. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed and did as he had done the first time. Then he cleaned his teeth with a siwak, performed ablution, entered his prayer place, and prayed two rakʿahs that were neither long nor short. Then he returned to his bed and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed and did as he had done, prayed, then performed witr. When he finished his prayer, I heard him say: “O Allah, place light in my sight, place light in my hearing, place light in my tongue, place light in my heart, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light in front of me, place light behind me, place light above me, place light below me, and grant me light on the Day of Resurrection, and make my light great.”"],[10598,"That his father sent him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need. He said, \"So I found him sitting among his companions in the mosque, and I was unable to speak to him. When he finished praying Maghrib, he stood up and bowed until the Muezzin called the Isha prayer, and the people followed. Then he prayed the prayer and stood in bowing until those who remained in the mosque left. Then he went to his house, and I followed him. When he heard my footsteps, he said, 'Who is this?' and turned to me. I said, 'Ibn Abbas.' He said, 'The cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ?' I said, 'The cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' He said, 'Welcome, the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . What brought you?' I said, 'My father sent me with something and something.' He said, 'Did you come at this time?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'If you did not come to your appointment at this time, then you are not leaving.' He entered his house, and I entered with him. I said, 'I would like to see the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' So he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and threw his gaze towards the sky and recited these verses from Surah Ali Imran, 'Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth,' until the end of the five verses, until he reached, 'Indeed, You do not fail in [Your] promise.' Then he said, 'O Allah, make light in my hearing, light in my sight, light beneath me, and give me light with You.' And beside him was a container filled with tooth stick from Arak, and he sharpened it, then rinsed, then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, and again he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and recited verses and invoked supplications, then he washed, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he slept until I heard him snore. Then he woke up and recited verses and invoked supplications, then he washed, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he slept until I heard him snore, and he recited the verses, then he invoked with the invocation, then he washed, then he stood and prayed a prayer I recognized he performs more rak'ahs in it. So I came to his left corner, and he took me by the ear and turned me until he positioned me to his right corner. Then he prayed two rak'ahs of Fajr, then he went out to the prayer."],[10599,"What would be conquered for his ummah after him, generation after generation, was shown to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was pleased with that. Then Allah ﷻ revealed {And your Lord will surely give you, and you will be pleased.} So Allah gave him in Paradise a thousand palaces, in each palace whatever befits it of youths and servants."],[10600,"Al-Mahdi led us in prayer and recited “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” aloud. I said something to him about that, and he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ibn ʿAbbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” aloud."],[10601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your Lord said: “By My might and majesty, I will surely exact retribution from the wrongdoer in this life and the next, and I will surely exact retribution from one who sees a wronged person and is able to help him but does not do so.”"],[10602,"When the Prophet ﷺ woke up at night, he would clean his teeth with a siwak, then perform ablution and recite {Indeed in the alternation of night and day...} to the end of the two verses. Then he would stand and pray two rakʿahs, then leave and sleep until he breathed deeply in sleep. Then he would get up and do the same again. Then he would return to his bed. Then he would get up and pray two rakʿahs, then do the same as he did the first time. Then he would perform witr with three."],[10604,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray during the day in pairs, two by two."],[10605,"On the day of the conquest, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while there were three hundred and sixty idols on the Kaʿbah; Iblis had fastened their feet with lead. He came with his staff and began striking each idol with it, and it would fall on its face, and he would say, “Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish,” until he had passed by all of them."],[10606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder or meat, then prayed and neither rinsed his mouth nor touched water."],[10607,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a limb and prayed without performing ablution."],[10608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a moist shoulder in the house of Ḍubāʿah bt. al-Ḥārith, then prayed and did not touch water."],[10609,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate meat and prayed without performing ablution."],[10610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder in the house of Ḍubāʿah bt. al-Ḥārith."],[10611,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder, then went out to prayer and did not renew his ablution."],[10612,"He saw the Prophet of Allah ﷺ eat from a roasted shoulder, then pray, and he did not perform ablution because of that."],[10613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Love Allah for the blessings with which He nourishes you, love me for the love of Allah, and love the people of my household for love of me.\""],[10614,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone continually asks pardon, Allah will appoint for him a way out of every distress, and a relief from every anxiety, and will provide for him from where he did not reckon. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1518)"],[10615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer is created susceptible to trials, oft-repentant, forgetting; when reminded, he remembers.\""],[10616,"A bird was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You.\" Then ʿAlī came, and he said: \"O Allah, and to me.\""],[10617,"Al-ʿAbbās sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I came to him in the evening while he was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymūnah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray during the night. When he had prayed the two rakʿahs before dawn, he said: \"O Allah, I ask You for mercy from You by which You guide my heart, gather my affairs, mend my brokenness, restore my affection, set right my religion, protect my absent ones, elevate my present ones, purify my deeds, whiten my face, inspire me with right guidance, and protect me from every evil. O Allah, grant me true faith and certainty after which there is no disbelief, and mercy by which I attain the honor of Your generosity in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for success at the time of decree, the hospitality of the martyrs, the life of the fortunate, the company of the prophets, and victory over the enemies. O Allah, I bring my need to You even if my judgment is short and my deeds are weak, for I am in need of Your mercy. So I ask You, O Decider of affairs, O Healer of hearts, as You make a way between the seas, to protect me from the punishment of the Blaze, from the cry of destruction, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever good my judgment falls short of, my deeds are too weak for, and my hopes do not reach—good that You have promised to any of Your servants or good that You bestow upon any of Your creation—I desire it from You and I ask You, O Lord of the worlds. O Allah, make us guides who are guided, not astray and not leading astray, at war with Your enemies and at peace with Your friends. We love people through Your love and we show enmity, through Your enmity, to those among Your creation who oppose You. O Allah, this is the supplication, and upon You is the response. O Allah, this is the effort, and upon You is the reliance. There is no power and no strength except with Allah. O Allah, Possessor of the strong rope and the right command, I ask You for security on the Day of Warning and Paradise on the Day of Eternity with the favored witnesses, those who bow and prostrate, and those who fulfill the covenants. Indeed, You are Merciful and Loving, and You do whatever You will. Glory be to the One who is clothed in might and has spoken it. Glory be to the One to whom praise is due alone. Glory be to the Possessor of the Throne and splendor. Glory be to the Possessor of power and generosity. Glory be to the One who has enumerated everything by His knowledge. O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my grave, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, and light below me. O Allah, increase me in light, grant me greater light, and place light for me.\""],[10618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hang the whip where the people of the household can see it.\""],[10619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it.”"],[10620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang the whip where the members of the household can see it, for it is a means of discipline for them.”"],[10621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hang your whip where your family can see it.”"],[10622,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain, saying: “O Allah, grant us a downpour that is relieving, abundant, widespread, swift, not delayed, beneficial, and not harmful.” Before long we were rained upon until everything flowed, until they came to him and said: “We have been flooded.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, around us and not upon us.”"],[10623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The child of zina is the worst of the three if he acts according to the deeds of his parents.”"],[10624,"Abu Bakr ؓ had a seat near the Prophet ﷺ from which he would not rise except for al-ʿAbbas, and that pleased the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day al-ʿAbbas approached, so Abu Bakr moved aside from his seat for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What is the matter with you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, your uncle has approached.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him, then turned to Abu Bakr smiling and said: “This al-ʿAbbas has approached wearing white garments, and his descendants after him will wear black, and twelve men from among them will rule.”"],[10625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blessing of horses is in their chestnut color.”"],[10626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The blessing of horses is in their chestnut color, and the most auspicious of them in forelock is that which has a white blaze, white stockings, and a free right foreleg.”"],[10627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever holds the stirrup of his Muslim brother, not seeking anything from him and not fearing him, will be forgiven.”"],[10628,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “O Allah, bless my ummah in its early morning on Thursday.”"],[10629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Buy slaves and share with them in their provisions, meaning their earnings. Beware of the Zanj, for their lifespans are short and their provisions are little.”"],[10630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting for the whole of the month of Rajab."],[10631,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, eighty of which are from my ummah.”"],[10632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When I was taken on the Night Journey, I reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary, and its lote fruits were like large earthenware jars.”"],[10633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, wala' (patronage) does not transfer and does not change.\""],[10634,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For one of you to raise a puppy after the year one hundred and fifty-four is better for him than to raise a child of his own loins.\""],[10635,"Allah sent to the Prophet ﷺ an angel from among the angels together with the angel Jibril ﷺ . The angel said to him: \"O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives you the choice between being a prophet-servant or a prophet-king.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to Jibril as if seeking counsel, and he gestured to him to be humble. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, a prophet-servant.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never seen eating while reclining until he met his Lord."],[10636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever separates from the Muslims by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck. Whoever dies without having an imam over him, his death is a death of ignorance. And whoever dies under a blind banner, rallying to a faction or supporting a faction, his killing is a killing of ignorance.\""],[10637,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are a tribe of Rabiʿa, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar. We cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a matter which, if we act upon it, we will enter Paradise, and we will call those behind us to it.\" He commanded them with four things and forbade them from four things. He commanded them to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to establish the prayer, to give the zakat, to perform Hajj to the House, and to give the khums from the spoils of war. He forbade them from four things: drinking from hantam jars, dubba' gourds, naqir vessels, and muzaffat vessels. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, from what should we drink?\" He said: \"Use these water-skins whose mouths are tied.\""],[10638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in the darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10639,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Those who love one another [for Allah's sake] are in the shade of Allah.\""],[10640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' before everything, and 'There is no god but Allah' after everything, will be protected from anxiety and grief.\""],[10641,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\" Hammam added: Qatada said: \"We do not know vomit except as something forbidden.\""],[10642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.\""],[10643,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The example of one who takes back his charity is like the dog that vomits and then returns to its vomit and eats it.\""],[10644,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"We do not have the evil example: the example of one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit and eats it.\""],[10645,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit.”"],[10646,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was told about the daughter of Hamzah, and her beauty was mentioned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you not know that she is the daughter of my brother through suckling? Do you not know that Allah has made unlawful through suckling what He made unlawful through lineage?”"],[10647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man’s paternal uncle is the twin of his father.”"],[10648,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for the fingers ten (camels) each, and for the hand fifty as an obligatory compensation.”"],[10649,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking a ruling. He had obligated upon himself a sacrificial camel in an oath he swore. He ruled for him a camel from the camels, and he rebuked the man from returning to it."],[10650,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon to the people, a man came, stepped over the people until he drew near to him, and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “Sit.” He sat. Then he stood a second time and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “Sit.” He sat. Then he stood a third time and said: “O Messenger of Allah, carry out the punishment upon me.” He said: “And what is your punishment?” He said: “I came to a woman unlawfully.” The Prophet ﷺ said to men among his companions, among them ʿAlī, Ibn ʿAbbās, Zayd b. Ḥārithah, and ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān: “Go and flog him one hundred lashes.” He had not been married. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, should we not flog the one with whom he committed it?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring him to me.” When he was brought, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Who is your partner?” He said: “So-and-so woman.” The Prophet ﷺ sent for her and called her, and asked her about that. She said: “He has lied, by Allah. I do not know him, and I am innocent of what he said. Allah is witness to what I say.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is your witness that you did it with her? For she denies that you did it with her. If you have a witness, I will flog her; otherwise I will flog you the punishment for slander.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have no witness.” So he ordered him to be flogged the punishment for slander, eighty lashes."],[10651,"A woman asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward for a woman's participation in battle?\" He replied, \"Obeying her husband and acknowledging his rights.\""],[10652,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The likeness of the one who takes back his gift is like the likeness of the dog that vomits then returns to its vomit.”"],[10653,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"The example of the one who gives charity and then takes it back is like that of a person who vomits and then consumes it again.\""],[10654,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The likeness of the one who gives charity then takes back his charity is like the likeness of the dog that vomits then eats its vomit.”"],[10655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept while prostrating until he snored, then he stood and prayed without performing ablution."],[10656,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[10657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbīr in the two ʿĪd prayers twelve times: in the first seven, and in the second five. He would go by one route and return by another."],[10658,"“The Prophet ﷺ would not drink nabīdh more than three days.”"],[10659,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted the liʿān between the ʿAjlānī man and his wife, and she was pregnant. Her husband said, “By Allah, I have not approached her since we pollinated the palm trees — al-ʿafr is the watering of palm trees after the watering from the wells is left off for two months.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, “O Allah, make it clear.” They claimed that the woman’s husband was thin in the forearms and shins, with reddish hair, and that the one with whom she was accused was Ibn al-Saḥmāʾ. She said, “Then she gave birth to a boy who was black, clear-skinned, with curly, tightly coiled hair, thick forearms, and plump shins.”"],[10660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned her.” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No, but that was a woman who had become notorious in Islam.”"],[10661,"To Ibn ʿAbbās, mentioning the two who engaged in liʿān: “Is she the woman about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned her’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No. That was a woman who had become notorious.”"],[10662,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conducted the liʿān between a man and his wife.”"],[10663,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have not had contact with my wife since the pollination of the palm trees — its pollination is that they are fertilized and then left unwatered for forty days after fertilization. I then found a man with my wife.” Her husband was pale-skinned, thin, with lank hair, while the one with whom she was accused was plump, tending towards darkness, with curly, tightly coiled hair, and had large buttocks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Allah, make it clear; O Allah, make it clear.” Then he conducted the liʿān between them, and she gave birth to a child resembling the one with whom she was accused."],[10664,"That he mentioned the two who engaged in liʿān in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and ʿĀṣim said something about that, then left. A man from his people came to him and mentioned that he had found a man with his wife. ʿĀṣim said, “I was not afflicted with this except because of my own statement.” So he took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what he had found with his wife. That man was pale-skinned, thin-fleshed, with lank hair, while the one he claimed to have found with his wife was reddish, fleshy. The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Allah, make it clear.” She gave birth to a child resembling the one her husband mentioned he had found with her, so the Messenger of Allah conducted the liʿān between them. A man said to Ibn ʿAbbās in the gathering, “Is she the one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If I were to stone a woman without clear evidence, I would have stoned this one’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “No. That was a woman who used to display herself openly in Islam.”"],[10665,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If I were to stone anyone without clear evidence, I would have stoned so-and-so. Suspicion has become apparent from her in her appearance, her speech, and those who enter upon her.”"],[10666,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forgot the Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr prayers on the day of the Confederates. He remembered after Maghrib, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “They distracted us from the prayer until the day departed. May Allah fill their graves with fire.” Then he prayed them after Maghrib."],[10667,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out with a forelock and said, “The women of the Children of Israel used to put this on their heads, and they were cursed and the mosques were forbidden to them.”"],[10668,"I wish that people would allocate between a third to a quarter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A third, and a third is a lot or significant.\""],[10669,"“Mutʿah was indeed practiced during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[10671,"Ibn ʿAbbās: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymūnah bt. al-Ḥārith while he was in iḥrām.”"],[10672,"Abu Bakr uncovered the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was covered with a cloth, looked at the face of the Prophet ﷺ, then leaned over him and kissed him."],[10673,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat meat from the shoulder of a sheep, then pray without performing ablution."],[10674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about khaṭṭ (geomancy), and he said: \"It is a remnant of knowledge.\""],[10675,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for ten years while the Qur'an was revealed to him, and in Madinah for ten years while it was revealed to him."],[10676,"He saw his Lord, Mighty and Majestic."],[10677,"Women have no say in the marriage contract. Maymūnah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Faḍl, and Umm al-Faḍl entrusted it to al-ʿAbbās, who married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[10679,"...to be praised for what he does — as one being punished? We shall surely be punished, all together. Ibn ʿAbbās said: What is the matter with you and this? It was revealed about the People of the Book. Then Ibn ʿAbbās recited: {And when God took a covenant from those who were given the Scripture: 'You shall make it clear to the people'} up to His saying: {Think not that those who rejoice in what they have done and love to be praised for what they have not done}. And Ibn ʿAbbās said: The Prophet ﷺ asked them about something, but they envied him and concealed it, telling him something else. They rejoiced and went out having made him think they had told him what he asked about, and they sought praise from him for that, rejoicing in what they had done in concealing from him what he asked about."],[10680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was never given victory in any battle like he was at Uḥud. That was denied, so Ibn ʿAbbās said: Between me and the one who denies it is the Book of God. God says: {And God did indeed fulfil His promise to you when you were slaying them by His permission}. Ibn ʿAbbās said: al-ḥass means killing. {Until when you lost courage} up to His saying: {And God has pardoned you, and God is bountiful to the believers}. He meant by this the archers. The Prophet ﷺ stationed them at a lookout and said: \"Protect our backs. If you see us being killed, do not come to our aid; and if you see us gaining spoils, do not share with us.\" When God granted the Prophet ﷺ spoils and allowed him the camp of the polytheists, the archers all turned away and entered the camp to plunder, while the ranks of the Prophet's companions had become interlocked — and he interlaced his right and left fingers. When the archers abandoned that position where they had been, the cavalry entered from that point upon the Prophet's companions, and they struck one another, and many Muslims were killed. From the beginning of the day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions had killed seven or nine of the standard-bearers of the polytheists. The Muslims made a retreat toward the mountain, but did not reach the place people call al-Ghār; they were below al-Mihrās. Satan cried out, \"Muḥammad has been killed!\" and we had no doubt it was true. We remained so, not doubting he had been killed, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared between the two mountain passes. I recognized him by the way he swayed when he walked. We rejoiced as if nothing had befallen us. He climbed toward us saying: \"God's anger is intense against a people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" And another time he said: \"O God, it is not for them to overcome us until they reach us.\" He stayed for a while, and then Abu Sufyān shouted from the foot of the mountain: \"Exalted be Hubal!\" — meaning his gods. \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not answer him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" When he said, \"Exalted be Hubal,\" ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: \"God is more exalted and more majestic.\" Abu Sufyān said: \"O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, you have done well.\" Then he repeated the same: \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"Here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, here is Abu Bakr, and here am I, ʿUmar.\" Abu Sufyān said: \"A day for the day of Badr. Days alternate, and war is a matter of give and take.\" ʿUmar said: \"No, they are not equal. Our slain are in Paradise and your slain are in the Fire.\" He said: \"You claim that. We would then be disappointed and losers.\" Then Abu Sufyān said: \"You will find mutilation among your slain, and that was not by the decision of our leaders.\" Then tribal pride overtook him, and he said: \"Indeed it happened, but we did not disapprove of it.\""],[10681,"God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed — those are the disbelievers}, {the wrongdoers}, {the transgressors}. Ibn ʿAbbās said: He revealed them concerning two groups of the Jews. One of them had subdued the other in pre-Islamic times, until they agreed and made a settlement that every slain person killed by the powerful group from the weak group would have a blood money of fifty wasq, and every slain person killed by the weak group from the powerful group would have a blood money of one hundred wasq. They remained on that until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived. Then the two groups submitted to the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — though the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not yet prevailed over them or subdued them, and there was a truce. The weak group killed a man from the powerful group, so the powerful group sent to the weak group: \"Send us one hundred wasq.\" The weak group said: \"Has this ever been so when their religion is one and their lineage is one? The blood money of some of them is half that of others. We only gave you this out of oppression and fear of you. But now that Muḥammad ﷺ has come, we will not give you that.\" War was about to break out between them, but then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a judge between them. The powerful group thought and said: \"By God, Muḥammad will not give you from them double what he gives them from you. They spoke the truth: they only gave us this out of oppression and subjugation. So send someone secretly to Muḥammad ﷺ to find out his opinion. If he gives you what you want, you will accept his judgment; but if he does not, you will be wary and not accept it.\" So they secretly sent people from the hypocrites to test the opinion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, God informed His Messenger of their entire affair and what they intended. Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {O Messenger, let not those who hasten into disbelief grieve you, from those who say} up to His saying: {And whoever does not judge by what God has revealed — those are the transgressors}. Then he said: By God, it was revealed concerning them, and God meant them."],[10682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his sword Dhū al-Faqār as booty on the day of Badr, and it was the one about which he saw the vision on the day of Uḥud."],[10683,"\"The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[10684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah in the year of the conquest for fifteen [days] shortening the prayer."],[10685,"The last surah of the Qur'an to be revealed in full was {When the help of Allah comes and the victory} [Q 110:1]."],[10687,"When Ali's companions, as they were marching to Basra, learned that the people of Basra had gathered in support of Talha and al-Zubayr, it distressed them and it weighed on their hearts. Ali said, 'By the One besides whom there is no god, he will surely prevail over the people of Basra, Talha and al-Zubayr will surely be killed, and there will surely come out to you from Kufa six thousand five hundred fifty men' - or 'five thousand five hundred fifty men,' al-Ajlah was unsure. Ibn Abbas said: That stayed in my mind. When the people of Kufa came, I went out and said, 'I will certainly see. If it is as he says, then it is a matter he heard; otherwise it is a trick of war.' I met a man from the army and asked him, and by Allah he did not delay in saying what Ali had said. Ibn Abbas said: And it was among the things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to tell him."],[10688,"Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did it."],[10689,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring could be heard, then he got up and prayed without performing ablution.\""],[10690,"The Prophet ﷺ went out intending to pray and passed by a cooking pot. He took a bone from it and ate it, then went on to pray without performing ablution."],[10691,"\"O Abu Al-Abbas, does the killer have a chance for repentance?\" Ibn Abbas replied, \"I'm amazed by your question. What do you say?\" He repeated the question to him again, and Ibn Abbas asked him, \"What do you say?\" After repeating the question two or three times, Ibn Abbas said, \"How can he repent? I heard your Prophet ﷺ say, 'The slain person will come on the Day of Resurrection, with his head held in one hand and his killer in the other, covered in blood until he reaches the throne. Then, the slain person will say to Allah, 'My Lord, this person killed me,' and Allah ﷻ will say to the killer, 'You are doomed,' and he will be taken to Hell.'\""],[10692,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and for a virgin her consent is her silence.\""],[10694,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and for a virgin her father seeks her consent, and her silence is her acknowledgment.\""],[10695,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A previously married woman has more authority over her own person, and a virgin is asked for her consent, and her consent is her silence.\""],[10696,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A previously married woman has more right to her own person than her guardian, and a virgin is asked for her consent, and her silence is her acknowledgment.\""],[10697,"A woman from Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has become senile. Allah's obligation of Hajj has overtaken him, but he is unable to perform it. Is it sufficient for him if I perform it on his behalf?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Yes.'"],[10698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The most hateful people to Allah are those who seek the ways of ignorance in Islam and those who unlawfully seek the blood of a person to spill his blood.\""],[10699,"Musaylimah the Liar came during the era of Allah’s Messenger ﷺ and began saying, “If Muhammad grants me the authority after him, I will follow him.” He arrived with a large number of his people. Allah’s Messenger ﷺ came to him, accompanied by Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, and in the hand of Allah’s Messenger ﷺ was a piece of a palm branch. He stood before Musaylimah among his companions and said, “If you were to ask me for this piece, I would not give it to you, and you will not go beyond what Allah has decreed for you. If you turn back, Allah will surely hamstring you. I see in you what I was shown, and this is Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas; he will answer you on my behalf.” Then he departed."],[10700,"Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said: Allah, Exalted is He, said: “The son of Adam belied Me, though it was not proper for him to belie Me, and he reviled Me, though it was not proper for him to do that. As for his belying Me, it is his claim that I am not able to recreate him as he was. As for his reviling Me, he says I have a son. Glorified am I above taking a consort or a son.”"],[10706,"Ibn Abbas said: I do not care about what you perform ablution for. I bear witness that I saw Allah’s Messenger ﷺ eat a meat shoulder and then stand up to pray without performing ablution. He said: Sulayman was present for that from both of them."],[10707,"The Prophet ﷺ went out to the prayer, and a meat shoulder was brought to him. He took a bite from it and then proceeded to the prayer without rinsing his mouth or purifying. The wording is from the hadith of Rawh b. al-Qasim."],[10708,"Ibn Abbas said: Shall I show you how Allah’s Messenger ﷺ used to perform ablution? He called for a vessel containing water, scooped a handful, and rinsed his mouth and nose. Then he took another handful, joined his hands with it, and washed his face. Then he took another and washed his right hand. Then he scooped another handful and washed his left hand. Then he took a handful of water, lowered his hand, and wiped his head and ears with it. Then he scooped another handful and sprinkled it on his feet while he had sandals on, and the left likewise, and he wiped the bottom of the sandals. Then he said, “Like this.”"],[10709,"Arbad b. Qays b. Juzayy b. Khalid b. Ja’far b. Kilab and Amir b. al-Tufayl b. Malik came to Madinah to Allah’s Messenger ﷺ. They reached Allah’s Messenger ﷺ while he was sitting, and they sat before him. Amir b. al-Tufayl said, “O Muhammad, what will you grant me if I accept Islam?” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “You will have what the Muslims have and you will bear what they bear.” Amir b. al-Tufayl said, “Will you grant me the authority after you if I accept Islam?” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “That is not for you nor for your people, but you may have the reins of the horses.” He said, “I am now in charge of the reins of the horses of Najd. Give me the desert and leave the settled land to you.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “No.” When they turned away from Allah’s Messenger ﷺ, Amir said, “By Allah, I will fill it against you with horses and men.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said, “Allah will prevent you.” When Arbad and Amir left, Amir said, “O Arbad, I will distract Muhammad with talk while you strike him with the sword. If you kill Muhammad, the people will only accept blood money and dislike war, and we will give them the blood money.” Arbad said, “I will do it.” They returned to him, and Amir said, “O Muhammad, stand with me so I may speak to you.” Allah’s Messenger ﷺ stood with him, and they withdrew to the wall, and Allah’s Messenger ﷺ stood speaking with him while Arbad drew the sword. When he placed his hand on the hilt of the sword, it stuck to the hilt, and he could not draw the sword. Arbad delayed striking Amir, so Allah’s Messenger ﷺ turned and saw Arbad and what he was doing, and he departed from them. When Amir and Arbad left Allah’s Messenger ﷺ and reached the harrat Waqim, they dismounted. Sa’d b. Mu’adh and Usayd b. Hudayr came out to them and said, “Depart, O enemies of Allah! May Allah curse you both.” Amir said, “Who is this, O Sa’d?” He said, “This is Usayd b. Hudayr, the one of the battalions.” They went on until they reached al-Raqm, where Allah, Exalted is He, sent a thunderbolt upon Arbad and killed him. Amir went on until he was at al-Harr, and then Allah sent a gland infection upon him. Night overtook him in the house of a woman from Banu Salul. He began touching the gland in his throat and saying, “A gland like the gland of a camel in the house of a Saluli woman,” wishing to die in her house. Then he mounted his horse and urged it on until he died upon it on his way back. Allah, Exalted is He, revealed concerning them: “Allah knows what every female carries and what the wombs decrease” up to His saying, “You have no protector besides Him.” He said: “The guardian angels” from Allah’s command protect Muhammad. Then he mentioned Arbad and what preceded him regarding it. He said: “It is He who shows you the lightning, causing fear and hope,” up to His saying, “And He is severe in stratagem.”"],[10710,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought fruit, he would give it to the youngest child present."],[10711,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from the shoulder of a sheep and then prayed without performing ablution."],[10712,"Allah’s Messenger ﷺ said: “A distinguishing sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill of Zamzam.”"],[10713,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no racing prize except for camels, horses, or arrows.”"],[10714,"O Messenger of God, what may I do with my wife while she is menstruating? He said: “Tie her waist-wrapper firmly, then do what you wish with her.”"],[10716,"The Prophet ﷺ came out while they were sitting and said: “Shall I not tell you who has the best standing among people?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “A man who holds the bridle of his horse” – or he said – “a horse in the path of God, until he is killed.” He said: “Shall I tell you who comes after him?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “A man isolated in a mountain pass who establishes the prayer, gives the zakat, and keeps away from the evils of people. Shall I tell you who is the worst of people?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The one who is asked by God but does not give by Him.”"],[10717,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Shall I not tell you who the best of people is? Among the best of people is a man holding the bridle of his horse in the path of God. Shall I tell you who comes after him? A man isolated with his flock, fulfilling God’s right concerning it. And shall I tell you who the worst of people is? A man who is asked by God but does not give by Him.”"],[10718,"May God forgive Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. By my life, this verse troubled the Muslims before him until God, exalted is He, sent down: “God does not burden any soul beyond its capacity. It has what it earned and against it what it incurred.” He said: Intrusive thoughts are what people cannot control, and God has decreed for every soul its recompense according to what it earned."],[10719,"May God forgive Abu ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. The Muslims found from this verse the same distress he found, so they complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Thus your Lord has said, so say: ‘We believe in what He has sent down, and we hear and obey. Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return.’” They said it as long as God willed them to say it, until God, exalted is He, sent down: “The Messenger has believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord” up to His saying “God does not burden any soul beyond its capacity.”"],[10720,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Pulpits of gold will be set up for the prophets, on which they will sit, while my pulpit will remain without me sitting on it” – or he said, “without me taking a seat on it – standing upright before my Lord because of my community, fearing that I might be sent to Paradise while my community remains behind me. So I will say: ‘My Lord, my community, my community!’ Then God Most High will say: ‘O Muhammad, what do you wish Me to do with your community?’ I will say: ‘My Lord, make their reckoning just.’ They will be summoned and their accounts will be settled. Some will enter Paradise by God’s mercy, and some will enter Paradise by my intercession. I will not cease interceding until I am given writs for men who had been dispatched to the Fire, until even Malik, the keeper of the Fire, says: ‘O Muhammad, you have left no one from your community for your Lord’s wrath to punish.’”"],[10721,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas on this pulpit narrating that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say these words at times of distress: “There is no god but God, the Great, the Forbearing. There is no god but God, Lord of the Great Throne. There is no god but God, Lord of the heavens and the earth and Lord of the Great Throne. Avert from me the evil of so-and-so.”"],[10722,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"It is permissible for a man to look at the slave girl he intends to purchase, other than her private parts, from her knees to the end of her garment.\""],[10723,"From the Prophet ﷺ: Jesus son of Mary ﷺ said: “Matters are only three: a matter whose right guidance has become clear to you, so follow it; a matter whose error has become clear to you, so avoid it; and a matter about which people differ, so refer it back to the one who has knowledge of it.”"],[10724,"The Prophet ﷺ said from the pulpit: “Shall I not tell you about the worst of you?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “The worst of you is the one who travels alone, flogs his slave, and withholds his aid.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “One who hates people and they hate him.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, if you wish, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Those who do not accept a slip, nor accept an excuse, nor forgive a sin.” He said: “Shall I not tell you about what is worse than that?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “One whose good is not hoped for and whose evil is not safe.”"],[10725,"On the authority of ʿAʾishah, they both said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque and there were voices like the buzzing of bees reciting the Quran. He said: “Islam will spread, then there will be a period of weakness for it. Whoever’s period of weakness leads to extremism and innovation, those are the people of the Fire.”"],[10726,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Good character melts away sins as water melts ice, and bad character spoils deeds as vinegar spoils honey.”"],[10727,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Two hungry wolves let loose among a flock of sheep are not more destructive to it than the son of Adam’s love of honor and wealth.”"],[10728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you ask by Allah, ask with the palms of your hands, and do not ask with their backs, and wipe your faces with them.”"],[10729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Verily, everything has a character, and the character of Islam is modesty.”"],[10730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Verily, everything has an honor, and the honor of gatherings is to face the qiblah. Whoever looks into his brother’s book without his permission, it is as if he looks into the Fire.”"],[10732,"She said: “Permit him if you wish,” so I let him in. When he sat down, he said: “Rejoice.” She said: “Also,” and he said: “There is nothing between you and meeting Muhammad ﷺ except that the soul leaves the body. You were the most beloved of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved only what is pure. Your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwāʾ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained until morning at the campsite, and the people woke up without water with them. So Allah ﷻ revealed: “And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth.” That was because of you, and Allah did not send down this concession for this Ummah except for you. And Allah the Exalted sent down your exoneration from above seven heavens, brought by the Trustworthy Spirit. Morning came and there was no mosque among the mosques of Allah in which Allah is remembered except that it was recited in it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.” She said: “Leave me from you, Ibn ʿAbbās. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I wish I had been something utterly forgotten.”"],[10733,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Sniff water into the nostrils twice, and the ears are part of the head.”"],[10734,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ and commanded fasting on it.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is a day that the Jews and Christians venerate.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the coming year comes, God willing, we will fast the ninth.” But the coming year did not arrive until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away."],[10735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Health and free time are two blessings in which many people are deceived.”"],[10736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah wills good for, He gives him understanding in the religion.”"],[10737,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two ʿĪd prayers: in the first rakʿah, the Opening of the Book and “Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High,” and in the second, the Opening of the Book and “Has there come to you the report of the Overwhelming?”"],[10738,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder, then prayed without touching water — the wording is that of the hadith of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān."],[10739,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder and did not perform ablution."],[10740,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, then he went out for prayer. A large dish containing meat and bread was brought to him and he ate from it and did not perform ablution (again)."],[10741,"I entered the house of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and found 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas there. We discussed ablution after eating food touched by fire. Ibn 'Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat food touched by fire, then pray without performing ablution. We said, 'Did you see him yourself?' He pointed to his eyes and said, 'My eyes saw it.'"],[10742,"The Prophet ﷺ ate from a shoulder (of meat), then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10743,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a shoulder or a foreleg, then lead the people in prayer without performing ablution.'"],[10744,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage: a bone with meat was brought to him while he was circumambulating the House on the Day of Sacrifice; he took a bite from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10745,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for prayer and a gift met him—a limb of a sheep. He ate a morsel or two from it, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[10747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever eats any of this vegetable of yours (garlic) should not approach our mosque, for the angels are harmed by what harms the children of Adam.'"],[10748,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'The Messenger of Allah was washed (after death) in his shirt, and 'Ali, al-Fadl b. 'Abbas, Salih b. 'Abbas, and Salih b. Shuqran, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, descended into his grave.'"],[10749,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: 'The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated on his camel during the Farewell Pilgrimage and touched the corner with his staff, disliking that the people be pushed away from him.'"],[10750,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated during the Farewell Pilgrimage on his she-camel al-Qaswa'."],[10751,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman who was insane and said: 'Which is dearer to you: that you be cured of this, or that you be patient and have Paradise?' She said, 'Paradise.'"],[10752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' in Madinah without fear or rain. I said to Ibn 'Abbas, 'Why do you think he did that?' He said, 'He wanted to make things easy for his community.'"],[10754,"Umm al-Fadl sent milk to the Prophet ﷺ and he drank it while he was addressing the people at Arafah."],[10755,"From the Prophet ﷺ."],[10756,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"The womb has a hook that clings to the waist of the Most Merciful; it joins whoever joins it and cuts off whoever cuts it off.\""],[10758,"It is from the Sunnah."],[10759,"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-five years old, Abu Bakr when he was at the same age, Umar b. al-Khattab when he was fifty-six, and Uthman when he was eighty-one."],[10760,"If the land is fertile, then aim for exploration and give the travelers their rights; for indeed, Allah is Kind who loves kindness. But if it is arid, then flee and rely on the camel (for transportation); for indeed, the land folds at night and be cautious of the wild animals on the road; for indeed, it is the abode of snakes and the hunting ground of predators."],[10761,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Nothing from the slaughter of the people of Jahiliyyah has given birth to me, and I have been born only from marriage, just like the marriage in Islam.\" Abu Al-Qasim Al-Madini said, \"He is Fulayh bin Sulayman, according to me.\""],[10762,"Ibn Abbas: Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that."],[10763,"About a slave who divorced his wife twice, then both were freed: may he marry her again? He said: Yes. It was asked: On whose authority? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ issued that ruling."],[10766,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If I live, God willing, until next year, I will fast the ninth, for fear of missing the day of Ashura.\""],[10767,"That he should come to me and ask me? The Messenger of God ﷺ went out humble, beseeching, and plainly dressed; he did not deliver a sermon like this one of yours, and he prayed two rak'ahs as he prayed on the Eid."],[10774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The martyrs are on a shining river at the gate of Paradise; their provision comes out to them morning and evening.\""],[10775,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Uthman b. Maz'un on the day he died and leaned over him as if advising him, then raised his head and they saw traces of weeping in his eyes, then leaned over him a second time, then raised his head and they saw him weeping, then leaned over him a third time, then raised his head with a sob. So they knew that he had died, and the people wept. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Stop; this is from Satan, so seek forgiveness from Allah.\" Then he said: \"Go away from you, Abu al-Sa'ib, for you have departed and have not been soiled by anything of it.\""],[10776,"The Prophet ﷺ, on the day Sa'd b. Mu'adh was buried, while sitting at his grave, said: \"If anyone were to be saved from the trial of the grave, Sa'd b. Mu'adh would have been saved, but he was squeezed with a squeeze, then released.\""],[10777,"Ibn Abbas: It is for the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[10778,"About the share of the near of kin, and he says: To whom does he think it should go? Ibn Abbas said: It is for the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it among them. Umar had offered us something from that which we considered less than our right, so we returned it to him and refused to accept it. He had offered to help their newlyweds, pay off their debtors, and give to their poor, but he refused to give them more than that."],[10779,"About the near of kin whom Allah mentioned in the Qur'an, about killing the children of the polytheists, and whether the Prophet ﷺ used to kill them, about when the orphanhood of an orphan ends, and about the slave and the woman who witness battle. He said: If I did not fear that he would fall into something evil, I would not write to him. So he wrote regarding the near of kin: We used to consider the kin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be them, but our people denied us that. As for the orphan, when he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is observed in them, his property is handed over to him, and his orphanhood has ended. As for the children, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not kill the children of the polytheists, and you should not kill them unless you know what al-Khidr knew about the boy when he killed him. Regarding the slave and the woman, do they have a share if they witness battle? He wrote to him that they have no fixed share, unless they are given something from the spoils of the people."],[10780,"That he commit an imprudence; I did not write to him. Then he wrote to him: As for the orphan, when he has a wet dream and sound judgment is perceived from him, orphanhood has ceased for him. As for the children, if you know about them what al-Khiḍr knew, then otherwise do not kill them. As for the slave, he used to be given a share. As for the women, they used to treat the wounded and give water. As for the fifth, we claim that it is for us, and our people claim that it is not for us."],[10781,"And about the slave and the woman who attend the spoils: is there anything for them from it? And about the orphan: when is the name of orphan removed from him? And about killing children. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Were it not that I hope that God will benefit him through my writing, I would not write to him. Then he said: Write, O Yazīd: As for the fifth, we used to hold that it was for us, but our people refused us that. As for the slave and the woman who attend the spoils, there is nothing for them from it, but they are given a small gift. As for the orphan, orphanhood is removed from him when he reaches puberty, and he becomes one of the poor Muslims. As for the children, do not kill them until you know from them the like of what al-Khiḍr knew about the boy before he killed him. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī."],[10785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no one who has two daughters and treats them well as long as they accompany him and he accompanies them, except that they will admit him to Paradise.\""],[10786,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, and the intoxicant from every drink.\""],[10787,"\"O Messenger of God, I sometimes think to myself about something concerning the Lord that I would rather be a cinder than speak of it.\" Shuʿbah said: One of them said: \"Praise be to God, who has only given you power over whispering.\" The other said: \"Praise be to God, who has turned its matter back to whispering.\""],[10788,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, a little of it and a lot, and intoxication from every drink.\""],[10790,"\"Wine itself is forbidden, a little of it and a lot, and intoxication from every drink.\""],[10791,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of God, shall we not sell it? He said: \"The One who forbade drinking it also forbade selling it.\""],[10792,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent.\""],[10794,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever conceals knowledge that he knows will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.\" He said: \"It is the testimony about a man: it is requested of him or not requested of him, and he knows it but does not guide its owner to it. So the knowledge is exactly this.\""],[10795,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The hudud punishments are not to be carried out in mosques, nor is retaliation to be taken against a parent for [killing] his child.”"],[10796,"“Indeed three [divorces] used to be made one during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[10797,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever is killed in the blind or by something thrown, while between them is a rock, a wipe, or a stick, then the blood money of be paid for him is the blood money for accidental killing. Whoever kills deliberately, then retaliation is upon him, and whoever tries to prevent that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the Angels, and all the people, and neither Sarf nor Adl will be accepted from him.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4789)"],[10800,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten the iftar, to delay the suhur, and to place our right hands upon our left [in prayer].”"],[10801,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed the best reciter among people is one who, when he recites, shows sorrow.”"],[10802,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram.”"],[10803,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in ihram.”"],[10804,"“The Prophet ﷺ was commanded that we prostrate on seven [parts] and that we not gather back our hair or clothing.”"],[10805,"The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven: his face, his palms, his knees, and his feet, and he was forbidden to gather back hair or clothing."],[10807,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven and was forbidden to gather back his hair and garments.”"],[10808,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ was commanded that we prostrate on seven bones and was forbidden to gather back hair or clothing.”"],[10809,"“The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven and that he gather back his hair or garments.”"],[10810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven body parts: the nose, the forehead, the palms, and the tips of the fingers, and not to gather back hair or clothing.”"],[10811,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10812,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I have been forbidden to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and I have been forbidden to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven (bones), and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck back the hair or the garment.\""],[10818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid, even if it is a hundred conditions.\""],[10819,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of fruit until it is fit to eat.\""],[10820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes possession of it.\""],[10821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you buy food, do not sell it until you take possession of it.\" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"I consider that other than that in sales is like food.\""],[10822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys food should not sell it until he receives it in full.\" And I think that everything is like it."],[10823,"The food that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited to be sold until it is received (taken possession of)."],[10824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of food before it is received."],[10825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you buys food, he should not sell it until he receives it.\""],[10826,"Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He who buys foodstuff should not sell it till he is satisfied with the measure with which he has bought it. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2126)"],[10827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of food until it is fully received."],[10828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid sharecropping (muzāraʿa), but he commanded that they be kind to one another."],[10829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to grant his brother [the use of] his land is better for him than taking a fixed remuneration.\""],[10830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit leasing land, but he said: \"For one of you to grant [the use of] his land to his brother is better for him than taking a remuneration for it.\""],[10831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For a man to grant his brother [the use of] his land is better for him than taking a fixed rent (kharj) for it.\""],[10832,"The Prophet ﷺ once said on earth, \"Giving it as a gift to your brother is better than collecting rent for it.\""],[10833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For one of you to grant it to his brother is better for him,\" and he did not prohibit leasing it."],[10834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For a man to let his brother cultivate [his land] is better for him than taking a rent (kharāj) for it.\""],[10835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The people of Madinah enter ihrām from Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, the people of Shām from al-Juḥfah, the people of Yemen from Yalamlam, and the people of Najd from Qarn.\""],[10836,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I made ẓihār from my wife, and her anklet pleased me last night, so I had intercourse with her before I made expiation.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Did not Allah, Mighty and Sublime, say: {before they touch one another}? Refrain until you make expiation.\""],[10837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited wearing silk, but there is no harm in wearing cotton or linen fabric."],[10838,"The Prophet ﷺ took in his hand a piece of gold and a piece of silk and said, \"Verily, these two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah and permissible for their females.\""],[10839,"The first to proclaim Islam openly was Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ"],[10840,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: \"If I remain until next year, I will certainly fast the ninth.\""],[10841,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to take back his gift, except a father.\""],[10842,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said: \"Horses belonging to the Muslims attacked a people among the polytheists, and they fought them and killed their children.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are with their fathers.\""],[10843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Silver has not been spent on anything more beloved to Allah than a sacrificial animal slaughtered on the day of Eid.\""],[10844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing is seen better for two who love each other than marriage.\""],[10845,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in his sermon, \"Verily, he guides to the best of manners, and indeed, he repels their evil.\""],[10846,"A man gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a she-camel as a gift, and he gave him a reward for it. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" So he gave him more. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"No.\" So he gave him more. He said: \"Are you satisfied?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I had resolved not to accept a gift except from an Ansari, a Qurashi, or a Thaqafi.\""],[10847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Remain in your places of dwelling, for emigration has ceased, but there remains jihad and intention. When you are called out, go forth.\""],[10848,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah, \"Shall we act according to what has been decreed and rely on it, or should we depend on something we strive for?\" He said, \"No, rather act according to what has been decreed, for the pens have dried.\" He said, \"Then what is the point of striving?\" He said, \"Act, for everyone will be facilitated (in their actions).\""],[10849,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Surat Tanzeel (al-Sajdah) and ten verses from the al-Mufassal, and sometimes he would say, \"Has there come upon man...\""],[10850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attach the fixed shares to the estate, and whatever the fixed shares leave goes to the nearest male.\""],[10851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Divide the estate among the heirs of the fixed shares according to the Book of Allah, and whatever the fixed shares leave goes to the nearest male.\""],[10852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attach the fixed shares to the Book of Allah, and what I have left goes to the nearest male.\""],[10853,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Give the Fara'id (the shares of the inheritance that are prescribed in the Qur'an) to those who are entitled to receive it. Then whatever remains, should be given to the closest male relative of the deceased .\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6732)"],[10854,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The evil eye is real. If anything could outstrip destiny, the evil eye would do so. And if you are asked to wash (for it), then wash.”"],[10855,"They used to consider performing ʿUmrah during the months of Hajj as one of the most wicked acts on earth. They used to call Muharram Safar and say: “When the wounds of the camel’s back heal, and the tracks fade away, and Safar passes, then ʿUmrah becomes permissible for the one intending it.”"],[10856,"And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform Umrah with Aisha in Dhu al-Hijjah except to refute the statements of the polytheists. For this place is from Quraish, and whoever criticizes their religion, they used to say, \"When the Yam (a type of fly) urinates and the donkey's tail is raised, then the Umrah is considered. So they used to prohibit Umrah until Dhu al-Hijjah and Muharram would pass. And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not perform Umrah with Aisha except to fulfill their statement."],[10857,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped, gave the cupper his fee, and used medication in the nose."],[10858,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he was asked about the slaughtering and the shaving, regarding which comes first and which comes later. He said: “There is no harm.”"],[10859,"“The one who takes back his gift is like the dog that goes back to its vomit.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2386)"],[10860,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fixed Dhul-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, Qarn for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. These are for their residents and for those who come to them intending Hajj or ʿUmrah. Anyone who is nearer than that should assume ihram from his starting point, even the people of Makkah from Makkah.”"],[10863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding Allah’s ﷻ statement {Then there is no rafath, no fusuq, and no jidal in Hajj}: “Rafath is lewd speech and soliciting women for intercourse; fusuq is all acts of disobedience; and jidal is a man arguing with his companion.”"],[10864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from selling food until he had taken full possession of it."],[10865,"“Triple divorce was considered one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and the first two years of ʿUmar’s caliphate.” Then ʿUmar said: “The people have become hasty in a matter in which they had been given respite. If only we could enforce it upon them.” So he enforced it upon them."],[10866,"“The three pronouncements were made one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, and three during the first part of ʿUmar’s rule.” Ibn ʿAbbas said: “Yes.”"],[10867,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[10868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather the hair or the clothes.”"],[10870,"About mutʿah marriage: because they used to trade in the middle of the year.”"],[10871,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who had dyed (his beard) with henna and said, \"How good this is.\" Then another passed by him who had dyed with henna and katam, and he said, \"How good this is.\" Then another passed by him who had dyed with saffron, and he said, \"This is better than all of that.\" And Tawus used to dye with saffron."],[10872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade intercepting the caravans and a resident selling on behalf of a Bedouin."],[10873,"\"The first to embrace Islam was Ali ؓ.\""],[10874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever splits the staff of the Muslims while the Muslims are in a complete state of Islam has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck.\""],[10875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The worst house is the bathhouse; voices are raised in it and private parts are exposed.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the sick are treated in it and filth is removed in it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever enters it, let him enter only covered.\""],[10876,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned wine, and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we make a drink from this millet.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[10877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A one-eyed or emaciated animal is not permissible as a sacrificial camel, and beware of the one that has been deliberately weakened.\""],[10878,"The Prophet ﷺ was given some game meat, but he returned it and said, \"We are forbidden to eat it.\""],[10879,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque on Friday and saw Abu Isra'il standing in the sun without seeking shade. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with him?\" They said, \"He vowed to stand and not seek shade and not break his fast.\" He said, \"Command him to sit, seek shade, and break his fast.\""],[10880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived on the morning of the fourth day, pronouncing talbiyah for Hajj. He ordered them to make it an Umrah, but that seemed grave to them. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what kind of exiting from ihram?\" He said, \"Complete exiting.\""],[10881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Beware of a house called the bathhouse.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt and benefits the sick.\" He said, \"Whoever enters it, let him cover himself.\""],[10882,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no vow except in that in which Allah is obeyed, and no vow involving severing ties of kinship, and no divorce or manumission regarding what one does not own.\""],[10883,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a khamisa."],[10884,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever revives dead land, he has the most right to it.”"],[10885,"The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his hands in every rak'ah, and the righteous said to do so after every takbirah."],[10886,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a woolen cloak alone."],[10887,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Cupping on the head is a cure for seven things, if the one performing it intends them: madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, toothache, headache, and a darkness he finds in his eyes.”"],[10888,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say after the tashahhud: “O God, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge with You from the trial of the Dajjal, and I seek refuge with You from the trials of life and death.”"],[10889,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {So recite what is easy of the Qur'an}: He said: “A hundred verses.”"],[10890,"“There is no divorce except with a waiting period, and no manumission except for the sake of God the Exalted.”"],[10891,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the Eid prayer without an adhan or iqamah, then he came to the women and admonished them and urged them to give charity. So how many necklaces and rings were thrown into Bilal's garment until it was filled, or as God willed."],[10892,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “This city is sacred; God made it sacred, and killing was not made lawful in it for anyone before me, but it was made lawful for me, so it is sacred by God's sanctity.”"],[10893,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: “There is no emigration after the conquest, but there is jihad and intention. And when you are called to mobilize, then mobilize.”"],[10894,"I traveled with the Messenger of God ﷺ in Ramadan, and he fasted until he reached Usfan, then he called for a vessel and drank from it so that the people could see him. Then he broke his fast when he entered Makkah and conquered Makkah in Ramadan. Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted while traveling and broke his fast, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break his fast.”"],[10895,"“The price of a shield at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ was ten dirhams.”"],[10896,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “Ghusl is obligatory on every Muslim every seven days, for his hair and his skin”—meaning for Friday. “Sa'id b. Miqlas is Sa'id b. Abi Ayyub.”"],[10897,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the Day of Sacrifice: “No deed of the son of Adam on this day is more excellent than blood that is shed, except a severed womb that is reconnected.”"],[10898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “One is not a believer of complete faith who does not regard affliction as a blessing and ease as a misfortune.” They said, “How is that, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Because affliction is followed only by ease, and likewise ease is followed only by misfortune. And one is not a believer of complete faith who is not in sorrow whenever he is not in prayer.” They said, “And why, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Because the one praying converses intimately with his Lord, and when he is not in prayer he only converses with the son of Adam.”"],[10899,"That you touch your buttocks to your heels in prayer.”"],[10900,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give good tidings and do not drive people away; and when you become angry, be silent.”"],[10901,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ shared among his companions on the day of Hudaybiyyah seven people in a cow.”"],[10902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am holding you by your waist-wrappers, saying, ‘Guard against the Fire, guard against the prescribed punishments.’ When I die, I will leave you, and I will be your forerunner at the cistern. Whoever reaches it will have succeeded. Then some people will be brought and will be taken to the left. I will say, ‘My Lord,’ and He will say, ‘They kept turning back on their heels after you.’”"],[10903,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man circumambulating the House while another man was leading him by a nose-ring due to a vow he had made, so he cut it and said: “Lead him by his hand.” And he passed by a man who had tied his hand to another person with a strap or a thread or something else, so he cut it and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Lead him by his hand.”"],[10904,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Circumambulation of the House is prayer, but God Almighty has permitted speech therein. So whoever speaks should speak only good.”"],[10905,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When one of you stands in prayer, let him not close his eyes.”"],[10906,"The Prophet ﷺ used to call the Farewell Pilgrimage the Pilgrimage of Islam.”"],[10907,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ ramaled at the House and between Safā and Marwah only because the polytheists had seen hardship in him and his companions, so he ramaled.”"],[10908,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The pilgrim in ihram may kill the crow, the kite, the scorpion, the vicious dog, and the mouse.”"],[10909,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The son of Adam has been commanded to prostrate on seven bones.”"],[10910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a shoulder blade and said: “Bring me a shoulder blade so that I may write for you a document after which you will never differ.” Those with him among the people began to make a clamor, so a woman among those present said: “Woe to you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is making a covenant with you.” Some of the people said: “Be quiet, for you have no intellect.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “You are the ones with no forbearance.”"],[10911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me a shoulder blade and an inkpot so that I may write for you a document concerning which no two men will differ.” He said: “They were slow in bringing the shoulder blade and the inkpot, so Allah took him.”"],[10912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night prayer should be performed in pairs of two, and the Witr prayer should be a single unit of prayer at the end of the night.\""],[10913,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the Day of the Conquest the meat of jallāla animals, their milk, and their backs.”"],[10914,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tamattuʿ until he died, and Abu Bakr ؓ performed tamattuʿ until he died, and ʿUmar and ʿUthman ؓ” — meaning the tamattuʿ of Hajj."],[10915,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the Kaʿba and said: “There is no god but Allah. How good you are, and how good your fragrance, and how great your sanctity! Yet the believer is greater in sanctity than you. Indeed, Allah ﷻ has made you sacred, and He has made inviolable from the believer his wealth, his blood, his honor, and that we should think ill of him.”"],[10916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “recited the talbiya in ʿUmra until he touched the Black Stone, and in Hajj until he threw the jamra.”"],[10917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “gave a grandmother one-sixth.”"],[10918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The excellence of knowledge is superior to worship, and the essence of the religion is piety.”"],[10920,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Ruqbā is not lawful, nor ʿumrā. Whoever is given something as ruqbā or ʿumrā, it belongs to him.”"],[10921,"We arrived with the Prophet ﷺ intending only Hajj, so we entered iḥrām for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated on his mount, touching the corner with a staff he had with him. Then he turned to the watering place and said: “Draw some water for me from it.” They drew a bucket for him, and he took a sip, rinsed his mouth, then spat it back into the bucket and said: “Return it to the well.” Then he said: “O Banū Hāshim, you are engaged in a righteous work. Were it not that you would be overcome for it or it would be taken as a sunna, I would have taken part with you.” Then he went to his dwelling and addressed his companions, saying: “ʿUmra has entered into your Hajj, so release yourselves from iḥrām, except those who have a sacrificial animal with them.” And he said: “Were it not that I have a sacrificial animal with me, I would have released myself from iḥrām with you.” Surāqa b. Mālik stood up and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this for this year of ours or forever?” He said: “Rather, forever.” They were pleased by whatever conformed to the practice of the people of the Jāhiliyya. The people of the Jāhiliyya used to say: when Ṣafar has passed, the fur has grown, and the wound has healed, then ʿUmra is lawful for the one performing ʿUmra."],[10922,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There will be rulers who are recognized and denounced. Whoever opposes them is saved, whoever keeps away from them is safe, and whoever mixes with them is ruined.”"],[10923,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no zakah on working oxen, but for every thirty cattle there is a tabiʿ (a one-year-old male calf), and for every forty there is a musinn (a two-year-old cow or bull).”"],[10924,"“At the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, three were made one.”"],[10925,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Tawaf is prayer, so speak little during it.”"],[10926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever imitates in poetry, he has no morals with Allah.\""],[10927,"Safwan b. Umayyah came to Madinah and slept in the mosque, placing a khamisah (a striped cloak) of his under his head. A thief came and stole it. He went to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that the thief's hand be cut off. Safwan said: “O Messenger of God, it is his.” He said: “Why did you not say so before you brought him to me?”"],[10928,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped and said: “Pay him his fee.”"],[10929,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Many a teacher of the letters of Abu Jad, who is learned in the stars, will have no share with God on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[10930,"He mentioned the Prophet's ﷺ statement about the Friday ghusl. I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: “Should he also apply perfume or oil if he has it for his family?” He said: “I do not know.”"],[10931,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ prescribed the prayer of travel as two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs, and prescribed the prayer of residence as four rakʿahs.”"],[10932,"I attended the Eid prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he began with the prayer before the sermon."],[10933,"The Prophet ﷺ passed while circumambulating the Kaʿbah and saw a man leading another man by a nose ring in his nose. The Prophet ﷺ cut it off, then ordered him to lead him by his hand."],[10934,"The Prophet ﷺ passed while circumambulating the Kaʿbah and saw a man whose hand was tied to another man with a strap, a string, or something else. The Prophet ﷺ cut it and said: “Lead him by your hand.”"],[10935,"The people used to leave in every direction, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “None of you should depart until his last act is at the House.”"],[10936,"When the Prophet ﷺ got up at night to perform tahajjud, he would say: “O God, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Maintainer of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the King of the heavens and the earth and all within them. To You belongs praise. You are the Truth, Your speech is true, the meeting with You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, the Hour is true, Muhammad ﷺ is true, and the prophets are true. O God, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have contended, and to You I have made judgment, so forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer. There is no god but You.”"],[10937,"God says: “And let them circumambulate the Ancient House” [Qurʾan 22:29]. And the Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated from behind it."],[10938,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever takes back his gift is like one who returns to his own vomit.”"],[10939,"The Messenger of God ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʻAqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[10940,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No one introduces into this community an innovation that did not exist before without dying while afflicted by it.” I myself saw Ibn Hishām when he was deposed and the agents of al-Walīd came and put a collar around his neck."],[10941,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Five things are met with five.” They said: “O Messenger of God, what are five met with five?” He said: “No people break a covenant but their enemy is given power over them; none judge by other than what God has sent down but poverty spreads among them; indecency does not appear among them but death spreads among them; none give short measure but vegetation is withheld from them and they are seized with years of drought; and none withhold the zakah but rain is withheld from them.”"],[10942,"After the takbir and after saying “I have turned my face toward Him who originated the heavens and the earth as a ḥanīf, a Muslim,” the Messenger of God ﷺ would say: “O God, to You belongs praise. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all within them. You are the Truth, Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. O God, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, with You I have contended, and to You I have made judgment, so forgive me for what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have made public. O God, You are my God; there is no god but You.” Then after this the Messenger of God ﷺ would recite."],[10943,"A leg of a wild donkey was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ at Kurāʻ al-Ghamīm, but he returned it to its owner and apologised to him, saying: “We are in a state of iḥrām.”"],[10944,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his own vomit.”"],[10945,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us the Qurʾan, and he would say: “Greetings, blessed words, prayers, and good things belong to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.” Yaḥyā b. Bukayr said: Al-Layth used to adopt this."],[10947,"He heard Ṭāwūs say: I said to Ibn ʻAbbās about sitting on the two heels, and he said: “It is the Sunnah.” I said: “We consider it harsh for a man.” He said: “It is the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.”"],[10948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[10949,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “Do not impose conditions of ruqba on your property; for whoever is given something as a ruqba, it belongs to the one to whom it is given.” Ruqba is when a man says: “This is for so-and-so as long as he lives; and if so-and-so dies, then it is for so-and-so.”"],[10950,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of Muzdalifah is a place of standing; and keep away from the interior of Muhassir. And all of Mina is a place of sacrifice.”"],[10951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever recites the surah in which the family of ʿImran is mentioned on Friday, ﷺ and His angels bless him until the sun sets.”"],[10952,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “Allah ﷻ created this city on the day He created the heavens and the earth, and fashioned it when He fashioned the sun and the moon. Whatever faces it from the sky is sacred. It was not lawful for anyone before me; it was made lawful for me only for an hour of a day, then it returned to being as it was.” It was said to him: “This is Khalid b. al-Walid killing people.” He said: “Arise, O so-and-so, and go to Khalid b. al-Walid and tell him to restrain his hand from killing.” The man went to him and said: “The Prophet of Allah ﷺ says: ‘Kill whom you are able to overpower.’” So he killed seventy people. Then someone came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He sent for Khalid and said: “Did I not forbid you from killing?” He replied: “So-and-so came to me and ordered me to kill whom I was able to overpower.” He sent to him: “Did I not command you?” He said: “You wanted one thing, and Allah wanted something else. Allah’s command prevailed over your command, and I could not do anything except what happened.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not respond to him at all."],[10953,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: “There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership.”"],[10954,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: “All of ʿArafah is a place of standing; and keep away from the interior of ʿUranah.”"],[10955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to gather up my garment or my hair.”"],[10956,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We were commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and we were ordered not to gather up a garment or hair.”"],[10957,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or give it to his brother.”"],[10958,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We have not seen anything like marriage for two people who love each other.”"],[10959,"“…that your heels touch your buttocks.”"],[10960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones, and not to tuck up hair or clothing.”"],[10961,"From the Prophet ﷺ that when he stood for the night prayer, he would say the takbīr and then say: “O Allah, Yours is the praise, the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth; Yours is the praise, the Light of the heavens and the earth; Yours is the praise, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and all within them. You are the Truth, Your word is the truth, Your promise is the truth, the meeting with You is true, the Garden is true, the Fire is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, by You I have disputed, and to You I have brought judgment. You are our Lord, and to You is the return. My Lord, forgive me what I have kept secret and what I have made public, what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed. You are my God; there is no god but You.”"],[10962,"“I scraped it off with idhkhir and wool”—that is, semen."],[10963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “We were commanded to prostrate on seven limbs and not to tuck up hair or clothing.”"],[10964,"… that you place your buttocks on your heels between the two prostrations.”"],[10965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a woman in her howdah, and she brought out a child and said, “O Prophet of Allah, is there Hajj for this one?” He said, “Yes, and you have a reward.”"],[10966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is killed in blind fighting or in a stoning with a stone or a stick, his blood money is the heaviest upon his ʿāqila. Whoever is killed by his own hand, retribution is on his hand. Whoever intervenes between him and that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither ṣarf nor ʿadl will be accepted from him.”"],[10967,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymūna while he was in iḥrām."],[10968,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the eclipse prayer, he said: “He recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed, then recited, then bowed; and the other rakʿah was the same.”"],[10969,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit, from a supplication that is not heard, from a heart that does not humble itself, and from a soul that is not satisfied. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from these four.”"],[10970,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while at Minā: “If the people of the gathering knew with whom they had settled, or among whom they had alighted, they would rejoice at the bounty from their Lord after forgiveness.”"],[10971,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while at Minā: “If the people of the gathering knew with whom they had settled, they would rejoice at the bounty after forgiveness.”"],[10972,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the ʿisha prayer one night until the people of the mosque had left, except ʿUthman b. Mazʿun—one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—and fifteen or sixteen men, not reaching seventeen. ʿUthman said, “I will not leave tonight until the Prophet ﷺ comes out, so that I may pray with him and learn what his matter is.” The Prophet ﷺ came out near the first third of the night, with Bilal, and he did not see anyone in the mosque when he heard the murmur of their speech in a corner of the mosque. He walked to them until he greeted them and said, “What keeps you sitting at this hour?” They said, “O Prophet of God, we waited for you to witness the prayer with you.” He said to them, “No nation before you has ever prayed this prayer of yours, and you have continued to be in prayer ever since.” And he said, “Indeed the stars are a safeguard for the sky; when the stars are effaced, what you are promised will come to the sky. I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I go, what my Companions are promised will come to them. My Companions are a safeguard for my nation; when my Companions go, what my nation is promised will come to it.”"],[10973,"“No one do I vouch for except the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[10974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever his prayer does not restrain from indecency and wrong does not increase from God except in distance.”"],[10975,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions “did not perform tawaf between al-Safa and al-Marwa except a single tawaf, for their hajj and their ʿumra.”"],[10976,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The son of Adam has three hundred and sixty joints; for each one of them, each day, is a charity.” He said, “The good word a man speaks is charity; a man’s helping his brother with something is charity; the drink of water he gives is charity; and removing harm from the road is charity.”"],[10977,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Were it not that the Rukn has been imprinted with the impurities of the Jahiliyya and its filths, and the hands of wrongdoers and sinners, it would be used to seek healing for every ailment, and it would remain today as it was on the day God created it. God only changed it to blackness so that the people of this world would not look upon the adornment of Paradise and that it will return to it. Indeed it is a sapphire from the sapphires of Paradise, which God placed when He sent down Adam at the site of the Kaʿba, before the Kaʿba existed. The earth then was pure, and no acts of disobedience had been done on it, and it had no inhabitants to defile it. A row of angels was placed for it on the boundaries of the sanctuary, guarding it from the inhabitants of the earth—its inhabitants then being the jinn, for whom it was not appropriate to look at it because it is something from Paradise. The angels were keeping them away from it, standing on the boundaries of the sanctuary, surrounding it on every side. For that reason it was called the sanctuary, because they form a barrier between them and it.”"],[10978,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Twelve thousand will come out of ʿAdan Abyan, supporting God and His Messenger. They are the best of those between me and them.”"],[10979,"“Whoever dwells in the desert becomes coarse; whoever follows the hunt becomes heedless; and whoever goes to the ruler is put to trial.”"],[10980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “No one who commits incest with a mahram will enter Paradise.”"],[10981,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is enough sin for you that you never cease to be quarrelsome.”"],[10982,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Jibril ﷺ to show himself in his true form. He said, “Call upon your Lord.” So he called upon his Lord, and a blackness appeared before him from the direction of the east, and it began to rise and spread. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, he fell down in a faint. Then he came to him, revived him, and wiped the spittle from the corner of his mouth."],[10983,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The death of a stranger is martyrdom. When he is at the point of death, he casts his gaze to his right and to his left and sees no one but strangers. He remembers his family and children and takes a breath; for every breath he takes, God erases two thousand thousand sins and records for him two thousand thousand good deeds.”"],[10984,"Ibn ʿAbbās said regarding the prostration in Ṣād: \"It is the repentance of a prophet; Allah commanded His prophet to follow him.\""],[10985,"{Those are they whom Allah has guided, so follow their guidance.}"],[10986,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while on a journey and he was reciting Sūrat Ṣād, \"and he prostrated in it.\""],[10987,"In His saying \"And indeed, We have given you, [O Muhammad], seven of the often repeated [verses]\", He said, \"These are the seven often repeated [verses]\"."],[10988,"The Prophet ﷺ \"performed cupping on the top of his foot while he was fasting.\""],[10989,"\"Concession was given to the elderly man while he is fasting, and the young man was forbidden.\""],[10990,"\"Allah, may He be exalted, made the prayer obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rakʿahs when resident, two rakʿahs when travelling, and one rakʿah in fear.\""],[10991,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The prayer of residence is four rakʿahs, of travel is two rakʿahs, and of fear is one rakʿah.\""],[10992,"\"Allah made the prayer obligatory upon the tongue of your Prophet ﷺ: four rakʿahs when resident, two rakʿahs when travelling, and one rakʿah in fear.\""],[10993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was aided by the east wind, and ʿĀd was destroyed by the west wind.\""],[10994,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: \"This is an ʿumrah from which we have benefited. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should come out of iḥrām completely. The ʿumrah has been incorporated into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10995,"The Prophet ﷺ made it an ʿumrah. They had arrived in Makkah four nights before ʿArafah, and he disliked that the Muslims should remain for four nights without circumambulating the House. He knew that if they circumambulated the House they would come out of iḥrām, except for those who had brought sacrificial animals. So he said three times: \"An ʿumrah from which we have benefited. Then the ʿumrah was incorporated into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[10996,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I was given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was sent to the red and the black, while the Prophet ﷺ was sent only to his own people specifically. I was aided by fear, so that the enemy would fear me from a distance of a month or two months' journey. War booty was made lawful for me, and it was not lawful for anyone before me. The earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification. And it was said to me, 'Ask and you shall be given,' so I reserved my supplication as intercession for my community. It will reach, if Allah wills, whoever died without associating anything with Allah.\""],[10997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day before the Tarwiyah: “Our resting place tomorrow, if Allah wills, will be at al-Khayf al-Ayman where the polytheists used to draw lots.”"],[10998,"Al-Fadl was older than me, and he used to let me ride behind him, so I would be in front of him. Once my brother and I rode behind on a female donkey and reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying with the people at Arafah. We dismounted in front of him and joined the prayer, leaving her to graze in front of him, and he did not interrupt his prayer."],[10999,"He instructed that a man should not pray more than one prayer with a single tayammum; then he should perform tayammum again for the next prayer."],[11000,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over Hamzah and saw what had been done to his body, he said, \"If it weren't for the sadness that it would cause the women, I would have left him until he was consumed by the stomachs of animals and the beaks of birds, until Allah resurrects him from there.\" He was saddened by what he saw, so he said, \"If I am victorious over the Quraysh, I will mutilate thirty of their men.\" Allah then revealed in this regard, \"So if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted\" until His saying, \"They are plotting.\" He then ordered that he be prepared for burial, so his body was prepared facing the qiblah, and the takbir (saying Allahu Akbar) was pronounced over him nine times. Then all the martyrs were gathered around him, and whenever a martyr was brought, he was placed next to Hamzah and the funeral prayer was performed for him and the martyrs together with him. This continued until the funeral prayer was performed for him and the martyrs seventy-two times. Then he stood up and faced his Companions until he saw them, and when the Quran was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pardoned and forgave and left the mutilation."],[11001,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Go on military expeditions and you will gain the daughters of the yellow ones.” Some of the hypocrites said: “He is tempting you with women.” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: “Among them are those who say, ‘Grant me leave and do not tempt me.’”"],[11002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled during Ramadan and both fasted and broke his fast. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke his fast."],[11003,"Two verses of Surat al-Maʾidah were abrogated: the verse of the sacrificial animal and the garlands, and the other verse: “So judge between them or turn away from them.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was given a choice in that matter: if he wished, he could judge between them, and if he wished, he could refer them to someone else’s judgment, until it was revealed: “So judge between them by what Allah has sent down.”"],[11004,"He forbade drinking from the ear of the cup and from its crack."],[11005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was helped against his enemy with terror casting a distance of two months’ journey."],[11006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Jesus, Moses, and Abraham (peace be upon them all). As for Jesus, he was reddish, with curly hair and a broad chest. As for Moses, he was dark-skinned, large-bodied, and straight-haired, as if he were from the men of the Zutt.” They said to him: “And Abraham?” He said: “Look at your companion.”"],[11007,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”"],[11008,"A man from the people of al-Awali would sometimes invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at midnight to share barley bread, and he would accept."],[11009,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on his mount, touching the corner with his staff."],[11010,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am the city of knowledge and ʿAlī is its gate, so whoever wants knowledge should come to its gate.”"],[11011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out when he went to the Banu Qurayzah on a donkey, and with him was Jibril (Gabriel) ﷺ on a white mule with a saddle made of silk. The flag-bearer led the way and they set off for an hour, then Jibril ﷺ said, \"O Muhammad, by the One Who sent you with the truth, I will not dismount from it until it is opened for you.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So he did not go back until it was opened for him.\""],[11012,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Ali and Fatima while they were laughing. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ , they remained silent. The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"Why were you both laughing, but when you saw me, you remained silent?\" Fatima replied, \"By my father, are you more beloved to the Messenger of Allah?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"This is Ali, who is dearer to me than you.\""],[11013,"“We are the family of Muḥammad ﷺ.”"],[11014,"When the verse “In it are men who love to purify themselves” was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ sent for ʿUwaymir b. Sāʿidah and said: “What is this purification for which God ﷻ has praised you?” They said: “O Messenger of God, no man or woman among us comes out of the privy without washing his private part—or he said his posterior.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is it.”"],[11015,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while he was in Makkah facing toward the Sacred House, and the Kaʿbah was between his hands, and after he emigrated for sixteen months, then he turned to the Kaʿbah.”"],[11016,"On the day of Khaibar, Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the eating of donkey meat. (Using translation from Bukhārī 4217)"],[11017,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “Fear God with the fear due to Him...” (the verse), and said: “If a drop of zaqqūm were dropped into the seas of this world, it would corrupt their livelihoods. How much worse for the one whose food it will be?”"],[11018,"That he used to consider the exception valid even after a year. Then he recited: “And never say of anything, ‘I will do that tomorrow,’ except [saying], ‘If God wills.’ And remember your Lord when you forget.” He said: “When you remember.” It was said to al-Aʿmash: “Did you hear this from Mujāhid?” He said: “Al-Layth related it to me from Mujāhid.”"],[11019,"A group of young men from the Banu Hashim came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, allow us to participate in this charity. We want our share to be distributed among the people, and we will fulfill our obligations just like everyone else.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"We, the family of Muhammad, are not allowed to receive charity. It is the impurities of people. But what would you think if I were to hold onto the ring of Paradise? Would anyone be preferred over you?\""],[11020,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ “used to combine Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and combine Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ during travel, without any urgent matter, or an enemy pursuing him, or fear of anything.”"],[11021,"I was in the house of my maternal aunt Maymūnah, and the Prophet ﷺ got up at night and performed ablution. I stood at his left side, and he turned me around with his hands and placed me on his right side."],[11022,"That the Prophet ﷺ “combined between Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ, in travel and in residence.”"],[11023,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange, so blessed are the strangers.”"],[11024,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night, in which a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever at night, and a believer at night and a disbeliever in the morning, and a people will sell their religion for a portion of this world.”"],[11025,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Have yourselves cupped on the fifteenth, seventeenth, nineteenth, or twenty-first, lest the blood surge within you and kill you.”"],[11026,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has three children born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant.”"],[11027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter.”"],[11028,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the most beloved of deeds to Allah after the obligatory ones is bringing joy to a Muslim.”"],[11029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of the conquest of Makkah (eating) the jallālah and (taking) spoils unlawfully."],[11030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts the day of ʿArafah, it will be an expiation for two years.”"],[11031,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts two days of al-Muḥarram, for each day he will have thirty good deeds.”"],[11032,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not one of us who does not honor the elderly, show mercy to the young, enjoin good, and forbid evil.”"],[11033,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ and ʿAlī ؓ among the gardens of Madinah. We passed by a garden, and ʿAlī ؓ said: “How beautiful this garden is, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Your garden in Paradise is more beautiful than it.” Then he gestured with his hand to his head and beard, then wept until his weeping grew loud. It was said: “What makes you weep?” He said: “Grudges in the hearts of a people that they will not show you until they lose me.”"],[11034,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"I have been given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was given the red and black camels, and indeed the prophets were sent only to their own people, while I was sent to all people. I was granted victory through fear, as the enemy would be afraid of me from the distance it takes to travel for a month. I was given the spoils of war, and the land was made for me a place of prayer and purification. And I was given intercession, and I have saved it for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11035,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said on the night he was taken on the Night Journey: “I saw Ibrāhīm and he resembled me. I saw Mūsā, tall with curly hair, as if he were from the men of Shanūʾah. I saw ʿĪsā, fair with a medium build and straight hair, as if his head were dripping with oil.”"],[11036,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī: “You are to me in the position of Hārūn to Mūsā.”"],[11037,"The Prophet ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “I will surely kill the ʿAmāliqah in a battalion.” Then Jibrīl ﷺ said: “Or ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ.”"],[11038,"He used to recite this variant: “{Mustakbirīna bihi sāmiran tahjurūn}.” He said: “The polytheists used to satirize the Messenger of Allah in their poetry.”"],[11039,"Speech is disliked in four situations: on the day of Friday (Jumuʿah), on the day of Fiṭr, on the day of Aḍḥā, and during the prayer for rain, when the imam ascends the pulpit; he speaks until he descends."],[11040,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, how is ablution performed?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water for ablution and washed his right hand three times, then he put his hand into the vessel, then he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, each three times, then he wiped his head and the outer part of his ears along with his head, then he washed his feet three times. Then he said, “This is ablution. Whoever adds to this has transgressed and wronged.”"],[11041,"When the Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between his companions, between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, and did not establish brotherhood between ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and anyone among them, ʿAlī ؓ went out angry until he came to a small watercourse and lay on his arm, and the wind blew dust over him. The Prophet ﷺ searched for him until he found him, then poked him with his foot and said to him, “Get up, for you are not fit to be called anything but Abū Turāb (father of dust). Are you angry with me because I established brotherhood between the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār and did not establish brotherhood between you and anyone among them? Are you not pleased that you are to me in the position of Hārūn to Mūsā, except that there is no prophet after me? Indeed, whoever loves you will be surrounded by security and faith, and whoever hates you, Allah will cause him to die the death of the Age of Ignorance, and he will be reckoned for his deeds in Islam.”"],[11042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “In Paradise there is a tree,” or “There is no tree in Paradise” – ʿAlī b. Jamīl was uncertain – “that does not have a leaf except that it is written on it: There is no god but Allah, Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah, Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, ʿUmar al-Fārūq, ʿUthmān Dhū al-Nūrayn.”"],[11043,"“When the sun sets, restrain your children, for it is an hour in which the devils spread out.”"],[11044,"From Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ – I think he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ – he said: “There are two insatiable ones whose craving is never satisfied: one insatiable in seeking knowledge, and one insatiable in seeking worldly gain.”"],[11045,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Ṣād (Sūrah 38)."],[11046,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: This tribe of Quraysh used to approach women in Makkah and enjoy them in every position, facing and from behind. When they came to Madinah and married among the Anṣār, and tried to do the same with them, they objected and said, “This is something we have never been approached with.” The matter spread until it reached the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah, exalted be He, revealed concerning that: “Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish” [Qurʾān 2:223] – facing or, if you wish, on her back, meaning by that the place of childbirth for the tilth; he says: come to the tilth from wherever you wish. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Ibn ʿUmar said, “In her back passage,” and Ibn ʿUmar erred, may Allah forgive him, for the matter was as I have explained."],[11047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever gives the call to prayer for seven years seeking Allah’s reward, a clearance from the Fire will be written for him.”"],[11048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A single jurist is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers.”"],[11049,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The best of them (women) is the one with the easiest dowry.”"],[11050,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The best of them (women) is the one with the easiest dowry.”"],[11051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever participates in forbidden bloodshed by even half a word will come on the Day of Resurrection with it written between his eyes: 'Despairing of God's mercy.'\""],[11052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in a state of ihram."],[11053,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine, so cleanse yourselves from it.\""],[11054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Muslims are partners in three things: water, pasture, and fire. Its price is unlawful.\""],[11055,"A man with a wound was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, seeking his permission to lance it. He permitted him."],[11056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Treat my uncle al-ʿAbbas well, for he is the remnant of my forefathers. Indeed, a man's paternal uncle is his father's counterpart.\""],[11057,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed for me and said: \"What an excellent interpreter you are.\" And Gabriel prayed for me twice."],[11058,"When ʿUmar embraced Islam, Gabriel ﷺ descended and said: \"O Muhammad, the inhabitants of heaven have rejoiced at ʿUmar's Islam.\""],[11059,"Seek goodness and needs from people of handsome faces."],[11060,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O people, ask God for your dead, and do not announce their deaths to people.\""],[11061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar used to place the deceased in the grave from the direction of the qiblah."],[11062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Adorn your voices with the Quran.\""],[11063,"\"They are people who disbelieved in ʿĪsā and then believed in Muḥammad.\" {And those who disbelieve—their allies are ṭāghūt; they bring them out of the light into darkness.} \"They are people who believed in ʿĪsā, then when Muḥammad was sent, they disbelieved in him.\""],[11064,"While the Prophet ﷺ was on the pulpit, he said \"Ameen\" three times. When asked about it, he said that Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, \"Whoever you are mentioned in front of and they do not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen. Jibril ﷺ continued, \"Whoever reaches the age where their parents, or one of them, are alive and they do not earn their forgiveness, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen. He further said, \"Whoever witnesses the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance them. Say Ameen.\" So I said Ameen."],[11065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which righteous deeds are more beloved to Allah and in which deeds are more virtuous than the ten days (of Dhul-Hijjah). So increase in these days the saying of Tahleel, Takbeer, and Tahmeed.\""],[11066,"We came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as pilgrims, and he commanded them, so they made it an ʿUmrah. Then he said, \"If I could go back and change what I have done, I would do as they have done, but the ʿUmrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he interlaced his fingers together. So the people exited ihrām except those who had the sacrificial animal with them. ʿAlī arrived from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"With what did you enter ihrām?\" He said, \"I entered ihrām with the same as you entered ihrām with.\" He said, \"Do you have a sacrificial animal with you?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then remain as you are, and you shall have a third of my sacrificial animal.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had brought one hundred camels as sacrificial animals."],[11067,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihrām for Hajj. When he arrived, he performed ṭawāf around the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, and he did not shorten his hair, and he did not exit ihrām, those who had brought the sacrificial animal. And he commanded those who had not brought the sacrificial animal to perform ṭawāf and saʿy and to shorten their hair or shave, and then to exit ihrām.\""],[11068,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man whose thigh was exposed, so he said, \"Cover it, for the thigh of a man is part of his nakedness.\""],[11069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the majority of the punishment in the grave is due to urine, so protect yourselves from urine.\""],[11070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever among you is unable to fight the enemy, or to endure the night in worship, let him remember Allah often.\""],[11071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better in the sight of Allah than Yūnus b. Mattā.'\""],[11072,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade inciting animals against one another.\""],[11073,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born on Monday, revelation came down to him on Monday, and he died on Monday.\""],[11074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Were it not that I would burden my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwāk at every prayer.\""],[11075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to perform ghusl behind the rooms, and no one ever saw his private parts.\""],[11076,"\"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a ring of silver.\""],[11077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"slaughtered his sacrificial animal on the day he was prevented, at al-Tanʿīm.\""],[11078,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on a mat.\""],[11079,"From Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His saying, {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you}, he said, \"He forbade himself his concubine.\""],[11080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled in Ramadan and fasted one day until the afternoon, then broke his fast, then fasted and completed the fast until night."],[11081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf and walked briskly in the first three rounds to show the polytheists that he and his companions had strength, and walked the remaining four."],[11082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not that my community would be burdened, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer.\""],[11083,"Regarding His saying {And those who commit immorality from among your women} up to His saying {until death takes them}, he said: \"They used to be confined in houses; if she died, she died, and if she lived, she lived,\" until this verse in Surat al-Nur was revealed: {The fornicatress and the fornicator, flog each one of them with a hundred lashes}, and Surat al-Hudud was revealed. So whoever committed something was flogged and released."],[11084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When a dead person is buried, he hears the sound of their sandals when they turn away from him departing.\""],[11085,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wear a shirt with short sleeves and length."],[11086,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿumrah in Ramadan."],[11087,"Allah's Messenger ﷺ said, “The first part of this matter (i.e., Islam) is prophethood accompanied by mercy; then there will caliphates accompanied by mercy; then there will be kingdoms accompanied by mercy; then there will be emirates accompanied by mercy; then they will bite at it like donkeys (i.e., they will fight over it.) So jihād is enjoined upon you; the best jihād is guarding the frontiers, and the best garrison is the one in ʿAsqalān.'"],[11088,"\"O Abu Abbas, I divorced my wife three times.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"You have disobeyed your Lord and your wife has become unlawful for you.\" Allah said, \"O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their prescribed waiting period.\""],[11089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did wipe [over the khuffs], but did he wipe after Surat al-Maʾidah was revealed?"],[11090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that the pen is lifted from three individuals: the sleeping person until they wake up, the insane person until they regain sanity, and the child until they reach understanding or reach puberty."],[11091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The ruin of my community lies in three things: tribalism, belief in predestination (al-qadariyyah), and narrating reports without verification.\""],[11092,"\"If you forget the exception, then make the exception when you remember. This is specific to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it is not for us to make an exception except in the connection of an oath.\""],[11093,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I do not ask you for any reward for the clear proofs and guidance I have brought you, except that you love Allah and draw near to Him through obedience to Him.\""],[11094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the sale of spoils of war before they were distributed."],[11095,"\"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited on the day of Khaybar the use of ropes for watering one's fields, and he said, 'Water your crops,not the crops of others. He also prohibited the selling of spoils of war before they are divided, and the consumption of the meat of domestic donkeys, as well as the consumption of any animals with fangs among the wild beasts.\""],[11096,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifted a camel in his presents to Abu Jahl, with a piece of silver attached to its head, to provoke the polytheists with it."],[11097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered as a sacrificial animal during the ‘Umrah of Hudaybiyyah the camel of Abu Jahl b. Hisham, which had a nose ring of gold — that is, the rein — and he did that only to enrage Quraysh."],[11098,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to go on a military expedition in the path of Allah.” He said, “Go to Syria, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has guaranteed Syria and its people for me. And keep to Ascalon in Syria, for when the mill turns in my nation, its people will be in goodness and well-being.”"],[11099,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.\" They said, \"What about those who cut their hair short?\" He said the same in the third time, \"And those who cut their hair short.\""],[11100,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever flees from two has indeed fled, but whoever flees from three has not fled.”"],[11101,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The forerunners are three: the forerunner to Moses was Joshua b. Nun, the forerunner to Jesus was the companion of Yasin, and the forerunner to Muhammad ﷺ was Ali b. Abi Talib.”"],[11102,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Fatimah to Ali, Fatimah said, “O Messenger of Allah, you have married me to a poor man who has nothing.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Are you not pleased, O Fatimah, that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, chose from the people of the earth two men, one of them your father and the other your husband?”"],[11103,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Ali to Fatimah, she said, “You have married me to a poor man who has no wealth.” He said to her, “Are you not pleased that Allah looked upon the earth and chose from it two men, making one of them your father and the other your husband?”"],[11104,"The Children of Israel, when one of them was killed intentionally, nothing was lawful for them except retaliation, but for you, blood money has been made lawful. Thus this one is commanded to pursue in a fair manner, and this one is commanded to pay with kindness. “That is a concession from your Lord.”"],[11105,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Ali to distribute his sacrificial animals, so he distributed them in portions. Then he came to him and said, “Distribute their saddle blankets and hides.”"],[11106,"You disobeyed your Lord, and your wife has become separated from you. So you did not fear Allah, that He might make a way out for you and provide for you from where you do not expect. And he recited: “O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their prescribed waiting period.”"],[11107,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When you pass by the meadows of Paradise, graze therein.” It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are the meadows of Paradise?” He said, “Gatherings of knowledge.”"],[11108,"The Prophet ﷺ would not fight a people until he had called them to Islam."],[11109,"The Jews used to say, “This world is seven thousand years, and we will be punished only one day in the Fire for every thousand years, so it will be only seven counted days.” Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed concerning that: “And they say, ‘The Fire will not touch us except for counted days’” up to His saying “abiding therein forever.”"],[11110,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade sleeping before the ʿIshāʾ prayer and engaging in conversation after it."],[11111,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people of Makkah, do not shorten the prayer for a distance of less than four barīd from Makkah to ʿUsfān.\""],[11112,"This verse was revealed concerning the Qadariyyah: {The Day they are dragged into the Fire on their faces: \"Taste the touch of Saqar. Indeed, We have created everything by measure.\"}"],[11113,"\"It was revealed concerning ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib. He had four dirhams, and he spent one at night, one by day, one secretly, and one openly.\""],[11114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Zamzam. We drew a bucket for him, and he drank, then he spat into the bucket, then we poured it back into Zamzam. Then he said: \"Were it not that you would be overcome, I would have drawn it with my own hand.\""],[11115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man will enter Paradise in which there will be no remaining people or rooms except they will say, 'Welcome, welcome to us.' Abu Bakr asked, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the reward of that man on that day?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, 'Indeed, you are that man, O Abu Bakr.'\""],[11116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam. In it is food that nourishes and a healing for illness. The worst water on the face of the earth is water in the valley of Barahūt, the remnant of Hadramawt, like the leg of a locust among creeping things. In the morning it flows abundantly, and by evening it has no moisture.\""],[11117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A habitual drinker of wine, an undutiful child, and one who constantly reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise.\""],[11118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In the last days there will come people whose faces are the faces of humans but whose hearts are the hearts of devils, like ravenous wolves. There is no mercy in their hearts. They shed blood and do not refrain from any evil. If you follow them they will deceive you; if you stay away from them they will backbite you; if they speak to you they will lie to you; if you entrust them they will betray you. Their young are arrogant, their youth are reckless, and their old do not enjoin good nor forbid evil. Seeking honor among them is humiliation, and seeking what is in their hands is poverty. The forbearing among them is led astray, and the one who enjoins good among them is accused. The believer among them is deemed weak, and the sinner among them is honored. The Sunnah among them is considered innovation, and innovation among them is considered Sunnah. At that time, their worst will be given power over them, and their best will supplicate but will not be answered.\""],[11119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A habitual drinker of wine, an undutiful child, and one who constantly reminds others of his favors will not enter Paradise.\" Ibn ʿAbbās said: This distressed me because believers commit sins, until I found that in the Book of Allah: regarding the undutiful child, {So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship?}; regarding the one who reminds of favors, {Do not invalidate your charities with reminders or injury}; and regarding wine, {Indeed, wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are only defilement} up to His saying {so avoid it}."],[11120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The angels rejoice at the departure of winter out of mercy for the hardship that befalls the poor believers.\""],[11121,"Al-Fadl and I ran ahead of the Prophet ﷺ, riding together on a donkey, while he was praying on the Day of ʿArafah, with no one between us and him to screen us from him."],[11122,"Muhammad ﷺ"],[11123,"He used to recite: “It is not for a prophet to be dishonest” [Quran 3:161]. “And how could it not be for him to be dishonest when he could be killed?” Allah said: “And they kill the prophets” [Quran 2:61]. “But the hypocrites accused the Prophet ﷺ of something,” so Allah revealed: “It is not for a prophet to be dishonest.”"],[11124,"“Whatever in the Quran is ‘qattala’ with a doubled letter, it is punishment; and whatever is ‘qatala’ with a single letter, it is mercy.”"],[11125,"About nabidh from earthen jars. Ibn ʿAbbās put his fingers in his ears and said: “May they be deaf if I have lied about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard him say: ‘All clay vessels are unlawful—white, red, black, and green.’”"],[11126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four things: about his life and how he spent it; about his body and how he wore it out; about his wealth and how he spent it and from where he earned it; and about love for us, the People of the House.”"],[11128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Perhaps you will remain after me until you meet a people who deny Allah’s decree and attribute sins to His servants. They derived their speech from Christianity. When that happens, disassociate yourselves from them before Allah.” Ibn ʿAbbās would raise his hands and say: “O Allah, I disassociate myself from them before You, as Your Prophet ﷺ commanded.”"],[11129,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The son of Adam has been commanded to prostrate on seven bones.”"],[11130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Iblis said to his Lord: “My Lord, Adam has been sent down, and I know that there will be a scripture and messengers. What are their scriptures and messengers?” He said: “Their messengers are the angels and the prophets among them, and their scriptures are the Torah, the Psalms, the Gospel, and the Criterion.” He said: “Then what is my scripture?” He said: “Your scripture is tattoo; your Quran is poetry; your messengers are soothsayers; your food is that over which Allah’s name is not mentioned; your drink is every intoxicant; your truth is lying; your house is the bathhouse; your traps are women; your muezzin is the flute; and your mosque is the markets.”"],[11131,"The history was in the year in which the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Medina and in which Abdullah Ibn Zubayr was born."],[11132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is given a gift while a group of people are with him, they are his partners in it.”"],[11133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever sees a gap in a row should fill it himself. If he does not, and someone passes by, let him step over his neck, for he has no sanctity.”"],[11134,"The Prophet ﷺ ruled by an oath and one witness."],[11135,"“The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dye with henna while in ihram and wear garments dyed with safflower while in ihram.”"],[11136,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its goodness appeared."],[11137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not sell fruit until its ripeness appears.”"],[11138,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ attended a funeral, gloom and deep thoughtfulness were seen upon him."],[11139,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at al-Uthāya, he was brought rose-henna, and he said: “It resembles the sweet basil of Paradise.”"],[11140,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by this verse: {And by the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness} (Q 91:7–8), he would stop and then say: “O Allah, grant my soul its righteousness; You are its Guardian and Master, and the best to purify it.”"],[11141,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him and without having killed a soul, he will meet Allah light of back (i.e., unburdened).”"],[11142,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Do not keep staring at lepers.”"],[11143,"The Prophet ﷺ consummated marriage with his maternal aunt Maymūna at Sarif, and she died at Sarif.” Al-Layth b. Saʿd said: “Zayn b. Shuʿayb was as he was named Zayn (i.e., a fine man).”"],[11144,"A man manumitted a slave of his, and the freedman died, so the Prophet ﷺ gave inheritance to the manumitter."],[11145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and ʿUmrah consecutively, for they eliminate sins just as the bellows eliminate the dross of iron.”"],[11146,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, a man fought in the path of Allah, seeking reward, until he was killed. Will he be in Paradise?” He said: “Yes.” When the man turned away, he called him back and said: “Jibrīl ﷺ came to me and said: ‘Unless he has a debt.’”"],[11147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Religion is sincere counsel.” It was said: “To whom, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “To Allah, to His Book, to His Prophet, to the leaders of the Muslims, and to their common people.”"],[11148,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fasts one day of Ramadan, seeking reward, his fast will be such that if all the people of the world were to gather from the time the world began until it ends and give him food and drink to the fullest, he would not seek from the people of Paradise any of that.”"],[11149,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj. May I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: \"Yes. Do you not think that if he owed a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would that not suffice him? For this is just like that.\""],[11150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Treat goats well, for they are a delicate asset and they are in Paradise. The wealth most beloved to Allah is sheep. And you should wear white, for Allah created Paradise white, so let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it. And the blood of a white sheep is greater in the sight of Allah than the blood of the two black ones.\""],[11151,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a fistula from which I constantly discharge. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When you perform ablution from your head to your feet, then no further ablution is required of you.\""],[11152,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Budayl b. Warqāʾ to Minā and he called out: \"These are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast them.\""],[11153,"I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to perform ablution, and he said: \"O Allah, give him understanding of the religion and teach him interpretation.\""],[11154,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years and died at the age of sixty-three."],[11155,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted a menstruating woman to depart before performing the farewell circumambulation if she had already performed it."],[11156,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by the grave of Prophet Moses ﷺ while he was praying at his grave."],[11157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a sword whose hilt was of silver and whose pommel was of silver, and it was called Dhū al-Faqār. He had a bow called al-Sadād. He had a quiver called al-Jumʿ. He had a coat of mail adorned with copper called Dhāt al-Fuḍūl. He had a spear called al-Nabʿāʾ. He had a shield called al-Dhaqan. He had a white buckler called al-Mūjiz. He had a black horse called al-Sakb. He had a saddle called al-Dāj. He had a gray mule called Duldul. He had a she-camel called al-Qaṣwāʾ. He had a donkey called Yaʿfūr. He had a carpet called al-Kurr. He had a short spear called al-Namir. He had a water-skin called al-Ṣādir. He had a mirror called al-Mudillah. He had scissors called al-Jāmiʿ. He had a staff of shawḥaṭ wood called al-Mushawwiq."],[11158,"Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh came to the Prophet ﷺ with a basket of fresh dates that he had brought from al-Ṭāʾif and handed it to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It removes the heaviness of the chest and clears the heart.\""],[11159,"Visiting the sick on the first day is a Sunnah, and after that it is voluntary."],[11160,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \"It was prescribed for them that ten should not flee from two hundred. Then it was lightened for them,\" and he recited: \"Now Allah has lightened [your burden] for you, and He knows that there is weakness among you\" (8:66). So it was prescribed \"that one hundred should not flee from two hundred.\""],[11161,"I was among those whom the Prophet ﷺ sent ahead from Muzdalifah to Minā with the women and children."],[11162,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿUkāẓ, Mijannah, and Dhū al-Majāz were markets in the Jāhiliyyah. When Islam came, they felt sinful [about trading there during Hajj], so Allah ﷻ sent down: {There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord} during the Hajj seasons."],[11163,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever sees a gap in a row, let him fill it with himself. If he does not do so, and someone passes by him, let him step on his neck, for he has no sanctity.\""],[11164,"\"All of them were killed at Badr by death or illness, and al-Ḥārith b. Qays, who was from the Hayāṭilah.\""],[11165,"From Abū Muḥammad al-Jazarī, who is Ḥamzah al-Naṣībī, from ʿAmr b. Dīnār, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever supports falsehood to thereby invalidate a truth has disowned the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. Whoever walks to the authority of Allah to humiliate it, Allah will humiliate him along with the disgrace He stores for him on the Day of Resurrection. The authority of Allah is the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet. Whoever is given authority over any matter of the Muslims and appoints over them a man while knowing that among them there is someone more deserving of it and more knowledgeable of the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger than him, has betrayed Allah, His Messenger, and all the believers. Whoever abandons the needs of the people, Allah will not look into his need until he fulfills their needs and gives them their due. Whoever consumes a dirham of ribā, it is like thirty-three acts of zinā. Whoever's flesh is nourished by unlawful gain, the Fire is more fitting for him.\""],[11166,"That he heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating a meaty bone, the muʾadhdhin came for the prayer, so he put it down and stood for prayer without touching water.\""],[11167,"Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"It is only a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alighted,\" meaning al-Abṭaḥ."],[11168,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only walked briskly in the ʿumrah because of the polytheists.\""],[11169,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"No one is given any authority except that well-being is spread out before him. If he accepts it, it is completed for him, but if he breaches it, there is opened for him that which he has no strength to bear.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: What does 'breaches it' mean? He said: \"He seeks out slips and private faults.\""],[11170,"We used to recognize the conclusion of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ [prayer] by his saying: \"Glory be to your Lord, the Lord of Might, above what they describe; and peace be upon the messengers; and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[11171,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the first fruits of the season, he would place them over his eyes and then say: \"O Allah, as You have fed us its first, feed us its last.\" Then he would order it to be given to the youngest child of his household."],[11172,"From two women who were stitching leather. One of them went out and claimed that her companion had struck her with an awl, while the other denied it. Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled: \"The oath is upon the defendant. If people were given what they claimed, men would claim the wealth of other men and their blood. But call her\" – so recite to her: {Indeed, those who purchase a small gain with the covenant of Allah and their oaths – those will have no share in the Hereafter}. He said: So I did that, and she confessed. That reached him, and he was pleased with it."],[11173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If people were given what they claimed, men would claim the wealth of other men and their blood, but the oath is upon the defendant.\""],[11174,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If people were given whatever they claimed, men would claim the wealth and lives of other people.”"],[11175,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to drink honey at Sawdah’s house, then he would enter upon ʿĀʾishah. She said: “I smell an odor from you.” Then he entered upon Ḥafṣah, and she said: “I smell an odor from you.” He said: “I think it is from a drink I had at Sawdah’s. By God, I will not drink it.” Then this verse was revealed: {O Prophet, why do you prohibit what God has made lawful for you?}"],[11176,"The dawn prayer was called, so I got up to pray the two rakʿahs before dawn. The Messenger of God ﷺ took my hand and pulled me, saying: “Will you pray dawn as four?”"],[11177,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “My community will drink wine in the end of time, and they will call it by another name.”"],[11178,"The Prophet ﷺ used to travel from Madinah to Makkah, fearing none but God, praying two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs."],[11179,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “How can a community be sanctified when the rights of its weak are not taken from its strong?”"],[11180,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “All of ʿArafah is a standing place, but keep away from the hollow of ʿUranah. And all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from the hollow of Muḥassir.”"],[11181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Two supplications are not veiled from God: the supplication of the oppressed, and a person’s supplication for their brother in his absence.”"],[11182,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed inside the Kaʿbah. Bilāl and al-Faḍl were at the door. Bilāl said: “He prostrated,” and al-Faḍl said: “He bowed.”"],[11183,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take it, O Banī Ṭalḥah, as a permanent, enduring trust; none but an oppressor will take it from you” – meaning the guardianship of the Kaʿbah."],[11184,"The Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[11185,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were invited to a trotter I would accept.”"],[11186,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed the people with his back toward the Kaaba, between the Black Stone and the door."],[11187,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is as if I am looking at a bow-legged black man, tearing it down stone by stone,” meaning the Kaaba."],[11188,"(The narrator Qutaibah said: This tradition has been narrated by Sa'id b. Abu Sa'id in my collection): The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: He who does not chant the Qur'an is not one of us. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1469)"],[11189,"“My mother and I were among those whom God excused.”"],[11190,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from the privy and was presented to him. They (the people) asked: Should we bring you water for ablution? He replied: I have been commanded to perform ablution when I get up for prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3760)"],[11191,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, will summon people on the Day of Resurrection by their names as a covering from Him upon His servants. But at the bridge (ṣirāṭ), God ﷻ will give every believing man a light and every believing woman a light and every hypocrite a light. When they are level upon the bridge, God will strip the light of the hypocrites, men and women. Then the hypocrites will say, ‘Wait for us so that we may take from your light,’ and the believers will say, ‘Our Lord, perfect for us our light.’ Then no one will remember anyone.”"],[11192,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: “O boy, preserve God and He will preserve you. Preserve God and you will find Him before you. Know God in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship. Know that what missed you was not going to befall you, and what befell you was not going to miss you. Know that creation, if they were to gather to give you something that God did not will to give you, they would have no power over it, or to turn away from you something that He willed to befall you, they would have no power over that. When you ask, ask God, and when you seek help, seek help from God. Know that victory comes with patience, relief with distress, and with hardship comes ease. Know that the pen has already run with what is to be.”"],[11193,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The partner is an intercessor, and the right of pre-emption (shufʿa) is in everything.”"],[11194,"Regarding His saying: “Until when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied” (12:110), he said: “They were human, so they weakened and thought that they had been given a false promise.” He recited: “Until the messenger says” (12:110)."],[11195,"ʿAbd al-Razzāq said—and I do not think that al-Thawrī did not inform us—from ʿUthmān b. al-Aswad, from Ibn Abī Mulayka, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill from Zamzam.”"],[11196,"It was said to Ibn ʿAbbās: “Muʿāwiya performed witr with one rakʿa.” He said: “Leave Muʿāwiya aside, for he was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11197,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God sends down every day one hundred and twenty mercies: sixty of them for those circumambulating, forty for those performing iʿtikāf around the House, and twenty of them for those looking at the House.”"],[11198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “My basin is a month’s journey; its corners are equal, its drinking vessels are as numerous as the stars of the sky. Its water is whiter than snow, sweeter than honey, and more fragrant than musk. Whoever drinks a single drink from it will never thirst after that, ever.”"],[11199,"Some of them said: “It is inherited magic.” Their opinion settled on it being inherited magic. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he grieved, covered his head, and wrapped himself. Then God sent down: “O you enveloped in garments, arise and warn, and magnify your Lord, and purify your garments, and shun idolatry, and do not grant favor to acquire more, and for your Lord be patient” (74:1–7)."],[11201,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"There is no day more virtuous than another in fasting except the month of Ramadan and the day of Ashura.\""],[11202,"\"I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ prefer any day over another except the day of Ashura.\""],[11203,"The Prophet ﷺ \"did not seek the superiority of any day over another after Ramadan except the day of Ashura.\""],[11204,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not fast any day seeking its superiority over another after Ramadan except the day of Ashura.\""],[11206,"The Prophet ﷺ \"performed ablution with one mudd of water and took the ritual bath with one sa' of water.\""],[11207,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"would sprinkle water on his family on the night of the twenty-third.\""],[11208,"\"I was among those whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led from the weak members of his family, from Muzdalifah to Mina.\""],[11209,"I heard Ibn Abbas say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me ahead among the weak ones or among the heavy baggage from Muzdalifah at night.\""],[11210,"He heard Ibn Abbas ؓ say: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, I saw myself last night in what a sleeper sees, as if I was praying near a tree, and as if I recited Surah al-Sajdah and prostrated, and I saw the tree as if it prostrated along with my prostration, and as if I heard it saying, 'O God, record for me thereby a reward with You, remove from me thereby a burden, make it for me a treasure with You, and accept it from me as You accepted it from Your servant Dawud.'\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So the Messenger of God ﷺ recited Surah al-Sajdah, and I heard him saying in his prostration the same as what the man reported from the words of the tree.\""],[11211,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while they were lending in dates for one year, two years, and three. He said, \"Whoever lends, let him lend in a known measure and a known weight for a known term.\""],[11212,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, Sufyan b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from ʿAbdullah b. Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah while they used to give advance payments for fruits for two and three years. He said: “Whoever gives an advance payment, let him give it in a known measure and a known weight, for a known term.”"],[11216,"“I travel, should I shorten the prayer during travel?” Ibn ʿAbbas ؓ said: “It is not shortening; rather it is its complete form and the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out secure, fearing none but Allah, and prayed two rakʿahs until he returned.”"],[11217,"“The Prophet ﷺ never fought a people until he called them (to Islam).”"],[11218,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fought a people except that he called them (to Islam).”"],[11226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever learns a branch of astrology has learned a branch of sorcery; the more he increases, the more he increases.\""],[11227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent his wives ahead from Jamʿ on the night before the crowding."],[11228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to send the families and the weak ahead to Mina from al-Muzdalifah."],[11229,"He informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to say that Al-Inakhah with Al-Muhasab is nothing. Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only waited for it until Aisha comes."],[11232,"A Bedouin came to him and asked for a drink, so he was given nabīdh to drink. He said: What is the matter with your brothers? They serve honey and milk, while you serve nabīdh? He said: It is not out of stinginess on our part, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for a drink, so we gave him nabīdh. He said: You have done well and been generous; so do likewise."],[11233,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him ahead from Muzdalifah among the weak members of his family."],[11234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[11235,"The Prophet ﷺ sent the weak members of his family ahead from Jamʿ at night."],[11236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did that only to show the polytheists his strength; so whoever wishes may do it, and whoever wishes may leave it—meaning raml."],[11237,"The Prophet ﷺ continued to say the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[11238,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I am the guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in its highest part, and a house in its lowest part for the one who gives up disputation while being in the right, gives up lying while joking, and improves his character toward people.”"],[11239,"I spent the night in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up during the night, loosened the water skin, performed wudu, then stood for prayer. I got up, performed wudu, then came and stood on his left. He took me by his right hand, turned me around from behind him, and placed me on his right, so I prayed with him."],[11240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Arafah with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him. The she-camel swerved with him while he raised his hands, not letting them go above his head. Then he continued in the same manner until Muzdalifah, with al-Fadl riding behind him. He did not stop reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrah."],[11241,"The Prophet ﷺ performed a single tawaf for both his Hajj and his Umrah."],[11243,"Do not go out on the day of Fitr until you have given the sadaqah and eaten something before going out."],[11244,"Ibn ‘Abbas said The Prophet ﷺ married Maimunah while he was in the sacred state(wearing ihram). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1844)"],[11245,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian, and the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"],[11246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.” Abu Muawiyah added in his narration: with me."],[11247,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who among you has begun this day fasting?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Who among you has visited a sick person?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Who among you has accompanied a funeral?” Abu Bakr said: “I have.” He said: “Whoever combines them in one day will enter Paradise.”"],[11248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House, said takbir in its corners, supplicated, then came out and prayed behind the Maqam."],[11249,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you wishes to give his brother his land, let him grant it to him as a gift, or let him let him cultivate it; and let him not give it to him for a third or a quarter.”"],[11250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11251,"A man complained to the Prophet ﷺ about celibacy and said, “Should I not castrate myself?” He said: “No. He who castrates or has himself castrated is not of us, but fast and let the hair of your body grow.”"],[11252,"Many a time I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while donkeys were braying in front of him."],[11253,"On the left of the Prophet ﷺ; then he took my hand and made me stand on his right, and he wiped over my head."],[11254,"That they should spend the nights in Makkah during the nights at Mina—meaning the family of Shaybah and the family of al-ʿAbbas."],[11255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought milk on the day of ʿArafah, and he drank it and gave it to the one on his right to drink."],[11256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the wailing woman and the woman who listens to her, and he said: “Women have no share in the funeral procession.”"],[11257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it will come on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire.”"],[11258,"Tamattuʿ in Hajj is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[11259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hating Banu Hashim and the Ansar is disbelief, and hating the Arabs is hypocrisy.”"],[11260,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: “We are the people, apart from other people.”"],[11261,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Black Stone is from the stones of Paradise, and there is nothing on earth from Paradise besides it. It was whiter than crystal, and were it not for the impurity of the pre-Islamic era that touched it, no afflicted person would touch it but that he would be healed.\""],[11262,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The thorns of the Haram are not to be cut, its game is not to be killed, its fresh herbage is not to be uprooted, and its lost property is not lawful to pick up except for one who announces it.\""],[11263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut in the Fajr prayer, supplicating against some people and for some people."],[11264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives a gift has more right to his gift as long as he is not recompensed for it. But if he takes back his gift, he is like one who vomits and then eats his own vomit.\""],[11265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no jalab in Islam.\""],[11266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to wipe over the leather socks until Allah took him."],[11267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting and in ihram, and he fainted. So he forbade people that day from a fasting person being cupped, out of dislike for weakness."],[11268,"From Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about semen that gets on a garment. He said: \"It is only like spittle or mucus; remove it from it with a piece of cloth or with idhkhir (a type of grass).\""],[11269,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah and his son went on Hajj on their camel and left me.\" He said: \"O Umm Sulaym, an Umrah in Ramadan suffices for a Hajj.\""],[11270,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who has not performed Hajj. Can I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"What do you think if your father had a debt, would you pay it off?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[11271,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the talbiyah for Umrah until he touched the Black Stone, and he recited the talbiyah for Hajj until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice."],[11272,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ went out from Madinah to Makkah when he conquered it, and that was in Ramadan while he was fasting. He fasted until he reached Qudayd, and it reached him that the people were suffering from thirst and hardship. So he called for water and drank, and he broke his fast. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke his fast."],[11273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine two prayers while traveling: Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[11274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"For a boy, two ʿaqiqahs; for a girl, one ʿaqiqah.\""],[11275,"\"He is Muhammad ﷺ. He drew near and came down to his Lord, exalted be He.\""],[11276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice two horned rams that were white with black markings. He would place his foot on their sides when he intended to slaughter them and say: \"In the name of Allah, from You and for You. O Allah, accept from Muhammad.\""],[11277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever grants a respite to a person in difficulty until he can pay, Allah will grant him respite for his sin until he repents.\""],[11278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Food on the wedding day for one day is a sunnah, food for two days is a virtue, and food for three days is showing off and seeking reputation.\""],[11279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Vehemence affects the best of my community.\""],[11280,"The Prophet ﷺ held gold and silk in his hand, moving them and saying, \"This is forbidden for the males of my Ummah.\""],[11281,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying sitting cross-legged with his buttons unfastened."],[11283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon ʿUmar while some of his companions were with him and said: \"Are you believers?\" They remained silent three times. Then ʿUmar said at the last of them: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And why is that?\" ʿUmar said: \"We hope for reward from Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Believers, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah.\""],[11284,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O people, seek medical treatment, for Allah has not created a disease except that He has created a cure for it except for death.\""],[11285,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Vinegar is an excellent condiment.\""],[11286,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Prophet ﷺ entered the Kaʿbah and there were six pillars inside. \"He stood at each pillar and supplicated, but he did not pray.\""],[11287,"And Ibn Abbas said, \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , went out on the day of Eid al-Fitr and performed two units of prayer, then he went to the women and Bilal was with him. He commanded them to give charity, and they began to throw it.\""],[11288,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade uncertain transactions.\""],[11289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no marriage except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, whether small or large.\""],[11291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution thoroughly."],[11292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the last ʿIsha prayer one night until the people slept, then woke, then slept, then woke. Then ʿUmar came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the prayer.\" So they prayed, and it was not mentioned that they performed ablution again."],[11294,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from bowing, he would say: \"O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever else You will after that.\""],[11295,"That you perform tawaf, and if it is easy, then touch the Black Stone. The stray one who had gone astray on the road to Makkah died missing. He said: Maʿmar b. Rashid and Salm b. Abi al-Dhayyal were lost and no trace of them was seen."],[11296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal on a night of wind and rain, and he called out: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[11297,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about someone who shaved before slaughtering, and he said: \"There is no harm.\""],[11298,"The Prophet ﷺ permitted the pilgrim in ihram to wear trousers if he cannot find a waist-wrapper, and leather socks if he cannot find sandals."],[11299,"This black woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I suffer from epileptic fits and I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah for me.\" He said: \"If you wish, be patient and Paradise will be yours, and if you wish, I will supplicate to Allah to heal you.\" She said, \"I will be patient,\" then said, \"But I become uncovered, so supplicate to Allah that I do not become uncovered.\" So he supplicated for her."],[11300,"I was among those who hurried in the baggage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of Muzdalifah."],[11301,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family ahead on the night of Muzdalifah and commanded them not to stone the Jamrah until the sun rose."],[11302,"The beginning of hastening (al-īḍāʿ) was only from the side of the desert people. They would stand at the edges of the people, having hung their bows and quivers. When they departed, they would rattle. The Messenger of God ﷺ was seen while the base of his she-camel's ear appeared to touch her withers, and he was saying: “O people, you must maintain calm. O people, you must maintain calm.”"],[11303,"“The īlāʾ of the people of the Jāhiliyyah was a year or two years. Then God set a time limit for īlāʾ. Whoever's īlāʾ is less than four months is not īlāʾ.” The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Saʿīd b. Manṣūr."],[11304,"“The Prophet of God ﷺ prayed with the people on the day of Fiṭr two rakʿahs without adhān or iqāmah. Then he delivered a sermon after the prayer. Then he took Bilāl by the hand and went to the women and preached to them. Then, after he had left them, he ordered Bilāl to go to them and order them to give charity.”"],[11305,"They waited for the prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque, and they slept. Then we woke up three times. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and prayed ʿIshāʾ, and he said: “Were it not that I would make it difficult for the people, I would command them to delay this prayer until this time.” We looked, and it was the middle of the night."],[11306,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ said, 'O sons of Abdul Muttalib, if you are given authority over this matter after me, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this house or praying at any hour they wish, whether during the day or night.'\""],[11307,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to send the baggage ahead at saḥar (the last part of the night). I was among those who were sent, meaning from Muzdalifah."],[11308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the best of the angels? Jibrīl ﷺ . And the best of the prophets is Ādam, and the best of women is Maryam bt. ʿImrān.”"],[11309,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say seven takbīrs over the people of Badr, and five takbīrs over Banū Hāshim. Then the last of his prayer was four takbīrs until he departed this world."],[11310,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Two qīrāṭs will be placed in his balance, each qīrāṭ like Mount Uḥud,” meaning for one who follows a funeral procession."],[11311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go out to some walls of the city when the day became hot, and it would be easy for him to perform purification there. If he had a need, he would fulfill it, otherwise he would perform ablution. When the sun disappeared from the horizon by the distance of a lance, he would stand up and pray four units of prayer without sitting in between, and then he would stand up and go to the mosque. Ibn Abbas said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer that you pray and we do not pray it?\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Whoever from my nation prays it, he has revived his night, during which the doors of the heavens are opened and supplication is answered.\""],[11312,"Al-ʿAbbās came to the Prophet ﷺ at a time when he did not usually come to him. It was said: “O Messenger of God, this is your uncle at the door.” He said: “Give him permission, for he has come for some matter.” When he entered upon him, he said: “What has brought you, O uncle, at this hour, and it is not your usual time when you come?” He said: “O son of my brother, I remembered the Jāhiliyyah and its ignorance, and the world seemed narrow to me despite its vastness. I said: Who will relieve me? And I knew that no one would relieve me except God, then you.” He said: “Praise be to God who put this in your heart. I wish Abū Ṭālib had taken his share, but God does what He wills.” He said: “Shall I grant you a gift?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I give you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Shall I grant you a gift?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “When there is an hour in which prayer is offered, not after ʿAṣr nor after sunrise, but between those, then perform your ablution thoroughly. Then stand before God and recite the Fātiḥah of the Book and a sūrah, if you wish make it from the beginning of the Mufaṣṣal. When you finish the sūrah, say: Subḥān Allāh, wa-l-ḥamdu li-llāh, wa lā ilāha illā llāh, wa-llāhu akbar fifteen times. Then when you bow, say that ten times. Then when you raise your head, say that ten times.”"],[11313,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was being cupped on Tuesday. I said: “You are being cupped on this day?” He said: “Yes. And whoever among you coincides with Tuesday, the night of the seventeenth of the month, let him not let it pass without being cupped. So be cupped.”"],[11314,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I did not pass by any group of angels except that they ordered me to perform cupping.”"],[11315,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, Iblīs has rebellious devils among the shayāṭīn. He says to them: ‘Go after the pilgrims and the mujāhidūn, and lead them astray from the path.’”"],[11316,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The key to prayer is purification, and its sanctification is the takbir, and its release is the taslim.”"],[11317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine two prayers during travel: Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha, while not pursuing an enemy nor being pursued by one."],[11318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you hear thunder, remember Allah, for it does not strike one who remembers.”"],[11319,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Wine is the mother of indecencies and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it may fall upon his mother, his maternal aunt, and his paternal aunt.”"],[11320,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Makkah to Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah when the sun had declined, and he prayed Zuhr, ʿAsr, Maghrib, and ʿIsha, then spent the night there until morning on the Day of ʿArafah. Then he went to ʿArafah and prayed Zuhr and ʿAsr when the sun had declined, then he proceeded to Muzdalifah and prayed Maghrib and ʿIsha there together, with no voluntary prayer between them."],[11321,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you has a nosebleed during his prayer, let him leave, wash the blood off, then repeat his ablution and restart his prayer.”"],[11322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the farewell tawaf at night, or by night."],[11323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning Marwah: “This is the place of sacrifice, and every ravine and path of Makkah is a place of sacrifice in the ʿUmrah.”"],[11324,"The angels did not fight alongside the Prophet ﷺ except on the Day of Badr, and on other occasions they were reinforcements. The Prophet ﷺ had only two horses with him: one belonging to al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad and the other to Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi."],[11325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not drink as a camel drinks; rather drink in two or three breaths, mention Allah’s name when you drink, and praise Allah when you finish.”"],[11326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed the shepherds to throw the pebbles at night."],[11327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked.”"],[11328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only walked briskly between al-Safa and al-Marwa to show the polytheists his strength."],[11329,"Al-Muhassab is not a ritual; it is merely a place where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped."],[11330,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymuna and said: \"Why did they not take its hide, tan it, and make use of it?\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion.\" He said: \"Only eating it is forbidden.\""],[11331,"A sheep died in the possession of one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not tan its hide and make it into a water skin?\""],[11332,"The Prophet ﷺ sent the weak members of his family from Muzdalifa at night."],[11333,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while fasting and in the state of ihram."],[11334,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while in the state of ihram."],[11335,"In his statement \"and upon those who are capable of it,\" he said \"they are required to do it.\" \"It is a ransom of feeding a poor person,\" \"only one.\" \"So whoever voluntarily does good,\" \"he increases the feeding of another poor person that is not obligated.\" \"So it is better for him.\" \"No one is exempted from this except for the elderly person who is not capable of fasting, or a sick person who knows that they will not recover.\""],[11336,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade al-ightiyal, then said: \"If it harmed anyone, it would harm the Persians and the Byzantines.\" Ibn Bukayr said: Al-ightiyal is for a man to have intercourse with his wife while she is breastfeeding."],[11337,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the Isha prayer one night, then came out with his head dripping water, and said: \"Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have loved for this prayer to be performed at this time.\""],[11338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the prayer one night until part of the night had passed. Umar came out and called to him: \"The prayer, O Messenger of Allah! The women and children have slept.\" He came out with water dripping from his side, wiping the water from his side, and saying: \"It is the time, were it not that I would burden my community.\""],[11339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever sells food should not sell it until they receive it in full.\" This was narrated by Qabeessah from Hammad ibn Salamah from Amr from Ata. It was also narrated by the companions of Hammad from Hammad from Amr from Tawoos. Similarly, it was narrated by the companions of Amr ibn Dinar, and this is the correct narration."],[11340,"A man bit the hand of another man during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and the latter pulled out his front tooth. The Prophet ﷺ declared it void. This is how Sa'id b. Amr narrated it from Sufyan from Amr from Ata from Ibn Abbas, and he erred in it. The companions of Ibn Uyayna narrated it from Ibn Uyayna from Amr from Ata from Safwan b. Ya'la b. Umayya from his father, and likewise the companions of Ata narrated it, which is the correct version."],[11341,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once."],[11342,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded that the plate be licked."],[11343,"That one should fight ten; but that was hard for them, so He removed that from them and it was reduced to fighting the enemy when they were twice as many."],[11344,"From Ibn Abbas: {It is not for a prophet to have captives} he recited until he reached {a great punishment}, meaning the spoils of Badr before He made them lawful for them, saying: \"Were it not that I do not punish those who disobey me until I have given them prior warning,\" {a great punishment would have touched you for what you took}."],[11345,"Al-Abbas used to say: \"By God, it was revealed concerning me when I told the Messenger of God ﷺ about my Islam and asked him to settle with me for the twenty uqiyyas that were found with me, but he refused to settle with me for them. So God gave me for the twenty uqiyyas twenty slaves, all of whom traded with my wealth in their hands, along with what I hope for of God's forgiveness.\""],[11346,"Ibn Abbas: The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed spoils among his companions that day, and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas received a goat, which he slaughtered for himself. When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood at ʿArafa, he ordered Rabiʿa b. Umayya b. Khalaf, who stood beneath the bridle of his she-camel and was a man with a loud voice, saying: \"Cry out, O people, do you know which month this is?\" So he cried out and the people said: \"The sacred month.\" Then he said: \"Cry out, do you know which land this is?\" They said: \"The sacred land.\" He said: \"Cry out, do you know which day this is?\" They said: \"The greater pilgrimage.\" He said: \"Cry out.\" So he said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ says: God ﷻ has made your blood and your property sacred, like the sanctity of this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours, and like the sanctity of this day of yours.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ completed his pilgrimage and said when he stood at ʿArafa: \"This is the standing place, and all of ʿArafa is a standing place.\" And he said when he stood at Quzah: \"This is the standing place, and all of Muzdalifa is a standing place.\""],[11347,"This verse abrogated her waiting period: she observes it in her family wherever she wishes, the words of God ﷻ {without being expelled}. ʿAtaʾ said: If she wishes, she observes the waiting period with her family, and if she wishes, she leaves, because of the words of God ﷻ {but if they leave, there is no blame upon you for what they do with themselves}."],[11348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Maymuna bt. al-Harith during that journey of his while he was in a state of ihram. The one who married him to her was al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Makkah for three days. Then Huwayṭib b. Abd al-Uzza b. Abi Qays b. Abd Wadd b. Naṣr b. Malik b. Ḥasal came to him on the third day with a group of Quraysh. Quraysh had entrusted him with expelling the Prophet ﷺ from Makkah. They said: \"Your term has ended, so leave us.\" He said to them: \"What harm would it do you if you left me to consummate the marriage among you and we prepared food for you, and you attended it?\" They said: \"We have no need of your food. Leave us.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ departed."],[11349,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray inside the House, but when he entered, he fell down in prostration, then raised his head and supplicated.\""],[11350,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed over the martyrs of Uhud, saying takbir over them nine times, nine times, then seven times, seven times, then four times, four times, until he met God ﷻ."],[11351,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"For a virgin, seven days; for a previously married woman, three days.\""],[11352,"Among what the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated with during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"O God, You hear my words and see my place and know my secret and my open affairs; nothing of my matter is hidden from You. I am the miserable, the poor, the seeker of help, the seeker of protection, the fearful, the apprehensive, the one who confesses and acknowledges his sin. I ask You as a humble beggar asks, and I beseech You as a sinful, abased person beseeches, and I call upon You as a fearful, blind person calls upon You, one whose neck is humbled before You, whose eyes overflow for You, whose body is humiliated, and whose nose is rubbed in the dust for You. O God, do not make me wretched in my supplication to You, and be always merciful to me, O Best of those who are asked and O Best of those who give.\""],[11353,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud: \"Greetings, good words, and prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\""],[11354,"He may circumambulate the House and walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa before going out to Arafah; and it is the sunnah of the people of Makkah to circumambulate the House and walk between al-Safa and al-Marwa after returning from Mina."],[11355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"All of Arafat is a standing place, but keep above the valley of ʿUrana; and all of Jamʿ (Muzdalifah) is a standing place, but keep above the valley of Muhassir.\""],[11356,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is old and cannot perform Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said: \"Would you pay off a debt if he owed it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then the debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being paid; perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[11357,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"An ʿUmrah in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj.\""],[11358,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why did you not make use of its skin?\" They said: \"It is carrion.\" He said: \"Tanning the hide purifies it.\""],[11359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, I asked Allah for three things for you: I asked Him to make your standing firm, to teach your ignorant, and to guide your astray; and I asked Him to make you generous, noble, and merciful. If a man were to stand between the Corner and the Maqam, pray, and fast, and then die hating the family of Muhammad ﷺ and being pleased with them, he would enter the Fire.\""],[11360,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of snakes while in ihram and within the Haram."],[11361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters the House, he leaves forgiven.\""],[11362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection it will be called out: Where are those who reached sixty?—that is the lifespan about which Allah ﷻ said: 'Did We not give you life long enough for whoever would remember to take heed?'\""],[11363,"While I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said to me: \"O boy, preserve Allah and He will preserve you; preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pens have been lifted and the pages have dried.\""],[11364,"O Messenger of Allah, I circumambulated the House before I threw the pebbles. He said: \"No harm.\""],[11365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When people differ, justice is with Mudar.\""],[11366,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The bad example is not for us: the one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[11367,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “When you sight the crescent of the month of Ramadan, fast; then when you sight it, break the fast.”"],[11368,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not see his Lord with his eyes; he saw Him only with his heart.”"],[11369,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, supported me with four ministers, chiefs.” We said, ‘O Messenger of God, who are these four?’ He said: “Two from the people of heaven and two from the people of earth.” I said, ‘Who are the two from the people of heaven?’ He said: “Gabriel and Michael.” We said, ‘Who are the two from the people of earth?’ He said: “Abu Bakr and ʿUmar.”"],[11370,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth, he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and God relents toward whoever repents.”"],[11371,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: The Messenger of God ﷺ delayed the night prayer one night until people slept and woke, and slept and woke. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab stood and said, ‘The prayer.’ The Messenger of God ﷺ came out with water dripping from his head and said: “Were it not that it would be difficult for my community, I would have commanded them to pray it at this time.”"],[11372,"I said to ʿAtaʾ: A man vowed to circumambulate on his knees seven times. He said: Ibn ʿAbbas said: “They were not commanded to circumambulate crawling, but let him circumambulate for his knee seven times and for his foot seven times.” I said: Did he not command him an expiation? He said: “No.”"],[11373,"We attended with Ibn ʿAbbas the funeral of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: When you lift her bier, do not jolt or shake it, and be gentle, for “the Messenger of God ﷺ had nine wives; he used to apportion for eight and not apportion for one.” ʿAtaʾ said: The one for whom he did not apportion was Safiyyah bt. Huyayy."],[11374,"That no one should go out on the day of Fitr until he has eaten, let him do so. He said: I have not failed to eat before going out since I heard that from Ibn ʿAbbas; I eat from the edge of the tariqah. I said: What is the tariqah? He said: Thin bread, or I drink milk, or nabidh, or water. I said: How do you interpret this? He said: I heard him, I think from the Prophet ﷺ, say: They used not to go out until the forenoon had extended, and they would say: We eat so that we are not rushed from the prayer. He said: “Sometimes I went out having tasted nothing but water.” Ibn ʿAbbas is the speaker."],[11375,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and ʿUmrah consecutively, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron.”"],[11376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A valid Hajj has no reward except Paradise.\""],[11377,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked one day at ʿUmar b. al-Khattab and smiled at him, then said: “O Ibn al-Khattab, do you know why I smiled at you?” He said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “God boasted to His angels on the night of ʿArafah about the people of ʿArafah in general, and He boasted about you in particular.”"],[11378,"O Messenger of God, I owe God a sacrificial animal, and I am wealthy, but I cannot find it. He said: “Slaughter a sheep.”"],[11379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will raise the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner on the Day of Resurrection, and they will have two eyes, a tongue, and two lips, testifying for whoever touched them with fidelity.”"],[11380,"The Prophet ﷺ applied perfume before entering the state of ihram."],[11381,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The child belongs to the marriage bed, and for the adulterer is the stone.”"],[11382,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his deputy over the prayer and other affairs of Madinah."],[11383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cover the faces of your dead, and do not imitate the Jews.”"],[11384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked during the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage about the ramy (stoning of the jamrah). He said: “Allah has prescribed the saʿy for you, so perform the saʿy.”"],[11385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever is afflicted with a calamity in his wealth or his body and conceals it without complaining to people, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him.”"],[11386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah created the Garden of ʿAdn, He created in it what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined. Then He said to it: ‘Speak.’ It said: ‘The believers have succeeded.’”"],[11387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing weapons in the lands of Islam or on the two Eid days unless in the presence of an enemy."],[11388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Love the Arabs for three reasons: because I am an Arab, the Quran is Arabic, and the speech of the people of Paradise is Arabic.”"],[11389,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite aloud “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” (In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."],[11390,"Ibn Abbas said: “You have in the Messenger of Allah an excellent example,” then he recited: “And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.”"],[11391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon that made the young women in their chambers hear it, and he said: \"O company of those who have submitted with their tongues but faith has not entered their hearts! Do not harm the believers, and do not pursue their faults, for whoever pursues the fault of his brother, Allah will pursue his fault, and whoever Allah pursues his fault, He will expose him, even if he is in the interior of his house.\""],[11392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Five are among the practices of the Messengers: modesty, forbearance, cupping, perfuming, and marriage.\""],[11393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Cupping is for pain in the molars and for drowsiness.\""],[11394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.\""],[11395,"to leave when she menstruates.\""],[11396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever provides food for a fasting person will receive the same reward.\""],[11397,"\"O Abu al-Abbas, what do you say about me?\" He said: \"What could I possibly say about you?\" He said: \"I am a clerk with a pen.\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The possessor of the pen will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in a coffin of fire, locked upon it with locks of fire. Then he will look at his pen: in what did he cause it to run? If he caused it to run in obedience to Allah and His good pleasure, the coffin will be unlocked from him, and if he caused it to run in disobedience to Allah, the coffin will plummet with him for seventy autumns, until the maker of the pen and the solderer of the inkpot.'\""],[11398,"about perfume and adornment.\""],[11399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of gaps,\" meaning in prayer."],[11400,"\"Beware of gaps,\" meaning in prayer, and he did not attribute it to the Prophet."],[11402,"that he heard Ibn Abbas say: \"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord, the Exalted, twice.\""],[11403,"that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him that she had been married off while she was unwilling, so she was separated from her husband. She had been previously married, and after that she married Abu Lubabah."],[11404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When my community wears light shoes with patches, men and women, and patches their sandals, Allah will disown them.\""],[11405,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade slaughtering sacrificial animals at night."],[11406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever keeps the left side of the mosque inhabited due to the fewness of its people, he will have two rewards.\""],[11407,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter.\""],[11408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one has a greater favor upon me than Abu Bakr ؓ. He supported me with his own self and his wealth, and he married his daughter to me.\""],[11409,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not drink wine. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is drunk. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not be alone with a woman who is not a mahram to him.\""],[11410,"The blacks were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Leave me alone regarding the blacks; indeed the black one is concerned only with his stomach and his private parts.\""],[11411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted for eighty horses on the day of Hunayn two shares each."],[11412,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever drinks a sip of wine, Allah will not accept from him his prayers and good deeds for three days. And whoever drinks a cup (of wine), Allah will not accept from him his prayers and good deeds for forty mornings. And the habitual drinker of wine, it is a right upon Allah that He gives him to drink from the river of Al-Khabal.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the river of Al-Khabal?\" He said, \"It is the pus of the people of Hellfire.\""],[11413,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to dye (his beard), he would take some oil and saffron, rub it between his hands, then rub it on his beard."],[11414,"ʿAtaʾ said: \"There is no divorce for one who does not possess the authority to dissolve his marriage, and no emancipation for one who does not own the slave,\" mentioning that from Ibn ʿAbbas and attributing it to the Prophet ﷺ."],[11415,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him perform a ritual bath.\""],[11416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding His saying {marked} [Quran 3:125]: \"It means 'distinguished.' The distinguishing mark of the angels on the day of Badr was black turbans, and on the day of Uhud red turbans.\""],[11417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no piece of land in which Allah is remembered with prayer except that it boasts over the lands surrounding it and rejoices at the remembrance of Allah, its extent reaching to the seven earths.\""],[11418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Harshness afflicts the best of my community.”"],[11419,"A man contracted chickenpox, so he isolated himself. He washed and then covered himself, but he passed away. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, and he said, \"They killed him. May Allah kill them! Wasn't the cure for skin diseases to ask for it to be rubbed on him?\""],[11420,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , \"Those who willingly accept Islam are from the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth, and those who do so reluctantly are those who are captured and brought to Islam from the prisoners of the nations, wearing chains and shackles. They will be led to Paradise while they are filled with hatred.\""],[11421,"The Prophet ﷺ cut off the access to the valleys and came with the sacrificial animal, but he was unable to perform tawaf around the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwa. As for you, the people of Mecca, delay your tawaf until you return."],[11422,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, sends down every day and night one hundred and twenty mercies. Upon this House descend sixty, for those circumambulating; forty, for those praying; and twenty, for those gazing at it.”"],[11423,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “God has an angel who, if he were told to swallow the seven heavens and the earths in a single morsel, he would do it. His glorification is: ‘Glory be to You, wherever You are.’”"],[11424,"From ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas and ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to teach us the istikhārah (prayer for seeking guidance) just as he taught us a sūrah from the Qur’an: “O God, I seek Your guidance by Your knowledge, and I seek Your decree by Your power. You have power and I have none, and You know and I do not know. You are the Knower of the unseen. O God, whatever You have decreed for me, make its outcome good.”"],[11425,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image of a statue, and the image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection in the Fire. The Most Merciful will say to them: ‘Give life to what you created,’ and they will remain in punishment until the image speaks, but it will not speak.”"],[11426,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A safeguard for the people of the earth from drowning is the rainbow, and a safeguard for the people of the earth from dissension is allegiance to Quraysh, the people of God. When any Arab tribe opposes them, they become a party of Iblīs.”"],[11427,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent to Waḥshī, the killer of Ḥamzah, inviting him to Islam. He sent back: “O Muḥammad, how can you call me to your religion while you claim that whoever kills, associates partners, or commits adultery meets a great punishment, with the torment doubled for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will remain in it disgraced—and I have done all that? Do you find any concession for me?” Then God, may He be glorified, revealed: “Except him who repents, believes, and works righteousness. For those, God will change their evil deeds into good deeds, and God is ever Forgiving, Merciful.” Waḥshī said: “O Muḥammad, this is a severe condition—‘except him who repents, believes, and works righteousness’—perhaps I cannot do this.” Then God revealed: “Indeed, God does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.” Waḥshī said: “O Muḥammad, I see there is a will after that, so I do not know whether I will be forgiven or not. Is there anything other than this?” Then God revealed: “O My servants who have transgressed against yourselves, do not despair of God’s mercy. Indeed, God forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.” Waḥshī said: “This is it,” and he came and embraced Islam. So the people said: “O Messenger of God, if we commit what Waḥshī committed [will we be forgiven too]?” He said: “This is for all Muslims generally.”"],[11428,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him, mercy overwhelms him. If he visits at the beginning of the day, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him until evening, and if he visits at the end of the day, seventy thousand angels ask forgiveness for him until morning.” It was said: “O Messenger of God, this is for the visitor, but what is for the sick person?” He said: “Multiples of this.”"],[11429,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take the blacks [as brothers], for three of them are among the leaders of the people of Paradise: Luqmān the wise, the Najāshī, and Bilāl the muezzin.” Abū al-Qāsim said: “He meant the Abyssinians.”"],[11430,"“Whoever arrives as a pilgrim and circumambulates the House and walks between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, his Hajj is completed and it becomes an ʿUmrah. Such is the practice of God and the practice of His Messenger ﷺ.”"],[11431,"From the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ."],[11432,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say: “We, the company of prophets, have been commanded to hasten our breaking the fast, to delay our predawn meal, and to place our right hands upon our left hands in prayer.”"],[11433,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “A gift to the ruler is embezzlement.”"],[11434,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, ‘There is no god but God.’ When they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is with God.”"],[11435,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Every inheritance that Islam found and was not divided is to be divided according to the Islamic division.”"],[11436,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded his wives and the weak among his family, and they were moved from Muzdalifah at night; then they went on until they threw the Jamrah of al-ʿAqabah.”"],[11437,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever enters the House enters into a good deed and exits from an evil deed, forgiven.”"],[11438,"That the Prophet ﷺ requested Suhail bin Amr to bring Zamzam water."],[11439,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God have mercy on those who shave.” They said, “And those who shorten, O Messenger of God?” He said, after three times: “And those who shorten.”"],[11440,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ came with the sacrificial animal and circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah before standing at ʿArafah.” As for you, O people of Makkah, delay your circumambulation until you return."],[11441,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is invalid; her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated the marriage with her, she is entitled to the dower for what he made lawful of her private part. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.”"],[11442,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, ʿUmar b. Qays narrated to us, from ʿAtaʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Kill the gecko, even if it is inside the Kaʿbah.”"],[11443,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, ʿUmar b. Qays narrated to us, from ʿAtaʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbas, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever reaches ʿArafah before dawn has caught the Hajj.”"],[11444,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The best rows for men are the first ones, and the worst are the last. The best rows for women are the last ones, and the worst are the first.”"],[11445,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Wine is the mother of abominations and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it may commit incest with his mother, his maternal aunt, or his paternal aunt.”"],[11446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his wives and the weak members of his family when they departed from Muzdalifah to leave at night and then continue until they passed Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[11447,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was in ihram because of a pain he had, and he used the siwak while he was in ihram."],[11449,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died from the meat which a Jewish woman had poisoned for him, his aorta was severed by the poison at the beginning of the year, and he would say: “I have not ceased to feel pain from it.”"],[11450,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Saad ibn Abi Waqqas a piece of meat from a goat and ordered him to sacrifice it."],[11451,"Some Muslims were with the polytheists and they swelled the ranks of the polytheists. An arrow would come and strike one of them and kill him, or he would be struck and killed. So God ﷻ revealed concerning them: {Indeed, those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves – they say, “In what condition were you?” They say, “We were oppressed in the land.”} – the verse."],[11453,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were to stone anyone without evidence, I would stone so-and-so, for suspicion has appeared in her appearance, her speech, and those who enter upon her.”"],[11454,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate a shoulder in the house of Maymunah bt. al-Harith, then he went out to the prayer and did not perform wudu."],[11455,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever says, ‘May God reward Muhammad on our behalf as he deserves,’ exhausts seventy scribes for a thousand mornings.”"],[11456,"The Prophet ﷺ changed the two garments of ihram at al-Tanʿim when he entered Makkah."],[11457,"The Messenger of God ﷺ assigned shares among his wives for a cow on the occasion of the sacrifice."],[11458,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11459,"The wife of Thabit b. Qays obtained a divorce, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to observe a waiting period of one menstrual period."],[11460,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Menstrual bleeding has spurts, and the blood of menstruation has an odor unlike anything else. When the menstrual period has ended, one of you should perform ghusl and then wash away the blood.”"],[11461,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was placed in his grave, Shuqran, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, took a velvet cloth that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to wear and buried it with him in the grave. He said, “No one will wear it after the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[11462,"Those who went down into the grave of the Messenger of God ﷺ were Ali, al-Fadl and Qutham the two sons of al-Abbas, and Shuqran the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Aws b. Khawli said to Ali ؓ, “O Ali, I adjure you by God concerning our share of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said, “Come down with the people.” So he went down, and they were five."],[11463,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would deliver two sermons on Friday while standing, sitting between them."],[11464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would deliver the sermon on Friday, on the day of Fitr, and on the day of Adha from the minbar. When the mu'adhdhin fell silent on Friday, he would stand and deliver the sermon."],[11465,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any female slave who bears a child to her master is free after his death.”"],[11466,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying in a single garment, wrapped in it, using its extra part to guard against the heat of the ground."],[11467,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would pray in a single garment, using its extra part to guard against the heat and cold of the ground."],[11468,"Concerning the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. We said, “Yes.” He said, “When the sun declined from its meridian while he was at his home, he would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting. If it had not declined while he was at his home, he would travel until it was time for Asr, then dismount and combine Zuhr and Asr. When Maghrib became due while he was at his home, he would combine it with Isha. If it had not become due while he was at his home, he would ride until Isha became due, then dismount and combine them.” Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn al-Miqdam said to me, “We have not heard this from Ibn Jurayj, and no one but you has brought it.”"],[11469,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey and set out when the sun declined, he would combine Zuhr and Asr. If he set out before that, he would combine them at the time of Asr."],[11471,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to mount before the sun declined, he would mount and delay Zuhr until he combined it with Asr. When he wanted to mount after the sun had declined, he would combine Zuhr and Asr before mounting. When he wanted to mount at the time of Maghrib, he would pray Maghrib and Isha before mounting. When he wanted to mount before the time of Maghrib, he would delay Maghrib until he combined it with Isha."],[11473,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lot, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done.”"],[11474,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would encourage night prayer, to the extent that he said, “Even if it is one rak'ah.” Then he went out for the prayer, and there was a man praying while the prayer was being established. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two prayers together?”"],[11476,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded the night prayer and encouraged it until he said: “Hold fast to the night prayer, even if it be one rakʿah.” And the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and found a man praying after the prayer had been established. And he also said: “Will you not desist? Two prayers together?”"],[11477,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: “O God, grant Ibn ʿAbbās wisdom and teach him the interpretation.”"],[11478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon and said, \"Indeed, Allah has given everyone their rights. Know that Allah has prescribed obligations, established practices, set limits, made certain things permissible and others forbidden, and has ordained the religion, making it easy, lenient, and comprehensive, and not burdensome. Know that there is no faith for those who do not have trustworthiness, and no religion for those who do not have covenants. Whoever breaks his promise will not receive my intercession, and he will not have access to my pond. Know that Allah has only allowed killing in three cases: a person who turns back from his faith, a married person who commits adultery, and one who kills another person, and he shall be killed in return. Have I conveyed the message?\""],[11479,"When the wind blew, the Prophet ﷺ would face it, kneel down, stretch out his hands, and say: “O God, I ask You for the good of this wind and the good of what it was sent with, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was sent with. O God, make it a mercy and do not make it a punishment. O God, make it winds and do not make it a wind.”"],[11480,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever goes to the authority of God on earth to humiliate him, God will humiliate his neck on the Day of Resurrection, along with what He stores up for him in the Hereafter.” Muslim added: “And the authority of God is the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11481,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to those who measure and weigh: “You have been put in charge of a matter in which the previous nations perished.”"],[11482,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Satan sends the strongest and most powerful of his companions against the one who does good with his wealth.”"],[11483,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Abū Dharr: “Which of the bonds of faith, I think he said, is most firm?” He said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Loyalty for the sake of God, enmity for the sake of God, love for the sake of God, and hatred for the sake of God.”"],[11484,"“Whoever drinks a drink that removes from him the intellect that he was given has come to one of the doors of major sins.”"],[11485,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever supports falsehood in order to defeat truth with his falsehood, the protection of God and the protection of His Messenger ﷺ are absolved from him.”"],[11486,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever combines two prayers without an excuse has come to one of the doors of major sins.”"],[11487,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said: “Whoever gives testimony by which the wealth of a Muslim man is made lawful to be taken or blood is shed, he has made the Fire obligatory upon himself.”"],[11488,"Narrated Ibn Abbas: The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no Muslim who takes care of an orphan between two Muslims, providing him with food and drink, except that he will enter Paradise immediately, except for the one who commits a sin that cannot be forgiven. And whoever takes care of my two dependents (i.e., his daughters), and treats them well, then he will enter Paradise.\" It was said, \"And who are his two dependents?\" He replied, \"His two eyes.\" And it was also narrated, \"And whoever takes care of three daughters, supports them, and treats them well, Allah will admit him into Paradise.\" Then a man from the Bedouins said, \"And what about two?\" He (Ibn Abbas) said, \"Two as well.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"This is the best of the hadiths, and it contains jewels and pearls.\""],[11489,"Nawfal b. al-Ḥārith sent his two sons to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to them: “Go to your uncle; perhaps he will use you for the ṣadaqāt and you may obtain something with which to marry.” They met ʿAlī, who said: “Where are you heading?” They told him of their need, and he said to them: “Go back.” So they went back. When evening came, he ordered them to go to the Prophet of God ﷺ. When they reached the door and asked permission, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: “Let down your curtain; my two cousins are coming in to me.” They told the Prophet of God ﷺ their need, and the Prophet of God ﷺ said to them: “Nothing of the ṣadaqāt is lawful for you, the people of the household, not even the water in which hands have been washed. In the fifth of the fifth there is what will suffice you, or be enough for you.”"],[11490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No flesh that grew from ill-gotten gain will enter Paradise.”"],[11491,"“The recitation of the Messenger of God ﷺ was loud enough for whoever was in the chamber to hear.”"],[11492,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “May God curse whoever takes as allies other than his true patrons. May God curse whoever alters the boundary markers of the land. May God curse whoever leads a blind man away from the road. May God curse whoever curses his parents. May God curse whoever slaughters for other than God. May God curse whoever has intercourse with an animal. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot. May God curse whoever does the deed of the people of Lot.”"],[11493,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from ʿAmr b. Abi ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbas, that a man clung to a debtor of his for ten dinars and said: “By God, I have no payment to give you today.” He said: “By God, I will not part from you until you pay or bring a guarantor who will pay on your behalf.” He said: “By God, I have no payment and I cannot find anyone to carry it for me.” So he dragged him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, this man clung to me, and I asked him to wait one month, but he refused unless I pay him or bring him a guarantor. I said: By God, I cannot find a guarantor and I have no payment today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will you not give him respite except for one month?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then I will carry it on your behalf.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ took it upon himself. The man went and brought him the amount he had promised. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “Where did you get this gold?” He said: “From a mine.” He said: “Go, for we have no need of it, and there is no good in it.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ paid it on his behalf."],[11494,"That I should bathe, and whoever does not bathe is not obligated, and I shall tell you how this is: The people were hard-pressed, wearing wool and working on their backs. Their mosque was narrow, and the roof was only a bower. The Messenger of God ﷺ went out one hot day and had sweated in that wool until odors arose, and they harmed one another. The Prophet ﷺ noticed those odors, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O people, when this day comes, bathe, and let each of you apply the best oil and perfume he can find.”"],[11495,"“Twenty men from the clients fought at Badr alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[11496,"“Drinkers were beaten in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ with hands, sandals, and sticks.”"],[11497,"On the day of Hunayn, the garment of the Messenger of God ﷺ caught on a tree while the people were gathered around him asking him for spoils. The Prophet ﷺ thought they had seized his cloak and said: “Let go of my cloak. Do you want me to be miserly? By God, if God were to give you spoils as numerous as the trees of Tihamah in livestock, I would distribute them among you, and you would not find me miserly, cowardly, or lying.” They said: “It was only a samurah tree that caught his clothes,” so they freed him."],[11498,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him in the mosque, then left. He stood, spread his legs, and urinated. The people rushed at him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not interrupt the man’s urination.” Then he said: “Are you not a Muslim?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “What made you urinate in our mosque?” He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I thought it was just one of the open grounds, so I urinated in it.” The Prophet ﷺ ordered a bucket of water to be poured over his urine."],[11499,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever cheats us is not one of us, and whoever shoots at us at night is not one of us.”"],[11500,"The Messenger of God ﷺ walked with them to Baqiʿ al-Gharqad, then sent them off and said: “Go in the name of God. O God, help them.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ returned to his house — meaning regarding the killing of Ibn al-Ashraf."],[11502,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a man who imagines during his prayer that he has broken his ablution when he has not. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Satan comes to one of you while he is praying until he opens his anus, making him imagine that he has broken his ablution when he has not. If one of you experiences that, he should not leave until he hears its sound with his ear or smells its odor with his nose.”"],[11503,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a woman with irregular bleeding, and he said, \"That is a kick from Satan in her womb.\""],[11504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever brings [a horse] to the race on the day of betting is not one of us.\""],[11505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would glance to the right and left during prayer without turning his neck behind his back."],[11506,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said, \"O young man, shall I teach you something through which Allah will benefit you?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Preserve Allah, and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah, and you will find Him before you. Become acquainted with Allah in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship. When you ask, ask Allah. When you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pen has dried concerning what will be on the Day of Resurrection. If all creation strove to benefit you with something that Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to, and if all creation strove to harm you with something that Allah has not decreed upon you, they would not be able to.\""],[11507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent some sheep to Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas to distribute among his companions, and they were performing tamattuʿ. There remained a billy goat, so Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas sacrificed it for his tamattuʿ."],[11508,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that when he would dispatch his armies he would say, \"Go forth in the name of Allah, fighting in the path of Allah those who disbelieve in Allah. Do not transgress, do not mutilate, do not kill children or those in monasteries.\""],[11509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them, for all ailments and for fever, this supplication: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Great. I seek refuge in Allah, the Magnificent, from the evil of every throbbing vein and from the evil of the heat of the Fire.\""],[11510,"\"No prophet has ever had a wet dream; rather, wet dreams are from Satan.\""],[11511,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever has sexual intercourse with a woman forbidden to him by close kinship, kill him.\""],[11512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If a dog laps from a vessel, it is to be washed seven times.\""],[11513,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the one who makes a woman lawful for her previous husband. He said, \"There is no marriage except a marriage of desire, not a marriage of deception, nor of one who mocks the Book of Allah; and the one who has not tasted the small amount of sweetness [of intercourse] has not [validly married].\""],[11514,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever has sexual intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill the animal. Whoever has sexual intercourse with a man, kill him,\" meaning the act of the people of Lot."],[11515,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Kill the doer and the one it is done to: the act of the people of Lut, and the one who comes to an animal, and the one who comes to a woman within the prohibited degrees.”"],[11516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All of Arafah is a standing place, and move up from the mountain pass of Safah.”"],[11517,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is more superior?\" He said, \"A gentle and lenient Hanifiyyah\"."],[11518,"Ibn Abbas asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Which religion is more beloved to Allah?\" He replied, \"The gentle Hanifiyyah religion.\""],[11519,"The verses in al-Ma'idah, {So judge between them with justice; indeed, Allah loves those who act justly}, were revealed concerning blood money among Banu Qurayzah and Banu al-Nadir. That is because the tribe of Banu al-Nadir had a higher status, so they used to pay the full blood money, while Banu Qurayzah used to pay half the blood money. They brought their dispute about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah revealed that concerning them. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them adhere to the truth in that matter and made the blood money equal."],[11520,"This verse {And do not pray loudly, nor too softly, but seek a way between that} was revealed because of those people. He said: “Do not pray loudly, lest they disperse from you, nor too softly, so that one who loves to hear it by eavesdropping without them may not hear it, perhaps they will call to some of what they hear and benefit from it.”"],[11521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his daughter Zaynab to her husband based on her first marriage, and he did not introduce anything new."],[11522,"“There is no harm and no reciprocation of harm.”"],[11523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a horned, large-eyed, virile ram."],[11524,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “A believer does not steal from the spoils.”"],[11525,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered the Friday sermon standing."],[11526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man says to another man, ‘O effeminate one,’ then flog him with twenty lashes. And if a man says to another man, ‘O Jew,’ then flog him with twenty lashes.”"],[11527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of unborn fetuses in the womb, the sale of semen, and the sale of a fetus that is itself pregnant."],[11528,"The pilgrim in ihram is given a concession to kill the snake, the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, and the biting dog."],[11529,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on the two Eids before the sermon."],[11531,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , sought the permission of the Quraysh regarding Al-Atirah. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we engage in Al-Atirah during the month of Rajab.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said to them, \"Engage in Al-Atirah as it was practiced during the time of ignorance (pre-Islamic era), but whoever among you desires to sacrifice for the sake of Allah, eat from it and give charity, then let them do so.\" Their practice of Al-Atirah was that they would slaughter animals and then rub the blood on the heads of their idols."],[11532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a call during the days of Mina, saying: \"Do not fast during these days, as they are days of eating, drinking, and sexual relations.\""],[11533,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The south wind does not stir a pool of rain in a valley but that it causes it to flow.\""],[11534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wear his ring on his right hand."],[11535,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honorable practice for women.\""],[11537,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting."],[11538,"Amr b. al-As ؓ led the people in prayer while he was junub. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and asked him about that. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I feared that the cold would kill me, and Allah ﷻ has said: {And do not kill yourselves. Indeed, Allah is ever Merciful to you}.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent about him."],[11539,"To a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Jew.\" The Prophet ﷺ had him flogged with twenty lashes."],[11540,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no sarurah in Islam.\""],[11541,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Provision is mount and riding camel.\""],[11542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fix a hadd for wine. Ibn Abbas said: A man drank an intoxicant and was found disgracing himself in a pit, so he was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he was opposite the house of al-Abbas, he slipped away and entered al-Abbas, who embraced him. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he laughed and said: \"Did he do that?\" And he did not ask about him."],[11543,"Ibn Abbas said: When the illness of Abdullah b. Ubayy in which he died occurred, the Prophet ﷺ came to him and they spoke words between them. Abdullah said: \"I have understood what you say. Grant me a favor: shroud me in your shirt and pray over me.\" So the Prophet ﷺ shrouded him in that shirt of his and prayed over him. Ibn Abbas said: And Allah knows best what kind of prayer it was. Muhammad ﷺ never deceived any person."],[11544,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I declared zihar upon my wife and then had intercourse with her before making expiation.” He said, “What led you to do that?” He said, “I saw her lower leg in the moonlight, and I fell upon her.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Keep away from her until you make expiation.”"],[11545,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ having declared zihar upon his wife and then had intercourse with her. He said, “O Messenger of God, I declared zihar upon my wife and then had intercourse with her before making expiation.” He said, “What led you to do that, may God have mercy on you?” He said, “I saw her anklet in the moonlight.” He said, “Do not approach her until you do what God ﷻ has commanded you.”"],[11546,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My mother died without performing Hajj and without leaving a will. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?” He said, “Tell me, if your mother had a debt and you paid it off?”"],[11547,"While Umm Salamah was one night lying beside the Messenger of God ﷺ, she got up as if she were concealing herself. He said, “What is the matter with you? Have you given birth?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “No harm. Perform your ablution and return to your place.”"],[11548,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Let the best among you give the call to prayer, and let your reciters lead you in prayer.”"],[11549,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ and ʿAʾishah ؓ used to bathe from a single vessel, and they would contend over the water.”"],[11550,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no contagion.” A Bedouin said, “O Messenger of God, we take a mangy sheep and cast it among the flock, and then the flock becomes mangy.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Bedouin, who made the first one mangy?”"],[11551,"He said, “There is no recitation in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers except the Opening of the Book.” Ibn ʿAbbas said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to recite, and the Messenger of God ﷺ indeed conveyed what was sent down to him from the messages of his Lord.”"],[11552,"A woman used to pick up dirt from the mosque, and she died. The Prophet ﷺ was not informed of her burial, so he said, “When one of you dies, inform me.” Then he prayed over her and said, “I saw her in Paradise because she used to pick up dirt from the mosque.”"],[11553,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When a parent looks at his child and it pleases him, the child has the reward of freeing a soul.” It was said, “O Messenger of God, what if he looks three hundred and sixty times?” He said, “God is greater.”"],[11554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The mother of a child is free, even if it is a miscarriage.”"],[11555,"“Indeed God ﷻ favored Muhammad over the inhabitants of the heavens and over the inhabitants of the earth.” A man said to him, “O Abu ʿAbbas, what is his favor over the inhabitants of the heavens?” He said, “God ﷻ says to the inhabitants of the heavens, {And whoever of them says, ‘I am a god besides Him,’ that one We shall recompense with Hell. Thus do We recompense the wrongdoers.} And God ﷻ said to Muhammad ﷺ, {Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that God may forgive you your past and future sins.} — the verse. It was said to him, “O Abu ʿAbbas, what is his favor over the prophets?” He said, “God ﷻ says, {And We did not send any messenger except with the tongue of his people.} And God ﷻ said to Muhammad ﷺ, {And We have not sent you except as a bringer of good tidings and a warner to all mankind.} So God sent him to humans and jinn.”"],[11556,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers, and he did not command us, though he had conveyed [the message]."],[11557,"I was at the side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day the sun eclipsed, and I did not hear him recite."],[11558,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood for a long while, then bowed for a long while, then stood for a long while, then bowed for a long while, then prostrated, then repeated the same."],[11559,"When this verse was revealed: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}, Persia sent to Quraysh: 'Dispute with Muhammad and say to him: What you slaughter with your own hand using a knife is lawful, but what Allah slaughters with a sword of gold is unlawful.' Then this verse was revealed: {And indeed the devils inspire their allies to dispute with you}. He said: 'The devils are from Persia and their allies are from Quraysh.'"],[11560,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: Allah ﷻ said: 'Whoever knows that I have power to forgive sins, I forgive him and do not care, as long as he does not associate anything with Me.'"],[11561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I would love for it to be in the heart of every person of my Ummah,' meaning Tabāraka alladhī bi-yadihi al-mulk."],[11562,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever's religion differs from the religion of the Muslims, strike his neck.' And he said: 'When he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, there is no way against him unless he commits something for which his prescribed punishment is carried out.'"],[11563,"One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ died. Ishaq said: I think he named her Safiyyah bt. Huyayy in Madinah. So I went to Ibn Abbas and informed him, and he prostrated. I said to him: 'Do you prostrate when the sun has not yet risen?' Ibn Abbas said: 'May you have no mother! Do you not know that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"When you see a sign, prostrate\"? And what sign is greater than the Mothers of the Believers departing from among us while we are still alive?'"],[11564,"\"Indeed, Muhammad ﷺ has seen his Lord.\" Ikrimah said, \"O Abu Abbas, does Allah not say: 'Vision perceives Him not, but He perceives [all] vision'?\" Ibn Abbas replied, \"I swear by your mother, that is only when He is in a manner that cannot be comprehended by sight.\""],[11565,"The spear was planted in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and he prayed toward it while women on camels passed beyond it."],[11566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every bond and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my bond and lineage.'"],[11567,"The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Abbas: 'O my uncle, shall I not teach you? Shall I not grant you? Shall I not tell you? Shall I not do for you ten qualities which, if you do them, Allah will forgive your sins: the first of them and the last, the old and the new, the secret and the open, the small and the great, the erroneous and the deliberate. You should pray four rakʿahs, reciting in each rakʿah the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation in the first rakʿah, say while standing: \"Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great\" fifteen times. Then bow and say it ten times while bowing. Then raise your head and say it ten times while standing. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times while sitting. Then prostrate and say it ten times. Then raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five. You do that in four rakʿahs. If your sins were like the foam of the sea or the sand of ʿAlij, Allah would forgive them for you.'"],[11568,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The fornicator does not commit fornication while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does one plunder a valuable plunder while he is a believer.'"],[11569,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed on a carpet."],[11570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Seek help through the midday nap for standing in prayer at night, and through eating the pre-dawn meal for fasting during the day.\""],[11571,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not come to women at night,\" meaning when one of you returns from a journey, he should not come to his wife except during the day. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey, and two men went ahead after the statement of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they came to their wives, and each one found a man with his wife."],[11572,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood.\""],[11573,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The death of a stranger is martyrdom.\""],[11574,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs: the ʿumrah of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, the ʿumrah of al-Qaḍāʾ the following year, his third ʿumrah from al-Jiʿrānah, and his fourth ʿumrah which was with his ḥajj."],[11575,"\"O Messenger of God, my mother died without making a will. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[11576,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ that his mother had died, \"Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I have a garden of palms, and I call you as witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf.\" Rawḥ said: Al-makhrafah is palm trees."],[11577,"About one [group], they reached al-Rawḥāʾ and said, \"You did not kill Muḥammad, nor did you mount the maidens with full breasts behind you. Evil is what you did.\" That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called the people to arms, and they responded until they reached Ḥamrāʾ al-Asad or Biʾr Abī ʿUyaynah. Then God, blessed and exalted, revealed: {Those who responded to God and the Messenger after the wound had befallen them}. Abū Sufyān had said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Your appointment is the season of Badr, where you killed our companions.\" So as for the coward, he turned back, and as for the brave one, he took up the equipment of fighting and trade. They came to him and found no one there, and they engaged in trading. Then God, blessed and exalted, revealed: {So they returned with favor from God and bounty, no harm having touched them}."],[11578,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Its thorny trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be startled, its fresh herbage shall not be cut, and its lost property is not lawful except to one who announces it.\" Al-ʿAbbās said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\" He said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\""],[11579,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God has made Makkah sacred, and it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be lawful for anyone after me. It was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day, then it is sacred by God's sanctity. Its trees shall not be cut, its game shall not be startled, and its fresh herbage shall not be cut.\" Al-ʿAbbās said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\" He said, \"Except for al-idhkhir.\""],[11580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God's anger is severe against the one whom the Messenger of God ﷺ has killed, and against the one who made the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ bleed.\""],[11581,"Ali paid Fatimah's mahr with an iron coat of mail."],[11582,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever listens to a people’s conversation while they dislike it will have molten lead poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever pretends to have seen a dream that he did not see will be charged with tying a knot between two grains of barley.”"],[11583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked a man, “Where did you stay?” He said, “With so-and-so (a woman).” He said, “Did she close her door on you?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that."],[11584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you stay with so-and-so and enter upon her?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that."],[11585,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “I marvel at the patience and generosity of my brother Yusuf, may Allah forgive him. When they sent to him to ask about the dream, had I been in his place I would not have done so until I came out. And I marvel at his patience and generosity, may Allah forgive him: he was summoned to come out, but he did not come out until he told them his excuse. Had I been in his place I would have hurried to the door. Were it not for the word, he would not have stayed in prison so long when he sought deliverance from other than Allah, in His saying: {Mention me in the presence of your lord}.”"],[11586,"In His saying {And We appointed not the vision which We showed thee but as a trial for mankind}, He said, \"It is a vision that the Prophet ﷺ saw on the night of his ascension, and it is not a dream.\""],[11587,"The moon was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so they said: “The moon has been bewitched.” Then the verse was revealed: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split} up to His saying {continuing}."],[11589,"Ali entered upon Fatimah on the day of Uhud and said: “Take this sword, it is not blameworthy.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “If you fought well, Sahl b. Hunayf and Abu Dujanah Simak b. Kharashah also fought well.”"],[11590,"Huyayy b. Akhtab and Kaʿb b. al-Ashraf came to Makkah to Quraysh and made a pact with them to fight the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said to them: “You are the people of ancient knowledge and the people of the Book, so tell us about us and about Muhammad.” They said: “What are you and what is Muhammad?” They said: “We slaughter the humped camels, give milk to drink mixed with water, free the captives, give water to the pilgrims, and maintain ties of kinship.” They said: “And what is Muhammad?” They said: “A solitary man who cut off our ties of kinship, and the thieves of the pilgrims, the Banu Ghifar, followed him.” They said: “Rather, you are better than him and more guided in the path.” Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed: {Have you not seen those who were given a portion of the Book, believing in jibt and taghut} to the end of the verse."],[11591,"“May you have no mother! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is sufficed by someone better than you.”"],[11592,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “May Allah curse the men who imitate women and the women who imitate men.”"],[11593,"“We used to eat, drink, bathe, and go out, then go out to the prayer place.”"],[11594,"I saw ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbbas eating at Arafah for some time, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fast it, nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar.”"],[11595,"that he should make himself steadfast — one man against ten — when the Muslims were few. When the Muslims became many, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded a man to be steadfast against two men, ten against twenty, and one hundred against two hundred.”"],[11596,"The first thing revealed to the Prophet ﷺ was that it was said to him: Cover yourself. After that his private parts were never seen."],[11597,"The Prophet ﷺ went out happily and said, \"Indeed, Allah has increased for you a prayer, and it is the Witr prayer.\""],[11598,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say anything improper. I forbade you from the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat and keep some. I forbade you from nabīdh, so drink, but do not drink anything intoxicating.”"],[11599,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed while wearing his sandals.\""],[11600,"that the Prophet ﷺ forbade sales involving uncertainty (gharar)."],[11601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat in a house wearing only a waist-wrapper, which he had thrown between his legs, with his thighs exposed. Abu Bakr came seeking permission to enter, so he granted him permission and he entered. Then Umar came, so he granted him permission and he entered. Then Uthman came, so he granted him permission. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he rose quickly and entered the inner room. That was hard for Aisha. When the people left, she said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr and Umar entered and you did not change your state, but when Uthman entered you stood up. He said: “O Aisha, should I not feel shy before one before whom the angels feel shy? Indeed the angels feel shy before Uthman.”"],[11602,"that the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.” Abu Kurayb added in his hadith: Then Umar woke up and went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam that day. Abu Kurayb said in his hadith: “O Allah, make Islam mighty.”"],[11603,"that a man prayed alone behind the rows, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to repeat the prayer."],[11604,"The people �— the people took their due from us."],[11605,"“They were nine men from the people of Nasibin.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them messengers to their people."],[11606,"“The last funeral prayer over which the Prophet ﷺ prayed, he said four takbirs over it.”"],[11607,"their elders hear from their young.” It was said to Ibn Abbas: Why is that? He said: “Because the young heard and the elders did not hear.”"],[11608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be guarded, so his uncle, Abu Talib, would send men from the Banu Hashim to guard him every day until this verse was revealed: \"O Messenger, convey that which has been revealed to you from your Lord\" until the statement of Allah: \"And Allah will protect you from the people.\" So his uncle wanted to send someone to guard him, but he said, \"O uncle, Allah has protected me from the jinn and mankind.\""],[11609,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted the testimony of a Bedouin regarding the sighting of the crescent of Ramadan."],[11610,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting and in ihram. A man called Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage and interceded for him with his masters."],[11611,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Loyalty (wala') belongs to the one who sets free.\""],[11612,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Loyalty (wala') belongs to the one who sets free.\""],[11613,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The best with which you can dye gray hair is henna and katam.\""],[11614,"\"Visiting a sick person once is a sunnah; anything more is supererogatory.\""],[11615,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar and cooked their meat. \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots to be overturned and forbade their meat that day.\""],[11616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Mount Hira and the mountain began to shake. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stay firm, O Hira, for there is nothing upon you but a prophet, a truthful one or a martyr.\" With him were the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, Zubayr, Abdul Rahman ibn Awf, Saad, and Sa'id ibn Zaid ibn Amr ibn Nufayl."],[11617,"\"The Prophet ﷺ stayed after the conquest for seventeen days praying two rak'ahs.\""],[11618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the 'Asr prayer with three rak'ahs and forgot one. He left and entered upon one of his wives. Then a man from his Companions called Dhu al-Shimalayn entered upon him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened?\" He said: \"What is that?\" He said: \"You prayed three.\" So he took him by the hand and went out to the people who had been with him and said: \"Did Dhu al-Yadayn speak the truth?\" They said: \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"He claims that I prayed three.\" They said: \"He has spoken truthfully. We thought that you had been commanded something regarding that.\" \"So he led them in one rak'ah, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness.\""],[11619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The sacrificial animal (adha) is obligatory on me and sunnah for you.\""],[11620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let none of you stand in a place where a man is killed unjustly, for the curse descends upon those who are present when they do not defend him. And let none of you stand in a place where someone is struck unjustly, for the curse descends upon those who are present when they do not defend him.\""],[11621,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions were swimming in a pool. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Let each man among you swim to his companion.\" So each man swam to his companion, and the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr remained. The Prophet ﷺ swam to Abu Bakr until he embraced him and said: \"I am to my companion, I am to my companion.\""],[11622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you pray, raise your lower garments, for whatever of your lower garments touches the ground is in the Fire.\""],[11623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and the masculine women, and the woman who tattoos and the woman who asks to be tattooed, and the woman who extends hair and the woman who asks to have it extended."],[11624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A believer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he drink alcohol while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer.\""],[11625,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Beware of qadar, for it is a branch of Christianity.\""],[11626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring was heard, then he got up and prayed without performing ablution."],[11627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two groups of my community have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.\""],[11628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the women who imitate men and the effeminate men."],[11629,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , ascended the pulpit with a thick bandage wrapped around his head. He praised and extolled Allah, then he said, \"Indeed, people are increasing in number while the Ansar (the helpers) are decreasing to the point where they will be like salt in a dish. So whoever among you assumes a position of authority and benefits some people while harming others, let him accept the good deeds of the righteous and overlook the mistakes of others.\" This was the last sermon that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , delivered before he passed away."],[11630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah: \"Allah, may He be glorified, will not punish you nor your child.\""],[11631,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day to his companions: \"Whom do you count as martyrs among you?\" They said: \"Whoever is killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, is a martyr.\" He said: \"The martyrs of my community would then be few. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the man who dies on his bed in the path of Allah is a martyr; the one who dies of a stomach ailment is a martyr; the one who is bitten is a martyr; the drowned one is a martyr; the one who suffocates is a martyr; the one mauled by a wild beast is a martyr; the one who falls from his mount is a martyr; the one killed by a collapsing building is a martyr; the one with pleurisy is a martyr; and the woman in childbirth whom her child kills, her child will drag her by her umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[11632,"Allah did not reveal {O you who believe} except that Ali is its chief and its noble one. And Allah reproached the companions of Muhammad ﷺ in more than one place, and He mentioned Ali only with good."],[11633,"When the women pledged not to display themselves as in the first ignorance, a woman said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I see you impose on us that we not display ourselves, but so-and-so has helped me and her brother has died.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go and help her, then come and pledge to me.\""],[11634,"\"I see that you have been made forbidden to me, so go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; perhaps you may seek something to return you to me.\" So she went, and he sat waiting for her at the edge of the well. She came to the Prophet ﷺ while a hairdresser was combing his head. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Aws b. al-Samit, as you know, is weak in judgment and unable, and he has declared zihar from me, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The most deserving of being shown kindness for good, if it were I, or to show kindness for good, if it were him, is he. He has declared zihar from me, O Messenger of Allah, so seek something to return me to him, may my father and mother be your ransom.\" He said: \"O Khuwaylah, we have not been commanded anything regarding your matter, and if we are commanded, I will inform you.\" While his hairdresser had finished one side of his head and started the other, Allah, may He be glorified, revealed, and when revelation came upon him his face would turn dark until he felt its coolness, and when it was lifted his face returned white like a heart. Then he spoke with what he was commanded. The hairdresser said to her: \"O Khuwaylah, I think it is now about your matter.\" She was seized by a shiver; a trembling overcame her, then she said: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from anything being sent down about me except good, for I sought from Your Messenger only good.\" When it was lifted from him, he said: \"O Khuwaylah, Allah has revealed about you and your husband: {Allah has heard the words of the woman who argues with you concerning her husband} up to His words {then return to what they said, then freeing a slave before they touch each other}.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no servant other than me, and I have no servant other than him.\" He said: {And whoever does not find, then fasting two consecutive months}. She said: \"By Allah, if he does not eat twice a day his sight dims.\" He said: {And whoever is unable, then feeding sixty poor people}. She said: \"By Allah, we have nothing in a day except an uqiyyah.\" He said: \"Then tell him to go to so-and-so and take from him half a wasq of dates and give it in charity to sixty poor people and take you back.\" She said: \"So I came, and when he saw me he said: 'What is with you?' I said: 'Good, and you are blameworthy. You have been commanded to go to so-and-so and take from him half a wasq of dates and give it in charity to sixty poor people and take me back.' So he went running until he brought it.\" She said: \"And I knew him before that as unable to carry on his back five sa's due to weakness.\""],[11635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us in the mosque of al-Khayf. He praised Allah and mentioned Him as He deserves, then said: \"Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah will gather his affairs, place his richness before his eyes, and the world will come to him submissively. And whoever makes the world his concern, Allah will scatter his affairs, place his poverty before his eyes, and nothing of the world will come to him except what is written.\""],[11636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever performs ablution after the full bath is not one of us.\""],[11637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallālah sheep, the price of a dog, the stud fee of a stallion, and the earnings of a cupper."],[11638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the people who are satiated in this world will be the people of hunger in the Hereafter tomorrow.\""],[11639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Adhere to sorrow, for it is the key to the heart.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how is sorrow?\" He said: \"Make yourselves hungry with hunger and thirsty.\""],[11640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, Mūsā b. ʿImrān passed by a man while he was writhing, so he stood calling upon Allah to heal him. It was said to him: 'O Mūsā, what afflicts him is not a share from Iblīs; rather, he made himself hungry for Me. He is the one who sees that I look at him every day many times. I marvel at his obedience to Me. So command him to supplicate for you, for he has with Me every day a supplication.'\""],[11641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever angers Allah in pleasing people, Allah will be angry with him and make those whom he pleased angry with him in His displeasure. And whoever pleases Allah in angering people ؓ, He will be pleased with him and make those whom he angered pleased with him in His pleasure, until He beautifies him and beautifies his speech and action in his eye.\""],[11643,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have committed adultery with my wife while she was menstruating.\" So he ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."],[11644,"\"There is no harm in cupping for the fasting person; it was only disliked because of weakness.\""],[11645,"\"It is the Mother of the Book.\""],[11646,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Be sincere to one another in knowledge, for the betrayal of one of you in his knowledge is more severe than his betrayal in his wealth, and indeed Allah, exalted is He, will question you on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11647,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will a town be destroyed while the righteous are in it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" It was said: \"Why, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Because of their negligence and their silence regarding the disobedience of Allah.\""],[11648,"While Ṣafwān b. Umayyah was sleeping in the mosque with his cloak under his head, a man came and pulled out his cloak and took it. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that his hand be cut. He said: \"I did not think that my cloak would cause the hand of a Muslim to be cut because of it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Why not before you brought him to me?\""],[11649,"The Prophet ﷺ left Madinah for Makkah and fasted until he reached Qudayd. A vessel of milk was brought to him, so he broke his fast while on his mount, and it was Ramadan, and the people broke their fast. Those who broke their fast said to those who had not broken their fast: \"Break your fast, O disobedient ones.\""],[11650,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ that he was asked about a woman who made a vow upon herself that she would certainly perform Hajj walking. He ordered her to perform Hajj riding."],[11651,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not fast before Ramadan; fast at its sighting and break your fast at its sighting. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty days.\""],[11652,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the circuit between al-Safa and al-Marwa on his mount."],[11653,"\"Those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves\" — they [the angels] said, \"In what condition were you?\" They said, \"We were oppressed in the land.\" They said, \"Was not God's earth spacious enough for you to emigrate therein?\" Those — their abode is Hell, and evil is the destination. He said: They were a group of Muslims in Makkah who went out with a group of the polytheists to fight and were killed alongside them, so this verse was revealed: \"Except the oppressed among men, women, and children who cannot devise a plan and are not directed to a way — for those, perhaps God will pardon them.\" Thus God excused those among them who had an excuse and destroyed those who had no excuse. Ibn Abbas said: I and my mother were among those who had an excuse."],[11654,"He said to his family: Carry me and take me out of the land of the polytheists to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: He died on the way before reaching the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Then the revelation came down: \"And whoever leaves his home emigrating to God and His Messenger,\" until he reached \"God is Forgiving, Merciful.\""],[11655,"In His saying ﷻ {And do not raise your voice in your prayer, nor be silent therein}, He said, \"Whenever he prayed, he raised his voice.\""],[11656,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: \"He is one-eyed, with curly hair, of a fair ruddy complexion, glowing white, as if his head is a serpent. He most resembles ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan among the people. But the utmost destruction — the utmost destruction — is that he is one-eyed, and that your Lord, Exalted is He, is not one-eyed.\""],[11657,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Dajjal has curly hair, is of a fair ruddy complexion, moon-like in brightness, as if his head is a branch of a tree. His left eye is obliterated, and the other is like a floating grape. The person who most resembles him is ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan. As for the utter destruction — the utter destruction — he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed.\""],[11658,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Dajjal has curly hair, is of a fair ruddy complexion, moon-like in brightness, as if his head is a branch of a tree. His left eye is obliterated, and the other is like a floating grape. The person who most resembles him is ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Qatan. As for the utter destruction — the utter destruction — he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed.\""],[11659,"A woman from among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed a full bath after major ritual impurity. The Prophet ﷺ came and performed ablution from the leftover water of her bath. She said, \"I bathed from it.\" He said: \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[11660,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came one day to bathe, and one of his wives said, \"O Messenger of God, it is the leftover of my bath.\" He said: \"Water does not become impure.\""],[11661,"One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ bathed in a large basin. The Prophet ﷺ came to perform ablution from it, or to bathe. She said to him, \"O Messenger of God, I was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Water is not made impure.\""],[11662,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade taking a living creature as a target."],[11663,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a people who had set up a pigeon and were shooting at it, and he said: \"Do not take a living creature as a target.\""],[11664,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar who had set up a pigeon as a target and were shooting at it. He said: “Do not take anything possessed of a soul as a target.”"],[11665,"These were men who had embraced Islam from the people of Makkah and wanted to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gained understanding of the religion, they wanted to punish them, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, indeed among your spouses and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them. But if you pardon, and overlook, and forgive, then indeed Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.}"],[11666,"A woman embraced Islam during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. Then her first husband came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “I embraced Islam along with her, and she knew of my embracing Islam along with her.” So the Prophet ﷺ took her away from her second husband and returned her to her first husband."],[11667,"“Amusing themselves and turning away from it.”"],[11668,"“The prophets were from the Children of Israel except for ten: Nuh, Hud, Lut, Shuʿayb, Ibrahim, Ismaʿil, Ishaq, ʿIsa, and Muhammad ﷺ and upon them all be peace. And there is no prophet who had two names except ʿIsa and Yaʿqub (peace be upon them).”"],[11669,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Let the beards grow full and trim the moustaches.” He said: “And Ibrahim ﷺ , the intimate friend of the Most Merciful, used to let his beard grow full and trim his moustache.”"],[11670,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to trim his mustache, and that Ibrahim Al-Khalil (Abraham) used to trim his mustache."],[11671,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that on buried treasure one-fifth is due.”"],[11672,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘A righteous dream is one of the seventy parts of prophecy.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3897)"],[11673,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A man should not have skin-to-skin contact with a man, nor a woman with a woman.”"],[11674,"They said: “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of those who died while they were praying toward Jerusalem?” So Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah would never let your faith be lost. Indeed Allah is to all people Kind and Merciful.}"],[11675,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, what of those who died while drinking wine?” So it was revealed: {There is no sin upon those who believed and did righteous deeds for what they have eaten} the verse."],[11676,"A man from Banu Sulaym passed by a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ with a flock of sheep, and he greeted them. They said: “He only greeted you to seek protection.” So they went to him, killed him, and took his sheep. Then they brought them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, when you travel in the way of Allah, verify} up to His saying {Thus you were before.}"],[11677,"Regarding His saying {Our Lord, we have believed, so write us down among the witnesses}, he said: “With Muhammad and his nation, for they have borne witness that he conveyed, and they have borne witness for the messengers that they conveyed.”"],[11678,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ after he finished at Badr, “Take the caravan; there is nothing beyond it.” Al-ʿAbbas said, while he was a captive in his bonds, “It is not fitting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Why?” He said, “Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you.”"],[11679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “People of my community will certainly recite the Qurʾan, and they will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game.”"],[11680,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to set out on a journey, he would say, “O Allah, You are the companion in the journey and the successor over the family. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from difficulty in the journey and sorrow on the return. O Allah, contract the earth for us and make the journey easy for us.” And when he returned, he would say, “Returning, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord.” And when he entered upon his family, he would say, “A return, a return to our Lord, a repentance that leaves no sin upon us.”"],[11681,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever builds a wall, let him support it against his brother’s wall.”"],[11682,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “If you disagree about the path, then measure seven cubits, and do not make it less than that.”"],[11683,"The Prophet ﷺ ate the shoulder of a sheep and said it was well-cooked. Then he wiped his hand with a wipe and prayed."],[11684,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder, then wiped his hand on a cloth that was beneath him, then stood and prayed."],[11685,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Yes.” He said, “There is no alliance in Islam, and every alliance made in the Jahiliyyah is only strengthened by Islam in intensity and force.”"],[11686,"“When you prostrate, press your hands to the ground.” Sharik added, “For you have been commanded to do that.”"],[11687,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “By Allah, I will certainly raid Quraysh; by Allah, I will certainly raid Quraysh.” Then he said the third time, “If Allah wills.”"],[11688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a caravan that had arrived containing some awqiyah of gold, and he gave it as charity to the widows of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib. He said, “I will not buy something for which I do not have its price.”"],[11689,"ʿAʾishah bought Barīrah from the Ansar to set her free, and they stipulated her walaʾ for themselves. She granted them that. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she informed him, and he said, “Walaʾ is only for the one who sets free.” Then he ascended the pulpit and said, “What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Any condition not in the Book of Allah is rejected, even if it is a hundred conditions.” Barīrah had a husband, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her the choice: if she wished, she could remain with her husband as she was, and if she wished, she could separate from him. She separated from him. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered and saw a leg of a sheep and said to ʿAʾishah, “Will you not cook this meat for us?” She said, “It was given as charity to Barīrah, and she gave it to us as a gift.” He said, “Cook it, for it is charity for her and a gift for us.”"],[11690,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the effeminate men and said, “Expel them from your homes.”"],[11691,"The Prophet ﷺ decided to divorce her. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to Aisha.' He did so, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame} upon them both if they make terms of peace between themselves; and peace is better. And whatever they agree upon by mutual consent is permissible."],[11692,"No, by Allah, I will never commit adultery. Then was revealed: {And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution}."],[11693,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ formed brotherhood among his Companions, so they began inheriting from each other because of that, until the verse was revealed: \"And those with close relationship are more entitled to inheritance from one another.\" So they started inheriting based on kinship."],[11694,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted during travel and broke his fast."],[11695,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, 'Give me a handful of pebbles.' He gave him the handful of pebbles, and the Prophet threw them at the faces of the people until none of them remained except that their eyes were filled with pebbles, and then the verse was revealed, 'And you did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw.'\""],[11696,"The Prophet ﷺ and those with him prayed towards Jerusalem for sixteen months, then the qiblah was changed afterwards."],[11697,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah (small palm-fiber mat)."],[11698,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a reed mat."],[11699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete the number, and the month is twenty-nine.'"],[11700,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not precede the month. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If there is an obstruction between you and it, then complete the number.'"],[11701,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete thirty.'"],[11702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not anticipate the month. Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If it is obscured from you, then complete the number.'"],[11703,"A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began speaking with clear speech. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, some poetry is wisdom.'"],[11706,"“Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom, and part of eloquence is sorcery.”"],[11707,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom.”"],[11708,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed, part of poetry is wisdom, and indeed, part of eloquence is sorcery.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to quote verses of poetry."],[11709,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no contagion, no bad omen in birds, no hāmah, and no ṣafar.” A man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, we take a mangy sheep and throw it among the flock, and then the flock becomes mangy.” He said, “Then who infected the first one?”"],[11710,"“O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died,” meaning a sheep. He said, “Why did you not take its skin?” They said, “Should we take the skin of a sheep that has died?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “Allah only said: {Say, ‘I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it, unless it is carrion, or flowing blood, or the flesh of swine.’} You would not eat it; rather, you would tan it and benefit from it.” So she sent for it, skinned its hide, tanned it, and made a water skin from it until it wore out at her place."],[11711,"A sheep belonging to Umm al-Aswad died, and she informed the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: {Say, ‘I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to one who eats it, unless it is carrion, or blood’} up to the end of the verse, and he said: “You are not going to eat it.” So she sent for it and skinned it. Ibn ʿAbbas said: They made its hide into a water skin, and I saw it after a year. Abu al-Ahwas said: “Umm al-Aswad” is a mistake; the correct is Sawdah."],[11712,"There were two co-wives, and there was a quarrel between them. One of them threw a stone at the other and caused her to miscarry a dead boy, and the woman died. He ruled that the diyah be paid by the ʿāqilah. Her paternal uncle said, “She miscarried, O Messenger of Allah, a boy whose hair had grown.” The father of the killer said, “He is lying. By Allah, he neither cried, nor reasoned, nor drank, nor ate. Such a one is not entitled to blood money.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is it the rhymed prose of the Age of Ignorance and its soothsaying? I prescribe for the boy a ghurrah (a slave, male or female).” Ibn ʿAbbas said: The name of one of them was Mulaykah and the other was Umm ʿUṭayf."],[11713,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while he was in iḥrām.”"],[11714,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Avoid drinking from gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels, and drink from water skins. If you fear its fermentation, then dilute it with water.”"],[11715,"A cooked lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and she sent it to the Prophet ﷺ. The people ate, but the Prophet ﷺ did not eat. Khālid b. al-Walīd said, “O Messenger of Allah, is it forbidden, so we should leave it?” He said, “No, but I find it repulsive.”"],[11716,"A lizard was gifted to one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and she sent it to the Prophet ﷺ. The people ate, except the Prophet ﷺ. Khālid b. al-Walīd said, “Is it forbidden, O Messenger of Allah, so we should leave it?” He said, “No, but I find it repulsive.”"],[11717,"\"In his statement 'Your mothers are forbidden for you', he said 'Seven prohibitions come from lineage and seven from marriage through affinity.' And in his statement 'and what is beyond that is lawful for you', he said 'from lineage.' And in his statement 'the Book of Allah upon you', he said 'the four books.'\""],[11718,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered ʿAlī to prepare a bath for him, then he gave him a garment and said, “Cover me, and turn your back to me.”"],[11719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not intercept caravans outside the market, do not leave animals unmilked [to deceive buyers], and do not bid against one another [merely to raise the price].”"],[11720,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A group of people from my community will recite the Quran but they will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes through the game.”"],[11721,"“They used to talk during prayer; a man’s servant would come to him while he was praying and speak to him about his need, so they were forbidden from speaking [during prayer].”"],[11722,"I was sleeping, and I was approached and told: “Tonight is the Night of Decree.” So I got up while drowsy, and my foot caught on one of the ropes of the tent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing praying. Ibn Abbas said: I looked into the night, and it was the twenty-third night. “The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi.”"],[11723,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It would not please me to have the red camels if I were to break the pact that is in Dar al-Nadwah.”"],[11724,"“The slaughtered animals of the Jews and Christians were only made lawful because they believed in the Torah and the Gospel.”"],[11725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever has land and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his neighbour.”"],[11726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “did not prohibit leasing land, but he commanded [us] to adhere to noble character.”"],[11727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever abandons a prayer will meet Allah while He is angry with him.”"],[11728,"The Prophet ﷺ “forbade buying fruit until it is ripe [and ready to be eaten].”"],[11729,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “I was aided by the east wind, and ʿAd was destroyed by the west wind.”"],[11730,"The Prophet ﷺ “used to prostrate on a mat.” Husayn — meaning al-Muʿallim — [narrated it]."],[11731,"The people disputed about the new moon during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then a Bedouin came and testified that he had seen it. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Do you testify that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God?” He said, “Yes.” So the Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal, and he proclaimed, “Fasting is tomorrow.”"],[11732,"\"There was no woman who offered herself to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[11733,"\"They were merchants who were not distracted by trade or selling from the remembrance of Allah.\""],[11734,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade blowing into food, drink, and fruit."],[11735,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Do not revile Tubbaʿ, for he had embraced Islam.”"],[11736,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “On every joint of a person there is a charity due each day.” Some of the people said, “This is difficult, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Enjoining good and forbidding evil is a charity; helping a weak person is a charity; and every step one of you takes to prayer is a charity.”"],[11737,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Every Muslim has a prayer due, and every step one of you takes to prayer is itself a prayer.”"],[11738,"He said to his people, “I will extinguish for you the fire of al-ḥadathān.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād, a man from his people, said, “By God, O Khālid, you have never said anything to us but the truth. So what is your affair and the affair of the fire of al-ḥadathān? You claim that you will extinguish it.” So ʿUmārah b. Ziyād went with him along with some people from his people until they came to it while it was emerging from a cleft in a mountain in a ḥarrah called Ḥarrat Ashjaʿ. Khālid drew a line for them and seated them inside it, and he said, “If I am delayed from you, do not call me by my name.” Then it came out as if it were reddish horses, following one another. Khālid faced it and began striking it with his staff, saying, “Bada bada, all is guidance, raw youths. The son of the shepherd of goats claimed that I would not come out of it while my clothes were still moist.” He entered the cleft with it and was delayed from them. ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said, “By God, if your companion were alive, he would have come out to you by now.” They said, “He forbade us to call him by his name.” He said, “Call him by his name.” So he came out to them, holding his head, and said, “Did I not forbid you to call me by my name? By God, you have killed me. So bury me, and when donkeys pass by you, including a dock-tailed donkey, then dig me up, for you will find me alive.” Then donkeys passed by them, including a dock-tailed donkey, and they said, “Dig him up, for he commanded us to dig him up.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said to them, “Do not let Muḍar say that we dig up our dead. By God, you will never dig him up.” Khālid had informed them that in his wife’s saddlebag there were two tablets, and if any matter became difficult for them, they should look at them, for they would see what they asked about. He also said, “Let no menstruating woman touch them.” When they returned to his wife, they asked her about them, and she brought them out while she was menstruating, so the knowledge that was in them departed. Abū Yūnus said: Simāk said: The son of Khālid b. Sinān came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, “Welcome to the son of my brother.” And Abū Yūnus is Ḥātim b. Abī Ṣaghīrah."],[11739,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to have skin-to-skin contact with a man, and a woman with a woman."],[11740,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade muḥāqalah and muzābanah. And ʿIkrimah used to dislike selling green fodder."],[11741,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights of Ramadan.”"],[11742,"The Prophet ﷺ had a coat of mail pawned with a Jew, and he did not find anything with which to redeem it until he died."],[11743,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a man from his companions to a Jew to kill him. He said, “O Messenger of God, give me permission to say something.” He said, “Say whatever seems appropriate to you, for war is deceit.”"],[11744,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “The fornicator does not fornicate while he is a believer.” ʿIkrimah said: I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, “How is faith removed?” He said, “Like this,” and he described it by interlacing his fingers, then he pulled them apart. “And if he repents, it returns to him.”"],[11745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a slave whom his master gives in marriage. He said, \"In whose hand is the divorce?\" He said, \"In the hand of the one who takes hold of the shank.\""],[11746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves off [hunting] snakes for fear of seeking them is not of us.\""],[11747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Sacrificial slaughter and ritual slaughter were prescribed for me but not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer but you were not commanded to do it.\""],[11748,"\"Sacrificial slaughter was prescribed for me but not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer but you were not commanded to do it.\""],[11749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a village at the distance of four farsakhs or two farsakhs on the day of Ashura: \"Whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast, and whoever has eaten, let him not eat for the rest of his day.\""],[11750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A woman may not be married in addition to her paternal aunt, nor in addition to her maternal aunt.\""],[11751,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There should be no harming or reciprocating harm. A person should secure a piece of wood on the wall of his neighbor. And if you have doubts about the road, then make it seven cubits.\""],[11752,"A cheese was brought to the Prophet ﷺ during the expedition of al-Ta'if, and his companions began striking it with their sticks and saying, \"We fear that it may contain carrion.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Put the knife into it and mention the name of Allah over it.\""],[11753,"The Prophet ﷺ did not enter the House during the Hajj, but he entered it in the year of the conquest. When he dismounted, he prayed four rak'ahs—or he said two rak'ahs—between the Stone and the door, facing the House, and said, \"This is the qiblah.\""],[11754,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed three [rak'ahs] and gave the salam. Dhu al-Shimalayn said, \"O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is it as Dhu al-Yadayn says?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Prophet ﷺ prayed one rak'ah and prostrated twice."],[11755,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"There is no believing servant except that he has a sin that he repeatedly falls into from time to time, or a sin upon which he persists and does not part with it until he departs from this world. Indeed the believer is created as one who is tried, repentant, and forgetful: when he is reminded, he remembers.\""],[11756,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When a noble person of a people comes to you, honor him.\""],[11757,"\"Water is required by water, in the case of a wet dream.\""],[11758,"“Prayer by anyone upon anyone is not appropriate except upon the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[11759,"“The Prophet ﷺ had raisin nabidh, and he would drink it that day and the next day; and if it was the third day, he would drink it, otherwise he would pour it out.”"],[11760,"The Prophet ﷺ “used to wear a ring on his right hand.”"],[11761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever sponsors an orphan, whether for themselves or for someone else, Paradise is guaranteed for them except if they commit an unforgivable act. And whoever loses their two honorable possessions, Paradise is guaranteed for them except if they commit an unforgivable act.\" \"Abu Sufyan is him, as far as I know, Sa'id bin Masruq, and Allah knows best.\""],[11762,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ singled us out with three things: that we perform wudu thoroughly, that we do not consume charity, and that we do not make donkeys cover horses."],[11763,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Khadijah, Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, “O Muhammad, convey my greetings of peace to Khadijah and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, with no noise in it and no fatigue.”"],[11764,"That the Prophet ﷺ “forbade eating mujaththamah, jallalah, and drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.”"],[11765,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade eating mujaththamah, jallalah, and drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin.”"],[11766,"That the Prophet ﷺ “forbade drinking directly from the mouth of a waterskin, eating mujaththamah, and drinking the milk of a jallalah.”"],[11767,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wishes his lifespan to be extended and his provision increased, let him maintain ties of kinship.”"],[11768,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “cursed men who imitate women and women who imitate men.”"],[11769,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “This and this are equal” – meaning the thumb and the little finger – “their blood money is equal.”"],[11770,"“The husband of Barirah was a slave.”"],[11771,"Ibn ʿAbbas said: I saw him in the streets of Madinah pressing his eyes shut. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning it with four—her masters stipulated the walaʾ for themselves. The Prophet ﷺ ruled that the walaʾ belongs to the one who manumits, and he gave her the choice, so she chose herself. He ordered her to observe the waiting period and gave her charity. She sent some of it to ʿAʾishah as a gift, and ʿAʾishah asked the Prophet ﷺ about it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is charity for her, but for us it is a gift.”"],[11772,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated seven times, and he did so at a brisk pace because he loved to show the people his strength."],[11773,"ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My sister has vowed to walk to the House.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Allah is in no need of your sister’s vow. Let her ride and offer a sacrificial camel.”"],[11775,"In his statement \"Mankind used to be one nation,\" he said, \"upon Islam.\""],[11776,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever forms an image will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection with blowing the soul into it. Whoever eavesdrops on people’s speech while they dislike that will have molten lead poured into his ear. And whoever falsely claims a dream will be tasked with tying together two grains of barley.”"],[11777,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbas: “I saw in al-Abtah an old foolish man who says the takbir when he prostrates and when he raises his head.” He said: “Is that not the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? May your mother lose you!”"],[11778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah bt. al-Harith while he was in ihram and consummated the marriage after he returned, at a place of water called Sarif."],[11779,"Jamilah bt. Salul came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I do not fault Thabit b. Qays in character or religion, but I cannot bear him, and I hate disbelief after Islam.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you return his garden to him?” She said: “Yes.” So the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take back from her what he had given her and not to take any more."],[11780,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever changes his religion, kill him.”"],[11781,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, my father is a very old, sick man for whom standing is difficult. Tell me which night I should seek so that Allah may grant me success in it—the Night of Decree.” He said: “Look for the seventh.”"],[11782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays from muzzy, and I fear it may be the unripe dates."],[11783,"That the Prophet ﷺ bookmarked Hassan and Hussein."],[11784,"The Quran was sent down on the Night of Decree in Ramadan to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was sent down in stages."],[11785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made two rakʿahs obligatory during travel just as He made four obligatory while settled."],[11786,"When the verse was revealed: “O Prophet, indeed We have sent you as a witness and a bringer of good tidings and a warner” [Qur’an 33:45], the Prophet ﷺ called ‘Ali and Mu‘adh, and he had already ordered them to go out to Yemen. He said: “Go forth, give good tidings and do not repel, make things easy and do not make them difficult, for it has been revealed to me: ‘O Prophet, indeed We have sent you as a witness’ over your nation, ‘and a bringer of good tidings’ of Paradise, ‘and a warner’ from the Fire, ‘and a caller’ to the testimony that there is no god but God, ‘and an illuminating lamp’ with the Qur’an.”"],[11787,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with his face dripping blood and said: “O Messenger of God, I followed a woman, then a man met me and did to me what you see.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God, may He be exalted, intends good for a servant, He hastens the punishment of his sin in this world; and when He intends evil for a servant, He withholds his sin until He confronts him with it on the Day of Resurrection, as if he were a donkey.”"],[11788,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “I saw the Dajjal as a fair-skinned, white, stout, curly-haired man, as if the hair of his head were branches of a tree, one-eyed, as if his eye were the morning star. I liken him to ‘Abd al-‘Uzza, a man of Khuza‘ah.”"],[11789,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Learn the two radiant suras, al-Baqarah and Al ‘Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for their companion. Learn al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the idle cannot master it.”"],[11790,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the images in the house—meaning the Ka‘bah—he did not enter until he ordered them erased. He saw Ibrahim and Isma‘il with divination arrows in their hands and said: “May God fight them! By God, they never sought omens with divination arrows at all.”"],[11791,"He said: “Whoever leaves them out of fear or dread of vengeance is not of us.” He said: And Ibn ‘Abbas said: “Snakes are the transformed jinn, just as apes were transformed from the Children of Israel.”"],[11792,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11793,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11794,"I witnessed Eid with the Prophet ﷺ and he delivered a sermon. He thought that the women hadn't heard, so he called them and advised them, saying, \"Give in charity.\" Then, the women started giving their rings, earrings, necklaces, and even their garments. The Prophet commanded Bilal to collect them in his garment until he distributed them."],[11795,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever changes his religion—or he said: reverts from his religion—kill him.” And he said: “Do not punish with God’s punishment,” meaning fire."],[11796,"“The husband of Barirah was a slave belonging to Banu So-and-so, people of the Ansar, called Mughith. By God, it is as if I am looking at him now, following her through the streets of Madinah, weeping.”"],[11797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The evil example is not for us: the one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit.”"],[11798,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like a dog that returns to its vomit. The evil example is not for us.”"],[11799,"“It is not abrogated. He used to recite it: ‘They will be collared with it.’ It is concerning the very old man who is obliged to fast but cannot bear it, so he breaks the fast and feeds.”"],[11800,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever makes an image will be required on the Day of Resurrection to blow the spirit into it, and he will never be able to blow, and he will be punished for it. Whoever listens to the speech of a people while they dislike that, molten lead will be poured into his ears. Whoever lies about his dream will be required to tie a knot in a barley grain” — or he said “between two barley grains” — “and he will be punished for it, and he will not do it.”"],[11801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered an ʿaqiqah for al-Hasan with a ram, and for al-Husayn with a ram."],[11802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a mukatab dies and leaves an inheritance, or becomes liable to a prescribed punishment, he inherits according to the portion of him that has been freed, and the prescribed punishment is carried out on him according to the portion of him that has been freed.”"],[11803,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the Night of Decree, he said: “Seek it in the ninth remaining, the seventh remaining, and the fifth remaining.”"],[11804,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram."],[11805,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting."],[11806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boast about your forefathers who passed away during the Jahiliyyah. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the dung that the beetle rolls with its nose is better than them.”"],[11807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not boast about your forefathers who died during the Jahiliyyah. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, what the beetle rolls with its nose is better than your forefathers who died during the Jahiliyyah.”"],[11808,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram, and consummated the marriage with her at Sarif when he was out of ihram."],[11809,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in Sad, and it is not one of the prescribed prostrations."],[11810,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating in Sad."],[11811,"That the Prophet ﷺ prostrated while he was in Makkah at [the recitation of] al-Najm, and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and the humans prostrated with him. And Hafs b. ʿUmar said in his hadith: Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ prostrated in Makkah, and the Jews, the Christians, and the polytheists prostrated with him."],[11812,"ʿAʾishah said to her: \"In disappointment! I see you are detaining us.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what is that?\" Safiyyah said, \"She has menstruated.\" It was said, \"She has already performed the ifadah.\" He said, \"Then no.\""],[11813,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to take from the heads while he was fasting—meaning kissing."],[11814,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped and paid the cupper; and if it had been impure, he would not have fed him."],[11815,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before I threw [the pebbles].\" He motioned with his hand and said, \"No harm.\" And he was not asked that day about anything regarding advancing or delaying except that he motioned with his hand and said, \"No harm.\""],[11816,"That he should not speak, nor seek shade, nor sit, and that he should fast his day. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Order him to speak, seek shade, sit, and fast his day.\""],[11817,"The Prophet ﷺ was traveling when he passed by a woman with her hair uncovered. He said, \"What is this?\" It was mentioned that it was a woman from the Quraysh tribe who had vowed to perform Hajj with her hair uncovered. He said, \"Tell her to cover her hair.\""],[11818,"The Prophet (PBUH) said, \"Between the pillar and the station, there is a binding obligation that relieves the person with a disability from making it.\""],[11820,"That a group of people came to the Prophet ﷺ with a woman and said, \"O Muhammad! What has been revealed to you regarding adultery?\" He replied, \"Go and bring me two men from the learned scholars of the Children of Israel.\" So they brought him two men, one of them was a young man with a good voice, while the other had his eyebrow covering his eye, and he had to raise it with a string. The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"I adjure both of you by Allah, do you know what Allah revealed to Moses regarding the adulterer?\" They replied, \"You have adjured us by a great oath. Indeed, we inform you that Allah revealed to Moses the punishment of stoning for the adulterer, and we were a youthful and attractive group, and our women were beautiful. This sin became widespread among us, so we did not enforce the punishment. Instead, we would flog (the adulterer).\" The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"Go and bring your companion and when she gives birth, stone her.\""],[11821,"That the Prophet ﷺ went out to a people who had set up a live pigeon as a target and were throwing it. He said, \"It is not permissible to eat its meat.\""],[11822,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to drink from a vessel in three breaths."],[11823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whatever of the izār extends below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[11824,"That the Prophet ﷺ would not blow into the drink."],[11825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His firm obligations be taken.\""],[11826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves that His concessions be taken, just as He loves that His firm obligations be taken.\""],[11827,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the dominion of debts, the dominion of enemies, the destruction of blessings, and the trials of the false Messiah.\""],[11828,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"You will surely bring clear proof for what you say, or you will be flogged with the prescribed punishment.\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, I am truthful, and Allah will surely send down my excuse.\" Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him, and they performed mutual cursing. When the fifth [oath] remained, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is binding, and I wished that you be shown mercy.\" Then she said, \"By Allah, I will not disgrace my people,\" and she proceeded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Observe her. If she gives birth to a white child with lank hair and short eyes, then it is for Hilal b. Umayyah; and if she gives birth to a dark-skinned child with curly hair and kohl-lined eyes, then it is for Sharīk b. al-Sahmāʾ.\" Then she gave birth to one for Sharīk."],[11829,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever listens to the conversation of a people, molten lead will be poured into his ear; and whoever falsely claims a dream will be tasked with tying together two grains of barley, and he will not be able to tie them.\""],[11830,"That the husband of Barirah was a slave, and I saw him striking his head against the walls in pursuit of her."],[11831,"Permission was granted for drinking from the mouths of water-skins."],[11832,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I did not pass by any group of angels except that they commanded me to practice cupping.\""],[11833,"The Prophet ﷺ used to apply kohl with ithmid before sleeping every night."],[11834,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, it weighed heavily upon him and people refrained from speaking to him."],[11835,"I spent the night at the Messenger of God ﷺ, and when the first dawn appeared, he got up and performed Witr with nine units, saying the salam between every two units."],[11836,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever spends a night with light food and drink, praying, the wide-eyed houris will crowd around him until morning.\""],[11837,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for seventeen days shortening the prayer."],[11838,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"What an excellent servant is the cupper! He removes blood, lightens the back, and sharpens the eyesight.\""],[11839,"The Prophet ﷺ placed a purple velvet cloth in his grave."],[11840,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting."],[11841,"The Prophet ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah at night, and he cupped him and gave him his fee."],[11842,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit.”"],[11843,"Umar b. al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side, and he said: “O Messenger of God, if only you would take a bed softer than this.” He replied: “What have I to do with this world? By Him in Whose hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who travels on a scorching day, seeks shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then moves on and leaves it.”"],[11844,"The Prophet ﷺ turned toward Uhud and said: “By Him in Whose hand is my soul, it would not please me if this Uhud were turned into gold for the family of Muhammad, which I would spend in the way of God, and then I die on the day I die leaving two dinars of it—except for two dinars I set aside for a debt, if I owe any.”"],[11845,"The Prophet ﷺ would pass consecutive nights on an empty stomach, while his family could find no evening meal. He said: “Most of their bread was barley bread.”"],[11846,"The Prophet ﷺ died “leaving neither dinar nor dirham, neither slave nor slave-girl; he left his coat of mail pawned to a Jew for thirty measures of barley.”"],[11847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You are a third of the people of Paradise, or half of the people of Paradise.”"],[11848,"When {When comes the help of God and the victory} was revealed until the end of the surah, he said: “The Prophet’s own soul was announced to him when it was revealed.” He said: “He then devoted himself to the utmost striving in the matter of the Hereafter that he had ever done.” After that, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Victory and the help of God have come, and the people of Yemen have come.” A man said: “O Messenger of God, who are the people of Yemen?” He said: “A people with tender hearts and soft hearts; faith is Yemeni, and understanding is Yemeni.”"],[11850,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went on a military expedition and had not finished with the enemy until the afternoon prayer was delayed past its usual time. When he had finished with them, he looked and saw that the afternoon prayer had been delayed into the evening, so he prayed. When he had finished his prayer, he called upon his enemy and said: “O God, whoever kept us from the middle prayer, fill their houses with fire, fill their bellies with fire, and fill their graves with fire.”"],[11851,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on one of his expeditions, and a man said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about the children [of the polytheists]?” The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent and did not answer him a word until he had finished his expedition and went around. Then he saw a boy who had fallen from a litter, and it was him. His caller announced: “Where is the one who asked about the children?” The man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he forbade killing their children and said: “God knows best what they would have done.”"],[11852,"When {When the help of Allah and the conquest comes (i.e., the victory over Makkah)},the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah and said, \"I have been informed of my death.\"So she cried, and he said to her, \"Do not cry, for you will be the first of my family to join me.\"So she smiled, and some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saw her and said, \"We saw you cry and smile.\"She said, \"He told me, 'I have been informed of my death,'\" so I cried.He then said, \"Do not cry, for you will be the first of my family to join me.\"So I smiled."],[11853,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his uncle al-Abbas: “O uncle, make much supplication for well-being.”"],[11854,"Dubaa bt. al-Zubayr b. Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, I intend to perform Hajj; should I make a condition?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “How should I say it?” He said: “Say: At Your service, O God, at Your service; my place of ending is wherever You detain me on the earth.”"],[11855,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The month of Sha'ban is a month of prayers, all of them are performed at Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha.\""],[11856,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Aslam—may God grant them peace—and Ghifar—may God forgive them.”"],[11857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah for seventeen nights shortening the prayer."],[11858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once passed by a piece of food, picked up a bone from it, ate from it, then performed prayer without performing ablution (wudu)."],[11859,"Indeed, Allah has chosen Ibrahim for His intimate friendship, and He has chosen Musa for His direct speech, and He has chosen Muhammad for His visions."],[11860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in ihram, and he said, \"Ihram is more stringent than fasting.\""],[11861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man who had put his foot on the side of a sheep while sharpening his blade, and it was looking at him with its eyes. He said, \"Why not before this? Do you want to kill it twice?\""],[11862,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever does not press his nose with his forehead to the ground when he prostrates, his prayer is not acceptable.\""],[11863,"He used to say the takbir when rising and when placing. I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said, \"May you have no mother! Is that not the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ?\""],[11864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while they were in ihram."],[11865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until his snoring was heard, then prayed and did not repeat the ablution."],[11866,"About the Prophet ﷺ regarding a situation where a woman becomes unconscious while she is menstruating, he said, \"Give charity with a dinar, and if you cannot find that, then with half a dinar.\""],[11867,"The Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah when he was not in ihram."],[11868,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever claims to have seen a dream he did not see will be ordered to tie a knot between two barley grains, and whoever makes an image will be ordered to blow into it, and whoever eavesdrops on people's conversation while they flee from him will have molten lead poured into his ear.\""],[11869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prostrate in anything of the mufassal since he moved to Madinah."],[11870,"A man from the Bedouins died and had no male relatives, but he had a freedman whom he had set free. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Was he not angry when he was angry and pleased when he was pleased?\" They said, \"Yes,\" so he made his freedman inherit his wealth."],[11871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the one who brands on the face."],[11872,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Mecca's conquest, 'Indeed, Allah, may His remembrance be glorified, made Mecca sacred on the day He created the heavens and the earth. It is sacred by the sanctity of Allah until the Day of Judgment. Its game should not be disturbed, its trees should not be cut, its grass should not be uprooted, and its prey should not be chased except by a skilled poet.' So Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said, 'Except for the incense, O Messenger of Allah, the needs of the people and homes require it.' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent for a while and then said, 'Except for incense, for it is permissible.'\""],[11873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground, then said: \"Do you know what this is?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. ʿImran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.\""],[11874,"\"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and the time of sacrifice came, so we shared in a cow seven [people] and in a camel ten [people].\""],[11875,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade that a woman be married upon her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt.\""],[11876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be given in marriage upon the paternal aunt and upon the maternal aunt, and he said: \"If you do that, you sever your ties of kinship.\""],[11877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"One day of a just ruler is better than sixty years of worship, and a legal punishment carried out justly on earth is more purifying for it than forty years of rain.\""],[11878,"I am not a mother for you, that is the prayer of my father Al-Qasim ﷺ ."],[11879,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"had cupping done and gave the cupper a dinar.\""],[11880,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that fruit be sold until it is edible, nor wool on the back, nor milk in the udder.\""],[11881,"Maʿiz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: \"Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or pressed?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Did you do such and such?\" without using a euphemism. He said: \"Yes.\" So he ordered him to be stoned."],[11882,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was \"praying, a sheep came running in front of him, and he raced it until he pressed his belly against the wall.\""],[11883,"The Prophet ﷺ came out during his illness with his head bandaged with a cloth, sat on the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: \"There is no one among the people who is more generous to me with his self and his wealth than Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah. If I were to take a close friend from among the people, I would have taken Abu Bakr, but the brotherhood of Islam is better.\" Then he said: \"No small door shall remain in the mosque but it shall be closed, except the small door of Abu Bakr.\""],[11884,"\"From al-musmat [the solid, compact one].\""],[11885,"\"Whoever dies with the scandalous wind in his belly, Allah will disgrace him before the witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11886,"There is no one from whose words some are not taken and some left except the Prophet ﷺ."],[11887,"from the food of two people competing to show off to each other.\""],[11888,"Beware of rhymed prose in supplication and avoid it, for I knew the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions not doing that."],[11889,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[11890,"Maʿiz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that he had committed zina. He turned away from him. Then he asked his people, \"Is he insane?\" They said, \"There is nothing wrong with him.\" He said, \"Did you do it with her?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he ordered that he be stoned. He was taken away, and he did not pray over him."],[11891,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Snakes are the metamorphosed jinn, just as apes and pigs were metamorphosed from the Children of Israel.\""],[11892,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Safiyyah, \"Make it a condition that my place (of residence) is wherever you confine me.\""],[11893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever imagines in his prayer that he has broken his ablution should not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell.\""],[11894,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj walking.\" He said, \"Let her ride, for Allah ﷻ is not in need of her walking.\""],[11895,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying when Abu Jahl came and forbade him from praying. Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed: 'And let him call his associates; We will call the zabaniyah.' Ibn ʿAbbas said: \"If he had done so, the zabaniyah would have seized him.\""],[11896,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon a bedouin to visit him when he was ill. When he entered upon a sick person to visit him, he would say: \"No harm, purification if Allah wills.\" The bedouin said, \"You say purification? No, rather it is a fever boiling on an old man, visiting him will be the graves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then yes, then.\" The wording is from the hadith of ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. al-Mukhtar."],[11897,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Badr: \"This is Jibril ﷺ , holding the head of a horse with him, upon him the implements of war.\""],[11898,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from Makkah, some young boys from Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib met him. He carried one in front of him and another behind him."],[11899,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done and gave the cupper his wage; had he known it to be impure, he would not have given it."],[11900,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated on a camel, and whenever he came to the corner, he pointed to it."],[11901,"Seven [relations] are prohibited by lineage and seven by marriage, and he recited this verse in Surah al-Nisa."],[11902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God made Makkah sacred; it was not made lawful for anyone before me, nor will it be made lawful for anyone after me. It was made lawful for me only for an hour of the day. Its fresh vegetation is not to be cut, its trees not to be felled, its game not to be startled, and its lost property is not to be picked up except by one who announces it.\" Al-Abbas said: \"O Messenger of God, except for idhkhir, for our goldsmiths.\" He said: \"Except for idhkhir.\""],[11903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Islam is ten portions, and he who has no portion has lost: the testimony that there is no god but God, and it is the creed; the second is prayer, and it is the fitrah; the third is zakat, and it is purification; the fourth is fasting, and it is the shield; the fifth is Hajj, and it is the law; the sixth is jihad, and it is warfare; the seventh is commanding the right, and it is faithfulness; the eighth is forbidding the wrong, and it is the proof; the ninth is the community, and it is affection; and the tenth is obedience, and it is protection.\""],[11904,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"We have no bad example: one who takes back his gift is like one who returns to his vomit.\""],[11905,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever listens to the talk of a people while they dislike him, molten lead will be poured into his ears. Whoever claims to have seen a dream he did not see will be charged to tie a knot between two grains of barley and will be punished, though he will not be able to tie it. And whoever makes an image will be punished until he blows the spirit into it, though he will never blow.\""],[11906,"The Messenger of God ﷺ embraced me and said: \"O God, teach him wisdom.\""],[11907,"He was called Mughith; it is as if I see him going around behind her weeping, his tears flowing onto his beard. The Prophet ﷺ said to al-Abbas: \"O Abbas, are you not amazed at the intensity of Mughith's love for Barirah and the intensity of Barirah's hatred for Mughith?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"If only you would take him back, for he is the father of your child.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, do you command me?\" He said: \"I am only an intercessor.\" She said: \"Then I have no need of him.\""],[11908,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to the watering place and asked for a drink. Al-Abbas said to al-Fadl: \"Go to your mother and bring the Messenger of God ﷺ a drink from her.\" He said: \"Give me to drink.\" He said: \"O Messenger of God, they put their hands in it.\" He said: \"Give me to drink.\" So he drank from it. Then he came to Zamzam while they were giving water and working in it. He said: \"Work, for you are engaged in righteous work.\" Then he said: \"Were it not that you would be overcome, I would go down and place the rope on this,\" meaning his shoulder, and he pointed to his shoulder."],[11909,"\"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ recited aloud, we recited aloud; and whenever he was silent, we were silent.\""],[11910,"The Messenger of God ﷺ set out in Ramadan to Hunayn while the people differed, some fasting and some not. When he was settled on his mount, he called for a vessel of milk or water and drank it. He said: \"Then he placed it on his mount, and the people saw him. Those not fasting said to those fasting: 'Break your fast.'\""],[11911,"that he should enter upon Fatimah. They said, 'Bring something.' He said, 'I do not find anything.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Where is your Hutamiyyah coat of mail?'"],[11912,"The Prophet ﷺ was not asked about anything on the Day of Sacrifice except that he said, 'No harm, no harm.'"],[11913,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What is forbidden by lineage is also forbidden by breastfeeding.'\""],[11914,"The wife of Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'By Allah, I do not find fault with him in character or religion, but I dislike disbelief after Islam.' He said, 'Will you return his garden to him?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'O Thabit, accept the garden and divorce her with one divorce.'"],[11915,"that he should eat it."],[11916,"that the Prophet ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram."],[11918,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram."],[11919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No one among the people has been more excellent to me in the blessing of family and wealth than Abu Bakr. If I were to take a close friend, I would take him, but there is the brotherhood of Islam or faith.'"],[11920,"the Prophet ﷺ: 'If you marry her, then return our daughter to us.'"],[11921,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr while he was in his tent, 'O Allah, I adjure You by Your covenant and Your promise. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today.' Abu Bakr took him by the hand and said, 'Enough, O Messenger of Allah, for you have implored your Lord persistently.' He was wearing the coat of mail, and he came out saying, 'The assembly will be defeated, and they will turn their backs. Nay, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter.'"],[11922,"that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the jallalah (an animal that eats filth), the mujaththamah (an animal tied and used as a target), and drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[11923,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin and breathing into a vessel."],[11924,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'Were it not that dogs are a community among the communities, I would have ordered the killing of every solid black one. So kill the muʿayyanah (the one with two spots above its eyes) among dogs, for it is the accursed one from the jinn.'"],[11925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the battle if he did not encounter the enemy early in the day, until the wind would blow and it would be time for the prayers. He used to say, \"O Allah, with You is the provision, with You is the movement, and there is no power or strength except with Allah.\""],[11926,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, when I eat meat I become aroused toward women and desire takes hold of me, so I have forbidden meat upon myself.” Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you, and do not transgress. Surely Allah does not love the transgressors. And eat of what Allah has provided for you, lawful and good}."],[11927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited an-naqīr, al-muzaffat, ad-dubbāʾ, al-jarr, and al-ḥantam."],[11928,"Al-ʿAbbās was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ on a camel that he had branded on its face with fire. He said, “What is this brand, O ʿAbbās?” He said, “A brand we used to apply in the pre-Islamic era.” He said, “Do not brand with fire.”"],[11929,"A blind man had a slave woman who was the mother of his child. She used to revile the Prophet ﷺ and speak much against him. He would forbid her but she would not stop, and he would rebuke her but she would not be deterred. One night she mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and he could not endure it, so he got up to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned on it until he killed her. In the morning her two children were between her legs, smeared with blood. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he stood and gathered the people, then said, “I adjure by Allah: a man who has a right upon me and did what he did, let him stand.” The blind man came forward wailing and said, “By Allah, O Prophet of Allah, I am the one who did it. She was the mother of my child, and I had from her two sons like pearls. She was indeed a gentle, kind companion to me, but she used to mention you and revile you. I would forbid her but she would not stop, and I would rebuke her but she would not be deterred. Last night she mentioned you and attacked you, and I could not endure it, so I got up to the dagger, placed it in her belly, then leaned on it until I killed her.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “I bear witness that her blood is wasted.”"],[11930,"“Our wine on that day was faḍīkh, and it was forbidden on the day it was forbidden, and it is nothing but your faḍīkh.”"],[11931,"That the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , used to recite in the Fajr prayer."],[11932,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men.”"],[11933,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men."],[11934,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed effeminate men and women who imitate men, and he expelled so-and-so."],[11935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Expel the effeminate men from your houses.” He said: And the Prophet ﷺ expelled an effeminate man, and ʿUmar expelled an effeminate man."],[11936,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The blood money of a mukātab is according to the portion of him that has been freed: the blood money of a free man, and according to the portion of him that remains enslaved: the blood money of a slave.”"],[11937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning a mukātab that he should pay according to the portion of him that has been freed the blood money of a free man."],[11938,"A mukātab was brought before the Prophet ﷺ and he said, “He pays for what he has paid of his kitāba the blood money of a free man, and for what he has not paid the blood money of a slave.”"],[11939,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The blood money of a mukatab (a slave who has contracted to purchase his freedom) is according to the extent of his freedom: the blood money of a free man for the portion that he has paid toward his freedom, and the blood money of a slave for the portion that remains in slavery.”"],[11940,"that he should slaughter himself or his child, then let him slaughter a ram.” Then he recited: “Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example.”"],[11941,"that the Prophet ﷺ “forbade selling animals on credit.”"],[11942,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Treat your children equally in gift-giving; if I were to prefer anyone, I would have preferred women.”"],[11943,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed his ihram garment at al-Tanʿim while he was in a state of ihram.”"],[11944,"When one of his daughters was proposed to, the Prophet ﷺ would come to her private chamber and say: “So-and-so is proposing to so-and-so.” If she stabbed the wall, he would not marry her off; but if she did not stab the wall, he would give her in marriage."],[11945,"that when the Prophet ﷺ married off Fatimah, he said: “O ʿAli, do not go in to your wife until you give them something.” ʿAli said: “I have nothing, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Give her your Hutamiyyah armor.”"],[11946,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “annulled the marriage of a virgin and a previously married woman whose fathers married them off against their will.”"],[11947,"that the Prophet ﷺ “was cupped and gave the cupper his wages.” “The name of Abu ʿAzzah is al-Hakam b. Tahman.”"],[11948,"A man from the Ansar had two stallions, and he brought them into a wall and closed the door on them. He then came to the Prophet ﷺ and wanted him to pray for him. The Prophet ﷺ was sitting, and there were some Ansar with him. He said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I have come with a need, and I had two stallions that I brought into a wall and closed the door on them. I would like you to pray that Allah makes them obedient to me.\" He said to his companions, \"Get up with us.\" So he went until he came to the door, and he said, \"Open.\" The man hesitated because he was worried about the Prophet ﷺ , but he said, \"Open.\" So he opened the door, and one of the stallions was close to the door. When the Prophet ﷺ saw it, he prostrated to it and said, \"Bring me something more powerful than it, and I will grant you what you want.\" So he brought some rubbish and he held it against the stallion's head, and the stallion submitted to him. Then he walked to the farthest corner of the wall to the other stallion, and when he saw it, it fell prostrate to him. He said to the man, \"Bring me something more powerful than it.\" So he held its head against something and it submitted to him. He said, \"Go, for they will not disobey you.\" When the companions of the Prophet ﷺ saw this, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, these two stallions that do not have reason prostrated to you, should we not then prostrate to you?\" He said, \"I do not command anyone to prostrate to another. Even if I were to command someone to prostrate to another, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.\""],[11949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You must keep to the first row and the right side, and beware of praying between the pillars.”"],[11950,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud in some prayers and remained silent in others. So we recite in the prayers in which the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited, and we remain silent in the prayers in which he remained silent.” It was said to him: “Perhaps the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited to himself.” He became angry and said: “Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be suspected? Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be suspected?”"],[11951,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “that he fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam.”"],[11952,"Three men came to the Prophet ﷺ. The first said, 'Peace be upon you.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you, and the mercy of Allah.' Then the second came and said, 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.' Then the third came and said, 'Peace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings.' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'And upon you.' Abu al-Fata was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you gave more to so-and-so and so-and-so, but you did not give my son anything.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We did not find any addition for him, so we replied to him with the like of what he said.'"],[11954,"He said: “Circumcision is a sunnah for men and an honor for women.”"],[11955,"From Ibn Abbas, I do not think but that he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ; he said: “The prayer is in the dwellings.”"],[11956,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed a man seeks a need, and Allah withholds it from him because what is better for him, and he accuses people, wronging them, and says, 'Who will satisfy me?'”"],[11957,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Three have no reckoning regarding what they eat, if it is lawful: the fasting person, the one who partakes of the pre-dawn meal, and the one stationed in the path of Allah.”"],[11958,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Soon you will see human devils; one of them hears a hadith and spreads it to others, and so he turns the people away from listening to it from the companion who narrated it.”"],[11959,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, Exalted is He, supported me with the sharpest-tongued and strongest-armed of the Arabs, the Banu Qaylah, the Aws and the Khazraj.”"],[11961,"“Allah gave speech to Musa, intimate friendship to Ibrahim, and the vision of Him to Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[11962,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not from us who performs ablution after the ritual bath.”"],[11963,"When the news of the death of Ja'far b. Abi Talib came, the Prophet ﷺ entered upon Asma' bt. 'Umays and placed 'Abdullah and Muhammad, the two sons of Ja'far, on his thigh, then said: “Jibril informed me that Allah, Exalted is He, caused Ja'far to be martyred, and that he has two wings with which he flies among the angels in Paradise.” Then he said: “O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his children.”"],[11964,"“From prophet to prophet until I was brought forth as a prophet.”"],[11965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the privy, then came out, and there was a covered vessel of water. He said, 'Who did this?' 'Abdullah said, 'I did.' He said, 'O Allah, teach him the interpretation of the Qur'an.'"],[11966,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Dubāʿa: “Perform Hajj and stipulate conditions and say: My place of dissolution is wherever You withhold me.”"],[11967,"That the Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[11968,"“A man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give half a dinar in charity.”"],[11969,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he disliked combining (in marriage) a paternal aunt and a maternal aunt, and two paternal aunts, and two maternal aunts."],[11970,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aisha and Hafsah while they were fasting. Then he left and came back while they were eating. He asked, \"Were you not fasting?\" They replied, \"Yes, we were, but we were given this food as a gift and we liked it, so we ate from it.\" He said, \"Fast for a day in its place.\""],[11971,"This verse was revealed on the day of Badr, \"And it is not for a prophet to take captives\". It was revealed regarding a red camel that was lost on the day of Badr. Some people said, \"Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it.\" So Allah revealed, \"And it is not for a prophet to take captives.\""],[11972,"From Ibn ʿAbbās regarding {It is not for a prophet to be dishonest}: He said: It concerned a red velvet cloak that was lost on the day of Badr, and they said he took it, so there was revealed {And it is not for a prophet to be dishonest}."],[11973,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning a woman in post-natal bleeding: “She performs ghusl, then enters ihrām, and carries out all the rites except the tawāf of the House.”"],[11974,"The poor people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Indeed, the rich people fast as we fast and pray as we pray, but they also have wealth from which they give charity and free slaves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"When you pray, say 'Subhanallah' thirty-three times, 'Alhamdulillah' thirty-three times, and 'Allahu Akbar' thirty-four times.\""],[11975,"“Your return is to Paradise.”"],[11976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no confinement after Sūrat al-Nisāʾ.”"],[11977,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited {A day that will make children grey-haired} and said: That is the Day of Resurrection, and that is a day when Allah, glorified be His mention, says to Adam: “Arise and send a delegation from your progeny to the Fire.” He said: “Of how many, O Lord?” He said: “From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine, and one will be saved.” That weighed heavily on the Muslims, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perceived that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he saw that in their faces: “The children of Adam are many, and Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj are from the children of Adam, and none of them dies until a thousand men from his own loins inherit from him. In them and their like is a shield for you.”"],[11978,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was consoled for his daughter Ruqayya, the wife of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān, he said: “Praise be to Allah; burying daughters is from the noble deeds.”"],[11979,"ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib said: “O Messenger of Allah, the Qurʾān slips away from my chest.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I teach you words by which Allah will benefit you and benefit whom you teach?” He said: “Yes, may my father and mother be your ransom.” He said: “Pray on the night of Friday four rakʿahs. In the first rakʿah recite the Opening of the Book and Yā Sīn; in the second, the Opening of the Book and Ḥā Mīm al-Dukhān; in the third, the Opening of the Book and Alif Lām Mīm Tanzīl al-Sajdah; and in the fourth, the Opening of the Book and Tabārak al-Mufaṣṣal. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah and extol Him, send blessings upon the prophets, and seek forgiveness for the believers. Then say: O Allah, have mercy on me by abandonment of sins forever as long as You keep me alive, and have mercy on me from burdening myself with what does not concern me, and grant me good insight into what pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honour and might that is not sought, I ask You, O Allah, O Merciful, by Your majesty and the light of Your countenance, to make my heart adhere to love of Your Book as You taught me, and grant me to recite it in the manner that pleases You from me. I ask You to illuminate my sight with the Book, loosen my tongue by it, relieve my heart through it, expand my chest by it, employ my body with it, strengthen me for that, and help me in it, for none helps me to good other than You, and none grants success to it except You. Do that for three Fridays, or five, or seven, and you will memorise it by Allah’s permission, and it never misses a believer.” Afterwards he came to the Prophet ﷺ after seven Fridays and informed him of his memorisation of the Qurʾān and the hadith. The Prophet ﷺ said: “A believer, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah! Teach Abū Ḥasan, teach Abū Ḥasan!”"],[11980,"That the Prophet ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, and they took booty. Among them was a man who said to them: “I am not one of you. I fell in love with a woman and followed her, so let me look at her, then do whatever seems right to you.” There was a tall, dark-complexioned woman. He said to her: “Accept Islam, Ḥubaysh, before life runs out. Have you considered, if I followed you and caught up with you with ornaments, or reached you at al-Khawāniq, was it not right that a lover should attain, one who undertook the night journeys and the midday heat?” She said: “Yes, may I be your ransom.” He said: They brought him forward and struck his neck. Then the woman came, fell upon him, let out one or two gasps, and died. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the news, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Was there not among you a merciful man?”"],[11981,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, I adjure you by God and kinship: we have eaten 'ilhiz'—meaning hair and blood.\" Then God ﷻ sent down: {And We seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves to their Lord, nor did they entreat Him}."],[11982,"One thousand men from Banu Sulaym witnessed with the Messenger of God ﷺ the day of the conquest of Makkah."],[11983,"Regarding His saying {And fear a day in which you will be returned to God}, \"It is the last verse that was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[11984,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, they were among the most dishonest people in measuring, so God ﷻ sent down {Woe to those who give short measure}, and after that they measured well."],[11985,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Khaybar, {When the victory of God and the conquest comes} was revealed to him, to the end of the story. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O 'Ali b. Abi Talib, O Fatimah, the victory of God and the conquest has come. {And you see people entering the religion of God in multitudes, then glorify the praise of your Lord and ask His forgiveness. Indeed, He is ever accepting of repentance}—bearing in mind that after me there will be jihad among the believers.\" He said, \"Against what shall we fight the believers who say, 'We believe'?\" He said, \"Against innovations in religion when they act according to opinion, and there is no opinion in religion. Religion is only from the Lord—His commands and His prohibitions.\" 'Ali said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you think if a matter arises for which no Qur'an was revealed and no Sunnah was specified from you?\" He said, \"Make it a consultation among the worshippers among the believers, and do not decide it by the opinion of a single individual. If I were to appoint a successor, no one would be more entitled to it than you because of your early entry into Islam, your kinship to the Messenger of God ﷺ, your being his son-in-law, and with you is the mistress of the women of the believers. And before that, there was the kindness of Abu Talib toward me; the Qur'an was revealed while I was keen to care for his children in return.\""],[11986,"'Ali said, \"O Messenger of God, you said to me on the day of Uhud, when I was kept from martyrdom and those who were martyred were martyred, 'Martyrdom is behind you.' He said, 'How will you be patient when this is dyed from this?' and he gestured with his hand to his beard and head.\" 'Ali said, \"Since you have made clear what you have made clear, that is not among the occasions of patience but rather among the occasions of glad tidings and honor.\""],[11987,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The sacrificial animal was prescribed for me and not prescribed for you, and I was commanded to pray the Duha prayer and you were not commanded to.\""],[11988,"Abu Barzah al-Aslami was a soothsayer who judged among the Jews in matters they brought to him for arbitration. Some Muslims brought a dispute to him for arbitration, so God ﷻ sent down: {Have you not seen those who claim that they believed in what was revealed to you and what was revealed before you, wishing to take their disputes to the tyrant while they were commanded to reject him} up to His saying {We intended nothing but good}."],[11989,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who drinks from a vessel of gold only pours into his belly the fire of Hell.\""],[11990,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God ﷻ created one hundred mercies, one of which He distributed among creation, and ninety-nine remain until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[11991,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The barefoot person has more right to the middle of the road than the one wearing sandals.\""],[11992,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the expedition of Tabuk and performed 'Umrah, and when he descended from the pass of 'Usfan, he commanded his companions to lean back against the mountain pass until he returned to them. He went and stopped at his mother's grave, and he conversed privately with his Lord for a long time. Then he wept, and his weeping intensified, and they wept because of his weeping. They said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ has not wept in this place except that something has happened in his community that they cannot bear.\" When they wept, he stood and returned to them and said, \"What makes you weep?\" They said, \"O Prophet of God, we wept because of your weeping. We thought that perhaps something had happened in your community that they cannot bear.\" He said, \"No, though some of it has occurred. But I stopped at my mother's grave and asked God to permit me to intercede for her on the Day of Resurrection, but God refused to permit me. So I felt mercy for her—she is my mother—and I wept. Then Jibril ﷺ came to me and said, {And Abraham's seeking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him. But when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of God, he disowned him}. So disown your mother as Abraham disowned his father. I felt mercy for her—she is my mother—and I called upon my Lord to lift four things from my community. He lifted two and refused to lift two. I called upon my Lord to lift from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, and that He not divide them into factions, and that He not make them taste the might of one another. God lifted from them stoning from the sky and drowning from the earth, but God refused to lift two: killing and chaos. He turned to his mother's grave only because she was buried under such-and-such, and 'Usfan was theirs.\""],[11993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called the two prostrations of forgetfulness al-Murāghamatayn (the two that make Satan choke with rage)."],[11994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not pray facing a grave, and do not pray upon a grave.\""],[11995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dug the trench while his companions had tied stones to their bellies out of hunger. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said: \"Have you been shown a man who can give us a meal?\" A man said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"As for no, go ahead and show us to him.\" So they went to the man, and there he was in the trench working on his portion of it. His wife sent word: \"Come, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come to us.\" The man came running and said: \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for him.\" He had a she-goat with her kid, so he jumped to her. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The kid is behind us.\" So he slaughtered the kid. The woman went to some flour she had, kneaded it, and baked it. She brought the pot and crumbled her large bowl, then brought it near to the Prophet ﷺ and his companions. The Prophet ﷺ placed his finger in it and said: \"In the name of Allah. O Allah, bless it. Eat.\" They ate from it until they had their fill, yet they ate only a third of it and two-thirds remained. Then he sent those ten who were with him: \"Go and send us your number.\" So they went, and those ten came in their place. They ate from it until they were full. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood and supplicated for the lady of the house, and pronounced blessings upon her and her household. Then they walked to the trench, and he said: \"Take us to Salman.\" There was a rock in front of him that he had been unable to break. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Leave me, so that I may be the first to strike it.\" He said: \"In the name of Allah,\" and struck it, and a piece, a third of it, fell off. He said: \"Allah is greatest! The palaces of Rome, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\" Then he struck again, and another piece fell off. He said: \"Allah is greatest! The palaces of Persia, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah!\" At that point the hypocrites said: \"We are digging a trench for our own protection, and he is promising us the palaces of Persia and Rome!\""],[11996,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting."],[11997,"The Prophet ﷺ set out in Ramadan at the time of the conquest and fasted until, when he was at Qudayd, he broke the fast, and his companions broke their fast, until they entered Makkah. The wording is that of Sulayman b. Harb."],[11998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked at a brisk pace (ramal) in his Hajj for the first three rounds from the Black Stone to the Black Stone, and walked the [remaining] four."],[11999,"The Prophet ﷺ was shrouded in two white garments and a red one."],[12000,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gifted one hundred camels to Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, with a silver nose ring.\""],[12001,"The Muslims captured one of the prominent men of the idolaters and killed him. Then they asked to ransom him, but the Prophet ﷺ forbade them to sell his corpse."],[12002,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam al-Zuhri over the collection of zakah. He took Abu Rafiʿ with him as a follower. Abu Rafiʿ came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about it. He said: \"O Abu Rafiʿ, charity is unlawful for Muhammad and for the family of Muhammad, and the client of a people is one of them.\""],[12003,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Leave Abu Qatadah and his spoils.\""],[12004,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Jibril ﷺ conversing privately with him, the horizon of the sky split open. Jibril began to draw near to the earth and sway. Suddenly an angel appeared before the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, Allah commands you to choose between being a prophet-servant and a king-prophet.\" The narrator said: Jibril motioned to me with his hand to be humble, and I knew that he was a sincere adviser to me, so I said: \"A servant-prophet.\" That angel then ascended to the sky. I said: \"O Jibril, I had wanted to ask you about this, but I saw in your state something that distracted me from asking. Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said: \"This is Israfil. Allah created him, on the day He created him, standing before Him with his feet together, not raising his gaze. Between him and the Lord are seventy veils of light, any of which, if he drew near to it, would burn him. Before him is a tablet. When Allah, may He be exalted, decrees something in the heaven or in the earth, that revelation ascends and strikes his forehead. He looks: if it pertains to my duty, He commands me with it; if it pertains to Mikhaʾil's duty, He commands him with it; and if it pertains to the Angel of Death's duty, He commands him with it.\" I said: \"O Jibril, what are you in charge of?\" He said: \"The wind and the hosts.\" I said: \"What is Mikhaʾil in charge of?\" He said: \"Vegetation and rain.\" I said: \"What is the Angel of Death in charge of?\" He said: \"Taking souls. I did not think he had descended except for the coming of the Hour. What you saw from me was only out of fear of the Hour's coming.\""],[12005,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he stipulated that the land, and all that was yellow and white, meaning gold and silver, belonged to him. The people of Khaybar said to him: \"We know the land better, so give it to us on condition that we work it and have half of the fruit, and you have the other half.\" He mentioned that he gave it to them on that condition. When the time came for the dates to be cut, he sent Ibn Rawahah to them, and he estimated the dates—this is what the people of Madinah call khars (estimation). He said: \"In this there is such-and-such and such-and-such.\" They said: \"You have demanded too much from us, O Ibn Rawahah.\" He said: \"Then I will undertake the estimation of the dates and give you half of what I have said.\" They said: \"This is the truth, and by it the heavens and the earth are established. We are satisfied that you take what you have said.\""],[12006,"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen."],[12007,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"Whatever of the lower garment is below the ankles is in the Fire.\""],[12008,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"A man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and claimed that he had had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to give a dinar in charity; if he could not find one, then half a dinar.\""],[12009,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding \"the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: he should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12010,"The Prophet ﷺ stood over the slain of Badr and said: \"May Allah reward you on my behalf, O band, with evil. You betrayed me though I was trustworthy, and you called me a liar though I was truthful.\" Then he turned to Abu Jahl b. Hisham and said: \"This one was more insolent toward Allah than Pharaoh. When Pharaoh was certain of destruction, he declared Allah's oneness, but when this one was certain of death, he called upon al-Lat and al-'Uzza.\""],[12011,"Salih, the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , seized the property of the people of Khaybar, except for themselves and their children. The Prophet then asked for the whereabouts of their utensils that were used in their weddings, to which they replied that the Prophet had expelled them and they had spent it. The Prophet said, \"See what you say, for if you hide it from me, I will consider it as your blood and that of your descendants.\" Then he called two men from the Ansar and said to them, \"Go to such and such a place and look for a hut with a patch on its roof. Remove the patch and bring me the utensils.\" They went and returned with the utensils. The Messenger of Allah struck their necks and sent for their offspring. Safiyya, who was their bride, was brought to him. He ordered Bilal to take her to his house. Bilal went with her to the house of the Messenger of Allah. He passed by her husband and brother, who were killed. When he returned to the Messenger of Allah, he said, \"Glory be to Allah! O Bilal, why did you bring a virgin girl and pass by two killed men while she saw them? Don't you have any mercy?\" Bilal replied, \"I intended to burn her chest.\" The Messenger of Allah then entered with her and spent the night with her. Abu Ayub brought his sword and sat next to the mattress. He said, \"If I had heard a shepherd or a monk, I would have been close to the Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet then went to Bilal's house and asked, \"Who is this?\" Abu Ayub said, \"I am Abu Ayub.\" The Prophet asked, \"Why are you here at this time?\" Abu Ayub replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, I brought a virgin girl and you had killed her husband and brother, so I was concerned for your safety. I thought I would be close to the Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, Abu Ayub,\" three times. The people then discussed this matter, with some saying it was his secret and others saying she was his wife. When they were leaving, they said, \"Look at the Messenger of Allah, if he covers her, then she is his wife, and if he doesn't cover her, then she is his secret.\" The Messenger of Allah covered her, put her on his knee, and said, \"Mount.\" The Messenger of Allah honored her by putting her foot on his knee, and he put his knee on her thigh, and they rode off together. Before that, he had offered her the choice to either be set free or be married to him, and she chose to be set free and married. And so he did."],[12012,"The Prophet ﷺ was distracted from the 'Asr prayer until the sun had set. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They distracted us from the middle prayer. May Allah fill their graves and their homes with fire.\""],[12013,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on a camel and touched the corner with his staff."],[12014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered one hundred camels as sacrificial animals. He slaughtered sixty of them himself and commanded a man from among his companions, who slaughtered the remaining forty. He ordered him to take a piece from each camel, string them on a thread, cook them in a pot, and then he ate from it and drank the broth."],[12015,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"Do not raise your hands except at seven places; when starting the prayer, when entering Al-Masjid Al-Haram and looking at the Kaaba, when standing on Safa and Marwa, when standing with the people on 'Arafah night and during the Stoning of the Jamarat.\""],[12016,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me from Muzdalifah to Mina among the weak members of his household. He took hold of the upper arm of each one of us and said: \"Do not throw the pebbles at the Jamrah until the sun has risen.\""],[12017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled during the month of Ramadan. His companions complained to him of thirst, so he called for water and drank, and then some of the people broke their fast while others continued to fast. Neither of the two groups criticized what the other had done."],[12018,"Regarding His saying: \"They ask you what they should spend. Say: 'The surplus'\" (Q 2:219), he said: \"What is beyond the needs of one's dependents.\""],[12019,"\"The first of them will be detained for the last of them.\""],[12020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived during the truce that was between him and the polytheists, while the polytheists were at the door of the assembly house, near the Black Stone. They had been saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions were suffering from hardship and weakness. When they touched the Black Stone, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"They have been saying that you are suffering from hardship and weakness, so walk briskly (ramal) for three circuits so that they may see that you have strength.\" When they touched the Black Stone, they lifted their legs and walked briskly. Then some of them said to others: \"Do they claim that they are suffering from hardship and weakness? They are not content with walking until they run at a fast pace.\""],[12021,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family from Muzdalifah at night, then he came to us one by one, striking us on our thighs. I was one of those he struck on the thigh. Then he said: \"O my son, do not throw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah until the sun has risen.\""],[12022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set free on the day of Taʾif those slaves of the polytheists who came out to him."],[12023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House on his camel and touched the corner with his staff. Then he came to the water station, and his paternal cousins were drawing water from it. He called for a drink, so a bucket was raised to him and he drank from it. Then he said: \"Were it not that people might think it and adopt it as a ritual, and then fight you over it, I would draw water with you.\" Then he went to Safa and Marwah and circumambulated them on his camel."],[12024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah al-Ansari, Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib, and Zayd b. Harithah. ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah lagged behind, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What kept you?\" He said: \"Friday, O Messenger of Allah—I am attending the Friday prayer, then I will set out.\" He said: \"A single morning or evening journey in the path of Allah is better than this world and all it contains.\" So he set out immediately."],[12025,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a woman who had been killed on the day of the Trench and said: \"Who killed this woman?\" A man said: \"I did, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Why?\" He said: \"She fought me for my sword.\" He then remained silent."],[12026,"\"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen. The Emigrants were sixty-odd men, and the Helpers were two hundred and thirty-six men. The bearer of the banner of the Emigrants was ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ, and the bearer of the banner of the Helpers was Saʿd b. ʿUbadah ؓ.\""],[12027,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: \"The number of the people of Badr was three hundred and thirteen. The Emigrants were sixty-odd men, and the Helpers were two hundred and thirty-six men. The bearer of the banner of the Emigrants was ʿAli b. Abi Talib ؓ, and the bearer of the banner of the Helpers was Saʿd b. ʿUbadah ؓ.\""],[12028,"ʿAmmar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: my father narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas who said: \"The distinguishing mark of the angels on the day of Badr was white turbans, which they had let down to their backs, and on the day of Hunayn it was red turbans. The angels did not fight on any day except the day of Badr; they were only there as numbers and reinforcement, not striking.\""],[12029,"ʿAmmar b. Abi Malik al-Janbi narrated to us: my father narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from Miqsam from Ibn Abbas ؓ who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped during Ramadan and fainted, and for that reason he disliked it.\""],[12030,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while fasting and in a state of ihram.\""],[12031,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebbles at the Jamrah on the day of sacrifice, then slaughtered, then shaved his head.\""],[12032,"The day of Badr was on the twenty-seventh of Ramadan."],[12033,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who has intercourse with a pregnant woman.\""],[12034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver the sermon."],[12035,"Two slaves went out on the day of al-Ta'if while the Prophet ﷺ was besieging them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set them free."],[12036,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Maymunah bt. al-Harith, and she delegated her affair to al-Abbas, so he gave her to him in marriage."],[12037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"I saw the angels washing them (the two of them).\""],[12038,"Regarding His saying: \"The month of Ramadan in which the Qur'an was sent down\" and His saying: \"Indeed, We sent it down on a blessed night,\" he said: \"It was sent down in Ramadan on the Night of Decree, on a blessed night, all at once, then it was sent down gradually at the positions of the stars over the months and days.\""],[12039,"When the Messenger of Allah returned from Uhud, the women of the Ansar cried over their martyrs. The Prophet ﷺ was informed of this and he said, \"But Hamza has no one to mourn him.\" So, the women of the Ansar returned and said to their womenfolk, \"Do not cry for anyone until you lament for Hamza.\" He said about them until this day, \"Do not cry except for Hamza.\""],[12040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us and took off his sandals, so we took off our sandals. When he finished the prayer, he said: \"Why did you take off your sandals?\" They said: \"We saw you take them off, so we took ours off.\" He said: \"I found wetness in them.\""],[12041,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver sermons to them while traveling, leaning on his bow."],[12042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver sermons to them while traveling, leaning on his bow."],[12043,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite the Opening of the Book (Surah al-Fatihah) over the funeral prayer."],[12044,"Ali b. Abi Talib was the standard-bearer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr. The standard-bearer of the Muhajirun was Ali, in all the battles, and Qays b. Sa'd b. Ubadah was the standard-bearer of Ali."],[12045,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray twenty units (rak'ahs) and the odd (witr) during Ramadan."],[12046,"That the letter of the Messenger of God ﷺ to the disbelievers was: {Come to a word that is equitable between us and you} until the end of the verse."],[12047,"When Abu Sufyan and his companions descended upon the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud, he said to his companions, \"I saw in a dream my sword Dhu al-Faqar broke, and I saw cows being slaughtered, and that is a calamity, and I saw upon me my coat of mail, and it is your city—they will not reach it, God willing.\""],[12048,"That on the day of Badr, the Messenger of God ﷺ had one hundred camels, and with him were two horsemen: one ridden by al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad and the other by Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and Sahl b. Hunayf. He said: His companions took turns riding the camels along the way, and the Messenger of God ﷺ and Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, \"took turns riding a camel.\""],[12049,"\"Al-'Uzza was in Batn Nahlah, al-Lat was in al-Ta'if, and Manat was in Qudayd.\" He said: 'Ali b. al-Ja'd said, \"Batn Nahlah is the garden of Banu 'Amir.\""],[12050,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about that, \"so he ordered him to cover his head and to take for him some trees from this 'aljan and place it upon his legs.\""],[12051,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw Hanzala b. al-Rahib and Hamza being washed by the angels.\""],[12052,"From Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Khalid b. al-Walid and 'Ali b. Abi Talib to Yemen. He placed 'Ali in command of the Muhajirun and placed Khalid in command of the Bedouins. He said: \"And if there is fighting, 'Ali is in command of all the people.\""],[12053,"That the Prophet ﷺ would \"throw the pebbles when the sun had declined, such that when he finished throwing them, he prayed Zuhr.\""],[12054,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the stoning of Ma'iz b. Malik, they came to him and informed him that they had done so. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"He has repented with such a repentance that if a tax-collector had repented with it, it would have been accepted from him.\""],[12055,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib in Paradise with two wings, flying wherever he wished.\""],[12056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The anger of God Almighty has intensified upon the one who claims that he is the king of kings.\""],[12057,"\"The Conquest was witnessed by one thousand eight hundred from Juhayna, one thousand from Muzayna, nine hundred from Banu Sulaym, four hundred and some from Banu Ghifar, and four hundred and some from Aslam.\""],[12058,"«Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ six children: ʿAbd Allah, al-Qasim, Ruqayyah, Umm Kulthum, and Fatimah; and Mariyah the Copt bore him Ibrahim.»"],[12059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «O company of the Ansar, who is your chief?» They said: Jadd b. Qays, and we honor him. He said: «He is not your chief; rather, your chief is ʿAmr b. al-Jamuh.» And he was generous."],[12060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to «throw the pebbles at the time of the sun’s decline, such that when he finished his throwing he prayed Zuhr.»"],[12061,"When the Prophet ﷺ stopped at al-Taʾif, he ordered a caller, and he called out: «Any slave who comes out is free.» Two slaves came out to him, and he set them free."],[12062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «O company of merchants, is any one of you unable, when he returns from his market, to recite ten verses, so that Allah writes for him a good deed for each verse?»"],[12063,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to throw the pebbles until the sun rose.»"],[12064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family on from Muzdalifah, then he said: «Do not throw the Jamrah until the sun rises.»"],[12065,"The Prophet ﷺ used to «wipe the sweat from his face during prayer.»"],[12066,"«ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud came upon Abu Jahl on the day of Badr while he was fallen, and he drew his sword and struck his neck, and his head flew off. Then he took his spoils and came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him that he had killed Abu Jahl. He made him swear by Allah three times, and he swore, and he gave him his spoils.»"],[12067,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed with tranquility upon him.» And he mentioned the hadith."],[12068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to «pray Zuhr and ʿAsr at Mina on the Day of Tarwiyah.»"],[12069,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed five prayers at Mina.»"],[12070,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr with [Surat] Bara'ah, then he sent Ali after him and he took it. Abu Bakr said, \"Has something happened concerning me?\" He said, \"No, you are my companion in the cave and at the Pond, and no one should deliver [it] on my behalf except me or Ali.\""],[12071,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr and ordered him to proclaim these words, then he sent Ali after him. While Abu Bakr was on part of the road, he heard the grumbling sound of the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr came out startled, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behold it was Ali. He handed him the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He appointed him over the pilgrimage season and ordered Ali to proclaim these words. They both set off and performed the Hajj. Ali stood during the days of Tashriq and proclaimed, \"The protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger is free from every polytheist. So travel freely in the land for four months. No polytheist should perform Hajj after this year, and no one should circumambulate the House naked, and none will enter Paradise except a believer.\" Ali kept proclaiming it, and when his voice became hoarse, Abu Hurayrah stood up and proclaimed it."],[12072,"A man had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to give half a dinar in charity."],[12073,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating: \"He should give a dinar or half a dinar in charity.\""],[12077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has intercourse with his wife during her menstruation should give a dinar in charity, and whoever has intercourse with her when the blood has stopped but she has not bathed should give half a dinar.\" All of that is from the Prophet ﷺ."],[12078,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife while she was menstruating: \"If it was fresh blood, he should give a dinar in charity, and if it was yellowish, then half a dinar.\""],[12079,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying while donkeys were fighting in front of him."],[12080,"The Prophet ﷺ had cupping done while he was fasting and in ihram."],[12081,"That the Prophet ﷺ has been cupped while fasting."],[12082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while he was in ihram and fasting."],[12083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while he was in ihram and had cupping done while he was fasting."],[12084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while he was in ihram."],[12085,"When the evening meal is served and the prayer is established, begin with the evening meal."],[12086,"Al-Sa'b b. Jaththamah gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a wild donkey as a gift. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Return it to him, for we are in ihram.'"],[12087,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A woman may not grant permission in her husband's house except with his permission, nor may she leave her bed to pray voluntarily except with his permission.'"],[12088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in a red Najrani suit that he used to wear and a shirt."],[12089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in three garments: in his shirt in which he died and an Anbijani suit."],[12090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in a suit that he used to wear and a shirt. Al-Fadl and a man from the Ansar washed him, and the Ansari was pouring water on them and washing under the garment. He was washed while wearing his shirt, which was not removed from him until he had been washed."],[12091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and mannish women."],[12092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' A man said, 'And those who shorten?' He said, 'O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.' A man said, 'And those who shorten?' He said the third or fourth time, 'And those who shorten.'"],[12093,"\"A donation of money never decreases, nor does a servant extend his hand with a charity except that it falls into the hand of Allah before it reaches the beggar, and a servant does not open a door of asking for something out of wealth except that Allah opens a door of poverty on him.\""],[12094,"The first to embrace Islam was Ali."],[12095,"From Ibn Abbas: Hamzah was killed on the day of Uhud, and a man from the Ansar was killed with him. Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib came with two garments to shroud Hamzah in, but there was no shroud for the Ansari. The Prophet ﷺ drew lots between the two garments, then each of them was shrouded in one garment."],[12096,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House and supplicated in its corners, then he came out and prayed two rak'ahs."],[12097,"The Prophet ﷺ ransomed the captives of Badr, and the ransom for each one of them was four thousand. ʿUqbah b. Abī Muʿayṭ was killed before the ransom. ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib went to him and executed him in retaliation. He said, 'Who will care for the children, O Muḥammad?' He said, 'The Fire.'"],[12098,"In His statement, \"And [remember] when those who disbelieved plotted against you to restrain you or kill you or evict you [from Makkah]. But they plan, and Allah plans. And Allah is the best of planners.\" Quraysh consulted one night in Makkah. Some of them said, \"Let's establish a case against him with evidence, seeking to discredit the Prophet ﷺ.\" Some of them said, \"Kill him!\" And some of them said, \"Expel him!\" Allah informed His Prophet ﷺ about this. Ali stayed in the bed of the Prophet ﷺ that night while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left until he reached the cave. The polytheists guarded it, thinking he was the Prophet ﷺ. When they woke up in the morning, they went after him and when they saw Ali, Allah foiled their plan. They asked, \"Where is your companion?\" He replied, \"I do not know.\" They searched for his footprints and when they reached the mountain, they became disoriented. They climbed the mountain and passed by the cave where they found spider webs covering its entrance. They stayed there for three [days]."],[12099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd to al-Ṭāʾif, and a man shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'How similar this is to the companion of Yā Sīn.'"],[12100,"A man would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from those who had set out, having mentioned only the Ḥajj, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, 'Go and exit the state of iḥrām with an ʿUmrah after he had performed ṭawāf.' The man would say, 'O Messenger of Allah, I set out intending only the Ḥajj.' He would say, 'It is not the Ḥajj, but rather it is an ʿUmrah.'"],[12101,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'There are no forty people who intercede for a believer except that Allah accepts their intercession.'"],[12102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us this supplication as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qur'an: 'O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Jahannam, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the false messiah al-Dajjāl, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave.'"],[12103,"He said to him, 'O young man, beware of reviling the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for it is destructive.'"],[12104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the illness of the sick, I would have delayed the ʿatamah prayer.'"],[12105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The one whose counsel is sought is entrusted.'"],[12107,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he drank, would breathe twice."],[12108,"\"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and then stood on his left side, so he took hold of me and made me stand on his right side.\""],[12109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no leader appointed over ten people except that he will be questioned about them on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[12110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the water distribution point, and a woman came with a son of hers and said, 'My son wants to go on a military expedition, and I am preventing him.' He said, 'Do not leave your mother until she gives you permission, or death takes her, for that is greater for your reward.'"],[12111,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Prayer is not to be performed facing a grave, nor upon a grave.'"],[12112,"\"Narrated by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Whoever makes a vow but does not specify it, then its expiation is like the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow in disobedience to Allah, then its expiation is like the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that they cannot afford, then its expiation is the expiation of an oath. And whoever makes a vow that they can afford, then let them fulfill it.'\""],[12113,"Ibn Abbas, Abdur-Rahman ibn Al-Azhar, and Miswar ibn Makhrama said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade praying after Asr prayer.\""],[12114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house and found a picture of Ibrahim and Maryam in it, so he said, \"As for them, they know that the angels do not enter a house with a picture. This is Ibrahim portrayed, so what is the matter with him that he is splitting?\""],[12115,"I spent the night with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He got up, performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs until that amounted to ten rak'ahs, then he performed Witr with three rak'ahs, then he lay down and slept until he snored; his sleep was with snoring. Then the muezzin called him to the Morning Prayer, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."],[12116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer after 'Asr."],[12117,"Ibn Abbas saw 'Abd Allah b. al-Harith praying while his head was tied up behind him, so he went and stood behind him and began to undo it, while the other remained still for him. Then when he finished, he came to Ibn Abbas and said, 'What do you have against my head?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"The likeness of this is the likeness of one who prays while bound hand and foot.\"\""],[12118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gold ring on the hand of a man, so he removed it and threw it away, and said: “Would one of you deliberately take an ember of fire and place it in his hand?” After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left, it was said to the man, “Take your ring and benefit from it.” He said, “No, by Allah, I will not take it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has thrown it away.”"],[12119,"A woman lifted up a child to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'Is there Hajj for this one?' He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12120,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was traveling on the road to Makkah, a woman spoke to him from her howdah, and she took hold of the upper arm of a child and lifted him up, saying, 'Is there Hajj for this one, O Messenger of God?' He said, 'For him is a Hajj, and for you is a reward.'"],[12121,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The sisters are believers: Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith, Salma the wife of Hamzah, and Asma' bt. 'Umays - she is their sister through their mother."],[12122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The foremost women of the people of Paradise after Maryam bt. 'Imran are Fatimah, Khadijah, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.'"],[12123,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Abu Bakr to lead the Hajj, and he did not approach the Ka'bah, but rather he headed to Dhu al-Majaz informing the people of their rites and conveying to them from the Messenger of God ﷺ, until they came to 'Arafah before Dhu al-Majaz. That was because they had not performed 'Umrah along with Hajj."],[12124,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had a gap between his front teeth; when he spoke, it was seen as light between his two front teeth."],[12125,"O Messenger of God, is there Hajj for this one? He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12126,"O Messenger of God, is there Hajj for this one? He said, 'Yes, and you have a reward.'"],[12127,"I slept in the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, while the Prophet ﷺ was with her, so that I might see how the Prophet ﷺ prayed at night. The Prophet ﷺ spoke with his family for a while, then slept. When it was the last third of the night or half of it, he got up and looked at the sky and recited: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding} until he recited these verses. Then he got up, performed ablution, and used the toothstick. Then he prayed eleven rak'ahs. Then Bilal called the Adhan for prayer, so he prayed two rak'ahs, then went out and led the people in the Morning Prayer."],[12128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Frequented House (al-Bayt al-Ma'mur) in the sky is called al-Surah, and it is aligned with the Sacred House, directly above it; if it fell, it would fall upon it. Every day seventy thousand angels enter it, never having seen it before. And it has in the sky a sanctity equal to the sanctity of Makkah.\" He said: \"And every day seventy thousand angels enter the House, never to enter it again ever.\""],[12129,"Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was forty years old. He remained in Makkah for thirteen years thereafter, then migrated to Madinah and stayed there for ten years, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three years old."],[12130,"When the Prophet ﷺ commanded the people to exit the state of ihram by performing an 'umrah during the Farewell Hajj, a man would come and say, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is the Hajj,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, \"It is not the Hajj; it is only an 'umrah.\""],[12131,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. I saw him get up during the night, relieve himself, then go to the water skin, untie its strap, and perform a wudu that was between two wudus. Then he returned to his bed and slept. Then he went to the water skin, untied its strap, performed the full wudu, and prayed. So I got up and did as he had done, then I came to him and stood on his left. He turned me around and placed me on his right. He prayed either eleven or thirteen rak'ahs, then slept until he snored. I heard him say in his prostration: \"O Allah, place light in my heart, place light in my hearing, place light in my sight, place light behind me, place light in front of me, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light above me, place light below me, and grant me great light.\" Then he slept until he snored, and Bilal came to him and called him to the prayer, and he went out."],[12132,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith. The Prophet ﷺ got up during the night, went to relieve himself, then came and washed his face and hands. Then he stood to pray during the night. He went to the water skin and performed a wudu between two wudus, not using much water but making it complete. Then he stood to pray. He said: I stepped aside, disliking that he should see that I was observing him, meaning I was watching him. Then I got up and did as he had done, and I stood on his left. He took hold of the part next to my ear and turned me around until I was on his right, while he was praying. His prayer was completed at thirteen rak'ahs, including the two rak'ahs of Fajr. Then he lay down and slept until he snored. Then Bilal came and called him to the prayer, and he got up and prayed without renewing his wudu."],[12133,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and I said, \"I will certainly memorize the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and how he performs it.\" He came from the mosque, went to a corner of the house, relieved himself, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and washed his face and hands. Then he lay down and remained as long as Allah willed. Then he got up, went to a corner of the house, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and performed a wudu between two wudus, not using much water but making the wudu complete. Then he came to the mosque. He said: I did as he had done, then I came and stood on his left. He took my hand, pulled it from behind me, and placed me on his right. He prayed eight rak'ahs, then prayed three rak'ahs of witr, then prayed two rak'ahs, then said: \"O Allah, grant me light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in front of me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light below me, and light above me. O Allah, give me light, grant me light, and magnify light for me.\""],[12134,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah, and I observed how many rak'ahs the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed. He got up, urinated, then came to the water skin, loosened its strap, and poured water into a bowl or a large dish. He washed his face and forearms, then slept. Then he got up and performed a good wudu between two wudus, then stood to pray. I came and stood on his left. He took hold of me and placed me on his right. The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the night was completed at thirteen rak'ahs. Then he slept, and his sleep was known by his snoring. He slept until he snored, then went out for the prayer. He used to say in his prayer or in his supplication: \"O Allah, place light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my heart, light on my right, light on my left, light in front of me, light behind me, light above me, and light below me, and grant me light.\""],[12135,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, both from Malik b. Anas, from Makhramah b. Sulayman, from Kurayb, that Ibn 'Abbas informed him that he spent the night at the house of his maternal aunt Maymunah. He said: \"She lay down across the width of the cushion, and the Prophet ﷺ and his family lay along its length. The Prophet ﷺ slept until midnight, or a little before it, or a little after it. Then he woke up, sat up, and wiped the sleep from his face with his hands. Then he recited the ten concluding verses of Surah Al 'Imran. Then he went to a hanging water skin, performed wudu from it and made his wudu excellent. Then he stood to pray. I did as he had done, then I went and stood at his side. He placed his hand on my head and took hold of my ear, twisting it. He prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then performed witr, and lay down until the mu'adhdhin came to him. He got up and prayed two light rak'ahs, then prayed the Fajr prayer.\""],[12136,"I spent the night at Maymunah's house, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her that night. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu and stood to pray. I stood on his left, and he took hold of me and placed me on his right. He prayed thirteen rak'ahs that night, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until he snored, and when he slept he would snore. Then the mu'adhdhin came to him, and he went out and prayed without renewing his wudu."],[12137,"My father sent me to the Prophet ﷺ with a gift. I came to him while he was in the house of Maymunah. He made me lie down on the rest of the cushion. When it was the middle of the night, he got up, looked at the sky, then recited the end of Surah Al 'Imran: 'Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth...' until he finished it. Then he went to a hanging water container, used the siwak, performed wudu and made it complete, and did not pour out much water. Then he moved me, so I got up and performed wudu. I stood on his left, and he turned me around, so I stood on his right. He began to recite while twisting my ear. He prayed ten rak'ahs, then performed witr, then slept, and when he slept he would snore. Then Bilal came to him and woke him for the prayer. He got up and prayed two light rak'ahs, then went out for the prayer."],[12138,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no one who, when they want to be intimate with their spouse, says: 'In the name of Allah, O Allah, protect us from Satan and keep Satan away from what You have blessed us with.' Then, if they are blessed with a child, Satan will not harm that child.\""],[12139,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of one who prays with his head tied back is that of one who prays while bound.\""],[12140,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of one who prays with his head tied back is only that of one who prays while bound.\""],[12141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the House and found in it an image of Ibrahim and an image of Maryam. He said, “As for them, they have heard that the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image. This is Ibrahim depicted, so what is the matter with him that he is seeking divination by arrows?”"],[12142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “All of Muzdalifah is a standing place, and keep away from the interior of Muhassir, and use pebbles like those thrown in khadhf.”"],[12143,"“We did not know the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except by his takbir.”"],[12144,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of Allah, I have been enlisted in such-and-such an expedition, while my wife intends to perform Hajj.” He said, “Return and perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man should not be alone with a woman, nor should he travel with her unless she has a mahram with her.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to join such-and-such an army, while my wife intends to perform Hajj.” He said, “Then perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A woman should not travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her unless she has a mahram with her.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to go out in such-and-such an army, while my wife wants to perform Hajj.” He said, “Go out with her.”"],[12147,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon: “A woman should not travel unless she has a mahram with her.” A man stood up and said, “I have been enlisted in the expedition, and I want to send my wife for Hajj.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12148,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “A man should never be alone with a woman unless she has a mahram with her, and she should not travel except with a mahram, and no man should enter upon her except with a mahram.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, my wife has set out for Hajj, and I have been enlisted in such-and-such an expedition.” He said, “Then turn back and perform Hajj with your wife.”"],[12149,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on a carpet.”"],[12150,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Muadh to Yemen, he said, “You will come upon a people of the Book. Let the first thing to which you call them be the worship of Allah. When they acknowledge that, then inform them that Allah ﷻ has obligated upon them five prayers in their day and night. When they do that, then inform them that Allah has obligated upon them a zakah to be taken from their wealth and returned to their poor. When they do that, then take from them, and beware of taking the best of their wealth.”"],[12152,"A man died and left no inheritance for anyone. So the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Seek out [relatives].\" They could not find anyone to inherit him, so the Prophet ﷺ gave his inheritance to his freed slave who was loyal to him and the one who freed him."],[12153,"“A man died in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and left no heir except a slave of his. He freed him and ﷺ gave him his inheritance.”"],[12154,"A man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and no heir was found to inherit from him, while he had a client whom the deceased had freed. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Give him his wealth.”"],[12155,"Do people raise their voices with dhikr upon finishing the prescribed prayer? Did the Prophet ﷺ do it? Ibn Abbas said: \"I knew it when I heard it.\""],[12156,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevents the Ethiopians of Banu al-Mughira from coming to you except that they fear you will reject them.\" He said: \"There is no good in the Ethiopians: when they are hungry they steal, and when they are full they fornicate. Yet they have two good qualities: feeding food and courage in battle.\""],[12157,"\"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, then woke up, performed ablution, and used the siwak. He did that several times during the night.\""],[12158,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"The siwak cleanses the mouth and pleases the Lord.\""],[12159,"From the Prophet ﷺ is it? If the Prophet ﷺ recited it, I recites it; and if the Prophet ﷺ did not recite it, I do not recite it. Then the man left and said to me: \"O Shu'bah, he rejected it.\" So I rejected it, and he said: \"Woe to you! If he had recited it, the people would have known it.\""],[12160,"\"I passed with al-Fadl b. al-Abbas on a donkey before the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he neither forbade us nor turned us back.\""],[12161,"\"I know of no harm in it, and I do not think the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it when he forbade except due to arrogance and pride, and we, praise be to Allah, are not like that.\" He said: \"What are these birds in the brazier?\" He said: \"Do you not see how we burned them with fire?\" When al-Miswar left, he said: \"Remove this garment from me and cut off the heads of these statues, or images.\""],[12162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"would show the whiteness of his armpits when he prostrated.\""],[12163,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Shu'bah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"sent him with his family to Mina on the Day of Sacrifice, and they threw the jamrah at dawn.\""],[12164,"\"He said, 'When he purifies himself from sexual impurity, he pours water with his right hand onto his left hand seven times.'\" Then he said, \"How many times have you poured water onto my hands, O Shu'bah?\" I said, \"I don't know.\" He said, \"You have no mother and what prevents you from knowing?\" Then he performed ablution for prayer and poured water over himself, and said, \"This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to purify himself.\""],[12165,"\"Seven are forbidden by lineage and seven by marriage.\" Then he recited: {Forbidden to you are your mothers} until he reached {and daughters of the sister}. Then he said: \"This is lineage.\" Then he recited: {And your mothers who nursed you} until he reached {and that you gather between two sisters}. Then he recited: {And do not marry what your fathers married of women}. Then he said: \"This is marriage.\""],[12169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only forbade domestic donkeys for fear of a shortage of riding animals."],[12170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the first thing that Allah created was the pen and the fish.\" He was asked, \"What is being written?\" He replied, \"Everything that will exist until the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he recited the letter \"Nun\" (which refers to a chapter of the Quran) and said, \"By the pen and by what they write.\" It was not lifted from Hammad ibn Zaid except by Muammal ibn Isma'il."],[12171,"Al-ʿAbbas came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"You have left rancor among us since you did what you did.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"They will not attain good until they love you for Allah and for my kinship. Do you hope—Sulayb, a tribe of Murad—for my intercession, while Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib do not hope for it?\""],[12172,"One day we woke up and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were weeping, with each woman's family around her. I went out to the mosque and found it filled with people. Then ʿUmar came and went up to the Prophet ﷺ, who was in an upper room. He greeted him but he did not answer. He said, \"Have you divorced your wives?\" He said, \"No, but I have made an oath of abstention.\" He stayed away for twenty-nine days, then came down to his family."],[12173,"The Prophet ﷺ entered into ihram after the prayer."],[12174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Security and well-being are two blessings in which many people are deceived.\""],[12176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"I do not ask you for any reward for it, except that you fulfill my right in regard to my kinship with you, and that you maintain the ties of kinship between me and you.\""],[12177,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated, he would turn the inside of his palms toward his face."],[12178,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"No one who has an atom's weight of pride will enter Paradise.\""],[12179,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not pass the miqat except in a state of ihram.\""],[12180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his leather socks, and his companions wiped over theirs. But did he wipe after Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed?"],[12181,"There was no clan of Quraysh except that the Prophet ﷺ was born of it or had kinship among them. Say, 'I do not ask you for any reward for it, except that you restrain me and refrain from me for my kinship with you.'"],[12182,"A man was thrown by his she-camel and died while in a state of ihram. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Wash him with water and sidr, shroud him in his two garments, and do not apply perfume to him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12183,"From Ibn Abbas, tracing it back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs after the last evening prayer (al-'isha al-akhirah), reciting in the first two rak'ahs 'Qul ya ayyuha al-kafirun' and 'Qul huwa Allahu ahad,' and reciting in the last two rak'ahs 'Tanzil al-Sajdah' and 'Tabaraka alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk,' they will be recorded for him as four rak'ahs from the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr).\""],[12184,"Healing is in three things: a drink of honey, a cupping incision, and cauterization with fire. And I forbid my community from cauterization."],[12185,"The passage translates to: \"Who is your Lord? What is your religion? Who is your Prophet? And in the Hereafter, there is something similar to that.\""],[12186,"\"The Quran was sent down all at once, then it was sent down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in stages (as stars).\""],[12187,"His father said to him: \"O my son, ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a garment from his clothes to shroud me in, and ask him to pray over me.\" Abdullah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you know the honor of Abdullah, and he has commanded me to ask you for a garment to shroud him in and for you to pray over him.\" So he gave him a garment from his clothes and intended to pray over him. Umar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you know Abdullah and his hypocrisy. Will you pray over him when Allah has forbidden you to pray over him?\" He said: \"And where?\" He said: \"{If you seek forgiveness for them seventy times, Allah will never forgive them.}\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then I will increase beyond seventy.\" Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {And do not pray over any one of them who has died, ever, nor stand at his grave} and Allah revealed: {It is all the same for them whether you seek forgiveness for them or do not seek forgiveness for them; Allah will never forgive them.} He said: A man entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and prolonged his sitting. The Prophet ﷺ went out three times so that the man would follow him, but he did not. Then Umar ؓ entered and saw the man, and he recognized the displeasure in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at his staying. He said: \"Perhaps you have annoyed the Prophet ﷺ.\" The man understood and stood up. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I stood up three times so that you would follow me, but you did not.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would appoint a doorkeeper, for your wives are not like other women, and it is purer for their hearts.\" Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless permission is given to you} to the end of the verse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Umar and informed him of that. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about the captives. Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, spare your people and take ransom from them, and use it to strengthen yourselves.\" Umar b. al-Khattab said: \"Kill them.\" He said: \"If you two were in agreement, I would not disobey you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ followed the advice of Abu Bakr. Then Allah, glorified be He, revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made slaughter in the land. You desire the goods of this world, but Allah desires the Hereafter.} He said: Then it was revealed: {And certainly We created man from an extract of clay} to the end of the verses. Umar said: \"Blessed be Allah, the best of creators.\" Then it was revealed: {So blessed be Allah, the best of creators.}"],[12188,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,\" the polytheists mocked him and said: \"Muhammad mentions the god of al-Yamamah.\" Musaylimah used to call himself al-Rahman. When this verse was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded not to recite it aloud."],[12189,"\"It is not forbidden for you.\" Then he recited: {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you?} \"But you owe the most severe of expiations: a slave.\""],[12190,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that an animal be made a target (by tying it and shooting at it).\""],[12191,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"When a man enters paradise, he will ask about his parents, his wife, and his children. It will be said to him that they have not reached your level of righteousness and deeds. He will then say, 'O Lord, I have done good for myself and for them.' He will be commanded to join them with him (in paradise). And Ibn Abbas recited the verse: 'And those who believed and their descendants followed them in faith...' until the end of the verse.\""],[12192,"In his saying, \"O man,\" Taha said."],[12193,"The daughter of Khalid b. Sinan came to the Prophet ﷺ. He spread his garment for her and said, \"The daughter of a prophet whom his people neglected.\""],[12194,"The Prophet ﷺ would not pray on the two Eids before the prayer or after it."],[12195,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Hajj is the jihad, and the Umrah is voluntary.\""],[12196,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drank while standing."],[12197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be at the end of time people who dye with black like the crops of birds; they will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[12198,"While Jibril ﷺ was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a creaking sound from above him. He raised his head and said: “This is a gate of heaven that has been opened today, never opened before except today.” An angel descended from it, and he said: “This is an angel who has descended to the earth, never descended except today.” He greeted and said: “Rejoice in two lights that you have been given, which no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah. You will not recite a single letter of them without being given it.”"],[12199,"O Messenger of Allah, I had intercourse with my wife while she was menstruating. The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to free a slave. The value of a slave on that day was a dinar."],[12200,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Be independent of people even with the stem of a toothbrush.\""],[12201,"A barren wind seized them on the Day of Badr."],[12202,"When the verse {Say: I ask of you no reward for it, save love of the near of kin} was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, who are your kin whose love has become obligatory upon us? He said: “Ali, Fatimah, and their two sons ؓ.”"],[12203,"When the verse {Those whom the angels take while they are wronging themselves} up to the end of the verse was revealed, he said: “There were people in Makkah who had embraced Islam. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Madinah, they disliked migrating and were afraid.” Then Allah, Exalted is He, revealed {Those whom the angels take} up to His saying {except the oppressed}."],[12204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bring me a sheet and an inkwell, so I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.” They said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is delirious.” Then they fell silent, and he fell silent. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall we not bring it to you afterwards?” He said: “After what?”"],[12205,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He was forbidden to use any living thing as a target."],[12206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not take any living thing as a target.”"],[12207,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prayed on the day of Eid Al-Fitr and did not pray before or after it, then he went to the women with Bilal, and he commanded them to give charity. So the woman threw her jewelry and her worn-out clothes.\""],[12208,"He heard the call, then did not come to it – then there is no prayer for him, except with an excuse."],[12209,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever hears the call and does not answer it without an excuse, then there is no prayer for him.”"],[12210,"The Prophet ﷺ interjected in the middle of his speech and said: “Indeed, some eloquence is magic.”"],[12211,"Death or to Makkah."],[12212,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not take anything with a soul as a target.\""],[12213,"The Messenger of God ﷺ expiated with a sa' of dates and commanded the people to do that; whoever could not find it, then half a sa'."],[12214,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to seek protection for Hasan and Husayn: \"I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of God from every devil, venomous creature, and every evil eye.\""],[12215,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters upon a sick person whose appointed time has not come and says in his presence seven times: 'I ask God, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,' he will be granted well-being.\""],[12216,"\"I spent the night with the Prophet ﷺ, and he called for a cushion of haircloth for me and placed it under my head.\""],[12217,"That He not make them into sects, and not make some of them taste the might of others, but He refused.\""],[12218,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Three persons whose prayer God does not accept: a leader of a people while they dislike him, a woman who spends the night while her husband is angry with her, and two brothers who have severed relations.\""],[12219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not have mercy on our young, respect our old, and recognize our right.\""],[12220,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said: \"There is no man who visits a sick person and says: 'I ask God, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you' seven times, while his appointed time has a delay, except that it is lightened for him.\""],[12221,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no deed more beloved to God than a deed performed during these ten days, except a man who goes out as a warrior with his own self and his wealth, then does not return.\""],[12222,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the night in which I was taken on the Night Journey, I found a pleasant fragrance. So I said, 'O Jibril, what is this pleasant fragrance?' He said, 'This is the fragrance of the comb of the daughter of Fir'awn and her children.' I asked, 'What is the matter with her?' He said, 'While she was combing the daughter of Fir'awn, the comb fell from her hand, so she said, 'In the name of Allah.' Fir'awn's daughter said to her, 'Is it my father or your Lord that you seek?' She said, 'Rather, my Lord and your Lord and the Lord of your father is Allah.' She said, 'Do you have a Lord other than my father?' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Then I will inform him about that.' She said, 'Yes.' So she informed him, and he called her and said, 'O so-and-so, do you have a Lord other than me?' She said, 'Yes, my Lord and your Lord is Allah.' So he commanded for a cow made of copper to be taken, and it was heated and her children were thrown into it one by one. She said, 'I have a request for you.' He said, 'What is it?' She said, 'I want my bones and the bones of my child to be gathered together and placed in one shroud, and we be buried together.' He said, 'That is upon you.' So her children continued to be thrown into the cow until it reached her infant son. It was as if she hesitated for his sake, so he said to her, 'O mother, go ahead, for the punishment of this world is easier than the punishment of the Hereafter.' Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Then four people stood up to speak, 'Eesa ibn Maryam, the companion of Jurayj, the witness of Yusuf, and the son of Fir'awn's maid. And the narration is from the Hadith of Abu 'Umar ad-Dariri.\""],[12224,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Sulayman, the Prophet of God ﷺ, when he stood in his place of prayer, saw a tree standing firmly before him. He said to it: 'What is your name?' It replied: 'The carob.' He said: 'For what purpose are you?' It replied: 'For the ruin of this house.' So Sulayman said: 'O God, conceal my death from the jinn so that humans know that the jinn do not know the unseen.' He carved it into a staff upon which he leaned, and the woodworm ate it, so it fell, and he collapsed. They estimated its consumption by the woodworm and found it to be a year. Thus it became clear to humans that if the jinn had known the unseen, they would not have remained in the humiliating punishment for a year. Ibn Abbas used to recite it thus: 'The jinn thanked the woodworm, and it used to bring water to it wherever it was.'\""],[12225,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Prostration is on seven body parts: the two hands, the two feet, the two knees, and the forehead; and raising the hands when you see the House, and on al-Safa and al-Marwa, and at ʿArafa, and at Jamʿ, and when throwing the jamarat, and when the prayer is called."],[12226,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Seventy prophets prayed in the Mosque of al-Khayf, among them Musa — it is as if I am looking at him, wearing two Qatwani cloaks, in a state of ihram, on a camel of the Shanu'a camels, muzzled with a fiber nose-rein that had two braids."],[12227,"From the Prophet ﷺ: When one of you sneezes and says 'al-hamdu lillah', the angels say 'Rabb al-ʿalamin'. Then when he says 'Rabb al-ʿalamin', the angels say 'May Allah have mercy on you'."],[12228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Black Stone was whiter than snow, but the sins of the children of Adam made it black.\""],[12229,"From the Prophet ﷺ: I was commanded to use the siwak so much that I feared for my teeth."],[12230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs, then said: Ask these people who claim that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the khuffs after Surah al-Ma'ida. By Allah, he did not wipe after al-Ma'ida. To wipe over the back of a piebald camel would be more beloved to me than to wipe over them."],[12231,"I have not seen a people better than the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They did not ask him except about thirteen matters until he passed away, all of them in the Qur'an. Among them: {They ask you about the sacred month}, {They ask you about wine and gambling}, {They ask you about orphans}, {They ask you about menstruation}, {They ask you about the spoils of war}, {They ask you what they should spend}. They would not ask except about what benefited them. He said: The first to circumambulate the House were the angels. Between the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner are graves of the prophets. When his people harmed him, a prophet would leave from among them and worship Allah in that place until he died."],[12232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — and al-Husayn b. Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabiʿ al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from ʿAta' b. al-Sa'ib, from Saʿid b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbas ؓ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I asked my Lord a question that I wish I had not asked. I said: O Lord, before me there were messengers, some of whom You subjected the winds to, and some of whom used to revive the dead. He said: Did I not find you an orphan and give you shelter? Did I not find you astray and guide you? Did I not find you poor and enrich you? Did I not expand your chest for you and remove from you your burden? I said: Yes, O Lord. And their wording is the same.[1]"],[12233,"A bowl of tharid was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Eat from its sides and do not eat from its middle, for the blessing descends in its middle."],[12234,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ to show him the rites. Thabir split open for him, and he entered Mina and showed him the jamarat, then showed him Jamʿ and showed him ʿArafat. When he was at the first jamra, Iblis appeared to him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank. Then he appeared to him again — until he mentioned Jamrat al-ʿAqaba — and he sank and went away."],[12236,"Jibril went with the Prophet ﷺ to show him the rites. He brought him to Jamrat al-ʿAqaba, and there was Iblis upon it. He commanded him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank into the earth. Then he came to the middle jamra, and there was Iblis, so he commanded him, and he threw seven pebbles at him, and he sank into the earth. Then he came to the third one and did the same to him. Then he brought him to Jamʿ, then he performed talbiya from ʿArafat."],[12237,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Eid, and he began praying before the sermon, without calling the adhan or iqamah. Then he rode his mount and delivered a sermon on it. After that, he approached the women and gave a sermon to them and urged them to give charity. He said, \"O women, give charity.\" So, women started throwing their garments, rings, and earrings into Bilal's garment."],[12238,"The Jews disputed with the Prophet ﷺ, saying: You eat from what we kill but do not eat from what Allah kills. Then Allah, exalted be He, sent down: {And do not eat of that over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned}."],[12239,"When it was revealed, it became difficult for the Muslims and hard on them, so Allah abrogated it and sent down: {Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity}."],[12240,"When the Quran descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would receive it with his tongue and lips, and from that he endured great hardship. Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it} (Q 75:16), meaning: to hasten to take it. He says: {Indeed upon Us is its collection and its recitation} (Q 75:17), meaning: to collect it in your heart and that you recite it. {So when We have recited it} (Q 75:18), meaning: when We have sent it down, {then follow its recitation} (Q 75:18), meaning: listen and be silent. {Then indeed upon Us is its explanation} (Q 75:19), meaning: to make it clear by your tongue. Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found relief."],[12241,"Regarding the words of Allah ﷻ: {Woe to you, and woe! Then woe to you, and woe!} (Q 75:34-35), is it something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, or something Allah sent down? He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it, then Allah sent it down.\""],[12242,"While I was circumambulating with the Prophet ﷺ, he heard a man say: 'O Allah, forgive so-and-so son of so-and-so.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is this?' He said: 'A man asked me to supplicate for him.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Your companion has been forgiven.'"],[12243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We wish that Musa had been patient with him, so that he would relate to us of their affair.'"],[12244,"The Prophet ﷺ married while in a state of ihram."],[12245,"Dreams of the prophets are revelation."],[12246,"Regarding His words: {You are the best nation produced for mankind} (Q 3:110), he said: 'They are those who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Madinah.'"],[12247,"Ma'iz came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed twice. Then he said: 'Take him away.' Then he said: 'Bring him back,' and he confessed twice more, until he confessed four times. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Take him away and stone him.'"],[12248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ma'iz b. Malik: 'Is what has reached me about you true?' He said: 'What has reached you about me?' He said: 'It has reached me that you committed intercourse with the slave girl of the Banu So-and-so.' He said: 'Yes.' Then he testified four times, and he ordered that he be stoned."],[12250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the shade of a chamber, and the shade was about to recede from him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man will come to you looking at you with the eyes of a devil. When he comes to you, do not speak to him.' They had not waited long before a man appeared before them. He called him and said: 'Why do you and your companions revile me?' He said: 'Call them.' So he called them, and they began swearing by Allah that they had not said or done anything, until he pardoned them. Then Allah ﷻ sent down: {On the Day when Allah will resurrect them all, and they will swear to Him as they swear to you} (Q 58:18), to the end of the verse."],[12253,"The Ansar's houses were far from the mosque, and they wanted to move closer to the mosque. Then the verse was sent down: {And We record what they have sent ahead and their traces} (Q 36:12), so they remained in their houses."],[12254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform qunut in the dawn prayer, supplicating against a clan of Banu Sulaym."],[12255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” Then he recited: {As We began the first creation, We will repeat it. [That is] a promise binding upon Us. Indeed, We will do it.} The first to be clothed will be Ibrahim, and men from my companions will be taken to the right and to the left. I will say, “My companions!” It will be said, “They kept turning back on their heels since you left them.” I will say as the righteous servant Isa ibn Maryam said: {I was a witness over them as long as I was among them; but when You took me up, You were the Observer over them, and You are, over all things, Witness.} {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, indeed it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.}"],[12256,"“Marry, for the best of this nation had the most wives.”"],[12257,"“There is no repentance for the murderer of a believer; no verse has abrogated it since it was revealed.”"],[12258,"“It was revealed among the last of what was revealed, and nothing has abrogated it.”"],[12259,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you?” No one answered him. Then he said: “Is there anyone from Hudhayl among you?” A man said, “I am,” and a man from them had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What prevented you from speaking when I spoke?” He said, “I thought, O Messenger of Allah, that something had been revealed about my people, and I disliked being the one to bring it to them.” He said: “No, indeed your companion is being detained by his debt.”"],[12260,"Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am ruined.” He said, “What has ruined you?” He said, “I turned my saddle [i.e., changed position during intercourse].” He did not reply to him until it was revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish;} he said, “From the front or the back, but avoid the anus and menstruation.”"],[12261,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, Iblis let out a wail at which his troops gathered to him. He said, “Despair of ever bringing the nation of Muhammad back to polytheism after this day of yours; but tempt them in their religion and spread wailing among them.”"],[12262,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done while fasting and in ihram.”"],[12263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “would not omit fasting on the White Days, whether traveling or resident.”"],[12264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a man from the Ansar. When he approached his house, he heard him speaking inside. When he asked permission and entered, he saw no one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “I heard you speaking to someone else.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I entered the room distressed by people’s talk because of the fever I had. Then a visitor came in to me, a man whose sitting I have never seen more noble nor whose speech finer, after you.” He said, “That was Jibril ﷺ . Indeed, among you are men such that if one of them swore by Allah, He would fulfill his oath.”"],[12265,"Quraysh came to the Jews and asked, “With what did Musa bring to you?” They said, “His staff and his hand white for the beholders.” They came to the Christians and asked, “How was Isa?” They said, “He healed the blind and the leper, and revived the dead.” Then they came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Call upon your Lord to make Safa gold for us.” He called upon his Lord, and this verse was revealed: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of the night and the day are signs for those of understanding.} So let them reflect on them."],[12266,"The Prophet ﷺ “would pray two rak‘ahs after Maghrib, prolonging the recitation in them until the people of the mosque dispersed.”"],[12267,"The Quraysh used to circumambulate the House naked, whistling and clapping, so Allah ﷻ revealed {Say, 'Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah?'} and they were commanded to wear clothes."],[12268,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {Verily, the friends of Allah—no fear shall be upon them, nor shall they grieve}: he said, \"Allah is remembered by seeing them.\""],[12269,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no days in which good deeds are more beloved to Allah or in which the good deed is better than the ten days.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, not even jihad?\" He said, \"Not even jihad, except for a man who goes out with himself and his wealth and does not return with anything.\""],[12270,"Narrated by the Prophet, ﷺ , \"There are no deeds during the ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah that are more beloved to Allah than performing Jihad in His cause, except for a man who goes out with his life and his wealth and does not return with anything from that.\""],[12271,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said, \"There are no days of this world in which deeds are more excellent than the ten days.\" A man said, \"Not even the like of them in the path of Allah?\" three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the third time, \"Except one who does not return.\""],[12272,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him that her sister had vowed to fast for a month, but she had embarked on the sea and died without fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fast on behalf of your sister.\""],[12273,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother died with a month's fast owed by her; shall I make it up on her behalf?\" He said, \"If your mother had a debt, would you pay it on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\" Sulayman said: al-Hakam and Salamah b. Kuhayl, while we were all sitting when Muslim narrated this hadith, said: We heard Mujahid mention this hadith from Ibn Abbas."],[12274,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother made a month's fast obligatory upon herself and she died.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you think if she had a debt, you would pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12275,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"My father died without performing Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" He said, \"If your father had a debt, would you pay it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12276,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[12277,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite on Friday in the dawn prayer: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan; and he used to recite in the Friday prayer: Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la and Hal Ataka Hadith al-Ghashiyah."],[12278,"When the Prophet ﷺ recited Sabbih isma Rabbika al-A'la, he said, \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.\""],[12279,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, Abu Bakr said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been expelled—we will all surely perish.\" When this verse was revealed: {Permission is given to those who fight because they have been wronged, and Allah is surely able to give them victory} {Those who have been expelled from their homes}, Abu Bakr knew that there would be fighting."],[12280,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs at night, then leave and use the siwak."],[12281,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be brief in the prayer, for behind you are the weak, the elderly, and the one with a need.”"],[12282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man hates the Ansar while believing in Allah and the Last Day, and no man loves Thaqif while believing in Allah and the Last Day.”"],[12283,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five prayers at Mina."],[12284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Umm Salamah: “This is ʿAli b. Abi Talib; his flesh is my flesh and his blood is my blood. He is to me of the station of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me.”"],[12285,"Al-Saʿb b. Jaththamah gifted the Prophet ﷺ — while he was at Qudayd — the hindquarter of a wild donkey, but he returned it while it was dripping blood."],[12286,"Al-Saʿb b. Jaththamah gifted the Prophet ﷺ the hindquarter of a wild donkey, dripping blood, but he returned it and said: “We are in a state of ihram.”"],[12287,"\"He heard the call but did not respond, so he has no prayer.\" This was narrated by Al-Qattarani from Sulaiman ibn Harb in a standing position, and it was also narrated by Ismail ibn Ishaq Al-Qadi from Sulaiman ibn Harb in a raised position."],[12288,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The first to be called to Paradise are the ḥammādūn — those who praise Allah in prosperity and adversity.”"],[12289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ said: “O son of Adam, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for what is in you, and I do not mind. Even if you were to come to Me with sins nearly filling the earth, I would meet you with nearly as much forgiveness, as long as you do not associate anything with Me. Even if your sins reached the height of the sky, then you sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you.”"],[12290,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , entered the Kaaba and offered two rak'ahs (units of prayer) in between the Sariyatayn (the two pillars in the Kaaba), then he left and offered two rak'ahs between the door of the Kaaba and the Hajar (the stone). Then he said, 'This is the qibla (direction of prayer).' Then he entered again and stood up to supplicate but did not offer prayer.\""],[12291,"“The polytheists used to say in the talbiyah: ‘Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, labbayka la sharika laka illa sharikan huwa laka tamlikuhu wa ma malak.’ Then Allah ﷻ revealed: ‘Do you have among those whom your right hands possess partners in what We have provided for you, so that you are equal in it, and you fear them as you fear yourselves?’”"],[12292,"I spent the night with my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up, startled, asked for water, performed wudu, then recited: “Indeed in the creation of the heavens and the earth…” to the end of the surah. Then he began al-Baqarah and recited it letter by letter until he completed it. Then he bowed and said: “Subhana Rabbiya al-ʿAzim.” Then he prostrated and said: “Subhana Rabbiya al-Aʿla.” Then he raised his head and said between the two prostrations: “Rabbi ighfir li wa-rhamni wa-jburni wa-rfaʿni wa-rzuqni wa-hdini.” Then he stood and recited in the second rakʿah Al ʿImran until he completed it. Then he bowed and prostrated, then he did as he had done in the first. Then he lay down. Then he got up, startled, and did as he had done in the first two, reciting letter by letter, until he had prayed eight rakʿahs, lying down between every two rakʿahs, and he performed witr with three. Then he prayed two rakʿahs of fajr. Then he said: “Allahumma ajʿal fi nafsi nuran wa fi qalbi nuran wa fi basari nuran wa fi samʿi nuran wa-jʿal bayna yadayya nuran wa min khalfi nuran wa ʿan yamini nuran wa ʿan shimali nuran wa min tahti nuran wa min fawqi nuran wa aʿzim li nuran.”"],[12293,"The Prophet ﷺ performed saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[12294,"The Prophet ﷺ continued the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at the Jamrah."],[12295,"When {And warn your closest kindred} was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ climbed al-Safa and said, \"Woe to the morning!\""],[12296,"\"Allah took the covenant of the prophets for their people.\""],[12297,"\"The borrowed item.\""],[12298,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, green jars, and wooden vessels, and that dates and raisins be mixed.\""],[12299,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I vowed to slaughter at Buwanah.\" He said, \"Perhaps there is something of the pre-Islamic era in your heart?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Fulfill your vow.\""],[12300,"\"The last verse revealed was {And fear a day when you will be returned to Allah}.\""],[12301,"\"Whoever followed him had mercy in this world and the hereafter, and whoever did not follow him was spared from what the rest of the nations were tested with: metamorphosis, sinking into the earth, and being pelted.\""],[12302,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade walking in a single sandal or a single leather sock, sleeping alone in a house, or relieving oneself in open land unless one bends down or faces an enemy unless he moves away from himself."],[12303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abu Isra'il while he was standing in the sun, and said, \"What is wrong with this man?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he vowed not to speak, not to sit, and to fast.\" He said, \"Tell him to speak, seek shade, sit, and complete his fast.\" He did not instruct him to offer expiation."],[12304,"He fell from his mount and his neck was broken, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Wash him with lote-tree leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12305,"The Prophet ﷺ came and found the Jews fasting on the day of Ashura. He asked, \"What is the significance of this day?\" They replied, \"This is the day when Allah saved Moses and drowned the people of Israel, so we fast it out of gratitude and commemorate it.\""],[12306,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say between the two prostrations, \"O Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me.\""],[12307,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother vowed to fast for a month, but she died before she could fast.\" He said, \"Do you think that if your mother had a debt, you would pay it?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Allah's debt is more deserving of being paid.\""],[12308,"I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah's house. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then came and prayed four rak'ahs, then slept, then woke up and said, \"Did the boy wake up? Did the boy stand?\" I came and stood on his left, so he turned me to his right. He prayed five rak'ahs, then prayed two rak'ahs, then slept until I heard his snoring—or he said, his heavy breathing—then he went out for the prayer."],[12309,"That al-Saʿb b. Jaththama sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was at Qudayd, a haunch of a wild donkey—or he said a hindquarter of a wild donkey—but he returned it (to him) while it was dripping blood, as he was in a state of ihram."],[12310,"That al-Saʿb b. Jaththama sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ, while he was in a state of ihram at Qudayd, and he returned it while it was dripping blood."],[12311,"That the Prophet ﷺ said on the day of the Trench: “They have distracted us from the middle prayer—may God fill their graves and their bellies with fire.”"],[12312,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “I owe (the freeing of) a slave, and I have a black non-Arab slave girl.” He said: “Bring her to me.” Then he said: “Do you testify that there is no god but God?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then free her.”"],[12313,"A black slave came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"A traveler passing by me while I am with my master's camels, can I give him some milk without their permission?\" The Prophet replied, \"No.\" The slave said, \"If I throw and hit myself, and continue to do so?\" The Prophet replied, \"Whatever you hit, leave what you don't hit.\""],[12314,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever shows off (riyaʾ), God will expose him; and whoever makes a show (sumʿa), God will make a show of him.”"],[12315,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray witr with three rak'ahs. In the first he would recite \"Glorify the Name of Your Lord, the Most High;\" in the second: \"Say: O You disbelievers!\" and in the third: \"Say: He is Allah, (the) One.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1702)"],[12316,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the Friday (prayer) Surat al-Jumuʿa and Surat al-Munafiqun."],[12317,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Friday (prayer) Surat al-Jumuʿa and Surat al-Munafiqun."],[12318,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the morning prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil and Hal Ata ʿala al-Insan."],[12320,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God cursed the Jews; fat was made forbidden for them, but they sold it and consumed its price.”"],[12321,"The Messenger of God ﷺ dispatched a military expedition that included al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad. When they reached the people, they found that they had dispersed, but one man with a great deal of wealth remained and did not leave. He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but God.” Al-Miqdad, however, leaned toward him and killed him. A man among his companions said to him: “You killed a man who said ‘there is no god but God’? By God, this will surely be mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ.” When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they said: “O Messenger of God, a man bore witness that there is no god but God, but al-Miqdad killed him.” He said: “Summon al-Miqdad for me.” Then he said: “O Miqdad, did you kill a man who said ‘there is no god but God’? What will you do with ‘there is no god but God’?” He said: Then God revealed: “O you who believe, when you go forth in the way of God, investigate, and do not say to one who offers you peace, ‘You are not a believer,’ seeking the goods of the life of this world; for with God are abundant gains. Thus you were before, and God conferred favor upon you.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He was a believing man who concealed his faith among a disbelieving people, and you killed him. Likewise, you yourself used to conceal your faith in Makkah.”"],[12322,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Majid b. Suhayl, from Yahya b. ʿAbbad, from Saʿid b. Jubayr, that Ibn ʿAbbas narrated to him that his father ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib sent him on an errand of his to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Maymuna bt. al-Harith was the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbas, so he entered upon her and found the Messenger of God ﷺ in the mosque. Ibn ʿAbbas said: I lay down in her room and resolved to count how many (rakʿas) the Messenger of God ﷺ would pray. He said: He came while I was lying down in the room after part of the night had passed and said: “Has the boy gone to sleep?” Then he took hold of a covering that was on Maymuna, threw part of it over himself, with part of it remaining on her. Then he stood and prayed two rakʿas at a time until he had prayed eight rakʿas. Then he performed witr with five, without sitting between them. Then he sat and praised God as He deserves, praising Him at length. Then the last of his words was: “O God, place for me a light in my heart, and place for me a light in my hearing, and place for me a light in my sight, and place for me a light on my right and a light on my left, and place for me a light before me and a light behind me, and increase me in light, and increase me in light, and increase me in light.”"],[12323,"“The Qur'an was separated from the Reminder and placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven, then Gabriel began to bring it down to the Prophet ﷺ, reciting it in a measured way.”"],[12324,"In his statement \"Indeed, We have sent it down in the night of decree,\" he said, \"The Quran was revealed as a whole and it was placed in the House of Honor in the lowest heaven. Jibril (Gabriel), ﷺ , revealed it to Muhammad, ﷺ , in response to the words in the lowest heaven and he revealed it to Muhammad, ﷺ , in response to the words of the people and their actions.\""],[12325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first call to prayer was only instituted to make it easy for the people of prayer to prepare for their prayer. So when you hear the call to prayer, perform the ablution thoroughly; and when you hear the iqamah, hasten to the first takbir, for it is the beginning and completion of the prayer; and do not rush the reciter in bowing and prostrating.\""],[12326,"The Ansar said among themselves: \"If we were to gather wealth for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would stretch out his hand and no one could come between him and it.\" So they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we intended to gather for you from our wealth.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Say: I do not ask you for it any reward, except love for the near of kin.} They went out disagreeing. Some of them said: \"Did you not see what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said?\" Others said: \"He only said this so that we fight for his family and support them.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Or do they say: He has fabricated a lie against Allah?} up to His saying: {And He it is who accepts repentance from His servants.} The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered them repentance, up to His saying: {And He responds to those who believe and do righteous deeds, and increases them from His bounty.} They are the ones who said this, that you should repent to Allah and seek His forgiveness."],[12327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jibril ﷺ : \"What prevents you from visiting us more often than you do?\" Then this verse was revealed: {And we do not descend except by the command of your Lord.}"],[12328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Regarding the prostration in Sad: Dawud prostrated it in repentance, and we prostrate it in thankfulness.\""],[12330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of my family is the likeness of the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns.\""],[12331,"Wine itself has been prohibited, and intoxication from every drink."],[12332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the weak members of his family at night to Muzdalifah and said to them: \"Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun has risen.\""],[12333,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting."],[12334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever speaks about the Book of Allah without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[12337,"A man insulted a father of al-Abbas from the pre-Islamic era, so al-Abbas slapped him. His people came and said: \"By Allah, we will surely slap him,\" and they took up arms. News of that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he ascended the pulpit and said: \"O people, which people of the earth do you consider most honorable in the sight of Allah?\" They said: \"You.\" He said: \"Indeed al-Abbas is of me and I am of him. Do not revile our dead, for you would harm our living.\" Then the people came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we seek refuge in Allah from your anger. Seek forgiveness for us.\""],[12338,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The lahd is for us, and the shaqq is for others.”"],[12339,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What becomes prohibited by suckling is what becomes prohibited by lineage.”"],[12340,"“Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives.”"],[12341,"When wine was forbidden, the companions of the Messenger of God went to one another and said: “Wine has been forbidden and made equivalent to idolatry.”"],[12342,"“He saw him.”"],[12343,"When God revealed {Except the oppressed among men, women, and children who cannot devise a plan and are not directed to a way} [Q 4:98], “the going out to the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[12344,"Regarding His saying {My Lord, make this a secure city and provide its people with fruits—whoever of them believes in God and the Last Day} [Q 2:126], Ibn ʿAbbas said: Abraham ﷺ had reserved it exclusively for the people, so God ﷻ revealed “and whoever disbelieves as well—I will provide for them just as I provide for the believers. I create a creation and do not provide for them; I give them enjoyment for a little while, then I will compel them to the punishment of the Fire.” Then Ibn ʿAbbas recited {To each We extend, these and these, from the gift of your Lord, and the gift of your Lord is not restricted} [Q 17:20]."],[12345,"“Whoever sees me in a dream has (really) seen me, for Satan cannot appear in my form.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3901)"],[12346,"“The place of the two feet, and the extent of His Throne cannot be measured.”"],[12347,"“Concession was given to the elderly man, the one afflicted by severe thirst, and the pregnant woman to break the fast in Ramadan.”"],[12348,"“I enjoin you to fear God, and beware of mentioning the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, for you do not know what has preceded for them.”"],[12349,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"If one does not find a lower garment (izār), he should wear trousers (sarāwīl) and whoever does not find shoes (na'alayn), should wear sandals (khuffayn).\""],[12350,"The Prophet ﷺ took a ring and wore it, then said: “This has distracted me from you since today—to it a glance and to you a glance.” Then he threw it away."],[12351,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning.”"],[12352,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to circumambulate the House wearing red outer garments, and it was not the misha'a."],[12353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My community has been given something that no other community was given at the time of calamity: {Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return}.\""],[12354,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas: \"{I swear by this city} - Makkah, {and you are free in this city} - Makkah, {and [by] a parent and what he fathered, We have certainly created man in hardship} - in uprightness and in erectness.\""],[12355,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah does not look at the one who lets his garment hang low.\""],[12356,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ does not look at the one who lets his lower garment hang low.\""],[12357,"\"A sheep passed in front of the Messenger ﷺ while he was praying, between him and the qibla, and it did not interrupt his prayer.\""],[12358,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Muslim al-Mula'i, from Mujahid and Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas ؓ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing of the wind was released against 'Ad except the size of the ring's opening; then it was sent upon them and carried them from the desert to the settled area. When the people of the settled area saw it, {they said, 'This is a cloud bringing us rain'} facing our valleys; the desert people were in it, so the desert people were thrown upon the settled people until they perished.\" He said: \"It raged against its keepers until it burst forth from the doors.\""],[12359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: \"Alif-Lam-Meem. The revelation of the Prostration and has there come to you the story of the dispute?\""],[12360,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Friday prayer Surat al-Jumu'ah and al-Munafiqun."],[12361,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying \"Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah,\" so he said: \"Who is Shubrumah?\" He said: \"My brother or a relative of mine.\" He said: \"Have you performed Hajj for yourself?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shubrumah.\""],[12362,"I heard Ibn Umar say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh in earthenware jars.\" So I went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: \"Ibn Umar spoke the truth.\" I said: \"What is the jar?\" He said: \"Made of clay.\""],[12363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best gift is a word of truth that you hear, then carry it to a Muslim brother of yours and teach it to him.\""],[12364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in every Friday morning prayer the chapter of \"Alif Lam Meem Tanzeel\" and \"Has there not come upon man a period of time.\""],[12365,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Wiping over the two socks is for the resident for one day and night, and for the traveler for three days and their nights.\""],[12366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was aided by the east wind, and 'Ad was destroyed by the west wind.\""],[12367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Fajr on the day of ʿAshura. When he finished, he said: \"Whoever among you has begun the day fasting, let him complete his fast; and whoever has not begun the day fasting, let him not eat anything. For this is a day on which Musa was given victory over Pharaoh, so the Jews fasted it in gratitude, and we have a greater right to gratitude.\""],[12368,"The Quran was sent down all at once to the nearest heaven, then it was sent down in portions afterwards to the Prophet ﷺ."],[12369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of your garments is white, so shroud your dead in it and clothe your living with it. And the best of your kohls is ithmid: it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight.\""],[12370,"From Ibn ʿAbbas, who raised the hadith to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever dies addicted to wine will meet Allah as a worshipper of an idol.\""],[12371,"Some Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Abu al-Qasim, we will ask you about some things. If you answer us correctly, we will follow you, believe you, and have faith in you.\" He then took from them the covenant that Isra'il took upon himself. They said: \"Allah is guardian over what we say.\" They said: \"Tell us about the sign of the Prophet ﷺ.\" He said: \"His eyes sleep, but his heart does not sleep.\" They said: \"Tell us how a woman conceives a female and how she conceives a male.\" He said: \"The two fluids meet. If the woman's fluid rises above the man's fluid, she conceives a female; and if the man's fluid rises above the woman's fluid, she conceives a male.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us about thunder: what is it?\" He said: \"An angel among the angels, entrusted with the clouds. He drives them wherever Allah wills.\" They said: \"What is this sound that is heard?\" He said: \"The angel's rebuke of the cloud when he drives it until it reaches where he commands it.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us what Isra'il forbade upon himself.\" He said: \"He lived in the desert and suffered from an ailment, and he found nothing that suited him except camel meat and their milk, so for that reason he forbade them.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" They said: \"Tell us who comes to you from the angels. For there is no prophet but an angel from among the angels comes to him with the message and revelation. So who is your companion? For only this remains.\" He said: \"Jibril ﷺ .\" They said: \"That is the one who descends with war and fighting. That is our enemy. If you had said Mika'il, the one who descends with rain, we would have followed you.\" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: {Say: Whoever is an enemy to Jibril...} the verse."],[12372,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he \"forbade killing any animal by tying it up and shooting it.\""],[12373,"The jinn used to ascend to the heaven to listen to the revelation. When they heard a word, they would add nine falsehoods to it. As for the word, it would be true, but what they added was false. When the Prophet ﷺ was sent, they were prevented from their listening posts. That was mentioned to Iblis, and before that stars were not thrown at them. Iblis said to them: \"This is because of something that has happened on the earth.\" So he sent his troops, and they found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing praying between two mountains. They came to him and told him, and he said: \"This is the event that has happened on the earth.\""],[12374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant."],[12375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"used to recite on Friday in the Fajr prayer: 'Alif Lam Mim. The Revelation of the Book...' (al-Sajdah) and 'Has there come upon man...' (al-Insan).\""],[12376,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with reciting \"Subhan\" and \"Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun\" and \"Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad\" in every unit (rak'ah) [of the prayer]."],[12377,"Nabidh was made for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of my maternal aunt in a water-skin."],[12378,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There are no days in which drawing near to Allah with a deed is more excellent than these ten days.\" It was said: \"Not even jihad?\" He said: \"Not even jihad, unless a man goes out with his own self and his wealth and returns with none of it.\""],[12379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever follows the Book of Allah, Allah will guide him from misguidance and protect him from an evil reckoning on the Day of Resurrection.\" That is because Allah says: {So whoever follows My guidance will not go astray or suffer.}"],[12380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no concubinage in Islam. Whoever engaged in concubinage during the pre-Islamic era, I have attached him to his ʿaṣaba. And whoever claims a child from an illegitimate union, he neither inherits nor is inherited from.”"],[12381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.”"],[12382,"“Umm Ḥufayd, my maternal aunt, sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. He ate from the clarified butter and the dried curd, and left the dabb lizards out of disgust. Had they been unlawful, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[12383,"“Umm Ḥufayd bt. al-Ḥārith b. Jazʾ, the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbās, sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some clarified butter, dried curd, and dabb lizards. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for them, and they were eaten at his table, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left them like one who feels aversion to them. Had they been unlawful, they would not have been eaten at the table of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor would he have ordered that they be eaten.”"],[12384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and the Jews were fasting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What is this?” They said: “This is a day on which Allah drowned Pharaoh and saved Moses.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am closer to Moses ﷺ than you,” and he ordered that it be fasted."],[12385,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to perform Hajj, and she died without performing it.” He said: “Do you think that if your sister had a debt, you would pay it off?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “The debt owed to Allah is more worthy of being paid. Perform Hajj on behalf of your sister.”"],[12386,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “My mother vowed to perform Hajj, but she died before performing it. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?” He said: “Do you think that if your mother had a debt, you would pay it off?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then perform Hajj on her behalf and settle what is owed by her, for Allah ﷻ is more deserving of fulfillment.”"],[12387,"“The death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was announced to him.” It was revealed to him: “When there comes the help of Allah and the victory”—the conquest of Makkah—“then ask forgiveness of your Lord, and know that your term has drawn near.”"],[12388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never fasted a complete month other than Ramadan. When he fasted, he would continue fasting so that one would say: “By Allah, he will not break his fast.” And when he broke his fast, he would continue not fasting so that one would say: “By Allah, he will not fast.”"],[12389,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-dubbāʾ, al-ḥantam, and al-muzaffat.”"],[12390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: “Allah knows best what they would have done, since He created them.”"],[12391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out with a group of his companions heading to the market of ʿUkāẓ. The devils had been prevented from hearing the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against them. The devils returned to their people, who said: “What is the matter with you?” They said: “We have been prevented from hearing the news of heaven, and meteors were sent against us.” They said: “Nothing has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven except something that has happened. So travel throughout the east and west of the earth and see what it is that has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven.” So they set out traveling the east and west of the earth, seeking what had prevented them from hearing the news of heaven. Those who had headed toward Tihāmah turned back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he and his companions were at Nakhlah, heading to the market of ʿUkāẓ, and he was “leading his companions in the dawn prayer.” When they heard the Quran, they listened and said: “By Allah, this is what has prevented you from hearing the news of heaven.” Then and there they returned to their people and said: “O our people, we have heard a wondrous Quran, guiding to right conduct, and we have believed in it, and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.” Then Allah revealed to His Prophet: “Say: It has been revealed to me”—and what was revealed to him was only the speech of the jinn."],[12392,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited al-Najm, and when he reached, \"Have you considered al-Lat and al-Uzza\" \"and Manat, the third, the other,\" Satan cast onto his tongue: Those are the exalted gharaiq (cranes), and their intercession is surely hoped for. When he prostrated, the Muslims and the polytheists prostrated, so Allah ﷻ revealed, \"And We did not send before you any messenger or prophet except that, when he recited, Satan cast,\" up to His saying, \"the punishment of a barren day\"; the Day of Badr."],[12393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seeing is not like being told.\" Allah said to Musa: \"Your people have been tested,\" but he did not throw down the Tablets. When he saw [them], he threw down the Tablets and broke them."],[12394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ said: \"If I take the two precious things of My servant (his eyes) and he is patient and seeks reward, I will not be satisfied with any reward for him less than Paradise.\""],[12395,"\"...that they should give something to their relatives among the polytheists, so they asked, and permission was granted to them.\" Then this verse was revealed: {It is not your responsibility to guide them, but Allah guides whom He wills. And whatever good you spend is for yourselves} until His saying {and you will not be wronged}."],[12396,"\"In His saying, 'And do not make your prayer too loud or too low, but seek between that a way.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the Qur'an with a loud voice during prayer. When the polytheists heard him, they insulted him and those who brought him. So Allah revealed to him, 'And do not make your prayer too loud.' Then the polytheists would hear him and insult him. 'And do not make your prayer too low.' He said, 'Inform your companions.' 'But seek between that a way.'\""],[12397,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {And when they hear what has been revealed to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears} he said: \"They were sailors - meaning seamen - who came with Ja'far b. Abi Talib from Abyssinia. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the Qur'an, they believed and their eyes overflowed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Perhaps when you return to your land you will change your religion.' They said: 'We will never change our religion.' So Allah ﷻ revealed that about their statement.\""],[12398,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymuna, and it was her night. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray, and I stood on his left. He took hold of my forelock or my hair and made me stand on his right."],[12399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no Muslim but he has a sin that afflicts him time after time. Indeed the believer is forgetful: when he is reminded, he remembers.\""],[12400,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said to her: \"What prevents you from performing Hajj?\" She said: \"We only have a camel used for carrying water, and my father and husband went on a military expedition with it.\" He said to her: \"Perform 'Umrah in Ramadan, for it is equal to a Hajj for you.\""],[12401,"The prohibition of wine was revealed concerning two tribes of the Ansar. They drank until, when they became intoxicated, they started playing with one another. When they sobered up, a man would see the marks on his face, his head, and his beard, and say: \"My brother So-and-so did this to me. By Allah, if he had been kind and merciful to me, he would not have done this to me.\" They had been brothers with no rancor in their hearts, but rancor fell into their hearts. So Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, wine, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through wine and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?} Then some people who were scrupulous said: \"It is defilement, and it is in the belly of So-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and So-and-so who was killed on the day of Uhud.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is not upon those who believe and do righteousness [any] blame concerning what they have eaten} [the rest of] the verse."],[12402,"A woman brought her son to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my son has madness, and it seizes him at our lunch and dinner, and he becomes troublesome to us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his chest and supplicated. He vomited a vomit, and out of his belly came something like a black puppy, and he was healed."],[12404,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah and Hal Ata 'ala al-Insan."],[12405,"Allah made the prayer obligatory through the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ: four rak'ahs when resident, and two rak'ahs when traveling."],[12406,"Ibn Abbas said: \"Marry, for the best of us was the one with the most wives.\""],[12407,"The Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-ʿAqabah."],[12408,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Prophet ﷺ got up to pray during the night, so I got up on his left side. He took me by the hand and placed me on his right side, wiped my chest, and said: “O Allah, grant him wisdom.”"],[12409,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the men among you who will be from the people of this world in Paradise?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The Prophet ﷺ is in Paradise, the Siddiq is in Paradise, the martyr is in Paradise, the newborn born into Islam is in Paradise, and a man who is in a remote part of a city and visits his brother only for the sake of Allah is in Paradise. Shall I inform you of your women who will be among the people of Paradise?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The loving, child-bearing woman who, when she becomes angry or is made angry, says: 'My hand is in your hand; I will not close my eyes in sleep.'”"],[12411,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Death has a terror. When one of you experiences the death of his brother, let him say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. And indeed to our Lord we are returning. O Allah, record him among the doers of good, place his record in ʿIlliyyin, and grant a righteous successor for his offspring among those who remain. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward and do not test us after him.'”"],[12412,"Thirty-nine men and a woman embraced Islam with the Prophet ﷺ. ʿUmar embraced Islam as the completion of forty, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O Prophet, sufficient for you is Allah and whoever follows you of the believers.}"],[12413,"I spent the night at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. When the Prophet ﷺ prayed ʿIsha, he returned to her, and it was her night. He prayed two rakʿahs, then turned and said: “Has the boy slept?” I was listening. He said in his prayer: “O Allah, place light in my heart, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my tongue, and grant me light.”"],[12414,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'Convey greetings of peace to ʿUmar and tell him that his approval is judgment and his anger is honor.'”"],[12415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever acts for the sake of Allah within the community and does what is correct, Allah accepts it from him; and if he errs, He forgives him. But whoever acts seeking to cause division and does what is correct, Allah does not accept it from him; and if he errs, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[12416,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station}, he said: “He will seat him between Himself and Jibril, and he will intercede for his Ummah. That is the praised station.”"],[12417,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever claims descent from other than his father, or affirms loyalty to other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[12418,"The Prophet ﷺ married while in a state of ihram and cupped while in a state of ihram."],[12419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married while in a state of ihram and cupped while in a state of ihram."],[12420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions performed ʿumrah from al-Jiʿrānah, so they uncovered their right shoulders and placed their cloaks under their armpits, then threw them over their left shoulders, and then they did ramal."],[12421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will surely raise the Stone on the Day of Resurrection with two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, bearing witness for whoever touched it in truth.”"],[12422,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {in a muddy spring}."],[12423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are a kind of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[12424,"I found in my father’s book. Abu al-Ashjaʿ gave us his father’s book, so we copied from it from Sufyān, from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUthmān b. Khuthaym, from Saʿīd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I slaughtered before I threw.” He said: “Throw, and there is no harm.” Then he said, “I shaved before I threw.” He said: “Throw, and there is no harm.”"],[12425,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.”"],[12426,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who mentioned his Lord, Exalted is He, saying: “When My servant remembers Me in private, I remember him in private; and when he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering better than the gathering in which he remembered Me.”"],[12429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of your garments is white, so dress your living in it and shroud your dead in it.”"],[12436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sit on the ground, eat on the ground, milk the ewe, and accept the invitation of a slave to barley bread."],[12437,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I engaged with a woman in what is short of intercourse.” So Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night}."],[12438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The resident and the visitor are equal therein.” He said: “Equal are the one who stays and the one who departs.”"],[12439,"The Jews said: 'Allah's hand is tied up.' May their hands be tied up and may they be cursed for what they said. Rather, both His hands are spread out, He spends as He wills."],[12440,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was diverted from Sham (Greater Syria) to Qibla (Kaaba), and he performed Salah toward the Kaaba in Rajab, during the first seventeen months of his stay in Madinah.\""],[12441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a group of traders and said, \"O group of traders.\" They responded to him and raised their necks. He said, \"Verily, Allah will resurrect you on the Day of Judgment as wicked except for those who are truthful, righteous, and fulfill their trust.\""],[12442,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'When Allah created the Pen, He said to it: Write. So it wrote everything that will occur until the Hour comes.'"],[12443,"I said to Ibn Abbas: 'Is there repentance for someone who intentionally kills a believer?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'Then what about His saying: {And those who do not call upon another god besides Allah, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery; and whoever does that will meet a penalty multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will abide therein humiliated — except for those who repent, believe, and do righteous work; then Allah will replace their evil deeds with good deeds}?' He said: 'This is a Makkan verse, which was abrogated by a Madinan verse: {But whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell, abiding therein forever, and Allah's wrath is upon him and He has cursed him and prepared for him a great punishment}.'"],[12444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water, and a bucket of Zamzam was brought to him. He drank from it while standing."],[12445,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, when he raised his head from bowing he would say: 'O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.'"],[12446,"I stayed overnight at the house of my maternal aunt Maymunah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up during the night, performed ablution three times each, then stood to pray. I got up and did as he did, then I stood on his left, so he positioned me on his right."],[12447,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade solid silk (garments)."],[12448,"He poured water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ablution at his maternal aunt Maymunah's house. When he came out, he said: 'Who placed my ablution water for me?' She said: 'My sister's son, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'O Allah, give him understanding in the religion and teach him interpretation.'"],[12449,"Thursday, and what a day Thursday was! A day on which the Prophet's ﷺ pain intensified.' And he mentioned the hadith."],[12450,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'I am holding you back by your waist-wrappers from the Fire, saying: Beware of Hell, beware of the prescribed punishments. When I die, I will be your forerunner, and your appointed place is at the Pond. Whoever reaches it will succeed. And some people will come and be taken to the left. I will say: O Lord, my community. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you, turning back on their heels.'"],[12451,"Adiyy b. Badda' and Tamim al-Dari used to travel to Makkah for trade. A man from Banu Sahm went out with them and died in a land where there was no Muslim. He entrusted his belongings to them, so they delivered his inheritance to his family but kept a silver cup inlaid with gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made them swear by Allah that they had not concealed it or disclosed it. Then they found the cup in Makkah, and they said: 'We bought it from Tamim al-Dari and Adiyy.' Two men from the heirs of the Sahmi stood up, swore, and took the cup. Concerning them, this verse was revealed: {O you who believe, testimony among you...} the verse."],[12452,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Moses ﷺ performed Hajj on a red camel, wearing a Qatwani cloak.'"],[12453,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah created a preserved tablet made of a white pearl, its pages are made of red ruby, and His pen is light for Him. Every day, He creates and provides sustenance, causes death and gives life, honors and humiliates, and does whatever He wills.\""],[12454,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my mother died and had not performed Hajj; shall I perform Hajj on her behalf?\" He said, \"Tell me, if your mother had a debt and you paid it off, would that settle it for her?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The debt owed to Allah is more deserving of being settled.\""],[12455,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah.\""],[12456,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not send a prophet to a people and take him back except that He makes a period of slackness after him, then He fills Hell from that period of slackness.\""],[12457,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Allah does not send a prophet among a people and then take him back except that He makes a period of slackness after him and fills Hell from that period of slackness.\""],[12458,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr in Madinah without travel or fear.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbas, \"Why do you think he did that?\" He said, \"He wanted not to cause hardship to anyone of his Ummah.\""],[12459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and combined Maghrib and ʿIsha in Madinah while he was resident, without fear or anything that compelled him to do so.\" They said, \"Why, O Abu ʿAbbas?\" He said, \"He wanted not to cause hardship to his Ummah.\""],[12460,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr and ʿAsr together in Madinah without fear or travel."],[12461,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha."],[12462,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and Maghrib and ʿIsha, on a journey or on the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[12463,"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and ʿAsr, and between Maghrib and ʿIsha, during travel."],[12464,"He said to his sons, \"O my sons, go out from Makkah for Hajj on foot, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'For the pilgrim who rides, for every step his mount takes there are seventy good deeds; and for the one who walks, for every step there are seven hundred good deeds.'\""],[12465,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ [said], \"Wash him with water and lote tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12466,"A man in ihram was thrown by his mount and his neck broke, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah."],[12467,"A man among us was thrown from his mount while he was in ihram, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey when a man's she-camel threw him and broke his neck, and he died while in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12469,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was traveling, and with him was a Muslim man in ihram, his camel stumbled and he fell from it, and his neck was broken. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in the two garments in which he entered ihram, and do not cover his face, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12471,"A man's she-camel threw him and killed him while he was in ihram, and he was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his face, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12472,"A man's camel threw him and broke his neck while he was in ihram. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Clothe him in two garments, wash him with water and lote leaves, and do not cover his head, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12474,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12475,"While a man was on his she-camel, it threw him and broke his neck, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with lote leaves and water, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head or his face, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote leaves, shroud him in his two garments, and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah\" or he said \"with matted hair.\""],[12477,"Mohammad said, \"Wash him and don't bring him near anything that he was prohibited from. Shroud him in his two garments, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection wearing them.\""],[12478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him and shroud him in his two garments, and do not touch him with anything that was forbidden to him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12479,"A Muslim man died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that he be washed and wrapped in two garments and not touched with perfume. And I am uncertain whether his head was covered or not. He said: \"This one will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah.\""],[12480,"A man was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he fell from his mount and died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be shrouded and washed, and that his face not be covered, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah, or he said uttering the talbiyah."],[12481,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"My brother’s camel threw him, and he died while he was in ihram.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, and do not perfume him, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection in ihram.\""],[12482,"A she-camel trampled a man in ihram and killed him, so the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought, and he said: \"Wash him and shroud him, but do not wash his head and do not bring perfume near him, for he will be resurrected uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12483,"He fell off his mount while he was in ihram, and it trampled him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought, and that was mentioned to him, so he said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not cover his face, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12484,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ on a camel while he was in ihram, and it killed him — Shuʿbah said, meaning he died — so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments with his head uncovered, and do not touch him with perfume, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah.\""],[12485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Wash him with water and lote-tree leaves, shroud him in his two garments, do not touch him with perfume, and do not cover his head, for he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with matted hair.\""],[12486,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not know the end of a surah until \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim\" was sent down upon him."],[12487,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a revelation with the phrase \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful\", he knew that the previous Surah had ended and he would then begin reciting the next one."],[12488,"Jibril ﷺ used to send down revelation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he said \"Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim,\" he began another surah."],[12489,"The Prophet ﷺ came out from the privy, then sat down and ate. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not perform ablution?\" He said: \"I have only been commanded to perform ablution for prayer; as for eating, no.\""],[12490,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was in ihram.\" This is how Muʿawiyah b. Hisham narrated it. But the companions of al-Thawri narrated it from al-Thawri, from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbas, and that is the correct version."],[12491,"\"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight rakʿahs together and five rakʿahs together without rain or fear.\" This is how al-Juʿfi Husayn narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah. But the companions of Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Ibn ʿUyaynah, from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd, and likewise the companions of ʿAmr b. Dinar narrated it from ʿAmr b. Dinar, from Jabir b. Zayd."],[12492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, walking, and uncircumcised.\""],[12493,"\"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and repeated it three times, then he said, 'Do you know why I gave the guarantee?' They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'Gabriel came to me and informed me that whoever you are mentioned in his presence and he does not send blessings upon you, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.' And whoever reaches both his parents or one of them in old age and does not enter Paradise through them, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.' And whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, he will enter Hellfire, so Allah distances him and insults him. Then I said, 'Ameen.'\""],[12494,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day with the people around him, and he said: \"Indeed Allah ﷻ has given every prophet a desire, and my desire is in standing in this night [prayer], so let no one pray behind me. And Allah has given every prophet a provision, and my provision is this fifth; so when I am taken, it belongs to the rulers of affairs after me.\""],[12495,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ supplicated, saying, “O Allah, bless us in our sa’ and our mudd, and bless us in our Makkah and our Madinah, and bless us in our Sham and our Yemen.” A man among the people said, “O Prophet of Allah, and our Iraq?” He said, “Therein is the horn of Satan and the barking of tribulations, and indeed coarseness is in the east.”"],[12496,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever hears the call and says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O Allah, bless him and convey him to the station of intercession (wasīlah) with You, and make us among those for whom he intercedes on the Day of Resurrection, intercession becomes incumbent for him.”"],[12497,"Amr b. Abi Asim al-Nabil reported to us: My father reported to us from Thawr b. Yazid: Maslama b. Abi Ata reported to me from Sa'id b. Jubayr, who said: Abdullah b. Abbas and Abdullah b. Umar testified before me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade (using) gourds, vessels coated with pitch, vessels coated with tar, and hantam jars.” I said, “What is hantam?” He said, “Every (vessel made of) clay.”"],[12498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah ﷻ makes lands flourish for a people and makes wealth fruitful for them, and He has not looked at them since He created them out of hatred for them.” It was said, “How is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Because of their maintaining ties of kinship.”"],[12499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf, then returned and came to the watering place, and said: “Give me a drink of what the people drink.”"],[12500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “combined between Zuhr and Asr in Madinah without fear.”"],[12501,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, indeed I love you so much that I remember you, and were it not that I come and look at you, I would think that my soul would depart. Then I remember that if I enter Paradise, I will be below you in station, and that distresses me, and I would love to be with you in rank.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not reply anything, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {And whoever obeys Allah and the Messenger, they will be with those whom Allah has favored} (the verse). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and recited it to him."],[12503,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “Which of you knows Quss b. Sa'ida al-Iyadi?” They said, “All of us know him, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “What became of him?” They said, “He perished.” He said: “I will not forget him at Ukaz in the sacred month, while he was on a red camel, addressing the people, saying: O people, gather, listen, and understand. Whoever lives dies, and whoever dies is gone, and everything that is to come will come. Indeed in the sky there is news, and in the earth there are lessons: a bed laid out, a ceiling raised, stars that move, and seas that do not diminish. Quss swore a true oath: if there is contentment on earth, there will certainly be discontent after it. Indeed Allah has a religion that is dearer to Him than the religion you follow. Why do I see people going and not returning? Are they pleased and staying, or are they left and sleeping?” Then he ﷺ said, “Is there among you anyone who can recite his poetry?” So some of them recited it."],[12505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The example of one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like a donkey carrying books, and the one who says to him ‘listen’ has no Jumu'ah.”"],[12506,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord ﷻ twice: once with his sight and once with his heart."],[12507,"He used to say regarding His saying, {And he certainly saw him on the clear horizon}: “I only mean Jibril ﷺ , that Muhammad ﷺ saw him in his form at the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary.”"],[12508,"The Prophet ﷺ had himself cupped while he was fasting and in ihram."],[12509,"I stood one night to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, and I stood on his left, so he gestured with his hand from behind him and took my hand—or my upper arm—until he made me stand on his right."],[12510,"I asked Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abdullah ibn Umar how the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was. They said, \"He would pray thirteen rakats, and he would perform witr with three rakats after the 'Isha prayer.\""],[12511,"\"In his saying 'Say, I do not ask you for it any payment, except for love of [my] relatives', he ﷺ said, 'Maintain my kinship ties and do not deny me.'\""],[12512,"Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer and the two units of prayer while traveling.\""],[12513,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, when were you written as a prophet?” He said, “When Adam was between the spirit and the body.”"],[12514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a sheep’s shoulder in the mosque, and he ate it; then he stood for prayer and did not touch water."],[12515,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade us to take anything with a soul as a target."],[12516,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking standing from Zamzam—and the wording is from the hadith of Abu Nuʿaym."],[12517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water, so we gave him Zamzam water. He drank while standing."],[12518,"I handed the Prophet ﷺ a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12519,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked for water and was brought a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12520,"I gave the Prophet ﷺ water from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12521,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ a bucket from Zamzam, and he drank while standing."],[12522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral after it had been buried."],[12523,"He told me that he witnessed the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"He came to a desolate grave, so he aligned them and loudly proclaimed Allahu Akbar four times.\" Sulaiman said, \"I asked Ash-Sha'bi, 'O Abu Amr, who informed you of this?' He said, 'Ibn Abbas.'\""],[12524,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a grave and said, “What is this?” They said, “He—or she—was buried last night.” Ibn ʿAbbas said, “So he lined us up behind him, then he prayed over it.”"],[12525,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a grave and said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"Someone was buried last night.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said, \"We formed rows behind him, then he prayed over him.\""],[12526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins, and he gave the cupper his wage. Had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."],[12527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Abu Taybah, and he cupped him, and he reduced his tax by half a saʿ or more."],[12528,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be cupped three times: on the two jugular veins or between the shoulder blades. A servant of his from Bayadah, called Abu Hind, cupped him. He used to pay his family a mudd and a half every day, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ interceded for him, so they reduced it by half a mudd. After that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give the cupper his wage, and had it been unlawful, he would not have given it to him."],[12529,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins and the withers."],[12530,"The Prophet ﷺ used to be cupped on the two jugular veins and the withers."],[12533,"A questioner asked while Ibn ʿAbbas was praying, and Ibn ʿAbbas said to him: O questioner. He said: At your service. He said: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And do you pray the five prayers? He said: Yes. He said: And do you fast Ramadan? He said: Yes. He said: It is incumbent upon us to help you. So he took off a garment he was wearing and clothed him with it. Then he said: At that, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Any Muslim who clothes a Muslim with a garment remains in Allah's protection as long as a patch of it remains on him.\""],[12535,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will surely send a man whom Allah will not disgrace.\" He sent for ʿAli while he was at the mill grinding, and none of you would have been grinding. They brought him with sore eyes, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, I can hardly see. He blew into his eyes, shook the banner three times, then handed it to him. Victory was granted to him, and he brought Safiyyah bt. Huyayy. Then he said to his cousins: \"Which of you will be my protector in this world and the Hereafter?\" three times, until he passed by the last of them. ʿAli said: O Prophet of Allah, I am your protector in this world and the Hereafter. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter.\" He said: And he sent Abu Bakr with Surat al-Tawbah, and he sent ʿAli after him. Abu Bakr said: O ʿAli, perhaps Allah and His Prophet are displeased with me. ʿAli said: No, but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting that anyone should convey from me except a man from me, and I am from him.\" He said: And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ placed his garment over ʿAli, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, and said: \"Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.\" And he was the first to embrace Islam after Khadijah among the people. He said: And ʿAli purchased his own life; he wore the Prophet's ﷺ garment, then stood in his place. He said: The polytheists were throwing stones at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr came and said: Come to me, O Messenger of Allah—Abu Bakr thought he was the Prophet of Allah. ʿAli said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ has set out toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him. Abu Bakr set out and entered the cave with him. ʿAli kept throwing stones as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to throw, writhing with his head wrapped in the garment, not removing it until morning. Then he uncovered his head when morning came, and they said: You are indeed despicable. Your companion, when we throw stones at him, does not writhe, but you writhe. We found that strange. He said: Then he set out with the people on the expedition of Tabuk. ʿAli said to him: Shall I go out with you? The Prophet ﷺ said: \"No.\" So ʿAli wept. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that you are not a prophet? It is not fitting that I should go unless you are my deputy.\" He said: And he said to him: \"You are the protector of every believer after me.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ closed the doors of the mosque except ʿAli's door, so he could enter the mosque while in a state of major ritual impurity, since it was his path and he had no other path. He said: And he said: \"Whoever's mawla I am, ʿAli is his mawla.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said: Allah has informed us in the Quran that He is pleased with them, with the companions of the tree, knowing what is in their hearts. Did He tell us that He became displeased with them afterwards? And he said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar when he said: Will you permit me to strike his neck—meaning Hatib: \"Would you have done it? And what do you know? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do whatever you wish?\""],[12536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered all the doors to be closed except ʿAli's door ؓ."],[12537,"A man from the Banu 'Amir came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was a healer and a physician, so he said, \"O Muhammad, you utter certain words. Can I heal you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then called him to Allah ﷻ and asked, \"Would you like me to show you a sign?\" He had some date-palms and a tree with him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called forth a stalk from it. The man approached him while he was prostrating and raising his head until he reached him. Then he stood in front of him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Return to your place.\" So he returned to his place. Al-'Amiri swore, \"By Allah, I will never deny what you say.\" Then he said, \"O people of Banu Sa'sa'a, by Allah, I will never deny anything he says.\""],[12538,"While we were washing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man came and knocked on the door, saying: I remind you of Allah—will you not give me today a share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? ʿAli said: Let him in and place him behind the curtain; he will hand us the water. We let him in, and he handed us the water. And ʿAli said: By Allah, I did not turn him except that another was with me turning him. He said: And I heard in the house: Do not remove the shirt from him."],[12539,"Do you see one who killed a believer deliberately, then repented, believed, and did righteous deeds, then was guided? He said: And how can repentance be his, when I heard your Prophet ﷺ say: The closest of creation to the Throne of the Merciful on the Day of Resurrection will be the believer who was killed unjustly, his head on his right and his killer on his left, and his jugular veins gushing blood, saying: My Lord, ask this one why he killed me? Why did he come between me and the prayer?"],[12540,"The first to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about nabidh were the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays. They came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of abundant vegetation, and we obtain fresh herbs, so he ordered us to prepare a drink. He said: \"Soak [dates or raisins] in waterskins, but do not soak in earthenware jars, nor in gourds, nor in vessels smeared with pitch, nor in hollowed-out stumps, for I have been forbidden wine, gambling, and the kubah, which is the drum, and every intoxicant is unlawful.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it becomes strong? He said: \"Pour water over it.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if it becomes strong? He said: \"Pour water over it.\" He said on the third or fourth time: \"When it becomes strong, then pour it out.\""],[12542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[12543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The price of wine is unlawful, the dower of a prostitute is unlawful, the price of a dog is unlawful, and the kubah is unlawful. If the owner of a dog comes to you seeking its price, then fill his hands with dust. Wine, gambling, and every intoxicant are unlawful.\""],[12544,"For Jibril ﷺ used to present the Quran to the Prophet ﷺ every year in Ramadan. He said: So he presented the Quran to him in the year in which the Prophet ﷺ passed away twice. Thus ʿAbdullah witnessed what was abrogated from it and what was changed. So the final recitation of ʿAbdullah is the latter one."],[12549,"This verse was revealed: {And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe.} \"So the people refrained from marrying them until the verse after it was revealed.\" {This day good things have been made lawful to you. The food of those given the Scripture is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them. And chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those given the Scripture. This day good things have been made lawful to you. The food of those given the Scripture is lawful for you, and your food is lawful for them. And chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those given the Scripture.} \"So the people married women of the People of the Scripture.\""],[12550,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Good conduct and good appearance are one part of seventy parts of prophethood.\""],[12551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Good conduct, good appearance, and moderation are one part of forty-five parts of prophethood.\""],[12552,"He said: We said to Ibn ʿAbbas: Have you considered the saying of Allah (glorified and exalted be He): {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his chest}? He said: \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood one day to pray, and a thought crossed his mind.\" The hypocrites who were praying with him said: Do you not see that he has two hearts, a heart with you and a heart with them? So Allah (glorified and exalted be He) revealed: {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his chest}."],[12553,"Two men came to the Prophet of God ﷺ with one need. One of them greeted, and the Messenger of God ﷺ noticed an unpleasant odor from his mouth. He said to him, \"Do you not use the tooth stick (siwāk)?\" He replied, \"I do, but I have not eaten any food for three days.\" So he ordered a man to host him and fulfill his need."],[12554,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not one of us who steals, robs, or indicates towards theft.\""],[12556,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ spread apart the thighs of al-Ḥusayn and kiss his private part.\""],[12557,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"If the one who begs knew what he incurs from it, he would not beg.\""],[12558,"\"If a Qur'an with which mountains were moved, or the earth were split asunder, or the dead were made to speak...\" He said: They said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"If it is as you say, then show us our forefathers from among the dead so we may speak to them, and open for us these mountains—the mountains of Makkah that have enclosed us.\" Then it was revealed: \"And if there had been a Qur'an with which mountains were moved, or the earth were split asunder, or the dead were made to speak...\""],[12559,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Mecca for ten years, then descended [to the verse]: \"{Say: 'My Lord, admit me with an entrance of truth and exit me with an exit of truth.'}\" Then, he migrated to Medina."],[12560,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The man who has nothing of the Qur'an inside him is like a ruined house.\""],[12561,"\"The Messenger ﷺ said, 'There is no one among you except that he has been assigned a companion from the jinn.' They asked, 'Even you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, but Allah has helped me against him, so he has become a Muslim.'\""],[12562,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us in haste while we were sitting, and his haste startled us. When he reached us, he greeted and then said: \"I came to you in haste to inform you about the Night of Decree, but I forgot it between me and you, so seek it in the last ten nights.\""],[12563,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"How can I know that you are the Messenger of God?\" He said, \"If I call this cluster from this palm tree, will you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The cluster came down from the palm tree until it fell to the ground, and it began to hop until it came to the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said to it, \"Return,\" and it returned until it went back to its place. The Bedouin said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God,\" and he believed."],[12564,"\"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of God ﷺ at night, and he would drink it the next day, and that night, and the next day, and that night, and the next day, until when evening came he would drink it and give it to others to drink, or he would order it and it would be poured out.\""],[12565,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to have raisins soaked for him, and he would drink it that day, the next day, and the day after that, until the evening of that night. Then he would order that it be given to others to drink or poured out.\""],[12566,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to have nabīdh soaked for him, and he would drink it the next day and the day after. When it was the third day, he would order it to be poured out.\""],[12568,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to have raisins soaked for him in a water-skin, and he would drink it from the evening, and the next day, and the day after that. If any remained, he would order it to be poured out or drunk.\""],[12569,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"used to have nabīdh soaked for him, and he would drink it that day and its night, and the next day and its night. When it was the third day, he would order that it be poured out or given to the servants to drink.\""],[12570,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a waterskin, and he would drink it the next day and its night, and the day after and its night. When it was the third day, he would order that it be poured out or he would give it to the servants to drink."],[12571,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would drink it that day and the next day and the third day. When evening came, he would pour it out or give it to the servants to drink, and he would not give the servants anything forbidden to drink."],[12572,"Raisins would be soaked for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would drink it the next day and the day after. When the evening of the third day came, he would pour it out or order that it be poured out."],[12573,"I heard Ibn Abbas saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, green jars, and hollowed wood.\""],[12574,"Wine itself was forbidden, the little of it and the much of it, and intoxication from every drink."],[12575,"I traveled with Ibn Abbas from Madinah to Syria and asked him: Did the Prophet ﷺ leave a will? He said: \"When the Prophet ﷺ fell ill with the illness in which he died, he was in the house of Aishah. He said: 'Call Ali for me.' She said: 'Shall we not call Abu Bakr, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Call him.' Then Hafsah said: 'Shall we not call Umar?' He said: 'Call him.' Then Umm al-Fadl said: 'Shall we not call al-Abbas, your uncle?' He said: 'Call him.' When they had gathered, he raised his head and did not see Ali, so he remained silent and did not speak. Umar said: 'Rise and leave the Prophet ﷺ, for if he had a need from us he would have mentioned it.' He did that three times, then said: 'Let Abu Bakr lead the people in prayer.' Aishah said: 'Abu Bakr was present, so Abu Bakr came forward to lead the people in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt some relief, so he went out leaning between two men. When the people sensed him, they glorified Allah, and Abu Bakr moved to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: 'Stay where you are.' The Prophet ﷺ began the recitation from where Abu Bakr had ended, with Abu Bakr standing and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting. Abu Bakr followed the Prophet ﷺ, and the people followed Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah did not finish the prayer until he became very heavy, so he went out leaning between two men, with his feet dragging on the ground. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and he did not leave a will.\""],[12576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever has enough to reach the Sacred House of Allah for Hajj but does not perform Hajj, and whoever has wealth that reaches the threshold of zakah but does not pay it, will ask to be sent back at the time of death.' A man said to him: 'Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas! Only the disbeliever asks to be sent back!' He said: 'I will recite to you the Qur'an: {O you who believe, spend from what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a short while}.'"],[12577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever has enough to perform Hajj but does not perform Hajj, or enough to pay zakah but does not pay it, will ask to be sent back at the time of death.' A man said to him: 'Fear Allah, O Abu Abbas! Only the disbeliever asks to be sent back!' He said: 'I will recite to you the Qur'an: {O you who believe, spend from what We have provided you before death comes to one of you and he says: My Lord, if only You would delay me for a short while, so that I may give charity and be among the righteous}.'"],[12578,"Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed on the day of Khaybar. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered it, the Muslims captured women from the People of the Book who had husbands. When a man wanted to approach one of these women, she would say: 'I have a husband.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about that, and Allah, glorified be He, sent down this verse: {And protected women among women} - the verse - meaning the captive women from the polytheists who are captured: there is no harm in that. I mentioned this to Sa'id ibn Jubayr, and he said: 'He spoke the truth.'"],[12579,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Goodness reaches the house in which food is eaten faster than a knife reaches the hump of a camel.'"],[12580,"My father narrated to me, dictating from his original book: Muhammad b. Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Umar Abu Yahya, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn Abbas, who said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing any living creature unless it harms.'"],[12581,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah, glorified be He: {And when the Prophet confided a matter to one of his wives}: He said: Hafsah entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in her house while he was having intercourse with Mariyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: 'Do not tell Aishah until I give you glad tidings: your father will take charge after Abu Bakr when I die.' Hafsah went and told Aishah that she saw the Prophet ﷺ having intercourse with Mariyah, and she told her that the Prophet ﷺ informed her that Abu Bakr would take charge after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umar after him. Aishah said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Who told you this?' He said: 'The All-Knowing, the All-Aware told me.' Aishah said: 'I will not look at you until you make Mariyah forbidden to yourself.' So he made her forbidden, and Allah, glorified be He, sent down: {O Prophet, why do you forbid}."],[12582,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The one killed defending his wealth is a martyr, the one killed defending his family is a martyr, and the one killed defending his own life is a martyr.\""],[12584,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Beautify your voices with the Qur'an.\""],[12585,"\"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' in Madinah without any reason.\" It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: \"What did he intend by that?\" He said: \"To make things easier for his Ummah.\""],[12586,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Today is the pledge, tomorrow is the race, and the goal is Paradise or the Fire. I am the first, Abu Bakr is the second, 'Umar is the third, and the people after that are in the race: the first, then the next.\""],[12587,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, when was your covenant taken?\" He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[12588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one has done me more favors than Abu Bakr. He gave me his daughter in marriage, helped me migrate to the abode of emigration, and if I were to take a close friend (khalil), I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but instead there is the brotherhood of affection until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12589,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a donkey called Ya'fur, and I began to sweat, so he ordered me to perform ghusl.\""],[12590,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"When Jibril ﷺ brought revelation to the Prophet ﷺ, he would not finish until the Prophet ﷺ began to speak the first of it, out of fear that he would faint. Jibril said to him: 'Why do you do that?' He said: 'Out of fear that I might forget.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {We will make you recite, so you will not forget}.\""],[12591,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah ﷻ spoke to Musa in one hundred and forty thousand words over three days. When Musa ﷺ heard the speech of human beings, he despised them because of what had entered his ears from the speech of the Lord ﷻ. Among what He confided to him was: \"O Musa, those who put on a show have not put on a show with anything like asceticism in this world, and those who seek closeness to Me have not drawn near with anything like piety from what I have forbidden them, and those who worship have not worshipped with anything like weeping out of fear of Me.\" Musa said: \"O Lord of all creation, O Master of the Day of Judgment, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, what have You prepared for them and how have You rewarded them?\" He said: \"As for the ascetics in this world, I will permit them to enter My Paradise, and they will settle wherever they wish. As for the pious who abstain from what I have forbidden them, on the Day of Resurrection, no servant will remain but that I will take him to account and scrutinize him, except the pious, for I will be shy of them, honor them, and admit them to Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep out of fear of Me, they will have the highest station, in which they will not be shared with.\"\""],[12592,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who is killed in the path of Allah facing forward, not turning back, will reach Paradise seventy years before the one killed while retreating. The sick of my Ummah will reach Paradise seventy years before their healthy ones. And the prophets before Sulayman b. Dawud will reach Paradise forty years before him because of the kingdom he had.\""],[12593,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A woman should not travel three miles except with a husband or with a mahram.' It was said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'People say three days.' He said: 'That is a mistake on their part.'\""],[12594,"Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Dahhak, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied the banner for 'Ali on the day of Khaybar, he supplicated for him for a little while and said: 'O Allah, help him and grant victory through him, have mercy on him and have mercy through him, support him and support through him. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and be an enemy to whoever is his enemy.'\""],[12595,"When the Prophet ﷺ intended to go out for the expedition of Tabuk, he said to Jadd Ibn Qais, \"O Jadd Ibn Qais, what do you say about fighting Bani Asfar (the yellow people)?\" Jadd replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who has companionship with women, and whenever I see the women of Bani Asfar (the yellow people), I become tempted. Therefore, grant me permission to stay behind and do not include me in the expedition, so that I do not become tempted.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed the verse {And among them are those who say, \"Grant me permission [to be exempted from fighting] and do not put me to trial.\" Unquestionably, they have fallen into trial.}"],[12596,"In His saying \"{Allah shall give them love}\" He said, \"Love in the hearts of the believers was revealed concerning Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah honor his face.\""],[12597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A thrifty person is never destitute.”"],[12598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They are two veils: the husband and the grave.”"],[12599,"Regarding His statement {For they do not lie to you} lightly — and thus he used to recite it — he said: “They are not able to not be a messenger, nor to not be the Qur’an as Qur’an. If they were to lie to you with their tongues, they would be lying to you, and that is nothing but a liar, and that is the denial.”"],[12600,"Regarding His statement {Do not say “ra’ina”}, he said: “They used to say to the Prophet ﷺ ‘attend to us, let us hear you,’ but ‘ra’ina’ is like your saying ‘give us.’ {And listen without being made to hear} — for the Prophet ﷺ — he said: “They say, ‘May you not hear.’ And ‘listen’ — for the Prophet ﷺ — ‘may you not hear.’ He said: {And if they had said, ‘We hear and obey’ and ‘listen and consider us,’ it would have been better for them.}”"],[12601,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent out a raiding party and they gained spoils, he would divide the spoils into fifths, then strike that fifth into five parts. Then he recited: {And know that whatever you gain as spoils, for Allah is one fifth of it} up to His saying {for Allah} — the key of the statement — {To Allah belongs whatever is in the heavens and the earth}. He made the share of Allah and the share of the Messenger one. {And to the near relatives} — he made these two shares a source of strength in horses and weapons. He made the share of the orphans, the needy, and the wayfarer such that he would not give it to anyone else. He made the remaining four shares: for a horse two shares, for its rider one share, and for a foot soldier one share."],[12602,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A safeguard for my community from drowning, when they board ships, is to say: ‘In the name of Allah, the King. {They have not estimated Allah with His true estimation. The earth, all of it, will be in His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand. Glorified and exalted is He above what they associate with Him.} {In the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage. Indeed, my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful.}’”"],[12603,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The nobles of my community are the bearers of the Qur’an.”"],[12604,"I said to Ibn Abbas: “What do you think about coitus interruptus?” He said: “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said anything about it, then it is as he said. Otherwise, I say about it: {Your women are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish.} Whoever wishes may practice coitus interruptus, and whoever wishes may leave it.”"],[12605,"\"Two units, two units, the sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[12606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hesitated in a verse during the dawn prayer. When he finished the prayer, he turned his face to the people and said: “Did Ubayy b. Kaʿb attend the prayer with you?” They said: “No.” He said: “The people thought he missed him only so that he could prompt him.”"],[12607,"“The Aws and the Khazraj had enmity between them in the pre-Islamic era. While they were sitting one day, they mentioned what was between them until they became angry, and some of them rose against others with weapons.” So the verse was revealed: {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you?} — the entire verse and the two verses after it up to {And remember the favor of Allah upon you when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together.}"],[12608,"From Ibn Abbas regarding {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you and His Messenger is among you?} He said: “The Aws were conversing when they mentioned the affairs of the pre-Islamic era, and they became angry until there was war between them. They took up weapons and some of them advanced against others.” So the verse was revealed: {And how could you disbelieve while the verses of Allah are recited to you} up to His saying {then He saved you from it.}"],[12609,"Ibn Abbas was asked: “How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ test women?” He said: “When a woman came to him to accept Islam, he made her swear by Allah that she had not left out of hatred for a husband, and by Allah that she had not left to acquire a dinar, and by Allah that she had not left out of desire for one land over another, and by Allah that she had left only out of love for Allah and His Messenger.”"],[12610,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed three ʿumrahs in Dhu al-Qaʿdah."],[12611,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"How can I be at ease when the Companion of the Horn has already taken the horn in his mouth?\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ inclined his forehead, \"waiting for when he is commanded, then he blows.\" They said, \"O Messenger of God, what shall we say?\" He said: \"{Sufficient for us is God, and how excellent a Trustee is He}.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: {So when the trumpet is blown}."],[12612,"\"In his saying, 'When the trumpet is blown', he (the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ) said, 'How can I feel comfortable while the companion of the horn has already taken the horn?' And he pointed to his forehead saying, 'Does he listen to when he is commanded?' So his companions asked, 'Then what should we say?' He said, 'Say: Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'\""],[12613,"\"...that He will give you more than it.\""],[12614,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the earnings of slave women.\" I said to Ibn ʿAbbas, \"And why did he forbid it?\" He said: \"Out of fear that they would be unable, and then you would be unable.\""],[12615,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray four (rakʿahs) before Jumuʿah and four after it, not separating between them."],[12616,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on his way out to Badr: \"God ﷻ has promised me Badr and to grant me their camp as spoils. Whoever kills an enemy shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if God wills, and whoever captures a captive shall have such-and-such of their spoils, if God wills.\" When they faced each other, God cast terror into the hearts of the polytheists. When they fought, God defeated them, and the swift among the people pursued them; they killed seventy and captured seventy."],[12617,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ: \"He has not fasted, the one who fasts forever.\""],[12618,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, by God, I have come to you from a people for whom no shepherd sets out provisions and no stallion passes by them.\" So he ascended the pulpit, praised God, and then said: \"O God, give us a rain that rescues, makes fruitful, abundant, covering (the earth), swift, and not delayed.\" Then he descended, and no one came to us from any direction except that he said, \"You have revived us.\""],[12619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Makkah is the sacred sanctuary of God: its fresh herbage is not to be cut, its trees are not to be felled, and its game is not to be startled.\" Al-ʿAbbas said, \"O Messenger of God, except idhkhir, for it is for our blacksmiths and for the roofs of our houses.\" He said, \"Except idhkhir.\""],[12621,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed over a deceased person, he would say: \"O God, forgive our living and our dead, our present and our absent, our females and our males. Whoever You keep alive from among us, keep him alive upon Islam; and whoever You take from among us, take him upon faith. O God, Your pardon, Your pardon.\""],[12622,"A slain person was killed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ whose killer was unknown. So he ascended his pulpit and said: \"O people, shall a person be killed while I am among you and it is not known who killed him? If the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth were to gather to kill a Muslim man, God would punish them without number or reckoning.\""],[12623,"About [avoiding] harming the Prophet ﷺ and refraining from following him."],[12624,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my father has died; should I free a slave on his behalf?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[12625,"The Prophet ﷺ sent an army and its flag was returned, so he sent another and its flag was returned with the head of a golden deer. And then the verse was revealed (And it is not for any prophet to embezzle)."],[12626,"From [the prohibition of] solid silk."],[12627,"On the right of the Throne—and both of Allah's hands are right—upon pulpits of light, their faces of light; they are not prophets, nor martyrs, nor truthful ones.\" It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who are they?' He said, \"Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah, the Exalted.\""],[12628,"We set out as pilgrims, and when we camped at Batn Nakhl, we sighted the crescent. Some of the people said, 'It is three nights old,' and others said, 'It is two nights old.' We came to Ibn Abbas and said, 'We sighted the crescent; some of the people said it is three nights old, and others said it is two nights old.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ extended it for its sighting, so it is [counted] on the night you sighted it.'"],[12630,"\"There is no man who is put in charge of ten people but that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand fettered to his neck until judgment is passed between him and them.\""],[12631,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray eight rak'ahs at night and then he would pray three rak'ahs of witr."],[12632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever hears the sound of a bell, or enters a church, or a synagogue, or a fire temple, or a place of idols, and says: 'There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah,' Allah will record for him a reward equal to the number of those who did not say it, or he will be recorded with Allah as a truthful one.\""],[12633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever establishes prayer, gives Zakat, performs Hajj, fasts during Ramadan, and treats guests kindly will enter Paradise.\""],[12634,"Abu Jahl said, 'If Muhammad returns to pray behind the Maqam, I will certainly assault him.' It was said, 'There he is, praying behind the Maqam.' So he went toward him, then turned back and said, 'By al-Lat and al-Uzza, battalions of [angels] came between me and him.' Ibn Abbas said, 'Had he moved, the guards of Hell would have seized him.' Then he recited: {Let him call his associates; We will call the guards of Hell}."],[12635,"\"Muhammad ﷺ preceded [in declaring] badhaq [intoxicating]. What intoxicates is forbidden.\""],[12636,"\"Do you know why this verse was revealed? O you who have believed, do not ask about things that, if they are shown to you, will distress you. There were people who used to mock the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by saying, 'Who is my father?' And he would also say, 'My camel has gone astray, where is my camel?' So Allah revealed this verse.\""],[12637,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying, and a kid went to pass in front of him, so he hurried to block it. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while a she-donkey belonging to al-Fadl b. al-Abbas was grazing that day in front of him."],[12638,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr with five [units] and prostrated twice for forgetfulness while sitting.\""],[12639,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted Usama b. Zayd behind him on the Day of ʿArafa until he reached Muzdalifa, then he mounted al-Fadl behind him until he reached Jamrat al-ʿAqaba, and he did not cease reciting the talbiya until he threw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba.\""],[12640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, the young boys of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, ahead on donkeys on the night of Muzdalifa, and he began patting our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw the jamra until the sun rises.\""],[12641,"\"I do not know whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the Zuhr and ʿAsr prayers or not, but we recite.\""],[12642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hurried us at night from Muzdalifa to Mina and carried us to the jamarat, and he began striking our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba until the sun rises.\""],[12643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us, the young boys of Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib, ahead on donkeys, patting our thighs and saying, \"My dear sons, do not throw Jamrat al-ʿAqaba until the sun rises.\""],[12644,"\"I came with a boy from Banu ʿAbd al-Muttalib on a donkey while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in prayer, so we sent the donkey away and entered the row, and two slave girls came racing, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them.\""],[12645,"What do you say about the grandfather? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying and his grandfather passed by in front of him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastened to face the Qibla. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one day and there was a donkey belonging to Al-Fadl ibn Abbas grazing in front of him."],[12646,"When you throw the jamra, everything becomes permissible for you except women. He said, \"As for me, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perfuming his head with musk. Is that perfume or not?\""],[12649,"The Angel of Death came to the Prophet ﷺ during the illness in which he passed away, and he asked permission while his head was in the lap of ʿAli. He said, \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\" ʿAli ؓ said, \"Go back, for we are busy with you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you know who this is, O Abu al-Hasan? This is the Angel of Death. Enter, rightly guided.\" When he entered, he said, \"Your Lord ﷻ sends you greetings of peace.\" He said, \"Where is Jibril?\" He said, \"He is not near me now; he will come.\" The Angel of Death left until Jibril descended upon him. Jibril ﷺ said to him while he was standing at the door, \"What brought you out, O Angel of Death?\" He said, \"Muhammad ﷺ requested you.\" When they both sat, Jibril said, \"Peace be upon you, O Abu al-Qasim. This is a farewell from me and from you.\" It has reached me that the Angel of Death did not greet any household before him, nor will he greet anyone after him."],[12650,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever curses my companions, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.\""],[12651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let every man eat from his sacrificial animal.\""],[12652,"The Prophet ﷺ \"used to pray two rakʿas, two rakʿas whenever he left his house until he returned.\""],[12653,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from his family as a traveler, he would pray two rak'ahs until he returned to his family."],[12654,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his family on the two Eids."],[12655,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."],[12656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bring out his wives on the two Eids."],[12660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, may He be exalted, says: 'Whoever shows enmity to a friend of Mine, I have declared war on him. I have never hesitated about anything I am going to do as I hesitate about the death of a believer: he dislikes death, and I dislike distressing him. Sometimes My believing friend asks Me for wealth, but I turn him from wealth to poverty; if I turned him to wealth, it would be bad for him. Sometimes My believing friend asks Me for poverty, but I turn him to wealth; if I turned him to poverty, it would be bad for him. Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, said: By My might, My majesty, My loftiness, My splendor, My beauty, and the elevation of My station, no servant gives preference to My desire over his own desire except that I fix his term before his eyes, and the heaven and earth guarantee his provision, and I am behind the trade of every trader for him.'"],[12661,"When the Prophet ﷺ broke his fast, he would say: 'For You I have fasted, and upon Your provision I have broken my fast, so accept from me; indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.'"],[12663,"When the people of the mosque were expelled and 'Ali was left, the people talked about that. It reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'I did not expel you of my own accord, nor did I leave him; rather, Allah expelled you and left him. I am only a commanded servant; whatever I am commanded, I do. I follow only what is revealed to me.'"],[12664,"Allah created the Garden of Eden with His hand, lowered its fruits into it, and split its rivers in it. Then He looked into it and said: 'The believers have succeeded.' He said: 'By My might, no miser shall be My neighbor in it.'"],[12665,"The Prophet ﷺ only banished al-Ḥakam b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ from Madinah to al-Ṭāʾif. While the Prophet ﷺ was in his room, he saw a person peeking at him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “The gecko, the gecko.” He looked, and it was al-Ḥakam. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave; do not live with me in Madinah as long as I remain.” So he banished him to al-Ṭāʾif."],[12666,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He cursed the women who visit graves, those who build mosques over them, and those who place lamps on them.”"],[12668,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating grapes by pulling them off the stem."],[12669,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in an open area with nothing in front of him.”"],[12670,"“The Prophet’s ﷺ share that Allah fed him is the fifth of the fifth.”"],[12671,"It was narrated from ‘Ali ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Witr with three raka’hs (Using translation from Aḥmad 685)"],[12672,"From Yazīd Abū Khālid al-Dālānī al-Wāsiṭī, from al-Minhāl b. ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ḥārith, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever enters upon a sick person and says: ‘I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,’ then he will be cured as long as his appointed time has not arrived.” Shuʿbah said: “He raised it once and did not raise it twice.”"],[12673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever enters upon a sick person and says: ‘I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you,’ then he will be cured as long as his appointed time has not come.”"],[12675,"The Prophet ﷺ “prayed over a deceased person after he had been buried.”"],[12676,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A prophet among the prophets complained to his Lord, may He be exalted, saying: ‘O Lord, one of Your servants believes in You and acts in obedience to You, yet You withhold the world from him and expose him to affliction, while another of Your servants disbelieves in You and acts in disobedience to You, yet You withhold affliction from him and present the world to him.’ So Allah, may He be exalted, revealed to him: ‘Affliction and servants belong to Me. There is nothing except that it glorifies Me, declares My oneness, and magnifies Me. As for My believing servant, he has sins, so I withhold the world from him and expose him to affliction until he comes to Me and I reward him with good deeds. As for My disbelieving servant, he has good deeds, so I withhold affliction from him and present the world to him until he comes to Me and I requite him for his sins.’”"],[12677,"Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Call upon your Lord to turn al-Ṣafā into gold for us; if it becomes gold by morning, we will follow you.” So he called upon his Lord, may He be exalted, and Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said: “Your Lord sends you greetings of peace and says: If you wish, al-Ṣafā will become gold for them, and whoever among them disbelieves I will punish with a punishment I have not inflicted on anyone in the worlds; or if you wish, I will open for them the gate of repentance and mercy.” He said: “Rather, the gate of repentance and mercy.”"],[12678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gabriel told me that the month has ended, it was twenty-nine days.\""],[12686,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Sodom and the surrounding towns were not destroyed until they used tooth-sticks and chewed gum in their gatherings.\""],[12688,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray two rakʿahs before dawn, then sleep until he snored and breathed heavily while prostrating or sitting, then he got up and prayed. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you slept.\" He said: \"Ablution is required only for one who sleeps lying down, for when he lies down his joints relax.\""],[12689,"The cousin of your Prophet ﷺ—meaning Ibn ʿAbbās—told me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the night I was taken on the Night Journey, I saw Mūsā b. ʿImrān ﷺ : a tall, curly-haired, brown-skinned man, as if from the men of Shanūʾah. And I saw ʿĪsā b. Maryam: a man of medium build, tending toward reddish-white, with straight hair. And I saw Mālik, the keeper of the Fire, and I saw the Dajjāl in signs that Allah ﷻ showed me.\""],[12690,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say at times of distress: \"There is no god but Allah, the Magnificent, the Forbearing. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the Noble Throne. There is no god but Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the Great Throne.\""],[12692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the illness of the sick, I would have delayed the last evening prayer.\""],[12693,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not fitting for a servant to say, 'I am better than Yūnus b. Mattā.'\""],[12694,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The worst food is the food of a walīmah, to which the well-fed are invited while the hungry are turned away.\""],[12695,"He used to teach us the ruku' (bowing) as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach them, then he would become still for us while bowing, such that if a drop of water were to be dripped between his shoulders, it would not move forward or backward."],[12696,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon the valley of Ibn al-Azraq and said, \"What is this valley?\" They said, \"The valley of Ibn al-Azraq.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Musa ﷺ descending, and he has a loud voice, calling upon his Lord with the talbiyah.\" Then he came upon a mountain pass and said, \"What is this mountain pass?\" It was said, \"The mountain pass of such and such.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Yunus b. Matta on a red camel with short hair, its halter made of palm fiber, wearing a woolen jubbah, and he is reciting the talbiyah.\" Abu al-Qasim said: Hammad b. Salama said \"Ibn al-Azraq,\" but it is actually \"al-Azraq.\""],[12697,"The Prophet ﷺ [said]: \"Do not curse it, for it is commanded, and whoever curses something that does not deserve it, the curse falls back upon him.\""],[12698,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying {And We made it a guidance for the Children of Israel}: He said, \"He made Musa a guidance for the Children of Israel.\" And regarding His saying {So do not be in doubt about meeting Him}: He said, \"About Musa's meeting his Lord, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[12699,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever sees something from his ruler that he dislikes, let him be patient, for there is no one who separates from the community and then dies except that he dies a death of Jahiliyyah.\""],[12700,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed your Lord is Merciful. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, it is written for him as ten times up to seven hundred times, up to many multiples. And whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, it is written for him as one good deed. But if he does it, it is written against him as one evil deed, or He erases it. And no one is destroyed upon Allah except the one who is destroyed.\""],[12702,"He said on a rainy day: \"Pray in your dwellings.\" Then he said, \"Are you surprised? The one who is better than us, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, did it.\""],[12703,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ibn Sa'id, 'I have hidden a treasure for you, so what is it?'\" He said, \"Humility.\" He said, \"Go away.\""],[12704,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The affair of this ummah will continue to be moderate or favorable until they speak about children and qadar.\""],[12705,"Muhammad ﷺ [said]: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor and the destitute, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12707,"Muhammad ﷺ [said]: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12708,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[12709,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants were the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants were women.\""],[12710,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah.\""],[12714,"Al-Zubayr donated a horse in the path of Allah, then he found a foal from its progeny being sold, and he was forbidden to buy it."],[12715,"\"They were a people who, during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, did not go on military expeditions with him due to illnesses, diseases, and pains, while others who were healthy also did not go with him. The sick ones were excused in contrast to the healthy.\""],[12716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O young men of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Whoever guards his private parts will have Paradise.\""],[12717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first from whom the earth will split open, and this is no boast.\""],[12718,"\"...to prohibit what Allah and His Messenger have prohibited, then let him prohibit nabidh made in earthenware jars.\""],[12719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek refuge at the end of his prayer from four things, saying: \"I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the Fire, I seek refuge in Allah from trials, both apparent and hidden, and I seek refuge in Allah from the trial of the one-eyed liar.\""],[12720,"\"I visited my maternal aunt, and it coincided with the night of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for a long portion of the night, performed ablution thoroughly, then stood to pray. I stood up, performed ablution, and came to his side. When he knew that I wanted to pray, he took my hand and placed me on his right. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and performed witr with seven or nine rak'ahs, then he performed two rak'ahs, then he lay on his side until I heard his breathing. Then the prayer was called, and he went out for the prayer.\""],[12721,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed, he kept his back straight; if water were poured on his back, it would have stayed."],[12722,"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was taken on the night journey and morning came upon him in Makkah, he sat apart in sorrow. The enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, came to him and said, as if mocking, \"Did anything happen?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He (i.e., the Prophet) said: 'I was taken by night to the Sacred House (Bayt al-Maqdis).'\" He said, \"Then you woke up among us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He did not show him that he was denying him, fearing that if he called his people to it they would reject it—the hadith. He said, \"What do you think if I call your people to you? Will you tell them what you told me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Abu Jahl said, \"O Banu Ka'b b. Lu'ayy, come!\" The gatherings dispersed until they sat down before them. Abu Jahl said, \"Tell your people what you told me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I was taken by night.\" He said, \"To where?\" He said, \"To the Sacred House (Bayt al-Maqdis).\" They said, \"Then you woke up among us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Some clapped, and some placed his hand on his head in astonishment, saying, \"A lie, he claims.\" Among the people were those who had traveled to that mosque and seen it. They said, \"Can you describe the mosque to us?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"I described it to them until some of the description became confused for me.\" He said, \"The mosque was brought forth while I was looking at it, until it was placed near the house of 'Aqil or the house of 'Iqal. I began to describe it while I was looking at it.\" The people said, \"As for the description, by Allah, he has hit the mark.\""],[12723,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"Which speech is most beloved to Allah?\" He said, \"The one who alights and departs (al-hāll al-murtaḥil).\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is al-hāll al-murtaḥil?\" He said, \"The companion of the Quran who strikes through its beginning until he reaches its end, and through its end until he reaches its beginning.\""],[12725,"The Prophet ﷺ passed wind from his shoulder and then prayed without performing ablution."],[12726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Remember Allah with a remembrance such that the hypocrites say, 'You are showing off.'\""],[12727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The people of Paradise are those who fill their ears with praise of people for good while he listens, and the people of the Fire are those who fill their ears with praise of people for evil while he listens.\""],[12728,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the two side-posts of the door while we were in the house and said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, is there anyone among you from other than you?\" They said, \"A son of our sister.\" He said, \"The son of a people's sister is from them.\" Then he said, \"O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, if distress, fever, hardship, or adversity befalls you, say: Allah, Allah, our Lord, He has no partner.\""],[12729,"Regarding His saying: {For him are successive [angels] before him and behind him} (Quran 13:11), he said, \"It refers to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[12730,"Regarding His saying: {On the Day when We will fold the heaven like the folding of a scroll for the records} (Quran 21:104), he said, \"The Prophet ﷺ had a scribe called al-Sijill.\""],[12731,"\"There was a beautiful woman who used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ. Some people would advance and some would delay in order to look at her.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {And We have already known the foremost among you, and We have already known the ones who lag behind} (Quran 15:24)."],[12732,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"The Greatest Name of Allah, when invoked with it, He answers, is in this verse from the family of Imran, 'Say: O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You wills.' until the end of it.\""],[12733,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that, for it is its expiation—except for divorce or manumission.\""],[12734,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin, and He would forgive them.\""],[12735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The expiation of sin is remorse.\""],[12736,"When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You, for all fortune is Yours.”"],[12737,"\"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Allah said, 'I have created good and evil, so blessed is the one upon whose hands good is determined, and woe to the one upon whose hands evil is determined.'\""],[12738,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “I have never seen anything more excellent in seeking or swifter in attaining than a good deed that is recent for an old sin. {Indeed, good deeds do away with evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.}”"],[12739,"“Glory be to Allah and with His praise. I seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him”—it is recorded as he said it, then it is hung upon the Throne, and no sin committed by its utterer can erase it until he meets Allah, and it remains sealed just as he said it."],[12740,"From Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ, and we do not know it except as a marfūʿ narration attributed to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Islam is built on five: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the prayer, and fasting Ramadan. Whoever abandons any one of them is a disbeliever whose blood is lawful.”"],[12741,"One of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ pitched a tent over a grave, not knowing it was a grave. Then suddenly a person inside was reciting “Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion” until he completed it. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I pitched my tent over a grave, not knowing it was a grave, and suddenly a person was reciting ‘Blessed is He’ until he completed it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is the preventer, it is the deliverer; it delivers him from the punishment of the grave.”"],[12742,"\"The demons.\""],[12743,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “In Hell there is a valley from which Hell seeks refuge four hundred times every day. That valley has been prepared for the ostentatious of the community of Muhammad ﷺ: for one who carries the Book of Allah, for one who gives charity for other than Allah’s sake, for those who perform pilgrimage to the House of Allah, and for one who goes out in the path of Allah.”"],[12744,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A slave who obeys Allah and obeys his masters—Allah will admit him to Paradise seventy autumns before his masters. The master will say: ‘O Lord, this was my slave in this world.’ He will say: ‘I rewarded him for his deeds and rewarded you for your deeds.’”"],[12745,"He informed him, saying: “I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight [rakʿahs] combined and seven [rakʿahs] combined.”"],[12746,"“I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eight and seven combined.”"],[12747,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed eight rakʿahs combined and seven rakʿahs combined, without illness or ailment.”"],[12748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “prayed in Madinah seven and eight: Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, and Maghrib and ʿIshāʾ.”"],[12749,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever cannot find an izār may wear sirwāl, and whoever cannot find sandals may wear khuffayn.”"],[12750,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Trousers are for one who does not find a waist cloth, and leather socks are for one who does not find sandals\"—meaning the pilgrim in ihram."],[12751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers; and if he does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks.\""],[12752,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"If the pilgrim in ihram does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers; and if he does not find sandals, then leather socks.\""],[12753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon to the people at Arafah and said: \"Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers.\""],[12754,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ giving a sermon at Arafat, saying: \"Whoever does not find sandals, let him wear leather socks; and whoever does not find a waist cloth, let him wear trousers.\""],[12755,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever does not find a waist cloth but finds trousers, let him wear them; and whoever does not find sandals but finds leather socks, let him wear them.\""],[12756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established a bond of brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Ibn Masʿud."],[12757,"\"...that Allah may will, and remember your Lord when you forget\" [Quran 18:24]—meaning to say 'if Allah wills.'"],[12758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Muhajirun because they migrated away from the polytheists; and among the Ansar there were also Muhajirun, because Madinah was a place where revelation descended, and they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-ʿAqabah."],[12759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever forgets to send blessings upon me has missed the path to Paradise.\""],[12760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that the meat of horses be eaten."],[12761,"The Prophet ﷺ was approached regarding the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: \"She is not permissible for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and the same prohibitions apply through suckling as apply through blood relations.\""],[12762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was sought for the daughter of Hamzah, and he said: \"She is not lawful for me. She is the daughter of my brother through suckling, and whatever is forbidden by lineage is forbidden by suckling.\""],[12763,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Will you not marry the daughter of Hamzah?\" He said: \"She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.\""],[12764,"\"The black dog and the menstruating woman cut off the prayer.\""],[12765,"The Prophet ﷺ combined two prayers during the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq."],[12766,"\"It is from the Sunnah to combine two prayers while traveling.\""],[12767,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The prostitutes are those who give themselves in marriage without evidence.\""],[12768,"Circumcision is a Sunnah for men and a noble act for women."],[12769,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The martyr will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and set up for reckoning, and the charitable person will be brought and set up for reckoning, then the people of affliction will be brought, and no scale will be set up for them and no register will be spread out for them; rather, reward will be poured upon them abundantly, until the people of well-being in the standing place will wish that their bodies had been cut with shears, because of the excellence of God's reward for them.\""],[12770,"Ibn Abbas said: \"The Fajr prayer is between the break of dawn and the rising of the sun's rays. Its time ends once the sun has risen. The Messenger of God ﷺ once set out at night and then stopped to rest, and he did not wake until the sun had risen, or part of it had risen. He did not pray until it had risen high, then he prayed, and it is the middle prayer.\""],[12771,"The Prophet ﷺ set the ransom for the people of Badr at four hundred."],[12772,"From the Prophet ﷺ, from the Trustworthy Spirit ﷺ , he said: \"The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'The servant's good deeds and bad deeds will be brought on the Day of Resurrection, and some will be subtracted from others. If one good deed remains, God will admit him into Paradise.'\" He said: I said: \"What if no good deed remains?\" He said: \"Those are they from whom We accept the best of what they did and overlook their misdeeds, among the companions of Paradise.\" He said: I said: \"What do you think of His saying: 'No soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for their eyes'?\" He said: \"It is the servant who does a deed in secret, and God conceals it for him on the Day of Resurrection, so he sees comfort for his eyes.\""],[12773,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The evil eye is real; the evil eye is real. It brings down the high mountain.\""],[12774,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The best door of righteousness is charity.\""],[12775,"\"If this verse was revealed to us, we would not take that day as a celebration.\" Ibn Abbas said: \"Indeed, it was revealed on two occasions: on the day of Jumu'ah (Friday) and on the day of Arafah.\""],[12776,"I was with my father in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a man with the Prophet ﷺ speaking to him in confidence. He seemed to be turning away from my father. We left him, and my father said to me, \"Did you not see your cousin? He was as if turning away from me.\" I said, \"O father, there was a man with him speaking to him in confidence.\" He said, \"Was there someone with him?\" I said, \"Yes.\" We returned and my father said, \"O Messenger of God, I said to ʿAbd Allah such-and-such, and he said to me such-and-such. Was there someone with you?\" He said, \"Yes. And did you see him, O ʿAbd Allah?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"That was Jibrīl. It was he who occupied me from you.\""],[12777,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream one day at midday, disheveled and dust-colored, with a bottle in his hand containing blood. I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, what is this?\" He said, \"This is the blood of al-Ḥusayn and his companions. I have been collecting it since today.\" That day was counted, and it was found that he was killed on that day."],[12778,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid. Her father was reluctant to marry her to him, so she prepared food and drink and invited her father and some people from Quraysh. They ate and drank. Khadījah said to her father, \"Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allah is asking for my hand in marriage. Stand up and marry me to him.\" He married her to him, and she perfumed him and dressed him in a fine garment. That is how they used to treat fathers when they married off their daughters. When the intoxication left him, he looked and saw that he was perfumed and wearing a fine garment. He said, \"What is the matter with me?\" She said, \"You married me to Muḥammad.\" He said, \"I married you to the orphan of Abū Ṭālib? No, by my life!\" Khadījah said, \"Are you not ashamed? Do you want to make a fool of yourself? You would tell Quraysh and the people that you were drunk?\" She kept at him until he consented."],[12779,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Khadījah, \"I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear that I may be possessed.\" Khadījah said, \"God would not do that to you, O son of ʿAbd Allah.\" Then she went to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said, \"If he is truthful, this is a nāmūs like the nāmūs of Mūsā. If he is sent while I am alive, I will support him, help him, and assist him.\""],[12780,"The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for fifteen years: seven or eight seeing the light and hearing the voice, and eight receiving revelation. He stayed in Madinah for ten years."],[12781,"The Prophet ﷺ used to give the sermon standing by a palm trunk before he took a pulpit. When he took the pulpit and moved to it, the trunk yearned for him. He embraced it, and it became still. He said, \"If I had not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[12782,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, \"How old was the Messenger of God ﷺ when he died?\" He said, \"I did not think someone like you among a people would be unaware of that.\" I said, \"I asked, and people differed, so I wanted to know your statement about it.\" He said, \"Can you calculate?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Take forty: he was sent at that age, and fifteen: his stay in Makkah, feeling secure and fearing, and ten: his emigration in Madinah.\""],[12783,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ died at the age of sixty-five.\" Al-Ḥasan used to say, \"He died at the age of sixty.\""],[12785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was taken at the age of sixty-five."],[12786,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had himself cupped and gave the cupper his wage. If it had been unlawful, he would not have given it."],[12787,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Abū Hilāl narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. Sīrīn, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ had himself cupped and paid him. If it had been impure, he would not have paid him.\""],[12788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had he known it to be impure, he would not have given it."],[12789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and gave the cupper his fee. Had it been unlawful gain, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not have given it."],[12790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had it been impure, he would not have given it."],[12791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and would not wrong a hired worker his wage."],[12792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done and paid its fee. Had he known that there was harm in it, he would not have given it."],[12794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to shorten the prayer between Madinah and Makkah, fearing none but God."],[12795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to shorten the prayer between Makkah and Madinah, fearing none but God."],[12796,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled from Makkah to Madinah and prayed two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but God — or he said: fearing none but God — and prayed two rakʿahs."],[12798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to travel from Madinah to Makkah fearing none but God, and prayed two rakʿahs, two rakʿahs."],[12800,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed between Makkah and Madinah two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed between Makkah and Madinah two rakʿahs, fearing none but God."],[12802,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out from Madinah to Makkah fearing none but God, and he prayed two rakʿahs until he went out."],[12803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs between Makkah and Madinah fearing none but God."],[12804,"Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman b. Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad b. Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad b. Sirin, from Ibn ʿAbbas: \"The Prophet ﷺ ate the meat off a shoulder bone, then stood and prayed and did not perform wudu.\""],[12805,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate the meat off a bone, then prayed and did not touch water."],[12806,"The Prophet ﷺ ate the meat off a shoulder bone, then stood and prayed and did not perform wudu."],[12807,"I was among those who hastened in the heavy baggage of the Prophet ﷺ from Jamʿ to Mina."],[12808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Dhul-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, Yalamlam for the people of Yemen, and Qarn for the people of Najd."],[12809,"Revelation came down to the Prophet ﷺ when he was forty years old. He stayed in Makkah thirteen years and in Madinah ten, and he died when he was sixty-three years old."],[12810,"The Messenger of God ﷺ extended his hand to Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah held back until he went and performed ghusl and came. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I was junub.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The Muslim does not become impure.\""],[12811,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a caller, and he called out on a rainy day: \"Pray in your dwellings.\""],[12812,"Al-Hasan: Did not the Prophet ﷺ stand for the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess that passed by him? Ibn ʿAbbas said: Indeed, and he sat down."],[12813,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood? The other said: Indeed, and he sat down."],[12814,"Regarding this verse: “And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person.” He said: “Then the other verse abrogated it: ‘So whoever among you witnesses the month, let him fast it.’”"],[12815,"Abu Ayyub ؓ divorced his wife. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, the divorce of Umm Ayyub was a sin (ḥūb).” Ibn Sīrīn said: “al-ḥūb means sin.”"],[12816,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: “When the first part of al-Muzzammil was revealed, their standing in prayer was like their standing in Ramadan, or similar to their standing in Ramadan, and there was a year between its beginning and its end.”"],[12817,"“I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a cloak of the finest Yemeni cloth.”"],[12818,"I heard him say: The Prophet ﷺ obtained spoils on the day of Hunayn and distributed them to the people. The Ansar said: “We fight, but the spoils go to others.” That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent word to them to gather. He came to them and said: “O assembly of Ansar, is there anyone among you other than yourselves?” They said: “No, except a son of a sister of ours and a client of ours.” He said: “The son of a people’s sister is one of them, and the client of a people is one of them.” He said: “O assembly of Ansar, are you not pleased that the people take away sheep and cattle, while you take Muhammad ﷺ?” They said: “We are pleased.”"],[12819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever among my ummah loses two children who die before him, Allah will admit him to Paradise.” ʿĀʾishah asked: “And someone who loses one child?” He said: “And whoever loses one child, O fortunate one.” She asked: “And one who has no child die before him?” He said: “I am the one who dies before my ummah; they have not been afflicted with the like of me.”"],[12820,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain, and people were rained upon until the canal flowed for forty days.” In the morning people said: “The star of such-and-such has proven true,” and among them were those who said: “This is a mercy that Allah has sent down.”"],[12821,"People were rained upon during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the people this morning there is one who is grateful and one who is ungrateful. They said: ‘This is a mercy that Allah has sent down,’ while others said: ‘The star of such-and-such has proven true.’ Then this verse was revealed: ‘Nay, I swear by the locations of the stars’ up to ‘You make your provision that you deny.’”"],[12822,"The polytheists used to say: “Labbayk, no partner has You.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “Woe to you, enough, enough.” Then they would say: “Except a partner who is Yours; You own Him and what He owns.” They said this while circumambulating the House."],[12823,"“I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the finest of Yemeni garments.”"],[12824,"The people would not look at Abu Sufyan or sit with him. He said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Three things I will give you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I have the finest and most beautiful Arab woman, Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan; I will give her to you in marriage.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And Muāwiyah – make him a scribe, place him before you.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And appoint me as a commander to fight the disbelievers just as I used to fight the Muslims.” He said: “Yes.”"],[12826,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God cursed the Jews. Fats were forbidden to them, but they sold them and consumed their price. When God, exalted is He, forbids eating something, He forbids its price.”"],[12827,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Some poetry contains wisdom, and some eloquence is sorcery.”"],[12829,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ used to delay the evening prayer (al-ʿatamah) until one third of the night. That is why it is called al-ʿatamah, because he used to delay it (yuʿtim) into the darkness.”"],[12830,"\"I passed by, along with a young boy from the Quraysh, riding a donkey in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying. He did not finish his prayer and two young girls from the Bani Abdul Mutallib clan came and took hold of his knees. He spread his arms between them and did not finish.\" This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Al-Hakam, from Yahya bin Al-Jazzaar, from Suhaib. Mansur contradicted this narration."],[12832,"That he said to ʿUmar: “You accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ with the best companionship, and he is pleased with you.”"],[12833,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas: How should I say prayer when I am in Mecca, and when I do not pray along with the Imam? He said: Two rak'ahs (of prayer) is the Sunnah of Abu'l-Qasim ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 688a)"],[12834,"\"That is the Sunnah of Abi Al-Qasim ﷺ , even if you feel reluctant.\""],[12835,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas: How should I say prayer when I am in Mecca, and when I do not pray along with the Imam? He said: Two rak'ahs (of prayer) is the Sunnah of Abu'l-Qasim ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 688a)"],[12839,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever makes an image in this world will be charged on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the spirit into it, but he will not be able to.”"],[12840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, then called for a sacrificial camel and marked the right side of its hump. Then he wiped the blood from it and garlanded it with two sandals. Then his mount was brought, and when he sat on it and it stood upright with him at al-Baydāʾ, he entered the state of iḥrām."],[12841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the state of iḥrām after the noon prayer from al-Baydāʾ."],[12842,"That God made it lawful and revealed regarding it the longest verse in the Book of God: {O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a fixed term, write it down}."],[12843,"The Prophet ﷺ used to visit the House every night during the nights of Minā."],[12844,"I asked Ibn 'Abbas about the Witr prayer. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is a rak'ah at the end of the night prayer. (Using translation from Muslim 753)"],[12845,"I do not know whether the Messenger of God ﷺ stoned it with six or seven."],[12848,"The banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ was black and his standard was white."],[12849,"To Ibn ʿAbbas, and he pointed to Muʿawiya: \"They serve water and honey, and the family of so-and-so serve milk, and you serve nabidh. Is it out of stinginess on your part or out of need?\" He said: \"We are neither stingy nor in need, but the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him, and we gave him some of this nabidh to drink. He drank from it and said: 'Do likewise.'\""],[12850,"The Messenger of God ﷺ intended to perform Hajj. A woman said to her husband: \"Take me on Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" He said to her: \"I do not have anything on which to take you on Hajj.\" She said: \"Take me on Hajj on your camel so-and-so.\" He said: \"That is dedicated to the cause of God.\" She said: \"Take me on Hajj on your water-carrying camel.\" He said: \"That one you and I use alternately.\" She said: \"Then sell your dates.\" He said: \"That is my food and yours.\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ arrived, the woman sent her husband to him and said: \"Convey to him my greeting of peace and God's mercy, and ask him what equals a Hajj with you.\" He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, my wife conveys to you the greeting of peace and God's mercy. She had asked me to take her on Hajj with you, and I said: I do not have anything on which to take you on Hajj. She said: Take me on Hajj on your camel so-and-so. I said: That is dedicated to the cause of God.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"If you had taken her on Hajj on it, it would have been in the cause of God.\" He continued: \"She said: Take me on Hajj on your water-carrying camel. I said: That one you and I use alternately. She said: Then sell your dates. I said: That is my food and yours.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at her eagerness for Hajj. He said: \"She instructed me to ask you what suffices as a Hajj with you.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Convey to her the greeting of peace and God's mercy, and tell her that an ʿumra in Ramadan equals a Hajj with me.\""],[12851,"From Ayyub, ʿAsim, and ʿAbd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Ziyadi, from ʿAbd Allah b. al-Harith, who said: Ibn ʿAbbas delivered a sermon to us on a rainy day. When the muezzin reached 'Come to prayer,' he ordered him to call out: 'Pray in your dwellings.' Some of them looked at one another, so he said: \"It seems you disapprove of this? One better than me did this, and it is a firm practice.\""],[12852,"When you reach 'Come to success,' say: 'Indeed, pray in your dwellings.' It was said: \"What is this?\" He said: \"One better than me did it.\""],[12853,"Because he sat on a white hide and it turned green and vibrated.\" Saʿid b. Bashir said: \"And Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to me that Qatada used to raise this hadith to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[12854,"May you be bereft of your mother! You are teaching us about its time? We used to combine the two prayers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[12859,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Among a man's happiness is a light beard.\""],[12860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever takes a span of Makkah without right, it is as if he has taken it from beneath the foot of the Most Merciful; and whoever takes anything from the rest of the earth without right will come on the Day of Resurrection with it hung around his neck from seven earths.\""],[12864,"\"When you see the crescent of Muharram, then count; when it is the ninth day, then enter the morning fasting.\" I said: \"Is that how Muhammad ﷺ used to fast?\" He said: \"That is how Muhammad ﷺ used to fast.\""],[12865,"“Whoever sees me in a dream has (really) seen me, for Satan cannot imitate me.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3903)"],[12866,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: \"What reports have spread among the people saying, 'Whoever circumambulates the House has become free of ihram'?\" He said: \"That is the sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ, even if you dislike it.\""],[12867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The first to deny was Adam. When Allah ﷻ created him, He wiped his back and brought forth his offspring and all that He would create until the Day of Resurrection. He began presenting them to him, and he saw among them a radiant man. He said: 'O Lord, which of my sons is this?' He said: 'This is your son Dawud.' He said: 'O Lord, how long is his life?' He said: 'Sixty years.' He said: 'O Lord, increase his life.' He said: 'No, unless you give him from your own life.' Adam's life was a thousand years, and he gave him forty years from his life. He said: 'So He wrote a document for him regarding that and made the angels witnesses.' When Adam was dying, the angels came to take his soul. He said: 'Forty years of my life remain.' They said: 'You gave them to your son Dawud.' He said: 'I did not do that; I did not give him anything.' Then Allah brought down the document and the angels testified against him. So Allah completed for Adam a thousand years and completed for Dawud a hundred years.\""],[12868,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Jibril ﷺ said: 'Prayer has been made beloved to you, so take from it as much as you wish.'\""],[12869,"\"Surat al-An'am was revealed all at once in Makkah at night, with seventy thousand angels around it glorifying Allah.\""],[12870,"A woman came to me seeking my allegiance. I took her to an enclosed place and I hit her with my hand and attempted to seduce her. I did everything with her except sexual intercourse. Umar said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is pregnant.\" He replied, \"Yes.\" Umar said to him, \"Go to Abu Bakr and ask him.\" So he went to him and told him what he had said to Umar. Abu Bakr said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is pregnant.\" He then went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the same thing he had told Abu Bakr and Umar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Woe to you, perhaps she is fighting for the cause of Allah.\" He replied, \"Yes.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and the Quran was revealed, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night.\" until the end of the verse. The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is this command specific to me or for the general public?\" Umar raised his hand and struck his own chest and said, \"No, by Allah, not for the sake of power, but for the general public.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said, \"Umar has spoken the truth.\""],[12871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah drowned Pharaoh, he said: 'I believe that there is no god except the One in whom the Children of Israel believe.' Jibril ﷺ said: 'O Muhammad, if you had seen me, I was taking mud from the sea and stuffing it into his mouth, fearing that mercy might reach him.'\""],[12872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no one among the children of Adam except that he has erred or thought of a sin, except Yahya b. Zakariyya.\""],[12873,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us with Usama b. Zayd riding behind him, and we gave him some of this drink—meaning the drink of the siqaya—and he said, \"You have done well; do it like this.\""],[12874,"We recited it in the time of the Prophet ﷺ for two years: “And those who do not call upon another god besides God, and do not kill the soul which God has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery” [Q 25:68]—the verse—then was revealed “except for one who repents” [Q 25:70]. I never saw the Prophet ﷺ rejoice with any joy more intense than his joy at this verse and at “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [Q 48:1]."],[12876,"The Prophet ﷺ circumambulated the House on his riding camel, touching the corner with his staff."],[12877,"We were in a circle in the mosque discussing the virtues of the prophets, which of them is best. We mentioned Noah and the length of his worship of his Lord, and we mentioned Abraham, the friend of the Merciful, and we mentioned Moses, God's interlocutor, and we mentioned Jesus son of Mary, and we mentioned the Messenger of God ﷺ. While we were doing that, the Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, \"What are you discussing among yourselves?\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, we were discussing the virtues of the prophets, which of them is best. We mentioned Noah and the length of his worship, we mentioned Abraham, the friend of the Merciful, we mentioned Moses, the interlocutor of the Merciful, we mentioned Jesus son of Mary, and we mentioned you, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"So whom did you prefer?\" We said, \"We preferred you, O Messenger of God, because God sent you to all mankind, forgave you your past and future sins, and you are the seal of the prophets.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Indeed, it is not appropriate for anyone to say, 'I am better than Yahya b. Zakariyya.'\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, how so?\" He said, \"Did you not hear how God described him in the Qur'an? He said: 'O Yahya, take the Scripture with strength.' And We gave him judgment while yet a boy' [Q 19:12]. Then he recited until he reached: 'a master, chaste, and a prophet from among the righteous' [Q 19:13–14]. He never committed an evil deed, nor did he intend one.\""],[12878,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he said, \"There is no human being but has in his head a wisdom held by an angel. When he humbles himself, it is said to the angel, 'Raise his wisdom,' and when he becomes arrogant, it is said to the angel, 'Lay his wisdom low.'\""],[12879,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was visited by two angels as a sleeping person sees. One of them sat at his feet and the other at his head. The one at his feet said to the one at his head, \"Strike a parable for this man and his community.\" He said, \"The example of this man and his community is like a group of travellers who reached the edge of a desert, but they had no provisions with which to cross the desert or return. While they were in that state, a man came to them wearing a striped robe and said, 'What do you think: if I bring you to lush meadows and full watering places, will you follow me?' They said, 'Yes.' So he set off with them and brought them to lush meadows and full watering places. They ate, drank, and grew fat. Then he said to them, 'Did I not find you in that earlier condition?' They said, 'Yes.' 'But did you not agree that if I brought you to lush meadows and full watering places you would follow me?' They said, 'Yes.' So one group among them said, 'By God, he has spoken truth; we will certainly follow him.' And another group said, 'We have accepted this place; we will stay here.'\""],[12880,"He saw his Lord, exalted is He, with his heart."],[12882,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping at al-Qahah while he was in a state of ihram."],[12883,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stayed in Makkah for thirteen years receiving revelation, and in Madinah for ten years, and he died at the age of sixty-three."],[12884,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out saying, \"Part of the decline of religion is inspecting the Nabataeans and their building of palaces in the garrison towns.\""],[12885,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Wear turbans and you will increase in forbearance.\""],[12886,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to a clan of the Arabs calling them to Islam, but they did not accept the letter and returned to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: “Indeed, if I had sent it to a people on the shore of Oman from the Azd Shanu’ah, and they submitted, they would have accepted it.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to al-Julanda calling him to Islam, and he accepted it and submitted, and he sent a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It arrived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away, so Abu Bakr made the gift an inheritance and divided it between Fatimah and the people."],[12887,"Four hundred men from Daws came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Welcome! The finest of people in faces, the sweetest of them in mouths, and the greatest of them in trustworthiness.”"],[12888,"When the delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Who are the people?” They said: “Rabiʿah.” He said: “Welcome to the delegation, not disgraced nor regretful.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are a clan of Rabiʿah, and we come to you from a distant land. Between us and you lies this clan of the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a decisive matter to which you call and to which we call those behind us, and by which we may enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four. I command you with faith in Allah, the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Do you know what faith is? It is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you give one-fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from four: from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.” He said: “And perhaps he said: and the muqayyar. Memorize them and call to them those behind you.”"],[12889,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbas say: The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this clan of Rabiʿah has been separated from you by the disbelievers of Mudar, so we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. Command us with a matter that we may adopt and to which we may call those behind us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: faith in Allah, the testimony that there is no god but Allah” — and he counted on his hand — “the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you pay one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade the dubba’, the muzaffat, the naqir, and the hantam.”"],[12891,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, there are disbelievers from the tribe of Mudar between us and you, and we can only come to you during the sacred months. So give us a command that we can convey to those behind us and invite them to it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Tell them that there are four testimonies: There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, establishing prayer, giving zakat, fasting in Ramadan, and paying one-fifth of what you have acquired. And I prohibit you from drinking the wine of grapes, and from the wine of dates, and from the wine of barley and wheat.\""],[12892,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we are this clan of Rabiʿah, and the disbelievers of Mudar have come between us and you, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with a matter that we may act upon and to which we may call those behind us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: faith” — and he explained it to them — “the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, and that you pay one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muqayyar.”"],[12893,"The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Greetings, O Messenger of Allah. We are from the tribe of Rabi'ah, but there are disbelievers from the tribe of Mudar among us. We can only come to you in the sacred month, so guide us and call those behind us to the same. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I command you to do four things: to have faith in Allah, bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and Muhammad is His Messenger, establish prayer, give zakat (charity), and pay one-fifth of the war booty. I forbid you from five things: do not consume carrion, blood, pork, or wine.\""],[12894,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot come to you whenever we wish. So inform us of what is lawful for us and what is forbidden to us.” He said: “I command you with four things and forbid you from four: that you establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, and give one-fifth of the spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12895,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month. So command us with what is lawful for us and what is forbidden to us.” He said: “I command you with one matter and forbid you from four. I command you with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakah, fasting Ramadan, and that you give one-fifth of what you take as spoils. And I forbid you from the dubba’, the hantam, the naqir, and the muzaffat.”"],[12896,"“The first Friday prayer established after the Friday prayer in Madinah was a Friday prayer in al-Bahrayn, in a village belonging to ʿAbd al-Qays called Juatha.”"],[12897,"From Ibn ʿAbbas: “The first Friday prayer was established in Madinah, then the Friday prayer of Juatha.”"],[12898,"He was a prophet who sent his brother and said: “Go to Makkah until you hear from him and bring me news of him.” His brother went to Makkah and heard news of the Prophet ﷺ, then returned to Abu Dharr and informed him that he enjoins good, forbids evil, and enjoins noble character. He said: “You have not satisfied me.” Then he took a waterskin containing water and a leather bucket, and set out until he came to Makkah. He was afraid to ask anyone about anything, and he did not meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until night fell. When it became dark, ʿAli b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: “Who is the man?” He said: “A man from Ghifar.” He said: “Come to your lodging,” and took him to his lodging, neither of them asking the other about anything. When morning came, he went out but did not meet him, so he stood aside in the mosque. ʿAli b. Abi Talib passed by him and said: “Is it not time for the man to know his lodging?” He took him along, neither of them asking the other about anything. On the third day, Abu Dharr made ʿAli promise that if he told him what he wanted, he would keep it secret and conceal it from others. He did so, and said: “It has reached me that a man has appeared in Makkah claiming to be a prophet. I sent my brother, but he did not bring me what would satisfy me, so I came myself to learn his news.” ʿAli b. Abi Talib said: “Then follow my tracks, for if I see something I fear for you, I will stand as if to urinate and return to you. If I see nothing, then follow my tracks.” So ʿAli went out, and Abu Dharr followed his tracks until they entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Dharr told him his news and heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then submitted. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, command me with your command.” He said: “Return to your people until my news reaches you.” He said: “No, by Allah, I will not return until I proclaim Islam openly.” He went out to the mosque and called out with the prayer, saying: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.” The polytheists said: “The man has turned Sabian! The man has turned Sabian!” and they beat him until he fell. Al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib passed by him, leaned over him, then said: “O people of Quraysh, you are merchants and your route passes by Ghifar. Do you want us to cut off the route from you?” So they left him alone. On the second day, he repeated the same words, and they beat him. Al-ʿAbbas passed by him and said the same to them, so they left him alone. This was the beginning of Islam for Abu Dharr ؓ."],[12899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The ʿumrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[12900,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Gabriel came to me during the final ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and said, \"The Umrah (lesser pilgrimage) during Hajj is valid until the Day of Resurrection.\" Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If I had known beforehand what I know now, I would have not brought the sacrificial animals and performed the Hajj rites.\""],[12901,"Allah is greater—the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, or he said: the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ."],[12902,"I heard Ibn Abbas say: “A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[12903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen rakʿahs at night."],[12904,"His freedman said to him: “Mutʿah was only when people were in need and women were few.” Ibn Abbas said to him: “You have spoken the truth.”"],[12905,"Do not seek a need from a blind man, and do not seek it at night. When you seek a need, face the man directly, for modesty is in the eyes. And seek your need early in the morning, for the Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless my Ummah in its early mornings.”"],[12906,"For the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with Zamzam water.”"],[12907,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Muhammad b. Maslamah a sword and said: “Fight the polytheists as long as they are fought. When you see two swords drawn among the Muslims, strike with it until it is notched, then stay in your house until a decisive death or a stray hand comes to you.” Then I came to Ibn Umar and he narrated to me the like of it from the Prophet ﷺ."],[12908,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ashajj ʿAbd al-Qays: “You have two qualities that Allah loves: forbearance and deliberateness.”"],[12909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the people of the East are ʿAbd al-Qays.”"],[12910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the advocate of whoever wrongs ʿAbd al-Qays.”"],[12911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive ʿAbd al-Qays,” three times."],[12916,"Regarding wine: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque. While he was talking intimately, he undid his wrap, then said: “Whoever has any wine, let him inform me.” The people began coming to him; one said, “I have a wineskin of wine”; another said, “I have a waterskin”; another said, “I have a small skin,” and whatever Allah willed that they had. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gather it in Baqiʿ of such-and-such, then inform me.” He stood and I stood with him, walking on his right, while he leaned on me. Abu Bakr caught up with us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me and placed me on his left and put Abu Bakr in my place. Then Umar b. al-Khattab caught up with us, and he took him and placed him on his left, so he walked between the two of them until, when he stood over the wine, he said to the people: “Do you recognize this?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, this is wine.” He said: “You have spoken the truth. Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its server, and the one who consumes its price.” Then he called for a knife and said: “Sharpen it.” They did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and began slashing the wine skins. The people said: “There is benefit in these skins.” He said: “Yes, but I only do this out of anger for Allah because of the displeasure that is in it.” He said: “And some of them add to this in the hadith more than others.”"],[12917,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: “Rather, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[12920,"Fulfill my need, O Commander of the Believers, for by Allah, my burden is great. I have become the father of ten, the brother of ten, and the uncle of ten. When Marwan turned away, while Ibn Abbas was sitting with Muawiya on his couch, Muawiya said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When the Banu al-Hakam reach thirty men, they will take the signs of Allah among them as a gain, His servants as slaves, and His Book as deceit. When they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be swifter than fruit’?” Ibn Abbas said: “O Allah, yes.” Then Marwan mentioned a need he had, and Marwan b. Abd al-Malik returned to Muawiya and spoke to him about it. When he turned away, Muawiya said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn Abbas, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned this and said: ‘Abu al-Jababirah the four’?” Ibn Abbas said: “O Allah, yes.” For that reason Muawiya claimed Ziyad."],[12921,"Some people from Himyar came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him about things. One of them said: “I love women, and I love to come to my wife from behind, so what do you think about that?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you wish} [Quran 2:223]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Come to her from the front or from the back, as long as it is in the vagina.”"],[12922,"Your Prophet ﷺ was born on Monday, and on Monday he left Makkah, and he entered Madinah on Monday, and he conquered Badr on Monday, and Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed on Monday: {This day I have perfected for you your religion} [Quran 5:3], and he raised the corner on Monday, and he died on Monday."],[12923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam consists of three hundred and thirteen ways. There is no way by which its adherent meets Allah except that he enters Paradise by it.”"],[12924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In the urine and milk of camels there is healing for those whose stomachs are afflicted with chronic diarrhea.”"],[12925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out to urinate and then wipe himself with dust. I would say, 'O Messenger of Allah, water is near you.' He would say, 'Perhaps I will not reach it.'"],[12926,"He was behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me while I was riding behind him: 'O boy, I will teach you some words. Preserve them: Preserve Allah and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. Know that if the nation gathered to benefit you, they would not benefit you except with something Allah has already written for you. The pens have dried and the pages have been folded.'"],[12928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Marry off the unmarried — three times — according to what the families agree upon, even if it is a handful of toothstick twigs (arak).'"],[12930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Sabaʾ — what is it? A man, a woman, or a land?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man who fathered ten sons. Six settled in Yemen and four in Syria. As for the Yemenis: Madhhij, Kindah, al-Azd, al-Ashʿariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar. As for the Syrians: Lakhm, Judham, ʿAmilah, and Ghassan.'"],[12931,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not guide you to a word that will save you from associating partners with Allah? {Say: O disbelievers} at the time of your sleep.'"],[12932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every bird with talons and every beast of prey with fangs."],[12933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every beast of prey with fangs and every bird with talons."],[12934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every predatory animal with fangs."],[12935,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'There will be a people at the end of time called the Rafidah, who reject Islam and cast it off. Kill them, for they are polytheists.'"],[12936,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and ʿAli was with him. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O ʿAli, there will be among my community a people who claim love for us, the People of the House. They will have a nickname and be called the Rafidah. Kill them, for they are polytheists.'"],[12937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes perform ghusl on Friday and sometimes he would leave it occasionally."],[12938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12939,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12940,"“I was not commanded to build lofty mosques.”"],[12941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was not commanded to build lofty mosques,” and he did not mention Layth."],[12942,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Three things—if a person is free from even one of them, then surely Allah will forgive him whatever else He wills: he who dies without associating anything with Allah, and is not a sorcerer following sorcerers, and does not bear malice against his brother.”"],[12943,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “Whatever Allah wills and you will.” He said: “You have set up a rival to Allah. Rather, say: Whatever Allah alone wills.”"],[12944,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Whatever Allah wills and you will.” He said: “You have made me an equal [to Allah]. Say: Whatever Allah wills.”"],[12945,"Some of his companions said: It was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he neither declared it lawful nor unlawful. Ibn Abbas said: “How bad is what you say! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent only as one who makes lawful and makes unlawful. Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith came to visit her sister Maymunah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. They brought with them food containing the meat of a dabb lizard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came after it had grown dark—meaning it had become night. Maymunah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dabb meat. So he held back from it, and Maymunah held back from it. Ibn Abbas said: And those with him ate it. If it had been unlawful, he would have forbidden them from it, and he said: “It is not found in our land, and we find it distasteful.”"],[12946,"Some of them said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I do not make it lawful, nor do I make it unlawful.” Ibn Abbas said: “How bad is what you said! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent only as one who makes lawful and makes unlawful. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Maymunah, and with him were al-Fadl b. al-Abbas, Khalid b. al-Walid, and a woman, and Maymunah. A table was brought with bread and dabb meat on it. He held back his hand and said: ‘This is meat I have not eaten, but eat.’ So Khalid b. al-Walid, al-Fadl b. al-Abbas, and the woman ate. Maymunah said: I will not eat food from which the Prophet ﷺ did not eat. So Maymunah did not eat.”"],[12947,"My father narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Yazid b. al-Asamm, from Ibn Abbas, that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, should I perform Hajj on behalf of my father?” He said: “Yes, if you do not add any good to him, you will not add any harm to him.”"],[12948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Truffles are a kind of manna, and their water is a cure for the eye.”"],[12949,"Ibn Abbas said: “Any man who claims descent from other than his parents, or claims allegiance to other than his masters who freed him, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels until the Day of Resurrection; neither turning away nor justice will be accepted from him.”"],[12950,"A group of Jews came to the Prophet of God ﷺ one day and said, “O Abu al-Qasim, tell us about matters we will ask you that none knows but a prophet.” He said, “Ask me whatever you wish, but grant me the covenant of God and what Jacob took upon his children: if I tell you something and you recognize it, you will follow me.” They said, “That is yours.” They said, “Four matters we ask you about: tell us which food Israel forbade upon himself before the Torah was sent down; tell us how the fluid of the woman is from the fluid of the man, and how the female and the male come from it; tell us how this unlettered prophet is among his people; and who is his guardian among the angels?” He said, “Upon you is the covenant of God: if I tell you, you will follow me.” So they gave him whatever covenant and pact he wished. He said, “I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah to Moses: do you know that Israel fell severely ill and his sickness lasted long, and he vowed that if God healed him, he would forbid the most beloved drink to him and the most beloved food to him, and the most beloved food to him was camel meat and the most beloved drink to him was its milk?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” He said, “I adjure you by God, besides whom there is no god: do you know that the fluid of the man is thick and the fluid of the woman is yellow and thin, and whichever of the two prevails, the child and resemblance are by God’s permission; if the man’s fluid prevails, it is male by God’s permission, and if the woman’s fluid prevails, it is female by God’s permission?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” He said, “I adjure you by the One who sent down the Torah to Moses: do you know that this unlettered prophet’s two eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep?” They said, “O God, yes.” He said, “O God, bear witness against them.” They said, “Now then, tell us who your guardian among the angels is, for at this point we will either join you or part from you.” He said, “My guardian is Gabriel ﷺ , and God ﷻ has never sent any prophet except that he was his guardian.” They said, “At this point we part from you. Had your guardian been other than him among the angels, we would have followed you and believed you.” He said, “What prevents you from believing him?” They said, “He is our enemy.” At that, God ﷻ said: {Whoever is an enemy to Gabriel—for it is he who brought it down upon your heart by God’s permission, confirming what was before it and as guidance and good tidings to the believers. Whoever is an enemy to God} up to {behind their backs as if they do not know}. Thus they incurred wrath upon wrath."],[12952,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to a woman of his people called Sawdah. She had children—five or six from a husband of hers who had died—so the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “What prevents you from me?” She said, “By God, O Prophet of God, nothing prevents me from you except that you are the most beloved of creation to me, but I honor you too much for these children to clamor at your head morning and evening.” He said, “Does anything other than that prevent you from me?” She said, “No, by God.” So the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “May God have mercy on you. The best women who ever rode the backs of camels are the righteous women of Quraysh—the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most protective of a husband in what he possesses.”"],[12953,"From the Prophet ﷺ he said, “Whoever drinks wine is impure for forty days. If he repents from it, God turns to him. If he returns, he returns impure. If he repents, God turns to him. If he returns, he returns impure for forty days. If he repents from it, God turns to him. If he goes back to it, it is a right upon God to make him drink from the pus of the people of Hell.” They said, “O Abu al-Abbas, what is the pus of the people of Hell?” He said, “The fats of the people of the Fire and their ichor.”"],[12957,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he stood one night in Makkah during the night and said, “O God, have I conveyed?—three times.” Then ‘Umar b. al-Khattab stood up—he was compassionate—and said, “O God, yes. You have been eager, striven, and given sincere counsel. O God, yes. You have been eager, striven, and given sincere counsel.” In the morning he said, “Faith will certainly prevail until it drives disbelief back to its homelands, and the seas will certainly be crossed with Islam, and there will certainly come upon people a time when they learn the Quran, teach it, and recite it, then say, ‘We have recited and taught, so who is better than us?’ Is there any good in those?” They said, “No, O Messenger of God, and who are those?” He said, “Those are from you, and those are the fuel of the Fire.”"],[12958,"In His saying \"They ask you about orphans. Say, 'Improvement for them is better,'\" and this was before the revelation of \"Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly are only consuming into their bellies fire. And they will be burned in a Blaze.\" The Muslims disliked eating with orphans and felt uncomfortable if they were to mix with them in any way, so they asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. So Allah revealed, \"Say, 'Improvement for them is better. And if you mix your affairs with them, then they are your brothers. And Allah knows the corrupter from the amender. And if Allah had willed, He could have put you in difficulty. However, He chose to facilitate for you.\"' He says, \"It is not to restrict you but [to promote] virtue;\" and He says, \"Whoever is rich, let him be abstinent, and whoever is poor, let him eat [only] in a fair manner.\" He says, \"The poor person may consume the wealth of the orphan to the extent of his needs, according to the standard of his living and his benefit from it, as long as he does not exceed [his needs].\""],[12959,"From Ibn ‘Abbas regarding His saying {When you are among them and lead them in prayer, let a group of them stand with you}: this is the prayer at times of fear. The imam stands, and with him stands a group of them, while a group takes their weapons and stands facing the enemy. The imam prays one rak‘ah with those with him, then remains seated in his position. They stand and pray the second rak‘ah for themselves while the imam remains seated. Then they depart until they come to their companions and stand in their position. Then the others come forward, and the imam prays the second rak‘ah for them. Thus “the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with the people on the day of Batn Nakhlah.”"],[12960,"\"In his statement 'there is no sin upon you to seek provision from your Lord,' it means that there is no harm for you in trade and business before and after Ihram. As for Ihram, the Messenger of Allah forbade getting married, arranging a marriage or sacrificing until he completes his Ihram.\""],[12961,"Regarding His saying {Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities}, he said: the greatest of major sins is associating partners with God, for God says {Whoever associates partners with God, God has forbidden Paradise to him}; and despairing of the mercy of God, for God says {No one despairs of the mercy of God except the disbelieving people}; and feeling secure from the plan of God, for God ﷻ says {No one feels secure from the plan of God except the losing people}. Among them is disobedience to parents, for God ﷻ made the disobedient a tyrannical wretch; killing the soul that God has forbidden except by right, for God, Blessed and Exalted, says {His recompense is Hell} the verse; slandering chaste women, for God, exalted is His mention, says {They are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment}; consuming the orphan’s property, for God ﷻ says {They only consume fire in their bellies, and they will burn in a blaze}; fleeing from battle, for God, Exalted, says {Whoever turns his back to them that day—unless swerving to fight or withdrawing to a company—has incurred wrath from God, and his abode is Hell, and wretched is the destination}; consuming usury, for God, Exalted, says {Those who consume usury do not stand except as one whom Satan has confounded by touch}; magic, for God, Exalted, says {And they certainly knew that whoever bought it would have no share in the Hereafter}; fornication, for God says {He will meet a penalty}—the punishment will be multiplied for him on the Day of Resurrection and he will abide therein humiliated; the false, sinful oath, for God says {Those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price} the verse; embezzlement, for God, Exalted, says {Whoever embezzles} will bring what he embezzled on the Day of Resurrection; withholding the obligatory zakat, for God, Exalted, says {Their foreheads, sides, and backs will be branded with it}; false testimony, for God ﷻ says {Whoever conceals it, his heart is sinful}; drinking wine, for God ﷻ equated it with idols; deliberately abandoning prayer or anything God has obligated, for the Messenger ﷺ says, “Whoever deliberately abandons prayer has freed himself from the protection of God and His Messenger”; breaking covenants; and severing ties of kinship."],[12962,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Prompt your dying ones to say the testimony that there is no god but God. Whoever says it at his death, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what about one who says it in good health?” He said, “That is more obligatory and more obligatory.” Then he said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if the heavens and the earths and all who are in them and between them and beneath them were brought and placed in one pan of the scale, and the testimony that there is no god but God were placed in the other pan, it would outweigh them.”"],[12963,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was eager for all people to believe and follow him in guidance, but God informed him that none believes except one for whom happiness had preceded in the first decree, and none goes astray except one for whom wretchedness had preceded in the first decree. Then God ﷻ said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Perhaps you would kill yourself with grief that they will not be believers}, meaning {If We willed, We could send down to them a sign from the sky, and their necks would remain bowed before it}."],[12964,"In his statement, \"Say, I do not ask of you any reward for it except love for my close relatives,\" he ﷺ said that the Messenger of Allah had kinship ties with all the Quraysh tribe. But when they denied him and refused to follow him, he said, \"O people! If you refuse to follow me, then protect my kinship ties among you. Let no one from the Arabs have a greater responsibility in protecting me and supporting me than you.\""],[12965,"In His saying {Those who, when afflicted with a calamity, say, \"Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return.\" It is those who will be awarded blessings and mercy from their Lord and it is those who are [rightly] guided.} Allah informs us that when a believer submits to the command of Allah and returns to Him, and then turns back to Him in times of affliction, three qualities of goodness are written for Him: prayer, mercy, and the realization of the path of guidance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever turns back to Allah in times of calamity, Allah will mend his calamity, better his outcome, and make for him a righteous successor that pleases Him.\""],[12966,"In his statement \"so that they may increase in faith with their faith,\" he said, \"Indeed Allah sent His Prophet with the testimony that there is no god but Allah, so when they believed in it, their pilgrimage increased, and when they believed in it, their jihad increased, and then He completed their religion for them.\" He said, \"This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed My favor upon you.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"So the firmest and most truthful faith of the people of the heavens and the people of the earth and the most complete of it is the testimony that there is no god but Allah.\""],[12967,"From Ibn ‘Abbas regarding His saying {And do not recite your prayer loudly nor in a whisper}: he said, “He does not pray ostentatiously for the people, nor does he abandon it out of fear of the people.”"],[12968,"In His saying \"And indeed, it is a reminder for you and your people,\" He said, \"It is an honor for you and your people.\""],[12969,"In his statement \"And remember the favor of Allah upon you and His covenant with which He bound you when you said, 'We hear and we obey'; and fear Allah. Indeed, Allah is Knowing of that within the breasts,\" it means that when Allah sent the Prophet ﷺ and revealed the Book to him, they said, \"We believe in the Prophet ﷺ and in the Book, and we affirm what is in the Torah.\" So Allah reminded them of His covenant with which they had bound themselves and commanded them to fulfill it."],[12970,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, {The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger and strive to make corruption in the land} (Qur'an 5:33): He said, \"A group from the People of the Book who had a covenant and pact with the Prophet ﷺ, but they broke the covenant and caused corruption in the land. So Allah gave His Prophet ﷺ the choice: if he wished, to kill them; if he wished, to crucify them; if he wished, to cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides. As for banishment, it is fleeing in the land. If one comes repentant and enters Islam, it is accepted from him and he is not taken to account for what came before him from him.\""],[12971,"In his saying, \"{If you are given this, take it, and if you are not given it, be cautious},\" they were the Jews. A woman among them committed adultery, and Allah had ruled in the Torah regarding stoning for adultery. So, they wanted to stone her. They said, \"Go to Muhammad, perhaps he has a dispensation in this matter.\" So, they went to him and said, \"O Abu al-Qasim, a woman among us has committed adultery. What do you say about her?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"How did Allah rule in the Torah regarding adultery?\" They said, \"Leave the Torah aside, what do you have in that matter?\" He said, \"Bring me your most knowledgeable person about the Torah that was revealed to Moses ﷺ.\" So, they brought him a man, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"By the One who saved you from the people of Pharaoh and split the sea for you and saved you, and drowned the people of Pharaoh, has Allah informed you about the ruling in the Torah regarding adultery?\" They said, \"He ruled for stoning.\""],[12972,"Abdullah b. Umar, whose kunya was Abu Abd al-Rahman, died in Makkah after the Hajj and was buried at al-Muhassab; and some people say at Fakhkh. His age when the Prophet ﷺ permitted him on the Day of the Trench to fight was fifteen years. The Trench was in Shawwal of the year four, so his age on the day he died was eighty-four."],[12973,"\"Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet ﷺ for sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him.\""],[12974,"\"Ibn Umar remained after the Prophet ﷺ for sixty years, with delegations of people coming to him.\""],[12975,"\"The age of Ibn Umar on the day he died was eighty-four.\""],[12976,"\"Abdullah b. Umar died in the year seventy-four and was buried at Fakhkh, and he was eighty-four years old.\""],[12977,"A spear of a man from the people of Syria struck him in his leg. Al-Hajjaj entered upon him to visit him and said, \"If I knew who struck you, I would strike his neck.\" He said, \"You are the one who struck me.\" He said, \"How?\" He said, \"On the day you brought weapons into the sanctuary of Allah.\""],[12978,"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, who did this to you so that I may take retribution for you from him? He said, \"By Allah, will you take retribution from him?\" He said, by Allah, I will take retribution for you from him. He said, \"What is the matter with the sanctuary of Allah and its security, that weapons are carried in it?\" He said, so he died from it."],[12979,"\"My father brought me on the day of Uhud to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was fourteen years old, and the Prophet ﷺ did not permit me. Then he brought me on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted a share for me.\" Nafi' said, \"I narrated this to Umar b. Abd al-Aziz, and he ordered that no one be allotted a share except one who was fifteen years old.\""],[12981,"\"He used to spend the night in prayer.\" Then he would say, \"O Nafi', has dawn broken?\" He would say no. \"Then he would resume prayer.\" Then he would say, \"O Nafi', has dawn broken?\" I would say yes. \"Then he would sit and seek forgiveness and supplicate until morning.\""],[12982,"\"I haven't been satisfied since I converted to Islam.\""],[12983,"A cloak. I said to Nafi', \"Did he eat meat?\" He said, \"When he fasted or traveled, it was the most common of his food.\""],[12984,"What prevents you from this matter when you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the son of the Commander of the Believers? He said, \"What prevents me from it is that Allah, Mighty and Sublime, has forbidden me the blood of my Muslim brother.\" He said, for Allah, Mighty and Sublime, says, {And fight them until there is no fitnah and the religion is entirely for Allah} (Qur'an 8:39). He said, so Ibn Umar said, \"We fought them until there was no fitnah and the religion was entirely for Allah, and you want me to fight until there is fitnah and the religion is for other than Allah.\""],[12985,"\"You are loved by the people, so go to Syria,\" Ibn Umar said, \"By my close proximity and companionship with the Prophet ﷺ, and the bond of kinship between us, he did not befriend him.\""],[12986,"that he should associate anyone else with me in it.”"],[12987,"“I saw on ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar two Maʿafiri garments, and his garment was halfway down his shins.”"],[12988,"“Ibn ʿUmar was given a gift of cloaks of silk brocade, among them a red cloak, and he divided them among his sons.”"],[12989,"“What the foolish will not despise you for, and the wise will not fault you for.” He said, “What is that?” He said, “What is between five dirhams and twenty dirhams.”"],[12990,"that a man should accompany him on a journey, and he stipulated that he should not accompany him on a jallal camel, “and do not vie with us for the call to prayer, and do not fast except with our permission.”"],[12991,"and that we should prepare his pre-dawn meal for him.”"],[12992,"“O shepherd of the sheep, is there any sheep to be slaughtered?” The shepherd said, “Its owner is not here.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “Say, ‘The wolf ate it.’” The shepherd raised his head to the sky and said, “Then where is God?” Ibn ʿUmar bought the shepherd and bought the sheep, then freed him and gave him the sheep."],[12993,"“Peace be upon you, O son of the one with two wings.”"],[12994,"“Isn’t it the best of your perfumes?”"],[12995,"and he said, “Indeed God is one God.”"],[12996,"About the Witr prayer, he began to say \"At the end of the night.\" So I said, \"Do you mean, do you mean?\" He said, \"Make your meaning at that star, and he pointed towards the sky. The night prayer is done in pairs, in pairs, and the Witr prayer is a single unit at the end of the night.\""],[12997,"A man said to Ibn ʿUmar, “I love you for the sake of God.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “But I hate you for the sake of God.” He said, “Why?” He said, “Because you embellish your call to prayer and take a wage for it.”"],[12998,"His son said to him, “What is this one saying?” He said, “This one says, ‘Know me, know me.’”"],[12999,"People have never exchanged anything among themselves better than covering a male. A man covers his horse, and its reward runs for him; a man covers his stallion, and its reward runs for him; a man covers his ram, and its reward runs for him."],[13000,"“O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I have entered ihram and I have gathered my hair.” He said, “Did you not hear ʿUmar during his caliphate say: Whoever braids his head or mats it should shave it?” He said, “O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, I did not braid it, but I gathered it.” Ibn ʿUmar said, “A she-goat and a he-goat, and the he-goat of a she-goat.”"],[13001,"No one curses anyone unless it's just one man."],[13002,"Garlic used to be crushed for Ibn ʿUmar, then strung on a thread and placed in the broth on a thread, and taken out on a thread, then thrown away, and he would eat."],[13003,"Ibn Umar said, \"Indeed, the best food is that which is free from harm to the teeth.\""],[13004,"I said to Ibn Sirin, “Did they used to joke?” He said, “They were only like other people. Ibn ʿUmar used to joke, recite poetry, and say, ‘...’ ”"],[13005,"“Give it to him.” But a man opposed it and bought it from him for a dirham, then brought it to him. Then the poor man came asking, and he said, “Give it to him.” But a man opposed him and bought it from him for a dirham. Then he wanted to return it but was prevented. “Had Ibn ʿUmar known about that bunch of grapes, he would not have tasted it.”"],[13006,"He used to enter the bathhouse, and the bath attendant would apply depilatory paste to him. When it reached his waist, he would say to the bath attendant, “Leave.”"],[13007,"Depilatory paste thins the skin."],[13008,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he performed ghusl, opened his eyes and inserted his fingers into his navel."],[13009,"Any surplus in it is a gift for you from me."],[13010,"“O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman, take it for what you gave me.” He said, “I swore an oath, and I would not help Satan against you by making you break your oath.”"],[13011,"I fear suspicion."],[13012,"Ibn ʿUmar, when he prayed alone during the days of tashriq, did not say the takbir after the prayer."],[13013,"“O Nafiʿ! Spend on us from our own wealth, for we have no need that charity be given to us.”"],[13014,"He used to recite this variant: “What! When we are decayed bones?” (79:11)"],[13015,"He saw Ibn ʿUmar with his waist-wrapper reaching halfway down his shins, his shirt above that, and his cloak above the shirt."],[13016,"I saw Ibn ʿUmar hastening between the two markers, saying, “I am doing it, I am doing it.”"],[13017,"“O Allah, make me among Your servants with the greatest share in every good You distribute this morning: light by which You guide, mercy You spread, provision You extend, harm You remove, affliction You lift, and tribulation You avert.”"],[13019,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The deceased is surely punished by his family’s weeping over him.”"],[13020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick man from among his companions while I was with him. He entered upon him while he was praying on a piece of wood, placing his forehead on the wood. He gestured to him, so he cast aside the wood and took a cushion. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Put it away from you. If you are able to prostrate on the ground, then do so; otherwise, gesture with a nod, and make your prostration lower than your bowing.”"],[13022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever intercedes to block one of the prescribed punishments of Allah has opposed Allah in His command.”"],[13023,"When we missed a man at Fajr and ʿIshāʾ, we would think ill of him."],[13024,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding a man who has a wife, then divorces her, then another man marries her and divorces her before consummating the marriage: is she lawful for the first? He said: “No, not until she tastes the honey [i.e., consummates the marriage with the second husband].” Abu al-Qasim said: Shuʿbah erred in this hadith in two places: in saying “from Salim b. Razin,” whereas it is Sulayman b. Razin, and in adding Saʿid b. al-Musayyib to the chain. It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri and Qays b. al-Rabiʿ from ʿAlqamah b. Marthad, from Sulayman b. Razin al-Ahmar, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, and that is correct."],[13025,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The deceased is tormented because of the wailing over him.”"],[13027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Refrain from (harming) the people of Lā ilāha illā Allāh; do not declare them disbelievers for a sin, for whoever declares the people of Lā ilāha illā Allāh disbelievers is closer to disbelief.”"],[13028,"“I performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ, with Abu Bakr, with Umar, and with Uthman ؓ, and all of them did not fast it, meaning the Day of Arafah.”"],[13029,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever mutilates his brother, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.” Al-Aṣamm, meaning Yazid b. Hurmuz, and Allah knows best."],[13030,"The Prophet ﷺ “prayed the fear prayer with these (group) one rakʿah and with these (group) one rakʿah.”"],[13031,"I heard Ibn Umar say: The delegation of Abd al-Qays came with al-Ashajj, and they asked the Prophet of Allah ﷺ about drinks, and he said: “Do not drink from ḥantamah, nor from dubbāʾ, nor from naqīr.”"],[13032,"“In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah.” Then when he began placing the bricks upon the laḥd, he said: “O Allah, protect her from Satan and from the torment of the grave.” Then when they leveled the mound over her, he stood beside the grave and said: “O Allah, make the earth withdraw from her sides, raise her soul, and grant her Your pleasure.” I said: “Are these things you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or things you said from your own opinion?” He said: “If I were capable of saying it, rather I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13033,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when you see them, pray.”"],[13034,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “The night prayer is two by two, and when you want to finish, pray one rakʿah, which will make odd for you what you have prayed.”"],[13035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever buys food should not sell it until he takes full possession of it.”"],[13036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “prohibited selling food purchased by measure until he takes full possession of it.”"],[13037,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The pilgrim in ihram should not wear the shirt, nor the qabāʾ, nor the trousers, nor the turban, nor the burnūs, nor anything touched by saffron or wars.”"],[13038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You should wear white garments, so wear them and shroud your dead in them.”"],[13039,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The two parties to a sale have the option (to cancel) as long as they have not separated.”"],[13040,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and it was a dark night. The Prophet’s ﷺ mu’adhdhin called the adhan, and he prayed. Then he ordered a crier to announce: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[13041,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and it was a dark night. The Prophet’s ﷺ mu’adhdhin called the adhan, and he prayed. Then he ordered a crier to announce: “Pray in your dwellings.”"],[13042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two people should not hold secret counsel apart from the third.”"],[13043,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People are like a hundred camels; you will hardly find among them a suitable riding camel.”"],[13044,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bilal gives the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan.”"],[13045,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when he was in a hurry on a journey, he would delay Maghrib until he combined it with the Isha prayer."],[13046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever misses the Asr (afternoon) prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been lost.\""],[13047,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the zakah on crops watered by rain and rivers one tenth, and on those watered by artificial irrigation half of one tenth."],[13048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Isha in the last part of his life. When he said the salam, he said: “Do you see this night of yours? After a hundred years, no one on the face of the earth today will remain.”"],[13049,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin the prayer with the takbir and raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders. Then when he said the takbir for bowing, he did the same. Then when he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he did the same. Then he said, “Our Lord, to You is praise,” and did the same."],[13050,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir in prayer, he would raise his hands level with his shoulders. When he bowed, he did the same. When he raised his head, he did the same. And when he said, “Allah hears the one who praises Him,” he said, “Our Lord, to You is praise,” and did the same. He did not do that in prostration."],[13051,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You belongs all praise,” then before prostrating he would say: “O God, curse so-and-so and so-and-so,” then he would say the takbir and prostrate—until God, exalted is He, sent down: “You have no part in the matter.”"],[13052,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups for one rakʿah while the other group faced the enemy. Then they left and stood in the position of their companions facing the enemy, and the others came and the Prophet ﷺ prayed one rakʿah with them. Then the Prophet ﷺ said the salam. Then these made up one rakʿah and those made up one rakʿah."],[13055,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Perform ablution after (eating) that which has been changed by fire.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 486)"],[13056,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.”"],[13057,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade a man to look at the private part of his brother."],[13058,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade praying in the middle of the road, relieving oneself there, or urinating there."],[13059,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking one another’s necks.”"],[13060,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The prayer of one sitting is like half the prayer of one standing.”"],[13061,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is God, the One.”"],[13062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and ʿUmar did not wear rings or seal letters, until Ziyad b. Abi Sufyan wrote to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab: “You write to us about matters that have no seals.” So at that point he adopted a ring and sealed with it."],[13063,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever preserves me regarding my Companions will come to me at my basin, and whoever does not preserve me regarding my Companions will not see me on the Day of Resurrection except from afar.”"],[13064,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling fruit until it begins to yellow or redden."],[13065,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a white shirt on ʿUmar and said: “Is this shirt of yours new or washed?” He said: “Rather, washed.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wear new, live praiseworthy, die as a martyr, and may God grant you the delight of your eye in this world and the Hereafter.” He said: “And you, O Messenger of God.”"],[13066,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when travel in a journey hurried him, he would delay the Maghrib prayer until he combined it with the Isha prayer."],[13067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform glorification (subhanAllah) while on his mount, not caring which direction he was facing."],[13068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever sells a slave who has property, the property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""],[13069,"We used to say during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman."],[13071,"He would walk in front of the funeral while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman walked ahead of it. My father narrated this Hadith, and indeed, the Hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is only from Zubair. It is the Hadith of Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, and the Hadith of Ibn Uyaynah seems like a fabrication."],[13072,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ , Abu Bakr, and Umar used to walk in front of the funeral.\""],[13073,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."],[13074,"And he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to walk in front of it, as did Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman.\""],[13075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim: he does not wrong him nor hand him over. Whoever is engaged in the need of his brother, Allah is engaged in his need. Whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress in this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. Whoever conceals a Muslim, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[13077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted the Muslims regarding what would gather them for prayer. They suggested the trumpet, but he disliked it because of the Jews. Then the bell was mentioned, but he disliked it because of the Christians. That night, Abdullah b. Zayd, a man from the Ansar, and Umar b. al-Khattab were shown the call (adhan) in a vision. The Ansari went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal, who then gave the call to prayer with it."],[13078,"Two men from the Ansar recited a surah which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taught them, and they used to recite it. One night they stood to pray and could not recall a single letter of it. In the morning they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is among what has been abrogated and caused to be forgotten, so turn away from it.\" Al-Zuhri used to recite it as {ma nansakh min ayatin aw nunsiha} with a damma on the nun and lightly (pronounced)."],[13079,"The most frequent oath of the Prophet ﷺ was: \"No, by the Turner of hearts.\""],[13080,"No head was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor on the day of Badr to Madinah."],[13081,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"commanded the sharpening of blades and that they be concealed from the animals.\""],[13082,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it on the Day of Hunayn, and we were not fornicators.\""],[13083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and he struck him with his foot and said, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" Ibn Sayyad said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered ones.\" He said, \"Then do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\""],[13084,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"I saw a black woman with disheveled hair coming out of Madinah until she stood at Mahya'ah, which is al-Juhfah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I interpreted it to mean that the plague of Madinah was transferred to al-Juhfah.\""],[13085,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with the boys, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him with his foot and said, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" Ibn Sayyad said, \"I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered ones.\" Ibn Sayyad said to him, \"Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\""],[13086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever comes to me as a visitor, with no known need except to visit me, it is incumbent upon me to be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[13087,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cupping on the head is for insanity, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and toothache.\""],[13088,"A boy came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I intend to go to this region for Hajj.\" He said, \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked with him and said, 'O boy, may Allah provide you with piety, direct you toward good, and suffice you against worry.'\" When the boy returned and greeted the Prophet ﷺ, he raised his head toward him and said, \"O boy, may your Hajj be accepted, your sin forgiven, and your expenditure replaced.\""],[13089,"He informed him that it was said to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Mu'arras, the resting place of the tree, \"Ask, for it is the blessed stony ground of Makkah.\""],[13090,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, Allah will build for him a house in the Fire.\""],[13091,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[13092,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw in a dream that I was given a large wooden cup full of milk, and I drank from it until I was filled, until I saw it flowing in my veins between the skin and the flesh. Some remained, and I gave it to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" They said, \"Interpret it, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said, \"This is knowledge that Allah gave you and filled you with, and some remained, so you gave it to 'Umar b. al-Khattab.\" He said, \"You have spoken correctly.\""],[13093,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Between my grave and my pulpit, there is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my pond.\" So, he quoted its foundation and said, \"I have written it from Muhammad ibn Bishr.\""],[13094,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful.”"],[13095,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A dog indeed diminishes two qirats every day, except a hunting dog or a sheepdog.” Abu al-Qasim said: “Diminishes, meaning from the reward of its owner.”"],[13096,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “From grapes comes khamr, from honey comes khamr, from raisins comes khamr, from dates comes khamr, and from wheat comes khamr. I forbid every intoxicant.”"],[13097,"When a deceased person died, the Messenger of God ﷺ would say: “Send him ahead to our forerunner. How excellent a forerunner for my community is Uthman b. Maz‘un.”"],[13098,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Kill snakes. Whoever finds the one with two stripes or the short-tailed one and does not kill them is not of us, for they are the two that snatch away sight and cause what is in women’s wombs to miscarry.”"],[13099,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom God has taught the Quran and he recites it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day, and a man to whom God has given wealth and he spends it during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.”"],[13100,"The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[13101,"The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[13102,"Ibn Umar said: “The oath of the Messenger of God ﷺ was: ‘No, by the Turner of hearts.’”"],[13103,"The oath by which the Messenger of God ﷺ used to swear was: “No, by the Turner of hearts.”"],[13104,"He used to curse al-Bayda’ or intended to curse it, and he said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not enter ihram except from Dhu al-Hulayfah.”"],[13105,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not enter ihram except from near the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah.”"],[13106,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: that he met Zayd b. ʿAmr b. Nufayl at the lower part of Baldah, and that was before revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ offered him a leather dining mat with meat on it, but he refused to eat. He said: 'I do not eat from what they slaughter for their idols. I eat only from that over which the name of God has been mentioned.'"],[13107,"From Zayd b. Harithah al-Kalbi, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'We used not to call him anything but Zayd b. Muhammad until the Qur'an came down: \"Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of God.\"'"],[13108,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he appointed Usamah b. Zayd as commander, and it reached him that the people were finding fault with Usamah b. Zayd and criticizing his command. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among the people and said: 'Indeed, you are finding fault with Usamah and criticizing his command, and you did the same with his father before. He was indeed worthy of command, and he was indeed the most beloved of all people to me. And this one after him is the most beloved of people to me, so treat him well, for he is among the best of you.' Salim said: 'I never heard ʿAbd Allah relate this hadith without saying: \"except Fatimah.\"'"],[13109,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ was approached while he was at al-Muʿarras in Dhu al-Hulayfah, in the belly of the valley, and he said: 'You are in a blessed pebbly plain.'"],[13110,"Regarding the dream of the Messenger of God ﷺ about Abu Bakr and ʿUmar, he said: 'I saw people gathered, and Abu Bakr stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and God forgives him. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab stood and it turned into a large bucket. I have never seen a champion among people do what he did, until the people settled by the watering place.'"],[13111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.' Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of God, one side of my lower garment hangs loose unless I take care of it.' He said: 'You are not one of those who do it out of pride.'"],[13112,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever says in any marketplace: 'There is no god but Allah, alone without partner. To Him belongs the dominion, and to Him belongs all praise, and He is capable of all things,' Allah will write for him a thousand thousand good deeds.\""],[13113,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is below the ankles is in the Fire.'"],[13114,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'I saw in a dream that people were gathered, and Abu Bakr b. Abi Quhafah stood and drew a bucket or two buckets, and in his drawing there was weakness, and God forgives him. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab took it, and it turned into a large bucket. I have never seen a champion do what he did, until the people settled by the watering place.'"],[13115,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever drags his garment out of pride, God will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.' Salim said: 'My father narrated to me that Abu Bakr said: \"O Messenger of God, one side of my lower garment hangs loose unless I take care of it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"You are not one of those who do it out of pride.\"'"],[13116,"While ʿUmar b. al-Khattab was riding in a group, the Messenger of God ﷺ heard him swearing by his father. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'God forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by God or remain silent.'"],[13117,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Three will not enter Paradise and three God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection. As for those who will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the woman who imitates men, and the cuckold. As for the three whom God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the habitual drinker of wine, and the one who reminds others of what he has given.'"],[13118,"You know that we used to say during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman—meaning in the caliphate."],[13119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was pressed for time on a journey, would combine Maghrib and ʿIshaʾ after the twilight had disappeared by an hour."],[13120,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned ʿAshuraʾ and said: \"It was a fast of the people of the Jahiliyyah, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may break the fast.\""],[13121,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"The night prayer is two rakʿahs at a time, two rakʿahs at a time; so when you fear the arrival of dawn, perform Witr with one rakʿah.\""],[13122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Everything has a source, and the source of taqwa is the hearts of those who know Allah.\""],[13123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The deceased is punished by the weeping of the living.\""],[13124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallalah (an animal that eats filth), its milk, and its riding."],[13125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you can be like the companion of the measure of rice, let him be like him.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is the companion of the measure of rice?\" He said: \"Three men went out, and the sky became cloudy over them, so they entered a cave. A rock came until it sealed the entrance over them. They tried to move it but could not. Some of them said to the others: 'You have fallen into a grave matter; let each man among you supplicate with the best deed he has performed, perhaps Allah will rescue us from this.'\" Then he mentioned the hadith of the cave in full."],[13126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not right for a Muslim who has wealth enough to make a will to spend even one night without his will being with him.\""],[13127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first from whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, then Abu Bakr, then ʿUmar. Then the people of al-Baqiʿ will come and be gathered with me, then I will wait for the people of Makkah and they will be gathered with me.\""],[13128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck the chest of ʿUmar b. al-Khattab with his hand three times when he accepted Islam, saying: \"O Allah, remove what is in his chest of rancor and replace it with faith,\" saying that three times."],[13129,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"When it is his seventh day, pour blood away from him and remove harm from him.\""],[13130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for livestock or hunting, two qirats are deducted from his good deeds each day.\""],[13131,"The Prophet ﷺ used to command us to be brief, and he used to lead us in prayer with (the surah) al-Saffat."],[13132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah does not look at a gray-haired adulterer, nor at a poor man who is arrogant, nor at one who drags his lower garment out of pride.\""],[13133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he returned from Hajj or ʿUmrah, would say whenever he ascended a mountain pass or a hillock: 'Allahu Akbar' three times, then say: 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. We are returning, repenting, worshiping, prostrating, to our Lord praising. Allah has been true to His promise, helped His servant, and defeated the confederates alone.'"],[13134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Dajjal will descend at this salt-marsh, and the last to go out to him will be women, so much so that a man will return to his mother, his sister, and his paternal aunt and tie her up securely, fearing that she might go out to him. Then Allah will enable the Muslims over him, and they will kill him and kill his followers, so much so that the Jew will hide under a tree or a stone, and the stone or the tree will say: \"O Muslim, here is a Jew under me, so kill him.\"'"],[13135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man from Qahtan will surely drive the people with a stick.'"],[13136,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No servant makes an image except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Bring to life what you have created.'"],[13137,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Allah loves the skilled worker.'"],[13138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from ʿArafat while saying: 'To You it hastens, its girth strap trembling, its religion differing from the Christians' religion.' Abu al-Qasim said: 'Abu al-Rabiʿ al-Samman, in my view, erred in raising this hadith to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, because what is well-known in the narration from Ibn ʿUmar is: from ʿArafat while he was saying...' then he mentioned the rajaz verse."],[13139,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'No servant makes an image except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Bring to life what you have created.'"],[13140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Islam is built on five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakat, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House.'"],[13141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever keeps a dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds.'"],[13142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they cause blindness and cause miscarriage. So whoever does not kill them is not one of us.'"],[13143,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, a qirat is deducted from his deeds, and a qirat is like Uhud.'"],[13144,"Woe to you, O Ashʿab, do not beg, for my father narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: 'There will surely come people on the Day of Resurrection with no morsel of flesh on their faces, having worn it away.'"],[13145,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar used to pray before the sermon on the two Eids."],[13146,"\"The Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Al-Isbal may apply to the Izar, the Qamis and the turban. Whoever drags any one of these out of vanity, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5334)"],[13147,"Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'Stand and strike the neck of this man.' Salim took the sword, took the man, and headed toward the gate of the palace. His father saw him heading off with the man and said: 'Do you think he will do it?' He sent someone after him twice or three times. When he brought him out, Salim said to him: 'Have you prayed the dawn prayer?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then take whichever road you wish.' Then he came back and threw down the sword. Al-Hajjaj said to him: 'Did you strike his neck?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'I heard my father here saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under Allah's protection until evening.\"' Ibn Umar said: 'He is shrewd. We named you Salim only so that you would remain safe.'"],[13148,"Al-Hajjaj said to him, \"What prevented you from killing him?\" Salim replied, \"My father informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, 'Whoever prays the Fajr prayer is in the protection of Allah throughout his day.' So I disliked killing a man whom Allah has protected.\" Al-Hajjaj then asked Ibn 'Umar, \"Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ ?\" Ibn 'Umar replied, \"Yes.\""],[13149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is khamr, and every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[13150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every intoxicant is unlawful.\""],[13151,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ doing that."],[13152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'How is the night prayer?' He said: \"Two by two. Then when you fear dawn, pray witr with one.\""],[13153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer and became confused during it. When he finished, he said to Ubayy b. Ka'b: \"Did you pray with us?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"What prevented you from prompting me?\""],[13154,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None may touch the Quran except one who is pure.\""],[13155,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought nabidh and he drank some of it."],[13156,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not make mosques thoroughfares, except for remembrance or prayer.\""],[13157,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram when his mount set off with him."],[13158,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Choose four of them.\""],[13159,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever fasts the days of Hajj and does not find a sacrificial animal when he performs tamattuʿ, then it is between the ihram of one of you until the Day of ʿArafah, and that is the last of them.\""],[13160,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The poor of my Ummah will enter Paradise before their rich by forty autumns.\" I said: \"Describe them to us.\" He said: \"They are those whose clothes are greasy, whose heads are disheveled, who are not granted permission at the gates, and who do not marry the protected women. The easts and wests of the earth are entrusted to them; they give all that is upon them and are not given all that is due to them.\""],[13161,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Jews were asked about Musa and they went to excess, adding and subtracting until they disbelieved. And the Christians were asked about ʿIsa and they went to excess concerning him, adding and subtracting until they disbelieved. And it will soon spread from me hadiths. So whatever comes to you of my hadith, recite the Book of Allah and test it. Whatever agrees with the Book of Allah, then I said it, and whatever does not agree with the Book of Allah, then I did not say it.\""],[13162,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah has forbidden wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[13163,"In his saying \"{§as a shining lamp},\" Muhammad's heart is the cavity, and the bottle is his heart, and the lamp is the light that is in his heart, it is lit from a blessed tree. The tree is Ibrahim, an olive tree that is not eastern nor western, neither Jewish nor Christian. Then he recited \"{Ibrahim was neither Jewish nor Christian, but he was a pure monotheist, Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists}\""],[13164,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer, and a man was turning the pebbles with his hand. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he turned to us and said: \"Which of you was turning the pebbles with his hand?\" A man stood up and said: \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said to him: \"That is your share from your prayer.\""],[13165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no good in the gathering of women, nor at a deceased person, for when they gather, they say and say.\""],[13166,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus until it wastes him away is better for him than to have it filled with poetry.\" And Muhammad b. al-Muthanna attributed Abu ʿUbaydah, saying: \"Abu ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar.\""],[13167,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard thunder and lightning, he would say: \"O Allah, do not kill us with Your wrath, and do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that.\""],[13168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed, would raise his hands when he began, when he said takbir for bowing, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[13169,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Muslims looked at the best of them and appointed him as successor, and he was Abu Bakr. When Abu Bakr died, the people looked at the best of the Muslims and appointed him as successor, and he was ʿUmar. When he died or was killed, the Muslims looked at the best of them and appointed him as successor, and he was ʿUthman. If you kill him, then bring me someone better than him, and by Allah, I do not think that you will do it.\" Abu al-Qasim said: \"Al-Qasim, from whom Qurrah b. Khalid narrated this hadith, is Abu Nuhayk of Basra, who is Ibn Muhammad.\""],[13170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If one of you is faced with a matter that he fears will escape him, then let him pray this prayer,\" meaning combining the two prayers."],[13171,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No parent has ever endowed their child with anything better than good manners.\""],[13172,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I forbade you from nabidh in earthenware jars, and I had forbidden you from visiting graves, and I had forbidden you from sacrificial meats. Now, containers do not make anything lawful or unlawful. Now, visit graves, for they soften the hearts.\" ʿAbdan added in his hadith: \"Now, I had forbidden you from the meats of sacrificial animals, so eat and store whatever you wish.\""],[13173,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The food of two suffices four, and the food of four suffices eight, so gather together over it and do not separate from it.\""],[13174,"The Prophet ﷺ asked about a man and said, \"Who knows him?\" A man among them said, \"I do.\" He asked, \"What is his name?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" He asked, \"What is his father's name?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" He asked, \"What is his clan?\" The man replied, \"I don't know.\" The Prophet said, \"You should not be acquainted with him until you know his name, his father's name, and his clan. If he falls ill, you should visit him, and if he dies, you should follow his funeral procession.\""],[13175,"He was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ among a group of his companions, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O these people, do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" They said: \"Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Do you not know that Allah has sent down in His Book that whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah?\" They said: \"Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and that obedience to you is part of obedience to Allah.\" He said: \"And obedience to Allah is that you obey me, and part of obeying me is that you obey your leaders. And if they pray sitting, then pray sitting, all of you.\""],[13176,"Narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Indeed the Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not wrong him, nor betray him, nor abandon him in a calamity that befalls him. And if he encounters the best of the Arabs and the mawali, they will love one another with a love from which they find no escape. And if he encounters the worst of the two groups, they will hate one another with a hatred from which they find no escape.\""],[13177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"People are like a hundred camels: one seeks a mount suitable for travel among them, but finds only one.\""],[13178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on my brother ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah. Wherever the prayer overtook him, he would make his camel kneel.\""],[13179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Eid and began by praying without any adhan or iqamah, then he delivered the sermon."],[13180,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he started the prayer, raised his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and he did not raise them above his ears."],[13181,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on a camel, facing whatever direction it took him."],[13182,"Umar b. al-Khattab gave a horse in charity to a man for the sake of Allah. Then Umar found him selling it, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I gave a horse in charity to so-and-so, and I found him selling it. Should I buy it?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not buy it, and do not take back your charity.\""],[13183,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The keys of the unseen are five,\" then he recited this verse: {Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. And no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware.}"],[13184,"Some people raided the camels of the Prophet ﷺ, drove them away, apostatized from Islam, and killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a believer. The Prophet ﷺ sent after them, and they were captured. He cut off their hands and feet and put out their eyes. It is said that this is ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar, and it is said ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUtbah, and Allah knows best."],[13185,"The Prophet ﷺ put out the eyes of the ʿUraynis only because they had put out the eyes of the shepherds."],[13186,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Bad omens are in the dwelling, the woman, and the horse.”"],[13187,"There was a wife under my care whom I loved, but my father disliked her. He ordered me to divorce her, but I refused. Then ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O ʿAbd Allah, divorce her.”"],[13188,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques.” I said, “As for me, I shall prevent my family; so whoever wishes may let his family go.” He turned to me and said: “May Allah curse you! May Allah curse you! May Allah curse you! You hear me say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they not be prevented, and you say this?” Then he wept and stood up in anger."],[13189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women their shares of the mosques when they ask your permission.” Bilal said, “By Allah, we shall prevent them.” Then ʿAbd Allah said, “O enemy of Allah, I say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and you say we shall prevent them?”"],[13190,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar say: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with ʿAʾishah behind him, Abu Bakr asked permission and entered. Then ʿUmar asked permission and entered. Then Saʿd b. Malik entered. Then ʿUthman b. ʿAffan asked permission while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was talking with his knee uncovered. He pulled his garment over his knee when ʿUthman asked permission, and said to his wife, “Move back.” They conversed for a while, then left. ʿAʾishah said, “O Prophet of Allah, my father and his companions entered and you did not adjust your garment over your knee, nor did you move me back from you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O ʿAʾishah, should I not feel shy before a man before whom the angels feel shy? By the One in whose hand is the soul of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the angels feel shy of ʿUthman just as they feel shy of Allah and His Messenger. Had he entered while you were close to me, he would not have spoken or raised his head until you left.”"],[13194,"“I only do as I saw the Prophet ﷺ do.”"],[13195,"When the rim of the sun starts appearing defer prayer till it completely appears, and when the rim of the sun disappears defer prayer till it completely disappears. (Using translation from Muslim 829)"],[13196,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not deliberately aim your prayers at the rising of the sun or its setting, for it rises between the two horns of Satan.”"],[13197,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs, as did Abu Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthman for part of his rule.”"],[13198,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gentleness is not given to the people of a household except that it benefits them.”"],[13199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the deceased is punished by the weeping of his family.”"],[13201,"“As for us, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to consider it hypocrisy. I do not know what you consider it to be?”"],[13203,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from embezzled wealth.” And you were in Basra."],[13204,"“I prayed with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ the prayer of fear. He arranged a group of us behind him, and another group faced the enemy. He said the takbir, then bowed with them and prostrated twice. Then the group that was with him departed and faced the enemy, and the other group came and lined up behind him. Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said the salam, and each man of the two groups stood and completed for himself one rakʿah and two prostrations.”"],[13207,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not pray the same prayer twice in a day.”"],[13208,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik who narrated to us from Ali bin al-Mubarak al-Sanaani that Ismail bin Abi Uwais narrated to me from Malik who narrated to us from Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi who narrated from Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Umar from Saeed bin Yasar that he said: \"I was traveling with Abdullah bin Umar on the road to Mecca. Saeed said: When I feared dawn, I stopped and performed the Witr prayer.\" Abdullah said: \"Is there not a good example in the Messenger of Allah?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer on a camel.\""],[13209,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying voluntarily on his donkey while he was heading to Khaybar.”"],[13210,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and ʿAli b. al-Mubarak al-Sanʿani narrated to me; Ismaʿil b. Abi Uways narrated to us; Malik narrated to me, from ʿAmr b. Yahya, from Saʿid b. Yasar, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on his donkey while he was heading to Khaybar.”"],[13211,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while he was on a donkey, heading toward Khaybar.” ʿAmr b. Yahya said: “That is facing toward Syria.”"],[13212,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying on his donkey while his donkey was heading toward Khaybar, making gestures (with his head)."],[13213,"Saʿīd b. Yasār, the freed slave of Shuqrān, the freed slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to me. He said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar say: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying on a donkey while heading toward Khaybar.”"],[13214,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on a donkey while he was heading toward Khaybar.”"],[13215,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever dies separated from the community dies a death of the Age of Ignorance.”"],[13217,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade meeting caravans (before they reach the market), a resident selling on behalf of a bedouin, and any of you proposing to a woman already betrothed to his brother until he marries her or gives her up.”"],[13218,"That no day he had named would come upon him except that he fasted on it, and that coincided with the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast. Ibn ʿUmar said: “You have a good example in the Messenger of God.” “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not fast on the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast, nor did he command fasting them.”"],[13219,"That that day would not pass him except that he fasted, and that day coincided with the day of sacrifice or the day of breaking the fast. Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “You have a good example in the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then he said: “He did not fast the day of breaking the fast or the day of sacrifice, nor did he consider fasting them a right.”"],[13220,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Mosque of Madinah, and the Mosque of Jerusalem.”"],[13221,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Every shepherd is responsible for his flock.”"],[13231,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever strikes his slave with a punishment he did not deserve, its expiation is to set him free.”"],[13232,"He said to the young man, “What do you need, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?” He said, “Woe to you! Do you love that Allah should look at you on the Day of Resurrection?” He said, “Glory be to Allah! What prevents me from loving that?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Allah will not look at a servant on the Day of Resurrection who drags his lower garment out of pride.’” He said, “That young man was never seen except with his garment raised until he died.”"],[13235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “No amputation for livestock except what is beyond the enclosure, and no amputation for fruit except what the drying-floor has gathered.”"],[13236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The dead person is tormented by the weeping of the living.”"],[13237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade continuous fasting for three days. They said, “But you fast continuously.” He said, “I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"],[13239,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to Arafah; among us were those reciting the talbiyah and among us were those saying takbir. The one saying takbir was not reproached for his takbir, nor was the one reciting the talbiyah reproached for his talbiyah. Abdullah ibn Umar was among those who said takbir."],[13240,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The small stream which God, Exalted is He, mentioned, {Your Lord has placed beneath you a small stream} (Q 19:24), is a river God brought forth for her to drink from.'"],[13241,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The fornicator does not commit fornication at the time he fornicates while he is a believer, nor does the wine-drinker drink wine at the time he drinks it while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal at the time he steals while he is a believer, nor does one seize a notable plunder while he is a believer.'"],[13242,"I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. Umar mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: 'Command him to take her back.'"],[13244,"Al-Qanabi narrated to us from Malik, from Qatan ibn Wahb, that Yuhannas, the freed slave of al-Zubayr, informed him that he was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar during the fitnah when a freed woman of his came to greet him and said: 'O Abu Abdir-Rahman, I wanted to leave, and times have become hard for us.' Abdullah ibn Umar said to her: 'Stay, you wretched one! For I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"No one endures its hardship and severity except that it will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection.\"'"],[13245,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Whoever fasts on Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday, then gives charity on Friday from the little of his wealth, every sin he has committed will be forgiven for him until he becomes like the day his mother gave birth to him, free from sins.'"],[13246,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'An angel descended upon me from heaven who had never descended upon any prophet before me and will not descend upon anyone after me. It was Israfil, and Gabriel was with him. He said: \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.\" Then he said: \"I am the messenger of your Lord to you. He commanded me to inform you: if you wish, you will be a prophet servant; and if you wish, a prophet king.\" I looked at Gabriel, and Gabriel gestured to me to be humble. The Prophet ﷺ then said: \"A prophet servant.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Had I said a prophet king, then if I wished, the mountains would have moved with me as gold.\"'"],[13247,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, this world is more insignificant to God than this lamb is to its owners. Were the world to equal the weight of a mustard seed with God, He would not have given it to anyone except His friends and beloved ones among His creation.'"],[13248,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever says: \"There is no god but God alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is the Ever-Living who does not die; in His hand is all good, and He is capable of everything,\" desiring by it only His Face, God will admit him by it into the gardens of bliss.'"],[13249,"I climbed onto a roof and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Hafsah's house relieving himself between two bricks, facing toward the Holy House."],[13250,"About the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: 'When he prayed, he would say \"God is greatest\" every time he raised and every time he lowered, in bowing and prostration. When he finished, he would say: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of God\" to his right and to his left.'"],[13251,"I said to Ibn 'Umar, 'I saw you wearing these sandals of tanned leather.' He said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing them and performing ablution while wearing them.'"],[13254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dye with it."],[13257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'We have not loved anything from your world except your women.'"],[13258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse while on the pulpit: \"And they did not appraise Allah with true appraisal\" to the end of the verse. The pulpit swayed like this and like that, meaning it shook."],[13259,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever guides a blind person forty steps, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.'"],[13260,"He said to him, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, will you perform Hajj on this?' He said, 'Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Do not abandon Hajj, even if on an old, broken-tusked camel worth ten dirhams.\" By Allah, no mount has come to me except this one, and I would not abandon Hajj.'"],[13267,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the new moon, he would say: “O Allah, let it appear upon us with security, faith, safety, Islam, and success in what You love and are pleased with. Our Lord and your Lord is Allah.”"],[13268,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing an izar that was rustling, and he said: “Who is this?” I said, ‘Abdullah. He said: “If you are Abdullah, then raise your izar.” So I raised my izar to the middle of my shins, and his izar remained like that until he died."],[13269,"When the verses that obligate punishment were revealed, such as His saying: “Those who devour the property of orphans unjustly” to the end of the verse, and like “Those who consume riba,” and like His saying: “And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell,” he said: We used to testify that whoever did any of this was in the Fire. But when His saying was revealed: “Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills,” we refrained from testifying, and we feared for them because of what Allah had made obligatory for them."],[13270,"From Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Every creature of the sea and land that does not have flowing blood, no zakat is due on it.”"],[13271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ has creatures whom He created for the needs of people. People turn to them in their needs. Those are the ones secure from the punishment of Allah.”"],[13272,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13273,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed them during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: “Verily, Allah has made your blood and your wealth sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed?” They said, “Yes.” He said: “O Allah, bear witness.” He said that three times, then said: “Beware, do not revert after me to disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"],[13274,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and the Fire, then it will be slaughtered. Then a caller will call out: ‘O people of Paradise, there is no death; O people of the Fire, there is no death.’ So the people of Paradise will increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of the Fire will increase in sorrow upon their sorrow.”"],[13275,"We were talking about the Farewell Pilgrimage while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, but we did not know what the Farewell Pilgrimage was. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood as a preacher, praised and extolled Allah, then mentioned the false messiah, the Dajjal, and expounded at length about him. Then he said: “Allah has not sent any prophet except that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Noah warned of him, and the prophets after him. He will emerge among you, and if any of his affairs is unclear to you, it should not be unclear that he is one-eyed in the right eye, as if it is a floating grape.”"],[13276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If people knew what is in solitude, no one would travel alone at night.”"],[13277,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Jibril kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.\""],[13278,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If there is ill omen in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house.\""],[13279,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water,\" or he said: \"Make it cool with water.\""],[13280,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Jibril ﷺ kept urging me to be good to the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.\""],[13281,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I have been given the keys of everything except five: {Indeed, God has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain} and He knows what is in the wombs; and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, God is All-Knowing, All-Aware.\""],[13282,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking help against his father. He said: \"He has taken from my wealth.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Do you not know that you and your wealth belong to your father?\""],[13283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a black-and-white ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise, do you recognize this?' They will crane their necks and look. And it will be said: 'O people of Hell, do you recognize this?' They will crane their necks and look. Then it will be slaughtered. Then it will be said: 'O people of Paradise, eternity, and no more death; and O people of Hell, eternity, and no more death.'\""],[13284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I know that the most beloved land to Allah is Mecca, and if it were not for my people forcing me out, I would not have left. O Allah, make the love of Medina in our hearts as you have made the love of Mecca in our hearts.\" And whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached Medina, his face would be recognized with delight and joy."],[13285,"We heard of the Farewell Pilgrimage while the Messenger of God ﷺ was alive among us, and we did not think it was his farewell. The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and mentioned the Dajjal, speaking at length about him. Then he mentioned of his affair what God willed him to mention. Then he said: \"Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, never sent a prophet but that he warned his nation of the Dajjal. Nuh warned his nation of him, then the prophets after him, one prophet after another.\" Then he said: \"Now, whoever of you is unclear about his affair, and the Messenger of God ﷺ hesitated to say it,\" then he said: \"except whoever of you is unclear about his affair, let it not be unclear to you that your Lord is not one-eyed, while he is one-eyed in the right eye, as if it were a floating grape. Now, have I conveyed?\" They shouted from the sides: \"Yes.\" He said: \"O God, bear witness,\" three times. Then he said: \"Do not revert after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\""],[13286,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"They will pass out of Islam as an arrow passes through the game.\""],[13287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not prevent the female servants of God from the mosques of God.\""],[13288,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Only two are envied, or as God willed him to say: a man whom God gave the Quran and he stands in prayer during the hours of night and day, and a man whom God gave wealth and he spends it.\""],[13289,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted to al-Zubayr the run of his horse in a land called Tharira. He let his horse run until it stopped, then threw his whip and said: \"Give him as far as his whip reached.\""],[13290,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ applied kohl, he would put three (drops/applications) in the right eye and two in the left, making it an odd number."],[13291,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Increase in planting (the trees of) Paradise, for its water is sweet and its soil is good. So increase in planting it (by saying): ‘There is no might nor power except with Allah (La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah).’”"],[13292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to spend the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah, and when he had prayed Fajr he would sit on his mount and enter the state of ihram (by saying the talbiyah)."],[13293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prostrate (for forgetfulness) on the day of Dhu al-Yadayn."],[13294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a dog laps in the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times.”"],[13295,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surat al-Najm in Makkah, and the people prostrated with him, such that a man would raise some earth to his forehead and prostrate on it, and even a man would prostrate on another man."],[13296,"\"From the Prophet, ﷺ , that he said, 'There is no surah, whether small or large, except that I have heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , recite it in its entirety during prayer.'\""],[13297,"ʿAmr b. Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿUmar, from Nafiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: A woman used to borrow jewelry in the time of the Prophet ﷺ and then keep it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let the woman repent to Allah (Mighty and Sublime) and to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and let her return what she has,” while she was listening. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Stand, O so-and-so, take her hand and cut it off.”"],[13298,"I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came, greeted him, and then turned away. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love this man.” He said: “Have you told him?” I said: “No.” He said: “Tell your brother.” So I went to him, greeted him, took hold of his shoulder, and said: “By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.” He said: “And I love you for the sake of Allah.” And I said: “Were it not that the Prophet ﷺ commanded me to tell you, I would not have done so.”"],[13299,"Make haste to observe the witr prayer before morning. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1436)"],[13300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a horse race, and he raced the jadhāʿ (young horses) to the goal."],[13301,"We used to withhold (judgment) regarding the killer (whether he would be forgiven) until the verse was revealed: “Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills.”"],[13302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mudabbar (a slave freed upon the owner’s death) is (counted) from the third (of the estate).”"],[13303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Tayammum is two strikes; one strike on the face and one strike on the hands up to the elbows.\""],[13304,"\"We ate a lizard in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found it repulsive. And we refrain from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finds repulsive.\""],[13305,"While the Prophet ﷺ was at al-ʿAqiq, it was said to him: “You are in the blessed valley,” or “in a blessed sandy plain.”"],[13306,"My maternal uncle ʿUthman b. Mazʿun sent me to bring him a blanket. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission while he was at the trench. He gave me permission and said to me, 'Whoever you meet, tell them that the Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to return.' That was during severe cold. I went out and met the people and said to them, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to return.' He said: 'By God, no two or even one of them turned back for me.'"],[13307,"Ibn ʿUmar was asked, 'Where did the Messenger of God ﷺ pray on the Day of the Confederates?' He said, 'He prayed in the heart of the mountain pass, near a ruin there. And the Messenger of God ﷺ granted permission for the people to leave, then he ordered me to call them, so I called them.'"],[13308,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey and passed over high ground or an elevated spot, he would say the takbir three times, then say: 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things.' Then he would say: 'Returning, repenting, worshiping, prostrating, praising our Lord. God has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and alone defeated the confederates.'"],[13309,"A raiding party seized food and honey as spoils during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the fifth was not taken from them."],[13310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Let one of you pray in his own mosque, and not chase after the mosques.'"],[13311,"Ibn Umar reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The most beloved names to Allah are Abdullah (servant of Allah) and Abdur Rahman (servant of the Most Merciful).\""],[13312,"A woman has no sacredness except in her face."],[13313,"The Prophet ﷺ designated al-Rabadhah as a protected reserve for the owners of the charity camels."],[13314,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about performing ablution after a full-body bath, and he said: 'What ablution is more comprehensive than the full-body bath?'"],[13315,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution after eating what fire has changed.'"],[13316,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call.' He asserted that Bilal used to give the call, and when Bilal came down, Ibn Umm Maktum would give the call."],[13317,"The Prophet ﷺ recited in the Maghrib prayer: 'Those who disbelieved and obstructed from the way of God.'"],[13318,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out from the mosque to al-Safa by the gate of Banu Makhzum."],[13319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to the cemetery walking and return walking, as did Abu Bakr and Umar."],[13320,"Abu Bakr As-Siddiq received something from Umar, then he said, \"Seek forgiveness for me, O my brother.\" This made Umar angry, and he said the same thing to him repeatedly, which made Umar even angrier. Abu Bakr mentioned this incident to the Prophet ﷺ, and they went to him and sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your brother asks you to seek forgiveness for him, so do not do so.\" Abu Bakr swore, \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a Prophet, every time he asks me I seek forgiveness for him.\" Then he said, \"There is no creation of Allah after you who is dearer to me than him.\" Abu Bakr said, \"And by the One who sent you with the truth, there is no one after you dearer to me than him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not hurt me with regard to my companion. Verily, Allah has sent me with guidance and the true religion. You said, 'You have lied,' and Abu Bakr said, 'You have spoken the truth.' If Allah had not named him my companion, I would not have taken him as a close friend. But the brotherhood of Allah is sufficient. So calm down, every fruit has gone bad except the fruit of the son of Abu Quhafa.\""],[13321,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bidding farewell to someone who was departing, then Abdullah said: \"I entrust to Allah your trust, your religion, and the conclusion of your deeds.\""],[13322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The right of pre-emption applies only where boundaries have not been set; once boundaries have been set, there is no pre-emption.\""],[13323,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received the leaders, he said, \"A person does not find anything within himself except that I take it as a sign from Gabriel, ﷺ .\""],[13324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.\""],[13325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ specified the miqat for their own people and for those who come upon them from among those who intend Hajj and Umrah: for the people of Madinah, Dhu al-Hulayfah; for the people of Sham, al-Juhfah; and for the people of Najd, Qarn."],[13326,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Were it not that I would impose difficulty on my community, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer.\""],[13327,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, bless my community in its early morning.\""],[13328,"During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to say: 'Who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter [the caliphate]?' We would say: 'Abu Bakr.' Then we would say: 'What do you think, if Abu Bakr dies, who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter?' We would say: 'Umar b. al-Khattab.' Then we would say: 'What do you think, if Umar b. al-Khattab dies, who will be the most entitled of the people to this matter?' We would say: 'Uthman.'"],[13329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while on the pulpit: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform ghusl.\""],[13330,"Whoever performs Hajj should make the last of his rites at the House, except for menstruating women, for whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession."],[13331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"In the prayer of fear, the imam stands with a group of people with him, and they prostrate one prostration while another group stands between them and the enemy. Then those who prostrated with their leader withdraw and take the place of those who have not prayed, and those who have not prayed come forward and pray with their leader one prostration. Then their leader departs, having completed his prayer, and each of the two groups prays one prostration for itself. If the fear is more severe than that, then on foot or mounted—and by 'prostration' he meant one rak'ah.\""],[13332,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Maghrib prayer: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, the One.'"],[13333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the Friday sermon twice, with a sitting between them."],[13334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the zakat al-fitr for every Muslim, free or slave, young or old: a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley."],[13335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, Allah will grasp the heavens with His right hand and the earths with His other hand'—I think he said: the other—'then He will say: I am the King.'"],[13336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had himself cupped while fasting and gave the cupper his wage. Had it been forbidden, he would not have given it."],[13337,"The Prophet ﷺ acquired a ring and wore it on his right hand."],[13338,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Allah, give us water.'"],[13339,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he saw no harm in women wearing silk brocade and silk."],[13340,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.'"],[13341,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed facing a camel."],[13342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to let his turban hang between his shoulder blades."],[13343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and wishes to break his fast, he may break it, unless his fast is that of Ramadan, making up Ramadan, or a vow.'"],[13344,"The Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ with a man and a woman from among them who had committed adultery. He said to them, \"How do you deal with someone who has committed adultery among you?\" They replied, \"We strike them.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what do you find in the Torah?\" They said, \"We do not find anything in it regarding this matter.\" Abdullah ibn Salam said to them, \"You have lied; in the Torah, there is stoning. Bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful.\" So the Torah was brought, and the part that he had studied from them was placed on his hand while he covered the verse about stoning. He then asked, \"What is this?\" When they saw that, they said, \"It is stoning.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they be stoned where the graves were. Abdullah said, \"I saw her companion leaning over her to protect her from the stones.\""],[13345,"That unripe dates and fresh dates be steeped together, and dried dates and raisins together."],[13346,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited prayer at sunrise and at sunset."],[13347,"The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed [the spoils of] the Trench except to six individuals: four from the Muhajirun—Talhah, al-Zubayr, Ali, and Sa'd—and from the Ansar, Abu Dujanah and al-Harith b. al-Simmah."],[13348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful.\""],[13349,"The Messenger of God ﷺ shaved his head during the Farewell Pilgrimage."],[13350,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Many a fasting person obtains nothing from his fasting but hunger and thirst, and many a person standing in prayer obtains nothing from his standing but sleeplessness.\""],[13351,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"It is enough sin for a man to neglect those whom he is responsible to feed.\""],[13352,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah and prostrate on it."],[13353,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a slain woman during one of his military expeditions and prohibited the killing of women and children."],[13354,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited a man from approaching two men who are conversing privately unless he seeks their permission."],[13355,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You must wear turbans, for they are the mark of the angels; and let them hang down behind your backs.\""],[13356,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever comes to the Friday prayer should perform the ritual bath.\""],[13357,"He intended to enter the state of consecration, came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, and spent the night there. When morning came, he mounted his riding camel, and when it stood upright with him, he pronounced the talbiyah. He asserted that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do that."],[13358,"About the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[13359,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, bless us in our Sham. O Allah, bless us in our Yemen.” He said it several times. When it was the third or fourth time, they said: “O Messenger of Allah, and in our Iraq?” He said: “Therein are earthquakes and trials, and from there the horn of Satan will rise.”"],[13360,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs except a hunting dog or a livestock dog.”"],[13361,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he observed iʿtikaf, his bed and his cot would be placed for him at the pillar of repentance on the side facing the qiblah, then he would lean against it."],[13362,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Allah has chosen ones among His creation whom He keeps alive in well-being, and when He takes their souls, He takes them to His Paradise. Those are the ones upon whom trials pass like patches of dark night while they remain in well-being from it.”"],[13363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a military expedition toward Najd, and ʿAbd Allah was in it. We captured many camels, and our shares reached twelve camels each, and the Messenger of Allah gave us an extra camel each as booty."],[13364,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ begin the talbiyah when his riding camel stood upright with him.”"],[13365,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over an adulteress who died during her postpartum bleeding along with her child.”"],[13366,"“A woman divorced three times is not lawful for her first husband until she marries another husband, he has intercourse with her, and she tastes his sweetness.”"],[13367,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar used to perform ablution washing each part three times, tracing that back to the Prophet ﷺ."],[13368,"\"The Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger, this refers to the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger ﷺ .\""],[13372,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great, ten good deeds are written for him for every letter. Whoever aids in a false dispute remains in Allah's displeasure until he withdraws. Whoever intercedes to prevent one of Allah's prescribed punishments has opposed Allah in His command. Whoever falsely accuses a believing man or woman, Allah will confine him in the mud of pus on the Day of Resurrection until he comes out of what he said, and he will not come out.'"],[13373,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'All flies are in the Fire except the bee.' And he used to forbid killing them and burning food. Sufyan said: 'It seems that burning food was in the land of the enemy.'"],[13374,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on the pulpit saying: 'The Compeller will take His heavens and His earths in His hand.' And he clenched his hand and began clenching and opening them, then he said: 'I am the Compeller. Where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned to his right and to his left until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lowest part, so much so that I said: 'Is it going to fall with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?'"],[13375,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'Wiping the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner removes sins completely.'"],[13376,"I said to Ibn 'Umar: 'I see you jostling at these two corners.' He said: 'If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Wiping them removes sins.\"'"],[13378,"\"And I heard him saying, 'Whoever drinks alcohol, his prayer will not be accepted by Allah for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But if he returns to it, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But if he returns to it again, his prayer will not be accepted. And it was the right of Allah to make him drink from the river of impurities.' We said, 'O Abu Abdullah, what is the river of impurities?' He said, 'It is the pus of the people of Hell.'\""],[13379,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There are three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the one who reminds others of his gifts, the one who drags his lower garment out of pride, and the one addicted to wine.' It was said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what is the one addicted to wine?' He said: 'Persisting in it.'"],[13380,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I joke but I speak only truth'? He said: 'Yes.'"],[13381,"And he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ jostling at it, and I heard him say: 'He does not put down a foot nor raise it except that a good deed is written for him for it.'"],[13382,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever drinks alcohol, his prayers will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. He said it three times. If he repeats the sin, it is upon Allah to make him drink from the river of filth.\" It was asked, \"What is the river of filth?\" He said, \"It is the pus of the people of Hell.\""],[13383,"A man said to Ibn Umar, \"O Abu Abdul-Rahman, why do I see you touching the two corners and not leaving them?\" Ibn Umar used to do that. He replied, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Indeed, touching them removes sins.'\""],[13385,"And I heard him say, \"Whoever drinks alcohol in this world, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he returns [to drinking], his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he returns [again], his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. If he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. If he drinks it for the fourth time, it is the right of Allah to make him drink from the mud of Khabeel.\" It was asked, \"What is the mud of Khabeel?\" He said, \"The pus of the people of Hell.\""],[13386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The measure is the measure of the people of Madinah, and the weight is the weight of the people of Makkah.'"],[13387,"About nabidh made in earthenware jars, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh in earthenware jars.' And Sulayman b. Harb said in his narration: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited.'"],[13388,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh in earthenware jars? He said: 'Yes.'"],[13389,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid nabidh in earthenware jars? He said: 'Yes. Tawus swore to us by Allah that he heard it from Ibn 'Umar.'"],[13390,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ forbade hunting with dogs and predatory animals.\""],[13391,"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid soaking (nabidh) in earthenware jars and gourds? He said: Yes."],[13392,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthenware jars."],[13393,"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So Umar went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the news. He commanded him to take her back. He said: I did not hear him add anything to that."],[13394,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have made them fond of Ammar; he calls them to Paradise while they call him to the Fire.\""],[13395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Part of the honor of a believer before Allah is the cleanliness of his garment and his contentment with little.\""],[13396,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a horse race, sending them from al-Hayfa' and its course ended at Thaniyyat al-Wada'. He also raced horses that had not been trained, and their course was from the thaniyya to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."],[13397,"I heard Ibn Umar say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from departing until his last visit is to the House, except menstruating women; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave them a concession to depart.\""],[13398,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The night prayer is in pairs, and when you fear dawn, then one (rak'ah).\""],[13399,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"It is not lawful for a man to give a gift or grant and then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The likeness of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is that of a dog that eats until it is full, and then vomits and returns to its vomit.\""],[13400,"Fruit is not to be sold until its ripeness is apparent."],[13401,"Regarding the jallalah (animal that eats filth)."],[13402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, respond to him; and whoever does you a favor, repay him. If you do not find anything with which to repay him, then supplicate for him until he sees that you have repaid him.\""],[13404,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Flies are in the Fire, and he forbade killing bees and that food be burned in the land of the enemy.”"],[13405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “All flies are in the Fire except bees.”"],[13406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The mu’adhdhin is forgiven as far as his voice reaches, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him.”"],[13407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of my shoulders and said: “Be in this world as a stranger or a passer-by.”"],[13408,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Permit women to go to the mosque at night.” His son said: “By Allah, we will not permit them, lest they take that as a means of deceit.” He said: “May Allah do such-and-such to you! You hear me say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and you say no?” Layth said in his hadith: “And they would go out unperfumed.”"],[13409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not prevent women from the mosques at night.” His son said: “By Allah, we will prevent them.” So he stretched out his hand and slapped him, and said: “I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you say what you say!”"],[13410,"“The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not witness any of your pastimes except racing and archery.”"],[13412,"“O Messenger of Allah, if only we were to take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.” Then it was revealed: {And take the Station of Ibrahim as a place of prayer}."],[13413,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take from this and leave this,” meaning he takes from the hair below his lower lip and leaves his beard."],[13414,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed effeminate men and masculine women.”"],[13415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever disowns his child in order to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of witnesses, retaliation for retaliation.”"],[13416,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about throwing the pebbles (ramy al-jimār), what is in it for him? I heard him say: “You will find that with your Lord when you are most in need of it.”"],[13417,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; whoever invites you, respond to him; and whoever gives you a gift of a sheep’s trotter, accept it.”"],[13418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the ʿishāʾ prayer until the one praying had prayed, the one waking had awakened, the sleepers had slept, and those who perform tahajjud had performed it. Then he came out and said: “Were it not that I would burden my community, I would have ordered them to pray at this time—or this prayer,” or something similar."],[13419,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The people of the Fire will be made huge in the Fire until the distance between the lobe of one of their ears and his shoulder becomes a journey of seven hundred years, the thickness of the skin of one of them becomes forty cubits, and his molar tooth becomes greater than Mount Uhud.” Their wording is one."],[13420,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand for the funeral of a Jew that passed by him."],[13421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to follow a funeral that has a wailing woman with it."],[13422,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mutilation."],[13423,"It is an innovation. Come out with us, for this is an innovation."],[13424,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions arrived as pilgrims. He said: “O people, enter iḥrām for ʿumrah, except those who have a sacrificial animal with them, for the ʿumrah has entered into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13425,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"],[13426,"We and he: when we met him we said to him what you like, and when we left him we said something else. He said: “That is what we used to consider hypocrisy while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[13427,"We crush unripe dates, then add ripe dates to it, then leave it and drink it. He said: “That is faḍūkh, and wine was forbidden while the majority of their drink was what you mention.”"],[13428,"That is al-faḍūkh. Wine was forbidden while it was our drink."],[13429,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ : \"Whoever drinks alcohol and lets it enter his stomach, his prayers will not be accepted from him for seven days. And if he dies while in that state, he dies as disbeliever. And if his mind is distracted from fulfilling any of the obligatory duties, his prayers will not be accepted from him for forty days. And if he dies during that time, he dies as disbeliever.\""],[13430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: He is Allah, the One (Q 112) equals one third of the Qur'an, and Say: O disbelievers (Q 109) equals one quarter of the Qur'an.” He used to recite them in the two rakʿahs of Fajr, and he said: “These two rakʿahs are what time has desired.”"],[13431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you are those with the softest shoulders in prayer.”"],[13432,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and shook his hand. He did not withdraw his hand from the man’s hand until the man withdrew his own hand. Then the man said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, what about ʿUthman?” He said: “That is a man from the people of Paradise.”"],[13433,"My grandmother ʿAʾishah bt. Yunus, the wife of al-Layth, narrated to me from Layth b. Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me during my lifetime.”"],[13434,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever performs Hajj and visits my grave after my death is like one who visited me during my lifetime.”"],[13435,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to follow a funeral procession in which there is a wailing woman.”"],[13436,"“that we pray in an elevated mosque.”"],[13437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O son of Adam, guarantee me two rakʿahs at the beginning of the day and I will suffice you for the rest of it.”"],[13438,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever drags his lower garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13439,"And I heard him say: “Do not abandon the two rakʿahs before the Fajr prayer, for in them are the ragāʾib (desirable rewards).”"],[13440,"And I heard him say: “Never disown your child, lest Allah disgrace you before all creation as you disgraced him in this world.”"],[13441,"And I heard him say: \"Do not die while you have a debt upon you, for there are only good deeds and bad deeds; there is no dinar or dirham there, as recompense and settlement, and He does not wrong anyone.\""],[13442,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"None of you should prevent his family from coming to the mosque.\""],[13443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the Day of the Conquest the meat of jallālah camels and their milk."],[13444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is not befitting for a believer to humiliate himself.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how does he humiliate himself?\" He said, \"By exposing himself to trials that he cannot bear.\""],[13445,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one hadith. He said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"Indeed among trees there is a tree whose likeness is that of the Muslim man.\" I wanted to say it is the date palm, but I looked and found that I was the youngest of the people, so I remained silent."],[13446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his wives to perform tamattuʿ and commanded them to depart."],[13447,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the House, and with him was al-Faḍl, and Bilāl stood at the door."],[13448,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Banū ʿAbd Manāf, let me not find you preventing anyone from circumambulating this House at any hour of the night or day.\""],[13449,"Ibn ʿUmar said: \"I have been given from it something that I do not think anyone has been given except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — meaning sexual intercourse.\""],[13450,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Among trees there is indeed a tree like the believing man.\" I wanted to say it is the date palm, but I looked at the faces of the people and found that I was the youngest of them in age, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm.\""],[13451,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The likeness of the believer is that of the date palm: whatever you take from it benefits you.\""],[13452,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ while he was eating the heart of a palm tree."],[13453,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he sneezed and praised Allah. They said, 'May Allah have mercy on you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'May Allah guide you and set your affairs aright.'"],[13454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Tell me about a tree whose example is like that of a believer.\" So, people started mentioning a tree from the trees of the valleys, and I thought to myself that it is the date palm tree. I wanted to say it, but then saw the people's teeth, so I hesitated, fearing that they may detest it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the date palm tree.\""],[13455,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam is built upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakat, fasting Ramadan, and the Hajj to the House, and the Hajj to this House—twice.'"],[13456,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ while the sun was on Quʿayqiʿan after the afternoon prayer. He said, 'Your lifespans compared to the lifespans of those who have passed are only like what remains of this day compared to what has passed of it.'"],[13457,"On the authority of the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"The example of a believer is like that of a palm tree.\""],[13458,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was eating heart of palm along with the people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Among the trees there is a tree like the Muslim man.' The people fell silent until I was about to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, as I was the youngest of the people. Then he said, 'It is the date palm.'"],[13459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I have been given five things that no prophet before me was given. I was sent to all people, the red and the black, whereas each prophet was sent only to his own people. I was aided with fear—my enemy is struck with terror at a distance of a month's journey. I was granted the spoils of war. The earth was made a mosque and a means of purification for me. And I was granted intercession, which I have reserved for my community.'"],[13460,"The Messenger of Allah performed Umrah four times, one of them in the month of Rajab."],[13461,"The forenoon (Duha) prayer is an innovation."],[13462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In the mosque of al-Khaif lies the grave of seventy prophets.\""],[13463,"I was sitting with Abdullah bin Umar, along with Urwah bin Zubair. Urwah asked him in which month did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Umrah? He replied, \"He used to perform Umrah in the month of Rajab.\""],[13464,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than twenty-five times—or he said, more than twenty times—recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[13465,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ reciting in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: 'Say: O disbelievers' and 'Say: He is Allah, [who is] One.'"],[13466,"He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ʿumrah twice before performing Hajj.' News of that reached ʿAʾishah, and she said: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ performed four ʿumrahs. ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar knew that; one of them was combined with his Hajj.'"],[13467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever asks you in the name of Allah, give to him, and whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him protection, and whoever presents you with a leadership, accept it.\""],[13468,"He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined us to be good to the neighbor, until we thought he would make him an heir.'"],[13469,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a gathering seeking Allah's forgiveness one hundred times, saying: 'My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, and accept my repentance; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.'"],[13470,"He was asked: 'What do you say about ʿAli ؓ?' He replied: 'He is that one—his house.' Then he was asked: 'What do you say about ʿUthman?' He said: 'What can I say about a man who sinned in a matter between him and his Lord, and He forgave him; and sinned in a matter between you and him, and you killed him?'"],[13471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking the necks of one another.”"],[13472,"He relied on Aisha's room and was asked in which month did the Prophet ﷺ perform Umrah? He said, \"In the month of Rajab.\""],[13473,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ as the tenth of ten. A man from the Ansar came and said, “O Prophet of Allah, who is the most astute of people and the most resolute of people?” He said, “The one among them who remembers death most, and the one who prepares for death most intensely before death descends. Those are the astute ones; they have gone with the honor of this world and the Hereafter.”"],[13475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of part of my body and said, “O Ibn Umar, be in this world like a stranger or a wayfarer, and count yourself among the occupants of the graves.”"],[13476,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever gives you a gift, accept it.”"],[13477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever asks by Allah, give him; whoever seeks refuge by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever gives you a gift of a foreleg or a shank, accept it.”"],[13478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The likeness of a believer is like that of a perfume seller: if you sit with him, he benefits you; if you walk with him, he benefits you; and if you partner with him, he benefits you.”"],[13479,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.”"],[13480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “All flies are in the Fire except the bee.” He used to forbid killing them and burning food."],[13481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Flies are in the Fire except the bee.” And they used to dislike killing it and burning food."],[13483,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us to intercept trade goods on the roads and forbade a resident to sell on behalf of a Bedouin."],[13484,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A resident must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin, nor buy for him.”"],[13485,"It was said to him: “When we enter upon the rulers, we say to them what we do not say when we leave them.” He said: “We used to consider that hypocrisy in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[13486,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ in some shade in Madinah, and he was looking for ʿAli ؓ, we came to a wall and looked into it. He saw ʿAli lying on the ground, covered in dust, and said: “I do not blame people for calling you Abu Turab.” I saw ʿAli’s face change and he was distressed by that. Then he said: “Shall I not please you, O ʿAli?” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said: “You are my brother and my minister. You will settle my debts, fulfill my promises, and discharge my obligations. Whoever loves you during my lifetime has fulfilled his vow. Whoever loves you during a lifetime from you after me, God will seal for him with security and faith. Whoever loves you after me but did not see you, God will seal for him with security and faith and grant him safety on the day of the greatest terror. And whoever dies hating you, O ʿAli, dies a death of the Jahiliyyah; God will call him to account for what he did in Islam.”"],[13487,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The first for whom I shall intercede on the Day of Resurrection are the people of my household, then the nearest of Quraysh, then the Ansar, then those who believed in me and followed me from Yemen, then the rest of the Arabs, then the non-Arabs. And the first for whom I shall intercede are the people of virtue.”"],[13488,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever dies in the morning, let him not take a midday nap except in his grave; and whoever dies in the evening, let him not spend the night except in his grave.”"],[13489,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade letting the lower garment hang below the ankles."],[13490,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God did not open upon ʿAd any of the wind with which they were destroyed except an amount like the place of a ring. It passed by the desert dwellers and carried off their livestock and their wealth, lifting them between the sky and the earth. When the settled people saw the wind and what was in it, they said: ‘This is a cloud bringing us rain.’ Then it cast the desert dwellers and their livestock upon the settled people.”"],[13491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The muʾadhdhin who seeks God’s reward is like a martyr writhing in his blood until he finishes his call to prayer, and every moist and dry thing bears witness for him. And when he dies, worms do not consume him in his grave.”"],[13492,"The Throne shook out of love for meeting God with Saʿd, and he was the last to come out of his grave. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Saʿd was squeezed in his grave, so I asked God to lighten it for him.”"],[13493,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The warrior in the path of Allah and the pilgrim to the House of Allah are the delegation of Allah: He called them and they answered Him.”"],[13494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, your Lord is Modest and Generous. He is too Modest to let His servant raise his hands in supplication and then return them empty. So when one of you raises his hands, let him say, 'O Ever-Living, there is no god but You, O Most Merciful of the merciful,' three times. Then, when he lowers his hands, let him pour out that goodness upon his face.\""],[13495,"“Emigration ceased after the conquest.”"],[13496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever parts with ʿAli has parted with me, and whoever parts with me has parted with Allah.”"],[13497,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The giver from abundance is not more virtuous than the taker when he is in need.”"],[13498,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him pay the zakat of his wealth. Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him say what is good or remain silent. Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, let him honor his guest.”"],[13499,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says: ‘Praise be to Allah, before Whose greatness all things humble themselves; praise be to Allah, before Whose might all things abase themselves; praise be to Allah, before Whose dominion all things submit; praise be to Allah, before Whose power all things surrender,’ and says it seeking nothing of what He has, Allah will record for him a thousand good deeds, raise him a thousand degrees by it, and entrust to him seventy thousand angels who seek forgiveness for him until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[13500,"“The Duha prayer is an innovation, and what an excellent innovation it is.”"],[13501,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr: “Say: O disbelievers” and “Say: He is Allah, the One.”"],[13502,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques of Allah.”"],[13503,"Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ, one of them from the Ansar and the other from Thaqif. The Ansari preceded him, so the Prophet ﷺ said to the Thaqafi: “O brother of Thaqif, the Ansari has preceded you.” The Ansari said: “I will start with him, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said to him: “O brother of Thaqif, ask about your need, and if you wish, I will tell you what you have come to ask about.” He said: “That would be more pleasing to me for you to do.” He said: “You ask me about your prayer, your bowing, your prostration, and your fasting, and you say: What is in it for me?” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth.” He said: “Pray the first part of the night and its last part, and sleep in its middle.” He said: “What if I pray in its middle?” He said: “You then…” He said: “When you stand for prayer and bow, place your hands on your knees, spread your fingers, then raise your head until every limb returns to its joint. When you prostrate, place your forehead firmly on the ground and do not peck. Fast the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth.” Then he turned to the Ansari and said: “Ask about your need, and if you wish, I will tell you.” He said: “That would be more pleasing to me.” He said: “You have come to ask me about your leaving your house heading for the Sacred House, and you say: What is in it for me? You have come to ask about your standing at ʿArafah, and you say: What is in it for me? About your throwing the pebbles, and you say: What is in it for me? About your circumambulation of the House, and you say: What is in it for me? About your shaving your head, and you say: What is in it for me?” He said: “Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth.” He said: “As for your leaving your house heading for the House, for every step your mount takes, Allah records a good deed for you and wipes away a sin from you. As for your standing at ʿArafah, Allah ﷻ descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of them to the angels, saying: ‘These are My servants who have come to Me disheveled and dusty from every deep ravine, hoping for My mercy and fearing My punishment, though they have not seen Me. How would it be if they had seen Me? If you had sins like the sand of ʿAlij, or like the days of the world, or like the drops of rain, Allah would wash them away from you.’ As for your throwing the pebbles, it is stored up for you. As for your shaving your head, for every hair that falls you have a good deed. When you circumambulate the House, you come out of your sins as on the day your mother gave birth to you.”"],[13504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The storyteller awaits wrath, the listener awaits mercy, the merchant awaits provision, the hoarder awaits curse, and the wailing woman and those around her of women—upon them is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.”"],[13505,"The Prophet ﷺ came out and spread his right palm and said: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, with the names of the people of Paradise, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans. No one is added to them or subtracted from them.” Then he spread his left palm and said: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a book from Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, for the people of the Fire, with their names, the names of their fathers, their tribes, and their clans. No one is added to them or subtracted from them.”"],[13506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to touch the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone, and he did not touch anything besides them."],[13507,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Permit women to go to the mosques at night.\""],[13508,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When something is entrusted to Allah, He protects it. I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the final deeds of your actions.\""],[13509,"The Prophet ﷺ secluded himself and addressed the people, saying, \"Indeed, when one of you stands in prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let each of you know what he is conversing with his Lord about, and let not one of you pronounce his recitation in prayer loudly over another.\""],[13510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you is praying, he should not let anyone pass in front of him. If the person refuses, he should fight him, for with him is a qarin (companion).\""],[13511,"He saw the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, mounting his riding animal."],[13512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fixed the miqat for the people of Madinah at Dhul-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham at al-Juhfah, for the people of Najd at Qarn, and for the people of Yemen at Yalamlam."],[13513,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"To proceed (amma baʿd).\""],[13514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever comes to Friday prayer should perform ghusl.\""],[13515,"I said to Ibn Umar: \"Did you witness the Pledge of Ridwan with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"What was he wearing?\" He said: \"A cotton shirt, a padded jubba, a cloak, and a sword. And I saw al-Nuʿman b. Muqarrin al-Muzani standing by his head, holding up the branches of the tree away from his head while the people were pledging allegiance to him.\""],[13516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered ihram when his mount stood upright with him."],[13517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not revile the face, for the son of Adam was created in the image of the Most Merciful, Exalted is He.\""],[13518,"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, indeed we are traveling and we meet people who say there is no predestination. So, if you meet them, inform them that Ibn Umar is innocent from them. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him, handsome in appearance, with a pleasant fragrance and clean clothes. He greeted the Prophet ﷺ and asked, \"Can I come close to you?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Approach.\" So, he came closer until his knees touched the knees of the Prophet ﷺ . Then he asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? \"The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It is to testify that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to perform Hajj pilgrimage to the House of Allah, fasting in the month of Ramadan, and to perform ablution from impurity.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a Muslim?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" The man asked again, \"Tell me about faith (Iman).\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Day of Judgment, and destiny, both its good and bad aspects.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a believer?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" The man then asked, \"Tell me about excellence (Ihsan).\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"To worship Allah as if you see Him, and if you do not see Him, then know that He sees you.\" The man asked, \"If I do that, am I a person of excellence?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" We said, \"We have never seen anyone more virtuous in appearance, with a better fragrance, and showing more respect to the Prophet ﷺ than this man. When the man left, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"Do you know who this man was?\" We replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This was Gabriel ﷺ . He came to teach you your religion.\""],[13519,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey when a Bedouin approached. When he drew near, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Where do you intend to go?\" He said: \"To my family.\" He said: \"Would you like something good?\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"That you bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" He said: \"Who will testify to what you say?\" He said: \"This tree.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came, plowing through the ground, until it stood before him. He asked it to testify three times, and it testified that he was as he said. Then it returned to its place of growth, and the Bedouin went back to his people and said: \"If they follow me, I will bring them to you; otherwise I will return to you and stay with you.\""],[13520,"A time came upon us when none of us thought that he was more entitled to the dinar and the dirham than his Muslim brother. Yet I am in a time when the dinar and the dirham are dearer to us than our Muslim brother. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When people are stingy with the dinar and the dirham, abandon jihad in the path of Allah, cling to the tails of cattle, and engage in ʿinah transactions, Allah will impose upon them a trial that He will not lift until they return.\""],[13521,"If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not once, not twice, not three times” — he counted seven times — “I would not have narrated it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Three will be on mounds of musk on the Day of Resurrection: grief will not terrify them, nor will they be frightened when people are frightened: a man who learned the Qur’an and stood with it, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and what is with Him; a man who called out every day and night five prayers, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and what is with Him; and a slave whom the bondage of this world did not prevent from obeying his Lord."],[13522,"A time came upon us when none of us thought he was more entitled to the dinar and the dirham than his Muslim brother. Then, when we reached the latter part of it, we awoke and the dinar and the dirham became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When people become miserly with the dinar and the dirham, deal in ʿīnah, and follow the tails of cattle, Allah will send upon them humiliation that He will not lift from them until they return to their religion.”"],[13523,"\"Regarding the sale of booty until it is divided.\""],[13524,"\"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ praying twenty-five times, and he used to recite in the two units of prayer before Fajr and the two units of prayer before Maghrib, 'Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun' and 'Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad'.\""],[13525,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah has cursed whoever reviles my Companions.”"],[13526,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you see those who praise people to their faces, throw dust in their faces.”"],[13527,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he looked for Bilal to give the call to prayer for them, but he was not found. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a man, and he gave the call to prayer in place of Bilal. After that, he wanted to give the iqamah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Only the one who gave the call to prayer gives the iqamah.”"],[13528,"Two festivals coincided during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: the day of Fitr and a Friday. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the Eid prayer, then turned to face them and said: “O people, you have attained good and reward. We shall hold the Friday prayer, so whoever wishes to attend the Friday prayer with us let him attend, and whoever wishes to return to his family let him return.”"],[13529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would make things difficult for my ummah, I would command them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"],[13530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not sit for any part of the night except that he passed the siwak over his mouth."],[13531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The least of my ummah are those who reach seventy.”"],[13532,"A man from Ethiopia came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Ask and inquire.\" The man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have been favored over us with appearance, colors, and prophethood. Have you considered that if I believed in what you believe in and did what you did, would I be with you in Paradise?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"You have been favored over us with appearance, colors, and prophethood. Have you considered that if I believed in what you believe in and knew what you knew, would I be with you in Paradise?\" The man said, \"Yes.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the whiteness of blackness in Paradise can be seen from a distance of a thousand years' travel.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever says 'There is no deity but Allah' will have a covenant with Allah. And whoever says, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,' one hundred thousand good deeds will be written for him, and four and twenty thousand good deeds more.\" A man asked, \"How can one be destroyed after this, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, a man will come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds as great as a mountain, but Allah will render them insignificant as dust. The blessings from the blessings of Allah will almost expire, except by the grace of Allah.\" This Surah was revealed, \"Has there not come upon man a period of time when he was not a thing mentioned?\" until His saying, \"And a great kingdom.\" Al-Habashi said, \"Indeed, my two eyes have seen what your two eyes cannot see in Paradise.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" Then he wept until his soul passed away. Ibn 'Umar said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placing him in his grave with his own hand.\""],[13533,"The Prophet ﷺ performed Umrah in the month of Rajab."],[13534,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever says, ‘Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,’ one hundred and twenty-four thousand good deeds are written for him. And whoever says, ‘There is no god but Allah,’ he will have a covenant with Allah on the Day of Resurrection by it.”"],[13535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not wake up from any part of the night except that he passed the siwak over his mouth."],[13536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Mention the good qualities of your dead and refrain from their faults.”"],[13537,"The Messenger of God ﷺ once led us in prayer. When he raised his head from the bowing, he said, “God hears the one who praises Him.” A man behind him said, “Our Lord, to You belongs abundant, good, blessed praise.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished, he said three times, “Who was the speaker just now?” The man said, “I, O Messenger of God.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw more than thirty angels rushing to it, each of them striving to be the first to write it down.”"],[13538,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw in a dream as if there were two bracelets of gold on his forearms, and he blew on them and they flew away. He said, “They are the two liars of my community: the one of Yemen and the one of Yamamah. They will not harm my community in anything.”"],[13539,"I went early in the afternoon to the Prophet ﷺ. Abu al-Hasan came, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Come close to me, O Abu al-Hasan.” He kept drawing him near until he took his ear between his lips. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ leaned to his left until the Messenger of God ﷺ raised his head like one startled, and said, “The wicked one knocked on his hearing at the door.” He said, “Go, O Abu al-Hasan, and lead him as a sheep is led to its milker.” Then there was ʿAli, who had brought al-Hakam, taking hold of both his ear and his cheek, until he made him stand before the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet of God ﷺ cursed him three times. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ said to ʿAli, “Sit aside.” Then some people from the Emigrants and the Helpers came to the Prophet of God ﷺ, and then the Prophet of God ﷺ called for him and said, “Indeed, this one will oppose the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ, and from his loins will emerge trials whose smoke reaches the sky.” A man among the Muslims said, “God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He is too insignificant and contemptible for that to come from him.” He said, “Yes, and some of you will be his partisans on that day.”"],[13540,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims, God will not look into his need until he looks into their needs.”"],[13541,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was gesturing with his palm like this, as if measuring something: “Whoever separates from the community of the Muslims by a handspan has removed the noose of Islam from his neck. And the dissidents will have their banners, which they will be reaching for from behind their backs on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever dies without an imam of the community dies a death of ignorance.”"],[13542,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ say: “Do not revile your dead, for reviling them is not lawful.”"],[13543,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say when he visited Abu Salamah while he was ill, and he heard the words of Umm Salamah while she was weeping. The Prophet of God refrained from entering when he heard her weeping over him with the Book of God, saying: “And the throes of death will come with the truth; that is what you used to turn away from.” Then he entered, greeted, and said, “May God compensate you, O Umm Salamah.” When he went out with Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr said to him, “I saw you, O Messenger of God, disliking to enter because they are wailing.” He said, “I do not enter a house in which there is wailing or a black dog.”"],[13544,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ: he came to a cloth merchant and bought a shirt from him for four dirhams. He went out wearing it, and there was a man from the Helpers who said, “O Messenger of God ﷺ, clothe me with a shirt; may God clothe you from the garments of Paradise.” So he took off the shirt and clothed him with it. Then he returned to the shopkeeper and bought a shirt from him for four dirhams, and two dirhams remained with him. Then he came upon a girl in the road weeping, and he said, “What makes you weep?” She said, “O Messenger of God, my family gave me two dirhams to buy flour with them, and I lost them.” The Prophet ﷺ gave her the remaining two dirhams. Then she turned away weeping, and he called her and said, “What makes you weep, when you have taken the two dirhams?” She said, “I fear they will beat me.” So he walked with her to her family, gave the greeting, and they recognized his voice. Then he returned and gave the greeting, then returned and gave the greeting, then returned a third time, and they responded. He said, “Did you hear the first greeting?” They said, “Yes, but we loved that you increase us in greeting. What has brought you here, may our father and mother be ransom for you?” He said, “This girl feared that you would beat her.” Her master said, “She is free for the sake of God, because of your walking with her.” The Prophet of God ﷺ gave them glad tidings of good and Paradise, then said, “God has indeed blessed the ten dirhams: God clothed His Prophet with a shirt, and a man from the Helpers with a shirt, and God freed a neck through them. I praise God, for it is He who provided us this by His power.”"],[13545,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Who will take this letter of mine to the tyrant of Byzantium?” He presented it to them three times. Then he said, “Who will go and have Paradise?” A man from the Helpers called ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Khaliq said, “I will take it, and I will have Paradise if I perish in that cause?” He said, “Yes, you will have Paradise whether you deliver it, or are killed, or perish. God has made Paradise obligatory for you.” He set out with the letter of the Prophet ﷺ until he reached the tyrant and said, “I am a messenger of the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds.” He was granted permission and entered upon him. The tyrant of Byzantium recognized that he had brought the truth from a sent prophet. Then he presented to him the letter of the Prophet ﷺ. He gathered the Byzantines before him and presented it to them, but they disliked what he brought. One man among them believed in it and was killed upon his belief. Then the man returned to the Prophet ﷺ and told him what had happened with him and the killing of the man. The Prophet ﷺ said at that: “God will raise him as a nation alone,” referring to that slain man."],[13546,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no believing servant who turns to God in repentance before death by a month except that God accepts it from him. And even less than that—before his death by a day or an hour, if God knows repentance and sincerity from him—except that God accepts it from him.”"],[13547,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on the day a man was placed in his grave: two angels came to him and said, “We will strike you with a blow.” He said to them, “For what will you strike me?” They struck him with a blow that filled his grave with fire. Then they left him until he recovered and the terror left him. He said to them, “For what did you strike me?” They said, “You prayed a prayer while not in a state of purity, and you passed by a wronged man and did not help him.”"],[13548,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say on a Friday when he prayed the afternoon prayer with the people while seated in the first two rakʿahs: a dog passed by to cut across his prayer, and Saʿd b. Abi Waqqas feared that it would pass in front of him, so he supplicated against the dog, and God destroyed it by His power. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer and saw that the dog had perished, he said, “Who among you supplicated against this dog?” No one spoke. The Prophet of God ﷺ repeated, and Saʿd said then, “I supplicated against it, O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be ransom for you. I feared that it would cut across your prayer, so I supplicated against it.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “How did you supplicate against it, O Saʿd?” Saʿd said, “Glory be to You, there is no god but You, O Possessor of majesty and honor. Destroy this dog lest it cut across the prayer of Your prophet.” The Prophet of God ﷺ said, “O Saʿd, you have supplicated on a day and in an hour with words that, had you supplicated against all that is between the heavens, it would have been answered for you. Rejoice, O Saʿd.”"],[13550,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When any of you dies, do not hold him back, and hasten with him to his grave, and let the opening of the Book (al-Fātiḥah) be recited at his head and the closing of al-Baqarah at his feet in his grave.”"],[13551,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no prayer for one who enters the mosque while the imam is standing praying; let him not pray alone by himself, but let him join the imam in the prayer.”"],[13552,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Slander, revilement, and fanatical pride are in the Fire, and they will never combine in the breast of a believer.”"],[13553,"“The Messenger of Allah performed ablution three times, three times.”"],[13554,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever fasts perpetually has neither fasted nor broken his fast.”"],[13555,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[13556,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: “No people withhold the zakāh of their wealth except that they are deprived of rain from the sky, and were it not for the beasts, they would not be given rain.”"],[13557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you, for there is no servant who spends the night pure except that an angel spends the night with him in his undergarment; he does not turn over at any hour of the night except that he says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, for he spent the night pure.”"],[13558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Purify these bodies, may Allah purify you. There is no servant who spends the night pure except that an angel spends the night in his undergarment; whenever he turns over at any hour of the night, the angel says: O Allah, forgive Your servant, as he spent the night pure.”"],[13559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Pray over whoever says lā ilāha illā Allāh, and pray behind whoever says lā ilāha illā Allāh.”"],[13560,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My Ummah will never unite upon misguidance. So, hold fast to the [united] group (the majority), for indeed, the Hand of Allah is with the [united] group.\""],[13562,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling the right of patronage (walāʾ) and giving it as a gift.”"],[13563,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling the right of patronage (walāʾ) and giving it as a gift.”"],[13564,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in whatever direction his mount faced."],[13565,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on his mount."],[13566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any two parties to a sale have no sale between them until they separate, except a sale with an option.”"],[13567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah seven times. Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have an excellent example."],[13569,"The Prophet ﷺ came and circumambulated the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah. Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ you have an excellent example."],[13570,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” Then he said: Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have an excellent example."],[13571,"I heard Ibn 'Umar say: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Makkah, he circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, then went out to al-Safa through the gate by which one goes out to it, and went between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” Ghundar added in his narration: Shu'bah said: Ayyub informed me, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, that it is a Sunnah."],[13572,"As for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he came and circumambulated the House, then prayed two rak'ahs, then went between al-Safa and al-Marwah."],[13574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “None of you should make his brother get up from his seat in order to sit in his place.”"],[13575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to relieve himself at al-Maghmas. Nafi' said: “About two miles from Makkah.”"],[13576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs except a livestock dog or a hunting dog."],[13577,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever has a slave jointly owned between him and another, and he frees his share, then it is assessed for him and he frees him.”"],[13578,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the drinker of wine and the one who serves it."],[13579,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade selling fruit until its goodness becomes apparent."],[13580,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah and in it there were three hundred and eighty idols. In his hand was a staff, and he began pointing at them and saying: “Truth has come and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish.” And the idols fell down."],[13581,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade (using) gourds and vessels smeared with pitch."],[13582,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed on us the sadaqah of Ramadan: one sa' of barley or one sa' of dates."],[13583,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the most beloved people to Allah? And what are the most beloved deeds to Allah?\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"The most beloved people to Allah are those who are most beneficial to others, and the most beloved deeds to Allah are bringing happiness to a Muslim or removing a distress from him, settling his debt or relieving his hunger. And I would prefer to walk with my brother in fulfilling his need over staying in itkaf in this Masjid (al-Nabawi) for a month.Whoever restrains his anger, Allah will cover his faults, and whoever suppresses his rage even though he could fulfill it, Allah will fill his heart with hope on the Day of Judgment. And whoever walks with his brother in fulfilling his need until he secures it, Allah will make his footing firm on the Day when feet will slip.\""],[13584,"\"The Prophet ﷺ made the date palm's boundaries extend to the length of its branches.\""],[13585,"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sun rises between the two horns of a devil.”"],[13586,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not wiping other than these two (the two khuffs)."],[13587,"While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a woman passed by. Some of the people said, “This is the daughter of Muhammad.” A man said, “Indeed the likeness of Muhammad among Banu Hashim is that of a fragrant herb in the midst of stench.” The woman went and informed the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ came, anger recognizable in his face, until he stood over the people and said: “What is the matter with statements that reach me from certain people? Indeed Allah, may He be exalted, created the heavens and the earth in seven (layers). He chose the highest of them and dwelt in it, and He settled whomever He willed of His creation in His heavens. He created the earth in seven (layers) and chose the highest of them, and He settled whomever He willed of His creation in it. He created the creation and chose from the creation the children of Adam, and chose from the children of Adam the Arabs, and chose from the Arabs Mudar, and chose from Mudar Quraysh, and chose from Quraysh Banu Hashim, and chose me from Banu Hashim. I am from the best to the best. So whoever loves the Arabs, it is out of love for me that he loves them, and whoever hates the Arabs, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.”"],[13588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform Hajj and 'Umrah consecutively, for they remove sins just as the bellows removes the dross of iron.”"],[13589,"He said to a man: “Sell me the fruit of your land for the measure you used to measure from it.” Ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade this, and it is muzabanah.”"],[13590,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rak'ahs before Zuhr, two rak'ahs after Jumu'ah, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, and two rak'ahs after Isha."],[13591,"I heard Ibn Umar say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at al-Hijr, he said, \"Do not enter upon these punished people.\" Then he ordered the dough, and it was thrown away."],[13595,"While we were around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he mentioned the fitnah or it was mentioned in his presence. He said, \"When you see that people's covenants have become corrupted, their trusts have become light, and they have become like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers. I stood up to him and said, \"How should I act at that time, may Allah make me your ransom?\" He said, \"Stay in your house, control your tongue, take what you know, leave what you reject, keep to the affairs of your own self, and leave the affairs of the common people.\""],[13596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How will you be in a time—or a time is about to come—when people will be sifted with a thorough sifting, and the dregs of people will remain, their covenants and trusts having become corrupted, and they will differ, and they will become like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers. They said, \"How should we be, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, and attend to the affairs of your own selves, and leave the affairs of your common people.\""],[13597,"He reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"How will you be when a time comes in which people will be sifted with a thorough sifting, and you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants have become corrupted and who have neglected their trusts, and they return to being like this\"—and he inserted his fingers into one another. They said, \"What should we do, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Take what you know and leave what you reject, and keep to your own special affairs, and leave the affairs of your common people.\""],[13610,"“I retained from the Messenger of God ﷺ a thousand proverbs.”"],[13611,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.” Then he said: “God, Mighty and Exalted, and His Messenger ﷺ have forbidden wine, gambling, the kubah (drum), and al-ghubayra (a fermented drink).”"],[13615,"One day I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in his house and he said: “Do you know who is with us in the house?” I said: “Who, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Jibril ﷺ .” I said: “Peace be upon you, O Jibril, and the mercy of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He has returned your greeting.”"],[13713,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Knowledge is three things, and whatever is beyond that is surplus: a decisive verse, an established sunnah, and a just obligatory share.”"],[13726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever feeds his brother until he is full and gives him water to drink until he is quenched, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seven trenches, each trench being a distance of five hundred years.”"],[13727,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There will be a caliph, he and his descendants are from the people of the Fire.”"],[13730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a man to marry a woman by divorcing another, nor is it lawful for a man to outbid a fellow man’s transaction until he gives it up, nor is it lawful for three people in open land to appoint one of themselves as their leader, nor is it lawful for three people in open land for two of them to hold private conversation without their companion.”"],[13735,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever stands up (in prayer) and recites Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad (Surah Al-Ikhlas) and Al-Lahus-Samad (Surah Al-Falaq), then he has recited a third of the Quran.\""],[13740,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which Islam is best? He said: \"That you feed food and greet with peace those you know and those you do not know.\""],[13743,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The first group to enter Paradise will be the poor among the emigrants who are boycotted by others. When they are commanded, they listen and obey, even if there is a person among them who has a need but it is not fulfilled until he dies while it is still in his chest. Indeed, Allah invites Paradise on the Day of Resurrection and it comes with its splendor and beautification. Allah will say, 'Where are My servants who fought in My cause, were harmed in My cause, and strived in My cause? Enter Paradise with no punishment, no accounting.' The angels will come and prostrate and say, 'Our Lord, we glorify You night and day, and who are these whom You have made superior to us?' The Lord, blessed and exalted be He, will say, 'These are My servants who fought in My cause, were harmed in My cause, and strived in My cause.' The angels will enter upon them from every gate, saying, 'Peace be upon you, for your patience. How excellent is the final home!'\""],[13744,"And he narrated that a man came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: I pledge allegiance to you for emigration and jihad, and I seek reward from Allah. He said: \"Is either of your parents alive?\" He said: Yes, both of them. He said: \"So do you seek reward from Allah?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Return to your parents and keep their company well.\""],[13745,"A man asked me, so I said: This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so go and ask him, then come back and tell me. He asked him, then returned and told me that he had asked him, and he said: \"It is the greatest of major sins and the mother of indecencies. Whoever drinks wine abandons prayer and may fall upon his mother, his paternal aunt, and his maternal aunt.\""],[13776,"The Prophet ﷺ seated him behind him and said: “O young man, shall I not grant you something? Shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you? Safeguard Allah and He will safeguard you; safeguard Allah and you will find Him before you. When you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that the pen has already dried with what is to be, and know that if the creatures were to intend something for you that was not written upon you, they would not be able to do it. And know that victory is with patience, relief is with distress, and with hardship comes ease.”"],[13780,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"ʿAli is my root and Jaʿfar is my branch\" or \"Jaʿfar is my root and ʿAli is my branch.\""],[13781,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Congratulations to you, O ʿAbd Allah. Your father is flying with the angels in the sky.\""],[13782,"From his father, regarding these words: \"There is no god but God, the Forbearing, the Magnificent. Glory be to God, Lord of the Noble Throne, and praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: \"Prompt your dying with them.\" They said: \"O Messenger of God, what about for the living?\" He said: \"Better and better.\""],[13785,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent an army and appointed Zayd b. Harithah as their commander. He said: \"If he is killed or martyred, your commander is Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib. If he is killed or martyred, your commander is ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah.\" They set off and met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Jaʿfar took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of God, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and God granted victory through him. Their news came to the Prophet ﷺ. He went out and ascended the pulpit, praised God and extolled Him, then said: \"To proceed: your brothers met the enemy. Zayd b. Harithah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Jaʿfar took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then ʿAbd Allah b. Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword among the swords of God, Khalid b. al-Walid, took the banner, and God granted victory through him.\" Then he gave the family of Jaʿfar three days before coming to them. Then he came to them and said: \"Do not weep for him after today.\" Then he said: \"Summon for me the sons of my brother.\" We were brought as if we were chicks. He said: \"Summon for me the barber.\" He ordered him, and he shaved our heads. Then he said: \"As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib. As for ʿAwn and ʿAbd Allah, they resemble me in my appearance and character.\" Then he took my hand and raised it, saying: \"O God, be a successor to Jaʿfar in his family, and bless ʿAbd Allah in the transaction of his right hand.\" He said this three times. Then our mother came and mentioned our orphanhood. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter?\""],[13788,"About killing them—meaning the snakes that are in houses."],[13789,"Sahl entered upon al-Hajjaj while leaning on his hand, and said to him: The Prophet ﷺ said concerning the Ansar: “Be good to their good-doers and pardon their wrongdoers.” He said: Who will testify for you? He said: These two at your sides, Abdullah b. Ja'far and Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Talhah. They said: Yes."],[13797,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped his head three times and said: “O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his family.”"],[13798,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sneezed, he praised Allah. It was said to him: May Allah have mercy on you. He said: “May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.”"],[13804,"I saw the ring of the Prophet ﷺ on his right hand."],[13807,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best meat is the meat of the back.”"],[13841,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed ʿIsha, he would perform four rakʿahs and make witr with one prostration, then sleep until he prayed after his prayer during the night."],[13852,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple from my nation.'"],[13856,"About the Prophet ﷺ , it was mentioned that he appointed an inheritance for himself because he was born on the bed of Zama'ah. He said to Sawda, \"As for you, seclude yourself from him.\""],[13872,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his uncle al-ʿAbbas to order his sons to cultivate clover, for it repels poverty. He said, “And al-qadb is lucerne.”"],[13873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever draws his sword then strikes with it, his blood is forfeited,” meaning he struck with it."],[13876,"About nabidh, he said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade earthenware jars and gourds.”"],[13877,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “If I were to take an intimate friend other than my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but he is my brother and my companion in the cave.”"],[13880,"\"The Prophet ﷺ cursed so-and-so and his son from this pulpit.\""],[13881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.\""],[13882,"'Utbah b. Farqad wrote to 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr asking his legal opinion about the grandfather. He wrote back: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If I were to take a close friend from my nation other than my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave.\" And Abu Bakr used to treat him like a father."],[13883,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Hajj: \"Which city is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"Mecca.\" He said, \"Which month is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"The month of Dhul-Hijjah.\" He said, \"Which day is the most sacred?\" They replied, \"The day of Sacrifice, the greatest day of Hajj.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you, like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this city of yours, until you meet your Lord.\""],[13884,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: \"This is the day of 'Ashura', so fast it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded its fasting.\""],[13887,"\"I saw Ibn al-Zubayr performing tawaf wearing a bartalah.\""],[13888,"\"And take provisions, for the best provision is God-consciousness.\""],[13892,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ curse al-Hakam and his offspring."],[13895,"Al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwam: \"O Messenger of God, which comfort will we be asked about? They are only the two black ones: water and dates.\" He said: \"Indeed that will be.\""],[13896,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is more virtuous than a thousand prayers in any other mosque.\""],[13897,"\"We ate grilled food with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day while we were in the mosque. Then the prayer was called, so we did not increase or add anything except that we wiped with pebbles.\""],[13901,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: After the prayer, when he had said the salam, before standing, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, raising his voice: \"There is no god but God, alone without partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things. There is no might nor power except by God; we worship none but Him. His is grace, His is bounty, and His is good praise. There is no god but God, sincere to Him in religion, even if the disbelievers hate it.\""],[13908,"I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting the verse: “They said: Two sorcerers supporting one another.”"],[13911,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to take a close friend, I would have taken him as a close friend.” He made the grandfather a father, to whom wealth may pass."],[13912,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Indeed before the Hour there will be thirty liars, among them al-Aswad al-‘Ansi, the man of San‘a’, and the man of al-Yamama.”"],[13914,"I heard ‘Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr say: The Prophet ﷺ recited the tashahhud: “In the name of Allah and by Allah, the Best of names. All greetings, pure words, and prayers are due to Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner, and that the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. O Allah, forgive me and guide me.” This was in the first two rak‘ahs."],[13917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Were it not that I would impose hardship on my ummah, I would have commanded them to use the siwak at every prayer.”"],[13920,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the house of Umm Salamah praying in a single garment, draping its two ends over opposite shoulders."],[13925,"Al-Mustanir b. Rizam the Jew struck my face with a hooked staff of shawhat wood and wounded me with a wound that reached the membrane of the brain or fractured the skull. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he uncovered it and spat into it, and nothing from it ever harmed me."],[13932,"That he said: O Messenger of God, we are in our desert, and by God's praise I pray there, so command me to one night of this month that I should descend to the mosque and pray in it. He said: \"Descend on the night of the twenty-third and pray it, and if you like to continue to the end of the month, then do so, and if you like to return to your family, then do so.\""],[13933,"That he said: O Messenger of God, tell me a night in which the Night of Decree is sought. He said: \"Were it not that people would only descend for the prayer except on that night, I would have told you, but seek it in the twenty-third of the month.\""],[13936,"From Damra b. Abdullah b. Unays and Abd al-Rahman b. Ka'b that they both heard Abdullah b. Unays say: I sat in the gathering of Banu Salima, and I was the youngest of them, on the morning of the twenty-first of Ramadan. They said: Who will ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for us when the Night of Decree is? I said: I will. So I went until I arrived at Maghrib on the night of the twenty-second, and I prayed the prayer with him. Then I stood for him at his door until he passed by me, and he brought me into his house. He called for supper for me and said to me: \"Eat supper.\" Indeed I saw myself holding back from it because of its scarcity. Then he called for his sandals and stood up and said: \"It seems you have a need?\" I said: Yes, men from Banu Salima sent me to you asking you when the Night of Decree is. He said: \"How many nights of the month have passed?\" I said: Twenty-two. He said: \"It is tonight.\" Then he returned and said: \"Or the next one, or the next one.\""],[13937,"That he asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Night of Decree. He said: \"I saw myself prostrating in water and mud.\" I said: Make it clear to me so that I may seek it out? He said: \"Seek it in the latter half.\" I said: In which part of the latter half? He said: \"In the twenty-third.\""],[13938,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the Night of Decree. He said: \"I saw it and then was made to forget it, so seek it in the latter half.\" Then he returned and asked him, and he said: \"In the twenty-third that passes of the month.\" Abd al-Aziz said: My mother told me that Abdullah b. Unays used to keep alive the night of the sixteenth until the night of the twenty-third."],[13941,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The greatest of major sins are associating partners with God, disobedience to parents, and the false oath. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one swears, even if it is about the like of a mosquito's wing, except that it becomes a black spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[13942,"\"That the Messenger of God ﷺ sent him on a military expedition alone.\""],[13946,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I saw myself on Laylat al-Qadr prostrating in water and mud.” Then the Prophet ﷺ led us in prayer on the night of the twenty-third, and I saw him prostrating in water and mud."],[13947,"From ʿAbd Allāh b. Unays, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he was asked about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Seek it tonight.” And that night was the night of the twenty-third. A man said: O Messenger of God, then it is the first of eight? He said: “Rather, the first of seven, since the month does not complete [thirty days].”"],[13953,"He narrated to us from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “Indeed, in Friday there is an hour in which no Muslim coincides while he is in prayer, asking God for good, except that He gives it to him.” Abū Hurayrah indicated with his hand that it was a small amount. When Abū Hurayrah died, I said: If only I went to Abū Saʿīd and asked him. So I went to him and asked him. Then I left him and entered upon ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām and asked him. He said: God created Adam on Friday and took him [in death] on Friday, and on it the Hour will occur, and it is the last hour. I said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said “in prayer,” but that is not an hour of prayer. He said: Do you not know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The one waiting for prayer is in prayer”? I said: Yes. He said: Then by God, it is it."],[13956,"ʿAbd Allāh b. Salām: O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim, and I would like to ask you about some things. He said: “Ask about whatever occurs to you.” I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about a man's resemblance to his mother, when the fluid is from the man. He said: “The man's fluid is white and thick, and the woman's fluid is red and thin. Whichever of them prevails over the other, the resemblance belongs to it.” I said: O Messenger of God, what will the people of Paradise eat when they enter it? He said: “An extra portion of fish liver.” I said: O Messenger of God, tell me about the signs of the Hour. He said: “A fire that emerges from the east and drives the people to their gathering place.” He said: I bear witness that you are a prophet."],[13975,"“Jesus ﷺ will be buried with the Messenger of God ﷺ and his two companions, and his grave will be the fourth.”"],[13980,"I entered the mosque of Madinah, and a man came and prayed two rakʿahs, making them brief, with a trace of humility upon him. A man said: Whoever would like to look at a man of the people of Paradise, let him look at this one. I followed him and told him, and he said: Glory be to God; no one should say what he does not know. I will tell you why that is. I saw a vision and related it to the Prophet ﷺ. I saw as if I were in a garden—and he mentioned its vastness, beauty, and greenness—with in its middle an iron pillar whose base was in the earth and its top in the sky. At its top was a handle. He said to me: Climb. I said: I cannot. Then a servant came to me and took hold of my clothes—that is, from behind me—and struck at the top of it, saying: Hold fast. I awoke with it in my hand. I related it to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “The garden is Islam, the pillar is the pillar of Islam, and the handle is the firm handhold, so you are upon Islam.” And behold, he was ʿAbdullah b. Salam."],[13987,"“Shall I not relate to you a hadith that is in the Book of God?” Then he mentioned a people who will come out of the Fire. Ibrahim will say, “O Lord, You have burned my children,” and they will come out of it."],[13988,"“Indeed we find the description of the Messenger of God ﷺ: ‘We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of good tidings, and a warner, and a protection for the unlettered. You are My servant and His messenger. I have named you al-Mutawakkil. He is not harsh, nor hard-hearted, nor clamorous in the markets, nor does he repay evil with its like; rather he pardons, forgives, and overlooks. And I will not take you until I have straightened the crooked creed by your testifying that there is no god but God, by which He opens blind eyes, deaf ears, and covered hearts.’” ʿAtaʾ b. Yasar said: Abu Waqid al-Laythi informed me that he heard Kaʿb al-Ahbar say the like of what Ibn Salam said."],[13993,"“By Him in whose hand is my soul, the nearest of people on the Day of Resurrection will be Muhammad ﷺ, sitting at His right upon the Throne.”"],[13994,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the pulpit: “It would not be difficult for you, if you could manage, to take two garments for Friday other than the two garments of work.”"],[13998,"He said: We discussed among ourselves and said, 'Which of us will go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and ask him which deeds are most beloved to God?' We were in awe that any one of us should stand up. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a man to us. Some of us began gesturing to one another, and he recited to us: 'Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies God' from its beginning to its end. Hilal said: 'Ata' b. Yasar recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: Hilal recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awza'i said: Yahya recited it to us from its beginning to its end."],[13999,"What is between ʿAyr and Uhud is sacred. The Messenger of God ﷺ declared it sacred. I would never cut a tree from it or hunt a bird."],[14057,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When the prayer is due and one of you has the need to defecate, let him begin with that, then pray afterwards, and let him not come to prayer while he is holding it back.”"],[14058,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us, saying: Dawud b. Qays narrated to us. And Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Razzaq from Dawud b. Qays, who said: I heard ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. Aqram narrating from his father that he was with his father at al-Qaʿ in Namirah, and a mounted party passed by us, and they made their camels kneel at the side of the road. He said to me, “My son, stay with our lambs until I approach these riders.” He said, so he approached them and I approached with him. Then the prayer was established, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among them, and I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ every time he prostrated."],[14065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man may free from his slave whatever he wishes—if he wishes, two-thirds, and if he wishes, a quarter.”"],[14066,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “For camels there is a farʿ, and for sheep there is a farʿ. And the ʿaqiqah is performed for a boy, and his head is not touched with blood.”"],[14119,"The Messenger of God ﷺ approached until he was in the midst of the dwellings of the Ansar and noticed the smell of roasting meat. He said: \"Who is this who has slaughtered?\" A man came out and said: \"O Messenger of God, this is a day on which food is undesirable.\" He said: \"Slaughter again.\" He said: \"By God, I have nothing but a jadhaʿah or a lamb of sheep.\" He said: \"Slaughter again\" three times, then said: \"Then slaughter it, and it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[14121,"I went with my father to the Prophet ﷺ as his people embraced Islam. He advised us, saying, \"Let the one among you who knows the most Qur'an lead you in prayer.\" As I knew the most Qur'an, they made me lead them."],[14122,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: \"O God, whoever believes in me, attests to my truthfulness, and knows that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth and children few, endear to him meeting You, and hasten for him the decree. And whoever does not believe in me, does not attest to my truthfulness, and does not know that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth abundant and prolong his life.\""],[14138,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: “O people, it is not lawful for me nor for anyone else of the spoils of the Muslims even the weight of this hair.” He took a hair from the withers of his she-camel, after what God had apportioned for me."],[14139,"The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned me when he wanted to send me with wealth to Abu Sufyan to distribute among Quraysh in Makkah after the conquest. He said: “Find a companion.” ʿAmr b. Umayya al-Damri came to me and said: “I have heard that you intend to set out and are seeking a companion, and I am your companion.” The Messenger of God ﷺ had said: “When you find a companion, inform me.” So I informed him, and he said: “Who?” I said: “ʿAmr b. Umayya al-Damri.” He said: “When he descends into the land of his people, beware of him, for the poet said: ‘Your brother al-Bakri, so do not trust him.’” We set out until we reached al-Abwaʾ. He said: “I need something from my people, so wait for me.” I said: “Go rightly guided.” When he turned away, I remembered the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I tied my camel tightly, then set off urging it quickly. When I was at al-ʿAsafir, there he was confronting me with a group. He said: “I urged my camel on, and I heard him, and when he saw that I had outdistanced him, they turned back, and he came to me and said: ‘I had a need from my people.’ I said: ‘Indeed.’ Then we went on until we arrived in Makkah, and I handed over the wealth to Abu Sufyan.”"],[14140,"O Messenger of God, you forbade incantations, but I use incantations for snakebite. He said: \"Recite them to me.\" So I recited them to him, and he said: \"There is no harm in these; these are covenants.\" He said: Then a man from the Ansar came who used incantations for scorpion stings, and he said: \"Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so.\""],[14147,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God (mighty and sublime) may support the religion through a wicked man.\""],[14148,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"O God, support ʿAli; O God, honor whoever honors ʿAli; O God, abandon whoever abandons ʿAli ؓ.\""],[14153,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif. He used to come out to us at night and narrate to us. One night he was late in coming to us; then he came out to us. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, you were late in coming to us tonight.” He said: “A portion (hizb) of the Qur’an came to me, and I disliked to interrupt it until I had finished it.” When morning came, we asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “How do you divide the Qur’an into portions?” They said: “Three, five, seven, nine, eleven, thirteen (surahs); and what is between Qaf and ‘al-Qur’an al-Majid’ to the end of the Mufassal is a good portion.” Thus narrated al-Walid b. Muslim from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Rahman al-Ta’ifi, from ʿUthman b. ʿAmr b. Aws, from his father; but Wakiʿ, Qurran b. Tammam and others disagreed with him, and narrated it from ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Rahman, from ʿUthman b. ʿAbd Allah b. Aws, from his grandfather Aws b. Hudhayfa."],[14154,"The Prophet ﷺ sent with me a sacrificial animal as a voluntary offering and said: “If any of it is injured, then slaughter it, then dip its shoe in its blood and strike it on its side, and leave it between the people and it.”"],[14160,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day he died left nothing except his weapon, his white mule, and a piece of land which he made as charity.”"],[14161,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, “and he recited Surat al-Najm and prostrated, and I prostrated with him.”"],[14165,"So he ordered that he be made thirsty. Then he called for a basin of water and called for the young horses, and they drank. Then 'Amr's horse came and folded its legs and drank. This is the behavior of a half-breed. He said, 'Do you not see?' He said, 'Yes, a half-breed recognizes a half-breed.' It reached 'Umar, and he wrote to him: 'It has reached me what you said to your commander, and it has reached me that you have a sword you call al-Sim'ama, and I have a sharp sword. By Allah, if I place it on your head, I will not lift it until I reach something with it.' He mentioned something from his inside. 'If it pleases you to know whether what I say is true, then return.'"],[14172,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed them and said: 'May Allah brighten [the face of] a person who hears my words and retains them. For many a bearer of jurisprudence has no understanding, and many a bearer of jurisprudence conveys it to one more understanding than himself.'"],[14173,"A letter from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to 'Umayr Dhu Murran and whoever accepts Islam from Hamdan. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah to you, besides whom there is no deity. Now then, your acceptance of Islam reached us upon our arrival from the land of the Romans. So rejoice, for Allah has guided you with His guidance. If you bear witness that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establish prayer, and give zakat, then you have the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger over your blood, your wealth, and the land of Alyun upon which you accepted Islam, its plains, mountains, springs, and pastures, without being wronged or restricted. For charity is not lawful for Muhammad nor for his household. Malik b. Murara al-Rahawi has guarded the unseen, fulfilled the trust, and conveyed the message. I command you, O Dhu Murran, to treat him well, for he is regarded with respect among his people, and may your Lord love you.'"],[14176,"Abu al-Darda': 'As for me, I will not abandon them. Whoever wishes to humble himself, let him humble himself.'"],[14177,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hama.'"],[14178,"From 'Urwa regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar, then from Banu Khansa' b. Mabdhul b. 'Amr b. Ghanm b. Mazin: 'Umayr, and he is given the kunya Abu Dawud b. 'Amir b. Malik b. Khansa' b. Mabdhul."],[14186,"From Abu ʿImran al-Jawni, I think only from Anas b. Malik, he said: Wahb b. ʿUmayr was present at Uhud as a disbeliever and was wounded, so he was among the slain. A man from the Ansar passed by him, recognized him, placed his sword in his belly until it came out of his back, then left him. When night fell and the cold struck him, he made his way to Makkah and recovered. He and Safwan b. Umayyah gathered in the Hijr, and Wahb said, 'Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would love to be the one who kills Muhammad myself.' Safwan said to him, 'How would you do it?' He said, 'I am a swift man whom no one can catch. I will come to him and deceive him, then strike him with the sword and join the horses, and no one will catch me.' Safwan said to him, 'Your dependents with my dependents, and your debt upon me.' So he went out, sharpening his sword and poisoning it, then set out for Madinah, intending only to kill the Prophet ﷺ. When he reached Madinah, ʿUmar b. al-Khattab saw him and was troubled and distressed. He said to the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, 'I have seen Wahb, and his arrival alarms me, for he is a treacherous man. Surround your Prophet.' The Muslims surrounded the Prophet ﷺ. Wahb came and stood before the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'May you have a pleasant morning, O Muhammad.' He said, 'Allah has replaced it for us with something better.' He said, 'I recall you used to say it while you were pleased.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'What has brought you here?' He said, 'I came to ransom your captives.' He said, 'What is the matter with the sword?' He said, 'Indeed, we carried it on the Day of Badr but did not succeed or prevail.' He said, 'What is the thing you said to Safwan in the Hijr: \"Were it not for my dependents and a debt upon me, I would be the one who killed Muhammad myself\"?' The Prophet ﷺ informed him of his affair. Wahb said, 'Hah! How did you say?' He repeated it to him. Wahb said, 'You used to tell us news of the people of the earth, and we disbelieved you. Now I see you tell news of the people of heaven. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give me your turban.' The Prophet ﷺ gave him his turban. Then he went out to Makkah. ʿUmar said, 'He came while he was more hateful to me than a pig, then he returned while he was dearer to me than some of my own children.'"],[14187,"The delegation of ʿAbd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ. When they wanted to leave, they said, 'You have memorized everything you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so ask him about nabidh.' So they came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land with bad water that does not suit us except with drink.' He said, 'What is your drink?' They said, 'Nabidh.' He said, 'In what do you drink it?' They said, 'In naqir (a hollowed-out palm trunk).' He said, 'Do not drink in naqir.' They said, 'By Allah, our people will not agree with us on this.' So they returned and asked him, and he told them the same. Then they came again, and he said, 'Do not drink in naqir, lest one of you strikes a blow from which he remains lame until the Day of Resurrection.' They laughed. He said, 'What are you laughing about?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Him who sent you with the truth, we drank in a naqir of ours, and some of us rose against others, and one struck a blow from which he is lame until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[14188,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Allah, exalted is He, has promised me to admit three hundred thousand of my community into Paradise.' ʿUmayr said, 'O Prophet of Allah, increase for us.' ʿUmar said, 'That is enough for you, O ʿUmayr.' He said, 'What is it to you and me, O Ibn al-Khattab? What harm is it to you if Allah admits us into Paradise?' ʿUmar said, 'Allah, Majestic and Mighty, if He wills, will admit people into Paradise with a single handful or a single scoop.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'ʿUmar has spoken the truth.'"],[14202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while Adi b. Hatim was in charge of the alms of his people—that is, an agent of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[14203,"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was sent with prophethood, and I do not know any of the Arabs who was more hateful or more averse to him than I, until I joined the Romans and became a Christian among them. When I heard about the good character he called people to and the people who had gathered around him, I traveled until I came to him and stood before him while Suhayb, Bilal, and Salman were with him. He said, 'O Adi b. Hatim, submit and you will be safe.' I said, 'Ah! Ah!' So I made my camel kneel, sat down, pressed my knee against his knee, and said, 'O Messenger of God, what is Islam?' He said, 'You believe in God, His angels, His Books, and His Messengers, and you believe in the divine decree, its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until the treasures of Kisra and Caesar are opened. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until a woman travels from al-Harrah—and there was no Kufah on that day—and circumambulates this Kaʿbah with no protector. O Adi b. Hatim, the Hour will not come until a money bag goes around seeking someone to accept it, and finds no one, and strikes it against the ground and says, 'Would that you had never existed; would that you were dust.'"],[14204,"A man said, 'When Uthman was killed, no two goats butted heads over it.' I said, 'Rather, many eyes were gouged out over it.'"],[14246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A woman must not travel more than three [days] except with a dhu mahram.”"],[14247,"“Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Yes. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: ‘O ʿAdī b. Ḥātim, submit and you will be safe.’ I said: ‘What is Islam?’ He said: ‘Testify that there is no god but Allah, and testify that I am the Messenger of Allah, and believe in the divine decrees, all of them: their good and their evil, their sweet and their bitter.’”"],[14304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There will not come upon you but a short time until a woman travels in a litter between Makkah and al-Ḥīrah, and no one takes hold of her halter. And there will not come upon one of you but a short time until a man walks with a handful of gold and does not find anyone to accept it. And there is none of you but will be presented to Allah ﷻ with no interpreter between him and Him. So whoever is able to shield himself from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so.'"],[14305,"We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we do not ask you about the obedience of one who fears Allah and does right, but about one who does such and such, mentioning evil.' He said: 'Fear Allah, and hear and obey.'"],[14308,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have dogs that we send after game, and we eat from what they catch for us?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[14316,"I said: O Messenger of God, I ask you about food that I leave only out of scrupulousness. He said: “Do not leave anything in which you have imitated Christianity.”"],[14317,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O ʿAdi, do not belittle my Companions. The treasures of Kisra will surely be opened, and a woman in a howdah will set out from al-Hirah under the protection of this House, and this wealth will surely be made lawful at the beginning of the day, then it will be cast aside at its end and no one will accept it.” ʿAdi said: I have indeed seen two of these, and the third will surely come to pass."],[14318,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about a person in a state of major ritual impurity who sleeps. He said: “He should perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[14319,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A time is near when it will be hard for a man to give out the zakat of his wealth.”"],[14332,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever swears an oath over the property of a Muslim man will meet God while He is angry with him.” It was said, “And what about the one who gives it up, O Messenger of God?” He said, “For him is Paradise.”"],[14336,"He threw a stone at a wife of his, and she died. He followed the Messenger of God ﷺ to Tabuk and told him his story. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You pay her blood money, and you do not inherit from her.”"],[14337,"The Messenger of God ﷺ made a protected area around every side of Madinah a barid in extent: its trees are not to be beaten, nor its branches cut, except for a stick used to drive animals."],[14371,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered his companions to fight, and a man from his companions was struck by an arrow. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'This one has made it obligatory.' And they said when he ordered them to fight, 'Then, O Messenger of God, we will not say as the Children of Israel said to Moses: \"Go, you and your Lord, and fight\" to the end of the verse, but we say: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; indeed, we are with you, among the fighters.'"],[14372,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for clothing, and he clothed me with two coarse garments. I saw myself wearing them, being among the most clothed of my companions."],[14373,"When he pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said to him, 'What is your name?' He said, 'Nashbah.' He said, 'You are ʿUtbah b. ʿAbd.'"],[14378,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about Paradise, and he mentioned the pool. He said, 'Is there fruit in it?' He said, 'Yes, and in it is a tree called Ṭūbā.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, which tree of our land does it resemble?' He said, 'It does not resemble any tree of your land. Have you been to Syria? There is a tree there called the walnut, which grows on a single trunk and whose top spreads out.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, what is the size of its root?' He said, 'If a young she-camel of your family's camels were to travel, you would not encompass its root until its collarbone breaks from old age.' He said, 'Are there grapes in it?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What is the size of a cluster from it?' He said, 'A month's journey for the piebald crow, without tiring.' He said, 'What is the size of a single grape from it?' He said, 'Your father and mother took a young she-camel, slaughtered it, and skinned its hide, then said, \"Make for us a bucket from it.\"' He said, 'O Messenger of God, will that grape suffice me and my family?' He said, 'Yes, and the generality of your clan.'"],[14383,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a bedouin came and said, “O Messenger of God, I hear you mention a tree in Paradise, and I know of no tree with more thorns than it — meaning the talh (acacia).” He replied, “The mottled buck — meaning the castrated one — in it are seventy colors of food, no one color resembling another.”"],[14384,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade clipping the tails, forelocks, and manes of horses. As for their tails, they are their fly whisks; as for their manes, they are for their warmth; and as for their forelocks, good is tied within them."],[14386,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No servant leaves his house in the morning or evening heading to the mosque except that his steps are — one step an expiation and one step a good deed.”"],[14387,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Take the pre-dawn meal (sahur) at the end of the night.” And he used to say: “It is the blessed meal.”"],[14388,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, “How was the beginning of your affair?” And he mentioned the hadith."],[14416,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ rebuked a man who had a Persian bow, saying, \"Throw it away.\" Then he pointed to the Arab bow and said, \"With this and with the spear of qana, you will gain power in the lands and be victorious over your enemy.\""],[14436,"Arfajah’s nose was injured on the Day of al-Kulāb, so he made a nose of silver, but it became foul, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to make a nose of gold."],[14437,"I came to Madinah and entered the mosque while the people were waiting for the prayer. A man came out to us with his head dripping from the ablution he had performed or from a bath he had taken. He led us in prayer. When we had prayed, the people began going to him saying, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about such-and-such? O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about such-and-such?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Thus, O people: indeed the religion of Allah is ease,” three times. Then I went out from the door and departed."],[14440,"When Abu Bakr returned and the people had completed their Hajj, ʿUrwah b. Masʿūd al-Thaqafī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. Then he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to return to his people. He said, \"I fear that they will kill you.\" He replied, \"If they found me sleeping, they would not wake me.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted him. He returned to al-Ṭāʾif and served dinner. Thaqīf came to greet him, so he called them to Islam and advised them sincerely. They accused him, disobeyed him, and made him hear such harm as he had not feared from them. They left him, and when the last part of the night came and dawn broke, he stood on an upper room in his house, called the adhān for prayer, and pronounced the shahādah. A man from Quraysh shot him with an arrow and killed him."],[14477,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave him a dinar to buy a sacrificial animal for him. ʿUrwah said: I bought two sheep for him with it, then sold one of them for a dinar and a sheep. “He prayed for blessing for me in trade.” And when he bought dust, he profited from it."],[14479,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ twist the forelock of his horse between his two fingers, then said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14482,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[14486,"The Prophet ﷺ came to a market and gave him a dinar, then said: “Buy a sheep for us.” So he went and bought two sheep for a dinar. Then a man met him and he sold him one sheep for a dinar. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ with a dinar and a sheep. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “May Allah bless you in the transaction of your right hand.” He said: “I would stand in the marketplace and not return to my family until I had profited forty thousand.”"],[14491,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “A woman may not be married in addition to her maternal aunt or her paternal aunt.”"],[14512,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a delegation of his people. When they entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Has anyone else come to you besides you?” They said: “Yes, a youth of ours whom we left behind with our baggage.” He said: “Send for him.” When I entered upon him while they were with him, he turned to me and said: “The giving hand is the upper one, and the begging hand is the lower one. And what suffices you, then do not ask. For God’s wealth is both asked for and given.”"],[14513,"“A delegation from Thaqif came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Ramadan, and he set up a tent for them in the mosque. When they embraced Islam, they fasted with him.”"],[14514,"Ata' narrated to me, a man from Banu Shaybah, and he was a very old man. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying at this station wearing two sandals of tanned leather.”"],[14528,"The Prophet ﷺ sent ten men as scouts and appointed over them 'Asim b. Thabit al-Ansari, the grandfather of 'Asim b. 'Amr. He mentioned it in full."],[14529,"'Umar b. al-Khattab sent for him to seek his help with some of the sadaqah, but he refused to work for him. Then he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When the Day of Resurrection comes, the ruler will be commanded and made to stand on the bridge of Jahannam. The bridge will be commanded and it will shake violently, and every bone in him will be dislocated from its place. Then Allah will command the bones and they will return to their places. Then He will question him. If he was obedient to Allah, He will seize him and give him a double portion of reward. But if he was disobedient to Allah, the bridge will twist with him and he will fall into Jahannam for seventy autumns.'\""],[14530,"I entered the mosque of Madinah, and the people were saying, \"We seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger.\" He said: I said, \"What did they say?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a khutbah on his minbar when a man stood up, took his son by the hand, and led him out of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah curse the leader and the led. Woe to this one one day—to this ummah from so-and-so, the one with the buttocks.\""],[14531,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah bt. 'Umar once, then took her back."],[14567,"From ʿIsmah b. Qays, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that he used to seek refuge in his prayer from the trial of the west."],[14573,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq met a man from the Arabs called ʿUfayr b. Abi ʿUfayr. Abu Bakr said to him: Did you hear from the Messenger of God ﷺ anything about love? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Love is inherited, and enmity is inherited.”"],[14574,"One of his paternal uncles came to the Prophet ﷺ and embraced Islam. When he returned, he passed by a mad Bedouin bound in iron. Some of them said to him: Do you have anything with which to treat him, for your companion has brought good? He said yes. He said: I then recited ruqya over him using the Mother of the Book for three days, twice each day, and he recovered. They gave me a hundred sheep, but I did not take them until I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. He said: Did you say anything other than this? I said no. He said, “Eat them, in the name of God. By my life, whoever eats by a false ruqya—you have eaten by a true ruqya.”"],[14586,"When ʿAli went out to Siffin, he appointed Abu Masʿud as his deputy over Kufah. There were men from the people of Kufah who had hidden themselves from ʿAli, and when he departed they appeared. People would come to Abu Masʿud and say, \"By Allah, Allah has destroyed his enemies and granted victory to the believers.\" Abu Masʿud would say, \"By Allah, I do not consider it a victory or well-being that one of the two parties prevails over the other.\" They said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"There will be reconciliation between the people.\" When ʿAli arrived, they mentioned that to him, and ʿAli said, \"Withdraw from our work.\" He said, \"And why is that?\" He said, \"We have found you not understanding a sound understanding.\" He said, \"As for me, there remains from my understanding what lets me know that the latter is worse.\""],[14602,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: A man from those before you was brought to account, and no good was found for him except that he used to mix with people and was wealthy. He would order his servant to be lenient with the one in difficulty. Allah ﷻ said: We are more entitled to that than him, so be lenient with him. Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah said in his hadith: We are more entitled than him to be lenient with him, so He was lenient with him."],[14603,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said: Men from my companions will surely be raised for me, until when I see them they will be snatched away before me. I will say: My companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."],[14604,"A man from the Ansar, whose kunya was Abu Shu'ayb, prepared food for the Prophet ﷺ and said: Bring with you five. The Prophet ﷺ said: Do you permit the sixth?"],[14641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “What harm would it have done to the owners of this one if they had benefited from its hide?”"],[14704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Every act of kindness is charity.”"],[14750,"While I was beating a slave boy of mine, I heard a voice from behind me: \"Know, Abā Masʿūd!\" I turned and it was the Messenger of God ﷺ. The whip fell from my hand out of awe of him. He said: \"Indeed, by God, God has more power over you than you have over this one.\""],[14756,"I attended a feast in which Abu Mas‘ud and Qurazah b. Ka‘b were present, and slave girls were singing. I said, “Glory be to Allah! Do you do this while you are companions of Muhammad ﷺ and people of Badr?” They said, “We were granted a dispensation for singing at weddings and for weeping without wailing.”"],[14757,"“It is not from the Sunnah to pray before the imam comes out on the day of Eid.”"],[14758,"We were with Ali when Abu Mas‘ud came to him. Ali said to him, “I see that you give legal opinions to the people.” He said, “Indeed I tell them that the last ones are worse.” Ali said, “Tell us what you heard the Prophet ﷺ saying about the hundred.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘A hundred years will not pass over the people while on the earth there is a blinking eye.’” Ali said, “You erred. He only said, ‘For whoever is on the face of the earth on that day – and there is no ease or joy except after the hundred.’”"],[14759,"Abu Mas‘ud said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military campaign, and the people were afflicted with hardship until I saw gloom on the faces of the Muslims and joy on the faces of the hypocrites. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he said, “By Allah, the sun will not set until Allah brings you provision.” Then Uthman knew that Allah and His Messenger would be truthful, so Uthman purchased forty camels with the food that was on them and sent nine of them to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw that, he said, “What is this?” They said, “Uthman has gifted it to you.” Then joy was recognized on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and gloom on the faces of the hypocrites. I saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands until the whiteness of his armpits was visible, supplicating for Uthman with a supplication I never heard him make for anyone before or after him: “O Allah, give Uthman; O Allah, do for Uthman.”"],[14760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a garden and then said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you.” Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq entered. Then he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you.” Then Umar entered. Then he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will now enter upon you. O Allah, make him Ali.” Then Ali ؓ entered."],[14763,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sat down in front of him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, as for greeting you with peace, we know it, but as for invoking blessings upon you, tell us how we should invoke blessings upon you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until we wished that the man who asked him had not asked him. Then he said, “When you invoke blessings upon me, say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.”"],[14774,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in a night?\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, can we bear a third of the Qur'an? He said: \"Is one of you unable to do so with Qul huwa Allahu ahad?\""],[14783,"Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari or Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud narrated that both of them said that they accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and that Jibril (Gabriel) came to the Prophet ﷺ after the sun had set. Jibril said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Dhuhr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the shadow of everything was equal to its height and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Asr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the sun had disappeared and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Maghrib prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the red twilight vanished and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Isha prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the dawn broke and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Fajr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him the next day when the shadow of everything was similar to its previous day's length and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Dhuhr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Dhuhr prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the shadow of everything was similar to its length the previous day and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Asr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Asr prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when the sun had set at a particular time and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Maghrib prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when a portion of the night had passed and said, \"O Muhammad, stand up and perform the Isha prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the Isha prayer. Then, Jibril came to him when it was dawn and said, \"O Muhammad, perform the Fajr prayer.\" So, the Prophet ﷺ stood up and performed the prayer. Then, Jibril said, \"There is a time period between these two (Fajr and sunrise).\""],[14787,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Quraysh, \"This affair will continue to be among you, and you will be its guardians, as long as you do not introduce innovations. Then He will set upon you the worst of His creation, and they will strip you as a branch is stripped.\""],[14788,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I perform a deed and keep it secret, but it becomes known, and I am pleased about that.\" He said, \"Two rewards are written for you: the reward of the secret and the reward of the open.\""],[14789,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and that was at the sun's decline. He said, \"Stand and pray,\" so he stood and prayed Zuhr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when his shadow was equal to his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed ʿAsr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when the sun had set and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Maghrib as three rakʿahs. Then he came to him when the twilight had disappeared and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed the later ʿIsha' as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when dawn broke and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Fajr as two rakʿahs. Then he came to him the next day for Zuhr when his shadow was equal to his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Zuhr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him when his shadow was twice his height and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed ʿAsr as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him at the first time when the sun had set and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Maghrib as three rakʿahs. Then he came to him after the twilight had disappeared and it had become dark and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed the later ʿIsha' as four rakʿahs. Then he came to him after dawn had risen and it had become bright and said, \"Stand and pray,\" and he prayed Subh as two rakʿahs. Then Jibril ﷺ said to him, \"Between these two is the time for prayer.\""],[14798,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ should come forward and lead them in prayer.”"],[14883,"I heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir say: The Prophet ﷺ said: “The two things I fear most for my community are their pursuit of signs and desires and their abandonment of the Qur'an and prayers; that the hypocrites learn it and argue with it against the people of knowledge.”"],[14884,"He heard ʿUqbah b. ʿAmir al-Juhani say: “For every gesture a man makes with his hand during prayer, a good deed or a degree is recorded for each finger.”"],[14889,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wickedness is seventy parts: for the Berbers sixty-nine parts, and for jinn and humans one part.”"],[14901,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “People are three: one who is safe, one who gains, and one who is ruined.”"],[14902,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Abu Bakr, \"When do you perform the Witr prayer?\" He replied, \"I pray two by two units of prayer, and then I perform the Witr prayer before I sleep.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"A cautious believer.\" The Prophet ﷺ asked Umar bin Khattab, \"How do you perform the Witr prayer?\" He replied, \"I pray two by two units of prayer, and then I sleep until I perform the Witr prayer at the end of the night.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"A strong believer.\""],[14927,"Abu Ayyub said to him: \"Why do you delay this prayer when you are one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Someone who did not accompany him will see you and think that this is its time.\" So we said: \"O Abu Ayyub, how did you use to pray it?\" He said: \"We used to pray it when the sun declines, hastening before the stars appear.\" \"Is that so, ʿUqbah?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[14955,"When {So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great} (Quran 56:96) was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Place it in your bowing.” And when “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High” (Quran 87:1) was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Place it in your prostration.”"],[14958,"She vowed to perform Hajj walking barefoot and unveiled. ʿUqbah asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Tell her to cover her head, ride, and fast for three days.”"],[14959,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whenever a person embarks on a journey alone, while remembering and mentioning Allah, an angel accompanies him. And whenever a person is alone with his hair or something similar, a devil accompanies him.\""],[14960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Let her ride, wear clothes, and fast.”"],[14961,"From the Prophet of Allah ﷺ: He saw Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left hand and said: “What is the matter with her that she eats with her left hand?” She said: “O Prophet of Allah, there is a sore on my right hand.” He said to her: “Even if it were a cow’s death?” Then the plague seized her and killed her."],[14969,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wears silk in this world, it will be forbidden for him in the Hereafter.”"],[14976,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Lands will be opened for you, and God will suffice you, so let none of you be too weak to play with his arrow.”"],[14980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever performs ablution and completes his ablution, then raises his head to the sky and says, ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God alone with no partner, and that Muḥammad is His servant and Messenger,’ eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter from whichever of them he wishes.”"],[14998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he applied kohl, applied it an odd number of times, and when he cleaned himself with stones, he cleaned himself an odd number of times."],[15001,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs ablution and perfects it, then prays a prayer in which he is mindful until he completes it, he will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.\""],[15005,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, will admit to Paradise because of a single arrow: its maker, who seeks reward in his craft for good, and the one who shoots it, and the one who gifts it.\" And he said: \"Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. Everything a man amuses himself with is false except training his horse, shooting with his bow, and playing with his wife.\""],[15006,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated it to me, so I went to him and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, Allah, may He be exalted, will admit three people to Paradise: its maker, who seeks reward in his craft for good, the one who shoots it, and the one who hands it to him. Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. And there is no amusement except three: a man training his horse, playing with his wife, and shooting with his bow. And whoever abandons archery after having learned it, out of aversion to it, then it is a blessing he has rejected—or he abandoned it.\""],[15007,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you of the best thing with which those who seek refuge seek refuge? Say: 'I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,' and say: 'I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.'\""],[15011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his companions. ʿUqba said: A jadhaʿa fell to my share. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a jadhaʿa has fallen to my share. He said: \"Sacrifice it.\""],[15014,"While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between al-Juhfa and al-Abwāʾ, a wind and darkness overtook us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began seeking refuge with \"I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak\" and \"I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,\" and he said: \"O ʿUqba, seek refuge, for no one has sought refuge with the like of them.\" He said: Then I heard him leading us in prayer with them."],[15015,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will never recite a surah more beloved to me, nor more effective, than 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.' So if you can manage not to abandon it in any prayer, do so.\""],[15016,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh b. Salmān from Muʿādh b. ʿAbdullāh b. Khubayb from his father from ʿUqba b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī that he said: While I was leading the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his mount during a military expedition, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say, O ʿUqba.\" I said: What shall I say? He said it a third time. I said: What shall I say? He said: \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" and he recited the surah until he completed it. Then he recited, \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak,\" and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he recited, \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind,\" and I recited with him until he completed it. Then he said: \"Refuge has never been sought with the like of them.\""],[15019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will be rulers after me who will lead you in prayer. If they complete its bowing and prostration, it is for you and for them. If they fall short in it, it is for you and against them.\""],[15020,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we used to take turns herding the animals. When it was my turn, I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was addressing the people, and I heard him say: \"There is no Muslim who performs ablution and does it well, then stands in his prayer and understands what he is saying in it, except that he departs as on the day his mother gave birth to him, free of sins, with no sin upon him.\" I could not contain myself at that and said: Excellent! Excellent!"],[15024,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “Any woman married off by two guardians belongs to the first of them.”"],[15032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Tonight verses were sent down to me, the like of which have never been seen: ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak’ and ‘Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of people.’”"],[15046,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit during Ramadan and said, \"I have stood on this pulpit and I know the Night of Qadr. So seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.\""],[15074,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ being gifted a leather container of honey. He accepted it and said: 'Protect my mountain pass,' so he protected it for him and wrote a document for him."],[15075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Preserve me in my Companions and my in-laws. Whoever preserves me in them, Allah will preserve him in this world and the Hereafter. And whoever does not preserve me in them, Allah will turn away from him, and whoever Allah turns away from is near to being seized.\""],[15076,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Upon you is the remembrance of your Lord, and pray your prayers at their earliest times, for Allah, exalted be He, will multiply for you.\""],[15084,"ʿIkrimah b. Abī Jahl b. Hishām, and he had no offspring. He had fled on the Day of the Conquest, until his wife asked the Prophet ﷺ for safe-conduct for him—she was Umm Ḥakīm bt. al-Ḥārith b. Hishām—and he granted him safety. She caught up with him in Yemen and brought him back to the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him, he stood up, embraced him, and said: \"Welcome to the emigrant rider.\""],[15085,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day I came to him: \"Welcome to the emigrant rider, welcome to the emigrant rider.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I will not leave any expense I spent against you without spending the like of it in the way of God.\""],[15086,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ to Bahrain. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ went out on a military expedition and we went out with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ dozed, then woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" We discussed who the ʿAmr might be. Then he dozed a second time, woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" Then he dozed a third time, woke and said: \"May God have mercy on ʿAmr.\" We said: \"Who is ʿAmr, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ.\" They said: \"What is the matter with him?\" He said: \"I remembered him. When I called people to give charity, he would come with charity and give generously. I would say: 'Where did you get this, O ʿAmr?' He would say: 'From God.' ʿAmr spoke the truth. ʿAmr has much good with God.\" Zuhayr said: \"When the strife occurred, I said I will follow this man about whom the Messenger of God said what he said, and I did not part from him.\""],[15091,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to them in the year of al-Muraysīʿ when they became Muslim: \"Part of the completeness of your Islam is that you pay the zakah on your wealth.\""],[15092,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar ؓ died while the quarters of Makkah were only called 'the freed ones': whoever was in need dwelled, and whoever was well-off housed others.\""],[15093,"I heard ʿAlqamah b. al-Ḥuwayrith, one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The fornication of the two eyes is looking.'\""],[15094,"\"I was among the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He built a dome for us near the house of Al-Mughirah. Bilal used to bring our iftar during Ramadan while we were traveling excessively.\""],[15095,"\"May you not be alarmed, may you be fatherless. The Messenger of God ﷺ had been employing you, and may you not be alarmed.\"… the hadith."],[15105,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for me his grant from him concerning this water where I am.”"],[15106,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, during the expedition of Tabuk, said, “If the plague occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it; and if you are elsewhere, do not advance into it.”"],[15112,"Ziyād said to him: \"You are of the bran of the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ.\""],[15117,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on an expedition. When we returned heading back to Madinah, the wife of a man who had been martyred with the Messenger of God ﷺ wept. He said: \"Who is this weeping woman?\" They said: \"Fāṭimah bt. ʿAdī.\" He said: \"You belong to ʿAʾidh b. ʿAmr.\" So he married her to his father and entrusted her to him."],[15120,"Sumayr b. Zuhayr al-Jasri said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother Salamah b. Zuhayr went out as an emigrant to Allah ﷻ and His Messenger, and the shepherds of your riding camels from Banu Ghifar met him and killed him during the sacred month. There had been blood between us and them in the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and asked them about that. They said: We found him driving your riding camels, so we wanted to seize him, but he resisted us, so we killed him. I do not know whether he made them swear an oath or believed them, except that he asked him about his brother's Islam but found no proof, so he paid him the blood money for the sanctity of the sacred month: fifty camels. He said: Those camels remained in his family's possession as the best livestock and the greatest in blessing."],[15146,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ expressing fear for his ummah regarding six traits: the rule of youths, the proliferation of police, bribery in judgment, the severing of family ties, the cheapening of blood, and a generation that takes the Qur'an as musical instruments, putting forward a man who is not the most knowledgeable among them nor the most virtuous, so that he may sing to them."],[15148,"So he informed him, and he gathered us together. He kept pressuring the Christian until he confessed. Then he ordered a piece of wood for him, and it was carved. Then he said: 'These people have a covenant, so fulfill your covenant with them as long as they fulfill theirs with you. But if they break it, then they have no covenant.' And he ordered for him to be crucified."],[15149,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us at midday, frightened, and said: 'Obey me as long as I am among you, and hold fast to the Book of God: make lawful what it makes lawful and forbid what it forbids.'"],[15150,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Visit the sick and follow funerals.'"],[15179,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: “War is deception.”"],[15180,"To the Messenger of God ﷺ: “My companion whom you saw with me bought a bow and gave it to me as a gift—should I take it from him?” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “No.” Then he waited until the beginning of the year, came back to him and said, “O Messenger of God ﷺ, should I take it?” He said: “No.” Then he waited until the beginning of the next year and said, “Should I take that bow, O Messenger of God?” He said: “No.” He said, “Should I not take it, O Messenger of God, so that it remains with him?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do you want to meet God, O ʿAwf, on the Day of Resurrection with an ember from Hell between your shoulder blades?”"],[15181,"The Messenger of God ﷺ judged between two men. The one against whom judgment was given said, “God is sufficient for me, and how excellent a Trustee is He.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Bring him back”—or he said, “Call the man to me?”—and said: “God praises prudence and blames incapacity. When something”—or he said, “a matter”—“overwhelms you, say, ‘God is sufficient for me, and how excellent a Trustee is He.’”"],[15194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Beware of sins that are not forgiven: misappropriation—whoever misappropriates anything will bring it on the Day of Resurrection—and consuming usury. Whoever consumes usury will be raised on the Day of Resurrection insane, thrashing about.” Then he recited: “Those who consume usury do not stand except as one stands whom Satan has touched with madness.”"],[15195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was observing iʿtikaf in the last ten nights of Ramadan. When it was the night of the twenty-third, he said: “Whoever would like to stand in prayer with us this night, let him stand in my place until a third of the night had passed.” Then he left, and I walked with him to Qutaybah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would lead us in prayer this night? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is enough for a man to stand with the imam until he departs; the standing of a night will be recorded for him.”"],[15196,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Storytellers are three: a ruler, one commanded, or a conceited boaster.”"],[15197,"I heard ʿAwf b. Malik say: I stood with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he began by using the toothstick, then performed ablution, then stood and prayed. I stood with him. He began and opened the recitation from al-Baqarah; he did not pass by a verse of mercy without stopping and asking, nor pass by a verse of punishment without stopping and seeking refuge. Then he bowed and remained bowing for the length of his standing, saying in his bowing: “Glory be to the Possessor of might, dominion, pride, and greatness.” Then he recited Al ʿImran, then surah by surah, doing the same."],[15201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of your leaders are those whom you love and who love you, and upon whom you invoke blessings and who invoke blessings upon you. The worst of your leaders are those whom you hate and who hate you, and whom you curse and who curse you.” We said: O Messenger of Allah, should we not then oppose them in that case? He said: “No, as long as they establish the prayer among you. Whoever has a ruler appointed over him and sees from him something of disobedience to Allah, let him hate what he does of disobedience to Allah, but he should not withdraw his hand from obedience.”"],[15202,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Dreams are of three kinds: among them are terrifying things from Satan to sadden the son of Adam; among them are what a man is concerned with in his waking state and sees in his sleep; and among them is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood.” I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: “I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[15203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O ʿAwf, count six things before the Hour: the first of them is my death; then the one that follows it is the conquest of Jerusalem; then the one that follows it is a death that will befall my ummah in Syria and will consume them like the sudden death of sheep; then the one that follows it is that wealth will overflow among you until a man is given a hundred dinars and remains dissatisfied with them; then the one that follows it is a trial that will occur among you and no Arab household will remain but it will enter it; then the one that follows it is that the Banu al-Asfar will make a peace treaty with you, and at the end of it they will gather eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand men.”"],[15204,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Among them are the abdal, and by them you are granted victory and by them you are given provision.\""],[15205,"He entered the mosque leaning on Dhu Kalaʿ while Kaʿb was telling stories to the people. ʿAwf said to Dhu Kalaʿ: \"Will you not forbid this nephew of yours from what he is doing? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No one tells stories to the people except a ruler, one commanded, or a boaster.'\""],[15209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Before the Dajjal there will be years of deception, in which rain will be abundant and vegetation will be scarce, the truthful will be disbelieved, the liar will be believed, the treacherous will be trusted, the trustworthy will be suspected, and the ruwaybidah will speak in them.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?\" He said: \"One to whom no heed is paid.\""],[15212,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to avarice, and from a desire that reverts to greed, and from greed that leads to what is not desired.\""],[15213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Jews split into seventy-one sects, the Christians split into seventy-two sects, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, my ummah will certainly split into seventy-three sects: one in Paradise and seventy-two in the Fire.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they?\" He said: \"The main body.\""],[15214,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with six or seven or eight men. He said: \"Give me your pledge.\" We pledged to him, and he took from us what he took from the women. Then he followed that with a light word and said: \"Do not ask people for anything.\""],[15215,"You have hastened its reward, and I will not eat it. Abu ʿUbaydah said the same. The Prophet ﷺ preceded me, and when he saw me he said: \"O owner of the camel.\""],[15218,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted with us for rest one night, and each one of us spread out his forearm on his mount's forearm. I woke up part of the night, and there was the Prophet's she-camel with no one in front of it. I set out looking for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and found Muadh b. Jabal and Abdullah b. Qays standing. I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' They said, 'We do not know, except that we heard a sound at the top of the valley,' like the sound of a millstone. It was not long before the Prophet ﷺ came to us and said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of intercession.' He said, 'You are among the people of my intercession.' Then we went together racing to the people, and found the people alarmed and missing their Prophet. He said: 'A messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between half of my nation entering Paradise and intercession, so I chose intercession.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we adjure you by Allah and by companionship to make us among the people of your intercession.' When they gathered around him, he said: 'I call you to witness that my intercession is for whoever of my nation dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[15222,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My intercession is for whoever of my nation dies without associating anything with Allah.'"],[15223,"The Prophet ﷺ judged between two men, and the one against whom judgment was given said, 'Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Bring the man back to me,' and said, 'What did you say?' So he told him. Then he said: 'Allah blames for incapacity, but you must be diligent. If a matter overwhelms you, say: Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'"],[15227,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day: 'I have come to know the last person of Paradise to enter Paradise. He used to ask Allah to keep him away from the Fire, but he did not ask for Paradise. When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, and he remains between that, he will say, \"O Lord, what is there for me here?\" He will say, \"This is what you used to ask Me for, O son of Adam.\" He will say, \"Yes, O Lord.\" While he is like that, a tree from the gate of Paradise appears to him, extending inside Paradise. He will say, \"O Lord, bring me near this tree so that I may eat from its fruit and shade myself in its shade.\" He will say, \"O son of Adam, did you not used to ask Me?\" He will say, \"O Lord, who is like You?\" He will keep seeing something better than something else and asking, until it is said to him, \"Go, and you will have what your feet walk over and what your eyes see.\" So he will walk until his feet are tired. He gestured with his hand and said, \"This and this.\" Then it is said, \"This is for you, and the like of it with it.\" He said: He will be pleased, so much so that He will give him something He has not given anyone among the people of Paradise. He will say, \"If I were permitted, I would feed the people of Paradise food and drink and clothing from what Allah has given me, and it would not diminish anything for me.\""],[15228,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"For one of you to have his belly filled with pus from his pubic area to his throat, churning, is better for him than to have it filled with poetry.\""],[15229,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one should relate stories to the people except a commander, one commanded to do so, or a schemer.\""],[15230,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military expedition. A man said, 'I will go out with you on condition that you give me a share of the spoils.' Then he said, 'By Allah, I do not know whether you will gain spoils or not, but give me something fixed.' So I gave him three dinars. We went on the expedition and obtained spoils. I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'I find for him in this world and the Hereafter nothing but these three dinars that he took.'"],[15232,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said to him: \"Hold on to six things before the Hour\" - the hadith."],[15233,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “My community is three thirds: a third will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment; a third will be given an easy reckoning, then will enter Paradise; and a third will be purged and exposed. Then the angels will come and say, ‘We found them saying, “There is no god but Allah alone,”’ and Allah will say, ‘They have spoken the truth; there is no god but Me. Admit them into Paradise for saying, “There is no god but Allah alone.” And carry their sins upon the people who denied the truth.’ This is the verse in which Allah, Exalted is He, said: {and they will surely carry their own burdens and other burdens along with their own burdens} and its confirmation is in the verse in which He mentioned the angels. Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He, said: {Then We made those whom We chose from among Our servants inherit the Book} and He made them three groups, and they are all categories: {among them is one who wrongs himself}—this is the one who is exposed and purged; {and among them is one who is moderate}—he is the one given an easy reckoning; {and among them is one who is foremost in good deeds by Allah’s permission}—this is the one who enters Paradise without reckoning or punishment. By Allah’s permission they will all enter it together, with no distinction made between them. {They will be adorned therein with bracelets of gold and pearls, and their clothing therein will be silk. And they will say, “Praise be to Allah who has removed from us sorrow. Indeed, our Lord is Forgiving and Appreciative—He who has settled us in the home of permanence out of His bounty. Neither fatigue will touch us therein, nor will weariness touch us therein.” And those who disbelieve will have the fire of Hell; neither will it be decreed for them that they die, nor will its punishment be lightened for them. Thus do We recompense every ungrateful one.}”"],[15234,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a tent of his and said, “O Messenger of Allah, may I enter?” He said, “Enter.” I said, “All of me?” He said, “All of you.” Then he said: “Hold fast to six things that will occur before the Hour. The first of them is the death of your Prophet,” and I wept. “Then the conquest of the Holy House (Jerusalem); then a tribulation that will enter every house of hair and clay; then wealth will overflow among you until a man will be given a hundred dinars and will be displeased with it; then a plague that will be among people like the quʿāṣ of sheep; and then a truce between you and the Banū al-Aṣfar, but they will betray you and march against you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand.”"],[15235,"My father’s delegation came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him as a young boy. He ordered two cloaks for each man and ordered one cloak for me. When we departed, one of the men sold me one of his two cloaks, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing two cloaks. He looked at me and said, “Where did you get this?” I said, “I bought them from so-and-so.” He said, “You were more entitled to it than he, since he squandered what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given him.”"],[15236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, forgive the Anṣār, the sons of the Anṣār, the sons of the sons of the Anṣār, and the clients of the Anṣār.”"],[15237,"The Banū Murra sent me with the zakāt of their wealth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I arrived before him in Madinah and found him sitting among the Emigrants and the Anṣār. I came to him with camels that were like the roots of the arṭā tree. He said, “Who is the man?” I said, “ʿIkrāsh b. Dhuʾayb.” He said, “Trace your lineage upward.” I said, “Son of Ḥurqūṣ b. Jaʿd b. ʿAmr b. al-Nazzāl b. Murra b. ʿUbayd, and these are the zakāt camels of the Banū Murra b. ʿUbayd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled then said, “These are the camels of my people; this is the zakāt of my people.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that they be branded with the brand of zakāt camels and added to them. Then he took my hand and went with me to the house of Umm Salama and said, “Is there any food?” A large bowl with tharīd and meat was brought to us, and we began to eat from it. I began to move my hand around its sides, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his left hand over my right hand and said, “O ʿIkrāsh, eat from one place, for it is one food.” Then a tray was brought to us containing different kinds of fresh dates. I began eating from what was in front of me, while the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved about the tray. Then he said, “O ʿIkrāsh, eat from wherever you wish, for it is not one kind.” Then water was brought to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his hands and wiped his face, forearms, and head with the moisture of his palms, then said, “O ʿIkrāsh, this is the ablution for what fire has changed.”"],[15240,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Hour will not come until a man from the clients rules over the people; he will be called Jahjāh.”"],[15241,"ʿAkkāf b. Wadāʿa al-Hilālī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?” He said, “No.” He said, “Nor a slave girl?” He said, “No.” He said, “And you are healthy and well-off?” He said, “Yes, praise be to Allah.” He said, “Then you are among the brothers of the devils. Either you will be one of the monks of the Christians, and then you are one of them, or you will be one of us, and then do as we do. For part of our sunna is marriage. The worst of you are your unmarried, and the most contemptible of your dead are your unmarried. Do you seek to entice the devils? He has no weapon against the righteous among men and women more effective than celibacy, except for the married—those are the purified, the ones kept free from indecency. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf! They are the female companions of David, the female companions of Joseph, and the female companions of Kursuf.” ʿAṭiyya said, “Who is Kursuf, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “A man among the Children of Israel who lived on one of the coasts of the sea, fasting by day and standing in prayer by night, never slackening in fasting or prayer. After that he disbelieved in Allah the Almighty because of a woman he fell in love with, and he abandoned the worship of his Lord, Mighty and Exalted. Then Allah reached him despite what had passed from him, and Allah turned to him in mercy. Woe to you, O ʿAkkāf! Marry, for you are among the sinners.” ʿAkkāf said, “I will not leave, O Messenger of Allah, until you marry me to whomever you wish.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I have married you, in the name of Allah and with His blessing, to Karīma bt. Kulthūm al-Ḥimyarī.”"],[15242,"Some people made noise near the Prophet ﷺ, and one of his companions said, “O Messenger of Allah, if only you would send someone to them to forbid them from this.” He said, “If I sent someone to them and forbade them from going to al-Ḥajūn, some of them would still go there even if they had no need of it.”"],[15243,"He requested a piece of land from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Wādī al-Qurā, and today it is called Buwayra of ʿUtayr.” He said, “And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he camped at Tabūk and prayed in Wādī al-Qurā.”"],[15258,"He wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and began with himself."],[15259,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Learn from your lineage that which connects you to your relatives, for maintaining family ties is a source of love for your family, wealth, and a means of prolonging your life.\""],[15260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this foul tree should not come near our mosque,\" meaning garlic."],[15265,"To his right, and I did not wait long before a woman came and stood behind the two of them. The young man said the takbir, so the two of them said the takbir. Then he bowed, so the two of them bowed. Then he prostrated, so the two of them prostrated. I said: \"O Abbas, a great matter!\" Al-Abbas said: \"A great matter indeed. Do you know the young man?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"He is Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew. Do you know who the woman is?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"This is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. Abd al-Uzza, the mistress of the women of Quraysh, the wife of my nephew. And this is Ali b. Abi Talib, my nephew.\" My nephew claims that his Lord, the Lord of the heavens and the earth, commanded him with this religion. By Allah, I do not know anyone on the face of the earth upon this religion other than these three.\""],[15288,"We entered upon al-Hasan during the severe pain that had afflicted him. A man said to him, 'I feel sorry for you for what I see.' He said, 'Brother, do not. By Allah, whatever is dearer to me is dearer to Allah. He said: {Whatever affliction befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.} So this is what my hands have earned. Then afterward the pardon of my Lord ﷻ will come to me in what remains.'"],[15289,"From Sabrah b. Ma'bad, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: A group of people from the common folk gathered with Mu'awiyah. He said, 'Let each man among you narrate a noble deed of his people and what virtue was among them.' The people narrated until the narration reached a young man from Juhaynah, and he narrated a narration but was unable to complete it. 'Imran b. al-Husayn turned to him and said, 'Speak, O brother of Juhaynah, with your mouth entirely, and I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Juhaynah are from me and I am from them. They became angry for my anger and pleased for my pleasure. I become angry for their anger and pleased for their pleasure. Whoever angers them has angered me, and whoever angers me has angered Allah.\"' Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan said, 'You have lied. The narration only came concerning Quraysh.' He said..."],[15324,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said to a man: “Did you fast any of the middle days of this month, meaning Shaʿbān?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then when you break your fast of Ramadan, fast one or two days.”"],[15325,"Part of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: “O Allah, forgive me for what I have done mistakenly, what I have done deliberately, what I have concealed, what I have declared openly, and what I have done out of ignorance.”"],[15326,"“Mutʿah is in the Book of Allah; the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid it, and no prohibition concerning it was revealed.” He said: “A man expressed his opinion about it to whatever extent he did.” The wording is that of the hadith of ʿĀrim. ʿĀrim and Khālid b. Khidāsh said: Saʿīd al-Barrād, and he is Ibn Abī Khayrah. Ibrāhīm b. al-Ḥasan said in his hadith: “He did not forbid it,” and did not mention the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[15327,"“The Prophet ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves and neither succeeded nor prospered.”"],[15334,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proclaimed the talbiyah for Ḥajj and ʿUmrah.”"],[15335,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said: “We performed Tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice.” He said: “A man expressed his opinion as he wished.”"],[15336,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, sincerely from his heart”—and he gestured with his hand toward the skin of his chest—“Allah will make his flesh forbidden to the Fire.”"],[15337,"\"On the Day of Judgment, the best of Allah's servants are those who constantly praise Him, and then a group of my ummah will never cease to fight against those who provoke them from the people of polytheism until they fight against the Dajjal.\""],[15338,"“I am narrating to you a hadith. If I recover from this pain of mine, do not relate it; and if I pass on my way, then relate it if you see fit, or leave it. We performed Tamattuʿ with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not forbid it to us until he died.” He said: “A man sees it according to his own opinion.”"],[15357,"It was said, “O Messenger of Allah, are the people of Paradise known from the people of the Fire?” He said, “Yes.” It was said, “Then for what do the workers act?” He said, “Act, for everyone is facilitated toward that for which he was created.”"],[15363,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum.” He returned the greeting, and the man sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Ten.” Then another came and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Llāh.” He returned the greeting, and the man sat down. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Twenty.” Then another came and said, “Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Llāh wa barakātuh.” He returned the greeting and said, “Thirty.”"],[15364,"He said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see the effect of His blessing upon him.”"],[15367,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “People will come out of the Fire through the intercession of the intercessors and enter Paradise, and they will be called the Jahannamīs.”"],[15371,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will bring out of the Fire a people by my intercession; they will be called the Jahannamiyyun.\""],[15372,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ, and they traveled through the night until, when they were near dawn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted for a rest, and sleep overcame them until the sun rose. The first to wake from his sleep was Abu Bakr, and no one would wake the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his sleep until the Prophet ﷺ woke on his own. Then ʿUmar woke and did something near his head; he began saying takbir and raising his voice until the Prophet ﷺ woke. When he saw that the sun had risen, he said: \"Depart.\" He traveled with us until the sun became bright, then he dismounted and led us in prayer. One man from the group withdrew and did not pray with us. When he finished, he said: \"O so-and-so, what prevented you from praying with us?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" So he commanded him to perform tayammum with clean earth, and he prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me ahead with a small group of riders to search for water, for we had become severely thirsty. While we were traveling, we came upon a woman with her legs dangling between two water skins. We said to her: \"Where is water?\" She said: \"Alas, alas, there is no water.\" We said: \"How far are you from water?\" She said: \"A day and a night.\" We said: \"Come with us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She said: \"And what is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" We did not give her any choice in the matter until we brought her before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We opened the two spouts and drank, forty thirsty men, until we were satisfied, and we filled every water skin and vessel we had. Then he said to us: \"Bring whatever you have.\" We gathered for her bits of bread and dates until we made a bundle for her. He said: \"Go and feed this to your family, and know that we have not taken anything from your water.\" When she came to her people, she said: \"We have met the most enchanting of people, or he is a prophet as they claimed.\" So Allah guided that tribe through that woman, and she and they embraced Islam."],[15373,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its inhabitants are the poor and needy, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its inhabitants are women.\""],[15374,"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never ate his fill of a morning or evening meal until he met Allah, Mighty and Exalted."],[15421,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Dajjal will emerge from the direction of Isfahan.”"],[15422,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Dajjal has eaten food and walked in the markets.”"],[15423,"This verse was revealed: “O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing,” while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey. Some of the people were dozing and some had dispersed, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his voice reciting it, and they gathered around the Prophet ﷺ, saying the Hour had come. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it and said, “Do you know which day that is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That is when Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, says to Adam: ‘Arise, O Adam, and send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He says, ‘What is the delegation of the Fire?’ He says, ‘Send forth from every thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.’” The people were struck silent, none of them showing even a tooth. He then said, “Work and rejoice, for you are among mankind but like a black mark on a camel’s back, or like a spot on a beast’s foreleg.” Then he said, “Know that you are alongside two creations that never enter anything without multiplying it: Yaʾjuj and Maʾjuj, along with those of the children of Iblis who perished.”"],[15424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[15425,"A man freed six slaves of his at the time of his death, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them and freed two of them."],[15426,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade mutilation. He would say: “Mutilation includes a man’s swearing that he will perform Hajj walking barefoot and on foot. Whoever swears to any of that, let him expiate for his oath and then ride.”"],[15427,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he made a stop for us to rest until the end of the night. We awoke with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the sun had risen. He said, “Depart! Depart!” So we departed until the sun was in the middle of the sky; then he dismounted, ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer. Each man among us prayed two rakʿahs, then he led us in prayer. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, should we repeat it tomorrow at its proper time?” He said, “Allah forbids us from riba, and would He accept it from us?”"],[15430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah ﷻ has chosen this religion for Himself, and nothing befits your religion except generosity and good character, so adorn your religion with both of them.”"],[15435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not deliver a sermon to us except that he commanded us to give charity and forbade us from mutilation."],[15436,"From ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn and Abū Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about His saying: {And pleasant dwellings in the Gardens of ʿAdn}. He said, \"A palace in Paradise of pearl, in which are seventy mansions of red ruby; in every mansion seventy rooms of green emerald; in every room seventy couches; on every couch seventy beddings of every color; on every bedding a woman; in every room seventy tables; on every table seventy kinds of food; in every room seventy serving boys and serving girls. And the believer will be given strength enough to come to all of that in a single morning.\""],[15443,"\"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ spoke truth, and you lied.\""],[15444,"A man freed six slaves during his illness, so the Prophet ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and enslaved four."],[15451,"A man from the Ansar freed six heads at his death, and he did not own any others. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he called them and cast lots among them; he allowed two and returned four to slavery."],[15457,"He passed by a storyteller who was telling stories. When he finished, he asked him, and he said: Verily we belong to God and to Him we return. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Recite the Qur’an and ask God by it before a people come who recite the Qur’an and ask people by it.\""],[15472,"We performed tamattuʿ during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not forbid us from it, and God ﷻ did not reveal anything concerning it."],[15476,"A man freed six of his slaves at the time of his death, and he had no wealth besides them. “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew lots among them, freed two, and returned four to slavery.”"],[15477,"“Indeed the Prophet ﷺ flogged for wine with palm stalks and sandals, forty lashes.”"],[15480,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[15490,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There is no obedience to a creature in disobeying Allah.\""],[15498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it.'"],[15499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be four tribulations: a tribulation in which blood is deemed lawful, a second in which blood and wealth are deemed lawful, and a third in which blood, wealth, and private parts are deemed lawful.”"],[15500,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A man standing in a row in the cause of Allah is better than the worship of sixty years.”"],[15529,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever swears a binding oath falsely and deliberately, let him take his place in the Fire with his face.\""],[15530,"A man freed six slaves at his death when he had no property besides them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ drew lots among them: he kept four as slaves and freed two."],[15555,"That when the death of the Negus reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, “Your brother the Negus has died, so pray over him.” He stood and prayed over him with the people behind him."],[15565,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Your brother al-Najashi has died, so pray over him.”"],[15575,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade hantam jars."],[15592,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God does not accept a prayer without purification, nor a charity from stolen wealth.\""],[15593,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would narrate to us at night about the Children of Israel, and we would not get up except for a great prayer."],[15600,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Makkah, he stayed there for eighteen nights praying with the people of Makkah two rak'ahs except for Maghrib. Then he would say: \"O people of Makkah, complete your prayer, for we are a traveling people.\""],[15629,"We were with the Prophet of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his voice with these two verses: “O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nurses.” When we heard that, we urged on our mounts, knowing he was about to say something. When they gathered around him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know which day that is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That is the day when Adam will call out, and his Lord will call him, saying, ‘Adam, arise and send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He will say, ‘O Lord, how many are to be sent to the Fire?’ He will say, ‘Of every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.’” When they heard that, they were struck speechless, so much so that none of them showed a smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what had come upon them, he smiled and said, “Work and receive glad tidings, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, with you are two creatures that have never been with anyone except that they made them numerous.” They said, “Who, O Prophet of Allah?” He said, “Gog and Magog, and those who perished among the children of Adam, and Iblis.” Then he said, “Work and receive glad tidings, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among the people only like a mole on the side of a camel, or a mark on the foreleg of a beast.”"],[15637,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “All of modesty is good.”"],[15640,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “What do you think about what people do today and toil in — is it something that was decreed for them and has passed from a predestination that preceded, or is it in what they will face from what their Prophet brought them and with which the proof was established against them?” He said, “Rather, it is something that was decreed for them and has passed.” He said, “Then why do they work?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever Allah created for one of the two stations, He grants him success for its action.” He said, “The confirmation of that is in the Book of Allah: ‘By the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness.’”"],[15641,"ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn said: We were discussing righteousness in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began to narrate to us, saying: “Among the nations before you there was a devoted worshiper, an owner of a hermitage, called Jurayj. He had a mother who would come to him and call him, and he would look down at her and speak to her. One day she came to him while he was in his prayer, facing it, and she called him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imitated her, placing his hand on his forehead. She kept calling him, raising her head and placing her hand on her forehead: “O Jurayj, O Jurayj,” three times, each time three times. All the while Jurayj said, “O Lord, my mother or my prayer?” She became angry and said, “O Allah, do not let Jurayj die until he looks at the faces of prostitutes.” He said, “The daughter of the king of the village became pregnant and gave birth to a boy. They said to her, ‘Who did this to you? Who is your companion?’ She said, ‘He is the owner of the hermitage, Jurayj.’ He was unaware until he heard the axes at the base of his hermitage. He began asking them, ‘Woe to you, what is the matter with you?’ but they did not answer him. When he saw that, he took a rope and let himself down, and they began dragging him by the nose, beating him, and saying, ‘Hypocrite, you deceive people with your deeds!’ He said to them, ‘Woe to you, what is the matter with you?’ They said, ‘You are the companion of the king’s daughter whom you got pregnant.’ He said, ‘What did she do?’ They said, ‘She gave birth to a boy.’ He said, ‘Is the boy alive?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Turn away from me.’ So they turned away, and he prayed two rakʿahs, then went to a tree, took a branch from it, then came to the boy while he was in his cradle, struck him with that branch, and said, ‘O tyrant, who is your father?’ He said, ‘My father is so-and-so the shepherd.’ They said, ‘If you wish, we will rebuild your hermitage with gold, and if you wish, with silver.’ He said, ‘Restore it as it was.’ Abū Ḥarb claimed that none spoke in the cradle except three: ʿĪsā ibn Maryam, the witness of Yūsuf, and the companion of Jurayj.”"],[15644,"A man freed six slaves at his death, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him, so he freed two and kept four as slaves."],[15649,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of al-khadhf (throwing pebbles with the fingers), for it breaks the tooth, puts out the eye, and does not harm the enemy.”"],[15654,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to God.”"],[15655,"He informed me of the people most hated by the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Keep it secret for me until I die? I said: Yes. He said: “The people most hated by the Messenger of God ﷺ were Banū Ḥanīfah, Banū Umayyah, and Thaqīf.”"],[15658,"The Prophet ﷺ died while he disliked three tribes: Banu Umayyah, Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif."],[15682,"Husayn came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Muhammad, ʿAbd al-Muttalib was better for his people than you: he fed them liver and hump, while you slaughter them.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What did Allah will that you say?” He said: “What do you command me to say?” He said: “Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul, and resolve for me the most upright of my affairs.”"],[15686,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a man has a right over another man and grants him a delay until its term, it is charity for him. If he grants him a delay after its term, then for each day it is charity for him.”"],[15687,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Indeed, I do not fear for Quraysh except their own selves.” I said: “And what is that?” He said: “Greedy and arrogant. If you live long, you will see them as the most greedy and arrogant of people, until you see the people among them like sheep between two watering-troughs: once to this one and once to that one.”"],[15688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day: “The prophets were presented to me. A prophet would come with no one but one man, and a prophet would come with no one but two men, and a prophet would come with no one but a small group. Then I looked and saw a great multitude, and I thought they were my community. When they drew near, they were the people of Musa. Then it was said to me: 'Look.' I looked and said: 'Who are these?' It was said: 'These are your community.' I rejoiced and was glad. Then it was said: 'Look.' I looked and saw another great multitude. It was said: 'These are your community.' I rejoiced and was glad. Then it was said to me: 'With these are seventy thousand of your community who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and the Muslims said: 'Who are these seventy thousand?' They agreed that they were those who were born in Islam and had not known anything of shirk. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out while we were on that, and he said: “They are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not practice augury from birds, and upon their Lord they rely.” Then ʿUkkashah stood and said: “Invoke Allah to make me one of them.” He said: “O Allah, make him one of them.” Then another man stood and said: “O Messenger of Allah, invoke Allah to make me one of them.” He said: “ʿUkkashah has preceded you to it.”"],[15690,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves His servant, the believer who is poor, abstaining from begging, and has dependents.\""],[15691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ loves the chaste, abstaining from begging, who has dependents.\""],[15692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Go raid the tribe of so-and-so with so-and-so.\" He said: We lined up the men, and the women were behind the men. Then when they returned, a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, may Allah forgive you.\" He said, \"Have you done something new?\" He said, \"When the people were defeated, I caught a man from the people and the women, and he said, 'I am a Muslim,' or he said, 'I have embraced Islam,' but I killed him. By Allah, I did not do it.\" He did not seek forgiveness for him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For what do I fight the people except for Islam? By Allah, I will not seek forgiveness for you,\" or as he said. He said: He died later, and his clan buried him, but in the morning the earth threw him out. Then they buried him again and guarded him, but the earth threw him out a second time. Then they said, \"Perhaps someone came while you were sleeping and took him out.\" So they buried him a third time and guarded him, but the earth threw him out a third time. When they saw that, they left him, or as he said."],[15693,"\"The Prophet ﷺ died when he was sixty-three years old.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3654)"],[15696,"I heard Abu Raja' al-Utaridi say, \"The Prophet ﷺ was sent while I was a small boy, calling to Paradise.\""],[15697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until he entered an orchard belonging to one of the Ansar, and he was drawing water in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"What will you give me if I water your orchard?\" He said, \"I strive to water it, but I cannot do that.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Will you give me one hundred dates that I choose from your dates?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the bucket, and it was not long before he watered it, until the man said, \"My orchard has been flooded.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ chose one hundred dates from his dates, and he and his companions ate until they were full, then he returned to him one hundred dates as he had taken from him."],[15698,"I witnessed Mu'awiya give al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad a donkey. A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called al-'Irbad b. Sariya stood up and said, \"What is it to you that you take it, and what is it to Mu'awiya that he gives it to you? It is as if I can see you on the Day of Resurrection carrying it on your neck with its head downwards.\""],[15699,"From al-'Irbad b. Sariya, who was a very old man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he loved to be taken in death. He used to supplicate, \"O Allah, my age has grown old and my bones have become weak, so take me to You.\" He said: While I was one day in the mosque of Damascus, there was a young man, one of the most handsome of men, wearing a green cloak, and he said, \"What is this that you supplicate with?\" I said, \"How should I supplicate, O son of my brother?\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, make my deeds good and let me reach my appointed term.\" I said, \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said, \"I am Riba'il, the one who removes sorrow from the hearts of the believers.\""],[15700,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us an exhortation that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so advise us.\" He said, \"I advise you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a black slave is placed over you. For whoever lives after me will see much difference. So hold firmly to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me, and bite onto it with the molar teeth. Beware of newly invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.\""],[15701,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ exhorted them one day after the dawn prayer, and the eyes shed tears and the hearts trembled. A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?\" He said, \"I advise you to fear Allah, and to hear and obey, even if a black slave is placed over you. For whoever of you lives after me will see much difference. Beware of newly invented matters, for they are misguidance. Hold firmly to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me, biting onto it with the molar teeth.\""],[15702,"That he heard ʿIrbaḍ b. Sāriya al-Sulamī saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us with an exhortation that made the eyes weep and the hearts tremble. We said, “O Messenger of God, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us?” He said, “I have left you upon the clear white path; its night is like its day. None deviates from it after me but is destroyed. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement. So hold fast to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs. And you must obey, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Bite onto it with the molar teeth. Indeed, the believer is like a compliant camel: wherever it is led, it follows.”"],[15704,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and admonished the people, encouraged them, and warned them, and said what God willed to be. He said: “Worship God and do not associate anything with Him. Obey those whom God has placed in authority over you, and do not dispute authority with its people, even if he is a black slave. Hold fast to what you know of the Sunnah of your Prophet and the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs, and bite onto it with the molar teeth.”"],[15705,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us one morning and admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said, “O Messenger of God, you have admonished us with the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever remains after me will see severe disagreement. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs, bite onto it with the molar teeth, and beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is misguidance.”"],[15706,"The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us after the morning prayer with a profound exhortation that made the eyes weep and the hearts tremble. A man from among his Companions said, “O Messenger of God, this is the admonition of one bidding farewell.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever of you lives will see much disagreement, so beware of newly invented matters, for they are innovation. Whoever of you reaches that, let him hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth.”"],[15707,"The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said, “O Messenger of God, it is as if it is the admonition of one bidding farewell, so give us a covenant.” He said: “I enjoin upon you fear of God, listening and obedience, even if it is an Abyssinian slave. Whoever of you lives after me will see much disagreement. So hold fast to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, divinely guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is misguidance.”"],[15708,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite the musabbiḥāt before he slept, and he said: “In them there is a verse that is better than a thousand verses.”"],[15709,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The martyrs and those who died on their beds will dispute before our Lord concerning those who died in the plague. The martyrs will say, ‘Our brothers, they were killed as we were killed.’ Those who died on their beds will say, ‘Our brothers, they died on their beds as we died.’ God will judge between them and say, ‘Look at the wounds of the plague-stricken.’ If their wounds resemble the wounds of the martyrs, they are of them and with them. So they look at the wounds of the plague-stricken and find that they resemble the wounds of the martyrs, and they join them.”"],[15710,"From the Prophet ﷺ that one day he stood among the people and said: “O people, soon you will be made into armies: an army in Syria, an army in Iraq, and an army in Yemen.” Ibn Ḥawāla said, “O Messenger of God, if I reach that time, choose for me.” He said: “I choose Syria for you, for it is the best land of the Muslims and the chosen portion of God from His lands. He gathers to it His chosen ones from His creation. Whoever refuses, let him go to his Yemen and drink from its ponds, for God has guaranteed me Syria and its people.”"],[15711,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ invited him to the pre-dawn meal in Ramadan and said: “Come to the blessed meal.” And I heard him say: “O God, teach Muʿāwiya the Book and reckoning, and protect him from the punishment.”"],[15712,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the servant of God and the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam ﷺ was still clay in his form. I will inform you about that: the supplication of my father Abraham, the glad tidings of Jesus, and the vision of my mother that she saw. In the same way the mothers of the prophets see visions. Indeed, the mother of the Messenger of God ﷺ, when she gave birth to me, saw a light that illuminated for her the palaces of Syria.”"],[15713,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “I am the servant of God and the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam ﷺ was still clay in his form. I will tell you about that: the supplication of my father Abraham, the glad tidings of Jesus, and the vision of my mother that she saw. In the same way the mothers of the prophets see visions.” And the mother of the Messenger of God ﷺ saw, when she gave birth, a light that illuminated from it the palaces of Syria."],[15714,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I am, with God in the Mother of the Book, the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still clay in his form. I will tell you its interpretation: the supplication of Abraham—the call, ‘And raise among them a Messenger from among themselves’—and the glad tidings of Jesus son of Mary, ‘And bringing good news of a Messenger who will come after me, whose name is Aḥmad,’ and the vision of my mother: she saw in her sleep that she gave birth to a light that illuminated from it the palaces of Syria.”"],[15715,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “This community will certainly crowd at the Basin like camels crowding when they come to drink for five.”"],[15716,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If I take from a servant his two precious ones while he is patient with them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise if he praises Me for them.”"],[15717,"The Lord ﷻ [said]: “If I seize from My servant his two precious ones while he is attached to them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise.”"],[15718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise. One of you says to his shepherd, ‘Go to the middle of the valley, for it is the most fertile and the most grassy.’”"],[15719,"I sold the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a young camel. I came to demand payment and said, “Pay me for my young camel.” He said, “Yes, I will certainly pay you.” He paid me and paid me well. Then a Bedouin came and said, “Pay me,” and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid him with an older camel. The Bedouin said, “This is better than my young camel, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The best of people are those who are best in repayment.”"],[15720,"He heard ʿIrbad b. Sariyah say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray for the first row three times and for the one after it once.”"],[15721,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once.” Maʿmar and ʿIkrimah did not mention Jubayr b. Nufayr in their hadith."],[15722,"“The Prophet ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once.” Hisham did not mention Jubayr b. Nufayr in the chain."],[15723,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for the first row three times and for the second once.”"],[15724,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every deed is cut off from its doer when he dies, except the one stationed in the way of Allah. His deeds will be increased for him and his provision will continue to be sent to him until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[15725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ admonished us one day with an eloquent admonition that made eyes shed tears and hearts tremble. A man among the Muslims said, “This seems like the admonition of one bidding farewell, so what do you enjoin upon us, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “I have left you upon the clear path; its night is like its day. No one among you will deviate from it after me except one who is destroyed. Whoever among you lives will see much disagreement, so beware of innovations, and adhere to my sunnah and the sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs; bite onto it with the molar teeth, and adhere to hearing and obedience, even if a slave is an Abyssinian.”"],[15726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah ﷻ says: ‘If I take the two precious ones of My servant while he is attached to them, I will not be satisfied for him with any reward less than Paradise if he praises Me for them.’”"],[15727,"\"From the Prophet ﷺ , he said: Allah the Almighty says, 'Those who love one another for My glory will be in my shade on a day when there is no shade except My shade.'\""],[15728,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, 'It is not lawful for you among predatory animals: any that has fangs, nor the domestic donkeys. And do not enter the houses of the People of the Book, and do not consume their wealth except what they give willingly. And do not strike—does any man among you think that he has become full, until he supposes, while reclining on his couch, saying: \"Allah ﷻ has not forbidden anything except in the Qur'an\"? Verily, by Allah, I have indeed narrated, commanded, and admonished.'"],[15729,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, when a man gives water to his wife, he is rewarded.' He (the narrator) said: 'So I went to her and gave her water, and I informed her of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[15730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever performs an obligatory prayer, he has an answered supplication; and whoever completes the Qur'an, he has an answered supplication.'"],[15731,"That the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade every fanged beast of prey, and every bird with talons, and he forbade al-mujaththama (animals tied up and used as targets), and that pregnant women be taken as concubines until they give birth to what is in their wombs."],[15732,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a hair from the booty and said: 'I have nothing of this except what one of you has, except the fifth, and it is returned to you. So return the needle and the thread. And beware of ghulūl (embezzlement from booty), for it is a disgrace and a shame.'"],[15733,"the Messenger of Allah forbade (the flesh of) domesticated donkeys on the Day of Khaibar. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4336)"],[15734,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade al-khulsa (snatching something quickly)."],[15735,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the slaughtered animals of the Christians and their festivals. He said: 'If you do not eat it, then feed me.'"],[15736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever licks the plate and licks his fingers, Allah will satisfy him in this world and the Hereafter.'"],[15737,"He is called al-Mandaqūn. He invited him to Islam, and the Christian mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and reviled him. So that was brought to ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ, and he sent for him and said: 'We have given them the covenant.' Ghurfah said: 'I seek refuge with Allah that we would give them covenants and pledges on condition that they harm us concerning Allah and His Messenger. We only gave them on condition that we leave them and their churches, that they say in them what they wish, and that we do not burden them beyond their capacity, and that we fight on their behalf, and that they be left to their own judgments—unless they come to us, and we judge between them by what Allah has revealed.' ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ said: 'You have spoken the truth.'"],[15738,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and the sacrificial camels were brought. He said: 'Call Abu Ḥasan for me.' So he called ʿAlī, and he said: 'Take the lower end of the spear,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took its upper end, and we slaughtered the sacrificial camels with it. When he finished, he mounted the mule and seated ʿAlī behind him."],[15739,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'There is no emigration after the conquest. It is only three: jihad, intention, and the gathering (on the Day of Resurrection).'"],[15740,"That they wanted to emigrate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but their fathers prevented them. They mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no emigration after the conquest. It is only jihad and intention.'"],[15741,"He is called Ghaylan b. Salama. He embraced Islam while he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them and leave six."],[15742,"Nafi' was a slave belonging to Ghaylan b. Salama, and he fled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam while Ghaylan was a polytheist. Then Ghaylan embraced Islam, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned his wala' to him."],[15743,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he said: \"If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the wife to prostrate to her husband.\""],[15744,"From Ghudayf or Abu Ghusayf, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever introduces satire in Islam, cut off his tongue.\""],[15745,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"If a man drinks wine, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, flog him; then if he repeats it, kill him.\""],[15746,"I mentioned Qays in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Qays; may Allah have mercy on Qays.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you invoke mercy on Qays?\" He said: \"Yes, for he followed the religion of my forefather Isma'il b. Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah. O Qays, protect Yemen! O Yemen, protect Qays! Qays are the horsemen of Allah on earth. By Him in whose hand is my soul, a time will come upon people when this religion has no helper other than Qays. Allah, exalted is He, has horsemen from the people of heaven who are marked, and horsemen from the people of earth who are taught. The horsemen of Allah from the people of earth are Qays. Qays is but an egg that split from us, the people of the House. Qays is the harm of Allah on earth—meaning the lion of Allah.\""],[15747,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of the food of my family except some donkeys I have.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth, for I only found repugnant the village-roving ones.\""],[15748,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"Nothing remains of my wealth except donkeys.\" He said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth; I only disliked for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15749,"Mis'ar said, and I think Ghalib is the one who asked the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth to feed my family except donkeys.\" He said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth, for I only forbid for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15750,"Abjar or the son of Abjar asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains of my wealth except donkeys.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Feed your family from the fat of your wealth; I only disliked for you the village-roving ones.\""],[15752,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a famine has befallen us, and the fattest of our wealth are donkeys.\" He said: \"Eat from the fattest of your wealth,\" and he said: \"I only found repugnant for you—or disliked for you—the village-grazing ones.\""],[15753,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a drought has befallen us, and the fattest of our wealth are donkeys.\" He said: \"Eat from the fattest of your wealth; I only found repugnant the village-roving ones.\""],[15754,"Some of the people were martyred in Syria on the day of Ajnadayn, and it is said on the day of Marj al-Suffar; both days were together in the year eighteen. He died when he was twenty-one years old."],[15755,"The Prophet ﷺ did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah, throwing seven pebbles while saying takbir with each pebble."],[15756,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him on the morning of Jam' (Muzdalifah), and he did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. He said: He threw it from below with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble: one takbir. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered and said: \"I have slaughtered here, and all of Mina is a place of slaughter, so slaughter in your dwellings.\""],[15757,"The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered near Jamrat al-Aqabah and said: \"I have slaughtered here, and all of Mina is a place of slaughter, so slaughter in your dwellings.\""],[15758,"From al-Fadl b. Abbas: \"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I did not stop hearing him say the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah. When he threw it, he stopped the talbiyah.\" The wording is from the hadith of al-Hasan b. al-Rabi'."],[15759,"The Prophet ﷺ said the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15760,"\"And by Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to walk with me the next morning after the gathering. A man from the Bedouins accompanied us, and he had his young daughter with him. While walking with the Prophet ﷺ , I became distracted and turned my face away from her. He continued to call me until he threw the pebble at the Jamarat.\""],[15761,"From al-Fadl b. Abbas, who was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on the morning of Muzdalifah: \"I did not stop hearing him say the tahlil (ihlal) until he reached the Jamrah. When he threw it, he stopped.\""],[15762,"That I should pray inside the Ka'bah? Whoever prays in it has left something behind him. But my brother told me that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered it, he fell prostrate between the two pillars, then sat down, and did not pray."],[15765,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him from Muzdalifah, and he did not cease saying the talbiyah until he threw Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[15822,"He was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he departed from Muzdalifah. A Bedouin came alongside him with a beautiful daughter of his. I began looking at her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept turning my face away from her. He did not cease reciting the talbiyah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[15824,"Al-Fadl b. al-‘Abbas was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ. The young man began glancing at the women and looking at them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept turning his face away with his hand from behind him. The young man kept glancing at the women, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O son of my brother, this is a day on which whoever controls his hearing, his sight, and his tongue will be forgiven.”"],[15828,"“He entered the Ka‘bah with the Prophet ﷺ while Bilal was at the door.” He said: “He did not pray,” while Bilal said: “He prayed.”"],[15834,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “Whoever wakes up in a state of major ritual impurity must not fast that day.” So my father sent to ‘A’ishah to ask her, and I went with him to her, and he asked her, and she said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wake up in a state of major ritual impurity without a wet dream, then he would wake up fasting.” So he returned to Marwan and told him, and he said: “Meet Abu Hurayrah and tell him.” He said: “He is my neighbor, and I dislike to confront him with what he dislikes.” He said: “I adjure you to go to him.” So he went to him and said: “O Abu Hurayrah, I disliked to confront you with what you dislike, but the governor adjured me.” So he told him, and he said: “Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas narrated it to me.”"],[15835,"Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas was asked: Did the Prophet ﷺ pray inside the House? He said: “No.”"],[15839,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in a desert and he performed the Asr prayer, and in front of him was a dog or a donkey belonging to us, and he did not forbid it or make us delay it.\""],[15842,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj or ‘Umrah or travel. He said: “Perform Hajj and ‘Umrah on behalf of your father.”"],[15846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not stand for any night prayer except that he used the siwak."],[15847,"That he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Muzdalifah until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah, and his mount did not lift a foot moving onward until he threw the pebbles at Jamrat al-‘Aqabah."],[15853,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stopped at a place during a journey or entered his house, he would not sit until he prayed two rakʿahs."],[15854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk, and the riding beasts became severely exhausted. They complained to him about that, and he saw that they were men who did not give their mounts rest. The Messenger of God ﷺ looked at a narrow pass through which the people were passing and stood at it while the people passed by, and he blew upon it and said, \"O God, make them carry in Your cause, for You carry the strong and the weak, the fresh and the dry, in sea and on land.\" So they remained strong, and we did not enter Madinah except while they were pulling at their reins."],[15855,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"God is more attentive to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Quran than the owner of a singing slave-girl is to his singing slave-girl.\""],[15897,"From Fadalah b. 'Ubayd that they were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition of theirs, and they acquired a necklace containing gold and jewels. They sold it for dinars. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Do not sell it like that,\" and he forbade them from that, and said: \"The jewels separately and the gold separately.\""],[15898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever abandons his brother for more than three days, he will be in the Fire, unless Allah rescues him by His generosity.\""],[15902,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for food. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, were you not fasting this day?' He said, 'Yes, but I vomited.'"],[15903,"He entered upon A'ishah and she brought out some hairs from the hair of the Prophet ﷺ, and it was red, dyed."],[15904,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Islam consists of three levels: a lower one, an upper one, and a chamber. The lower one is Islam, which the common Muslims have entered; none of them is asked but that he says, \"I am a Muslim.\" The upper one is the superiority of their deeds, some Muslims being better than others. As for the highest chamber, it is striving in the path of Allah; none attains it except the best of them.'"],[15905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The earth is Allah's earth and the servants are Allah's servants. Whoever revives dead land, it is his.'"],[15906,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Three are the barren ones: a leader who, if you do good, does not thank, and if you do wrong, does not forgive; a neighbor who, if he sees good, buries it, and if he sees evil, spreads it; and a wife who, if she is present with you, harms you, and if you are absent from her, betrays you.'"],[15907,"That they were supplications with which the Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate."],[15908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me, he said: 'Guard the five prayers.' I said, 'These are times in which I have occupations, so command me with a comprehensive matter that, if I do it, will suffice me.' He said, 'Guard the two afternoon prayers.' I said, 'What are the two afternoon prayers?' He said, 'A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.'"],[15909,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and whoever had an 'arif would stay with his 'arif, and whoever did not have an 'arif would stay in the Suffah. I stayed in the Suffah. A man called out to him on Friday, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, dates have burned our stomachs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Soon, or whoever of you lives, will be given platters in the morning and evening, and you will clothe the walls as the Ka'bah is veiled.'"],[15910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl on Friday, the day of 'Arafah, and the Day of Sacrifice."],[15911,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'What is lawful for us from dead meat?' He said, 'What is your food?' He said, 'We drink in the evening and drink in the morning.' He said, 'That is hunger,' and he permitted them dead meat in that situation. Abu Nu'aym said: 'Uqbah explained it to me, saying, 'A cup in the evening and a cup in the morning.'"],[15912,"'Abd al-Malik b. 'Ata' al-'Amiri al-Bakka'i brought out to us a letter from the Prophet ﷺ for them and said to us, 'Write it down,' but he did not dictate it to us. He claimed that the son of the daughter of al-Fujay' narrated to him: 'This is a letter from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to al-Fujay' and whoever follows him, that he has submitted, and whoever establishes prayer, gives zakah, obeys Allah and His Messenger, gives a fifth of the spoils, supports the Prophet of Allah, testifies to his Islam, and separates from the polytheists, he is secure with the security of Allah and Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[15913,"From Furāt b. Ḥayyān—and the Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered that he be killed, and he was a spy for Abū Sufyān and an ally—he passed by a circle of the Anṣār and said, \"I am a Muslim.\" A man among them said, \"O Messenger of God, he says, 'I am a Muslim.'\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Among you are men who reveal their faith to me; among them is al-Furāt b. Ḥayyān.\""],[15914,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the alliance of the pre-Islamic era. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Perhaps you are asking about the ally of Lakhm and Tamīm?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Islam only increases it in strength.\""],[15915,"He said to him, \"I would not go ahead of you while you are older than me and earlier in migration, and the mosque is your mosque.\" Furāt said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say something about you, so I will never go ahead of you.\" He said, \"Did you witness him on the day I came to him at al-Ṭāʾif and he sent me as a spy?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So Ḥanẓala went forward and led them in prayer. Then Furāt said, \"O Banū ʿAjlān, I put this man forward only because the Messenger of God ﷺ sent him as a spy to al-Ṭāʾif, and he came back and reported the news to him. He said, 'You have spoken the truth. Return to your dwelling, for you have been present tonight.' When he turned away, he said to us, 'Take this man and his like as your imams.'\""],[15916,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I fight with those of my people who come forward against those who turn away?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then when I turned away, he called me and said, \"Call them to Islam; if they refuse, then fight them.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, tell me about Sabaʾ: is it a man or a woman?\" He said, \"It is a man of the Arabs who had ten sons; six of them went south, and four went north. As for those who went south: al-Azd, Kinda, Madhḥij, al-Ashʿariyyūn, Ḥimyar, and Anmār, from whom are Bajīla. As for those who went north: ʿĀmila, Ghassān, Lakhm, and Judhām.\""],[15917,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, we have neighbors from Sabaʾ—people of might, dominion, and arrogance. Give me permission to call them to Islam; if they refuse, then give me permission to fight them with my people and those who obey me.\" So he gave him permission. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ had a change of mind and said, \"You mentioned the matter of Sabaʾ as you did. Call them to Islam; if they respond, accept from them and refrain from them; and if they refuse, do not confront them until my command comes to you.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, do you think Sabaʾ is a land or a woman?\" He said, \"It is neither a land nor a woman; rather, it is a man who fathered ten tribes. Six of them went south and four went north. The Yemenis are Madhḥij, al-Azd, Kinda, Ḥimyar, al-Ashʿariyyūn, and Anmār.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Anmār?\" He said, \"The father of Bajīla and Khathʿam. And four of them went north: Lakhm, Judhām, Ghassān, and ʿĀmila.\""],[15918,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, shall I not fight those of my people who turn back with those who come forward?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then it occurred to me, and I said, \"O Messenger of God, no—rather the people of Sabaʾ: they are mightier and stronger.\" So the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me and gave me permission to fight Sabaʾ. When I left him, God revealed concerning Sabaʾ what He revealed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"What has the Ghaṭafānī done?\" He sent to my dwelling and found that I had already departed, so he brought me back. When I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, I found him sitting among his companions. He said, \"Call the people. Whoever responds to you, accept from them; and whoever refuses, do not be hasty until you have spoken to me.\" A man among the people said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Sabaʾ? Is it a land or a woman?\" He said, \"It is not a land or a woman; rather, it is a man who fathered ten of the Arabs. Six of them went south and four went north. As for those who went north: Lakhm, Judhām, ʿĀmila, and Ghassān. As for those who went south: al-Azd, Kinda, Ḥimyar, al-Ashʿariyyūn, Anmār, and Madhḥij.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of God, what is Anmār?\" He said, \"They are those of whom are Bajīla and Khathʿam.\""],[15919,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Do you dislike your two days and the two days of Hamdān?\" He said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God—the destruction of family and clan.\" He said, \"Verily, it is better for those of you who remain.\""],[15920,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about Sabaʾ, saying, \"O Messenger of God, what is Sabaʾ? Is it a man, a mountain, or a valley?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No; rather, it is a man who fathered ten. Four went north and six went south. Those who went north: Lakhm, Judhām, ʿĀmila, and Ghassān. Those who went south: Ḥimyar, Madhḥij, al-Azd, Kinda, al-Ashʿariyyūn, and Anmār, from whom is Bajīla.\""],[15922,"From ʿUrwa, in naming those who witnessed the ʿAqaba pledge from the Anṣār, then from Banū Bayāḍa: Farwa b. ʿAmr; and he witnessed Badr."],[15923,"From Jābir: \"The Prophet ﷺ used to send a man from the Anṣār of Banū Bayāḍa called Farwa b. ʿAmr, and he would estimate the fruit of the people of Madinah.\""],[15924,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ used to send Farwa b. ʿAmr to estimate the palm trees. When he entered a garden, he would calculate what was in it from the branches, then strike some of them against others according to what he saw in them, and he would not err.\""],[15925,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim while I have two sisters as wives.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Divorce whichever of them you wish.”"],[15926,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I had two sisters whom I had married in the Jāhiliyyah. He said, “When you return, divorce one of them.”"],[15927,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim while I have two sisters as wives.” He said, “Divorce whichever of them you wish.”"],[15928,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, we are owners of grapevines and vineyards, and the prohibition of wine has come down. What should we do?” He said, “Make them into raisins.” They said, “What should we do with the raisins?” He said, “Soak them in the morning and drink in the evening, and soak them in the evening and drink in the morning.” They said, “O Messenger of God, should we not leave it until it ferments?” He said, “Do not put it in large jars or gourds; put it in water skins, for if it is delayed beyond its pressing, it becomes vinegar.” I said, “O Prophet of God, we are as you know, our region is as you know, and we live among those you know. Who is our guardian?” He said, “God and His Messenger.”"],[15930,"“We brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ the head of al-ʿAbsī, the liar.”"],[15931,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, “Our land is cold and we have vineyards. What should we do with them?” He said, “Make them into raisins.” Then he mentioned something similar."],[15932,"I came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “We make food and drink and feed it to our cousins.” He said, “Does it intoxicate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “It is forbidden.” When I was taking leave of him, I mentioned it to him and said, “O Prophet of God, they will not be able to abstain from it.” He said, “Whoever cannot abstain from it, strike his neck.”"],[15933,"I said, “O Messenger of God, we are as you know, our region is as you know, and we have settled among those you know. Who is our guardian?” He said, “God and His Messenger.” He said, “I said, ‘Sufficient for me.’”"],[15934,"From Ibn al-Daylamī, who was the nephew of the Negus and had served the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever recites ‘Say: He is God, the One’ one hundred times in prayer or otherwise, God will record for him a clearance from the Fire.”"],[15935,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There will be a sound in Ramadan.” They said, “O Messenger of God, at its beginning, or in its middle, or at its end?” He said, “No, rather in the middle of Ramadan, when the night of the middle is the night of Friday, there will be a sound from heaven by which seventy thousand will be thunderstruck, seventy thousand will be struck dumb, seventy thousand will be blinded, and seventy thousand will be made deaf.” They said, “O Messenger of God, who among your community will be safe?” He said, “Whoever stays in his house, seeks refuge through prostration, and raises his voice in glorifying God with takbīr, then another sound will follow it. The first sound is the sound of Gabriel, and the second is the sound of Satan. The sound is in Ramadan, the turmoil is in Shawwāl, the tribes are separated in Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and raids are made on pilgrims in Dhū al-Ḥijjah and in Muḥarram. And what is Muḥarram? Its beginning is a trial for my community, and its end is a joy for my community. A riding camel in that time with its saddle will be enough for a believer to escape from a village that yields a hundred thousand.”"],[15936,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque when his gaze fixed upon a man walking in the mosque. He said, “O so-and-so.” He replied, “At your service, O Messenger of God.” He did not dispute the speech except to say, “O Messenger of God.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Do you testify that I am the Messenger of God?” He said, “No.” He said, “Do you read the Torah?” He said, “Yes, and the Gospel.” He said, “And the Qur’an?” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if I wished I could read it.” Then he adjured him, “Do you find me in the Torah and the Gospel?” He said, “I find you, your like, your appearance, and your emergence. We had hoped that it would be from among us, but when you came forth, we were confused as to whether you are he. Then we looked and saw that you are not he.” He said, “And why is that?” He said, “Because with him from his community are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning or punishment, whereas with you there are only a few.” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am he, and they are indeed my community, and they are more than seventy thousand, and seventy thousand.”"],[15937,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when his gaze fell upon a man. He called the man, and a Jewish man wearing a shirt, trousers, and sandals approached. The man began saying, \"O Messenger of Allah,\" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responded, \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The man refused to respond, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not say anything except, \"O Messenger of Allah\" to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him, \"Do you read the Torah?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" He then asked, \"And the Gospel?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"And the Furqan?\" He replied, \"Yes,\" while adding, \"And I swear by the Lord of Muhammad, if I wished, I could recite it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then asked, \"I ask you by the One who revealed the Torah and the Gospel, have you found me mentioned in them?\" He replied, \"Yes, we find a description like yours coming out from your homeland. We used to hope that you would be among us. Then when you came out, we realized that you were the one. But when we looked again, we realized that you were not the one. So he asked, \"Where am I from?\" He replied, \"We find among his nation seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being held to account, and indeed you are only a few.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached and said the Takbeer twice and then said, \"By the One whom my soul is in His Hand, I am indeed the one, and my nation is more than seventy thousand and seventy thousand.\""],[15938,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When revelation came down upon him, his gaze would melt while his eyes were open, and he would devote his hearing and sight and heart to what came from Allah. When it finished, he said to a scribe: Write: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home] and those who strive in the cause of Allah} — the verse. Then the blind man stood up and said: What is our sin? Revelation came down upon him, so we said to the blind man: Revelation is descending upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He remained standing, saying: I repent to Allah. When it finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Write: {other than those who have a disability}."],[15939,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ among those Bedouins who came to him, and we sat waiting for him. He came out with anger on his face, and sat for a long time without speaking. Then he said: \"I came out to you when the Night of Decree and the Messiah of Misguidance had become clear to me, and I came out to explain them to you and give you glad tidings about them. But at the entrance of the mosque I met two men arguing, with Satan between them, so I came between them and forgot it, and it was snatched away from me. I shall give you a hint of it.\""],[15940,"He informed him that he saw the Prophet ﷺ and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"As for the Night of Decree, seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights.\""],[15941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I saw the Night of Decree, then I was made to forget it, so seek it in the last ten nights.\""],[15942,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were sitting waiting for him, when he came out to us with anger on his face. He sat for a long time without speaking, then it was relieved from him, and he said: \"I came out to you when the Night of Decree and the Messiah of Misguidance had become clear to me, and I came out to you to explain them to you. But I met two men at the mosque arguing, with Satan between them, so I came between them, and it was snatched away from me. So seek it in the last ten nights. As for the Messiah of Misguidance, he is bald on the forehead, one-eyed, broad-chested, with blood in him, as if he were Ibn al-‘Uzzā or Ibn al-‘Uzzā ibn so-and-so.\""],[15943,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in winter and found them praying in hooded cloaks and wraps, with their hands inside them.\""],[15944,"His grandfather Fudayk came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Establish the prayer, give the zakāh, abandon evil, and dwell among the land of your people wherever you wish.\""],[15945,"Qays b. ʿĀṣim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I buried alive eight daughters of mine in the Jāhiliyyah. He said: \"Free a slave for each one of them.\" I said: I am a camel owner. He said: \"Then offer a camel for each one of them, if you wish.\""],[15946,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about oaths of alliance. He said: \"Whatever oath of alliance existed in the Jāhiliyyah, hold fast to it, but there is no oath of alliance in Islam.\""],[15948,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him \"to wash with water and lote leaves.\""],[15949,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought a private audience, then embraced Islam. \"The Prophet ordered him to wash with water and lote leaves.\" So he washed. The prayer was called, and he entered between Abū Bakr and ʿUmar and stood between them. When the prayer was over, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Qays b. ʿĀṣim asked me about three matters that no one except Abū Bakr asked me about.\""],[15950,"To the Prophet ﷺ: I buried alive in the Jāhiliyyah twelve daughters, or thirteen daughters. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Free a life for each one of them.\""],[15951,"“My sons, fear Allah and make your eldest your leader, for when a people make their eldest their leader they succeed their father, but when they make their youngest their leader he is disparaged among your peers. You must acquire wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Beware of begging from people, for it is the last of a man’s earnings. When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not wailed over. When I die, bury me in a land where Bakr b. Wa’il will not know of my burial, for I used to raid them in the Jahiliyyah.”"],[15952,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he saw me I heard him say, “This is the chief of the Arabs.” When we dismounted, I went to him and began to speak with him. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what wealth is there upon which I will bear no blame, from a guest who seeks my hospitality and from dependents who have become numerous?” He said, “Excellent wealth is forty, and the most is sixty. Woe to the owners of two hundred, except the one who gives from its milk and its strength, lends its back for riding, and slaughters its fat ones and feeds the contented and the beggar.” I said, “O Prophet of Allah, how noble and beautiful are these qualities! O Messenger of Allah, no valley in which I am can accommodate the abundance of my camels.” He said, “How do you manage?” I said, “The camels go out in the morning and the people go out, and whoever wishes takes hold of a camel’s head and goes off with it.” He said, “What do you do about lending the backs for riding?” I said, “I do not lend out the young nor the old toothless one that has turned away.” He said, “Is your wealth dearer to you or the wealth of your clients?” I said, “My own wealth is dearer to me than the wealth of my clients.” He said, “You shall have from your wealth what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave away and sent forth; otherwise it is gathered against you.” I said, “By Allah, if I remain alive I will certainly exhaust its number.” Al-Hasan said, “By Allah, he did so. When death came to Qays, he said, ‘O my sons, take from me, for I find no one more sincere to you than myself. When I die, make your elders your leaders and do not make your young ones your leaders, lest people deem you foolish and then hold you in contempt. You must set right your wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Beware of begging, for it is the last of a man’s earnings; no one begs except that he abandons his earning. When I die, do not wail over me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding wailing. Shroud me in the clothes in which I used to pray and fast. When you bury me, do not bury me in a place where anyone can see me, for there were scratches between me and Bakr b. Wa’il in the Jahiliyyah, and I fear that they will exhume me and then do something by which your religion and your worldly life would be lost.’” Al-Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said, “He advised them in life and advised them in death.”"],[15953,"“O my sons, when I die, make your eldest your leader so that you may succeed your fathers, and do not make your youngest your leader, for that would disparage you among your allies. Do not appoint a wailing woman over me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding wailing. You must set right your wealth, for it is a means of honor for the generous and by it one is made independent of the vile. Do not give away the necks of the camels except to those entitled to them, and do not withhold them from what is due to them. Beware of every root of evil; whatever pleases you one day, what displeases you is more. Beware of the sons of your enemies, for they are enemies to you on the path of their fathers. When I die, bury me in a place where this clan of Bakr b. Wa’il cannot see me, for there were scratches between me and them in the Jahiliyyah, and I fear that they will exhume me and thereby corrupt their worldly life and corrupt your hereafter.’ Then he called for his quiver and ordered his eldest son, whose name was ‘Ali, saying, ‘Take out an arrow from my quiver.’ He took it out, and he said, ‘Break it,’ so he broke it. Then he said, ‘Take out two arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Break them,’ so he broke them. Then he said, ‘Take out three arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Break them,’ so he broke them. Then he said, ‘Take out thirty arrows,’ and he took them out, and he said, ‘Bind them with a bowstring,’ so he bound them. Then he said, ‘Break them,’ but he could not break them. He said, ‘O my sons, thus are you in unity, and thus are you in division.’ Then he began to recite poetry.”"],[15954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant, and between the Fijar and the Elephant were twenty years. He said: They named it the Fijar because they acted wickedly and made lawful things they had forbidden. Between the Fijar and the building of the Kaaba were fifteen years, and between the building of the Kaaba and the sending of the Prophet ﷺ were five years. So our Prophet ﷺ was sent when he was forty years old."],[15955,"“I and the Messenger of Allah were born in the Year of the Elephant, so we are of the same age.”"],[15959,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, in how many days should I recite the Quran? He said, “In fifteen.” He said, “I find myself stronger than that.” He said, “In a week.” He said, “I find myself stronger than that.” He continued reciting it like that for a time until he grew old and used to bandage his eyes. Then he reverted and used to recite it in fifteen days. He said, “Would that I had accepted the first concession of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[16013,"Abu Malik al-Janbi 'Amr b. Hashim narrated to us: Muslim al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Mujahid, who said: I used to lead my master Qays b. al-Sa'ib, and he would say: Has the sun declined? When I said yes, he prayed Zuhr. And he would say: This is what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do. The Prophet ﷺ used to pray 'Asr while the sun was white and lively. The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Maghrib while a fasting person would wonder whether to break his fast. And the Prophet ﷺ used to pray Fajr when light spread over the sky."],[16016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah with one divorce. Her two maternal uncles, Qudamah and 'Uthman, the sons of Maz'un, came to her. She said: By Allah, he did not divorce me out of satiety. The Prophet ﷺ came and entered, and she covered herself with her garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: \"Take Hafsah back, for she fasts much and prays much, and she will be your wife in Paradise.\""],[16038,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was in Madinah, until the stars became visible to them. The Prophet ﷺ stood and prayed two rakʿahs, prolonging the standing. When he finished his prayer, he turned to the people and said: “When you see any of these signs, it is only a warning from God ﷻ. When you see them, pray like the most recent prayer you have prayed.”"],[16040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “After me there will be rulers over you who delay the prayers. The prayers are for you and against them. So pray with them as long as they pray facing the qiblah with you.”"],[16057,"that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Perform the Fajr prayer when it is light, for it is greater in reward.\""],[16058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you guards his sick one from water.\""],[16059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah ﷻ decreed His creation, He lay on His back, placed one of His legs over the other, and said: 'It is not appropriate for anyone of My creation to do this.'\" Abū Saʿīd said, \"No doubt, by Allah, I will never do it.\""],[16081,"Abu Muslim, a shaykh who used to be in the mosque of Hammam, narrated to us from Qatadah, from Muʿawiyah b. Qurrah, from his father, who said: “In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we used to be driven away from praying between the pillars.”"],[16084,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about vessels. He said: “Vessels do not make anything forbidden. So soak [dates or raisins] in whatever you wish, but avoid every intoxicant.”"],[16087,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I slaughter a sheep and I feel compassion for it.' He said, 'And the sheep—if you show compassion to it, Allah will show compassion to you.'"],[16088,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I take a sheep to slaughter it and I feel compassion for it.' He said, 'And the sheep—if you show compassion to it, Allah will show compassion to you.'"],[16090,"From his father: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Show me the seal.' So I put my hand into the collar of his shirt until I placed my hand on it."],[16091,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and put my hand into his collar opening. He did not stop making supplication for me while I was touching the seal. I saw on his shoulders something like a wen—the seal of prophethood."],[16092,"We lived through a period of our time with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had no food except the two black things: dates and water."],[16093,"'O my son, if you are in a gathering whose good you hope for, and a need causes you to hurry away, and you say, \"Peace be upon you,\" then you will be their partner in whatever they attain in that gathering.'"],[16094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Fasting the white days is the fasting of the whole age and its breaking of the fast.'"],[16095,"A man used to visit the Prophet ﷺ and he had a son with him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Do you love him?' He said, 'May Allah love you as I love him.' Then his son died. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Where is so-and-so?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, his son has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Would it not please you that you will not come to any gate among the gates of Paradise except that he will come until he opens it for you?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is that for him specifically or for all of us?' He said, 'No, rather for all of you.' And the wording is that of the hadith of 'Amr b. Marzuq."],[16096,"From the Prophet ﷺ: 'A group of people from my ummah will continue to be victorious; those who abandon them will not harm them until the Hour begins.'"],[16097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When the people of Sham become corrupt, there is no good in you.'"],[16098,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped his head and sought forgiveness for him."],[16099,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had milked and tied the udder."],[16100,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, 'By Him in whose hand is my soul, they both (referring to the father and mother) have greater weight on the Day of Judgment than anyone else.'\""],[16101,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The superiority of Aishah over women is like the superiority of tharid over all other foods.”"],[16102,"My father said: “When you pass by a gathering, greet its members. If they are engaged in good, you are their partner in it; and if they are engaged in something else, you will have a reward.” Thus I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say."],[16103,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever says ‘Allahu Akbar’ once at sunset on the seashore, raising his voice, God will grant him for every drop in the sea ten good deeds, erase from him ten evil deeds, and raise him ten degrees, the distance between each two degrees being a hundred years’ journey on a swift horse.”"],[16104,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when modesty was mentioned in his presence. They said, “O Messenger of God, is modesty part of the religion?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Rather, it is the entire religion.”"],[16105,"I set out with my father to the Messenger of God ﷺ and found him with his buttons undone. He turned me around behind him and placed his hand on the seal [of prophethood]."],[16106,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever eats from these two plants should not come near us in our mosque. If you must eat them, then kill their odor by cooking.”"],[16107,"When the Prophet of God ﷺ sat, a group of his companions would sit with him. Among them was a man who had a small son who would come to him from behind his back and sit in front of him, until the boy died. The man then refrained from attending the circle, remembering God and grieving over him. The Prophet ﷺ missed him and said, “Why do I not see so-and-so?” They said, “O Messenger of God, his young son whom you saw has died, and that has kept him from attending the circle.” The Prophet ﷺ met him and asked about him, and was told that he had died. He consoled him, then said, “O so-and-so, which would you prefer: to enjoy him for your entire life, or that tomorrow you will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you find him already there ahead of you, opening it for you?” He said, “O Prophet of God, that he precedes me to the gates of Paradise and opens them for me is dearer to me.” He said, “That is yours.” A man from the Ansar stood up and said, “O Messenger of God, may God make me your ransom, is this for so-and-so specifically, or for every Muslim whose child has died as a forerunner?” He said, “Rather, for every Muslim whose child has died as a forerunner, that will be his.”"],[16108,"I went to embrace Islam when the Prophet ﷺ was sent, and I wanted to bring with me two or three men into Islam. I came to the watering place where people gathered, and there I saw the shepherd of the village who tended their sheep. He said, “I will not tend your sheep for you.” They said, “Why?” He said, “A wolf comes every night and takes a sheep, while this idol of ours stands there, causing no harm, bringing no benefit, changing nothing, and disapproving of nothing.” They returned, and I hoped they would embrace Islam. When morning came, the shepherd came running, saying, “Good news! Good news! The wolf came and is now bound before the idol.” I went with them, and they kissed it and prostrated to it, saying, “This is what you should do.” Then I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him this story. He said, “Satan toyed with them.”"],[16109,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The earth will be filled with oppression and injustice as it was filled with equity and justice, until God sends a man from me whose name is my name and whose father’s name is my father’s name. He will fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and injustice. He will remain among you seven or eight years; if more, then nine. The sky will not withhold any of its rain, nor the earth any of its vegetation.”"],[16110,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Whoever is near death and places his will in accordance with the Book of God, that will be an expiation for what he neglected of his zakat during his life.”"],[16111,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “We used to have lords and goddesses whom we worshiped besides God. We called upon them, but they did not answer; we asked them, but they did not give. We have come to you, and God has guided us through you, so now we worship God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Prosperous is he who has been granted sound intellect.”"],[16113,"A man from his people and others from the Arabs came to him and said, \"Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Muttalib has come out calling to a religion other than ours.\" Qabath stood up and went to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he entered upon him, he ﷺ said to him, \"Sit down, O Qabath.\" Qabath was taken aback. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"You are the one who said, 'If the women of Quraysh came out with their sleeves, they would repel Muhammad and his companions.'\" Qabath said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, my tongue did not move with it, nor did my lips murmur it, nor did anyone hear it from me. It was nothing but something that crossed my mind. I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" He ﷺ said, \"And what you have brought is truth.\""],[16114,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The prayer of two men, one of whom leads the other, is purer with God than the prayer of four praying separately; the prayer of four, one of whom leads them, is purer with God than the prayer of eight praying separately; and the prayer of eight, one of whom leads them, is purer with God than the prayer of a hundred praying separately.\""],[16115,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"The prayer of two men, where one of them leads the other, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of four men performed individually. And the prayer of four men, where one of them leads the others, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of eight men performed individually. And the prayer of eight men, where one of them leads the others, is more virtuous in the sight of Allah than the prayer of one hundred men performed individually.\" Ishaq ibn Rahawayh said, \"Qabath (the narrator) has fully comprehended the words of the Prophet ﷺ .\""],[16116,"I heard 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan say to Qabath b. Ashyam al-Laythi, \"O Qabath, are you older or the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He replied, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ is greater than I, and I am older than him. The Messenger of God ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant, and he was sent as a prophet at the head of forty years from the Elephant.\""],[16117,"From 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ from Quraysh, then from Banu Jumah: Qudamah b. Maz'un."],[16118,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting Jamrat al-'Aqabah on a reddish camel, with no striking, no driving, and no saying 'to you, to you.'"],[16119,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting Jamrat al-'Aqabah on a reddish camel of his, with no striking, no driving, and no saying 'to you, to you.'"],[16120,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pelting the Jamrah from the bottom of the valley."],[16121,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulating the House on a camel and touching the corner with his staff. This is the wording of 'Abbad b. Musa."],[16122,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon on the evening of 'Arafah wearing a Yemeni striped garment."],[16123,"I entered a trellis in Madinah where Qarazah b. Ka'b and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari were, and he mentioned a hadith of theirs in which they said, \"And we have been given a concession to weep at times of calamity, without wailing.\""],[16124,"A questioner asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"If an aggressor attacks me,\" and he ordered him to fight him. He said, \"What about us?\" He ﷺ said, \"If he kills you, you will be in Paradise; and if you kill him, he will be in the Fire.\""],[16125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Adopt the ways of Ma'add, be rough and hardy, and walk barefoot.\""],[16126,"It was said to Qutham b. al-Abbas: How did 'Ali inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the exclusion of al-Abbas? He said: \"Because he was the first of us to join him and the closest of us in attachment to him.\""],[16127,"It was said to Qutham b. al-Abbas: How did 'Ali inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to your exclusion? He said: \"He was the first of us to join him and the closest of us in attachment to him.\""],[16128,"From ʿUrwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Sawād b. Kaʿb — whose name is Kaʿb Ẓufur —: Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān b. Zayd."],[16129,"From Ibn Shihāb, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Anṣār, then from Banū Ẓufur: Qatādah b. al-Nuʿmān."],[16211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a man, “He is from the people of the Fire.” People kept waiting to see what would happen to him until the day of Hunayn, when he fought and displayed great valor. They informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of that, and he said, “He is from the people of the Fire.” Then the man was wounded, and he took an arrow from his quiver and slit his own throat. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has confirmed your words.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Arise, Bilal, and announce that none enters Paradise except a believer, and that Allah ﷻ may support this religion even through a wicked man.”"],[16213,"From his father, who raised it to the Prophet ﷺ as I think, regarding His saying, “It is the same for us whether we grieve or are patient; we have no escape.” He said: The people of the Fire say, “Come, let us be patient.” So they are patient for five hundred years. When they see that it does not benefit them, they say, “Come, let us grieve.” They then weep for five hundred years. When they see that it does not benefit them, they say, “It is the same for us whether we grieve or are patient; we have no escape.”"],[16216,"We went out from Madinah intending [to meet] the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with us went out the pilgrim of our people from among the polytheists. Then he mentioned something similar."],[16219,"He had a debt owed to him by 'Abd Allah b. Abi Hadrad. He demanded it from him until their voices rose. The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by them and said, 'O Ka'b,' and gestured with his hand as if he meant half. So he took half of what was owed to him and left half."],[16226,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The example of the believer is like a stalk of grain that the wind turns over: at one time it knocks it down, and at another it straightens it. The example of the disbeliever is like a firmly rooted cedar tree standing on its trunk, which nothing bends until it is uprooted all at once.'"],[16229,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ eat with three fingers, then I saw him lick his three fingers when he wanted to wipe them."],[16230,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Two hungry wolves sent among a flock of sheep are not more destructive to it than a man's greed for wealth and honour is to his religion.\""],[16231,"A black slave-girl of theirs slaughtered a sheep for them with a flint. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about that, and he commanded us to eat it."],[16232,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Aws b. al-Hadathan during the days of Tashriq, and he called out: \"Truly, none will enter Paradise except a believer, and the days of Mina are days of eating and drinking.\""],[16234,"A slave-girl came tending sheep for me, and a wolf ate a sheep. I struck the slave-girl's face, then I regretted it and came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. I said: \"O Messenger of God, if I knew she was a believer I would set her free.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the slave-girl: \"Who am I?\" She said: \"The Messenger of God.\" He said: \"And who is God?\" She said: \"The One who is in the heaven.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Set her free, for she is a believer.\""],[16239,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"People must stop raising their eyes to the sky [during supplication in prayer], or their eyesight will be snatched away.\""],[16240,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever seeks knowledge for one of three things—to contend with fools by it, to boast with it before scholars, or to attract people’s attention to himself—\" then he said concerning it harsh words."],[16241,"When the day of Uhud came and we reached the mountain pass, I was the first to recognize him. I said, 'This is the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He gestured to me with his hand to be silent. Then he put his armor on me and wore my armor. I was struck until I received twenty or he said 'some ten odd wounds,' everyone who struck me thought I was the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[16242,"Twelve men from the Aqabah pledge, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had commanded them to bring him seventy men the following year. We stayed for a year, one of us going to his companion with provisions, riding gear, and food until seventy men from us came to him."],[16243,"Ka'b: I was never in a military expedition in which I had more ease in mounts and provisions than in that expedition. When the Messenger of God ﷺ set out, I said, 'I will prepare tomorrow and then catch up with him.' I began my preparations, but evening came and I had not finished. Then I said, 'I will work hard on my preparations tomorrow, and the people are still near—I will catch up with them.' Evening came and I had not finished. When the third day came, I began my preparations, evening came and I had not finished. I said, 'How far! The people have traveled for three days.' So I stayed behind. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned, people began making excuses to him. I came and stood before him and said, 'I was never in an expedition in which I had more ease in mounts and provisions than in this one.' The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away from me and commanded the people not to speak to us, and commanded our women to stay away from us. One day I climbed over a wall and found Jabir b. Abdullah there. I said, 'O Jabir, I adjure you by God: do you know that I ever betrayed God and His Messenger even for a single day?' He remained silent and would not speak to me. Then one day, while I was in that state, I heard a man on the hill path calling, 'Ka'b! Ka'b!' He approached me and said, 'Give good news to Ka'b.'"],[16244,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was detaining a debtor of mine. He gestured to me with his hand and said, 'O Ka'b, take half and leave half.'"],[16245,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever visits a sick person plunges into mercy, and when he sits with him, he intercedes for him therein.'"],[16246,"He wanted to marry a Jewish or Christian woman, so he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he forbade him, saying, 'She will not make you chaste.'"],[16251,"Ka'b b. Ujrah shaved his head, and the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded him to ransom himself, so he ransomed himself with a cow."],[16252,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Ka'b b. Ujrah while he was in ihram: 'Have the creatures of your head harmed you?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Shave and ransom yourself, either by fasting three days, or by feeding six poor people, each poor person a sa' of dates, or by sacrificing a sheep.'"],[16254,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , met me and wiped my head and said, \"This is sufficient for your harm.\" Then the lice scattered and he said, \"Go and shave your head and give charity to six poor people.\""],[16295,"Every hair on my head had lice from its root to its tip. When the Prophet ﷺ saw me, he commanded me to shave. Then this verse was revealed, and he said, \"Feed six poor persons with three sa's of dates.\""],[16296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw crawling creatures on his face and said, \"I see, O Ka'b, that the vermin of your head have harmed you?\" He said, \"Yes indeed, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Shave your head, and feed six poor persons, or fast three days, or sacrifice a ewe.\""],[16323,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed his vigor and activity. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only this were in the cause of Allah!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If he went out striving to provide for his young children, then he is in the cause of Allah. If he went out striving to provide for two elderly parents, then he is in the cause of Allah. If he went out striving for himself to keep himself chaste, then he is in the cause of Allah. And if he went out for show and pride, then he is in the cause of Satan.\""],[16324,"\"Shall I not give you a gift? I said yes, so he said give it to me. We said, O Messenger of Allah, how do we send blessings upon you, the people of the household, as Allah has taught us how to send peace? He said, Say: O Allah, send peace upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.\""],[16325,"\"Can I give you a gift?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How do we greet you, O Messenger of Allah? And how do we pray upon you?\" He said, \"Say: 'O Allah, send peace and blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent peace and blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.'\" Al-Zubair bin 'Adiy narrated from 'Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla."],[16327,"When the verse {Indeed, Allah and His angels confer blessings upon the Prophet} was revealed... (the rest of the hadith)."],[16332,"We said to the Prophet ﷺ , \"We have already known how to greet you, but how should we send blessings upon you?\" He replied, \"Say: Allahumma salli 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin, kama sallaita 'ala Ibrahim wa 'ala ali Ibrahim, innaka hamidun majid. Wa barik 'ala Muhammadin wa 'ala ali Muhammadin, kama barakta 'ala Ibrahim wa 'ala ali Ibrahim, innaka hamidun majid.\""],[16333,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you with peace, so how do we pray upon you?\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, send your blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as you have sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are worthy of praise and glory. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are worthy of praise and glory.\""],[16346,"A blind man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “I hear the call, but perhaps I cannot find a guide and it is difficult for me. Should I set up a mosque in my house?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Does the call reach you?” He said, “Yes.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you hear the call, then go out.”"],[16367,"I attended one of the two Eids with Ka'b. When the people left, most of them went to the mosque, and I saw him heading toward the house. I said, \"O my father, will you not head to the mosque? For I see the people heading to it.\" He said, \"Much of what you see is rudeness and lack of knowledge. These two rak'ahs are the supererogatory prayer of this day until the prayer calls you.\""],[16368,"I went out with my father, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, on the day of Eid to the prayer place. He sat before the imam came, and the imam did not come until when the imam had finished, they departed going toward the mosque as if they were a neck (a group). I said to him, \"Do you not see the people?\" He said, \"This is an innovation and abandonment of the Sunnah.\""],[16371,"To Umar: \"I slaughtered a cow.\""],[16378,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No man performs ablution in his house and then goes out intending prayer except that he is in prayer until he finishes his prayer, so he should not interlace his fingers in prayer.”"],[16379,"“He slaughtered a cow.”"],[16380,"You heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard him say: “The daughter of a brother and the daughter of a sister are not made lawful through breastfeeding.”"],[16381,"\"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you, but how do we send blessings upon you?' The Prophet ﷺ replied, 'You say, O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, shower blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You showered blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'\""],[16383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not guide you to the best character of the people of this world and the Hereafter? Whoever maintains ties with the one who cuts him off, forgives the one who wrongs him, and gives to the one who deprives him.” Luwayn said: It is said—and Allah knows best—ʿAbd Allah b. Abi al-Husayn is given the kunya Abu al-Husayn. Abu al-Ahwas narrated from Abu Ishaq from ʿAbd Allah b. Abi al-Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and he did not mention Kaʿb b. ʿUjrah."],[16384,"I attended two gatherings with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As for one of them, a funeral was brought and it was said: This is so-and-so, and what a bad man he was; and he was spoken of with evil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you testify to that?” They said: Yes. He said: “It is confirmed.” As for the other, the funeral of a man was brought and they said: This is so-and-so, and they spoke well of him. He said: “Do you testify to that?” They said: Yes. He said: “It is confirmed.”"],[16385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us while we were nine, among whom were six from the non-Arabs. He said: “There will be rulers. Whoever affirms their lies, assists them in their wrongdoing, and carries out their plots is not of me nor am I of him, and he will not come to the Pond.”"],[16388,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to shave his head because of lice. He said: “Fast three days, or feed six poor people, or slaughter a sacrifice.”"],[16392,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me, when lice harmed me, to shave my head, then to fast three days or feed six poor people, and he knew that I had nothing to sacrifice.\""],[16393,"\"Narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which there is no disagreement.\" So he narrated from Ka'b b. 'Ujrah that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever visits a sick person wades in mercy, and when he sits with him, he is immersed in it.\" He said: He said to his companions: \"We are immersed, if Allah wills.\""],[16398,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, may Allah protect you from rulers who will come after me. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to the Pond.\""],[16399,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he mentioned a tribulation and brought it near. A veiled man passed by, and he said: \"This one, on that day, will be upon the truth.\" I stood up and took hold of his upper arms, and I turned his face toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this one?\" He said: \"Yes.\" And it was 'Uthman b. 'Affan."],[16402,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was telling us about the trials. A man with a face covering passed by, so he said: “This one and his companions will be upon guidance on that day.” So I got up and caught up with him, and I uncovered the veil from his head, and behold it was Uthman b. Affan. I said: O Messenger of God, this one? He said: “Yes.”"],[16409,"“Abu al-Yasar Kab b. Amr died in the year fifty-five in Madinah.”"],[16410,"What did he do? Was he killed? I said: God is mightier for him and more supportive than that. He said: What do you want with me? I said: Capture, but the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing you. He said: I am not the first to be crucified. So I captured him, then I brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[16411,"A woman came to me to buy dates from me. I said: In the house there are dates better than this. She entered the house with me, and I leaned toward her, pinched her, and kissed her. Then I became remorseful. I went to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him, and he said: Cover yourself and do not tell anyone. But I could not bear it, so I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Did you betray a warrior in his family with something like this?” until I wished I had not embraced Islam except at that very hour, until I thought I was among the people of the Fire. The Messenger of God ﷺ lowered his head for a long time, then God revealed to him: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day} to the end of the verse. Abu al-Yasar said: So I came to him and he recited it to me. His companions said: O Messenger of God, is this for him specifically or for the people generally? He said: “Rather for the people generally.”"],[16412,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty or waives [the debt] for him, God will shade him in His shade on the day there is no shade except His shade.”"],[16415,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever would like to seek shade from the scorching heat of Hell, let him give respite to a debtor or waive [the debt] for one in difficulty.”"],[16420,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Whoever provides financial relief or grants respite to a debtor, Allah will provide shade for him on the Day when there will be no shade except His shade.\""],[16428,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; and Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar al-Raqqī narrated to us; and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Shaybah al-Ḥizāmī narrated to us; and Muʿādh b. al-Muthannā narrated to us, saying: Musaddad narrated to us. They said: Sufyān b. ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ṣafwān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣafwān, from Umm al-Dardāʾ, from Kaʿb b. ʿĀṣim, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16432,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16434,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16438,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fasting while traveling is not an act of righteousness.\""],[16439,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness.”"],[16440,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage on the middle of the days of Tashriq, saying: “Is this day sacred?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Indeed your sanctity among yourselves is like the sanctity of this day of yours. Shall I tell you who the Muslim is? The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. Shall I tell you who the believer is? The one whom the Muslims trust with their lives and their wealth. And shall I tell you who the emigrant is? The emigrant is the one who abandons the evil deeds that Allah has forbidden him. And the believer is inviolable to the believer, like the sanctity of this day: his flesh is forbidden to him to eat it in his absence and to backbite him; his honor is forbidden to him to violate it; his face is forbidden to him to slap it; and harming him is forbidden to him to harm him; and it is forbidden to him to push him with a shove that knocks him down.”"],[16441,"Karāmah bt. al-Ḥusayn b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb al-Māzinī narrated to me – and ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb was in charge of the Prophet’s baggage on the day of Badr – she said: I heard my father narrate from Abū ʿAyyāsh al-Zuraqī, from Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh: Kaʿb b. ʿĀṣim al-Ashʿarī narrated to me, saying: “I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on the middle of the days of sacrifice by the Jamrah.”"],[16442,"“And the name of Abū Sulmā was Rabīʿah b. Riyāḥ b. Qurẓ b. al-Ḥārith b. Māzin b. Thaʿlabah b. Thawr b. Hadmah b. Lāṭī b. ʿUthmān b. Muzaynah.”"],[16444,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed every nation has a trial, and the trial of my nation is wealth.”"],[16445,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Retaliation is of three types: a prince, one commanded, or an arrogant one.”"],[16446,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “If the son of Adam were given two valleys of wealth, he would wish for a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.”"],[16447,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his head once, like this, until he reached the back of the head.”"],[16448,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his head from its front to its back, and he brought his hands out from beneath his ears.”"],[16449,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water into his nose three times, taking fresh water for each one, and washed his face three times. When he wiped his head, he said, “Like this,” and he gestured with his hand from the front of his head until he reached the bottom of his neck from the back of it."],[16450,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was performing ablution, and the water was flowing from his face over his beard and chest; he was separating between rinsing the mouth and sniffing water into the nose."],[16451,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution, and he wiped over his head."],[16452,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution, and he wiped the inside of his beard and the back of his neck."],[16453,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for the conquest of Makkah, he appointed Abu Ruham Kulthum b. al-Husayn al-Ghifari as his deputy over Madinah."],[16454,"He heard Abu Ruham al-Ghifari, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we traveled one night, I rode close to him, and drowsiness overcame me. I would start awake and find my mount near his mount, and its closeness alarmed me for fear of striking his foot in the stirrup, so I would draw my mount back. This continued until part of the night had passed, when sleep overpowered my eyes and my mount jostled against his foot in the stirrup and struck his foot. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass' (a word of pain). I said, 'Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Move on.' The Prophet ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the long, reddish, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. Then he said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, short, curly-haired, hairless ones who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' The narrator said: I tried to remember among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, those are a group from Aslam who stayed behind.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar.'"],[16455,"He heard Abu Ruham, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I spent a night traveling close to him. Then he mentioned the hadith."],[16456,"He heard Abu Ruham, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he returned, he traveled at night through al-Akhdar, and I rode close to him. Drowsiness was cast upon us, and I kept waking and finding my mount near his mount, and its closeness alarmed me until I feared striking his foot in the stirrup, so I held my mount back. This continued until part of the night had passed, when sleep overcame my eyes and my mount jostled against the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the stirrup and struck his foot. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'Move on.' The Prophet ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the group of reddish, tall, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. Then he said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, short, curly-haired ones who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' The narrator said: I tried to remember among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam who had stayed behind. They had been allies among us. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar.' Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated it from al-Zuhri, and between the nephew of Abu Ruham and Ibn Ukaymah there is a connection."],[16457,"He heard Abu Ruham Kulthum b. Husayn, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the expedition to Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One night I traveled with him while we were at al-Akhdar, close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Drowsiness was cast upon us, and I kept waking and finding my mount near the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and its closeness alarmed me for fear of striking his foot in the stirrup. I kept steering my mount away from him until part of the way had passed, and we were in part of the night, when sleep overcame my eyes and my mount jostled against the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his foot in the stirrup. I did not wake except at his saying, 'Hass.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' He said, 'Move on.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then began asking me about those who had stayed behind from Banu Ghifar, and I informed him. He asked me, 'What happened to the group of reddish, tall, hairless ones?' I told him that they had stayed behind. He said, 'What happened to the dark-complexioned, curly-haired, short ones?' I said, 'By Allah, I do not recognize these as being from us.' He said, 'Yes, those who have livestock with branded young she-camels?' I then remembered them among Banu Ghifar, but I could not recall them until I remembered that they were a group from Aslam who had been allies among us. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, those are a group from Aslam who had been allies among us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What prevents any one of those, when he stays behind, from carrying an active man on one of his camels in the path of Allah? Indeed, the dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Emigrants from Quraysh, the Ansar, Ghifar, and Aslam.'"],[16458,"I and my brother were present at Khaybar, and we had horses. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted us six shares: four shares for the two horses and two shares for us. We sold our two shares for two young camels."],[16459,"And from his brother: They were both horsemen on the day of Khaybar, and they were given six shares: four for their two horses and two for themselves. They sold the two shares for two young camels."],[16460,"He informed him that Safwan b. Umayyah sent him during the conquest to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with milk, a young gazelle, and truffle-like plants, while the Prophet ﷺ was at the upper part of the valley. I entered without seeking permission and without greeting. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Go out and say: Peace be upon you, may I enter?' That was after Safwan had embraced Islam. Abu 'Asim said: Al-daghabis is a plant that grows in the desert."],[16461,"A bedouin man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Tell me of a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Are these two your greatest concerns?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Speak the truth and give from your surplus.' He said, 'By Allah, I cannot speak the truth at every moment, and I cannot give from the surplus of my wealth.' He said, 'Feed people and spread peace.' He said, 'This is also difficult.' He said, 'Do you have camels?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then look to a camel from your camels and a water skin, then go to a household who do not drink water except every other day, and give them water. Perhaps you will not lose your camel or tear your water skin until Paradise becomes due for you.' The bedouin went off saying 'Allahu Akbar,' and neither his water skin was torn nor his camel lost until he was killed as a martyr."],[16462,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would gather us—me, ‘Abd Allah, ‘Ubayd Allah, and Qutham—then he would spread his arms like this, extend his span, and say, “Whoever reaches me first will have such-and-such.”"],[16463,"From Kariz b. Samah, who had been a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: It was said, “O Messenger of God, pray against the Banu ‘Amir.” He said, “I was not sent as an invoker of curses.”"],[16464,"“The Prophet ﷺ tied a red banner for the Banu Sulaym.”"],[16465,"She heard her father asking the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “I vowed to sacrifice at Buwanah.” He asked, “Is there an idol or a tyrant worshipped there?” He said, “No.” He said, “Fulfill your vow.”"],[16466,"Kardam b. Sufyan al-Thaqafi came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I vowed to slaughter a herd of camels at Buwanah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “Upon an idol?” He said, “No.” He said, “Upon one of the gatherings of the Jahiliyyah?” He said, “No.” He said, “Fulfill your vow wherever it may be, O Kardam. There is no vow and no oath in disobedience to God.”"],[16467,"“O Messenger of God,” and he inclined toward him, then said, “Where is the year of the army of ‘Ithran?” The Prophet ﷺ recognized that army; I was in that army. Tariq b. al-Muraqqa’ said, “Who will give me a spear for its reward?” I said, “And what is its reward?” He said, “The first daughter born to me, I will marry her to him.” So I gave him my spear. Then it slipped from him somewhat. Later I learned that a daughter had been born to him and had reached maturity. I said, “Give me my wife in marriage.” He refused except with a dowry. The Prophet ﷺ said, “How old is she?” He said, “She has seen gray hair.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “It is better for you that you neither sin nor cause him to sin. Leave her.”"],[16468,"He was called Abu Tha‘labah. On a hot day I had sandals and he had none. He said, “Give me your sandal.” I said, “No, unless you marry me to your daughter.” He said, “Give it to me, and I will marry her to you.” When we departed, he sent my sandals back to me and said, “You have no wife with me.” I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Leave her; there is no good for you in her.”"],[16469,"I set out with my father from Madinah for some need, heading to Makkah. That was when the Prophet ﷺ was first mentioned in Makkah. He brought us to a sheep owner. In the middle of the night a wolf came and took a lamb from his flock. The shepherd jumped up and said, “O dweller of the valley, your neighbor!” We heard a voice but saw no speaker: “O wolf, release it.” The lamb came running, without a bite, until it entered the flock. And it was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in Madinah: {And there were men among mankind who sought refuge in men among the jinn} (the verse)."],[16470,"It is also said: Hillan b. Ghaniyy b. Yu‘sir b. Sa‘d b. Qays Ghaylan b. Mudar."],[16471,"From ‘Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, ally of Hamzah b. ‘Abd al-Muttalib. Abu Marthad died in the year twelve, at the age of sixty-six."],[16472,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.”"],[16473,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Do not sit at graves, and do not pray toward them.”"],[16474,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed with him, then I left him. I came to him after a year and said: “O Messenger of Allah, do you not recognize me?” He said: “No.” I said: “I am the one who was with you last year.” He said: “What has changed you after me?” He said: “I have not eaten food during the day since I parted from you.” He said: “Who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast one day of the month of Surur.” I said: “Give me more,” and he increased for me until he said: “Fast three days of the month.”"],[16475,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ come out from the mountain pass of al-Matabikh until he came to the well of prayer, wearing a waist-wrapper wrapped around him, and he prayed two rakʿahs of Zuhr or ʿAsr, crossing its two ends."],[16476,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying near the upper well in a single garment."],[16477,"He told him that he used to trade in wine during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came from Syria with wine in leather skins, intending to trade with it. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have brought a good drink.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Kaysan, it has been forbidden.” Kaysan said: “Shall I go and sell it, O Prophet of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It has been forbidden, and its price is forbidden.” So Kaysan went to the skins, took them by their legs, and poured them all out."],[16478,"He told him that his father carried wine to Madinah before the Prophet ﷺ forbade it. He came to him and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What have you carried, O Abu Rafiʿ?” He said: “Wine, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you not know that it has been forbidden after you?” He said: “Should I sell it to the Jews?” He said: “Its seller is like its drinker.” So Abu Rafiʿ split his skins open at al-Bathaʾ."],[16479,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “ʿIsa son of Maryam ﷺ will descend at the white minaret in Damascus.”"],[16480,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from Yemen, and I pledged allegiance to him and accepted Islam at his hand."],[16481,"A Bedouin said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” He said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” He said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Then trials will occur like the night.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Not at all, by the One in whose hand is my soul! You will surely return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16483,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the Bedouins came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” The Bedouin said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Then trials will occur like the shadows.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul! You will surely return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16484,"While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the Bedouins of Najd came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, is there an end to Islam?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He will bring Islam upon them.” The Bedouin said: “Then what, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then trials will occur like the shadows.” The Bedouin said: “Not at all, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul! You will return in them as striking serpents, some of you striking the necks of others.”"],[16486,"From ʿUrwah regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of the conquest from the Muslims of Quraysh, then from Banu Muharib b. Fihr: Kurz b. Jabir."],[16487,"He went out with his father to a funeral which the Prophet ﷺ attended, while I was a boy old enough to understand. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"God loves that when a worker performs a deed, he does it well.\""],[16488,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"O people, seek Paradise with all your effort and flee from the Fire with all your effort, for Paradise's seeker does not sleep, and the Fire's fleer does not sleep. Indeed, the Hereafter today is surrounded by hardships, and this world is surrounded by desires.\""],[16489,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The eldest among brothers is in the position of the father.\""],[16490,"Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was the husband of the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the son of her maternal aunt. His mother was Hala bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza b. Qusayy, the sister of Khadija bt. Khuwaylid on her father's side, and her mother was Fatima bt. Za'ida. He is al-Asamm b. Jundub b. Harim b. Rawaha b. Hujr b. ‘Abd b. Ma‘is b. ‘Amir b. Lu'ayy. It is said that the name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was Mihsham, and he was called Jirw al-Batha'. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. al-Hasan and Yahya b. Muhammad narrated to me, saying: \"The name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was Laqit.\" Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. al-Dahhak narrated to me from his father, saying: \"The name of Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was al-Qasim, and that is the established name. Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ died in Dhu al-Hijja in the year twelve.\""],[16491,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, became Muslim while her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a polytheist. Then he became Muslim after some time, and no marriage was renewed. ‘Abd al-Razzaq said: \"Ma‘mar mentioned from Jabir from al-Sha‘bi.\""],[16492,"He informed him that Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza b. ‘Abd Shams b. ‘Abd Manaf had married the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ among the ransom captives, and Zaynab came to him. ‘Amr said: \"I think they were both confirmed upon their marriage from the time of ignorance.\""],[16493,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, became Muslim while her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a polytheist. Then he became Muslim after that, and the Prophet ﷺ confirmed them upon their marriage."],[16494,"The Messenger of God ﷺ returned Zaynab to Abu al-‘As under the first marriage and did not renew anything. There was disagreement about this, and others said with a new marriage."],[16495,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, became Muslim a year before her husband Abu al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘. Then he became Muslim, and the Prophet ﷺ returned her to him with a new marriage."],[16496,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my father is old and cannot perform Hajj, Umrah, or carry a burden.\" He ﷺ said, \"Perform Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father and carry the burden for him.\" \"And the wording is from the hadith of Ali ibn Abdul Aziz.\""],[16497,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj or ‘Umrah or travel.\" He said, \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and ‘Umrah.\""],[16498,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the believer is like the bee: it eats only what is good and produces only what is good.\""],[16499,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The likeness of the believer is like the bee: it eats only what is good and produces only what is good.\""],[16500,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A dream is one of forty parts, or one of forty-six parts, of prophethood. It is upon the leg of a bird; when it is interpreted, it comes to pass.” Shuʿba said in his narration, and I think he said: “Do not interpret it except with affection or sound judgment.”"],[16501,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The dream of a believer is one part of forty parts of prophethood. It is upon the leg of a bird as long as he does not relate it. When he relates it, it comes to pass.”"],[16502,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A dream is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood. A dream is suspended upon the leg of a bird until its owner relates it. When he relates it, it comes to pass. So let him relate it only to a knowledgeable person, a sincere adviser, or a beloved friend.”"],[16503,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A dream is upon the leg of a bird as long as it is not interpreted. When it is interpreted, it comes to pass.”"],[16504,"We said: “O Messenger of God, will all of us see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? And what is the sign of that in His creation?” He said: “Does not each of you see the moon clearly with it?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “God is greater.”"],[16505,"I said: “O Prophet of God, will all of us see our Lord?” He said: “Yes.” I said: “What is the sign of that in His creation?” He said: “Does not each of you look at the moon on the night of the full moon? It is only a creature among the creatures of God, and God is greater and more majestic.”"],[16506,"He said, \"Indeed, we used to slaughter sacrificial animals in the month of Rajab, and we would eat from them and feed others. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no harm in that.' And Waki' said, 'I will never abandon it.'\""],[16507,"I said: “O Messenger of God, where was our Lord before He created the heaven and the earth?” He said: “He was in a cloud, beneath which was air and above which was air. Then He created His Throne upon the water.”"],[16508,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God, exalted is He, laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of His relief.” Abu Razin said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of God, does the Lord laugh?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘We will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs.’”"],[16509,"I said: “O Messenger of God, how does God revive the dead?” He said: “Have you not passed by a valley of your people and found it barren, then passed by it and found it green, then passed by it and found it barren, then passed by it and found it green? Thus does God revive the dead.”"],[16510,"I said: “O Messenger of God, where is my mother?” He said: “Your mother is in the Fire.” He said: “Then where are those of your family who have passed away?” He said: “Are you not content that your mother be with my mother?”"],[16511,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked questions and found fault with them. But when Abu Razin asked him, he answered him and was pleased by that."],[16512,"I arrived at Kufa with a companion of mine to bring back sandals from there. We went early to the market, while it had not yet arisen. I said to my companion, 'If only we entered the mosque' - and the mosque in those days was where the date-sellers were. So we entered, and there was a man from Qays called Ibn al-Muntafiq. I heard him saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was described to me and made clear to me, so I sought him in Makkah and was told he was in Mina. I sought him in Mina and was told he was at Arafat. I caught up with him while he was among a group of his companions riding. It was said to me, \"Move aside from the path of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave the man alone; what does he need?\" I drew near until I took hold of the nose-rein of his camel or its halter, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about what will save me from the Fire and what will bring me to Paradise.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head to the sky, then lowered it, then turned his face toward me and said, \"If you have been brief in the question, you have asked about something tremendous and lengthy. So remember from me: worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prescribed prayer; pay the obligatory zakat; fast Ramadan; and whatever you would love people to do to you, do it to them; and whatever you would hate people to do to you, leave people alone from it. Let the camel go,\" or \"the mount.\" Hammam said: \"As for Hajj, he had already performed Hajj when he asked him.\""],[16513,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, \"At Arafah.\" So I went to him, and I started to draw near to him until the neck of my mount passed the neck of his mount. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, teach me what will save me from the punishment of Allah and admit me to His Paradise.\" He said, \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him; establish the prescribed prayer; pay the obligatory zakat; perform Hajj and Umrah,\" and I think he said, \"and fast Ramadan; and look at what you would love people to bring to you and do it to them, and what you would hate them to bring to you, leave them alone from it.\" \"Ibn Awn was confused in the chain of this hadith and did not control it from Muhammad b. Juhadah, but Hammam controlled it.\""],[16517,"from the Prophet ﷺ about game that disappears from its owner. He said, \"Perhaps the vermin of the earth killed it.\""],[16518,"I set out with a companion of mine until we reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but we did not find him. Aisha fed us dates and prepared for us some porridge. Then the Prophet ﷺ came walking briskly, swaying. He said, \"Have you fed them anything?\" We said, \"Yes.\" While we were in that state, the shepherd drove the sheep to the enclosure, and in his hand was a newborn lamb. He said, \"Has it given birth?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then slaughter a sheep.\" Then he turned his face toward us and said, \"Do not think\" - and he did not say \"Do not think\" - \"that we slaughtered the sheep because of you two. We have a hundred sheep, and we do not want them to increase beyond that. When a lamb is born to the shepherd, we order him to slaughter a sheep.\""],[16520,"that he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned something, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers.\""],[16521,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly and pass between the fingers, and when you inhale water into the nose, do it deeply, unless you are fasting.\" \"Their wording is identical.\""],[16523,"He said: \"We have a neighbor who drinks wine and commits vile acts, so raise his matter to the authority.\" He said: \"I killed ninety-nine alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ; I would not love that I had killed the like of them and that I had uncovered the veil of a Muslim.\""],[16524,"Laqit b. Sabira al-Sakuni: \"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my two legs crooked, not touching the ground. He supplicated for me, and I walked on the ground.\""],[16525,"I saw Lubayy b. Labba al-Asadi, and he was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ or had met the Prophet ﷺ. A horse of his won, and he draped it with an Adeni striped cloak, and I saw on him a garment of silk or a fine cloak."],[16526,"\"I have not filled my belly with food since I became Muslim with the Prophet ﷺ; I eat what suffices me and drink what suffices me.\" Al-'Ala' said: \"He means my strength.\""],[16527,"He informed him that he was sitting in the market when a woman passed carrying a child. The people rose, and I rose with them, and we went until we reached the Prophet ﷺ while he was saying: \"Who is the father of this child with you?\" She remained silent. A young man beside her said: \"I am his father, O Messenger of God.\" He turned to her and said: \"Who is the father of this child with you?\" She remained silent. The young man said: \"O Messenger of God, she is young in age, recently wed, and she will not speak to you. I am his father, O Messenger of God.\" The Prophet ﷺ looked at some of his companions as if asking them about him. They said: \"We know nothing but good,\" or something like that. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Have you been married?\" He said: \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be stoned. We went out with him and dug for him until we made it possible, then we threw stones at him until he became still. Then we returned to our gatherings. While we were thus, an old man came asking about the stoned man. We stood up to him, seized him by the collar, and took him to the Prophet ﷺ. We said: \"O Messenger of God, this man came asking about the wicked one.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Stop! He is more fragrant to God than the scent of musk.\" We left with the old man, and behold, he was his father. We reached him and helped him with his washing, shrouding, and burial. He said: \"I do not know whether he said the prayer over him or not.\""],[16528,"We were boys working in the market. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered a man and he was stoned. A man came asking us about him, so we brought him to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, this man came asking us about this wicked one who was stoned today.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not say wicked. By God, he is more fragrant to God than musk.\""],[16529,"We were boys running to the market. A man who confessed to adultery was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he was stoned. A man came asking us about the place of that stoned man. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of God, this man is asking us about that wicked one.\" He said: \"Do not say wicked. By God, he is more fragrant to God than musk.\""],[16530,"My father said to me: 'O my son, when I die, bury me in a niche grave. When you place me in my niche, say: \"In the name of God and upon the creed of the Messenger of God.\" Then scatter the soil over me gently. Then recite at my head the opening of al-Baqarah and its conclusion, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say that.'"],[16531,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness and We bring you as a witness against these?}, the Messenger of God ﷺ wept and said: \"O Lord, this I witnessed over those among whom I was present, so how about those whom I did not see?\""],[16532,"It was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar a cooked sheep. He and Bashir bin Al-Bara' bin Ma'rur ate from it, then both of them became seriously ill. Eventually, Bashir died. When he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the Jewish woman who had presented it and said, \"What did you feed us, may Allah curse you?\" She replied, \"I poisoned you.\" He asked, \"What made you do that?\" She said, \"I heard you mention that if you were a prophet, it would not harm you, but if you were not, I wanted to relieve people from you.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to be crucified."],[16533,"Urwa reported: \"Regarding the naming of the one who witnessed the Battle of Badr from the Ansar, then from the tribe of Banu Zuhrā ibn ‘Abd al-Ashhal: Muhammad ibn Muslimah ibn Khalid ibn ‘Adi ibn Majda‘ah ibn Harithah ibn al-Harith.\""],[16534,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from the Aws, from Banu Harithah: Muhammad b. Maslama.\""],[16535,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Harithah: Muhammad b. Maslama b. Khalid b. 'Adi b. Majda'a b. Harithah b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj b. 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Aws, and he was an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal.\""],[16536,"Muhammad ibn Muslimah passed away in Medina in the year forty-three, at the age of seventy-seven years."],[16537,"\"Muhammad b. Maslama died in Safar in the year forty-three.\""],[16538,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When Allah casts the proposal of a woman into the heart of a man, there is no harm in him looking at her.\" This is what Yahya ibn Al-Ala'a reported from Al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Uthman."],[16539,"I sought to marry a woman, so I began to hide myself to look at her. It was said to him, “Do you do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into the heart of one of you the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Hafs b. Ghiyath narrated it thus, and Yazid b. Harun concurred with him."],[16540,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslamah directing his gaze at the daughter of al-Dahhak. I said, “Glory be to God! You look at her while you are one of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Yahya b. Sa‘id narrated it from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathma, just as Hafs b. Ghiyath and Yazid b. Harun narrated it from al-Hajjaj."],[16541,"I was sitting with Muhammad b. Maslamah when the daughter of al-Dahhak passed behind him, and he began to track her with his gaze. I said, “Glory be to God! You do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts the desire to propose to a woman into a man’s heart, there is no harm in his looking at her.’”"],[16542,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.” Abd al-Wahid b. Ziyad narrated it thus from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his father."],[16543,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.” Abu Mu‘awiya narrated it thus from al-Hajjaj, from Sahl b. Muhammad b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sulayman b. Abi Hathma."],[16544,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari look at the daughter of al-Dahhak, who was on a wall playing, and he kept looking at her. It was said to him, “Do you look at her while you are a companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Indeed I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘When God casts into a person’s heart the desire to propose to a woman, there is no harm in his looking at her.’” Hammad b. Salama narrated it thus and contradicted others in it. The narrators differed concerning al-Hajjaj b. Artah in this hadith. The correct version in my view, and God knows best, is what Hafs b. Ghiyath and Yazid b. Harun narrated from al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma, from his paternal uncle Sahl b. Abi Hathma, from Muhammad b. Maslamah."],[16545,"Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra (a slave, male or female).” Umar said, “If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that.” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule in it a ghurra."],[16546,"Umar consulted the people about the fetus that a woman miscarries. Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” Umar said, “If you are truthful, bring someone to testify with you.” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule that."],[16547,"Al-Mughira said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” Umar said, “Who will testify with you if you are truthful?” Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule that."],[16548,"Al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule in it a ghurra, a male or female slave.” He said, “Then bring me someone to testify with you.” So Muhammad b. Maslamah came to him."],[16549,"A grandmother came to Abu Bakr seeking her inheritance from her son or daughter. Abu Bakr said, “I find nothing for you in the Book of God, and I have not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule anything for you. I will ask the people this evening.” When he had prayed Zuhr, he turned to the people and said, “A grandmother has come to me asking for her inheritance from her son or daughter. I find nothing for her in the Book, and I have not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ rule anything for her. Has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning her?” Al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba stood and said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule for her one-sixth.” So Abu Bakr gave her one-sixth. Then he said, “Did anyone hear that with you?” Muhammad b. Maslamah stood and said, “I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ rule for her one-sixth.” So Abu Bakr gave her one-sixth. Then during the caliphate of Umar, the other grandmother—the one who differed from her—came to him. Umar said, “The ruling was only for the other one, not you. But if you both are present, then the sixth is between you, and whichever of you is alone, it is hers.”"],[16550,"A grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asking about her inheritance in the Book of God. Abu Bakr said to her, “You have nothing in the Book of God, and I do not know of anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Go back until I ask the people.” He asked the people, and al-Mughira b. Shu‘ba said, “I was present when the Messenger of God ﷺ gave her one-sixth.” Abu Bakr said, “Is there anyone else with you?” Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari stood and said the like of what al-Mughira said, so Abu Bakr carried it out for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar b. al-Khattab asking about her inheritance. He said, “You have nothing in the Book of God. The ruling that was made was only for the other one, not you. I will not add anything to the prescribed shares, but it is that sixth. If you both are present, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone, it is hers.”"],[16551,"She said: 'I have a right in what he left, so what is my right?' Abu Bakr said: 'I do not know of anything for you in the Book of God. I will ask; so return.' When he had prayed the noon prayer, he said: 'Who heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ regarding grandmothers?' al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: 'I heard him.' He said: 'How did you hear him?' He said: 'He gave the grandmother a sixth.' He said: 'Does anyone other than you know that?' Then Muhammad b. Maslamah stood and said: 'He spoke the truth; it is as he said.' So the woman came and he gave her a sixth. When Abu Bakr ؓ passed away, and it was Umar ؓ, a woman came to him about the like of that and said what the woman who had spoken to Abu Bakr had said. He replied to her with the like of his answer. Then he asked, and they said: 'al-Mughirah said such-and-such, and Muhammad b. Maslamah testified with him.' So he gave her a sixth. Then Umar said on his own initiative: 'If you two are both present, it is for you both; but whichever of you is alone with it, it is for her.'"],[16552,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, what should I do when the worshippers differ?' He said: 'Go out with your sword to the harrah and strike it with it. Then enter your house until a decree of death comes to you or an erring hand.'"],[16553,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed judgment on the Banu Qurayzah, the Aws felt distressed by that. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent to every house of the Aws two captives, and he sent to the Banu Harithah two captives."],[16554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he stood up to pray, \"Allahu Akbar, I have directed my face towards the One who created the heavens and the earth, purely submitting to Him, and I am not of those who associate partners with Allah. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, the Lord of the worlds, who has no partner. And with that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no deity but You. Glory be to You, and praise be to You.\" Then he recited, and when he bowed he said, \"O Allah, to You I have bowed, and in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord, I have bowed for You, and my hearing, my sight, my flesh and my blood have bowed for Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\" Then he raised his head and said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, to You is the praise, filling the heavens and the earth and whatever You will of anything after that.\" And when he prostrated he said, \"O Allah, to You I have prostrated, and in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. You are my Lord, I have prostrated for You, and my face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and opened its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.\""],[16555,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say in his prostration: 'O God, to You I prostrated, in You I believed, and to You I submitted, and You are my Lord. My face prostrated to the One who created it and shaped it and split open its hearing and its sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.' And when he bowed he said: 'O God, to You I bowed, in You I believed, to You I submitted, and upon You I relied. You are my Lord. My hearing, my sight, my blood, my marrow, my bone, and my sinew have humbled themselves to God, Lord of the worlds.' Then he raised his head from bowing and said: 'God hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord, and to You be praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, and filling whatever You will of anything after.'"],[16556,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'O Muhammad b. Maslamah, there will be tribulation, division, and difference. When that occurs, break your sword, break your arrows, cut your bowstring, and sit in your house.' And indeed the tribulation occurred, and I did what the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me. Then I turned and saw a sword hanging from the tent pole, so I drew it, and it turned out to be a sword of wood. He said: 'I did what the Prophet ﷺ commanded me, and I took this to frighten people with it.'"],[16557,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'There will be division, tribulation, and difference. Strike your sword against the side of Uhud and sit in your house until an erring hand comes to you or God grants you relief.'"],[16558,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Your Lord has fragrant breezes in the days of your lifetime, so expose yourselves to Him, that perhaps a breeze of them may touch you and you will never be wretched after it.'[1]"],[16559,"Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'I arrived from a journey, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of my hand and did not let go of my hand until I let go of his.'"],[16560,"The Prophet ﷺ ate meat at the end of the matter, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[16561,"I passed by and saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on al-Safa with his cheek against the cheek of a man. I went on, and it was not long before the Messenger of God ﷺ called me and said: 'O Muhammad b. Maslamah, what prevented you from greeting?' Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'O Messenger of God, I saw you doing something with this man that you had not done with anyone else among the people, and I disliked to cut you off from your conversation. Who was it, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'It was Gabriel ﷺ . He said: \"What is wrong with Muhammad b. Maslamah that he did not greet? If he had greeted, we would have returned the greeting to him.\"' He said: 'What did he say to you, O Messenger of God?' He said: 'He kept advising me about the neighbor until I expected that he would command me to make him an heir.'"],[16562,"Your cousin—meaning the Messenger of God ﷺ—handed me a sword and said: 'Fight with it as long as the enemy is fought with it. But when you see people killing one another, take it to a rock and strike it against it, then keep to your house until a decree of death or an erring hand comes to you.' He said: 'Let him go.'"],[16563,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'After me there will be tribulations. If you encounter any of them, bring your sword to the side of the harrah and strike it with it, then join al-Rabadhah and be the owner of a camel until an erring hand or a decree of death kills you.'"],[16564,"He came to his sheep and caught two hares; he slaughtered them with a sharp white stone, then brought them to the Prophet ﷺ holding them. He said, “O Messenger of God, I slaughtered them with a sharp white stone.” He said, “Eat both of them.”"],[16565,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with two hares hanging from his hand and said, “O Messenger of God, I came to some sheep of mine and found these two hares, but I had no iron blade with which to slaughter them, so I slaughtered them with a sharp white stone. May I eat them?” He said, “Yes.”"],[16566,"He caught two hares and slaughtered them with a sharp white stone, then asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he commanded him to eat them."],[16567,"I slaughtered two hares with a sharp white stone and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded me to eat them."],[16568,"I slaughtered two hares with a sharp white stone, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him and said, “Should I eat them?” He said, “Yes.”"],[16569,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ and said, “Is there anyone among you who has eaten today?” We said, “Some of us have eaten and some have not.” He said, “Whoever has not eaten should complete his fast, and whoever has eaten something should complete the rest of his day.” Then he sent word to the people of al-ʿArūḍ, ordering them to do likewise."],[16570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ: “Whoever among you has eaten should abstain for the rest of his day, and whoever has not eaten should fast.” And he sent word to the people of al-ʿArūḍ and ordered them to fast it."],[16571,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered his caller on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ: “Whoever is fasting should continue his fast, and whoever has eaten or drunk should complete his fast.”"],[16572,"I was tending sheep for my family in the mountain pass of Uḥud when I caught two young rabbits. I took a stone and slaughtered them with its edge. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said, “Eat it.”"],[16573,"I heard Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib say, “I was born in Abyssinia.”"],[16574,"When my mother brought me from the land of Abyssinia after Ḥāṭib died, she came to the Prophet ﷺ, and one of my hands had suffered a burn from fire. She said, “O Messenger of God, this is Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib, and he has been afflicted with this burn from fire.” Muḥammad b. Ḥāṭib said, “I would not tell a lie about the Messenger of God ﷺ; I do not know whether he blew or wiped over my head and prayed for blessing for me and my descendants.”"],[16575,"Some food from a cooking pot fell on my hand, so my mother took me to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said some words over it: “Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind,” and I think he also said, “Heal, for You are the Healer.”"],[16576,"The cooking pot fell on my hand and it got burned. I was taken to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he would blow on it and say, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people.\" I think he also said, \"And heal, You are the Healer.\""],[16577,"I came near a cooking pot of ours while I was a young boy, and my hand got burned. My mother caught up with me and brought me to a man at al-Batha'. She said, \"O Muhammad, Muhammad's hand got burned.\" The Prophet ﷺ began to blow on it."],[16578,"I came near a cooking pot belonging to my mother and tipped it over onto myself while I was a boy, and my mother took me to the Prophet ﷺ. He performed ruqya on me and said, \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, there is no healer but You.\" He said, I did not retain the words, so I asked my mother about them and she told me during the time of Uthman."],[16579,"I reached for a cooking pot that we had, and my hand got burned. My mother took me to a man in the cemetery and said to him, \"O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"At your service, at your service.\" Then she brought me close to him, and he began to blow and speak words that I did not understand. Later I asked my mother what he was saying, and she said, \"He was saying: 'Remove the affliction, Lord of the people, and heal; You are the Healer, there is no healer but You.'\""],[16580,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I have seen a land with palm trees, so go out.\" He said: So Hatib and Ja'far went out across the sea to the Negus, and I was born on the ship."],[16581,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The separation between the lawful and the unlawful is the voice and the striking of the duff.\""],[16582,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"If one of you is deprived of a wife and children, let him take up jihad.\""],[16583,"'Umar looked at the son of Abdul Hamid, whose name was Muhammad, and a man was speaking to him, saying, \"May Allah do such and such to you, O Muhammad,\" and began to insult him. So 'Umar called him and said, \"O son of Zayd, I do not see Muhammad ﷺ being insulted because of you. By Allah, you will never be called Muhammad as long as I am alive.\" So he named him Abdul Rahman. Then he sent to the Banu Talha, who were seven men, and their leader and elder was Muhammad bin Talha, to change their names. Muhammad said, \"I remind you by Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, for by Allah, Muhammad ﷺ named me Muhammad.\" So he said, \"Stand up, there is no way to change something named by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[16584,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: Three things; if you see them, then it is near, it is near: the destruction of the inhabited and the building up of ruins, that raiding becomes a support, and that a man becomes obstinate with his trust like a camel rubbing against a tree."],[16585,"From his father, who was among those who accompanied the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ came to them in the mosque of Banu Zufar and sat on the rock that is in the mosque of Banu Zufar today, with him Abdullah b. Mas'ud, Mu'adh b. Jabal, and some of his companions. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded a reciter, and he recited until he came to this verse: {How will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?} The Messenger of God ﷺ wept until his jaws trembled, then said, \"O Lord, I bore witness over those among whom I lived, so what about those I did not see?\""],[16586,"The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived in Madinah when I was two weeks old, and I was brought to him. He wiped my head and said, \"Name him with my name, but do not give him my kunya.\" I performed the Farewell Pilgrimage with him when I was ten years old. He said: Muhammad lived long until his head grew gray, but the place where the Prophet's hand had touched did not turn gray."],[16587,"He was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ at the Farewell Pilgrimage when he was ten years old and had a forelock."],[16588,"Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Jahsh b. Ri'ab b. Ya'mar b. Sabira b. Murra b. Kathir b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzayma b. Mudrika b. Ilyas b. Mudar b. Nizar, an ally of Banu Umayya. His paternal grandmother was Umayma bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of God ﷺ. His father was killed as a martyr on the Day of Uhud, and his paternal aunt was Zaynab bt. Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ."],[16589,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he passed by Ma'mar while he was sitting at his house in the market with his thighs uncovered. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, cover your thighs, for the thighs are 'awrah.\""],[16590,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Ma'mar while I was with him, and his thighs were uncovered. He said, \"O Ma'mar, cover your thighs, for the thigh is 'awrah.\""],[16592,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from Banu 'Adi passed by us with his thigh uncovered. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[16593,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the market, and he passed by Ma'mar at his door with his thigh uncovered. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[16595,"That he heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"If a man were killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, then killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, he would not enter Paradise until his debt is settled, and there is neither gold nor silver there; it is only good deeds and bad deeds.\""],[16596,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, if I am killed in the path of God?\" He said, \"Paradise.\" When he turned away, he said, \"Except for debt. Gabriel ﷺ confided to me just now.\""],[16597,"I heard Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Jahsh, who was a companion, say that a man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you think if I fight in the path of God until I am killed?\" He said, \"Paradise.\" When the man turned away, he said, \"Bring him back to me.\" When he came, he said, \"Gabriel ﷺ said, 'Unless he has a debt.'\""],[16598,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: Gabriel ﷺ said to me, \"If a servant is killed in the path of God while he has a debt, he will not enter Paradise until his debt is settled.\""],[16599,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the courtyard of the mosque. He raised his head to the sky and said, \"Glory be to God! What strictness has been sent down?\" We remained for the rest of our day and night. When morning came, I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, what strictness has been sent down?\" He said, \"If a man were killed in the path of God, then brought back to life, then killed, then brought back to life, he would not enter Paradise while he has a debt.\""],[16600,"\"Zaynab bt. Jahsh used to wash the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ in a brass basin.\" 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar said, \"I saw that basin.\""],[16601,"From Muhammad b. Abi 'Amira, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If a servant were dragged on his face from the day he was born until the day he dies of old age in obedience to God, he would consider that insignificant on the Day of Resurrection and would wish to increase it just as he wishes to increase reward and recompense.\""],[16602,"From 'Urwa, \"In naming those who attended al-'Aqaba from the Ansar, then from the Aws, from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal: Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan, and he was a naqib and he attended Badr, and he was the first to pledge allegiance to Islam at al-'Aqaba.\""],[16603,"From Ibn Shihāb: \"Regarding the naming of those who were present at al-ʿAqabah from the Anṣār: Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān, and he was a naqīb (leader).\""],[16604,"\"Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān died in the year twenty, and his name was Mālik.\""],[16605,"\"The first to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of al-ʿAqabah was Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān. He said, 'O Messenger of God, between us and the people there are ropes—and ropes means alliances and covenants—so perhaps we will cut them, then you will return to your people, and we will have cut the ropes and fought the people for your sake.' The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at his words and said, 'Blood for blood, destruction for destruction.' When Abū al-Haytham was satisfied with what the Messenger of God ﷺ said in reply, he turned to his people and said, 'O people, this is the Messenger of God ﷺ. I bear witness that he is truthful, and today he is in God's sanctuary and safety, among his people and clan. Know that if you bring him out, the Arabs will cast you off with a single bow. If you are pleased to fight in the way of God and to lose wealth and children, then call him to your land, for he is truly the Messenger of God ﷺ. But if you fear desertion, then from now on.' ʿAbdullāh said, 'We have accepted from God and His Messenger what He has given us, and we have given you of ourselves what you asked of us, O Messenger of God. So let us, O Abū al-Haytham, be alone with the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him.' Abū al-Haytham said, 'I am the first to pledge allegiance.' Then they all pledged allegiance. Satan shouted from the top of the mountain and said, 'O Quraysh, this is the Khazraj and the Aws allying themselves with Muḥammad to fight you.' They were alarmed and frightened by that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not let this sound frighten you, for it is only the enemy of God, Iblīs; no one you fear hears him.' The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and shouted at Satan, saying, 'O son of Azabb, this is your doing, and I will soon be free to deal with you.'\""],[16606,"\"I missed the ʿIshāʾ prayer one night, and I kept tossing and turning without sleep. I said, 'If only I went out to the mosque and prayed what was decreed for me.' So I did, then I leaned against a corner of it. ʿUmar entered and, when he saw me, he did not recognize me and said, 'Who is this?' I said, 'Abū Bakr.' He said, 'What brought you out at this hour?' I said, 'Hunger.' He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you out.' Before long, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered. When he saw our dark shapes, he did not recognize us and said, 'Who are these two?' ʿUmar rushed ahead of me and said, 'This is Abū Bakr and this is ʿUmar.' He said, 'What brought you two out at this hour?' We told him the news. He said, 'And I, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Come with us to the house of al-Wāqimī.' We came to the door and asked permission. The woman came out, and he said, 'Where is so-and-so?' She said, 'He went to fetch fresh water for us from the orchard of Banū Ḥārithah.' She opened the door, and we entered. Before long he came carrying a water-skin on his back, and he hung it on a palm branch. Then he came to us and said, 'Welcome! What better visitors have visited the people than the visitors who visited me tonight?' Then he brought a cluster of unripe dates, and we began picking them in the moonlight and eating. Then he took the knife and went among the sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, 'Beware of the milking ewe'—or he said, 'the one with milk.' He slaughtered a sheep for us, skinned it, cut it into the pot, and ordered the woman, who kneaded and baked. Then he brought us bread and meat, and we ate. Then he went to the water-skin, which the wind had cooled, and gave us water to drink. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Praise be to God. We went out only because hunger drove us out, and we did not return until we had this. This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16607,"He heard Umar bin Al-Khattab say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out at noon and found Abu Bakr in the mosque, so he asked him, \"What brought you out at this hour?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"What brought you out, O Messenger of Allah?\" Then Umar bin Al-Khattab came and asked, \"What brought you out?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"What brought both of you out?\" Umar sat down and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started talking to them. Then he said, \"There is strength in both of you that can go to this palm tree and bring back food, drink, and dates.\" They both said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Come with us to the house of Abu Al-Haytham bin Tayhan Al-Ansari.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went ahead of us, greeted and sought permission three times, and Umm Al-Haytham listened to his greetings from behind the door, hoping that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would increase his greetings for her. When he wanted to leave, Umm Al-Haytham hurried after them and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard your greetings, but I wanted you to increase your greetings for us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her kindly, then he said, \"Where is Abu Al-Haytham?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he is nearby. He went to fetch water for us. Come in, for the time is near, if Allah wills.\" So she spread a sheet for them under the tree, and Abu Al-Haytham came rejoicing to meet them. His eyes were comforted by seeing them. He climbed a palm tree and cut off some bunches for them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Count (the bunches), O Abu Al-Haytham.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you are eating from its fruit and its dates. Then he brought them water and they all drank. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is part of the blessings that you asked about.\" Abu Al-Haytham got up to slaughter a sheep for them, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Beware of debt.\" Umm Al-Haytham started kneading dough and baking for them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his head, as did Abu Bakr and Umar, near the dish, so they were awakened and found food laid out before them. They ate until they were satisfied, and then Abu Al-Haytham brought the remaining bunches, and they ate from its dates and its fruit. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeted them and prayed for them with goodness."],[16608,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ went out at an hour when he did not usually go out. Then Abū Bakr went out, and he said to him, \"What brought you out, O Abū Bakr?\" He said, \"Hunger brought me out.\" He said, \"And I, what brought me out is what brought you out.\" Then ʿUmar went out, and he said to him, \"What brought you out, O ʿUmar?\" He said, \"By the One who sent you with the truth, hunger brought me out.\" Then some of his companions came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to them, \"Come with us to the house of Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān.\" They went, and when they reached Abū al-Haytham's house, his wife said, \"Abū al-Haytham has gone to fetch fresh water for us, so go around to the garden.\" She opened the garden gate for them, and they sat down. Abū al-Haytham came, and his wife said to him, \"Do you know who is with you?\" He said, \"No.\" She said, \"With you are the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions.\" He entered, tied his horse to a palm tree, then came to them and greeted them warmly and welcomed them. Then he went to his date-palm grove, brought a cluster, picked fresh dates for them, and brought it and poured it before them. Then Abū al-Haytham reached for a small flock of his in a corner of the garden to slaughter a sheep for them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"As for one with milk, no.\" He took a sheep, slaughtered it, skinned it, cut it into pieces, and cooked it with water and salt. Then he went to his wife and asked her, \"Do you have anything?\" She said, \"Yes, we have some barley that we were saving.\" They ground it together, then she kneaded it and baked it. Abū al-Haytham broke the bread and poured that cooked meat over it. Then he brought it to the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions, and they ate. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, do you not have a servant?\" He said, \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, we have no servant.\" He said, \"When you hear that captives have come to us, come to us and we will provide you with a servant.\" Captives came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abū al-Haytham came to him while two boys—or he said two youths—were before him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, choose one of them\"—or he said, \"choose between them.\" Abū al-Haytham said, \"O Messenger of God, choose for me.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ rolled up his sleeves and said, \"The one whose advice is sought is entrusted. O Abū al-Haytham, take this one.\" When Abū al-Haytham turned away with him, he said, \"O Abū al-Haytham, treat him well, for I saw him praying.\" He said, \"Yes, we will feed him from what we eat and clothe him from what we wear, and we will not burden him with work he cannot bear.\" Abū al-Haytham went to his family, and they rejoiced greatly and said, \"Praise be to God who provided us with a servant to serve us and help us with our property.\" Abū al-Haytham said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me concerning him.\" His wife said, \"Yes, we will feed him from what we eat and clothe him from what we wear, and we will not burden him with work he cannot bear.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined me concerning him.\" His wife said, \"Glory be to God! A servant whom God and His Messenger have given us—do you want to deprive us of him?\" Abū al-Haytham said to the boy, \"You are free for the sake of God. If you like to stay with us, we will feed you from what we eat and clothe you from what we wear, and we will not burden you with work except what you can bear. And if you wish, go wherever you wish.\""],[16609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out at an hour when he did not usually go out and when no one would meet him. Abū Bakr came to him, and he said, \"What brought you out, O Abū Bakr?\" He said, \"I went out to the Messenger of God ﷺ to look at his face and greet him.\" Before long, ʿUmar came, and he said, \"What brought you out, O ʿUmar?\" He said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"And I have felt some of what you feel. Come with us to Abū al-Haytham b. al-Tayhān al-Anṣārī.\" He was a man with many horses and sheep, but he had no servant. They went to him and did not find him, but found his wife. He said, \"Where is your companion?\" She said, \"He went out early to fetch fresh water from the canal of Banū So-and-so.\" Before long, he came with a water-skin and set it down. Then he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, embracing him and ransoming him with his father and mother. He took them to the shade of his garden and spread a mat for them. Then he went to a palm tree and brought a cluster. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Why did you not pick out its fresh dates?\" He said, \"I wanted you to enjoy its fresh and unripe dates.\" They ate and drank from that water. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, this is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection: this cool shade, the fresh dates, and the water.\" He said, \"Go and prepare food for them.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not slaughter a milking animal.\" He slaughtered a young she-goat or a kid for them, then came to them and they ate."],[16610,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ went out and came upon Abū Bakr and ʿUmar ؓ. He said, \"What brought you two out of your houses?\" They said, \"Hunger.\" He said, \"And I, by the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing brought me out except what brought you two out. Get up.\" They got up with him, and he went to a man from the Anṣār. The Anṣārī was not there, but his wife was. He said to her, \"Where is so-and-so?\" She said, \"He went to fetch fresh water for us.\" While they were thus, the Anṣārī came carrying a water-skin. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ and his two companions, he said, \"God is greatest! No one is more honored than our guests.\" He hung up the water-skin, cut a cluster of dates for them—unripe, fresh, and dry—and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Why did you not pick out the best?\" He said, \"Choose, O Messenger of God, with your own eyes.\" He took the knife, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, \"Beware of the milking ewe.\" He slaughtered for them, and they ate. When they finished, the Prophet ﷺ said to them, \"You will surely be asked about this blessing on the Day of Resurrection. Hunger drove you out of your houses, and you did not return until you had obtained this blessing.\""],[16611,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar came to us, and we fed them fresh dates and gave them water to drink. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[16612,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The one whose advice is sought is entrusted.\""],[16613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum,' ten good deeds are written for him. Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Allāh,' twenty good deeds are written for him. Whoever says 'al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatu Allāh wa barakātuhu,' fifty good deeds are written for him.\""],[16614,"On the authority of Muhammad b. Ishaq: \"In naming those who attended Badr: Abu Usayd Malik b. Rabi'a b. al-Budn b. 'Amir b. 'Awf b. Haritha b. 'Amr b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'ida b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. Haritha b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. 'Amir.\""],[16615,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi lost his sight before the killing of 'Uthman, and he said: \"Praise be to Allah who granted me my sight during the life of the Prophet ﷺ; then when Allah willed the trial for His servants, He withheld my sight from it.\""],[16616,"\"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi, whose name was Malik b. Rabi'a, died in the year thirty, at the age of ninety.\""],[16617,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi said to me after he had lost his sight: \"O my nephew, if you and I were now at Badr, and Allah restored my sight, I would show you the mountain pass from which the angels came out upon us, without any doubt or dispute.\""],[16618,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then Banu Sa'ida, and in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.\" Sa'd b. 'Ubada said: \"I see that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has only favored others over us.\" He said: \"You have been favored over many.\""],[16619,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he was leaving the mosque, when men and women had mingled on the road, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Step back, for it is not for you to occupy the center of the road. Keep to the edges of the road.\" And the woman would cling to the wall until her garment would catch on something from the wall due to her clinging."],[16620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr when we lined up for battle: \"If they draw near you, shoot them with arrows.\""],[16621,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When they draw near you, shoot them with arrows.\""],[16622,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us with some companions, and we went out with him. We set off until we reached a walled garden called al-Shawt, and then we reached two walled gardens and sat between them. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sit here.\" The Jawniyya woman had been brought and secluded in the house of Umayma bt. al-Harith b. Sharahil, and with her was a nurse of hers. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, he said: \"Give yourself to me.\" She said: \"Does a queen give herself to a commoner?\" He reached out his hand to place it upon her, and she said: \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" He said: \"You have sought refuge with One who grants refuge.\" Then he came out to us and said: \"O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two Raziqi garments and send her back to her family.\""],[16623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib: \"O Abu al-Fadl, do not leave your house, you and your sons, tomorrow until I come to you.\" So they waited for him until he came after the sun had risen high. He entered upon them and said: \"Peace be upon you.\" They said: \"And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\" He said: \"How are you this morning?\" They said: \"Well; we praise Allah.\" Then he said: \"Come close, come close, come close; move toward one another.\" Until when they had made room for him, he enveloped them with his cloak and said: \"O Lord, this is my uncle and the like of my father, and these are my household, so shield them from the Fire as I shield them with this cloak of mine.\" He said: \"Then the threshold of the door and the walls of the house said 'Amen,' saying: 'Amen, Amen, Amen.'\""],[16624,"It is called the Well of Goods, into which the Prophet ﷺ spat and blessed. Abu Umayr cut the fruit of his wall and put it in his room. The Ghul would come to his water trough and steal his dates, spoiling them. Abu Umayr complained to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"That is the Ghul, O Abu Umayr. Listen to her and when you hear her entering, say 'In the name of Allah, the Messenger of Allah has prevented me.' Then the Ghul said, 'O Abu Umayr, let me go and I will not burden you. I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and bring you a proof from Allah that I will not go to your house or steal your dates.' I will guide you to a verse from the Book of Allah that you can recite over your house, so that you do not go to your family or uncover your utensils.' She gave him the proof that pleased him, and said, 'The verse that I guide you to is Ayat al-Kursi.' Then she went and disappeared. Abu Umayr came to the Prophet ﷺ and narrated the story to him, where she had gone. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'She told the truth, but she is a liar.'"],[16625,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom, I have seen a place for a market; will you not look at it?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So he stood with him until he came to the place of the market. When he saw it, it pleased him, and he struck it with his foot, then said: \"This is an excellent market of yours; let it not be diminished, and let no tax be imposed upon it.\""],[16626,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Muhammad b. Salih al-Tammar narrated to us, from Yazid b. Zayd, from Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi, who said: \"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the grave of Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. They began to pull the striped cloak over his face, and his feet would become uncovered; and they pulled it over his feet, and his face would become uncovered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Place it over his face, and put some of this shrub over his feet.'\" He said: \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head and saw his companions weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A time will come upon people when they go out to the countryside and find there food, clothing, and mounts—or he said: mounts—and they write to their families: Come to us, for you are in a land of passage and drought. But Madinah is better for them, if only they knew. No one patiently endures its hardship and severity except that I will be an intercessor and a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[16627,"Regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving the Ansar a choice, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The best of the tribes of the Ansar are the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then Banu Saʿidah, and in all of the Ansar there is good.\" Abu Usayd said: If I were to say anything other than the truth, I would have started with my own grandfather. And Abu Usayd was a Saʿidi."],[16628,"Abu Usayd, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him, saying: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"The best dwellings of the Ansar are the dwellings of Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then the dwelling of al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the dwelling of Banu Saʿidah, and in all the dwellings of the Ansar there is good.\" Abu Usayd said: If I were a liar, I would have started with my own people, Banu Saʿidah. That reached Saʿd b. ʿUbadah, and he felt distressed about it. He said: We were created and we became the least important of the four. Saddle my donkey for me so I can go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His nephew Sahl said to him: Will you go to reject the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Allah and His Messenger know best. So he ordered his donkey to be unsaddled."],[16629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbd al-Ashhal, then Banu Saʿidah, then Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.\""],[16630,"The people came to the Prophet ﷺ for the digging of the trench, pledging allegiance to him upon emigration. When he finished, he said: \"O company of Ansar, do not pledge allegiance upon emigration. The people only emigrate to you. Whoever meets Allah while loving the Ansar, he meets Allah while Allah loves him. And whoever meets Allah while hating the Ansar, he meets Allah while Allah hates him.\""],[16631,"While I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man from the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any way I can be dutiful to my parents after their death? He said: Yes, four qualities: praying for them, seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their promises after their death, honoring their friends, and maintaining the ties of kinship that you have only through them. He said: This is what remains upon me."],[16632,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no prayer after the ʿAsr prayer.\""],[16633,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mixing dates and raisins together."],[16634,"I heard Abu Usayd al-Saʿidi, while Ibn ʿAbbas was giving a legal opinion allowing a dinar for two dinars, and Abu Usayd said to him harshly. Ibn ʿAbbas said: I did not think anyone who knows my relation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say such a thing to me, O Abu Usayd. Abu Usayd said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A dinar for a dinar, a dirham for a dirham, a saʿ of wheat for a saʿ of wheat, a saʿ of barley for a saʿ of barley, a saʿ of salt for a saʿ of salt, no excess between any of that.\" Ibn ʿAbbas said: This is something I said by my own opinion, and I had not heard anything about it."],[16635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with olive oil, for it comes from a blessed tree.\""],[16636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it comes from a blessed tree.\""],[16637,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me about the night he was taken on the night journey."],[16639,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"On the night I was taken on the night journey, I did not pass by any angel among the angels except that they ordered me to be cupped.\""],[16640,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and we stopped at a place. They slept through the prayer until the sun rose. The Prophet ﷺ got up, ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer, and they performed ablution and prayed two rak'ahs. Then Bilal gave the iqamah, and the Prophet ﷺ led us in prayer. Then he narrated to us what will happen until the Day of Resurrection, which those who memorized it memorized and those who forgot it forgot."],[16641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept at dawn and did not wake up until the sun had risen. He woke up, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer. Then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he gave the order and prayed Fajr."],[16642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and then narrated to us what will happen until the Hour is established."],[16643,"About the Prophet ﷺ in one of his sermons, he said, \"O Allah, forgive those who shave their heads.\" A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who trim their hair?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And those who trim their hair too.\""],[16644,"He witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Day of the Tree and the Day of the Hady, when it was detained before reaching its place of sacrifice. A man from the polytheists said, 'O Muhammad, what compels you to bring these people upon us while we are unwilling?' He said, 'These are better than you and your forefathers. They believe in Allah and the Last Day. By the One in whose hand is my soul, he has indeed ؓ.'"],[16645,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a man and he did not host me or offer me hospitality. Then he passes by me—should I host him?' He said, 'Rather, host him.'"],[16646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw 'Ali wearing worn-out clothes and said, 'Do you have any wealth?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'From what kind of wealth?' I said, 'From everything; Allah has given me.' He said, 'Then let Allah's blessing and honor upon you be seen.'"],[16650,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing two cloaks or two wraps. He said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth.\" He said, \"Then let the favor of Allah be seen on you.\" The next morning I went to him wearing a red fine garment."],[16651,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing shabby clothes and was in a poor appearance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, of all kinds of wealth.\" He said, \"Then let what Allah has provided you be seen on you.\""],[16652,"My father entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in patched garments. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me camels, cattle, and sheep.\" He said, \"Then let what Allah has granted you be seen on you.\""],[16653,"That ‘Awf b. Mālik, meaning his father, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing worn-out clothes. He said, \"O ‘Awf b. Mālik, do your camels not give birth when their ears are sound, and then you go to some of them and slit their ears and say, 'This is a baḥīrah,' and you go to some of them and split their ears and then say, 'This is a ṣurum'? Do not do so. Allah's forearm is stronger than your forearm, and Allah's razor is sharper. Everything Allah has given you is lawful, so do not make anything of your wealth unlawful.\" Then he said to him, \"O ‘Awf b. Mālik, which of your slaves is more beloved to you: the one who obeys you and follows your command, or the one who does not obey you and does not follow your command?\" He said, \"Rather my slave who obeys me and follows my command.\" He said, \"Thus are you before your Lord, Exalted is He.\""],[16654,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and began asking the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw his poor appearance, he said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" He said, \"Yes, every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me camels, sheep, and horses.\" He said, \"When Allah grants you wealth, let it be seen on you.\""],[16655,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was in poor appearance. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you have any wealth?\" I said, \"Yes, of every kind of wealth. Allah has granted me.\" He said, \"When you have wealth, let it be seen on you.\""],[16657,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who saw him in poor condition. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Do you not have wealth?” He said: He replied, “Yes.” He said, “Then let the blessing of God be visible upon you.”"],[16658,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing worn-out clothes. He said, “Do you have wealth?” I said, “Yes, of every kind of wealth God has given me,” and he enumerated horses, camels, slaves, and sheep. He said, “When God gives you good, let it be visible upon you.”"],[16659,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ in a shabby condition. He said to me, “Do you have any wealth?” I said, “Yes, camels, sheep, and slaves.” He said, “Then why is it not visible upon you?”"],[16662,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ saw him disheveled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He said to him, “What wealth do you have?” He said, “Of every kind of wealth God has given me.” He said, “When God bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him.”"],[16664,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he said the takbīr to enter prayer, raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing—the wording is the same."],[16665,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when he entered prayer, raised his hands to the top of his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[16666,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the takbir, raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and when he raised his head from bowing he did likewise."],[16667,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he said the takbir until they were level with his ears, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."],[16668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the takbir, raised his hands until they were near his ears, and when he bowed he did the same, and when he raised his head from bowing he did the same."],[16669,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ raise his hands until they were level with the tops of his ears. Yazīd b. Zurayʿ added: \"and when he bowed likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing likewise.\""],[16670,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he said the takbir, when he intended to bow, and when he raised his head from bowing, around his ears."],[16671,"He said to them: \"Put forward a man from among you to lead you in prayer, and I shall tell you why I do not lead you in prayer. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever visits a people should not lead them in prayer; let a man from among them lead them.'\""],[16672,"He said to his companions: \"Shall I show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was?\" That was at a time other than prayer time. He stood, then bowed, saying the takbir, then raised his head and stood for a short while, then prostrated, then raised his head and waited, then prostrated, then raised his head and waited for a short while, then prostrated. The wording is that of ʿĀrim."],[16673,"\"I am going to lead you in prayer, but I do not intend the prayer; I only want to show you how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray.\" Ayyūb said: I asked Abū Qilābah, \"How was his prayer?\" He said, \"Like the prayer of our shaykh, ʿAmr b. Salamah. The shaykh would complete the takbirs, and when he raised his head from the first rakʿah he would lean on the ground and then stand.\""],[16674,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as young men and stayed with him for about twenty nights or days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"When you return to your families,\" or he said, \"to your lands, teach them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful. \"Command them to pray such-and-such a prayer at such-and-such a time, and such-and-such a prayer at such-and-such a time. When the prayer is due, let one of you call the adhan, and let the eldest of you lead the prayer.\" The wording is that of the hadith of ʿĀrim."],[16675,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The eldest of a people should lead them in prayer.\" Malik b. al-Ḥuwayrith, when he raised his head from the second prostration, would sit and then rise."],[16676,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of young men of similar age and stayed with him for twenty nights. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was merciful, gentle, and forbearing. He thought that we missed our families and longed for them, so he asked us about those we had left behind, and we told him. He said: \"Return to your families, stay with them, teach them, and command them.\" And he said: \"When the prayer is due, let one of you call the adhan, and let the eldest of you lead the prayer.\""],[16677,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you are with your companion, call the adhan and the iqamah, and let the elder of you two lead the prayer.\""],[16678,"Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ intending to travel. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you two set out, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\""],[16679,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him and to a companion of his, \"When the prayer time arrives, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\""],[16680,"The Prophet ﷺ said to him and to a companion of his, \"When the prayer time arrives, then give the call to prayer (adhan), then say the iqamah, and let the older of you lead the prayer.\" I said to Abu Qilabah, \"Then where does the recitation come in?\" He said, \"They were close in age.\""],[16681,"About the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: He would pray at other than prayer times, and when he raised his head from the second prostration in the first rak'ah, he would sit upright, then stand, supporting himself on the ground.\""],[16682,"The Prophet ﷺ made us recite it. On that day, He will not punish nor bind."],[16683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When Allah wants to create a soul and the man has intercourse with the woman, his fluid flies into every vein and nerve of hers. Then on the seventh day, Allah ﷻ makes green for him every vein between him and Adam.\" Then he recited: {In whatever form He willed, He assembled you}."],[16684,"\"Shall I not tell you how your Prophet ﷺ used to pray?\" We said, \"Yes.\" So he stepped forward and prayed two rak'ahs, making them brief. Abu Qilabah and I differed about his knees: I said he kept them close to the ground, and Abu Qilabah said he kept them apart."],[16685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever I am his mawla (patron), Ali is his mawla.\""],[16686,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali: \"Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa?\""],[16687,"Malik b. al-Huwayrith said: \"The first of the men to embrace Islam was Ali, and among the women, Khadijah.\""],[16688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the steps of the pulpit and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended another step and said, \"Ameen.\" Then he ascended another step and said, \"Ameen.\" He said, \"Jibril ﷺ came to me and said, 'O Muhammad, whoever reaches the age of his parents or one of them and does not enter Paradise, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen. And whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen. And whoever hears your name and does not send blessings upon you, may Allah distance him.' Say Ameen, so I said Ameen."],[16689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.\""],[16690,"\"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I never prayed behind an imam of a people whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[16691,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we never prayed behind an imam whose prescribed prayer was lighter than his."],[16692,"That his father Malik and his paternal uncles Qays and Ubayd, the sons of al-Khashkhash, came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about a man from their cousins raiding the people. So the Messenger of God ﷺ wrote for them: \"This is a letter from Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, to Malik, Ubayd, and Qays, the sons of al-Khashkhash. You are granted security as Muslims for your blood and your property. You will not be taken to account for the crime of others, and none will commit a crime against you except your own hands.\""],[16693,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"God does not accept from a suqqūr any sarf or ʿadl.\" It was said, \"What is a suqqūr, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"One who brings a man to his wife [for illicit intercourse].\""],[16694,"That he was present with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the conquest [of Makkah], at Khaybar, and at al-Ta'if. He was a poet, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, give me a ruling about poetry.\" He said, \"For the space between your chest and your shoulder to be filled with pus is better than for it to be filled with poetry.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, wipe over my head.\" He placed his hand on my head, and after that I never uttered a line of poetry. Malik lived to old age until his head and beard turned white, but the place where the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ had been did not turn white."],[16695,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ate food one day and then said, \"Cover for me so that I may bathe.\" I said, \"Were you in a state of major ritual impurity, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I informed Umar b. al-Khattab of that, and he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said to him, \"This one claims that you ate while you were in a state of major ritual impurity?\" He said, \"Yes, when I have performed ablution I eat and drink, but I do not pray or recite until I bathe.\""],[16696,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"This companion of yours is indeed a memorizer and a destroyer. The last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined upon us was that he said: 'Whoever memorizes something from me, let him relate it. And whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[16697,"Malik said: \"This companion of yours is heedless and a destroyer. The Messenger of God ﷺ enjoined us during the Farewell Pilgrimage, saying: 'Hold fast to the Quran, for you will return to a people who desire hadith from me. Whoever understands something, let him relate it. And whoever fabricates a lie against me, let him take a seat or something from Hell.'\" \"I do not know which of the two he said.\""],[16698,"From Hassan, the freed slave of Malik b. Abdullah al-Khath'ami, and Malik was one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"I saw Malik b. Abdullah performing ablution, and on his shin there was a vein inscribed 'For God.' I began to look at it, and he said, 'What are you looking at? Indeed, no writer wrote it.'\""],[16699,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Abu Qatadah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever sees me in a dream will see me while awake, and Satan cannot imitate me.\""],[16700,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of God, God has forbidden him to the Fire.\""],[16701,"It was said to him: \"Will you not ride, since God has carried you?\" He said: \"Indeed the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever's feet become dusty in the path of God, God has forbidden him to the Fire.'\""],[16702,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a man praying when the prayer had already been commenced. He spoke to him something I do not know what it was. When we finished, we surrounded him saying, \"What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say to you?\" He said: \"He said: 'It is likely that he will pray the morning prayer as four [rakʿahs].'\""],[16703,"He said to his brother Malik b. Haidah, \"Go with us to the Prophet ﷺ, for he knows you but does not know me. He has detained some people of Banu Bahdam, my neighbors.\" So they came to him, and Malik b. Haidah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam and my neighbors have embraced Islam, so release them.\" He did not answer him. Then he repeated it, and he did not answer him. Then he repeated it, and he did not answer him. Then he stood up, enraged, and said, \"If you do that, they claim that you call to the matter but act contrary to it.\" I began to rebuke him and forbid him. He said, \"What is he saying?\" They said, \"He says such and such.\" He said, \"If he does that, that is upon me, not upon them for it. Leave him his neighbors.\""],[16704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no Muslim over whom three rows pray but that it becomes obligatory [for him to be forgiven].\" He said: When Malik met the people of a funeral procession, he would divide them into three rows."],[16705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire: a bone from the bones of the one he freed for a bone from his own bones.\""],[16706,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever reaches one of his parents and then is not forgiven, may Allah distance him. And whoever takes in an orphan between two parents into his food and drink until Allah makes him self-sufficient, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\""],[16707,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslims into his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes absolutely obligatory for him. Any man who reaches his parents or one of them and then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him. Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire.\""],[16708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslim parents until he becomes self-sufficient, Allah has made Paradise absolutely obligatory for him.\""],[16709,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes in an orphan between two Muslims into his food and drink until he becomes independent of him, Paradise becomes absolutely obligatory for him. And whoever frees a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire, each limb of his ransoming a limb of his.\""],[16710,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"If you meet a collector of tithes, kill him\" — meaning by that the one who takes zakat without right."],[16712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the delegation of Hawazin at Hunayn when he asked them about Malik b. Awf al-Nasri: \"What has Malik done?\" They said, \"He is in al-Ta'if.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Inform Malik that if he comes to me as a Muslim, I will return to him his family and his wealth and give him a hundred camels.\" So this reached Malik, and he left al-Ta'if. Malik had feared for himself from Thaqif, lest they learn that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to him what he said and detain him. So he ordered a mount of his to be prepared, and he ordered a horse of his to be brought to him from al-Ta'if. He left at night, mounted his horse, and caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reaching him at al-Ji'ranah or Makkah. He returned to him his family and his wealth and gave him a hundred camels."],[16713,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a well, and in it was a black man, dead. He said: He looked into the well, and there he was thrown into the well. The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"Why is he thrown into the well?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he was harsh in religion; he would pray sometimes and sometimes not pray.\" He said, \"Woe to you, take him out.\" So the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be washed and shrouded. He said, \"Carry him.\" And he said, \"The angels almost preceded us.\" He said: And he prayed over him."],[16714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is prompted at death to say the testimony that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise.\""],[16715,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Leave people alone so that some may obtain from others, but if your brother seeks your sincere advice, then advise him sincerely.”"],[16716,"From ʿUrwa: “Regarding the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of God ﷺ among the Muslims, then among the Ansar, then among the Banū ʿAbd al-Ashhal: Maḥmūd b. Maslama.”"],[16718,"“Mu‘āwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān died with four nights having passed of Rajab in the year 60.” Ibn Kathīr said: “His age was in his seventy-some years, up to eighty.”"],[16719,"“Muʿāwiya died in the year sixty, and his age was between seventy-something and eighty.”"],[16720,"He heard Muʿāwiya say: “The Messenger of God ﷺ died at sixty-three, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar did too, and I am sixty-three.”"],[16721,"“Muʿāwiya was tall, fair-skinned, and bald on the front of his head.”"],[16722,"“Muʿāwiya came to us, and he was the fairest of people and the most handsome of them.”"],[16723,"“I saw Muʿāwiya at al-Abṭaḥ with a white head and beard as if it were snow.”"],[16724,"Muʿāwiya set out from Syria intending Makkah and stopped at a place between Makkah and Madinah called al-Abwāʾ. He looked into an ancient well and was struck by facial paralysis. He hastened his journey until he arrived in Makkah. The chamberlain came to him and said, “O Commander of the Faithful, the people are at the door; I do not miss any face.” He said, “Then spread out for me, then.” Then he called for a turban, wrapped it around his head, and split it over his face. Then he went out, praised God and extolled Him, and then said: “To proceed: If I am granted health, then indeed the righteous before me were granted health, and I would not wish to conceal that I hope to be among them. If one of my limbs has become ill, I cannot count my healthy ones. If some of your elite have found fault with me, I have been at war against your common people. I have no desire to wish from God more than what He has given me. May God have mercy on a man who prays for my well-being.” The voices rose with supplication and he was moved to tears. Marwān said to him, “What makes you weep, O Commander of the Faithful?” He said, “I recalled what I had turned away from: my age has advanced, my bones have become thin, tears have increased in my eyes, I have been struck in my best part and what appears of me. Were it not for my desire for Yazīd, I would have perceived my right course.”"],[16725,"I was taking a midday nap in a church in Jericho, which at that time was a mosque where people prayed. Then ʿAwf b. Mālik awoke from his sleep, and there was a lion with him in the room walking toward him. He rose in alarm to his weapon, and the lion said to him, “Wait! I have only been sent to you with a message for you to convey.” I said, “Who sent you?” He said, “God sent me to you so that you may inform Muʿāwiya the traveler that he is among the people of Paradise.” I said, “Who is Muʿāwiya?” He said, “The son of Abū Sufyān.”"],[16726,"I raided with Muʿāwiya b. Abī Sufyān in the land of the Romans, and a fox fell into his saddle. He called out, “O servants of God, O Muslims!” The first to answer was Muʿāwiya, and he dismounted and the people dismounted. They said, “We will suffice the commander.” He said, “Indeed, it has reached me that the first to bring aid is Gabriel, so I desired to be the second.”"],[16727,"Ali ﷺ : \"My slain and Muawiyah's slain are in Paradise.\""],[16728,"I heard Mujalid ibn Sa'id saying, \"May Allah have mercy on Mu'awiya, how strong was his love for the Arabs.\""],[16729,"Abu Sufyan: Leave your brother."],[16730,"I heard al-A'mash say: If you saw Muawiyah, you would say, 'This is the Mahdi.'"],[16731,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ with the arrowhead of a Bedouin near al-Marwah saying, \"When he prohibited mut'ah.\""],[16732,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ during his Umrah at al-Marwah with an arrowhead.\""],[16733,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ near al-Marwah with an arrowhead during his Hajj.\""],[16734,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ near al-Marwah with an arrowhead.\""],[16735,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Marwah with the arrowhead of a Bedouin.\""],[16736,"He informed him, \"That he saw the Messenger of God ﷺ shorten his hair with an arrowhead.\" We said to Ibn Abbas, \"This has only reached us from Muawiyah.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Muawiyah was not accused regarding the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[16737,"Muawiyah said to me, \"Have you considered one who performs tamattu' and drives the sacrificial animal—does he touch anything of his hair?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"I bear witness that I took from the hair of the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Marwah when he finished his circumambulation with an arrowhead from his quiver.\""],[16738,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"That he prohibited wearing gold.\""],[16739,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"That he prohibited wearing jewelry and gold.\""],[16740,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri ؓ, who said: Mu'awiya came out to a circle in the mosque and said, \"What made you sit?\" They said, \"We sat to remember Allah.\" He said, \"By Allah, nothing made you sit except that?\" They said, \"By Allah, nothing made us sit except that.\" He said, \"Indeed, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you. No one of my standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has fewer hadiths from him than I. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to a circle of his Companions and said, 'What made you sit?' They said, 'We sat to remember Allah and praise Him for guiding us to Islam and blessing us with you.' He said, 'By Allah, nothing made you sit except that?' They said, 'By Allah, nothing made us sit except that.' He said, 'Indeed, I did not make you swear out of suspicion of you. Jibril ﷺ came to me and informed me that Allah ﷻ boasts of you to the angels.'\""],[16741,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Do not pry into people, lest you corrupt them.\""],[16742,"\"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and 'Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16743,"\"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16744,"I heard Muawiyah say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three.\""],[16745,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away at the age of sixty-three, Abu Bakr passed away at the age of sixty-three, and 'Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three."],[16746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah ﷻ placed truth upon the tongue and heart of 'Umar.\""],[16747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us on the day of 'Ashura and said, \"This is a day whose fasting is not prescribed for you, and I am fasting. Whoever wishes to fast may fast, and whoever wishes to break it may break it.\""],[16748,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Excellent is the tribe of al-Azd and the Ash'aris.\" Mu'awiya said, \"It was not like that; he said, 'They are from me and to me.'\""],[16749,"[He said] to Mu'awiya during the exchange between them regarding the pledge to Yazid: \"And you, O Mu'awiya, informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If there are two caliphs on earth, kill one of them.'\""],[16750,"When you come to my tent, stand among the people and inform them of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the traders are wicked.\" A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not permitted trade?\" He said, \"Indeed, they speak and lie, and they swear and sin.\""],[16751,"About something that Muawiyah saw in the prayer, he said: \"I prayed with him (Muhammad) the Friday prayer in the enclosure. When he finished, I stood in my place and prayed. When he entered (the enclosure), he sent for me and said, 'Do not repeat what you did when you pray the Friday prayer. Do not connect it with another prayer until you speak or leave. For the Prophet ﷺ commanded that.' Additionally, he added in his narration, 'Do not connect it with another prayer until you speak or leave.'\""],[16752,"Mu'awiya said, \"Do not do that, for I know the Messenger of Allah ﷺ better.\""],[16753,"About the two prostrations that are prayed after Jumu'ah in the mosque and the two prostrations after 'Asr.\" Mu'awiya said, \"And I know the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ better.\""],[16754,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon in Madinah on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while in his hand was a lock of hair. He said, “Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding this.” And he said, “Those before you were destroyed only when their women adopted this.”"],[16755,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon, saying, “O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and Allah has not prescribed its fasting. I am fasting, so whoever wishes to fast, let him fast, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break it.’”"],[16756,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Juhaynah is from me and I am from them. They are angry for my anger and pleased for my pleasure. I become angry for their anger and pleased for their pleasure. Whoever angers them has angered me, and whoever angers me has angered Allah.” Muʿāwiyah said to him, “He only said this hadith about the Quraysh.” ʿImrān said, “I heard it from the Prophet ﷺ, while you were dead at that time.”"],[16757,"We were sitting around Muʿāwiyah’s bed, and he came out to us and said, “What were you talking about?” They said, “We were talking about something from the talk of the Anṣār.” Muʿāwiyah said, “Shall I give you more, a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They said, “Yes, O Commander of the Believers.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Whoever loves the Anṣār, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Anṣār, Allah hates him.’”"],[16758,"I heard Muʿāwiyah: when the muʾadhdhin said the takbīr twice, he said the takbīr twice; and when he bore witness twice, he bore witness twice. Then he turned to me and said, “This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say at the adhān.”"],[16759,"He heard the muʾadhdhin say the takbīr, and he said the takbīr; and he bore witness as he bore witness. Then he said, “This is how Muʿāwiyah narrated to us that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say as the muʾadhdhin said. When he said, ‘I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah,’ he said, ‘And I bear witness,’ then he was silent.”"],[16762,"I entered with Muʿāwiyah upon ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers. She said, “O Muʿāwiyah, you killed Ḥujr and his companions, and you did what you did. Were you not afraid that I would hide a man for you who would kill you in retaliation for Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr?” He said, “No, for I am in a secure house. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘Faith restrains assassination; a believer does not assassinate.’ O Mother of the Believers, how am I regarding your needs, your messengers, and your affairs?” She said, “Good.” He said, “Then leave me and Ḥujr until we meet before Allah.”"],[16763,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is pleased that men stand up for him when they see him coming, let him take a seat in the Fire.”"],[16764,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade false hair, and false hair is when a woman attaches hair."],[16765,"“That the Prophet ﷺ forbade false hair.”"],[16766,"“O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden you false hair.” He then brought a black rag and threw it before them, then said, “It is this: a woman puts it on her head and then covers herself with a veil over it.”"],[16767,"Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and stood on the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand. He said, “I did not think that anyone would do this, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called it false hair.”"],[16768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whomever God wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.\""],[16769,"I was sitting with Mu'awiyah, and when the muezzin gave the call to prayer and said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God,\" Mu'awiyah said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God.\" Then the muezzin said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" Then the muezzin said, \"Come to prayer,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" Then he said, \"Come to success,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" Then he said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" Then he said, \"There is no god but God,\" and Mu'awiyah said, \"There is no god but God.\" Then Mu'awiyah said, \"This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[16770,"That Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Come to prayer.\" He said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" He said, \"Come to success.\" He said, \"There is no might and no power except with God.\" He said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" Mu'awiyah said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest.\" He said, \"There is no god but God.\" He said, \"There is no god but God.\" Then he said, \"This is how I heard your Prophet ﷺ say.\""],[16771,"He heard Mu'awiyah on the pulpit of the Prophet ﷺ with a lock of hair in his hand, saying, \"I found this among my family, and they claimed that women add it to their hair. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'God has cursed the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who has them attached.'\""],[16772,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A life grant is permissible for its recipients.\""],[16773,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"A life grant is permissible.\""],[16774,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A life grant is like an inheritance.\""],[16775,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"The people with the longest necks are the Muadhin (callers to prayer).\""],[16776,"We entered upon Mu'awiyah, and the caller called to prayer. He said, \"God is greatest, God is greatest,\" and Mu'awiyah said just as he said. He said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God,\" and he said the same again. He said, \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God,\" and he said the same. Then he said, \"This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say.\""],[16777,"I witnessed 'Uthman delivering a sermon on the pulpit standing, and I witnessed Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon sitting. He said, \"Indeed, I have not been ignorant of the Sunnah, but I have grown old, my bones have become frail, and your needs have increased. I wanted to attend to some of your needs while sitting, then stand and take my share of the Sunnah.\""],[16778,"Listen carefully, O son of my brother, to a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Talhah is among those who have fulfilled their vow.\""],[16779,"He saw Mu'awiyah delivering a sermon on the pulpit with a lock of hair in his hand, and he heard him say, \"Where are your scholars, O people of Madinah? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the like of this, and he said: 'The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted these.'\""],[16780,"He heard Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, with a lock of hair in his hand, saying, \"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding the like of this, and saying: 'The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted these.'\""],[16781,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; ḥ, and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān in the year of his ḥajj while he was on the pulpit, and he took a lock of hair that was in the hand of a guard, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: 'The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.'\" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī."],[16782,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted it.\""],[16783,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this lock of hair, saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted it.\""],[16784,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were punished only when their women adopted the like of this.\""],[16785,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the like of this and saying: \"The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.\""],[16786,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and said: \"Where are your scholars?\" He brought out a bundle of hair from his sleeve and said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding this, and he said: 'The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted the like of this.'\""],[16787,"That he heard Muʿāwiyah delivering a sermon, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and its fasting has not been made obligatory upon us. Whoever among you wishes to fast, let him fast, for I am fasting.'\" So the people fasted."],[16788,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; ḥ, and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he heard Muʿāwiyah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ in the year of his ḥajj while he was on the pulpit, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This day is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast.'\""],[16789,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; they said: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥumayd b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Muʿāwiyah came to Madinah and said: \"Where are your scholars? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on this day,\" and he said: \"I am fasting, so whoever wishes, let him fast, and whoever wishes, let him break his fast\"—meaning the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ."],[16790,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"This day is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes, let him fast it\"—meaning the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ."],[16791,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting. Whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break his fast.\""],[16792,"He informed him that he heard Muʿāwiyah while he was delivering a sermon to the people on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, saying: \"O people of Madinah, where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Its fasting has not been prescribed for you, but I am fasting.'\" And he was saying that: \"Whoever among you wishes to fast it, let him fast, and whoever wishes to break his fast, let him break his fast.\""],[16793,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “This is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and its fasting has not been made obligatory upon you, but I am fasting. So whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may break the fast.”"],[16795,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “When God desires good for someone, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16796,"“And what is that?” They said: “You prayed two rakʿahs while ʿUthmān prayed four.” He said: “I prayed two rakʿahs with the Messenger of God ﷺ.” They kept at him until he went out and prayed four."],[16797,"“Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say, when he was building the mosque, to ʿAmmār: ‘You are indeed eager for jihād, and you are among the people of Paradise, and the transgressing party will kill you’?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then why did you kill him?” He said: “By God, you keep slipping in your urine. Did we kill him? It was only the one who brought him who killed him.”"],[16798,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿAmmār: “The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[16799,"I was with Muʿāwiyah after the ʿaṣr prayer, and he saw people praying two rakʿahs after it. He said: “What is this prayer? We prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we did not see anyone praying it.”"],[16800,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in a single garment."],[16801,"Muʿāwiyah used to say: “By God, I have never feared speaking before anyone as I feared before ʿĀʾishah, and I never heard her speech except that it reminded me of the speech of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[16802,"Muʿāwiyah began saying to some of those present: “Do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ said such and such?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “Did he not also say concerning tamattuʿ with ḥajj and ʿumrah, and then forbid it?” Those who confirmed the first report said: “No, by God, he did not say this, and we do not know that he said it.”"],[16803,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the people: “If the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting.” Al-Qasim said: “The people marveled at Mu'awiyah's truthfulness.”"],[16804,"“This is a sunnah I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and with Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ.” They said: “Your paternal cousin completed it as four [rak'ahs].” He said: “I only remember this.”"],[16805,"“You are praying a prayer that the Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray, and he used to forbid it,” meaning the two rak'ahs after 'Asr."],[16806,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever drinks wine, flog him.” He said it three times. “Then if they drink a fourth time, kill them.”"],[16807,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If he drinks wine, flog him.” He said at the fourth time: “Kill him.”"],[16808,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever dies without a pledge of allegiance on his neck dies a death of Jahiliyyah.”"],[16809,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard the muezzin say “Allahu Akbar,” he said the like of his words. When he said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,” he said the like of his words. When he said “Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah” twice, he said the like of his words."],[16810,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say while Bilal was calling the adhan: When he said “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar,” the Prophet of God said “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar.” Then he said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah,” and the Prophet of God said “Ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah.” Then he said “Ashhadu anna Muhammadan Rasul Allah,” and the Messenger of God ﷺ said the like of it, then he fell silent."],[16811,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever forgets something in his prayer, let him prostrate twice while sitting.”"],[16812,"“This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.”"],[16813,"“This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.”"],[16814,"He says the like of what he says until he reaches his saying “Hayya 'ala al-salah, hayya 'ala al-falah,” and he says “La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.” Then he says the like of what he says. Then he said: “This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say.”"],[16815,"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it."],[16816,"He saw Muʿāwiyah lead the people in prayer, and he stood up after two rakʿahs. The people glorified Allah (to alert him), but he gestured to them to stand up. When he finished his prayer, he performed two prostrations before the salutation, and the people prostrated with him. Then he said: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �Whoever is assailed by doubt in his prayer should perform two prostrations while sitting.�"],[16817,"The Prophet ﷺ said: �Whoever forgets something in his prayer should perform two prostrations.�"],[16818,"He said that there would be a king from Qaḥṭān. Muʿāwiyah became angry and stood up, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: To proceed: It has reached me that some men among you speak of things that are not in the Book of Allah and are not reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. That is due to your ignorance. Beware of vain desires that mislead their people. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: �This matter (authority) rests with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that Allah throws him on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16819,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �This matter rests with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that Allah throws him on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16820,"He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �This matter will remain with Quraysh. No one opposes them except that he is thrown on his face, as long as they uphold the religion.�"],[16821,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us, from Yazīd b. Ziyād, from Muḥammad b. Kaʿb al-Quraẓī, who said: Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān said while on the pulpit: �O people, there is none to withhold what Allah gives, and none to give what Allah withholds, and no one possessed of fortune benefits from his fortune before Him. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion.� Then he said: �I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on these wooden planks.�"],[16822,"\"O people, there is no one who can prevent what Allah has given, nor is there anyone who can give what Allah has prevented. And the wealth and status of a person cannot benefit them from Allah. Whoever Allah wants good for, He will give them understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[16823,"I heard Muʿāwiyah b. Abī Sufyān delivering a sermon in Madinah, saying: You will certainly know, O people, that there is none to withhold what Allah gives, and none to give what Allah withholds, and no one possessed of fortune benefits from his fortune before Him. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on these wooden planks."],[16824,"�Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. This wealth is green and sweet. Whoever takes it by right will be blessed in it.� Then he said: �I heard these words from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the pulpit. The listener who obeys has no argument against him, and the listener who disobeys has no argument for him.�"],[16825,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: �Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion and inspires him with right guidance.�"],[16826,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: �O Allah, there is none to withhold what You give, and none to give what You withhold. Whomever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion.�"],[16827,"Some people during the time of Muʿāwiyah used to attend the dawn prayer and then sit with the storyteller of the congregation. When he finished, they would move to a corner of the mosque and remember Allah and recite the Book of Allah until the day grew bright. Muʿāwiyah was informed of them and came hurrying—or walking quickly—until he stood before them and said: I have come to give you glad tidings from Allah for what He has provided you. A group of people during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—I think he said—used to do something like what you do. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, as if I am imitating his walk, until he stood before them and said: �Rejoice! By Him in Whose hand is my soul, Allah ﷻ boasts of you to the angels.�"],[16828,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever loves the Ansar, it is out of love for me that he loves them, and whoever hates the Ansar, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.”"],[16829,"Mu'awiya delivered a sermon and said something that the people disapproved of, so they rebutted him. That pleased him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “There will be rulers who speak and are not rebutted; they will tumble into the Fire, one following another.”"],[16830,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out until he climbed the pulpit, mentioned the martyrs of Uhud, prayed over them, and prolonged the prayer. Then he said, “A servant among God's servants was given the choice by God between this world and what is with Him, and he chose what is with God.” None understood it except Abu Bakr, who said, “We would ransom you with our fathers and mothers.” He said, “Gently, O Abu Bakr. The best of people in my eyes in companionship and in generosity with his wealth is the son of Abu Quhafa.”"],[16832,"Come to prayer, come to success. He said, “There is no might nor power except with God. This is how I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say it.”"],[16833,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I am not of idle play, and idle play is not of me.”"],[16834,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever adds to his hair something that is not part of it, he is adding falsehood to it.”"],[16835,"I heard Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan in Madinah, with a lock of women's hair in his hand, saying: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the like of this and said, “The Children of Israel were destroyed only when their women adopted this.”"],[16836,"I heard Mu'awiya, while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16837,"What is the matter with your women that they put on their heads the like of this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Any woman who puts on her head hair from someone else's hair, it is falsehood.”"],[16839,"He heard Mu'awiyah on the minbar, and with him was a bundle of women's hair, so he said: 'What is the matter with Muslim women that they do this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Any woman who adds hair to her head that is not from it, it is falsehood.”'"],[16840,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group in this nation fighting upon the command of God; the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them, nor the abandonment of those who abandon them, until the command of God, the Exalted, comes to them while they are upon that.\""],[16841,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever hears the muezzin and says the like of what he says, he will have the like of his reward.\""],[16842,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade al-shighar (a type of marriage in which a man gives his daughter or sister in marriage to another on the condition that the other gives his daughter or sister in marriage to him, with no dower between them)."],[16843,"…that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Mu'awiyah said: 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.' Then Mu'awiyah said: 'Thus I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[16844,"I heard Mu'awiyah while he was on the minbar in Madinah saying: 'O people of Madinah, where are your jurists? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid the like of this forelock'—and he placed it on his head, and I did not see it on a bride nor on anyone else more beautiful than it was on Mu'awiyah."],[16845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, on the day of 'Ashura' we used to fast it in the pre-Islamic era, then God prescribed for us the fasting of Ramadan, and removed from us the fasting of 'Ashura', so whoever wishes may fast it and whoever wishes may break his fast.'"],[16846,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not hasten to something that you think that if you hasten to it you will attain it, even though God has not decreed it for you; and do not delay from something that you think that if you delay from it, it will pass you by, even though God has decreed it upon you.\""],[16847,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not be importunate in asking; for by God, none of you asks me for something and the asking brings it out from me, and I give it to him while I am averse to it, and then he is blessed in what I gave him.\""],[16848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a man asks me for something and I withhold it so that you may intercede and thus be rewarded.\""],[16850,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me not to come to my family at the first sight of the new moon, not to perform ablution with copper water, and to use the tooth-stick whenever I rose from my siesta."],[16851,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said concerning Laylat al-Qadr, “Twenty-seven.”"],[16852,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Seek Laylat al-Qadr on the night of the twenty-seventh.”"],[16853,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ — and he would mention these words, often narrating them on Fridays: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in religion. This wealth is green and sweet; whoever takes it with its due right will be blessed in it. Beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter.”"],[16854,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it with its due right will be blessed in it.”"],[16855,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said in his sermon — I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Beware of mutual praise, for it is slaughter.”"],[16856,"“You certainly pray this prayer — we accompanied the Messenger of God and saw him, and we did not see him pray this prayer after the prayer” — meaning after Asr."],[16857,"Muawiya entered a house in which were Abdullah b. Amir and Ibn al-Zubayr. Ibn al-Zubayr remained seated while Abdullah b. Amir stood, and he was the more dignified of the two men. Muawiya said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16858,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16859,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever is pleased to have people stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16860,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever is pleased to have men stand for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[16861,"“Leveling graves is from the Sunnah. The Jews and Christians have raised (theirs), so do not imitate them.”"],[16862,"To a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16863,"I was among a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the presence of Mu‘āwiyah. Mu‘āwiyah said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16864,"I heard Mu‘āwiyah, while a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ was with him, say, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16865,"One day, while the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were with him: “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combining Hajj and ‘Umrah?” They said, “O Allah, no.”"],[16867,"I was in the presence of Mu‘āwiyah, and with him were some people from the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār. Mu‘āwiyah said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from silver vessels?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combining Hajj and ‘Umrah?” They said, “O Allah, yes.”"],[16868,"Mu‘āwiyah performed Hajj and summoned a group of the Anṣār. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not learn that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid silk saddle cloths?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leopard saddle cloths?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16869,"He witnessed Mu‘āwiyah while some people from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ were with him. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.” He said, “I adjure you by Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16870,"Mu‘āwiyah performed Hajj and summoned a group of the Anṣār inside the Ka‘bah. He said, “I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid gold?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade leopard saddle cloths?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “And I bear witness. Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade silk?” They said, “O Allah, yes.” He said, “And I bear witness.”"],[16871,"When Mu‘āwiyah pledged allegiance to Yazīd, he performed Hajj and passed by Madinah. He addressed the people and said, “We have pledged allegiance to Yazīd, so pledge allegiance.” Al-Ḥusayn b. ‘Alī ؓ stood up and said, “I, by Allah, am more entitled to it than him. My father is better than his father, my grandfather is better than his grandfather, my mother is better than his mother, and I am better than him.” Mu‘āwiyah said, “As for your saying that your grandfather is better than his grandfather, you have spoken the truth: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than Abū Sufyān b. Ḥarb. As for your saying that your mother is better than his mother, you have spoken the truth: Fāṭimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is better than the daughter of Majdal. As for your saying that your father is better than his father, his father contended with your father, and Allah ruled in favor of his father over your father. As for your saying that you are better than him, he is more capable than you and more intelligent. What would please me with the like of you is a thousand.”"],[16872,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The enemy will not prevail over a people if they—” or he said, “I saw them with a man from Banū Bakr b. Wā’il.”"],[16873,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “The matter will only increase in severity, the people will only increase in avarice, and the Hour will not come except upon the worst of people.”"],[16874,"I heard Muawiyah, while he was in blessed Makkah on the day of Ashura, say: The Messenger of God ﷺ fasted it and said: “Whoever among you has not fasted, let him fast it.”"],[16875,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade wearing gold except in small pieces, and riding on leopard skins.”"],[16876,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade riding on leopard skins and wearing gold except in small pieces.”"],[16877,"Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan said: “The people of Makkah expelled the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the caliphate shall not be among them, and the people of Madinah killed Uthman ؓ, so the caliphate shall never return to them.”"],[16878,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “My community will remain triumphant over the people until the command of God comes.”"],[16879,"I entered upon Muawiyah while he was writhing in pain, and his sore was between his shoulders. He said: It does not please me that I should not find what you see. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No harm afflicts a believer in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins.”"],[16880,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “No Muslim is afflicted with harm in his body except that it is an expiation for his sins.” And this is the severest harm."],[16881,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he returns, flog him; then if he returns, kill him.”"],[16882,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him three times; if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck.”"],[16883,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns a fourth time, strike his neck.”"],[16884,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever drinks wine, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he returns, lash him; if he does it a fourth time, kill him.”"],[16885,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Quraysh are the governors of the people in good and evil until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[16886,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed those who shred sermons into pieces like the shredding of poetry.”"],[16887,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever supplicates with these five phrases, he will not ask Allah for anything except that He gives it to him: ‘There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. There is no god but Allah, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah.’”"],[16888,"Muawiyah: “I have not ceased to aspire to the caliphate since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: ‘If you rule, then do good.’”"],[16889,"“I prayed with Muawiyah, the Commander of the Believers. He stood in the second rakʿah, so the people said subhan Allah to him. He gestured to them with his hand to stand. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated two prostrations for that, then left.” And he said: “Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.”"],[16890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves that the children of Adam stand up for him, the Fire is due for him.”"],[16891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of you is the best of you to his family.”"],[16892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out upon a group of companions gathered together and said: “What has gathered you?” They said: “We remember Allah and what He has blessed us with and what He saved us from of ignorance and its ignorance.” He said: “By Allah, is it for that that you gathered?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you are truthful, Allah Almighty will boast of you to the angels.”"],[16893,"Your location until I come to you, so he came out to us while he stumbled. When he prayed Asr, he said, \"Shall I inform you about something that the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Indeed, they used to pray the first prayer with him, then they would sit down and he would come out to them and say, 'What kept you after I left?' They would say, 'Nothing.' He would then say, 'If you were to see towards your Lord, a door from the sky was opened and I see your angels competing with each other in presenting you in front of Allah while you are waiting for the prayer.'\""],[16894,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no sin except that Allah may forgive it, except one who was a polytheist or killed a believer deliberately.”"],[16895,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every sin may be forgiven, except that a man dies while he is a disbeliever or he kills a believer deliberately.”"],[16896,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except the man who dies as a disbeliever, or a man who killed a believer deliberately.”"],[16897,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a statement by which Allah benefited me. I heard him say: “Turn away from the people. Do you not see that if you follow suspicion in the people, you will corrupt them, or you would almost corrupt them?”"],[16898,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16899,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The listener who obeys has no case against him, and the listener who disobeys has no case for him.”"],[16900,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “O people, do not rush ahead of me into bowing and prostrating. Whatever I get ahead of you with when I bow, you will catch up with it when I rise. I have become heavy”—meaning, I have grown older. The wording is from the hadith of Sulayman b. Bilal."],[16901,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: “Do not rush ahead of me with bowing and prostrating, for whatever I get ahead of you with when I prostrate, you will catch up with it when I rise, and whatever I get ahead of you with when I bow, you will catch up with it when I rise. I have become heavy.”"],[16902,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16903,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade asking difficult, unnecessary questions."],[16904,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “What remains of this world is only affliction and tribulation. The likeness of any one of you is like a vessel: if its top is good, its bottom is good.”"],[16905,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A man transgressed against himself. He came to a man and said, “The other man killed ninety-nine people, all of them wrongfully. Is there any repentance for me?” He said, “No.” So he killed him. Then he came to another and said, “The other man killed a hundred people, all of them wrongfully. Is there any repentance for him?” He said, “If I told you that God does not accept the repentance of one who repents, I would have lied to you. Here is a place where there are people who worship. Go to them and worship God with them.” So he set out toward them and died on that path. The angels of mercy and the angels of punishment disputed over him, so God sent an angel to them and said, “Measure between the two places. Whichever he is closer to, he belongs to them.” They found him closer to the monastery of the penitents by a finger’s length, so he was forgiven. The wording is from the hadith of al-Walid."],[16906,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “God is not overcome, nor deceived, nor informed of what He does not know. Whomever God intends good for, He grants him understanding in the religion.”"],[16908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My nation will continue to stand up for the truth, fighting against those who fight them and oppose them until the Day of Judgment.\""],[16909,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding of the religion.\""],[16910,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah who gives. So whoever I give a gift to while I am content with it, he is blessed in it. And whoever I give a gift to because of greed of the soul and intense asking, he is like one who eats but is never satisfied.\""],[16911,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the pulpit: \"I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah who gives. So whoever I give a gift to while I am content with it, he is blessed in it. And whoever I give a gift to because of greed of the soul and intense asking, he is like one who eats but is never satisfied.\""],[16912,"He was speaking with Muawiyah when the muezzin called the adhan. He ordered him to listen quietly, then he said takbir as he said takbir. Then when the muezzin said 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' he said 'And we bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' When the muezzin said 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' he said 'And we bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' Ibn Hubayra said: I asked him, 'Is this something you saw or heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He replied, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say takbir when he heard the muezzin. When he said 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,' he said 'And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.' And when he said 'I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,' he said 'And I bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah.'\""],[16913,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The eye is the string that ties the anus. When the eye sleeps, the string is untied, so whoever sleeps must perform ablution.\""],[16914,"Muawiyah gave a sermon to the people and mentioned in his sermon that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade seven things, and I convey that to you and forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, images, displaying adornment, skins of beasts of prey, gold, and silk."],[16915,"O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them: wailing, poetry, displaying adornment, images, skins of beasts of prey, singing, gold, heat, and silk."],[16916,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nine things, and I forbid you from them. Indeed among them are wailing, singing, images, poetry, gold, heat, saddles, and silk."],[16917,"What are these hadiths that have reached me from you that you narrate? I have resolved to banish you from Syria. He replied: By Allah, were it not for females, I would not love to remain there even for an hour. Muawiyah said: What is the hadith you narrate about tila (a beverage)? He replied: Indeed, it is not lawful for me to say about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say. I heard him say: \"Whoever falsely attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[16918,"He heard Muawiyah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand on the pulpit one day before Ramadan and say: \"Fasting is on such and such a day, and we are going to fast in advance. Whoever wishes to fast in advance may do so, and whoever wishes to leave it may do so.\""],[16919,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"You will conquer lands where wormwood grows.\""],[16920,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone.”"],[16921,"Write to the ruler of Armenia a reply to his letter—may your mother be bereaved of you—and do not stir them up with anything, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Leave the Turks alone as long as they leave you alone.”"],[16922,"Muawiyah, if I had approached you before this period, I would have cut off a part of you, then I would have stood up and prayed Dhuhr in Makkah. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: \"The people of the Book divided into seventy-two sects, and this nation will divide into seventy-three sects, all of them are in the Fire except one, which is the group (Al-Jama'ah).\" And he said: \"There will come out from my nation people who deal with desires as the dog deals with its master. Not a vein or a joint will be left except that they enter it.\" By Allah, O Arabs, if you do not uphold what Muhammad, ﷺ , brought, then others among the people are more deserving of upholding it."],[16923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the people of the Book divided into seventy-two sects in their book, and this Ummah (nation) will divide into seventy-three sects, all of which are in the Fire except one, and that is the group. And indeed, there will emerge from my Ummah (nation) people who will interpret these desires just as the dog licks its owner's hand, and there will not remain a vein or joint except that they will enter it.\""],[16924,"Mu’awiya showed them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then brought them back until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began."],[16925,"He showed them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began. Al-Walid said: And ‘Abdullah b. al-‘Ala’ b. Zabr reported to me from Abu al-Azhar from Mu’awiya likewise, and Hariz b. ‘Uthman reported to me from ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Maysara from al-Miqdam b. Ma’dikarib from the Messenger of God ﷺ the like of it."],[16926,"He attended Mu’awiya performing ablution, and he wiped his ears, their outer and inner parts, and said: “This is the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[16927,"About Mu’awiya’s ablution, showing them the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ: he performed ablution three times, except for washing his feet, which was without a fixed number."],[16928,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “If you pursue the private faults of people, you will corrupt them, or you will almost corrupt them.” Abu al-Darda’ would say: A word Mu’awiya heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ by which God benefited him."],[16929,"He used to teach the people the tashahhud while on the pulpit, from the Prophet ﷺ: “Greetings, prayers, and good words are due to God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.”"],[16930,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade difficult and obscure questions. Ishaq said: Rawh b. ‘Ubada narrated to us from al-Awza’i who said: “Al-ghulutat are the hard and severe questions.”"],[16931,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There will continue to be a group from my nation, steadfast, unharmed by those who abandon them, until the command of God comes, while they are victorious over the people.”"],[16932,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Adhere to truthfulness, for it leads to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for it leads to wickedness, and both are in the Fire.”"],[16933,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Emigration is of two kinds: one is to abandon evil deeds, and the other is to emigrate to God and His Messenger. Emigration does not cease as long as repentance is accepted, and repentance continues to be accepted until the sun rises from the west. When it rises, it will rise upon every heart with what is in it, and people will have enough of deeds.”"],[16934,"I accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and listened to him, and I heard most of his prayer was that he would say: “Glory be to You, Lord of the worlds.”"],[16935,"“Fulfill my need, O Commander of the Believers, for by Allah my burden is great: I have become father of ten, brother of ten, and uncle of ten.” When Marwān turned away while Ibn ʿAbbās was sitting with Muʿāwiyah on his couch, Muʿāwiyah said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘When the sons of al-Ḥakam reach thirty men, they will take the signs of Allah among them as spoils, His servants as slaves, and His Book as corruption. When they reach four hundred and ninety-nine, their destruction will be quicker than the ripening of fruit’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “O Allah, yes.” Then Marwān mentioned a need of his, and Marwān b. ʿAbd al-Malik referred it back to Muʿāwiyah, and he spoke to him about it. When he turned away, Muʿāwiyah said: “I adjure you by Allah, O Ibn ʿAbbās, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned this one and said: ‘Abū al-Jabābirah al-Arbaʿah (father of the four tyrants)’?” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “O Allah, yes.”"],[16936,"I heard Muʿāwiyah on the pulpit, and he narrated little from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, exalted is He, brought forth the progeny of Adam from his loins until they filled the earth, and they were like this.” Jaʿfar clasped his hands, one over the other."],[16937,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"There will always be a group of my Ummah who will remain steadfast in the command of Allah. Those who betray them or oppose them will not be able to harm them until the command of Allah comes and they will be prominent among the people.\""],[16938,"He mentioned to them the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he wiped his head until water dripped from his head or nearly dripped, and that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the wiping of his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck with them, then returned them until he reached the place from which he began."],[16939,"I heard Abū al-Azhar say: Muʿāwiyah stood at Dayr Misḥal, which is at the gate of Homs, and said: “Indeed, the fast is on such-and-such a day, and we will begin tomorrow.” Then Mālik b. Hubayrah stood up to him and said: “O Muʿāwiyah, is this an opinion you have formed or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Fast the month and its beginning.’”"],[16940,"He used to send a guard from his guards to me, like the guards of Kūbah and Qarū, saying: “Indeed, this is the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. The Prophet ﷺ used to fast it, and we are fasting. So whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast.”"],[16941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A nation is not deemed holy in which justice is not carried out and the weak does not take his right from the strong without stammering.”"],[16942,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Goodness is a habit and evil is obstinacy.” Ibn Bint Shuraḥbīl added in his hadith from the Prophet ﷺ: “And whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion.”"],[16943,"We were sitting in the mosque when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “You talk about how I am the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in groups,” meaning one after another. Then he recited this verse and said: {Say: He is able to send upon you punishment from above you or from beneath your feet} until he reached {For every report there is a fixed time, and you will come to know}. Then he said: “A band of my community will not cease fighting for the truth, victorious, not caring who abandons them or opposes them, until the command of Allah comes upon that.” Then he recited this verse: {O Jesus, I will take you and raise you to Me and purify you from those who disbelieve, and I will make those who follow you above those who disbelieve until the Day of Resurrection.}"],[16945,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Hijrah will not cease until repentance ceases” – three times – “and repentance will not cease until the sun rises from its west.”"],[16946,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A community is not sanctified if its weak cannot take their right from its strong without being oppressed.” Then he said: If he says yes, carry him to me by post. So he asked him and he said yes, so he carried him by post from Egypt to Syria. Muawiya asked him and he informed him, so Muawiya said: “I too have heard it, but I wished to confirm it.”"],[16947,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed, every intoxicant is forbidden to every believer.”"],[16948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever dies without an imam dies a death of Jahiliyyah.”"],[16949,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16950,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever Allah wishes good for, He gives him understanding in religion.”"],[16951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade obscure and ambiguous questions."],[16952,"From the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: “I am only a conveyer, and Allah guides; and I am a distributor, and Allah gives. Whoever receives something from me with good conduct and desire, that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives something with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats but is never satisfied.”"],[16953,"Abu Hazzan Atiyya b. Abi Jamilah narrated to them, tracing it back to Muawiya b. Abi Sufyan, and Muawiya tracing it back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he said: “I am only a conveyer, and Allah guides; and I am only a distributor, and Allah gives. Whoever receives something from us with good conduct and good desire, that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives something from us with bad conduct and bad desire, that is the one who eats but is never satisfied.”"],[16954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am only a deliverer (of the message), while Allah guides and divides, and Allah gives. So whoever receives from me something with good guidance and good desire, then that is the one who is blessed in it. And whoever receives from me something with bad desire and bad guidance, then that is the one who eats but does not feel satisfied.\""],[16955,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will not cease to be a group from my ummah standing upon the command of Allah, not harmed by those who oppose them or forsake them, until the command of Allah comes while they are victorious over the people.”"],[16956,"I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If Allah wants to do good to a person, He makes him comprehend the religion. I am just a distributor, but the grant is from Allah. (And remember) that this nation (true Muslims) will keep on following Allah's teachings strictly and they will not be harmed by any one going on a different path till Allah's order (Day of Judgment) is established.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 71)"],[16957,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Who-ever loves to meet Allah, Allah (too) loves to meet him and who-ever hates to meet Allah, Allah (too) hates to meet him\".ʿAisha, or some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ said, \"But we dislike death.\" He said: It is not like this, but it is meant that when the time of the death of a believer approaches, he receives the good news of Allah's pleasure with him and His blessings upon him, and so at that time nothing is dearer to him than what is in front of him. He therefore loves the meeting with Allah, and Allah (too) loves the meeting with him. But when the time of the death of a disbeliever approaches, he receives the evil news of Allah's torment and His Requital, whereupon nothing is more hateful to him than what is before him. Therefore, he hates the meeting with Allah, and Allah too, hates the meeting with him.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6507)"],[16958,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding riding on the skins of beasts of prey and the building of tall structures."],[16959,"It was sent down on the day of Arafah on a Friday. Then he recited this verse: “So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous work and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.” And he said: It is the last verse that was sent down."],[16960,"‘Whoever lies upon me intentionally, then let him take his seat in the Fire’. (Using translation from Muslim 3)"],[16961,"I heard Mu'awiyah on the pulpit saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no one's wealth or fortune avails against You.'"],[16962,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O Allah, whoever I cursed in the pre-Islamic era and then entered Islam, make that a means of nearness to You for him.'"],[16963,"In his sermon he said: 'The wealth is our wealth and the fay' is our fay'. Whomever we wish we give, and whomever we wish we withhold.' No one responded to him. On the second Friday he said the same and no one responded. On the third Friday he made the same statement, so a man from those present in the mosque stood up to him and said: 'No, rather the wealth is our wealth and the fay' is our fay'. Whoever comes between us and it, we will take him to Allah with our swords.' Mu'awiyah descended, sent for the man, and admitted him. The people said: 'The man is doomed.' Then the people entered and found the man with him on the couch. Mu'awiyah said to the people: 'This man has revived me, may Allah revive him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be leaders after me who will speak and no one will refute them; they will plunge into the Fire as monkeys plunge.\" I spoke on the first Friday and no one replied to me, so I feared that I might be one of them. Then I spoke on the second Friday and no one replied to me, so I said to myself: I am one of the people. Then I spoke on the third Friday, and this man stood up and replied to me, so he revived me, may Allah revive him.'"],[16964,"He said: 'It is not from the Sunnah to fast while traveling.'"],[16965,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say many times: When the muezzin calls the adhan and pronounces the shahadah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pronounce the shahadah as he does. When the muezzin says 'Hayya 'ala al-salah', he would say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah.' When the muezzin says 'Hayya 'ala al-falah', he would also say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah.'"],[16966,"I heard Mu'awiyah say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat milk, then stand and pray without performing wudu.'"],[16967,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O people, knowledge comes only by learning, and fiqh comes only by understanding. Whoever Allah wills good for, He grants him understanding in the religion. It is only the scholars among His servants who truly fear Allah.'"],[16968,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ten houses in the Hijaz are more enduring than twenty houses in Syria.'"],[16969,"Mu'awiyah came out to us after we had prayed Zuhr while we were supplicating to Allah. He said: 'Stay where you are until I come to you.' He came out to us wearing a cloak and after he prayed 'Asr he said: 'Shall I not tell you something that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did? They prayed the first prayer with him, then sat until they prayed 'Asr with him. He came out to them and said: \"Have you been sitting here all this time?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"If you could see your Lord, blessed and exalted, He opened a gate of the gates of heaven and boasted to His angels about your gathering while you were waiting for the prayer.\"'"],[16970,"Mu'awiyah entered upon 'Ammar, and when he left his presence he said: 'O Allah, do not make his death at our hands, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The transgressing faction will kill 'Ammar.\"'"],[16971,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ said: 'O Messenger of Allah, among us are men who practice tiyarah (bird omens).' He said: 'That is something you find within yourselves; it will not harm you.' They said: 'Among us are men who go to soothsayers.' He said: 'Do not go to any soothsayer.'"],[16972,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about tiyarah, and he said: 'That is something you find within yourselves; it will not harm you.'"],[16973,"Mu'awiya b. al-Hakam al-Sulami, who was one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: What do you think about things we used to do in the pre-Islamic era? We used to practice tiyara (drawing evil omens from birds). The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"That is something one of you finds in his heart, so do not let it deter you.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we also used to go to soothsayers. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not go to soothsayers.\""],[16974,"From Mu'awiya b. al-Hakam, similar to the hadith of Malik: \"In the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ there were eleven rak'ahs, and he would lie down on his right side.\""],[16975,"I set out to a small flock of sheep that a slave girl of mine was tending in the direction of Uhud and al-Jawwaniyya, and I found that a wolf had taken one of its sheep. I am a man from the children of Adam, and I get angry as they get angry, so I struck her a blow. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him, and he made that seem grave to me. I said: O Messenger of God, should I not free her? He said: \"Yes, bring her to me.\" So I brought her to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: \"Where is God?\" She said: 'God ﷻ is in heaven.' He said: \"Who am I?\" She said: 'You are the Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: \"Free her, for she is a believer.\""],[16976,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ: I had a slave girl who was tending some small sheep in the direction of Uhud when I looked at her one time and found that a wolf had gone off with one of them. I am one of the children of Adam and I get angry as they get angry, but I slapped her a slap. The Messenger of God ﷺ made that seem grave to me, so I said: Should I not free her? He said: \"Bring her to me.\" So I brought her, and he said: \"Where is God?\" She said: 'In heaven.' He said: \"Who am I?\" She said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ.' He said: \"Free her, for she is a believer.\""],[16978,"I said: O Messenger of God, among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something you find in your hearts, so it will not harm you.\" He said: I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" He said: And among us are men who draw lines (in the sand). He said: \"A prophet drew lines, so whoever's line coincides with his knowledge, he knows.\""],[16979,"I said: O Messenger of God, we are people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God has brought Islam, and there are men among us who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, so let it not deter them.\" He said: O Messenger of God, and men among us go to soothsayers. He said: \"No, do not go to them.\" He said: And men among us draw lines. He said: \"A prophet of the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\""],[16980,"I said: O Messenger of God, among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something you find in your chests, so it will not harm you.\" I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" I said: And among us are men who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet drew lines, so whoever's line coincides with his knowledge, he knows.\""],[16981,"I said: O Messenger of God, we are a people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God has brought Islam, and among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\" I said: And among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, so it will not harm them.\" I said: And among us are men who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\""],[16982,"He said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are a people who have only recently left the pre-Islamic era, and God ﷻ has brought Islam, and there are men among us who draw lines. He said: \"A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines, so whoever's line coincides with his, that is it.\" He said: And among us are men who practice tiyara. He said: \"That is something they find in their chests, but it will not harm them.\" I said: And among us are men who go to soothsayers. He said: \"Do not go to them.\""],[16983,"While I was with the Prophet ﷺ , a man from the people sneezed, so I said, \"May Allah have mercy on you.\" The people stared at me with their eyes. I said, \"May their mothers be excused, why are you looking at me?\" He (the Prophet) said, \"The people struck their hands on their thighs.\" When I saw that they silenced me, I remained silent. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, I did not see a better teacher before or after him. Verily, he did not strike me, nor did he humiliate me, nor did he curse me. But he said, 'Indeed, our prayer is not for the purpose of talking to people, rather it is for glorifying Allah, praising Him, and reciting the Quran.'\""],[16985,"I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and a man from the people sneezed, so I said: May God have mercy on you. The people stared at me, so I said: Woe is my mother! What is the matter with you that you look at me? They began striking their hands on their thighs, so I knew they were signaling me to be quiet, but I remained silent. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished praying—may my father and mother be his ransom—he did not strike me, nor scold me, nor revile me. Then he said: \"Indeed, this prayer is not permissible for any of people's speech in it. It is only glorification, magnification, and recitation of the Qur'an,\" or as the Messenger of God ﷺ said."],[16986,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and a man among the people sneezed. So I said, \"May Allah have mercy on you\" or \"May Allah have mercy on all of you.\" Then the people stared at me, so I said, \"May my mother and father be sacrificed for me\" (a common Arabic expression of confusion or surprise), then they began hitting their thighs with their hands. I realized that the people were trying to silence me with their eyes. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, I have never seen a teacher who was more gentle in teaching than him, neither before nor after him. He did not scold, reproach, or insult me. He said, \"In this prayer, there is no place for people's speech. It is only for glorifying Allah, declaring His greatness, and reciting the Quran.\" \"And Ayyub did not mention 'Ata' ibn Yasar in his narration.\""],[16987,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Woe to the one who speaks and makes his people laugh by lying. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16988,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Woe to the one who speaks and lies to make the people laugh. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16989,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the one who talks to people and lies to make them laugh — woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16990,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Woe to the one who talks to people falsely to make them laugh. Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16991,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say about the one who talks to people and makes them laugh: \"Woe to him, woe to him.\""],[16994,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16995,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother\" — he said it three times. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your father.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, then whom? He said: \"Then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16996,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother, then your mother, then your mother, then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16997,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[16998,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your father.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[17000,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat with the utmost devotion? He said: \"Your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Then your mother.\" I said: Then whom? He said: \"Your father, then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.\""],[17002,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we ask one another for our wealth among ourselves. He said: \"Yes, a man may ask in times of strife between him and his people, but when it reaches the point of pressing need or near destitution, he should refrain.\""],[17003,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a people who ask one another for our wealth among ourselves. He said: \"One of you may ask in cases of need and strife, to set things right between his people, but when it reaches the point of pressing need or near destitution, he should abstain.\""],[17006,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: By Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by these fingers of mine that I would not follow you or follow your religion. I have come to a man who understands nothing except what Allah ﷻ and His Messenger ﷺ teach me. I ask you by Allah: With what did your Lord send you to us? He said: \"Sit down.\" Then he said: \"With Islam.\" I said: What is the sign of Islam? He said: \"That you bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that you establish prayer, give zakah, and abandon shirk. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim; they are two brothers, two supporters. Allah does not accept from a polytheist who associates partners with Him after his Islam any deed. My Lord is calling me and asking me whether I have conveyed to His servants, so let the one who is present among you convey to the one who is absent. You will be called with your mouths bridled with the fidam. The first thing that one of you will be asked about is his thigh and his palm.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this our religion? He said: \"Yes. You will be gathered on your faces, on your feet, and as riders.\""],[17010,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection you will be called with your mouths muzzled with the fadam.” Then he said: “Indeed, the first part of any of you to be made visible will be his thigh and his palm.”"],[17011,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will be gathered on foot and riding, and you will be dragged on your faces.”"],[17012,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He gestured with his hand towards Syria and said: “O people, indeed you will be gathered on foot and riding, and you will be dragged on your faces, with your mouths muzzled with the fadam, and the first part of any of you to begin will be his thigh.”"],[17015,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is asked by his master for surplus wealth and does not give it to him, it will be turned into a bald-headed snake on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17016,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one asks a master for surplus that he has and withholds it, except that his surplus which he has will come on the Day of Resurrection as a bald-headed snake.”"],[17017,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man does not approach his leader asking for favors from him, and the leader withholds them, except that Allah will make him on the Day of Resurrection a coward, deafening his favor that he withholds.\""],[17021,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “For every forty grazing camels, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his camels as an ordinance from the ordinances of your Lord. It is not lawful for Muhammad or for the family of Muhammad.”"],[17022,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “For every grazing herd of camels, for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Camels are not to be separated from their condition. Whoever gives it as a trader will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, I will take it and half of his wealth as an ordinance from the ordinances of our Lord. The family of Muhammad has no share in it.”"],[17023,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “For every grazing herd of camels, for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel is due. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his camels as an ordinance from the ordinances of our Lord. It is not lawful for the family of Muhammad to have any of it.”"],[17026,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what parts of our private areas may we expose and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife and those whom your right hand possesses.” He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if we are among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees your private area, then do so.” They said: What if one of us is alone by himself? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.” And he placed his hand over his private area."],[17027,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private areas, what may we expose of them and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses.” I said: What if we are among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees your private area, then do so.” I said: What do you think if one of us is sitting alone? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[17028,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private areas, what may we expose of them and what may we leave? He said: “Cover your private area except from your wife or those whom your right hand possesses.” Al-Hajabi added in his narration: I said: What about people being among one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees it, then let no one see it.” I said: What if one of us is alone? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[17029,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what may we expose of our private areas and what may we leave? He said: “Guard your private area except from your wife and those whom your right hand possesses.” I said: What if we are among one another? He said: “Guard your private area as much as you can.” He said: What if we are in seclusion? He said: “Allah is more deserving that one be shy before Him.”"],[17030,"I said: O Messenger of God, our private parts—what may we expose of them and what must we guard? He said: “Guard your private part except from your wife or what your right hand possesses.” I said: When people are with one another? He said: “If you can ensure that no one sees it, then let no one see it.” I said: O Prophet of God, what about one of us when he is alone? He said: “God is more deserving that one be modest before Him.”"],[17033,"The Prophet ﷺ detained some people from my tribe on suspicion. A man from my tribe came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon and said: O Muhammad, why are my neighbors being held? The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. He said: Some people say that you forbid something and then make it lawful for yourself. The Prophet ﷺ said: “What are you saying?” I began to intervene between them with words, fearing that he would hear it and invoke against my tribe an invocation after which they would never prosper. The Prophet ﷺ kept on until he understood it, then said: “They have said it,” or he said: “He has said it regarding them. By God, if I had done so, it would be against me and not against them. Release his neighbors for him.”"],[17035,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion, then someone interceded for him and he released him."],[17036,"I said: O Prophet of God, our wives—what may we do with them and what must we avoid? He said: “Your field, so come to your field as you wish, except that you do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except within the house. Feed when you eat, clothe when you clothe yourself. How could it be otherwise, since some of you have been intimate with some?”"],[17037,"I said: O Messenger of God, our wives—what may we do with them and what must we avoid? He said: “Your field, so come to your field as you wish, except that you do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not abandon except within the house. Feed when you eat, clothe when you clothe yourself. How could it be otherwise, since some of you have been intimate with some?”"],[17040,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Three eyes will not see the Fire: an eye that stood guard in the path of God, an eye that wept out of fear of God, and an eye that lowered its gaze from what God has forbidden.”"],[17041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “A black woman who is childbearing is better than a beautiful one who does not give birth. I will vie with you in numbers among the nations, even by the miscarried fetus that remains bloated at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to him: Enter Paradise. He will say: O Lord, and my parents? It will be said to him: Enter Paradise, you and your parents.”"],[17042,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: God said: “I am as My servant thinks of Me.”"],[17043,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “God, exalted is He, created one hundred mercies. One mercy is among His creation, by which they show mercy to one another, and He reserved for His friends ninety-nine.”"],[17044,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Anger spoils a matter just as vinegar spoils honey.”"],[17045,"When charity was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, he would not eat from it, and when a gift was brought to him, he would eat from it."],[17046,"Food would be brought to the Prophet ﷺ. If it was charity, he would not eat from it, and if it was a gift, he would eat from it."],[17047,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do you refrain from mentioning the wicked? Mention him with what is in him so that people may know him.”"],[17048,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no backbiting for the immoral person.”"],[17049,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, of which you are eighty rows, and the rest of humanity make up the remainder, and you will complete seventy nations, you being the best and most honorable of them in the sight of God ﷻ.”"],[17050,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever changes his religion, kill him. God does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam.”"],[17051,"I said, “O Messenger of God, what is the right of my neighbor upon me?” He said, “If he falls ill, visit him; if he dies, attend his funeral; if he asks you for a loan, lend to him; if he is in need, cover him; if good befalls him, congratulate him; if a calamity befalls him, console him; do not raise your building above his building so as to block the wind from him, and do not annoy him with the smell of your cooking pot unless you ladle out some for him.”"],[17052,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Stick to Greater Syria.”"],[17053,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “It is from God ﷻ, not from His Messenger: may God curse the one who cuts down lote trees.”"],[17054,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no might and no power except with God; it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise.”"],[17055,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Secret charity extinguishes the wrath of the Lord.”"],[17056,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give a gift?” He said, “To the one whose door is nearer to you.”"],[17057,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I have two neighbors; which of them should I give a gift to?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"(Give) to the one whose door is nearer to you.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2595)"],[17058,"The Prophet ﷺ recited, {On that Day God will pay them in full their true recompense}, and he said it like that."],[17059,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wiping his hand on his thigh and saying, {On that Day God will pay them in full their true recompense, and they will know that God is the Clear Truth}."],[17060,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “You complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and the most honored of them in the sight of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.”"],[17063,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: There was a servant among the servants of Allah to whom Allah gave wealth and children. A portion of his life passed, and a portion remained. He said to his sons: “What kind of father have I been to you?” They said: “The best of fathers.” He said: “By Allah, I will not leave with anyone any wealth that came from me to him, except that I will take it back—or you will do to me what I say to you.” So he took a covenant from them. He said: “If not, then when I die, burn me with fire, then crush me, then look for a windy day and scatter me, that perhaps I may elude Allah.” He said: So he was summoned and gathered, and it was said to him: “What made you do what you did?” He said: “I feared Your punishment.” He said: “Go forth, for you have been forgiven.”"],[17067,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the most honored of them in the sight of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.”"],[17068,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “You will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles on your mouths. The first part of a person to speak will be his thigh and his hand.”"],[17069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In Paradise there is a sea of water, a sea of wine, a sea of milk, and a sea of honey; then rivers are split open from them afterwards.”"],[17070,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, with what did our Lord send you to us? He said: “That you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, and give the zakat. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim. This is your religion; wherever you are, it will suffice you.”"],[17071,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of one of our wives over him? He said: “That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, and do not shun her except within the house.”"],[17073,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not come to you until I had sworn by the number of these fingers of mine that I would not come to you. By the One who sent you with the truth, what is it with which Allah sent you? He said: “With Islam.” I said: What is Islam? He said: “That you submit your heart to Allah, direct your face to Allah, pray the obligatory prayer, and pay the obligatory zakat. Two brothers, supporters: Allah does not accept the repentance of a servant who associates partners with Him after his Islam.”"],[17075,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the wife of one of us upon him?' He said, 'That you feed her when you eat, clothe her when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile her, and do not abandon her except in the house.'"],[17076,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'What is the right of the woman upon the husband?' He said, 'That he feeds her when he eats, clothes her when he clothes himself, does not strike the face, does not revile, and does not abandon except in your house.'"],[17077,"Gabriel ﷺ descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Muhammad, Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah al-Muzani has died. Would you like to pray over him?' He said, 'Yes.' Then he struck with his wings, and no tree or hill remained but that it lowered itself, and his bier was raised for him until he saw it, and he prayed over him. Behind him were two rows of angels, in each row seventy thousand. The Prophet ﷺ said to Gabriel, 'O Gabriel, what made him reach this station with Allah?' He said, 'His love for \"Say: He is Allah, the One,\" and his recitation of it coming and going, standing and sitting, and in every state.'"],[17078,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was marching to Tabuk when Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, would you like to attend the funeral of Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah al-Muzani?' He said, 'Yes.' Gabriel made a gesture with his hand like this, and the mountains and hills parted for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came walking, and with him was Gabriel ﷺ , and with Gabriel were seventy thousand angels, and he prayed over Mu'awiyah b. Mu'awiyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Gabriel ﷺ , 'By what did Mu'awiyah attain this?' He said, 'By his frequent recitation of \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\" He used to recite it standing, sitting, lying down, and walking. This is what brought him to what he attained.'"],[17079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is better for one of you to postpone his family and wealth than to miss the time of Asr prayer.\""],[17080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People wake up in a barren state, then Allah brings them provision from Himself, and they wake up associating partners, saying, \"We were given rain by such-and-such a star.\"'"],[17081,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'If there is healing in anything, it is a drink of honey, a cupping incision, or a branding with fire, but I do not like to be branded.'"],[17082,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, 'A morning or an evening in the path of Allah is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[17083,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A morning in the path of Allah or an evening is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[17084,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'A morning in the path of Allah or an evening is better than the world and what it contains.'"],[17085,"I prayed Maghrib with the Prophet ﷺ, and he forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs, then left. A man said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs.\" He ordered Bilal to make the iqamah for prayer, then he completed that rak'ah. The people asked about the man who said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you forgot.\" It was said, \"Do you know him?\" I said, \"No, unless I see him.\" He passed by me, and I said, \"He is this one.\" They said, \"This is Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah.\""],[17087,"I was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn. He said, \"What is your name?\" I said, \"Ghurab.\" He said, \"You are Muslim.\""],[17088,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you pray the morning prayer, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that day, protection from the Fire will be written for you. And when you pray Maghrib, say before speaking to anyone the like of that; for if you die that night, protection from the Fire will be written for you.\""],[17089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition. When we descended upon the people, I advanced ahead of my companions on my horse. The women and children came out to meet us, crying out. I said to them, \"Do you want to secure yourselves?\" They said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" They said it. Then my companions came and blamed me, saying, \"We were about to get the spoils, and you prevented us.\" Then we returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Do you know what he did? Allah has written for him such-and-such reward for every person.\" Then he brought me near him and said, \"When you pray the morning prayer, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that day, Allah will write for you protection from the Fire. And when you pray Maghrib, say before speaking to anyone: 'O Allah, protect me from the Fire' seven times. For if you die that night, Allah will write for you protection from the Fire.\""],[17090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for him a document of instruction to those after him whom Allah would put in authority, and sealed it."],[17091,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepting the pledge of women in the year of the conquest on al-Safa. A woman whose hand seemed like a man's hand came forward, and he refused to accept her pledge until she went and changed her hand with yellow dye. And a man came to him with a ring of iron on his hand, and he said, \"Allah has not purified a hand that has a ring of iron on it.\""],[17092,"He used to enter Madinah and take care of his business in the market, then return to his family. When he put down his cloak, he remembered that he had not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"By Allah, I have not prayed in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he told us: 'Whoever of you goes down to this town should not return to his family until he prays two rak'ahs in this mosque, then returns to his family.'\""],[17093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him over the captives of Qurayzah. He would look at the private part of a boy; if he saw that pubic hair had grown, his neck was struck; if it had not grown, he put him among the spoils of the Muslims."],[17094,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinate, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[17095,"A green jar containing camphor was given as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he divided it among the Muhajirun and the Ansar. He said, \"O Umm Sulaym, prepare nabidh for us in it.\""],[17096,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in what he instructed al-'Ala' when he dispatched him to al-Bahrayn. He said, \"It is not permissible for anyone to be ignorant of the obligatory duties and the sunnahs, and what is beyond that is permissible for him.\" And he wrote to al-'Ala': \"Treat the Magians according to the sunnah of the People of the Book.\""],[17097,"I heard Ibn Mukhallad say: “I was born when the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, and he died when I was ten years old.”"],[17098,"\"The Prophet ﷺ came when I was four years old, and he passed away when I was fourteen. The hadith of Abdur Rahman ibn Mahdi is with me, and Allah knows best.\""],[17099,"In the year sixty-two, Maslamah b. Makhlad died."],[17100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Strip women of clothing, and they will keep to the curtained litters.”"],[17101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The emigrants will precede the people to Paradise by forty autumns, enjoying themselves therein while the people are held back for the reckoning. Then the second group will be [preceded by] a hundred autumns.”"],[17102,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning Mu'awiyah: “O Allah, give him authority in the lands and protect him from the evil of the punishment.”"],[17103,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning Mu'awiyah: “O Allah, teach him the Book and arithmetic, and give him authority in the lands.”"],[17104,"“I have not come to you as a visitor, but I have come to you with a need. Do you remember the day when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever learns of a fault of his brother and conceals it, Allah will conceal his fault on the Day of Resurrection’?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “It is for this that I have come.”"],[17105,"Mu'awiyah said: “No Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her religion than Muhammad ﷺ, and no Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her worldly life than me.” Ma'n b. Yazid al-Sulami said: “No Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man better for her in her religion than Muhammad ﷺ, and no Qurayshi woman gave birth to a Qurayshi man worse for her in her worldly life than you.” He said: “And why?” He said: “Because you have accustomed them to a practice, and it is as if I see them seeking it from someone other than you, and you will bring them cast down in the roads.” He said: “Woe to you! By Allah, I have been concealing it from myself since such and such a time.”"],[17106,"A Bedouin came and took hold of the halter of the Prophet's ﷺ she-camel and said: “O Prophet of Allah, guide me to a deed that will bring me near to Paradise and distance me from the Fire.” He said: “You have been brief in your question, but you have asked broadly. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, and whatever you would dislike people to do to you, dislike it for them.”"],[17107,"I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I, my father, and my grandfather. He proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage. I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favor. My father came with two dinars intending to give them in charity. He placed them with a man, and I took them and brought them to him. He said: “By Allah, I did not intend you.” I brought the dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “You have what you intended, O Yazid, and you, O Ma'n, have what you took.”"],[17108,"“I brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ruled in my favor. He proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage, and I and my grandfather gave allegiance to him.”"],[17109,"“I gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and my grandfather. I brought a dispute to him and he ruled in my favor, and he proposed marriage on my behalf and gave me in marriage.” Then Ma'n said: “Booty is not lawful until it is distributed, and none of it is accepted until it is distributed to the people.”"],[17110,"We were in the land of the Romans, and a man from the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ from Banu Sulaym, called Ma'n b. Yazid al-Sulami, was appointed as our commander. He said: I acquired a red jar containing dinars, so I brought it to him. He took a fifth of it and said: 'Were it not that I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"There is no extra share (nafal) except from the fifth,\" I would have given it to you.' He said: Then he offered me from his own share, but I said: 'I have no need of it.'"],[17111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Gather in your mosques, and when a group gathers, let them inform me.' We were the first of the people to gather, so we came to him and informed him. He came walking with us until he sat with us. A speaker among us spoke and said: 'Praise be to God, besides whose praise there is no stopping point, and beyond whom there is no passage,' or something like this. The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry and stood up. We blamed one another and said: 'God favored us that he came to us first of the people, and he did such and such.' We came to him and found him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so. We spoke to him, and he came back with us until he sat in his previous place, or near it. Then he said: 'Indeed, praise be to God. Whatever He wills, He places before Him, and whatever He wills, He places behind Him. Indeed, some eloquence is magic.' Then he turned to us, spoke to us, commanded us, and taught us."],[17112,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17113,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd, or beside Ludd.'"],[17114,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, and he mentioned the Dajjal, then said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, the son of Maryam will certainly kill him at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17115,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17116,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17117,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17118,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: 'The son of Maryam will kill the Masih at the gate of Ludd.'"],[17119,"From his uncle Mujammi' b. Jariyah, who said: We returned with the Messenger of God ﷺ from Madinah until, when the Messenger of God ﷺ reached Kura' al-Ghamim, the people began to spread the news toward the Messenger of God ﷺ. Some of the people said to others: 'What is with the people?' He said: 'It was revealed to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' So we were stirred until we found the Messenger of God ﷺ standing at Kura' al-Ghamim. When the people gathered, he recited to them: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.' Some of the people said: 'O Messenger of God, is it a victory?' He said: 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, it is the victory.' Then it was divided among the people of al-Hudaybiyyah into eighteen shares. The army was one thousand five hundred, including three hundred horsemen, and the horseman received two shares. The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn al-Tabba'."],[17120,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out for the funeral of a man from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf until he reached the cemetery. He said: 'Peace be upon the inhabitants of the graves' three times: 'Whoever of you is among the believers and Muslims, you are our predecessors and we are your followers. May God grant us and you well-being.'"],[17121,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Qasim b. Muhammad, from Mujammi' and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid: 'A man of theirs called Khidham married his daughter called Khansa', but she disliked it. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he annulled it. We used to say that she was a previously married woman (thayyib).'"],[17122,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Your brother, the Negus, has died, so pray over him.” Ibn Abi Shaybah added in his narration: “And we lined up behind him in two rows.”"],[17123,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded that a neighbor should not prevent his neighbor from fixing a wooden peg in his wall."],[17124,"He informed him that two brothers from the Banu al-Mughirah, one of them swore an oath of manumission against his companion that he would not let him place a wooden beam in his wall. They then met Mujammi‘ b. Yazid and some men from the Ansar, who said, “We bear witness that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘A neighbor shall not prevent his neighbor from placing a wooden beam in his wall.’” So he said, “O my brother, I have come to know that it has been decreed in your favor against me, so why did you set up pillars instead of against my wall?” And he set up pillars. ‘Amr said, “And I saw those pillars.”"],[17125,"Makhramah b. Nawfal, whose kunyah was Abu al-Miswar, died in the year 54, at the age of seventy. It has also been said that he was one hundred and fifteen years old. He accepted Islam on the day of the conquest and was among those whose hearts were reconciled."],[17126,"“When the Messenger of God ﷺ proclaimed Islam openly, all the people of Makkah embraced it, and that was before the prayer was made obligatory, so much so that when he would recite a verse of prostration, they would prostrate, though none of them could even prostrate due to the crowding.” Until the leaders of Quraysh arrived — al-Walid b. al-Mughirah, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, and others — for they had been in al-Ta’if at their estates. They said, “Will you abandon the religion of your forefathers?” And so they disbelieved."],[17127,"“Al-Miswar b. Makhramah died on the day the news of Yazid b. Mu‘awiyah’s death came to Ibn al-Zubayr, in the year 64. Ibn al-Zubayr prayed over him at al-Hajun. He was struck by a stone from a catapult while he was praying in the Hijr, and he lingered for five days, then died in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal in the year 64. He was born two years after the Hijrah, and was brought to Madinah in the latter part of Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 8, and he witnessed the year of the conquest when he was six years old. The Prophet ﷺ died when he was eight years old.” Meaning al-Miswar b. Makhramah."],[17128,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not walk about naked.”"],[17129,"Subay‘ah al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a few nights until she gave birth. When she had completed her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry after she had given birth, and he permitted her, so she married."],[17130,"Subay‘ah bt. al-Harith’s husband died, and she gave birth after eight or seven [days]. The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded her to get married."],[17131,"Subay‘ah al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a few nights until she gave birth. When she had recovered from her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry after she had given birth, and he permitted her, and she married."],[17132,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Hisham b. ‘Urwah, from his father, from al-Miswar b. Makhramah: Subay‘ah bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyyah’s husband died while she was pregnant, and she did not remain except for a short while until she gave birth. When she had recovered from her postnatal bleeding, she received a marriage proposal. She asked the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission to marry, and he permitted her, and she married."],[17133,"Subay‘ah gave birth a few days after her husband’s death. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked permission to marry, and he permitted her."],[17134,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Subay'ah to marry when she became pure from her post-natal bleeding. Thus said Ibn Ashkib, 'Asim b. 'Umar."],[17135,"Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah's husband died while she was pregnant. Only a few nights passed before she gave birth. She sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ when she became pure from her post-natal bleeding, and he permitted her, so she married."],[17136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to his companions and said: \"Allah ﷻ sent me as a mercy to all people, so convey on my behalf, may Allah have mercy on you, and do not differ as the disciples differed concerning 'Isa ﷺ . He called them to the like of what I call you to. As for those whose place was near, they answered and submitted. As for those whose place was far, they disliked it, so 'Isa ibn Maryam complained of that to Allah ﷻ. Then they woke up and each man among them spoke the language of the people to whom he was sent. 'Isa ibn Maryam ﷺ said to them: 'This is a matter which Allah has firmly resolved for you, so go and do it.' The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We, O Messenger of Allah, will convey on your behalf, so send us wherever you wish.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Abd Allah b. Hudhafah to Kisra, sent Salit b. 'Amr to Hawdhah b. 'Ali, the ruler of al-Yamamah, sent al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami to al-Mundhir b. Sawa, the ruler of Hajar, sent 'Amr b. al-'As to Jayfar and 'Abbad, the two sons of al-Julanda, kings of Oman, sent Dihyah al-Kalbi to Caesar, sent Shuja' b. Wahb al-Asadi to al-Mundhir b. al-Harith b. Abi Shimr al-Ghassani, and sent 'Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri to the Negus. They all returned before the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except al-'Ala' b. al-Hadrami, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was in al-Bahrayn."],[17137,"From al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam, each of them confirming the other, they said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah with some ten and a few hundred of his companions, until when they were at Dhu al-Hulayfah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded the sacrificial animal and marked it, then entered ihram for 'umrah. He sent ahead of him a spy from Khuza'ah to inform him about Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ traveled until when he was at Ghadir al-Ashtat, near 'Usfan, his Khuza'i spy came to him and said: 'I left Ka'b b. Lu'ayy and 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, and they have gathered the Ahabish against you and gathered forces against you, and they will fight you and bar you from the Sacred House.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Advise me. Do you think I should raid the dependents of these who have helped them, and capture them? If they stay put, they stay bereaved and robbed, and if they come, it will be a neck cut off by Allah. Or do you think we should head for the House, and whoever bars us from it, we fight?' Abu Bakr said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best, O Prophet of Allah. We have only come as pilgrims, and we have not come to fight anyone, but whoever comes between us and the House, we will fight him.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Then set out in the afternoon.' So they set out, until when they were on part of the road, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Khalid b. al-Walid is at al-Ghamim with a cavalry of Quraysh as an advance guard, so take the right.' By Allah, Khalid was not aware of them until he saw the dust of the army, so he set off galloping as a warner to Quraysh. The Prophet ﷺ traveled until when he was at the mountain pass from which they would descend upon them, his mount knelt down. The people said: 'Hal! Hal!' They said: 'Al-Qaswa' has become stubborn.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Al-Qaswa' has not become stubborn, and that is not her nature, but she was held back by the One who held back the elephant.' Then he said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, they will not ask me for any plan by which they honor the sacred things of Allah but that I will grant it to them.' Then he prodded her and she leaped up with him, and he turned away from them until he stopped at the farthest part of al-Hudaybiyyah at a small water hole. The people were only drawing water from it sparingly. It was not long before the people exhausted it. They complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of thirst. He drew an arrow from his quiver, then commanded them to place it in the water. By Allah, it kept gushing for them with enough to drink until they left it. While they were thus, Budayl b. Warqa' al-Khuza'i came to them with a group of his people from Khuza'ah, and they were the trusted advisers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the people of Tihamah. He said: 'I left Ka'b b. Lu'ayy and 'Amir b. Lu'ayy, and they have camped at the water holes of al-Hudaybiyyah, and with them are the camels with young, and they will fight you and bar you from the House.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'We have not come to fight anyone, but we have come as pilgrims. War has worn down Quraysh and harmed them. If they wish, I will make a truce with them for a period, and they should leave the way open between me and the people. If I prevail, then if they wish to enter into what the people have entered, they may do so, and if not, they will have rested. But if they refuse, then by the One in whose hand is my soul, I will fight them for this cause of mine until my neck is severed, or Allah will surely carry out His command.' Budayl said: 'I will convey to them what you say.' He went until he came to Quraysh and said: 'We have come to you from this man, and we heard him say something. If you wish, we will present it to you.' Their foolish ones said: 'We have no need for you to tell us anything about him.' Those of sound judgment among them said: 'Give us what you heard him say.' He said: 'I heard him say such and such,' and he told them what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi stood up and said: 'O people, am I not the father?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Am I not the child?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you suspect me?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you not know that I called upon the people of 'Ukaz, and when they failed me, I came to you with my family and children and those who obeyed me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'This man has offered you a plan of right guidance, so accept it and let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' He went to him and began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar to what he had said to Budayl. 'Urwah said at that: 'O Muhammad, do you think that if you exterminate your people, have you heard of anyone among the Arabs who destroyed his own family before you? And if it is the other way, by Allah, I see faces and I see a rabble of people likely to flee and abandon you.' Abu Bakr said: 'Suck the clitoris of al-Lat! Would we flee and abandon him?' He said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'Abu Bakr.' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, were it not for a favor you owe me that I have not repaid, I would answer you.' He kept speaking with the Prophet ﷺ, and whenever he spoke to him, he took hold of his beard. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah was standing at the head of the Prophet ﷺ with a helmet, and with him was a sword. Whenever 'Urwah reached his hand to the beard of the Prophet ﷺ, he struck his hand with the scabbard of the sword and said: 'Take your hand away from the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' 'Urwah raised his head and said: 'Who is this?' He said: 'This is al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah.' He said: 'O treacherous one, am I not striving to rectify your treachery?' Al-Mughirah had accompanied a people in the Jahiliyyah, killed them, and taken their wealth, then came and embraced Islam. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'As for Islam, I accept it, but as for the wealth, I have nothing to do with it.' Then 'Urwah began to gaze at the companions of the Prophet ﷺ with his eyes. He said: 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not spit but that it fell into the hand of one of them and he rubbed it on his face and skin, and when he commanded them, they hastened to his command, and when he performed ablution, they almost fought over his ablution water, and when he spoke, they lowered their voices in his presence, and they did not stare at him out of reverence for him.' 'Urwah returned to his companions and said: 'O people, by Allah, I have gone as an envoy to kings, and I have gone as an envoy to Caesar, Kisra, and the Negus. By Allah, I have never seen a king whose companions honor him as the companions of Muhammad honor Muhammad. By Allah, he did not spit but that it fell into the palm of one of them and he rubbed it on his face and skin, and when he commanded them, they hastened to his command, and when he performed ablution, they almost fought over his ablution water, and when they spoke, they lowered their voices in his presence, and they did not stare at him out of reverence for him. He has offered you a plan of right guidance, so accept it.' A man from Banu Kinanah said: 'Let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' When he appeared before the Prophet ﷺ and his companions, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is so-and-so, and he is from a people who honor sacrificial camels, so send them out to him.' They were sent out to him, and the people met him reciting the talbiyah. When he saw that, he said: 'Glory be to Allah, it is not right for these people to be barred from the House.' When he returned to his companions, he said: 'I saw the sacrificial camels garlanded and marked, and I do not think they should be barred from the House.' A man among them called Mikraz b. Hafs said: 'Let me go to him.' They said: 'Go to him.' When he appeared before them, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'This is Mikraz b. Hafs, and he is a wicked man.' He began to speak with the Prophet ﷺ. While he was speaking with him, Suhayl b. 'Amr came and said: 'Come, let us write a treaty between us and you.' He called for the scribe. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' Suhayl said: 'As for \"the Most Gracious,\" by Allah, I do not know what it is, but write: In Your name, O Allah, as you used to write.' The Muslims said: 'By Allah, we will not write it except with: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Write: In Your name, O Allah.' Then he said: 'This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, has agreed upon.' Suhayl said: 'By Allah, if we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have barred you from the House nor fought you. But write: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By Allah, I am the Messenger of Allah, even if you deny me. Write: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'On condition that you leave the way open between us and the House so that we may circumambulate it.' Suhayl said: 'By Allah, the Arabs will never say that we were taken by force, but you may have it next year.' So he wrote. Suhayl said: 'And on condition that no man from us comes to you, even if he follows your religion, but that you return him to us.' The Muslims said: 'Glory be to Allah, how can he be returned to the polytheists when he has come as a Muslim?' While they were thus, Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. 'Amr came dragging his chains, having escaped from the lower part of Makkah, until he threw himself among the Muslims. Suhayl said: 'This, O Muhammad, is the first one with whom I make you agree that you return him to me.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'We have not yet concluded the treaty.' He said: 'By Allah, then I will never make peace with you for anything.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Then grant him to me.' He said: 'I will not grant him to you.' He said: 'Yes, then do it.' He said: 'I will not do it.' Mikraz said: 'Yes, we grant him to you.' Abu Jandal said: 'O assembly of Muslims, shall I be returned to the polytheists when I have come as a Muslim? Do you not see what I have suffered?' He had been severely tortured for the sake of Allah. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: 'By Allah, I never doubted since I embraced Islam except on that day. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Are you not truly the Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Are we not on the truth and our enemy on falsehood?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?' He said: 'I am the Messenger of Allah, and I do not disobey Him, and He will help me.' I said: 'Did you not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?' He said: 'Yes, but did I tell you that you would come to it this year?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You will come to it and circumambulate it.' Then I went to Abu Bakr and said: 'O Abu Bakr, is this not truly the Prophet of Allah?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Are we not on the truth and our enemy on falsehood?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why do we accept humiliation in our religion?' He said: 'O man, he is the Messenger of Allah, and he does not disobey his Lord, and He will help him. So hold fast to his stirrup until you die. By Allah, he is upon the truth.' I said: 'Did he not tell us that we would come to the House and circumambulate it?' He said: 'Yes, but did he tell you that you would come to it this year?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'You will come to it and circumambulate it.' When he finished the treaty, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Arise and slaughter, then shave.' By Allah, not one of them stood up until he said it three times. When none of them stood up, he got up and entered upon Umm Salamah and mentioned to her what he had encountered from the people. Umm Salamah said: 'O Prophet of Allah, do you want that? Go out, then do not speak a word to any of them until you slaughter your sacrificial camel and call your barber to shave you.' He got up and went out, and did not speak to anyone among them until he did that: he slaughtered his sacrificial camel and called his barber, who shaved him. When they saw that, they arose and slaughtered, and some of them began to shave others, until some of them almost killed others out of grief. Then believing women came, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {O you who believe, when believing women come to you as emigrants} until He reached {the ties of the disbelieving women}. That day 'Umar divorced two wives he had in polytheism. One of them was married by Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan and the other by Safwan b. Umayyah. Then the Prophet ﷺ returned to Madinah. Abu Basir, a man from Quraysh, came, and he was a Muslim. They sent two men after him and said: 'The pact you made with us.' So he handed him over to the two men. They went out until when they reached Dhu al-Hulayfah with him, they dismounted to eat from some dates of theirs. Abu Basir said to one of the two men: 'By Allah, I think this sword of yours, O so-and-so, is good.' The other drew it and said: 'Yes, by Allah, it is good. I have tried it and tried it again.' Abu Basir said: 'Show me, let me look at it.' He handed it to him, and he struck him with it until he died. The other fled until he came to Madinah and entered the mosque running. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: 'This man has seen something terrifying.' When he reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'By Allah, my companion has been killed, and I will be killed.' Abu Basir came and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, by Allah, Allah has fulfilled your protection. You returned me to them, then Allah saved me from them.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Woe to his mother, a kindler of war, if only he had someone.' When he heard that, he knew that he would return him to them, so he went out until he reached the coast. Abu Jandal b. Suhayl escaped from them and joined Abu Basir. No man from Quraysh who had embraced Islam left but that he joined Abu Basir, until a band of them gathered. By Allah, they did not hear of any caravan of Quraysh headed to Syria but that they intercepted it, killed them, and took their wealth. Quraysh sent to the Prophet ﷺ, adjuring him by Allah and kinship, to send to them, and whoever came to him would be safe. The Prophet ﷺ sent for them, and Allah ﷻ revealed: {And it is He who restrained their hands from you and your hands from them in the interior of Makkah} until He reached {the arrogance of the Jahiliyyah}. Quraysh's arrogance was that they did not acknowledge that he was the Prophet of Allah, did not acknowledge 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' and came between him and the House."],[17139,"He heard al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam relating from the news of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of al-Hudaybiyyah. Among what 'Urwah reported to me from them was that they said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the treaty with Suhayl b. 'Amr on the day of al-Hudaybiyyah for the agreed period, among what Suhayl b. 'Amr stipulated upon him was that he said: 'No one from us shall come to you, even if he follows your religion, but that you return him to us and leave the way between us and him.' Suhayl refused to make peace with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except on that condition, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the treaty with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned Abu Jandal b. Suhayl that day to his father Suhayl b. 'Amr. No man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but that he returned him during that period, even if he was a Muslim. Then believing women came as emigrants. Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt left to join the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant. Her family came asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return her to them, until Allah ﷻ revealed concerning the believing women what He revealed."],[17140,"The affair of al-Hudaybiyyah from its beginning to its end.\""],[17141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he divided Khaybar, divided it into eighty shares. The men were one thousand eight hundred, and the horses were two hundred. For the horses, four hundred shares, each share for eighteen hundred shares, and for every hundred shares a commander. 'Umar b. al-Khattab was a commander, 'Ali a commander, Talhah a commander, al-Zubayr a commander, and 'Asim b. 'Adi a commander. The share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with 'Asim b. 'Adi."],[17142,"He informed him that 'Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl while he was married to Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Fatimah heard of that, she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him: 'Your people are saying that you do not become angry for your daughters, and here is 'Ali marrying the daughter of Abu Jahl.' Al-Miswar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit, and I heard him declare the shahadah, then he said: 'To proceed: I married Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi', and he told me and was truthful to me. Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad, is a part of me, and I dislike that you should tempt her. By Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined with one man.' So 'Ali abandoned the proposal."],[17144,"He said to him: 'Do you have any need you would command me with?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Will you give me the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I fear that the people may overpower you for it. By Allah, if you give it to me, no one will ever reach it until my soul reaches here. 'Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl in addition to Fatimah. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing the people about that on this pulpit of his, and I was then a youth. He said: 'Fatimah is from me, and I fear that she will be tempted in her religion.' Then he mentioned the in-law relationship of Banu 'Abd Shams and praised Abu al-'As in his marriage alliance with him. He said: 'He was truthful to me and promised me and fulfilled it. I do not forbid what is lawful nor make lawful what is forbidden, but by Allah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah will never be joined.'"],[17145,"Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl and set a date for the marriage. Fatimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Your people are saying that you do not become angry for your daughters, and 'Ali has proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: 'Fatimah is but a part of me, and I dislike that she be tempted.' He mentioned Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' and praised him well, and said: 'He will never join the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the daughter of the enemy of Allah.'"],[17146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'None of you should pray while he finds any impurity,' meaning feces or urine."],[17147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A child does not inherit until it cries out at birth.' Its crying out is that it screams, cries, or sneezes."],[17148,"Regarding a sale or a gift she had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' 'A'ishah said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' So 'A'ishah said: 'It is for Allah a vow upon me that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr sought intercession with her when her avoidance of him grew long, and 'A'ishah said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him, nor will I break my vow that I made ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad brought Ibn al-Zubayr, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr rushed to the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman began adjuring 'A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said to her: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ indeed forbade what you already know of abandonment, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, and she freed forty slaves for that vow of hers. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[17149,"It is narrated from 'Awf b. al-Harith b. Tufayl, the son of 'A'ishah's maternal uncle, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that 'A'ishah told him that 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr said about a sale or a gift that 'A'ishah had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' She said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' 'A'ishah said: 'Then it is for Allah a vow that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her when her avoidance of him grew long, and she said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him ever, nor will I break my vow that I made ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Banu Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad brought him, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Yes, enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not know that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and 'Abd al-Rahman began adjuring 'A'ishah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade what you already know of abandonment, for it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, then she freed forty slaves for her vow. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[17151,"'Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Tufayl, the son of 'A'ishah's ؓ maternal uncle, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that 'A'ishah was told that 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr said about a sale or gifts that 'A'ishah had given: 'By Allah, 'A'ishah must stop, or I will place her under a restriction.' She said: 'Did he say this?' They said: 'Yes.' She said: 'It is for Allah a vow upon me that I shall never speak a word to Ibn al-Zubayr ever.' Then Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her through people when she prolonged his abandonment, and she said: 'By Allah, I will not accept anyone's intercession for him, nor will I break my vow ever.' When that grew long for Ibn al-Zubayr, he spoke to al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth, who were from Banu Zuhrah, and said: 'I adjure you both by Allah to enter me upon 'A'ishah, for it is not lawful for her to vow to sever ties with me.' So al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad b. 'Abd Yaghuth brought him, wrapping him in their cloaks, until they sought permission to enter upon 'A'ishah. They said: 'Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. May we enter?' 'A'ishah said: 'Enter.' They said: 'All of us, O Mother of the Believers?' She said: 'Yes, enter, all of you,' while 'A'ishah did not realize that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered, Ibn al-Zubayr entered the curtain, embraced 'A'ishah, and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar b. Makhramah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Aswad began adjuring 'A'ishah by Allah to speak to him and accept from him, and they said to her: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade abandonment as you know, and he said: \"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights.\"' When they repeated the reminder and the admonition to 'A'ishah, she began to remind them and weep and say: 'I have made a vow, and the matter of a vow is serious.' They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr, then she freed forty slaves for her vow. Then she used to remember that vow of hers after she had freed forty slaves and weep until her tears soaked her veil."],[17152,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at 'Arafat. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Now then, indeed the people of shirk and idols used to depart from this place when the sun was on the tops of the mountains like turbans of men on their faces, and we depart after it sets. And they used to depart from al-Mash'ar al-Haram when the sun was spread out.'"],[17153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing will be darknesses on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[17154,"Tell him to meet me at a time he mentioned. So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and said: 'There is no tie, lineage, or in-law relation dearer to me than your lineage and your in-law relation, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fatimah is a branch of me. What pleases her pleases me, and what distresses her distresses me. On the Day of Resurrection, all lineages will be cut off except my lineage and my tie.\" And under you is her daughter; if I married her to you, that would distress her.' So he went away excusing him."],[17155,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever takes something from the land will be made to carry around his neck on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths.'"],[17156,"A Jew passed by me while I was behind the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ was performing ablution. His garment fell on his back, and there was the seal of prophethood on his back. The Jew said: 'Lift his garment from his back.' So I went to lift the Prophet's ﷺ garment from his back, and the Prophet ﷺ blew a handful of water in my face."],[17157,"And he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every tie and lineage will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my tie and my lineage.\"'"],[17158,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in prayer, and he left out something he did not recite. A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it was such and such.' He said: 'Why did you not remind me of it?' He said: 'I thought it had been abrogated.'"],[17159,"From 'Urwah, on the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, then from Banu Salimah: Mu'adh b. Jabal b. 'Amr b. 'A'idh b. 'Adi b. Ka'b b. Udayy b. Sa'd b. 'Adi b. Asad b. Saridah b. Tazid b. Jusham, and he attended Badr."],[17160,"From Ibn Shihab, on the naming of those who attended Badr from the Ansar: Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[17161,"Because he was the maternal brother of Suhayl b. Muhammad b. al-Jadd b. Qays b. Sakhr b. Khansa' b. Sinan b. 'Ubayd b. 'Adi b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salama\""],[17162,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and the one who raises his age says thirty-two years."],[17163,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and the one who raises his age says thirty-two years."],[17164,"I heard Malik b. Anas say: Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and one who speaks says thirty-two."],[17165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Mu'adh b. Jabal is ahead of the scholars by a bowshot.\""],[17166,"\"Mu'adh b. Jabal passed away when he was thirty-three or thirty-four years old.\""],[17167,"\"Mu'adh b. Jabal died in the plague of 'Amwas in the year seventeen or eighteen.\""],[17168,"\"So he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ to intercede with his creditors, and he did.\" But they did not reduce anything for him. Had anyone been let off for another's intercession, Mu'adh would have been let off for the Messenger of God's ﷺ intercession. \"Then the Prophet ﷺ summoned him, and he did not cease until he sold his property and divided it among his creditors.\" Mu'adh stood up with no property. \"Then when the Prophet ﷺ performed the Hajj, he sent him to Yemen to set him right.\" He said: Mu'adh was the first to do business with this wealth, and he arrived before Abu Bakr from Yemen when the Messenger of God ﷺ had already passed away."],[17169,"That the affair of this community in its latter time will return to being brothers openly and enemies in secret. And we seek refuge with God from our letter descending other than the place it descended from our hearts, for we wrote it only as sincere counsel to you. Peace be upon you. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ wrote back to them: From 'Umar b. al-Khattab to Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah and Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ. Peace be upon you both. Now then, your letter reached me in which you mention that you had admonished me and that my own affairs are important to me. I have become the one entrusted with the affair of this community, its red and its black; the noble and the lowly, the enemy and the friend sit before me, and for everyone there is a share of justice. You wrote: Look how you are in that situation, O 'Umar. Indeed, there is no power and no strength for them in that except through God. You wrote warning me of what the nations before us were warned of, and it is ancient. Indeed, the alternation of night and day, with the death terms of people, brings near every distant thing and brings every new thing and brings every promised thing until people come to their abodes of Paradise or the Fire. You wrote warning me that the affair of this community will return in its latter time to being brothers openly and enemies in secret. But you are not those people, and this is not the time of that; that is a time when desire and fear appear, when some people's desire for one another will be for the good of their worldly affairs. You wrote seeking refuge with God from your letter descending other than the place it descended from your hearts, and that you wrote it as sincere counsel to me. You have spoken truly, so do not stop writing to me, for I cannot do without you. Peace be upon you both."],[17170,"He said: The Commander of the Faithful says to you: Put this toward some of your needs. So he said: May God maintain him and have mercy on him. Then he said: Come, O slave girl, take these seven to so-and-so and these five to so-and-so, until he had distributed it all. The boy returned and told him, and he found that he had prepared the like of it to Mu'adh b. Jabal. He said: \"Take this to Mu'adh b. Jabal and leave it in the house until you see what he does.\" So he took it to him, and he said: The Commander of the Faithful says to you: Put this toward some of your needs. He said: May God have mercy on him and maintain him. Come, O slave girl, go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such, and go to the house of so-and-so with such-and-such. Then Mu'adh's wife looked in and said: By God, we are poor, so give us. And nothing remained in the cloth except two dinars, so he tossed them to her. The boy returned to 'Umar and told him, and he was pleased and said: \"They are brothers, one from another.\""],[17171,"Do you know what the qanit is? They said no. He said: \"The one obedient to God.\""],[17172,"Mu'adh, when he would perform the night prayer, would say: \"O Allah, eyes have slept and stars have set, and You are the Ever-Living, the Sustainer. O Allah, my pursuit of Paradise is slow and my fleeing from the Fire is weak. O Allah, appoint for me guidance with You that You will return to me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break the promise.\""],[17173,"I enjoin upon you two matters: if you preserve them, you will be preserved. You are not free from need of your share of this world, and you are more in need of your share of the Hereafter. So prefer your share of the Hereafter over your share of this world until it becomes firmly established for you, so that it departs with you wherever you depart."],[17174,"\"You have not ceased to annoy me since today.\" She said: \"It was certainly distressing to me to annoy you.\" He said: \"An angel of stern rebuke has not ceased that whenever you said 'Woe to such-and-such,' he said: 'Are you indeed like that?' and I say: 'No.'\""],[17175,"\"I saw Mu'adh b. Jabal killing lice and fleas in the mosque.\""],[17176,"From one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Two men do not love each other for the sake of Allah except that Allah sets down for them a seat upon which they are made to sit until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, finishes the reckoning.\" Mu'adh b. Jabal said: \"Abu Ubaydah has spoken the truth.\""],[17177,"A hadith I heard from the occupant of this grave—meaning the Prophet ﷺ: \"Indeed, the least amount of ostentation is shirk (polytheism), and the most beloved of servants to Allah are the pious, the hidden ones, who when they are absent are not missed, and when they are present are not recognized. Those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge.\""],[17178,"'Abd Allah said to him: \"What is the matter with you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, that you are talking to yourself?\" He said: \"What is with me? The enemy of Allah wants to divert me from what I heard from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me: 'You will now struggle for the rest of your life in your house, not going out to the gathering. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever strives in the path of Allah has a guarantee upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever visits a sick person has a guarantee upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Whoever goes to the mosque in the morning or evening has a guarantee upon Allah. Whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone with evil has a guarantee upon Allah.' So the enemy of Allah wants to make me leave my house for the gathering.\""],[17179,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Five things: whoever does one of them has a guarantee upon Allah—whoever visits a sick person, or goes out with a funeral procession, or goes out as a warrior, or enters upon his leader intending to honor and respect him, or sits in his house so that people are safe from him and he is safe from people.\""],[17180,"Mu'adh b. Jabal informed him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with a changed complexion and said: \"I am Muhammad. I have been given the openings of speech and its closings, so obey me as long as I am among you. And when I am taken away, then upon you is the Book of Allah: make lawful its lawful and forbid its forbidden. Death has come to you; it has come to you with rest and relief. It is a decree from Allah that has preceded. Trials have come to you like patches of dark night. Whenever messengers pass, messengers come. Prophethood has been abrogated and has become kingship. May Allah have mercy on one who takes it by its right and departs from it as he entered it. Hold back, O Mu'adh, and count.\" He said: When I reached five, he said: \"Yazid, may Allah not bless Yazid.\" Then his eyes shed tears and he said: \"Husayn has been announced dead to me, and I was brought his soil and informed of his killer. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one is killed among a people who do not defend him except that Allah causes division between their chests and hearts, sets their worst ones over them, and clothes them in factions.\" Then he said: \"Alas for the offspring of the family of Muhammad from a successor appointed, living in luxury, who will kill my successor and the successor of the successor. Hold back, O Mu'adh.\" When I reached ten, he said: \"Al-Walid is the name of a Pharaoh, a destroyer of the laws of Islam. Before him is a man from his household. Allah will surely draw his sword, and there will be no sheath for it. The people will differ and will be like this\"—and he interlaced his fingers—then he said: \"After one hundred and twenty: swift death and rapid killing. In that is their destruction. Then a man from the descendants of al-Abbas will rule over them.\""],[17181,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when they mentioned a man who was with him, and they said: \"How incapable he is!\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You have backbitten your brother.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we said what is in him.\" He said: \"If you said what is not in him, then you would have slandered him.\""],[17182,"Mu'adh b. Jabal wanted to travel, so he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said: \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give me more.\" He said: \"And when you do wrong, then do good.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give me more.\" He said: \"Be upright and make your character good.\""],[17183,"That you should rely upon me. I have narrated to you a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Whoever dies with 'there is no god but Allah' in his heart, certain of it, enters Paradise.\""],[17184,"While he was ill, he said: Uncover for me the curtain of the dome; I shall relate to you a hadith that, were it not for the state I am in, I would not relate to you. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies affirming 'There is no god but God' with certainty from his soul enters Paradise.\""],[17185,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal was near death, he said: Raise from me the curtains of the dome, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies worshipping God, associating nothing with Him, enters Paradise.\""],[17186,"Mu'adh said: Uncover for me the curtain of the dome, for were it not for what has come upon me from God I would not inform you of what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger enters Paradise.\""],[17187,"Someone who witnessed Mu'adh b. Jabal when death came to him informed us, saying: Raise from me the curtain of the dome so that I may relate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Nothing prevented me from relating it to you except that you might rely upon it. I heard him say: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely from his heart enters Paradise and the Fire will not touch him.\""],[17188,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Whoever gives a man security and then kills him, the Fire is guaranteed for him, even if the slain man was a disbeliever.\""],[17189,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with two men of the Ash'aris, one on my right and the other on my left, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was cleaning his teeth. Both of them asked for appointment to office. He said: \"O Abu Musa—or, O 'Abd Allah—\" I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not reveal to me what was in their minds, and I was not aware that they were seeking office. It was as if I could see his tooth-stick beneath his lip. He said to me: \"We do not appoint over our work anyone who desires it. But go, O Abu Musa—or, O 'Abd Allah b. Qays—\" So he sent him to Yemen, then followed him with Mu'adh b. Jabal. When he arrived, he placed a cushion for him and said: \"Dismount.\" There was a man bound in chains. He said: \"What is this?\" He said: This man was a Jew, then he embraced Islam, then he returned to his religion—the religion of evil. He said: \"I will not sit until he is killed, by the decree of God and His Messenger,\" three times. So he ordered it and he was killed."],[17190,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him and Mu'adh b. Jabal to Yemen and ordered them to teach the people the Qur'an. Mu'adh came to Abu Musa to visit him, and there was a man bound with iron at his place. He said: O my brother, were we sent to torment people, or were we sent to teach them and command them with what benefits them? He said to him: He embraced Islam and then disbelieved. He said: By the One who sent Muhammad with the truth, I will not leave until I burn him with fire. Abu Musa said: We still have a remnant of him among us. Mu'adh said: By God, I will never leave. So firewood was brought, the fire was kindled in it, and he threw him in."],[17191,"A man embraced Islam and then became a Jew. Mu'adh came to him while he was with Abu Musa and said to him: What is this? He said: He embraced Islam and then became a Jew. He said: \"I will not sit until you kill him, by the decree of God and His Messenger.\""],[17192,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said while we were sitting on a carpet: \"There will be a trial.\" They said: How should we act? He said: He returned his hand to the carpet, grasped it, and said: \"They will do like this.\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned to them: \"There will be a trial,\" but many of the people did not hear him. Mu'adh b. Jabal said: Do you not hear what the Messenger of God ﷺ is saying? They said: What did he say? He said: He says: \"There will be a trial.\" They said: What then should we do, O Messenger of God, and how should we act? He said: \"Return to your former affair.\""],[17193,"We came to the Messenger of Allah while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you doing something that I have not seen you do in a prayer.\" He said, \"It was a voluntary prayer of desire and caution. I asked Allah three times in it, so He gave me two and prevented me from one. I asked Him not to subject my Ummah to an enemy other than themselves, who would overpower them, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to send upon them a calamity that would destroy them, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to make their misfortune between themselves, so He turned it away from me.\""],[17194,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"No servant dies bearing witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, tracing that back to a certain heart, except that he enters Paradise.\" It was said to him: Did you hear this from Mu'adh? He said: I heard this from Mu'adh relating it from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[17195,"I entered the congregational mosque in Basra and sat with an old man with white head and beard. He said: Mu'adh b. Jabal narrated to me from the Messenger of God ﷺ that he said: \"No soul dies bearing witness that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, tracing that back to a believing heart, except that God forgives him.\" I said: Did you hear this from Mu'adh b. Jabal? It was as if the people rebuked him. He said: Do not rebuke him or reproach him; leave him. I heard that from Mu'adh b. Jabal tracing it from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I said to the people: Who is this? They said: 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah."],[17198,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out while Mu'adh b. Jabal was at the door. When he saw him, he said: \"O Mu'adh.\" He said: At your service, O Messenger of God. He said: \"Whoever dies associating nothing with God enters Paradise.\" Mu'adh said: O Messenger of God, shall I not inform the people? He said: \"Leave them; let them vie with one another in deeds, for I fear they will rely upon it.\""],[17199,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” Muadh said: “O Messenger of God, shall I not give the people this glad tidings?” He said: “I fear they will rely on it.”"],[17200,"I heard him say that Muadh was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ when he told him: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.”"],[17201,"On the authority of Attab, the freedman of Hurmuz, a man from the people of Wasit, on the authority of Anas b. Malik, who said: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with this hand of mine to hear and obey as much as I could, and I heard him narrate that Muadh b. Jabal was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ told him: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever dies not associating anything with God will enter Paradise.” Muadh said: “O Messenger of God, shall I not give the people this glad tidings?” He said: “Indeed I fear they will rely on it.”"],[17202,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God sincerely from his heart will enter Paradise.”"],[17203,"Abdullah b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us; Salamah b. Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Anas b. Malik, that he heard him say: Muadh b. Jabal came to me and I said: “Where have you come from, O Muadh?” He said: “I have come from the Prophet of God ﷺ.” I said: “What did he say to you?” He said: “Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely will enter Paradise.” I said: “Should I go and ask the Prophet ﷺ?” He said: “Go.” So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of God, Muadh b. Jabal told me that you said: ‘Whoever bears witness that there is no god but God sincerely will enter Paradise.’” He said: “Muadh spoke the truth, Muadh spoke the truth, Muadh spoke the truth.”"],[17204,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, with nothing between me and him but the rear frame of the saddle, when he said to me: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God, and at your command.” He said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed God’s right upon His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he rode on for a while and said: “O Muadh b. Jabal.” I said: “At your service and at your command.” He said: “Do you know what the servants’ right upon God is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed the servants’ right upon God is that He not punish them.”"],[17205,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service.” He said: “Give the people the glad tidings that whoever says, ‘There is no god but God,’ will enter Paradise.”"],[17206,"I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ when he said: “O Muadh b. Jabal, do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That they associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what their right upon Him is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That He not punish them.”"],[17207,"You heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ seated me behind him and said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know, if they do that, what their right upon Him is? Their right upon Him is that He not punish them.”"],[17210,"Relate to us some of the rare hadiths of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I was riding behind the Messenger of God ﷺ on a donkey when he said: “O Muadh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God.” He said: “Do you know what God’s right upon His servants is?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, the right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what the servants’ right upon God is if they do that?” I said: “God and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Indeed, their right upon God, if they do that, is that He not punish them.”"],[17212,"Muadh b. Jabal seized the devil during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I came to him and said: “I have heard that you seized the devil during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: “Yes. The Messenger of God ﷺ handed over to me the dates of the zakat, and I put them in a room of mine. I would find a shortfall in them every day, so I complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He told me: ‘It is the work of the devil, so lie in wait for him.’ I lay in wait for him one night. When a portion of the night had passed, he came in the form of an elephant. When he reached the door, he slipped in through the crack of the door in a form other than his own. He approached the dates and began gobbling them. I tightened my clothes around me, then I grabbed him around the middle, and I said: ‘I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. O enemy of God, you have gotten at the dates of the zakat and taken them, while they are more entitled to them than you. I will certainly bring you before the Messenger of God ﷺ so that he will expose you.’ He made a pact with me that he would not return. In the morning I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to me: ‘What happened to your captive?’ I said: ‘He made a pact with me that he would not return.’ He said: ‘He will return, so lie in wait for him.’ So I lay in wait for him the second night. He did the same as before, and I did the same as before, and he made a pact with me that he would not return, so I let him go. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ to inform him, and there was his caller calling out: ‘Where is Muadh?’ He said to me: ‘O Muadh, what happened to your captive?’ I told him, and he said: ‘He will return, so lie in wait for him.’ So I lay in wait for him the third night. He did the same as before, and I did the same to him, and I said: ‘O enemy of God, you made a pact with me twice, and this is the third time. I will certainly bring you before the Messenger of God so that he will expose you.’ He said: ‘I am a devil with dependents, and I only came to you from Nasibin. If I could find something other than this, I would not have come to you. We used to be in this city of yours until your companion was sent. When two verses were sent down upon him that drove us out of it, we settled in Nasibin. They are not recited in any house except that the devil does not enter it for three days. If you let me go, I will teach them to you.’ I said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘The Throne Verse and the end of Surat al-Baqarah, from His saying, “The Messenger has believed in what was sent down to him,” to the end of it.’ So I let him go. Then I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ to inform him, and there was his caller calling out: ‘Where is Muadh b. Jabal?’ When I entered upon him, he said to me: ‘What happened to your captive?’ I said: ‘He made a pact with me that he would not return,’ and I told him what he had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: ‘The wicked one spoke the truth, though he is a liar.’ He said: So after that I would recite those two verses over it and would not find any shortfall in it."],[17213,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband because of his right over her. No woman will find the sweetness of faith until she fulfills her husband’s right, even if he asks her for herself while she is on a camel saddle.”"],[17214,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, this matter began as mercy and prophethood, then it will become mercy and caliphate, then it will become rule that is biting, then it will become oppressive rule, then it will become corruption on the earth. They will approve of silk, adultery, and alcohol, and they will be provided for in these matters until they meet Allah.\""],[17215,"We heard the Messenger of Allahﷺ saying, \"Verily, this matter [Islam] began as mercy and prophecy, then it will be caliphate and mercy, then it will become a biting monarchy and forcefulness, and then corruption on the earth, where they indulge in adultery, silk, and alcohol and are victorious in that. They will continue to be provided for until they meet Allah, the Blessed and Exalted.\""],[17216,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said to him: “Any man who apostatizes from Islam, call him; if he repents, accept it from him, and if he does not repent, strike his neck. And any woman who apostatizes from Islam, call her; if she repents, accept it from her, and if she refuses, seek her repentance.”"],[17217,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, may He be exalted, has given you as charity a third of your wealth at your death, as an increase for you in your lives, so that He may make it purification for your deeds.”"],[17218,"He used to perform ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a cup patched with brass and give him drink in it."],[17219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The head of this matter is Islam; whoever submits is safe. Its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its hump is jihad; none attains it except the best of them.”"],[17220,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for patience.” He said: “You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Him for well-being.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Possessor of majesty and honor.” He said: “Your supplication has been answered.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing.” He said: “Do you know what the completion of blessing is?” He replied: “A supplication I made, hoping for good.” He said: “Part of the completion of blessing is seeking refuge from the Fire and entering Paradise.”"],[17221,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for patience.” He said: “You have asked Allah for affliction, so ask Allah for well-being.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Possessor of majesty and honor.” He said: “Your supplication has been answered, so ask.” He passed by a man who was saying: “O Allah, I ask You for the completion of Your blessing.” He said: “Son of Adam, do you know what the completion of blessing is?” He replied: “A supplication I made, hoping for good through it.” He said: “The completion of blessing is entering Paradise and deliverance from the Fire.”"],[17224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ during the expedition of Tabuk."],[17225,"He informed him that they went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Tabuk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together. He said: One day he delayed the prayer, then came out and prayed Zuhr and ‘Asr together, then entered, then came out and prayed Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together. Then he said: “Tomorrow, if Allah wills, you will come to the spring of Tabuk. You will reach it at mid-morning, so whoever reaches it must not touch any of its water until I come.” He said: We arrived, and two men had already reached it before us. The spring was like a sandal strap, trickling with a little water. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked them: “Did you touch any of its water?” They said: Yes. He rebuked them and said to them whatever Allah willed him to say. Then they scooped a little water from the spring with their hands until it collected in something, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ washed his face and hands in it, then poured it back into the spring. The spring then flowed with abundant water and the people drew water. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Soon, O Mu‘adh, if you live long enough, you will see this place filled with jinn.” This is what al-Dabarī said, and he erred; it is only “filled with gardens.”"],[17226,"I heard Mu‘adh b. Jabal say: “We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk. He would not set out until the heat had abated, then he would combine Zuhr and ‘Asr. Then when evening came, he would stop and combine Maghrib and ‘Isha’.”"],[17227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ during the expedition of Tabuk until we returned."],[17228,"We went out with the Prophet ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and he used to pray Zuhr and ‘Asr together and Maghrib and ‘Isha’ together."],[17229,"The Prophet ﷺ went on the expedition of Tabuk in intense heat, and he combined Zuhr and ‘Asr and Maghrib and ‘Isha’."],[17230,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' during the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[17231,"\"The Prophet ﷺ combined Zuhr and 'Asr, and Maghrib and 'Isha' during the expedition of Tabuk.\""],[17232,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and he seated me behind him. I touched nothing softer than the skin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did I find a scent more fragrant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"O Mu'adh, have you heard any sound since last night?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"A messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever of my Ummah dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not go out to the people and give them glad tidings?\" He said, \"Leave them; let them race for the straight path.\""],[17233,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took my hand one day and said, \"O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you.\" Mu'adh said to him, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, and I, by Allah, love you.\" He said, \"I enjoin you, O Mu'adh, never to omit saying after every prayer: 'O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.'\" Mu'adh enjoined this upon al-Sunabihi, al-Sunabihi enjoined it upon Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman enjoined it upon 'Uqbah b. Muslim."],[17234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four matters: about his life and how he spent it, about his youth and how he wore it out, about his wealth and from where he acquired it and on what he spent it, and about his knowledge and what he did with it.\""],[17235,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Three things, whoever does them has committed a crime: whoever raises a banner unjustly, or disobeys his parents, or walks with an oppressor—he has committed a crime. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: {Surely We will exact retribution from the criminals}.\""],[17236,"\"Relate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you have not forgotten and that has not become confused for you.\" He said, \"Seat me.\" So some of the people took his hand and some sat behind him. Then he said, \"I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I have not forgotten and that has not become confused for me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no prophet who did not warn his people about the Dajjal, and I warn you about the matter of the Dajjal: he is one-eyed, and my Lord is not one-eyed. Between his eyes is written 'kafir,' which the literate and the illiterate will read. With him are a Paradise and a Fire, but his Fire is a Paradise and his Paradise is a Fire.'\""],[17237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not permissible for a woman to allow anyone into her husband's house without his permission, and she should not leave the house when he dislikes it. She should not abandon her husband's bed, even if he is more unjust than she is. She should not forsake him, even if he is oppressing her, until she goes to him and apologizes. If he accepts her apology, then Allah accepts her apology."],[17239,"O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stuck out his tongue, then placed his finger on it. Mu'adh was appalled and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for all that we say and will it be recorded against us?\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck Mu'adh's shoulder several times and said, \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O son of the mother of Mu'adh! Do people topple onto their faces in the Fire of Hell except because of the harvests of their tongues?\""],[17240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nothing weighs an servant's scale like a riding animal on which he spends in the cause of Allah or carries others on it in the cause of Allah.\""],[17241,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The people of Paradise will enter Paradise hairless, beardless, with kohl-lined eyes, at the age of thirty-three.\""],[17242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever says when he finishes the morning prayer, before speaking: “There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise; in His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,” ten times, will be given for them seven [rewards]. Ten good deeds will be written for him, ten evil deeds will be erased from him, ten degrees will be raised for him, and they will be for him equal to freeing ten slaves. They will be a protection for him from Satan and a shield from what is disliked, and no sin will overtake him that day except associating partners with Allah. And whoever says them when he finishes the sunset prayer will be given the like of that for a third of it."],[17243,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves beauty, and I love to be praised,” as if he feared for himself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What prevents you from loving to live praiseworthy and die missed? I was only sent to perfect the beauties of character.”"],[17244,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever seeks knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, or to argue with the foolish in gatherings, will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.”"],[17245,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise if I do it.” He said: “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: you establish the obligatory prayer, you pay the prescribed zakah, and you do not associate anything with Allah.”"],[17246,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The Milky Way in the sky is the sweat of the serpent beneath the Throne.”"],[17247,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to send Muadh to Yemen, he consulted some of his companions, among them Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Usayd b. Hudayr. He consulted them, and Abu Bakr said: “Were it not that you consulted us, we would not have spoken.” He said: “In matters about which nothing has been revealed to me, I am like one of you.” Then the people spoke, each one speaking according to his own opinion. He said: “What do you think, O Muadh?” He said: “I think what Abu Bakr said.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah, exalted is He, hates, above His heaven, that Abu Bakr ؓ should err.”"],[17248,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform ablution once, twice, and three times—three times; he used to do all of that."],[17249,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform tayammum with clean earth, and I never saw him wipe his hands and face except once."],[17250,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe his face with the edge of his garment during ablution."],[17251,"The Prophet ﷺ recited it: “Can your Lord [cause a table spread to descend]?”"],[17252,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Khaybar, and we captured sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed a portion of them among us, and that sufficed us, and he placed the rest in the spoils of war."],[17253,"The Prophet ﷺ used to urge his companions to engage in single combat."],[17254,"Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ divided among us the livestock of Khaybar, and some remnants of it remained, so he sold them and put their price into the shares."],[17255,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was skinning a sheep, and he said to me, “O Mu'adh, bring it here or show me,” then he pushed it twice between the flesh and the skin, then said, “O Mu'adh, like this,” then he went on to the prayer."],[17256,"Whichever part of the day you wish: if you wish, in the morning, and if you wish, in the evening. I said, 'But the people dislike it in the evening.' He said, 'And why?' I said, 'They say that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The change in the breath of the fasting person is more fragrant with God than the scent of musk.\"' He said, 'Glory be to God! The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded them to use the tooth-stick when he commanded them, while he knew that there must be some change in the mouth of the fasting person even if he uses the tooth-stick. He was not one to command them to deliberately make their mouths foul. There is no good in that at all; rather, there is evil in it, except for one who is afflicted with an affliction he cannot avoid.' I said, 'And dust in the path of God is likewise? Only the one forced to it and who finds no way around it is rewarded?' He said, 'Yes. As for one who throws himself into affliction deliberately, he has no reward from that.'"],[17257,"The Messenger of God ﷺ only commanded ablution from that which fire has changed by washing the hands and mouth for cleanliness, and it is not obligatory."],[17258,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A pregnant woman, if she kills intentionally, is not to be killed until she gives birth to the child in her womb and until she is provided for; and if she commits adultery, she is not to be stoned until she gives birth to the child in her womb and until she is provided for.\""],[17259,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ: he said, \"Whoever recites the Qur'an and acts according to what is in it and dies in the community, God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the noble scribes and the judges. Whoever recites the Qur'an while it slips away from him and he does not abandon it, he will have his reward twice. Whoever is eager for it, cannot do it, and does not abandon it, God will raise him on the Day of Resurrection with the nobles of his people, and they will be given superiority over all creatures as eagles are given superiority over other birds, and as a spring in a meadow is preferred over what surrounds it. Then a caller will call out, 'Where are those whom tending livestock did not distract from reciting My Book?' They will stand, and each of them will be clothed with the crown of honor and given victory in his right hand and eternity in his left. If his parents were Muslims, they will be clothed with a garment better than the world and what is in it, and they will say, 'How is this for us?' It will be said, 'Because of what your child used to recite of the Qur'an.'\""],[17260,"While we were riding with the Prophet ﷺ, his mount went ahead, then my mount caught up with his until I thought his mount recognized the tread of my mount, until my knee bumped his knee. I said, 'O Messenger of God, I have wanted to ask you many times, but I am prevented by this verse: {O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if they are shown to you, will distress you}.' He said, 'What is it, O Mu'adh?' I said, 'The deed that admits to Paradise and keeps me away from the Fire.' He said, 'You have asked about a great thing, and yet it is easy: the testimony that there is no god but God and that I am the Messenger of God, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan.' Then he said, 'Shall I inform you of the head of this matter, its pillar, and its peak? Jihad.' Then he said, 'Fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sins.' Then he said, 'Shall I tell you what gives people mastery over all that?' He took hold of his tongue and placed it between two of his fingers. I said, 'O Messenger of God, will everything we say be recorded against us?' He said, 'May your mother be bereaved of you! Do people ever fall on their faces in the Fire except because of what their tongues reap? You remain safe as long as you are silent, but when you speak, it is written either for you or against you.'"],[17261,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A person will be with the one he loves.\""],[17262,"When the Prophet ﷺ was in his prayer, he would raise his hands opposite his ears, and when he said the takbir he would lower them, then he would pause. Sometimes I saw him place his right hand over his left. When he finished the Opening of the Book, he would pause; when he finished the surah, he would pause; then he would raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir, and bow. We would not bow until we saw him bowing. Then he would stand upright from his bowing until every limb returned to its place. Then he would raise his hands opposite his ears, say the takbir, and fall into prostration. He would make his forehead and nose touch the ground. Then he would rise as if he were an arrow, not leaning on his hands. When he sat in the last part of his prayer, he would lean on his left thigh, his right hand on his right thigh, and point with his finger when he supplicated. When he said the salam, he would quickly stand up.\""],[17263,"The Messenger of God ﷺ rode a donkey of his called Ya'fur, whose halter was made of palm fiber. He said, 'Ride, O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Go on, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Ride.' So he mounted me behind him, and the donkey threw us down. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up laughing. Then he mounted a second time and said, 'Ride,' and I rode. The donkey carried us as far as God willed. He said: he reached back with his hand and struck my back with a whip or a stick that he had, and said, 'O Mu'adh b. Umm Mu'adh, do you know what right God has over people?' I said, 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'God's right over His servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.' Then he rode on as far as God willed, then he reached back with his hand and struck my back, and said, 'O Mu'adh b. Umm Mu'adh, do you know what right the servants have over God if they do that?' I said, 'God and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'The right of the servants over God is that He will admit them to Paradise if they do that.'"],[17264,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ, he set out on the expedition to Tabuk and traveled by night one night, and we traveled by night with him. Then he prayed the morning prayer and we prayed with him, then he went on in the morning and we went with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ rode on, and the groups and camels dispersed, eating as they went, and he was wearing a Najrani cloak. My eye caught the ring of the Messenger of God's she-camel while he was asleep, and I thought it would fall off. While I was like that, my she-camel let out a cry that broke it, and its hoof twisted, and the she-camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ was startled by its striking, and the Prophet ﷺ woke up. He turned and saw me, and said, 'O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of God.' He said, 'Come closer.' I came closer, and he said that three times, and I came closer until the two mounts were side by side. Mu'adh said to himself, 'There is a word in my mind that has taken hold of me and made me ill; I have not asked you about it, and I have not heard anyone ask you about it.' He said, 'Ask me, O Mu'adh.' I said, 'Tell me, O Messenger of God, about a deed that will admit me to Paradise.' He said, 'Excellent, excellent! You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy: you testify that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, establish prayer, give zakat, and worship God alone.'"],[17265,"That he should give the people their stipends and raid with them. While he was giving the people — and that was at the end of time — a man from the people of the countryside came and said, 'O Mu'adh, order my stipend for me, for I am a man from the people of the countryside from such-and-such a place, so perhaps I may reach my family before nightfall.' He said, 'No, by Allah, I will not give you until I give these,' meaning the people of Madinah. 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"All the prophets will enter Paradise forty years before Sulayman b. Dawud, and the poor of the Muslims will enter Paradise forty years before their rich, and the righteous slaves will enter Paradise forty years before the others, and the people of cities will enter Paradise forty years before the people of the countryside because of the virtue of the cities, the congregations, the Friday prayers, and the circles of remembrance. And when a trial occurs, they are singled out for it rather than them.\"'"],[17266,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Glad tidings to the one who increases in remembrance of Allah during jihad in the path of Allah, for for every word there are seventy thousand good deeds, each good deed tenfold, along with what he has with Allah of increase.\" It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about spending?' He said, \"Spending is according to the measure of that.\" 'Abd al-Rahman said: I said to Mu'adh, 'Spending is only seven hundredfold.' Mu'adh said, \"Your understanding is little. That is only when they spend while residing with their families, not on a raid. When they raid and spend, Allah stores for them from the treasury of His mercy what the knowledge of servants and their description cannot comprehend. Those are the party of Allah, and the party of Allah are the victorious.\""],[17267,"I said to Mu'adh, 'I love you and I love your speech.' He said, 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah's majesty will be in the shade of Allah's Throne on the Day of Resurrection, when there is no shade except His shade.\"'"],[17268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Those who love one another for Allah will be in His shade on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[17269,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah's glory will be in the shade of the throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[17270,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of the Throne.\""],[17271,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be in the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[17272,"\"And by Allah, do you love me?\" I said. \"By Allah, indeed I love you for the sake of Allah,\" he said. He replied, \"Rejoice, for I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will be shaded by His throne on the day when there will be no shade except His shade.'\""],[17273,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Abu Hazim b. Dinar, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani that he said: I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a young man with bright front teeth, long of silence, and the people were with him; when they differed about something they referred it to him and issued from his opinion. I asked about him and was told, 'Mu'adh b. Jabal.' The next day I went early and found that he had preceded me in going early, and I found him praying. I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him from in front and greeted him and said, 'By Allah, I love you for Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said, 'By Allah?' I said, 'By Allah.' He said: Then he took hold of the knot of my cloak and pulled me to him and said, 'Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah said, \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another for My sake, and those who sit together for My sake, and those who give to one another for My sake, and those who visit one another for My sake.\"'"],[17274,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade.\""],[17275,"I entered the mosque of Hims and there were men narrating hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, among them a young man with dark, wide eyes and bright front teeth. When he spoke, the people all listened to his speech, and when they disputed about something they accepted his word. He was Mu'adh b. Jabal. We sat with him and I said, 'I love you.' He took hold of my clothing and pulled me to him until my knee touched his knee, then said, 'Shall I give you glad tidings from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who narrates it from Allah ﷻ? He said: \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another, sit together, visit one another, and give to one another for My sake.\"'"],[17276,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who narrates from Allah ﷻ, he said: \"My love has become incumbent for those who love one another, sit together, and give to one another for My sake.\""],[17277,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Those who love one another for Allah are in the shade of Allah's Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. People will be terrified and they will not be terrified, and people will fear and they will not fear.\" He said: Then I got up from him and went to 'Ubadah b. al-Samit. 'Ubadah said, 'And better than it: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"My love has become due for those who love one another for My sake, and My love has become due for those who sit together for My sake, and My love has become due for those who visit one another for My sake.\"'"],[17278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah brighten a servant who hears my words and does not add to them, for many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more receptive than him.\""],[17279,"O Messenger of God, teach me a deed which, if I do it, I will enter Paradise? He said: \"Do not associate anything with God, even if you are burned; obey your parents, even if they expel you from your property; do not drink wine, for it is the key to every evil; do not ever abandon the prayer deliberately, for whoever abandons the prayer deliberately, God's protection is removed from him; do not dispute authority with its people, even if you think you have a right; spend on your family according to your means, and do not lift the stick from them; make them fear God; do not steal from the spoils; do not flee from battle.\""],[17280,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The first thing my Lord forbade me after the worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men.\""],[17281,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: On the Day of Resurrection, the one deprived of intellect, the one who perished in the interval between prophets, and the one who perished as a child will be brought. The one deprived of intellect will say: \"O Lord, if You had given me intellect, no one to whom You gave intellect would have been more fortunate with his intellect than me.\" The one who perished as a child will say: \"O Lord, if You had given me a lifespan, no one to whom You gave a lifespan would have been more fortunate with his lifespan than me.\" The one who perished in the interval will say: \"O Lord, if a messenger from You had come to me, no human to whom a covenant from You came would have been more fortunate with Your covenant than me.\" Then the Lord, Exalted is He, will say: \"I command you with a command; will you obey Me?\" They will say: \"Yes, by Your might, O Lord.\" He will say: \"Go and enter Hellfire.\" If they were to enter it, it would not have harmed them at all. Then tongues of fire will emerge upon them, and they will think that it has destroyed everything God created. Then He will command them a second time, and they will return as before. Then the Lord, may He be glorified, will say: \"I created you with My knowledge, and to My knowledge you will return.\" Then the Fire will take them."],[17282,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Shall I inform you about the kings of the people of Paradise?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Every weak and oppressed person with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid; if he were to swear by God, God would fulfill his oath.\""],[17283,"The Messenger of God ﷺ one day mentioned the trials, magnifying them and emphasizing their severity. Ali b. Abi Talib said: \"O Messenger of God, what is the way out of them?\" He said: \"The Book of God. In it is the account of those before you, the news of those after you, and the judgment of what is between you. Whoever abandons it out of arrogance, God will crush him. Whoever seeks guidance in other than it, God will lead him astray. It is the firm rope of God, the wise reminder, and the straight path. It is the one about which, when the jinn heard it, they said: {Indeed, we have heard a wondrous Quran.} It is the one with which tongues do not differ, and much repetition does not wear it out.\""],[17284,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, whoever believes in me, testifies to my truthfulness, and bears witness that what I have brought is the truth, then make his wealth and children few and hasten his taking to You. And whoever does not believe in me, does not testify to my truthfulness, and does not know that what I have brought is the truth from You, then make his wealth and children abundant and prolong his life.\""],[17285,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever feeds a believer until he satisfies him from hunger, God will admit him through a gate of Paradise that no one will enter except one like him.\""],[17286,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Verily, Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient person. Whoever meets God having broken his pledge of allegiance will meet Him while maimed. Whoever deliberately departs from the community by a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck. Whoever dies without there being an imam of the community over him to whom obedience is due dies a death of ignorance.\""],[17287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The banner of the treacherous one on the Day of Resurrection will be raised near his buttocks.\""],[17288,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I was shown that I was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and I balanced it. Then Abu Bakr was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and he balanced it. Then Umar was placed in a scale and my community in the other, and he balanced it. Then Uthman was placed in a scale, and he balanced it. Then the scale was raised.\""],[17289,"Twelve, and she left their father in their house; the youngest of them was one whose beard had fully grown. She stood up and greeted Mu'adh while two men from her sons held her upper arms. She said: \"Who sent you, O man?\" Mu'adh said to her: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me.\" The woman said: \"The Messenger of God sent you, and you are the messenger of the Messenger of God? Will you not tell me, O messenger of the Messenger of God, what is the right of a husband over his wife?\" Mu'adh said: \"She should fear God as much as she can, and she should listen and obey.\" She said: \"I adjure you to tell me what is the right of a husband over his wife.\" Mu'adh said to her: \"Are you not satisfied to listen and obey and fear God?\" She said: \"Yes, but I left the father of these as an old man in the house.\" Mu'adh said: \"By the One in Whose hand is Mu'adh's soul, if you were to return to him and find that leprosy had torn his flesh and pierced his nostrils, and you found his nostrils flowing with pus and blood, then you placed them in your mouth in order to fulfill his right, you would never fulfill it.\""],[17290,"I came to the mosque of Damascus and there was a group of companions of Muhammad ﷺ , and among them was a young man with intense black eyes and a radiant face. Whenever they disagreed about something, they would refer it to the young man. So, I asked my companion, \"Who is this?\" He said, \"This is Mu'adh ibn Jabal.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be upon pulpits of light, under the shade of the Throne of the Most Merciful on a day when there is no shade except His shade.'\""],[17291,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Those who love each other for the sake of Allah will be in the shade of the Throne on a day when there is no shade except His shade. They will be on pulpits of light and will be envied by the Prophets and the truthful (Siddeeqeen).\""],[17292,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The things I fear most for my community are three: a man who recites the Book of God until you see splendor upon him, and he has been granted the cloak of Islam by God, then he draws his sword and strikes his neighbor with it, accusing him of polytheism.\" It was said: \"O Messenger of God, is the one who accuses more deserving of it or the one accused?\" He said: \"The one who accuses. And a man to whom God grants authority, so he says: 'Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God.' He lies. It is not for a caliph to be a shield apart from the Creator. And a man whom stories make light-headed; every time he finishes one tale, he tells a longer one. If he reaches the Dajjal, he will follow him.\""],[17293,"We raided with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and we captured some sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ distributed a portion of them among us and placed the remainder in the spoils."],[17294,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen and said: “Perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave. I have sent you to a people whose hearts are tender; they fight for the truth. Fight with those of them who obey you against those who disobey you. Then they will return to Islam, until a woman hastens to her husband, a child to his parent, and a brother to his brother. So alight between the two tribes, al-Sakūn and al-Sakāsik.”"],[17295,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Take the stipend as long as it is a stipend. But when it becomes bribery in religion, do not take it. You will not abandon it; poverty and need will prevent you. Indeed, the millstone of Islam is turning, so turn with the Book wherever it turns. Indeed, the Book and the ruling authority will separate, so do not part with the Book. Indeed, there will be rulers over you who decide for themselves what they do not decide for you. If you disobey them, they will kill you, and if you obey them, they will lead you astray.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what should we do?” He said, “As the companions of Jesus son of Mary did: they were sawn with saws and carried on wood. Death in obedience to God is better than life in disobedience to God.”"],[17296,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjāl will occur within seven months.”"],[17297,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjāl will occur within seven months.”"],[17299,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: “R aiding is of two kinds. As for one who raids seeking the countenance of God, obeying the imam, spending generously, sharing with his companion, and avoiding corruption in the land, then his sleeping and his waking are entirely good. As for one who raids out of pride, show, and reputation, disobeying the imam, and spreading corruption in the land, he will not return even with his basic needs.”"],[17300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the Night of Decree. He said, \"It is in the last ten nights, on the seventh, or the fifth, or the third.\""],[17301,"He said, “By God?” twice or three times. I said, “By God.” Then he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘My love or my mercy is assured for those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, visit one another for My sake, and give generously to one another for My sake.’”"],[17302,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Seek refuge in God from greed that leads to avarice, from greed for what is not to be desired, and from greed for what cannot be desired.”"],[17303,"The Prophet ﷺ underwent cupping while fasting."],[17304,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Which deed is most beloved to God Almighty?” He said: “That you die with your tongue moist from the remembrance of God.”"],[17305,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people of Paradise will not regret anything except an hour that passed them in which they did not remember God.”"],[17306,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Seek help in fulfilling needs through concealment, for every possessor of a blessing is envied.”"],[17307,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ who said: “Do you know what God will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they will say?” They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “He will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection: Did you love to meet Me?” They will say: Yes, O Lord, we hoped for Your pardon and Your forgiveness. He said: “Then I have made My pardon and My forgiveness binding for you.”"],[17308,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever eats or drinks or kills game and forgets to mention God’s name, let him eat from it as long as he did not deliberately omit the naming.”"],[17309,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about hoarding, what it is. He said: “When he hears of reduced prices it grieves him, and when he hears of high prices he rejoices at it. What an evil servant is the hoarder: if God lowers prices he is sad, and if God raises them he rejoices.”"],[17310,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If my community knew what benefit it has in fenugreek, they would buy it even for its weight in gold.”"],[17311,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever walks to a person of innovation to honor him has helped in the demolition of Islam.”"],[17312,"Abu Abdullah, a man from al-Anbar, narrated to us, from Thawr b. Yazid, from Khalid b. Ma‘dan, from Mu‘adh b. Jabal, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about borrowing dough and bread. He said: “Glory be to God! This is only among noble character traits: take the small and give the large, or take the large and give the small. The best of you is the one who is best in repayment.”"],[17313,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “O people, adopt fear of God as a trade: provision will come to you without capital or commerce.” Then he recited {And whoever fears God, He will make for him a way out and provide for him from where he does not expect}."],[17314,"The Messenger of God ﷺ attended the marriage contract of a man among his companions and said to him: “Upon goodness and harmony, a blessed bird, and abundance in provision. May God bless you all. Play the tambourine over his head.” A tambourine was brought and struck, and trays bearing fruit and sugar were brought and scattered over him. The people withheld their hands, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “What is the matter with you that you do not snatch?” They said: O Messenger of God, did you not forbid snatching? He said: “I only forbade you from snatching from military expeditions; as for wedding feasts, no.” He said: Then he pulled it away from them and they pulled it away from him."],[17315,"The Prophet ﷺ was in our house displaying horses. ‘Uyaynah b. Hisn entered upon him and said to the Prophet ﷺ: You know more about horses than I, and I know more about men than you. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Which men are best?” He replied: Men who carry their swords on their shoulders, display their lances on the withers of their horses, and wear striped cloaks from the people of Najd. The Prophet ﷺ said: “You have lied. The best of men are the men of Yemen; faith is Yemeni. The largest tribe in Paradise is Madhhij, and the people consumed by Himyar are better than their consumers; Hadramawt is better than Kindah. May God curse the four kings: Jamd, Mishrah, Mikhwas, and Abda‘a, and their sister al-‘Amarradah.”"],[17316,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to perform ablution with water as long as it has not become stagnant, turning green or yellow.”"],[17317,"And concerning prayer in a single garment, and what is lawful for a man from his menstruating wife? Mu‘adh said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about that, and he said: “When the two circumcised parts meet, the major ablution becomes obligatory. As for prayer in a single garment, wrap it around yourself. As for what is lawful from a menstruating woman, what is above the waist-wrapper is lawful, but abstaining from that is better.”"],[17318,"You asked me about what I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “The major ablution is obligatory after major ritual impurity.”"],[17319,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever ties the jizyah around his neck has disowned what Muhammad ﷺ brought.”"],[17320,"I answered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Leave me, for I will not return. So he let him go. When he went to the Prophet ﷺ the next morning, he said: “O Mu‘ādh, what did your captive do?” He said: I released him. On the second night, he sensed him and seized him. He again pleaded with him and swore that he would not return, so he let him go. On the third night, he sensed him, seized him, and again he pleaded and swore that he would not return, but he refused to release him. He said: Let me go and I will teach you a verse that, if you recite it, we will not approach that place. He taught him the Verse of the Throne, so he let him go. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning and told him what had happened, and he said: “He spoke the truth, though he is a liar.”"],[17321,"I heard Abū Shaybah say: Mu‘ādh was walking with a man, and he lifted a stone from the road and said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lifts a stone from the road, a good deed is written for him, and whoever has a good deed will enter Paradise.”"],[17322,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found him standing in prayer. He remained standing until morning, then he prostrated a prostration in which I thought his soul had been taken. He looked at me and said: “O Mu‘ādh, did you see?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, yes, I saw you prostrate a prostration in which I thought your soul had been taken. He said: “Do you know why?\" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I prayed as much as my Lord decreed, and my Lord came to me and said: O Muhammad, what shall I do with your ummah? I said: My Lord, You know best. He repeated it three or four times, and the last time He said: What shall I do with your ummah? I said: You know best, O Lord. He said: I will not grieve you over your ummah. So I prostrated to my Lord and your Lord, thankful, for He loves the thankful.”"],[17323,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit its doer into Paradise. He said: “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one whom Allah makes it easy. Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayers, pay the obligatory zakāh, fast Ramadān, and perform Hajj to the House. I will tell you the head of this matter, its pillar, and its peak. The head is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, its pillar is prayer, and its peak is jihād. I will tell you the gates of goodness: fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and a servant’s prayer in the middle of the night.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “Their sides forsake their beds” [Q 32:16]. “I will tell you what is more controlling than all of that.” He shook his mount, and I drew near to the people, then I drew near to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is more controlling than all of that? He gestured with his hand to his tongue. I said: The tongue? As if I was careless about it. He said: “May your mother bereave you, O Mu‘ādh b. Jabal! Will people be thrown into the Fire of Hell on their faces except by the harvest of their tongues?”"],[17324,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Caution will not avail against destiny, but supplication benefits against what has descended and what has not descended. So hold fast to supplication, O servants of Allah.”"],[17325,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If a nobleman of a people comes to you, honor him.”"],[17326,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.” The interval between two milkings is the time it takes to milk her for the one who milks her."],[17327,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah, a Muslim man, for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. If he is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come with the color of saffron and the fragrance of musk. Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah bears the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come with the color of saffron and the fragrance of musk. Whoever is wounded in the way of Allah bears the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks for martyrdom sincerely from himself, then dies or is killed, has the reward of a martyr. Whoever is wounded or suffers an injury in the way of Allah, on the Day of Resurrection it will come at its fullest, its color like saffron and its fragrance like musk.”"],[17330,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever fights in the way of Allah for the interval between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom sincerely from his heart in the way of Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Whoever is wounded with a wound in the way of Allah or suffers an injury, on the Day of Resurrection it will come at its fullest, its color like saffron and its fragrance like musk. Whoever departs with wounds in the way of Allah is sealed with the seal of the martyrs.”"],[17331,"The last words with which I parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were that I said: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: \"That you die while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[17332,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No soul dies while having with Allah the weight of an ant of good except that it is sealed over with clay.\""],[17333,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"It is not lawful for a woman to give permission in her husband's house while he is unwilling, nor to go out while he is unwilling, nor to obey anyone in that matter, nor to be harsh with him, nor to forsake his bed, nor to strike him—even if he is more unjust than her—until she pleases him. If he is pleased and accepts from her, then with her it is good; Allah accepted her excuse and made her face fair, and there is no sin upon her. But if he refuses to be pleased with her, then she has indeed conveyed her excuse.\""],[17335,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: \"That you die while your tongue is moist with the remembrance of Allah.\""],[17337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The building of Bayt al-Maqdis is the ruin of Yathrib; the ruin of Yathrib is the coming of the great battle; the coming of the great battle is the conquest of Constantinople; and the conquest of Constantinople is the emergence of the Dajjal.\""],[17338,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah, may He be exalted, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban and forgives all His creation except for a polytheist or one who harbors enmity.\""],[17339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delayed the dawn prayer with us until the sun almost rose. When he had prayed the dawn prayer with us, he said: \"Last night I prayed what was decreed for me, then I laid my side in the mosque. My Lord came to me in the most beautiful form and said: O Muhammad, do you know what the highest assembly disputes about? I said: No, my Lord. He said it three times. I said: No, my Lord. Then He placed His hand between my shoulders, and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and everything was revealed to me and I knew it. I said: About ranks and expiations. He said: What are the ranks? I said: Feeding food, spreading peace, and praying while people are asleep. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: What are the expiations? I said: Performing ablution thoroughly in extreme cold, waiting for prayer after prayer, and walking to the Friday prayers. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: Ask, O Muhammad. I said: O Allah, I ask You for the doing of good deeds, the abandonment of evil deeds, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. And when You intend a trial among Your servants, take me to You without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You and the love of deeds that bring me near to Your love.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Learn these words and study them, for they are true.\""],[17340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise, a house in the middle of Paradise, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for one who abandons disputation even if he is right, abandons lying even in jest, and has good character.\""],[17341,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand and said: \"Indeed I love you, O Mu'adh.\" He said: I said: \"And I, by Allah, love you, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"I enjoin upon you words that you should say after every prayer: My Lord, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\""],[17342,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, returning that to a certainty in the heart, will enter Paradise.\""],[17343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen months after coming to Madinah. Then Allah revealed a verse commanding him to turn to the Ka'bah. He said: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven} (the verse)."],[17344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever's last words are 'There is no god but Allah' will enter Paradise.\""],[17345,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not keep looking at those afflicted with leprosy.”"],[17346,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Say: He is God, the One (Qul Huwa Allāhu Aḥad) is equivalent to one-third of the Qur’an.”"],[17347,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “No woman harms her husband in this world but that his wife from the ḥūr al-ʿīn will say: ‘Do not harm him, may God destroy you! He is only a guest with you, soon to part from you to us.’”"],[17348,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “You will alight at a place called al-Jābiyah or al-Jūbiyyah, where a disease like the gland of a camel will afflict you. Through it God will cause your souls and your offspring to be martyred, and He will purify your deeds by it.”"],[17349,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the most hateful of creation to God ﷻ is one who believed and then disbelieved.”"],[17350,"There will be trials in which wealth becomes abundant and the Qur’an is spread open, so that a man, a woman, the young, the old, the believer, and the hypocrite all read it. Yet he reads it and is not followed; so he says: ‘By God, I will definitely read it openly,’ but he is still not followed. Then he heads to a mosque and innovates speech that is not from the Book of God nor from the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance. Beware of it, for it is an innovation of misguidance.”"],[17351,"“What makes you weep?” I said: “By God, I am not weeping over any worldly thing I might obtain from you, nor over any kinship between me and you, but I weep over what I used to hear from you; it is now departing.” He said: “Do not weep. Knowledge and faith—their affair is that whoever seeks them finds them. Seek knowledge where Ibrāhīm sought it, for he asked God and was not forgetful. And after me, seek it from four men; if you do not find it with them, then search among the people. Seek knowledge from ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, Abū al-Dardāʾ, Salmān, and ʿAbdullāh b. Salām. And beware of the deviation of the wise man, for Satan casts misguided wisdom upon the tongue of a wise man. Take knowledge when it comes to you.” He said: “I said to Muʿādh b. Jabal: ‘How can I know the deviation of the wise man and the judgment of the hypocrite?’ He said: ‘Indeed, truth is light.’ And beware of making hasty judgments in matters. Some men among the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ said one day: ‘Our sons are better than us; they were born upon Islam and did not associate partners, whereas we had associated partners.’ That reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: ‘We are better than our sons, and our sons are better than their sons, and our sons’ sons are better than their sons’ sons.’”"],[17352,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Indeed, he is the tenth of ten.”"],[17353,"He said concerning the plague: “A mercy from your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.”"],[17354,"The plague struck Syria, so Muʿādh stood and addressed them in Ḥimṣ, saying: “Indeed, this plague is a mercy from your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.”"],[17355,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has never sent a prophet but that among his nation were Qadariyyah and Murjiʾah, who confuse his nation’s affair for him. Indeed, God ﷻ has cursed the Qadariyyah and the Murjiʾah on the tongue of seventy prophets.”"],[17356,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Muʿādh b. Jabal: “Whoever abandons the prayer deliberately has indeed been absolved of God’s protection.”"],[17357,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O Mu‘adh b. Jabal, whoever abandons the prayer has indeed absolved himself of the protection.”"],[17358,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no Muslim who sleeps upon the remembrance of Allah in a state of purity, then awakens during the night and asks Allah for good of this world and the Hereafter except that He grants it to him.” Musa b. Isma‘il added: Hammad said: Abu Zabyah passed by us and narrated to us from Mu‘adh from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[17359,"That the Prophet ﷺ saw a man wearing a cloak of silk, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “A collar of fire.”"],[17360,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “There is no servant who stands in this world in a position of reputation-seeking and showing-off except that Allah will make him heard of on the heads of the creation on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17361,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Abdullah b. Salam is the tenth of ten who are in Paradise.”"],[17362,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the Isha prayer, and he delayed it for us until someone said: \"He has prayed and did not come out, and few people said that he will come out.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, \"Take this prayer as a means of darkness, for you have been given preference with it over the rest of the nations, and no one before you has prayed it.\""],[17363,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the ‘Isha prayer one night, and he delayed it until one might think that he had already prayed and was not going to come out. Then he came out afterward, and a person said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I thought that you had prayed and were not going to come out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Delay this prayer (i.e., pray it later into the night), for you have been favored with it over all other nations, and no one before you prayed it.”"],[17364,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with him, advising him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward Madinah and said: “Indeed these people of my household think that they are the closest of people to me, but it is not so. My allies among you are the God-fearing, whoever they may be and wherever they may be. O Allah, I do not permit for them the corruption of what You have set right. By Allah, my nation will be overturned from its religion just as a vessel is overturned in the wide watercourse.”"],[17365,"That when he sent him to Yemen, he went out with him advising him, while Mu‘adh was riding and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking beneath his mount. When he finished, he said: “O Mu‘adh, it may be that you will not meet me after this year of mine, and perhaps you will pass by my mosque and my grave.” Mu‘adh b. Jabal wept out of grief at the separation from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Do not weep, O Mu‘adh, for weeping is from Satan.”"],[17366,"“Indeed this matter is the mercy of your Lord, the call of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you. O Allah, grant the family of Mu‘adh their share of this matter.”"],[17367,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Jerusalem, that a man will be given a thousand dinars and be dissatisfied with them, a tribulation whose heat will enter the house of every Muslim, a death that will seize people like the sheep-pox, and that we will raid the Romans and they will march with twelve banners, under each banner twelve thousand.”"],[17368,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ on a red camel. He said: “Mu‘adh.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you know what is the right of Allah upon the servants?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “His right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.” Then he said: “Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?” I said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “Their right upon Him is that He admits them to Paradise.”"],[17369,"I was traveling with the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a donkey called Ya‘fur."],[17370,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Avoid the three things that provoke curses: defecating in water sources, in the middle of the road, and in the shade."],[17371,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he used to avoid urine and commanded his companions to do so. Mu'adh said: The majority of the punishment of the grave is from urine. Ibn Abi Maryam said concerning the hadith of 'Abdullah b. Hurayth."],[17372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to collect zakat from the people of Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every thirty, a tabi' (one-year-old male calf); from every forty, a musinnah (two-year-old female); from sixty, two tabi's; from seventy, a musinnah and a tabi'; from eighty, two musinnahs; from ninety, three tabi's; from one hundred, a musinnah and two tabi's; from one hundred and twenty, three musinnahs or four tabi's. And he commanded me not to take anything below that until it reaches a musinnah or a jadha'ah (a one-year-old sheep or goat). He said: 'The awqas (young animals below the zakat threshold) have no obligatory due.' Awqas means the young ones."],[17373,"The Messenger of Allah took my hand and said, \"Verily, I love you, O Mu'adh. Do not forget to say in every prayer: 'O Allah, help me to remember You, to be grateful to You, and to worship You excellently'. Ibn Lahiah As-Sunabihi is not mentioned.\""],[17374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you wish, I will tell you the first thing Allah ﷻ will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection. He will say: 'Did you love to meet Me?' They will say: 'Yes, our Lord.' He will say: 'Why?' They will say: 'We hoped for Your mercy and Your pardon.' He will say: 'My mercy has become binding for you.'"],[17375,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen. He led them in the dawn prayer and recited Surah al-Nisa'. When he reached {And Allah took Ibrahim as an intimate friend} (Quran 4:125), a woman said: 'The eye of Ibrahim's mother has been delighted.'"],[17377,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon people is?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'His right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. Do you know, O Mu'adh, what people's right upon Allah is if they do that? That He will not punish them.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give the people glad tidings?' He said: 'Leave them; let them act.'"],[17378,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ when he said: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is and what the servants' right upon Allah is? Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. The servants' right upon Allah is that He will not punish anyone who dies without associating anything with Him.'"],[17379,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a donkey called 'Ufayr when he said to me: 'O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is? That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. And the servants' right upon Allah is that He will not punish anyone who does not associate anything with Him.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give the people glad tidings?' He said: 'Do not give them glad tidings, lest they rely on that alone.'"],[17381,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for everything we say?' He said: 'May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh b. Jabal! Will people be thrown into Hellfire on their faces for anything other than the harvests of their tongues?'"],[17382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. When I had set out, he sent after me and I returned. He said: 'Do you know why I sent for you? Do not take anything without knowledge, for it is misappropriation. Whoever misappropriates will bring what he misappropriated on the Day of Resurrection. This is why I called you back; now go on with your task.'"],[17383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen and commanded him to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' (one-year-old male) or tabi'ah (one-year-old female), from every forty a musinnah (two-year-old female), and from every adult person one dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments."],[17384,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every forty a musinnah, and from every thirty a tabi' or tabi'ah, and from every adult person one dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afiri garments."],[17385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from every drachma or equivalent a certain amount, and he commanded me to take from every thirty cows a sale, and from every forty sheep a sheep known for its age, and he commanded me to take from watered land a tenth or its equivalent, and from dry land half of its tenth."],[17386,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him, when he sent him to Yemen, to take from every thirty cattle a tabi' (one-year-old male or female) and from every forty a musinnah (two-year-old cow), and from every person who has reached puberty a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir garments."],[17388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen and commanded me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi' or tabi'ah—that is, a jadha' (one-year-old)—and from every forty a musinnah, and from every person who has reached puberty a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir garments."],[17390,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When one of you comes to prayer while the imam is in a certain state, let him do as the imam does.”"],[17393,"Prayer was transformed through three stages, and fasting was transformed through three stages. As for the stages of prayer: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis (Jerusalem) for seventeen months. Then Allah revealed: {We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven, and We will surely turn you to a qiblah with which you will be pleased} (2:144). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned toward the Ka'bah. This was one stage. They used to gather for prayer and call one another to it until they struck the bell or nearly did so. Then a man called 'Abdullah b. Zayd came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, if I were to tell you that while I was between sleep and wakefulness, I saw a figure wearing two green garments standing and facing the qiblah, saying, ‘Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar’ until he finished the adhan, repeating each phrase twice. Then at the end of his adhan he said, ‘Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, la ilaha illa Allah.’ Then he paused for a while, then stood and said the same as he had said, except that he added, ‘Qad qamat al-salah.’” He said, “Teach it to Bilal.” So Bilal was the first to call the adhan with it. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, something like what came to 'Abdullah b. Zayd came around me, except that he preceded me to you.” These are two stages. People used to come to prayer after the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed part of it, and they would signal to them with their fingers how many rak'ahs he had prayed: one, two. Then Mu'adh came after the Prophet ﷺ had already prayed part of the prayer, and he entered the prayer. He said, “I will not find him in any state except that I am in it, then I will make up what I missed.” He came after part of the prayer had been missed and entered the prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, Mu'adh stood up to make up what he had missed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Mu'adh has set a precedent for you, so do likewise.” These are the three stages. As for the stages of fasting: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and began fasting three days every month. He fasted 'Ashura and fasted for seventeen months from Rabi' to Rabi' to the month of Ramadan. Then Allah ﷻ made the month of Ramadan obligatory upon him and revealed to him: {Fasting is prescribed for you} up to His saying: {a ransom of feeding a poor person} (2:183-184). So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished fed a poor person instead, and that sufficed him. Then Allah established fasting for the resident healthy person and granted a concession for the sick and the traveler, and fixed the feeding for the elderly person who cannot fast. And He revealed to him: {The month of Ramadan in which was revealed the Qur'an, a guidance for the people and clear proofs of guidance and criterion. So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it} (2:185). They used to eat, drink, and approach their wives as long as they had not slept. When they slept, they refrained from that. Then a man called Sirmah spent his day fasting while working. He came to his family and slept before breaking his fast. In the morning he was still fasting. The Prophet ﷺ saw him late in the day and he was extremely exhausted. He said, “Why do I see you exhausted?” He said, “I worked yesterday, then I came and slept before breaking my fast.” Then 'Umar came after having approached his wife after sleeping, and he mentioned that to him. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {It has been made permissible for you the night preceding fasting to go to your wives} (2:187) to the end of the verse."],[17394,"We used to come to prayer, and when a man came after having missed part of the prayer, the one next to him would signal to him how much he had missed, and he would make it up. So we were among those bowing, prostrating, standing, and sitting. One day I came after having missed part of the prayer, and I was signaled what I had missed. I said, “I will not find him in any state except that I am in it.” So I was in the same state as I found them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, I stood up and prayed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the people and said, “Who said such and such?” They said, “Mu'adh b. Jabal.” He said, “Mu'adh has set a precedent for you, so follow him. When one of you comes after having missed part of the prayer, let him pray with the imam what remains, and when the imam finishes, let him make up what he missed.”"],[17395,"People at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when one of them missed part of the prayer, would ask and they would signal to him how much he had missed, so he would pray what he had missed and then enter with them in their prayer. Mu'adh came while the people were sitting in their prayer, so he sat with them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, he stood and made up what he had missed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do as Mu'adh b. Jabal did.”"],[17396,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “His right upon them is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what their right upon Him is if they do that?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Their right upon Him is that He will not punish them.”"],[17397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was on a donkey, and he said, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is and what the servants' right upon Allah is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him, and the servants' right upon Allah is that if they do that, He will not punish them.”"],[17398,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said, “O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon the servants is?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Indeed, Allah's right upon the servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what the servants' right is if they do that?” I said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “That He will not punish them.”"],[17400,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who meets a woman he does not know, and he does not do anything with her except talk?\" So Allah revealed the verse, \"Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to the man, \"Perform ablution and then pray.\" Mu'adh said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is this command specific to him or is it for all believers in general?\" The Prophet ﷺ said three times, \"No, it is for all believers in general.\""],[17401,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man has been afflicted by a woman whom it is not permissible for him to have relations with. He has not left anything that can afflict him from his wife except that it has afflicted him, except that he has not had intercourse with her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Perform ablution well, then stand and pray.\" Then Allah revealed this verse {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night. Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.} Mu'adh then asked, \"Is this for him specifically, O Messenger of Allah, or for all Muslims in general?\" He said, \"For all Muslims in general.\""],[17402,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations. When he finished the prayer, we said, 'O Messenger of God, you performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations?' He said, 'It was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to set over my community an enemy from other than them who would uproot them, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to destroy them with a drought year, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, but He withheld that from me.'"],[17403,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations. When he finished, I said, 'O Messenger of God, you performed a prayer and lengthened its standing, its bowing, and its prostrations.' He said, 'It was a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord in it for three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to set over my community an enemy from other than them who would uproot them, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set over them a drought year that would destroy them with hunger, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make their violence among themselves, but He withheld that from me and kept it away from me.'"],[17405,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Among the things I fear most for my community are three: the slip of a scholar, the disputation of a hypocrite using the Quran, and a worldly life that is opened up for you.'"],[17406,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'The virtue of the congregational prayer over the prayer of a man alone is twenty-five.'"],[17407,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'Two men among the Children of Israel traced their lineages in the time of Moses ﷺ , one of them a Muslim and the other a polytheist. The polytheist traced his lineage and said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so,\" until he counted nine forefathers. Then he said to his companion, \"Trace your lineage, may you have no mother.\" He said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and I disavow whoever is beyond that.\" Then Moses called out among the people and gathered them, then said, \"Judgment has been given between you two. As for you, who traced your lineage to nine forefathers, you will be the tenth of them in the Fire. As for the one who traced his lineage to his two parents, you are a man of the people of Islam.\"'"],[17408,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Two men among the Children of Israel traced their lineages, one of them a Muslim and the other a disbeliever. The disbeliever said, \"Trace your lineage.\" The disbeliever traced his lineage to nine forefathers, and the Muslim said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, and I disavow whoever is above them.\" Then the caller of Moses ﷺ went out: \"O you two who traced your lineages, I have judged between you. As for you, O disbeliever, you traced your lineage to nine forefathers, so you are the tenth of them in the Fire. As for you, O Muslim, you limited yourself to two Muslim parents, so you are from the people of Islam and are disavowed of whoever is besides them.\"'"],[17409,"Two men exchanged insults in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and there were two men with him. One of them became angry until he began to writhe because of anger. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, would remove what is in him of anger.' I drew near to him and said, 'O Prophet of God, what is it, O Prophet?' I wanted to know [the word for] anger. I drew near to him and said, 'O Prophet of God, what is it, O Prophet of God?' I wanted to know whether it was specific to him or general for the believers. He said, 'O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed.' I drew near to the man and said it to him, but he did not say it, and he only increased in anger."],[17410,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became severely angry. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, God would remove from him what he feels.' It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'What is it?' He said, 'O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan the accursed.'"],[17411,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became angry. He said, 'I know a word that, if he said it, his anger would go away: I seek refuge in God from Satan the accursed.'"],[17412,"Two men exchanged insults in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became severely angry, until I imagined that his nose was writhing. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'I know a word that, if this angry man said it, God would remove it from him: I seek refuge in God from Satan the accursed.'"],[17413,"The Prophet ﷺ was delayed from the dawn prayer with us until the sun was almost upon us. Then he came out and prayed with us, and he made his prayer brief. Then he turned away and faced us and said, 'Stay in your places. Let me inform you what delayed me from you today in this prayer. In this night of mine I prayed as much as God willed, then sleep overcame my eyes and I slept. I saw my Lord, exalted is He, in the best and most beautiful form. He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"I do not know, O Lord.\" Then He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"I do not know.\" He placed His palm between my shoulders, and I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breasts, and I came to know everything and perceived it. Then He said, \"O Muhammad.\" I said, \"At Your service, O Lord.\" He said, \"What does the highest assembly dispute about?\" I said, \"About expiations.\" He said, \"What are they?\" I said, \"Walking on foot to the Friday prayers, completing ablution in the cold, and degrees.\" He said, \"What are those?\" I said, \"Feeding food, gentle speech, and praying at night while people sleep.\" He said, \"Ask.\" I said, \"O God, I ask You for good deeds, abandonment of evil acts, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. When You intend a trial among Your creation, save me to You without being tried. I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and the love of an action that brings me near to Your love.\"'"],[17415,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise and keep me far from the Fire.\" He said, \"You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy: that you worship God and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan. And if you wish, I will tell you of the gates of goodness.\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a man's standing in the depths of the night seeking the face of God.\" He said: Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds}."],[17418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"You must have good character, for the best of people in character are the best of them in religion.\""],[17419,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are, and follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it, and treat people with good character.\""],[17420,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it, and treat people with good character.\""],[17421,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me.\" He said, \"Fear God wherever you are.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Follow up a bad deed with a good deed that will erase it.\" I said, \"Tell me more.\" He said, \"Treat people with good character.\""],[17422,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslims who lose three children but that God will admit their parents to Paradise through the abundance of His mercy.\" They said, \"And two, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And two.\" They said, \"And one, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And one.\" Then he narrated that \"the miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[17423,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There are no two Muslim spouses who lose three children but that God will admit their parents to Paradise through the abundance of His mercy.\" I said, \"What do you think if they are two?\" He said, \"And two.\" I said, \"What do you think if it is one?\" He said, \"And one.\" Then he said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord to Paradise when she seeks reward for it.\""],[17425,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The one with three is assured.\" Mu'adh b. Jabal said, \"And two, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"And the one with two.\""],[17426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “There are no two Muslim parents who lose three children in Islam before they reach maturity except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.” Mu'adh said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, and two?” He said, “And two.” I said, “And one?” He said, “And one, to the point that a miscarried fetus will drag its mother by its umbilical cord if she seeks reward for it.”"],[17427,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me to Paradise.” He said, “Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, and pay the obligatory zakah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Shall I not guide you to the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; whoever submits is safe. As for its pillar, it is prayer. As for the peak of its hump, it is jihad in the way of Allah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a servant’s standing in the depths of the night.” Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds} (Q 32:16). “Shall I not inform you of what is more controlling than all that?” Then a rider or riders approached, and I thought they would distract the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from me, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Shall I not guide you to what is more controlling than all of that?” He pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we say?” He said, “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh! Do people get thrown into the Fire on their faces except by the harvests of their tongues?”"],[17429,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking him, and it was said to me, “He has gone out.” I went on, and no one I passed but said, “He passed by a while ago.” I found him standing in prayer. When he finished his prayer, I said, “You have prayed a long prayer.” He said, “I prayed with hope and fear. I asked Allah for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to give dominance over them to an enemy from outside them, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make their harm among themselves, and He refused it to me.”"],[17430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed a prayer one day and prolonged it. When he finished, I said, “O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the prayer today.” He said, “I prayed a prayer of hope and fear. I asked Allah three things for my ummah, and He granted me two and refused one. I asked that no enemy from other than them be given power over them, and He granted it to me. I asked that He not destroy them by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked that He not make their harm among themselves, and He refused it to me.”"],[17431,"Umar was indeed among the people of Paradise. Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in wakefulness or sleep is true. He said, “While I was in Paradise, I saw therein a dwelling and said, ‘For whom is this?’ It was said, ‘For Umar b. al-Khattab.’”"],[17433,"“By Allah, Umar is in Paradise,” and I would not love to have red camels in exchange for what I said, but you dispersed before I could tell you why I said that. Then he told them: “The dream that the Prophet ﷺ saw concerning Umar.” He said, “And the dream of the Prophet ﷺ is true.”"],[17434,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, to whom should I give from the surplus of what Allah has bestowed upon me?” He said, “Begin with your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest and the nearest. And do not forget the neighbors and the one in need.”"],[17435,"“The Quran was sent down from seven gates upon seven letters, all of them healing and sufficient.”"],[17436,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take from date palms, wheat, barley, and raisins (or he said, from grapes)."],[17437,"“The Prophet ﷺ imposed the tithe on what the sky watered, on what was watered by springs, and on what springs irrigated among grains. As for melons, cucumbers, vegetables, greens, pomegranates, and sugarcane, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has pardoned them.”"],[17438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever grows a single gray hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever shoots an arrow in the way of Allah, a degree will be raised for him by it.”"],[17439,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever is placed in charge of any affair of the Muslims and hides himself from the weak among the Muslims, Allah will hide Himself from him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17440,"I was sitting beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said to me, \"O Mu'adh, do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?\" I replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"To worship Him alone and not associate anything with Him.\" Then he said, \"O Mu'adh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?\" I replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He will not punish them.\""],[17441,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a donkey. He said to me, \"O Mu'adh b. Jabal, what is the right of Allah upon His servants?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.\" Then he said to me, \"O Mu'adh, what is the right of the servants upon Allah if they do that?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That He will not punish them.\""],[17442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Mu'adh, do you know what the right of Allah upon His servants is?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him. Do you know what the right of the servants upon Allah is if they do that? That He will not punish them.\""],[17444,"'Umar b. al-Khattab went out to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Mu'adh b. Jabal weeping at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"What makes you weep, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"Something I heard from the occupant of this grave makes me weep.\" He said, \"And what is it?\" He said, \"I heard him say: 'A small amount of showing off is polytheism. Whoever shows enmity to the friends of Allah has declared war on Allah. Allah loves the hidden, pious ones who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, they are not invited or recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance, emerging from every dusty, dark place.'\""],[17446,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed him on Friday. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished praying, he came to Mu‘adh and said to him, “O Mu‘adh, why did I not see you?” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, a Jew has against me an uqiyyah of gold, so I set out to come to you, but he detained me from you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O Mu‘adh, shall I not teach you a supplication with which you may supplicate? Even if you had a debt like Mount Ṣabir, Allah would discharge it for you—and Ṣabir is a mountain in Yemen. So supplicate with it, O Mu‘adh. Say: allāhumma mālika al-mulk, tuʾtī al-mulka man tashāʾu wa-tanziʿu al-mulka mimman tashāʾ, wa-tuʿizzu man tashāʾu wa-tudhillu man tashāʾ, bi-yadika al-khayr, innaka ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr. tūliju al-layla fī al-nahār wa-tūliju al-nahāra fī al-layl, wa-tukhriju al-ḥayya mina al-mayyit wa-tukhriju al-mayyita mina al-ḥayy, wa-tarzuqu man tashāʾu bi-ghayri ḥisāb. raḥmāna al-dunyā wa-l-ākhirah wa-raḥīmahuma, tuʿṭī man tashāʾu minhumā wa-tamnaʿu man tashāʾu, irḥamnī raḥmatan tughniynī bihā ʿan raḥmati man siwāk (O Allah, Owner of sovereignty: You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty from whom You will; You honor whom You will and You abase whom You will. In Your hand is all good; indeed You are over all things competent. You cause the night to enter into the day and You cause the day to enter into the night; You bring forth the living from the dead and You bring forth the dead from the living; and You provide for whom You will without account [Al Imran 3:26-27]. O Most Merciful of this world and the Hereafter, and their Most Compassionate: You give to whom You will of them and You withhold from whom You will. Have mercy on me with a mercy by which You will make me independent of the mercy of anyone besides You.”)"],[17447,"'Amr b. Bakr b. Bakkar al-Qa'nabi narrated to me: Mujashi' b. 'Amr b. Hassan al-Asadi narrated to us: al-Layth b. Sa'd narrated to us from 'Asim b. 'Umar b. Qatada, from Mahmud b. Labid, from Mu'adh b. Jabal that a son of his died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to him consoling him for his son. He wrote to him: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah, besides whom there is no god, to you. To proceed: May Allah make your reward great, inspire you with patience, and grant us and you gratitude. For our souls, our wealth, and our families are among Allah's pleasant gifts and His deposited trusts. He lets us enjoy them until a term and takes them back at a known time. We ask Him for gratitude for what He gives and patience when He tests. Your son was among Allah's pleasant gifts and His deposited trusts. Allah let you enjoy him in happiness and joy, and took him from you with a great reward: prayer, mercy, and guidance, if you seek recompense. So be patient, and do not let your anguish nullify your reward, lest you regret. Know that anguish does not bring back the dead nor repel grief. What is to come is as if it has already happened. Peace.\""],[17448,"He used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then come to his people and pray with them."],[17449,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Where are the foremost?\" They said, \"Some people have gone ahead and some have stayed behind.\" He said, \"Where are the foremost who are engrossed in the remembrance of Allah? Whoever loves to graze in the meadows of Paradise, let him remember Allah often.\" The wording is that of the hadith of 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Aban."],[17450,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs these five prayers and fasts the month of Ramadan — I do not know whether he mentioned the zakah of his wealth or not — it is a right upon Allah to forgive him, whether he emigrates or stays where his mother gave birth to him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I go out and announce it to the people?\" He said, \"No, leave the people to act, for Paradise has one hundred levels; between each two levels is like what is between heaven and earth, and the highest of them is al-Firdaws.\""],[17453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishes prayer, gives zakah, and fasts Ramadan, it is a right upon Allah to forgive him.\" Then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Hisham b. Sa'd."],[17454,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me.\" He said, \"You must fear Allah as much as you can. Remember Allah at every stone and tree. Whatever evil you have done, offer repentance to Allah for it: the secret by secret, and the open by open.\""],[17455,"A man had a claim against me, and I feared him. So I stayed home and remained for two days without going out. Then I went out and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “O Muʿādh, what kept you back?” I said: A man had a right over me; I feared him until I became ashamed, and I disliked that he should meet me. He said: “Shall I not instruct you in some words you can say—if you have debts like mountains, Allah will pay them off for you?” I said: Yes. He said: \"Say: (O Allah, Owner of Sovereignty, You give sovereignty to whom You will and You take sovereignty away from whom You will,’ up to His saying, ‘without reckoning,’ to the end, [Al Imran 3:26-27] Merciful of this world and the Hereafter and Compassionate to them both; You grant of them to whom You will and You withhold of them from whom You will. O Allah, enrich me so that I have no need of poverty, pay off my debt for me, and cause me to die in Your service and in striving in Your path.)\""],[17456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If a woman knew the right of her husband, she would not sit down as long as his lunch and dinner are present until he finishes.\""],[17457,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Two phrases, one of which has no barrier before the Throne, and the other fills what is between heaven and earth: 'There is no god but Allah' and 'Allah is the Greatest.'\" Ibn 'Umar said to Ibn Abi 'Amra, \"Did you hear him say that?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar wept until his beard was dyed with his tears.\" Then he said, \"They are two phrases that we hold onto and love.\""],[17458,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to some Arab villages and ordered me to take the land’s share.” Al-Ashjaʿī said, “meaning the third and the fourth.”"],[17459,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed me over the alms of the Muslims, and I placed it in an upper room.” Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[17460,"Muʿādh was in Yemen, and they brought up to him the case of a Jew who died and left a Muslim brother. Muʿādh said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease,’ so he made him inherit.”"],[17461,"A man among us died a Jew or a Christian and left a Muslim son. That was brought to Muʿādh’s attention, and he made the son inherit. He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease.’”"],[17462,"And he said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Islam increases and does not decrease.’” The shaykh said, “ʿAmr b. Kurdī is ʿAmr b. Abī Ḥakīm, from whom Shuʿbah narrated.”"],[17463,"“on my right side since I became Muslim.”"],[17464,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I shall place my intercession for those who die without associating anything with God.”"],[17465,"From Muʿādh b. Jabal: When the Prophet ﷺ traveled, the Emigrants used to be nearest to him. One night we missed him from his place, and we feared something had happened to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so we went looking for him. We found a sound like the rumbling of a mill, and we met him returning. I said, “We missed you, O Messenger of God, and feared something had happened to you.” He said, “No, but a messenger came to me from my Lord and gave me the choice between admitting half of my community to Paradise or intercession, and I chose intercession.” We said, “We ask you by the right of Islam and the right of our companionship that you make us among them.” He said, “Then you are among them.” Then two men came and said the same, and he said to them, “Yes.” Then another came, until the people were numerous, and he said, “I shall place in my intercession whoever of my community dies without associating anything with God.”"],[17466,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Satan is the wolf of man, like the wolf of sheep, seizing the stray and isolated one. Beware of the ravines; keep to the main body, the congregation, and the mosques.”"],[17467,"The Prophet of God ﷺ used to say, “Satan is the wolf of man, like the wolf of sheep, seizing the stray, the outlying, and the remote sheep.”"],[17469,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ did not say anything to me about the shortfalls of cattle.”"],[17470,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “There is no divorce over what one does not possess, and no manumission over what one does not possess.”"],[17472,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is no divorce for what one does not own, and no freeing for one who does not own.”"],[17473,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “No human being has performed a deed more saving for him from God’s punishment than the remembrance of God.” They said: Not even jihad in the path of God? He said: “Not even, unless you strike with your sword until it breaks,” three times."],[17474,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Do not hasten the affliction before it descends, and draw near and be steadfast; for if you hasten it before it descends, the flood will surely sweep you away here and here.”"],[17475,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If I adopt a pulpit, my forefather Abraham adopted it; and if I adopt the staff, my forefather Abraham ﷺ adopted it.”"],[17476,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If slavery were to remain upon anyone of the Arabs, it would today be only captivity or ransom.”"],[17477,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “There is nothing due on shortfalls.”"],[17478,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever equips a warrior or looks after his family with good, he is with us.”"],[17479,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Indeed, men who are neither prophets nor martyrs will have pulpits of light placed for them on the Day of Resurrection, their faces being light, and they will be safe on the Day of Resurrection from the greatest terror.” A man said: O Prophet of God, who are those? He said: “They are those who separate from their tribes, loving one another for God.”"],[17480,"So narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ that we may benefit from. He said: Yes, and what hour of lying is this? I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever dies while certain of three things—that God is true, that the Hour is coming, and that God will resurrect those in the graves—. And Ibn Sīrīn said: I forgot whether he said “enters Paradise” or “is saved from the Fire.”"],[17481,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah, Paradise becomes guaranteed for him.\""],[17482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, between the edge of the Fire and its bottom there is a rock whose weight equals seven pregnant camels with their fat, their flesh, and their offspring. It falls into it from the edge of the Fire until it reaches its bottom over seventy autumns.\""],[17483,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him to Yemen, he said to him: \"How will you judge if a case comes to you?\" He said: \"I will judge by the Book of Allah.\" He said: \"And if it is not in the Book of Allah?\" He said: \"Then by the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"And if it is not in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"I will exert my own judgment and spare no effort.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck his chest and said: \"Praise be to Allah Who has guided the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to that which pleases the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[17484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me as a zakat collector to the people of Yemen and ordered me to take from cattle: from every thirty a tabi' — the tabi' being a one-year-old — or a tabi'ah, and from every forty a musinnah. He said: They proposed that I take what is between forty and fifty, between sixty and seventy, and between eighty and ninety; but I refused them and said to them: 'Until I ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that.' So I came and informed the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered me to take from every thirty a tabi', from forty a musinnah, from sixty two tabi'ahs, from seventy a musinnah and a tabi', from eighty two musinnahs, from ninety three tabi's, from one hundred a musinnah and two tabi's, from one hundred and ten two musinnahs and a tabi', and from one hundred and twenty three musinnahs or four tabi's. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me not to take anything from what falls between those numbers until it reaches a musinnah or a jadha'. He also asserted that the awqas (gaps between the specified numbers) have no obligatory zakat."],[17485,"The people said: 'O Mu'adh, supplicate to Allah to lift this punishment from us.' He said: 'It is not a punishment, but it is the call of your Prophet and the death of the righteous before you, and a martyrdom by which Allah singles out whomever He wills among you.'"],[17486,"When death came to him, he wept. They said: 'What makes you weep?' He said: 'By Allah, I do not weep out of fear of death, nor over a worldly life I leave behind me. But I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"They are only two handfuls: a handful in the Fire and a handful in Paradise, and I do not know in which of the two handfuls I will be.\"'"],[17487,"I witnessed al-Hasan at the time of his death while he was making his will. He said to the scribe: 'Write: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what al-Hasan testified. He testified that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, truthfully from his heart. Whoever testifies to this at his death truthfully will enter Paradise.' I heard that from Mu'adh b. Jabal; he enjoined it at his death, narrating it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[17488,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by the One Who sent you with the truth, something arises in my chest such that being a burnt coal is dearer to me than speaking of it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Praise be to Allah. Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of mine, but he is content with the trivial acts among your deeds.'"],[17489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Six are among the signs of the Hour: my death, the conquest of Jerusalem, a death that takes people like the quza' that afflicts sheep, a man being given a thousand dinars and being displeased with them, a tribulation whose fear enters the heart of every Muslim, and the Byzantines invading us and marching with eighty banners.'"],[17490,"From Makhul, who raised it to Mu'adh b. Jabal, and Mu'adh raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'Keep your children, your disputes, your legal penalties, your buying and your selling away from your mosques. Perfume them on the day of your gathering, and place your purification facilities at their doors.'"],[17491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Obey every ruler, pray behind every imam, and do not revile any of my Companions.'"],[17492,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah (There is no might nor power except with Allah).'"],[17493,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a camel with a packsaddle fastened on it. He said, “O Mu’adh.” I replied, “At your service, happily.” He said, “Do you know what is God’s right upon His servants?” I said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “God’s right upon them is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him.” Then he said, “Do you know what is the servants’ right upon God if they do that?” I said, “God and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Their right upon Him, if they do that, is that He forgives them and admits them to Paradise.”"],[17494,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I have come from a people who prostrate to one another. Should we not do that for you?” He said, “If I were to command a human being to prostrate to a human being, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands.”"],[17495,"Mu’adh b. Jabal said: I said, “O Messenger of God, give me counsel.” He said, “Worship God as though you see Him, count yourself among the dead, remember God ﷻ by every rock and every tree, and if you commit a bad deed, then perform beside it a good deed: the secret for the secret and the open for the open.” Then he said, “Shall I not tell you what gives a person most control over that?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He took hold of the tip of his tongue. I said, “O Messenger of God, it is as if he is taking it lightly.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “And does anything cast people upon their faces into the Fire except this?” And he took hold of the tip of his tongue."],[17496,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent him to Yemen. When he came to them, he said, “O people, I am the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ to you. He informs you that the return is to God: to a Garden or a Fire, eternal abiding and no death, and residence and no departure.”"],[17497,"From Ibn Ishaq in naming those who attended Badr: Mu’adh b. ’Afra’, and he is Mu’adh b. al-Harith b. Rifa’a b. Sawda’ b. Malik b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar. ’Afra’ is his mother, and she is the mother of ’Awf and Mu’awwidh. All of them attended Badr. ’Afra’ is the daughter of ’Ubayd b. Tha’laba b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[17498,"He was circumambulating the House, and he circumambulated after ’Asr and did not pray. A man from Quraysh said to him, “What prevents you from praying?” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid prayer after two prayers: after Subh until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17499,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “There is no prayer after two prayers: after the morning prayer until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17500,"From his grandfather Mu’adh, a man of Banu Taym, that he was circumambulating after ’Asr with Mu’adh b. ’Afra’ and did not pray. I said, “What prevented you from praying?” He said, “The Prophet ﷺ forbade prayer in two hours: after Subh until the sun rises, and after ’Asr until the sun sets.”"],[17501,"It is said: Yazid b. Hushaym b. al-Khazraj attended Badr, killed Abu Jahl, and ’Ikrima b. Abi Jahl cut off his hand. Then he lived until the time of ’Uthman ؓ."],[17502,"While I was standing in the ranks on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and left and found myself between two young boys of the Ansar, of recent teeth. I wished I were between stronger men than them. One of them nudged me and said, “Uncle, do you know Abu Jahl?” I said, “Yes, and what do you need with him, nephew?” He said, “I have been told that he insults the Messenger of God ﷺ. By Him in whose hand is my soul, if I see him, my blackness will not part from his blackness until the more hasty of us dies.” I marveled at that. Then the other nudged me and said the same to me. It was not long before I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people. I said to them, “This is your companion you ask about.” They rushed at him with their swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and told him. He said, “Which of you killed him?” Each of them said, “I killed him.” He said, “Did you wipe your swords?” They said, “No.” He looked at the two swords and said, “Both of you killed him.” He ruled his spoils for Mu’adh b. ’Amr b. al-Jamuh. They were Mu’adh b. ’Afra’ and Mu’adh b. ’Amr b. al-Jamuh."],[17503,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say in his sermon at al-Banawa or al-Nabawa near al-Ta’if: “You will soon know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire, or the best of you from the worst of you.” Nafi’ said, “I do not know except that he said, ‘the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire.’” A man said, “By what, O Messenger of God?” He said, “By good praise and bad praise. You are witnesses of one another.”"],[17504,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When you give names, make them express servitude.”"],[17505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting with the legs drawn up and wrapped in a cloth on Friday while the imam is delivering the khutbah."],[17506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting with the legs drawn up and wrapped in a cloth on Friday."],[17507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives up fine clothing while able to afford it, out of humility for Allah (Mighty and Majestic), Allah will call him before the heads of all creatures on the Day of Resurrection and let him choose from the garments of faith to wear whichever he wishes.\""],[17508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever gives up fine clothing out of humility while able to afford it, Allah will call him before the heads of all creatures on the Day of Resurrection and let him choose from the garments of Paradise to wear whichever he wishes.\""],[17510,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats food and says: 'Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it for me without any strength or power on my part,' Allah forgives his previous sins. And whoever puts on a garment and says: 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided it for me without any strength or power on my part,' Allah forgives his previous sins.\""],[17511,"A man came to a gathering in which the Prophet ﷺ was present and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum.\" He replied to his greeting and said: \"Ten good deeds.\" Then another came and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh.\" He said: \"Twenty.\" Then another came and said: \"Al-salām ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh wa barakātuh.\" He said: \"Forty.\" And he said: \"This is how the merit increases.\""],[17512,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah (Exalted is He) said: 'My servant does not remember Me within himself except that I remember him in an assembly of My angels, and he does not remember Me in an assembly except that I remember him in the highest company.'\""],[17515,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The utmost coarseness, disbelief, and hypocrisy belongs to one who hears Allah's caller calling to prayer and inviting to success but does not respond to him.\""],[17517,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Enough misery and failure for a believer is to hear the mu'adhdhin calling the iqamah for prayer and not respond to him.\""],[17518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites 'Qul huwa Allāhu aḥad' ten times, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\" ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: \"Then we should increase it, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah is more abundant and better.\""],[17520,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah will be recorded on the Day of Resurrection with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous—and how excellent are those as companions.\""],[17522,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the path of Allah, Allah will record him with the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous.\""],[17523,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever stands guard behind the Muslims in the path of God as a volunteer, not compelled by any authority, will not see the Fire with his own eyes except as the fulfillment of the oath, for God, exalted is He, says: {And there is none of you but will pass over it}.\""],[17525,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Remembrance surpasses spending in the path of God by a hundredfold.\""],[17526,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Remembrance in the path of God is multiplied above spending by seven hundredfold.\""],[17528,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that a man asked him: \"Which of the mujahidin has the greatest reward?\" He said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" He said: \"And which of the fasting people has the greatest reward with God?\" He said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" Then he mentioned prayer, zakat, Hajj, and charity, and in all of that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one of them who remembers God the most.\" Then Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to Umar ؓ: \"O Abu Hafs, those who remember God have gone away with every good.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed.\""],[17529,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"It is a duty upon one who leaves a gathering to greet them, and a duty upon one who comes to a gathering to greet.\" A man stood up while the Messenger of God ﷺ was speaking and did not greet, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"How quickly he forgot!\""],[17531,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever builds a building without wrongdoing or aggression, or plants a tree without wrongdoing or aggression, will have a continuous reward as long as anyone of God's creation ﷻ benefits from it.\""],[17532,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever builds a building without wrongdoing or aggression will have its reward as long as anyone of the Most Merciful's creation ﷻ benefits from it.\""],[17533,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever gives for God's sake, withholds for God's sake, loves for God's sake, and hates for God's sake has completed his faith.\""],[17534,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"The best of virtues is that you maintain ties with one who cuts you off, give to one who deprives you, and forgive one who insults you.\""],[17536,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he said: \"Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out will be called by God before the heads of all creatures and given the choice of any of the wide-eyed maidens he wishes. And whoever refrains from wearing fine clothes while able to do so out of humility for God ﷻ will be called by God before the heads of all creatures and given the choice of any of the robes of faith he wishes.\""],[17538,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out, God will let him choose any of the wide-eyed maidens on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever gives up a garment of beauty while able to wear it, God will clothe him with the cloak of faith. Whoever arranges the marriage of a servant of God, God will place the crown of sovereignty on his head.\""],[17539,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever steps over the Muslims on Friday has taken a bridge to Hell.\""],[17540,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he used to say: \"The one who laughs in the prayer, the one who turns around, and the one who cracks his fingers are all of one rank.\""],[17541,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The one who turns around in the prayer, the one who laughs, and the one who cracks his fingers are all of one rank.\""],[17542,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"That I should see off a warrior in the path of God and help him with an early morning departure or an evening departure is more beloved to me than the world and all that it contains.\""],[17544,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he commanded his companions to go on a military expedition. Then he saw a man who had stayed behind. The man said: \"Until I pray the noon prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then greet him and bid him farewell, and he may supplicate for me with a supplication that will be a precedence on the Day of Resurrection.\" So when the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed, the man came forward greeting him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Do you know by how much your companions have preceded you?\" He said: \"Yes, they have preceded me by their early morning departure yesterday and today.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, they have preceded you by a distance greater than what is between the two easts and the two wests in excellence.\""],[17546,"That he asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the best of faith. He said: \"The best of faith is that you love for the sake of God, hate for the sake of God, and set your tongue to work in the remembrance of God.\" He said: \"And what else, O Messenger of God?\" He said: \"And that you love for people what you love for yourself, hate for them what you hate for yourself, and that you say what is good or remain silent.\""],[17548,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: \"Shall I inform you why God named Abraham His intimate friend who fulfilled? Because he used to say every morning and every evening: 'Glory be to God when you enter the evening and when you rise in the morning,' until he completed the verse.\""],[17550,"On the authority of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that he used to say: \"The verse of glory: To God belongs praise, who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence.\""],[17551,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The verse of glory is: 'And say: Praise be to God, who has not taken a son, and has no partner in dominion, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence.'\""],[17552,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Mount these animals sound and dismount from them sound.\""],[17553,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a group of people who were standing on their mounts and riding beasts. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Mount them sound, dismount from them sound, and do not make them chairs for your conversations and gatherings. For perhaps a mounted beast is better than its rider and more remembering of God than him.\""],[17554,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever protects a believer from a hypocrite who backbites him, God will send an angel to protect his flesh on the Day of Resurrection from the fire of Hell. And whoever slanders a Muslim with something intending to disgrace him by it, God will detain him on the bridge of Hell until he comes out of what he said.\""],[17555,"I went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, the expedition of such and such. The people cramped the campsites and cut off the road. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent a caller who announced among the people: 'Whoever cramps a campsite or cuts off a road, there is no military expedition for him.'"],[17556,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he sent a caller to announce: “Whoever constricts a dwelling place or cuts off a road, there is no jihad for him.”"],[17557,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When you hear the muezzin repeating the call to prayer, say what he says.”"],[17558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are servants whom Allah will neither speak to, purify, nor look at on the Day of Judgment.\" They asked, \"Who are those, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Those who disrespect their parents, those who are desirous to be away from them, those who disown their children, and those who are ungrateful to the people who have shown them kindness and disassociate themselves from them.\""],[17559,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has servants whom He will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He purify them, and for them is a painful punishment.” It was said, “Who are they, O Messenger of God?” He said, “One who disavows his parents and turns away from them, one who disavows his child, and a man upon whom a people bestowed favor but he denied their favor and disavowed them.”"],[17560,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a military expedition, and a woman came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband goes out on this expedition, and I offer his prayers and fast according to his fasting, and I worship through his worship. So guide me to an action by which I can attain the same reward as him.\" He said, \"Can you stand in prayer continuously without sleeping, and fast without breaking your fast, and remember Allah without forgetting?\" She replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone who can do that?\" He said, \"Even if you were to be confined and tied, you would not be able to attain even a tenth of that.\""],[17561,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My husband has gone out as a warrior in the path of God, and I used to follow his prayer when he prayed and his actions. So tell me of a deed that will make me reach his deed until he returns.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “Can you stand without sitting, remember without slackening, and fast without breaking the fast until he returns?” She said, “I cannot do that, O Messenger of God.” He said, “By Him in whose hand is my soul, if you did that, you would not reach a tenth of his deed until he returns.”"],[17562,"On the authority of the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever sits in his place of prayer from the dawn prayer until he prays the forenoon prayer, he will only say what is good. His sins will be forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea.\" And the wording belongs to the Hadith of Rishdeen."],[17563,"It is reported from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Whoever recites the beginning of Surat al-Kahf and its end, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head; and whoever recites all of it, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head, from the earth to the sky.\""],[17564,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.”"],[17565,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever says ‘Glory be to God, the Magnificent’ a tree is planted for him in Paradise. And whoever recites the Qur’an, masters it, and acts upon what is in it, God will clothe his parents on the Day of Resurrection with a crown whose light is more beautiful than this moon.”"],[17566,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever teaches knowledge, for him is a reward as long as anyone acts upon it, without diminishing the reward of the one who acts.”"],[17567,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever is dutiful to his parents, blessedness be to him; God will increase his lifespan.”"],[17568,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ give the grandmother a sixth."],[17569,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no servant who is entrusted with a flock and is deceitful toward it except that he enters the Fire.”"],[17570,"I heard it said of these non-Arabs: “We were commanded that if one of us dropped a morsel, he should pick it up, remove whatever harm was on it, and eat it, and not leave it for Satan.”"],[17572,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If a morsel of any of you falls, let him remove any harm from it and eat it, and not leave it for the Shaytan.\""],[17573,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When a morsel of any of you falls, let him remove whatever harm is on it and eat it.”"],[17574,"Regarding the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was accepting the people’s pledge of allegiance: “He did not pledge them upon death; he pledged them upon not fleeing, and he used to shake hands with women from beneath the garment.”"],[17575,"He has a place of refuge. I shall surely narrate to you a hadith that I have not narrated to you: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no servant whom Allah has placed in charge of a flock and who dies while being dishonest to it, except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17576,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Any man whom Allah has placed in charge of a flock and who dies while being dishonest to it, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17577,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah will not place a servant in charge of a flock who dies while being dishonest to it, except that Allah has forbidden Paradise to him.”"],[17580,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The punishment of this community is the sword, and their appointed time is the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and bitter.”"],[17581,"“The Prophet ﷺ gave the grandmother one-sixth.”"],[17582,"Who knows the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the grandfather? Maʿqil b. Yasar said: “He ruled for him one-sixth.”"],[17583,"Who knows what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding the grandfather? Maʿqil b. Yasar said to him: “I do.” He said: “How much is for him?” He said: “One-sixth.” He said: “Who is with him?” He said: “I do not know.” He said: “May you not know.”"],[17584,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the grandfather one-sixth.”"],[17585,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of a grandfather among us for one-sixth.”"],[17586,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I take a goat to slaughter it and then I take pity on it.” He said: “If you take pity on it, Allah will take pity on you.”"],[17587,"From Al-Hasan regarding the saying of Allah, the Exalted: {So do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms}, he said: Ma'qil b. Yasar narrated to me that it was revealed concerning him. He said: I married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her, then left her until when her waiting period ended, he proposed to her. I said, 'I married you to her, prepared her trousseau for you, and honored you, yet you divorced her. Then you come to propose to her? No, by Allah, she will never return to you, ever.' He was a man of no harm, and she wanted to go back to him, so Allah revealed this verse. So I said, 'Now I will do it, O Messenger of Allah.' So I married her to him."],[17588,"From my right, and I gave her in marriage."],[17589,"So he narrated to him and asked him and was courteous to him. While they were thus, Ma'qil said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no governor who is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not sincerely advise those behind him but Allah will cast him into Hell on his face on the day when Allah gathers the first and the last.'"],[17590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Al-Madinah is my place of emigration and my resting place in the earth. It is a duty upon my ummah to honor my neighbors as long as they avoid major sins. Whoever among them does not do that, Allah will give him to drink from the pus of the people of Hell.' We said: 'O Abu Yasar, what is the pus of the people of Hell?' He said: 'The extract of the people of the Fire.'"],[17591,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Muslims protect each other, their blood is equal, and a believer is not killed for an unbeliever, nor is a person with a covenant killed within their covenant.\""],[17592,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever Allah places in charge of a flock and he dies while he is deceiving it, Allah will certainly forbid Paradise to him.'"],[17593,"'I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever is put in charge of a flock and does not surround them with sincere advice will not find the scent of Paradise, and indeed its scent can be detected from a distance of a hundred years' journey.' So Ibn Ziyad said: 'Would that you had told me this before now.' He said: 'Now, were it not for the state I am in, I would not have told you this.'"],[17594,"'Ma'qil, I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If I knew that I had any life left, I would not have told it to you. I heard him say: 'There is no servant whom Allah places in charge of a flock who dies on the day he dies while he is deceiving his flock but Allah will forbid Paradise to him.'' And the wording is that of 'Ali b. al-Ja'd."],[17595,"That she wished to return to him, but Ma'qil prevented her, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed concerning that: {And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms}."],[17596,"Ma'qil said: 'I do not think I will survive what I am in, but I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'And what is it?' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no one who is placed in charge of a flock and dies on the day he dies while he is deceiving it but he will not find the scent of Paradise,' or he said: 'he will be from the people of the Fire.' He said: 'Would that you had told me this hadith before this day?' He said: 'Were it not for what I am in, I would not have told you.'"],[17597,"That he married his sister to a man in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. She remained with him as long as she did, then he divorced her with a single divorce and did not take her back until the waiting period ended. Then he desired her and she desired him. He proposed to her along with the other suitors. So [Ma'qil] said to him: 'O you wretch! I honored you with her and married you to her, then you divorced her. By Allah, she will never return to you, ever, for the rest of your life.' But Allah knew his need for her and her need for him, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed: {And when you divorce women and they have fulfilled their term, do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands when they have agreed between themselves on reasonable terms} to the end of the verse. When Ma'qil heard it, he said: 'I hear and obey my Lord.' Then he called him and said: 'I will marry you to her and honor you.'"],[17598,"'Indeed, I will tell you a hadith that, were it not for the state I am in, I would not have reported. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever Allah places in charge of a flock and does not surround those behind it with sincere advice is among the people of the Fire.' He said: 'Should this not have been before now?'"],[17599,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever enters into one of the prices of the believers in order to raise it against them, it is a duty upon Allah to punish him in the great fire of Hell.'"],[17600,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever enters into any of the prices of the Muslims in order to raise it against them, it is a right upon God to cast him into a great part of the Fire.”"],[17602,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.”"],[17603,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came upon a man who was having himself cupped while he was fasting, and he said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast.”"],[17604,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one for whom it is done."],[17605,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the woman who attaches hair extensions and the one who requests it."],[17606,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “That one of you be stabbed in the head with an iron needle is better for him than touching a woman who is not lawful for him.”"],[17607,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “That a man be stabbed in the head with an iron needle is better for him than touching a woman who is not lawful for him.”"],[17608,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17609,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Deeds during turmoil are like emigration to me.”"],[17610,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17611,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.”"],[17612,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17614,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Worship during turmoil or tribulation is like emigration to me.”"],[17615,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two groups of my community do not receive my intercession: a tyrannical, oppressive ruler, and one extreme in religion who bears witness against them and then disavows them.”"],[17616,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Two men of my community do not receive my intercession: a tyrannical, oppressive ruler, and another extreme in religion, deviating from it.”"],[17617,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “For everything there is a key, and the key of the heavens is saying ‘There is no god but God.’”"],[17618,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any people among whom the call to prayer is sounded in the morning are in God’s protection until evening, and any people among whom the call to prayer is sounded in the evening are in God’s protection until morning.”"],[17619,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Cupping on Tuesday, on the seventeenth of the month, is a remedy for a year’s ailment.”"],[17620,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Your Lord, the Exalted, says, \"O Son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship, and I will fill your heart with contentment and your hands with provision. O Son of Adam, do not distance yourself from Me, for then I will fill your heart with poverty and your hands with occupation.\""],[17621,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God does not listen to anything as He listens to the muezzins’ call to prayer and a beautiful voice reciting the Qur’an.”"],[17622,"While on the road, I saw the like of it and picked it up and moved it aside. He took my hand and said, “O son of my brother, what made you do what you did?” I said, “O uncle, I saw you do something and I did the same.” He said, “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, ‘Whoever removes an annoyance from the path of the Muslims, a good deed is recorded for him, and whoever has a good deed accepted from him enters Paradise.’” This is the wording of the hadith of al-‘Abbas al-‘Anbari."],[17623,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ conquered Khaybar, the people captured donkeys and plundered them until the cooking pots boiled over. The Messenger of God ﷺ came, and it was said that the people’s donkeys had been slaughtered. The Prophet ﷺ forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, and a man began to overturn his cooking vessel with the head of his bow or the post of his house."],[17624,"We were in Madinah, and it had abundant fruit, and the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade fadikh (a drink made from dates)."],[17625,"Wine was forbidden while we were drinking fadikh, and I began pouring it out, saying, “This is the last time for wine.”"],[17626,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no man who takes charge of a people and then does not protect them as he protects himself and his family except that God will admit him into the fire of Hell.”"],[17627,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when al-Mughira b. Shuʿba entered, wearing leather socks. He was the first person I saw wearing leather socks in Islam. The people began touching them and saying, “What is this?” They said, “These are leather socks.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “You will soon have many leather socks.” They said, “O Messenger of God, what do you command us regarding ablution for prayer?” He said, “Wipe over them, or perform ablution while wearing them.”"],[17628,"A man mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that he had found a woman of beauty and noble lineage, except that she was barren. He forbade him from marrying her, then he returned and he again forbade him, and said: “Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast of your numbers.”"],[17629,"ʿUthman b. ʿAffan used to suffer greatly from prostatic fluid, so he sent a man to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is prostatic fluid. Every male emits it. Wash it with water, perform ablution, and pray.”"],[17630,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said, \"Recite it for your deceased,\" meaning Surah Yasin."],[17631,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-Baqarah is the pinnacle of the Qur'an, and its two last verses came down with every verse. Eighty angels descended with them. Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Ya-Sin are connected to one another; they will be together in Paradise. The heart of the Qur'an is Surah Ya-Sin. Whoever recites it seeking Allah, the home, and the hereafter, Allah will forgive him. Recite it during the prayer for your deceased.\""],[17632,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Act according to the Book of God and do not reject anything of it. Whatever is unclear to you, ask the people of knowledge about it and they will inform you. Believe in the Torah and the Gospel, for in them is clarification and intercession, and what is lawful is confirmed.”"],[17633,"Indeed, God used to benefit us through knowledge by sitting with you. You used to narrate to us from the Prophet ﷺ. Maʿqil said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Whoever is given charge of any affair of the Muslims and does not surround them with sincere counsel as he surrounds his own household, let him take his seat in the Fire.” He said: I have never heard this from you before today. He said: “I would not have narrated it to you except while I am in this state of mine.” He said: Then Ziyad went out dragging his garment."],[17634,"When her father became gravely ill, Ziyad heard of it and came until he sought permission at the door. I sat by my father, and Ziyad entered. He recognized death in my father’s face and said: “O Maʿqil, will you not provide us with something from you? God used to benefit us through things we heard from you.” He said to him: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘There is no governor over a community, whether large or small, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.’” He lowered his head for a while, then bowed it, then raised his head and said: “O Maʿqil, is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, or is it from hearsay?” He said: “Rather, I heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[17637,"He said: Narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor appointed over any community of my nation, whether small or large, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.”"],[17638,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor placed in charge of a community, whether small or large, who then does not act justly among them except that God will cast him into the Fire.”"],[17639,"My father fell ill with the illness in which he died. Ziyad came to visit him and said: “Allow him to enter alone.” So they allowed him. When he entered upon him, he said: “Your hadith used to benefit us, so narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.” He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “There is no governor who rules over any community of my nation, whether small or large, who does not act justly among them except that God will cast him on his face into the Fire.” That distressed him, and he said: “Is this something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, or did you hear it from his Companions?” He said: “Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[17640,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ and came upon a place where there was garlic. Some people ate from it, then came to the prayer area. The Messenger of God ﷺ noticed its smell and said: “Whoever eats of this plant should not approach our prayer area.” The wording is from the hadith of Abu al-Walid."],[17641,"We were in Madinah, and it had abundant fruit. “The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us fadikh.”"],[17642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God, might and majesty be to Him, has disliked for you gossip and speculation, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth.\""],[17643,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever buys a slave intending to manumit him should not stipulate manumission for his owners, for that is his contract from slavery.\""],[17644,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"There is no ruler who is entrusted with a flock and does not protect it and advise them sincerely, except that he will not enter Paradise with them.\""],[17645,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Act upon the Quran, deem lawful what it deems lawful, deem unlawful what it deems unlawful, follow its example, and do not disbelieve in any part of it. Whatever is unclear to you, refer it to God or to the ruler after me, so that they may inform you. And believe in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and what the prophets received from their Lord. Let the Quran and its clear explanations heal you, for it is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, a witness whose testimony is believed, and for every verse of it there is light until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, I have been given Surat al-Baqarah as part of the Remembrance, and I have been given Ta-Ha and al-Tur from the tablets of Moses, and I have been given the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, and I have been given the Mufassal as an additional portion.\""],[17646,"\"We went on Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Aisha taking off her clothes. He asked her, 'What is wrong with you?' She responded, 'I have been informed that you have made your Ihram lawful and made the people accompanying you lawful.' He said, 'Indeed, whoever does not have a sacrificial animal, but as for us, we have not made our Ihram lawful yet, as we still have bodily impurities until we reach Arafat.'\""],[17647,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has disliked for you three things: disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding while demanding.\""],[17648,"There was an oath between two neighbors of mine, and the oath fell upon one of them. Then I heard Maqil b. Yasar say: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever swears an oath by which he seizes the property of his brother will meet God while He is angry with him.'\""],[17650,"\"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah while I was lifting a branch of the tree from his face. We pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee, and we did not pledge allegiance to him upon death.\" We said to him, \"How many were you?\" He said, \"One thousand four hundred.\""],[17651,"\"I was lifting the branches of the tree from the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" The people pledged allegiance that they would not flee, and they were then one thousand four hundred."],[17652,"\"I saw myself on the day of the tree while the Prophet ﷺ\" was accepting the people's allegiance, and I was lifting a branch of its branches from his head. We did not pledge allegiance to him upon death, but rather we pledged allegiance to him that we would not flee."],[17653,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"There is no shepherd who betrays his flock except that he will be in the Fire.\""],[17655,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever separates is not one of us.\" Asad said: \"He separates between a child and his mother, and between siblings.\""],[17656,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ: \"A case involving a grandfather was brought to him, and he gave him a third or a sixth.\""],[17657,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever says in the morning three times: 'I seek refuge in the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from the accursed devil,' and recites three times the end of Surat al-Hashr, Allah appoints over him seventy thousand angels who send blessings upon him until evening. If he dies on that day, he dies as a martyr. If he says it in the evening, the like of that is for him.\""],[17658,"I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he said to me, \"Would you like Fatimah?\" meaning his daughter. I said, \"Yes.\" He stood, leaning on me, and said, \"Indeed, another will bear the burden, while the reward will be yours.\" It was as if there was nothing upon me until we entered upon Fatimah. He said to her, \"How do you find yourself?\" She said, \"By Allah, my grief has intensified, my need has intensified, and my illness has prolonged.\" He said, \"Are you not pleased that I have married you to the one who was earliest in Islam of my Ummah, the most knowledgeable of them, and the most forbearing of them?\""],[17659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to judge among my people. I said, \"I am not good at it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.\""],[17660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to judge among my people. I said, \"I am not good at judging.\" He said, \"Judge among them, for Allah ﷻ is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.\""],[17661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Al-Baqarah is the summit of the Quran and it is accompanied by eighty angels with every verse of it. Allah revealed 'There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence' from beneath the Throne, so Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Yasin were attached to it. The heart of the Quran is Surah Al-Baqarah, and whoever recites it seeking Allah and the Last Home, Allah will forgive him. Recite it over your dead.\""],[17662,"\"She is entitled to a dower like that of her peers, without reduction or excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up among a group from Ashja' and testified, \"Indeed the Prophet ﷺ ruled that in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'iyyah.\""],[17663,"About a man who married a woman and did not assign her a dower and did not consummate the marriage until he died, he made them repeat [the question], then said, \"Indeed I will give my opinion concerning her. If it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is wrong, it is from myself. I hold that she is entitled to a dower like that of a woman from among her peers, without reduction or excess, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Ma'qil b. Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"I testify that you have ruled concerning her with the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq,\" a woman from Banu Rawas, a clan from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, and this is what Sufyan adopts."],[17664,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq the like of what you have ruled.\" Ibn Mas'ud was pleased."],[17665,"'Abdullah was brought a case of a man who left behind his wife and had not consummated the marriage with her. They referred it back to him concerning her for a month, and he did not rule anything. He said, \"I will give my opinion concerning her. If it is wrong, it is from myself, and if it is correct, it is from Allah: the like of her peers' dower, upon her the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Abu Sinan al-Ashja'i stood up and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq with that.\" 'Abdullah was pleased with that."],[17666,"From 'Abdullah concerning a man who married a woman and then died leaving her, and he had not consummated the marriage and had not assigned her a dower. He said, \"She is entitled to the full dower, upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance.\" Ma'qil b. Sinan said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rule with that in the case of Barwa' bint Washiq.\""],[17667,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was being cupped on the eighteenth of Ramadan, and he said, \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[17668,"He informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Ghifar, Aslam, Juhaynah, and Muzaynah are allies of Allah ﷻ and His Messenger.\""],[17669,"He informed him that Ma'qil ibn abi Maqil al-Asadi, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to him: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade facing the two qiblas (Kaaba in Makkah and Masjid al-Aqsa in Jerusalem) while in a state of impurity (due to feces and urine).\""],[17670,"He narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ forbade facing either of the two qiblahs with excrement or urine."],[17671,"That his mother Zaynab came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Ma'qil had promised me that he would not perform Hajj unless I was with him. He performed Hajj on his riding camel, but I was not able. I asked him for the harvest of his date palms, and he said: It is the sustenance of my family. I asked him for a young camel he had, and he said: It is in the way of Allah, I will not give it to you. He said: 'Abu Ma'qil, what does Umm Ma'qil say?' He said: She is truthful. He said: 'Give her your young camel, for Hajj is the way of Allah.' So he gave her his young camel. She said: I am a woman who has become ill and old, and I fear I will not live to perform Hajj until I die. Is there anything that suffices for Hajj? He said: 'Yes, an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.' So she performed Umrah in Ramadan."],[17672,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr: al-Miqdad b. Amr."],[17673,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad b. Amr.\""],[17674,"\"Because he adopted and allied with him. He was dark-skinned, large-bellied, dyed his beard yellow, had an aquiline nose and a long nose. He died in Madinah at the age of seventy, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ prayed over him.\""],[17675,"\"I saw al-Miqdad, and he was huge.\""],[17676,"I saw al-Miqdad, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sitting on a chest from the chests of the money-changers in Hims, having become too large for it due to his bone size, intending to go on a military expedition. I said: Allah has excused you. He said: The surah of the sending forth refused us: {Go forth, light and heavy}."],[17677,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad was from Kindah.\""],[17678,"\"I was the companion of al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad in the Jahiliyyah. He was a man from Bahra'. He shed blood among them, so he fled to Kindah and allied with them. Then he shed blood among them, so he fled to Makkah and allied with al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth.\""],[17679,"It is only four thousand. He disputed with him before Umar. Uthman said: I lent him seven thousand. Al-Miqdad said: Will you swear that it is seven thousand? He said: You have been fair. But he refused to swear. He said: Take what he gives you. He said: By Allah, besides whom there is no deity, it is only seven thousand? He said: What prevents you from swearing that this is night and this is day?"],[17680,"\"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad died at al-Jurf, and men carried him to Madinah on their necks in the year thirty-three. Uthman b. Affan prayed over him. He was called Abu Ma'bad, and his age was about seventy.\""],[17681,"That I should ask the Prophet ﷺ about pre-ejaculate fluid, and his daughter was my wife. So I instructed al-Miqdad, and he asked him. He said: \"In it is ablution.\""],[17682,"Ali b. Abi Talib said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me about a man who plays with his wife and talks to her and then emits pre-ejaculate fluid. Were it not that I feel shy before him and that his daughter is my wife, I would have asked him. So al-Miqdad asked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He should wash his penis, then perform ablution, then sprinkle water on his private part.\""],[17683,"I said to al-Miqdad: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for were it not that his daughter is under me, I would ask him about one of us who draws near his wife and emits madhy but does not control that and does not touch her. So al-Miqdad asked the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you emits madhy and does not touch her, let him wash his penis and his testicles.\""],[17684,"Ali said to me: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who plays with his wife and madhy comes out of him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who plays with his wife and madhy comes out of him? He said: \"He washes his private part and performs wudu as he would for prayer.\""],[17685,"A man came and praised Uthman, so al-Miqdad stood up and threw dirt in his face. Uthman said to him: What is with you? He said: As for me, I will not leave anything I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17686,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17687,"When we emigrated to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided us into groups of ten, so I was among the ten who were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We had a sheep whose milk we drank among ourselves. One night he was late, and we had set aside his share. I got up while hungry and drank it. Then the Prophet ﷺ came while I had not slept. He came to the vessel in which we used to put the milk and looked but found nothing in it. I jumped up and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I slaughter it for you? He said: \"No.\""],[17688,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ and he divided us: ten in a house, ten in a house. I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and we had a sheep that sustained us."],[17689,"When we arrived in Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ grouped us in tens, ten in each house. I was among the ten among whom the Prophet was. He said: We had only a sheep whose milk we shared. When the Prophet ﷺ was late, we would drink and leave the Prophet's ﷺ share. One night he was late, and we slept. Al-Miqdad said: The Prophet ﷺ has taken long; I do not think he will come tonight. Perhaps someone invited him. He said: So I drank it. When the night passed, he came and entered. When he entered, he gave the greeting without raising his voice, then went to the bowl. When he saw nothing, he was silent, then said: \"O Allah, feed the one who fed us tonight.\" So I jumped up, took the knife, and brought it to him. He wiped its udder, and something came out, then he drank, then slept."],[17690,"A delegation from the people of Iraq was sent to Uthman, and they began praising him. Al-Miqdad began throwing dirt in their faces and said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dirt in the faces of the praisers.\""],[17691,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except that I heard Talha narrating about the Day of Uhud.\""],[17692,"I arrived in Madinah with two companions of mine. We sought hospitality from people, but no one hosted us. So we came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, severe hunger has befallen us, and we sought hospitality from people, but no one hosted us. He took us to his home, where he had four she-goats. He said: \"O Miqdad, milk them.\" The Prophet ﷺ apportioned a share for each of us, and I used to do that. I set aside the share of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he was late. I lay down on my bed, and my soul said to me: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a household of the Ansar and ate and drank with them. If only you drank this drink. My soul kept at me until I drank it. When it settled in my belly, regret over what had passed and what had just happened seized me. My soul said to me: Now he will come thirsty and find nothing. So I lay down and covered myself with the garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and gave a greeting that the awake could hear but that would not wake the sleeping one. Then he came to the vessel, uncovered it, and saw nothing. He said: \"O Allah, feed the one who fed me and give drink to the one who gave me drink.\" I seized the opportunity of his supplication and got up, took the blade, and approached the goats. I looked for the fattest among them to slaughter. I approached one and felt her, and found her full of milk. I looked at another and found her full of milk. I looked at the next and found her full of milk. I looked at all of them and found them all full of milk. I took the vessel and milked into it, then said: Drink. He said: \"The news first, O Miqdad.\" I said: Drink, then the news. He said: \"Some of your misdeed, O Miqdad.\" So he drank, then said: \"Drink.\" I said: Drink, O Messenger of Allah. He drank until he was satisfied. Then I took from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and drank. Then I told him the news. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is a blessing that descended from heaven. Why did you not tell me so I could give your two companions to drink?\" I said: If you and I get it, I do not care who misses it."],[17694,"And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When you see the praisers, throw dirt in their faces.\""],[17695,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us, when we see the praisers, to throw dirt in their faces.\""],[17696,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17697,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17699,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers."],[17700,"And he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to throw dust in the faces of the flatterers.”"],[17701,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you hear the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17702,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces.”"],[17703,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I and a man from the polytheists exchange two blows and he cuts off my hand, then when I move to strike him he says: “There is no god but Allah.” Should I kill him or spare him? He said: “Rather spare him.” I said: Even if he cut off my hand? He said: “Even if he did.” I repeated it twice or three times, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you kill him after he says: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ then you are like him before he said it, and he is like you if you kill him.”"],[17704,"He reported to him from al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was a man from Kindah and an ally of Banu Zuhrah. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the polytheists and we exchange two blows, and he cuts off one of my hands, then I strike him and later am able to kill him, but when I intend to bring my weapon down upon him he says: “There is no god but Allah.” Should I kill him or leave him? He said: “Rather leave him.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands? He said: “Even if he did.” I repeated it, and he said: “If you kill him after he says: ‘There is no god but Allah,’ then you are in his position before he said it, and he is in your position before you kill him.”"],[17705,"He reported to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off my hand, then he said that after cutting it off. Should I kill him? He said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he said the word that he said.”"],[17706,"Al-Miqdad said to the Prophet ﷺ: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him after he has said it, O Prophet of Allah? He said: “Do not kill him.” He said: He cut off my hand, then he said that after cutting it off? The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, he will be in your position before you kill him, and you will be in his position before he said his word that he said.”"],[17707,"He reported to him that al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr al-Kindi, who was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, related to him that he said: O Messenger of Allah, if I meet a man from the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with the sword and cuts it off, then he takes refuge from me behind a tree and says: “I have submitted to Allah.” Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said it? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off. Should I kill him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not kill him. For if you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he said his word that he said.”"],[17708,"He informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"What do you think of a man from the disbelievers who fought me, and we exchanged two blows. He struck one of my hands with a sword and cut it off, then he sought refuge from me behind a tree and said, 'I have embraced Islam.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" He said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, he would be in your position before you killed him, and you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17709,"He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and fight him, and he cuts off my hand, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" He said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17710,"He informed him from al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—he was a man from Kindah and an ally of Banu Zuhrah—that he said: \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers, and he and I exchange two blows. He strikes me and severs one of my hands, then I strike him. Then I am able to kill him, but when I intend to strike him with my weapon, he says, \"There is no god but Allah.\" Should I kill him or leave him?'\" He said: \"No, rather leave him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands?\" He said, \"Even if he did.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, even if he cut off one of my hands?\" He said, \"Even if he did.\" I repeated it, and he said: \"If you kill him after he says, 'There is no god but Allah,' then you are in his position before he said it, and he is in your position before you kill him.\""],[17712,"\"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you kill him, then you are in his position before he uttered his word that he said, and he is in your position before you kill him.\""],[17713,"He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the polytheists and he fights me, and he strikes one of my hands and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him after he has said that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him after he has said that.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he cut off one of my hands, then he said that after cutting it off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you kill him, then he is in your position before you kill him, and you are in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17714,"He informed him that al-Miqdad b. ʿAmr was an ally of Banu Zuhrah and was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He informed him that he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I meet a man from the disbelievers and we fight, and he strikes one of my hands with a sword and cuts it off, then he seeks refuge from me behind a tree and says, 'I have submitted to Allah.' Should I kill him, O Messenger of Allah, after he has said that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, he would be in your position before you killed him, and you would be in his position before he uttered his word that he said.\""],[17716,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman b. Yasar, from al-Miqdad, that ʿAli ordered him to ask the Prophet ﷺ about a man who approaches his wife and emits madhy—what is incumbent upon him? For his daughter is with me, and I feel shy to ask him. Al-Miqdad said: \"So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: 'When one of you experiences that, let him wash his private part and perform wuduʾ as he does for prayer.'\""],[17717,"A man from Ghafiq owed a man from Mahrah one hundred dinars during the time of ʿUthman. They acquired good spoils of war. The Mahri said, \"I will hasten to you seventy dinars on condition that you cancel the hundred from me.\" The hundred was disputed. The Ghafiqi agreed to that. Then al-Miqdad passed by them, and he took hold of the rein of his mount to make him a witness. When he related the account to him, he said: \"Both of you have been warned of war from Allah and His Messenger.\""],[17718,"How amazing are people whom I passed by just now, wishing for tribulation, claiming that Allah would test them in it as He tested His Messenger ﷺ and his companions. By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The fortunate one is he who is kept away from tribulations,\" repeating it three times, \"and if he is tested, he remains patient.\""],[17719,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The heart of the son of Adam changes more quickly than a pot when it reaches a full boil.\""],[17720,"\"Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, I wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed.\" He turned to him and said: \"What makes a man wish for a gathering that Allah has kept him from, when he does not know how he would have been had he witnessed it? By Allah, there were people present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom Allah will cast on their faces into Hell—they did not answer him nor believe him. Will Allah not deprive one of you? Do you not recognize the favors of your Lord, believing in what your Prophet ﷺ brought? You have been spared affliction through others. By Allah, the Prophet ﷺ was sent in the harshest condition in which any prophet was sent—in a period of cessation and ignorance, when they saw no religion superior to idol worship. He came with a criterion that distinguished between truth and falsehood and separated a father from his child, until a man would see his father, son, or brother as a disbeliever, and Allah had opened the lock of his heart to faith, and he would know that whoever enters the Fire has perished. His eye would not be pleased while he knows that his close friend is in the Fire. And indeed it is that which Allah, exalted is He, said: {Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and offspring comfort to our eyes}.\""],[17721,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There will not remain on the face of the earth a house of mud or of hair but that Allah will bring Islam upon them either through the might of a mighty one or the humiliation of a humiliated one. Either He honors them and guides them to Islam, or He humiliates them and they pay the jizyah.”"],[17722,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “On the Day of Resurrection, the sun will be brought near to the creation until it is from them at a distance of a mīl.” Sulaym said: By Allah, I do not know what he meant by “mīl”—a distance on land, or the mīl (kohl stick) used to apply kohl to the eye? He ﷺ said: “Then people will be in sweat according to their deeds. Among them will be one whose sweat reaches his ankles, among them one whose reaches his knees, among them one whose reaches his waist, and among them one who will be bridled by sweat completely.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured toward his mouth."],[17723,"I will not speak good or evil about anyone until I see what his deeds are sealed with, after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He was asked: And what did you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed the heart of the son of Adam changes more violently than a pot when it reaches a full boil.”"],[17724,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “People will be gathered—from a miscarried fetus to a decrepit old man—as thirty-three-year-olds, in the form of Adam, the beauty of Joseph, and the character of Job, with kohl-lined eyes, having luxuriant hair.”"],[17725,"That the Prophet ﷺ asked them about fornication, so they said: It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He then said: “For a man to fornicate with ten women would be better for him than to fornicate with his neighbor's wife.” He said: And he asked them about theft, so they said: It is forbidden; Allah and His Messenger have forbidden it. He then said: “For a man to steal from ten houses would be easier for him than to steal from his neighbor's house.”"],[17726,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves Allah and His Messenger sincerely, not falsely, and meets the believers and loves them, and regards the affairs of the pre-Islamic era as having the status of a fire into which he is thrown, then he has tasted the taste of faith.” Or he said: “Then he has attained the summit of faith.” The doubt is from Safwan."],[17727,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “When the leader seeks to stir up discord among the people, he corrupts them.”"],[17728,"“These two eyes have prospered indeed, having seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then al-Miqdad's anger welled up and he said: “O people, do not wish for something that Allah has kept hidden, for how many have seen him and yet not benefited from seeing him.”"],[17729,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an expedition, and when I returned, he asked me: “How do you find yourself?” I said: I did not cease until I thought I had servants of my own. And by Allah, I will never again be appointed over two men after this."],[17730,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray toward a column, a wooden post, or a tree except that he would place it between his right eyebrow and his left eyebrow, and he would not face it directly."],[17731,"From Duba'ah bt. al-Zubayr—and she was the wife of al-Miqdad—she said: People used to go to relieve themselves only after a gap of two or three days, and they would defecate like camels. Then one day al-Miqdad went out to relieve himself until he reached al-Khabkhabah, which is in Baqi' al-Gharqad. He entered a ruin for his need. While he was sitting, a rat brought out from a hole a dinar, and it kept bringing out dinar after dinar until it reached seventeen dinars. I brought them and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of the story. He said: “Did your hand follow the hole?” I said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth. He said: “There is no zakah due on them. May Allah bless you in them.” Duba'ah said: Its last of them did not run out until I saw cords of silver in the house of al-Miqdad."],[17732,"Al-Miqdad went to relieve himself and entered a ruin. There was a rat bringing out from a hole a dinar, dinar by dinar, until it brought out seventeen dinars. Then it brought out the end of a green cloth. Al-Miqdad said: I stood up and pulled the end of the cloth, and I found in it a dinar, making eighteen dinars. Al-Miqdad took them and sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. When he entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, he told him the story and said: Take its charity, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Did you reach your hand into the hole?” Al-Miqdad said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Miqdad: “May Allah bless you in them.”"],[17733,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Something I heard from you that I doubted.\" He said, \"If any of you doubts a matter, let him ask me about it.\" He said, \"Your statement about your wives: 'I hope for them after me the truthful ones (al-ṣiddīqīn).'\" He said, \"Who do you count as al-ṣiddīqīn?\" We said, \"Our children who die young.\" He said, \"Rather, al-ṣiddīqīn are those who give charity.\" He said it three times."],[17734,"It is called subḥa. \"The Prophet ﷺ allotted for his horse a share and for him a share.\""],[17735,"To al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, \"O Abū Karīma.\""],[17736,"\"Al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib was given the kunya Abū Yaḥyā. Al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib died in the year eighty-seven, and he was ninety-one years old.\""],[17737,"\"I saw five of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ trim their moustaches, let their beards grow, and dye them yellow; among them was al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib.\""],[17738,"I came to al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib while he was in a village some miles from Ḥimṣ on the day of Eid. We said, § \"Come out and lead us in the Eid prayer.\" He said, \"No, pray individually.\""],[17739,"\"I saw Abū Umāma al-Bāhilī and al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, and upon them were two burnūses.\""],[17740,"I heard al-Miqdām b. Maʿdī Karib, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while most people were saying, \"The decree is in one hundred years,\" meaning after one hundred years the Resurrection will occur. Al-Miqdām said, \"You have said too much. Allah will not be unable to delay this community half a day,\" meaning five hundred years."],[17741,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right upon every Muslim. If the guest remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a debt upon him: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17742,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right upon every Muslim. If the guest remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a right upon him, or a debt: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17743,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Hosting guests is a duty upon every Muslim. Whoever begins his morning in his home, then he has a debt upon him, if he wishes, he may fulfill it, and if he wishes, he may leave it.\""],[17744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The night of the guest is an obligatory right. If he remains in his courtyard in the morning, then it is a debt upon him: if he wishes, he may collect it, and if he wishes, he may forgo it.\""],[17745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves behind a dependent (kallan), then it is to Allah and His Messenger—or he said, then it is to us—and whoever leaves behind wealth, then it is for his heirs. And I am the heir of the one who has no heir: I inherit his wealth and release his captive. The maternal uncle is the patron of the one who has no patron: he inherits his wealth and releases his captive.\""],[17746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, they are my responsibility, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian: I inherit his wealth and ransom his prisoner. The maternal uncle is the guardian of the one who has no guardian: he inherits his wealth and ransoms his prisoner.\""],[17747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever leaves behind a debt or a bequest, it is upon me. And whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his inheritors. And I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian, so I will repay his debt and inherit his wealth. And the paternal uncle is the guardian of the one who has no guardian, so he will repay his debt and inherit his wealth.\""],[17748,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever leaves behind a debt or dependents, they are my responsibility, and whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his heirs. I am the guardian of the one who has no guardian: I ransom his prisoner and inherit his wealth.\""],[17749,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The martyr has nine qualities with Allah\" – or he said \"ten qualities\" – \"he is forgiven with the first drop of his blood; he is shown his seat in Paradise; he is adorned with the adornment of faith; he is protected from the punishment of the grave; he is married to the wide-eyed houris; he is safe from the greatest terror; a crown of dignity is placed on his head, a ruby better than the world and all it contains; he is married to ninety-two wives from the wide-eyed houris; and he intercedes for seventy of his relatives.\""],[17750,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade riding on the skins of wild beasts."],[17751,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one has eaten food better than that which he eats from the work of his own hand, and Dawud used to eat only from the work of his own hand.\""],[17752,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing with his hand and saying: \"None of you has eaten food in this world better for him than that which he eats from the work of his own two hands.\""],[17753,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No one of the children of Adam has eaten food that is better for him than that which he eats from the work of his own two hands.\" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"And Dawud ﷺ used to eat from the work of his own two hands.\""],[17754,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whatever you feed your wife is charity for you, whatever you feed your child is charity for you, whatever you feed your servant is charity for you, and whatever you feed yourself is charity for you.\""],[17755,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hasan is from me, and Husayn is from Ali.\""],[17757,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, enjoins you concerning your mothers—three times; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers—twice; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17759,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17760,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your mothers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning your fathers; indeed Allah enjoins you concerning the nearest kin, then the next nearest.\""],[17761,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: \"You should take the pre-dawn meal, for it is the blessed nourishment.\""],[17762,"He was on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they camped beside enclosures belonging to the Jews at Khaybar. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took [fruit] from them, so the Jews went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Khalid b. al-Walid, and he called out: \"The prayer is to be held in congregation, and none will enter Paradise except a Muslim.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"What becomes lawful for you from the property of those under covenant without right to it?\" They said: \"Whatever we find in the Book of Allah as lawful we deem lawful, and whatever we find as unlawful we deem unlawful.\" \"Indeed, I forbid the property of those under covenant, every fanged beast of prey, and whatever has been subjected for service among riding animals except what Allah has named.\""],[17763,"From the Prophet ﷺ: he said: \"Measure out your food, and you will be blessed in it.\""],[17764,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A human being fills no vessel worse than the belly. Sufficient for the son of Adam are morsels that keep his back upright. If it must be, then one third for food, one third for drink, and one third for himself.\""],[17765,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The son of Adam has not contained a vessel worse than the belly. Sufficient for the Muslim are morsels that keep his back upright. If it must be, then one third for his food, one third for his drink, and one third for himself.\""],[17767,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Seek refuge in Allah from greed that leads to an unsound disposition, and from greed that leads to something not to be coveted.\""],[17768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people and praised Allah and spoke highly of Him. He then said, \"Indeed, Allah advises you regarding women. Indeed, Allah advises you regarding women. Verily, they are your mothers, and your daughters, and your aunts. Surely, a man from the People of the Book marries a woman, and he does not refer to her family lineage. So, one of them would not be pleased with her companion.\""],[17770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade things, until he mentioned domestic donkeys."],[17771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a leader seeks out suspicions about people, he corrupts them.”"],[17772,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “There is no man placed over a people except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection leading them with a banner before him that he carries, and they follow him. He will be asked about them, and they will be asked about him.”"],[17773,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this matter is among your people, so advise them concerning us.” He said to them: “I remind you of Allah: do not oppress my community after me.” Then he said to the people: “There will be rulers after me, so render obedience to them. Indeed, the ruler is like a shield; protection is sought with it. If they act rightly and command you to good, then that is for you and for them. But if they do evil in what they command you, then that is upon them, and you are free of it. Indeed, when a ruler pursues suspicion about people, he corrupts them.”"],[17774,"I heard al-Miqdam b. Ma'di Karib say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought water for ablution.” He performed ablution, washing his palms three times, then washing his face three times, then washing his forearms three times, then rinsing his mouth and sniffing water into his nose three times each, then wiping his head and his ears, their outer and inner parts, and washing his feet three times each."],[17776,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ” perform ablution, and when he reached wiping his head, he placed his palms on the front of his head, then passed them until he reached the back of the neck, then returned them to the place where he began."],[17777,"“These two eyes have prospered that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Miqdam became angry and said: “O people, do not wish for a matter that Allah has hidden from you.”"],[17778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Obey your rulers whatever the case. If they command you to something of what I brought you, then they are rewarded for it and you are rewarded for obeying them. If they command you to something of what I did not bring you, then it is upon them and you are free of it. That is because when you meet Allah, you will say: ‘Our Lord, no injustice.’ He will say: ‘No injustice.’ Then you will say: ‘Our Lord, You sent messengers to us and we obeyed them by Your permission; You appointed successors over us and we obeyed them by Your permission; and You placed rulers over us and we obeyed them for You.’ He will say: ‘You have spoken truth. It is upon them and you are free of it.’”"],[17779,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “A time will come upon people when whoever does not have yellow or white will not enjoy life.”"],[17780,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When it is the end of time, people will inevitably need dirhams and dinars; a man will use them to maintain his religion and his worldly life.”"],[17781,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him of that.\""],[17782,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one fills a vessel worse than the belly. If his self overcomes him, then let him leave a third for himself.”"],[17783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one dies as a miscarried fetus or decrepit old person — rather people are between that — except that he will be resurrected as a thirty-year-old. Whoever is from the people of Paradise will have the appearance of Adam, the form of Joseph, and the heart of Job. Whoever is from the people of the Fire will be made huge and magnified like mountains.”"],[17784,"We said to Al-Miqdam ibn Ma'di Karb Al-Kindi, \"O Abu Kareemah, people claim that you never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" He said, \"Indeed, by Allah, I did see him and he even took hold of my earlobe like this. And I used to walk with my uncle, then he said to my uncle, 'Do you think he remembers?' We said, 'O Abu Kareemah, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' He said, 'I heard him say, 'All that is between the umbilical cord and the toothless old man will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with the creation of Adam, the heart of Ayyub, and the beauty of Yusuf, darkened with kohl.' We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then what about the disbeliever?' He said, 'He will be enlarged for the Fire until his skin becomes forty cubits thick and the molar tooth will be like Uhud.''"],[17785,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The night of the guest is an obligatory right. If he wakes up deprived at his dwelling place, his aid becomes obligatory upon the Muslims until they take for him his right from his crops and his livestock because of the hospitality he was denied.”"],[17786,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The sun will draw near to the people on the Day of Resurrection until it is about two miles away from them, and its heat will intensify and scorch them. They will be in sweat according to their deeds: among them is one whom sweat reaches his ankles, among them is one whom it reaches his knees, among them is one whom it reaches his waist, and among them is one whom the sweat bridles completely.” He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gesturing with his hands toward his mouth. Ibrahim b. 'Irq said: This is how 'Umar b. Khath'am narrated it from Sulaym, from al-Miqdam."],[17787,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any man who is a guest of a people and they do not offer him hospitality, he has the right to demand from them the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17788,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever stays with a people, it is their duty to offer him hospitality. If they do not offer him hospitality, then he has the right to punish them with the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17789,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the Book and what equals it. Soon a satiated man reclining on his couch will say: 'Between us and you is this Book; whatever we find in it of lawful we declare lawful, and whatever we find in it of unlawful we declare unlawful.' Indeed, it is not so. The fanged beasts of prey are not lawful, nor domestic donkeys, nor the lost property of a person under covenant unless he has no need of it. And any man who is a guest of a people and they do not offer him hospitality, it is his right to seize from them the equivalent of his hospitality.”"],[17790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was given the Book and the like of it. Soon a satiated man reclining on his couch will say: 'Adhere to the Qur'an; whatever you find in it of lawful, declare it lawful, and whatever you find in it of unlawful, declare it unlawful.' Indeed, the domestic donkey is not lawful for you, nor any fanged beast of prey, nor the lost property of a person under covenant unless its owner has no need of it. And whoever stays with a people, it is their duty to offer him hospitality.”"],[17791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You will conquer lands in which there are houses called bathhouses. It is forbidden for the males of my ummah to enter them.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, they remove sickness and cleanse dirt.” He said: “Then they are lawful for the males of my ummah in waist-wrappers, and forbidden for the females of my ummah.”"],[17792,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib entered upon him while angry. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is it between us and Quraysh? When they meet each other, they meet with cheerful faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with something other than that.” The Prophet ﷺ became angry until his face turned red, then said: “Faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger. A man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father.”"],[17793,"Al-'Abbas entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh meet each other with radiant faces and meet us contrary to that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until sweat flowed between his eyes, then said: “A servant will not taste the sweetness of faith until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.”"],[17794,"Al-'Abbas came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ angry, and he said: “What brought you?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is it between us and Quraysh?” He said: “What is it between you and them that brought you here?” He said: “They meet one another with radiant faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with something other than that.” He became angry until a vein between his eyes throbbed. When his anger subsided, he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.” Then he said: “What is the matter with men who harm me concerning al-'Abbas? Verily, a man's paternal uncle is of the same stock as his father.”"],[17795,"Some people from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, we hear harsh words from some people; one of them says: 'The likeness of Muhammad is only that of a palm tree that grew in a dung heap.'” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said: “O people, who am I?” They said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “I am Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. We never heard him trace his lineage before that. Allah created His creation and placed me among the best of His creation. Then He divided them into two groups and placed me in the better group. Then He made them into tribes and placed me among the best of them as a tribe. Then He made them into households and placed me in the best household. So I am the best of you in household and the best of you in person.”"],[17796,"Some people from the Ansar said to the Prophet ﷺ: “We hear from some people of Quraysh, until one of them says: 'The likeness of Muhammad is only that of a palm tree that was planted in a dung heap.'” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O people, who am I?” They said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “I am Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib.” They said: “We never heard him trace his lineage before that at all.” Then he said: “Allah created His creation, then divided them into two groups and placed me in the better group. Then He made them into tribes and placed me among the best of them as a tribe. So I am the best of you in household and the best of you in person.”"],[17797,"The Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib gathered and said: Will you not ask the Messenger of God ﷺ to assign to you what he assigned to the Banu So-and-so — to assign to you the collection of the poor-due? They met 'Ali and spoke to him, and he said: God ﷻ and His Messenger have refused that for you — that He should assign to you the filth of people's hands, or he said: the washings of people's hands. 'Abd al-Muttalib said to his father: Send me. So al-'Abbas sent his son al-Fadl. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and entered, and he gave each one of us special attention. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What are you two doing here?\" I said: O Messenger of God, your people and the sons of your paternal uncle have sent us so that you assign to them what you have assigned to the people of the poor-due. He said: God and His Messenger have refused for you that you should eat the filth, or he said: the washings of people's hands."],[17799,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in the Masjid al-Haram while the people were circumambulating the Kaaba between him and the Qiblah without any barrier between him and them."],[17801,"He saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying toward the House with no one between him and the circumambulation area."],[17802,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed at the edge of the circumambulation area with no barrier between him and the circumambulation area. This is the wording of 'Abd Allah b. Salih. Ibn 'Abd al-Hakam said in his hadith: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he finished his sa'y, he prayed at the edge of the circumambulation area with no barrier between him and those circumambulating."],[17803,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying near the Corner while men were passing in front of him."],[17804,"The Prophet ﷺ came out of the Ka'bah and stood near the Corner and prayed two rak'ahs while people were passing in front of him circumambulating the House, men and women."],[17805,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray near the Corner by the water-dispensing place while men and women were passing in front of him."],[17806,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ praying near the Black Corner while men and women were passing in front of him with no barrier between him and them."],[17807,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a man praying while seated and said: \"The prayer of one seated is half the prayer of one standing.\" So the people forced themselves to stand."],[17808,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a vessel of nabidh, and he poured water over it until it became mild, then he drank from it."],[17809,"The Messenger of God ﷺ circumambulated the House on a hot, thirsty day and asked for water. A man said: O Messenger of God, we have a drink made from this raisin — shall I give you some to drink? He said: \"Yes.\" The man sent to his house and brought a large cup. The Prophet ﷺ brought it near his mouth and found it had a strong smell, so he disliked it and returned it."],[17810,"From his father Muti', whose name was al-'As, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Muti'. He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he killed that group of people: \"Makkah will not be invaded after this year, and no one of Quraysh will be killed patiently after this year.\""],[17811,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the Day of the Conquest: 'No Qurayshī is to be executed in retaliation after this day.'"],[17812,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: 'No Qurayshī is to be executed in retaliation after this day until the Day of Resurrection.' And no one from the rebellious Quraysh embraced Islam except Muṭīʿ; his name had been al-ʿĀṣ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Muṭīʿ."],[17814,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ after I had prayed with my family, and the prayer was called, so I sat down. When he finished praying, he said: 'Are you not a Muslim?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What prevented you from praying with the people?' He (the narrator) said: 'I had prayed with my family.' He said: 'Then pray with the people even if you have already prayed with your family.' This is how Sufyān narrated it from Zayd b. Aslam from Bishr b. Miḥjan, and he erred in it; it is actually Busr b. Miḥjan. Thus narrated Mālik and the companions of Zayd b. Aslam."],[17815,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us: Mālik informed us; and ʿAlī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl b. Abī Uways narrated to us: Mālik narrated to me, from Zayd b. Aslam, from a man of Banū al-Dīl called Busr b. Miḥjan, from his father, that he was in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was called to prayer, so he stood up and led them in prayer, then returned, while Miḥjan was still in his place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I prayed with my family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'When you come, pray with the people even if you have already prayed.'"],[17816,"I prayed ẓuhr or ʿaṣr in my house, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat with him. The prayer was called, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed, but I did not pray. When he finished, he said: 'Are you not a Muslim?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is the matter with you that you did not pray?' I said: 'I had already prayed in my house.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'When the prayer is called, pray even if you have already prayed.'"],[17817,"I went to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him about a matter. Then the prayer was established and I was sitting. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then he left and found me sitting. He said to me, \"Are you a Muslim?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"So what prevented you from praying with us?\" I said, \"Indeed, I have already prayed in my saddlebag.\" He said, \"Even if you have already prayed in your saddlebag.\""],[17818,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to us, from Zayd b. Aslam, from Busr b. Miḥjan, from his father, who said: I prayed ẓuhr or ʿaṣr in my house, then I went out to the mosque and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sitting with people around him. I sat with them. Then the prayer was called, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and prayed with the people, then came out and found me sitting in the place where he had seen me. He said: 'Are you not a Muslim man?' I said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I am indeed a Muslim.' He said: 'What prevented you from entering and praying with the people?' I said: 'I had already prayed with my family.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When you have prayed with your family and then come to the mosque and find the people praying, pray with them.'"],[17820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and found a man who had finished his prayer and was reciting the tashahhud, saying: 'O Allah, I ask You by Allah, the One, the Eternal Refuge, who neither begot nor was begotten, nor is there to Him any equivalent, to forgive me my sins; indeed You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has been forgiven, he has been forgiven, he has been forgiven.'"],[17821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me until we climbed Uḥud and looked over Madinah. He said: 'Woe to its mother, a town whose people will abandon it when it is most flourishing! The Dajjāl will come to it and will find at every one of its entrances an angel with a drawn sword.' Then he descended until he came to the mosque, and there was a man standing and praying and reciting. He said: 'Do you see him? That is ʿAbd Allāh b. Qays. He is indeed an awwāh (one who sighs much in prayer), a forbearing man.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I give him the good news?' He said: 'Beware, do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.' Then he descended further, and when we reached the mosque, we found Burayda al-Aslamī at one of the gates of the mosque. In the mosque there was a man who prolonged his prayer, and Burayda was a man who liked to joke. He said: 'O Miḥjan, will you not pray as Sukba prays?' He did not answer him, and returned. When he came to his house, he said: 'The best of our religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest; the best of your religion is its easiest' — three times."],[17823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. Then he came upon me while I was leaving on the road from Madinah, and he took me by the hand, and we went until we climbed Uḥud. He turned toward Madinah and said: 'Woe to its mother, a town whose people will abandon it when it is most flourishing.' I said: 'O Prophet of Allah, who will eat its fruit?' He said: 'The birds and beasts of prey in health, and the Dajjāl will not enter it. Every time he wants to enter it, an angel with a drawn sword will meet him at every one of its entrances.' Then he turned and came until he was at the door of the mosque, and there was a man praying. He said: 'Does he say it truthfully?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so; this is the man who prays the most among the people of Madinah.' He said: 'Do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.'"],[17824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Ḥājiz, to the right of Madinah, on an errand. When I returned, I went with him until he climbed Uḥud and looked over Madinah. He said: 'Woe to your mother, a town whose people will abandon you when you are at your best.' Then he descended, and I descended with him, until we came to the door of the mosque. He saw a man praying, and he put his hand on my shoulder and illuminated him with his light. He said: 'Does he say it truthfully?' He said it three times. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is so-and-so, and he is the most devoted worshipper among the people of Madinah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Beware, do not let him hear you, for you will destroy him.' He said it three times."],[17825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The righteous will depart one after another, until only worthless people remain, like the dregs of dates and barley. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17826,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The righteous will depart one after another, and the righteous will be taken, the first and then the first, until only worthless people remain, like the dregs of dates and barley. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17827,"A man struck his brother, so he fled, and we found him with Abu Bakr. We took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he let us exact retaliation from him."],[17828,"That is, he meant al-Munqa` b. Tamim."],[17829,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with the sadaqah of our camels, and he ordered that it be accepted. I said, “In it are two she-camels as a gift for you.” So the gift was set aside from the sadaqah. A few days later, people began saying that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was going to send Khalid b. al-Walid to the slaves of Egypt — or he said “to Egypt” (Abu Ghassan was unsure) — and would allocate the sadaqah to them. I said, “By Allah, we have no property with us or with our families other than that, and their sadaqah is here.” So I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a she-camel of his, and with him was a black man whose head was level with the head of the Prophet ﷺ. I had never seen anyone taller than him. As I drew near, he seemed to lean toward me, but the Prophet ﷺ held him back. I said, “The people have been saying such-and-such.” The Prophet ﷺ raised his hand until I saw the whiteness of his armpits and said: “O Allah, I do not permit them to tell lies about me.” Al-Munqa` said: “I never narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except a statement that a Book has spoken or a Sunnah that has been established. Lies are told about him during his lifetime, so how will it be after his death?”"],[17830,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like when one of you puts his finger in the sea; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17831,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in the sea; let him see what he brings back.” Then he took hold of two joints of my forefinger."],[17832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in this sea; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, and indicated with his finger: “By Allah, the world compared to the Hereafter is only like what one of you brings back when he puts his finger in the sea and then takes it out; let him see what he brings back.”"],[17834,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The world compared to the Hereafter is only like when one of you walks to the sea and dips his finger in it.”"],[17835,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The righteous will depart, the first and then the first, until only something like the dregs of dates remain. Allah will pay no heed to them.”"],[17836,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The righteous will depart one after another.”"],[17837,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ suffering from gout and complained to him, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The midday heats have belied you.\""],[17838,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Return the needle and the thread; whoever embezzles a needle or thread will be burdened to bring it, and he will not be able to bring it.\""],[17839,"From al-Mustawrid, a man of Banū Fihr who had companionship [with the Prophet], that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world compared to the Hereafter is only like a man dipping his finger into the sea and then withdrawing it.\""],[17840,"I was in the riding party with the Messenger of God ﷺ when his eye fell upon a discarded lamb that they had cast aside. He said, \"Do you consider this worthless to its owners?\" They said, \"It is because of its worthlessness that they cast it aside.\" He said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the world is more worthless to God than this is to its owners.\""],[17841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I and the Hour have been sent like these two,\" [and he indicated with] the index and middle fingers."],[17842,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Ibn Lahīʿa narrated to us, from al-Ḥārith b. Yazīd, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Jubayr, who said: We were in a gathering in which al-Mustawrid and ʿAmr b. Ghaylān b. Salama were present. Al-Mustawrid said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever undertakes a task for us and has no wife, let him take a wife; whoever has no servant, let him take a servant; whoever has no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; and whoever has no mount, let him take a mount.\" Abū Bakr said, \"You have said much, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Whoever takes anything beyond that is an embezzler.\""],[17843,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever undertakes a task for us, if he has no wife, let him marry; or if he has no servant, let him take a servant; or if he has no dwelling, let him take a dwelling; or if he has no mount, let him take a mount. Whoever takes anything beyond that is an embezzler or a thief.\""],[17844,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever is our agent, let him acquire a wife; if he has no servant, let him acquire a servant; and whoever has no dwelling, let him acquire a dwelling.\""],[17845,"\"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ\" when he performed ablution, he would rub between the toes of his feet with his little finger."],[17846,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Every nation has a term, and the term of the nation of Muḥammad is one hundred years.\" He said, \"When it passes the hundred, what God promised it will come to it.\""],[17847,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Every nation has a term, and the term of my nation is one hundred years. When one hundred years pass over my nation, what God promised it will come to it.\" Ibn Lahīʿa said, \"That is, an abundance of tribulations.\""],[17848,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The likeness of the world in relation to the Hereafter is only as when a man dips his finger into the sea and then withdraws it—with how much does it return?\""],[17849,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I was sent in the very time of the Hour, and I preceded it just as this one precedes,\" and he gestured with his two fingers, the index and the middle finger."],[17850,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The world has taken nothing from the Hereafter except as a needle dipped into the sea takes from its water.\""],[17851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever consumes a meal at the expense of his brother, Allah will feed him a meal like it from the Fire of Jahannam.\""],[17852,"He narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever consumes a meal at the expense of a Muslim man in this world, Allah will feed him the like of it in Jahannam; and whoever is clothed with a garment at the expense of a Muslim man, Allah will clothe him with the like of it from Jahannam; and whoever takes a stand on behalf of a Muslim for show, Allah will make him stand in a position of notoriety and show.\""],[17853,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Hour will not come until the Romans are the most numerous of people.\" This reached 'Amr b. al-'As, who said: \"What are these reports that are mentioned from you?\" Al-Mustawrid said to him: \"I said what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" 'Amr said: \"If you say that, they are the most forbearing of people at the time of calamity, the most patient of people at the time of affliction, and the best of people to their weak and their poor.\""],[17854,"I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The righteous will depart one after another, and there will remain the dregs of society, like the dregs of dates and barley, and Allah will pay no attention to them.\""],[17855,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at Arafah and said, \"Every household among the Muslims should offer a sacrifice and have a meal called 'Ateerah.' Do you know what 'Ateerah' means? It means what you call Rajabiyyah.\""],[17856,"We were standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"O people, indeed, every household has a sacrifice and an 'Atirah in every year. Do you know what is 'Atirah? It is what people call Al-Rajabiyah.\""],[17857,"I arrived to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Arafah and he was saying, \"Do you know it?\" I do not know what they (the people) responded to him. So the Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is upon the people of every household to sacrifice a sheep in every Rajab and a sheep in every Eid al-Adha.\""],[17858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whomever you seize of the men of the Jews, kill him.\" Muhayyisa jumped upon Ibn Sunayna, a man from the Jewish merchants whom he used to associate with and do business with, and killed him. Huwayyisa at that time had not yet embraced Islam and was older than Muhayyisa. When he killed him, Huwayyisa began to beat him and say: \"O enemy of Allah, you killed him? By Allah, perhaps there is fat in your belly from his wealth.\" I said: \"By Allah, if he had ordered me to kill you, I would have struck your neck.\" He said: \"By Allah, it was the first thing of Huwayyisa's Islam.\" He said: \"By Allah, if Muhammad ordered you to kill me, you would kill me?\" Muhayyisa said: \"Yes, by Allah.\" Huwayyisa said: \"By Allah, a religion that has reached this point is truly astonishing.\" So Huwayyisa embraced Islam."],[17859,"He was called Nafi' Abu Tayba. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him about his earnings (from cupping). He said: \"Do not touch it.\" He returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Feed it to your watering camel; put it in its stomach.\""],[17860,"He was called Abu Tayba, and he earned a great deal. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the earnings of the cupper, he sought a concession from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he refused him. He continued to speak with him and mention his need to him until he said to him: \"Throw its earnings into the belly of your watering camel.\""],[17861,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission regarding the earnings of the cupper, and he forbade him from it. He did not cease to go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mention his need to him until he gave him permission to feed it to his watering camel and his slaves."],[17862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A community in which the right of the weak is not taken without him being made to suffer is not sanctified.\""],[17863,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me wanting my wealth.\" He said: \"Remind him of Allah.\" He said: \"What if he does not take heed?\" He said: \"Then seek help against him from the Muslims around you.\" He said: \"What if there is no one around me?\" He said: \"Then seek help against him from the authority.\" He said: \"What if the authority sells me out?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fight in defense of your wealth until you are among the martyrs of the Hereafter or you prevent that.\""],[17864,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, if a man comes to me wanting my property, how do you command me?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" I said, \"What do you think if I do that and he does not refrain?\" He said, \"Seek help from the Muslims.\" I said, \"What do you think if I do that and I find no one among the Muslims?\" He said, \"Seek help from the ruler.\" I said, \"What do you think if the ruler forsakes me and insists only on seizing my property?\" He said, \"Then fight him until you defend your property or you become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter.\""],[17865,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"What do you think about a man who meets me in a desolate land wanting my property?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what if he does not take heed?\" He said, \"Then seek help against him from other Muslims besides yourself.\" He said, \"What if there is no one around me?\" He said, \"Then seek help against him from the ruler.\" He said, \"What do you think if the ruler refuses to help me?\" He said, \"Then fight in defense of your property until you become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter or you defend your property.\""],[17866,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"What do you think if a man comes to me wanting to take my property?\" He said, \"Remind him of God.\" He said, \"What do you think if I remind him of God and he does not take heed?\" He said, \"Seek help against him from the ruler.\" He said, \"What do you think if the ruler forsakes me?\" He said, \"Seek help from the Muslims who are present with you.\" He said, \"What do you think if no one is present with me?\" He said, \"Then fight in defense of your property, or you will be killed and become one of the martyrs of the Hereafter.\""],[17867,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"A tribulation will convulse the earth like the horns of cattle.\" Then a veiled man passed by, and he said, \"This one and his companions will be upon guidance on that day.\" And it turned out to be ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[17868,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the road to Madinah when he said, \"What will you do in a tribulation that will spread through the regions of the earth like the horns of cattle?\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, what should we do?\" A man was in front of him, so he said, \"Follow this man and his companions.\" I went quickly to that man, who was hastening, and I took hold of him and turned him toward the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"This one, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He was ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān.\""],[17869,"While we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the road to Madinah, he said, \"What will you do about a tribulation that will arise in the regions of the earth like the horns of cattle?\" They said, \"What should we do, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"You must adhere to this man and his companions,\" or \"Follow this man and his companions.\" I hurried until I turned the man around and said, \"O Prophet of God, this one?\" He said, \"This one.\" And it turned out he was ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[17870,"He said: \"By God, were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would not have stood in this place.\" When Muʿāwiyah heard mention of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he seated the people and said: \"While we were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ, ʿUthmān passed by, having combed his hair and wearing a waist-wrapper. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'A tribulation will surely emerge from under my foot—or from under this foot of mine—and this man and whoever follows him will be upon guidance on that day.' I stood up and took hold of ʿUthmān's shoulder and turned him toward the Messenger of God ﷺ, and I said, 'This one?' He said, 'Yes, this one and whoever follows him will be upon guidance on that day.'\" Then ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥawālah al-Anṣārī stood up from near the pulpit and said, \"You are indeed the companion of this affair?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"By God, I was present at that gathering, and if I had known that I had anyone in the army who would confirm it, I would have been the first to speak of it.\""],[17871,"He heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"A group of my community will continue to be upon the truth, victorious over those who oppose them, and they will be like a vessel among eaters until the command of God comes and they are in that state.\" We said, \"O Messenger of God, where are they?\" He said, \"On the outskirts of Jerusalem.\" He said: And he also told me that \"al-Ramlah is the elevated place, because it faces west and east.\""],[17872,"The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe. I said, \"O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate for them that He sends them rain.\" He said, \"O God, give us abundant, wholesome, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday or so before we were rained upon.\""],[17873,"\"Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, may your father be for God's sake, and be careful.\" He said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against the Muḍar tribe, so I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of God, God has granted you and answered you and aided you, and your people have been destroyed. So supplicate to God for them that He sends them rain.' He said, 'O God, give us abundant, wholesome, fertile, swift, plentiful, widespread, immediate, not delayed, beneficial and not harmful rain.'\" He said, \"It was not even a Friday before we were rained upon.\""],[17874,"I said: O Messenger of God, which part of the night is most heard? He said: \"The last part of the night. Then prayer is accepted until dawn breaks. Then no prayer until the sun is at the height of a spear or two spears. Then prayer is accepted until the shadow stands as a spear. Then no prayer until the sun declines. Then prayer is accepted until the sun is the length of a spear or two spears. Then no prayer until the sun sets.\""],[17875,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I and the caretaker of an orphan, for him or for another, will be in Paradise like these two,\" and Sufyan gestured with his two fingers."],[17876,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The caretaker of an orphan, for him or for another, if he is God-fearing, will be with me in Paradise like these two,\" meaning the forefinger and the middle finger."],[17877,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying over a funeral when a woman came with a censer wanting the funeral, so he shouted at her until she entered the thickets of Madinah."],[17878,"We went out with a group of merchants selling cloth, and with them was a weigher who weighed for a fee. We arrived at Makkah, and the Prophet ﷺ bought trousers from them, and he said to the weigher: \"Weigh and give more.\""],[17879,"I saw my father clip his nails and then bury them. He said: My little daughter, \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[17880,"I heard my father narrate, and he had lived through the Jahiliyyah and Islam. He said: I set up traps for myself at al-Abwa'. A gazelle fell into one of the traps, and the rope flipped over. We went out following its tracks, and I found a man who had taken it. We disputed and took the matter to the Prophet ﷺ. We found him camped at al-Abwa' under a tree, shading himself with a leather mat. He judged it between us as two halves. I said: O Messenger of God, these are my traps on its leg. He said: \"That is it.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we are at a water source, and camels come to us thirsty, so we give them water. Is there any reward for us in that? He said: \"Yes, in every living being with a warm liver there is reward.\" I said: O Messenger of God, tall camels meet us with their udders tied, and we are hungry. He said: \"Say: O owner of the camels, O owner of the camels, three times. If he comes, then fine; otherwise, untie their udder straps, milk, drink, and retie their udder straps, and leave for the milk its channels.\""],[17881,"We were on a military expedition, and with us was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Mujashi' from Banu Sulaym. Sheep became scarce, so he ordered a caller, who announced that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A jadha'ah fulfills what a thaniyyah fulfills.\""],[17882,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: O Messenger of God, this is my brother Mujalid b. Mas'ud, so accept his pledge of allegiance for emigration. He said: \"There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but I will accept his pledge for Islam.\""],[17883,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with my brother Ma'bad to pledge allegiance for emigration. He said: \"The people of emigration have gone with what is in it.\" I said: Then upon what will you accept his pledge? He said: \"I will accept his pledge upon Islam, or faith, and jihad.\" Later I met Ma'bad, and I asked him, and he was the older of the two, and he said: He spoke the truth."],[17885,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon emigration, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rather, we pledge allegiance upon Islam, for there is no emigration after the conquest, and you will be among the followers in excellence.”"],[17886,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of the conquest and said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is my brother Mujalid b. Mas'ud, so accept his pledge upon emigration.” He said: “There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but I accept his pledge upon Islam.”"],[17887,"He said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night he departed from al-Ji'ranah until he entered the evening as a performer of 'umrah, then entered Makkah at night and completed his 'umrah, then left that same night and arrived at al-Ji'ranah as if he had spent the night there. Then when the sun had passed its zenith, he departed from al-Ji'ranah into the valley of Sarif until the road met the Madinah road at Sarif.” Muharrish said: “That is why his 'umrah was hidden from many people.”"],[17888,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah, then returned as if he had spent the night there.” That is why his 'umrah was hidden from many people."],[17889,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah from al-Ji'ranah, and I looked at his back as if it were an ingot of silver, and he arrived in the morning as if he had spent the night there.”"],[17890,"From 'Urwah: “Among those named as having witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi.”"],[17891,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, to a tribe of Hudhayl, and among the Muslims killed there was, from Banu Hashim, Marthad b. Abi Marthad.”"],[17892,"After Uhud, a group from 'Adal and al-Qarah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, there is Islam among us, so send with us a group of your companions to teach us the religion, recite the Qur'an to us, and teach us the laws of Islam.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent six of his companions, including Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. He mentioned the story, saying: “As for Marthad b. Abi Marthad, Khalid b. al-Bukayr, and 'Asim b. Thabit, they said: 'By Allah, we will never accept a covenant or pact from a polytheist.' They fought them until they killed them.”"],[17893,"From Ibn Shihab, naming those killed on the day of al-Raji': Marthad b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi."],[17894,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you want your prayer to be accepted, let the best among you lead you, for they are your delegation between you and your Lord.”"],[17895,"From Marthad, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah drew two lines in His book, then lifted the pen and wrote in one of them the creation, and wrote in the other what the creation will do.”"],[17896,"That the Prophet ﷺ was urinating, or he said: I passed by him while he had urinated, so I greeted him and he did not return my greeting until he finished his ablution, then he returned my greeting."],[17897,"That he greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting until he had performed ablution."],[17898,"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him while he was performing ablution. He did not return my greeting until he finished, then he returned my greeting and apologized to me, saying: 'Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I disliked mentioning Allah while not in a state of purity.'"],[17899,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with three people on a riding beast, and he said: 'The third is cursed.'"],[17900,"I heard Muhajir, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, say: 'I served the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for years, and he never said to me about anything I did, \"Why did you do it?\" nor about anything I left, \"Why did you leave it?\"' Ibn Bukayr said: 'This Bukayr mentioned in the hadith is my grandfather.'"],[17901,"From Mas'ud, the servant of his grandfather Farwah Abu Tamim, he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr passed by me. Abu Bakr said to me: \"O Mas'ud, go to Abu Tamim, your master, and tell him to send with us a guide who will take us by the most hidden route, and a camel and provisions.\" So I went to my master and told him, and he sent me along with a camel and a skin of milk. I came to them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray with Abu Bakr on his right. I stood behind them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pushed Abu Bakr in the chest, and we stood behind him.'"],[17902,"That the Prophet ﷺ named him Muta' and said to him: 'O Muta', you are obeyed among your people.' And he said to him: 'Go to your companions,' and he mounted him on a piebald horse and gave him the banner, saying: 'Whoever enters under this banner of mine is safe from punishment.'"],[17903,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu al-Najjar: Abu Muhammad al-Ansari, whose name is Mas'ud b. Aws b. Asram b. Zayd b. Tha'labah b. Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar."],[17904,"That a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ bought a Berber slave girl for two hundred dinars, then he sent her to Abu Muhammad al-Badri, one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who had been at Badr, and he gave him the Berber slave girl as a gift. When she came to him, he said: 'This is one of the Magians whom the Prophet ﷺ forbade, along with those who associate partners with Allah.' I narrated this hadith to a man, and he told me that Yahya b. Sa'id narrated to him that an uncle of his died in the Maghrib and he had been at Badr."],[17905,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Mas'ud b. Sa'd b. Khalid."],[17906,"From Ibn Shihab, in naming those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, then from Banu Zurayq: Mas'ud b. Sa'd b. Qays."],[17907,"Narrated by the Prophet, ﷺ , he said, \"The servant will continue to ask and request while he is wealthy until he shaves his face [i.e., until death], and he will not have any standing before Allah.\""],[17908,"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the Makhzumi woman who stole a velvet cloth: 'We will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That she be purified is better for her,' and he ordered that her hand be cut off."],[17909,"We heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that distressed us greatly, for she was from Quraysh. We came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to him, saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'That she be purified is better for her.' When we heard the softness of the Messenger of Allah's words, we went to Usamah b. Zayd and spoke to him, saying: 'Intercede for us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning this woman, and we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he stood among us as a preacher and said: 'O people, why do you insist so much regarding one of the limits set by Allah that has fallen upon a maidservant among the maidservants of Allah? By the One in whose hand is my soul, if Fatimah daughter of Muhammad had committed what this woman has fallen into, I would cut off her hand.' The people despaired, and he cut off her hand."],[17910,"When the woman stole that velvet cloak from the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ and he ordered that her hand be cut off, that weighed heavily on us. She was a woman of Quraysh, so we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and spoke to him, saying, \"We will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs.\" He said, \"Let her be purified; that is better for her.\" When we heard the gentleness in the Messenger of God's ﷺ words, we went to Usama b. Zayd and said to him, \"Will you not speak to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the matter of this woman, for we will ransom her for forty uqiyyahs?\" When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he stood up to give a sermon and said, \"O people, why do you keep pressing me regarding one of the prescribed punishments of God that has fallen upon a servant woman among God's maidservants? By Him in whose hand my soul is, if Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, had done what this woman did, I would carry out the punishment on her.\""],[17911,"\"I sent a sheep to the Messenger of God ﷺ and then went off on some errand. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent half of it back to them.\" I returned to Umm Khunas, his wife, and found meat with her. I said, \"O Umm Khunas, what is this meat?\" She said, \"This is the meat that your beloved ﷺ sent back to us from the sheep you sent to him.\" He said, \"Why do you not feed your dependents from it since the morning?\" She said, \"This is their leftover, and I have fed all of them. They used to slaughter two or three sheep, and it was not enough for them.\""],[17912,"Masruq b. Wa'il came to the Messenger of God ﷺ in Madinah at al-'Aqiq, embraced Islam, and his Islam was good. He said, \"O Messenger of God, I would like you to send to my people a man to call them to Islam and to write a letter for us to my people, that perhaps God may guide them by it.\" So he said to Mu'awiya, \"Write for him: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. To the Afnad of Hadramawt: regarding performing prayer, giving zakat, charity according to one's means, the animal kept at home for milk, and the fifth on hidden treasures; on well-irrigated land one-tenth. No combining, no separating, no shighar marriage, no tying a pregnant camel's legs to prevent her young from nursing, no keeping animals away from water to gather them for zakat, no driving them to the collector, no two camels tied together in one hobble. Whoever withholds zakat has committed usury. Every intoxicant is forbidden.\" And he sent Ziyad b. Labid al-Ansari to them. As for combining, it is not gathering flocks together; as for separating, it is not separating them to reduce the number; as for shighar, it is a man marrying off his daughter on condition that the other marries him to his daughter without a dowry; as for shinaq, it is tying a camel in its resting place; and as for ijba', it is selling fruit before it is safe from blight."],[17913,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"There is no ill omen, but good fortune may be in three things: a woman, a horse, and a house.\""],[17914,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I am away from water for a month and I have my family with me; may I have intercourse with them?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, I am away for months.\" He said, \"Even if you are away for thirty years.\""],[17915,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"You must be truthful, for it leads to Paradise.\""],[17917,"That his grandfather, Mazin b. Khaythama, and Hubayl b. Ka'b, one of the Banu Mazin, were sent by Mu'adh b. Jabal on the day he encamped between al-Sakun and al-Sakasik and fought until the people submitted as delegations to the Messenger of God ﷺ. \"And he established brotherhood between al-Sakun and al-Sakasik.\""],[17918,"Rifa'a b. Zayd came as a delegate to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he wrote a document for him in which was: \"In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of God, to Rifa'a b. Zayd. I have sent him to his people generally and to those who join them, calling them to God and to His Messenger. Whoever believes is in the party of God and in the party of His Messenger ﷺ, and whoever turns away has protection for two months.\" When he came to his people, they answered him. Then he traveled until he stopped at the Harra of al-Rajla'. He had not stayed long when Dihya al-Kalbi came from Qurayza, where the Messenger of God ﷺ had sent him, until when he was in one of their valleys called Shinan, with merchandise of his, al-Hunayd b. 'Uways and his father al-'Uways al-Duba'i—a branch of Judham—raided him and seized everything he had. Then a group of Rifa'a's people went to him, and among those who came was al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al. They met them and fought, and Qurra b. Ashqar al-Dala'i threw a stone at al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al, hitting his heel and bloodying it, and said, \"I am the son of Uthala!\" Then al-Nu'man b. Abi Ji'al shot him with an arrow, hitting his knee, and said, \"I am the son of Iqala!\" Hassan b. Milla al-Dabbi had accompanied Dihya al-Kalbi before that and taught him the Opening of the Book. They recovered what was in their hands and returned it to Dihya. Then Dihya came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him their news, and asked him for the blood of al-Hunayd and his father 'Uways. That is what stirred up Zayd and Judham. So the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Zayd b. Haritha and sent an army with him. Ghatafan, Judham, Wa'il, and those of Salman and Sa'd b. Hudhayl had already set out when Rifa'a came to them with the letter of the Prophet ﷺ. He stopped at the Harra of al-Rajla', and Rifa'a was at Kura' al-Ghamim, with him a horseman from Banu al-Dubayb, while the rest of Banu al-Dubayb were at Wadi Madariq on the side of the Harra."],[17919,"On the authority of his grandfather, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ: He commanded applying prepared antimony at bedtime and said, \"Let the fasting person avoid it.\""],[17920,"The Prophet ﷺ was at Qudayd when a man came to him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Have you eaten anything today for the day of Ashura?\" He said, \"No, except that I drank some water.\" He said, \"Then do not eat anything until the sun sets, and command those behind you to fast this day.\""],[17921,"Matar b. al-'Ala' narrated to me: my aunt Amina bt. Abi al-Sha'tha' and Qutba, her freedwoman, narrated to me that they saw Madluk, Abu Sufyan, and heard him say: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my freedmen and embraced Islam. Amina said, \"I saw that the part of the Prophet's ﷺ head that he wiped was black, while the rest of his hair had turned white.\""],[17922,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period saying to the people: “Say: There is no god but God, and you will prosper.” Some of them spat in his face, some threw dust at him, and some insulted him, until midday came. Then a young girl came with a bowl of water and washed his face and hands, and he said: “O my little daughter, do not fear poverty or humiliation for your father.” I asked: Who is this? They said: Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, and she was a radiant young girl."],[17923,"I performed Hajj with my father. When we were at Mina, there was a gathering. I said to my father: What is this gathering? He said: Around this Sabian (i.e., the Prophet). And there was the Messenger of God ﷺ saying: “O people, say: There is no god but God, and you will prosper.”"],[17924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When Allah decrees for a man to die in a certain land, He grants him a need therein.\""],[17925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “When God ﷻ decrees a servant’s death in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[17926,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He was asked, which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God alone, then jihad, then an accepted Hajj, which surpasses all other deeds as the distance between the rising of the sun and its setting.”"],[17927,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God and jihad in His path.” Then [the man’s thigh] trembled, and he said: Then what? He said: “Then a deed that is better than all other deeds, except like an accepted Hajj.”"],[17928,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in God and jihad in His path.” Then the questioner’s thigh trembled, and he said: Then what? He said: “Then a deed that is better than all other deeds, except like an accepted Hajj.”"],[17929,"While the Messenger of God ﷺ was speaking to his companions, he said to them: “A group of riders will appear to you from this direction; they are the best people of the East.” Umar b. al-Khattab stood up and went in that direction, where he met thirteen riders. He welcomed them, drew near, and asked: Who are the people? They said: A group from Abd al-Qays. He said: What has brought you to this land? Trade? They said: No. He said: Are you selling these swords of yours? They said: No. He said: Perhaps you have come seeking this man? They said: Yes. He walked with them, talking, until he saw the Prophet ﷺ and said: This is your companion whom you seek. The people threw themselves from their saddles; some ran, some jogged, and some walked until they reached the Prophet ﷺ and took his hand and kissed it, then sat with him. Al-Ashajj, who was the youngest of the group, stayed behind; he made the camels kneel, hobbled them, gathered the people’s belongings, then came walking slowly until he reached the Prophet ﷺ, took his hand and kissed it. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “You have two qualities that God and His Messenger love.” He said: What are they, O Prophet of God? He said: “Forbearance and deliberateness.” He said: O Prophet of God, is it a disposition I was created with, or a character I have acquired? He said: “Rather, it is a disposition you were created with.” He said: Praise be to God who created me with what God and His Messenger love. Then the people turned to some dates they had and began eating. The Prophet ﷺ spoke to them about the dates, naming this one such-and-such and that one such-and-such. They said: Yes, O Prophet of God, we are not more knowledgeable of their names than you. He said: “Yes.” Then they said to a man among them: Feed us from the remainder of the portion left in your bag. He brought them barni dates. The Prophet ﷺ said: “This is barni. It is among the best of your dates; it is a medicine with no disease in it.”"],[17930,"The Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest, and on his sword there was gold and silver."],[17931,"I heard my grandfather Mazidah al-Abdi say: “The Prophet ﷺ tied the banners of the Ansar and made them yellow.”"],[17932,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ that year, and they forgot it."],[17933,"I went out for Hajj and passed by people praying at a mosque, saying: This is the tree of the pledge of Ridwan, when the Messenger of God ﷺ accepted the pledge. I went to Said b. al-Musayyib and informed him. He said: My father told me that he was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ under the tree. He said: When we went out the following year, we forgot it and could not locate it. Said said: “If the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ did not know it, and you know it, then you are more knowledgeable.”"],[17934,"“I saw the tree, then I came to it later but did not recognize it.”"],[17935,"that his father came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “What is your name?” I said, “Hazn.” He said, “You are Sahl.” He said, “I will not give up its name.” Saʿīd said, “That harshness remains among us to this hour.”"],[17936,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his grandfather, “What is your name?” He said, “Hazn.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Rather, you are Sahl.” He said, “I will not change a name my father gave me.” So that harshness has remained among us ever since."],[17937,"When death approached Abū Ṭālib, and Abū Jahl b. Hishām and ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Umayya were with him, the Prophet ﷺ came to him and said, “O uncle, say ‘There is no god but Allah,’ a word with which I will plead for you before Allah.” They said, “O Abū Ṭālib, will you turn away from the religion of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, you do not guide whom you love, but Allah guides whom He wills, and He knows best those who are guided}."],[17938,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[17939,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Woe to the heels from the Fire.”"],[17940,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you must do it, then once,” meaning wiping the pebbles."],[17941,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a man who smooths the pebbles and dust where he prostrates: “If you must do it, then once.”"],[17942,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not wipe while you are praying, but if you must do it, then once,” meaning smoothing the pebbles."],[17943,"that he asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping during prayer, and he said, “Once, or leave it.”"],[17944,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to him regarding wiping during prayer, “If you must do it, then once.”"],[17945,"from the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “The Throne shook at the death of Saʿd b. Muʿādh.”"],[17946,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ observed iʿtikāf in a dome of palm leaves whose door was a mat, while the people were in the mosque.”"],[17947,"The ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was made of iron coated with silver. Sometimes it would be on my hand, and Mu'ayqib was in charge of the ring of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[17948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Fire is forbidden for the one who is gentle, soft, easygoing, and close to the people.\""],[17949,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[17950,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, when were you a prophet? He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[17951,"I heard a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Maymun b. Sunbad say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The uprightness of my community is through its wicked ones.\""],[17952,"Beware of our youth. Maymun or Mihran, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me that he passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"O Maymun – or Mihran – we are a household forbidden from receiving charity, and our freed slaves are from ourselves, so do not consume charity.\""],[17953,"I entered upon Umm Kulthum bt. Ali with something from the charity, and she said: A freed slave of ours called Kaysan or Hurmuz informed me that he passed by the Prophet ﷺ. He said: He called me, so I came, and he said: \"O so-and-so, we are a household forbidden from taking charity, and the freed slave of a people is from themselves, so do not consume charity.\""],[17954,"From al-Munaydhir, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was in Ifriqiya, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever says in the morning: 'I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet,' I am the guarantor to take him by the hand until I admit him to Paradise.\""],[17955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to al-Mundhir b. Sawa: \"Whoever prays our prayer, faces our qibla, and eats our slaughtered meat, that is the Muslim who has the protection of Allah and the protection of the Messenger ﷺ.\""],[17956,"That the Muslims said on the day of the Battle of Ma'una when the enemy surrounded them: \"O Allah, we cannot find anyone to convey our message to Your Messenger other than You. O Allah, convey our greetings and inform him of our situation.\""],[17958,"From al-Miswar b. Makhramah and Marwan b. al-Hakam, they said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions set out from al-Hudaybiyyah, numbering some one hundred and ten companions, until they reached Dhu al-Hulayfah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ garlanded the sacrificial animal and marked it, then entered ihram for Umrah."],[17959,"On the authority of his family, during the era of the Messenger of God ﷺ, he said: A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, my father has died and had obligated himself to walk to Makkah and to slaughter a camel, but he left no wealth. Should I fulfill it on his behalf by walking for him and slaughtering a camel from my own wealth?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Yes, fulfill it on his behalf, and slaughter, and walk. Do you not see that if your father owed a debt to a man and you paid it on his behalf from your wealth, would the man not go back satisfied? And God is more deserving that He be satisfied.”"],[17960,"He polished the sword of the Messenger of God ﷺ Dhu al-Faqar, and it had a silver pommel, rings on its scabbard, and a silver ring in its middle."],[17961,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever circumambulates the House seven times without engaging in idle talk therein, it is like the reward of freeing a slave.”"],[17962,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he went out one night, having delayed the Isha prayer until a short while—or an hour—of the night had passed, while the people were waiting in the mosque. He said, “What are you waiting for?” They said, “We are waiting for the prayer.” He said, “Indeed, you will continue to be in prayer as long as you wait for it.” Then he said, “Indeed, it is a prayer that no one among the nations before you ever prayed.” Then he raised his head toward the sky and said, “The stars are a safeguard for the sky; if the stars are obliterated, there will come to the sky what they are promised. I am a safeguard for my Companions; when I am taken, there will come to my Companions what they are promised. My Companions are a safeguard for my community; when my Companions are taken, there will come to my community what it is promised. O Bilal, give the call to commence.”"],[17963,"There was a military expedition with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and none of them had a mount except he would alternate riding it, apart from me. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ would dismount and then say to me, “Ride.” I would say, “I have strength,” until he did that two or three times, then he would say, “You are nothing but a water channel.” He said: “It became one of the names dearest to me.”"],[17964,"And the first of the emigrants to come to us was Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, one of the Banu 'Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy. I said to him, “What has the Messenger of God ﷺ done?” He said, “He is in his place, and his companions are following in my footsteps.”"],[17965,"When the pilgrimage season came, a group of the Ansar from Banu Malik b. al-Najjar performed Hajj, among them Mu'adh b. 'Afra' and As'ad b. Zurara, and from Banu Zurayq Rafi' b. Malik and Dhakwan b. 'Abd Qays, and from Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan, and from Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf 'Uwaym b. Sa'ida. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to them and told them the news of what God had chosen for him of prophethood and honor, and he recited the Quran to them. When they heard his words, they listened and their souls were at peace with his call. They recognized what they used to hear from the People of the Book of their mention of him by his description and what he called them to, so they believed him and had faith in him, and they were among the means of good.” Then they said to him, “You have known what is between the Aws and the Khazraj of bloodshed. We love what God has guided to and commanded you with, and we are for God and for you striving. We advise you to do as you see fit. Stay, in the name of God, until we return to our people and tell them of your affair and call them to God and His Messenger. Perhaps God will make peace between us and unite our affair, for today we are distant from one another and hateful to one another. If you come to us today while we have not reconciled, we will have no unified support for you. But we will appoint for you the next year's pilgrimage season.” The Messenger of God ﷺ was pleased with what they said. So they returned to their people and called them secretly, and told them about the Messenger of God ﷺ and what God had sent him with, and what he called to with the Quran, until there remained hardly a house among the houses of the Ansar but some people had embraced Islam in it without fail. Then they sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Send us a man from your side to call the people with the Book of God, for that is more like to be followed.” The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Dar, to them. He stayed among Banu Ghanm with As'ad b. Zurara, calling people secretly. Islam spread and its people increased, while they kept their calling hidden. Then As'ad b. Zurara and Mus'ab b. 'Umayr set out until they came to the well of Murri—or near it—and sat there. They sent for a group of the people of the land, and they came to them in secret. While Mus'ab b. 'Umayr was talking to them and reciting the Quran to them, Sa'd b. Mu'adh was informed about them. He came to them in his protective gear, carrying a spear, until he stood over them and said, “Why do you come to us in our homes with this solitary, unique, abandoned stranger, making fools of our weak ones with falsehood and calling them to it? I do not want to see you after this in anything of our protection.” So they went back. Then they returned a second time to the well of Murri—or near it. Sa'd b. Mu'adh was informed of them a second time, and he threatened them with a lesser threat than the first. When As'ad saw some softness in him, he said, “O son of my maternal aunt, listen to his words. If you hear something objectionable, reject it from him; and if you hear something good, respond to it.” He said, “What does he say?” Mus'ab b. 'Umayr recited to them: “Ha Mim. By the clear Book, indeed We have made it an Arabic Quran that you may understand.” Sa'd b. Mu'adh said, “I hear nothing but what I recognize.” He went back, and God had guided him, but he did not show Islam to them until he returned to his people. He called Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal to Islam and made his Islam public, saying, “Whoever doubts it, whether young or old, male or female, let him bring us something more guided than it and we will take it. By God, a matter has come in which necks will be struck.” Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal accepted Islam upon Sa'd's conversion and his call, except for those not mentioned. It was the first house among the houses of the Ansar to accept Islam entirely. Then Banu al-Najjar expelled Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and were harsh on As'ad b. Zurara. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr moved to Sa'd b. Mu'adh and remained with him, calling people and God guiding through his hands, until there remained hardly a house among the houses of the Ansar but some people had embraced Islam in it without fail. Their nobles accepted Islam, and 'Amr b. al-Jamuh accepted Islam, and their idols were broken. The Muslims became the most honored of its people, and their affair became sound. Mus'ab b. 'Umayr returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ and was called “the reciter.”"],[17966,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by Mus'ab b. 'Umayr when he returned from Uhud, and he stood over him and his companions and said, “I bear witness that you are alive with God. So return them and pray over them. For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no one greets them but they return the greeting until the Day of Resurrection.”"],[17967,"A boy from among us set out and came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I am going to ask you a question.” He said, “What is it?” He said, “I ask you to make me one of those for whom you will intercede on the Day of Resurrection.” He said, “Who ordered you to ask this, or who taught you this, or who guided you to this?” He said, “No one ordered me to do this except my own self.” He said, “Then you are among those for whom I will intercede on the Day of Resurrection.” The boy went away joyful to tell his family. When he turned away, he said, “Bring the boy back to me.” They brought him back, dejected, fearing that something had occurred. He said, “Help me on behalf of yourself by increasing in prostration.”"],[17968,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Indeed God, exalted is He, is gentle and loves gentleness, and is pleased with it, and assists with it what He does not assist with harshness. So when you ride these dumb beasts, alight them at their resting places. If the land becomes barren, travel swiftly upon them, for the land is folded by night what it is not folded by day. Beware of camping in the middle of the road, for it is the path of the beasts and the refuge of snakes.”"],[17969,"“Three slaves belonging to Banu Ghifar” witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ, and 'Umar used to give them one thousand for each man."],[17970,"The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith on the day of Hunayn and said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"The son of your mother.\" He said good to him."],[17971,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah b. Abi 'Amir b. Mas'ud b. Mu'attib b. Malik b. Ka'b b. 'Amr b. Ma'd b. 'Awf b. Qays b. Munabbih; his kunyah is Abu 'Abd Allah. His mother was a woman from Banu Nasr b. Mu'awiyah. He governed Basra for about two years, then he governed Kufa and died there in the year fifty. The first of his expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ was al-Hudaybiyyah."],[17972,"Al-Mughirah died in the year fifty."],[17973,"'Umar b. al-Khattab, when he first sent to Kufa, sent Abu 'Ubayd al-Thaqafi, Abu al-Mukhtar, and he was killed. Then he sent Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, and he remained five years, then he removed him. Then he sent 'Ammar b. Yasir, and he remained a year, then he removed him, and he sent al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, and he remained a year. Then 'Umar was killed. When 'Uthman was appointed, he sent Sa'd to Kufa, and he remained a year, then he removed him and sent al-Walid b. 'Uqbah, and he remained five years, then he removed him and sent Sa'id b. al-'As, and he remained five years, then he removed him and sent Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he remained a year. Then 'Uthman ؓ was killed and there was the fitnah. Then the first whom Mu'awiyah appointed over Kufa was al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, for nine years; then he died. Then he sent Ziyad b. Abihi, and he remained four years, then he died. Then he sent al-Dahhak b. Qays, and he remained three years, then he removed him. Then he sent al-Nu'man b. Bashir, and he remained four months. Then Mu'awiyah died and there was the fitnah. Then there was the affair of Muslim b. 'Aqil and his companions."],[17974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went to relieve himself, and I went with him with a water vessel, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was wearing a Syrian jubba. When the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished relieving himself, he performed wudu and wiped over the khuffs."],[17975,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said regarding the skin of a dead animal: \"Its tanning is its purification.\""],[17976,"'Umar consulted the people about the miscarriage of a woman. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said, \"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ decree a ghurrah, a male or female slave.\" He said, \"Will you bring me someone who testifies with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified for him."],[17977,"He tied his garments on and took with him a shield, then set off until they came to him. He said to the people, \"Throw me a burnus,\" and he sat on it. The 'ilj said, \"You Arabs, I know what brought you to come to us. You are a people who do not find in your lands enough food to fill you, so take, we will give you of food what you need. We are a people of Magians, and we hate to kill you; you are encroaching on our land.\" Al-Mughirah said, \"By God, that is not what brought us. But we were a people who worshipped stones and idols. Whenever we saw a stone better than another, we threw it away and took the other, and we did not know a Lord until God sent to us a Messenger from among ourselves. He called us to Islam, and we followed him. He commanded us to fight our enemy, those who abandoned Islam. We did not come for food, but we came to kill your fighters and take your offspring captive. As for what you mentioned of food, by my life, we did not find enough food to fill us, and sometimes we did not find enough water to quench our thirst. So we came to this land of yours and found in it abundant food. No, by God, we will not leave it until it is ours or yours.\" The 'ilj said in Persian, \"He spoke truth, and your eye will be gouged out tomorrow at al-Qadisiyyah.\" His eye was gouged out the next day; an arrow hit him."],[17978,"From Abu Firas, a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, who said: I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ wanting to marry. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Go to so-and-so and look at what they have, for that is more conducive to love. If you are pleased with her, I will marry you to her.\" So he went to them and greeted them and said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me. Did he command you to show me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So she unveiled herself from her curtain and said, \"Look.\" He said, \"I married her, and I have never married anyone dearer to me than her. I have married sixty women.\""],[17979,"Four descended into the grave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, one of them 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah used to be called the one with the most recent contact with the Messenger of God ﷺ. So I will be the last of the people to have contact with him."],[17980,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night on a journey. He said, \"Do you have water with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He dismounted from his mount and walked until he was hidden from me in the darkness of the night. Then he came, and I poured water on him from the vessel. He washed his hands and face, and he was wearing a woolen jubba. He could not get his forearms out of its tightness until he brought them out from the bottom of the jubba and washed his forearms and wiped his head. Then I reached to remove his khuff, and he said, \"Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure,\" and he wiped over them."],[17981,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. He performed wudu and wiped over his khuffs."],[17982,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he dismounted and said, \"Is there any water for purification?\" So I brought him water, and he washed his hands and face. Then he went to wash his forearms, but the jubba was tight on him—it was a jubba of the Roman-style cloaks—so he drew his arms out from under the jubba, pulling them out, and washed his forearms. Then I reached for his leather socks, and he said, \"Leave the leather socks, for I put my feet into them while they were pure.\" Then he wiped over the leather socks."],[17983,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you wipe over your leather socks?\" He said, \"Yes, for I put them on while they were pure.\""],[17984,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Do you have any water with you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" So he dismounted from his riding camel, then walked until he was hidden from me. When he returned, I met him with the water vessel, and he performed ablution: he washed his palms and his face. He was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he took his hand out from under the jubba and washed his forearms, then wiped his head. Then I reached for his leather socks to remove them, and he said, \"Leave them, for I put them on while they were pure.\" Then he wiped over his leather socks."],[17985,"I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night when he said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"I am al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah.\" He said, \"Hold on.\" So I held his she-camel for him, and he went off until I could no longer see him. Then he came back, and I helped him perform ablution. He rolled up his sleeves, but the sleeve of the jubba was tight, so he took his hands out from under it and performed ablution: he washed his hands, his face, and his forearms, and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"Will you not remove your leather socks?\" He said, \"I put them on while they were pure.\""],[17986,"The Prophet ﷺ tapped my back with a stick he had with him, and he turned aside, and I turned aside with him until we reached—I do not know where in the land. He made his camel kneel and dismounted, then went off until he was hidden from me. Then he came back and said, \"Do you have any water with you?\" I had a small water skin with me, so I poured water for him. He washed his palms and his face, then went to wash his forearms while wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he took his hands out from under the garment and washed his hands, his face, and his forearms, and wiped—Ibn 'Awn said: he mentioned something about his forelock and his turban, but I am not sure whether I got it right—and he wiped over his leather socks. Then he said, \"Do you need anything?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have no need.\" So we set off and came to the people, and Ibn 'Awf had already led them in the dawn prayer. He had prayed one rak'ah with them, and I went to alert him, but he prevented me. So we prayed what we caught up with and made up what we had missed."],[17987,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he went to relieve himself while wearing a Roman jubba. Then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, and he said, \"I put them on while I was in a state of purity—or while I had performed ablution.\""],[17988,"I helped the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform ablution, and he wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather, you forgot. This is what my Lord, Mighty and Exalted, commanded me.\""],[17989,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went to relieve himself. Then he gestured to me, and I brought him water. He was wearing a Syrian jubba that had no sleeves, so he threw it over his shoulders and said, \"Pour water over me.\" So I poured water over him, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. And this was a sunnah: for the traveler, three days and their nights; for the resident, one day and one night."],[17991,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he went out to relieve himself, and al-Mughirah followed him with a water vessel containing water. He poured water over him until he finished his need, then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17992,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the socks.\""],[17993,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17994,"That he poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from his vessel, and he washed his face. Then he went to wash his forearms, but his sleeves were too tight for his forearms, so he took them out from under the jubba—and it was made of wool—then he washed them and wiped over his leather socks."],[17995,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[17996,"He informed him that he went on the campaign of Tabuk with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ went aside to relieve himself, and I carried a water vessel with him before the dawn prayer. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned to me, I began to pour water from the vessel onto his hands. He washed his hands three times, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, then washed his face. Then he tried to pull his jubba off his forearms, but the sleeves of his jubba were too tight, so he inserted his hands into the jubba up to the elbows, then he performed ablution over his leather socks. Then he came forward, and I came with him until we found that the people had put 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf forward to lead them in prayer. The Prophet ﷺ caught one of the two rak'ahs and prayed the last rak'ah with the people. When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf said the salam, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to complete his prayer. That alarmed the Muslims, and they said subhan Allah excessively. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he turned to them and said, 'You have done well' or 'You have been correct,' expressing his approval that they had prayed the prayer at its time. Ibn Shihab said: Isma'il b. Muhammad b. Sa'd narrated to me from Hamza b. al-Mughira b. Shu'ba the like of the hadith of 'Abbad b. Ziyad, and he added: Al-Mughira said: I rushed to inform 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, but the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Leave him.' And he mentioned something similar."],[17997,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks."],[17998,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the tops of the leather socks."],[17999,"That 'Umar ؓ consulted them regarding a woman's miscarriage, meaning the stillborn fetus. Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said: I said to him, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding it that a slave or slave girl is due.' 'Umar said: If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that. I brought Muhammad b. Maslama, and he came and said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding it that a slave or slave girl is due.'"],[18000,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever sells wine, let him also butcher pigs.'"],[18001,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over the turban and the leather socks."],[18002,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his forelock."],[18003,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks, wiped the front of his head, placed his hands on the turban, and wiped over the turban. He did not mention al-Hasan."],[18005,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. He said: 'Stay back, O Mughira, and proceed, O people.' Then he went and relieved himself, and I brought him a water vessel. When he finished, I poured water from it for him. He washed his face, then he tried to take his hands out of a Byzantine jubba he was wearing, but the sleeves of the jubba were too tight, so he took his hands out from under the jubba and washed them, then he wiped over his leather socks, then he prayed."],[18006,"He has not relied on God who seeks ruqya or cauterizes."],[18007,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'He has not relied on God who cauterizes or seeks ruqya.'"],[18008,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'He has not relied on God who seeks ruqya or cauterizes.'"],[18009,"The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding the fetus: a ghurra, a male slave or a female slave."],[18010,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid mutilation."],[18011,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day of Hunayn stand over a slain man from Thaqif and say, 'May God distance you, for you used to hate Quraysh.'"],[18012,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished his prayer, he would say, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[18013,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: Al-Mughirah wrote to him that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say when he finished the prayer, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.' And he used to forbid idle talk, excessive asking, wasting wealth, withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not], disobedience to mothers, and burying daughters alive."],[18014,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ when he finished the prayer. He said, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[18015,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he would say, 'There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from his fortune against You.'"],[18016,"[He asked him] to write to him something he had heard from the Prophet ﷺ. He wrote to him: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'God dislikes for you three things: idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth.'"],[18017,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'God, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden you disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not]. And He dislikes for you idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth.'"],[18018,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, 'God, Exalted be He, dislikes idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth, and He forbade burying daughters alive, disobedience to mothers, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not].'"],[18019,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'God dislikes for you three things: idle talk, excessive asking, and wasting wealth. And He has forbidden disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding [what is due] and demanding [what is not].'"],[18021,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a group of the Ansar who were shooting at a pigeon. He said, 'Do not take a living creature as a target.'"],[18022,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he finished from a prayer, said: “There is no god but Allah.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[18024,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful.”"],[18025,"That he should write to him something from the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge from three things: from disobedience to mothers, from burying daughters alive, and from “withhold and give.” And I heard him forbid three things: from “it was said and he said,” from wasting wealth, and from excessive asking. And I heard him say: “O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18027,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said the taslim, said: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18028,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18029,"That he should write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade from ‘it was said and he said,’ excessive asking, wasting wealth, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and ‘withhold and give.’”"],[18030,"Muʿāwiyah wrote to al-Mughīrah: Write to me something you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying after the prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after his prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18033,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer, when he said the taslim: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18034,"That he should write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he wrote to him in his own handwriting: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say when he finished from the prayer: “There is no god but Allah, alone without partner; His is the dominion, and His is the praise, and He is over all things powerful. O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and no possessor of fortune can benefit from You his fortune.”"],[18036,"Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: If I saw a man with my wife, I would strike him with the sword. That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: “Do you marvel at Saʿd’s jealousy? By Allah, I am more jealous than Saʿd, and Allah is more jealous than me. And because of that He forbade immoralities, what is apparent of them and what is concealed. And no person is more beloved to Him than one who offers excuses, than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; because of that He sent His messengers as bearers of good tidings and warners. And no person is more beloved to Him than praise, than Allah, mighty and majestic is He; and because of that He promised Paradise.” The wording is that of the hadith of Abu al-Walīd."],[18038,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he struck my mount’s neck with his hand, then said: “Do you have water with you?” I said: Yes, this is a small waterskin of water with me. He said: “Leave it.” Then he dismounted and relieved himself, then came to me and said: “Do you want to relieve yourself?” I said: No. He said: “Then he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, and sniffed water three times, then washed his face three times. Then he wanted to take out his forearms, but he had on a woolen jubbah that was tight, and he could not take his forearms out of it, so he took his hands out from under the jubbah, then washed his forearms three times each, then wiped his head and wiped over the leather socks. Then we traveled and caught up with the people while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading them in prayer, and I wanted to alert him to the Prophet’s ﷺ presence, but he prevented me. So we prayed one rakʿah with him, then we made up the second.” The wording is that of the hadith of Hishām b. ʿAmmār."],[18039,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he concluded the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18040,"From al-Mughira b. Shuʿba: He wrote to Muʿawiya that the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he concluded the prayer, would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18041,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say after the prayer: \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner or associate. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is the Ever-Living who never dies. In His hand is all good, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, there is no one who can prevent what You have given, and no one can give what You have prevented. And there is no might or power except with You.\""],[18042,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say when he finished the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18044,"About the last thing the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, so he wrote to him that he would say after giving the salutation: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You,” after he had given the salutation to his right and to his left. He would give the salutation to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen, and to his left until the whiteness of his left cheek was seen."],[18045,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Beware of he-said-she-said, withholding and demanding, disobedience to mothers, burying daughters alive, and squandering wealth.”"],[18046,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say at the end of every prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18047,"From the Prophet ﷺ with this same hadith."],[18049,"He asked him to write to him something he had heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he wrote to him: When he prayed and finished, he would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner.” Ibn ʿAwn said: I think he said: “His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18051,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ would say at the end of his prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18052,"Did you hear the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything at the end of the prayer? Al-Mughira b. Shuʿba said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say at the end of the prayer: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18053,"Muʿawiya wrote to al-Mughira b. Shuʿba: Did the Messenger of God ﷺ say anything after the prayer? He said: He would say: “There is no god but God alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable. O God, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails nothing against You.”"],[18054,"The Messenger of Allah wiped over the top and the bottom of the leather socks. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 550)"],[18055,"A woman was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ who had struck her co-wife with a tent pole and killed her and what was in her womb. The Messenger of God ﷺ made her blood money the responsibility of the woman’s male relatives, and for the fetus there was a ghurra: a male or female slave. A man from the people stood up and said: “O Messenger of God, how can we pay blood money for one who did not eat, drink, cry out, or raise its voice?” He said: “This one speaks with the speech of a soothsayer. For it there is a ghurra: a male or female slave.”"],[18057,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade three things: undutifulness to mothers, burying daughters alive, and withholding and demanding (miserliness), and he prohibited he-said-she-said, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth."],[18058,"He heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ and then wrote to him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, exalted be He, dislikes for you three things: undutifulness to mothers, burying daughters alive, withholding and demanding, he-said-she-said, excessive questioning, and squandering wealth."],[18059,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he said, “O Mughīrah, take the water vessel.” So I took it, then I went out with him. The Messenger of God ﷺ went away until he was hidden from me, relieved himself, then came back wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He tried to take his hand out of its sleeve, but it was too tight, so he took his hand out from below it. I poured water for him, and he performed ablution as for prayer, wiped over his leather socks, and then prayed."],[18060,"He performed ablution for the Prophet ﷺ, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks and over the turban."],[18061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to relieve himself, and I followed him with a vessel of water. When he finished, I began pouring water for him. He washed his face, and he was wearing a Roman or Syrian jubbah whose sleeve was tight, so he took his hand out from below it, washed his forearms, and wiped over the turban and the leather socks."],[18062,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If the imam forgets and has stood up completely, he must perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness; but if he has not stood up completely, there is no forgetfulness upon him.”"],[18063,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said, “What will you do? He will not harm you.” I said, “Should I not kill Ibn Ṣayyād?” He said, “What would you do by killing him? If he is the Dajjal, you will never be able to kill him, and if he is not the Dajjal, what will you do with him?”"],[18064,"We used to pray the noon prayer with the Prophet of God ﷺ in the midday heat. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: “Cool the prayer, for the intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell.”"],[18065,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. The Prophet of God said, “Why do you ask about him? He will not harm you.”"],[18066,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about him—meaning the Dajjal—more than I did. He said, “He will not harm you.” I said, “They say that with him there is a river and such.” He said, “He is too insignificant to God for that.”"],[18068,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said, “Why do you ask about him? You will not live to see him. Indeed, he will not emerge until inheritance is no longer divided and no one is alarmed for booty.”"],[18069,"No one asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I did. He said to me, “What harm can he do to you?” I said, “They say that with him there is a mountain of bread and a river of water.” He said, “He is too insignificant to God for that.”"],[18070,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that with the Dajjal are rivers of water and mountains of bread. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\" I was among the people who asked about him the most, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"It is not that which will harm you.\""],[18071,"The Prophet ﷺ was not asked about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"O my son, and what will afflict you from him?\" I said: The people say that with him are food and drink. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[18072,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"And what are you asking me about him?\" He said: I said: The people say that with him are a garden and a fire, and food and drink. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[18073,"No one asked the Prophet ﷺ about the Dajjal more than I asked him. He said: \"What troubles you about him that you ask about him? He will not harm you.\" I said: They claim that with him are rivers and food. He said: \"He is more insignificant to Allah than that.\""],[18074,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group of people from my Ummah prevailing over the people until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[18075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be a group of people from my Ummah prevailing until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[18076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will always be a group from my Ummah (nation) who will remain steadfast on the truth, visible and apparent, until the Hour (Day of Judgment) is established.\""],[18077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There will not cease to be people from my Ummah prevailing until Allah's command comes to them while they are prevailing.\""],[18078,"I was with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ when a horse was presented to him. A man said: \"Carry me on this.\" He said: \"To carry a boy who has ridden horses despite his being unskilled is dearer to me than to carry you on it.\" The man became angry and said: \"I, by Allah, am a better horseman than you and your father.\" I became angry when he said that to the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I stood up to him, seized his head, and dragged him on his nose, and it was as if his nose was the spout of a waterskin. The Ansar wanted to exact retaliation from me. That reached Abu Bakr, and he said: \"It has reached me that some people claim that I will let them exact retaliation from al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. To expel them from their homes is closer to me than to let them exact retaliation from Allah's restrainers who restrain His servants.\""],[18079,"He was at the head of the Prophet ﷺ with a sword, and he was veiled. 'Urwah began to touch the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was speaking. Al-Mughirah said to him: \"You must stop your hand or it will not return to you,\" while al-Mughirah was wearing a sword. 'Urwah said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who is this?\" He said: \"This is your nephew, al-Mughirah.\" He said: \"O treacherous one, I have not washed my head from your treachery.\""],[18080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Al-'Anaqah does not create a foster relationship.\" We said: \"What is al-'Anaqah?\" He said: \"A woman who gives birth and the milk slows in her breast, so she breastfeeds her neighbor once or twice.\""],[18081,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ came to the tribe of Bani Fulan, and he ordered his legs to be noosed and he felt faint, standing.\""],[18082,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to a people's trash dump, and I brought him water. He performed ablution while wearing a Roman jubbah with short sleeves. He took his hand out from under that jubbah, washed his face, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks, then stood and prayed."],[18083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated in the trash dump of Banu so-and-so and said: \"O Mughirah, do you have water with you?\" He said: \"Yes, a waterskin of water.\" He was wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He performed ablution and wiped over his feet while wearing leather socks."],[18084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to a people's waste area and urinated standing."],[18085,"Al-Mughira said: We were astray, then Allah sent a prophet among us and guided us to His religion and provided us with a grain that is in these lands of yours. When we ate from it and fed our families, they said, \"We cannot bear to remain until you bring us to these lands.\" He said, \"Then we will kill you.\" He said, \"If you kill us, we will enter Paradise, and if we kill you, you will enter the Fire.\""],[18086,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted and relieved himself. Then he came, and I poured water for him from a water skin that I had with me. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18087,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went aside to relieve himself. When he finished, I brought him a water skin containing water and poured it for him. He performed ablution, and he had on a jubba with narrow sleeves, so he brought his hand out from under the jubba and washed his forearms and wiped over his leather socks."],[18088,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah hears the one who praises Him,\" he would say, \"O Allah, there is no one to withhold what You give, and no one to give what You withhold, and no one's wealth avails him against You.\""],[18089,"Al-Mughira stood and praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\""],[18091,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18092,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18093,"A co-wife struck her fellow co-wife with a tent pole and killed her. Judgment was given for her blood money [to be paid] by the killer's male relatives, and for what was in her womb, a ghurra. The Bedouin said, 'Will you make me pay for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out nor wailed? Should such a one be requited?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Is it rhymed prose like the rhymed prose of the Bedouins?' Abu Hudhayfah added in his hadith: And judgment was given for what was in her womb as a ghurra."],[18094,"A man of Hudhayl had two wives. One of them threw at the other a stone or a tent pole and caused her to miscarry. That was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ judged in it a ghurra. Her guardians said, 'How should we pay blood money for one who neither cried out nor wailed nor drank nor ate? Should such a one be requited?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Is it rhymed prose like the rhymed prose of the Bedouins?' And he judged its blood money upon the woman's guardians."],[18099,"While I was traveling one night, I came to a riding camel of a rider among the caravan. Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said: I said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'I am the Messenger of God.' So I held back until he caught up with me, and I kept pace with him. Then he dismounted and went aside to relieve himself. He said, 'Do you have water?' I said, 'Would it harm you?' He said, 'Then I brought him water, and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. We did not part until we had prayed the dawn prayer.'"],[18100,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ relieve himself, then perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks.'"],[18101,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Najran. They said to me, among what they said, 'According to what you recite, {O sister of Harun}, there was between Musa and 'Isa what you know.' He said: So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, 'Would you not have informed them that they used to be named with their names and with the names of the righteous who came before them?'"],[18102,"That he stood in the first two rak'ahs, and they glorified [to alert him], but he did not sit. When he finished his prayer, he prostrated twice after the salam. Then he said, 'Thus did the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[18103,"'The Prophet ﷺ recited the tashahhud when he raised his head from the two prostrations of forgetfulness.'"],[18104,"Yes, he is a man who comes after people have settled in their homes and taken their rest. It is said to him, \"Enter Paradise,\" and he says, \"O Lord, how can I enter it when people have settled in their homes and taken their rest?\" He said, \"Are you not pleased that you have what a king has among the kings of the world?\" He said, \"I am pleased, my Lord.\" He said, \"You have that and the like of that and the like of that and Sufyan (a narrator) interlocked his fingers five times and he said, 'I am pleased, my Lord.'\" He said, \"You have that and what your soul desires and your eyes find delight in.\" He said, \"I am pleased, my Lord.\" Moses said, \"O Lord, inform me about the highest rank of the people of Paradise.\" He said, \"Those are the ones you wished for and I will inform you about them. I planted their honor with my own hands and sealed it with my own seal and no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and it has not occurred to human heart.\" And the confirmation of that is the statement of Allah, \"No person knows what is kept hidden for them of joy as a reward for what they used to do\" (Quran 32:17)."],[18105,"I heard al-Mughira while he was delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a campaign. 'He went off for a need, and I followed him with a water vessel. He brought out his hands from a jubbah he was wearing that had narrow sleeves, and he brought them out from beneath it. He washed his face and hands, wiped his head, and wiped over his leather socks.'"],[18106,"It was said to al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, 'From where did the Prophet ﷺ have leather socks?' He said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi gave them to him as a gift.'"],[18107,"That he saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and wipe over his leather socks. I said, 'O Abu 'Amr, and from where did the Prophet ﷺ have leather socks?' He said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi gave them to him as a gift.'"],[18108,"'I was among those who dug the grave of the Prophet ﷺ.' He said: We dug a lahd for him. When the Prophet ﷺ was placed in the grave, I threw down the axe, then I said, 'The axe, the axe.' So I descended and placed my hands on the lahd. Al-Mughira used to say, 'I am the closest of people in time to the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[18109,"A man said in the presence of al-Mughira b. Shu'ba, 'May God bless Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets; there is no prophet after him.' Al-Mughira said, 'It is enough for you to say, Seal of the Prophets, for we used to be told that 'Isa b. Maryam is to come forth. If he is to come forth, then he was before him and after him.'"],[18110,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[18111,"The Prophet ﷺ urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks and sandals."],[18112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his military expeditions and dismounted to relieve himself. I brought him water for ablution while he was wearing a tight jubbah. He brought his hand out from under it, and I poured water over it. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18113,"I would sit rather than stand upright, but this is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with us."],[18114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ preferred to pray on a tanned fur or a straw mat."],[18115,"He walked with the Prophet ﷺ and came to one of those valleys. He entered it, relieved himself, then came out and performed ablution, removing his leather socks. When he put them back on, he later noticed an odor, so he repeated the ablution and wiped over the leather socks. I said, \"Did you forget, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said, \"No, rather you forgot. This is what my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.\""],[18116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather you forgot. This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[18117,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you forget?\" He said, \"Rather you forgot. This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[18118,"One day I ate, then came to the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was praying. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, he said, \"Whoever has eaten anything from this plant should not approach our mosque.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand.\" He gave it to me, and I placed it on my chest. He saw that it was bandaged, and said, \"Except for a valid excuse.\""],[18119,"The Prophet ﷺ noticed the smell of garlic and said, \"Who is this?\" Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba said, \"I adjure you, or I swear to you, O Messenger of Allah, to put your hand in.\" When he did, there was a bandage on his chest. He said, \"I see that you have an excuse.\""],[18120,"The last military expedition we went on with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he commanded us to wipe over our leather socks: \"For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night, as long as he does not take them off.\""],[18121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then prayed and placed me on his right side."],[18122,"I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his journeys, and we traveled until, when it was the time of pre-dawn, he went off to a secluded spot and hid from me. Then he came and called for water for ablution, wearing a Syrian jubbah with tight sleeves. He took his hand out from beneath the jubbah, washed his face and hands, and wiped over his leather socks."],[18123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate some food, and then the prayer was commenced. He stood up, having already performed ablution before that. I brought him water to perform ablution, but he scolded me. That distressed me, by Allah, so I complained to Umar. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah has been hurt by your scolding him, and he fears that you may hold something against him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I hold nothing against him but good. However, he brought me water to perform ablution, but I had only eaten food. If I had done so, the people after me would have done it.\""],[18124,"I heard Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah saying, \"If the Prophet ﷺ intended to pray until the soles of his feet or shins became swollen, it would be said to him, and he would say, 'Should I not be a grateful servant?'\""],[18125,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray until his feet would crack. It was said to him, \"Hasn't Allah forgiven you for your past and future sins?\" He said, \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[18126,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray until his feet swelled. He was asked about it and was told that Allah had forgiven his past and future sins. He replied, \"Should I not be a grateful servant?\""],[18127,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"My solace and comfort has been placed in prayer.\""],[18128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not revile the dead, for you would hurt the living.\""],[18129,"I heard al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah say: The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see them, supplicate to Allah and pray until it clears.\""],[18130,"The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see them, you must supplicate until it clears.\""],[18131,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, died, the sun eclipsed. The people said, \"It eclipsed because of Ibrahim's death.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said, \"O people, the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah. So when that happens, pray until it clears.\""],[18132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no one but has a companion from the jinn assigned with him.\" They said, \"Even you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Even me, but Allah helped me against him, so he became a Muslim, and he only commands me to good.\""],[18133,"That the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his socks."],[18134,"And he said, \"Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\""],[18135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the two liars,\" or he said, \"the liars.\""],[18136,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the liars.\""],[18137,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while thinking it is a lie is one of the liars.\""],[18138,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding the waist-wrap of Sufyan b. Sahl, who is Ibn Abi Sahl, and saying, \"Do not let your lower garment hang low, for Allah does not love those who let their lower garments hang low.\""],[18139,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taking hold of the cloak of Sufyan b. Sahl while saying, “O Sufyan, do not let your garment hang below the ankles, for Allah does not love those who let their garments hang low.” This is how Yazid b. Harun narrated it from Sharik, from ‘Abd al-Malik b. ‘Umayr, from Husayn b. ‘Uqbah, and he said: Sufyan b. Sahl."],[18140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The slogan of my Ummah on the Sirat will be: ‘Sallim, sallim (Grant safety, grant safety).’”"],[18141,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The slogan of my Ummah on the Sirat will be: ‘Rabbi sallim (My Lord, grant safety).’”"],[18142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise, and in Paradise they will be called the Jahannamiyyun. They will call upon Allah to remove that name from them, and Allah will erase it from them, when they have come out of the Fire.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[18143,"The Prophet ﷺ performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks."],[18144,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at his stopping place, and I followed him. He said, “Where did you leave the people?” I said, “I left them at such-and-such a place.” He made his mount kneel and dismounted, then went away and concealed himself from me. He stayed away for about as long as a man takes to relieve himself, then came back and said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” So I poured water over his hands, and he washed his face and his hands, and wiped his head. He was wearing a Syrian jubbah whose sleeves were tight, so he inserted his hand from beneath the jubbah and raised it up over his hands, then washed his hands and his face, and wiped his head and his leather socks. Then he said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then we rode on until we caught up with the people.”"],[18145,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over his forelock and his turban, and wiped over his leather socks,” and I was witnessing that."],[18146,"Two matters I will not ask anyone about after having witnessed them with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: wiping over the leather socks, and the prayer of an imam behind one of his subjects. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we stopped at a place. The Prophet ﷺ went aside to relieve himself. When he had finished, I brought him water. He performed wudu while wearing a jubbah with tight sleeves, so he took his hand out from beneath the jubbah, and he wiped over his forelock, over his turban, and over his leather socks. Then we came to the people while they were praying, and the people had put ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf forward as imam. We caught one rak‘ah with them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made up the other rak‘ah."],[18147,"I came with the Prophet ﷺ to ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf, and he stepped back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him, and we prayed what we caught up with, and made up what we had missed."],[18148,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. When it was the pre-dawn time, I urged on my mount and came along with him. He went off until he disappeared from me, then came back and said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “I have no need.” He said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” So he performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks. Then he went on until he reached the people while they were praying, with ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Awf leading them. He moved at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured with his hand to ‘Abd al-Rahman, meaning, “Stay in place.” So we prayed what we caught up with, and made up what we had missed."],[18149,"And (that) I should send blessings upon a man from my subjects, and I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiping over his socks and praying behind Abdur Rahman ibn Awf."],[18150,"“I poured water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face and his forearms, and wiped over his forelock, over the turban, and over the leather socks.”"],[18151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “wiped over his forelock, over his turban, and over his leather socks.”"],[18152,"He poured water from a small waterskin for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: He performed ablution and washed his face, wearing a narrow-sleeved Syrian jubbah. He brought out his hands and washed them, and wiped over his turban and his leather socks. We came to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf while he was praying, having already led them in one rak'ah. We prayed with him the rak'ah we caught up with and made up the rak'ah we had missed."],[18153,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks and the turban."],[18154,"I asked al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah: Did any of the Companions lead the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer besides Abu Bakr? He said: Yes. I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on such-and-such a journey. When it was the last part of the night, he struck the neck of my riding camel and turned aside, and I turned aside with him. He relieved himself, then said, 'O Mughirah, your need?' I said, 'I have no need.' He said, 'Is there any water?' He called for a waterskin or small waterskin, washed his hands, and washed his face. Then he went to uncover his forearms, but the sleeve of a Syrian jubbah he was wearing was too tight. He brought his hands out from under the jubbah and washed his hands, wiped his forelock, and wiped over the leather socks. He said: Then we reached the people when the prayer had been called and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf was leading them and had already prayed one rak'ah with them. I went to inform him, but he stopped me. We prayed the part we caught up with and made up what we had missed."],[18156,"The Prophet ﷺ poured water, washed his hands, then washed his face. When he wanted to wash his forearms, he was wearing a narrow-sleeved Syrian jubbah. He brought his hands out from under the jubbah, washed his forearms, then wiped his forelock, wiped his head and over his turban and his leather socks."],[18157,"He raised it to the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider walks behind the funeral procession, and the walker walks behind it, on its right, and on its left. The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and forgiveness and mercy are invoked for its parents.'"],[18158,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and well-being and mercy are invoked for its parents.' Sufyan did not raise it (to the Prophet)."],[18159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes in relation to it, and the child is prayed over.'"],[18160,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes, and the child is prayed over.'"],[18161,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: 'The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be where he wishes, and the child is prayed over.'"],[18162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection, and their owners are helped through them.'"],[18163,"I prayed beside the Prophet ﷺ and he smelled from me the odor of garlic. He said, 'What is this odor?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my chest was ailing, so I ate it.' The Prophet ﷺ did not find fault with it."],[18164,"My father- it is as if I can see him, long-haired and one-eyed- came to him. When he returned to us, we asked him: What did he say to him? He said: When I praised Allah and extolled Him, I said: 'We were the farthest of people in abode, the most severe of people in hunger, the greatest of people in misery, and the farthest of people from every good, until Allah sent to us a Messenger who promised us victory in this world and Paradise in the Hereafter. We have not ceased to recognize from our Lord, since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, success and victory, until we came to you.'"],[18165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ withdrew, and I withdrew with him. I approached him, and he said, “Do you have water with you?” I said, “Yes.” He washed his palms and his face, then began to wash his forearms while wearing a jubba. It was tight, so he brought his hand out from underneath the jubba and washed both arms, then wiped over his leather socks. Then he came to pray while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading the people in prayer. When they saw the Prophet ﷺ, they cleared their throats. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān started to step back, but he gestured to him, “Continue.”"],[18166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lagged behind, and I lagged behind with him. He relieved himself, and I brought him the water vessel. He performed ablution and washed his face. He intended to wash his forearms, but he was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba and washed his face and forearms, and wiped over his turban and leather socks. Then we came to the people while ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf was leading them in the dawn prayer. When he saw the Prophet ﷺ, he wanted to step back, but he gestured to him to continue his prayer. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I prayed one rakʿah behind ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf. When he finished his prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed another rakʿah for himself, and did not add anything to it."],[18167,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him a woman I intended to marry. He said, “Go and look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.” So I came to a woman of the Anṣār and proposed to her through her parents, informing them of the Prophet’s ﷺ statement. They seemed to dislike that. The woman heard that while she was in her chamber, and she said, “If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to look, then look; otherwise I implore you not to.” It was as if she considered it a grave matter. He said, “So I looked at her, and then I married her.”"],[18171,"I proposed to a girl from the Anṣār and mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Have you seen her?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then look at her, for that is more likely to create affection between you.”"],[18172,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ to make me the imam of my people. He said, “Lead the prayer as the weakest of the people would pray, and do not appoint a muʾadhdhin who takes payment for his call to prayer.”"],[18173,"I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He ordered a side of meat to be roasted for me, and he trimmed my mustache with a blade over a toothstick, clipping it. Then Bilāl came to call him to prayer, so he threw down the blade and said to him, “May your hands be dusty.” My mustache had grown full, so he trimmed it for me."],[18174,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and he ordered a stick to be brought, which was then sharpened. He took the stick and started scraping his own teeth with it, and then Bilal came to call him for prayer. He threw away the stick and asked, \"Why are his hands dirty?\" I said, \"It's because he had just fulfilled a promise and cleaned his teeth with a miswak (a teeth cleaning twig).\""],[18175,"I had Suhoor (pre-dawn meal) with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consisting of grilled meat. He was using a toothstick (miswak) and said, \"Your mustache has fulfilled its duty, O Mu'ghirah!\" Then, he trimmed it with a blade (sharp edge)."],[18176,"I sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah cut for me from the side of a sheep with a knife. Bilal called the Adhan for Fajr prayer, so he threw the knife and said, \"Why do his hands not have soil on them?\" My mustache was long, and I had fulfilled my vow, so he said, \"Shall I trim it for you?\" So he trimmed it on a siwak stick."],[18177,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad narrated to us, from Muḥammad b. ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from al-Mughīrah b. Shuʿbah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he went out on one of his journeys—and when he went to relieve himself, he would go far—told me to follow him with water for ablution. He came wearing a Syrian jubba, brought his hand out from beneath it, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[18178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he went to relieve himself, would go far. He went to answer the call of nature during one of his journeys and said, “Bring me water for ablution.” I brought him water, and he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[18179,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far. He said, “Follow me with water.” So I followed him with a water skin. He was wearing a Syrian jubba with tight sleeves, so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubba, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks."],[18180,"“I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, he would go far.”"],[18181,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"I have thought about a certain woman; will you permit me to see her?\" He said: \"Yes.\" And indeed I used to contrive for her among the trunks of the palm trees so that she would pass by me."],[18182,"Abu Bakr said: \"I do not find anything for you in the Book of Allah, and I have not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give a ruling for you in anything. I will ask the people this evening.\" When he prayed Zuhr, he turned to the people and said: \"A grandmother has come to me asking about her inheritance from her grandson or her granddaughter's son, and I have not found anything for her in the Book, nor have I heard the Prophet ﷺ rule anything for her. Has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning her?\" Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah stood up and said: \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.\" He said: \"Did anyone hear that with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah stood up and said: \"I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth.\" So Abu Bakr gave her a sixth. When it was the caliphate of Umar, the other grandmother came to him. Umar ؓ said: \"The ruling was only for someone other than you, but if you both come together, then the sixth is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers.\""],[18183,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. H. And Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us: Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. H. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us. H. And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us: Amr b. Marzuq narrated to us. They said: Malik reported to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Uthman b. Ishaq b. Kharashah, from Qabisah b. Dhu'ayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ asking him about her inheritance in the Book of Allah. Abu Bakr said to her: \"You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and I do not know of anything for you in the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so go back until I ask the people.\" He asked the people, and al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: \"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he gave her a sixth.\" Abu Bakr said: \"Is there anyone else with you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari stood up and said the like of what al-Mughirah said, so Abu Bakr carried it out for her. Then the other grandmother came to Umar b. al-Khattab asking him about her inheritance. He said: \"You have nothing in the Book of Allah, and the ruling that was given was only for someone other than you, and I am not going to add anything to the fixed shares, but it is that sixth, so if you both come together, it is between you, and whichever of you is alone with it, it is hers.\" The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abd al-Hakam."],[18184,"Al-Mughirah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah (a slave).\" Umar said: \"If you are truthful, bring someone who knows that.\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rule in it with a ghurrah."],[18185,"Al-Mughirah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah of a male or female slave.\" Umar said: \"Who will confirm you?\" Muhammad b. Maslamah testified for him."],[18186,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with a ghurrah.\" Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari testified for him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled with it."],[18187,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted something, he would distance himself."],[18188,"\"That he was with two men of his people who were disbelievers, and he killed them and took their spoils, then he came to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ disapproved of what he had done, and he offered him their spoils, but he did not accept it.\""],[18189,"\"That he accompanied a group of polytheists and found them heedless, so he killed them and took their property, then he brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He disapproved of what he had done and refused to accept it.\""],[18190,"Al-Mughirah said: \"I said to Umar: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in it with the ghurrah.' Umar said: 'If you are truthful, bring me someone who knows this with you.' Muhammad b. Maslamah said: 'I bear witness that the Prophet ﷺ ruled in the miscarriage of a woman with the ghurrah.' So Umar ؓ ruled accordingly.\""],[18191,"\"That he accompanied a group of polytheists and found them heedless, so he killed them and took their property, then he brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused to accept it.\""],[18192,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and informed us of what would happen in his community until the Day of Resurrection. He who grasped it grasped it, and he who forgot it forgot it.\""],[18193,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a journey and encamped, then he went to relieve himself. I followed him with a water vessel, and when he came back I met him and poured water for him. He performed ablution, and he had on leather socks, so he wiped over them, then he prayed the morning prayer.\""],[18194,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey, and al-Mughira was on that journey. He said: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to relieve himself, so I followed his tracks with a water vessel and cleared the way for him. He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18196,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."],[18197,"The Prophet ﷺ said: On the night of the cave, Allah commanded a tree and it grew in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah commanded the spider and it wove in front of the Prophet ﷺ, and He commanded two wild pigeons and they stood at the mouth of the cave. The young men of Quraysh approached, one man from every clan, with their staffs, clubs, and swords, until when they were about forty cubits from the Prophet ﷺ, some of them hurried to look into the cave. He saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so he returned to his companions. They said to him, \"What is wrong with you? Why did you not look into the cave?\" He said, \"I saw two pigeons at the mouth of the cave, so I knew that no one was inside.\" The Prophet ﷺ heard what he said and knew that Allah had protected him by means of them. So he supplicated for them, invoked blessings upon them, prescribed their recompense, and they were settled in the Haram."],[18198,"I sought permission to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between Makkah and Madinah. He said, \"Meet me tonight, even if you are exhausted,\" and I did not prefer anything over him until morning."],[18199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[18200,"Regarding what he witnessed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Tabuk, he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the expedition of Tabuk, and he wiped over his leather socks.\""],[18201,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, they both said: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, from Ma'mar b. 'Abd Allah b. Nadla, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever hoards is a sinner.\""],[18202,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\" Muhammad said: Sa'id used to hoard, and Ma'mar used to hoard."],[18203,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[18204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\" I said to Sa'id, \"You hoard.\" He said, \"Ma'mar used to hoard.\""],[18205,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[18206,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[18207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[18208,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me to announce among the people in Mina: \"The days of tashriq are days of eating and drinking.\""],[18209,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Food for food, like for like.\""],[18210,"\"Sell it, then buy barley with it.\" The boy went and took a sa' and some of a sa' extra. When he came, Ma'mar informed him of that, and Ma'mar said, \"Why did you do that? Go and return it. Do not take except like for like, for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Food, like for like.' And our food that day was barley.\" It was said, \"It is not like it.\" He said, \"I fear that it may resemble riba.\""],[18211,"I heard Ma'mar say: I used to saddle the mount for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, tonight I found looseness in my saddle straps.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I fastened them as I always fasten them, but someone who grudges me that wants to replace me.\" He said, \"Indeed, I will not do that.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his Hajj, he ordered me, and I took the razor and sharpened it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Ma'mar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has given you access to the lobe of his ear while the razor is in your hand.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I regard that as a favor and grace to me.\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then increase that.\""],[18212,"That the Prophet ﷺ, when he stood in prayer, would grasp his left hand with his right hand. He said: And I saw 'Alqamah do it."],[18213,"That the Prophet ﷺ would give salutation to his right and to his left."],[18214,"That he prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he said, \"Not of those who incurred anger, nor of those who went astray,\" he said Amin, lowering his voice with it."],[18215,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him land in Hadramawt."],[18216,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came with a leather strap around his neck. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this man and my brother were in a pit digging it, and the pickaxe fell and struck his companion's head and killed him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Pardon him.\" He refused. Then he stood and mentioned similar words, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Pardon him.\" He refused. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Take him away, for if you kill him, you will be like him.\" He went out with him until he passed by, then called out, \"Do you not hear what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says?\" He returned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you kill him, you will be like him.\" He said, \"Yes, I pardon him.\" Then he went out dragging his strap until he disappeared from us."],[18217,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man was brought with a leather strap being led. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the guardian of the slain man, \"Will you pardon him?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you take the blood money?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you kill him?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Take him away.\" He turned away from him, then he said, \"Come, will you pardon?\" similar to his first statement. The guardian of the slain man gave a similar answer three times. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the fourth, \"Indeed, if you pardon, he will bear your sin and the sin of your companion.\" So he left him. He said: I saw him dragging his strap."],[18221,"“I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he stood for prayer raise his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing he did that.”"],[18236,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever wrongfully usurps a man's land will meet God while He is angry with him.”"],[18237,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ bowed, he would spread his fingers, and when he prostrated, he would press his fingers together."],[18272,"I was a boy who could not understand my father’s prayer. Alqama b. Wa’il narrated to me from my father Wa’il b. Hujr, who said: “I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbir, he raised his hands, then wrapped himself and took his right hand with his left and placed his hands inside his garment. When he wanted to raise his head from bowing, he raised his hands, then prostrated and placed his forehead between his palms. When he raised his head from prostration, he raised his hands, until he finished his prayer.”"],[18273,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating on the ground, placing his forehead and his nose in his prostration.”"],[18280,"“The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution, rinsed his nose with water, and interlaced his fingers with his fingers.”"],[18281,"The Prophet ﷺ called for a bucket of water, drank from it, then spat into it."],[18282,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and it would not please me to have, in exchange for my face [i.e., my seeing him], the face of any man from the Bedouin Arabs. I saw him praying: he would say the takbīr when rising and when prostrating, and he would give salām to his right and to his left when he finished, until I could see the whiteness of his cheek from here and here."],[18283,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he began the prayer, raise his hands until the tips of his thumbs were level with the lobes of his ears."],[18326,"“I prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he gave salutation to his right: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of God and His blessings,’ and to his left: ‘Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.’” Mūsā b. Qays narrated it thus from Salama, who reported from ʿAlqama b. Wāʾil, and he added in the salutation “and His blessings.”"],[18379,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us and said, \"You claim that I am among the last of you to die, but I am the first of you to die, and you will follow me in bands, destroying one another.\""],[18380,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"Whoever goes to a soothsayer and asks him about something, repentance is withheld from him for forty nights; and if he believes what he said, he has disbelieved.\""],[18404,"I tried to be seen by the Prophet ﷺ at the mosque of al-Khayf. His companions said to me, “Move away, O Wathilah,” meaning, get out of the Prophet’s ﷺ sight. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Leave him, for he has only come to ask.” So I drew near and said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God. Give us a ruling about a matter we can take from you after you are gone.” He said, “Let your own self help you.” I said, “How can I do that?” He said, “Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, even if the muftis give you a fatwa.” I said, “How can I know that?” He said, “Place your hand over your heart, for the heart is at rest with what is lawful and is not at rest with what is unlawful. The scrupulousness of a Muslim is that he leaves the small matter for fear of falling into the major one.” I said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, what is bias?” He said, “It is when a man helps his people in wrongdoing.” I said, “Who is the greedy?” He said, “The one who seeks a livelihood from an unlawful source.” I said, “Who is the scrupulous?” He said, “The one who halts at what is doubtful.” I said, “Who is the believer?” He said, “The one from whom people feel safe regarding their wealth and their lives.” I said, “Who is the Muslim?” He said, “The one from whose tongue and hand people are safe.” I said, “Which struggle is most excellent?” He said, “A word of justice before a tyrannical ruler.”"],[18407,"I set out as an emigrant to the Messenger of God ﷺ. When the people came, some standing and some sitting, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not see anyone sitting without approaching him and asking, “Do you need anything?” He began with the first row, then the second, then the third, until he came near me and said, “Do you need anything?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “What is your need?” I said, “Islam.” He said, “It is better for you.” He said, “Will you emigrate?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “A desert emigration or a permanent emigration?” I said, “Which of them is better?” He said, “The permanent emigration is that you stay with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the desert emigration is that you return to your desert, and you must hear and obey in your hardship and ease, in what you dislike and what you like, and when others are preferred over you.” He said, “So I stretched out my hand to him and pledged allegiance to him.” He said, “He made an exception for me when I did not make one for myself, saying, ‘In what you are able.’” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ called for the expedition to Tabuk. I went out to my family and found my father sitting in the sun with his back to it. I greeted him with the greeting of Islam. He said, ‘Have you become a Sabian?’ I said, ‘I have submitted.’ He said, ‘Perhaps God will make it good for you and us.’ I accepted that from him. While I was with him, my sister came to me and greeted me. I said, ‘O sister, provide me with the provision a woman gives her brother going on a campaign.’ She brought me dough in a bucket, and the bucket was in a provision bag. I set out, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had already departed. I began calling out, ‘Is there anyone who will carry a man in exchange for his share?’ An old man from the Ansar called out to me and said, ‘His share is ours on condition that we carry him alternating behind us and that his food is with us.’ I said, ‘Yes, go with the blessing of God.’ I went out with the best companion. He gave me a mount beyond what I had stipulated and favored me with food besides what he ate with it, until God granted us spoils. I obtained some young camels and drove them until I came to him while he was in his tent. I called him and he came out and sat on a saddlebag from his camel’s saddlebags. Then he said, ‘Drive them away from you.’ I drove them away. Then he said, ‘Drive them toward you.’ I drove them toward him. He said, ‘I do not see your young camels except as noble.’ I said, ‘They are only your share of the spoils that I stipulated for you.’ He said, ‘Take your young camels, O son of my brother, for we did not intend anything other than your share.’"],[18408,"I said, “O Prophet of God, tell me.” He said, “If you wish, I will tell you what you came to ask about; and if you wish, ask.” I said, “Rather tell me, O Messenger of God, for that is more pleasing to my soul.” He said, “You came to ask about certainty and doubt.” I said, “That is it, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Certainty is what settles in the chest and the heart is at rest with it, even if the muftis give you a fatwa. Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt, for good is tranquility and doubt is unease. When you doubt, leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt.” I said, “O Prophet of God, may my father and mother be your ransom, what is bias?” He said, “That you help your people in wrongdoing. The scrupulous is the one who halts at doubtful matters, and the greedy for this world is the one who seeks it from an unlawful source, and sin is what causes unease in the chest.”"],[18417,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"It is not permissible for a woman to dispose of any of her wealth except with her husband's permission, once he has taken charge of her marriage.\""],[18418,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You will continue to be in good as long as there remains among you someone who saw someone who saw me and accompanied me.\""],[18422,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God ﷻ said: \"I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let My servant think as he wishes.\""],[18423,"I saw Wathilah b. al-Asqa' enter the mosque of Damascus and pray in it. He spat under his left foot and then rubbed it. When he finished, I said to him: \"Do you spit in the mosque when you are one of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.\""],[18426,"We entered upon Yazid b. al-Aswad to visit him, and Wathilah b. al-Asqa' entered upon him. When he saw him, he extended his hand and wiped his face and chest with it, for he had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ with that hand. Wathilah said: \"What do you think of your Lord?\" He said: \"Good.\" Wathilah said: \"Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say that God says: 'I am as My servant thinks of Me; if good, then good, and if evil, then evil.'\""],[18427,"He narrated to him, saying: I was in the Suffah, and they were twenty men. We were struck by hunger, and I was the youngest of the group, so they sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to complain to him of their hunger. He looked around in his house and said, \"Is there anything?\" They said, \"Yes, here is a piece of bread and some milk.\" He said, \"Bring it to me.\" He crumbled the bread into fine crumbs, then poured the milk over it, then carried it in his hand until he made it like tharid. Then he said, \"O Wathilah, call ten of your companions for me and leave ten behind.\" I did so. Then he said, \"Sit down. In the name of Allah.\" They sat down. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the top of the tharid and said, \"Eat from around it. In the name of Allah. Indeed, blessing comes to it from above it, and because it is replenished.\" He said: I saw them eating, picking between their fingers until they became full with satiety. When they had finished, he said to them, \"Depart to your place and send your companions to me.\" I stood up, amazed at what I had seen. Then he turned to the ten and commanded them similarly, and they ate until they became full with satiety, and there was still some left in it."],[18434,"A group from Banu Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we take captives and we practice coitus interruptus with them.\" He said, \"And you indeed do that?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"There is no soul that Allah wills to come forth from the loins of a man except that it comes forth, whether he wishes or refuses. So there is no harm upon you if you do not do it.\""],[18435,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the most wicked of falsehoods is for a man to claim descent from other than his father, or to lie against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or to lie about what his own eyes have seen.\""],[18436,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No man goes to a fortune-teller and asks him anything except that repentance is withheld from him for forty nights. If he believes what the fortune-teller says, then he has disbelieved in Allah.\""],[18437,"I met Wathilah b. al-Asqa' and said, \"You gave allegiance with this hand of yours to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Give me your hand so that I may kiss it.\" He gave it to me, and I kissed it."],[18438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has three children born to him and does not name one of them Muhammad has been ignorant.\""],[18439,"A man entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in it alone, so he moved aside for him. The man said, “O Messenger of Allah, the place is spacious.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, a Muslim has a right.”"],[18440,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He is not one of us who does not show mercy to our young and honor our elders.\""],[18441,"I went out intending to see 'Ali. It was said to me, \"He is with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So I went to him and found them in an enclosure of reeds. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn were gathered together under a garment. He said, \"O Allah, indeed You have made Your blessings, Your mercy, Your forgiveness, and Your good pleasure upon me and upon them.\""],[18450,"I heard my father say: 'Indeed he succeeds who purifies himself and mentions the name of his Lord and prays'—the throwing of wheat on the day of Fitr before the prayer in the prayer place."],[18451,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer in Makkah as two rak'ahs, the prayer of a traveler."],[18463,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Zuhr at al-Batha' two rak'ahs, then he traveled and prayed Asr two rak'ahs until he arrived in Madinah, where he completed it."],[18464,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Abtah, and the Prophet ﷺ was in a dome of tanned leather. He performed ablution from a stone basin, and Bilal came out with the leftover water. Then he prayed Zuhr and Asr while men, women, and donkeys passed in front of him from beyond the spear."],[18491,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever sees me, then he has indeed seen me, for Satan is not able to resemble me.”"],[18493,"“We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage, and we continued to pray two rak‘ahs until we returned.”"],[18494,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man praying who had let his garment hang down, and he cut it off from him."],[18495,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood."],[18496,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda and found Umm al-Darda in worn-out clothing. He said, \"What is the matter with you, O Umm al-Darda?\" She said, \"Your brother Abu al-Darda stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day, and he has no need for anything of this world.\" Abu al-Darda came and welcomed Salman and brought him some food. Salman said to him, \"Eat.\" He said, \"I am fasting.\" Salman said, \"I swear you must break your fast.\" He refused to eat until he ate with him, so he ate with him. Then he spent the night at his place. When it was night, Abu al-Darda wanted to get up, but Salman prevented him. Then he said, \"O Abu al-Darda, your body has a right over you, your Lord has a right over you, and your family has a right over you. Give every rightful one his due.\" When it was near dawn, he said, \"Now get up if you wish.\" So they both got up, performed ablution, and prayed. Then they went out to the prayer. Abu al-Darda approached to inform the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Your body has a right over you, just as Salman said.\""],[18498,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbid the earnings of a cupper and the dower of a prostitute."],[18502,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with two men from Banu 'Amir. He said, \"What people are you from?\" We said, \"From Banu 'Amir.\" He said, \"You two are from me.\""],[18506,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, and the dower of a prostitute. He cursed the woman who tattoos and the one who asks to be tattooed, and the one who consumes riba and the one who pays it."],[18512,"From the Prophet, ﷺ who said, \"Whoever sees me in a dream, it is as if he has seen me in wakefulness, for surely Satan cannot take my form.\""],[18517,"\"I drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at al-Abṭaḥ when the sun had declined from its meridian. Bilāl went out and called the adhān for the prayer.\""],[18518,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ in a red leather tent. He said: \"I saw Bilāl bring out his ablution water, and I saw the people rushing to that water. Whoever got some of it wiped himself with it, and whoever did not get any of it took from the moisture on his companion's hand. Then I saw Bilāl bring out a short spear and plant it in the ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out wearing a red ḥulla with his garments raised, and he prayed two rakʿahs with the people facing the spear. I saw people and animals passing in front of the spear.\""],[18519,"I was with my uncle in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon. He said, \"The affairs of my Ummah will continue to be righteous as long as twelve caliphs pass.\" He lowered his voice with this statement, so I asked my uncle who was in front of me, \"What did he say, uncle?\" He replied, \"O my son, all of them will be from the Quraysh.\""],[18520,"\"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at al-Abṭaḥ in a leather tent. Bilāl went out and called the adhān for the Ẓuhr prayer. Then he entered and helped him perform ablution, then brought out the leftover water in a small vessel. We crowded around it—some getting it with their hands and others being sprinkled with whatever water was destined for them. Then he entered and brought out a short spear and planted it between him and the qibla, while a woman and a donkey passed by. Then he called the iqāma, and the Prophet ﷺ came out wearing a red ḥulla, as if I were looking at the gleam of his shins. He led us in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, two rakʿahs each.\""],[18521,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying at al-Abṭaḥ, having planted a short spear in front of him, while a donkey and a woman passed in front of him.\""],[18536,"O Salama, \"Nothing remains of what I used to know except this prayer; and there is no soul that I would like to protect me from death, not even the soul of a fly.\""],[18537,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"I was sent and the Hour are like this from this; it almost overtook me.\""],[18549,"Abu Juḥayfah saw me carrying a garment to the bleacher, and on it was written ‘a devil.’ He forbade me, and this is the correct [version]."],[18569,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, “An ʿumrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj.”"],[18570,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “If a man gets up from his seat and then returns to it, he has more right to it.”"],[18585,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18586,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the people, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18587,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat it."],[18588,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18589,"A man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18590,"He saw a man praying in a row behind the people, not praying with the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18591,"A man prayed behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer, and he repeated it."],[18592,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying alone in a row, so he ordered him and he repeated the prayer."],[18593,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18594,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who prays alone behind the row. He said: 'He should repeat it.'"],[18595,"A man prayed alone behind the rows, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him and he repeated it."],[18596,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18598,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18599,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18600,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Do not use animals as pulpits.” And I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The worst of these beasts of prey is the fox.”"],[18601,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ in a row by myself, and when he finished he said: “Repeat the prayer.”"],[18602,"I prayed behind the row, so he ordered me and I repeated my prayer."],[18603,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered him to repeat it."],[18604,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone behind the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18605,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left and there was a man praying alone behind the people. He said, \"O you who are praying alone, why don't you join them and enter with them, or bring someone to stand beside you if the place becomes tight for you? Repeat your prayer, for indeed, there is no prayer for you.\""],[18606,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18607,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was praying behind the row by myself, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."],[18608,"A man prayed alone behind the row, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[18609,"I prayed in a row by myself behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."],[18610,"I heard Wabisa b. Ma'bad say: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about everything, even about the dirt that is under the fingernails, and he said: “Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt.”"],[18611,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ when he bowed in his prayer: if water had been poured on his back, it would have settled there."],[18612,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he said, 'Let those present convey to those who are absent.'"],[18613,"That he heard Wābisa b. Maʿbad, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, say: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about righteousness and sin, and he said, 'O Wābisa, you have come to ask me about righteousness and sin.' I said, 'Indeed, by the One who sent you with the truth, it is for this that I came to ask you.' He said, 'Righteousness is that which your heart feels at ease with, and sin is that which wavers in your heart, even if people give you rulings about it.'"],[18614,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, intending not to leave anything of righteousness and sin without asking him about it. I went to him while he was among a group of Muslims around him, and I began to step over them to draw near to him. Some of them rebuked me, saying, 'Step back, O Wābisa, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said, 'I want to draw near to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave Wābisa; come near me, O Wābisa.' So he brought me close until I stood before him. Then he said, 'Will you ask me, or shall I inform you?' I said, 'No, rather you inform me.' He said, 'You have come to ask about righteousness and sin.' I said, 'Yes.' He gathered his fingertips and began tapping them on my chest, and said, 'Righteousness is that which the soul feels at ease with and the heart feels at ease with, and sin is that which wavers in the soul and hesitates in the chest, even if people give you rulings about it, whatever rulings they give you.'"],[18615,"The Prophet ﷺ sent al-Walīd b. ʿUqba b. Abī Muʿayṭ to Banū al-Muṣṭaliq as a collector of zakāt."],[18616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Some people from the people of Paradise will go to some people from the people of the Fire and say, \"Why did you enter the Fire? By Allah, we did not enter Paradise except because of what we learned from you.\" They will say, \"We used to say and not act.\"'"],[18617,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe their heads and supplicate for them. I was brought to him while I had been perfumed with khalūq, and he did not wipe my head, nor touch me, and nothing prevented him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khalūq. So he did not touch me because of the khalūq."],[18619,"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children to him, and he would wipe their heads and supplicate for blessing for them. I was brought to him while I was perfumed with khalūq, and he did not wipe my head, and nothing prevented him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khalūq. So he did not wipe my head because of the khalūq. Abu al-Qāsim said: This is how Zayd b. Abī al-Zarqāʾ narrated it, from Jaʿfar, from Thābit b. al-Ḥajjāj, from ʿAbdallāh al-Hamdānī, from Abū Mūsā, from al-Walīd b. ʿUqba; but the correct chain is from ʿAbdallāh al-Hamdānī, who is Abū Mūsā, from al-Walīd b. ʿUqba."],[18620,"I had leprosy, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for me, and I was cured of it."],[18622,"I said, 'O Muhammad, how does the one who comes to you come to you?' meaning Jibrīl ﷺ . The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He comes to me from the sky; his two wings are pearls, and the soles of his feet are green.'"],[18623,"Musaylima, Ibn Shighāf, and Ibn al-Nawwāḥa sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We arrived before him, and the two of them preceded me in speaking, for they were older than me. They pronounced the testimony of faith, then said, 'We bear witness that you are a prophet, and that Musaylima is after you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you say, O boy?' I said, 'I bear witness to what you bore witness to, and I reject what you rejected.' He said, 'Then I bear witness, as many as the grains of dust of the world, that Musaylima is a liar.' Then he said, 'Seize them both.' So they were seized, and he ordered that they be taken to the house of Kaysān. Then a man from his Companions interceded for them, and he released them."],[18624,"From Wāqid, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, 'Whoever obeys Allah, Exalted is He, has remembered Him, even if his prayer, fasting, and recitation of the Qur'an are little. And whoever disobeys Allah has not remembered Him, even if his prayer, fasting, and recitation of the Qur'an are abundant.'"],[18626,"The Prophet ﷺ would turn away once to his right and once to his left."],[18627,"“I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and I saw him turn away from both of his sides.” This is Muslim's wording, and Sulayman b. Harb said: “He would turn away to his right and to his left.”"],[18628,"“I was with the Prophet ﷺ one day, and he used to lead us in prayer, and he would turn away to his right and to his left, from both of his sides.”"],[18629,"The Prophet ﷺ would turn away when he had prayed, to his right and to his left, meaning the taslīm."],[18630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lead us in prayer and then turn away to his right and to his left."],[18631,"“The Prophet ﷺ would lead us and he would turn away on both of his sides.”"],[18632,"“The Prophet ﷺ would hold his left with his right in prayer.”"],[18633,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ stand to pray. He said: “I saw him when he placed one hand over the other, the right over the left.”"],[18634,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place one of his hands over the other in prayer.”"],[18635,"“The Prophet ﷺ would lead us, and he would take his left with his right.”"],[18636,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, food that I do not leave except out of scrupulousness.” He said: “Let nothing creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.”"],[18637,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the food of the Christians. He said: “Let no food resemble Christianity in your chest.” He said: “And I saw him placing one of his hands over the other.”"],[18638,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a man came to him and said, \"There is food from which I refrain out of scruple; may I eat it?\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18639,"I heard the Prophet of God ﷺ when a man asked him, saying, \"Among foods there is a food from which I refrain out of scruple.\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18640,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, I leave food because of some purpose in my soul concerning it.\" He said, \"Let not anything creep into your soul or your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18641,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"We leave some food out of scruple from it.\" He said, \"Let not any food creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18642,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about the food of the Christians. He said, \"Let not any food creep into your chest that resembles Christianity.\""],[18643,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ that he was asked if there is any time during the day that prevents us from performing prayers. He answered, \"No, except during the rising and setting of the sun. For it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets between the two horns of Satan.\""],[18652,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"God will torture those who torture people in this world.\""],[18670,"Some people in Basra in the time of Ziyad used to take dirhams for dinars on credit. A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Hisham b. 'Amir al-Ansari stood and said: 'Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling gold for silver on credit, and he informed us that that is riba.'"],[18707,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever is afflicted by bloodshed or injury, he is between one of three options. If he desires a fourth, then restrain him: between exacting retaliation, pardoning, or taking the blood money. If he takes one and then transgresses after that, for him is the Fire, abiding eternally therein forever."],[18708,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The most insolent of people against God is a man who kills someone other than his killer, or seeks revenge for a blood of the pre-Islamic era among the people of Islam, and one who makes his eyes see in sleep what they did not see.\""],[18710,"Abu Shuraih b. 'Amr al-Khuza'i—who was among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ—informed him that on the day of the conquest, Banu Ka'b encountered a man from Hudhayl whom they were seeking for a blood feud from the pre-Islamic era. He was in the sacred precinct, heading toward the Messenger of God ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, but they killed him. When the news of his killing reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, he became angrier than he had ever been. Banu Ka'b went to Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ seeking their intercession with the Prophet ﷺ. When evening came, he stood before the people, praised God as He deserves, then said: To proceed: God made Makkah sacred, and people did not make it sacred. God made it permissible for me only for an hour of the day yesterday, then it became sacred as God made it sacred. The most hostile of people against God are three: a man who kills within it, a man who kills someone other than his killer for a pre-Islamic blood feud, and by God, I will certainly pay the blood money for this man whom you killed. Abu Shuraih said: So the Messenger of God ﷺ paid his blood money."],[18715,"I took the hand of the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of Sacrifice and went with him to the house. I said to the servant girl: Feed us from the meat of your sacrificial animal. He said: \"It is not a sacrificial animal; it is only a sheep for meat. The sacrificial animal is only after the prayer.\" I said: O Messenger of God, we have a fosterling of ours, a jadha'ah. Should I sacrifice it? He said: \"Yes, but it will not suffice for anyone after you.\""],[18717,"He slaughtered a sheep early, then mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered our young sheep early. He asked: \"Before the prayer?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"That is a sheep for meat.\" He said: I have a jadha'ah that is dearer to me than a musinnah; will it suffice for me? He said: \"Yes, but it will never suffice for anyone after you.\""],[18718,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ led the prayer. Then I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: I went out with my sacrificial animal to the prayer place and slaughtered it before the prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Sacrifice another instead.\" I looked for one among the goats but did not find any, so the Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to sacrifice a jadha' from the sheep."],[18719,"I met my maternal uncle, and with him was a banner. I said, \"Where are you going?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him—to strike his neck and kill him.\""],[18720,"My maternal uncle, Abu Burdah, passed by me with a flag. I said, \"Where to?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife—I will bring his head.\""],[18721,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the tribes to supplicate for them, and he left a tribe without coming to them. They found that objectionable, so they searched a companion of theirs and found a necklace in the pack-saddle of a man among them; he had stolen it. So they returned it, and he came to them and prayed over them."],[18722,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"The world will not pass away until it belongs to a base son of a base man.\""],[18723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No servant of my community sends blessings upon me with a sincere heart but Allah will bless him ten times for it, record ten good deeds for him, raise him ten degrees by it, and erase ten bad deeds from him.\""],[18724,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"It is not lawful for anyone to strike anyone more than ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18725,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, \"No one is to be lashed more than ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18726,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"No lashing above ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No one is lashed ten lashes except in a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah.\""],[18728,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"A man from the soothsayers will come forth who will study the Quran with a study no one after him will achieve.\""],[18729,"It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which earning is best?\" He said, \"A man's work with his own hand.\""],[18730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best earning of a man is his child, and every righteous sale.\""],[18731,"I was walking with the Prophet ﷺ on one of the roads of Madinah, and he passed by some food. He inserted his hand [into it] and pulled out on his hand some bad food. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever cheats is not one of us.\""],[18732,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Drink in moderation, and do not get intoxicated.\""],[18733,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen, and he invited him to Islam, so he accepted Islam. He wiped over his head and prayed for blessing for him, and he lodged him with Yazid b. Abi Sufyan. Then when Abu Bakr equipped the army for Syria, he went out with them and did not return."],[18734,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass by a man who had food in a container. He looked at it and said: \"You have cheated him. Whoever cheats us is not one of us.\""],[18735,"I heard Abu al-Hamra' say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come to the door of Ali and Fatimah for six months, saying: \"Allah only desires to take away impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly.\""],[18736,"From Abu al-Hamra', the servant of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When I was taken on the Night Journey to heaven, I entered Paradise and saw on the leg of the Throne written: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I supported him with Ali and aided him.\""],[18737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the house of Habbar b. al-Aswad and heard the sound of singing. He said: \"What is this?\" It was said: A wedding. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying, repeating: \"This is marriage, not fornication.\""],[18738,"Habbar married off his daughter, and at her wedding he beat the bellows and the sieve. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard that and said: \"What is this?\" They said: Habbar married off his daughter, and at her wedding he beat the bellows and the sieve. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Proclaim the marriage, proclaim the marriage. This is marriage, not fornication.\""],[18739,"He said to Ma'iz b. Malik: Go to the Prophet ﷺ and tell him your story. So he came to him and told him, but the Prophet ﷺ turned away from him several times. He kept repeating that to the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ sent to his people and said: \"Does he have insanity?\" They said: No. He said: \"Is he a virgin or a previously married man?\" They said: Rather, a previously married man. He said: So he ordered that he be stoned. He said: \"Woe to you, O Hazzal! If you had covered him with your cloak, it would have been better for you.\""],[18740,"There was a slave girl who tended sheep for her family. A man from among us called Ma'iz b. Malik came to her and had intercourse with her. She came and told my grandfather Hazzal. So my grandfather Hazzal began encouraging him to confess before the Prophet ﷺ, saying: Woe to you! If you do not do so, Allah will send down upon His Messenger [a revelation] informing him of your affair. He did not stop until Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was fornication. He turned away from him three or four times. Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered that he be stoned. He said: A man faced him with the jawbone of a camel and struck his shin with it, knocking him down, and they stoned him until they killed him while he was calling for help from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Indeed, if he had come to me, he would not have returned to that.\" Then he said to the one who encouraged him: \"Woe to you, O Hazzal! If you had covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you,\" and he struck his hand on the knee of Hazzal."],[18741,"He informed me, saying: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina on a she-camel, and behind him rode al-Fadl b. Abbas.\""],[18742,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ while I was riding behind my father, and he was on his she-camel al-Adba' on the Day of Sacrifice, with the people around him. I said to my father: What is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying? He said: He is saying: \"Throw the pebbles like the small stones used for throwing.\""],[18743,"I was riding behind my father, and I saw the Prophet ﷺ on a camel saying: \"Labbayk, for Hajj and Umrah together.\""],[18744,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The beggar has a right even if he comes on a horse.”"],[18745,"A man from my people gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some dates as a gift. He said: “What kind of dates are these?” The man said: “Juzami.” He said: “O Allah, bless the Juzami.”"],[18746,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying on his mount, facing towards the east.”"],[18747,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on his she-camel, saying: “Beware of treachery, for it is an evil inner characteristic. Beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of miserliness, for it destroyed those before you; it led them to shed their blood and sever their ties of kinship.”"],[18748,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.”"],[18749,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.”"],[18750,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on a red she-camel.”"],[18751,"The gathering brought us together in Tripoli, among us Hubayb al-Ghifari and Amr b. al-As, both companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Amr said: “The most virtuous is Ramadan.” Al-Ghifari said: “We do not differentiate between the make-up of Ramadan; Allah only said: ‘a number of other days.’”"],[18752,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lets his garment drag out of pride, he will be dragged into the Fire.”"],[18753,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever lets his garment drag out of pride, he will be dragged into the Fire,” meaning his lower garment."],[18754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to my people of Aslam and said: “Command your people to fast this day, the day of Ashura. Whoever among them you find has already eaten in the first part of his day, let him fast the rest of it.”"],[18755,"“Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani died in the year seventy-five.”"],[18756,"I said, O Messenger of God, give me a ruling concerning the luqatah (found property). He said, \"What is found on a well-traveled road or an inhabited one, announce it for a year; if you do not find its owner, it is yours. And what you find in an uninhabited village or a road that is not well-traveled, on it is the khums (one-fifth).\" I said, O Messenger of God, give me a ruling concerning my bow. He said, \"Eat whatever your bow returns to you.\" I said, \"What if it disappears from me?\" He said, \"Even if it disappears from you, after you have not seen in it the trace of an arrow or a blade.\""],[18757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs."],[18758,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, that the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18759,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs."],[18760,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, from Abu Tha'labah, who said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the snatched kill (al-khatfah), the plundered property (al-nuhbah), the animal that is tied up and shot (al-mujaththamah), and every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18761,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ forbidding every predator possessing fangs."],[18762,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18763,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ declaring forbidden the flesh of domestic donkeys and every predator possessing fangs."],[18764,"Every predator possessing fangs was declared forbidden."],[18765,"He told him, he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the killing of any toothed animal from the wild beasts.\""],[18766,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ \"forbade eating every predator possessing fangs.\""],[18767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ declared forbidden the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[18768,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every predator possessing fangs and the flesh of domestic donkeys."],[18769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that pregnant women be had intercourse with, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18770,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding every beast of prey with fangs."],[18771,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18772,"He heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating every beast of prey with fangs.'"],[18773,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every beast of prey with fangs."],[18774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of every beast of prey with fangs."],[18775,"He informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding every beast of prey with fangs."],[18776,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the vessels of the idolaters. He said: 'Eat in them, drink, and cook, if you find no alternative.' He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with fangs."],[18777,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the enemy and we need their vessels.' He said: 'Avoid them as much as you can. If you find nothing else, wash them and eat and drink in them.'"],[18778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade in the year of Khaybar the meat of domestic donkeys, and that a pregnant woman from the captives be had intercourse with until she gives birth, and every beast of prey with fangs."],[18779,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who raised his gaze and lowered it, then said: 'A small calamity.' Abu Tha'labah said: 'A small calamity of good or a small calamity of evil?' He said: 'A small calamity of good.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land with game. What is lawful for us from it and what is forbidden to us?' He said: 'The domestic donkey and every beast of prey with fangs are forbidden. Whatever your bow and your trained dog bring back to you is lawful for you.' Then he asked him about something concerning the People of the Book and their vessels. He said: 'If you find an alternative to them, do not approach them. If you need them, wash them, then eat and drink in them.'"],[18780,"He heard Abu Tha'labah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book and we eat with them in their vessels, and our land is a land of game where we hunt with the bow, the trained dog, and the dog that is not trained. Tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.' He said: 'As for what you mentioned, that you are in the land of the People of the Book and eat in their vessels: if you find vessels other than theirs, do not eat in them; if you find nothing else, wash them and eat in them. As for what you mentioned about the matter of game: whatever you hunt with your bow and mention the name of Allah over it, eat it. As for what your dog that is not trained catches, if you reach it while it is still alive and slaughter it, eat it; if you do not reach it before it dies, do not eat it. As for what your trained dog catches, eat what it holds back for you, and mention the name of Allah over it.'"],[18781,"On the authority of Abu Tha'laba, he raised it: Mu'awiya once [raised it] and another time did not raise it: \"Indeed, Allah will not let this Ummah be unable [to hold out] for half a day. And when you see the Levant as a man's dining table and his household, then at that point Constantinople will be conquered.\""],[18782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The jinn are of three types: a type that has wings and flies through the air, a type that are snakes, and a type that settles and travels.\""],[18783,"He raided Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they were struck by hunger. They found domestic donkeys there, so the people slaughtered some of them. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, who called out among the people: \"The meat of domestic donkeys is not lawful for anyone who bears witness that I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So they overturned their pots with what was in them. They found onions and garlic in their gardens and ate from them while they were hungry, and they suffered. When the people went to the mosque, the smell of the mosque was onions and garlic. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this foul plant should not come near us.\""],[18784,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the one who finds his game after three [days]: \"He may eat it unless it has become putrid.\""],[18785,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"My Lord will never be unable to delay my Ummah for half a day.\""],[18786,"He raided Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the people were hungry. He found domestic donkeys there, so the people slaughtered some of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed, so he ordered 'Abd al-Rahman, who announced among the people: \"The meat of domestic donkeys is for the one who does not bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah.\" So they overturned their pots with what was in them. They found onions and garlic in their gardens. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever eats from this plant should not come near us.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Plunder is not lawful, nor is any predator with fangs lawful, nor is the mujaththamah lawful.\""],[18787,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a gold ring on his hand, so he began tapping it with a stick he had. When the Prophet ﷺ became inattentive, he threw it away. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I think we have only caused you pain and made you incur a loss.\""],[18788,"A man sat by the Prophet ﷺ wearing a gold ring. The Prophet ﷺ tapped his hand with a stick he had in his hand, then the Prophet ﷺ became inattentive to him, and the man threw away his ring. The Prophet ﷺ looked at him and said: \"Where is your ring?\" He said: \"I threw it away.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I think we have caused you pain and made you incur a loss.\""],[18789,"He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, and we cook in their pots and drink from their vessels.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you do not find other than them, wash them with water.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game, so what should we do?\" He said: \"If you send your trained dog and mention the name of Allah, then eat. And if it is not trained and you slaughter it, then eat. And if you shoot your arrow and mention the name of Allah, then eat.\""],[18790,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"We need the vessels of the polytheists on our journeys, and we cook in them and drink from them.\" He said: \"Wash them with water, then cook in them and drink.\""],[18791,"I heard Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani say: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.\" He looked up at me and then down, and said: \"A little prophet-like one.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, a little prophet-like one of good or a little prophet-like one of evil?\" He said: \"Rather a little prophet-like one of good. Do not eat the meat of domestic donkeys, nor any predator with fangs.\""],[18793,"He informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"We live as neighbors to the People of the Book, and they cook pork in their pots and drink wine from their vessels.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you find other than them, then eat in them and drink. And if you do not find other than them, wash them with water, then eat in them and drink.\""],[18794,"I heard Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani say: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, inform me of what is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me.' He raised his gaze toward me and then lowered it, and said, 'Righteousness is what the soul feels at ease with and the heart feels assured about, and sin is what the soul does not feel at ease with and the heart does not feel assured about.'"],[18795,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at a place and encamped, the people would scatter from him into the ravines and valleys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and said, 'That is only from Satan.' After that, when they stopped at a place, they would draw close together, so much so that you would say, 'If a cloth were spread over them, it would cover them all,' or something like that."],[18796,"I came to Abu Tha'laba al-Khushani and said, 'O Abu Tha'laba, what do you do about this verse?' He said, 'Which verse?' I said, 'His saying: {O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.}' He said, 'By Allah, you have asked one who knows about it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said, \"Rather, enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong, until you see miserliness obeyed, passion followed, the world preferred, and each person impressed with his own opinion. Then keep to your own self and leave alone the affairs of the common people. For behind you are days of patience, in which the one who is patient is like one grasping a live coal. The one who works good in that time will have the reward of fifty men.\"' Someone other than 'Utbah b. Abi Hakim added to me: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the reward of fifty men among us or among them?' He said, 'No, rather the reward of fifty men among you.'"],[18797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, the most beloved of you to me and the closest of you to me in the Hereafter in seating are those of you with the best character, and the most hateful of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter are those of you with the worst character, the prattlers, the boasters, and the self-important pretenders to understanding.'"],[18798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah has made obligations obligatory, so do not neglect them; and He has prohibited things, so do not violate them; and He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not search into them.'"],[18799,"that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Allah [audits] his servants during the night of the middle of [month of ] Shaʿbān then forgives the Believers and [purposefully] overlooks the disbelievers and leaves the people of hate in their hatefulness until they let go of it.\""],[18800,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed your religion is prophethood and mercy, then caliphate and mercy, then rule and compulsion, then tyrannical rule, and then a biting monarchy in which even the free and silk are considered permissible.'\""],[18801,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I shoot with my bow, and some of what I hunt I am able to slaughter properly and some I am not. What of it is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me? And I am in the land of the People of the Book, and they eat pork and drink wine in their vessels, so may I eat and drink in them?' He said, 'He raised his gaze toward me and lowered it, then said, \"A little turn of fortune.\"' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a little turn of fortune for good or a little turn of fortune for evil?' He said, 'Rather a little turn of fortune for good.' Then he said, 'Whatever your bow returns to you and you have mentioned the name of Allah over it, then eat it. And if you find an alternative to the vessels of the disbelievers, then do not eat in them; but if you find no alternative, then wash them thoroughly with water and then eat in them.'"],[18802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, Allah looks upon His servants on the night of the middle of Sha'ban, and He forgives the believers, grants respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of malice with their malice until they call upon Him.'"],[18803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast Sha'ban and Ramadan, joining them both together."],[18804,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then he would visit Fatimah, then he would go to his wives. He returned from a journey and prayed two rak'ahs in the mosque, then he came to Fatimah. She met him at the door of the house and began kissing his mouth and his eyes and weeping. He said, 'What makes you weep?' She said, 'I see you disheveled and exhausted, and your clothes have become worn out.' He said to her, 'Do not weep, for Allah has sent your father with a matter by which there will not remain on the face of the earth any house of mud, or stone, or fur, or hair except that Allah will bring into it honor or humiliation, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.'"],[18805,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rak'ahs in it, then he would begin with the house of Fatimah, then he would go to the houses of his wives. He entered upon her, and she placed her hand on his cheek and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, your clothes have become worn out.' He said, 'O Fatimah, Allah has sent your father with a matter by which there will not remain a house of mud or fur except that Allah will bring into it honor through your father, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.'"],[18807,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Regarding buried treasure, one-fifth is due.”"],[18808,"Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land whose people are People of the Book; they eat the flesh of swine and drink wine. How do you command us regarding their vessels and cooking pots?” He said, “If you find other vessels, use them; otherwise, wash them with water, then eat and drink in them.”"],[18810,"Two children of mine died, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, two children of mine have died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever has two children die, Allah will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.\" Then Abu Hurayrah met me and said: Are you the one to whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke about the two children? I said: Yes. He said: That he spoke to me about it is dearer to me than whatever Palestine would be closed off from."],[18811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Is there zakah on donkeys? He said: \"No, except the unique, isolated verse: {Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it}.\""],[18812,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we come to the land of the People of the Book. I asked him about their vessels. He said: \"Wash them, then cook in them.\""],[18813,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, write for me a land grant. He said: \"How can I write when it is in the land of war?\" He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they will surely possess what is under their feet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with that, so he looked at his companions and wrote for him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of game; what is lawful for us of what is forbidden to us? He said: \"When you send your trained dog or your taught dog, and you mention Allah's name, and it seizes and kills, then eat. When you send your dog that is not trained, whatever you catch while it is still alive and slaughter, then eat; whatever you do not catch alive, do not eat. And whatever your arrow returns to you with, eat.\""],[18814,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Our land is a land of game. I shoot my arrow and mention Allah's name, I send my trained dog and mention Allah's name, and I send my dog that is not trained and mention Allah's name. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whatever your arrow holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your trained dog holds back for you and you mentioned Allah's name, eat. Whatever your dog that is not trained holds back for you and you catch it alive and slaughter it, eat. If you do not catch it alive, do not eat.\""],[18815,"\"Yazid b. Abi Sufyan died in Syria in the year eighteen, and he had appointed Mu'awiyah as his successor, and 'Umar confirmed him.\""],[18816,"When Abu Bakr sent Yazid b. Abi Sufyan to Syria, he went out walking with him. Yazid said to him: Either ride or I will dismount. He said: I will not ride and you will not dismount. I am seeking reward for my steps."],[18817,"From Ya'la b. 'Ata' al-Ta'ifi, from Jabir b. Yazid b. al-Aswad, from his father, who said: We prayed Fajr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He turned around and saw two men behind the people. He summoned them, and they were brought trembling. He said: What prevented you two from praying with the people? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed at our mounts. He said: Do not do that. When one of you prays at his mount and then catches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer."],[18818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf. After he finished, he saw two men at the back of the mosque. He sent for them, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What is the matter with you that you did not pray with us?\" They said, \"We already prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"When one of you comes to the congregation and has already prayed in his home, let him pray with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18819,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed a prayer. When he finished his prayer, he noticed two men at the back of the people. He ordered that they be brought, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with us?\" They said, \"O Prophet of Allah, we prayed in the camps, then we came.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"When you two have prayed in your camps and then catch the prayer, pray it, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.\""],[18820,"We prayed the dawn prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina. There were two men at the back of the mosque who did not pray. He called for them, and they were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"Do not do that. When you two have prayed in your camps and then come to the imam while he has not prayed, pray with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for you.\""],[18821,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He prayed the dawn prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the mosque. They were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What is the matter with you that you did not pray with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our camps, then we came while you were praying, so we sat down.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you has prayed in his camp and then comes while the imam is praying, let him pray with him, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18822,"I prayed the morning prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he said the salutation, he faced the people and noticed two men among the last of the people who had not prayed with the people. He said, \"Bring me these two men.\" They were brought trembling in their shoulders. He said, \"What prevented you from praying with the people?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in the camps.\" He said, \"Do not do that. When one of you has prayed in his camp and then catches the prayer with the people, let him pray it with them, for it will be a supererogatory prayer for him.\""],[18823,"I attended the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque of al-Khayf. When he finished the prayer, he noticed two men sitting to the side. They were brought trembling in their shoulders. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What prevented you from the prayer?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we prayed in our camps.\" He said, \"When you have prayed in your camps and then catch the prayer with the people, pray it with them. The one you prayed in your camps is the obligatory prayer.\""],[18825,"I performed the farewell Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and I prayed the morning prayer with him in Mina. When he finished his prayer, he saw two men behind the people who had not prayed with them. He said, \"Bring those two men to me.\" They were brought to him trembling. He asked them, \"Did you not pray with us?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our camps, and we thought that we would not be able to catch the prayer.\" He said, \"Do not do that when you have already prayed in your camps, and then if you catch the prayer, pray it, and it will be a voluntary prayer for you.\" One of them said, \"Ask Allah to forgive me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"O Allah, forgive him.\""],[18827,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give me your hand.\" He gave it to me, and it was cooler than snow and more fragrant than musk."],[18828,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The people crowded around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and at that time I was among the strongest and most vigorous of men. I pressed through the people until I took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed it on my chest. I never found anything cooler or more fragrant than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[18829,"I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one hundred verses of the poetry of Umayyah b. Abi al-Salt. Whenever I passed a verse, he said, \"Continue.\" And I heard him say in that gathering, \"The neighbor has more right to his property that is close to him.\""],[18830,"My father Yazid went out with some dinars to give as charity. He gave them to me and said, \"Give them to a man from the mosque.\" I gave them to someone else. Then I went to my father and told him. He said, \"That is not what I intended.\" I took the matter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to me, \"O Ma'n, you have what you took,\" and to my father, \"O Yazid, you have what you intended.\""],[18831,"When the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn and the disbelievers pursued them, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of earth and threw it in their faces, saying, \"Turn back! May the faces be ugly!\" None of us met his brother except that he complained of grit and was wiping his eyes."],[18832,"From Yazid b. 'Amir, who witnessed Hunayn with the polytheists then embraced Islam. He said: We asked him about the terror that Allah cast into their hearts on the day of Hunayn, how it was. He took a pebble and threw it at a basin, and it made a ringing sound. He said, \"We would feel in our chests something like that.\""],[18833,"Saʿīd b. al-Sāʾib al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to us, from Nūḥ b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah, from Yazīd b. ʿĀmir, who said: I came while the Prophet ﷺ was in prayer—either in Ẓuhr or in ʿAṣr—and I had already prayed them at home. When I found the Prophet ﷺ in prayer, I sat down and did not join them in prayer. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to us and saw me sitting, and said, “Have you not become Muslim, O Yazīd?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of God, I have become Muslim.” He said, “What prevents you from entering prayer with the people?” I said, “I had prayed at home, and I thought that you had already prayed.” He said, “When you come to prayer and find the people praying, then pray with them, even if you have already prayed; it will be a supererogatory prayer for you, and this one will be the prescribed one.”"],[18834,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “O Yazīd, love for people what you love for yourself.”"],[18835,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not compete with one another except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur'an, so he recites it during the night and during the day, or a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it and gives in charity.\" A man said: \"If Allah had given me what He has given so-and-so, I would do like him.\" And a man to whom Allah has given wealth, so he spends it and gives in charity, another man said: \"Like that.\""],[18836,"From his paternal uncle Yazīd b. Thābit: They went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ one day with a funeral procession, until when they reached al-Baqīʿ, he said, “What is this?” They said, “This is so-and-so, a freedwoman of Banū so-and-so.” He recognized her and said, “Why did you not inform me about her?” They said, “We buried her at midday while you were taking a nap, so we did not want to disturb you.” Then he stood and the people lined up behind him, and he said four takbīrs over her. Then he said, “No one among you should die while I am still among you unless you inform me, for my prayer for him is a mercy.”"],[18837,"From his paternal uncle Yazīd b. Thābit, who was older than Zayd, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we reached al-Baqīʿ, he noticed a new grave and asked about it. They said, “So-and-so.” He recognized her and said, “Should you not have informed me?” They said, “You were taking a nap and fasting, so we disliked to trouble you.” He said, “Do not do that. Let me not know of anyone among you who dies while I am still among you unless you inform me, for my prayer over him is a mercy for him.” Then he came to the grave, and we lined up behind him, and he said four takbīrs over it."],[18838,"He was with the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions when a funeral procession appeared. When he saw it, he stood up, and his companions stood up, and they remained standing until it had gone far. By God, I do not know whether it was from being disturbed by it or from the narrowness of the place. I do not think it was anything but the funeral of a Jew or a Jewess, and we did not ask him about his standing."],[18839,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “None of you should take his brother’s belongings, neither in jest nor in earnest. If one of you takes his brother’s staff, let him return it.”"],[18840,"When the Prophet ﷺ supplicated and raised his hands, he wiped his face with his hands."],[18841,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave us a grant in addition to our share of the khums, and I received an old camel."],[18842,"From Yazīd b. Salamah al-Juʿfī, who said: Yazīd said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, “I have heard from you many hadiths, and I fear that the first of them will make me forget the last, so tell me a word that will be comprehensive.” He said, “Fear God regarding what you know.”"],[18843,"From Yazīd b. Salamah al-Juʿfī, who said: “O Messenger of God, what do you think if we have rulers who take from us the right that is due to them and withhold from us the right that is due to us?” Al-Ashʿath said to him, “Sit down.” He repeated it a second time, then a third, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Upon them is what they are burdened with, and upon you is what you are burdened with.”"],[18844,"A man from his family died while he was not on the religion of Islam. He said: My sister inherited from him instead of me, because she was on his religion. Then my father became Muslim and witnessed Ḥunayn with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he died, and I secured his inheritance. He had left behind a slave boy and palm trees. Then my sister became Muslim and disputed with me over the inheritance before ʿUthmān. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Arqam told him that ʿUmar ruled that whoever becomes Muslim before an inheritance is divided is entitled to his share. ʿUthmān ruled accordingly, and she took the former inheritance and shared with me in this one. The wording is from the hadith of Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī."],[18845,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Your slaves, your slaves! Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear. If they commit a sin that you do not wish to forgive, then sell the servants of God and do not punish them.”"],[18846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When a man makes a bond of brotherhood with another man, let him ask him about his name, his father's name, and from what tribe he is, for that is more conducive to affection."],[18847,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: No one kills a sparrow except that it will cry out on the Day of Resurrection, saying: 'O Lord, this one killed me in vain; he neither benefited from killing me, nor did he leave me to live in Your earth.'"],[18848,"O Messenger of Allah, what is Saba'? Was he a prophet or a woman? He said: Rather, he was a man of the Arabs. He said: What did he beget? He said: He begot ten sons. Six dwelt in Yemen and four in Syria. Those in Yemen were Kindah, Madhhij, al-Azd, al-Ash'ariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar. And in Syria: Lakhm, Judham, 'Amilah, and Ghassan."],[18849,"I came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, and he asked me about al-Yamamah: in which tribe is the numerical majority of its people? I wanted to say in Banu 'Abd Allah b. al-Du'al, but then I disliked lying to the Prophet of Allah, so I said: The majority among them is in Banu 'Ubayd. He said: You have spoken the truth. A land that has grown despite hardship, and its people will never perish. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why is that? He said: Because they work with their own hands and share their food with their slaves."],[18850,"From Yazid b. Shajarah, and Yazid b. Shajarah was one whose word and deed were trusted. He said: He gave us a sermon and said: O people, remember the blessing of Allah upon you. How excellent is the blessing of Allah upon you! You see among green, yellow, and red, and in the saddles there is what there is. He used to say: When the people form rows for prayer and are arrayed for battle, the gates of heaven are opened, as are the gates of Paradise and the gates of Hell, and the wide-eyed houris are adorned and look out. When a man advances, they say: 'O Allah, grant him victory.' When he retreats, they veil themselves from him and say: 'O Allah, forgive him.' So strike hard at the faces of the enemy, may my father and mother be your ransom, and do not disgrace the houris. For the first drop of his blood that is shed atones for every sin he has committed, and two wives from the wide-eyed houris descend to him, wiping the dust from his face and saying: 'Your time has come.' And he replies: 'Your time has come.' Then he is clothed in one hundred garments, not of the weaving of the children of Adam but of the vegetation of Paradise, which, if placed between two fingers, would be spacious enough. He also used to say: I have been informed that swords are the keys to Paradise. This wording is from 'Abd al-Samad b. Hassan."],[18851,"\"That the world has become filled with green, red, and yellow, and in the houses there is nothing. So if you meet the enemy, go forward, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No man takes a step in the way of Allah except that the houris of Paradise look at him. And if he is delayed, they become shy and conceal themselves from him. And if he is martyred, the first drop of blood from him will be an expiation for his sins, and two houris of Paradise will descend upon him, shaking off the dust from his face, and they will say, 'Welcome to you.' And he will say, 'Welcome to both of you.'\""],[18852,"From 'Urwah, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, from the Banu Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Yazid b. Zam'ah. Ibn Lahi'ah said it thus, and in my view this is an error."],[18853,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, then from the Banu Asad: Yazid b. Zam'ah b. al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib. A horse of his called al-Janah bolted with him and killed him."],[18854,"From Ibn Shihab, in the naming of those who were martyred on the Day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Quraysh, then from the Banu Asad: Yazid b. Zam'ah."],[18855,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man from Banu Tamim has taken all my wealth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: I have no wealth to give you. Then he said: Would you like to be appointed as 'arif over your people? Or shall I appoint you as 'arif over your people? I said: No. He said: Indeed, the 'arif will be thrust into the Fire with a shove."],[18856,"When the Prophet ﷺ prayed over a deceased person, he would say the takbir four times, then say: O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your maidservant is in need of Your mercy, and You are free from need of punishing him. If he was a doer of good, then increase his good; and if he was a doer of evil, then overlook [his sins]. Then he would supplicate as Allah willed him to supplicate."],[18857,"I went on the expedition of hardship with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ya'la used to say: That expedition is the most reliable of my deeds in my sight. I had a hired hand, and he fought a man. One of them bit the other, and the one who was bitten pulled his hand from the biter's mouth, tearing out one of his front teeth. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he declared the tooth to be of no consequence. I think he said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He leaves his hand in your mouth for you to gnaw it, as if it were in the mouth of a male camel biting it.'"],[18858,"I participated in the Battle of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , alongside Abu Bakr As-Siddiq. This battle was one of my greatest achievements, and I hired a helper to fight alongside me. During the battle, my helper got into a fight with another man and he bit his hand, causing him to lose his two fingers. The injured man then complained to the Prophet ﷺ about what happened. The Prophet ﷺ dismissed the complaint and said, \"Would you want your hand to make him suffer by biting it like a stallion bites?\""],[18859,"I went on the expedition of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a refractory young camel, and I had a hired hand with me. My hired hand fought a man, and the man bit him. He pulled his hand from the man's mouth, and his front tooth fell out. He was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him: 'Would he leave his hand in your mouth for you to gnaw it as a stallion gnaws?' So he declared the tooth to be of no consequence."],[18860,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ after biting another man's hand. The one bitten pulled his hand away, and the biter's front tooth fell out. The Prophet ﷺ made it void and said: \"You wanted to bite it as a stallion bites.\""],[18861,"From his father and his paternal uncle Salamah b. Umayyah: The two of them went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and a companion of ours was with us. A man fought with him and bit him, so our companion pulled his hand out of his mouth, and a part of his mouth fell out. He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked for compensation. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Will one of you go to his brother and bite him like a stallion bites, then come asking for compensation?\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ made it void."],[18862,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah wearing a jubbah and showing traces of khaluq. Hammam said: Or he said traces of yellow dye. The man said: \"How do you order me to proceed in my 'umrah?\" Revelation came down upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he was covered with a cloth. Ya'la used to say: \"I wished that I could see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation came to him.\" 'Umar said to me: \"Would you like to see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation is coming down upon him?\" So he lifted the edge of the cloth, and I looked at him, and he was snoring. Hammam said: \"I think he also said: like the snoring of a young virgin.\" When it was over, he said: \"Where is the one asking about the 'umrah? Remove the jubbah, and wash off from yourself\"—either he said \"the traces of khaluq\" or \"the traces of yellow dye,\" Hammam was unsure—\"and do in your 'umrah what you do in your hajj.\""],[18863,"I said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab: \"I wish I could see the Messenger of God ﷺ when revelation came down upon him.\" He said: \"We were on a journey with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He stopped at a place, and a bedouin came to him wearing a jubbah dyed with saffron. He said: 'O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah, and the people are mocking me. What should I do?' The Messenger of God ﷺ remained silent. Then God sent down revelation. 'Umar gestured to me with his hand, so I put my head into the tent. There was the Messenger of God ﷺ with his eyes and forehead red. When it was over, he said: 'Where is the one asking about the 'umrah?' The man said: 'It is I, O Messenger of God.' He said: 'Remove your jubbah, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.'\""],[18864,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while we were with him and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram while wearing khaluq, a woolen jubbah, and a turban.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Remove your turban and your shirt, wash off this yellow dye from yourself, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.\""],[18865,"I wished to see the Prophet ﷺ when revelation came down upon him. When we were at al-Ji'ranah, revelation came down upon him, so he covered himself with a cloth. 'Umar called me and uncovered the cloth from his face, and I saw him snoring with his face red. Before that, a bedouin had come to him wearing patched garments, smeared with khaluq, and said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah while wearing this. How do you order me to proceed?\" He did not answer him until revelation came down upon him. When it was over, he said: \"Where is the questioner?\" The man said: \"Here I am.\" He said: \"What do you think? If you were in ihram for hajj and this was on you, what would you do?\" He said: \"I would remove these patched garments and wash off this khaluq.\" He said: \"Then go and remove these patched garments, wash off this khaluq, and do in your 'umrah what you would do in your hajj.\""],[18867,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ at al-Ji'ranah wearing a jubbah, with his beard and head dyed yellow. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram while I am as you see.\" He said: \"Wash off the yellow dye, remove the jubbah, and whatever you would do in your hajj, do it in your 'umrah.\""],[18868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by al-Ji'ranah when he returned from Hunayn and distributed their spoils. A bedouin came to him wearing a shirt or a jubbah and having dyed himself with yellow dye. He said: \"O Messenger of God, I have entered ihram for 'umrah. What do you think?\" He did not answer him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ—the bedouin repeated: \"I have entered ihram for 'umrah. What do you think?\" He did not answer him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ withdrew for revelation, and 'Umar stood up to cover him with his cloth. Ya'la b. Munyah said: \"I love to see the Messenger of God ﷺ while revelation comes to him.\" 'Umar called him, so he put his head under the cloth and found him snoring like a sleeping person. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, called the bedouin, and ordered him to remove his jubbah and his shirt. He said to him: \"Wash, and wear the lower garment and the cloak, and do in your 'umrah what you do in your hajj.\""],[18869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The most beloved of you to me and the nearest of you to me in the Hereafter in sitting will be the best of you in character. And the most hated of you to me and the farthest of you from me in the Hereafter in sitting will be the worst of you in character: the talkative, the eloquent boasters, and those who speak with affectation in religious matters.\""],[18870,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God has made obligations, so do not neglect them; He has forbidden things, so do not violate them; He has set limits, so do not transgress them; and He has remained silent about things out of mercy, not out of forgetfulness, so do not search into them.\""],[18871,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"God looks upon His servants on the night of mid-Sha'ban and forgives the believers, gives respite to the disbelievers, and leaves the people of malice with their malice until they call upon Him.\""],[18872,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ and saw three amazing things from him. He said: We stopped at a land with many trees, and he said to me: \"Go to those two trees and tell them that the Messenger of God ﷺ commands them to come together.\" I went to them and said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ commands you to come together.\" They came together, and the Messenger of God ﷺ relieved himself. Then he said: \"Go and tell them to separate.\" I told them, and they separated. A woman came with a child and said: \"O Messenger of God, this child suffers epileptic fits seven times a month.\" He said: \"Bring him closer to me.\" He spat into his mouth and said: \"Get out, enemy of God! I am the Messenger of God.\" Then he said to her: \"When you return, inform me of what he does.\" When he returned, she met him with two rams and some ghee and aqit. He said to me: \"Take from her one of the two rams and what she has with it.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, I have not seen that from him.\" Then a camel came to him, and he saw its eyes flowing with tears. He said: \"To whom does this belong?\" They said: \"To the family of so-and-so.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for them and said: \"What is wrong with this camel that it complains about you?\" They said: \"It was a water-carrying camel for us, and it grew old, so we wanted to slaughter it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave it among the camels.\" So they left it."],[18874,"Abdullah b. Ya'la b. Murrah al-Thaqafi narrated to me, from his father, who said: One day I applied depilatory paste and then perfumed myself with khaluq. I came to the Prophet ﷺ, extended my hand to him, and said, “O Messenger of God, pray for me.” He said, “What is this on your hand?” I said, “I applied depilatory paste and then perfumed myself with khaluq.” He said, “Do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Do you have a concubine?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it three times.”"],[18875,"A prescribed prayer was due while we were with the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ led us, and he did not advance ahead of us. I said to Abu Sahl, “What prompted him to do that?” He said, “The place was narrow.”"],[18876,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a smear of khaluq on him and said, “Wash this off yourself.”"],[18877,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me wearing khaluq and said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it off yourself, then wash it off yourself, then do not do it again.” He said: I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again until this moment."],[18878,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a yellow stain of saffron on him. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Wash this off yourself, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So he washed it and did not do it again."],[18880,"I passed by the Prophet ﷺ wearing khaluq. He said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So I washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again."],[18881,"I passed by the Messenger of God ﷺ wearing saffron khaluq. He said, “O Ya'la, do you have a wife?” I said, “No.” He said, “Go and wash it, then wash it, then wash it, then do not do it again.” He said: So I went and washed it, then washed it, then washed it, then never did it again."],[18882,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in prayer. I went to a sister of mine and smeared my face with some khaluq. When the Prophet ﷺ passed by, he wiped the faces of others and left me. It was said, “The Prophet ﷺ left you only because of the khaluq on your face.” So I went to a well among the wells of Madinah and plunged into it. When the next prayer came, I came to him, and he wiped my face, then said, “The boy has returned with the good of his religion.”"],[18883,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever wrongfully takes anything from the earth will come on the Day of Resurrection carrying its dust to the gathering place.”"],[18884,"I heard Ya'la al-Thaqafi say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever takes land without right will be burdened with carrying its dust to the gathering place.”"],[18885,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Any man who wrongfully takes a handspan of land, God will oblige him to bring it until he reaches the end of the seventh earth, then he will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection until judgment is passed among the people.”"],[18886,"From Ya'la b. Murrah al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Whoever steals a handspan of land or a crop will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection to the lowest of the earths.”"],[18887,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, “Give me this camel as a gift, or sell it to me.” He said, “It is yours, O Messenger of God.” So he branded it with the zakah brand, then sent it off."],[18888,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Whoever usurps a handspan of land or more will be made to carry it on the Day of Resurrection until he reaches the water, then he will carry it to the gathering place.”"],[18889,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Answer your brother, for you are for him on one of two things: either it is good, so you are most entitled to witness it, or it is otherwise, so you forbid him from it and command him to do good.”"],[18890,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Do not mutilate the servants of God.”"],[18891,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Do not mutilate the servants of God.”"],[18892,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not depict my servants.'\""],[18893,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Whoever finds a small lost item, a garment or the like, let him announce it for three days. Whoever finds more than that, six days. If its owner comes, then it is his, otherwise let him give it as charity. Then if its owner comes, let him inform him.”"],[18894,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ and were invited to a meal. There was Husayn playing in the road. The Prophet ﷺ hurried ahead of the people, then spread out his arms. Husayn began to dart here and there while he made him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one hand on his chin and the other between his head and his ears, then embraced him and kissed him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Husayn is from me and I am from him. May God love whoever loves him. Hasan and Husayn are two grandsons among the descendants of the prophets.”"],[18895,"Ya‘la b. Murrah reported to him that they went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ to a meal to which they had been invited. There was Husayn playing with some boys in the street. The Messenger of God ﷺ went ahead of the people and opened his arms. The boy began to dart here and there while the Messenger of God ﷺ made him laugh, until he caught him. He placed one hand under his chin and the other on the top of his head, then drew him close and kissed him, and said, “Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May God love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a tribe among the tribes of Israel.”"],[18896,"He saw Hasan and Husayn coming walking toward the Messenger of God ﷺ. When one of them came, he placed his hand on his neck. Then the other came, and he placed his other hand on his neck. He kissed this one, then kissed that one, then said, “O God, I love them, so love them. O people, indeed children are a cause of miserliness and cowardice.”"],[18897,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the last footstep that the Lord of the Worlds will tread upon is with His face.\""],[18898,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he went away to relieve himself. Two dark-complexioned women came and joined each other. The tree of Talhah or Sumrah came, and it circled around them and returned to its place. Then a camel came dragging its tether along the ground until it became wet with the tears around it. He said to his companions, \"Do you know what this camel is saying?\" They said, \"What is it saying?\" He said, \"Its people wanted to slaughter it, so it called out for help. So it was sent back to me,\" He said, \"Will one of you undertake to do good to it?\" They said, \"Of course, by Allah, we will always honor it.\" Then he passed by two graves in which two people were being punished. He said, \"They are being punished, but the sins for which they are being punished are not significant.\" Then he took two fresh moist date-palm stalks and placed them on their graves. He said, \"Perhaps their torment will be lightened as long as these date-palm stalks remain moist.\""],[18899,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18900,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18901,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “When God wills to take a servant’s soul in a land, He creates for him a need there.”"],[18902,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Should I perform ablution after eating camel meat?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Should I pray in their resting places?” He said, “No.” He said, “Should I perform ablution after eating sheep meat?” He said, “No.” He said, “Should I pray in their folds?” He said, “Yes.”"],[18903,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for a she-camel and said, “Who will milk her?” A man said, “I will.” He said, “What is your name?” He said, “Murra (bitter).” He said, “Sit down.” Then another stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Murra.” He said, “Sit down.” Then another stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Jamra (ember).” He said, “Sit down.” Then Ya‘īsh stood up, and he said, “What is your name?” He said, “Ya‘īsh (he lives).” He said, “Milk her.”"],[18904,"‘Abdullāh b. Dāwūd b. Dilhāth b. Ismā‘īl b. ‘Abdullāh b. Musri‘ b. Yāsir b. Suwayd al-Juhanī, the Companion of the Prophet, narrated to us. He said: My father Dāwūd narrated to me, from his father Dilhāth, from his father Ismā‘īl, from his father ‘Abdullāh, from his father Musri‘, from his father Yāsir b. Suwayd, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched him in a cavalry unit or a military expedition while his wife was pregnant. A child was born to him, and his mother carried him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, this child has been born while his father is with the cavalry, so name him.” The Prophet ﷺ took him, passed his hand over him, and said, “O Allah, increase their men, shorten their days, do not make them needy, and do not let their young ones experience want.” Then he said, “Name him Musri‘ (swift), for he has hastened into Islam.”"],[18905,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he had some people from Rabī‘a with him disputing over blood money. He was saying, “The upper hand is better than the lower hand: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the next closest and the next closest.” Then he said, “Who is this with you, O Abū Rimtha?” I said, “My son.” He said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then I looked and saw on the cartilage of his shoulder something like a camel’s dropping or a pigeon’s egg. I said, “Shall I treat this for you? I am from a household that practices medicine.” He said, “The one who placed it will treat it.”"],[18906,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw him, my father said to me, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I shuddered when he said that to me, for I had thought that the Messenger of Allah was something unlike people. But he was a human with abundant hair, having traces of henna, and wearing two green cloaks. My father greeted him, then they sat talking for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “Truly?” He said, “Truly, I bear witness to it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at the confirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father’s oath concerning me. Then he said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.” My father saw something like a wen between his shoulders and said, “I am like the most skilled of men in medicine; shall I not treat it?” He said, “Gently; its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18907,"I entered with my father upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My father saw what was on his back and said, “Let me treat what is on your back, for I am a physician.” He said, “You are a kind companion, but Allah is the Physician.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Who is this with you?” He said, “My son; I bear witness to you concerning him.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Indeed, you will not be held liable for him, nor will he be held liable for you.” And he mentioned that he saw traces of henna on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[18909,"I came with my father to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Do you love him? Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18910,"I set out with my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw on his shoulder something like an apple. My father said to him, “I am a physician; shall I not lance it?” He said, “Its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18911,"He entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his. He said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18912,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I saw him, my father said, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I shuddered when I saw that, for I had thought that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was something unlike people. But he was a human with abundant hair, having traces of henna, and wearing two green cloaks. My father greeted him, then they sat and talked for a while. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “Truly?” He said, “I bear witness to that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at the confirmation of my resemblance to my father and at my father’s oath concerning me. Then he said, “Indeed, he will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, “And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.” Then my father looked at something like a wen between his shoulders and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am like the most skilled of men in medicine; shall I treat it?” He said, “No, its physician is the One who created it.”"],[18913,"I entered the mosque with my father, and there was the Prophet ﷺ sitting in the shade of the Ka‘ba. He said to me, “Do you see the man in the shade of the Ka‘ba? That is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I was seized with a severe trembling. He was wearing two green garments, or two green cloaks, and had traces of henna. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Is this your son?” He said, “Yes, by the Lord of the Ka‘ba.” He said, “He will not be held liable for you, nor will you be held liable for him.”"],[18914,"I set out with my father to the Prophet ﷺ, and there he was with abundant hair, having traces of henna, wearing two green garments."],[18915,"I and my father were going towards the Messenger of God ﷺ. When we were partway, he met me, and my father said, “Do you know who this is?” I said, “No.” He said, “This is the Messenger of God ﷺ.” I had thought that the Messenger of God ﷺ did not resemble people. [He said:] And behold, it was a man with long hair, on which there was a trace of henna, wearing two green cloaks. It was as if I were looking at the gleam of his shins. He said to my father, “Who is this with you?” He said, “My son, by God, truly.” The Messenger of God ﷺ laughed at my father’s swearing about me, then said, “You have spoken truth. Indeed, he will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ recited this verse: “No bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another.”"],[18916,"I went to the Prophet peace be upon him, and with me was my son. I said to my son, when I saw him, \"This is the Prophet of Allah.\" Then he (my son) had a seizure. So I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"O Prophet of Allah, I am a physician and my father was a physician from a family of physicians. Show me your back, if there is a lump on it, I will treat it, and if it is something else, I will inform you. For there is no one more knowledgeable than me regarding injuries and wounds.\" He said, \"There is no physician except Allah, and upon him are two green bandages, and he has hair that has turned gray, and his beard is red.\" Then he said, \"Is this your son?\" I said, \"Yes, I swear by the Lord of the Kāba.\" He said, \"Is it from yourself?\" I said, \"I testify to it.\" He said, \"Indeed, it does not harm you nor does it harm him.\""],[18917,"I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was giving a sermon, saying: “The upper hand is the one that gives. Your mother and your father, then your sister and your brother, then the nearest to you, then the nearest.” Then some people from Banu Yarbuʿ came and said, “O Messenger of God, this is Banu Yarbuʿ that killed so-and-so.” He said, “Indeed, no soul will bear the crime of another.”"],[18918,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he had hair that reached his shoulders, dyed with henna and katam."],[18919,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ praying, then he gave the greeting of peace to his right and to his left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks."],[18920,"An imam of ours, known as Abu Rimthah, led us in the afternoon prayer in our prayer place. With us was a man who had been present at the first takbir of the prayer. When Abu Rimthah finished, the man stood up to make up [what he had missed]. Abu Rimthah looked and said, “I prayed this prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr and Umar were standing in the front row to his right. There was a man who had been present at the first takbir of the prayer. The Prophet ﷺ prayed, then gave the greeting of peace to the right and left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks. Then he turned around and faced the people. The man who had caught with him the first takbir of the prayer stood up to make up [what he had missed]. Umar jumped towards him, grabbed him by the shoulders, and shook him, then said, ‘Sit down, for the People of the Book were only destroyed because there was no separation between their prayers.’ The Prophet ﷺ raised his eyes to him and said, ‘God has guided you to the right course, O Ibn al-Khattab.’”"],[18921,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and wiped my head."],[18922,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf."],[18923,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf, seated me in his lap, and prayed for blessing for me."],[18924,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ take a piece of barley bread, place a date on it, and say, “This is a condiment for this,” then he ate it."],[18925,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me."],[18926,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named me Yusuf."],[18927,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man and woman from the Ansar: “Perform ʿumrah in the month of Ramadan, for an ʿumrah in it is like a Hajj.”"],[18928,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What is it upon any one of you to take two garments for Friday besides the two garments of his household's work?\""],[18929,"Yasir b. 'Amr was a chieftain in the time of al-Hajjaj."],[18930,"The Prophet ﷺ died when I was ten years old."],[18931,"As'ad b. Zurarah, who was the grandfather of Muhammad, was afflicted with a pain in his throat called quinsy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will indeed reach or strive to the utmost in the case of Abu Umamah with an excuse.\" So he cauterized him with his own hand, and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What a bad death for the Jews; they will say, 'Could he not have warded off death from his companion?' I have no power for him or for myself against Allah in anything.\""],[18932,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Battle of Hunayn. We traveled on an intensely hot day, and we alighted under the shade of trees. When the sun declined, I put on my armor, mounted my horse, and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in his tent. I said: \"Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Has the time for departure come?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Then he said: \"O Bilal!\" Bilal sprang up from under a samurah tree as if his shadow were the shadow of a bird. He said: \"At your service and at your command; I am your ransom.\" He said: \"O Bilal, saddle my horse for me.\" He brought out a saddle whose two sides were of palm fiber, with no ornament and no pride. He saddled it, and he mounted, and we mounted. We faced them that evening and that night. The two cavalries exchanged glances. The Muslims turned their backs in flight, as Allah had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.\" Then he spurred his horse forward, took a handful of dust, and the one who was closer to him than I was to him informed me that he threw it in their faces and said: \"Ugly be the faces!\" So Allah routed them. Ya'la b. 'Ata' said: Their sons narrated to me from their fathers that they said: \"Not one of us remained but that his eyes and mouth were filled with dust, and we heard a clattering from the sky and the earth like the passing of iron over a basin.\" The wording is that of 'Affan."],[18933,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, two riders appeared. When he saw them, he said: \"Two Kindis, two Madhhijis.\" When they came to him, they were indeed two men from Madhhij. One of them drew near to give him the oath of allegiance. When he took his hand, he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what about one who saw you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you? What will he have?\" He said: \"Tuba (glad tidings) for him.\" He said: \"Then he wiped over his hand and departed.\""],[18934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"I am riding tomorrow to the Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of salam with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[18935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We are going tomorrow to some Jews, so do not initiate the greeting of salam with them. If they greet you, then say, 'And upon you.'\""],[18936,"Sariq bought from a man who had recited Surah al-Baqarah some cloth that he had brought, and they haggled. Then the man disappeared, but he later caught up with him and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Sell, O Sariq.\" He said: \"I went with him and the Prophet's companions bargained with me for him for three days. Then it occurred to me, so I set him free.\""],[18937,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and 'A'ishah in a single garment, half of it over the Prophet ﷺ and half of it over 'A'ishah.\""],[18938,"Sa'd asked the Prophet ﷺ about the bequest, and he said to him: \"A fourth.\""],[18939,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the matter of gambling. 'Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever plays gambling and then gets up to pray is like one who performs ablution with pus and the blood of a pig.\" Then it is said: \"Will Allah accept his prayer?\""],[18945,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with my son, and he said: 'What children do you have?' I said: So-and-so, so-and-so, and 'Abd al-'Uzza. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best of your names are 'Abd Allah, 'Abd al-Rahman, and al-Harith.'"],[18952,"Abu Amr b. Hafs said: \"By Allah, you have not been just. You dismissed an agent whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed, you sheathed a sword which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had unsheathed, you lowered a banner which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had raised, and you envied the son of your uncle.\" Umar said: \"You are a close relative and young in age.\""],[18956,"Muawiya said to him: \"Did you not go out with the people?\" He said: \"Yes, but I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I wanted to place it with you, fearing that you might not meet me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'O people, whoever among you is given authority over something and then closes his door against a needy Muslim, Allah will close His gate against him entering Paradise. And whoever's main concern is this world, Allah will forbid him from my company, for I have been sent with the ruin of this world, not with its construction.'\""],[18957,"A slave girl from Khaybar passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"To whom does she belong?\" They said: \"To so-and-so.\" He said: \"Does he have intercourse with her?\" It was said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then what will he do with her child? Will he claim it as his when it is not his child, or will he enslave it while it grows up in his hearing and sight? I have considered cursing him with a curse that would enter with him into his grave.\""],[18968,"Abū Saʿd: “Preserve the testament of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Then ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān said: “And what is that?” He said: “Preserve [the rights of] their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers.” Abū Saʿd was the husband of Asmāʾ bt. Yazīd b. al-Sakan b. ʿAmr b. Ḥarām."],[18975,"I brought a debtor to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Stay close to him.” Then he passed by him at the end of the day and said: “O brother of the Banū al-ʿAnbar, what do you intend to do with your captive?” The Messenger of God ﷺ was narrating to the people on the pulpit, and he descended to my grandfather, wiped his face, and bestowed upon him a fine garment."],[18976,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Were it not for devoted worshippers bowing, suckling infants, and grazing livestock, the punishment would have been poured upon you, then crushed to bits.”"],[18977,"I said: “O Messenger of God, whom should I treat with utmost kindness?” He said: “Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, and your freed slave who is next to you—that is a binding right and a joined kinship.”"],[18978,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a garment of Maʿāfir clothing was brought. Abū Sufyān said: “May God curse this garment and the one who made it.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not curse them, for they are from me and I am from them.”"],[18979,"I heard Abū Zamʿah al-Balawī, one of the companions of the tree—he pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ beneath it. One day he came to the mosque of al-Fusṭāṭ and stood in the open courtyard. He had heard some strictness from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, so he said: “Do not be harsh with the people, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘A man of the Children of Israel killed ninety-seven people, then went to a monk and said: “I have killed ninety-seven people; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “No,” so he killed the monk. Then he went to another monk and said: “I have killed ninety-eight people; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “No,” so he killed him. Then he went to a third and said: “I have killed ninety-nine people, including two monks; do you find any repentance for me?” He said: “You have done great evil. If I were to say that God is not forgiving and merciful, I would lie. So repent to God.” He said: “As for me, I will not part from you after what you have said.” So he stayed with him on the condition that he not disobey him, and he served him. One day a man died and his reputation was ugly. When he was buried, he sat by his grave and wept bitterly. Then another died, and his reputation was good. When he was buried, he sat by his grave and laughed heartily. His companions found this objectionable, so they gathered before their leader and said: “How can you take in this killer of souls? He has done what you saw.” It troubled him and them. So he came to their leader once while accompanied by a companion of his, and he spoke with him, asking: “What do you command me?” He said: “Go and kindle a oven.” He did, then came back with the news that he had done so. He said: “Go and throw yourself into it.” The monk became distracted from him, and the other went and threw himself into the oven. Then the monk came to his senses and said: “I think the man has thrown himself into the oven because of my words.” He went to him and found him alive in the oven, sweating. He took him by the hand and pulled him out of the oven, then said: “It is not fitting for you to serve me; rather, I will serve you. Tell me about your weeping over the first deceased and your laughing over the other.” He said: “As for the first, when he was buried I saw the evil he was experiencing, and I remembered my own sins and wept. As for the other, I saw the good he was receiving and laughed.” After that he became one of the great men of the Children of Israel.’”"],[18980,"I went to the Prophet ﷺ , then I entered between him and his garment and held onto it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"Water.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"Salt.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not permissible to prevent?\" He said, \"If you do good, it will be good for you.\""],[18981,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever says ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[18986,"He witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ while he was besieging the people of al-Ta’if, and he would lead us in the afternoon prayer at a time when, if a person shot his arrows, he could see where the arrows fell."],[18987,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: “There is no prophet after me, and no community after you. So worship your Lord, establish your five prayers, fast your month, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.”"],[18988,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting. He said: “Fast one day of the month.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am capable of more.” He said: “Fast two days of the month.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, give me more.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Give me more, give me more—fast three days of every month.”"],[18989,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: “What kept you?” He said: “I recited this verse: {O you who believe, take care of your own selves; those who have gone astray will not harm you if you are guided}.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him: “Those among the disbelievers who go astray will not harm you if you are guided.”"],[18990,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the perfection of piety?” He said: “That you do in private the deed you do in public.”"],[18997,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: God, Blessed and Exalted, said: \"Whoever is not content with My decree and does not bear patiently My trial, let him seek a lord other than Me.\""],[19003,"I was sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he turned to us and said: \"Who would love to wake up and never fall ill?\" We started answering him and said: \"We would, O Messenger of God.\" He said: then we recognized it in his face, and he said: \"Would you love to be like braying donkeys?\" They said: \"No, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Would you not love to be people of trial and people of expiation? For by the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, God tests the believer with trial, and He does not test him with it except for His honor toward him. God has granted him a station that he did not reach by any of his deeds, so He tests him with trials that will make him attain that degree.\""],[19006,"She said to him—and he had a male camel and a female camel—\"Give me your male camel so I can perform Hajj on it.\" He said: \"It is dedicated for the sake of God.\" She said: \"It is for the sake of God that I perform Hajj on it.\" She said: \"Then give me the female camel and perform Hajj on your male camel.\" He said: \"I do not prefer anyone over myself.\" She said: \"Then give me some of your provision.\" He said: \"I have no surplus beyond what I will take with me and leave for you all. If I had any with me, I would give it to you.\" She said: \"If you do what you do, then convey my greetings to the Messenger of God ﷺ when you meet him and tell him what I said to you.\" When he met the Messenger of God ﷺ, he conveyed her greetings and told him what she had said. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Umm Taliq spoke the truth. If you had given her your male camel, it would have been in the way of God; if you had given her your female camel, it would have been in the way of God; and if you had given her some of your provision, God would have replaced it for you.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, what equals a Hajj?\" He said: \"An 'Umrah in Ramadan.\""],[19014,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not look in any direction without seeing Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith fighting. So the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Indeed Abu Sufyan is the best of my family, or among the best of my family.\""],[19015,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"Indeed a man was given the choice by his Lord to live in this world as long as he wished, eating from it, or to meet his Lord; and he chose meeting his Lord.\" Abu Bakr wept. The companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do you not marvel at this old man? The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord gave the choice between this world and meeting his Lord, and he chose meeting his Lord.\" Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of them about what the Messenger of God ﷺ meant. Abu Bakr said: \"We would ransom you, O Messenger of God, with our wealth and our children.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"No one among people has been more generous to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah. If I were to take a close friend, I would take Ibn Abi Quhafah, but [our relationship is] the love and brotherhood of faith. Your companion is the beloved of God.\""],[19016,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade his companions on the day of al-Hijr from using their well, so the one with dough threw away his dough and the one with hays threw away his hays."],[19021,"That he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Sirmah al-Ansari both saying: \"We captured some female captives during the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq—that is the expedition in which the Messenger of God ﷺ obtained Juwayriyah bt. al-Harith. Among us were those who wanted to take them as wives, and among us were those who wanted to enjoy them and then sell them. We discussed withdrawal (coitus interruptus) and mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'It does not matter if you do not practice withdrawal, for God has decreed whatever He is creating until the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[19026,"That the Prophet ﷺ \"forbade eating the dab (lizard).\""],[19031,"From the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: \"If one of you owns something that is worth the price of a slave, let him manumit it, for every limb of it will ransom a limb of him from the Fire.\""],[19032,"\"He cooked a pot for the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Hand me a foreleg'—and he used to like the foreleg—so I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' so I handed him the foreleg. He said: 'Hand me the foreleg,' and I said: 'O Prophet of God, how many forelegs does a sheep have?' He said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if you had remained silent, you would have given me forelegs as long as I asked for it.'\""],[19033,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among the worst of thieves is he who steals the tongue of the ruler. Among the gravest of sins is he who seizes the property of a Muslim without right. Among good deeds is visiting the sick, and part of perfecting that visit is that you place your hand upon him and ask him how he is. Among the most excellent of intercessions is that you intercede between two people in a marriage until you bring them together. Among the clothing of the prophets is the shirt before the trousers. And among the things by which supplication is answered is sneezing.”"],[19034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no group of people who gather together to study the Book of Allah except that they are guests of Allah, and the angels surround them, and tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them to those who are near to Him. And there is no servant who leaves his home in search of knowledge, fearing that he may die or be harmed, except that he is like a traveler on the path of Allah. And whoever goes slower than him in his actions, his lineage will not make him go faster.\""],[19035,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Abu Suwayd, that the Prophet ﷺ “prayed for those who had partaken of the pre-dawn meal.”"],[19036,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of God, so-and-so has died, so pray over him.” Umar said: “He was a transgressor, so do not pray over him.” The man said: “O Messenger of God, do you not recall the night in which you were accompanied on guard duty? For he was among them.” The Messenger of God ﷺ stood and prayed over him, then followed until he came to his grave, and sat until he was done with him. Then he threw three handfuls of earth over him and said: “The people praise you with evil, but I praise you with good.” Umar said: “And what is that, O Messenger of God?” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Leave us be, O Ibn al-Khattab. Whoever strives in the path of God, Paradise is assured for him.”"],[19062,"the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , was commanded to pray for the people of Al-Baqi and he prayed for them three times in his night prayer. When he prayed for them the third time, he said, \"O Abu Muawiyah, saddle my mount for me.\" So I saddled the mount for him, and he rode and went to the people of Al-Baqi. Then he alighted and stood among them. He said, \"May you be refined by what you have faced from among the tribulations that come one after another, like pieces of a dark night. Some of them are worse than the others. May you be refined by what you have faced from them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , came and said, \"O Abu Muawiyah, I have been given, or I have been given the choice of the keys of what Allah will open for my nation after me, whether it is Paradise or meeting with my Lord.\" I said, \"By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, I chose the meeting with my Lord.\" He said, \"I have chosen the meeting with my Lord.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , did not stay except for seven or eight nights before he passed away."],[19081,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A settled person should not sell for a bedouin. Leave the people alone so that some may benefit from others; and if a man asks his brother for sincere advice, then let him advise him.' This is how Mansur b. Abi al-Aswad reported it from Hakim b. Abi Yazid, and he added to the people's narration in this hadith: 'A settled person should not sell for a bedouin.'"],[19083,"Abu Sulayman, the freed slave of Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed me that Abu al-Ramda al-Balawi informed him that a man among them drank wine, and they brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was flogged. Then he drank a second time, and they brought him, and he flogged him. I do not know whether he said on the third or the fourth time: he was ordered to be placed on a calf, and I struck his neck."],[19089,"Subay'ah gave birth after her husband's death by twenty-three nights. She desired [marriage]. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and he was informed, and he said: \"If she does, then her term has been fulfilled.\""],[19090,"I came to the Messenger of Allah and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am the man who came to you first.\" He said, \"Why do I not see you looking thin?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have not eaten any food during the day since I pledged allegiance to you.\" He said, \"Who told you to torture yourself?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am strong.\" He said, \"Fast the month of patience and two days after it.\" I said, \"I am strong.\" He said, \"Fast the month of patience and three days after it, and fast the sacred months.\""],[19093,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ undergo cupping.\""],[19096,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from a journey and greeted him. When I went to leave, he said: \"Wait for lunch, O Abu Umayyah.\" I said: \"I am fasting, O Prophet of Allah.\" He said: \"I inform you about the traveler: Allah has waived fasting and half of the prayer for him.\""],[19097,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Among the signs of the Hour are three, one of which is that knowledge will be sought from the young.\""],[19102,"We were with Anbasah b. Sa'id. One day I rode to al-Hajjaj, and a man called Abu Ghadiyah al-Juhani came to him. Abd al-A'la b. Abd Allah said, 'Get up to him and bring him down, and say: Now you will return.' So we went out to him and said, 'Now you will return.' He dismounted. Abd al-A'la entered and asked for water. He was brought water in a glass cup, but he refused to drink from glass. Then he was brought it in a cup of naddar wood, and he drank. He said: 'I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was returning wealth to my family.' Rashid b. Abyad, who was with me at Abd al-A'la's, said, 'With this right hand of yours?' Abd al-A'la rebuked him and said, 'Divide it for him.' He said: 'And I witnessed his sermon on the day of al-Aqabah, while he was saying: \"Indeed your blood and your wealth are forbidden to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this month of yours, in this land of yours. Indeed, do not return after me to disbelief, striking one another's necks.\" Then, when the day came that Uthman was besieged, I heard a man saying, \"Indeed, will you not kill this one?\" I looked at him, and behold, it was Ammar. Had it not been for those behind him from his companions, I would have pinned his belly to the ground. I said, \"O God, if You will, let me meet him.\" Then when the day of Siffin came, I saw a man of evil leading a battalion on foot. I looked at the armor, and it had slipped from his knee, and I thrust him, and behold, it was Ammar.'"],[19108,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No journey should be undertaken except to the Sacred Mosque, this mosque of mine, and the Aqsa Mosque.'"],[19109,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever is wealthy enough to marry and then does not marry is not of me.'"],[19115,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar appeared, so he said: “Praise be to Allah who has strengthened me through them.”"],[19116,"There was a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Abu Al-Khattab who asked the Prophet ﷺ about Witr prayer. The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"I prefer to perform Witr prayer during the second half of the night. Surely, Allah descends from the highest heaven to the lowest heaven and says, 'Is there anyone who asks so I may grant? Is there anyone who seeks forgiveness so I may forgive? Is there anyone who supplicates so I may respond?' Until the dawn comes up.\""],[19117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see women placing on their heads something like the humps of cattle, then let them know that no prayer will be accepted from them.”"],[19118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knocked on my door while I had been intimate with my wife. I disliked going out to him until I performed ghusl, so I was slow in coming to him. I caught up with him and informed him. He said to me: “Did you ejaculate?” I said: “No.” He said: “Indeed, only wudu was required of you.”"],[19119,"The Prophet ﷺ once prayed and entered his house, and amongst the people was a man with long hands who the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call \"Dhu al-Yadayn\" (the one with two hands). Dhu al-Yadayn said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did the prayer become shorter or did you forget?\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"It did not become shorter nor did I forget.\" He said, \"But you forgot the prayer.\" The Prophet ﷺ then advanced and prayed two Rak'ahs with them, then he made the salutation and pronounced the Takbeer and prostrated like his first prostration, or even longer. Then he pronounced the Takbeer and raised his head, then he pronounced the Takbeer and prostrated like his first prostration, or even longer. Then he pronounced the Takbeer and raised his head, and Muhammad did not preserve the salutation afterwards, or not?\""],[19122,"I was in Madinah and a woman passed by me, so I grabbed her side while I could hear the Messenger—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—accepting the people’s pledges. I went to him and he would not accept my pledge, saying: “The one who pinched yesterday.” I said: “By Allah, I will not do it again, O Messenger of Allah,” so he accepted my pledge."],[19125,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Hold fast to obedience to your leaders and do not oppose them, for obedience to them is obedience to Allah, and disobedience to them is disobedience to Allah. Allah sent me to call to His way with wisdom and good exhortation. Whoever succeeds me in that is from me, and I am from him.”"],[19126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will be after me successors (khulafaʾ), and after the successors commanders (umaraʾ), and after the commanders kings (muluk), and after the kings tyrants (jababirah). Then a man from my household will emerge and fill the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice. Then al-Qahtani will be given authority. By the One who sent me with the truth, he will not be less than him.”"],[19127,"“I saw on the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud two coats of mail.”"],[19128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever gives water to a thirsty person and quenches his thirst, a gate of Paradise is opened for him and it is said to him, ‘Enter through it.’ And whoever feeds a hungry person and satisfies him, and gives water to a thirsty person and quenches his thirst, all the gates of Paradise are opened for him and it is said to him, ‘Enter through whichever you wish.’”"],[19129,"Mismaʿ saw me praying behind the middle pillar of the House and said: My father narrated to me from my grandfather that “he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray two rakʿahs behind it.”"],[19130,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"A group of people will travel without having any company from these blessings, meaning a camel or anything. No one among you should be accompanied by a stray person, and no one should turn away a seeker if you seek profit and safety. No one should be accompanied by someone from the people if you truly believe in Allah and the Last Day. There will be no sorcerer or sorceress, no fortune-teller or fortune-telling woman, no astrologer or astrologer woman, and no poet or poetess. If Allah wants to punish any of His servants, He sends him to the lower heaven. Therefore, abstain from disobeying Allah in the evening.\""],[19131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The grave says to the dead person when he is placed in it: ‘Woe to you, son of Adam! What deceived you about me? Did you not know that I am the house of trial, the house of darkness, the house of solitude, and the house of worms? What deceived you about me when you used to pass by me strutting (faddadan)?’ If he was righteous, an advocate of the grave answers on his behalf, saying: ‘What do you think if he was one of those who enjoined good and forbade evil?’ The grave then says: ‘Then I will return to him as greenery, and his body will return as light, and his soul will ascend to the Lord of the Worlds.’” A man said: “O Abu al-Hajjaj, what is al-faddad?” He said: “The one who strides forward with one foot and drags the other, like your walk, O son of my brother, at times; and at that time he was dressing and adorning himself.”"],[19132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Cursed is the one who begs by the Face of Allah, and cursed is the one who is asked by the Face of Allah and then refuses the one asking him.”"],[19133,"From Abu Nuhaylah, a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that he was struck by an arrow, and it was said to him, “Pull it out.” He said: “O Allah, decrease the pain but do not decrease the reward.” It was said to him, “Make supplication.” He said: “O Allah, make me among those brought near, and make my mother among the fair maidens with wide, lovely eyes (al-hur al-ʿin).”"],[19134,"Abu ʿAtiyyah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and mentioned that a man had died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Did any of you see him engaged in any good deed?” A man said: “Yes, I stood guard with him one night in the cause of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and those with him stood up, and when he was placed in the grave, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ scooped up earth with his hand and threw it, then said: “Your companions think that you are among the people of the Fire, but I testify that you are among the people of Paradise.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿUmar b. al-Khattab: “Do not ask about people’s deeds, but ask about their innate nature (fitrah).”"],[19135,"And he is one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ bought a horse from a bedouin. He went ahead to pay him the price of his horse, and the Prophet ﷺ walked quickly while the bedouin walked slowly. Some men began to intercept the bedouin and bargain with him over the horse, not knowing that the Prophet ﷺ had already bought it, until one of them offered the bedouin more than the price for which the Prophet ﷺ had bought the horse. The bedouin called out to the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “If you are buying this horse, then buy it; otherwise I will sell it.” When the Prophet ﷺ heard the bedouin’s call, he said: “Did I not already buy it?” The bedouin said: “No, by Allah, we have not made a transaction.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, I did buy it.” People began to crowd around the Prophet ﷺ and the bedouin while they were arguing. The bedouin kept saying: “Bring a witness who testifies that I sold it to you.” Every Muslim who came said to the bedouin: “Woe to you! The Prophet ﷺ would never say anything but the truth.” Then Khuzaymah came and listened to the exchange between the Prophet ﷺ and the bedouin. The bedouin kept saying: “Bring a witness that I sold it to you.” Khuzaymah said: “I testify that you have sold it.” The Prophet ﷺ turned to Khuzaymah and said: “On what basis do you testify?” He said: “By affirming your truthfulness, O Messenger of Allah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the testimony of Khuzaymah equal to the testimony of two men."],[19136,"My brother and I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque of al-Khayf praying, and we had already prayed the obligatory prayer in the house, so we did not pray with them. He said: “What prevented you two from praying with us?” We said: “We had already prayed the obligatory prayer in the house.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a man prays the obligatory prayer in his house and then finds a congregation, let him pray with them, and his prayer in his house will be a supererogatory prayer.”"],[19137,"He came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a man from his people while he was in Madinah after his migration there. We found him striking the necks of captives at a small water source, and he continued until the blood flowed over the water. Safwan said: 'the blood flowed,' meaning it covered the water."],[19138,"From Abu Wahb al-Jushami, who was a Companion: He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Name yourselves with the names of the prophets. The most beloved of names to God are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, and the truest of them are Harith and Hammam, and the ugliest of them are Harb and Murrah. Tether horses, wipe their forelocks and hindquarters – or he said their flanks – and put garlands on them, but do not put bowstrings as garlands. Upon you are every dark bay with a blaze and white stockings, or a chestnut with a blaze and white stockings, or a black with a blaze and white stockings.'"],[19139,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The oath by which a man seizes the property of his brother – may it sever the womb.'"],[19140,"I saw Abu Amr al-Ansari, who was a Badri, an Aqabi, and an Uhudi, fasting and writhing from thirst. He was saying to a servant of his: 'Woe to you, shield me.' The servant shielded him until he drew his bow with a weak draw and shot three arrows. Then he said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of God, whether it falls short or reaches its target, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.' It was said that he was killed at sunset."],[19141,"The Prophet ﷺ went out on the day of Fitr to the prayer ground, with Ubayy b. Ka'b on his right and Umar – or he said Ibn Umar – on his left. When he finished, he passed by the door of Abu Kathir or Abu Kabir, while the butchers were in their courtyard and the people had recently left the pre-Islamic era. He said to them: 'How do you sell?' They said: 'Such and such.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Sell however you wish, but do not mix dead meat with slaughtered meat before the people. O people, beware: do not hoard, do not bid each other up, do not go out to meet caravans, no urban dweller may sell for a bedouin, no man may sell over the sale of his brother, and no man may propose over the proposal of his brother until he gives permission. A woman should not ask for the divorce of another woman in order to overturn her vessel; let her marry, for her provision is upon God ﷻ.'"],[19142,"The Prophet saw me and saw a red man. He said, \"You are the father of the rose.\""],[19143,"Abu Tayba passed by us in the month of Ramadan. We said: 'Where have you come from?' He said: 'I cupped the Prophet ﷺ.'"],[19144,"I heard my father say: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'O Messenger of God, is it part of tribalism that a man loves his people?' He said: 'No, but tribalism is that a man helps his people in wrongdoing.'"],[19145,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, two children of mine have died in Islam.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever has two children die in Islam, God will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.'"],[19146,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, two children of mine have died in Islam.' He said: 'Whoever has two children die in Islam, God will admit him to Paradise by the abundance of His mercy toward them.' Later, he met Abu Hurayra and said to him: 'Are you the one to whom the Messenger of God ﷺ said that about the two children?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'That he said it to me is dearer to me than Hims and Palestine being conquered for me.'"],[19147,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. When he wanted to perform ghusl, he would say: 'Turn away from me.' So I would turn my back to him. Then Hasan or Husayn was brought, and he urinated on his chest. I came to wash it, and he said: 'The urine of a girl is washed, but the urine of a boy is sprinkled with water.'"],[19148,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever supports two daughters, or two sisters, or two maternal aunts, or two paternal aunts, or two grandmothers, he is with me in Paradise like these two' – and the Messenger of God ﷺ joined his index finger and the one next to it. 'If they are three, he is given relief. If they are four or five, then O servants of God, help him, lend to him, lend to him, strike him, strike him.'"],[19149,"We entered upon Abu Ma'bad al-Juhani to visit him. We said: 'Will you not hang something (as an amulet)?' He said: 'Death is closer than that. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever hangs something (as an amulet), he is entrusted to it.'"],[19150,"\"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and believed in him and affirmed him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ gave me a drink of sawiq. The Messenger of God ﷺ drank the first of it and I drank the last of it, and I have not ceased to find its moisture on my heart when I thirst and its coolness when I am exposed to the sun.\""],[19151,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The woman with prolonged menstrual bleeding leaves off prayer during the days of her menstrual periods, then she performs ghusl and prays, then performs wudu for every prayer.\""],[19152,"\"Sneezing, postpartum bleeding, drowsiness, nosebleed, menstruation, vomiting, and yawning in prayer are from Satan.\""],[19153,"The Prophet ﷺ said, Enjoining, all that is good is a Sadaqa.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6021)"],[19154,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, it is like the ransom of a slave from the Children of Isma'il.\""],[19156,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say one day when the month of Ramadan had begun: \"If the servants knew what is in the month of Ramadan, the servants would wish that the month of Ramadan were a whole year.\" A man from Khuza'ah said: \"O Messenger of God, tell us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Paradise is adorned for the month of Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the beginning of the year, until when it is the first night, a wind blows from beneath the Throne and rustles the leaves of the trees of Paradise. The wide-eyed houris look at that and say: 'O Lord, make for us from Your servants in this month spouses by whom our eyes will be delighted and their eyes will be delighted by us.' There is no servant who fasts the month of Ramadan except that God marries him to a wife each day from the wide-eyed houris confined in pavilions. Upon each woman among them are seventy garments, no garment of the same color as another, and she is given seventy kinds of perfume, no kind resembling another. Each woman among them is on a couch of ruby studded with pearls, on seventy beds whose linings are of rich brocade, and above the seventy beds are seventy canopied couches. For each woman among them are seventy servant boys to serve her and seventy servant boys to receive her, and with each servant boy is a platter of gold containing a kind of food, the last of which he finds the same pleasure as the first. Her husband is given the like of that on a couch of red ruby, upon him are two bracelets of gold studded with red ruby. This is for every day he fasted from the month of Ramadan, besides the good deeds he has done.\""],[19157,"Abu Jubayrah b. al-Dahhak: Among us this verse was revealed, meaning the Banu Salamah. The Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, and there was no man among us but had two or three names. When a man was called by a name, they would say: \"O Messenger of God, he dislikes this.\" So it was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames} - the verse."],[19158,"Among us, the company of the Ansar, this verse was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames}. The Messenger of God ﷺ arrived and a man had two or three names. The Messenger of God ﷺ would sometimes call them by some of those names, and it would be said: \"O Messenger of God, he becomes angry from this.\" So it was revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames}."],[19159,"The Ansar used to give charity and give what God willed, then a year of drought befell them and they withheld, so God revealed: {And do not throw yourselves into destruction}."],[19160,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I and the Hour were sent like this,\" and he joined the middle finger and the index finger, \"so I preceded it as this preceded this.\""],[19162,"The Prophet ﷺ saw him standing in the sun and said: \"What is the matter with him?\" They said: \"He vowed to stand in the sun and fast and not speak.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"Sit, seek shade, speak, and fast.\""],[19163,"I heard Abu Asib, the servant of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , say that the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said, \"Jibril came to me with fever and plague, so I held the fever in Medina and sent the plague to the Sham as a testimony for my Ummah and a punishment for the disbelievers.\""],[19164,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"When you see the believing man given asceticism in this world and paucity of speech, draw near to him, for he has received wisdom.\""],[19165,"On the authority of 'Urwah, regarding \"the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Khaybar from the Ansar, then from the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, with the Messenger of God ﷺ: Abu al-Diyah or Abu Sabah.\""],[19166,"Nubayh b. Wahb narrated to me from Abu 'Aziz b. 'Umayr, the brother of Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who said: I was among the captives on the day of Badr, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Treat the captives kindly.\" I was among a group of the Ansar, and when they brought their lunch and dinner, they would eat dates and feed me bread, following the instruction of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to them."],[19167,"Abu Qays died, and he was one of the righteous of the Ansar. His son Qays proposed to his wife, and she said: \"I consider you as a son, and you are one of the righteous of your people, but I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and seek his advice.\" So she went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Abu Qays has died.\" He said to her something good. She said: \"His son Qays has proposed to me, and he is one of the righteous of his people, but I used to regard him as a son.\" He said to her: \"Return to your house.\" Then this verse was revealed: {And do not marry those [women] whom your fathers married}."],[19168,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Trustworthiness is among the Azd, and modesty is among Quraysh.\""],[19169,"From his grandfather Abu Hasan, who was a participant in Badr and a Companion of the 'Aqabah pledge, who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man got up and forgot his sandals. Another man took them and placed them under himself. The man came back and said: \"My sandals.\" The people said: \"We have not seen them.\" A man said: \"Here they are.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What about frightening a believer?\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did it only in jest.\" He said: \"What about frightening a believer?\" two or three times."],[19170,"\"We caught two fledglings of a dubsi bird in the markets when Abu al-Hasan, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entered, and he took a mitikhah and struck him with it.\""],[19171,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Remove from yourself the hair of disbelief and get circumcised.\""],[19172,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek good from those with handsome faces.\""],[19174,"\"Fatimah's kunyah is Umm Abiha (the mother of her father).\""],[19175,"\"More than one person told me that Fatimah was the youngest of them and the most beloved of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" and al-Zubayr b. Bakkar claimed that Ruqayyah was younger than Fatimah."],[19176,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a son al-Qasim, and he was the eldest of his children, then Zaynab, then 'Abd Allah, who was called al-Tayyib and also called al-Tahir. He was born after prophethood and died young, then Umm Kulthum, then Fatimah, then Ruqayyah, in this order, the first then the first. Al-Qasim died in Makkah, then 'Abd Allah died.\""],[19177,"\"Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was given the kunyah Umm Abiha. It is said she was the youngest child of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Khadijah, and it is also said she was the twin of 'Abd Allah, son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[19178,"Fatimah died six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Ali b. Abi Talib buried her at night."],[19179,"Fatimah lived six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[19180,"Ali buried Fatimah at night."],[19181,"Ali buried Fatimah at night."],[19182,"Fatimah remained six months after the Prophet ﷺ, then she died."],[19183,"Aisha said: Fatimah lived six months after the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[19184,"Fatima stayed after the Prophet ﷺ for three months, and she was not seen smiling after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that her tooth corner moved."],[19185,"When death came to Fatimah, she instructed Ali to prepare a washing place for her, so she washed and purified herself, and she called for her shroud garments. She was brought coarse, rough garments, and she put them on and touched some of the perfume. She instructed Ali not to uncover her when she died and to wrap her as she was in her garments. I said to him: Did she teach anyone to do that? He said: Yes, Kathir b. Abbas, and he wrote on the edges of his shroud: Kathir b. Abbas bears witness that there is no god but God."],[19186,"I heard Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah say: Fatimah bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ died when she was twenty-seven years old."],[19187,"Fatimah died when she was twenty-eight years old. Her birth was when Quraysh were building the Kaaba. Quraysh built the Kaaba seven years and six months before the Prophet's ﷺ mission. The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for ten years after his mission, then he emigrated and stayed ten years. Then Fatimah lived after him six months and died in the year eleven of the Hijrah."],[19188,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said: O people of the gathering, lower your gazes until Fatimah bt. Muhammad passes. She will pass wearing two green or red garments."],[19189,"I used to see the Messenger of God ﷺ kissing Fatimah, so I said: O Messenger of God, I see you doing something I did not see you do before. He said to me: O Humayra, when I was taken on the night journey to heaven, I was admitted into Paradise and stood by a tree of the trees of Paradise. I had not seen in Paradise a tree more beautiful than it, nor whiter leaves, nor better fruit. I took a fruit from its fruit and ate it, and it became a drop in my loins. When I descended to earth, I had intercourse with Khadijah, and she conceived Fatimah. So when I long for the scent of Paradise, I smell the fragrance of Fatimah. O Humayra, Fatimah is not like the women of human beings, nor does she suffer illness as they suffer."],[19190,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Fatimah: God becomes angry for your anger and is pleased for your pleasure."],[19191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months whenever he went out for the dawn prayer and say: The prayer! {Indeed Allah only intends to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with a thorough purification}."],[19192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. ‘Imran, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ.”"],[19193,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. ‘Imran, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ .”"],[19194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is an angel from the angels who sought permission from his Lord to greet me and visit me. He did not descend down to the earth before this moment, and he gave me glad tidings that Hasan and Husayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise and their mother is the leader of the women of Paradise.\""],[19195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “An angel from the sky who had never visited me asked Allah’s permission to visit me, and he gave me glad tidings, or informed me, that Fatimah is the foremost lady of the women of my ummah.”"],[19196,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which of your household is most beloved to you? He said: “The most beloved of my family to me is Fatimah.”"],[19197,"I entered with my maternal aunt upon ‘A’ishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: “Fatimah.”"],[19198,"My maternal aunt said: O Mother of the Believers, who was the most beloved of the people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: “His daughter Fatimah.”"],[19199,"He informed him that he heard the Prophet ﷺ on the pulpit saying: “My daughter is only a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what harms her harms me.”"],[19200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised and extolled Allah, then said: “My daughter – meaning Fatimah – is only a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what harms her harms me.”"],[19201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah is a part of me; whoever angers her angers me.”"],[19202,"‘Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “Fatimah is a part of me; what harms her harms me, and what angers her angers me.”"],[19203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Fatimah is a branch from me; what angers her angers me, and what gladdens her gladdens me.”"],[19204,"Ali b. Abi Talib proposed to me. That reached Fatimah, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Asma' is getting married to Ali.\" He said, \"It was not for her to offend Allah and His Messenger.\""],[19205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Fatimah one day while Ali was standing, she was lying down, and her sons were beside her. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a milch camel and milked it for them. He brought it, and al-Husayn woke up and began trying to drink before him until he cried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your brother asked for water before you.\" Fatimah said, \"It is as if al-Hasan is more preferred by you.\" He said, \"He is not more preferred by me than him; they are both in the same position with me. Indeed I, you, these two, and this sleeping one will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[19206,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us while I was sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so he went to a waterskin of ours and poured some from it. Then he brought the vessel, and al-Husayn got up to ask him for water. He said, \"Your brother asked for water before you; he will drink, then you will drink.\" Fatimah said, \"It is as if he is the more beloved of the two to you.\" He said, \"He is not the more beloved of the two to me; they are both in one position with me. Indeed I, you, these two, and this sleeping one will be in one place.\""],[19207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fatimah guarded her chastity, so Allah has forbidden her and her descendants to the Fire.\""],[19208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground and said, \"Do you know what this is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best women of the people of Paradise are Maryam bt. Imran, Asiyah bt. Muzahim, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[19209,"I will tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I have kept seeking martyrdom for that hadith but have not been granted it. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk saying, while we were traveling with him, \"Allah commanded me to marry Fatimah to Ali, so I did.\" Jibril ﷺ said, \"Allah built a garden of hollow pearl, between each hollow and the next a pearl of ruby studded with gold, and made its roofs green chrysolite, and placed in it arches of pearl crowned with ruby. Then He placed over it chambers, a brick of silver, a brick of gold, a brick of pearl, a brick of ruby, and a brick of chrysolite. Then He placed in it springs flowing in its corners, and it was bordered with rivers, and He placed over the rivers domes of pearl linked with chains of gold, and it was bordered with various trees, and He built in every branch a dome, and placed in every dome a couch of white pearl whose covering is fine silk and brocade, and its ground was spread with saffron and perfumed with musk and ambergris, and He placed in every dome a houri. The dome has one hundred doors, at each door two guardians and two trees, in every dome a spread, and around the domes was written the Verse of the Throne.\" I said, \"O Jibril, for whom has Allah built this garden?\" He said, \"He built it for Fatimah, your daughter, and Ali b. Abi Talib, besides her other gardens, as a gift He bestowed and to delight your eyes, O Messenger of Allah.\""],[19210,"Abu Bakr came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I, and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fatimah to me.\" He was silent about it, or he turned away from him. Abu Bakr returned to Umar and said, \"I am ruined and have ruined you.\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"I proposed Fatimah to the Prophet ﷺ and he turned away from me.\" He said, \"Stay where you are until I go to the Prophet ﷺ and seek the like of what you sought.\" Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you know my sincerity and my precedence in Islam, and I, and I...\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Marry Fatimah to me.\" He turned away from him. Umar returned to Abu Bakr and said, \"He is awaiting Allah's command concerning her. Come with us to Ali so that we may order him to seek the like of what we sought.\" Ali said, \"They came to me while I was on a path. They said, 'Your cousin's daughter is being proposed to.' They alerted me to a matter, so I got up dragging my cloak, one end on my shoulder and the other on the ground, until I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know my precedence in Islam and my sincerity, and I, and I...' He said, 'And what is that, O Ali?' I said, 'Marry Fatimah to me.' He said, 'What do you have?' I said, 'My horse and my body armor.' He said, 'As for your horse, you cannot do without it. As for your armor, sell it.' So I sold it for four hundred and eighty, and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and placed it in his lap. He took a handful from it and said, 'O Bilal, buy us perfume with it and order them to prepare her.' He made for her a bed carved with straps and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber, and filled the house with a heap, meaning sand. He said, 'When she comes to you, do not do anything until I come to you.' She came with Umm Ayman and sat on one side of the house while I was on the other side. The Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Here is my brother.' Umm Ayman said, 'Your brother whom you have married to your daughter.' The Prophet ﷺ entered and said to Fatimah, 'Bring me water.' She went to a bowl in the house, put water in it, and brought it to him. He rinsed his mouth into it. Then he said to her, 'Stand up,' and he sprinkled between her breasts and on her head. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for her and her descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said to her, 'Turn around,' so she turned around, and he sprinkled between her shoulders. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for her and her descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said, 'Bring me water.' I did what he wanted: I filled the bowl with water and brought it to him. He took some with his mouth, then spat it into it, then poured it on my head and before me. Then he said, 'O Allah, I seek refuge for him and his descendants with You from the accursed Satan.' Then he said, 'Enter upon your family with the name of Allah and blessing.'"],[19212,"Ali b. Abi Talib entered upon Fatimah and saw that she had applied kohl and worn dyed clothing, meaning during their Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ. He said to her, \"Who ordered you to do this?\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Ali said, \"I went off incensed against Fatimah, seeking a ruling from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'She has spoken truly, she has spoken truly.'\""],[19213,"A man came to Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O daughter of the Messenger of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leave anything with you that you might give me as a gift?\" She said, \"O servant girl, bring that palm-stalk.\" She looked for it and did not find it. She said, \"Woe to you, look for it, for it is equal to me to al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\" She looked for it, and it turned out she had used it as a broom in her sweeping. In it was written: Muhammad ﷺ said, \"He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his harm. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent. Allah loves the modest, the forbearing, the weak, the chaste, and He hates the obscene, the vulgar, the begging importunate. Modesty is part of faith and faith is in Paradise. Obscenity is part of vulgarity and vulgarity is in the Fire.\""],[19214,"O Abdullah, he disliked that. That remained among the oaths of al-Nu'man upon him until al-Husayn obeyed him concerning riding. He said, \"Since you have sworn, you have burdened me with what I dislike. Ride on the front of your mount and I will ride behind you, for I heard Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A man is more entitled to the front of his mount and the front of his bed, and to pray in his own home, except an imam who gathers the people to him.'\" Al-Nu'man said, \"The daughter of Muhammad the Messenger of Allah has spoken truly. I heard my father Bashir say as Fatimah said, and the Messenger of Allah said, 'except one who gives permission.' So Husayn rode on the saddle and the Ansari rode behind him.\""],[19215,"From his mother Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us on the evening of Arafah and said, \"Allah has boasted of you and forgiven you generally, and Ali specifically. I am the Messenger of Allah to you, not favoring my kin. This is Jibril informing me that the truly fortunate one is the one who loves Ali during his life and after his death, and the truly wretched one is the one who hates Ali during his life and after his death.\""],[19216,"When 'When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Fatimah and said, \"My soul has been announced to me as departing,\" so she wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me.\" So I laughed. Some of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saw her and said to her, \"I saw you weep and laugh.\" She said, \"He said to me, 'My soul has been announced to me,' so I wept. Then he said, 'Do not weep, for you are the first of my family to join me,' so I laughed.\""],[19217,"Fatima wept over the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “O my father, from his Lord how near he is! O my father, to Gabriel I announce his death! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode.”"],[19218,"“That you should pour dust over the Messenger of God ﷺ. O my father, from his Lord how near he is! O my father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. O my father, to Gabriel we announce his death. O my father, he answered a Lord who called him.”"],[19219,"A’ishah said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ fell ill in my house. Fatimah came walking to him—and by the One in Whose hand is A’ishah’s soul, her walk was just like the walk of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ whispered something to her and she wept; then he whispered to her and she laughed. I said: ‘I have never seen laughter closer to weeping than this day.’ I said: ‘O Fatimah, tell me what he said to you.’ She said: ‘I would not do that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ has seen your place.’ When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, she asked her and she said: ‘The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, but this year he reviewed it with me twice, and I think I am only being called by it, so I will answer. Fear God.”’ She said: ‘So I grieved.’ Then he whispered to me and said: ‘Are you not pleased that your husband is the first of the Muslims in Islam and the most knowledgeable of them in knowledge? For you are the mistress of the women of my community, just as Maryam was mistress over the women of her people.’”"],[19220,"A’ishah used to say: “In the illness in which the Messenger of God ﷺ was taken, he said to Fatimah: ‘O my little daughter, lean over me.’ So she leaned over him and he whispered to her for a while. Then she uncovered and she was weeping while A’ishah was present. Then after a while the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘Lean over me, O my little daughter.’ So she leaned over him and he whispered to her for a while. Then she uncovered from him and laughed. A’ishah said: ‘I said: O my little daughter, tell me what your father whispered to you.’ Fatimah said: ‘He whispered to me in a state of secret, and you thought that I would disclose his secret while he is alive. That distressed A’ishah that there should be a secret kept from her. When God took him, A’ishah said to Fatimah: ‘O my little daughter, will you not tell me that report?’ She said: ‘As for now, yes. He whispered to me the first time and told me that Gabriel ﷺ used to review the Qur’an with him once every year, and that he reviewed the Qur’an with him twice this year. He told me that he told him that no prophet lived except half the lifespan of the one before him, and that he told me that ‘Isa son of Maryam lived one hundred and twenty years, and I think I will only depart at the head of sixty. That made me weep. And he said: “O my little daughter, among the women of the Muslims there is no woman with a greater affliction than you, so do not be less than a woman in patience.” And he whispered to me the second time and told me that I am the first of his family to join him, and he said: “You are the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise except what there is of the virgin Maryam daughter of ‘Imran.” So I laughed at that.’”"],[19221,"Her walk was like the walk of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: “Welcome to my daughter,” and seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered a conversation to her and she wept. I said to her: “The Messenger of God ﷺ singled you out with his conversation and then you weep?” Then he whispered a conversation to her and she laughed. I said: “I have never seen joy closer to grief than this day.” I asked her about what he said, and she said: “I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” Until when he was taken, I asked her and she said: “He whispered to me and said: ‘Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, and this year he reviewed it with me twice, so I do not think it is except that my term has come, and you are the first of my household to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am for you.’ So I wept at that. Then he said: ‘Are you not pleased that you will be the mistress of the women of the community, or the women of the Muslims?’ So I laughed at that.”"],[19222,"The wives of the Messenger of God ﷺ gathered, and not one of them was absent. Fatimah came walking, and her walk did not differ from the walk of her father ﷺ. He said: “Welcome, O my daughter,” and seated her on his right or on his left. Then he whispered something to her and she wept; then he whispered to her and she laughed. We said to her: “The Messenger of God ﷺ singled you out among us with a secret, and you weep?” When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, I said to her: “Tell me what he whispered to you.” She said: “I would not divulge the secret of the Messenger of God ﷺ.” When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, I said to her: “I ask you by the right I have over you, tell me.” She said: “As for now, yes. He whispered to me and said: ‘Gabriel used to review the Qur’an with me once every year, and this year he reviewed it with me twice, and I do not think that is except at the approach of my term. So fear God and be patient, for what an excellent predecessor I am for you.’ So I wept. Then he whispered to me and said: ‘Are you not pleased that you will be the mistress of the women of the believers’—or he said ‘the women of this community’—so I laughed.”"],[19223,"I said to Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ: “I saw you lean over the Prophet ﷺ during his illness and weep, then lean over him a second time and laugh.” She said: “I leaned over him and he told me that he was dying, so I wept. Then I leaned over him and he told me that I am the first of his household to join him and that I am the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise except what there is of Maryam daughter of ‘Imran, so I laughed.”"],[19224,"While I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a room and he was playing with me and I was playing with him, Fatimah entered. The Messenger of God ﷺ took her by the hand and seated her behind him, and whispered to her something I do not know what it was. I looked at Fatimah weeping. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to me and spoke to me and played with me. Then he turned to her and played with her and whispered to her something. I looked at Fatimah, and there she was laughing. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and went out. I said to Fatimah: “What did the Messenger of God ﷺ whisper to you?” She said: “Not every time the Messenger of God ﷺ confides in me do I tell you.” I said: “I remind you of God and the womb.” She said: “He told me that he will be taken and that his term has come, so I wept at parting from the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he turned to me and whispered to me that I am the first of his household to join him, so I laughed at meeting the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[19225,"Fatimah daughter of the Prophet ﷺ entered, and he whispered something to her and she wept. Then he called her for something and she laughed. When he died, I said: “Tell me what made you weep and then made you laugh.” She said: “His own death was announced to him, so I wept. Then he whispered to me and said: ‘You are the first of my family to join me,’ so I laughed.” A’ishah said: “She lived only six months after him.”"],[19226,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called Fatimah during his illness and whispered to her, and she wept. Then he whispered to her and she laughed. I asked her about that: “What did you see—that he whispered to you and you wept, then whispered to you and you laughed?” She said: “The Messenger of God ﷺ told me of his death, so I wept. Then he told me that I am the first of his family to follow him, so I laughed.”"],[19227,"And he told me—meaning the Messenger of God ﷺ—that I am the first of his family to join him."],[19228,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called Fatimah after the conquest and whispered to her, and she wept. Then he spoke to her and she laughed. Umm Salamah said: “I did not ask her until when the Messenger of God ﷺ died. I asked Fatimah about her weeping and her laughter, and Fatimah said: ‘He told me that he will die, then he told me that I am the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise after Maryam daughter of ‘Imran. That is why I laughed.’”"],[19229,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her one day and said, \"Where are my sons?\" referring to Hasan and Husayn. She replied, \"We woke up and there is nothing in our house that they can taste.\" Ali said, \"I will take them, for I fear that they will cry for you and you have nothing with you.\" So he went to a certain Jew, and the Prophet ﷺ followed him and found them playing with some dates in front of them. He said, \"O Ali, won't you turn my sons over before the heat becomes intense for them?\" Ali replied, \"We woke up and there is nothing in our house. If you sit, O Prophet of Allah, until I gather some dates for Fatimah.\" So the Prophet ﷺ sat until some dates were gathered for Fatimah, and he put them in a piece of cloth. Then he turned to carry one of them, while I carried the other, until we turned them over."],[19230,"On the authority of Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that she brought al-Hasan and al-Husayn to the Messenger of God ﷺ during the illness in which he died, and said, “O Messenger of God, these are your two sons, so give them something as inheritance.” He said, “As for al-Hasan, he has my awe and my nobility, and as for Husayn, he has my courage and my generosity.”"],[19231,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Every children of a female have a paternal clan to which they belong, except the children of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and their paternal clan.”"],[19232,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque, he said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy,” and whenever he left, he said the like, except that he said, “The gates of Your bounty.”"],[19233,"Whenever the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque, he sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your mercy,” and whenever he left, he sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the gates of Your bounty.”"],[19234,"“Zaynab was the eldest of the daughters of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[19235,"To the Messenger of God ﷺ was born al-Qasim, who was the eldest of his children, then Zaynab. He said: Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ was married to Abu al-As b. al-Rabi b. Abd al-Uzza b. Abd Shams, and she bore him Ali and Umamah. Ali was being nursed among the Banu Ghadirah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took him away from them while his father was still a polytheist. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Whoever shares with me in anything, I have more right to it; and any disbeliever who shares with a Muslim in anything, he has more right to it than him.” Al-Zubayr said: Umar b. Abi Bakr al-Mu’ammal narrated to me: Ali b. Abi al-As b. al-Rabi, the son of Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, died when he had nearly reached puberty, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had seated him behind him on his riding camel on the Day of the Conquest."],[19236,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ asked permission of Abu al-As b. al-Rabi to go to the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of God ﷺ had emigrated, and he gave her permission. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then Abu al-As b. al-Rabi caught up with her in Madinah, and he sent word to her: “Obtain a guarantee of safety from your father.” So she put her head out from the door of her room while the Messenger of God ﷺ was leading the people in the dawn prayer, and she said, “O people, I am Zaynab, and I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished the prayer, he said, “I did not know of this until I heard it just now. The lowest of the Muslims may grant protection.”"],[19237,"“Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ granted protection to Abu al-As, and the Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection. And Umm Hani bt. Abi Talib granted protection to her brother Aqil, and the Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection.”"],[19238,"Zaynab emigrated to the Messenger of God ﷺ while her husband was a disbeliever. Then the Muslims captured Abu al-As b. al-Rabi, and Zaynab said, “I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” The Prophet ﷺ upheld her protection and said, “The lowest of the Muslims may grant protection.”"],[19239,"Among the captives on the day of Badr was Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Shams, the son-in-law of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the husband of his daughter Zaynab. Abu al-As was one of the notable men of Mecca in wealth and trustworthiness. He belonged to Halah bint Khuwaylid, and Khadijah was his maternal aunt. Khadijah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to marry Zaynab to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not oppose her; that was before revelation came down upon him. She regarded him as being in the place of her own child. When Allah honored His Prophet with prophethood, Khadijah and his daughters believed in him, affirmed him, bore witness that what he had brought was the truth, and followed his religion, while Abu al-As remained firm upon his polytheism. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married Utbah ibn Abi Lahab to one of his two daughters, Ruqayyah or Umm Kulthum. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ openly confronted Quraysh with the command of Allah and they openly opposed him, they said: You have relieved Muhammad of his concern, so return his daughters to him and occupy him with them. They went to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi and said: Separate from your wife, and we will marry you to any woman you wish. He said: No, by Allah, then I will not separate from my wife, and I would not love to have, in place of my wife, any woman of Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to praise him favorably regarding his relation by marriage, as it has reached me. They then went to the wicked Utbah ibn Abi Lahab and said: Divorce your wife, the daughter of Muhammad, and we will marry you to any woman of Quraysh you wish. He said: If you marry me to the daughter of Aban ibn Said ibn al-As, or the daughter of Said ibn al-As, I will separate from her. So they married him to the daughter of Said ibn al-As, and he separated from her, though the enemy of Allah had not consummated the marriage with her. Allah removed her from his hand as an honor for her and a humiliation for him, and Uthman ibn Affan married her after him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while in Mecca, was not able to declare lawful or unlawful, being overcome in his affair. Islam had already separated Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when she became Muslim, from Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi, except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not able to separate them. So she remained with him upon her Islam while he remained upon his polytheism, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ migrated to Medina, while she was still living with him in Mecca. When Quraysh marched to Badr, Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi marched among them, and he was taken among the captives on the day of Badr, and he was in Medina with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn Ishaq said: Yahya ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: When the people of Mecca sent for the ransom of their captives, Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent ransom for Abu al-As, and with it she sent a necklace of hers which Khadijah had given to her when she was brought in to Abu al-As at the time he consummated the marriage with her. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he felt intense tenderness for her, and said: \"If you think it proper to release her captive for her and return her property to her, then do so.\" They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So they released him and returned to her what belonged to her. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taken from him and made him promise that he would clear the way for Zaynab to come to him, as this was among the conditions he imposed upon him for his release. That was not made public by him nor by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that it would be known. But when Abu al-As left for Mecca and his way was clear, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Zayd ibn Harithah and a man of the Ansar immediately, and said: \"Be at the valley of Yajij until Zaynab passes by you, then accompany her until you bring her to me.\" So they went out to their place, and that was a month after Badr, or thereabouts. When Abu al-As arrived in Mecca, he ordered her to join her father, and she went out openly. Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm said: I was told from Zaynab that she said: While I was preparing in Mecca to join my father, Hind bint Utbah met me and said: O daughter of my uncle, if you need any goods that would help you on your journey, or money by which you may reach your father, then I have what you need, so do not hold back from me, for what enters between men does not enter between women. She said: By Allah, I do not think she said that except intending to do it, but I feared her, so I denied that I intended such a thing. Then I prepared myself. When I finished my preparations, my brother-in-law Kinanah ibn al-Rabi, my husband’s brother, brought me a camel, so I mounted it. He took his bow and his quiver, then went out with her by day, leading her while she was in her howdah. The men of Quraysh spoke of that, so they went out in pursuit of her until they caught up with her at Dhu Tuwa. The first to reach her was Habbar ibn al-Aswad ibn al-Muttalib ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, and Nafi ibn Abd al-Qays al-Zuhri at Qaynah of Banu Abi Ubaydah ibn Utbah ibn Nafi, the one in Ifriqiyyah. Habbar frightened her with the spear while she was in her howdah, and the woman was pregnant, as they claim; when she was terrified, she miscarried what was in her womb. Her brother-in-law dismounted and scattered his quiver, then said: By Allah, no man will come near me but that I will put an arrow into him. So the people drew back from him. Abu Sufyan came among the chiefs of Quraysh and said: O man, hold back your arrows from us so that we may speak to you. So he held back, and Abu Sufyan approached and addressed him, saying: You have not acted correctly. You went out with a woman openly before the people, while you know our calamity and disaster, and what has come upon us from Muhammad. If his daughter goes out to him openly from among us, the people will think that this is due to humiliation that befell us because of our calamity that occurred, and that it is weakness and feebleness on our part. By my life, we have no need to detain her from her father, but return the woman until the talk dies down and the people say that we have turned her back; then take her out secretly and send her to her father. He said: So he did so, and she stayed for several nights until, when the people had quieted down, he took her out at night until he handed her over to Zayd ibn Harithah and his companion, and they brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu al-As remained in Mecca, while Zaynab was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Islam had separated the two of them. Then, shortly before the conquest, Abu al-As went out as a merchant to Syria. He was a trustworthy man, carrying property of his own and property belonging to men of Quraysh who had entrusted merchandise to him. When he finished his trade, he returned with the caravan, and a detachment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him. They captured what was with him, while he escaped them in flight. When the detachment arrived with what they had captured of his property, Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi came under cover of night until he entered upon Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and sought her protection, so she granted him protection; he had come seeking his property. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out for the morning prayer, as Yazid ibn Ruman narrated to me, he pronounced the takbir and the people pronounced the takbir. Zaynab came out from the women’s section and said: O people, I have granted protection to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave salams from the prayer, he turned to the people and said: \"O people, did you hear?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"Indeed, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I knew nothing of anything that had happened until I heard it; and indeed the least of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed until he entered upon his daughter and said: \"O my little daughter, honor his lodging, but do not let him have access to you, for you are not lawful for him.\" Ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the detachment who had seized the property of Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi: \"This man is one of us, as you know, and you have seized property belonging to him. If you do good and return to him what is his, then we would love that; but if you refuse, then it is the fay of Allah which He has granted you, and you have the greater right to it.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, rather, we will return it. So they returned his property to him, until a man would bring a rope, another man would bring an old waterskin and a small waterskin, and one of them would even bring a pack peg, until, when they had returned all of his property to him and he was missing nothing from it, he carried it to Mecca. He returned to every owner of property among Quraysh his property, from those who had entrusted merchandise to him. Then he said: O assembly of Quraysh, is there any property of yours still with me that he has not taken? They said: No, and may Allah reward you with good, for we have found you to be chaste and noble. He said: Then I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. By Allah, nothing prevented me from accepting Islam with him except fear that you would think I only wanted to consume your wealth. But now that Allah has delivered it to you and I am free of it, I have accepted Islam. Then he set out until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19240,"On the authority of A’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that when the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, his daughter Zaynab left Makkah with Kinanah or the son of Kinanah. They went out after her, and Habbar b. al-Aswad caught up with her and kept thrusting her camel with his spear until he threw her down, and she miscarried what was in her womb and bled. She was carried away, and the Banu Hashim and the Banu Umayyah disputed over her. The Banu Umayyah said, “We have more right to her,” because she was married to their son Abu al-As. She was with Hind bt. Utbah b. Rabiah, and Hind kept saying to her, “This is because of your father.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Zayd b. Harithah, “Will you not go and bring Zaynab?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Take my ring and give it to her.” So Zayd set out, and he kept acting gently until he met a shepherd. He said, “For whom are you herding?” He said, “For Abu al-As.” He said, “Whose sheep are these?” He said, “For Zaynab bt. Muhammad.” He walked with him for a while, then said, “Would you like me to give you something that you will give to her and not mention it to anyone?” He said, “Yes.” So he gave him the ring, and the shepherd went off and brought his sheep in and gave her the ring. She recognized it and said, “Who gave you this?” He said, “A man.” She said, “Where did you leave him?” He said, “At such-and-such a place.” She remained silent until nightfall, then she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her, “Mount in front of me on my camel.” She said, “No, but you mount in front of me.” So he mounted and she mounted behind him until she arrived. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say, “She is the best of my daughters; she suffered because of me.” This reached Ali b. Husayn, so he went to Urwah and said, “What is this hadith that has reached me from you, that you narrate it diminishing the right of Fatimah?” Urwah said, “By God, I would not like to have everything between the east and the west if I were to diminish a right that belongs to Fatimah. But after this, I will never narrate it again.”"],[19241,"\"These people gathered around a pagan idol. Then suddenly, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared and called the people to believe in the oneness of Allah. The day broke and people started to disperse from around him. Then a woman appeared, carrying a cup and a handkerchief. The Prophet ﷺ took it from her, drank from it, performed ablution, and then raised his head towards her and said, 'O my daughter, cover your neck and do not fear any harm for your father.' I asked, 'Who is she?' They said, 'She is Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[19242,"“A man brought Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ, and two men of Quraysh caught up with him and fought him until they overpowered him and took her away from him, and she fell on a rock and miscarried and bled. Then they took her to Abu Sufyan, and the women of Banu Hashim came to him, and he handed her over to them. Then she came after that as an emigrant, and she remained ill until she died from that illness. They used to consider her a martyr.”"],[19243,"Zaynab bt. the Messenger of God ﷺ died, and we went out with him. We saw the Messenger of God ﷺ deeply troubled and intensely sad. We said, “We will not speak to him” until we reached the grave, and he had not yet finished its niche. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down and we sat around him, and he spoke to himself for a little while and kept looking at the sky. Then the grave was finished, and the Messenger of God ﷺ went down into it. I saw him become even sadder. Then he finished and came out, and I saw that he was relieved and smiled. We said, “O Messenger of God, we saw you troubled and sad, and we could not speak to you, and then we saw you relieved. What was that?” He said, “I was remembering the narrowness of the grave and its distress and the weakness of Zaynab, and that was hard for me, so I called upon God to lighten it for her, and He did. She was squeezed with a squeeze that was heard by all between the two horizons except jinn and humans.”"],[19244,"When Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ died, grief appeared in the Prophet ﷺ, then it was relieved. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you grieving then it was relieved.' He said, 'I saw Zaynab and her weakness, and that was made easy for her and for me. She was squeezed with a squeeze that reached the two horizons.'"],[19245,"Ruqayyah was with Utbah b. Abi Lahab. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab}, the Prophet ﷺ asked Utbah to divorce Ruqayyah, and Ruqayyah asked him for that. So he divorced her, and Uthman b. Affan ؓ married Ruqayyah, and she died with him."],[19246,"Ruqayyah bint Rasul Allah ﷺ was with Utbah b. Abi Lahab, but he parted from her. Uthman b. Affan married Ruqayyah in Makkah, and she emigrated with him to the land of Abyssinia. She bore him Abdullah, by whom he was given his kunya. She came with him to Madinah, and he stayed behind from Badr because of her, with the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him a share along with the shares of the people of Badr. He said, 'And my reward, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'And your reward.'"],[19247,"Ruqayyah died on the day Zayd b. Harithah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came with the good news of Badr."],[19249,"Utaybah b. Abi Lahab married Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ but did not consummate the marriage until the Prophet ﷺ was sent. Ruqayyah was with his brother Utbah b. Abi Lahab. When Allah ﷻ sent down {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab}, Abu Lahab said to his two sons Utaybah and Utbah, 'My head is forbidden from your heads if you do not divorce the two daughters of Muhammad.' Their mother, bint Harb b. Umayyah, who is the carrier of firewood, said, 'Divorce them, my sons, for they have become dear to him.' So they divorced them. When Utaybah divorced Umm Kulthum, he came to the Prophet ﷺ after parting from Umm Kulthum and said, 'I disbelieve in your religion and I have parted from your daughter. You do not love me and I do not love you.' Then he attacked him and tore the shirt of the Prophet ﷺ while he was leaving for Syria as a merchant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, I ask Allah to set His dog upon you.' He went out in a trading party of Quraysh until they stopped at a place in Syria called al-Zarqa at night. A lion surrounded them that night, and Utaybah began to say, 'Woe to my mother! By Allah, it will eat me just as Muhammad prayed against me. Ibn Abi Kabshah made me weep while he is in Makkah and I am in Syria.' The lion came at him from among the people, seized his head, and crushed him with a bite, killing him. Zuhayr b. al-Ala said: Hisham b. Urwah narrated to us from his father that when the lion surrounded them that night, they went away and slept, and Utaybah was placed in their midst. The lion came stepping over until it seized Utaybah's head and crushed him. Uthman b. Affan, may Allah have mercy on him, succeeded after Ruqayyah to Umm Kulthum, ؓ ."],[19250,"Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ was with Utaybah b. Abi Lahab, the one whom the lion ate, but he parted from her. When Ruqayyah died with Uthman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Kulthum to him, and she died with him without bearing him any child. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'If I had ten, I would marry them all to you.'"],[19251,"Uthman married Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ, and she died with him without bearing him any child."],[19252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood by the grave of his second daughter who had been with Uthman and said, 'Is there any father of a widow? Is there any brother of a widow? Uthman married her. If they had been ten, I would have married them all to Uthman. I did not marry him except by revelation from heaven.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Uthman at the door of the mosque and said, 'O Uthman, this is Jibril informing me that Allah ﷻ has married Umm Kulthum to you with a dowry like Ruqayyah's and with companionship like hers.'"],[19253,"He informed him that he saw on Umm Kulthum bint Rasul Allah ﷺ a striped silk garment."],[19254,"He saw on Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ a striped silk garment. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani said: This is how Ma'mar narrated it, as Zaynab, and he erred. The correct is Umm Kulthum."],[19255,"He informed him that he heard Abu Qatadah say: The Prophet ﷺ used to pray while Umamah bint Zaynab bint al-Nabi ﷺ, who is the daughter of Abu al-As b. al-Rabi b. Abd al-Uzza, was on his neck. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he stood from prostration, he took her and put her back on his neck."],[19256,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all from Malik b. Anas, from Amir b. Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, from Amr b. Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah: The Prophet ﷺ prayed while carrying Umamah bint Abi al-As b. al-Rabi. When he bowed, he put her down, and when he stood, he carried her."],[19257,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leading the people in prayer while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was on his shoulder. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose from prostration he returned her."],[19258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while carrying Umamah bint Abi al-‘As on his neck. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose he raised her."],[19259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to prayer carrying Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed he put her down from his shoulder, and when he finished his prostration he carried her on his shoulder. He continued doing that with her until he finished his prayer."],[19260,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come out carrying Zaynab's daughter on his shoulder while leading the people in prayer. When he stood he carried her, and when he bowed he put her down."],[19261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As was on his shoulder. When he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her."],[19262,"He heard Abu Qatadah saying, \"While we were sitting in the mosque, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying Umamah, the daughter of Abu Al-As, on his shoulder. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while she was on his shoulder, and when he prostrated, he put her down until he finished his prayer.\""],[19263,"He heard Abu Qatadah say: \"While we were sitting in the mosque waiting for the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying his daughter's daughter Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab. He was carrying her on his shoulder, saying the takbir while she was on his shoulder. When he bowed he placed her on the ground, and when he stood he returned her to his shoulder until he finished his prayer, doing that.\""],[19264,"I heard Abu Qatadah al-Ansari say: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying with the people while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As was on his shoulder. When he prostrated he put her down.\""],[19265,"\"While we were sitting in the mosque waiting for the prayer, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ on his shoulder—her mother was Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he bowed he placed her on the ground, and when he stood he returned her to his shoulder until he finished his prayer, doing that with her.\""],[19266,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying with his daughter's daughter Umaymah—or Umamah bint Abi al-‘As. He would carry her when he stood and put her down when he sat, until he finished his prayer."],[19267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying while carrying Umamah bint Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, daughter of Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘. When he bowed he put her down, and when he stood he carried her, until he finished his prayer."],[19268,"The prayer in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while carrying Umamah was the Fajr prayer."],[19269,"A necklace of onyx studded with gold was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his wives were gathered in a room, all of them, while Umamah bint Abi al-‘As b. al-Rabi‘ was a young girl playing with dust in a corner of the room. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How do you see this?\" We looked at it and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have never seen anything more beautiful or more wonderful than this.\" He said, \"Hand it back to me.\" When he took it he said, \"By Allah, I will place it on the neck of the most beloved of the household to me.\" ‘A’ishah said: The earth darkened between me and him, fearing that he would place it on the neck of someone other than me among them, and I saw that they were all struck by the same thing that struck me, and we all fell silent. Then he came with it and placed it on the neck of Umamah bint Abi al-‘As, and we were relieved."],[19270,"And Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' bequeathed his daughter Umamah to al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam along with his estate, so al-Zubayr married her to 'Ali b. Abi Talib after the death of Fatimah bint Rasul Allah ﷺ. Fatimah ؓ had enjoined that upon him. 'Ali b. Abi Talib was killed while Umamah bint Abi al-'As was with him, and she did not bear him any child. Umm al-Haytham al-Nakha'iyyah said concerning that:"],[19271,"\"Abu al-Hayyaj b. Abi Sufyan b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib succeeded to [the marriage of] Umamah bint Abi al-'As b. al-Rabi'—and her mother was Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ.\""],[19272,"Umamah bint Abi al-'As—her mother was Zaynab bint Rasul Allah ﷺ—was married to 'Ali b. Abi Talib. When he died leaving her, he had said to her: \"Do not marry; and if you desire marriage, then do not deviate from the advice of al-Mughirah b. Nawfal.\" Then Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan proposed to her. She came to al-Mughirah seeking his counsel, and he said to her: \"I am better for you than he, so entrust your affair to me.\" She did so. He invited some men and married her. Umamah bint Abi al-'As died while married to al-Mughirah b. Nawfal, and she did not bear him any child. Thus Zaynab has no descendants."],[19274,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. Her father desired to marry her to him. She prepared food and drink and invited her father and a group from Quraysh. They ate and drank until they became intoxicated. Then Khadijah said to her father: \"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah has proposed to me; arise and marry me to him.\" So he married her to him. She perfumed him and dressed him in a fine garment, for such was their practice with fathers when they gave their daughters in marriage. When the intoxication left him, he looked and saw himself perfumed and wearing a fine garment. He said: \"What is the matter with me?\" She said: \"You married me to Muhammad.\" He said: \"I married you to the orphan of Abu Talib? No, by my life!\" Khadijah said: \"Are you not ashamed? You want to make a fool of yourself, informing Quraysh and the people that you were drunk.\" She kept at him until he consented."],[19275,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married fifteen women. Of them, six were from Quraysh, one from the allies of Quraysh, seven from the rest of the Arabs, and one from the Children of Israel. In the Jahiliyyah, he married only one of them, and only she bore him children. The first woman he married in the Jahiliyyah was Khadijah bint Khuwaylid b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy. Before him, she had been married to 'Atiq b. 'A'idh b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum. Then after 'Atiq, Abu Halah Hind b. Zurarah b. Nabbash b. Habib b. Surad b. Salamah b. Jarwah b. Usayd b. 'Amr b. Tamim succeeded to her marriage. She bore him Hind b. Hind.\" Zuhayr said: Yunus b. 'Ubayd said: Hind passed through al-Basrah while traveling, and he died there; on that day neither market nor pasture was held. The Prophet ﷺ married her after those two. She bore him in the Jahiliyyah 'Abd Manaf, and she bore him in Islam two boys and four girls."],[19276,"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , married Khadijah bint Khuwaylid in Makkah. Before that, she was married to Atiq Ibn Abi A'idh Al-Makhzumi. Then he married Aisha in Makkah. He did not marry a virgin other than her. Then he married Hafsa bint Umar, who was previously married to Khunays Ibn Hudhafah As-Sahmi. Then he married Sawda bint Zam'a, who was previously married to As-Sakan Ibn Amr, the brother of Bani 'Amir Ibn Lu'ayy. Then he married Umm Habiba, the daughter of Abu Sufyan, who was previously married to Ubaydullah Ibn Jahsh Al-Asadi, Asad Ibn Khuzaymah. Then he married Zaynab bint Jahsh, who was previously married to Zayd Ibn Harithah. Then he married Maymuna bint Al-Harith and he took Juwayriya bint Al-Harith, from the Banu Mustaliq tribe as a captive in his raid when he demolished the Mannat Al-Muraysi. And he took Safiyya bint Huyayy bin Akhtab from the Banu Nadir tribe. She was among those whom Allah gave him as spoils of war. He divided her among his companions and offered her to Rayhana bint Zayd from the Banu Quraiza tribe, then he emancipated her and she reunited with her family while still maintaining her seclusion. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , divorced Al-Aliyah bint Zabyan and separated from the sister of Banu Amr bin Kilab and the sister of Banu Al-Jawna Al-Kindiyyah because of the beauty that was in them. Zainab bint Khuzaymah Al-Hilaliyyah passed away while the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , was alive. It has reached us that Al-`Aliyah bint Zabyan got married before Allah prohibited his wives. She married her cousin from her own people and bore children with him."],[19277,"\"The first woman whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married was Khadijah. Then he married Sawdah bint Zam'ah. Then he contracted marriage with 'A'ishah in Makkah and consummated it with her in Madinah. In Madinah he married Zaynab bint Khuzaymah al-Hilaliyyah. Then he married Umm Salamah. Then he married Juwayriyyah bint al-Harith; she was among those whom Allah granted him as spoils. Then he married Maymunah bint al-Harith—she was the one who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ. Then he married Safiyyah bint Huyayy; she was among those whom Allah granted him as spoils on the day of Khaybar. Then he married Zaynab bint Jahsh, who had been the wife of Zayd b. Harithah. Zaynab bint Khuzaymah died while married to the Prophet ﷺ, and Khadijah also died in Makkah. He married a woman from Banu Kilab of Banu Rabi'ah called al-'Aliyah bint Zabyan, and he divorced her when she was brought in to him.\""],[19278,"That the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, 'A'ishah bint Abi Bakr, Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, Hafsah bint 'Umar, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, Juwayriyyah bint al-Harith, Maymunah bint al-Harith, Zaynab bint Jahsh, Sawdah bint Zam'ah, and Safiyyah bint Huyayy—until there were gathered with him nine besides Khadijah, including al-Kindiyyah from Banu al-Jawn and al-'Aliyah bint Zabyan from Banu 'Amir of Banu Kilab, and Zaynab bint Khuzaymah, a woman from Banu Hilal. Al-Zuhri said: 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr informed me: When al-Kindiyyah was brought in to the Prophet ﷺ, she said: \"I seek refuge in Allah from you.\" He said: \"You have sought refuge in a Mighty One. Join your family.\""],[19279,"Ibn Abi Mulaykah and 'Amr b. Dinar said: Nine women were gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, including Safiyyah, besides Khadijah; all of them died while he was still alive. 'Uthman b. Abi Sulayman added two women besides the nine, both from Banu 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, both of whom he married. One of them was called Umm al-Masakin, and she was the best of his wives to the poor. He married a woman from Banu al-Jawn, but when she came to him she sought refuge from him, so he divorced her. He married a woman from Kindah but did not consummate the marriage with her. After the Prophet ﷺ she married, and 'Umar separated them and beat her husband. She said: \"Fear Allah, O 'Umar! If I am one of the Mothers of the Believers, then impose the veil upon me and give me what you have given them.\" He said: \"That is not the case.\" She said: \"Then let me marry.\" He said: \"No, by the blessing, and I will not entice anyone to that.\""],[19280,"The mother of all the sons and daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—other than Ibrahim—was Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. In the Jahiliyyah she was called al-Tahirah, daughter of Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy. Her mother was Fatimah bint Za'idah bint Jundub—he is al-Asamm b. Sakhr b. 'Abd Ma'is b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy. Her mother was Halah bint 'Abd Manaf b. al-Harith b. Munqidh b. 'Amr b. Ma'is b. 'Amr b. Lu'ayy. Her mother was al-'Ariqah, whose name was Qilabah bint Sa'd b. Sahm b. 'Amr b. Husays b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy. Hibban b. 'Abd Manaf, the full brother of Halah, was the one who shot Sa'd b. Mu'adh, may Allah have mercy on him, on the day of the Trench, saying: \"Take it, for I am the son of al-'Ariqah!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah make your face sweat in the Fire.\" The arrow struck Sa'd's median vein—may Allah have mercy on Sa'd—and he died as a martyr. Before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid had been married to 'Atiq b. 'A'idh b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. Makhzum, and she bore him Hind b. 'Atiq. Then Abu Halah Malik b. Nabbash b. Zurarah b. Wafdan b. Habib b. Salamah b. 'Adi of Banu Usayd b. 'Amr b. Tamim, an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy, succeeded to her marriage. She bore him Hind b. Abi Halah. So Hind b. 'Atiq, and Hind and Halah, the sons of Abu Halah Malik b. Nabbash b. Zurarah, were half-brothers of the children of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Khadijah bint Khuwaylid through their mother."],[19281,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Khadijah in Makkah. She was the first woman he married. Before him, she had been married to Abu Halah al-Tamimi. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when he was twenty-one years old, and she died seven years after his mission began.\" Al-Zubayr said: 'Umar b. Abi Bakr al-Mu'ammili narrated to me that 'Amr b. Asad married Khadijah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when he was twenty-five years old, while Quraysh was building the Ka'bah. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from Khalid b. Isma'il from Ibn Jurayj who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married when he was thirty-seven years old. Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. 'Urwah from his father who said: 'Amr b. Asad said: \"Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah is proposing to Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. This stallion—his nose is not to be struck [i.e., he is no one to be refused].\" Al-Zubayr said: Muhammad b. Hasan narrated to me from Muhammad b. Fulayh from Yazid b. 'Iyad from Ibn Shihab who said: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid was married to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before the Qur'an was revealed to him. Then the Qur'an was revealed to him while she was his wife. She was the first to believe the Prophet ﷺ and have faith in him. She died in Makkah three years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left for Madinah."],[19282,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry any other woman while Khadijah was alive until she died.\""],[19283,"I heard al-Zuhri say: \"The Prophet ﷺ did not marry any other woman while Khadijah was alive until she died.\""],[19284,"“Khadijah died three years or so before the Prophet ﷺ left for Madinah, and he married Aishah close to Khadijah’s death. He did not marry another wife while Khadijah was alive.”"],[19285,"“Khadijah died in Makkah three years before the Hijrah. She was the first of the women and men to believe in the Prophet ﷺ. He married no other woman in the pre-Islamic period, and none of his children came from any woman but her.”"],[19286,"“Khadijah died three years before the Prophet ﷺ left (Makkah).”"],[19287,"“Khadijah died three years before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated.”"],[19288,"\"Khadijah passed away before the obligation of prayers was ordained.\""],[19289,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Khadijah during her final illness and said to her: “What I see of you grieves me, O Khadijah, but Allah may bring much good out of what grieves (you). Do you know that Allah has married me along with you in Paradise to Maryam bint ʿImran, Kulthum the sister of Musa, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh?” She said, “Has Allah done that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Yes.” She said, “May it be with harmony and children.”"],[19290,"“When Khadijah died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was so deeply grieved by it that people feared for him, until he married Aishah.”"],[19291,"“Khadijah was the first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, along with ʿAli b. Abi Talib.”"],[19292,"“I came to Makkah to buy perfume and fragrance for my family, and I stayed with al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, who was a merchant. While I was with him at sunrise, I saw a young man come and look up at the sky, then turn his gaze toward the Kaʿbah. Soon a boy came and stood to his right, and then a woman came and stood behind them. The young man said ‘Allahu akbar’ and the other two said ‘Allahu akbar’; he bowed and they bowed; he prostrated and they prostrated. I said, ‘O ʿAbbas, this is something momentous.’ Al-ʿAbbas said, ‘Momentous indeed. Do you know who the young man is?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘This is Muhammad b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, my brother’s son. Do you know who the woman is?’ I said, ‘No.’ He said, ‘This is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzza, the leading woman of Quraysh, the wife of my brother’s son. And this is ʿAli b. Abi Talib, my brother’s son. My brother’s son claims that his Lord, the Lord of the heavens and the earth, has commanded him to this religion. By Allah, I know of no one on the face of the earth on this religion except these three.’”"],[19293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground. Then he said, “Do you know what these are?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The best women of Paradise are: Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. ʿImran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[19294,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The foremost women of Paradise are Maryam bt. ʿImran, then Fatimah bt. Muhammad, then Khadijah, then Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[19295,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Suffice you among the women of all the worlds: Maryam bt. ʿImran, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh.”"],[19296,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of its women is Maryam bt. ʿImran, and the best of its women is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid.”"],[19297,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The best of its women are Maryam bt. ʿImrān and Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid.”"],[19298,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Khadījah bt. Khuwaylid. He said: “I saw her on a river among the rivers of Paradise, in a house of hollow pearl; there is no idle talk in it and no toil.”"],[19299,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Khadījah, Jibrīl ﷺ came to him and said: “O Muhammad, convey to Khadījah greetings of peace from me, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no harm and no toil.”"],[19300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil."],[19301,"From Abū Hurayrah and Abū Saʿīd: They said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[19302,"Jibrīl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “Here is Khadījah coming to you with a vessel containing condiment, food, and drink. When she comes to you, convey to her greetings of peace from her Lord, and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[19303,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil."],[19304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Jibrīl said to me: ‘Give Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.’”"],[19305,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was commanded to give Khadījah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, in which there is no clamor and no toil.”"],[19306,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to mention Khadījah often, so I said: “How often you mention Khadījah! Allah has replaced Khadījah for you with an old woman with reddish gums who died long ago.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry with an anger like I never saw him become angry, and he said: “Allah granted me from her what He did not grant me from any of you.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, forgive me, may Allah forgive you. By Allah, you will never hear me mention Khadījah after this day with anything you dislike.”"],[19307,"I was never jealous of any wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I was jealous of Khadījah, and she had died three years before he married me, because of what I used to hear of his mentioning her. His Lord commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, and indeed, when he slaughtered a sheep, he would keep sending portions of it to Khadījah’s friends."],[19308,"I was never jealous of anyone as I was jealous of Khadījah because of what I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention of her. She said: “Allah commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl.”"],[19309,"I did not feel jealous of any of the wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I felt jealous of Khadijah because of how often he ﷺ mentioned her."],[19310,"Halah bt. Khuwaylid, the sister of Khadijah, asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. He likened her asking permission to Khadijah's asking permission and was gladdened by that. He said, 'O Allah, Halah!' I became jealous, and I have not been jealous of anyone as I was jealous of Khadijah. Minjab added in his narration: 'because of how often he mentioned her. He married me three years after her.'"],[19311,"I did not feel jealous of any woman as I felt jealous of Khadijah, and that is only because of how often the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned her."],[19312,"When the Prophet ﷺ was brought something, he would say, 'Take it to so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadijah.'"],[19313,"From the Prophet ﷺ, Aishah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Khadijah, he never tired of praising her and asking forgiveness for her. One day he mentioned her and jealousy overcame me until I said, 'Allah has compensated you with someone better than an old woman.' She said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ become angry with such anger that I sank into myself. I said to myself, 'O Allah, if You remove the anger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from me, I will never mention her with anything bad as long as I live.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what I had experienced, he said, 'What did you say? By Allah, she believed in me when the people disbelieved in me, she affirmed my truthfulness when the people called me a liar, and she was granted children from me when you were deprived of them from me.' He then went back and forth to me for a month."],[19314,"When the Prophet ﷺ mentioned Khadijah, he would praise her. I said, 'Why do you mention her when Allah has replaced her for you with someone better?' He said, 'Allah has not replaced her for me with anyone better than her. She believed in me when the people called me a liar, she shared her wealth with me when the people deprived me, and Allah granted me children from her when He did not grant me from any other.'"],[19315,"A woman entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Food was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he began eating from it and placing it before her. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do not keep your hands busy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This woman used to visit us in the days of Khadijah. Indeed, honor or preservation of the covenant is part of faith.' When he mentioned Khadijah, what takes hold of women from jealousy took hold of me, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has replaced for you an old woman with a young one.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and then said, 'What is my fault if Allah granted her children from me and did not grant you?' I said, 'By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never mention her after this except with good.'"],[19316,"Gabriel was with the Prophet ﷺ when Khadijah came. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Gabriel, this is Khadijah.' Gabriel ﷺ said, 'Convey to her greetings from Allah and from me.'"],[19317,"Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was at Hira. He said, 'This is Khadijah. She has come with a dish of dates mixed with butter (hays) in her small basket. Say to her that Allah conveys greetings to her.' When she came, he said to her, 'Gabriel informed me of you and of the hays in your basket before you arrived, and said that Allah conveys greetings to her.' She said, 'He is Peace, and from Him is peace, and upon Gabriel be peace.'"],[19318,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Khadijah, 'I hear a voice and see a light, and I fear that I may be possessed.' Khadijah said, 'Allah would not do that to you, O son of Abdullah.' She then went to Waraqah b. Nawfal and mentioned that to him. He said, 'If he is truthful, then this is a namus (angel of revelation) like the namus of Moses. If he is sent while I am alive, I will strengthen him, help him, and assist him.'"],[19319,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, where are my children from you?' He said, 'In Paradise.' I said, 'Without any deeds?' He said, 'Allah knows best what they would have done.' I said, 'Then where are my children before you?' He said, 'In the Fire.' I said, 'Without any deeds?' He said, 'Allah knew what they would have done.'"],[19320,"Mus'ab b. Abdullah narrated to me."],[19322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married A'ishah when she was six years old, and she was brought to him when she was nine, and her dolls were with her, and he died when she was eighteen."],[19324,"A'ishah died in the year fifty-seven."],[19325,"Do not bury me with them; bury me with my companions in al-Baqi'. I will never be pure again."],[19326,"The Prophet ﷺ adopted me, Um Abdullah, and I have never had any children."],[19327,"To the Prophet ﷺ: All your wives have a kunyah except me. The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Take the kunyah Umm 'Abd Allah.' So she was called Umm 'Abd Allah until she died, though she never gave birth."],[19328,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not give me a kunyah? All your wives have one. He said, 'Yes, take the kunyah by your son 'Abd Allah.' So she was given the kunyah Umm 'Abd Allah."],[19330,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have a kunyah except me. He said, 'You are Umm 'Abd Allah.'"],[19331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave A'ishah a kunyah though she had no child."],[19332,"The Prophet ﷺ married A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq. He did not marry any other virgin. She was then six years old. They claimed that Gabriel said, 'This is your wife,' before he married her. He married her in Makkah before the Hijrah and after Khadijah's death. Then he consummated the marriage with her in Madinah when she was nine, and he died when she was eighteen."],[19333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was brought a girl in a piece of silk after Khadijah's death, and it was you.' I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass. Then I was brought a girl again in a piece of silk, and I uncovered her, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass. A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me after Khadijah's death before his departure from Makkah, when I was seven or six years old. When we came to Madinah, women came to me while I was playing on a swing, and I had bangs. They prepared me and adorned me, then they brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was nine."],[19334,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I was brought you in a piece of silk in a dream on three nights, and it was said: This is your wife. I uncovered the cloth, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass.'"],[19335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw you in a dream twice. A man was carrying you in a piece of silk and saying: This is your wife; uncover her. So I uncovered her, and it was you. I said: If this is from Allah, He will bring it to pass.'"],[19336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was presented to him when I was nine, and he died when I was eighteen."],[19337,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine."],[19338,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was taken to him when I was nine years old. He came in to me while I was playing with dolls, and I had girlfriends who played with me. Sometimes they felt shy of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would send them to me."],[19339,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six years old and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine years old, and she remained with him for nine years."],[19340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old and consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."],[19341,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was six, and she was taken to him when she was nine, and she stayed with him for nine years."],[19342,"The Prophet ﷺ married her three years before his departure from Makkah, or close to that, and he married her when she was six years old. Then he consummated the marriage with her after his arrival in Madinah, and she was nine years old on the day of consummation."],[19343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when she was seven and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine, and he died leaving her when she was eighteen."],[19344,"I married the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was six years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."],[19345,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me at nine years of age, and I accompanied him for nine years."],[19346,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was seven years old and consummated the marriage with her when she was nine."],[19347,"I was taken to the Prophet ﷺ when I was nine years old, and I stayed with him for nine years."],[19348,"The Prophet ﷺ married Aisha when she was nine years old, and she remained with him for nine years."],[19349,"Khawlah bt. Hakim b. Umayyah b. al-Awqas, the wife of Uthman b. Maz'un, and that was in Makkah: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry?\" He said, \"Whom?\" She said, \"If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Who is the virgin?\" She said, \"The daughter of the most beloved of Allah's creation to you, Aishah bt. Abi Bakr.\" He said, \"And who is the previously married woman?\" She said, \"Sawdah bt. Zam'ah; she has believed in you and followed you in what you are upon.\" He said, \"Go and mention them both to me.\" So she came and entered the house of Abu Bakr and found Umm Ruman, the mother of Aishah, and said, \"O Umm Ruman, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to seek Aishah's hand for him.\" She said, \"I wish you would wait for Abu Bakr, for he is coming.\" So Abu Bakr came and she said, \"O Abu Bakr, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to seek Aishah's hand for him.\" He said, \"Is she suitable for him when she is only the daughter of his brother?\" So he sent me back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I mentioned that to him. He said, \"Go back to him and say to him: You are my brother in Islam and I am your brother, and your daughter is suitable for me.\" So she went to Abu Bakr, and he said to Khawlah, \"Call the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me.\" He came, and he gave her in marriage to him. On that day I was a girl of six years.\""],[19350,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years, and consummated the marriage with me when I was a girl of nine years."],[19351,"The Prophet ﷺ married her when she was nine years old, and he died when she was eighteen years old."],[19352,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated, he left us and left his daughters behind. When he settled in Madinah, he sent Zayd b. Harithah and with him Abu Rafi', his freedman, and gave them two camels and five hundred dirhams which he took from Abu Bakr, with which they were to buy what they needed of riding animals. Abu Bakr sent with them Abdullah b. Urayqit al-Du'ali with two or three camels, and he wrote to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr to transport his family: the mother of Abu Bakr, Umm Ruman, myself, my brother, and Asma', the wife of al-Zubayr. They set out together until they reached Qudayd. Zayd b. Harithah bought three camels with those five hundred dirhams, then they all entered Makkah and found Talhah b. Ubayd Allah intending to emigrate. We all set out together, and Zayd and Abu Rafi' departed with Fatimah, Umm Kulthum, and Sawdah bt. Zam'ah. Zayd carried Umm Ayman and her children Ayman and Usamah. They accompanied us until when we were at al-Bayda' of Namir, my camel bolted while I was in a litter with my mother in it. My mother began saying, \"Oh my daughter! Oh my bride!\" until our camel was caught, and it had descended from the mountain pass, the pass of Harsha, and Allah granted safety. Then we arrived in Madinah, and I alighted with the family of Abu Bakr. The Prophet ﷺ came down to me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time was building the mosque and some houses around the mosque, and he lodged his family in them. We stayed in them for some days. Then Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what prevents you from consummating marriage with your wife?\" He said, \"The bridal gift.\" So Abu Bakr gave him twelve uqiyah and a nashsh, and he sent it to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with me in this house of mine in which I am now, which is the one in which he died and was buried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ brought Sawdah bt. Zam'ah with him into one of those houses, and he used to stay with her. The Prophet ﷺ had married me while I was playing with the girls, and I was not told that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had married me until my mother took me and confined me in the house. Then it occurred to me that I had been married, but I did not ask her until she herself told me."],[19353,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Aishah to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr had already given her in marriage to Jubayr b. Mut'im. So he dissolved that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her when she was a girl of six years. He left her for three years, then consummated the marriage with her when she was a girl of nine years."],[19354,"I adorned Aishah for the Prophet ﷺ until I brought her in to him. When she entered upon him, we were brought a vessel of milk, and the Prophet ﷺ drank from it, then handed it to Aishah. She turned away, so I said, \"Take it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" She took it and drank, then handed it to me and I drank. I began rotating the vessel so that I might find the spot from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had drunk. Then I handed it to a woman with me, and she said, \"I do not desire it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not combine lying and hunger.\""],[19355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I was wearing a hawf, and no sooner had he married me than shyness was cast upon me. Sufyan said: A hawf is a garment of leather straps that the Bedouins clothe their daughters with."],[19356,"They fattened me with everything, but I did not gain weight, so they fattened me with cucumber and fresh dates, and I gained weight."],[19357,"When the Prophet ﷺ married me, my family fattened me with everything, but I did not gain weight, so they fed me cucumber and fresh dates, and I gained weight upon that in the best manner."],[19358,"My mother approached me with everything with which women are approached, but I did not respond to that. So they fed me cucumber and dates when they wanted to present me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I responded in the best manner."],[19359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me, and I was brought in to him in Shawwal. So which of the Prophet's ﷺ wives was more favored with him than I?\" He said: And she used to like her women to enter upon their husbands in Shawwal."],[19360,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was a girl of six years, and consummated the marriage with me when I was a girl of nine years, and he consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal. So which of your women was more favored with him than I? And she used to like her women to enter upon their husbands in Shawwal."],[19361,"She said about one who dislikes marriage in Shawwal: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me in Shawwal, and I was entered upon him in Shawwal.'"],[19362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Aisha bint Abu Bakr in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with her in Medina during Shawwal, after sixteen months of his migration to Medina. Aisha passed away on the night of Tuesday, in the seventeenth night of Ramadan, after the Witr prayer, in the fifty-eighth year. She was buried on the same night."],[19363,"On the authority of Nafi and others from the people of knowledge, they said: \"We performed prayer upon Aisha and Umm Salamah, the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, in the middle of Al-Baqi' cemetery, and Abu Hurayrah was the Imam (leading the prayer) on the day that we prayed upon Aisha. Abdullah ibn Umar attended, and Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr and Abdurrahman ibn Abi Bakr entered the grave of Aisha. She passed away in the year sixty-eight during the month of Ramadan, seventeen nights had passed after the Witr prayer, and she was buried on the same night.\""],[19364,"The Prophet ﷺ 'unveiled Aisha in her family's home before he consummated the marriage with her.'"],[19365,"I was given qualities no other woman was given: he married me when I was six years old, and the angel brought him my image in his palm, so he looked at it. He consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old. I saw Jibril, and no woman besides me saw him. I was the most beloved of his wives to him, and my father was the most beloved of his companions to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill with his final illness, and no one attended him but me and the angels."],[19366,"I was given seven things that none of the Prophet's ﷺ wives were given: I was among the people most beloved to him in person, and my father was among the people most beloved to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me as a virgin, and he did not marry any virgin other than me. Jibril used to descend upon him with revelation while I was with him under a blanket, and that was not done for anyone besides me. I had two days and two nights, while his wives had one day and one night. And my innocence was sent down from heaven, and groups of people almost perished because of me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death between my chest and neck."],[19367,"I was given six things that no woman after Maryam was given: Jibril descended with my image in his palm when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was commanded to marry me. He married me as a virgin, and he did not marry any virgin other than me. My innocence was sent down from heaven. And he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[19368,"'There are seven qualities in me that were not in any other woman except what Allah gave Maryam bt. Imran, and by Allah I do not say this to boast over any of my companions.' Abdullah b. Safwan said to her, 'And what are they, O Mother of the Believers?' She said, 'The angel descended with my image. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven, and I was given to him when I was nine. He married me as a virgin, and no one among the people shared me with him. Revelation used to come to him while I and he were under one blanket. I was the most beloved of people to him, and the daughter of the most beloved of people to him. Verses of the Quran were sent down concerning me, and the ummah almost perished because of me. I saw Jibril, and no one among his wives besides me saw him. He was taken in death in my house, and no one attended him but me and the angel.'"],[19369,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Isa b. Yunus narrated to us from Umar b. Sa'id from Ibn Abi Mulaykah that Abu Amr Dhakwan, the freed slave of Aisha, informed him that Aisha said: 'Among the blessings Allah bestowed upon me is that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death in my house, on my day, and between my chest and neck, and that Allah joined my saliva with his at the moment of death.' She said, 'My brother Abd al-Rahman entered upon me while I was supporting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against my chest, and in his hand was a siwak. He began looking at it, so I said, \"Shall I take it for you?\" He gestured with his head, yes. So I softened it for him, then I handed it to him, and he passed it over his teeth. In front of him was a small leather water container—or she said a wooden bowl—with water in it. He began dipping his hand in it, then wiping his face and saying, \"There is no god but Allah. Death has its agonies.\" Then he raised his hand and said, \"In the highest company,\" until he was taken, and his hand fell ﷺ.'"],[19370,"'Among Allah's blessings upon me and His good favor toward me is that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house and on my day, and was taken between my chest and neck, and my saliva was joined with his on the day he was taken.' He said: I said to her, 'This being in your house and on your day and between your chest and neck, how was your saliva joined with his?' She said, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abu Bakr entered upon me on the morning of Monday with a fresh siwak in his hand. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ staring at it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was fond of the siwak.' So I said, 'Split it and hand it to me.' He split it in two and handed it to me. I chewed it to soften it, then I put it in the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ mouth, and he used it as a siwak. Thus my saliva was joined with his.'"],[19371,"She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt pain that day when he returned from the mosque, so he lay down in my lap. A man from the family of Abu Bakr entered upon me with a green siwak in his hand.' She said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at his hand with a look, and I knew he wanted it. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to give you this siwak?\" He said, \"Yes.\"' She said, 'So I took it and chewed it for him until I softened it, then I gave it to him. He used it as a siwak more vigorously than I had ever seen him use a siwak before. Then he put it down. I found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ growing heavy in my lap, so I went to look at his face, and behold his gaze was fixed, and he was saying, \"Rather, the highest companion from Paradise.\" I said, \"You were given the choice and you chose, by the One who sent you with the truth.\"' She said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken in death.'"],[19372,"She said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, his back was leaning against me. Abd al-Rahman b. Abu Bakr entered with a siwak in his hand, and the Prophet ﷺ called for it. I took the siwak, softened it, then handed it to him. He began using it as a siwak, then his hand grew heavy and he grew heavy upon me, while saying, \"O Allah, in the highest company.\"' She said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken, while he was between my chest and neck.'"],[19373,"I heard Aisha say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died on my day, in my house, and between my chest and neck, and Allah joined my saliva with his.' She said, 'Abd al-Rahman entered upon me with a siwak. The Prophet's ﷺ hand had grown weak, so I took it, chewed it, then I brushed his teeth with it.'"],[19374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died between my arms and chest. After seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ die while he had a cup of water in which he would put his hand and wipe his face with the water, I will never dislike the severity of death for anyone. Then he said, \"O Allah, assist me in the agony of death.\""],[19375,"I heard Aisha say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing with the rider of a white horse, holding the horse's forelock. When he came to me, I said, 'Who is the rider of the horse?' He said, 'So you saw him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'And whom does he resemble?' I said, 'Dihyah b. Khalifah al-Kalbi.' He said, 'That was Jibril, and he conveys greetings to you.' I said, 'And upon him whom he sent, and upon you and upon him be peace.'"],[19376,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ with a man on a hackney, wearing a turban that he had fastened behind him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was placing his hand on the hackney's mane. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this?' He said, 'Did you see him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Who is he?' I said, 'Dihya al-Kalbi.' He said, 'That is Jibril ﷺ .'"],[19377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Aisha, this is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19378,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'This is Jibril, and he is conveying greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; you see what we do not see.'"],[19379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19381,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw you speaking with Dihya al-Kalbi while your hand was on the horse's mane.' He said, 'Did you see him?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is Jibril, and he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; from such a companion and such a guest, how excellent a companion and how excellent a guest.'"],[19382,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Aisha, Jibril conveys greetings of peace to you.' I said, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19383,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Aisha, 'This is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.' So Aisha said to him, 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19384,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'Jibril conveys to you greetings of peace from your Lord.' She said, 'I say: to my Lord be peace, and from Him be peace, and upon Jibril be peace.'"],[19385,"Jibril asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Who is this with you?' He said, 'Aisha.' He said, 'Convey to her greetings of peace from me.' He said, 'Excellent, excellent, O Aisha, this is Jibril, he conveys greetings of peace to you.'"],[19386,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the house, a man entered upon us on a horse. The Prophet ﷺ stood, then returned. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this?' He said, 'This is Jibril, and he has commanded me to convey greetings of peace to you.' So I said, 'Return the greeting to him: to him from me be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.'"],[19387,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished from the Confederates, he entered the place of washing to bathe. Then Jibril came and said, 'O Muhammad, you have put down your weapons, but we have not put down our weapons yet; go to Banu Qurayza.' Aisha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw him through the dust, with dust bound around his head.'"],[19388,"\"It was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him, and I closed the door between me and him. When it was lifted from him, he said, 'O Aisha, Gabriel ﷺ is greeting you.'\""],[19389,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: 'Indeed it eases death for me that I have been shown you as my wife in Paradise.'"],[19390,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, who are your wives in Paradise?' He said: 'Indeed you are among them,' or he said: 'Behold, you are among them.' It occurred to me that that was because he had not married a virgin other than me."],[19391,"She is the wife of the Messenger of God ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter."],[19392,"She is the wife of our Prophet ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter, but God tested us to know whether we obey her or him."],[19393,"A man disparaged Aisha in the presence of Ali, so Ammar said to him: 'Be quiet, despised and reviled! Would you harm the beloved of the Messenger of God ﷺ?'"],[19394,"A man was with Ali and spoke ill of Aisha, so Ammar said to him: 'Who is this one whom you disparage, the wife of our Prophet ﷺ in Paradise? Be quiet, despised!'"],[19395,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Salama: 'O Umm Salama, do not harm me concerning Aisha, for by God, revelation has never descended upon me while I was under the blanket of any woman among you except her.'"],[19396,"Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: The wives of the Prophet ﷺ sent Fatima to the Prophet ﷺ. She sought permission while he was lying with me under my cloak, and he granted her permission while I remained silent. She said: 'O Messenger of God, your wives have sent me to ask you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafa.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: 'O my little daughter, do you not love me?' She said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then love her.'"],[19397,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Many men have reached perfection, but among women none have reached perfection except Maryam daughter of Imran and Asiya wife of Pharaoh.' And the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19399,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19400,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed the excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.'"],[19401,"I heard Anas b. Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.”"],[19402,"Al-Qa‘nabī narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to us. Ḥ And ‘Alī b. al-Mubārak al-Ṣan‘ānī narrated to us: Ismā‘īl b. Abī Uways narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated to me, from ‘Abd Allāh b. ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Ma‘mar Abī Ṭuwālah, from Anas b. Mālik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over food,” or “The excellence of tharid over food is like the excellence of ‘A’ishah over women.”"],[19403,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The excellence of ‘A’ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over food.”"],[19404,"“O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “‘A’ishah.” He said, “From the men?” He said, “Abū Bakr.”"],[19405,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him on the expedition of Dhāt al-Salāsil. So I came to him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “‘A’ishah.” I said, “From the men?” He said, “Her father.” I said, “Then who?” He said, “‘Umar.” I said, “Then who?” And he counted several men."],[19407,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is most beloved to you?” He said, “And why?” I said, “So that I may love whom you love.” He said, “‘A’ishah.”"],[19409,"She said concerning ‘A’ishah: “The Prophet ﷺ could not restrain his love for her.”"],[19410,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day, “By Allah, O ‘A’ishah, it is not hidden from me when you are pleased and when you are angry.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, how do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ but when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “You have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.”"],[19411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry.” I said, “And how do you know that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “When you are pleased with me and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ and when you are angry and you swear, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I only avoid your name.”"],[19412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Indeed I know when you are pleased with me and when you are angry with me.” I said, “From where do you know that?” He said, “When you are pleased with me, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Muhammad,’ and when you are angry with me, you say, ‘No, by the Lord of Abraham.’” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I only avoid your name.”"],[19413,"I raced the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I beat him."],[19414,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he stopped at a place. He said to his companions, “Go ahead.” Then he said, “Come, so I can race you.” So I raced him and I beat him. Later, I went out with him on another journey after I had put on weight. We stopped at a place, and he said to his companions, “Go ahead.” Then he said, “Come, so I can race you.” So I raced him, and he beat me. He struck me between my shoulders and said, “This is for that.”"],[19415,"I raced the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I beat him. Then when I had gained weight, he raced me and beat me. He said, “O Aisha, this is for that.”"],[19416,"Aisha said to Abu Bakr, “I saw three moons fall into my room.” Abu Bakr said, “Three of the best people on earth will be buried in your house.” Yahya said: I heard people saying that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in her house, Abu Bakr said, “One of your moons, and he is the best of them.”"],[19417,"Abu Bakr said, “If your dream is true, three of the best people on earth will be buried in your house.” When the Prophet ﷺ died, Abu Bakr said to her, “The best of your moons, O Aisha.” And Abu Bakr and Umar were buried in her house."],[19418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Did any of you see a dream?” Aisha said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw three moons fall into my room.” He said to her, “If your dream is true, there will be buried in your house—I think he said—the best of the people of Paradise.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, and he is the best of her moons. Then Abu Bakr passed away, then Umar passed away, and they were buried in her house."],[19419,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys until we were at al-Bayda’ or Dhat al-Jaysh, and my necklace broke. The Prophet ﷺ stayed to search for it, and the people stayed with him, but they had no water with them. The people came to Abu Bakr and said, “Do you see what Aisha has done? She has detained the Prophet ﷺ and the people, and they have no water with them.” So he admonished me and said to me whatever Allah willed him to say, and he began poking me in my side with his hand. Nothing prevented me from moving except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting on my thigh. He slept until morning without wudu’, and Allah sent down the verse of tayammum. Usayd b. Hudayr said, “This is not the first of your blessings, O family of Abu Bakr.” Then we made the camel I had been riding stand up, and we found the necklace beneath it."],[19420,"Aisha’s necklace fell, so the Prophet ﷺ sent some men to search for it. Morning overtook them while they had no water, so they prayed without purification and complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ. Then tayammum was revealed. Ma‘mar said: Ayyub informed me that Abu Bakr passed by Aisha and said, “You have detained the people and caused them hardship.” Ma‘mar said: Hisham reported from his father, and Ayyub also said it. When tayammum was revealed, Abu Bakr was pleased with that and said, “I did not know you were so blessed. No disliked matter befalls you except that Allah makes in it good for the Muslims.”"],[19421,"She borrowed a necklace from Asma’, and it fell from her neck. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he sent men to search for it, and they searched and found it. The time for prayer came, so they prayed without purification, then they returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. Then Allah sent down the concession. Usayd b. Hudayr said, “May Allah reward you with good. By Allah, no disliked matter befalls you except that Allah makes for you and for the believers good from it.”"],[19422,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ were two groups: one group included Aisha, Hafsa, Safiyya, and Sawda, and another group included Umm Salama and the rest of the Prophet’s ﷺ wives."],[19423,"Whenever Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a journey, he used to draw lots amongst his wives, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take with him the one on whom lot fell. He drew lots amongst us during one of the Ghazwat which he fought. The lot fell on me and so I proceeded with Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah's order of veiling (the women) had been revealed. I was carried (on the back of a camel) in my howdah and carried down while still in it (when we came to a halt). So we went on till Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished from that Ghazwa of his and returned. When we approached the city of Medina he announced at night that it was time for departure. So when they announced the news of departure, I got up and went away from the army camps, and after finishing from the call of nature, I came back to my riding animal. I touched my chest to find that my necklace which was made of Zifar beads (i.e. Yemenite beads partly black and partly white) was missing. So I returned to look for my necklace and my search for it detained me. (In the meanwhile) the people who used to carry me on my camel, came and took my howdah and put it on the back of my camel on which I used to ride, as they considered that I was in it. In those days women were light in weight for they did not get fat, and flesh did not cover their bodies in abundance as they used to eat only a little food. Those people therefore, disregarded the lightness of the howdah while lifting and carrying it; and at that time I was still a young girl. They made the camel rise and all of them left (along with it). I found my necklace after the army had gone. Then I came to their camping place to find no call maker of them, nor one who would respond to the call. So I intended to go to the place where I used to stay, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me (in my search). While I was sitting in my resting place, I was overwhelmed by sleep and slept. Safwan bin Al-Muattal As-Sulami Adh-Dhakwani was behind the army. When he reached my place in the morning, he saw the figure of a sleeping person and he recognized me on seeing me as he had seen me before the order of compulsory veiling (was prescribed). So I woke up when he recited Istirja' (i.e. \"Inna li l-lahi wa inna llaihi raji'un\") as soon as he recognized me. I veiled my face with my head cover at once, and by Allah, we did not speak a single word, and I did not hear him saying any word besides his Istirja'. He dismounted from his camel and made it kneel down, putting his leg on its front legs and then I got up and rode on it. Then he set out leading the camel that was carrying me till we overtook the army in the extreme heat of midday while they were at a halt (taking a rest). (Because of the event) some people brought destruction upon themselves and the one who spread the Ifk (i.e. slander) more, was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai Ibn Salul.\" (Urwa said, \"The people propagated the slander and talked about it in his (i.e. ʿAbdullah's) presence and he confirmed it and listened to it and asked about it to let it prevail.\" ʿUrwa also added, \"None was mentioned as members of the slanderous group besides (ʿAbdullah) except Hassan bin Thabit and Mistah bin Uthatha and Hamna bint Jahsh along with others about whom I have no knowledge, but they were a group as Allah said. It is said that the one who carried most of the slander was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul.\" ʿUrwa added, \"ʿAisha disliked to have Hassan abused in her presence and she used to say, 'It was he who said: My father and his (i.e. my father's) father and my honor are all for the protection of Muhammad's honor from you.\"). ʿAisha added, \"After we returned to Medina, I became ill for a month. The people were propagating the forged statements of the slanderers while I was unaware of anything of all that, but I felt that in my present ailment, I was not receiving the same kindness from Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I used to receive when I got sick. (But now) Messenger of Allah ﷺ would only come, greet me and say,' How is that (lady)?' and leave. That roused my doubts, but I did not discover the evil (i.e. slander) till I went out after my convalescence, I went out with Um Mistah to Al-Manasi' where we used to answer the call of nature and we used not to go out (to answer the call of nature) except at night, and that was before we had latrines near our houses. And this habit of our concerning evacuating the bowels, was similar to the habits of the old 'Arabs living in the deserts, for it would be troublesome for us to take latrines near our houses. So I and Um Mistah who was the daughter of Abu Ruhm bin Al-Muttalib bin ʿAbd Manaf, whose mother was the daughter of Sakhr bin 'Amir and the aunt of Abu Bakr As-Siddiq and whose son was Mistah bin Uthatha bin ʿAbbas bin Al-Muttalib, went out. I and Um Mistah returned to my house after we finished answering the call of nature. Um Mistah stumbled by getting her foot entangled in her covering sheet and on that she said, 'Let Mistah be ruined!' I said, 'What a hard word you have said. Do you abuse a man who took part in the battle of Badr?' On that she said, 'O you Hantah! Didn't you hear what he (i.e. Mistah) said? 'I said, 'What did he say?' Then she told me the slander of the people of Ifk. So my ailment was aggravated, and when I reached my home, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, and after greeting me, said, 'How is that (lady)?' I said, 'Will you allow me to go to my parents?' as I wanted to be sure about the news through them. Allah's Apostle allowed me (and I went to my parents) and asked my mother, 'O mother! What are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter! Don't worry, for scarcely is there a charming woman who is loved by her husband and whose husband has other wives besides herself that they (i.e. women) would find faults with her.' I said, 'Subhan-Allah! (I testify the uniqueness of Allah). Are the people really talking in this way?' I kept on weeping that night till dawn I could neither stop weeping nor sleep then in the morning again, I kept on weeping. When the Divine Inspiration was delayed. Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAli bin Abi Talib and Usama bin Zaid to ask and consult them about divorcing me. Usama bin Zaid said what he knew of my innocence, and the respect he preserved in himself for me. Usama said, '(O Messenger of Allah ﷺ!) She is your wife and we do not know anything except good about her.' ʿAli bin Abi Talib said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Allah does not put you in difficulty and there are plenty of women other than she, yet, ask the maid-servant who will tell you the truth.' On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira (i.e. the maid-servant) and said, 'O Barira! Did you ever see anything which aroused your suspicion?' Barira said to him, 'By Him Who has sent you with the Truth. I have never seen anything in her (i.e. Aisha) which I would conceal, except that she is a young girl who sleeps leaving the dough of her family exposed so that the domestic goats come and eat it.' So, on that day, Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up on the pulpit and complained about ʿAbdullah bin Ubai (bin Salul) before his companions, saying, 'O you Muslims! Who will relieve me from that man who has hurt me with his evil statement about my family? By Allah, I know nothing except good about my family and they have blamed a man about whom I know nothing except good and he used never to enter my home except with me.' Saʿd bin Muʿadh the brother of Banu ʿAbd Al-Ashhal got up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I will relieve you from him; if he is from the tribe of Al-Aus, then I will chop his head off, and if he is from our brothers, i.e. Al-Khazraj, then order us, and we will fulfill your order.' On that, a man from Al-Khazraj got up. Um Hassan, his cousin, was from his branch tribe, and he was Saʿd bin Ubada, chief of Al-Khazraj. Before this incident, he was a pious man, but his love for his tribe goaded him into saying to Saʿd (bin Muʿadh). 'By Allah, you have told a lie; you shall not and cannot kill him. If he belonged to your people, you would not wish him to be killed.' On that, Usaid bin Hudair who was the cousin of Saʿd (bin Muʿadh) got up and said to Saʿd bin 'Ubada, 'By Allah! You are a liar! We will surely kill him, and you are a hypocrite arguing on the behalf of hypocrites.' On this, the two tribes of Al-Aus and Al Khazraj got so much excited that they were about to fight while Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept on quietening them till they became silent and so did he. All that day I kept on weeping with my tears never ceasing, and I could never sleep. In the morning my parents were with me and I wept for two nights and a day with my tears never ceasing and I could never sleep till I thought that my liver would burst from weeping. So, while my parents were sitting with me and I was weeping, an Ansari woman asked me to grant her admittance. I allowed her to come in, and when she came in, she sat down and started weeping with me. While we were in this state, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, greeted us and sat down. He had never sat with me since that day of the slander. A month had elapsed and no Divine Inspiration came to him about my case. Allah's Apostle then recited Tashah-hud and then said, 'Amma Badu, O ʿAisha! I have been informed so-andso about you; if you are innocent, then soon Allah will reveal your innocence, and if you have committed a sin, then repent to Allah and ask Him for forgiveness for when a slave confesses his sins and asks Allah for forgiveness, Allah accepts his repentance.' (continued...) (continuing... 1): -5.462:... ... When Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears ceased flowing completely that I no longer felt a single drop of tear flowing. I said to my father, 'Reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf concerning what he has said.' My father said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' Then I said to my mother, 'Reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf concerning what he has said.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' In spite of the fact that I was a young girl and had a little knowledge of Qur'an, I said, 'By Allah, no doubt I know that you heard this (slanderous) speech so that it has been planted in your hearts (i.e. minds) and you have taken it as a truth. Now if I tell you that I am innocent, you will not believe me, and if confess to you about it, and Allah knows that I am innocent, you will surely believe me. By Allah, I find no similitude for me and you except that of Joseph's father when he said, '(For me) patience in the most fitting against that which you assert; it is Allah (Alone) Whose Help can be sought.' Then I turned to the other side and lay on my bed; and Allah knew then that I was innocent and hoped that Allah would reveal my innocence. But, by Allah, I never thought that Allah would reveal about my case, Divine Inspiration, that would be recited (forever) as I considered myself too unworthy to be talked of by Allah with something of my concern, but I hoped that Messenger of Allah ﷺ might have a dream in which Allah would prove my innocence. But, by Allah, before Messenger of Allah ﷺ left his seat and before any of the household left, the Divine inspiration came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So there overtook him the same hard condition which used to overtake him, (when he used to be inspired Divinely). The sweat was dropping from his body like pearls though it was a wintry day and that was because of the weighty statement which was being revealed to him. When that state of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was over, he got up smiling, and the first word he said was, 'O ʿAisha! Allah has declared your innocence!' Then my Mother said to me, 'Get up and go to him (i.e. Messenger of Allah ﷺ). I replied, 'By Allah, I will not go to him, and I praise none but Allah. So Allah revealed the ten Verses:- - \"Verily! They who spread the slander Are a gang, among you.............\" (24.11-20) Allah revealed those Qur'anic Verses to declare my innocence. Abu Bakr As-Siddiq who used to disburse money for Mistah bin Uthatha because of his relationship to him and his poverty, said, 'By Allah, I will never give to Mistah bin Uthatha anything after what he has said about Aisha.' Then Allah revealed:-- \"And let not those among you who are good and wealthy swear not to give (any sort of help) to their kinsmen, those in need, and those who have left their homes for Allah's cause, let them pardon and forgive. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is oft-Forgiving Most Merciful.\" (24.22) Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said, 'Yes, by Allah, I would like that Allah forgive me.' and went on giving Mistah the money he used to give him before. He also added, 'By Allah, I will never deprive him of it at all.' Aisha further said:.\" Messenger of Allah ﷺ also asked Zainab bint Jahsh (i.e. his wife) about my case. He said to Zainab, 'What do you know and what did you see?\" She replied, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I refrain from claiming falsely that I have heard or seen anything. By Allah, I know nothing except good (about ʿAisha).' From amongst the wives of the Prophet ﷺ Zainab was my peer (in beauty and in the love she received from the Prophet) but Allah saved her from that evil because of her piety. Her sister Hamna, started struggling on her behalf and she was destroyed along with those who were destroyed. The man who was blamed said, 'Subhan-Allah! By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, I have never uncovered the cover (i.e. veil) of any female.' Later on the man was martyred in Allah's Cause.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 4141)"],[19424,"When the people of the slander said what they said about her and Allah declared her innocent. He said: Each of them narrated to me a portion of the hadith that Aisha ؓ narrated, and some of their hadith confirms the others, though some were more retentive than others. They claimed that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to go out on an expedition, he would draw lots among his wives, and whichever of them came out in the lot, he would take her with him. Aisha said: He drew lots among us for an expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah had revealed the hijab. I would descend and be carried in my howdah. We traveled until, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished that expedition and we approached Madinah returning, he announced departure one night. I got up when he announced departure to relieve myself. When I had finished my business, I came back to my baggage and found that a necklace of mine made of onyx beads had broken. So I went back searching for my necklace. The group that was loading the camels came and carried my howdah and placed it on my camel that I used to ride, thinking I was inside. At that time women were light; they had not become heavy with flesh, and they ate only small amounts of food. So the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah. I was a young girl. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and I came to their campsite, but there was no one there to call or answer. So I went to the place where I had been and thought that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting at my place, sleep overcame me and I fell asleep. Safwan b. al-Mu‘attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He set out early at night and reached my place in the morning. He saw the dark shape of a sleeping person and came to me. He recognized me when he saw me, as he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up when he uttered the words of recovery upon recognizing me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. He did not speak a word to me, and I did not hear a word from him except his utterance of recovery, until he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He led me on the mount until we reached the army after they had halted. Then those who were destroyed were destroyed. The one who assumed the greater part of the slander was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after arriving while the people were spreading the words of the slanderers. I was unaware of any of that, but it troubled me in my illness that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the kindness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter upon me, say, “How is this one?” and then leave. That troubled me, and I was unaware of the evil until I went out after I recovered. Umm Mistah went out with me toward al-Manasi‘, which was our place for relieving ourselves. We would not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were made near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to the open desert for relieving ourselves. We were bothered by having privies near our houses. So I set out with Umm Mistah, who was the daughter of Abu Ruhm b. al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf, and her mother was the daughter of Sakhr b. Amir, the grandmother of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her son was Mistah b. Uthatha b. al-Muttalib. I and Umm Mistah headed back to my house after we had finished our business. Umm Mistah tripped over her long outer garment and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said to her, “How bad what you said! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?” She said, “O you, have you not heard what he said?” I said, “What did he say?” Then she told me the words of the slanderers. I became more ill in addition to my illness. When we returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us, greeted, and said, “How is this one?” I said to him, “Will you permit me to go to my parents?” At that time I wanted to confirm the news from them. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, “O mother, what are the people talking about?” She said, “O daughter, take it lightly. By Allah, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives except that they say much against her.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! The people have been talking about this?” I spent that night until morning with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. She said: Then I woke up crying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, and he consulted them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ based on what he knew of his wife’s innocence and the affection he felt for them. Usama said, “O Messenger of Allah, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good of her.” As for Ali, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not restricted you; there are many women besides her. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira and said to her, “O Barira, have you seen anything that makes you suspicious?” Barira said, “By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything about her that I would hold against her, except that she is a young girl who sleeps off from the dough of her family, and a domestic animal comes and eats it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood that day and sought excuse against Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. He said while on the pulpit, “O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me concerning my household? By Allah, I know nothing but good about my household, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used to enter upon my family only with me.” She said: Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh al-Ansari stood and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers the Khazraj, command us and we will do your command.” Sa‘d b. Ubada stood up, who was the chief of the Khazraj that day. Before that he had been a righteous man, but zeal carried him away, and he said to Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, “You lie! By the life of Allah, you will not kill him, nor can you.” Usayd b. Hudayr stood up, who was the cousin of Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh, and said to Sa‘d b. Ubada, “You lie! By the life of Allah, he will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.” The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, rose up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was calming them until they became silent, and he became silent. She said: I spent that day with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept through my night, with no sleep and tears not ceasing, and they thought that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and sat down. He had not sat with me since the accusation was made. He had stayed a month without receiving revelation concerning my matter. He testified and then said, “To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will soon prove your innocence; but if you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses his sin and then repents, Allah turns to him.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped until I could not feel a drop. I said to my father, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” He said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to my mother, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” She said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.” I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, “By Allah, I know that you have heard this talk until it settled in your hearts and you believed it. So if I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows I am innocent, you will not believe me. And if I confess to you something, and Allah knows I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except the father of Yusuf when he said: ‘So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the One sought for help.’” Then I turned and lay on my bed. By Allah, at that time I knew that I was innocent and that Allah would prove my innocence, but by Allah, I did not think that Allah would send down revelation concerning me that would be recited, for my matter was too insignificant in my view for Allah to speak about me with a recited command. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see a dream in his sleep by which Allah would prove my innocence. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave his place, and no one from the household went out, until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent down revelation upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of the intense condition, until sweat like pearls poured from him even on a cold day, due to the weight of the Quran being revealed to him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, he was laughing. The first word he spoke was, “As for Allah, He has declared you innocent.” My mother said, “Get up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said, “By Allah, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but Allah.” Allah, Mighty is His mention, sent down: “Indeed, those who came with the slander…” the whole ten verses. When Allah sent down this about my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who was supporting Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship and poverty, said, “By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.” Then Allah sent down: “And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.” Abu Bakr said, “Yes, by Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me.” So he restored to Mistah the support he used to give him and said, “By Allah, I will never take it away from him.” Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about my matter. He said, “O Zaynab, what do you know or what have you seen?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good.” Aisha said: She was the one who rivaled me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and Allah protected her by her piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf, and she perished among those who perished among the people of the slander. Al-Zuhri said: This is what has reached us of the account of these people from the hadith of Aisha."],[19425,"All of them narrated to me a portion of her hadith, and some were more retentive than others and more accurate in narrating. I have memorized from each man among them the hadith he narrated to me, and some of their hadith confirms others. They claimed that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to go out on a journey, he drew lots among his wives, and whichever of them came out in the lot, he took her with him. She said: He drew lots among us for an expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the hijab had been revealed. I was carried in a howdah and descended in it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished that expedition and returned, and we approached Madinah, he announced departure one night. I got up when they announced departure and walked until I had passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business, I came back to the baggage and felt my chest, and found that a necklace of mine made of onyx beads had broken. So I went back searching for my necklace, and its search detained me. The people who were loading my camel came and carried my howdah and placed it on my camel that I rode, thinking I was inside. At that time women were light; they had not become heavy and flesh had not covered them, and they ate only small amounts of food. So they carried it, and I was a young girl. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and I came to their campsite, but there was no one in it. I headed to my place where I had been, and I thought that they would miss me and return to me. While I was sitting at my place, sleep overcame my eyes. Safwan b. al-Mu‘attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He reached my place in the morning and saw the dark shape of a sleeping person. He came to me, and he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up at his utterance of recovery when he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He led me on the mount until we reached the army after they had halted, resting at noon. Then those who were destroyed were destroyed. The one who assumed the greater part of the slander was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. I arrived in Madinah and fell ill there for a month, while the people were spreading the words of the slanderers, and I was unaware of any of that. But it troubled me in my illness that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah the kindness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter, greet, and say, “How is this one?” Then he would leave. That troubled me, and I remained unaware until I recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah toward al-Manasi‘, our place for relieving ourselves. We would not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were made near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in the open desert. I and Umm Mistah, daughter of Abu Ruhm, were walking when she tripped over her long outer garment and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said to her, “How bad what you said! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?” She said, “O you, have you not heard what they said?” I said, “What did they say?” She told me the words of the slanderers, and I became more ill in addition to my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said, “How is this one?” I said, “Permit me to go to my parents.” At that time I wanted to confirm the news from them. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, “What are the people talking about?” She said, “O daughter, take the matter lightly. By Allah, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives except that they say much against her.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! The people have been talking about this?” She said: I spent that night until morning with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. Then I woke up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to consult them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ based on what he knew of his wife’s innocence and the affection he felt for them. Usama said, “She is your wife, O Messenger of Allah, and we know nothing but good.” As for Ali, he said, “O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not restricted you; there are many women besides her. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barira and said to her, “Have you seen anything from her that makes you suspicious?” Barira said, “No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything about her that I would hold against her, except that she is a young girl who sleeps off from the dough until a domestic animal comes and eats it.” She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood that day and sought excuse against Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me concerning my family? By Allah,” he said it three times, “I know nothing but good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used to enter upon my family only with me.” She said: Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh stood and said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck; and if he is from our brothers the Khazraj, command us and we will do your command.” Sa‘d b. Ubada stood, who was the chief of the Khazraj and had been a righteous man before, but zeal carried him away. He said, “You lie! By the life of Allah, you will not kill him, nor can you do that.” Usayd b. Hudayr said, “You lie! By the life of Allah, he will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.” The two tribes Aws and Khazraj rose up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He came down to calm them until they became silent, and he became silent. I wept all day with tears not ceasing and no sleep soothing my eyes. My parents came to me in the morning, and I had wept through my day and night until I thought that weeping would split my eye. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and sat down. He had not sat with me since the accusation was made. He had stayed a month without receiving revelation concerning my matter. He testified and then said, “To proceed, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will soon prove your innocence; but if you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses a sin and then repents, Allah turns to him.” When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech, my tears stopped until I could not feel a drop. I said to my father, “Respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about what he said.” He said, “By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to my mother, and she said the same. I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, “By Allah, I know that you have heard what has been said, and it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. So if I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows I am innocent, you will not believe me. And if I confess to you something, and Allah knows I am innocent of it, you will believe me. By Allah, I find no example for me and you except the father of Yusuf when he said: ‘Patience is most fitting…’” She said: Then I turned on my bed, hoping that Allah would prove my innocence. But by Allah, I did not think that revelation would be sent down concerning my matter that would be recited, for I was too insignificant in my view for the Quran to speak about my matter. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would see a dream that would prove my innocence. She said: By Allah, he did not leave his seat, and no one left the house, until revelation came down upon him. He was seized by what used to seize him of the intense condition, until sweat like pearls poured from him on a cold day. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved, and he was laughing. The first word he spoke was, “O Aisha, praise Allah, for Allah has declared you innocent.” My mother said to me, “Get up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said, “By Allah, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but Allah.” Allah sent down: “Indeed, those who came with the slander…” the whole verses. When Allah sent down this about my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who was supporting Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship, said, “By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.” Then Allah sent down this verse: “And let not those of virtue among you…” to the end of the verse. Abu Bakr said, “Yes, I love that Allah should forgive me.” So he restored to Mistah the support he used to give him. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my matter. He said, “O Zaynab, what do you know and what have you seen?” She said, “I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good about her.” Aisha said: She was the one who rivaled me, and Allah protected her by her piety."],[19429,"When the people of the slander said about her what they said, and God declared her innocent. Each of them narrated to me a portion of the hadith that was narrated to me from Aisha, and some of their hadith confirms others, even though some of them were more retentive of her hadith than others. They mentioned that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to set out on a journey, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them the lot fell upon, he would take her with him. Aisha said: He cast lots among us during a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ after the veil had been revealed. I was carried in my howdah and brought down while in it. We traveled until, when the Messenger of God ﷺ had finished that expedition of his and returned, and we drew near to Madinah, he announced one night that we would depart. I got up when he announced the departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business and came back to my mount, I found that a necklace of mine made of A'far beads had broken, so I went back to look for my necklace, and my search for it detained me. The group that used to make me ready came and lifted my howdah onto my camel, the one I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. At that time we were light, as meat had not made us heavy; one of us would eat only a morsel of food, so the people did not notice the lightness of the howdah when they lifted it. I was a young girl, so they set the camel moving and went on. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and came to their camp, but there was no one there to call out or answer. I went to the place where I had been staying, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I fell asleep. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami had been behind the army, and he traveled on and arrived at my place in the morning. He saw the form of a sleeping person and recognized me when he saw me, for he had seen me before the veil. I woke up when he uttered \"inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un\" upon recognizing me, and I covered my face with my outer garment. By God, he did not speak a word to me, and I did not hear a word from him until he made his camel kneel, pressed down on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He set off leading the camel with me until he caught up with the army after they had halted in the extreme heat of midday. Then those who perished from the people of the slander perished, and the one who took upon himself the greatest share of the sin was Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after we arrived, while the people were indulging in the talk of the slanderers, and I was unaware of any of that. What disturbed me during my illness was that I did not perceive from the Messenger of God ﷺ the kindness that I used to see from him when I was sick; he would only enter upon me and say, \"How is that one of you?\" then leave. That disturbed me, but I was unaware of the evil until I went out after I had recovered, along with Umm Mistah, to the place for relieving ourselves, which was our open-air toilet. We would only go out at night to night, and that was before we had small closets near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to the desert for defecation, and we were annoyed by having closets near our houses. So I went out with Umm Mistah toward my house after we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled in her long garment and said, \"May Mistah perish!\" I said, \"What a bad thing you have said! Do you revile a man who was present at Badr?\" She said, \"O you, have you not heard what he said?\" I said, \"What did he say?\" She informed me of the talk of the slanderers, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of God ﷺ came in and said, \"How is that one of you?\" I said, \"Will you permit me to go to my parents?\" At that time I wanted to make sure of the news from them. He permitted me, and I went to my mother and father and said, \"O mother, what are the people talking about?\" She said, \"O daughter, take it lightly, for by God, rarely is a beautiful woman loved by a man who has other wives but that they speak much against her.\" I said, \"Glory be to God! Have the people really been talking about that?\" She said, \"Yes.\" I wept that night until morning, my tears not ceasing and I could not sleep. Then I spent the next day weeping. The Messenger of God ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to seek their counsel about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he advised the Messenger of God ﷺ according to what he knew of his wife's innocence and the affection he had in his heart for them, and said, \"O Messenger of God, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good about her.\" As for Ali b. Abi Talib, he said, \"O Messenger of God, God has not made things narrow for you; there are many women besides her. If you ask the slave girl, she will tell you the truth.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ called Barīra and said to her, \"O Barīra, have you seen anything that causes you doubt?\" Barīra said, \"No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen any fault in her that I could find, except that she is a young girl who sleeps and lets her family's dough be eaten by the domestic animals.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ stood that day and asked to be excused from Abdullah b. Ubayy. He said while on the pulpit: \"O assembly of Muslims, who will excuse me from a man whose harm to my family has reached me? By God, I know nothing but good about my family. They have mentioned a man of whom I know nothing but good, and he never used to enter upon my family except with me.\" Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, \"O Messenger of God, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you command us and we will do your command.\" Sa'd b. Ubada, who was the leader of the Khazraj, stood up, and he had been before that a righteous man, but zeal took hold of him, and he said to Sa'd b. Mu'adh, \"You have lied! By the life of God, you shall not kill him, and you are not able to kill him.\" Usayd b. Hudayr, who was the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood up and said to Sa'd b. Ubada, \"You have lied! By the life of God, we will kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.\" The two tribes, the Aws and the Khazraj, became agitated until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He kept calming them down until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I remained that day with my tears not ceasing and I could not sleep, while my parents were with me. I had spent two nights and a day without sleeping or my tears ceasing, thinking that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter upon me. I granted her permission, and she began to weep with me. While we were thus, the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon us and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since the talk had begun, and he had waited a month without receiving revelation concerning my affair. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ pronounced the testimony of faith when he sat down, then said: \"Now then, O Aisha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, God will soon declare your innocence. If you have committed a sin, ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges a sin and then repents to God, God accepts his repentance.\" When he finished his speech, my tears dried up so that I did not feel a single drop. I said to my father, \"Answer the Messenger of God about what he said.\" He said, \"By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.\" I said to my mother, \"Answer the Messenger of God.\" She said, \"By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.\" I said, while I was a young girl who did not read much of the Quran, \"You, by God, have heard this talk until it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent, and God knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me. But if I confess to something, and God knows that I am innocent, you will surely believe me. By God, I find for myself and for you no example except the father of Joseph, who said: 'So patience is most fitting. And God is the one sought for help against what you describe' (Quran 12:18).\" Then I turned away and lay down on my bed. She said: At that time I knew that I was innocent and that God would declare my innocence, but by God, I did not think that God would send down concerning my affair a revelation that would be recited, for my affair was too insignificant in my own eyes for God to speak about me in a matter that would be recited. But I hoped that God would show His Messenger a dream in which He would declare my innocence. By God, the Messenger of God ﷺ had not left his seat, and no one of the household had gone out, when God sent down revelation upon him. He was seized by the intense state that used to seize him, until sweat dripped from him like pearls on a cold day, because of the weight of the Quran that was being revealed to him. When the state left the Messenger of God, he recovered and was smiling. The first words he spoke were: \"O Aisha, God has declared your innocence.\" My mother said to me, \"Get up and go to him.\" I said, \"By God, I will not get up and go to him, and I will praise no one but God.\" Then God sent down: \"Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you...\" the ten verses in full. When God sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to spend on Mistah because of his kinship and poverty, said, \"By God, I will never spend anything on him again because of what he said about Aisha.\" Then God sent down: \"And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give...\" the verse. Abu Bakr said, \"Yes, by God, I love that God should forgive me.\" So he returned to spending on Mistah as he used to, and said, \"By God, I will never withhold it from him.\" Aisha said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, \"O Zaynab, what do you know or what have you seen?\" Zaynab said, \"I protect my hearing and my sight. By God, I know nothing but good.\" She was the one who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, but God protected her through her piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf and perished among those who perished from the people of the slander. Ibn Shihab said: This is what has reached us of the hadith of these people."],[19433,"Where the people of the slander said about her what they said, and God declared her innocent of all of it. A group narrated to me parts of her account, and some of them were more retentive of her account than others and more precise in its presentation. I have retained from each one of them the hadith that he narrated to me from Aisha. Aisha said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ intended a journey, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them the lot fell upon, he took her with him. He cast lots among us for a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the veil had been prescribed. I was carried in my howdah and set down in it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ finished that expedition of his and returned, and we drew near Madinah, he announced one night the departure. I got up when they announced departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business, I came back to the camp and felt for my chest, and found that a necklace of mine made of Yemeni onyx beads had broken. I went back searching for my necklace, and the search for it detained me. Then the people who were saddling my camel came and lifted my howdah and loaded it onto my camel that I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. Women in those days were light, not heavy, and flesh had not weighed them down; they ate only a morsel of food. So the people did not find the howdah heavy when they lifted it, and they loaded it. I was a girl of tender age. They set the camel going and departed. I found my necklace after the army had gone on. I came to their campsite and there was no one in it. I went to the place where I had been staying, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I slept. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, had halted in the rear of the army and then set off in the night. He reached my place in the morning and saw the dark shape of a sleeping person. He came to me, and he had seen me before the veil. I woke up at his saying 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we shall return.' By God, he did not speak a word to me, nor did I hear from him any word other than his utterance of 'Indeed we belong to God and to Him we shall return,' until he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, and I mounted it. He set off leading the mount with me until we reached the army after they had halted to rest in the midday heat. Then those who perished perished. The one who took upon himself the greater part of the slander was Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill there for a month. The people were spreading the talk of the slanderers while I was unaware of any of that. What troubled me during my illness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of God the gentleness I used to see from him when I was sick. He would only enter, greet, and then say, 'How is that one of yours?' That troubled me, and I was unaware of anything until I recovered. I went out with Umm Mistah toward the open area for relieving ourselves. We did not go out except from night to night, and that was before privies were built near our houses. Our practice was the practice of the early Arabs in going out to relieve themselves. I and Umm Mistah bt. Abi Ruhm were returning after we had finished our business, walking, when Umm Mistah stumbled over her long garment and said, 'May Mistah perish!' I said to her, 'How bad is what you said! Do you revile a man who was present at Badr?' She said, 'O you there, have you not heard what he said?' I said, 'And what did he say?' She informed me of what the slanderers said, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of God entered and said, 'How is that one of yours?' I said, 'Permit me to go to my parents.' She said: At that time I wanted to ascertain the news from them. The Messenger of God permitted me, so I went to my parents and said to my mother, 'What are the people talking about?' She said, 'My little daughter, take the matter lightly. By God, there is rarely a woman who is beautiful and loved by a husband who has co-wives but that they speak much against her.' I said, 'Glory be to God! Have the people really been talking about this?' She said: I spent that night until morning, with my tears not ceasing and no sleep touching my eyes. In the morning, the Messenger of God ﷺ called Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd, when the revelation was slow in coming, to consult them about separating from his wife. She said: As for Usama, he advised him according to what he knew of the innocence of his wife and what he knew in himself of affection for them. Usama said, 'O Messenger of God, she is your wife, and we know nothing but good.' As for Ali, he said, 'O Messenger of God, God has not made things narrow for you; women other than her are many. Ask the servant girl, and she will tell you the truth.' The Messenger of God called Barira and said to her, 'Have you seen anything from Aisha that troubles you?' Barira said, 'No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have not seen anything from her that I could fault her for, except that she is a young girl who sleeps over the dough until the domestic animal comes and eats it.' She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up that same day and sought to be excused from Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. The Messenger of God said, 'Who will excuse me from a man whose harm to my family has reached me?' He said it three times. 'By God, I know nothing but good about my family, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he never enters upon my family except with me.' Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, 'I, by God, O Messenger of God, will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, we will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you will command us and we will do to him as you command.' Sa'd b. Ubada stood up, and he was the chief of the Khazraj. He had been a righteous man before that, but zeal overcame him. He said, 'You have lied, by God's life, you will not kill him, and you cannot kill him.' Usayd b. Hudayr b. Simak stood up and said to Sa'd b. Ubada, 'You have lied, by God's life, he will surely kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of hypocrites.' The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, rose up in excitement while the Messenger of God was standing on the pulpit, calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. I wept that day and night, my tears not ceasing and no sleep touching my eyes, until I thought that weeping would split my liver. While I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I permitted her. She sat weeping with me. While we were like that, the Messenger of God entered and sat down, and he had not sat with me since what was said about me had been said. A month had passed and nothing had been revealed to him concerning my affair. The Messenger of God recited the testimony of faith, then said, 'To proceed, O Aisha, I have received such and such about you. If you are innocent, God will declare you innocent, and if you have committed a sin, then ask God for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant acknowledges a sin and then repents, God turns to him in forgiveness.' When the Messenger of God finished his speech, my tears stopped until I felt not a drop of them. I said to my father, 'Answer the Messenger of God regarding what he said.' He said, 'By God, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of God.' I said the same to my mother, and she said the same. I said, while I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Quran, 'By God, I know that you have heard what has been talked about, and it has settled in your hearts, and you have believed it. If I say that I am innocent, and God knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me in that. And if I confess to you a matter, and God knows that I am innocent of it, you will surely believe me. By God, I find no likeness for me and for you except what Abu Yusuf said: {So patience is most fitting.} And I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Quran.' Then I turned on my bed, hoping that God would declare me innocent of what I was innocent of. But by God, I did not think that revelation would be sent down concerning my affair, recitation that would be recited. For I considered myself too insignificant for Quran to be revealed about me. But I hoped that God would show His Messenger a dream in which He would declare me innocent. She said: By God, the Messenger of God had not left his seat, nor had anyone of the household gone out, when revelation came down upon him. He was seized by the intense distress that used to seize him at the time of revelation, until drops like pearls on a cold day were dripping from him. Then it was lifted from him while he was smiling. The first thing he said was, 'O Aisha, praise God, for God has declared you innocent.' My mother said to me, 'Get up and go to the Messenger of God ﷺ.' I said, 'No, by God, I will not get up to him, and I will not praise anyone but God, may He be glorified and exalted.' And God sent down {Indeed, those who came with the slander} and the rest of the verses. When God sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who had been spending on Mistah b. Uthatha because of his kinship with him, said, 'By God, I will never spend anything on Mistah after what he said about Aisha.' Then God sent down this verse: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give...} to the end of the verse. Abu Bakr said, 'Yes, I would love for God to forgive me,' and he returned to giving Mistah what he used to spend on him. She said: The Messenger of God had asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, 'O Zaynab, what do you know and what have you seen?' She said, 'I protect my hearing and my sight. By God, I know nothing but good about her.' Aisha said: She was the one among the Prophet's wives ﷺ who used to rival me. God protected her through piety. Her sister Hamna used to fight on her behalf, and she perished among those who perished."],[19434,"(the wife of the Prophet) \"Whenever Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a journey, he would draw lots amongst his wives and would take with him the one upon whom the lot fell. During a Ghazwa of his, he drew lots amongst us and the lot fell upon me, and I proceeded with him after Allah had decreed the use of the veil by women. I was carried in a Howdah (on the camel) and dismounted while still in it. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ was through with his Ghazwa and returned home, and we approached the city of Medina, Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to proceed at night. When the order of setting off was given, I walked till I was past the army to answer the call of nature. After finishing I returned (to the camp) to depart (with the others) and suddenly realized that my necklace over my chest was missing. So, I returned to look for it and was delayed because of that. The people who used to carry me on the camel, came to my Howdah and put it on the back of the camel, thinking that I was in it, as, at that time, women were light in weight, and thin and lean, and did not use to eat much. So, those people did not feel the difference in the heaviness of the Howdah while lifting it, and they put it over the camel. At that time I was a young lady. They set the camel moving and proceeded on. I found my necklace after the army had gone, and came to their camp to find nobody. So, I went to the place where I used to stay, thinking that they would discover my absence and come back in my search. While in that state, I felt sleepy and slept. Safwan bin Mu'attal As-Sulami Adh-Dhakwani was behind the army and reached my abode in the morning. When he saw a sleeping person, he came to me, and he used to see me before veiling. So, I got up when I heard him saying, \"Inna lil-lah-wa inn a ilaihi rajiun (We are for Allah, and we will return to Him).\" He made his camel knell down. He got down from his camel, and put his leg on the front legs of the camel and then I rode and sat over it. Safwan set out walking, leading the camel by the rope till we reached the army who had halted to take rest at midday. Then whoever was meant for destruction, fell into destruction, (some people accused me falsely) and the leader of the false accusers was ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. After that we returned to Medina, and I became ill for one month while the people were spreading the forged statements of the false accusers. I was feeling during my ailment as if I were not receiving the usual kindness from the Prophet ﷺ which I used to receive from him when I got sick. But he would come, greet and say, 'How is that (girl)?' I did not know anything of what was going on till I recovered from my ailment and went out with Um Mistah to the Manasi where we used to answer the call of nature, and we used not to go to answer the call of nature except from night to night and that was before we had lavatories near to our houses. And this habit of ours was similar to the habit of the old 'Arabs in the open country (or away from houses). So. I and Um Mistah bint Ruhm went out walking. Um Mistah stumbled because of her long dress and on that she said, 'Let Mistah be ruined.' I said, 'You are saying a bad word. Why are you abusing a man who took part in (the battle of) Badr?' She said, 'O Hanata (you there) didn't you hear what they said?' Then she told me the rumors of the false accusers. My sickness was aggravated, and when I returned home, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, and after greeting he said, 'How is that (girl)?' I requested him to allow me to go to my parents. I wanted then to be sure of the news through them I Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed me, and I went to my parents and asked my mother, 'What are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter! Don't worry much about this matter. By Allah, never is there a charming woman loved by her husband who has other wives, but the women would forge false news about her.' I said, 'Glorified be Allah! Are the people really taking of this matter?' That night I kept on weeping and could not sleep till morning. In the morning Messenger of Allah ﷺ called ʿAli bin Abu Talib and Usama bin Zaid when he saw the Divine Inspiration delayed, to consul them about divorcing his wife (i.e. ʿAisha). Usama bin Zaid said what he knew of the good reputation of his wives and added, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Keep you wife, for, by Allah, we know nothing about her but good.' ʿAli bin Abu Talib said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Allah has no imposed restrictions on you, and there are many women other than she, yet you may ask the woman-servant who will tell you the truth.' On that Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Barirah and said, 'O Barirah. Did you ever see anything which roused your suspicions about her?' Barirah said, 'No, by Allah Who has sent you with the Truth, I have never seen in her anything faulty except that she is a girl of immature age, who sometimes sleeps and leaves the dough for the goats to eat.' On that day Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and requested that somebody support him in punishing ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul. Allah's Apostle said, 'Who will support me to punish that person (ʿAbdullah bin Ubai bin Salul) who has hurt me by slandering the reputation of my family? By Allah, I know nothing about my family but good, and they have accused a person about whom I know nothing except good, and he never entered my house except in my company.' Saʿd bin Muʿadh got up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! by Allah, I will relieve you from him. If that man is from the tribe of the Aus, then we will chop his head off, and if he is from our brothers, the Khazraj, then order us, and we will fulfill your order.' On that Saʿd bin 'Ubada, the chief of the Khazraj and before this incident, he had been a pious man, got up, motivated by his zeal for his tribe and said, 'By Allah, you have told a lie; you cannot kill him, and you will never be able to kill him.' On that Usaid bin Al-Hadir got up and said (to Saʿd bin 'Ubada), 'By Allah! you are a liar. By Allah, we will kill him; and you are a hypocrite, defending the hypocrites.' On this the two tribes of Aus and Khazraj got excited and were about to fight each other, while Messenger of Allah ﷺ was standing on the pulpit. He got down and quieted them till they became silent and he kept quiet. On that day I kept on weeping so much so that neither did my tears stop, nor could I sleep. In the morning my parents were with me and I had wept for two nights and a day, till I thought my liver would burst from weeping. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, an Ansari woman asked my permission to enter, and I allowed her to come in. She sat down and started weeping with me. While we were in this state, Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and sat down and he had never sat with me since the day they forged the accusation. No revelation regarding my case came to him for a month. He recited Tashah-hud (i.e. None has the right to be worshipped but Allah and Muhammad is His Apostle) and then said, 'O ʿAisha! I have been informed such-and-such about you; if you are innocent, then Allah will soon reveal your innocence, and if you have committed a sin, then repent to Allah and ask Him to forgive you, for when a person confesses his sin and asks Allah for forgiveness, Allah accepts his repentance.' When Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his speech my tears ceased completely and there remained not even a single drop of it. I requested my father to reply to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf. My father said, By Allah, I do not know what to say to Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said to my mother, 'Talk to Messenger of Allah ﷺ on my behalf.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to Allah's Apostle. I was a young girl and did not have much knowledge of the Qur'an. I said. 'I know, by Allah, that you have listened to what people are saying and that has been planted in your minds and you have taken it as a truth. Now, if I told you that I am innocent and Allah knows that I am innocent, you would not believe me and if I confessed to you falsely that I am guilty, and Allah knows that I am innocent you would believe me. By Allah, I don't compare my situation with you except to the situation of Joseph's father (i.e. Jacob) who said, 'So (for me) patience is most fitting against that which you assert and it is Allah (Alone) whose help can be sought.' Then I turned to the other side of my bed hoping that Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah I never thought that Allah would reveal Divine Inspiration in my case, as I considered myself too inferior to be talked of in the Holy Qur'an. I had hoped that Messenger of Allah ﷺ might have a dream in which Allah would prove my innocence. By Allah, Allah's Apostle had not got up and nobody had left the house before the Divine Inspiration came to Allah's Apostle. So, there overtook him the same state which used to overtake him, (when he used to have, on being inspired divinely). He was sweating so much so that the drops of the sweat were dropping like pearls though it was a (cold) wintry day. When that state of Messenger of Allah ﷺ was over, he was smiling and the first word he said, ʿAisha! Thank Allah, for Allah has declared your innocence.' My mother told me to go to Messenger of Allah ﷺ . I replied, 'By Allah I will not go to him and will not thank but Allah.' So Allah revealed: \"Verily! They who spread the slander are a gang among you . . .\" (24.11) When Allah gave the declaration of my Innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to provide for Mistah bin Uthatha for he was his relative, said, 'By Allah, I will never provide Mistah with anything because of what he said about Aisha.' But Allah later revealed: -- \"And let not those who are good and wealthy among you swear not to help their kinsmen, those in need and those who left their homes in Allah's Cause. Let them forgive and overlook. Do you not wish that Allah should forgive you? Verily! Allah is Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful.\" (24.22) After that Abu Bakr said, 'Yes ! By Allah! I like that Allah should forgive me,' and resumed helping Mistah whom he used to help before. Messenger of Allah ﷺ also asked Zainab bint Jahsh (i.e. the Prophet's wife about me saying, 'What do you know and what did you see?' She replied, 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I refrain to claim hearing or seeing what I have not heard or seen. By Allah, I know nothing except goodness about Aisha.\" Aisha further added \"Zainab was competing with me (in her beauty and the Prophet's love), yet Allah protected her (from being malicious), for she had piety.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2661)"],[19435,"I was with al-Walid b. 'Abd al-Malik one night as he was reciting Surat al-Nur while reclining. When he reached {Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you} until he reached {And the one who took upon himself the greater part of it will have a great punishment}, he sat up and said, 'O Abu Bakr, who took upon himself the greater part of it? Was it not 'Ali b. Abi Talib?' I said to myself, 'What should I say? If I say no, I fear I will encounter evil from him, and if I say yes, I will have brought a grave matter against a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, something he did not say.' Then I said to myself, 'Allah has accustomed me to truthfulness for good.' 'No, O Commander of the Faithful.' He struck the bed with his staff two or three times, then said, 'Then who?' He repeated that several times. I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.' 'Urwa b. al-Zubayr, Sa'id b. al-Musayyab, 'Alqama b. Waqqas, and 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Utba narrated to me, and some of the people had better wording than others, but each of them memorized his hadith, that 'A'isha said: 'Ali made a suggestion concerning my affair, may Allah forgive him. Then she said: When the Messenger of Allah intended a journey, he would cast lots among his wives. He went on the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq and drew lots among his wives, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah after the hijab had been revealed. I was carried in my howdah and taken down from it. We traveled until when the Messenger of Allah finished that expedition and returned, and we drew near to Madinah, he announced departure one night. I got up when he announced departure and walked until I passed beyond the army. When I had finished my business and came back to my mount, I noticed that a necklace of mine made of onyx of Zafar had broken, so I went back searching for my necklace, and that search detained me. The group that was loading the mounts came and lifted my howdah onto my camel that I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. Women at that time were light, not weighed down by flesh, for one of us would eat only a morsel of food, so the people did not find the lightness of the howdah strange when they lifted it. I was a young girl of recent age. They sent the camel off and departed. I found my necklace after the army had gone on. I came to their camp, and there was no one to call or answer. I made for my place where I had been, thinking that they would miss me and come back to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me and I slept. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He traveled through the night and reached my place in the morning. He saw the black shape of a sleeping person and recognized me when he saw me, for he used to see me before the hijab. I woke up at his istirja' when he recognized me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, he did not speak a word to me, nor did I hear from him anything except his istirja' when he made his mount kneel and stepped on its foreleg, so I mounted it, and he set off leading the mount with me until he brought me to the army after they had stopped in the intense midday heat. Then those who perished among the people of the slander perished. The one who took upon himself the greater part of the sin was 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul. We arrived in Madinah, and I fell ill for a month after our arrival. The people were spreading the words of the slanderers while I was unaware of any of that, and what made me suspicious in my illness was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah the gentleness that I used to see from him when I was ill. He would only enter upon me and say, \"How is this one of you?\" then leave. That made me suspicious, but I did not know of the evil until I went out after I had recovered, I and Umm Mistah, toward my house when we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled and said, 'May Mistah perish.' I said, 'What a bad thing you have said. Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?' She said, 'O you, have you not heard what he said?' I said, 'And what did he say?' She told me about the slander of the people of the lie, and I became more ill on top of my illness. When I returned to my house, the Messenger of Allah entered upon me and said, \"How is this one of you?\" I said, 'Will you permit me to go to my parents?' He said, \"Yes.\" At that time I wanted to ascertain the news from them, so he permitted me, and I went to my mother and father. I said, 'O mother, what are the people talking about?' She said, 'O my daughter, take it lightly. By Allah, seldom is a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives but that they speak much against her.' I said, 'Glory be to Allah! Have the people really spoken of this?' She said, 'Yes.' I cried that night until morning, my tears did not stop, and I did not taste sleep. Then I continued crying in the morning. The Messenger of Allah called 'Ali b. Abi Talib and Usama b. Zayd when the revelation was delayed, to consult them about separating from his wife. As for Usama, he indicated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he knew of the innocence of his wife and what he knew in his heart of affection for them, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, she is your family, and we know nothing but good.' As for 'Ali b. Abi Talib, he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Allah has not put you in difficulty, and there are many women besides her. If you ask the servant girl, she will tell you the truth.' So the Messenger of Allah called Barira and said, \"O Barira, have you seen anything suspicious?\" Barira said, 'No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything against her that I could fault, except that she is a young girl who falls asleep over her family's dough, and the domestic animal comes and eats it.' On that day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and sought someone to excuse him from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul, saying, \"O people of Islam, who will excuse me from a man whose harm has reached me in my family? By Allah, I know nothing about my family but good, and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good, and he used not to enter upon my family except with me.\" Sa'd b. Mu'adh stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws, I will strike his neck, and if he is from our brothers of the Khazraj, you command us and we will do as you command.' Sa'd b. 'Ubada stood up, and he was the chief of the Khazraj that day, and before that he had been a righteous man, but zeal took hold of him, and he said to Sa'd b. Mu'adh, 'You lie, by the life of Allah, you will not kill him, and you are not able to kill him.' Usayd b. Hudayr, who was the cousin of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, stood up and said to Sa'd b. 'Ubada, 'You lie, by the life of Allah, he will certainly kill him, for you are a hypocrite arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.' She said: The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, were stirred up until they were about to fight, while the Messenger of Allah was standing on the pulpit. He kept calming them until they fell silent, and he fell silent. She said: I wept that day, my tears did not stop, and I did not taste sleep, and my parents were with me. I had wept for two nights and a day, thinking that weeping would split my liver. While they were sitting with me and I was weeping, a woman of the Ansar asked permission to enter, and I gave her permission, and she sat weeping with me. While we were in that state, the Messenger of Allah entered upon us and sat down. She said: He had not sat with me since what was said to me had been said, and a month had passed without revelation concerning my affair. She said: When he sat, the Messenger of Allah pronounced the tashahhud, then said, \"To proceed, O 'A'isha, it has reached me about you such and such. If you are innocent, Allah will declare your innocence, but if you have committed a sin, then ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him, for when a servant admits his sin and then repents to Allah, Allah turns to him in forgiveness.\" She said: When the Messenger of Allah finished his words, my tears dried up until I felt not a drop of them. I said to my father, 'Answer the Messenger of Allah about what he said.' He said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.' I said to my mother, 'Answer the Messenger of Allah.' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah.' I said, though I was a young girl who did not recite much of the Qur'an, 'By Allah, you have heard this talk until it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it. If I tell you that I am innocent, and Allah knows that I am innocent, you will not believe me about that. But if I admit a sin, while Allah knows that I am innocent, you will certainly believe me. By Allah, I find no example for myself and for you except the father of Yusuf, when he said, {So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe}.' Then I turned and lay down on my bed, knowing then that I was innocent and that Allah would declare my innocence. But by Allah, I did not think that Allah would send down revelation concerning my affair that would be recited, for my affair in my own estimation was too insignificant for Allah to speak about me in a matter to be recited. Rather, I hoped that Allah would show His Messenger a vision in sleep by which He would declare my innocence. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah did not leave his seat, nor did anyone of the household leave, until Allah sent down revelation upon him, and he was seized by what used to seize him of the intense experience, until drops of sweat like pearls flowed from him on a cold day because of the weight of the Qur'an that was being revealed to him. When the Messenger of Allah was relieved, he was relieved while smiling. The first word he spoke was, \"O 'A'isha, as for Allah, He has declared your innocence.\" My mother said to me, 'Get up and go to him.' I said, 'No, by Allah, I will not get up and go to him, and I praise none but Allah.' And Allah sent down {Indeed, those who came with the slander are a group among you}, the ten verses in full. When Allah sent down this concerning my innocence, Abu Bakr, who used to spend on Mistah because of their kinship and his poverty, said, 'By Allah, I will never spend anything on Mistah again, because of what he said about 'A'isha.' So Allah sent down {And let not those of virtue and wealth among you swear not to give...} the verse. Abu Bakr said, 'By Allah, I love that Allah should forgive me,' and he resumed the spending on Mistah that he used to give, and said, 'By Allah, I will never withdraw it from him.' 'A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah asked Zaynab bt. Jahsh about my affair, saying, \"O Zaynab, what do you know or have you seen?\" Zaynab said, 'I protect my hearing and my sight. By Allah, I know nothing but good.' She was the one who rivaled me among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, but Allah protected her through piety. Her sister Hamna began to fight on her behalf and perished among those who perished from the people of the slander. Al-Zuhri said: This is what has reached us from the hadith of these people."],[19439,"The people indeed spoke about this matter and it spread, and the Messenger of Allah stood up as a preacher concerning it, and I was not aware of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, along with a group of his companions, upon a Nubian slave girl of mine, and the Messenger of Allah said, “What do you know about Aisha?” She said, “I know of no fault in her except that she sleeps and the sheep enters and eats her dough and her mat.” He said, “I am not asking you about this.” She said, “Then what about?” When she understood, she said, “Glory be to Allah! I know of Aisha only as the goldsmith knows the pure red gold.” Then the Prophet ﷺ went out, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “Advise me, O assembly of Muslims, concerning a people who have maligned my family, while I have never known any evil in them, and they have maligned them by one who, by Allah, I have never known any evil in, and I have never been absent except that he was with me, and he never entered my house except that I was present.” Sa'd b. Mu'adh said, “I think their necks should be struck.” A man from the Khazraj said, “You have lied, by Allah. By Allah, if they had been from your own clan, you would not have ordered their killing.” Hassan was from the Khazraj, until there was a dispute between the Aws and the Khazraj in the mosque. Among those who spread it were Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh, along with others. It was spoken about in the presence of Abdullah b. Ubayy, and he would listen to it, encourage it, and spread it. Aisha said: One night I went out with the mother of Mistah for my need, and while we were walking, she stumbled and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said, “Glory be to Allah! Do you curse your son Mistah, who is among the first emigrants and who witnessed Badr?” Then she walked for a while and stumbled again and said the same thing, and I said the same to her. She said, “By Allah, I do not curse him except because of you.” I said, “What is my affair?” She informed me of the matter. Then I went to relieve myself and returned, and I fell ill with fever. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, “What is the matter with you, O Aisha?” I said, “I have a fever; give me permission to go to my parents.” So he permitted me, and I went. My mother was downstairs and my father was on the roof of the house praying. My mother said, “What is the matter with you, O Aisha?” I said, “The mother of Mistah told me such-and-such.” She said, “Have you only now heard of it?” So I wept, and she wept. My father heard the weeping and said, “What is the matter with my daughter?” My mother said, “She has heard of that matter just now.” He said, “O my daughter, return to your house until we come to you tomorrow.” So he came the next day, while there was a woman from the Ansar with the Prophet ﷺ. Her presence did not prevent the Prophet ﷺ from speaking. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “To proceed: O Aisha, if you have done wrong and erred, then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent.” I said to my father, “Speak.” He said, “With what shall I speak?” I said to my mother, “Speak.” She said, “With what shall I speak?” So I praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “To proceed: By Allah, if I say to you that I did it — while Allah knows that I did not do it — you would say, ‘She has confessed to what she did not do.’ And if I say that I did not do it — while Allah knows that I did not do it — you would say, ‘She has lied.’ And I find no example for myself and for you except what the righteous servant said: {So patience is most fitting. And Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe}.”"],[19440,"When the matter concerning me that was mentioned came up, and I knew nothing of it, the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to address the people. He pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: advise me concerning people who have slandered my family. By God, I have never known any evil in my family, and they have slandered them by means of one of whom, by God, I have never known any evil. He has never entered my house except when I was present, and I have never been absent on a journey but that he was absent with me.\" Saʿd b. Muʿādh stood up and said: \"We think, O Messenger of God, that we should strike their necks.\" A man from the Khazraj stood up—and the mother of Ḥassān b. Thābit belonged to the clan of that man—and said: \"You have lied. By God, if they had been from the Aws, you would not have liked to strike their necks.\" This went on until there was almost evil between the Aws and the Khazraj in the mosque, and I knew nothing of it. When evening came that day, I went out for some need of mine, and Umm Misṭaḥ was with me. She stumbled and said: \"May Misṭaḥ perish!\" I rebuked her and said: \"Do you revile your own son?\" She said: \"By God, I do not revile him except because of you.\" I said: \"In what matter concerning me?\" She related the story. I said: \"Has this really happened?\" She said: \"Yes, by God.\" I returned to my house as if the need for which I had gone out I had not gone out for at all, and I found no trace of it, little or much. I fell ill and said to the Messenger of God: \"Send me to my father's house.\" He sent the servant boy with me. I entered the house and found Umm Rūmān downstairs, and Abū Bakr was above in the house reciting. My mother said: \"What has brought you, my little daughter?\" I told her and mentioned the story to her. It had not affected her as it had affected me. She said: \"My little daughter, take the matter lightly. By God, rarely is there a beautiful woman loved by a man who has co-wives but that they envy her and speak about her.\" I said: \"Does my father know about it?\" She said: \"Yes.\" I said: \"And the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" She said: \"Yes.\" She said: I was moved to tears and wept. Abū Bakr heard my voice while he was above in the house reciting, so he came down and said to my mother: \"What is the matter with her?\" She said: \"The matter that was mentioned about her has reached her.\" His eyes overflowed, and he said: \"I adjure you, my little daughter, return to your house.\" She said: So I returned. She said: The Messenger of God came to my house and asked my maidservant about me. She said: \"By God, I know no fault in her except that she would sleep until the sheep came in and ate her leaven or her dough.\" She said: One of his companions rebuked her and said: \"Tell the truth to the Messenger of God.\" She said: \"Glory be to God, I know nothing about her except what the goldsmith knows about red gold.\" The matter reached that man about whom it had been said concerning her, and he said: \"Glory be to God, I have never uncovered any female.\" ʿĀʾishah said: He was killed as a martyr in the path of God. She said: My parents came to me in the morning and stayed with me until the Messenger of God entered upon me after he had prayed the afternoon prayer. My parents were on my right and left. The Prophet ﷺ pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: O ʿĀʾishah, if you have committed a sin or wronged, then repent to God, for God accepts repentance from His servants.\" She said: A woman of the Anṣār had come and was sitting at the door. I said: \"Are you not ashamed before this woman to mention something?\" He admonished me, so I turned to my father and said: \"Answer him.\" He said: \"What shall I say?\" I turned to my mother and said: \"Answer him.\" She said: \"What shall I say?\" When they did not answer him, I pronounced the testimony of faith, praised God, and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: \"To proceed: By God, if I say to you that I did not do it—and God bears witness that I am truthful—that will not benefit me with you. You have spoken about it and your hearts have absorbed it. And if I say that I did it—and God bears witness that I did not—you will say she has confessed against herself. By God, I find no likeness for me and for you except—\" She said: I sought the name of Yaʿqūb but could not recall it, so I said: \"—except the father of Yūsuf when he said: {So patience is most fitting, and God is the one sought for help} [Q 12:18].\" She said: Then revelation came down upon the Messenger of God at that very moment, and it was lifted from him. I could discern joy in his face while he was wiping his forehead and saying: \"Rejoice, O ʿĀʾishah, for God has declared your innocence.\" She said: I was as angry as I had ever been. My parents said to me: \"Rise and go to him.\" I said: \"By God, I will not rise to him, nor praise him, nor praise you two. But I praise God who sent down my innocence. You heard it, so did you not deny it? But I praise God who sent down my innocence.\" As for Zaynab bt. Jaḥsh, God protected her through her religion, and she said nothing but good. As for her sister Ḥamnah, she perished among those who perished. Those who spoke about it were Misṭaḥ b. Uthāthah, Ḥassān b. Thābit, Ḥamnah, and the hypocrite ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy b. Salūl—he was the one who instigated it and gathered them, and he took upon himself the greater part of it. Abū Bakr swore that he would never again benefit Misṭaḥ with any benefit. Then God revealed: {Let not those of virtue and affluence among you swear not to give to the near of kin and the needy} [Q 24:22]—meaning Abū Bakr—{to give to the near of kin and the needy}—meaning Misṭaḥ—{Do you not love that God should forgive you? And God is Forgiving, Merciful} [Q 24:22]. Abū Bakr said: \"Yes, by God, O Lord, we love that You forgive us.\" So he returned to benefiting him as he used to."],[19442,"Umm Mistah entered upon me, and we went out to Hayr 'Ad. Umm Mistah stepped on a bone or a thorn and said, “May Mistah perish.” I said, “What a bad thing you have said about a man from the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ .” She said, “I bear witness that you are among the heedless believing women. Do you know what has flown upon you?” I said, “No, by God.” She said, “How long has it been since the Messenger of God was with you?” I said, “The Messenger of God does with his wives whatever he wishes; he begins with whichever of them he wishes and comes to whichever he wishes.” She said, “Verily he has closed over you such-and-such.” I fell down in a faint. It reached Umm Ruman, my mother, and when the matter reached her, she came to me, carried me, and took me to her house. It reached the Messenger of God that Aisha had heard of the matter, so he came to her, entered upon her, sat beside her, and said, “O Aisha, God has made repentance ample.” This only increased my distress beyond what I already had. While we were like that, Abu Bakr came, entered upon me, and said, “O Messenger of God, what are you waiting for regarding this one who betrayed you and disgraced me?” She said, “This increased my distress upon distress.” She said, “Then he sent for Ali and said, ‘O Ali, what do you think regarding Aisha?’ He said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You must tell me what you think regarding Aisha.’ He said, ‘God has given women ample alternatives, but send for Burayrah, her servant, and ask her; perhaps she has become aware of something of her affair.’ So he sent for Burayrah, and she came. He said to her, ‘Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of God?’ She said, ‘Yes.’ He said, ‘Then I will ask you about something, so do not hide it from me.’ She said, ‘Yes, O Messenger of God. There is nothing you ask me about except that I will inform you of it, and I will not hide from you anything, God willing.’ He said, ‘You have been with Aisha, so have you seen anything of her that you dislike?’ She said, ‘No, by the One who sent you with prophethood. I have not seen anything from her since I have been with her except one trait.’ He said, ‘And what is it?’ She said, ‘I kneaded dough for myself and said to Aisha, “Guard this dough until I fetch a firebrand and bake.” She got up to pray and became heedless of the dough, then a sheep came and ate it.’ Then he sent for Usamah and said, ‘O Usamah, what do you think regarding Aisha?’ He said, ‘God and His Messenger know best.’ He said, ‘You must tell me what you think about her.’ He said, ‘Then I think you should keep her until God brings about something for you regarding her.’ She said, ‘It was only a short while before revelation descended, and joy kept being seen on the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and her vindication came from heaven, meaning from God. The Messenger of God said, “Rejoice, O Aisha, then rejoice, O Aisha, for God has informed me of your vindication.” I said, “Without praise from you or your companion.” She said, “At that point I spoke. And when he came to her, he used to say, ‘How is that one of yours?’”"],[19443,"I said: O Mother of the Believers, or O my mother, will you not tell me how it was—meaning the affair of the slander? She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ married me while I was playing in the rain in Makkah, and I had nothing that men desire, and I was six years old. When it reached me that he had married me, God cast modesty upon me. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ emigrated and I was with him, and I was brought to him, and he had come to me when I was nine years old. The Messenger of God set out on a journey and took me out with him. I was light in a howdah of mine that had curtains. When they departed, I sat in it, and they lifted it while I was inside, and they tied it on the back of the camel. They halted at a campsite. I went out for my need and returned, and they had hastened to depart. I sat in the howdah, and they had seen me when I moved the curtains. When I sat in it, I struck my hand on my chest and found that I had forgotten a necklace that was with me. So I went out quickly seeking it, and returned, and the people had departed. I saw nothing but dust from afar. They had placed the howdah on the camel's back, thinking I was in it because of my lightness. Then there was a man holding the head of his camel. I said: Who is the man? He said: Safwan b. al-Mu'attal al-Sulami. Are you the Mother of the Believers? I said: Yes. He said: Indeed we belong to God and to Him we return. I said: Turn your face away from me and put your foot on the foreleg of your camel. He said: I will do so, with the blessing of an eye and honor. She said: Then I caught up with the people when they halted, and he went and set me down by the howdah. The people looked at me and I was unaware. She said: I noticed the coldness of my parents and the coldness of the Messenger of God, and I did not know what had been said, until my servant or my foster-daughter entered and said such-and-such. She said: A man of the Muhajirun said to me: How heedless you are! A shivering fever seized me, and my mother took every garment in the house and threw it over me. The Messenger of God consulted some of his companions and said: \"What do you think?\" Some of them said: There are many women, and you can find a replacement. Some said: You are the Messenger of God, and revelation descends upon you, and our affair follows your affair. Some said: By God, God will make it clear, so do not hasten. She said: My father's face became as if yellow orpiment had been poured on it. She said: The Messenger of God entered upon me and saw what I was in. He said: \"What is wrong with her?\" My mother said: Because of what is with her, because of what you all said. And it was said. He did not speak and did not say anything. She said: That increased me in what I was already feeling. She said: He came to me and said: \"Fear God, O Aisha. If you have done any of this, repent to God, for God accepts repentance from His servants and forgives evil deeds.\" She said: I sought the name of Ya'qub but could not recall it, so I said: Only I say as the father of Yusuf said: \"So patience is beautiful, and God is the one sought for help against what you describe.\" \"I only complain of my anguish and my sorrow to God, and I know from God what you do not know.\" She said: While the Messenger of God was with his companions and his face was as if orpiment had been melted on it, until revelation descended upon him. When revelation came to him, he did not blink, and his companions knew that revelation was coming to him. They began to look at his face, and it was beaming and brightening. When the revelation was completed, he said: \"Rejoice, O Abu Bakr, God has sent down the excuse of your daughter and her innocence.\" He went to her and gave her the good news. She said: And he recited to him what had been revealed concerning me. She said: Abu Bakr came hurrying, almost falling. She said: I said: By the praise of God, not by the praise of your companion from whom you came. The Messenger of God came and sat at my head, and took my hand. I pulled my hand away from him. Abu Bakr struck me and said: Will you pull your hand away from the Messenger of God, or do such a thing to the Messenger of God? The Messenger of God laughed. She said: This was my affair."],[19444,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I wore a huf (amulet). No sooner did he marry me than Allah cast upon me modesty and the huf.” He said: “The huf is something the Bedouins make for children from suras (chapters of the Qur’an) that the Bedouins put on their sons.”"],[19445,"When my exoneration came down from heaven, the Prophet ﷺ came and informed me of that. I said, 'Praise be to Allah, not to you.'"],[19446,"I was accused of that of which I was accused while I was unaware. While the Prophet ﷺ was sitting with me, he then sat up straight, wiped his face, and said: 'O Aisha, rejoice.' I said: 'By the praise of Allah, not by your praise.' Then he recited to me these verses: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women} and the verses."],[19447,"When I learned of what they were saying, I resolved to go to a well and throw myself into it."],[19449,"When what happened regarding my necklace took place, the people of the slander said what they said. Then I went out with the Prophet ﷺ on another expedition, and my necklace also fell, such that searching for it detained the people until dawn broke. I met from Abu Bakr whatever Allah willed. He said to me, 'O my little daughter, on a journey you are a burden and a trial, and the people have no water.' Then Allah sent down the concession of tayammum. Abu Bakr said, 'Indeed, by Allah, O my little daughter, you are, as I have known, blessed.'"],[19450,"«The Messenger of God ﷺ summoned Ali and Usama and consulted them.» As for Usama, he spoke well and said, \"Your family, and we know nothing but good; this is falsehood and lying.\" As for Ali, he said, \"Women are many, and you are able to seek out and ask the young woman, for she will tell the truth.\" And he mentioned the Hadith of the Ifk."],[19451,"While I was sitting with Aisha, a woman from the Ansar came and said, \"Allah has done such and such to so-and-so and so-and-so.\" Aisha asked, \"What is that?\" The woman replied, \"So-and-so and so-and-so.\" Aisha said, \"Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard about it?\" The woman answered, \"Yes.\" Aisha asked, \"And Abu Bakr?\" The woman replied, \"Yes.\" Aisha then fainted and when she regained consciousness, she had a high fever. Her clothes were thrown on her and the Prophet ﷺ came and she was lying down. He asked, \"What is wrong with her?\" They said, \"She has been overcome by a fever caused by distress.\" He said, \"Perhaps her condition is because of a conversation she had with someone.\" So he sat down and Aisha said, \"By Allah, if I was to take an oath with you that you would not believe me, and if I were to confess to you, you would not accept my confession. My likeness and your likeness is like the likeness of Jacob and his sons. (Allah knows) I called upon my father and he did not answer me. I called upon my mother and she did not answer me. I called upon my aunt and she responded to my call.' [Allah says] 'And Allah is the One whose help is to be sought over that which you describe. (12:18)' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and the excuse was revealed to him. He came back and said, 'It is due to the praise of Allah, not due to the praise of me or anyone else.'\""],[19452,"When the Prophet ﷺ traveled, he traveled with one of his wives and drew lots among them. He traveled with Aisha bt. Abi Bakr. She had a howdah, and the howdah had men who carried it and set it down. The Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions made a stop, and Aisha went out for a need and went far off, and no one noticed her. The Prophet ﷺ and the people woke up and had already departed. The men who carried the howdah came and carried it, thinking only that she was inside it, and they set off. Aisha came back and found that they had departed, so she sat in her place. A man from the Ansar called Safwan b. al-Mu'attal woke up; he did not approach women. He came near her, and he had a camel with him. When he saw her, he mounted her, and he had seen her before the veil. He led the camel with her until they reached the people, with the Prophet ﷺ and Aisha with him. They spoke much about it, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, and it weighed heavily on him until he withdrew from her and consulted Zayd b. Thabit and others about her. He said, \"O Messenger of God, leave her; perhaps God will bring about something for you concerning her.\" Ali b. Abi Talib said, \"Women are many.\" The Prophet ﷺ then charged her, and Aisha went out one night walking among women, and Umm Mistah stumbled and said, \"May Mistah perish.\" Aisha said, \"How bad is what you have said! Do you say this about a man among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" She said, \"You do not know what they are saying,\" and she told her the news. Aisha fell down unconscious. Then the Quran came down with her excuse in Surat al-Nur: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you} until it reached {and the one who took upon himself the greater part of it will have a great punishment}. And it came down: {And let not those of virtue among you swear} until His saying {and God is Forgiving, Merciful}. Abu Bakr used to give to Mistah and be kind to him and maintain ties with him, and he was one of those who spoke much against Aisha. Abu Bakr swore that he would not give him anything. Then this verse came down: {Do you not love that God should forgive you?} The Prophet ﷺ commanded him to go to her and give her good news. Abu Bakr came and told her of her excuse and what God had sent down. She said, \"No, by your praise, nor by the praise of your companion.\""],[19453,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Aisha, \"O Aisha, God has sent down your excuse.\" She said, \"By God's praise, not by your praise.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ left Aisha's presence, then he sent for Abdullah b. Ubayy and had him flogged with two hadd punishments, and he sent for Mistah and Hamnah and had them flogged."],[19455,"«When the Prophet ﷺ intended a journey, he cast lots among his wives.»"],[19456,"The man about whom it was said what was said said, \"By God, I have never uncovered a female since I have been born, and he was killed as a martyr in the path of God.\" Urwah did not name him."],[19457,"«...to strike Hassan b. Thabit with the sword, one blow.»"],[19459,"From Ibn Abbas regarding: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you}: «He means they brought the lie against Aisha; four of you.»"],[19460,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood are a group among you}: He said, \"The companions of Aisha.\""],[19461,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr regarding {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood} meaning «the lie» {a group among you} meaning «Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul the hypocrite, Hassan b. Thabit, Mistah b. Uthathah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh.»"],[19462,"From Qatadah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed, those who brought the falsehood} meaning the lie. He said, \"This concerns Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, and what was spread about her and said to her.\""],[19463,"From Ibn Abbas regarding {Do not consider it evil for you; rather it is good for you}: «He means good for the Messenger of God ﷺ and an exoneration for the mistress of the women of the believers, and good for Abu Bakr and the mother of Aisha and Safwan b. al-Mu'attal. Do not consider what was said to you of the lie evil for you; rather it is good for you because you will be rewarded for that.»"],[19464,"«Whoever waded into the matter of Aisha, according to the extent to which he waded into her matter.»"],[19465,"Will you leave this one while he enters upon you, and he is one of those who undertook the greater part of it among them? She said, \"And I did not see him except that a great punishment had befallen him.\""],[19466,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}? She said, \"And what punishment is more severe than blindness?\" Then she said, \"Indeed he defends or attacks on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[19467,"A'ishah said, \"Or do you not see that he is in great punishment? And Hassan's sight was afflicted.\""],[19468,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}? A'ishah said, \"Is he not in great punishment? There, his sight has already gone.\""],[19469,"Allah: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a painful punishment} in the recitation of 'Abd Allah. Then she said, \"Is he not in punishment? His sight has been taken away.\" Then he recited to her a verse he had composed about her: \"A chaste and dignified woman, not suspected of any fault, and she rises hungry from the flesh of unwary women.\""],[19470,"\"And the one who took charge of his arrogance was Abdullah bin Ubayy.\""],[19471,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {And the one who undertook the greater part of it} \"He means its spreading and broadcasting.\" {Among them} \"He means 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.\" {For him is a great punishment} \"He means in this world the flogging—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged him eighty lashes—and in the Hereafter his destination is to the Fire.\""],[19472,"{The one who undertook the greater part of it}: 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul, Mistah b. Uthathah, Hassan b. Thabit, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh; and most of that was from 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy."],[19473,"From Mujahid concerning His saying {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}: he said, \"'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Salul.\""],[19474,"\"She was not innocent of him nor was he innocent of her.\" {For him is a great punishment}: \"And in this verse there is a lesson for all Muslims: when there is a sin among them by someone who assisted it by deed or word or alluded to it or was pleased by it or approved it, then he shares in that sin according to the measure of what came from him. And when a sin occurs among the Muslims, then one who witnessed it and disliked it is like one who was absent, and one who was absent and approved it is like one who witnessed it.\""],[19475,"From Qatadah concerning His saying {And the one who undertook the greater part of it among them—for him is a great punishment}: he said, \"The one who undertook the greater part of it was Hassan b. Thabit and Mistah b. Uthathah.\""],[19476,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted about her, and they said good, and they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is a lie and falsehood,\" and the believing women—he means Zaynab bt. Jahsh and Barirah, the freedwoman of A'ishah, and all the wives of the Prophet ﷺ—said, \"This is a great lie.\""],[19477,"\"Because among them was Zaynab bt. Jahsh.\" {Of themselves good} \"Should not some of them have thought good of others, since they did not see this?\" {And they said, \"This is a slander\"} \"Should they not have said, 'This accusation is a clear lie'?\""],[19478,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {Why, when you heard it, did you not say, \"It is not for us to speak of this. Exalted are You, O Allah; this is a great slander?\"} He said: \"You should say, 'You have lied,' and say, 'This is a clear lie.' By my life, not to repeat evil about your Muslim brother when you hear it is better for you and safer than spreading it, broadcasting it, and believing it.\""],[19479,"In his saying \"{If only when you heard it, the believing men and believing women had thought well of one another}\", some of them said to others, \"Why don't you listen to his saying?\""],[19480,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{Why did they not bring four witnesses to it?} If they had, they and those who testified would be liars. {And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars.} He means: the lie itself.\""],[19481,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr regarding His saying: {Why did they not bring} meaning \"for the slander\" {four witnesses to it? And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars} meaning \"those who slandered Aisha.\""],[19482,"From Abu Sakhr: \"{Why did they not bring four witnesses to it? And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars.} Everyone who slanders a Muslim and then does not bring four witnesses is a slanderer upon whom the punishment for slander is due.\""],[19483,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter} meaning: had it not been for what Allah graciously bestowed upon you and concealed you with, {a great punishment would have touched you for what you plunged into} meaning: from the lie. {A great punishment} meaning: one without end.\""],[19484,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: \"{And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter} In it there is an inversion; He says: {If it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter, a great punishment would have touched you} meaning 'would have befallen you' {for what you plunged into} meaning 'for what you said concerning the slander.' {A great punishment} 'the punishment would have befallen you in this world and the Hereafter.'\""],[19485,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy, a great punishment would have touched you for what you plunged into.} He said: \"This is concerning the affair of Aisha ؓ and what was said; the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ almost perished because of it.\""],[19486,"From Ibn Abbas: \"{When you received it with your tongues and said with your mouths that of which you had no knowledge} He says: 'Allah knows the opposite of it.' {And you thought it was insignificant while it was, in the sight of Allah, tremendous.} He says: 'You slandered the mistress of the women, the mother of the believers, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and attributed to her what was not in her and never entered her heart. I created her pure and protected her from every indecency.'\""],[19487,"And I heard from so-and-so. {And you said with your mouths} meaning 'with your tongues,' meaning 'from slandering her.' {That of which you had no knowledge} meaning 'without knowing that what you said of slander was true.' {And you thought it was insignificant} He says: 'You thought that slander was a minor sin.' {While it was, in the sight of Allah, tremendous} meaning 'in the burden.'"],[19488,"From Mujahid in his statement, \"When you received it with your tongues,\" he said, \"Some of you narrate it from others.\""],[19489,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {When you received it} \"You narrated it one from another.\""],[19490,"I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah say: Aisha used to recite this verse: {When you received it with your tongues} and she would say: \"It is only the lie of a liar.\" And Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: \"She knows best about it; it was only revealed concerning her.\""],[19491,"I heard Aisha recite it: {When you received it with your tongues}"],[19492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Usamah regarding the affair of 'A'ishah when she was accused of the slander, \"What do you say?\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah! It is not lawful for us to speak of this. Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\""],[19493,"\"That we speak of this. Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\" He means by the slander, the great fabrication, like His saying regarding Maryam: {And their saying about Maryam is a great slander}."],[19494,"{\"That we speak of this\"} meaning \"with the accusation, and our eyes did not see it.\" {Glory be to You} meaning \"should you not say, 'Glory be to You'?\" {This is a great slander} meaning should you not say the like of what Sa'd b. Mu'adh al-Ansari said? That is because when Sa'd heard the saying of those who spoke about the affair of 'A'ishah, he said, \"Glory be to You! This is a great slander.\" And the slander is that which one fabricates, saying what did not happen."],[19495,"\"That you should ever return to the like of it, if you are believers.\" He means Mistah b. Uthathah, Hamnah bt. Jahsh, and Hassan b. Thabit. {If you are believers} he says, \"if you are truthful in Allah and His Messenger.\""],[19496,"\"That you should ever return to the like of it\" meaning \"the accusation.\""],[19497,"Regarding His saying {Allah admonishes you that you should ever return to the like of it}, he said, \"He forbids you.\""],[19498,"In His saying \"Allah advises you to never return to the like of it\""],[19499,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {And Allah makes clear to you the verses} \"He means the verses that He sent down regarding 'A'ishah and the declaration of her innocence.\" {And Allah is Knowing, Wise} \"Knowing of what is in your hearts of regret for what you indulged in; Wise in that He decreed eighty lashes for the slander.\""],[19500,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: {And Allah makes clear to you the verses} meaning \"what He mentioned of admonitions.\""],[19501,"\"That immorality should spread among those who believe\" \"He means the chaste men and chaste women among the believers.\" {For them is a painful punishment} \"He means painful.\" {In this world and the Hereafter} \"He means in this world the flogging, and in the Hereafter the punishment in the Fire.\" {And Allah knows, and you do not know} \"He means He knows what you have entered into and the severity of the punishment in it, and you do not know the severity of Allah's wrath upon the one who did this.\""],[19502,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Indeed, those who love that immorality should spread among those who believe}: it appears in a hadith concerning the affair of 'A'ishah."],[19503,"About Qatadah in his saying \"Indeed, those who love for immorality to be spread among the believers, for them is a painful punishment\" meaning \"adultery\"."],[19504,"\"That it should become widespread and apparent, i.e., adultery.\" {Among those who believe} meaning \"Safwan and 'A'ishah.\" {For them is a painful punishment} meaning \"painful.\" {In this world and the Hereafter} So the punishment of 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy in this world was the prescribed punishment, and in the Hereafter the punishment of the Fire. {And Allah knows, and you do not know}."],[19505,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Indeed, those who love that immorality should spread among those who believe}: \"That adultery should appear. For them is the punishment of the Fire.\""],[19506,"{And Allah is Kind} – meaning, from mercy, Merciful to you since you regretted and returned to the truth."],[19507,"{And Allah is Kind} – meaning, Kind to you when He pardoned and did not punish you for what you said of slander."],[19508,"That I may accept your repentance.” {And Allah is Hearing, Knowing} – “of your words, knowing of what is in your hearts of remorse and repentance.”"],[19509,"From Sa'id b. Jubayr: {O you who believe, do not follow the footsteps of Satan} – meaning, “Satan's beautification until he slandered 'A'ishah.” {And whoever follows the footsteps of Satan} – meaning, “Satan's beautification.” {For he commands immorality} – meaning, “acts of disobedience,” {and wrongdoing} – “what is not recognized, meaning like what was said about 'A'ishah.” {And had it not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy} – meaning, “His blessing,” {none of you would have been pure} – meaning, “none of you would ever have been righteous.” {But Allah purifies whom He wills} – meaning, “He makes righteous whom He wills.”"],[19510,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear not to give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. And let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.} He said: Abu Bakr swore that he would not benefit an orphan in his care who spread that – meaning regarding 'A'ishah. When this verse was revealed, he said: I love that Allah should forgive me, and I will be better to him than I was."],[19511,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear...} He said: Abu Bakr swore not to benefit an orphan who was in his care. 'Abd al-Malik said: He is Mistah b. Uthathah b. 'Abbad b. al-Muttalib. He spread that. When this verse was revealed, {Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?}, Abu Bakr said: Yes, I love that Allah should forgive me, and I will be better to the orphans than I was."],[19512,"{That they give to the near of kin, the needy, and the emigrants in the way of Allah. And let them pardon and overlook.} “I have placed in you, O Abu Bakr, virtue, and given you wealth, knowledge of Allah, and recognition of kinship. So be compassionate, O Abu Bakr, toward Mistah, for he has kinship, emigration, poverty, and witnessed events I approved of, among them Badr.” {Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?} – meaning, “so forgive Mistah.” {And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful} – meaning, “for I am forgiving to those who err, merciful to My allies.”"],[19513,"In his saying (And let not those of virtue and abundance among you swear not to give [aid] to their relatives and the needy), it is said that there were people from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ who accused Aisha with something foul and spread it, talked about it, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore not to give charity to anyone who talks about such things and does not give to them. So Allah said, \"Let not those of virtue and abundance among you swear not to give [aid] to their relatives and the needy.\" He ordered them to join their kinship and give from their wealth as they used to do before that, so Allah commanded to forgive them and to pardon them."],[19514,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {And let not those of virtue among you and wealth swear...} up to {...the needy}. He says: Those of virtue and wealth among you should not swear not to give to the near of kin... up to {Forgiving, Merciful}. This verse was revealed about a man of Quraysh called Mistah, who had kinship with Abu Bakr and was an orphan in his care. He was among those who spread about 'A'ishah what they spread. When Allah revealed her innocence and excuse, Abu Bakr swore that he would not give him anything. He said: Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? He said: Yes. He said: So pardon and overlook. Abu Bakr said: No, I will not withhold from him any good I used to give him before today."],[19515,"\"Do not compete\" meaning do not swear oaths \"the people of virtue among you\" meaning in wealth \"and abundance in provision\" meaning Abu Bakr \"and let them pardon and overlook\" meaning and let them forgive someone who is well-regarded \"to give to their near relatives\" meaning the near relative Mas'adah ibn Uthatha, for he was a relative of Abu Bakr's maternal cousin because Mas'adah was poor \"and to the emigrants in the cause of Allah\" because he was one of the emigrants \"Do you not love\" meaning Abu Bakr \"that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful\" meaning Forgiving of sins, Merciful towards the believers. So the Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Bakr, \"Do you not love that Allah should forgive you?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then pardon and overlook.\" Abu Bakr said, \"I have pardoned and overlooked. I will not prevent him from good after today.\""],[19516,"Regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter} – every one who slanders a chaste woman Allah curses. He said: “No, this verse was revealed specifically regarding the affair of 'A'ishah.”"],[19517,"“Adultery.” I said: Allah says {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women...} He said: “This was revealed specifically regarding 'A'ishah.”"],[19518,"The Prophet ﷺ flogged Hassan b. Thabit, 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy, Mistah, and Hamnah bt. Jahsh, each of them eighty lashes for slandering 'A'ishah. Then they repented after that, except 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy among the hypocrites; he died upon his hypocrisy."],[19519,"From Salamah b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak b. Muzahim, he said: This verse was revealed specifically regarding the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware, believing women} – the verse."],[19520,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} He said: It was revealed concerning the affair of 'A'ishah ؓ."],[19521,"From Ibn 'Abbas: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste women} \"meaning the pure ones\" {unaware, believing women} \"meaning those who affirm the oneness of Allah and His messengers\" {are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment} \"meaning He expelled them from faith.\""],[19522,"From Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} He means \"the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. The people of hypocrisy accused them, so He made the curse and wrath obligatory for them, and they incurred wrath from Allah. All of that concerns the wives of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[19523,"From al-Kalbi regarding His saying: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed} \"This verse specifically refers to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. As for whoever accuses a Muslim woman, he is an evildoer, as Allah said, or he may repent.\""],[19524,"He recited Surat al-Nur and explained it. When he reached this verse: {Indeed, those who accuse chaste, unaware and believing women are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} he said: \"This is about 'A'ishah and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. He did not grant repentance to those who did that, but He granted repentance to those who accuse a believing woman other than the wives of the Prophet ﷺ.\" Then he recited: {And those who accuse chaste women and then do not produce four witnesses - lash them with eighty lashes and do not accept from them testimony ever. And those are the defiantly disobedient.} \"For these He made repentance.\" {Except for those who repent after that and correct themselves, for indeed Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.} \"He made repentance for those who accuse a believing woman, but He did not make repentance for those who accuse a wife of the Prophet ﷺ.\" Then he recited this verse: {They are cursed in this world and the Hereafter, and for them is a great punishment.} \"Some of the people wanted to stand up to Ibn 'Abbas to kiss his head for the excellence of his explanation.\""],[19525,"From Qatadah regarding His saying: {On that Day Allah will pay them in full their true due} \"the people of truth will be given their truth, and the people of falsehood their falsehood, and they will know that Allah is the clear truth.\""],[19526,"'Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul doubted the religion, and he was the chief of the hypocrites. He wanted the doubt to be removed from him and to be certain when certainty would not benefit him.\""],[19527,"{and they will know that Allah is the clear truth} meaning \"the clear justice.\""],[19528,"{And good women are for good men} meaning by good women 'A'ishah. Allah made her good for His Messenger ﷺ. Jibril ﷺ brought her to him in a piece of silk before she was formed in her mother's womb, and said to him: \"This is 'A'ishah bt. Abi Bakr, your wife in this world and your wife in the Hereafter, in place of Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid.\" That was at the death of Khadijah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delighted with her for himself and his eye was comforted by her. Then he said: {And good men are for good women} \"meaning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Allah made him good for Himself and made him the master of the children of Adam.\" {Good women} meaning 'A'ishah ؓ."],[19529,"\"The good (deeds) mean the beautiful (words) for the good people among men and women who believe in the believers (men) and the believers (women) are better, and the good men and women for the good (deeds) because the good (words) are suitable for them.\""],[19530,"In his saying, \"The evil women are for the evil men, and the evil men are for the evil women, and the good women are for the good men, and the good men are for the good women.\" He said, \"This was revealed concerning Aisha when the hypocrite accused her falsely and slandered her. Allah exonerated her from that. Abdullah ibn Ubayy was the evil one, so he was the one more deserving of having evil women, and they were more deserving of having him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was good, so he was more deserving of having good women, and Aisha was a good woman, and she was more deserving of having a good husband.\""],[19531,"The woman with Abdullah bin Ubayy was a hypocrite, and then the Quran was revealed with the verse {The impure women} meaning \"the woman of Abdullah\" {are for the impure men} meaning \"Abdullah bin Ubayy\" {and impure men are for impure women} meaning \"Abdullah bin Ubayy is for his wife\" {and pure women are for pure men} meaning \"Aisha and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ \" {and pure men are for pure women} meaning \"the Prophet ﷺ \" {They are free from what they say} until the end of the verse."],[19532,"From Salamah b. Nubayt, from al-Dahhak b. Muzahim, regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men} he said: \"evil words from speech are for evil people.\" And regarding His saying: {And good words are for good men} he said: \"good words from speech are for good people.\""],[19533,"In his saying, \"The good and the evil,\" he said, \"It is the bad speech and the good speech. The good speech is for the believers and the bad speech is for the disbelievers.\""],[19534,"Regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men} he said: \"evil words from speech are for evil people, and evil people are for evil words from speech. And good words from speech are for good people, and good people are for good words from speech.\""],[19535,"From Mujahid regarding His saying: {Evil words are for evil men, and good words are for good men} he said: \"evil speech and good speech - for the good believer and for the evil disbeliever.\""],[19536,"Regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and good women are for good men}, he said: “The evil words are for the evil people, and the good words are for the good people.”"],[19537,"In his statement \"evil women are for evil men, and good women are for good men\", he said \"evil women are from the speech of evil people, and good women are from the speech of good people\"."],[19538,"In his saying \"The evil women for the evil men,\" he said, \"The evil speech is for the evil people.\" And in his saying, \"The good women for the good men,\" he said, \"The good speech is for the good people.\""],[19539,"In his saying, \"Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women,\" it is said that evil women belong to evil men from among the people, and evil men belong to evil women from among the people, and good women belong to good men from among the people. Don't you see that you hear the word \"evil\" from a righteous man and you say, \"May Allah forgive so-and-so, this is not from his character nor from what he says.\""],[19540,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women}, he said: “Evil words are for evil men, and evil men are for evil words. {And good women are for good men} he said: “And good words are for good men. It was revealed concerning those who said about the Prophet's wife ﷺ what they said of slander.” And it is also said: “Evil women are for evil men: evil deeds belong to the wicked, and good deeds belong to the good.”"],[19541,"When the people indulged in talk about Aisha's affair, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Aisha. She said: I came while I was trembling without fever. He said: “O Aisha, what are the people saying?” I said: No, by the One who sent you with the truth, I will not offer any excuse to you until my innocence comes down from heaven. Then Allah revealed fifteen verses of Surah al-Nur concerning her. Then al-Hakam recited until he reached {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women}. He said: “Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women, and good women are for good men, and good men are for good women.”"],[19542,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Evil women are for evil men, and evil men are for evil women}: “of speech and action.” {And good women are for good men, and good men are for good women}: “of speech and action.”"],[19543,"From Ibn Abbas: {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “He means Allah's declaration of innocence from the lie of Abdullah b. Ubayy b. Salul.” {For them is forgiveness}: “He means protection in this world and forgiveness in the Hereafter.” {And noble provision}: “He means the provision of Paradise and a great reward.”"],[19544,"{For them is forgiveness} means “for their sins,” {and noble provision} means “good provision in Paradise. When Aisha's innocence was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ embraced her, and she is among his wives in Paradise.”"],[19545,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: He said: “Everyone is declared innocent of speech that is not rightfully his.”"],[19546,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “Whoever is good is declared innocent of every evil word he utters; Allah will forgive it. And whoever is evil is declared innocent of every righteous word he utters; Allah will reject it and not accept it from him.”"],[19547,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say}: “That is because whatever good word a disbeliever says belongs to the believer, and whatever evil word a believer says belongs to the disbeliever. Each sees speech that is not rightfully his.”"],[19548,"In his saying, \"{They are absolved of what they say},\" he said, \"Here Aisha is cleared, \"{They have forgiveness and noble provision}.\""],[19549,"From Qatadah regarding His saying {Those are declared innocent of what they say, for them is forgiveness and noble provision}: “Forgiveness for their sins, and it is Paradise.”"],[19550,"“The expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq was in Sha'ban of the year six. In that expedition, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Aisha with him after drawing lots among his wives, and her lot came out. In that expedition, the people of falsehood said what they said about her, and Allah ﷻ sent down her innocence.”"],[19551,"“It was in the year six of the Hijrah, the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq. In this expedition, the people of falsehood said about Aisha what they said, and the Quran was revealed concerning her: {Indeed, those who came with falsehood...} the verses.”"],[19552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ flogged them eighty lashes each."],[19553,"When my exoneration was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the pulpit and mentioned that and recited the Quran. When he descended, he ordered two men and a woman, and they were flogged with their prescribed punishment."],[19554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will flog those who slandered Aisha eighty lashes each before all creatures. My Lord will seek forgiveness for the Muhajirun among them, and I will consult you, O Aisha.\" Aisha heard the speech and wept while she was in the house. Then she said: \"By the One who sent you with the truth as a prophet, your joy is more beloved to me than my own joy.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing, and said: \"The daughter of her father.\""],[19555,"To me, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have been to you like Abu Zar'in father to Umm Zar'in.\" Then he started narrating the Hadith of Umm Zar'in and her companions. One of them said, \"My husband is Ayayaa Tabaaqaa, every sickness has a cure except for his stubbornness or foolishness or when he combines them all.\" Another said, \"My husband is the meat of a skinny camel in a rough and steep mountain, he is neither fat nor easy to move.\" Another said, \"My husband is Al-Asannaaq, if I remain silent, he divorces me, and if I speak, he suspends me.\" Another said, \"My husband is someone who becomes restless when he drinks, and when he sleeps, he snores. He doesn't insert his hand in the pot, but still knows what's boiling.\" Another said, \"My husband's news is incomplete, I fear that I won't complete it.\" Urwah said to her, \"These are five women complaining.\" Another said, \"My husband is a free man, like the night of Tihama. He is not hot, nor cold, nor afraid.\" Another said, \"When he enters, he roars, and when he leaves, he becomes a lion. He doesn't ask about his properties.\" Another said, \"My husband's scent is the scent of thyme and musk. I smell it more than others smell it.\" Another said, \"My husband is tall and his hairs are long, he has a great pile of ashes. Our house is close to the marketplace.\" Another said, \"My husband is Abu Malik, and who is Abu Malik? He is a man with many camels, but few blessed ones. When they hear the sound of female singers, they know it's them.\" Another said, \"My husband is Abu Zar' and who is Abu Zar'? He is a man from noble lineage, with ears and body full of fat. I managed to deceive him, so I deceived him to get pregnant. I am the daughter of Abu Zar', and who is the daughter of Abu Zar'? Her clothes are filled, and her cloak is small. She is the best among women, but her neighbors hate her. Her father and mother obey her. She is the servant of Abu Zar', and who is the servant of Abu Zar'? She never spreads our secrets, nor spoils our reputation, nor misbehaves in our house. Abu Zar' came to me when I was in labor, and he pat me until he took me to Sahil, Taee and Dayis. I am with him, I drink, and I relax. In the morning, when I wake up, I say that I am not ugly. Abu Zar' left me, and the female camels were in labor. He saw a woman with two sons playing under her, with pomegranates on both sides. Abu Zar' married her, and divorced me. After that, I married a young man, who rode a fast horse and carried a piercing spear. He pleased me and provided me with a rich gift. He came to me on every occasion as a husband should. He said to me, 'I am your husband, and you are my wife. If I gathered everything from him, I would put it in a smaller vessel than the vessels of Abu Zar', and it wouldn't fill it.' Aisha said, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'So I have been to you like Abu Zar'in father to Umm Zar'in.'\""],[19558,"Eleven women sat (at a place) and promised and contracted that they would not conceal anything of the news of their husbands. The first one said, \"My husband is like the meat of a slim weak camel which is kept on the top of a mountain which is neither easy to climb, nor is the meat fat, so that one might put up with the trouble of fetching it.\" The second one said, \"I shall not relate my husband's news, for I fear that I may not be able to finish his story, for if I describe him, I will mention all his defects and bad traits.\" The third one said, \"My husband, the \"too-tall\"! if I describe him (and he hears of that) he will divorce me, and if I keep quiet, he will keep me hanging (neither divorcing me nor treating me as a wife).\" The fourth one said, \"My husband is (moderate in temper) like the night of Tihama: neither hot nor cold; I am neither afraid of him, nor am I discontented with him.\" The fifth one said, \"My husband, when entering (the house) is a leopard (sleeps a lot), and when going out, is a lion (boasts a lot). He does not ask about whatever is in the house.\" The sixth one said, \"If my husband eats, he eats too much (leaving the dishes empty), and if he drinks he leaves nothing; if he sleeps he sleeps he rolls himself (alone in our blankets); and he does not insert his palm to inquire about my feelings.\" The seventh one said, \"My husband is a wrong-doer or weak and foolish. All the defects are present in him. He may injure your head or your body or may do both.\" The eighth one said, \"My husband is soft to touch like a rabbit and smells like a Zarnab (a kind of good smelling grass).\" The ninth one said, \"My husband is a tall generous man wearing a long strap for carrying his sword. His ashes are abundant (i.e. generous to his guests) and his house is near to the people (who would easily consult him).\" The tenth one said, \"My husband is Malik (possessor), and what is Malik? Malik is greater than whatever I say about him. (He is beyond and above all praises which can come to my mind). Most of his camels are kept at home (ready to be slaughtered for the guests) and only a few are taken to the pastures. When the camels hear the sound of the lute (or the tambourine) they realize that they are going to be slaughtered for the guests.\" The eleventh one said, \"My husband is Abu Zarʿ and what is Abu Zarʿ (i.e., what should I say about him)? He has given me many ornaments and my ears are heavily loaded with them and my arms have become fat (i.e., I have become fat). And he has pleased me, and I have become so happy that I feel proud of myself. He found me with my family who were mere owners of sheep and living in poverty, and brought me to a respected family having horses and camels and threshing and purifying grain. Whatever I say, he does not rebuke or insult me. When I sleep, I sleep till late in the morning, and when I drink water (or milk), I drink my fill. The mother of Abu Zar and what may one say in praise of the mother of Abu Zar? Her saddle bags were always full of provision and her house was spacious. As for the son of Abu Zar, what may one say of the son of Abu Zar? His bed is as narrow as an unsheathed sword and an arm of a kid (of four months) satisfies his hunger. As for the daughter of Abu Zar, she is obedient to her father and to her mother. She has a fat well-built body and that arouses the jealousy of her husband's other wife. As for the (maid) slave girl of Abu Zar, what may one say of the (maid) slavegirl of Abu Zar? She does not uncover our secrets but keeps them, and does not waste our provisions and does not leave the rubbish scattered everywhere in our house.\" The eleventh lady added, \"One day it so happened that Abu Zar went out at the time when the milk was being milked from the animals, and he saw a woman who had two sons like two leopards playing with her two breasts. (On seeing her) he divorced me and married her. Thereafter I married a noble man who used to ride a fast tireless horse and keep a spear in his hand. He gave me many things, and also a pair of every kind of livestock and said, Eat (of this), O Um Zar, and give provision to your relatives.\" She added, \"Yet, all those things which my second husband gave me could not fill the smallest utensil of Abu Zar's.\" ʿAisha then said: Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"I am to you as Abu Zar was to his wife Um Zar.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5189)"],[19559,"For me, Messenger of Allah ﷺ , you were like a father who plants and a mother who waters. So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who is Abu Zar and who is Umm Zar?\" He said, \"Ten women gathered together and swore that they would not lie about their husbands. One of them said, 'I will not tell his secret, for I fear I will not be able to carry it.' Another said, 'He is like a wild bull on a mountain, neither fat nor thin, so he cannot be easily reached or moved.' Another said, 'When he eats, he devours and when he drinks, he drinks passionately, and his hands do not go into the dish without bringing out the bones.' Another said, 'He is like a night of full moon, neither hot nor cold, and there is no fear in him.' Another said, 'When he enters, he becomes like a leopard, and when he comes out, he becomes like a lion, and he does not ask about what he has entrusted.' Another said, 'His scent is like that of basil, and his touch is like that of a rabbit.' Another said, 'He is tall and slim, with mighty shoulders and ashes around him, and he is close to the house and can be easily called for.' Another said, 'He is a wealthy man, with many camels that travel long distances, though there are few blessings in their paths.' When they hear the sound of the flute, they are certain that he is the one.' Another said, 'He is Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is Abu Zar?' She replied, 'He is a man of blessings and agriculture who has made me forget my adornments, my ears and the flesh of my arms. He has possessed my own self, and whenever I am with him, I feel calm. I awake in the morning and drink. I quench my thirst and do not feel repulsed. I say, 'I will never be disgusted.' He took me from my family and placed me in the family of Suhayl, where I reside with loud noises, echoes, cracks, and dust. He is the son of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the son of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'His resting place is like a mountain peak, and the length of a sugar cane is enough for him.' She is the daughter of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the daughter of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'Her clothes are perfect, and her cloak is tied around her waist. She is a source of joy for her father and mother, and a decoration for her family. She is not metaphorical, but rather a servant of Abu Zar.' I asked, 'Who is the servant of Abu Zar?' She replied, 'He does not spread our secrets widely, nor does he spoil our manners. Abu Zar left me, and the camels began to give birth. He then saw a woman with two sons, like young leopards, playing under her. He married her and divorced me, and so I married a young man secretly. He left me poor, and took his share, then he brought me a lot of gifts and said, 'This is for your family, O Umm Zar.' I said, 'If all of this were placed in a vessel from Abu Zar's belongings, it would not be enough to fill it.' Aisha said, 'So I said, O Messenger of Allah, you are better for me than Abu Zar to Umm Zar.'"],[19560,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said to Aisha, \"O Aisha, I have been to you like Abu Zar's sowing (father of Zar) to Um Zar's sowing (mother of Zar) except that Abu Zar divorced and I do not divorce.\""],[19561,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"I was to you like the father of a seed to the mother of a seed.\""],[19562,"\"I took pride in the wealth of my father during the days of ignorance, as it amounted to a hundred thousand ounces. The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'Be silent, O Aisha, for in my eyes, I am to you as Abu Zar would be to Umm Zar.' Then, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ started talking about how eleven women had gathered during the pre-Islamic days and made a covenant to inform each other about their husbands without lying. It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The night is a night of famine, without heat or cold, without fear.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The wind is the wind of Zarnab, and it carries the scent of rabbits, and I am the majority, and the people are in majority.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. It is a column with lofty pillars, a tall palm trunk, and a great heavy fire, close to the house where people gather.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Malik, and Malik who? He has many grazing camels, a few blessings. When they hear the sound of strainers, they are certain that it is they.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I mention my husband, and when I mention him, I mention Ojara and Buja, and I fear that I will not mention him.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. When he enters, he is like a cheetah, and when he leaves, he is like a lion. He does not ask about what he entrusted.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The flesh of a camel is lean on a mountain, neither in the fat nor in the easy ascent. It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'By Allah, I do not know. When he eats, he gulps, when he drinks, he gasps, when he slaughters, he says \"help me\", and when he sleeps, he snores, and his palm does not enter the palm of his hand, so he knows how to emit semen.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Al-Asnanq. If he speaks, I am divorced, if he is silent, I am praised.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'The consequences of every disease has a cure, and it is either a tanner, a speck, or he gathers them all for you.' It was asked, 'Is it you, O Fulanah?' She said, 'I married Abu Zar, and who is Abu Zar? He is someone from adornments in my ears and full of fat in my shoulder, and he himself boasted, so I met him in a booty of war. He placed me between those who were staying and those who were returning, between the runners and the walker, and the taker of shares. I sleep with him, and I wake up in the morning and drink, and I have my morning food, and he has given me abundance from every creature as a gift.' Aisha said, 'So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, indeed, you are better than Abu Zar.'\""],[19564,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said, \"O Aisha, I was to you like Abu Zar'a to Umm Zar'a.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There was a village from the villages of Yemen in which there were twelve women. They went to a gathering and some of them said to others, 'Come, let us mention our husbands and speak truthfully about them.' It was said to the first one, 'Speak.' She mentioned the hadith (narration) and the second woman, who was 'Umrah bint 'Amir, spoke. It was said to the third one, 'Speak.' She was Hubbah bint Ka'ab. It was said to the fourth one, 'Speak.' She was Hudhud bint Abi Haramah. It was said to the fifth one, 'Speak.' She was Kabshah. It was said to the sixth one, 'Speak.' She was Hind. It was said to the seventh one, 'Speak.' She was Hubbah bint Alqamah. It was said to the eighth one, 'Speak.' She was Asma bint 'Abd. It was said to the ninth one, 'Speak.' She was not named. It was said to the tenth one, 'Speak.' She was Kubayshah bint Al-Arqam. It was said to Umm Zar'a, 'Speak.' She was Bint Al-Uka'il bin Sa'adah. She said, 'Abu Zar'a and who is Abu Zar'a?' Then she mentioned the hadith."],[19565,"I used to play with toys, and my friends would come to me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, they would flee from him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would catch them and bring them back to me."],[19566,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to me while I was playing with dolls."],[19567,"Abd Allah b. Maslama al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hisham b. Urwa narrated to me from his father, from Aisha, that she used to play with dolls—meaning toys—in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My friends would come and hide from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send them to me so they could play with me."],[19568,"I used to play with these dolls, and my slave girls would come to me and play with me. When they saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ they would hide, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send them to me."],[19569,"I used to play with dolls during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19570,"I used to play with dolls during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me while I was on a swing."],[19572,"By Allah, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with spears in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was screening me with his cloak so that I could look at their play from between his ears and his shoulder. Then he stood for my sake until I was the one who departed. So appreciate the capacity of a young girl eager for amusement."],[19573,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at the door of my room while the Abyssinians were playing with their spears in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ screened me with his cloak so that I could look at their play. He kept standing for my sake until I was the one who departed. So appreciate, O son of my sister, the capacity of a young girl eager for amusement."],[19574,"The Prophet ﷺ placed my chin on his shoulder so that I could look at the Abyssinians' spear play, until I was the one who turned away from them."],[19575,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while two slave-girls were with Aisha, singing during the days of Mina, and the Prophet ﷺ was lying with his garment covering his face. Abu Bakr said: \"Is this done in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" The Prophet ﷺ uncovered his face and said: \"Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are the days of Eid.\""],[19576,"Abu Bakr ؓ entered upon me on a day of Eid while two slave-girls were with me, singing and mentioning the day of Bu'ath, the day on which the champions of Aws and Khazraj were killed. Abu Bakr said: \"Servants of God! Is the pipe of Satan in the presence of the Messenger of God?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Abu Bakr, every people has a festival, and today is our festival.\""],[19577,"Abu Bakr entered upon her while the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her on the day of Fitr or Adha, and two slave-girls were with her singing. Abu Bakr said: \"The pipe of Satan?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave us, O Abu Bakr, for every people has a festival, and our festival is this day.\""],[19578,"She had two slave-girls singing on a day of Eid, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her and did not forbid them. Abu Bakr entered and scolded them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Leave her, O Abu Bakr, for every people has a festival, and this is our festival.\""],[19579,"The exonerated truthful one, daughter of the truthful, beloved of the Beloved of God, narrated to me."],[19580,"The truthful one, daughter of the truthful, the innocent, the exonerated, narrated to me such-and-such."],[19581,"It was said to him: \"Was Aisha skilled in the laws of inheritance?\" He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I saw the elders of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ asking her about the laws of inheritance.\""],[19582,"I never saw anyone more eloquent than Aisha ؓ."],[19583,"A man said: \"All the Mothers of the Believers are dearer to me than Aisha.\" I said: \"As for you, you have contradicted the Messenger of God ﷺ; she was the dearest of them to him.\""],[19584,"I never saw a woman more knowledgeable in medicine, expenditure, or poetry than Aisha."],[19585,"I said to Aisha: \"O Mother of the Believers, I am not surprised at your insight into poetry, for I say you are the wife of the Messenger of God ﷺ and the daughter of the most learned of people. But I am surprised at your insight into medicine.\" She said: \"O son of my sister, when the Messenger of God ﷺ advanced in age and fell ill, delegations came, and remedies were described to him, so from that.\""],[19586,"We arrived as emigrants and took a rugged mountain pass, and a strong, unruly camel I was riding bolted with me. By God, I will never forget my mother’s words: “O little bride!” I climbed onto its head, and I heard someone saying: “By God, I think its reins have been thrown.” So I threw them, and it began to turn around as though a person were standing beneath it holding it."],[19587,"I entered with Abu Bakr when he first came to Madinah, and there was Aisha lying down, overcome by fever. Abu Bakr came to her and said, “How are you, my little daughter?” and kissed her cheek."],[19588,"Mu‘awiyah — by God, I have never seen any orator more eloquent or more astute than Aisha ؓ."],[19589,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “If the knowledge of all the women of this community were gathered — including the wives of the Prophet ﷺ — Aisha’s knowledge would be greater than theirs.”"],[19591,"“Umar fathered ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Umar and his full sister Hafsah bt. ‘Umar, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and ‘Abd al-Rahman the elder; their mother was Zaynab bt. Maz‘un b. Habib b. Wahb b. Hudhafah b. Jumah. She was among the emigrant women; before the Prophet ﷺ she had been married to Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi. Her father and her paternal uncle Zayd attended Badr, and her maternal uncles ‘Uthman, Qudamah, and ‘Abd Allah b. her maternal aunt, and al-Sa’ib b. ‘Uthman attended Badr.”"],[19592,"Hafsah became widowed from Khunays b. Hudhafah al-Sahmi, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ and had attended Badr, and he died in Madinah. I met Abu Bakr and offered her to him, but he remained silent, and what troubled me troubled me. Then when the Messenger of God ﷺ married her, I said to him, “What made you do what you did?” He said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ had mentioned her, and for that reason I kept silent.” The wording is that of the hadith of Musa b. ‘Uqbah and Ibn Abi ‘Atiq."],[19593,"A slave girl of Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, cast a spell on her, and she confessed it against herself. Hafsah ordered ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Zayd, and he killed her. ‘Uthman disapproved of that, so ‘Abd Allah went to him and said, “She cast a spell on her and confessed it.” ‘Uthman had disapproved of what she did without the ruler’s authority."],[19594,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ divorced Hafsah, then took her back.”"],[19595,"Umar entered upon Hafsah while she was crying, so he said, \"What makes you cry? Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced you. Indeed, if the Prophet ﷺ has divorced you, he will return you to me because of me. By Allah, if he has divorced you, I will never speak to you again.\""],[19596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ intended to divorce Hafsah, but Gabriel came and said, “Do not divorce her, for she fasts much and prays much, and she will be your wife in Paradise.”"],[19597,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah, and that reached ‘Umar b. al-Khattab, so he placed dust on his head and said, “God will not care about you, O Ibn al-Khattab, after this.” Then Gabriel descended upon the Prophet ﷺ and said, “God commands you to take Hafsah back out of mercy for ‘Umar.”"],[19598,"“Hafsah died in the year Ifriqiya was conquered, and she died while Marwan was governor of Madinah.”"],[19599,"Yazid b. Abi Habib said: \"Mu'awiyah b. Hudayj raided Ifriqiyah three times: the first in the year thirty-four, the second in the year forty, and the third in the year fifty.\""],[19622,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rak'ahs of dawn when dawn broke."],[19623,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Five creatures, there is no blame on the one who kills them while in ihram: the crow, the mouse, the vicious dog, and the kite."],[19625,"It is not permissible for a woman believing in Allah and the Hereafter to observe mourning on the dead for more than three (days), except in case of her husband. (Using translation from Muslim 1491)"],[19626,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The coming out of Ibn Sayyad is only due to an anger that will seize him.”"],[19627,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “Whoever does not resolve to fast before dawn, there is no fast for him.”"],[19628,"She said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting down until a year or two before his death. Then he would pray his voluntary prayer sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until his recitation became longer than a longer one.”"],[19629,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reported to him, saying: “I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting at all until a year before his death. Then he would pray his voluntary prayer sitting, and he would recite the surah slowly until it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19630,"“I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before his death. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, and he would recite the surah slowly until his recitation of it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19631,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before he passed away. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, reciting the surah slowly until his recitation became longer than a longer one.”"],[19632,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray sitting in his voluntary prayer until a year or two before he passed away. Then I saw him pray sitting in his voluntary prayer, reciting the surah slowly until his recitation of it became longer than his recitation standing.”"],[19633,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: “I did not see the Messenger of God ﷺ pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting until one or two years before God took him. Then I saw him pray in his voluntary prayer while sitting, reciting the surah slowly until it became longer than a longer one.”"],[19635,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “A company will surely come to this House to raid it, until when they are in a desert of the land, the middle of them will be swallowed up, and the first of them will call out to the last of them, and none of them will remain except the fugitive who tells about them.” A man said to my grandfather: I bear witness that you have not lied about Hafsah, and Hafsah did not lie about the Messenger of God ﷺ. Sufyan said: And Umayr b. Qays used to narrate it from Umayyah."],[19636,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would use his right hand for his food, drink, and clothing, and his left hand for anything else."],[19637,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down, he placed his right hand under his right cheek. His right hand was for his food, drink, purification, and water, and his left hand for anything else."],[19638,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Prophet ﷺ would kiss while fasting."],[19639,"The Prophet ﷺ would kiss while fasting."],[19640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would touch the face of some of his wives while fasting."],[19641,"The Prophet ﷺ would kiss some of his wives while fasting."],[19642,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ would fast three days of the month: Monday, Thursday, and the Monday of the following week."],[19643,"The Prophet ﷺ would fast on Monday, Thursday, and the Monday of the coming week."],[19644,"Four things the Prophet ﷺ never abandoned: fasting on Ashura, the ten days, three days of every month, and the two rak'ahs before dawn."],[19645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me one day and placed his garment between his thighs. Abu Bakr came seeking permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then Umar came seeking permission, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then some people came, and he granted them permission. Then Ali came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him permission while he was in that state. Then Uthman came seeking permission, and he covered himself with his garment and then granted him permission. They spoke for a while and then left. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr, Umar, Ali, and some of your companions entered upon you while you were in your state without changing. But when Uthman entered, you covered yourself with your garment.' He said, 'Should I not feel shy before one before whom the angels feel shy?'"],[19646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'People from my Ummah will attack this House, until when they are in the desert, the first of them will be swallowed up, and the middle of them will not return—or he will be saved.'"],[19647,"From Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Utarid b. Hajib brought a garment that Chosroes had given him. Umar b. al-Khattab said, 'Will you not buy it, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Only one who has no share will buy it.'"],[19648,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyyah will enter the Fire, if God wills.” I said, “O Messenger of God, has not God said, {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, an inevitability decreed}?” He said, “Have you not heard Him say, {Then We shall save those who were God-fearing, and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees}?”"],[19649,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and His Messenger to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over her husband.”"],[19650,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day—or who believes in God and His Messenger—to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over her husband.”"],[19651,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and His Messenger to mourn for more than three days, except over a husband.”"],[19653,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “I hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyyah will enter the Fire, if God wills.” I said, “O Messenger of God, {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, an inevitability decreed}.” He said, “Have you not heard Him say, {Then We shall save those who were God-fearing, and leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees}?”"],[19654,"He informed him that he said to Ḥafṣah, “Does one of you become angry at the Prophet ﷺ for a day until nightfall?” She said, “Yes.”"],[19655,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr when the dawn became bright."],[19656,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Five creatures there is no sin upon the one who kills them in the state of iḥrām: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the rabid dog, and the kite.”"],[19657,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever does not resolve to fast before dawn has no fast.”"],[19659,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Let none of you cease from seeking to have a child; for when a man dies and has no child, his name is cut off.”"],[19660,"Ḥafṣah said, “Avoid this man, for we used to speak of the Dajjāl emerging from an outburst of anger he would have.” And Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī reported the like of it."],[19661,"The Prophet ﷺ would perform two light prostrations when dawn broke."],[19662,"Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said, “O Messenger of God, what is the matter with you that you have not exited [ihram]?” — the hadith."],[19663,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Ibn Sayyad emerges only out of anger that overtakes him.”"],[19664,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, what is the matter with the people? They have exited ihram, but you have not exited ihram from your umrah.' He said: 'I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until I slaughter.'"],[19665,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray the two rakʿahs of Fajr when dawn broke."],[19666,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to make the two rakʿahs just before Fajr light."],[19667,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two light-raka'at when he saw the dawn."],[19668,"When the call for the Morning Prayer was given, the Prophet ﷺ would prostrate two prostrations before the Morning Prayer, making them light."],[19669,"When the muezzin finished the call for the Morning Prayer, the Prophet ﷺ would pray two light rakʿahs before the prayer was established."],[19670,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rakʿahs after Fajr."],[19671,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the two rakʿahs of Fajr when dawn broke."],[19672,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to exit [ihram] during his Hajj that he performed."],[19673,"The Prophet ﷺ matted his hair when he performed Hajj and shaved when he exited [ihram]."],[19674,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded his wives to exit [ihram] in the year of the Farewell Hajj."],[19675,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, when dawn broke, would not pray except two light rakʿahs."],[19677,"From the Prophet ﷺ something, except that he narrated once from a woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ that a dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and some of his companions began eating it, among them Saʿd. Then a woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ called out to him that it was a dabb. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Eat it, there is no harm in it, but it is not from the food of my people.\""],[19678,"She heard Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrate that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is not lawful for a woman who believes in God and the Last Day to mourn over a deceased person for more than three days, except over a husband.\""],[19680,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, she said, I said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Why have the people exited ihram while you have not?\" He said, \"I have matted my hair and garlanded my sacrificial animal, so I will not exit ihram until the sacrificial animal is released.\""],[19681,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever goes to a diviner (ʿarrāf), God will not accept his prayer for forty days.\" [Mawqūf]"],[19682,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel will have the fire of Hell gurgling in his belly.\""],[19683,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19684,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ wanted to sleep, he would place his right hand under his right cheek and then say, \"O God, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.\""],[19685,"ʿUmar said, \"Shall I buy it for you, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Only the one who has no share of the Hereafter wears it.\""],[19686,"Four things the Prophet ﷺ never abandoned: fasting ʿĀshūrāʾ, the ten days (of Dhū al-Ḥijjah), and three days of every month."],[19687,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Fast three days of every month, or from the month Monday, Thursday, and the following Thursday.\""],[19688,"The translation of the passage into English is: \"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast three days every month, on Mondays and Thursdays.\""],[19689,"She was called al-Shifāʾ, and she used to perform ruqyah for the ant (i.e., a skin condition called namlah). The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"Teach it to Hafsah.\""],[19690,"The Prophet ﷺ was placing his garment between his thighs when Abu Bakr sought permission from him, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Umar sought permission, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Ali sought permission among some of the Prophet's companions, and he granted him permission while in that state. Then Uthman sought permission, and he clothed himself with his garment, and they conversed. Then they left, and I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr sought permission and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Umar sought permission, and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Ali sought permission among some of your companions, and you granted him permission while you were in that state. Then Uthman sought permission and you clothed yourself with your garment.\" He said, \"Should I not be shy about something from which the angels are shy?\" Ibn Juraij said, \"And my father informed me with a similar narration.\""],[19691,"On the authority of ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr, regarding the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia with Jaʿfar b. Abī Ṭālib from the Banū Asad b. Khuzaymah: ʿUbayd Allāh b. Jaḥsh b. Riʾāb died in the land of Abyssinia as a Christian, and with him was Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān, whose name is Ramlah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her afterward; ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān gave her in marriage to him in the land of Abyssinia. Umm Ḥabībah's mother was Ṣafiyyah bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, the sister of ʿAffān b. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, the paternal aunt of ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān."],[19692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Ḥabībah while she was in the land of Abyssinia; the Negus gave her in marriage to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not send anything to her. The dowers of the Prophet's ﷺ wives were four hundred dirhams."],[19693,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Ḥabībah bt. Abī Sufyān b. Ḥarb b. Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams b. ʿAbd Manāf b. Quṣayy b. Kilāb b. Murrah b. Kaʿb b. Luʾayy b. Ghālib b. Fihr b. Mālik. Umm Ḥabībah's name is Ramlah. ʿUthmān b. ʿAffān ؓ gave Umm Ḥabībah ؓ in marriage to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because Umm Ḥabībah's mother was Ṣafiyyah bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, and Ṣafiyyah was the paternal aunt of ʿUthmān, the full sister of ʿAffān. Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasanah brought Umm Ḥabībah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[19708,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me, so I said: \"Would you be interested in my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan?\" He said: \"What would I do?\" I said: \"Marry her.\" He said: \"Your sister?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Would you like that?\" I said: \"Yes, I am not leaving you alone, and the one I love—or she said: the one most entitled—to share good with me is my sister.\" He said: \"She is not lawful for me.\" She said: \"By God, I have been told that you are seeking Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\" He said: \"The daughter of Abu Salamah?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"By God, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful to me. She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. Thuwaybah nursed me and her. So do not offer me your daughters or your sisters.\""],[19733,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever consistently performs four rak'ahs before the noon prayer and four after it will be forbidden to Hell.\""],[19734,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19735,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19736,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, Allah will forbid his body to the Fire.\""],[19737,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his private part, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19738,"Indeed my sister Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a night or day, apart from the obligatory prayers, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\" So I have not abandoned them since I heard them."],[19739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day and night, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19740,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19741,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his penis, let him perform wudu'.\""],[19742,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever bows four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four rak'ahs after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.\""],[19743,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19744,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, a house will be built for him in Paradise.”"],[19746,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19747,"The Prophet said: “Whoever prays four before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19749,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire.”"],[19750,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in his night and day, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.”"],[19751,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build a house for him in Paradise.”"],[19752,"He entered upon Umm Habibah, and she gave him sawiq to drink. Then he got up to pray, and she said to him, “Perform wudu, O son of my brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.’”"],[19753,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.”"],[19754,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Perform wudu from what the fire has touched.”"],[19755,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Wudu is required from what the fire has touched.”"],[19756,"He informed him that he entered upon his maternal aunt Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. She prepared sawiq for him, and he drank it. She said, “O my son, perform wudu, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Wudu is required from what the fire has touched.’”"],[19757,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[19758,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded ablution from food that the fire has touched."],[19759,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"Perform ablution from what the fire has touched.\""],[19760,"He entered upon Umm Habibah and she gave him a cup of sawiq to drink, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth. She said to him, \"O son of my sister, will you not perform ablution? For the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution from what the fire has changed or touched.'\""],[19761,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, the angels do not accompany a companion in which there is a bell.\""],[19762,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19763,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19764,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19765,"Abu Hurairah reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “The angels do not accompany the fellow travelers who have a dog or bell (with them).” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2555)"],[19766,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Truly, the caravan that has a bell in it is not accompanied by the angels.\""],[19767,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19768,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The angels do not accompany a traveling group in which there is a bell.\""],[19769,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, God builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[19770,"\"We used to do it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , we would walk from Jam' to Mina.\" Al-Humaidi added in his narration: Sufyan and Salim ibn Shawwal said: \"There was a man from the people of Makkah whom we never heard anyone narrating from except 'Amr ibn Dinar. This is the narration.\""],[19771,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[19772,"Some people from the people of Yemen came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he taught them prayer, the customary practices, and the obligatory duties. They said, 'O Messenger of God, we have a drink we make from wheat and barley.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Do not make it.'"],[19773,"Sufyān said to him: 'Repeat to me the hadith of Umm Ṣāliḥ.' He said: 'Umm Ṣāliḥ narrated to me.' And ʿAbbās b. Muḥammad al-Mujāshiʿī narrated to us: Muḥammad b. Abī Yaʿqūb al-Kirmānī narrated to us: Muḥammad b. Yazīd b. Khunays al-Makkī narrated to us, from Saʿīd b. Ḥassān, who said: Umm Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, from Ṣafiyya bt. Shayba, from Umm Ḥabība, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'All the speech of the son of Adam is against him, not for him, except commanding good, forbidding evil, or remembrance of God.' A man among the people said: 'How severe this hadith is!' Sufyān al-Thawrī said: 'And what is its severity? Has not your Prophet ﷺ come to you from your Lord ﷻ, and He said: \"On the day the Spirit and the angels stand in rows, they will not speak except one whom the Most Merciful permits, and he speaks what is right. That is the True Day\" [78:38]? And He said: \"There is no good in much of their private conversation, except for one who commands charity, or good, or reconciliation between people\" [4:114], to the end of the verse.'"],[19774,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was in her house and heard the caller to prayer. He said as he says. When he said, 'Come to prayer,' the Messenger of God ﷺ rose to pray."],[19775,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever prays twelve rakʿahs in a day, apart from the obligatory prayer, God will build for him a house in Paradise.'"],[19776,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The angels do not accompany a group in which there is a bell.'"],[19777,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Perform ablution from what fire has touched.'"],[19779,"'We used to do it at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ in the dark before dawn from Muzdalifa to Minā.'"],[19780,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ in a garment, on me and on him; in it was what was.'"],[19781,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19782,"The Prophet ﷺ used to kiss while fasting."],[19783,"'And the Prophet ﷺ married her, and the Negus paid a dowry on his behalf of four hundred dinars.'"],[19784,"Some people from the people of Yemen came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he taught them the customary practices, prayer, and the obligatory duties. They said, 'We have a drink we make from wheat and barley.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Al-ghubayrāʾ?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then do not consume it.' They said, 'But they will not abandon it.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever does not abandon it, strike his neck.'"],[19785,"Zubayr ibn Bakkar said: \"Um Salama, before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , was with Abu Salama, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Asad, and she gave birth to Salama, Umar, and Zainab, then she passed away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then became responsible for her.\""],[19786,"He heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , say: \"No Muslim is afflicted with a calamity and says 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return. O Allah, I seek recompense for my calamity from You. O Allah, replace it for me with something better than it,' except that Allah will replace it for him with something better.\" So when Abu Salamah passed away, Umm Salamah said: \"Indeed, we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we will return. O Allah, I seek recompense for my calamity in Abu Salamah from You. O Allah, replace him for me with someone better.\" So I kept saying to myself that someone better than Abu Salamah would come, until the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , proposed to me. So I said: \"I am afflicted and I am possessive, and I am old.\" The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , said: \"As for being old, I am older than you. As for being possessive, I supplicate to Allah to remove it from you. And as for children, they are in the hands of Allah and His Messenger.\" So Umar bin Abu Salamah married me to him."],[19787,"that the Prophet ﷺ married Umm Salamah for household goods worth ten dirhams"],[19788,"Umm Salamah: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, I said to him: 'I have three shortcomings: I am advanced in age, I am a woman who has children, and I am a very jealous woman.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'As for age, I am older than you. As for the children, they belong to Allah and His Messenger. As for jealousy, I will pray to Allah and He will remove it from you.' So the Prophet ﷺ married her. When he entered upon her, he said: 'You and your family have honor with me. I have not spent seven nights with any of my wives, and if I spend seven with you, I will spend seven with my other wives.'"],[19789,"The first of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ who passed away was Zainab bint Jahsh, she passed away during the caliphate of Umar. The last of them to pass away was Umm Salamah, she passed away during the time of Yazid bin Muawiyah, at the age of sixty-two."],[19790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me after the afternoon prayer and prayed two rak'ahs. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs?' He said, 'I used to pray them after noon, but something came to me and kept me busy until I prayed the afternoon prayer, so I prayed them now.'"],[19791,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed them in her house"],[19795,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her when he married her: 'If you wish, I will spend seven nights with you, then I will spend seven nights with the rest of my wives.'"],[19799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Jibril kept enjoining me to use the siwak until I feared for my molars.'"],[19800,"O Messenger of Allah, is there jihad upon women? He said, 'Their jihad is here,' and he gestured with his hand toward Makkah."],[19828,"A man gave a woman a sheep as charity, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to accept it."],[19829,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me one day and prayed two rak'ahs after 'Asr. I had not seen him pray them, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are these two rak'ahs?\" He said, \"The delegation of Banu Tamim arrived, and I used to pray two rak'ahs after Zuhr, but I had not prayed them, so these are those two.\""],[19832,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to prefer to travel on Thursday."],[19833,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you sees in his dream what he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge from what he saw.\""],[19836,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us, from Abd Rabbihi b. Sa'id, from Abu Salama, from Umm Salama, who said: Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah gave birth half a month after her husband's death, then two men proposed to her, one of them young and the other middle-aged. She inclined to the young man, but the middle-aged man said: \"She is not lawful.\" Her family was absent, and he hoped that when her family came, they would prefer him over her. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"You have become lawful, so marry whomever you wish.\""],[19837,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ghusl from a single vessel with one of his wives."],[19838,"Subay'ah gave birth half a month after her husband's death."],[19846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever has an animal that he wants to slaughter, then when the crescent of Dhul Hijjah appears, he should not touch any of his hair or nails until it is slaughtered.\""],[19847,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Let her go, O Umm Salamah, for every nation has a celebration, and this is our celebration day.\""],[19872,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik, from Nafi', from Sulayman b. Yasar, from Umm Salamah that a woman used to experience irregular bleeding during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on her behalf. He said, \"She should consider the number of nights and days in which she used to menstruate in the month before she was afflicted with what she has, and she should abandon the prayer for that amount of the month. When that period has passed, she should bathe, fasten a cloth, and then pray.\""],[19889,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed 'Asr, he would leave and then pray two rak'ahs in his house."],[19893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more prompt in praying Zuhr than you, and you are later in praying 'Asr than him."],[19904,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ under a covering and I menstruated. He said: \"Go back and tie your lower garment tightly around you, then return.\""],[19905,"Some people sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her on which days the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted most. She said: \"Saturday and Sunday,\" and he would say: \"They are two festival days for the polytheists, so I love to differ from them.\""],[19920,"Asma' wept over Ja'far or Hamzah for three days, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to stop weeping and to apply kohl."],[19921,"One day, while the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was resting in her house and a man from his companions was with him, they were conversing when a man came and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how much charity is due on such-and-such dates?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Such-and-such.\" The man said: \"So-and-so has transgressed against me and taken from me such-and-such dates, increasing by one sa'.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"How will it be when someone is appointed over you who transgresses against you more severely than this transgression?\" The people plunged into discussion and the talk overwhelmed them until one of them said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if a man is absent from you with his camels, livestock, and crops, and he pays the zakah of his wealth, but someone transgresses against him regarding the right? What should he do while he is absent from you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever pays the zakah of his wealth with a good heart, seeking thereby the face of Allah and the hereafter, and does not withhold anything of his wealth, and establishes the prayer, then pays the zakah, and someone transgresses against him regarding the right, he takes up arms and fights, and is killed, he is a martyr.\""],[19922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel only causes the fire of Hell to gurgle in his belly.\""],[19925,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, meaning to his wives: \"The one who is kind to you after me is indeed the truthful and dutiful one. O Allah, give Ibn 'Awf to drink from Salsabil.\""],[19926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting one day in my house and said: \"Let no one enter upon me.\" I waited, and Husayn entered. I heard the sobbing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping. I looked, and there was Husayn in his lap or beside him, and he was wiping his head and weeping. I said: \"By Allah, I did not know when he entered.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Jibril was in the house and said: 'Do you love him?' I said: 'In this world, yes.' He said: 'Your community will kill this one in a land called Karbala.' Jibril took some of its soil and showed it to the Prophet ﷺ. When Husayn was surrounded and killed, he said: 'What is the name of this land?' They said: 'Karbala.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: a land of grief and affliction.'\""],[19927,"A single vessel of about half a faraq used to be set for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would begin with it; he and I would wash together."],[19937,"I had a gold gazelle, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to give it as charity, and I did so."],[19938,"She said: There was a woman who had prolonged bleeding during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and Umm Salamah asked the Prophet ﷺ about her situation. The Prophet ﷺ said: Let her note the number of days and nights she used to menstruate before the bleeding that she has now, and their portion of the month, and leave off prayer for that amount. When that passes, she should perform ghusl, then bind a cloth over her private part and pray."],[19963,"I heard Umm Salama say, \"Abu Bakr went out during the time of the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , as a merchant to Busra. Abu Bakr was not prevented from suspecting the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , with his share of the profits from trade. This was due to their admiration for the gains of trade and their love for it. The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , did not prevent Abu Bakr from sharing in his trade because of his love for his company and his trust in Abu Bakr. He was pleased with his company, as the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , admired trade and had a liking for it.\""],[19968,"The Messenger of God ﷺ would fondle her while she was menstruating, with a waist-wrapper on her."],[19993,"On the evening of the day of sacrifice, the Messenger of God ﷺ saw Wahb b. Zam'ah and a man from the family of Abu Umayyah wearing shirts. The Prophet ﷺ said to Wahb, “Have you performed the ifadah, O Abu 'Abd Allah?” He said, “No.” He said, “Take off your shirt.” Wahb said, “Why is that, O Messenger of God?” He said, “This is a day in which I permit you, when you have thrown the Jamrat al-'Aqabah, to become free of everything forbidden to you in the state of ihram except women. But if evening comes and one of you has not performed the ifadah, he remains in a state of ihram until he performs it.”"],[19994,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was wrapping her head veil. He said, “One fold, not two folds.”"],[19999,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Any woman who takes off her clothes outside her own house, God tears away His veil from her.”"],[20000,"Yahya b. Sulaym b. Zayd, the client of the Messenger of God ﷺ, narrated to us from al-Sa'b b. 'Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah: Umm Salamah told me that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “There will certainly come upon people a time in which the truthful one lies, the liar is believed, the trustworthy one betrays, the treacherous one is entrusted, a man gives testimony without being asked to testify, swears an oath without being asked to swear, and the happiest person in the world will be Luka' b. Luka', who does not believe in God and His Messenger.”"],[20001,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Abu Salamah when his gaze had already become fixed. He closed his eyes and said, “When the soul is taken, the sight follows it.” Some of his family clamored, so he said, “Do not pray against yourselves except for good, for the angels say 'Amen' to what you say.” Then he said, “O God, forgive Abu Salamah, raise his degree among the rightly guided, and be his successor among his descendants who remain. Forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds. O God, make his grave spacious for him and fill it with light.”"],[20004,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, “In heaven there are two angels: one commands severity and the other commands gentleness, and each is right. They are Jibril and Mika'il. There were two prophets: one commanded gentleness and the other commanded severity, and each was right—he mentioned Ibrahim and Nuh. I have two companions: one commands gentleness and the other commands severity, and each is right—he mentioned Abu Bakr and 'Umar.”"],[20007,"She said on the day 'A'ishah died: \"Today the most beloved person in the world to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has died.\" Then she said: \"I seek Allah's forgiveness; except for her father.\""],[20014,"Umm Salamah, when Abu Salamah died, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what should I say?\" He said: \"Say: 'O Allah, forgive him and grant me a beneficial successor from him.'\" I said it, and Allah granted me the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a successor."],[20015,"The Prophet ﷺ never left my house in the morning without raising his eyes to the sky and saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from leading astray or being led astray, from slipping or being made to slip, from wronging or being wronged, and from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly.\""],[20022,"She was delousing the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Zaynab, the wife of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, came and began talking to me while I talked to her, and I raised my eyes to her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Attend to your delousing, for you are not talking to her with your eyes.\" Zaynab said: \"Then I began to complain of the narrowness of the dwelling.\" He said: \"This is just as the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un did; her place did not suffice her until she moved onto his head.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Thus it is for any emigrant woman who stakes out a plot in Madinah; she has her plot.\" So she inherited her share from 'Abdullah's house and secured her house in Madinah."],[20030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray thirteen raka'ah in the night, but when he became old or weak, he would pray seven raka'ah."],[20036,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “When sins become widespread in my Ummah, Allah will envelop them all in punishment.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will there not be righteous people among the people on that day?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “Then what will happen to them?” He said, “What befalls the people will befall them, and then they will attain forgiveness from Allah and His good pleasure.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu al-Rabi'."],[20037,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he would depilate, would begin with his pubic area, and that is what he would attend to."],[20038,"Umm Salamah: A daughter of mine fell ill, so I steeped something for her in a jug of hers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while it was boiling and said, “What is this?” I said, “My daughter fell ill, so I steeped this for her.” He said, “Indeed, Allah did not place your cure in what has been forbidden to you.”"],[20039,"This verse: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the House, and to purify you thoroughly” is about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn."],[20040,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me with a distressed face. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, why do I see you distressed?” He said, “The dinars that they brought to us—I forgot them in the corner of my bed. I forgot to distribute them before evening.”"],[20042,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he became angry, his face would turn red."],[20043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Sit at the door so that no one enters upon me.” So I stood at the door when al-Husayn came, and he was a young boy. I went to grab him, but the boy got ahead of me and entered upon his grandfather. I said, “O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom. You commanded me that no one should enter upon you, and your son came. I went to grab him, but he got ahead of me.” When that prolonged, I looked from the door and found you turning something in your palm while your tears were flowing and the boy was on your belly. He said, “Yes, Jibril came to me and informed me that my Ummah will kill him, and he brought me the soil upon which he will be killed. It is that which I am turning in my palm.”"],[20044,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Indeed, among my Companions are those who will not see me after I die.”"],[20045,"“We never sifted flour for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever.”"],[20046,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Why didn’t you make use of its hide?”"],[20047,"I heard Umm Salamah say: 'Ali was upon the truth; whoever followed him followed the truth and whoever abandoned him abandoned the truth—a covenant taken before this day of his.'"],[20051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the desert when a caller cried out to him, 'O Messenger of Allah!' He turned but saw no one. Then he turned again and saw a gazelle tied up. It said, 'Come near me, O Messenger of Allah.' He came near it and said, 'What do you need?' It said, 'I have two fawns in that mountain. Untie me so I can go nurse them, then I will return to you.' He said, 'Will you do that?' It said, 'May Allah punish me with the punishment of a she-camel that withholds her milk if I do not.' So he released it, and it went and nursed its two fawns, then came back and he tied it again. The Bedouin woke up and said, 'Do you need anything, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, release this one.' So he released it, and it ran off saying, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.'"],[20055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not gulp down his drink; he would drink two or three times."],[20066,"The Prophet ﷺ recited this verse: \"Indeed, he has done a non-righteous deed.\""],[20067,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, 'Bring me your husband and your two sons.' She brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw over them a Fadakite cloak, then placed his hand upon them and said, 'O Allah, these are the family of Muhammad, so place Your blessings and benedictions upon the family of Muhammad, for You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.' Umm Salamah said, 'I lifted the cloak to enter with them, but he pulled it from my hands and said, 'You are upon good.'"],[20068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, 'Bring me your husband and your two sons.' She brought them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw over them a cloak, then said, 'These are the family of Muhammad, so place Your blessings and benedictions upon the family of Muhammad as You placed them upon the family of Ibrahim; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'"],[20069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited every intoxicant and every narcotic."],[20070,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, “that they not disobey you in what is right,” he said: “Wailing.”"],[20071,"The Prophet ﷺ took a garment and wrapped it over ʿAlī, Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn, then recited this verse: “Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.”"],[20075,"“O Messenger of Allah, my hands have become calloused from the mill, kneading bread and dough.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “If Allah provides you something it will come to you. I shall direct you to something better than that. When you lie down in your bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. That is better for you than a servant. And when you pray the morning prayer, say ten times after the morning prayer and ten times after the sunset prayer: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death. In His hand is all good, and He is capable of all things.’ Each one of them is recorded as ten good deeds, erases ten evil deeds, and each one is like freeing a slave from the children of Ishmael. No sin committed that day is lawful to remain except that it erases it, unless it be associating partners with Allah. ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner’—it guards you from every devil and from every thing between your saying it in the morning and your saying it in the evening.”"],[20076,"Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was speaking with a man, and he said, “O Umm Salamah, who is this?” I said, “Diḥyah al-Kalbī.” I did not know that it was Jibrīl ﷺ until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ telling his companions what had taken place between them. I said to Abū ʿUthmān, “Who narrated this to you?” He said, “Usāmah b. Zayd.”"],[20080,"I performed Hajj with my master and entered upon Umm Salamah. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Pronounce talbiyah, O nation of Muhammad, for a Hajj and an ʿUmrah.”"],[20088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded giving charity. Zaynab, the wife of Abdullah b. Mas'ud, said, “Will it suffice me for charity that I give to my husband, who is poor, and to the orphans of my brother, on whom I spend in any case?” He said, “Yes.” She was a skilled craftswoman."],[20104,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that a daughter of hers had lost her husband and complained of her eyes, and she wanted to apply kohl to her. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"One of you used to throw a dung pellet at the head of the year, but it is only four months and ten [days].\""],[20111,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a sheep's shoulder, and he ate from it, then prayed without touching water."],[20125,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"A woman whose husband has died should not dye her hair, nor apply kohl, nor wear perfume, nor wear a dyed garment, nor wear jewelry.\""],[20131,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"The one who drinks from a silver vessel only makes the fire of Hell gurgle in his belly.\""],[20135,"On the authority of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: There was shouting in the room of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he came out wearing a cloak thrown over his shoulders and said: 'What are these people doing?' They said: 'They are disputing, O Messenger of God.' The Prophet of God ﷺ judged between them, then said: 'I judge between you, and it may be that one of you is more eloquent in presenting his case than his brother, so I judge in his favor based on what I discern. If I award someone something that is not his due, I am only giving him a portion of the Fire.'"],[20136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whoever enters the state of iḥrām from Jerusalem, his past sins will be forgiven.\""],[20137,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Umm Salamah, do not harm me concerning A'ishah, for revelation has not descended upon me while I was with any of my wives except A'ishah; indeed revelation descended upon me while she was with me under my blanket.\""],[20164,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever says every day: 'O Allah, forgive me and the believing men and women,' a reward equal to every believer will be added to his account.\""],[20167,"She asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, about nabidh. She said: I will inform you what the Messenger of God ﷺ used to forbid his family from: He used to forbid us from mixing raisins with dates."],[20168,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is not appropriate for anyone to be in a state of major ritual impurity in this mosque except me and Ali."],[20169,"I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was weeping. I said: What makes you weep? She said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ—meaning in a dream—with dust on his head and beard. I said: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of God? He said: I have just witnessed the killing of al-Husayn."],[20173,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: None loves Ali except a believer, and none hates him except a hypocrite."],[20177,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The one consulted is entrusted."],[20178,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When evil appears on the earth, God sends His punishment upon the people of the earth. I said: O Messenger of God, what if there are righteous people among them? He said: Yes, even if there are righteous people among them, what befalls the people will befall them too; then they will return to God's mercy and forgiveness."],[20179,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ali: Are you not content to be to me as Aaron was to Moses, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[20180,"Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr came to the Prophet ﷺ while she was ill, and he said to her, “Will you not come out with us on this journey of ours?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am ill and I fear my illness will hold me back.” He said, “Enter ihram for Hajj and say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You hold me back.”"],[20182,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray Witr with seven or five Rak’ah, and he would not say Salam or speak in between them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1192)"],[20186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Angels do not accompany a group that has a bell in it.”"],[20187,"The Prophet ﷺ used to wake up in a state of janabah and then fast."],[20188,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever loves Ali has loved me, and whoever loves me has loved Allah. Whoever hates Ali has hated me, and whoever hates me has hated Allah.”"],[20209,"«I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a roasted side (of meat), and he ate from it, then stood for prayer and did not perform wudu.»"],[20210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Whoever is tested with judging between Muslims, let him treat them equally in the seating, in gesture and gaze, and let him not raise his voice against one of the two litigants more than the other.»"],[20211,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to «perform wudu from what fire has touched.»"],[20223,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when I began menstruating, so I left the bed. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Wrap a waist-wrapper around yourself and come back.”"],[20224,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite “In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds,” letter by letter."],[20225,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever spends on two daughters, two sisters, or two female relatives, seeking reward for his spending on them until God suffices them and enriches them from His bounty, they will be a screen for him from the Fire.”"],[20228,"“My abundant wealth may destroy me, for I am the wealthiest of Quraysh.” She said: “My son, give charity, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘Among my Companions are those who will never see me after I die.’” So 'Abd al-Rahman went out and met 'Umar and told him what Umm Salamah had said. 'Umar came and entered upon her and said: “Am I one of them?” She said: “No, and I will never say that to anyone after you.”"],[20229,"May your face be rubbed in dust, for the Prophet ﷺ said to a freed slave of ours called Rabah, whom he saw prostrating: “May your face be rubbed in dust, O Rabah.”"],[20232,"And the Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever possesses one of three qualities, Allah will marry him to the wide-eyed maidens of Paradise: whoever has a hidden, desirable trust and fulfills it out of fear of Allah, or a man who pardons his killer, or a man who recites ‘Say: He is Allah, the One’ after every prayer.”"],[20233,"I heard Umm Salamah say: “Ali is upon the truth; whoever follows him follows the truth, and whoever abandons him abandons the truth—a covenant pledged before his death.”"],[20234,"I came to Umm Salamah to inform her about al-Husayn, and she said to me in what she narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in my house one day when Fatimah came to him with some porridge. He said: “Go and bring your husband—or your cousin—and your two sons.” She went and brought Ali, Hasan, and Husayn, and they ate from that food while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a bed of ours, with a Khaybar cloak beneath him. He took the cloak and wrapped them in it, then raised his hands toward the sky and said: “O Allah, these are my family and my household, so remove impurity from them and purify them thoroughly.” Umm Salamah said: “O Messenger of Allah, am I not of your household?” He said: “You are upon good.”"],[20240,"Sometimes the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dyed his cloak and waist-wrapper with saffron or wars, then went out wearing them."],[20241,"The Prophet ﷺ used to perform nine or ten units of non-obligatory prayers, without separating them with a greeting or speech."],[20250,"“I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from one vessel, about half a faraq, taking turns in washing together, he starting before me.”"],[20251,"Ibn 'Abbas and some people sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her which days the Messenger of God ﷺ fasted most. She said, “Saturday and Sunday were the days he fasted most of all, and he would say, ‘They are the two festival days of the polytheists, so I like to differ from them.’”"],[20252,"“I and the Messenger of God ﷺ used to bathe from one vessel, both of us in a state of janabah, until my hand and his hand differed.”"],[20256,"The Prophet ﷺ used to make the intention to fast at night, then he would get up in the morning and say, “Do you have anything?” We would say, “We have nothing. Are you not fasting?”"],[20263,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not harm me regarding Aisha, for revelation has not descended under the blanket of any one of you except Aisha ؓ.”"],[20265,"The Prophet ﷺ was occupied and missed performing the two units (rak'ahs) before Asr prayer, so he performed them after Asr prayer."],[20266,"The Prophet ﷺ used to be intimate with her while he was fasting."],[20267,"When the Prophet ﷺ wanted to sleep while in a state of major ritual impurity, he would perform ablution as for prayer; and when he wanted to eat, he would wash his hands and then eat."],[20268,"She said to the Prophet ﷺ: “I have not performed the farewell circumambulation of the House.” He said: “When you have prayed, circumambulate from behind the people on your camel.”"],[20269,"that the Prophet ﷺ commanded her to pray the morning prayer in Makkah."],[20270,"Umm Salamah: O Messenger of God, a woman whose husband has died—do you permit kohl? He said, \"One of you used to, when her husband died, take a piece of dung and throw it behind her back, then say: 'I will not apply kohl until this dung is transformed.' But it is only four months and ten days.\""],[20271,"Al-Harith ibn Abi Rabia and Abdullah ibn Safwan entered upon Umm Salama and I was with them. They asked her about the army that would be swallowed up, and this was during the time of Ibn Zubayr. She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A person will seek refuge by entering the House, then Allah will send a wind, and when they are in an open plain of land, they will be swallowed up.'\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will they be swallowed up with those who are reluctant?\" He said, \"They will be swallowed up along with them, but they will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection according to their intentions.\""],[20272,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"An army will raid this House until, when they are at a desert tract of the land, they will be swallowed up.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, what about the one who is compelled?\" He said, \"He will be resurrected according to his intention.\""],[20273,"that you should marry until you complete the waiting period, the longer of the two terms. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, \"Marry whomever you wish.\""],[20274,"that you should marry until you complete the waiting period, the longer of the two terms. She remained for twenty nights, then she gave birth. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he said, \"Marry.\" And Fatimah bint Qays used to narrate from the Messenger of God ﷺ when she was given an irrevocable divorce that he commanded her to move to Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind, and she could set down her garments in his presence before her waiting period ended. And Muhammad b. Usamah b. Zayd used to narrate that whenever she mentioned anything of that, Usamah threw at her whatever was in his hand."],[20275,"that the Prophet ﷺ ate from the shoulder of a sheep, then the call to prayer was made, and he prayed without touching water—the afternoon prayer."],[20276,"that a woman asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"O Messenger of God, I have a daughter whom I married off, and she was afflicted with measles so that her hair fell out, and we want to present her to her husband.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May God curse the one who attaches hair extensions and the one who asks for them.\""],[20277,"O Messenger of God, is there an obligation for a woman to perform ghusl if she has a wet dream? He said, \"Yes, if she sees fluid, let her perform ghusl.\""],[20278,"It was my night on which the Messenger of God ﷺ would come to me, on the evening of the Day of Sacrifice. He came to me, and Wahb b. Zam'ah entered upon me, and with him another man from the family of Abu Umayyah, both wearing shirts. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Have you performed the ifadah circumambulation yet, O Abu Abdullah?\" He said, \"No, by God, O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"Remove your shirt from yourself.\" So he removed it from his head, and his companion removed his shirt from his head. Then he said, \"Why, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"This is a day on which permission has been given to you: when you have thrown the pebbles, you may exit ihram from everything that was forbidden to you except women. But if you have intercourse before you circumambulate this House, you become in a state of ihram as you were before throwing the pebbles.\""],[20281,"that the Prophet ﷺ performed i'tikaf the first year during the first ten days, then he performed i'tikaf during the middle ten days, then he performed i'tikaf during the last ten days. And he said, \"I saw the Night of Decree in them, but I was made to forget it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ continued to perform i'tikaf during them until the Messenger of God ﷺ passed away."],[20282,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever drinks from vessels made of gold and silver, is actually swallowing fire from the Hellfire.\""],[20283,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on this pulpit: \"I will precede you to the Kawthar. While I am upon it, you will pass by me in groups, and you will be turned away. I will call out: 'Come, come!' A caller will call out and say: 'They have introduced innovations after you.' So I will say: 'Away with them!'\""],[20284,"that while she was combing her hair, nothing startled her except the Messenger of God ﷺ calling from the pulpit, saying: \"O people, while I was at the Pond, you were brought to me group by group. A group of you went this way and that way. I said, 'What is wrong with them? Come to me.' A crier cried out and said, 'They have changed after you.' So I said, 'Away with them, away with them!'\""],[20285,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, is a woman required to perform ghusl if she sees in her dream that her husband has intercourse with her? He said: “Yes, if she sees the fluid.” Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, does that happen to a woman? He said: “Yes, may your forehead be covered with dust. From where does the resemblance to maternal uncles come? May you be bereft of your mother! Whichever of the two fluids reaches the womb first will prevail in determining resemblance.”"],[20286,"She said: I know of the largest amount of wealth that came to the Prophet ﷺ until Allah took him. There came to him in the darkness of the night a bag containing eight hundred dirhams and a letter. He sent it to me, and it was my night. Then he returned after the last 'isha prayer and prayed in the room at a prayer place of his, and I had prepared a bed for him and for myself. So I waited. He prolonged the prayer, then went out, then came back, and he kept doing that until the call for the dawn prayer was given. He prayed and then returned and said: “Where is that bag that distracted me last night?” He called for it and distributed it. Then he said: “Woe to you!” I said: O Messenger of Allah, you did something you had not done before. He said: “I was praying, and it was brought to me, so I would leave the prayer to look at it, then return and pray.”"],[20287,"From the Prophet ﷺ similarly."],[20288,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw some camels, on one of which was a bell. When he heard its sound, he said: “What is this?” A man said: The julyul. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And what is the julyul?” He said: The bell. He said: “Yes, go and cut it off and throw it away.” So he did, then the man returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, what does it matter? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The angels do not accompany a group that has a bell with it.”"],[20290,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wake up in a state of janabah and fast that day."],[20291,"She said: I used to perform ghusl together with the Messenger of Allah from a single vessel."],[20292,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me, and he woke up with his eyes red. He shook his head and said: “Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near.” I said: What is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “A gap has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this,” and he formed a circle with ten fingers. The narrator said: I do not know whether [it was] like a ring or like a fingertip. I said: Do you fear for us destruction, O Messenger of Allah, even though righteous people are among us? He said: “Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.” Umm Ruman said: 'A'ishah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this hadith, and he narrated it to me just as Umm Salamah said."],[20293,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever enters ihram for an 'umrah from Bayt al-Maqdis, it will be forgiven for him.”"],[20294,"When the Prophet ﷺ mentioned what he mentioned about the izār, Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of Allah, what about women? He said: “They should let it down by a handspan.” She said: Then their feet will show. He said: “Then a cubit, and let them not add to that.”"],[20295,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said about the hem, Umm Salamah said: What about us? He said: “Let it hang down a handspan.” She said: Then the feet will be exposed. He said: “Let it hang down a cubit.”"],[20296,"She said: One of us, when she performed ghusl, would take care that no one saw her yellow [traces]."],[20297,"She said: My eye has become accustomed to kohl that contains perfume, and her husband had died. Is it permissible for me to apply kohl? She said: “By Allah, I do not command you to do anything that Allah and His Messenger have forbidden.”"],[20298,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “It is not lawful for a woman to mourn more than three days, except a woman mourning her husband for four months and ten days.”"],[20299,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not apply perfume while you are in ihram, and do not touch henna, for it is perfume.”"],[20300,"From a freedwoman of hers whom she sent to Umm Salamah; she said: I heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me while I was in my waiting period following the death of Abu Salamah: “Do not comb your hair with perfume or with henna, for it is a dye.” I said: With what should I comb my hair, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “With lote-tree leaves; wrap your head with it.”"],[20301,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me when Abu Salamah had died, and I had put some aloe on my eye. He said: “What is this, O Umm Salamah?” I said: It is only aloe, O Messenger of Allah; there is no perfume in it. He said: “It brightens the face, so apply it at night and remove it during the day.”"],[20302,"I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was praying in a shift and a headcover. I asked her about decorative embroidery on a garment. She said: “We used to wear a garment like this — referring to a garment she had with silk embroidery on it — in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[20303,"He used to say: I have a hadith which, if I wanted to consume the world by means of it, I would consume it, but Allah will not ask me about a hadith I raise to the ruler. My father said: I said: What is it? He said: When Zayd went out, I came to my maternal aunt the next day and said to her: O mother, Zayd has gone out. She said: The poor man, he will be killed as his fathers were killed. I said to her: Men of understanding have gone out with him. She said: I was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when they discussed the caliphate. Umm Salamah said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when they discussed the caliphate after him. They said: The descendants of Fatimah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They will never attain it, ever; rather it will be among the descendants of my paternal uncle, my father’s full brother, until they hand it over to the Dajjal.”"],[20304,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “Fast three days of every month, from its beginning: Monday, Thursday, and the following Thursday.”"],[20305,"“Nothing was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than a shirt.”"],[20306,"“Maymunah bint al-Harith b. Hazn b. Bujayr b. al-Haram b. Ruwaybah b. Abd Allah b. Hilal b. Amir b. Sa'sa'ah — she is the one who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[20307,"“Maymunah entrusted her affair to Umm al-Fadl, and Umm al-Fadl entrusted it to al-Abbas, so he married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[20308,"“Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year of al-Harrah, in the year sixty-three.”"],[20309,"“I saw the Mother of the Believers Maymunah shaving her head after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I said to Yazid b. al-Asamm: He said: “I think she was letting herself go.”"],[20310,"She said: I screened the Prophet ﷺ while he performed ghusl from janabah. He began by washing his hands, then poured water with his right hand over his left and washed his private part and whatever had been affected by it. Then he struck his hand on the wall or the ground, then performed wudu as for prayer except for his feet, then poured water over himself, then moved his feet aside and washed them."],[20311,"She said: I brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ his water for ghusl from janabah. He washed his hand twice or three times, then inserted his hands into the vessel and poured water from them over his private part and washed it with his left hand. Then he struck his left hand on the ground and rubbed it vigorously. Then he performed wudu as for prayer, then poured three handfuls of water over his head, filling his palms, then washed the rest of his body. Then he moved away from that spot and washed his feet. Then I brought him the towel, but he returned it."],[20312,"She said: I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ghusl from janabah. He tilted the vessel over his right hand and washed it twice or three times, then poured water over his private part and washed it with his left hand. Then he struck his hand on the ground and washed it, then rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, washed his face and hands. Then he poured water over his head and body, then moved aside and washed his feet. Then I handed him the towel, but he did not take it and began shaking the water off his body."],[20313,"The Prophet ﷺ took the bath of Janaba. (sexual relation or wet dream). He first cleaned his private parts with his hand, and then rubbed it (that hand) on the wall (earth) and washed it. Then he performed ablution like that for the prayer, and after the bath he washed his feet. (Using translation from Bukhārī 260)"],[20314,"She said: I placed, or water was placed, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his ghusl. He poured water with his right hand over his left until he cleaned it, then poured water with his right hand over his private part and washed it with his left and whatever had been affected by it until he cleaned it. Then he wiped his hand on the wall, on the dust, then washed it until he cleaned it. Then he rinsed his mouth, sniffed water into his nose, and performed wudu as for prayer. Then he poured water over his head and his body, then moved from his place and washed his feet."],[20315,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in any other except the mosque of the Kaʿbah.”"],[20316,"She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “A prayer in it – meaning his mosque – is better than a thousand prayers in any other mosque except the mosque of the Kaʿbah.”"],[20317,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I both became junub, so I performed ghusl from a large basin, and some water remained from my washing. The Prophet ﷺ came and performed ghusl from it. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, it is leftover from my washing.” He said, “Water does not become junub.”"],[20318,"She said: “I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel.”"],[20319,"Maymuna said: “I used to perform ghusl, I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from a single vessel.”"],[20320,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to “perform ghusl with water leftover from Maymuna’s ghusl.”"],[20321,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Why did you not tan its hide?”"],[20322,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Why did you not tan it and make use of it?” They said, “It is carrion.” He said, “Tanning the hide is its purification.”"],[20323,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of ours, which had been given to her as charity. He said, “What is wrong with the people of this [sheep] that they did not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?” They said, “O Messenger of God, it is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.” It was said to Sufyan that Maʿmar does not say “and tan it” in it, and says that al-Zuhri rejected tanning. Sufyan said, “But I memorized it, and we only wanted from him this phrase that others transmitted: ‘Only its eating is forbidden.’” Sufyan sometimes did not mention Maymuna in it, but when he was asked about it, he said Maymuna in it."],[20324,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us: Sufyan b. ʿUyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from ʿUbayd Allah b. ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUtba, from Ibn ʿAbbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Why did they not remove its hide, tan it, and benefit from it?” They said, “It is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.”"],[20325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymuna and said, “Why did you not make use of its hide?” They said, “How, when it is dead, O Messenger of God?” He said, “Only its meat is forbidden.”"],[20326,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Why did you not benefit from its skin?” They said, “O Messenger of God, it is dead.” He said, “Only its eating is forbidden.”"],[20327,"A sheep died and the Prophet ﷺ was asked about it. He said, “Only its meat is forbidden to you, and its hide is permitted for you.”"],[20328,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said, “Were the people of this [sheep] unable to benefit from its hide?”"],[20329,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said, “Take it and what is around it and throw it away, and eat your clarified butter.”"],[20330,"A mouse fell into clarified butter and died. The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked, and he said, “Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it.” Al-Humaydi said: It was said to Sufyan that Maʿmar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Saʿid, from Abu Hurayra. Sufyan said, “I never heard al-Zuhri narrate it except from ʿUbayd Allah, from Ibn ʿAbbas, from Maymuna, from the Prophet ﷺ. I heard it from him many times.”"],[20331,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter, and he said, “Throw it away and what is around it, and eat it.”"],[20332,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked about a mouse falling into clarified butter. He said, “If it is solid, throw it away and what is around it; if it is liquid, do not approach it.”"],[20333,"Maymuna said: The Messenger of God ﷺ woke up one morning in low spirits and spent the evening likewise. I said, “O Messenger of God, why do I see you in low spirits?” He said, “Gabriel promised me he would come to me, and he has never broken his promise to me.” They looked, and there was a puppy under a wooden couch of theirs. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered that puppy to be taken out, and ordered that place to be washed with water. Then Gabriel came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You promised me you would come to me, and you have never broken your promise to me.” He said, “Did you not know that we do not enter a house containing a dog or an image?”"],[20334,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ woke up one day gloomy. Maymuna said: I said, “O Messenger of God, I have found your appearance strange today.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Gabriel had promised me he would meet me tonight, but he did not meet me. By God, he has not broken his promise to me.” She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ remained so all that day. Then a puppy came to his mind under a mat of ours. He ordered it to be taken out, then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled it on its place. When evening came, Gabriel met him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him, “You had promised me you would meet me last night.” He said, “Yes, but we do not enter a house containing a dog or an image.” That morning the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered the killing of dogs, even ordering the killing of the big dog of the large orchard, while leaving the dog of the small orchard."],[20335,"One day the Messenger of God ﷺ came out looking dejected. I said, \"Why do I see you dejected?\" He said, \"Gabriel promised me, and he has not broken his promise.\" He remained like that all day and night. I had a dog under a bed of ours, so he ordered it removed. Then he took some water in his hand and sprinkled it in its place. Then Gabriel came and said, \"We do not enter a house where there is an image or a dog.\" She said: He would be spoken to about the small dog of the orchard, but he never permitted it."],[20336,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, \"Whoever takes on a debt intending to repay it, God will settle it for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[20337,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, took on a debt of eight hundred dirhams. It was said to her, \"Will you take a debt when you have nothing to repay it with?\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'Whoever takes on a debt while being determined to repay it, God will help him repay it.'\""],[20338,"A year of famine struck the people, and the Bedouins would come to Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ would order a man to take another man by the hand and host him and give him supper. One night a Bedouin came, and the Messenger of God ﷺ had some food and a little milk. The Bedouin ate it and left nothing for the Messenger of God ﷺ. Then he brought him one or two more nights, and he kept eating it all. So I said, \"O Messenger of God, O God, do not bless this Bedouin; he eats the food of the Messenger of God ﷺ and leaves him nothing.\" Then he brought him one night, and he ate only a little of the food and drank only a little of the milk. I said to the Messenger of God ﷺ, \"That's it.\" Then he brought him one night after he had embraced Islam, and he said, \"The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, while the believer eats with one intestine.\""],[20340,"From Maymuna bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he would keep his arms away from his sides so that his back was visible, and he would open his armpits."],[20341,"When the Prophet ﷺ prostrated, if a small animal had wanted to pass beneath him, it could have passed, because of the gap he left."],[20342,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms away from his sides, so much so that if a small animal wanted to pass under his hands, it would pass."],[20343,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrated, he kept his arms away from his sides until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen, leaning on his right side and relaxing his left."],[20344,"A dabb lizard was gifted to Maymuna. Two men from her people came to her, so she ordered it to be prepared and served it to them. Then the Prophet of God ﷺ came while they were eating. He welcomed them, then he took some food to eat. When he brought a morsel to his mouth, he said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"A dabb lizard that was gifted to us.\" She said: He put down the morsel, and the two men wanted to throw away what was in their mouths, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Do not do that. You are people of Najd and you eat it, but we are people of Tihamah and we find it repulsive.\""],[20345,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were both ritually permitted (not in ihram).\""],[20346,"The Messenger of God ﷺ married her while she was ritually permitted (not in ihram)."],[20347,"From one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, Maymunah — and he was her brother through breastfeeding — from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “There is no Muslim over whom a community prays [the funeral prayer] except that they are granted intercession for him.” Abu al-Malih used to say: “The community is forty or more.”"],[20348,"Maymunah said to me: “O son of my brother, come, let me recite a ruqyah over you with the ruqyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said: “In the name of Allah I recite over you, and Allah heals you from every disease in you. Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people; heal, for there is no healer but You.”"],[20349,"From al-Hilaliyyah, she who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that she had a black slave girl and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I want to free this one.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you not ransom with her your brother's daughter or your sister's daughter from tending sheep?”"],[20350,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Do not make nabidh in the muzaffat or in the naqir.”"],[20351,"Narrated Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , she said, \"My sister, Umm Hufaidh, gifted me with a dish of meat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his dinner and Khalid bin Al-Walid was with him, who is her nephew. She presented the dish of meat to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ leaned towards it, thinking it was chickens. So, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you know what this is?' He replied, 'No.' Then, he took his hand off it. So, I said, 'This is lizard meat.' He said, 'That is the food of the people of the desert.' Khalid asked, 'Is it Haram (forbidden)?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'No.' Then, Khalid ate from it, with the Prophet ﷺ looking on.\""],[20352,"From the Prophet ﷺ, likewise."],[20353,"I freed a slave girl of mine, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and I told him of her manumission. He said: “May Allah reward you. But if you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater in reward for you.”"],[20354,"She freed a slave girl of hers without asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was her day on which he would come to her, she said: “Are you aware, O Messenger of Allah, that I have freed my slave girl so-and-so?” He said: “Have you done so?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Indeed, if you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater in reward for you.”"],[20355,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder at her place, then prayed without performing wudu’."],[20356,"I said: “I perform witr with three [rak‘ahs], then go out to the prayer fearing that I might miss it.” He said: “It is not valid except with five or seven.” I informed Mujahid and Yahya b. al-Jazzar of his statement, and they said to me: “Did you not ask him from whom?” [He said:] “So I asked him, and he said: ‘From the trustworthy one, from Maymunah and ‘A’ishah, from the Prophet ﷺ.’”"],[20357,"Maymunah bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me, saying: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was opposite him, and I was menstruating; and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated.”"],[20358,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was opposite him, and I was menstruating; and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated."],[20359,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have intimate contact with his wives while they were menstruating, instructing them to wear a waist-wrapper."],[20360,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah (small mat)."],[20361,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[20362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah that had been spread for him in the mosque."],[20363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray on the khumrah."],[20364,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to have intimate contact with any of his wives while she was menstruating, he would order her to wear a waist-wrapper and then have contact with her."],[20365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray wearing a woolen cloak, part of it on him and part on one of his wives while she was menstruating. Humaydi said in his version: 'part on me and part on him while I was menstruating.'"],[20366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was sleeping beside him; when he prostrated, his garment would touch me while I was menstruating."],[20367,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never left my house without raising his gaze to the sky and saying: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from going astray or being led astray, from slipping or being made to slip, from acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly, and from wronging or being wronged.'"],[20368,"She asked: 'Where is the man from?' I said: 'From the people of Iraq.' She asked: 'From which people of Iraq?' I said: 'From the people of Kufa.' She asked: 'From which people of Kufa?' I said: 'From Banu Amir.' She then said: 'Welcome, near you are on nearness, and spacious you are on spaciousness. So what has brought you?' I said: 'There occurred between Ali, Talhah, and al-Zubayr what occurred, so I came and pledged allegiance to Ali.' She said: 'Then join him, for by Allah, he has not gone astray nor been led astray.' She repeated that three times."],[20369,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The believer eats in one intestine, while the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.'"],[20370,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said one day: 'What will you be when religion is corrupted, blood is shed, adornment becomes widespread, buildings are raised high, two brothers differ, and the Ancient House (the Kaaba) is burned?'"],[20371,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood between the row of men and the row of women and said to the women: \"When you hear the adhan of this Abyssinian, say what he says.\""],[20372,"From the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives when she was menstruating, with a cloth upon her reaching to the knees or to the middle of the thighs.\" Ibn Jurayj mentioned it from Ibn Shihab, from Habib, the mawla of 'Urwah, from Nudbah."],[20373,"Regarding the bed of his wife, while the daughter of Mishrah was with him that day, she said: \"What is the matter with you?\" She said: \"This is how he treats me when I menstruate.\" She said: \"So I went to Maymunah and informed her.\" He said: \"And she said: 'She sent me to him saying: What is it that you do? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with one of us while she was menstruating, and she had nothing on except her waist-wrapper, reaching to the middle of her thigh.'\""],[20374,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives while she was menstruating, if she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees, with which she wrapped herself.\""],[20375,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives while she was menstruating, if she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees.\""],[20376,"That the mole of Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , looked and saw that his bed was separated from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. So she returned to Maymuna and informed her of her return message. Then she said, \"I saw his bed separate from mine, so I think there has been a separation between them.\" Maymuna said to them, \"Go back to the wife of Ibn Abbas and ask her about it.\" So I returned and asked her, and she said, \"There is no separation between us, but when I have my period, he separates his bed from mine.\" Maymuna sent a message to Abdullah expressing her anger towards him, and she said, \"O Abdullah, do you prefer to go against the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? By Allah, if a woman from her husbands wears a garment that does not reach the halfway point of her thighs, he can have intimate relations with her.\""],[20377,"Nudbah, the freed slave woman of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Maymunah sent her to 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas, who was the son of her sister. She said: \"I went to him and found him having separated his bed from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. She said: 'Where is he? Is he angry with his wife?' It was said: 'No, but when she menstruates, he distances himself from her.' She said: 'So I returned to Maymunah and informed her how I found him.' She said: 'Call him for me.' So I called him for her, and she said: 'Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do? By Allah, he used to be intimate with a woman from among his wives when she had a waist-wrapper reaching to the middle of the thighs or the knees.'\""],[20378,"While she was sitting with Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, Ibn 'Abbas entered upon her. She said: \"Why do I see you disheveled?\" He said: \"Umm 'Ammar, my hairdresser, is menstruating.\" She said: \"O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enter upon one of us while she was reclining and menstruating, knowing that, and he would recline upon her and recite the Quran while reclining upon her. And he would enter upon her while she was standing and menstruating, and he would recline in her lap and recite the Quran. And she would stand while menstruating and spread the mat for him in his prayer place, and he would pray on it. O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand?\""],[20379,"\"O my dear son, why do I see your head disheveled?\" He said: \"My hairdresser, Umm 'Ammar, is menstruating.\" She said: \"O my dear son, what does menstruation have to do with the hand? Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating, and he would pray upon her.\""],[20380,"Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to her that some men from Quraysh passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey. The Prophet ﷺ said to them: \"Why don't you take its skin?\" They said: \"It is carrion.\" He said: \"Water and qaraz (acacia pods) purify it.\""],[20381,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said: \"Throw it away and what is around it, and eat the rest.\""],[20382,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a mouse that falls into clarified butter. He said: \"If it is solid, throw it away and what is around it; but if it is liquid, do not go near it.\""],[20385,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep belonging to a female client of Maymunah, which had been given to her from charity. He said, \"Why did they not take its hide and tan it and benefit from it?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is dead.\" He said, \"Only its eating is forbidden.\""],[20386,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Why did you not tan its hide and make use of it?\""],[20387,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs."],[20388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day looking sluggish. I said, \"Why do I see you sluggish?\" He said, \"Gabriel promised me and did not break [his promise], so he remained thus for that day and its night. In the house there was a dog under a couch of ours, so he took it out and took water with his hand and wiped its place with it. Then Gabriel came and said, 'We do not enter a house in which there is a picture or a dog.' He was consulted about the small dog of the garden, but he did not give permission for it.\""],[20389,"\"I used to perform ghusl together with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from a single vessel.\""],[20390,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[20391,"\"I placed water for the Prophet ﷺ to perform ghusl, and he performed ghusl from janabah. He tilted the vessel with his left hand over his right and washed his palms, then poured water over his private part and washed it, then rubbed his hand on the ground, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water and washed his face and forearms, then poured water over his head, then poured water over the rest of his body, then moved aside and washed his feet.\" She said, \"Then I brought him a cloth, but he cast it aside and began shaking off the water with his hand like this.\""],[20392,"I performed ghusl from janabah, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and performed ghusl with the water left over from my ghusl. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I had performed ghusl from it.\" He said, \"Water does not carry janabah.\""],[20393,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Water is not made impure by anything.\""],[20394,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ was brought a towel, but he did not touch it, and he began shaking off the water with his hand like this,\" meaning shaking it off."],[20395,"Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali went out in a funeral. When the deceased was placed on the bed, he approached the people and said, \"Straighten your rows and improve your intercession.\" Then Abu Al-Malih said, \"Abdullah bin Salit informed me, and he was the brother of Maymunah, the mother of the believers, from Maymunah, from the Prophet ﷺ , who said, 'Whoever prays upon him, a nation will intercede for their brother.' And the nation is forty to one hundred, the group is ten to forty, and the individual is three to ten.\""],[20396,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The sisters are believers,\" meaning Maymunah bint al-Harith, Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, Salma the wife of Hamzah, and Asma' bint Umays."],[20397,"On the authority of Maymunah: They disputed about the Prophet ﷺ's fasting on the Day of Arafah. Maymunah said: 'I shall send him some dates for you. If he is not fasting, he will not leave them.' So she sent him a bowl of milk, and he drank it while the people were watching."],[20398,"I prayed with Abu al-Malih over a funeral. He said: 'Straighten your rows and let your intercession be good, and if I were to choose a man, I would choose him.' Abdullah b. Abi al-Salil narrated to us, from one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, Maymunah—and he was her foster brother—that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'There is no Muslim man over whom a community prays but they are granted intercession for him.' Abu al-Malih said: 'The community is from forty to one hundred.'"],[20399,"On the authority of Maymunah, and Yazid was an orphan in her care. He mentioned that a siwak was always kept in a vessel. If work or prayer occupied her, otherwise she would take the siwak and use it."],[20400,"The Prophet ﷺ married me at Sarif while we were both in the state of ihram (or: not in ihram)."],[20401,"The Prophet ﷺ married her while he was not in ihram, and she was my maternal aunt."],[20402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah while he was not in ihram."],[20403,"When the Prophet ﷺ sat, he would settle on his left thigh."],[20404,"A dabb (spiny-tailed lizard) was gifted to us, so I cooked it. Two men from my people, the Quraysh, entered, and I offered it to them as a treat. Then the Prophet ﷺ entered while they were eating. He placed his hand, then lifted it and said: 'What is this?' I said: 'A dabb that was gifted to us; I cooked it.' He pushed it away. They went to throw away what was in their hands, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: 'Eat, for you are people of Najd and you eat it, while we are people of Tihamah and we find it repulsive.'"],[20405,"Maymunah narrated to me: 'When one of us was menstruating and stood up intending to return, he would instruct her to wrap herself with a waist-wrapper, and then he would engage in intimacy with her.'"],[20407,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray while I was beside him, and sometimes his garment would touch me when he prostrated."],[20408,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in a khamisah (a black rectangular cloak), part of which was over her while she was menstruating."],[20409,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray on a khumrah (a small mat)."],[20410,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray in his mosque on a small mat of his. He would touch me with his hands while I was sleeping beside him, and I was menstruating."],[20411,"On the authority of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet (PBUH), who said: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying, \"My Ummah will always remain upon good as long as they do not introduce (or tolerate) the child of Zina (illegitimate child) among them. But if they introduce it (or tolerate it), then I fear that Allah will afflict them with a punishment.\""],[20412,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I manumitted a slave girl of mine. The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and I informed him of her manumission. He said, “May Allah reward you. Indeed, had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.”"],[20414,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The world is sweet and green.\""],[20415,"The people doubted whether the Prophet ﷺ was fasting on the Day of ʿArafah. Maymunah sent him some milk while he was standing at the standing place, and he drank from it while the people were looking."],[20416,"I heard Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, say: “The Prophet ﷺ used to lie with me while I was menstruating, and between me and him was a garment.”"],[20417,"Some of her family said to her, “Do not do it,” and they disapproved of it. She said, “Yes, indeed I heard my Prophet and close friend ﷺ say: ‘There is no Muslim who incurs a debt intending to repay it except that Allah will repay it on his behalf in this world.’”"],[20419,"Nudbah, the freed slave woman of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, sent her to Ibn ʿAbbas, who was the son of her sister. She said: I came and found that his bed had been moved away from the bed of his wife, the daughter of Mishrah. I said, “Where is he? Is he angry with his wife?” They said, “No, but when she menstruates, he keeps apart from her.” I returned to Maymunah and told her how I had found him. She said, “Call him for me.” So I called him, and she said to him, “Do you turn away from what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do? By Allah, he used to touch a woman from among his wives when she had garments on, reaching the middle of the thighs or the knees.”"],[20420,"From the Hilaliyyah woman who was with the Prophet ﷺ, that she had a black servant girl. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to manumit this one.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Will you not help your brother’s sons with her in tending the sheep?”"],[20421,"I asked him if I can offer three units of prayer after Isha and then go out for prayer, fearing that I might miss it. He replied, \"It is not correct except with five or seven (units of prayer).\" So, I asked him from whom did he hear this? He said, \"From a trustworthy person, from Maymunah, from Aisha, from the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[20422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.”"],[20423,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to us one day: “How will you be when religion becomes confused, the common people become prominent, reports differ, and the Ancient House is burned?”"],[20424,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her when she freed her servant, \"If you had ransomed your family with her from the livestock of the sheep, it would have been better.\""],[20425,"The Prophet ﷺ used to pray two rakʿahs before ʿAsr."],[20426,"The Prophet ﷺ ate a shoulder at her place, then prayed and did not perform ablution."],[20427,"I heard Maymunah say: I manumitted my slave girl during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.”"],[20428,"Her family said to her, \"You take loans while you do not have what to repay?\" She said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever incurs a debt while telling himself he will repay it, Allah will help him with it.'\""],[20429,"Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, took a loan of three hundred dirhams. It was said to her, \"O Mother of the Believers, you take loans while you do not have [the means]?\" She said, \"Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever incurs a debt and intends to repay it, Allah will help him with it.'\""],[20430,"He heard Maymuna say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a shoulder cut, then prayed without performing wudu'.\""],[20431,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Ha Mim 'Ayn Sin Qaf and said, \"O Maymuna, do you recite Ha Mim 'Ayn Sin Qaf? I have forgotten what is between its beginning and its end.\" I recited it, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it."],[20432,"\"Maymuna was shrouded in a dyed yellow garment.\""],[20433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said, \"Is there any food?\" I said, \"No, except a bone that was given to a female client of ours from the charity.\" He said, \"Bring it, for it has reached its proper place.\""],[20434,"\"Sawda bt. Zam'a b. Qays b. 'Abd Shams b. 'Abd Wudd b. Nasr b. Malik b. Hasl b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her after Khadija bt. Khuwaylid in Makkah.\""],[20435,"Then \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Sawda bt. Zam'a. She had previously been married to al-Sakran b. 'Amr, the brother of Banu 'Amir b. Lu'ayy.\""],[20436,"Khawla bt. Hakim b. al-Awqas, the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un, and that was in Makkah, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry?\" He said, \"Who?\" She said, \"If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman.\" He said, \"Who is the previously married woman?\" She said, \"Sawda bt. Zam'a. She has believed in you and followed you in what you are upon.\" He said, \"Go and mention her to me.\" She said, \"I left and entered upon Sawda and said, 'O Sawda, what good and blessing has Allah brought to you?' She said, 'What is that?' Khawla said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to propose to you on his behalf.' She said, 'I would love that. Enter upon my father and mention that to him.' I said, 'He is an old man and has been left behind from the Hajj.' So I entered upon him and greeted him with the greeting of the people of the Jahiliyyah. Then she said, 'Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib sent me to propose to Sawda on his behalf.' He said, 'A noble equal. What does your companion say?' She said, 'She desires that.' He said, 'Call her to me.' So I called her. He said, 'O Sawda, this woman claims that Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib is proposing to you, and he is a noble equal. Would you like me to marry you to him?' She said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then call him for me.' So I called him and he came, and he married her to him. Then her brother 'Abd Allah b. Zam'a came from the Hajj and began to pour dust on his head. After he had become Muslim, he said, 'I was foolish on the day I poured dust on my head because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Sawda bt. Zam'a.'\""],[20437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not favor some of us over others in the division [of nights]. Rarely did a day pass except that he visited us and drew near each woman among us without intercourse, until he reached the one whose day it was and spent the night with her. Sawda bt. Zam'a said to him, and she had become old, and he intended to separate from her: \"My day with you and my share are for 'A'isha.\" He accepted that from her. About her it was revealed: {And if a woman fears from her husband ill-treatment or aversion, there is no sin upon them both if they make terms of peace between them} (Qur'an 4:128)."],[20438,"And she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not desire what women desire.\""],[20439,"\"Sawda gifted her day to 'A'isha, so he used to allocate to 'A'isha her own day and Sawda's day.\""],[20440,"When Sawdah bint Zam'ah became old, she gave her day to 'A'ishah, so the Prophet ﷺ would allot to 'A'ishah the day of Sawdah."],[20441,"that the Prophet ﷺ should divorce her. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, keep me and do not divorce me, and give my day to 'A'ishah.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame} upon them if they make peace between themselves, and peace is better. Whatever they agree upon is permissible."],[20442,"The Prophet ﷺ wanted to separate from Sawdah, so he called Abu Bakr and 'Umar to witness her divorce. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have no desire for this world except to be gathered on the Day of Resurrection among your wives, so that I may have the same reward as them.'"],[20443,"From al-Haytham or Abu al-Haytham — Abu Bakr was unsure — that the Prophet ﷺ divorced Sawdah once. She sat in his path, and when he passed by she asked him to take her back and to give her allotted share of him to whichever of his wives he wished, hoping to be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as his wife. So he took her back and accepted that."],[20444,"Sawdah was a large woman whose body frightened people."],[20445,"Sawdah and Zaynab said: 'The camel will never move us again after what we heard from the Prophet ﷺ,' meaning his saying, 'This is the last, then the riding of mats.' He said: So his wives performed Hajj except those two."],[20446,"From Sawdah bint Zam'ah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, when 'Uthman b. Maz'un walks, he prays for us until he comes to us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'If you knew what death knows, O daughter of Zam'ah, you would know that it is more severe than you imagine.'"],[20447,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. Sweat will bridle them and reach the lobes of their ears.' I asked, 'Will we see one another?' He said, 'People will be preoccupied. {Every man that Day will have concern enough to make him heedless of others}.'"],[20448,"The captives of Badr were brought while Sawdah bint Zam'ah was with the family of 'Afra' at their camel resting place, at 'Awf and Mu'awwidh, the two sons of 'Afra'. That was before the veil was imposed on them. She said: It was said, 'The captives of Badr have been brought.' So I went to my dwelling and there I saw Suhayl b. 'Amr, his hands bound together to his neck in a corner of the room. When I saw him, I could not control myself and said, 'Abu Yazid, you surrendered what was in your hands. Why did you not die nobly?' She said: By Allah, nothing alerted me except the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from inside the house: 'Against Allah and His Messenger?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I could not control myself when I saw Abu Yazid, so I said what I said.'"],[20449,"that she gave her day to 'A'ishah."],[20451,"We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, 'Why did you not make use of its hide?' We sent for it, skinned it, tanned the hide, and made it into a water skin. We drank from it until it became an old worn-out skin."],[20452,"So we tanned its hide and used to make nabidh in it until it became an old worn-out skin."],[20453,"Sawda, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"We had a sheep that died, so we tanned its skin, and we continued to soak [dates] in it until it became worn out like an old waterskin.\""],[20454,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a dead sheep and said: \"Why did you not make use of its hide?\""],[20455,"We had a sheep that died, so we threw it away. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: \"What happened to your sheep?\" We said: \"It died, so we threw it away.\" He said: \"Why did you not benefit from its hide?\" I said: \"It is carrion.\" Then he recited this verse: {Say, \"I do not find within that which was revealed to me [anything] forbidden to one who would eat it unless it be a dead animal...\"} (Qur'an 6:145) [and said]: \"He has only forbidden you from eating it.\" So they sent for its hide, tanned it, and used it until it became an old waterskin among them."],[20456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why did you not take its skin, tan it, and benefit from it?\""],[20457,"\"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj; should I perform Hajj on his behalf?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you think that if your father had a debt and you paid it off, would that be sufficient for him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then perform Hajj on his behalf.\""],[20458,"\"Among the women who emigrated from the Banu Asad were Zaynab bint Jahsh and some other women,\" and he mentioned them."],[20459,"Then \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh, and before that she was married to Zayd b. Harithah.\""],[20460,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh b. Ri'ab b. Asad b. Khuzaymah; her mother was Umaymah bint 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"She was the first of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to die.\""],[20461,"\"Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year twenty.\""],[20462,"\"Zaynab bint Jahsh died during the caliphate of 'Umar ؓ.\""],[20463,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"Zaynab bint Jahsh used to boast over the other wives of the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'Your families married you off, but Allah married me from above the heavens.'\""],[20464,"The Prophet ﷺ entered his house with 'Umar b. al-Khattab, and there was Zaynab bint Jahsh praying; while in her prayer she was supplicating. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"She is indeed devoted and humble [awwahah].\""],[20465,"A number of men from Quraysh proposed to me, so I sent my sister Hamnah to the Messenger of God ﷺ to consult him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, \"Where is she in comparison to one who will teach her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet?\" She said, \"And who is he, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"Zayd b. Harithah.\" Hamnah became extremely angry and said, \"O Messenger of God, will you marry the daughter of your paternal aunt to your freedman?\" She said: She came to me and informed me, and I became angrier than she had been, and I said something even stronger than what she had said. Then God revealed: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair}. She said: So I sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"I seek God's forgiveness and I obey God and His Messenger. Do what you see fit.\" So he married me to Zayd. I used to disparage him, and he complained about me to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ admonished me, but I returned to my behavior and rebuked him with my tongue. He complained about me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Keep your wife and fear God.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, I will divorce her.\" She said: So he divorced me. When my waiting period ended, I was not aware of anything until the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me in my house while my hair was uncovered. I said, \"This is a command from heaven.\" I said, \"O Messenger of God, without a proposal or witnesses?\" He said, \"God is the matchmaker, and Gabriel is the witness.\""],[20466,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zaid, \"Mention it to her.\" Zaid said, \"So I departed and said, 'O Zainab, rejoice! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends his regards to you.' She said, 'I don't do anything until I consult my Lord.' So she went to her mosque and the Qur'an was revealed, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her without seeking permission.\""],[20467,"If the Messenger of God ﷺ had concealed anything of the revelation, he would have concealed this verse: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose, and you feared the people, while God has more right that you fear Him. So when Zayd had accomplished his desire from her, We married her to you}."],[20468,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ concealed something of the Book of God, he concealed this verse: {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed and you had blessed}, up to His saying {accomplished his desire from her, We married her to you}."],[20469,"Concerning His saying {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed and you had blessed}, he said, \"God blessed him with Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ blessed him with manumission.\"{Keep your wife}, Qatadah said: Zayd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Zaynab's tongue has become harsh toward me, and I want to divorce her.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Fear God and keep your wife.\" The Prophet ﷺ wanted him to divorce her, but he feared what people would say if he commanded him to divorce her, so God revealed: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose, and you feared the people, while God has more right that you fear Him. So when Zayd had accomplished his desire from her}.He said: When Zayd divorced her, {We married her to you}."],[20470,"Regarding His statement: “and if the one who Allāh had favored says…” (Aḥzāb 33:37) and he was Zayd b. Ḥārithah: Allah had favored him with Islam, and “and you had blessed” the Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed him [from slavery].[Regarding] “and hold on to your wife and fear Allah and you hide within yourself what Allah has made known and you fear people...” (Aḥzāb 33:37), he said, he used to hide within himself [that] he liked that he would divorce her.. He said that al-Ḥasan said, \"No Āyah was revealed upon him more severe that His statement, '...and you hide within yourself', and if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were to hide anything from the Waḥī, he would have hidden it.\"[Regarding] “then when Zayd had fulfilled his desire with her,” [means] when Zayd had divorced her, “we married you to her.” He said, Zayb b. Jaḥsh used to boast to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"As for you all, your fathers married you off. And as for me, then the Owner of the Throne married me off.\"[Regarding] \"... fear Allah,\", he said, meaning O Prophet of Allah her [lack of] character has been hard on me and I am divorcing this woman. And the Prophet ﷺ, when he said this, said, \"Hold on to your wife and fear Allah.\""],[20471,"From Qatadah concerning His saying {And when you said to the one whom God had blessed}, \"with Islam,\" {and you had blessed}, \"that you manumitted him.\" {Keep your wife}, \"he is Zayd b. Harithah.\""],[20472,"It was revealed concerning Zaynab bt. Jahsh: {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose}."],[20473,"From Ibn Jurayj concerning His saying {And you concealed within yourself what God was to disclose}, \"In the heart of the Messenger of God ﷺ was his love for Zayd's divorcing her and his marrying her, but God insisted that He disclose what the Prophet ﷺ had concealed in his heart.\""],[20474,"“I never saw the Messenger of Allah give a wedding feast for any of his wives like the feast he gave for Zainab, for which he slaughtered a sheep.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1908)"],[20475,"Concerning His saying {The established way of God among those who passed away before}, he said, \"David and the woman whom he married, whose husband was named al-Yasa'. That is a precedent for Muhammad and Zaynab.\""],[20476,"Concerning His saying {And the command of God is a decree decreed}, \"Thus it is part of His established way regarding David and the woman, and the Prophet ﷺ and Zaynab.\""],[20477,"That the Messenger of God ﷺ came to the house of Zayd b. Harithah and asked permission. Zaynab gave him permission while she had no head covering, so she threw the sleeve of her chemise over her head. He asked her about Zayd, and she said, \"He went out a short while ago, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, murmuring to himself. Zaynab said: I followed him and heard him saying, \"Blessed is the Turner of hearts.\" He kept saying it until he disappeared."],[20478,"Zainab said, \"I am the one whom Allah married from the heavens.\" Aisha said, \"I am the one whom Sufwan bin al-Muattal blamed when he carried me.\" Then Zainab said to her, \"What did you say when you rode?\". She said, \"I said 'Allah is sufficient for me, and He is the best disposer of affairs.'\" Zainab said, \"You said the word of the believers.\""],[20479,"About Qatadah's saying, \"And it is not for a believing man or believing woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter, that they should [thereafter] have any choice about their affair. And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly strayed into clear error.\" He said, \"This verse was revealed regarding Zainab bint Jahsh, who was the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, and she accepted, thinking that he was proposing to her for himself. However, when she found out that he was proposing to her on behalf of Zaid bin Harithah, she refused and disputed. So Allah revealed this verse, 'And it is not for a believing man or believing woman...'.\""],[20480,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to Zaynab, who was the daughter of his paternal aunt, while he intended her for Zayd. She thought he intended her for himself, but when she learned he intended her for Zayd, she refused. Then God revealed: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman, when God and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair}. So she accepted and submitted."],[20481,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for one of his wives, meaning Zaynab. Umm Sulaym prepared some hays (a dish of dates, clarified butter, and dried curd), then placed it in a stone pot while they were at that time in severe hardship. She said, \"Take this to the Messenger of God ﷺ, convey my greetings to him, and tell him that this is a small gift from us.\" So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, Umm Sulaym sent this to you, and she sends you her greetings and says to you, 'O Messenger of God, this is a small gift from us to you.'\" He looked at it and said, \"Put it down.\" I placed it in a corner of the house. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Go and invite so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so,\" naming many men, \"and any Muslims you meet.\" So I invited those he named and any Muslims I met, and I came back while the house, the bench area, and the chamber were full. We asked Anas, \"How many were they?\" He said, \"About three hundred.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ called me to bring the pot, so I brought it. He placed his hand on it, pronounced the name of God, and supplicated. Then he said, \"Let them form circles of ten, and let each person eat from what is in front of him.\" They formed circles of ten, pronounced the name of God, ate, and left. Whenever one group finished, they departed and others came to take their place, until all of them had eaten. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Take it away.\" I do not know whether it was more when I placed it or when I lifted it. Some groups of people remained in the house of the Messenger of God ﷺ conversing, and they prolonged their talk, which weighed heavily on the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ was the most modest of people, and they were unaware that they were burdening him, for it was difficult for him to tell them. So the Messenger of God ﷺ stood up and left them. When they saw that the Messenger of God ﷺ had returned, they thought they had overstayed, so they rushed to the door and departed. Anas said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came and let down the curtain and entered. He remained for a short while, and revelation came down upon him. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came out reciting: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission}, to the end of the verses. Anas said: I am the most recent of people in connection with these verses; the Messenger of God ﷺ recited them to me."],[20482,"He informed me of the most amazing thing I saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He said, \"When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bint Jahsh, my mother said to me, 'O Anas, indeed the Prophet of Allah ﷺ has become a groom and I do not see that he has had breakfast. So come with this empty bag of dates and a container of milk, enough for a long time.' So she prepared a meal for him, and she said, 'O Anas, take this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wife.' When I brought the bag of dates with the container of milk to the Prophet ﷺ , which had the meal, he said, 'Place it in the corner of the house and go call Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, and some of his companions. Then call the people of the mosque and whoever you see on the way.' I was surprised by the little amount of food and the large number of people he commanded me to invite, so I disliked disobeying him until the house and the room were filled. He asked, 'O Anas, do you see anyone else?' I said, 'No, O Prophet of Allah.' He said, 'Bring that container.' So I brought the container, and he dipped three fingers into it, and the container began to increase and rise until they all ate from it and left, and there remained in the container almost the same amount as I brought. He said, 'Place it in front of Zaynab.' So I left and plugged the door with a mat.\" Thabit said, \"We asked, 'O Abu Hamzah, how many were the ones who ate from that container?' He said, 'I estimate it to be seventy-one or seventy-two.'\""],[20483,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ held a wedding feast for Zaynab bint Jahsh with bread and meat.\""],[20484,"I am the most knowledgeable of people about this verse. When Zaynab was given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she was with him in the house. He prepared food, then the people came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out while the people remained in their places, then return while the people were still sitting. Then Allah revealed: {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission for a meal, without waiting for its preparation. But when you are invited, enter, and when you have eaten, disperse, and do not linger for conversation. Indeed, that was troubling the Prophet, and he is shy of you, but Allah is not shy of the truth. And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a screen.} So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set up the screen, and the people got up."],[20485,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: \"The verse of the screen was revealed concerning Zaynab bint Jahsh.\""],[20486,"Anas said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became a bridegroom with Zaynab bint Jahsh. He had married her in Madinah. He invited the people to a meal after the sun had risen high. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat, and some men sat with him after the people had left, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and walked, and I walked with him until he reached the door of Aishah's room. Then he thought that they had left, so he returned, and I returned with him, and there they were, still standing. So he drew a curtain between me and him, and the verse of the screen was revealed.\""],[20488,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman and was impressed by her. He went in to Zaynab bint Jahsh and satisfied his need with her, then came out and said: \"When a woman approaches, she takes the form of a devil, and when she leaves, she leaves in the form of a devil. So whoever finds that, let him go to his wife, for that will subdue what is in himself.\""],[20489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives: \"The first of you to follow me will be the one with the longest hand among you.\" Aishah said: \"After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever we gathered, we would stretch our hands against the wall to see who was the longest. We continued doing that until Zaynab bint Jahsh b. Ri'ab died. She was a short woman, and she was not the tallest of us. Then we realized that by 'length of hand' the Prophet ﷺ meant charity. She was a skilled woman who worked with her hands and gave charity from it in the way of Allah.\""],[20490,"He prayed with Umar over Zaynab, and she was the first of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to die. He liked that he himself would lower her into her grave, so he sent to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ asking who should lower her into her grave. They said: 'Whoever used to see her in her lifetime should lower her into her grave.'"],[20491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to us saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his thumb and the finger next to it. She said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\" Abd al-Razzaq did not mention Umm Habibah in the chain from Ma'mar."],[20492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to her alarmed, saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his thumb and the finger next to it. Zaynab said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20493,"Al-Zuhri narrated to us, and we do not need anyone else in it: Urwah b. al-Zubayr informed me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah bint Umm Habibah, from her mother Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from sleep with his face red, saying: \"There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and Sufyan held up ten fingers. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\" Sufyan said: I remember in this hadith four women from al-Zuhri, and they had seen the Prophet ﷺ: two of his wives, Umm Habibah and Zaynab, and two of his stepdaughters, Zaynab bint Umm Salamah and Habibah bint Umm Habibah, whose father was Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh, who died in the land of Abyssinia."],[20494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from his sleep alarmed, saying: \"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a gap like this has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj,\" and he made a circle with his two fingers, the thumb and the one next to it. I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be destroyed while there are righteous people among us?\" He said: \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20495,"\"I used to comb the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[20496,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, all of them from Malik b. Anas, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr, from Humayd b. Nafi', from Zaynab bt. Umm Salamah, who said: I entered upon Zaynab bt. Jahsh when her brother died. She called for perfume and applied some of it, then said, \"I have no need for perfume, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for a deceased person more than three days, except for a husband, four months and ten days.'\""],[20497,"That the Prophet ﷺ was sleeping with her while Husayn was crawling in the house. She became heedless of him, and he crawled until he reached the Prophet ﷺ, climbed onto his belly, and then placed his penis on his navel. She said: The Prophet ﷺ woke up, and I got up to him and removed him from his belly. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Leave my son.\" When he finished urinating, he took a jug of water and poured it over him, then said, \"Water is poured over a boy, and a girl is washed.\" She said: He performed wudu, then stood to pray while holding him. When he bowed and prostrated, he put him down, and when he stood, he carried him. When he sat, he began supplicating and raising his hands and speaking. When he finished the prayer, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do something today that I have not seen you do before.\" He said, \"Jibril came to me and informed me that my son will be killed.\" I said, \"Then show me.\" So he brought me red soil."],[20498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke from his sleep with his face red, and he was saying, \"There is no god but Allah. Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Today a breach has been opened in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj like this,\" and he held up his hand, meaning ten. Zaynab said: I said, \"Will we perish while there are righteous people among us?\" He said, \"Yes, when wickedness becomes widespread.\""],[20499,"I entered upon Zaynab bt. Jahsh and her face was red. I said, \"What is the matter with you?\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was sleeping and struck me with a majassa he had with him.\" I said, \"What is the majassa?\" She said, \"The white palm branch.\" He said, \"By Allah, this is the time when great tribulations have descended.\" She said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we perish while there are righteous people among us?\" He said, \"Yes, then those who fear Allah will be saved.\""],[20500,"\"We had a pot of yellow dye in which I would dip the head of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[20501,"I asked the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she said: She is a woman with prolonged menstrual bleeding. He said, \"She should sit for the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ghusl, delay Zuhr and hasten Asr, perform ghusl and pray, delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and pray them together, and perform ghusl for Fajr.\""],[20502,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave women inheritance in their allotted plots of land."],[20503,"The Prophet ﷺ took a midday nap in my house when Husayn approached, and he was a boy, until he sat on the belly of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then placed his penis in his navel. She said: I got up to him, and he said, \"Bring me water.\" I brought him water, and he poured it over him, then said, \"A girl is washed, and water is poured over a boy.\""],[20504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Khuzaymah, and she is Umm al-Masakin (Mother of the Poor). She was named that because of her frequent feeding of the poor. She was from Banu Hilal b. 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, and she died while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive. She did not remain with him except a short while."],[20505,"One day I was with Zaynab, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we were making something for her with red ochre. While we were doing that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us. When he saw the red ochre, he turned back. When Zaynab saw that, she knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what she had done. She took water and washed her clothes and covered up every trace of red. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, looked in, and saw nothing, so he entered."],[20506,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zainab bint Khuzayma al-Hilaliyya, the mother of the poor. She was previously married to Huthayn or Tufayl ibn al-Harith. She died in Madinah, being his first wife to pass away."],[20507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith b. Abi Dirar from Banu al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah captive in his expedition in which he demolished Manat, the expedition of al-Muraysi'."],[20508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith b. Abi Dirar b. 'A'idh b. Malik b. al-Mustaliq of Khuza'ah captive, and the name of al-Mustaliq is Khuzaymah, on the day he fought Banu al-Mustaliq."],[20509,"Juwayriyyah bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died in the year fifty-six."],[20510,"Juwayriyah was a slave of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he freed her, made her emancipation her dower, and freed every captive from Banū al-Muṣṭaliq."],[20511,"Juwayriyah said to the Prophet ﷺ: Your wives boast over me and say, “The Messenger of God ﷺ did not marry you.” He said, “Did I not make your dower great? Did I not free forty of your people?”"],[20512,"I wrote to Nāfiʿ asking him whether the call to Islam preceded fighting. He wrote back to me that that was at the beginning of Islam, and that the Messenger of God ﷺ raided Banū al-Muṣṭaliq while they were heedless and their cattle were being watered. He killed their fighting men, took their women and children captive, and Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith fell to him. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, who was in that army on that day, narrated this hadith to me."],[20513,"The Messenger of God ﷺ chose Juwayriyah for himself."],[20514,"The Messenger of God ﷺ learned that Banū al-Muṣṭaliq were gathering forces against him, led by al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, the father of Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith, wife of the Prophet ﷺ. When the Messenger of God ﷺ heard of them, he set out against them until he met them at a watering place of theirs called al-Muraysīʿ, on the side of Qudayd toward the coast. The people pressed upon one another and fought. God defeated Banū al-Muṣṭaliq; al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, Juwayriyah's father, was killed along with others of them who were killed, and God granted His Messenger their children and women as spoils. The Messenger of God ﷺ took many captives from them and divided them among the Muslims. Among the women taken that day was Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith b. Abī Ḍirār, the leading woman of her people."],[20516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by her early in the morning while she was praying in the mosque. Then he passed by her again close to midday and asked, \"Are you still doing the same thing?\" She replied, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shall I teach you some words that are equivalent to freeing slaves? They are: Subhan Allah (Glory be to Allah) the number of His creations three times, Subhan Allah satisfaction with Himself three times, Subhan Allah the weight of His Throne three times, and Subhan Allah the ink of His words.\" Her name was Burrah, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Juwayriyah."],[20517,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by her after he had prayed the dawn prayer, or after the dawn prayer, while she was remembering God until the forenoon had risen and she was still doing so. He said, “Since I left you I have said three phrases that are greater and weightier, or more balanced, than what you have said: ‘Glory be to God as many times as the number of His creatures; glory be to God as much as pleases His Self; glory be to God as much as the weight of His Throne; glory be to God as much as the ink of His words.’”"],[20520,"Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, by God, O Messenger of God. I have no food except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20521,"From Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Is there any food?” She said, “No, by God, except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20522,"We had a freedwoman who was given something as charity. I prepared it, and he—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20523,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon her and said, “Do you have any food?” She said, “No, by God, except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20524,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me and said, “Is there any food?” I said, “No, except a bone given to our freedwoman from charity.” He said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place.”"],[20525,"He informed him that Juwayriyah bt. al-Ḥārith, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, told him that her freedwoman had been given some meat as charity, so she prepared it. When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned, he said, “Do you have any supper?” I said, “O Messenger of God, such-and-such a woman was given a portion of meat as charity, and I prepared it.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Bring it close, for it has reached its proper place,” and he ate some of it."],[20526,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of fire, or a garment of His fire.\""],[20527,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world, Allah will clothe him with a garment of fire.\""],[20528,"The Prophet ﷺ used to dislike that food be eaten until the heat of its steam had gone."],[20529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Safiyyah bt. Huyayy b. Akhtab captive from the Banu al-Nadir on the day of Khaybar, while she was a bride married to Kinanah b. Abi al-Huqayq."],[20530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Safiyyah bt. Huyayy captive from the Banu al-Nadir, and she was among what Allah granted him as spoil."],[20531,"A’ishah said “Safiyyah was called after the word safi (a special portion of the Prophet).” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2994)"],[20532,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped at Khaybar while Safiyyah was a bride in her bridal finery. She saw in a dream as if the sun descended until it fell on her chest. She related that to her husband, and he said, \"By Allah, you desire nothing but this king who has come down upon us.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered it and struck off her husband's neck in execution. Some of the young men of the Prophet ﷺ then showed interest in marrying her, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw dates for them on a leather mat and said, \"Eat the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah for Safiyyah.\""],[20533,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her, \"What is this greenness in your eyes?\" She said, \"I told my husband, 'I saw in what a sleeper sees a moon that fell into my lap,' and he slapped me and said, 'Do you want the king of Yathrib?'\" She said, \"And nothing was more hateful to me than the Messenger of Allah; he killed my father and my husband. But he kept apologizing to me and said, 'O Safiyyah, your father stirred up the Arabs and did such and such,' until that left my heart.\""],[20534,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20535,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20536,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20537,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20538,"The Prophet ﷺ freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dower."],[20539,"He informed him that the Prophet ﷺ ascertained that Safiyyah was free from pregnancy by a menstrual period."],[20540,"The Prophet ﷺ held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with saweeq and dates."],[20542,"It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah had said, “(You are) the daughter of a Jew,” so she wept. The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was crying and said, “What is the matter with you?” She said, “Hafsah said to me that I am the daughter of a Jew.” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “You are the daughter of a prophet, and your uncle is a prophet, and you are under (married to) a prophet—so in what does she boast over you?” Then he said, “Fear Allah, O Hafsah.”"],[20543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upset with Safiyyah over something. Safiyyah said to me, 'Would you like to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pleased with me? Then my day will be yours.' So I put on a veil of mine dyed with saffron and sprinkled it with water, then came and sat beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to me, 'Move away from me, for it is not your day.' I said, 'That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills,' and I told him the matter, and he became pleased with her."],[20544,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey when Safiyyah's camel became ill. Zaynab had an extra mount, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Safiyyah's camel has become ill; would you give her a camel?' She said, 'Should I give to that Jewess?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and boycotted her for the remainder of Dhu al-Hijjah, all of Muharram, Safar, and some days of Rabi', until she had packed up her belongings and her bed, thinking that he had no need of her. Then one day as she was sitting at midday, she saw his shadow approaching, and she put her bed and belongings back."],[20545,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in i'tikaf in the mosque. I came to him at night and talked with him, then I stood up to leave, and he stood up with me to escort me back. Her residence was in the house of Usamah b. Zayd. Two men of the Ansar passed by, and when they saw the Prophet ﷺ they hastened. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Slow down! It is Safiyyah bint Huyay.' They said, 'Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Satan runs through the son of Adam like blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts'—or he said, 'evil.'"],[20546,"Safiyyah bint Huyay, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me: I came to the Prophet ﷺ to talk with him while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque. He stood up with me one night to escort me to my house. Two men of the Ansar met him, and when they saw him they felt shy and turned back. He said, 'Come here; it is only Safiyyah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ.' They said, 'Allah forbid! Glory be to Allah.' He said, 'I am not telling you that you should think evil, but I know that Satan runs through a person like blood.'"],[20547,"Safiyyah bint Huyay, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that she came to visit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in i'tikaf in the mosque during the last ten days of Ramadan. She spoke with him for a while, then she stood up to leave, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up with her to escort her. When she reached near the door of the mosque, by the door of Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, two men of the Ansar passed by. They greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then went on. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, 'Slow down! She is Safiyyah bint Huyay.' They said, 'Glory be to Allah, O Messenger of Allah,' and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said weighed heavily on them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Satan reaches through a person to the extent of the blood, and I feared that he might cast something into your hearts.'"],[20550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed me and made my emancipation my dower."],[20551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to me while I had four thousand date pits in front of me, with which I was glorifying Allah. He said, 'O daughter of Huyay, what is this?' I said, 'I am glorifying Allah with them.' He said, 'I have glorified Allah since I stood at your head with more than this.' I said, 'Teach me, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Say: Glory be to Allah as many times as the number of things He has created.'"],[20552,"Ali, the messenger of Allah, entered while I was crying, so he said, \"What is making you cry, O daughter of Huwayy?\" I said, \"It has reached me that Aisha and Hafsah are preferred over me and they say, 'We are better than her, we are the daughters of the cousin of the Messenger of Allah, and his wives.'\" He said, \"Did you not say, 'How can they be better than me when my father is Harun, my uncle is Musa, and my husband is Muhammad?\""],[20553,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'An army will surely attack this House, and when they are in a desert plain, the earth will swallow the middle of them. Then the first of them will call out to the last of them, and all of them will be swallowed up. None of them will escape except the fugitive who reports about them.'"],[20554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'People will not cease attacking this House until an army comes to attack it. When they are in a desert plain, the first of them and the last of them will be swallowed up, and the middle of them will not escape.' It was said, 'What if there are among them those who are unwilling?' He said, 'Allah will resurrect them according to their intentions.'"],[20555,"We went out for Hajj and passed by Madinah. We entered upon Safiyyah bint Huyay and asked her about beverages. She said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade nabidh made in earthen jars.' Thus ends the hadith of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, ؓ ."],[20556,"Asma' bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq died in the year seventy-three, a few nights after her son 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr. She was a sister of 'A'ishah through her father. The mother of Asma' bint Abi Bakr was Qutaylah bint 'Abd al-'Uzza b. 'Abd As'ad, of the Banu Malik b. Hasal. On the day she died, Asma' was one hundred years old. She was born twenty-seven years before the calendar, and seventeen years before the sending of the Prophet ﷺ. Asma' was born to Abu Bakr when he was twenty-one years old."],[20557,"that he should descend.\""],[20584,"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to wear saffron-dyed gowns while in ihram."],[20587,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was praying toward the corner, after he was commanded to proclaim openly what he was commanded, and he was reciting: \"{So which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?}\" while the polytheists were listening."],[20588,"\"We slaughtered a horse and ate it, we and the family of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[20595,"We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr was with us. When we were at al-'Arj, we dismounted, with 'A'isha beside him and I beside my father. Abu Bakr sat waiting for his servant. Our mount and the mount of the Messenger of God ﷺ were one. The servant appeared without his camel. Abu Bakr said to him: \"Where is your camel?\" He said: \"I lost it last night.\" She said: \"One camel, and you lose it?\" He began to beat him while the Messenger of God ﷺ smiled and said: \"Look at this offender and what he is doing.\""],[20596,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit and said: \"O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of God. They do not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life. So when you see that, hasten to prayer, charity, and remembrance of God. I have seen among you fifty thousand or seventy thousand—Fulayh was uncertain—entering Paradise without reckoning, like the image of the moon on the night of the full moon.\" A man stood and said: \"Supplicate God to make me one of them.\" He said: \"O God, make him one of them. O people, you will not ask me about anything that has been revealed except that I will inform you of it.\" A man stood and said: \"Who is my father?\" He said: \"Your father is so-and-so,\" referring to the father to whom he was attributed."],[20597,"I heard Asma' bt. Abi Bakr say: \"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was weighing something and counting.\" He said: \"O Asma', do not count, lest God count against you.\" Asma' said: \"After that day, I never counted or numbered anything that God created.\""],[20609,"Asma bint Abi Bakr said: \"O Messenger of God, I have no wealth except what al-Zubayr brings into his house. May I give small amounts from it?\" He said: \"Give small amounts as much as you are able, and do not withhold, lest God withhold from you.\""],[20610,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , saying, \"I do not possess anything except something which Zubair gives me.\" He said, \"Be humble and do not exaggerate, for it will be shown to you.\""],[20611,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I have no wealth from which to give small amounts except what al-Zubayr brings into my house.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O Asma, give small amounts, and do not withhold, lest it be withheld from you.\""],[20614,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “A woman entered the Fire on account of her cat.”"],[20625,"She said on the night of Jamʿ: O my son, has the moon set? She was praying, and had alighted near Muzdalifah. I said: No. She prayed a little, then said: O my son, has the moon set? He said: The moon had set. I said: Yes. She said: Then depart. So we departed and went on with her until she threw the pebble at the Jamrah, then she returned and prayed the morning prayer at her lodging. I said to her: O you, you have gone very early in the dark. She said: “O my son, the Prophet of God ﷺ gave permission for the women’s litters.”"],[20629,"He said to her: O mother, the Commander of the Faithful has commended you to me. Do you have any need? She said: I have no need of you, and I am not your mother; rather, I am the mother of the crucified one. Wait, let me tell you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “In Thaqif there will emerge a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already seen him – she meant al-Mukhtar – and as for the destroyer, it is you. Al-Hajjaj said: a destroyer of the hypocrites."],[20630,"Peace be upon you, O Abu Khubayb – he said it three times. I had forbidden you from this – he said it three times. You used to fast constantly and stand in prayer constantly, and maintain ties of kinship. This reached al-Hajjaj: the standing of Abd Allah b. Umar, so he had him brought down and threw him into the graves of the Jews. Then he sent to Asma bint Abi Bakr that she should come to him, and her sight had gone. She refused. So he sent to her: Either you come, or I will send someone to drag you by your forelocks. She said: By God, I will not come to you until you send someone to drag me by my forelocks. His messenger came back to him and told him. He said: O boy, hand me my sandals. He handed him his shoes, and he got up walking with a swagger until he came to her. He said: How do you see what God has done to the enemy of God? She said: I see that you ruined his worldly life for him, and he ruined your hereafter for you. As for what you used to taunt her about, the one with the two belts – indeed, I had two belts: one with which I covered the food of the Messenger of God ﷺ from ants, and one that women cannot do without. And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Among Thaqif there is a destroyer and a liar.” As for the liar, we have come to know him; and as for the destroyer, you are the one. He said: Then he left."],[20632,"When al-Hajjaj entered upon her, it was said to her: This is the commander al-Hajjaj. She said: Indeed, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have already seen him; and as for the destroyer, it is you."],[20633,"We entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and asked her about mut‘a. She said: “We practiced it during the lifetime of the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[20637,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When a person enters his grave, his righteous deeds surround him – prayer and fasting. The angel comes to him from the direction of prayer and turns him back, and from the direction of fasting and turns him back. Then he calls to him: Sit up. So he sits up. He says to him: What do you say about this man? He said: Which man? He said: Muhammad. He said: By God, I do not know; I heard people saying something and I said it. The angel says: Upon that you lived, and upon that you died, and upon that you will be resurrected. He said: And a beast is prepared for him in his grave, black and dark, with a whip whose lash is a live coal. It strikes him as long as God wills; no one hears his voice except that he would pity him."],[20638,"When Ibn al-Zubayr was killed, she had something that the Prophet ﷺ had given her in a miscarriage. She lost it, so she ordered that it be searched for. When she found it, she fell down in prostration."],[20707,"She heard a woman ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"I have a co-wife, and I pretend from my husband what I do not actually receive, to anger her by that. Is there any sin on me in that?\" He said, \"The one who pretends to have been given what he was not given is like the one who wears two garments of falsehood.\""],[20716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The believing sisters are Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ; Umm al-Fadl, the wife of al-Abbas; Asma' bt. Umays, the wife of Ja'far; and the wife of Hamzah—she is their sister through their mother.\""],[20717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she had some spurge that she was crushing. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What are you doing with this?\" She said, \"O Prophet of Allah, I will give it to so-and-so to drink.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is a disease.\" Then he entered upon her while she had some senna with her. He said, \"What are you doing with this?\" She said, \"So-and-so will drink it.\" He said, \"If anything could ward off death, senna would ward it off.\""],[20724,"\"She gave birth at Dhul-Hulayfah, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to perform ghusl and enter ihram.\""],[20727,"I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"You are not like that.\""],[20730,"She gave birth to Muhammad b. Abi Bakr at Dhu al-Hulayfah. Abu Bakr asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he instructed him to tell her to perform ghusl and enter ihram."],[20731,"Al-Qa'nabi reported that 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who narrated from Mujahid, who narrated from Asma bint 'Umais, that she came to the Prophet ﷺ with the two sons of Ja'far. She said, \"The people have killed the sons of your brother.\" He said, \"Cover them for them.\""],[20732,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at her sons, the sons of Ja'far, and said, \"Why are their bodies so thin?\" She said, \"The evil eye afflicts them quickly; should I perform ruqyah for them?\" He said, \"With what?\" She presented words that had no harm, and he said, \"Perform ruqyah for them.\""],[20747,"When revelation came down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would almost fall unconscious. One day it came down upon him while he was in 'Ali's lap, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Did you pray 'Asr, O 'Ali?\" He said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah.\" He called upon Allah, and He returned the sun for him until he prayed 'Asr. She said, \"I saw the sun rise after it had set, when it was returned, until he prayed 'Asr.\""],[20748,"'Ali proposed to me, and that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he said, \"She should not harm Allah and His Messenger.\""],[20749,"'Umar said to Asma' bt. 'Umays, \"We preceded you in the Hijrah.\" She replied, \"Yes, by Allah, you did precede us, and we were among the barefoot and naked, while you were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—he taught your ignorant and instructed your learned, and commanded you to noble character.\""],[20750,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, some people claim that we are not among the female emigrants.\" He said, \"Whoever says that has lied. You have two emigrations: you emigrated to the Negus and you emigrated to me.\""],[20751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Among the misfortune of a person in this world are three: a bad house, a bad wife, and a bad mount.\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is a bad house?\" He said, \"Its courtyard being narrow and its neighbors being wicked.\" It was said, \"What is a bad mount?\" He said, \"Its refusing to be ridden and its poor condition.\" It was said, \"What is a bad wife?\" He said, \"Her womb being barren and her character being bad.\""],[20754,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her, \"What do you use as a laxative?\" She said, \"I used to use shubrum.\" He said, \"Hot, hot.\" She said, \"Then I used senna as a laxative.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If there were in anything a cure for death, it would be senna.\""],[20755,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Half of what is dug for my ummah of graves is from the evil eye.\""],[20756,"Asma bint 'Umays was a friend of Aisha, whom she prepared and presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a wife along with me. We found nothing to drink except a small quantity of milk. The Prophet ﷺ drank from it and then handed it to the girl. She felt shy, so I said, \"Do not reject the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" The girl drank from it and then he said, \"Give it to your companions.\" We replied, \"We do not desire it.\" He said, \"Do not gather falsehood and hunger.\" I said, \"If any of us says that she desires something, is it considered falsehood?\" He said, \"Verily, falsehood is written as falsehood, even if it is a joke.\""],[20757,"\"What an evil servant is the one who fancies himself and becomes vain forgetting the Most Great, the Most High. What an evil servant is the one who forces and behaves hostility, forgetting the Compeller, the Most High. What an evil servant is the one who is heedless and diverted, forgetting about the graves and the trials. What an evil servant is the one who is violent and tyrannical, forgetting his beginnings or his end. What an evil servant is the one who seeks the world through the religion. What an evil servant is the one who seeks the religion through his desires. What an evil servant is the one who puts all hope in his own zeal. What an evil servant is the worshipper who is misled by his desire. What an evil servant is the one whose aspirations humiliate him.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2448)"],[20758,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her for some of his needs, then he left. So, she complained to him about her need. He said, \"How would it be for you if you were tested with a slave who has been granted control over the rivers of the earth and its fruits, and whoever follows him, he feeds him and clothes him, and whoever disobeys him, he withholds from him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the slave girl is confined to the oven for an hour to bake bread, and I am almost tempted during my prayer, so what about us in that case?\" He said, \"Allah will protect the believers on that day with what He protects the angels from glorification. Indeed, there will be between his eyes a mark that each believer, whether literate or illiterate, will read.\""],[20765,"I went with my brother to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was wearing two bracelets of gold. He said: \"Would it please you for Allah to adorn you with two bracelets of fire?\" So I removed them and threw them away, and I do not know which of the people took them."],[20767,"The Prophet ﷺ recited this verse: \"Say: O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\""],[20768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: \"Before his emergence there will be three years when the sky withholds a third of its rain and the earth a third of its vegetation.\" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[20771,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he saw a woman wearing two bracelets of gold. He said: \"Would it please you for Allah to adorn you with two bracelets of fire?\" She took them off her hand and threw them away, and I do not know who took them."],[20798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever defends the flesh of his brother in his absence, it is incumbent upon Allah to protect him from the Fire.”"],[20799,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Whoever defends the honor of his brother in his absence, it is incumbent upon Allah, Exalted is He, to free him from the Fire.”"],[20800,"\"The Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , passed away on the day his shield was held as collateral by a Jewish man for a measure of barley.\""],[20801,"I heard Asmā’ bt. Yazīd say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque one day while a group of women were sitting. He gestured with his right hand in greeting, smiled at them, and said: “Beware of ingratitude toward those who bestow favors.” A woman said: “I seek refuge in Allah, O Messenger of Allah, from ingratitude for Allah’s favors.” He said: “Indeed, one of you remains long without a husband, then Allah provides her a husband, and she gains a child and delight of the eye. Then she becomes angry one time and swears by Allah: ‘I have never seen any good from him ever.’ That is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors; that is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors; that is part of ingratitude for Allah’s favors.”"],[20803,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: “Woe to your mother, Quraysh, for your familiarity with the winter and summer journey.”"],[20804,"Indeed I was holding the rein of al-‘Aḍbā’, the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when al-Mā’idah descended upon him, and it nearly broke the camel’s neck from its weight."],[20805,"Al-An‘ām descended upon the Prophet ﷺ all at once, while I was holding the rein of the Prophet’s she-camel ﷺ; indeed, from its weight it nearly broke the camel’s bone."],[20807,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was wearing rings of gold and a bracelet of gold. He said: “Would it please you that Allah seal you with a ring of Fire and bracelet you with a bracelet of Fire?” So I abandoned them. And he said: “Is one of you unable to make a ring of silver and smear upon it some saffron, ambergris, and wars?”"],[20808,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ one day when a drink was brought. He drank, then gave it to the people and they drank. The vessel passed by a man among the people, and he said: “I am fasting.” Some of the people said: “He does not break his fast; he fasts every day.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He has neither fasted nor broken his fast—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20809,"A drink was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was passed around among the people, among them a man who was fasting. It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, he fasts the whole time.” He said: “He has not fasted—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20810,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He has not fasted—the one who fasts perpetually.”"],[20811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used not to shake hands with women."],[20812,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, I and a daughter of my paternal aunt, to pledge allegiance to him, and he said: “I do not shake hands with women.”"],[20813,"She was among the women from whom the Messenger of God ﷺ took the pledge, and with her was her maternal aunt, who wore gold rings and two gold bracelets. He kept turning his gaze away from her until, when he had finished, he said: “What is this? Would it please you for God to adorn you with ornaments of fire?” She said: I seek refuge in God from the Fire. So she removed her rings and threw them down before her, and she struggled with her bracelets but could not remove them, so she went to him and snapped them off, then threw them somewhere—we do not know what he did with them. She said: I said, “O Messenger of God, we women must adorn ourselves for our husbands; will you permit us two gold earrings?” He refused, saying: “It is enough for one of you to take two silver earrings, then take two threads dyed with saffron and rub them between her fingers until they turn yellow, and it will look like gold.”"],[20814,"O Messenger of God, what is this good deed that we have been forbidden to disobey you in? He said: “That you do not wail.” I said: “O Messenger of God, the Banu so-and-so helped me mourn my paternal cousin so-and-so, and I must repay them.” He refused me, but I repeated it to him several times, and he permitted me to repay them. After repaying them, I never wailed again, nor did I wail otherwise, up to this very hour. No woman remained but she has wailed, except me."],[20815,"She pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ on the day he took the pledge from the women. She leaned forward and stretched out her hand to pledge allegiance, but he withdrew his hand and said: “I do not shake hands with women; I only take their pledge verbally.” She said: I was wearing a garment and jewelry. He said: “O Asma!” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of God, and may you be granted happiness.” He said: “Would it please you to be branded with this jewelry?” I said: “And what is that, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Whoever wears gold, or adorns any of his children with something like a small earring or a locust leg, will be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20816,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while his armor, which he used to fight in, was pawned with a Jewish man for a measure of barley, which he had taken as food for his family."],[20817,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the ʿaqīqah: “For a boy, two sheep; for a girl, one sheep.”"],[20818,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not kill your children secretly. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the practice of coitus interruptus will catch up with a rider on his horse until it throws him down.”"],[20819,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Do not kill your children secretly, for the one who carries out coitus interruptus will catch up with a rider and hurl him from the back of his horse.”"],[20820,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was sitting with some friends, and he said, \"Beware of the curse of the one who is grateful.\" I was the boldest among them to ask him, so I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the curse of the one who is grateful?\" He replied, \"Perhaps one of you will have a long life with her parents, then Allah will bless her with a husband and children. Then she gets angry and disbelieves, saying, 'By Allah, I have never seen any good from you.'\""],[20821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever leaves behind two dinars leaves behind two cauterizing brands.”"],[20822,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was invited to the funeral of a man from the Ansar. When the bier was placed down, the Prophet of God ﷺ stepped forward to pray over him, then turned and said: “Does your companion owe a debt?” They said: “Yes, O Messenger of God, two dinars.” He said: “Pray over your companion.” Abu Qatadah said: “We will pay it on his behalf, O Prophet of God.” So he prayed over him."],[20823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Let your tears cease and your grief depart, for your son is the first one at whom God laughed and for whom the Throne shook.”"],[20824,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever builds a mosque for God, God will build for him a house in Paradise.”"],[20825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Any woman who adorns herself with a necklace of gold will have the like of it placed around her neck from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20826,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women to give him allegiance. He stipulated upon us what is in the Qur’an: “that you do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill your children, and do not bring slander that you fabricate.” Then he said to us: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not shake hands with us? He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women.”"],[20827,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik (ḥ). And Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us (ḥ). And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us. They both said: Mālik b. Anas narrated to us from Muḥammad b. al-Munkadir from Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group of women to give him allegiance. We said: We give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not kill our children, will not bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves. Come, let us give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman, or the like of my word to one woman.”"],[20828,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ regarding women, and he said, \"Take the pledge not to associate anything with Allah, not to steal, and not to commit adultery.\" Then he said, \"To the best of your ability and within your means.\" We said, \"May Allah and His Messenger be kinder to us than ourselves.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us your pledge.\" He said, \"I do not shake hands with women. My statement to a hundred women is the same as my statement to one woman.\""],[20829,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women. He said: “You give allegiance that you will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, and will not commit adultery” — the verse. Then he was silent, then said: “In what you are able and can bear.” They said: Allah and His Messenger know better and are more merciful to us than ourselves. We said: O Messenger of Allah, accept our allegiance. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman.”"],[20830,"He heard Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah say that she gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women. Then he said: “In what you are able.”"],[20831,"She gave allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, and he stipulated upon her what he stipulated upon the believing women in the Book of Allah. Then he said: “In what you are able, O daughter of Ruqayqah.”"],[20832,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ among a group of women. We said: We give you allegiance, O Messenger of Allah, that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is good. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In what you are able and can bear.” We said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us. So accept our allegiance, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred is like my word to one.”"],[20833,"Ḥukaymah bt. Umaymah bt. Ruqayqah narrated to me from her mother, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to urinate in a wooden vessel, then place it under his bed. He urinated in it, then came and wanted it, and found that the vessel had nothing in it. He said to a woman called Barakah, who served Umm Ḥabībah and had been brought by her from the land of Abyssinia: “Where is the urine that was in the vessel?” She said: I drank it. He said: “You have shielded yourself from the Fire with a barrier.”"],[20834,"\"The wives of the Prophet ﷺ used to create a mixture of musk and saffron, and they would apply it to the lower parts of their hairline before becoming forbidden. Afterwards, they would continue to be forbidden in the same way.\""],[20835,"From Umaymah, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: I was pouring water for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his ablution when a man entered and said: Counsel me. He said: “Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut into pieces or burned with fire. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to abandon your family and your worldly possessions, then abandon them. Do not drink wine, for it is the root of every evil. Do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever does that has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger removed from him. Do not flee on the day of battle, for whoever does that returns with wrath from Allah, and his abode is Hell — an evil destination. Do not increase the boundaries of your land, for whoever does that will carry it on his neck on the Day of Resurrection from the extent of seven earths. Spend on your family from your means, and do not lift your staff from them, and make them fear Allah.”"],[20836,"I heard my aunt, who had performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilāl or Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call.” One would ascend and the other would descend. We would cling to him, as you are, until we took the pre-dawn meal."],[20837,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Ibn Umm Maktūm or Bilāl gives the call to prayer at night, so eat and drink until Bilāl or Ibn Umm Maktūm gives the call.” It was only that one of them would give the call, and the other would then ascend. We would take him by the hand and say: as you are, until we took the pre-dawn meal."],[20838,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my son ʿAbdullāh b. Salamah — and he had been a participant in Badr — was killed on the day of Uḥud. I would like to move him so that I can find comfort in his nearness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted her. She placed him alongside al-Mijdhar b. Ziyād on a camel of hers, in a cloak. She passed by the two of them, and people were amazed at them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at them and said: “Their deeds made them equal.” ʿAbdullāh was a large, heavy man, while al-Mijdhar was lean of flesh. He is the one who says [the poem]."],[20839,"\"Busrah bint Safwan asked the Prophet ﷺ about a woman who hits with her hand and it causes her private part to bleed. He said, 'Perform ablution, O Busrah.'\""],[20840,"He and Marwan discussed ablution due to touching the private part. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan narrated to me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding ablution due to touching the private part. It was as if Urwah did not accept his narration as marfu'. So Marwan sent a guard to her, and he returned and informed them that she had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding ablution due to touching the private part."],[20841,"He heard Marwan saying: Busrah bint Safwan informed me; she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his private part should perform ablution.'"],[20842,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'A man should perform ablution due to touching the penis.'"],[20843,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20844,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Whoever touches his private part should perform ablution.'"],[20845,"He said: Ablution is required due to touching the penis. Urwah denied that, so Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me of it. So he sent to Busrah, and she said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned what ablution is required from, and he mentioned touching the penis.'"],[20846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he should perform ablution.'"],[20847,"That ablution is required due to touching the penis when a man reaches it with his hand. I denied that and said: No ablution is required from touching it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning what ablution is required from, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ablution is required from touching the penis.' Urwah said: 'I kept arguing with Marwan about that until he called a man from his guard and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan, and he asked her about what she had narrated to him regarding that. Busrah sent back the same as what Marwan had narrated to me from her.'"],[20848,"That ablution is required due to touching the penis when a man reaches it with his hand. I denied that and said: No ablution is required for the one who touches it. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioning what ablution is required from, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And ablution is required from touching the penis.' Urwah said: 'I kept disputing with Marwan until he called a man from his guard and sent him to Busrah to ask her about what she had narrated regarding that. Busrah sent to him the same as what he had narrated to me from her.'"],[20849,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20850,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20851,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik; and Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Malik informed us; and Bakr b. Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr b. Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hazm that he heard Urwah b. al-Zubayr saying: I entered upon Marwan b. al-Hakam, and he mentioned what ablution is required from. Marwan said: Busrah bint Safwan informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis should perform ablution.'"],[20852,"That the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20853,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'A man performs wudu from touching the penis.'"],[20854,"It was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what requires wudu, and he said: 'And whoever touches the penis must perform wudu.'"],[20855,"Marwan discussed with me the touching of the penis, and I said: 'No wudu is required for it.' He said: 'Busrah bt. Safwan narrates something about it.' So he sent a messenger to her, and he mentioned that she narrated to him that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his private part must perform wudu.'"],[20856,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20857,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.'"],[20858,"I heard Urwah say: Marwan sent for Busrah and asked her about this hadith, and she narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he must perform wudu.'"],[20859,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever touches his private part must not pray until he performs wudu.'"],[20860,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"If one of you feels something he should perform ablution.\""],[20861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his private part, he must perform wudu.' He said: 'I objected to him, so he sent for her, and she narrated it to him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was present.'"],[20862,"About touching the penis, and he saw no harm in it. Then Marwan sent one of his guards to Busrah bt. Safwan, and he said: 'She narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"When a man touches his private part with his hand, he must not pray until he performs wudu.\" ' So he returned and said: 'She said yes.' After that, my father used to say: 'Whoever touches his groin or his testicles must perform wudu.'"],[20863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When one of you touches his penis, he must perform wudu.'"],[20864,"Whoever touches his private part must perform wudu. Urwah objected to that, so he said: 'O policeman, go to Busrah bt. Safwan and ask her, for she said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever touches his penis must perform wudu.\" '"],[20865,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, or his testicles, or his groin, let him perform ablution.”"],[20866,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever touches his penis, or his testicles, or his groin, let him perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[20867,"…about touching the penis, and I did not see any obligation on him to repeat the ablution. So Marwan summoned one of his guards and sent him to Busrah bint Safwan. He asked her about that, and she informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, let him repeat the ablution.”"],[20868,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis or his testicles, let him perform ablution.”"],[20869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution as he does for prayer.”"],[20870,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, ablution becomes obligatory upon him.”"],[20871,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his groin, or his testicles, or his penis, let him not pray until he performs ablution.”"],[20872,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution.” Urwah said: Then I asked Busrah, and she confirmed it."],[20873,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “If one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution.”"],[20874,"Hisham heard the hadith of his father about touching the penis. Yahya said: Then I asked Hisham, and he said: My father informed me."],[20875,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “If one of you touches his penis, let him perform ablution.”"],[20876,"From Busrah bint Safwan al-Kinaniyyah—and she was Marwan’s maternal aunt—she said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of God, is ablution required for any of us if she touches her private part? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever touches his private part, whether among men or women, ablution is required upon him.”"],[20877,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O these people, when you hear of an army being swallowed up nearby, then the Hour has drawn near.\""],[20878,"And I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, \"O people, when you hear of a sinking here nearby, then the Hour has drawn near.\""],[20879,"I heard Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr say: Buthayna bt. al-Dahhak, the sister of Thabit, and she is the one whom Muhammad b. Maslama proposed to."],[20880,"In three of the sunnah, meat was given as charity to Ali, so I gifted it to Aisha, and she kept it until the Messenger of God ﷺ entered. He said, \"What is this meat?\" She said, \"Meat that was given as charity to Barirah, and she gifted it to us.\" He said, \"For Barirah it is charity, and for us it is a gift.\" She said, \"And I had a contract of emancipation for nine uqiyyahs.\" Aisha said, \"If they wish, I will count them a single count.\" I said, \"They say: unless they stipulate the wala' for themselves.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Stipulate and stipulate, for the wala' belongs to the one who manumits.\" She said, \"And I was manumitted, and I had the choice.\""],[20881,"that I should take charge of this affair. She used to say, \"O Abdul-Malik, I see in you qualities that make you worthy to take charge of this community. If you are appointed to it, beware of bloodshed, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'A man will be turned away from the gate of Paradise, even though he is able to look at it, because of a cupping-glassful of blood that he sheds from a Muslim without right.'\""],[20882,"The Prophet ﷺ had a wooden bowl in which he would urinate and would place it under his bed. He got up and looked for it but could not find it, so he asked, \"Where is the bowl?\" They said, \"Barrah, the servant of Umm Salamah, who came with her from the land of Abyssinia, drank it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"She has protected herself from the Fire with a barrier.\""],[20883,"She said: My father asked permission of the Prophet ﷺ to enter between him and his shirt, and he permitted him. So he entered between him and his shirt from behind him, and he began to embrace him and wipe his chest against the Prophet's ﷺ back. He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"Water.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"Salt.\" He said, \"O Messenger of God, what is it that it is not lawful to withhold?\" He said, \"If you do good, it is better for you.\" And his statement ended with water and salt. She said: That man would not withhold any amount of water, even if it was little."],[20884,"I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ while I was in an upper room of mine between Safa and Marwah, and he was saying, \"God has prescribed the sa'y for you, so perform the sa'y.\""],[20885,"From his grandmother, the mother of his father, Tuwaylah bt. Aslam, who was among the women who gave allegiance. She said: We were at our place of prayer among the Banu Harithah when Abbad b. Bishr b. Qayzi said: The Messenger of God ﷺ has turned to face the Sacred House, or the Kaaba. So the men moved to the place of the women, and the women to the place of the men, and they prayed the remaining two prostrations toward the Kaaba."],[20886,"I heard Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam b. Abi Ziyad say: Salih, the freed slave of al-Taw'amah, and she is the daughter of Umayyah b. Khalaf."],[20887,"The name of Bashir was Zahm, and the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Bashir."],[20888,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ go out to prayer shaking his head and beard from the traces of henna."],[20889,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik; ḥ (turning to another chain) and Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us; ḥ (turning to another chain) and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us; they both said: Mālik reported to us, from Abū al-Aswad Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Nawfal, from ʿUrwah b. al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, from Judāmah bt. Wahb al-Asadiyyah, who said: She informed me that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I had intended to forbid al-ghīlah (sexual intercourse with a nursing mother) until I recalled that the Persians and Romans do that and it does not harm their children.\""],[20890,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among some people while he was saying: \"I had intended to forbid al-ghīlah (sexual intercourse with a nursing mother), but I looked into the Persians and Romans, and found that they have intercourse with their nursing mothers, yet it does not harm their children at all.\" Then they asked him about ʿazl (coitus interruptus), and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"That is the hidden waʾd (burying alive), and it is: 'When the buried girl is asked' (Qur'an 81:8).\""],[20891,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I wanted to forbid al-ghiyāl (sexual intercourse with nursing mothers), but I found that the Persians and Romans have intercourse with their nursing mothers, and it does not harm them at all.\""],[20892,"My father took me to the Prophet ﷺ after I had responded to my father's camels. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for the blessing of my daughter.\" The Prophet ﷺ sat me in his room, placed his hand on my head, and prayed for me with blessings."],[20893,"I was with Umm Salamah, the Mother of the Believers, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"O my mother, have I conveyed to you?\" She said: A young son of hers said, \"O mother, why is he calling his mother?\" She said: I said, \"O my son, he means his community (ummah),\" and he was saying: \"Verily, your honors, your wealth, and your blood are inviolable to you, like the inviolability of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours.\""],[20894,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Give charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire.\" So Zaynab came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband is in need; is it permissible for me to give back to him?\" He said: \"Yes, you will have two rewards.\""],[20895,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The best generation is my generation.\""],[20896,"Jamīlah bt. Ubayy b. Salūl came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not find fault with Thābit b. Qays in character or religion, but I cannot stand him out of dislike, and I hate to commit disbelief within Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you return to him his garden?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to take from her what he had given her as dowry, and not to increase."],[20897,"Jamīlah bt. Ubayy b. Salūl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not find fault with Thābit in character or religion, but I hate disbelief within Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you return to him his garden?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So she returned it to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ separated them. [Note:] Jamīlah bt. Thābit b. Abī al-Aflaḥ al-Anṣārī, the wife of ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb."],[20899,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed the name of ʿĀṣiyah and said: \"You are Jamīlah.\""],[20900,"Ḥalīmah bt. Abī Dhuʾayb al-Saʿdiyyah of Saʿd b. Bakr b. Hawāzin—and she is the mother of the Prophet ﷺ who suckled him and weaned him—narrated to me; she narrated, saying: A barren, drought-stricken year befell us and left us with nothing, so we went out among a group of women from Banū Saʿd b. Bakr to Makkah seeking suckling infants. When we arrived in Makkah, there was not a woman among us but the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was offered to her, and she would refuse him and dislike him. That was because he had no father, and the wet-nurses only hoped for good from the fathers. A woman would say, \"What shall I do with this one? What can his mother do for me?\" So they disliked him. She said: He was offered to me, and I refused him. No woman of my people remained but found a suckling infant. When they were about to depart for their lands, I feared returning without a suckling baby, so I said to my husband, \"Perhaps I should take that orphan boy; it would be better than returning without a suckling infant.\" So I went to his mother and took him, and brought him to my dwelling. I had a son whom I was nursing, and he would stay awake much of the night from hunger, unable to sleep. When I put the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to my breasts, they turned to him with whatever milk he wished, until he drank his fill, and his brother drank his fill, and slept. My husband got up in the middle of the night to an old she-camel of ours, by Allah, to see if it would yield a drop of milk. She said: His hand fell upon her udder and found it full of milk, ready to be milked. So he came to me and said, \"O daughter of Wahb, by Allah, I think this soul is blessed.\" Then he told me the news of the old she-camel, and I told him the news of what I had seen from my breasts that night. We went out riding a she-donkey of ours that had previously been too weak to catch up with the other donkeys. When we were upon it heading toward our lands, it would go ahead of the people until they would shout at me, \"Woe to you, O daughter of Abū Dhuʾayb! You have left us behind. This she-donkey of yours has something special about it.\" She said: We arrived with him in the lands of Banū Saʿd b. Bakr, and we knew nothing but blessing. Indeed, our shepherd would go out with our sheep and graze them, and our people would send out their sheep. When it was near night, they returned, and our sheep would come back full of milk, while not a single sheep among theirs yielded a drop. They would say to their shepherds, \"Woe to you! Graze where the shepherd of the daughter of Abū Dhuʾayb grazes.\" She said: It remained like that with us. Then one day he was behind our houses among some young lambs of ours, playing with his brother, when his brother came running and said, \"That Qurayshī brother of mine has been killed!\" So we hurried to him, his father and I, and met him with a pale face. We began to embrace him, sometimes I and sometimes his father, saying to him, \"What is the matter with you, O my son?\" He would say, \"I do not know. Two men came to me, threw me down, split open my belly, and began stirring it.\" His father turned to me and said, \"I think this boy has been afflicted. Take him to his family quickly before the matter gets worse for us.\" She said: I had no goal until I brought him to Makkah to his mother, and I said to her, \"O foster mother, I have weaned my son and he has recovered from the ailment, so keep him.\" She said, \"What is the matter with you, are you abandoning him? You used to ask me to leave him with you—it is as if you fear Satan for him.\" First, let me tell you about myself and about him: When I gave birth to him, I saw that a light came out of me that illuminated the palaces of Buṣrā in the land of Syria."],[20901,"I heard Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Numayr say: \"Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasanah—Ḥasanah was his mother, and she was among those who emigrated to Abyssinia.\""],[20902,"From Ḥiqqah bt. ʿAmr—and she had prayed facing the two qiblahs with the Prophet ﷺ—that when she intended to enter iḥrām, she would place her cloak in her lap, wear whatever of her clothes she wished, including the dyed yellow garment, and then pronounce the talbiyah."],[20903,"Ibn Ishaq said: \"Hamnah bint Jahsh was among the women of Banu Asad who emigrated, from the women he mentioned.\""],[20904,"\"I saw with my own eyes Hamnah bint Jahsh on the day of Uhud giving water to the thirsty and treating the wounded.\""],[20905,"\"I suffered from prolonged menstrual bleeding (istihada) for seven years, and I complained about that to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'That is not menstruation, but rather it is a vein, so perform ghusl.' So she would perform ghusl at the time of every prayer, and she would perform ghusl in a large basin, and one could see the yellowish tinge of blood in the basin.\""],[20906,"\"I used to have a long, heavy menstrual period, so I went to the Prophet ﷺ to seek his advice and inform him about it. I found him in my sister Zainab's house, so I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a need.' He said, 'What is it? May Allah facilitate it for you.' I said, 'I have a long, heavy menstrual period that prevents me from praying and fasting. What should I do?' He said, 'Use a piece of cloth called a qursuf, as it takes away the blood.' I said, 'It is more than that.' He said, 'Then use a tampon.' I said, 'It is more than that.' He said, 'Then wear a cloth.' She said, 'It is more than that, O Messenger of Allah. It only stops during the hajj ministration.' He said, 'I will tell you two options; whichever one you choose and do, you will be exempted from the other. If you can handle both of them, then you know your situation best.' He said, 'This is a rukhsah (dispensation) from among the dispensations of Satan.' He said, 'You will menstruate for six or seven days, according to the knowledge of Allah, then take a bath. When you see that you have become pure and are certain about it, then pray twenty-four nights and days, or three and twenty nights and days, and fast. This will be sufficient for you.' He said, 'Do this every month, like how women menstruate and become pure according to their menstrual and purification times. If you are able to delay the Dhuhr (noon) prayer and hasten the Asr (afternoon) prayer, then take a bath for both of them. If you are able to delay the Maghrib (sunset) prayer and hasten the Isha (evening) prayer, then take a bath for both of them. Combine between the prayers and take a bath with the Fajr (dawn) prayer. Do the same during fasting if you are able to do so.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And it is most amazing that you use a tampon.' Meaning, seek forgiveness.\""],[20907,"\"I suffered from an irregular menstruation, so I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Use a loincloth and insert cotton.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, it is more severe than that; I gush forth blood profusely.' He said: 'Use that internally and secure it, and consider your menstruation according to God's knowledge as six or seven days each month. Then perform ghusl, fast, and pray for twenty-three or twenty-four days. Delay the noon prayer and advance the afternoon prayer, and perform ghusl once for both, and perform ghusl for the dawn prayer. This is the more beloved of the two matters to me.'\""],[20908,"\"I used to suffer from severe, heavy prolonged menstrual bleeding, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to seek his ruling and ask him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bint Jahsh. I said: 'O Messenger of God, I have a need to discuss with you.' He said: 'What is it, O you?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, it is a matter about which—by God—there is no escape, and I am shy about it.' He said: 'What is it, O you?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I suffer from severe, heavy prolonged menstrual bleeding. What do you think about it? It has prevented me from praying and fasting.' He said to her: 'I prescribe for you cotton, for it will take away the blood.' I said: 'It is more than that.' He said: 'Indeed, I will command you with two matters; whichever of them you do, it will suffice you in place of the other. If you are able to do both, you know best. This is only a strike from the strikes of Satan. So pray and fast for twenty-four nights and their days, for that will suffice you; and do likewise every month, just as women menstruate and become pure according to the time of their menstruation and purity. If you are able to delay the noon prayer and hasten the afternoon prayer, and perform ghusl once for both, then pray the noon and afternoon prayers together, then delay the sunset prayer and hasten the night prayer and combine the two prayers, then do so. And perform ghusl with the dawn prayer, and pray accordingly; do so, and pray and fast if you are able to do that.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'And this is more pleasing to me.'\""],[20909,"\"From his grandmother.\""],[20910,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Abu Yazid Yusuf b. Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us; Abdullah b. Abd al-Hakam narrated to us. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us. They said: Ibn Anas informed us from Zayd b. Aslam from Ibn Bujayd from his grandmother that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.\""],[20911,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.\""],[20912,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Do not repel the one who asks, even with a burnt hoof.\""],[20913,"\"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'Do not turn away a beggar, even if with a burnt hoof.'\""],[20914,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; Abdullah b. Yusuf informed us: Malik narrated to us from Zayd b. Aslam from Amr b. Mu'adh al-Ash-hali from his grandmother that she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O believing women, let not one of you disdain to give to her neighbor, even if it be a burnt trotter of a sheep.\""],[20915,"\"I said: 'O Messenger of God, a poor man stands at my door until I feel ashamed, but I find nothing to give him.' He said: 'Put in his hand, even if a burnt hoof.'\""],[20916,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a beggar comes to me and I have nothing to give him.\" He said, \"Do not turn him away empty-handed even if it is with a date.\""],[20917,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O believing women, let not one of you disdain to give to her neighbor, even if it be the burnt foot of a sheep.\""],[20918,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Perform the Fajr prayer when it is bright, for that is greater in reward.”"],[20919,"Al-Hawlaa bt. Tuwayt passed by her while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her. She said: “This al-Hawlaa—they claim that she does not sleep at night.” He said: “Take on of deeds what you can bear, for by Allah, Allah does not tire until you tire.”"],[20920,"Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas struck her a blow whose severity she did not know. She came to the Prophet ﷺ in the darkness before dawn and mentioned to him what had happened to her. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Take back from her [what you gave].” She said: “Indeed what he gave me is with me just as it was.” He said: “Then take back from her.” So he took back from her, and she stayed with her family."],[20922,"From Habiba bt. Sahl, a woman whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had intended to marry, but Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas proposed to her and married her. Thabit b. Qays had harshness in his character, so he struck her. She came at dawn to the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: “Who is this?” She said: “I am Habiba, O Messenger of Allah. Neither I nor Thabit.” Thabit came following her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you strike her?” He said: “Yes, I struck her.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Take back from her [what you gave].” She said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have everything he gave me.” He said: “So he took back from her, and she sat in her house.”"],[20923,"Habiba bt. Sahl was married to Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, for he was an ugly man. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I see him, and were it not for fear of Allah, I would spit in his face.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Will you return to him his garden that he gave you as a dower?” She said: “Yes.” He sent for him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated the two of them. That was the first khulʿ in Islam."],[20924,"Abu Bakr asked permission of the Prophet ﷺ, when he saw his lightness, to go to Bint Kharija, and he granted him permission—in a long hadith."],[20925,"I was sitting in Aisha’s house when the Prophet ﷺ entered and said: “There are no two Muslims who have three small children die, who have not reached the age of sin, but Allah will admit them to Paradise by the virtue of His mercy toward them.”"],[20926,"She was with Aisha when the Prophet ﷺ came and entered upon her. He said: “There are no two Muslims who have three children die, who have not reached the age of sin, but they will be brought on the Day of Resurrection until they are made to stand at the gate of Paradise. It will be said to them: ‘Enter Paradise.’ They will say: ‘Until our parents enter.’ It will be said to them: ‘Enter Paradise, you and your parents.’”"],[20927,"I saw myself among women of Quraysh in the house of Abu Husayn while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was between al-Safa and al-Marwa. She said: I heard him when he reached the place of saʿy saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.”"],[20928,"From Bint Tajra, one of the women of Banu ʿAbd al-Dar, she said: I entered the house of the family of Abu Husayn with women of Quraysh. The Prophet ﷺ looked at me while he was performing saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwa. I saw him running in the middle of the valley, and his lower garment was twisting around from the intensity of the saʿy until I said: I can see his knees. And I heard him saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.”"],[20929,"\"And indeed, I was among the women of Quraysh in the house of Abu Hussein, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking between Safa and Marwa, and I heard him saying, 'Hurry up, for the act of walking between Safa and Marwa has been prescribed for you.' She said, 'And truly, his garment was swirling around him due to the intensity of his walking.'\""],[20930,"I looked at the Prophet ﷺ while he was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwa, and I was among women of Quraysh. He was performing saʿy at the rear of the people, saying: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you.” I looked at him, and he was performing saʿy, and his lower garment was twisting around from the intensity of the saʿy."],[20931,"I heard ʿAbd Allah b. Nabih from his grandmother Safiyya bt. Shayba from Habiba bt. Abi Tajra, who said: I looked out from an opening between al-Safa and al-Marwa and looked down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was performing saʿy between al-Safa and al-Marwa and saying to his companions: “Perform saʿy, for Allah has prescribed saʿy upon you. If you could have seen him from the intensity of the saʿy, his lower garment was turning around his belly and thighs until I saw the whiteness of his thighs.”"],[20932,"Her husband said to her, \"Look, O mother of Muhammad, what are you talking about? Indeed, speaking about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without certainty is a severe offense.\" She said, \"Woe to me, what benefit do I have in speaking to them about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ if it does not benefit them, and I would be lying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The dunya (world) is green and sweet, so whoever takes wealth with a good intention will be blessed with it. And many are those who try to deceive in the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger for their own selfish desires, and they will have the fire on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[20933,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Indeed this wealth is green and sweet; so whoever acquires it by its right will be blessed for him in it, and many a one who plunges into whatever his soul desires of the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Hamzah, and they mentioned worldly matters. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah will bless him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger in whatever his soul craves — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20935,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Hamzah were discussing the world, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes its surplus is blessed, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the day he meets Him.”"],[20936,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he and Hamzah were mentioning the world, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green; whoever takes it by its right will be blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the day he meets his Lord.”"],[20937,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was discussing the world with Hamzah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes its surplus is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20938,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah blesses him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20939,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed this wealth is sweet and green; so whoever takes it by its right is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20940,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Hamzah, and Khawlah, the wife of Hamzah, was there, and they discussed the world. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is sweet and green; so whoever takes it by its right, Allah blesses it for him, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20941,"Hamzah and the Prophet ﷺ were discussing the world, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed the world is green and sweet; so whoever takes it by its right is blessed for him in it, and many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I made for him a kharīzah (a dish of meat and flour), and I presented it to him. He placed his hand in it and found it hot, so he withdrew it and said: “O Khawlah, we cannot endure heat or cold. O Khawlah, Allah has granted me al-Kawthar, and it is a river in Paradise. No creatures are more beloved to me to come to it than your people. O Khawlah, many a one plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger in whatever his soul craves — for him is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20944,"From Khawlah bt. Qays b. Quhd, who was the wife of Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he was killed leaving her. She came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ to visit him. She said: “O Prophet of Allah, I have been wanting to meet you and ask you about something that was mentioned to me, that you mention that you have a ḥawḍ (basin) between such and such.” He said to her: “Yes, and the people most beloved to me — or the people most beloved to me — to come to it are your people.” She said: “I brought him some ʿaṣīdah (porridge) in a bowl, and when he placed his hand in it, it burned him, and he said: ‘Ḥass!’ Then he said: ‘The son of Adam, if heat afflicts him, says “ḥass”, and if cold afflicts him, says “ḥass.”’”"],[20945,"“Yes, and the most beloved of those who come to me are your people.” This is how Abū Khālid narrated it from Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm, and the correct version is the ḥadīth of Ḥammād b. Zayd."],[20946,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “God has not sanctified a nation whose weak do not take their right from their strong without being impeded.” Then he said: “If a debtor departs from his creditor in this matter while he is pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the water send blessings upon him. But if a debtor departs while he is displeased, then oppression is recorded against him each day and night, each Friday, and each month.”"],[20947,"There was a basket of dates for a man from the Banu Sa'ida, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded a man from the Ansar to distribute it. He distributed the dates, but the man refused to accept them. The Prophet ﷺ asked him, \"Are you rejecting the command of the Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Yes, for who is more deserving of justice than the Messenger of Allah?\" Upon hearing this, the eyes of the Prophet ﷺ filled with tears and he said, \"He spoke the truth, for who is more deserving of justice than me, the Messenger of Allah? By the sanctity of Allah, a nation will not be honored if the weak do not receive their rights from the strong, and the strong do not protect them.\" Then he said, \"O Khawla, fulfill his rights and give it to him, for there is no enemy who comes out of his enemy's presence satisfied, except that the beasts of the land and the fish of the sea pray for him, and there is no enemy who oppresses his enemy, except that Allah writes a sin against him for every day and night.\""],[20948,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of what expiates sins? Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the prayers, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous prayer.”"],[20949,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Shall I inform you of the expiations of sins?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of God.” He said, “Performing ablution thoroughly despite difficulties, taking many steps to the mosques, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous prayer.”"],[20950,"He heard her say: “My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel.”"],[20951,"“My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel during ablution.”"],[20952,"I heard Umm Subayyah al-Juhaniyyah say: “My hand alternated with the Prophet’s ﷺ in ablution from a single vessel.”"],[20953,"I heard Umm Subayyah say: “My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed in ablution from a single vessel.”"],[20954,"Sometimes I contended with the Prophet ﷺ over the vessel, performing ablution, I and he, from a single vessel."],[20955,"“My hand and the hand of the Messenger of God ﷺ differed over a single vessel during ablution.”"],[20956,"She was among those who gave themselves to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20957,"Khawlah bt. Hakim was among those who gave themselves to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[20958,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: “Whoever alights at a place and says, ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of God from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him until he departs from that place.”"],[20959,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When one of you alights at a place, let him say: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ for nothing will harm him until he departs from it.”"],[20960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he departs.”"],[20961,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If one of you enters a house and says, 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,' nothing from that house will harm him until he leaves.\""],[20962,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik. Ḥ. And Abū Yazīd al-Qarāṭīsī narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us. Ḥ. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh b. Yūsuf narrated to us. They both said: Mālik informed us, that it reached him from Yaʿqūb b. ʿAbdullāh b. al-Ashajj, from Busr b. Saʿīd, the mawlā of the Ḥaḍramīs, from Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, from Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he departs from it.”"],[20963,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever alights at a place and says: ‘I seek refuge in all the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created,’ nothing will harm him in that place until he moves on from it.”"],[20964,"The Prophet ﷺ came out one day holding one of his daughter's children, saying: “By Allah, you make people stingy, cowardly, and ignorant, and you are among the sweet basil of Allah, and the last place where the Lord of the worlds set foot was Wajj.” Ibn Abī ʿUmar added in his narration: Sufyān said: The last expedition the Prophet ﷺ undertook was to al-Ṭāʾif. And the poet said: “I will surely seek you out with the tread of the one who moves about.”"],[20965,"Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: “O Messenger of Allah, a woman sees in her dream what a man sees.” He said: “If she sees that, she should perform ghusl.”"],[20966,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a ruling about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees: Is ghusl obligatory upon her? He said: “Yes, if she sees the fluid.”"],[20967,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: “Nothing is required of her, just as a man, if he does not ejaculate, is not required to perform ghusl until he ejaculates.”"],[20968,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a woman who sees in her dream what a man sees. He said: “Nothing is required of her, just as a man, if he does not ejaculate, nothing is required of him.”"],[20969,"The righteous woman Khawlah bt. Ḥakīm claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Children are a cause of grief, cowardice, ignorance, and stinginess, and the last place where Allah, may He be exalted, set foot was Wajj.”"],[20970,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, I menstruate and I have only one garment.” He said: “Wash it and pray in it.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, the trace of blood remains in it.” He said: “It will not harm you.”"],[20971,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you have a ḥawḍ?” He said: “Yes, and the people I most love to come to it are your people.” Thus narrated Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar, and the people said it is from Khawlah bt. Qays."],[20972,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The world is sweet and green, and there will be men who wade into the wealth of God and His Messenger without right. For them is the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20973,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? For there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20974,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? For there is none among you, a woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it, except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20975,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what suffices you? Indeed, there is none among you who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[20976,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us, praised God, and extolled Him. Then he said: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20977,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is none among you, a woman who adorns herself with gold, except that she will be punished for it.”"],[20978,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon and saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? There is none among you, a woman who wears gold and displays it, except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20979,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, saying: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20980,"The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us, praised God, and extolled Him. Then he said: “O assembly of women, is there not for you in silver what you may adorn yourselves with? Indeed, there is no woman who adorns herself with gold and displays it except that she will be punished with it.”"],[20981,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ when he had a fever, and the fever had become severe upon him. I said: “You, O Messenger of God, the fever has become severe upon you. If only you would call upon God, He would remove it from you.” He said: “The people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them.” She said: A waterskin had been suspended for him on a tree, and he lay down beneath it, with water dripping onto his heart."],[20982,"We entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ among the women of the Emigrants to visit him, and he was feverish. He ordered a waterskin containing water, and it was suspended on a tree. He made the water drip onto his heart due to the severity of what he felt. We said: “O Messenger of God, if only you would call upon God, He would remove what is upon you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them, then those next to them.”"],[20983,"She entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered a waterskin, which was suspended on a tree. Then he lay down beneath it, and it began dripping onto his heart. I said: “Call upon God, and He will remove it from you.” He said: “Indeed, the people most severely tried are the prophets, then those next to them.”"],[20984,"I visited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among some women, and he had hung up a waterskin that was dripping on him due to the severity of the fever. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate, its severity would leave you.' He said, 'The people most severely tried are the prophets, then the righteous, then the next best and the next best.'"],[20985,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ when he had a fever. He ordered a waterskin, and it was hung on a tree; then he lay down beneath it, and the water began to drip on his heart. I said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate to Allah and He would remove it from you.' He said, 'Among the people most severely tried are the prophets, then those who follow them, then those who follow them.'"],[20986,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was suffering from fever, and he had hung up a waterskin that was dripping on his heart. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is this?' He said, 'We, the company of prophets, have affliction multiplied upon us.'"],[20987,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no good in a gathering of women except at a funeral, for when they gather, they say and say.'"],[20988,"One day he came in to me and spoke to me about something while he was somewhat vexed, so I answered him back, and he said, 'You are to me like my mother's back.' Then he went out and sat down; then he called his people, then he returned to me and wanted me for himself, but I refused him. He struggled with me and I struggled with him, and I overcame him as a woman overcomes a weak man. I said, 'No, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Khuwaylah, you will not reach her until Allah judges between me and you.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining to him about what I had encountered from him. He said, 'Your husband and your cousin; fear Allah.' Then Allah revealed: {Allah has heard the statement of she who disputes with you concerning her husband and complains to Allah} until it reached the expiation. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Order him to free a slave.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he has no slave to free.' He said, 'Then let him fast two consecutive months.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, he is an old man; by Allah, he is not able to fast.' He said, 'Then let him feed sixty poor people.' I said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he does not have anything to feed.' He said, 'Rather, we will help him with a basket of dates—and the basket is a large measure that holds thirty sāʿs.' I said, 'And I will help him with another basket.' He said, 'You have done well; order him to give it in charity.'"],[20989,"From Khawlah bint al-Ṣāmit—her husband was ill, and he called her, but she delayed. He said to her, 'If I approach you or have intercourse with you, then you are to me like my mother's back.' She went to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about that to him, but he did not reply to her with anything, as nothing had reached him about it. Then she came to him another time, and the Prophet ﷺ came and said, 'Free a slave.' He said, 'I do not have one.' He said, 'Fast two consecutive months.' He said, 'I am not able.' He said, 'Then feed sixty poor people, thirty sāʿs.' He said, 'I do not possess that unless you help me.' So the Prophet ﷺ helped him with fifteen sāʿs, and the people helped him until it reached the amount. He said, 'By Allah, there is no one more in need of it than me and my household.' He said, 'Take it, you and your household.' Abu al-Qāsim said: Thus said Khawlah bint al-Ṣāmit, and she is Khawlah bint Thaʿlabah, the wife of Aws b. al-Ṣāmit."],[20990,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah does not sanctify a nation whose weak cannot take their right from their strong without stammering.' And he said: 'Whoever leaves his debtor while pleased with him, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the seas pray for him. And whoever leaves his debtor while angry with him, it is written against him every day and night, every week and month, that he has wronged.'"],[20991,"About her mother, who was a servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , it was narrated that a scorpion entered the house and went under the bed and died. The Prophet ﷺ stayed for a few days without receiving revelation. He said, \"O Khawla, what happened in the house of the Messenger of Allah? Gabriel does not come to me. Did something happen in the house of the Messenger of Allah?\" I said, \"By Allah, a day has not passed upon us that is better than our day.\" He then put on his shoes and went out. I said, \"If I prepare the house and sweep it, I will sweep under the bed.\" So I took the broom and went under the bed, and there was something heavy. I kept sweeping until I took it out, and it was a dead scorpion. I took it with my hand and threw it behind the house. Then the Messenger of Allah came hearing his beard quivering, and whenever he received revelation, his beard would quiver. He said, \"O Khawla, cover me.\" So Allah revealed: \"By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers (the earth), your Lord has neither forsaken you nor hated you.\""],[20992,"Khālidah bint Anas, the mother of the Banū Ḥazm al-Sāʿidiyyah, came to the Prophet ﷺ and presented incantations to him, and he ordered them."],[20993,"From her maternal aunt Khulaydah bint Qaʿnab, who was among the women who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him. She said: A woman came to him wearing a gold bracelet, and he refused to accept her pledge. She left the crowd, threw away the bracelet, then came and he accepted her pledge. She went out to look for the bracelet, and when she went to look for it, it had been taken away."],[20994,"She was a servant of the Prophet ﷺ called Khaḍrah."],[20995,"Her father married her off while she was a previously married woman, and she disliked that. She went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he rejected the marriage."],[20996,"My father married me off while I was unwilling, and I was a virgin. I complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'Do not marry her off while she is unwilling.'"],[20997,"Her father married her off while she was a matron, and she was unwilling, so the Prophet ﷺ “rejected her marriage.”"],[20998,"Her case was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he ordered a man, and her father married her to a man from Banu Amr b. Awf; and she longed for Abu Lubabah."],[20999,"Khansa’ bt. Khidam was married by her father while she was unwilling, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ, “and he rejected her marriage.”"],[21000,"The Prophet ﷺ met her coming from the bathhouse and said, “From where are you coming, O Umm al-Darda’?” She said, “From the bathhouse, O Messenger of God.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Any woman who puts down her garments in other than her own house has torn the veil between her and God.”"],[21001,"I heard Umm al-Darda’ say, “I came out of the bathhouse and the Messenger of God ﷺ met me and said, ‘From where, O Umm al-Darda’?’ I said, ‘From the bathhouse.’ He said, ‘By the One in Whose hand is my soul, no woman puts down her garments in other than the house of one of her mothers except that she is a tearer of every veil between her and the Most Merciful, Blessed and Exalted.’”"],[21002,"“Did you hear anything from the Prophet ﷺ?” She said, “Yes. I entered upon him while he was sitting in the gathering, and I heard him say, ‘The first thing to be placed in the Balance is good character.’”"],[21003,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “Whoever guards a post on any of the coasts of the Muslims for three days, a year’s garrison duty is fulfilled on his behalf.”"],[21004,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “God created disease and remedy, so treat yourselves, but do not treat with what is forbidden.”"],[21005,"I said, “O Messenger of God, does rage harm?” He said, “Yes, as leaf-stripping harms trees.”"],[21006,"“Supplicate God for good for us, for the Prophet ﷺ used to say, ‘The supplication of the wronged for his brother in his absence is answered; at his head is an angel who says ameen to his supplication; whenever he supplicates for good for him, he says, “Ameen, and for you the like.”’” He said, “Then I went out to the market and met Abu al-Darda’, and he narrated to me from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it.”"],[21007,"The Messenger of God ﷺ met her one day and said, “From where have you come, O Umm al-Darda’?” She said, “From the bathhouse.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, “No woman removes her garments in other than her own house except that she has torn the veil between her and God.”"],[21008,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “The best thing to be placed in the Balance on the Day of Resurrection is good character.”"],[21009,"She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with jewelry and said, “I have given this as charity.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is not permissible for a woman to do anything with her wealth except with her husband’s permission. Have you asked Ka'b’s permission?” She said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Ka'b and asked, “Have you permitted Khayrah to give her jewelry as charity?” He said, “Yes.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted it from her. [She was] al-Kharqā’, the black woman who used to remove harmful things from the mosque of the Prophet ﷺ."],[21011,"Durrah bint Abī Lahab was married to al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Nawfal, and she bore him ʿUqbah, al-Walīd, and Abū Muslim. Then she came to the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah, and the people spoke much about her parents. She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, did the disbelievers beget anyone other than me?” The Prophet ﷺ said to her, “And what of that?” She said, “The people of Madinah have hurt me regarding my parents.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “When you pray ẓuhr, pray where I can see you.” The Prophet ﷺ prayed ẓuhr, then turned toward her and faced the people, saying: “O people, do you have lineage while I have no lineage?” ʿUmar jumped up and said, “May Allah be angry with whoever angers you.” He said, “This is my cousin, so let no one say anything to her but good.”"],[21012,"From the husband of Durrah bint Abī Lahab, from her: She said, “I was with ʿĀ’ishah when a man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ who had called out to him while he was on the pulpit, saying, ‘O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best?’ She said: The man came and was seized, and he said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, I have no sin; so-and-so ordered me.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The best of people is the most pious of them, the most commanding of good, the most forbidding of evil, and the most upholding of kinship ties.’”"],[21013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us and asked for water. I went to a jug and gave him water to drink. A man wearing two green garments asked him, and he said, “Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, establish prayer, and give zakāh.” Then he said, “The best of my ummah is my generation, then those who follow them.” Shuʿbah erred in the chain of this hadith."],[21014,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us when I married the daughter of Abū Lahab and said, “Is there any entertainment?”"],[21015,"There were women sitting with her from the family of Zuraiq. You are the daughter of Abu Lahab, who says, \"May the hands of Abu Lahab perish, and may he himself perish. His wealth and what he earned will never suffice him.\" What will your migration benefit you? So the pearl of the Prophet ﷺ came to her and she complained to him about what had been said to her. He calmed her down and said, \"Sit down.\" Then he prayed Dhuhr with the people and sat on the pulpit for an hour, then he said, \"O people, why am I being harmed in my family? By Allah, my intercession will reach those who deserve it, whether they are alive or dead, and it will reach every soul and tribe on the Day of Judgment.\""],[21016,"Years of drought befell Quraysh, which dried up the udders and emaciated the bones. While I was lying down overcome by grief or troubled, suddenly a caller cried out with a hoarse voice, saying: “O assembly of Quraysh, this Prophet who has been sent—his days have overshadowed you, and this is the time of his rising stars. So hasten to life and fertility! Look for a man among you who is of middle rank, great in stature, large in body, white with radiance, with thick eyelashes, smooth cheeks, and a prominent nose. He has a mark that he suppresses, and a practice that guides to him. Let him and his children set out, and let one man from every clan descend to him. Let them sprinkle water, touch perfume, and touch the corner [of the Kaʿbah]. Then let them climb Abū Qubays, then let the man supplicate and the people say āmīn. Then you will be rained upon as much as you wish.” By Allah, I woke up terrified, my skin trembling and my mind bewildered. I related my vision and lay in the mountain passes of Makkah. By the sanctity and the sacred sanctuary, there remained no one in the valley but that he said, “This is Shaybah al-Ḥamd.” The leaders of Quraysh came to him, and one man from every clan descended to him. They sprinkled, touched, and touched the corner, then climbed Abū Qubays and lined up around him, their pace not slackening until they stood on the summit of the mountain. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib stood, and with him was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a boy who had reached puberty or nearly so. He raised his hand and said: “O Allah, Remover of hardship and Reliever of distress, You are the One who teaches without being taught, and the One who is asked without being withheld from. These are Your male and female servants at the courtyards of Your sanctuary, complaining to You of their year, which has destroyed the camel and the hoofed animal. O Allah, send upon us abundant, fruitful rain.” By the Lord of the Kaʿbah, they did not leave until the sky poured forth its water and the valley overflowed with its torrents. I heard the elders and nobles of Quraysh—ʿAbd Allāh b. Judʿān, Ḥarb b. Umayyah, and Hishām b. al-Mughīrah—saying to ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, “Congratulations to you, O father of the valley, for through you the people of the valley have lived.” And concerning that, Ruqayqah bint Abī Ṣayfī says…"],[21017,"When the Prophet ﷺ came seeking support in al-Ṭā’if, he entered upon me, and I brought him a drink of sawīq. He said, “O Ruqayqah, do not worship their idol and do not pray to it.” She said, “Then they will kill me.” He said, “If they say that to you, say: My Lord is the Lord of this idol. And if you see it, turn your back to it.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left me."],[21023,"He said, “I would not like you to do that unless you have a reward in it.” So she and he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman with a craft by which I earn, and I have nothing, nor does my husband or my child. They distract me, so I cannot give charity.” He said, “You have a reward in that for what you spend on them.”"],[21024,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'I am a woman of craftsmanship by which I seek [livelihood], but neither I, nor my husband, nor my children have anything; they preoccupy me so that I do not give charity.' He said: 'You will have a reward for that, whatever you spend on them.'"],[21025,"Rāʾiṭah, the sister of ʿAbdullāh al-Thaqafiyyah, was married to Ibn Masʿūd. She was a skillful woman who made things and sold from her craft. She said to Ibn Masʿūd: 'You and your child have kept me too busy to spend in the path of Allah, so I am unable to spend in the path of Allah.' He said: 'I would not like you to do that if you had no reward in it.' So I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'Spend on them, for you have the reward of whatever you spend on them.'"],[21026,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrating about the wife of Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās al-Anṣārī that there occurred something between her and her husband, and he was a man of harshness. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke with him, and he sent for Thābit b. Qays. They spoke in his presence as Allah willed, then he accepted a ransom from her and she ransomed herself from him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to observe an ʿiddah of one menstrual period."],[21027,"I obtained a khulʿ from my husband, then I came to ʿUmar and asked him: 'What ʿiddah is incumbent upon me?' He said: 'There is no ʿiddah upon you unless it is a recent matter, in which case you should wait until you menstruate once.' She said: 'Indeed, in that matter, the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is followed concerning Maryam al-Maghāliyyah, who was married to Thābit b. Qays b. Shammās and obtained a khulʿ from him.'"],[21028,"Regarding the ablution of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , she said, \"Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us and visit us, and he would perform ablution with this container and with a similar container, which was about a Mudd in size. She said, \"He would first wash his hands, then he would rinse his mouth and nose, then he would wash his face three times, then he would wash his hands three times, then he would wipe his head twice, and he would wipe both the outward and inward parts of his ears, and then he would wash his feet three times, three times.\""],[21030,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, and I poured water for him. He rinsed his mouth, snuffed water, and washed his face three times, each three times, his forearms three times, each three times, and wiped his head twice, starting from the back before the front, and wiped the back of his ears, and inserted his fingers into the holes of his ears, and washed his feet three times, each three times."],[21031,"The Prophet ﷺ used to come to us, and we would bring him a water vessel of ours containing water, taking a mudd and a half or two-thirds of the Madinan mudd. I would pour for him, and he would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth and snuff water, wash his face three times, wipe his head once, and wipe his ears, their outer and inner parts, and purify his feet."],[21032,"Regarding the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He used to perform ablution at her house, so I came to her and asked her, and she brought out a vessel, about a mudd and a quarter by the Hashimi measure. She said: 'I used to bring out his ablution water in this. He would begin by pouring onto his right hand and washing it three times before putting it into the vessel, then rinse his mouth and snuff water three times, wash his face three times, wash his right hand three times and his left hand three times, then wipe his head from front to back.' Sufyān described how he wiped his head until he reached its beginning. This is the wording of Ibn Abī ʿUmar's ḥadīth. Ibn Abī ʿUmar added in his narration: Sufyān said: 'Ibn ʿAjlān added to me, from Ibn ʿAqīl, who said: al-Rabīʿ said: Then he wiped his temples and cheeks, then returned them to the middle of his head, then extended them to the back of his neck, then wiped his ears, then washed his feet.'"],[21033,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and wiped the front of his ears and their back."],[21034,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped his head with the leftover water that was on his hand, starting from the back of his head, then drawing it to the front, then drawing it back to the back."],[21035,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution washing each part three times."],[21036,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us frequently. She said: 'He came to us, and we placed for him the water vessel. He performed ablution: he washed his palms three times, then rinsed his mouth and snuffed water once, washed his face three times and his forearms three times, wiped with what remained of his ablution water twice, starting from the back, then returned his hands to his forelock, and washed his feet three times, each three times.'"],[21037,"I assisted the Prophet ﷺ in ablution. I brought him a water vessel that held a mudd or a mudd and a third. He said: 'Pour.' He performed ablution, wiping the front of his head and the outer and inner parts of his ears."],[21038,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us, performed ablution, wiped the front of his head, and wiped the outer and inner parts of his ears."],[21039,"I heard al-Rubayyiʿ bt. Muʿawwidh b. ʿAfrāʾ say: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. I would pour ablution water for him, and he would perform ablution at our place using a water vessel of ours, containing a mudd and a half, and a mudd and a third. I would pour water over his palms three times, then I would set it down for him, and he would rinse his mouth, inhale water, wash his face three times, his hands three times, wipe his head and his ears, then wash his feet three times, three times."],[21040,"About the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ, she said: Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution in a vessel like this one, indicating with her hand toward a small water skin that holds a mudd and a third, according to the first (report), as I believe. He rinsed his mouth, inhaled water, washed his face and hands three times, then wiped the front of his head and the back of his head, and wiped his ears along with the back of his head, and washed his feet."],[21041,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. She narrated to us that he said: “Pour ablution water.” So I poured for him into a water vessel, which is a small water skin that holds a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a quarter of water. He said: “Pour over my hand.” He washed his palms three times, then said: “Place it down.” She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ then performed ablution while I was watching. He washed his face three times, rinsed his mouth and inhaled water once, washed his right hand three times, washed his left hand three times, wiped his head twice, beginning with the back of his head then the front of it, and wiped both his ears, their outer and inner sides, washed his right foot three times, and washed his left foot three times."],[21042,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to come to us. I would take a water vessel of ours holding a mudd and a half, or a mudd and a third, and pour water over him. He would wash his hands three times, rinse his mouth, inhale water, wash his face three times, wipe his head twice, then wash his feet three times, three times."],[21043,"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed ablution at her place. He wiped his head, wiping his entire head from above the hair, every side of the hair’s direction, without disturbing the hair from its state."],[21044,"She saw the Messenger of God ﷺ performing ablution. She said: He wiped his head, the front of it and the back of it, and his temples and his ears once."],[21045,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ fill his hands with water, then pour it, then wipe his head, its front and back, then return to the middle of his head and wipe, and he brought his hands to his head and wiped his ears, their insides and outsides, and he took hold of the lobes of his ears."],[21046,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and called for ablution water. A vessel was brought that could hold a mudd and a third, or a mudd and a half, of the Prophet’s mudd ﷺ. He performed ablution: he washed his face, then washed his hand, wiped his head, and wiped the back of his head until reaching its middle, in each wipe."],[21048,"I heard al-Rubayyiʿ bt. Muʿawwidh b. ʿAfrāʾ say: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ perform ablution. He took fresh water for his head, moving his hands back and forth over it."],[21049,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ a basket of fresh dates and hairy cucumbers. He gave me a handful of jewelry, or gold."],[21050,"We were in Madinah on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ, and the young girls were beating the duff and singing. Al-Rabīʿ entered upon us, and we mentioned that to her. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the morning of my wedding, while I had two young girls singing and lamenting my fathers who were killed at Badr, and they were saying: ..."],[21051,"I said to al-Rubayyi‘ bt. Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afra’: Describe for me the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, “If you had seen him, you would have seen the sun rising.”"],[21052,"Mu‘awwidh b. ‘Afra’ sent me with a basket of fresh dates, upon which were small cucumbers with fuzz, to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to love cucumbers. Some good ones had just arrived from Bahrain, so he filled his hand with them and gave them to me."],[21053,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and entered upon me on the morning my marriage was consummated. He sat on my bed, and some young servant girls began playing a tambourine and lamenting those of my forefathers who were killed at Badr, until one of them said..."],[21055,"On the morning of the day of Ashura, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent word to the villages of the Ansar around Madinah: “Whoever began the day fasting should complete his fast, and whoever began the day not fasting should fast the rest of his day.” So we used to fast it, and we would have our young children fast as well. We would make them a toy of wool and take it to the garden, and if one of them cried for food, we would give him that until it was time to break the fast."],[21056,"\"We used to accompany the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in battles, not fighting, but providing water to the soldiers and treating the wounded.\""],[21057,"“We used to go on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We would give water to the people, serve them, and bring the dead and wounded back to Madinah.”"],[21058,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — and if I had wished, because of my closeness to him, I could have kissed the seal between his shoulders — saying about Sa‘d b. Mu‘adh on the day he died: “The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for him.”"],[21059,"Did you hear your mother mention anything about fasting on Ashura? She said, \"Yes, I heard my mother Ruqayyah say that the Messenger of Allah, may ﷺ , used to give great importance to it. He would even call his grandchildren and the grandchildren of Fatimah, who were still breastfeeding, on that day. He would put his spittle in their mouths and tell their mothers, 'Do not breastfeed them until nightfall.' His spittle would suffice them.\""],[21060,"On the day of Qurayzah and al-Nadir, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with Safiyyah bt. Huyayy, holding her by the arm. When she saw the captives, she said, “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.” So he released her arm from his hand, freed her, proposed to her, and married her, giving her as her dowry Ruzaynah."],[21061,"From her mother Ruzaynah, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hafsah, the Mother of the Believers, visited Aishah, the Mother of the Believers, one day. Sawdah entered upon them wearing a garment of Yemeni cloth and a head covering, and on the inner corners of her eyes were two dots like lentils of aloe and saffron. ‘Alilah said, “I lived to see women adorning themselves with it for their husbands.” Hafsah said to Aishah, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ will enter upon us and find us plain, while she among us is glowing. I will ruin her adornment today.” Aishah said, “Fear Allah, O Hafsah.” Sawdah said, “What are you saying?” She was hard of hearing. She said, “The one-eyed man has come out.” Sawdah said, “The one-eyed man has come out?” She said, “Yes.” She said, “Where shall I hide?” She said, “Go to the tent.” It was a tent made of palm branches where they cooked pots, and in it were spider webs. She went and entered it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them while they were laughing, unable to speak to him from laughter. He said, “Why the laughter?” They gestured with their hands toward the tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the tent and found Sawdah trembling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “What is the matter with you?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, the one-eyed man has come out.” He said, “He has not come out, and he will never come out.” Then he entered, took her by the hand, and began brushing dust and spider webs off her."],[21062,"Shaybah bint Al-Aswad, the niece of my mother, told me that my grandmother, Rawdah, said to me, \"I used to be a companion to a woman in the city. When the Prophet ﷺ migrated from Makkah to Madinah, my guardian, Rawdah, told me to stand at the door of our house and inform her when this man passes by.\" She continued, \"So I stood and the Prophet ﷺ came with a group of his companions. I held onto a corner of his cloak and he smiled at me. Shaybah said, \"I think he wiped his hand on my head.\" I asked my guardian, \"O guardian, this is the man who has come.\" So my guardian and those who were with her in the house came out. Islam was presented to them, and they embraced Islam.\" Shaybah added, \"Rawdah was with me in the house in Bani Sulaym. Whenever the neighbors purchased a slave, servant, garment, or food, they would say to her, 'O Rawdah, place your hand on it.' And everything she touched would be blessed.\""],[21063,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when a woman came to him with a son of hers and said, “O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah for blessing in him, for three of my children have died.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Since you embraced Islam?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “That is a strong protection.” A man said, “Listen, O Rahma, to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying.”"],[21064,"Zaynab bt. Abi Salamah asked him, “What have you named your daughter?” He said, “I named her Barrah.” She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade this name. You have named her Barrah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not praise yourselves; Allah knows best who among you are truly righteous.” They said, “What should we name her?” He said, “Name her Zaynab.”"],[21066,"“My name was Barrah, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Zaynab.”"],[21067,"She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was bathing. He took a handful of water and threw it in my face, saying, “Get back, O little foolish one.”"],[21068,"He entered upon Zaynab bt. Abi Salamah, and she narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with Umm Salamah, and he came in to her with al-Hasan and al-Husayn and Fatimah. He placed al-Hasan on one side and al-Husayn on the other side and Fatimah in his lap, then he said: “The mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O people of the household. Indeed, He is Praiseworthy, Glorious.” I and Umm Salamah were sitting, so Umm Salamah wept. He looked at her and said: “What makes you weep?” She said: O Messenger of Allah, you have singled out these and left me and my daughter. He said: “You and your daughter are of the people of the household.”"],[21070,"My mother said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, he would wash, saying: “Go and enter.” She said: So I entered, and he sprinkled water on my face, then said: “Return.” Al-‘Attaf said: My mother said: “I saw the face of Zaynab when she was a very old woman, and nothing of her face had diminished.”"],[21071,"Kulayb b. Wa’il narrated to us: The stepdaughter of the Prophet ﷺ narrated to me—I think she was Zaynab—she said: “The Prophet of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds and hantam jars.” He said: And I think it included “naqir.”"],[21072,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When you go out to the ‘isha prayer, do not touch perfume.”"],[21073,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the ‘isha prayer, she should not touch perfume.”"],[21074,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[21075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[21076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When one of you women attends the mosque, she should not touch perfume.”"],[21078,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whichever of you women goes out to the mosque should not touch perfume.”"],[21079,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and said: “Whichever of you women attends the ‘isha prayer should not touch perfume.”"],[21080,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Give charity, even from your jewelry.” Zaynab said to ‘Abd Allah: Would it suffice for me to make my charity for you and for the orphaned sons of my brother? ‘Abd Allah was light of hand. ‘Abd Allah said: Ask the Prophet ﷺ about that. Zaynab said: So I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a woman from the Ansar. Zaynab said to her: She has come to ask about the same thing I came to ask about. Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and do not tell him who we are: Would it suffice for me to make my charity for my husband and the orphaned sons of my brother? Bilal went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Which of the Zaynabs? He said: The wife of ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ud and a woman from the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tell her that she has two rewards: the reward of charity and the reward of kinship.”"],[21081,"Bilal came out, and we said to him: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Would it suffice for us, of spending, to spend on our husbands and those our laps have sheltered? He entered and asked him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “Two rewards: the reward of charity and the reward of kinship.”"],[21083,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any reward for me if I give charity to the children of Abdullah from other than me? He said: \"You will have two portions of the reward.\""],[21084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in the mosque and said: \"O assembly of women, give charity,\" and he mentioned the hadith."],[21085,"O Abu Abdur-Rahman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to me while I was among a group of women from the Ansar and said: \"Give charity, even if from your jewelry.\" So ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whether my spending on you and on my brother's children will suffice for me as charity, otherwise I will spend it in the path of Allah. He said: I feel shy to ask him, so you ask him. So I went to the door of the Prophet ﷺ and there was a woman from the Ansar whose need was my need. Bilal came to us, and we said: O Bilal, convey our greetings and the mercy of Allah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that we have our husbands and the children of our brothers; if our spending on our husbands and the children of our brothers will suffice for us, otherwise we will spend in the path of Allah. Bilal entered and told him, and he said: Convey to them greeting and the mercy of Allah, and inform them that their spending on their husbands and the children of their sisters is doubled - a double for maintaining ties and a double for charity."],[21086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Charity given to a relative is multiplied twice in reward.\""],[21087,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave her fifty wasqs of dates at Khaybar and twenty wasqs of barley in Madinah.\""],[21088,"Zaynab bint Qays bin Makhrama wrote to me, saying, \"When she arrived, she left me 10,000 and she was among those who prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ facing both Qiblas.\""],[21089,"She said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father died and left a slave girl, and she gave birth to a boy, and we suspected her. He said: \"Bring him to me.\" When they brought him to him, he looked at him and said: \"The inheritance is his. As for you, veil yourself from him.\""],[21090,"From Zainab bt. Nubayt b. Jabir, wife of Anas b. Malik, she said: Abu Umamah entrusted my mother and my maternal aunt to the Prophet ﷺ, and a gold and pearl ornament called ri'ath was brought to him. She said: \"He adorned them with the ri'ath.\""],[21091,"From his grandfather Abdullah b. Hisham, who had met the Prophet ﷺ; his mother Zainab bt. Humaid took him to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, he is young. \"So he wiped his head and supplicated for him.\""],[21092,"Sahlah bt. Suhayl b. Amr came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, lives with us in our house, and he has reached what men reach and knows what men know. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him, and you will become unlawful to him.\""],[21093,"The wife of Hudhayfah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon me while I am not wearing my outer garment, and I feel something in myself. He said: \"Breastfeed him, and what you feel will go away from you.\""],[21094,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Sahlah bt. Suhayl to breastfeed Salim to remove what was in the heart of Abu Hudhayfah.\""],[21095,"Sahlah bt. Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see something in the face of Abu Hudhayfah regarding Salim. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him.\" She said: He is an adult. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: \"Do I not know that he is a man?\" She said: So she did so, then came to him and said: By the One who honored you as He honored you, I no longer see anything in the face of Abu Hudhayfah."],[21096,"On the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Abu Hudhayfa b. Utba b. Rabi'a b. Abd Shams, who was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, adopted Salim as a son just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted Zayd b. Haritha. Anyone who adopted a man in the pre-Islamic era, the people would call him (the adopted son) by his (adoptive father's) name and he would inherit from his legacy, until Allah revealed concerning that: {Call them by their fathers' names; that is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your clients.} So they were returned to their fathers. Whoever had no known father was a client. Aisha said: And Sahla bt. Suhayl b. Amr al-Qurashi, then al-Amiri, was married to Abu Hudhayfa b. Utba b. Rabi'a. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Allah revealed that, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we used to consider Salim a son, and he used to stay with me and with Abu Hudhayfa in one house, and he would see me while I am in a state of undress, and Allah has revealed about them what you know. So what do you think about his situation, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Breastfeed him.\" So she breastfed him five sucklings, and he became forbidden by them, and he took the status of her son through breastfeeding."],[21097,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, the client of Hudhayfa, enters upon me and he has a beard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Breastfeed him.\" I said: How can I breastfeed him when he has a beard? He said: \"Breastfeed him.\" So she breastfed him, and he used to enter upon her."],[21098,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, should one of us perform ghusl if she has a wet dream? He said: \"Yes, if she sees the fluid.\""],[21101,"My husband died while with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage; he was Sa'd b. Khawla. I remained after him for two months, then I gave birth to what was in my womb. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak, a brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, passed by and entered upon my in-laws. He had wanted me for himself, and I had prepared for marriage and adorned myself. He said: What is the matter with you, O Subay'a? I said: I want to marry. He said: No, by Allah, it is four months and ten days. So I put on my clothes and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Umm Salama, and asked him. He said: \"You are lawful, so marry.\""],[21102,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for no one dies there except that I will be an intercessor or witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[21103,"Ask Subay'a al-Aslamiyya how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ instructed her when her husband died. She said: \"He gave me the ruling that when I give birth, I may marry.\""],[21104,"That he enter upon Subay'a bt. al-Harith al-Aslamiyya and ask her about her hadith and what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her when she miscarried. Umar b. Abd Allah wrote to Abd Allah b. Utba informing him that Subay'a told him that she was married to Sa'd b. Khawla, who was from Banu Amir and was among those who witnessed Badr. He died leaving her during the Farewell Pilgrimage while she was pregnant. She gave birth after his death. When she recovered from her postpartum bleeding, she adorned herself for suitors. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak, a man from Banu Abd al-Dar, entered upon her and said: Why do I see you adorned? Perhaps you want to marry. By Allah, you are not to marry until four months and ten days pass over you. Subay'a said: When he said that to me, I gathered my clothes upon me until evening, then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He gave me the ruling that I was lawful on the day I gave birth, and ordered me to marry if I wished."],[21105,"Marwan sent Abd Allah b. Utba to Subay'a bt. al-Harith to ask her about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for her. She informed him that she was married to Sa'd b. Khawla, who died leaving her during the Farewell Pilgrimage and was a Badri. She gave birth before four months and ten days had passed since his death. Abu al-Sanabil b. Ba'kak met her when she had recovered from her postpartum bleeding and had applied kohl. He said: Perhaps you want to marry. It is four months and ten days from your husband's death. She said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him what Abu al-Sanabil said. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You are lawful when you gave birth.\""],[21106,"On the authority of his mother, Salma bt. Qays, who was one of the aunts of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She had prayed with him facing both qiblas and was one of the women of Banu Adi b. al-Najjar. She said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him among a group of women from the Ansar. When he stipulated for us that we should not associate anything with Allah, not steal, not commit adultery, not kill our children, not bring a slander we fabricate between our hands and feet, and not disobey him in what is right, he said: \"And do not deceive your husbands.\" She said: So we pledged allegiance to him. Then we left, and I said to one of the women: Go back and ask the Messenger of Allah what he prohibited us regarding our husbands' wealth. She asked him, and he said: \"That she takes his wealth and gives it to someone else.\""],[21108,"On the authority of Umm al-Mundhir al-Ansariyya, who was one of the aunts of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was Ali, who was recovering from an illness. In the house there was a hanging cluster of dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it while standing, and Ali was with him. He said: \"Do not eat from that, for it does not suit you.\" Then he sat down, and I made for him chard and barley. He said: \"Eat from this, for it is better for you.\""],[21109,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dislike taking from the top of the food."],[21110,"From his grandmother Salmā, who served the Prophet ﷺ, she said: When one of us had a headache, the Prophet ﷺ would say, “Go and have cupping done,” and if he had a pain in his leg, he would say, “Go and dye it with henna.”"],[21111,"The Prophet ﷺ never got a sore or a thorn but that he placed henna on it."],[21112,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “A house with no dates has no food.”"],[21113,"From his mother, who served the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “A house with no dates, its family goes hungry.”"],[21114,"I visited al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī, ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaʿfar, and ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās, and they said, “Describe for us some food that the Prophet ﷺ used to enjoy eating.” She said, “O my sons, you would not desire it today.” So she got up, took some barley, ground it, sifted it, made it into a loaf, seasoned it with oil, sprinkled pepper over it, and brought it to them, saying, “The Prophet ﷺ used to love this.”"],[21115,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Abū Rāfiʿ to the Banū Umayya b. Zayd to kill the dogs, and he sent another man to kill the dogs."],[21116,"His grandmother Salmā, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, told her that she had prepared a meat stew for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and served it. He ate, with some of his Companions, and a little of it remained. A Bedouin passed by the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ called him, and the Bedouin took all of it with his hand. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Put it down.” Then he said, “Say the name of Allah, and eat from the nearest part of it, and you will be satisfied.” He ate until he was full, and some of it remained."],[21118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a sheep to Abū Rāfiʿ, and that was on the day of the trench, as far as I know. Abū Rāfiʿ roasted it and put it in a basket, then set off with it. The Prophet ﷺ met him returning from the trench and said to him, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” So I handed it to him. Then he said, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” So I handed it to him. Then he said, “O Abū Rāfiʿ, hand me the foreleg.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, does a sheep have more than two forelegs?” He said, “If you had kept silent, you would have handed me whatever I asked for.”"],[21119,"She said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ in the markets when he said, “A man from the people of Paradise will appear to you.” Then I heard a rustling sound, and it was ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ."],[21120,"Salmā, the wife of Abū Rāfiʿ, came complaining about her husband Abū Rāfiʿ. She said, “O Messenger of Allah, he beats me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What is the matter with you and her?” He said, “She annoys me.” He said to her, “How do you annoy him?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, he passed wind and then stood to pray. I said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever passes wind should repeat his ablution.”’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, “Do not beat her.”"],[21121,"On the authority of Salma, the freedwoman of Abu Rafi', the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me some words that I can say without becoming excessive (in my supplications).\" He said: \"Say: 'Allahu Akbar' ten times. Allah will say, 'This is for Me.' And say: 'Subhan Allah' ten times. Allah will say, 'This is for Me.' And say: 'Allahumma ighfirli' (O Allah, forgive me) and you will find that you have done (repentance).' Say it ten times and Allah will say, 'You have repented.'\""],[21122,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “The believing sisters.” Then he mentioned the hadith."],[21123,"Set him free."],[21124,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Abu Ammar and Umm Ammar, “Be patient, O family of Yasir, for your appointment is Paradise.”"],[21125,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him, and he said, \"Go and perform ablution, then come back so I can pledge allegiance to you.\""],[21126,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ to give him my oath of allegiance, and he said: “Go and dye yourself with henna, then come back so that I may accept your allegiance.”"],[21127,"Umar passed by Talha after the death of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was dejected. He said to him, \"What is the matter with you? Has the leadership of your paternal cousin upset you?\" He said, \"No, but I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'I know a phrase which, if a person says it at the time of his death, it will be a light in his record, and his body and soul will find relief from it at death.' I did not ask him about it until he died.\" Umar said, \"I know it. It is the phrase he wanted his uncle to say. If he knew of anything more saving than it, he would have commanded him with it.\""],[21128,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bt. al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and said to her, “O aunt, perform Hajj.” She said, “I am a heavy woman and I fear being held back.” He said, “Perform Hajj and stipulate that my place of release is wherever I am held back.”"],[21129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the Shaytan has not met 'Umar since he embraced Islam except that he fell upon his face.\""],[21130,"I was present at the death of Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Whenever I and my sister cried out, and the women cried out, he did not forbid us. But when he died, he forbade us from wailing. He carried him to the edge of the grave, with al-Abbas at his side. Al-Fadl b. Abbas and Usamah b. Zayd went down into his grave. I was weeping at his grave, and the sun eclipsed. The people said, 'This is because of his death.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It does not eclipse for the death of anyone or for his life.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gap in the grave and ordered that it be filled. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit him?' He said: 'Indeed, it benefits him and does not harm him, but it harms the eye of the living.' He died on Tuesday, ten nights having passed from Rabi' al-Awwal in the year ten."],[21131,"The son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was attended. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and every time I and my sister cried out, he forbade us from wailing. Al-Fadl b. al-Abbas washed him, along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and al-Abbas. He was placed on a bier and then carried. I saw him sitting at the edge of the grave, with al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib at his side. Al-Fadl b. Abbas and Usama b. Zayd descended into his grave. I was crying aloud at the grave, and no one forbade me. The sun was eclipsed that day, and the people said it was because of the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The sun is not eclipsed for the death or life of anyone.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed a gap in the bricks and commanded that it be filled, saying: 'When a servant does a deed, Allah loves that he perfects it.' He died on Tuesday, four nights having passed of Rabi' al-Awwal, in the year ten."],[21132,"Sarra' bt. Nabhan—who was a lady of standing in pre-Islamic times—told me: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Do you know which day this is?\" She said: It was the day you call the Day of Rūs. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"This is the middle of the Days of Tashrīq.\" He said: \"Do you know which land this is?\" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"This is al-Mashʿar al-Ḥarām.\" Then he said: \"I do not know; perhaps I will not meet you after this. Verily your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours in this land of yours, until you meet your Lord and He asks you about your deeds. Let those of you who are nearest convey to those farthest. Have I conveyed?\" When he came to Madinah, he remained only a short while until he died."],[21133,"The neighborhood dug in the house of Kilāb and discovered a treasure from the ʿĀd people. Kilāb said, 'It is our house,' while the neighborhood said, 'We dug it up.' They brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ruled in favor of the neighborhood and took the fifth from them. With our share of that, we bought a hundred camels, and we brought them to the neighborhood. The zakāh collector wanted to collect zakāh from us, but we refused and went to the Prophet ﷺ about that. He said, 'If you have mixed them with others, then no, otherwise there is nothing due from you this year.' He also said, 'When the zakāh collector departs from a people while he is pleased with them ؓ, and when he departs while he is angry with them, Allah is angry with them.'"],[21134,"I heard Sarrā’ bt. Nabhān al-Ghanawiyyah say: Nusayb, our slave, asked the Prophet ﷺ about snakes—which of them should be killed? She said: I heard him say, “Kill those of them that appear, the large and the small, the black and the white, for whoever among my Ummah kills one, it will be a ransom for him from the Fire; and whoever is killed by one, he is a martyr.”"],[21135,"I asked his wife just now, 'By Allah, will you be sold, O Sallama, on account of the debt?' I said, 'If Allah has decreed that against me, I will seek reward.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him my story. He said, 'Who is in charge of the estate of al-Hubab?' They said, 'His brother Abu al-Yusr b. ʿAmr.' He was summoned, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Set her free. When you hear of slaves that have come to us, come to me and I will compensate you for her.' So they set her free. Slaves then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he summoned Abu al-Yusr and said, 'Take from these slaves a boy for your brother's son.' He went and took a weak, sickly boy and left the strong, robust ones. I said, 'What prevented you from taking one of the strong ones?' He said, 'By Allah, I feared for my brother's son.' It was not long before he died. Ibn Ishaq said: I narrated this hadith to Rabiʿa b. ʿAbd al-Rahman, and he said, 'By Allah, ʿUmar only freed them because of this hadith.'"],[21136,"The Messenger of God ﷺ passed by me in the early days of Islam while I was tending sheep. He said, “O Salāma, what do you testify?” I said, “I testify that there is no god but God and that Muḥammad is the Messenger of God.” He smiled, laughing."],[21137,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “In Thaqīf there is a liar and a destroyer.”"],[21138,"From Salāma bt. al-Ḥurr, sister of Kharsha bt. al-Ḥurr, she said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “A time will come upon people when they will stand for an hour and not find an imam to lead them in prayer.”"],[21139,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “Among the signs of the Hour is that the people of the mosque will push one another forward and not find anyone to lead them in prayer.”"],[21140,"I saw Samrāʾ bt. Nahīk, and she had met the Prophet ﷺ. She wore a thick garment and a thick head covering, and in her hand was a whip. She disciplined people, enjoined good, and forbade evil."],[21141,"I was present when Fatimah was in labor and experiencing pain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and asked, \"How is she?\" We said, \"She is struggling.\" He said, \"When she gives birth, do not precede me in doing anything.\" She gave birth, and I wrapped the baby in a yellow cloth and cleaned him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and asked, \"How is she?\" I said, \"She has given birth, O Messenger of Allah, and I wrapped the baby in a cloth and cleaned him.\" He said, \"You have disobeyed me.\" I said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from the disobedience of Allah and His Messenger.\" I cleaned and wrapped the baby, and I could not find anything better than that. He said, \"Bring him to me.\" So I removed the yellow cloth and wrapped him in a white cloth, and he blew into him and dressed him in his own garments. Then Ali came and asked, \"What did you name him, O Ali?\" He said, \"I named him Ja'far, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No, but his name is Hasan, and after him will be Husayn, and you, O Ali, are the father of goodness.\""],[21142,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed for rain on Friday in the mosque, raised his hands, and said, “Seek forgiveness from your Lord; indeed He is ever Forgiving,” and he turned his cloak."],[21143,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Abū Jahm b. Ḥudhayfa over the spoils of war, and he struck a man with his bow, causing a wound that exposed the bone. The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled for it a compensation of fifteen camels."],[21144,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ one day to ask him something, and he began to make excuses to me while I was blaming him. Then the time for the noon prayer came, and I left. My daughter, who was married to Shuraḥbīl b. Ḥasana, came to me, and I found Shuraḥbīl in the house. I began to blame him, and he said, “O girl, do not blame me, for I had a garment that the Messenger of God ﷺ borrowed.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for him. I have been blaming him since today, not knowing his situation.”"],[21145,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was sitting with Ḥafṣa bt. ʿUmar. He said, “Why don't you teach this one the incantation for namla as you taught her writing?”"],[21146,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ when a man asked him, “Which deeds are best?” He said, “Faith in God, striving in the path of God, and an accepted pilgrimage.”"],[21147,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I want to strive in the path of God.” He said, “Shall I not direct you to a striving with no hardship in it?” The man said, “Yes.” He said, “Pilgrimage to the House.”"],[21148,"She heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The best deeds are faith in God, striving in the path of God, and an accepted pilgrimage.”"],[21149,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked which deeds are most virtuous, and he said: “Faith in God, striving in the cause of God, and an accepted Hajj.”"],[21150,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ to ask him for something, and he began to make excuses to me while I was reproaching him. Then the prayer time arrived, so I left and went in to see my daughter, who was married to Shurahbil b. Hasanah. I found Shurahbil in the house and said, “The prayer time has come and you are still in the house!” I began to reproach him, but he said, “O maternal aunt, do not blame me, for we had a garment that the Prophet ﷺ borrowed.” I said, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for him! I have been reproaching him since today when this is his situation, and I did not realize it.” Shurahbil said, “It was nothing but a worn-out cloak that we had patched.”"],[21151,"She used to perform a ruqyah incantation of hers from the pre-Islamic era (jahiliyyah), and when Islam came she said, “I will not perform it until I ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for permission.” So I went to him and sought his counsel, and he said, “Perform the ruqyah as long as it contains no shirk (associating partners with God).”"],[21152,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while a woman called al-Shifaʾ was with her, performing ruqyah for namlah (a skin ailment). The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: “Teach it to Hafsah.”"],[21153,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his grandmother al-Shifaʾ: “Teach Hafsah your ruqyah.”"],[21154,"“We saw women among the qawaʿid (older women past childbearing age) praying the obligatory prayers with the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[21155,"“We saw the qawaʿid women praying with the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque.”"],[21156,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ laying the foundations of the Mosque of Qubaʾ. Sometimes I saw him carrying a huge stone and pressing it against his belly. We would come to take it from him, but he would say, “Leave it and carry another one.” And Jibril ﷺ was directing him toward the Kaʿbah."],[21157,"I looked at the Messenger of God ﷺ when he arrived and alighted and laid the foundations of this mosque, the Mosque of Qubaʾ. I saw him taking a stone or a rock until the stone pressed against him, and I saw the whiteness of the dust on his belly and navel. A man from among his companions would come and say, “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of God, give it to me and let me spare you.” He would say, “No, take a stone like it,” until he had laid its foundations. And he said, “Jibril ﷺ is the one directing it toward the Kaʿbah.” She said: It was said that it was the mosque most accurately oriented toward the qiblah."],[21158,"“The Prophet ﷺ proposed to a woman from Kalb, and he sent ʿAʾishah to look at her.” Shaymaʾ bt. al-Harith b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzza b. Rifaʿah, the foster sister of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[21159,"“The Prophet ﷺ brought the women into one of the fortresses of Madinah on the Day of the Trench.” Hassan b. Thabit was a brave man, so he brought him in with the women and locked the door. A Jew came and sat at the gate of the fortress. Safiyyah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib said, “Go down, Hassan, to this infidel and kill him.” He said, “I would not put myself at risk for this infidel.” So she wrapped herself with a cloak, took a stone pestle, went down to him, and cut off his head."],[21160,"Safiyyah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib did not cover her head in front of the Messenger of God ﷺ nor in front of ten of the first Muhajirun: Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, her brother; Jaʿfar and ʿAli, the two sons of Abu Talib, the sons of her brother; al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwam, her son; ʿUthman b. ʿAffan, the son of her sister's daughter—his mother was Arwa bt. Kurayz, and her mother was al-Baydaʾ Umm Hakim bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; Abu Salamah b. ʿAbd al-Asad and Abu Sabrah b. Abi Ruhm, the two sons of her sister Barrah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; and the mother of Tulayb b. Numayr b. Wahb b. ʿAbd Qusayy, Arwa bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib; and the mother of ʿAbd Allah and Abu Ahmad the blind poet—his name was ʿAbd b. Jahsh b. Riʾab b. Yaʿmur b. Hubayrah b. Murrah b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzaymah—Umaymah bt. ʿAbd al-Muttalib. Safiyyah died during the caliphate of ʿUmar b. al-Khattab."],[21163,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and I offered him a shoulder blade I had been scraping; he ate it, then stood for prayer.\""],[21164,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for Uhud, he placed his women in a fortress called Fari', and placed with them Hassan b. Thabit.\" Hassan would watch for the Prophet ﷺ; if he pressed against the polytheists, he pressed with him in the fortress, and if he returned, he returned behind him. She said: Some people from the Jews came, and one of them climbed the fortress until he looked down upon us. I said to Hassan, 'Get up and kill him.' He said, 'That is not in me; if that were in me, I would have been with the Prophet ﷺ.' Safiyyah struck his head until she cut it off. When she cut it off, she said, 'O Hassan, get up and throw his head at them, for they are below the fortress.' He said, 'By Allah, that is not in me.' She said: So I took his head and threw it at them. They said, 'By Allah, we knew that Muhammad would not leave his family unguarded with no one with them,' and they dispersed and went away. She said: Sa'd b. Mu'adh passed by before, and upon him was a trace of yellow perfume, as if he had been a new groom before that, and he was saying"],[21165,"When the people were at ease on the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated on a camel, touching the Stone with a staff in his hand, then entered the Ka'bah while I watched. He saw a group of idols, stood up, broke them, and threw them away while I watched."],[21166,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wet a cloth while he was in the Ka'bah, then began striking the images that were in it.\""],[21167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated in the year of the conquest, when he entered Makkah, on his mount around the House, touching the corner with his staff."],[21168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform the sa'y, for the sa'y has been prescribed for you.\""],[21169,"I came to Safiyyah bint Shaybah, an elderly woman, and said to her, \"Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marry while he was in ihram?\" She said, \"No, and he married her while they were both out of ihram.\""],[21170,"\"Safiyyah bint 'Umar b. al-Khattab was with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar.\""],[21171,"She used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday and said, \"If one of you finds nothing but a green twig, let him break his fast with it.\""],[21172,"She used to say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on Saturday.\""],[21173,"that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Do not fast on Saturday except in what is obligatory upon you, and if one of you finds nothing but the bark of a tree, let him chew it.\""],[21174,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Do not fast on Saturday except in what its fasting is obligatory upon you, and if one finds nothing but the bark of a tree or a grape vine, let him chew it.\""],[21175,"She heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, \"Do not fast on Saturday unless it is a day that has been prescribed for you. And if one of you does not find anything except a piece of wood or the bark of a tree, let him chew on it.\""],[21177,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Do not fast on Saturdays unless it is an obligatory fast prescribed by Allah upon you.'\""],[21178,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in Madinah, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him.\" This is how Salih b. Abi al-Akhdar narrated it, and he was contradicted in its chain of transmission."],[21179,"From Sumaytah, a woman from Banu Layth b. Bakr who was in the care of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: I heard her telling Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for he will die as a martyr and intercession will be made for him.\""],[21180,"From an orphan woman who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in Madinah, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[21181,"From al-Dariyyah, a woman from Banu 'Abd al-Dar who was in the care of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies in it, I will be a witness or an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[21182,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[21183,"that Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I want to perform Hajj; should I make a condition?\" He said: \"Yes.\" She said: \"How should I say it?\" He said: \"Say: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me on earth.\""],[21184,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[21185,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: say: 'O Allah, my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[21186,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Make a condition: 'My place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[21187,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Duba'ah: \"Perform Hajj and make a condition: say: 'O Allah, indeed my place of leaving ihram is wherever You detain me.'\""],[21188,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib while she was ill. She said, \"I intend to perform Hajj, but I am ill.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition. Say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[21189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib: \"Do you intend to perform Hajj?\" She said, \"I am ill.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition, and say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[21190,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, who was married to al-Miqdād b. al-Aswad, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to her: \"Perhaps you intend to perform Hajj?\" She said, \"By Allah, I find myself only in pain.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition. Say: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[21191,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to a merchant, \"Perform Hajj and make a condition that my place of confinement is where you have detained me.\""],[21192,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to stipulate a condition in her ihram."],[21193,"She saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat a shoulder, then stand for prayer without performing wudu."],[21194,"She (Aisha) lifted some meat for the Prophet ﷺ, he took a bite from it, then he prayed without performing ablution."],[21195,"From Zaynab bint Nubayṭ, from Dubāʿah bint al-Zubayr, that the Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition.\""],[21196,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded her to enter ihram. She said, \"I am ill.\" He said to her: \"Stipulate a condition that my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\" When Ibn ʿAbbās heard this hadith, he said: \"Praise be to Allah. I would have done it, but I had not heard anything about it.\""],[21197,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was complaining of illness, and I mentioned Hajj to him. He said: \"Perform Hajj and stipulate a condition: O Allah, my place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[21198,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I was ill and said: \"Do you not intend to perform Hajj this year?\" She said, \"I am sick, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Perform Hajj and say: My place of exiting ihram is wherever You detain me.\""],[21199,"She had a sheep in her house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to her: \"Feed us from your sheep.\" She said to the messenger, \"Nothing remains with us except the neck, and I am ashamed to send it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" The messenger returned to him and informed him. He said: \"Go back to her and tell her: Send it, for it is the guide of the sheep, the closest part of the sheep to good, and the farthest from harm.\""],[21200,"My mother ʿAmrah bint Rawāḥah said to him: \"Come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and have him witness it.\" He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, saying: \"I have given my son al-Nuʿmān a gift, and ʿAmrah asked me to have you witness that.\" He said: \"Do you have any other children besides him?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Have you given all of them the like of what you gave al-Nuʿmān?\" He said, \"No.\" Some of these hadith narrators said: \"This is injustice,\" and others said: \"This is coercion. Have someone other than me witness this.\" Mughīrah said: \"Would it not please you that they be equal to you in dutifulness and kindness?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then have someone other than me witness this.\" Mujālid mentioned in his hadith: \"They have a right over you that you treat them justly, just as you have a right over them that they be dutiful to you.\""],[21201,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Going out is obligatory upon every possessor of a waist-wrapper.\""],[21202,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Going forth is obligatory upon every one who wears a loincloth.”"],[21203,"She prepared for the Prophet ﷺ a shelter in the form of palm branches, swept it and perfumed it, and slaughtered a sheep for him, from which he ate. Then he performed ablution and prayed the noon prayer (zuhr). Then she offered him some of its meat, and he ate and prayed the afternoon prayer (asr) without performing ablution."],[21204,"Her father went out with his zakat of two saʿs of dates and with his daughter ʿAmrah until he came to the Prophet ﷺ. He poured out the two saʿs, then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have a need to present to you.” He said: “And what is it?” He said: “That you supplicate for blessing for me and for her, and that you wipe her head, for I have no child other than her.” She said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on me.” She said: “I swear by Allah, it was as though the coolness of the palm of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upon my liver ever after.”"],[21205,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This world is sweet and green. Whoever takes from it with its due right, Allah blesses him in it. And many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection, the day he meets Him.”"],[21206,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: “This world is sweet and green. Whoever obtains something from it lawfully, that is the one for whom it is blessed. And how many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger will have the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[21207,"She entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, she and her sisters, to pledge allegiance to him; they were five. They found him eating dried meat. He chewed a piece of dried meat for them, then handed me the piece, and each one of them chewed a morsel of it. Then they met Allah without finding any bad breath in their mouths."],[21208,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him, and he took from her the pledge: “That you will not commit adultery, nor steal, nor bring a child that you falsely attribute to your husband, whether openly or secretly.” She said: “As for the open attribution, I know it. As for the hidden attribution, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know it. And it has occurred to me that it is harming the child, so I will never harm a child, ever.” He said: “And she never harmed a child of hers until she died.” The wording is that of the hadith of Ibn Abi Fudayk."],[21209,"I came with my mother Burayrah bt. al-Harith al-ʿAtwariyyah among some women of the Muhajirun, and we pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ while he had pitched a tent for him in al-Abtah. He took from us the pledge that we would not associate anything with Allah, [and the rest of] the verse. When we affirmed and stretched out our hands to pledge to him, he said: “I do not touch the hands of women.” Then he sought forgiveness for us, and that was our pledge."],[21210,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed ʿUthman b. Mazʿun on his cheek after he had died, and it is not known that he kissed anyone other than him."],[21211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is too great for Allah to take the two precious things of a Muslim and then admit him to the Fire” – meaning his two eyes."],[21212,"I was with my mother Raʾitah bt. Sufyan, a woman of Khuzaʿah, while the Prophet ﷺ was taking allegiance from the women, saying: “I take your allegiance upon your not associating anything with Allah, not stealing, not committing adultery, not killing your children, not bringing slander that you fabricate between your hands and feet, and not disobeying me in what is right.” She said: They lowered their heads. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Say: Yes, in what we are able to do.” So they said: “Yes, in what we are able to do.” I was saying as they said, and my mother was saying: “Say: Yes,” and I would say: “Yes.”"],[21213,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of the two blind ones.” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what are the two blind ones?” He said: “The torrent and the fierce camel.”"],[21214,"I saw a rider appear on Abu Qubays and shout: 'O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth for three things.' Then he took a rock from Abu Qubays and threw it at the washtub, and the rock split. There did not remain a single house among the houses of Quraysh but that a piece of it entered it, except the houses of Banu Zuhrah. Al-Abbas said: 'This is indeed a vision. Conceal it and do not mention it.' Al-Abbas went and met al-Walid b. Utbah b. Rabi'ah and mentioned it to him. Al-Walid mentioned it to his father, and the report spread. Al-Abbas said: 'I went out in the morning circumambulating the Ka'bah while Abu Jahl was among a group of Quraysh talking about Atikah's vision. When Abu Jahl saw me he said: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation, come to us. When I finished, I came and sat with them. Abu Jahl said: O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, is it not enough that your men prophesy until your women prophesy? Atikah claimed in her vision that he said: go forth for three things. We will wait for these three. If what she says is true, it will come to pass, and if the three pass without any of that happening, we will write against you a record that you are the most lying household among the Arabs.' Al-Abbas said: 'By Allah, my only response was to deny that and reject that she had seen anything.' Al-Abbas said: 'When evening came, a woman from among the daughters of Abd al-Muttalib came to me and said: Are you content that this wicked one attacks your men and then attacks your women while you listen and offer no objection? By Allah, if Hamzah had been present, he would not have said what he said. I said: By Allah, he did it and I offered no objection. By Allah, I will confront him, and if he returns to it I will suffice you.' Al-Abbas said: 'I went out on the third day after Atikah's vision, angry that I had missed something I wished to catch. By Allah, I was walking toward him—he was a light man with a sharp face, sharp tongue, and sharp eyes—when he came out toward the gate of the mosque hurrying. I said to myself: What is with him, may Allah curse him? Is all this fear of me that I might revile him? Then it turned out he had heard what I had not heard: he heard the voice of Damdam b. Zur'ah b. Amr al-Ghifari shouting in the valley, having cut the nose of his camel, turned his saddle, and torn his shirt, saying: O Quraysh, Muhammad has set out with his companions. I think you will not catch them. Help, help!' Al-Abbas said: 'Then what came of the matter distracted me from him and distracted him from me.'"],[21215,"Atikah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was living with her brother al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib. She saw a vision shortly before Badr and was alarmed. She sent to her brother Abbas that night when she was alarmed and woke from her sleep, saying: I saw a vision and fear destruction for your people. He said: What did you see? She said: I will not tell you until you promise me that you will not mention it, for if they hear it they will harm us and make us hear what we dislike. Abbas promised her. She said: I saw a rider coming on his mount from the upper part of Makkah, shouting at the top of his voice: O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth in two or three nights. Then he entered the mosque on his mount and shouted three shouts in the mosque. Men, women, and children gathered around him and the people were terrified by him with the greatest terror. Then I saw him on the back of the Ka'bah on his mount, and he shouted three shouts: O treacherous ones, O wicked ones, go forth in two or three nights, until he made the people between the two mountains of Makkah hear. Then he went to a great rock, pulled it from its base, and sent it upon the people of Makkah. The rock came with a rumble until when it was at the foot of the mountain, it shattered. I do not know of any house or dwelling in Makkah but that a piece of that rock entered it. I feared that evil would befall your people. Abbas was alarmed by it and left her. At the end of that night he met al-Walid b. Utbah b. Rabi'ah, who was a close friend of al-Abbas. He told him Atikah's vision and ordered him not to mention it to anyone. Al-Walid mentioned it to his father, Utbah mentioned it to his brother Shaybah, and the report circulated until it reached Abu Jahl b. Hisham and spread widely. When morning came, Abbas went out to circumambulate the House. He found Abu Jahl, Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, Umayyah b. Khalaf, Zam'ah b. al-Aswad, and Abu al-Bakhtari among a group talking. When they saw Abbas circumambulating the House, Abu Jahl called out: O Abu al-Fadl, when you finish your circumambulation, come to us. When he finished, he came and sat. Abu Jahl said: O Abu al-Fadl, what vision did Atikah see? He said: She saw nothing. He said: Indeed. Is it not enough for you, O Banu Hashim, with the lies of men, that you have come to us with the lies of women? We and you were like two racehorses, competing for glory for a long time. When the knees drew level, you said: Among us is a prophet. Nothing remains but for you to say: Among us is a prophetess. I do not know among Quraysh a household more lying in men or more lying in women than you. They harmed him that day with the severest harm. Abu Jahl said: Atikah claimed that the rider said: go forth in two or three nights. If these three pass, your lying will become clear to Quraysh, and we will write a document and hang it on the Ka'bah that you are the most lying household among the Arabs, man and woman. Is it not enough for you, O Banu Qusayy, that you took the hijabah, the council, the watering, the provision, and the support, until you came to us claiming a prophet from among you? They harmed him that day with the severest harm. Abbas said to him: Gently, O you who dyes his anus, will you stop? Lying is in you and your household. Those present said to him: O Abu al-Fadl, you were not ignorant or senile. Abbas met severe harm from Atikah for spreading her report. When it was the evening of the third night of the nights in which Atikah saw the vision, the rider whom Abu Sufyan had sent, Damdam b. Amr al-Ghifari, came to them and said: O Banu Ghalib, go forth. Muhammad and his companions have set out to intercept Abu Sufyan, so protect your caravan. Quraysh were terrified with the greatest terror and feared Atikah's vision, and they went forth on every difficult and tractable mount."],[21217,"A'ishah said: 'Atikah bt. Zayd was married to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq.'"],[21218,"She said, \"I sent a slaughtered sheep to the Prophet ﷺ, but he rejected it and said, 'Send a sheep that does not produce milk.'\""],[21219,"From Umm Ma'bad: a clothing allowance and something from the produce of Yemen and tar for her camels used to come to her. Uthman passed by her and she said: 'Where is my clothing allowance and where is the produce of Yemen that used to come to me?' He said: It is yours, O Umm Ma'bad, with her. He followed her until he gave it to her."],[21220,"Abu Bakr addressed us and prohibited us, or he prohibited, praying on pack-saddles."],[21221,"She was called Azzah, and she was among the early women. She said: Abu Bakr addressed us and said: 'Do not pray on pack-saddles.'"],[21222,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"When an elderly man and an elderly woman commit adultery, stone them to death immediately for the pleasure they have enjoyed.\""],[21223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-Ghumaysa': 'No, until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness.'"],[21224,"From Ali b. Husayn regarding His saying: {and a believing woman if she gives herself to the Prophet} — that it was Umm Sharik al-Azdiyyah who gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ."],[21225,"When Fatimah bt. Asad b. Hashim, the mother of Ali b. Abi Talib, died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and sat at her head and said: 'May Allah have mercy on you, O my mother. You were my mother after my mother. You fed me while you went hungry, and clothed me while you went unclothed, and denied yourself good things and gave them to me, seeking thereby the face of Allah and the Hereafter.' Then he ordered that she be washed three times. When the water with the camphor was brought, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poured it with his hand. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed his shirt and clothed her in it, and shrouded her with a garment over it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Usamah b. Zayd, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Umar b. al-Khattab, and a black slave to dig, and they dug her grave. When they reached the lahd, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dug it with his hand and removed its earth with his hand. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and lay down in it, then said: 'O Allah, who gives life and causes death, and He is living and does not die, forgive my mother Fatimah bt. Asad, prompt her with her proof, and widen her entrance, by the right of Your Prophet and the prophets before me, for You are the most merciful of the merciful.' He said the takbir over her four times, and he, al-Abbas, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ placed her in the lahd."],[21226,"Fatimah bt. Muhammad used to suffice him for the inside, and Fatimah bt. Asad used to suffice him for the outside, meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[21227,"I said to my mother, Fatimah bt. Asad b. Hashim: 'Suffice Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for carrying water and going for needs, and she will suffice you for the service of the inside: grinding and kneading.'"],[21228,"A client of mine died and left his daughter, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided his wealth between me and his daughter, giving me half and her half."],[21229,"A slave of ours who had a contract of manumission died—she had freed him—and he left his daughter. The Messenger of God ﷺ divided his inheritance, giving his daughter half and Umm al-Fadl the remaining half."],[21230,"She freed a slave of hers, then he died and left his daughter and his mistress, the daughter of Hamzah. His daughter inherited half, and the daughter of Hamzah inherited half."],[21231,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter, so he divided it between the two of them."],[21232,"The daughter of Hamzah's client died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided the wealth between them in two halves."],[21233,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter, so the Prophet ﷺ gave the daughter of Hamzah half and his daughter half."],[21234,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy, and he died leaving a daughter. The daughter of Hamzah took half and his daughter took half during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[21235,"He said: \"Do you know what the daughter of Hamzah is to me? She is my sister through my mother. She freed a man, and he died, so his inheritance was divided between her and her.\" I said: \"During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"During the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[21236,"A daughter of Hamzah b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib freed a slave boy of hers, and he died during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ leaving a daughter, so the two of them divided the wealth between them in two halves."],[21237,"The daughter of Hamzah freed a slave boy of hers during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he died leaving a daughter. So the Prophet ﷺ gave the daughter of Hamzah half and gave his daughter half."],[21238,"A client of the daughter of Hamzah died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Prophet ﷺ gave his daughter half and the daughter of Hamzah half."],[21239,"A daughter of Hamzah, who was a sister of ʿAbd Allah b. Shaddad b. al-Had through his mother, her client died leaving his daughter and the daughter of Hamzah, so the Messenger of God ﷺ divided the wealth into two halves."],[21240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifted me a striped silk garment and told me, “Make it into veils among the Fatimahs.” So I tore from it three veils: a veil for Fatimah bt. Asad, a veil for Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ, and a veil for Fatimah bt. Hamza."],[21241,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.”"],[21242,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh used to have prolonged vaginal bleeding, so she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, “It is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, leave the prayer, and when it ends, perform ghusl and pray.”"],[21243,"that Fatimah b. Abu Hubaysh said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I have irregular bleeding, shall I abandon the prayer?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"That is only from a vein and it is not menstruation. When the menstruation begins, then abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash off the blood and pray.\""],[21244,"Fatimah bt. Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “When menstruation begins, leave it for its usual duration, then wash away the blood and pray.”"],[21245,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh sought the Prophet’s ﷺ legal opinion and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and perform wudu, for it is only a vein, not menstruation.”"],[21246,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and pray.”"],[21247,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I am a woman who has prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash away the traces of blood from yourself and pray.”"],[21248,"“O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and the blood does not stop from me.” He said, “Abandon the prayer during the days of your menstruation. When the days of your menstruation pass, perform ghusl and perform wudu for every prayer.”"],[21249,"Abdullah b. Maslama al-Qa’nabi narrated to us, my father Maslama b. Qa’nab narrated to me, from Hisham b. Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself and pray.”"],[21250,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and I see blood.” He ordered her to sit out the days of her menstrual cycles. When her time of purity came, she performed ghusl, then performed wudu for every prayer. He said, “It is only a vein from you.”"],[21251,"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh al-Asadiyya came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his legal opinion. She was a woman who had prolonged vaginal bleeding and said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not become pure. Should I abandon the prayer because of this?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “That is only a vein, not menstruation. When it begins, abandon the prayer, and when it ends, wash the blood from yourself, then pray.”"],[21252,"“O Messenger of Allah, I have prolonged vaginal bleeding and do not become pure. Should I then abandon the prayer?” He said, “That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation begins, abandon the prayer, and when it departs” or he said “ends,” “perform ghusl to wash away the blood and pray.”"],[21253,"From Fatimah bt. Qays, of Banu Asad of Quraysh, that she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to her that she was suffering from prolonged menstrual bleeding. Fatimah claimed that he said: \"That is only a vein. When the menstrual period comes, then abandon the prayer; and when it departs, then wash away the trace of blood from yourself, then pray.\""],[21256,"I reached into a pot of ours and burned my hand. My mother took me to a man sitting in the cemetery and said to him, \"O Messenger of God.\" He said, \"At your service, and at your command.\" Then she brought me close to him. He began to blow gently and speak words I did not know what they were. My mother asked afterwards what he used to say. She said he used to say: \"Remove the affliction, Lord of the people. Heal, for You are the Healer; there is no healer except You.\""],[21257,"\"Abu Hudhayfah b. Utbah went with her and her sister Hind to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" When he stipulated conditions upon them, Hind said, \"Or do you know of any of these faults and blemishes among the women of your people?\" Abu Hudhayfah said, \"Pledge allegiance to him, for thus are the conditions stipulated.\""],[21260,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ did not assign her any lodging or maintenance.\""],[21278,"To return to her dwelling, and he asked her what prompted her to move before her waiting period ended. She sent to inform him that her maternal aunt Fatimah bint Qays had given her the ruling that the Messenger of God ﷺ had ruled for her when Abu ʿAmr b. Hafs al-Makhzumi divorced her—she was to go out, or move. Marwan sent Qabisah b. Dhu'ayb to Fatimah bint Qays to ask her about that, and she informed him that she had been the wife of Abu ʿAmr b. Hafs al-Makhzumi. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ had appointed ʿAli over part of Yemen, and her husband went out with him. He sent her a divorce that remained for her, and he instructed ʿAyyash b. Abi Rabiʿah and al-Harith b. Hisham to spend on her. They said, \"By God, she has no maintenance unless she is pregnant.\" She asked his permission to move, and he permitted her. She said, \"Where shall I move, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"To Ibn Umm Maktum,\" and he was blind; she could put down her garments with him and he would not see her. She remained there until her waiting period ended, and the Prophet ﷺ married her to Usamah b. Zayd. Qabisah returned to Marwan and informed him of that, and Marwan said, \"I have not heard this tradition except from a woman; we shall adhere to the established practice that we found the people upon.\" Fatimah said when that reached her, \"Between me and you is the Book of God. God said, 'Divorce them at their waiting periods' up to His saying, 'You do not know; perhaps God will bring about something after that.'\" She said, \"What matter will be brought about after the three divorces? It is only the man's taking back his wife. So how can you say she has no maintenance if she is not pregnant? How can a woman be detained without maintenance?\""],[21280,"\"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to do that.\" Then she related her story and said, \"I argue against you with the Book of Allah. Allah says in His Book: {When you divorce women, divorce them at their 'iddah, and keep count of the 'iddah, and fear Allah, your Lord. Do not turn them out of their houses, nor shall they leave, unless they commit a clear immorality.} {You do not know; perhaps Allah will bring about after that a matter.} The confinement was not for the sake of revocation. Then He said: {When they have reached their term} the third, {then retain them with kindness or release them with kindness.} By Allah, Allah did not mention after the third any confinement after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to do that.\" He said: So I returned to Marwan and informed him, and he said, \"The statement of a woman, the statement of a woman.\" Then he ordered regarding the woman, and she was returned to her house until her 'iddah was completed.\""],[21284,"She said: I entered upon Fatimah bt. Qays, and her husband had divorced her three times. She said, \"He gave me as mut'ah three sa's of barley and three sa's of dates.\" She said, \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to stay with Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is blind and will not see me when I remove my head covering.\" He said, \"When you become lawful, do not act before me.\" When I became lawful, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Did anyone mention you?\" I said, \"Yes, Mu'awiyah and Abu Jahm.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"As for Abu Jahm, he is harsh in character with his wives, and as for Mu'awiyah, he has no wealth. But marry Usamah.\" I said, \"Usamah?\" out of disdain for the matter of Usamah. Then I said, \"Hearing and obedience to Allah and His Messenger.\" So he married me to Usamah. \"And Allah honored me through Ibn Zayd, and Allah elevated me through Ibn Zayd, and Allah benefited me through Ibn Zayd.\""],[21285,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant her lodging or maintenance.\""],[21335,"I entered upon Fatimah bint Qays and asked her about her divorce. She mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have no dwelling nor maintenance.\" She said, a caller for the congregational prayer announced and ascended the minbar, and said, \"Tameem Al-Dari informed me,\" and he mentioned the hadith of Al-Jassasah in its entirety."],[21337,"The Prophet ﷺ visited a woman of the Ansar while she was in pain. He said to her: 'How do you find yourself?' She said: Fine, except that Umm Mildam has afflicted me—meaning the fever. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Be patient, for it removes the filth of the son of Adam as the bellows removes the filth of iron.'"],[21346,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a drink on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He drank from it, then handed it to me, and I drank, and I was fasting. I said, “O Messenger of God, I drank while I was fasting.” He said, “Were you making up something for yourself?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then it does not harm you.”"],[21347,"From his grandmother Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib: The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “God favored Quraysh with seven qualities that were not given to anyone before them, nor will they be given to anyone after them. God favored Quraysh in that I am from them, for prophethood is among them; the guardianship of the Kaaba is among them; the provision of water to pilgrims is among them; He aided them against the elephant; they worshiped God for ten years during which no one else worshiped Him; and God revealed a surah of the Quran concerning them that was not revealed concerning anyone else.”"],[21389,"That she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was judging between people, and he continued judging between them until the day had risen. Then he stood and prayed the forenoon prayer, eight rak'ahs."],[21398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest. I said, 'Will you not excuse me from 'Ali?' He said, 'What is the matter with him?' I said, 'A man came to me and sought my protection, and 'Ali said, \"Get away from me, or I will run you through with the spear,\" and he struck me on the front of my head.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Ali would not strike you.'"],[21407,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed in Makkah two rak'ahs and four, and did not repeat it."],[21408,"Umm Hani' came with two men, and 'Ali wanted to kill them. She went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, 'We have granted protection to those whom Umm Hani' has protected.'"],[21411,"He ate a shoulder, then prayed and did not perform ablution — meaning the Prophet ﷺ."],[21412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed overnight in my house on the night he was taken on the Night Journey. I missed him during the night, and sleep was withheld from me for fear that some of Quraysh had waylaid him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Jibril came to me, took me by the hand, and brought me out. There, at the house, was a riding beast, smaller than a mule and larger than a donkey. He mounted me upon it, then departed until he brought me to Jerusalem. He showed me Ibrahim, whose physical appearance resembled mine and mine resembled his. He showed me Musa, dark-skinned, tall, with lank hair; I likened him to the men of Azd Shanu'ah. He showed me 'Isa son of Maryam, of medium height, fair with a reddish tinge; I likened him to 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. He showed me the Dajjal, his right eye obliterated; I likened him to Qatan b. 'Abd al-'Uzza. I wanted to go out to Quraysh and tell them what I had seen, but she took hold of his garment and said, \"I remind you of Allah: you will go to a people who will reject you and deny your words, and I fear they will assault you.\" She said: He pulled his garment from my hand, then went out to them. He came to them while they were sitting and told them what he had told me. Jubayr b. Mut'im stood up and said, \"O Muhammad, if I were the young man I used to be, you would not have uttered this while you are among us!\" A man from the people said, \"O Muhammad, did you pass by camels of ours in such-and-such a place?\" He said, \"Yes, by Allah, I found them; they had lost a camel of theirs and were searching for it.\" He said, \"Did you pass by the camels of Banu so-and-so?\" He said, \"Yes, in such-and-such a place; a red she-camel of theirs had broken down, and I found them with a wooden bowl of water, and I drank what was in it.\" They said, \"Tell us their number and how many herdsmen were among them.\" He said, \"I was too preoccupied to note their number.\" Then he left. The camels were brought, and he counted them and learned how many herdsmen were among them. Then he came to Quraysh and said, \"You asked me about the camels of Banu so-and-so: they are such-and-such, and among their herdsmen are so-and-so and so-and-so. You asked me about the camels of Banu so-and-so: they are such-and-such, and among their herdsmen are Ibn Abi Quhafah and so-and-so and so-and-so. They will reach you in the morning at the mountain pass.\" So they went early to the pass to see if he had spoken the truth. They met the camels and asked, \"Did a camel of yours go astray?\" They said, \"Yes.\" They asked the other group, \"Did a red she-camel of yours break down?\" They said, \"Yes.\" They said, \"Did you have a wooden bowl?\" Abu Bakr said, \"By Allah, I placed it there, and no one drank from it or poured it on the ground.\" Abu Bakr confirmed him and believed in him, and from that day he was called al-Siddiq."],[21413,"Umm Hani' bint Abi Talib went out displaying her adornment, her two earrings showing. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said to her, 'Know that Muhammad will not avail you anything.' So she came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with people who claim that my intercession will not reach my household? Indeed, my intercession will reach Ha and Hukm' — Ha and Hukm are two tribes."],[21414,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has become heavy; teach me something I can say while I am sitting.' He said, 'Say Allahu Akbar one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred adorned, accepted camels. Say Subhan Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred saddled, bridled horses that you would ride in Allah's cause. Say Alhamdu lillah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred slaves from Banu Isma'il whom you would set free. Say La ilaha illa Allah one hundred times; it leaves no sin and no deed outpaces them.'"],[21416,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her on the Day of the Conquest and prayed Duha six rak'ahs."],[21417,"She said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Duha in my house on the Day of the Conquest, eight rak'ahs.'"],[21418,"The Prophet entered and said, \"Why do I not see any blessings with you?\" So I said, \"Which blessings do you want?\" He said, \"Indeed, Allah has sent down three blessings: sheep, palm trees, and fire.\""],[21419,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ praying Duha — except Umm Hani', for she mentioned that on the day of the conquest of Makkah he performed ghusl in her house and prayed eight rak'ahs. I never saw him pray a lighter prayer, but he completed its bowing and prostration."],[21420,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, and I said, 'It is not that I have no desire for you, O Messenger of Allah, but I would not like to marry while my children are young.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Why? The best women who have ridden camels are the women of Quraysh — the most tender to a child in his infancy and the most protective of a husband with regard to what he possesses.'"],[21421,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me and said, 'Do you have anything?' I said, 'No, except dry pieces of bread and vinegar.' He said, 'No household is poor that has vinegar as a condiment.'"],[21422,"The Prophet ﷺ was given a sleeveless garment as a gift. He sent it to Ali, who started wearing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali, \"I would not be pleased with something that I am not pleased with for myself. I did not give it to you for you to wear it, but I dressed you in it so that it may serve as a distinction between the Fatimah lines.\""],[21423,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me on the day of the conquest of Makkah, covered with dust. He ordered a bowl, and I can almost see the traces of dough in it. I poured water into it, and he ordered a garment to be placed between me and him as a screen. Then he stood and poured water over himself, then he stood and prayed Duha eight rak'ahs. Mujahid said: I narrated this hadith to Ibn 'Abbas, and he said, 'That is the Ishraq prayer.'"],[21424,"that she said: O Messenger of God, I have grown old and weak, so teach me a supplication by which I may attain [reward]. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “O Umm Hāniʾ, if you glorify God one hundred times, it is better than one hundred slaves you would set free. And if you praise God one hundred times, it is better than one hundred horses you would mount in the way of God. And if you declare God’s oneness one hundred times, no deed will outstrip it, and no sin will remain with it.”"],[21425,"that she asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Will we visit one another when we die, and will some of us see others? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “The souls will be birds that cling to trees, until when the Day of Resurrection comes, every soul will enter its body.”"],[21426,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “I gave to my maternal aunt Fākhitah bt. ʿAmr a servant boy, and I commanded her not to make him a butcher, nor a goldsmith, nor a cupper.”"],[21427,"that her husband went out in pursuit of runaway slaves until when he was at the edge of al-Qudūm, which is a mountain, he caught up with them and they killed him. So she came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to him that her husband had been killed and that he had left her in a dwelling that was not his, and she asked permission to move. He gave her permission. She departed, and when she was at the door of the room, he ordered that she be called back. He told her to repeat her account to him, and she did. Then he ordered her not to leave her husband’s house until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21428,"from Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, she informed her that she was married to a man of the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj. He went out in pursuit of runaway slaves of his and caught up with them at the edge of al-Qudūm, and they attacked him and killed him. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: “Until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21430,"that her husband went out in pursuit of a servant boy of his and was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked his permission to move to her family. He gave her permission, but when she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21431,"that Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd, whose husband was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm, asked the Prophet ﷺ permission to go to her family in Madinah. He gave her permission, then said: “No, until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21432,"that Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, informed her that her husband went out until when he was six miles from Madinah at the edge of a mountain called al-Qudūm, thieves attacked him and killed him. Furayʿah was among the Banū al-Ḥārith b. al-Khazraj in a dwelling that did not belong to her husband; it was only a residence. Their brothers came, among them Abū Saʿīd, and said: We have no surplus to give you and keep you, and nothing suits us except that we be together, and we fear loneliness for you, so ask the Prophet ﷺ. She came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked his permission to be with them. He said: “Do so if you wish.” She turned away, and when she was in the room, he said: “Come back, repeat what you said.” She repeated it, and he said: “Stay in your dwelling until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21433,"from Furayʿah bt. Mālik, sister of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that her husband went out in pursuit of runaway slaves of his and was killed at the edges of al-Qudūm. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned to him her situation and mentioned moving to her brothers. The Prophet ﷺ gave her permission. When she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term: four months and ten days.”"],[21434,"that she was with her husband in one of the villages of Madinah, and he pursued runaway slaves and they killed him. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned to him the loneliness and that she was in a house that was not hers, and that she asked permission to go to his brothers in Madinah. He gave her permission, then called her and said: “Stay in your house in which the news of his death came to you until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21435,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that her husband had been killed at al-Qudūm and that she had family. He ordered her to move, but when she turned away, he called her and said: “Stay in your house until the prescribed period reaches its term: four months and ten days.”"],[21437,"My husband set out seeking runaway slaves until when he was at the edge of al-Qudūm, they caught up with him and killed him. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: My husband was killed at the edge of al-Qudūm, and my husband left me neither a dwelling nor wealth, and I want to move to my brothers so that it would be better for our affairs. She said: He gave me permission. I went out, and when I was in part of the room, the Prophet ﷺ called me and said: “Stay in the house in which the news of your husband’s death came to you until the prescribed period reaches its term.”"],[21438,"From al-Furay'ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that her husband Bakkar hired some 'uluj (non-Arab laborers) to work for him, and they killed him. She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I said, 'I am not in a dwelling that belongs to him, nor does any provision from him come to me, so I will move to my family and my orphans and take care of them.' He said, \"Do so.\" Then it occurred to him otherwise, and he said, \"Observe your waiting period where the news reached you.\""],[21439,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik. (H) And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us; 'Abdullah b. Yusuf narrated to us; Malik informed us; from Sa'd b. Ishaq b. Ka'b b. 'Ujrah; from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b; from Furay'ah bint Malik, that her husband was struck down at the edge of al-Qudum, so she sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ to go to her family. Then he said, \"No, not until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[21440,"My husband went out in search of some 'uluj (laborers) of ours, and he caught up with them at the edge of al-Qudum, and they killed him. News of his death came to me while I was in a house far from the houses of my family. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked his permission to go to my family, and he gave me permission. Then he said, \"No, not until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[21441,"That her husband went out in search of some 'uluj (laborers) belonging to him, until when he was at the edge of al-Qudum, they killed him. The news reached her while she was in a house far from her family, so he gave her permission. Then when she was in the room, he called her back and said, \"Stay where the news came to you until the prescribed term reaches its end.\""],[21446,"\"That she saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eat bread and meat and then pray without performing ablution.\""],[21447,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, so we brought him a foreleg of a sheep, and he ate. When the prayer time came, he rinsed his mouth, then stood and prayed without performing ablution.\""],[21448,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ visited them, ate the shoulder of a sheep, then prayed without performing ablution.\""],[21450,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed part of the prayer with him. When he finished the prayer, I stood up, and he looked at me—and she was a tall woman—and said, \"If the son of this woman was fighting from behind the barrier.\" She said, \"By Allah, it was indeed so, O Messenger of Allah, but he died.\" She said, \"Write a document for me,\" and I had three daughters with me. So he wrote: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Qaylah and the three women: \"They shall not be wronged in any right, nor shall they be compelled into marriage. Every believer or Muslim is a guardian and helper for them. If they do well, let them not do evil.\""],[21451,"Qaylah bint Makhramah, when she had taken her place in bed after the late evening prayer, would say: In the name of Allah, and upon Allah I rely. I have laid my side down for my Lord, and I ask His forgiveness for my sin. She would say this repeatedly, then she would say: I seek refuge in Allah and in His perfect words, which neither a righteous person nor a wicked person can overstep, from the evil of what descends from the heaven and what ascends into it, from the evil of what descends into the earth and the evil of what comes out from it, from the evil of the trials of the day and the evil of those that come by night, except one that comes with good. I believe in Allah and hold fast to Him. Praise be to Allah, to whose power every thing has submitted; praise be to Allah, before whose might every thing has humbled itself; praise be to Allah, before whose greatness every thing has lowered itself; and praise be to Allah, before whose dominion every thing has bowed in humility. O Allah, I ask You by the bonds of might from Your Throne, by the utmost mercy from Your Book, by Your highest majesty, by Your greatest Name, and by Your perfect words, which neither a righteous person nor a wicked person can overstep, that You look upon us with a merciful look, leaving no sin of ours except that You forgive it, no poverty except that You mend it, no enemy except that You destroy him, no unclothed person except that You clothe him, no debt except that You settle it, and no matter in which there is benefit for us in this world and the Hereafter except that You grant it to us, O Most Merciful of the merciful. I believe in Allah and hold fast to Him. Then she would say: Glory be to Allah thirty-three times, Allah is greater thirty-three times, and praise be to Allah thirty-four times. Then she would say: O my daughter, this is the chief concluding practice: the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him seeking a servant from him, and he said: \"Shall I not direct you to something better than a servant?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So he instructed her to say these hundred at the time of lying down after the late evening prayer."],[21452,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Marwah, having come out of ihram from an 'umrah. I sat by him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who buys and sells. Sometimes I want to sell a commodity and I ask for it a price higher than what I intend to sell it for, then I reduce it until I sell it for what I intend. And when I want to buy a commodity, I offer for it less than what I intend to take it for, then I increase until I take it for what I intend.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not do that, O Qaylah. When you want to sell a commodity, ask for it the price you intend to sell it for, whether you are given it or refused. And when you want to buy a commodity, offer for it the price you intend to take it for, whether you are given it or refused.\""],[21453,"A learned man (habr) from among the learned men came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, what an excellent people you are, were it not that you associate partners with Allah.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"You say when you swear: 'By the Ka'bah.'\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused for a while, then said, 'Whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah.' Then he said, 'O Muhammad, what an excellent people you are, were it not that you set up rivals to Allah.'\" He said, \"Glory be to Allah! And what is that?\" He said, \"You say to a man, 'What Allah wills and you will.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ paused, then said, \"He has spoken. So whoever says, 'What Allah wills,' let him put between them, 'then you will.'\""],[21455,"A Jew and a learned man (habr) came to the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"You associate partners with Allah and you set up rivals. You say, 'No, by the Ka'bah,' and you say, 'What Allah wills and you will.'\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to say, \"No, by the Lord of the Ka'bah,\" and to say, \"What Allah wills, then you will.\""],[21456,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me while I had a water-skin hanging, so he drank from the mouth of the water-skin while standing. I then cut off the mouth of the water-skin, seeking blessing through that."],[21457,"I said, “O Messenger of God, I buried alive four of my sons in the Jāhiliyyah?” He said, “Free four slaves.” She said, “So I freed your father Saʿīd, his two sons Maysarah and Jubayr, and the mother of Maysarah.” She said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ said to us, “The blood of a fair-skinned woman is purer in the sight of God than the blood of a black-skinned woman.”"],[21458,"ʿAkkāf b. Wadāʿah came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said, “O ʿAkkāf, do you have a wife?” He replied, “O Messenger of God, I will not leave until you marry me to whomever you wish.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I have married you, in the name of God and with blessing, to Karīmah bt. Kulthūm al-Ḥimyarīyah.”"],[21459,"Kulaybah – or Kulthūm – bt. Burthun al-ʿAnbarīyah called me and said, “O my son, this man took my zarbiyyah (ornamental carpet) which I used to wear.” So I met the man and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and I said, “O Messenger of God, this man took my mother’s zarbiyyah.” He said, “Return to him his mother’s zarbiyyah.”"],[21460,"Lubābah bt. al-Ḥārith b. Ḥazn b. Bujayr b. Rībah b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Hilāl b. ʿĀmir b. Ṣaʿṣaʿah b. Muʿāwiyah."],[21461,"The Prophet ﷺ broke his fast at ʿArafah; she brought him milk and he drank."],[21462,"The Messenger of God ﷺ broke his fast at ʿArafah, and Umm al-Faḍl sent him milk, so he drank at ʿArafah."],[21463,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought milk at ʿArafah and he drank while he was delivering the sermon."],[21464,"I brought Umm Ḥabībah bt. al-ʿAbbās to the Prophet ﷺ when she was a little girl, and I placed her in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. She urinated, so I struck her on the back, then picked her up. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Stop.” Then he called for a cup of water and poured it over the place where she had urinated, then said, “Pour water over the place of urination.”"],[21465,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite Surah Al-Mursalat during Maghrib prayer."],[21466,"that Umm Al-Fadl bint Al-Harith heard him reciting \"By those sent forth in succession\" and she said, \"O my son, you reminded me of your recitation of this Surah, for it is the last thing I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer.\""],[21467,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray Maghrib, and he recited therein “By those sent forth in succession” (al-Mursalāt). That was the last prayer he prayed; he did not pray after it."],[21468,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting in the Maghrib prayer with the Mu'assalat verses, which are well-known."],[21469,"“(She was) Lubabah” that she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting ‘By the winds sent forth one after another...’[Al-Mursalat (77)] in the Maghrib. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 831)"],[21470,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting the Mu'awwidhat (Surahs of seeking refuge from evil) in Maghrib prayer."],[21471,"His mother, Umm al-Faḍl bt. al-Ḥārith, informed him that she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in Maghrib “By those sent forth in succession,” and then he did not pray until God Almighty took his soul."],[21472,"Umm al-Faḍl heard me while I was reciting “By those sent forth in succession,” and she said, “O my son, this is the last sūrah I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ recite in the Maghrib prayer.”"],[21473,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Maghrib with us in his house, wearing a single garment wrapped around him. He did not pray any prayer after it until he was taken ﷺ."],[21474,"O Messenger of Allah, I had a wife and I married another woman in addition to her, and the first one claimed that she had breastfed the younger one. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[21475,"A woman was divorced by her husband, then he married another woman, and his wife claimed that she had breastfed her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[21476,"O Messenger of Allah, I married a woman while I already had another wife, and she claimed that she had breastfed the younger one. He said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[21477,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about a single suckling: does it create a marriage prohibition? He said: “No.”"],[21478,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “One suckling or two sucklings do not create a marriage prohibition, nor do one or two breastfeedings.”"],[21479,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: “One or two breastfeedings, or one or two sucklings, do not create a marriage prohibition.”"],[21480,"While I was sitting at the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was ill, I wept. He said: “What makes you weep?” I said: I fear for you, and we do not know what we will face from the people after you. He said: “You are the ones who will be deemed weak after me.”"],[21481,"May Allah bless His Messenger. He recited in the Maghrib prayer “By those sent forth in succession” (al-Mursalat). He did not lead us in Isha until Allah, Exalted is He, took him."],[21482,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us from Malik. And Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us from Abu al-Nadr, the freedman of ‘Umar b. ‘Ubayd Allah b. Ma‘mar, from ‘Umayr, the freedman of Ibn ‘Abbas, from Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith, that some people differed in her presence on the day of ‘Arafah about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some said he was fasting, and others said he was not fasting. So she sent him a bowl of milk while he was standing on his camel, and he drank it at ‘Arafah."],[21483,"They were uncertain about the fasting of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at ‘Arafah. Umm al-Fadl said: “I will resolve that for you.” So she sent him a large cup of milk and he drank from it."],[21484,"He heard Umm al-Fadl saying, \"People had doubts about fasting on the Day of Arafah, while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I sent him a container of milk and he drank it while he was in Arafah.\""],[21485,"The people were uncertain about the Prophet's ﷺ fasting on the day of ‘Arafah. I said: “I will resolve that for you.” So I sent him a vessel containing milk, and he drank."],[21486,"Umm al-Fadl came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I saw part of your body in my house.” He said, “Good is what you saw. Fatimah will give birth to a boy and you will nurse him with the milk of Qutham.” She said, “So she brought him, carrying him, to the Prophet ﷺ. Then she took him and placed him in his lap, and he urinated. So I slapped him with her hand, and he said, ‘You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you.’ She said, ‘Give me your waist-wrapper so that we may wash it.’ He said, ‘The urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled.’”"],[21487,"Umm al-Fadl said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if part of your body was in my house.” He said, “Good. Fatimah will give birth and you will nurse him.” Then she gave birth to Hasan or Husayn, and she nursed him. Then she brought him to the Prophet ﷺ one day and placed him in his lap, and he urinated, so she struck his shoulder. The Prophet ﷺ said, “You have hurt my son, may Allah have mercy on you.””"],[21488,"Al-Hasan b. Ali urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so I said, “Give me your garment and wear another.” He said, “The urine of a female is washed, and the urine of a male is sprinkled.”"],[21489,"I said to the Prophet ﷺ, “I saw in a dream as if a part of you was in my house.” He said, “Good. Fatimah will give birth to a boy and you will nurse him in your house.” Then she gave birth to Hasan, and he was in my house. I brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he urinated on him. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, throw away this garment so that I may wash it.” He said, “The urine of females is washed, and the urine of a male is not washed.”"],[21490,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream a distressing vision.” He said, “And what is it?” She said, “May Allah keep you righteous; it is severe.” He said, “What is it?” She said, “I saw as if a piece of your body was cut off and then placed in my lap.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Good have you seen. Fatimah will give birth, if Allah wills, to a boy who will be in your lap.” Then Fatimah gave birth to Hasan, and he was in her lap. I entered with him upon the Prophet ﷺ and placed him, and he urinated on him. I went to take him, and he said, “Leave my son, for my son is not impure.” Then he called for water and poured it on him."],[21491,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: He stood one night in Makkah during the night and said, “O Allah, have I conveyed?” three times. Then Umar b. al-Khattab stood up and said, “O Allah, yes. You have striven, advised, and exerted yourself.” In the morning he said, “Faith shall certainly prevail until it drives disbelief back to its homelands, and they shall certainly cross the seas with Islam. And there shall come upon people a time when they learn the Quran, and they learn it and recite it, then they say, ‘We have recited and we have learned, so who is better than us?’ Is there any harm in those?” They said, “No, O Messenger of Allah. And who are those?” He said, “Those are the fuel of the Fire.”"],[21492,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon al-Abbas while he was ill and wishing for death. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O uncle, do not wish for death, for if you are a good-doer, then being delayed will increase you in good upon your good, and if you are an evildoer, then being delayed so that you may seek pardon for your evil is better for you. So do not wish for death.”"],[21493,"“I was a woman who went out with the Prophet ﷺ tending to the wounded.”"],[21494,"He is called Dawud; Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan gave birth to him. From Layla bt. Qanif al-Thaqafiyyah, she said: “I was among those who washed Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The first thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us was the waist-wrapper, then the shift, then the head-cover, then the outer sheet, then she was wrapped in the final garment.”"],[21495,"“Where to, O Umm Abdullah?” I said, “You have harmed us in our religion, so we go in Allah’s land where we will not be harmed in the worship of Allah.” He said, “May Allah accompany you.” Then he left, and my husband Amir b. Rabi’ah came to me, and I told him about the softness I saw in Umar. He said, “Do you hope that he will become Muslim?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “By Allah, he will not become Muslim until the donkey of al-Khattab becomes Muslim.”"],[21496,"Among the women who witnessed the Aqabah were Lubaysah and her sister, the two daughters of Ka’b b. Amr b. Awf, and she is Umm Umarah whose son Musaylimah seized."],[21497,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, and she called for food for him. He invited her to eat with him, and she said, “I am fasting.” He said, “When a fasting person eats in their house, the angels invoke blessings for them until they finish their eating and complete it.”"],[21498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to see me, and I brought him some fruit or food. Some of the people withdrew and did not eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with them?\" I said, \"They are fasting.\" He said, \"No fasting person has people who are not fasting eat in his presence except that the angels send blessings upon them until evening.\""],[21499,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I see that everything is only for men; I do not see women being mentioned with anything.\" Then it was revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} (Quran 33:35)."],[21500,"A woman called Umm 'Umara came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the Quran is only revealed concerning men.\" Then Allah revealed this verse: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women}."],[21501,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see that everything is only for men.\" Then Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, revealed: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} - the verse."],[21502,"From Maymunah - not Maymunah the wife of the Prophet ﷺ - that she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is the land of gathering and resurrection. Go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers.\" She said, \"What do you think about someone who is unable to undertake the journey to go there?\" He said, \"If he cannot do that, then let him send oil to it to be used as fuel for its lamps. Whoever sends a gift to it is like one who prayed in it.\""],[21503,"From Maymunah, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis.\" He said, \"It is the land of gathering and resurrection. Go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers.\" She said, \"What do you think if we are unable to undertake the journey to it or to go to it?\" He said, \"Then send to it oil to be used as fuel for its lamps, for whoever sends a gift to it is like one who prayed in it.\""],[21505,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a man who kissed his wife while they were both fasting. He said, \"They have broken their fast.\""],[21506,"Narrated by Maymunah bint Sa'd, the freed slave woman of the Prophet ﷺ , that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about the child born out of wedlock, and he said, \"There is no goodness in them. Two sandals that I use in fighting are dearer to me than freeing a child born out of wedlock.\""],[21507,"She said, \"Give us a ruling, O Messenger of Allah, about a man who forgot to pray until the sun rose or set. What is its expiation?\" He said, \"When he remembers it, let him pray it and perform his prayer well, and let him perform ablution and perform his ablution well. That is its expiation.\""],[21508,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about fasting.\" He said, \"Three days from every month. Whoever is able to fast them, then indeed each day expiates ten bad deeds, and it cleanses from sin as water cleanses a garment.\""],[21509,"She said, \"Give us a ruling, O Messenger of Allah, about stolen property.\" He said, \"Whoever consumes it while knowing that it is stolen has shared in the sin of its thief.\""],[21510,"\"Indeed, it is a veil from the Fire for the one who performs it well, seeking thereby the face of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted.\""],[21511,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about the dog.\" He said, \"It is a leftover of the Jahiliyyah, and Allah has made us free from need of it.\""],[21512,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about the ghusl from janābah. He said: Wet the roots of the hair and clean the skin, for the likeness of those who do not perform the ghusl well is like a tree that water strikes, yet its leaves do not sprout and its roots are not watered. So fear God and perform the ghusl well, for it is among the trust you have been charged with and the secrets you have been entrusted with. She said: I said: How much water suffices for the head, O Messenger of God? He said: Three handfuls."],[21513,"I said: O Messenger of God, may one of us eat while he is junub? He said: He should not eat until he performs wuḍūʾ. She said: I said: O Messenger of God, may the junub sleep? He said: I do not like that he sleep while he is junub until he performs wuḍūʾ and does his wuḍūʾ well, for I fear that he may die and Jibrīl ﷺ will not attend him."],[21514,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about the Friday prayer. He said: In it there is an hour in which the servant does not call upon his Lord but that He answers him. I said: Which hour is it, O Messenger of God? He said: That is when the imam stands."],[21515,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about a man who erred in his prayer and does not know how much he prayed. He said: He should depart, then stand in his prayer until he knows how much he prayed, for that is only whispering that comes to him and makes him forget his prayer."],[21516,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, from what is the punishment of the grave? He said: From the trace of urine. So whoever is afflicted by urine, let him wash it, and if he finds no water, let him wipe it with pure dust."],[21517,"She said: Give us a ruling, O Messenger of God, about one who did not go on campaign but gave his wealth so that others campaign with it: does he have a reward, or the one who set out? He said: He has the reward of his wealth, and the one who set out has the reward of what he counted upon from that."],[21518,"From Maymūnah bt. Saʿd, who was a servant of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The likeness of a woman who walks proudly in adornment in other than her own people is like the darkness of the Day of Resurrection: she has no light."],[21519,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: No woman goes out in a display of perfume, and men look at her, but that she remains in God's displeasure until she returns to her house."],[21520,"From Maymūnah bt. ʿAsīb, the freedwoman of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that a woman from Ḥarīsh came to the Messenger of God ﷺ on a camel and called out: O ʿĀʾishah, help me with a supplication from the Messenger of God ﷺ that will calm me or reassure me. He said to her: Place your right hand on your heart and say: In the name of God. O God, heal me with Your healing, and cure me with Your cure, and enrich me with Your bounty from all besides You, and ward off from me Your harm. Rabīʿah said: I supplicated with it and found it good. Al-Muntajiʿ said: I think Rabīʿah said in this hadith that the woman was jealous."],[21521,"She heard her father asking the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: I vowed that I would certainly slaughter at Buwānah. He said: Is there an idol or a tyrant worshipped there? He said: No. He said: Fulfill your vow where you vowed."],[21522,"Her father met the Prophet ﷺ while she was riding behind him, and he asked him, saying: I vowed to slaughter at Buwānah. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Is there an idol there? He said to him: No. He said: Then fulfill your vow where you vowed."],[21523,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and his toe that is next to the big toe was longer than the big toe, meaning of the foot."],[21524,"He hears of me and does not see me but that he loves me. I said, \"And how do you know that, O Abu Hurayrah?\" He said, \"My mother was a polytheist woman, and I used to call her to Islam, but she refused me. One day I called her, and she made me hear about the Messenger of God ﷺ what I disliked. So I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ weeping and said, 'O Messenger of God, I used to call my mother to Islam, but she refused me, and I called her and she made me hear about you what I disliked. So supplicate to God to guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O God, guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah.' He said, 'I went out running to give her the good news of the supplication of the Messenger of God ﷺ. When I came to the door, it was closed, and I heard the splashing of water and she heard the sound of my feet. She said, \"O Abu Hurayrah, stay where you are,\" and she opened the door, put on her shift, and hurried to her veil. Then she said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but God and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God.\" So I returned to the Messenger of God ﷺ weeping from joy as I had wept from sorrow, and I said, \"O Messenger of God, God has answered your supplication for my mother. So supplicate to God to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to us.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'O God, make Your servant and Your female servant beloved to Your believing servants, and make them beloved to the two of them.'\""],[21525,"About his grandmother Maria, who was a servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , she said, \"I have never seen a hand softer than that of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[21526,"\"I stooped for the Messenger of God ﷺ until he climbed a wall on the night he fled from the polytheists.\""],[21527,"I complained of a pain in my throat, so I came to her, and she put for me cow's ghee. She said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Its milk is a cure, its ghee is a remedy, and its meat is a disease.'\""],[21528,"that it should be recent from you, so you seek to be clear of it by one menstrual period. Al-Rubayyi' said, \"ʿUthman took that only from the saying of the Prophet ﷺ to Maryam al-Maghaliyyah, the wife of Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas, and I obtained divorce from him by khulʿ.\""],[21529,"that the Prophet ﷺ said to Nuʿma bt. Jaʿfar, \"Why do I see the bodies of the sons of Jaʿfar emaciated? Do they have a need?\" She said, \"No, but the evil eye is quick to affect them. Should I perform ruqyah on them?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She presented some words to him that were acceptable, and he said, \"Perform ruqyah on them with it.\""],[21530,"We prayed Zuhr or ʿAsr in the mosque of Banu Harithah, and we faced the mosque of Jerusalem (Iliya), and we prayed two rakʿahs. Then someone came to inform us that the Messenger of God ﷺ had turned to face the Sacred House. So the men moved to the place of the women, and the women moved to the place of the men, and we prayed the remaining two prostrations while facing the Sacred House. A man from Banu Harithah told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Those are men who believed in the unseen.'"],[21531,"I was with ʿAʾishah, and she had slaughtered a sheep of hers. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered with a small staff in his hand, which he threw down, then he went to the mosque and prayed two rakʿahs in it, then he went to his bed and lay down on it. Then he said, \"Is there any breakfast?\" We brought him a large bowl containing barley bread, and in it was a piece, and a piece of the stomach, and in it was the foreleg. She said, \"He took a piece of the stomach, and while he was chewing it, she said, 'We slaughtered a sheep today, and we did not keep anything except this.' She said, 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No, rather all of it was kept except this.\"'\""],[21532,"\"We washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ. He ordered us to wash her with lote-tree leaves three times, or if not, five times, or if not, more than that. We considered that more than that would be seven times.\""],[21577,"I heard this from the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , regarding women who do not have a jilbab (outer garment): Do they witness the celebration? She said: Yes, by my father. Whenever she spoke about the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , she would say: By my father, I heard the Messenger of Allah, ﷺ , saying, \"Allow the unmarried women and those who menstruate to attend the Eid prayer and the supplication of the Muslims, but let them stay away from the prayer area.\""],[21579,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to go out on the day of the two Eids, even the young girls and unmarried women. Ḥafṣah said: A woman said to Umm ʿAṭiyyah, “And the menstruating women?” She said, “And the menstruating women go out, keeping away from the prayer place, and remember Allah.”"],[21580,"“He took a pledge from us at the time of the oath of allegiance that we would not wail. None of them fulfilled it except five: Umm Sulaym, Umm al-ʿAlāʾ, the daughter of Abī Sabrah, Umm Muʿādh the daughter of Abī Sabrah, and another woman.”"],[21581,"We gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ. He recited to us that we should not associate anything with God, and he forbade us from wailing. A woman among us withdrew her hand and said, 'O Messenger of God, so-and-so helped me (in mourning), and I want to repay her.' He said nothing to her. She went away, then came back and said, 'No woman among us fulfilled it except Umm Sulaym, Umm al-'Ala', the daughter of Abu Sabrah, and the wife of Mu'adh.'"],[21582,"Among what the Messenger of God ﷺ took from us at the pledge of allegiance was that we should not wail."],[21583,"We gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and among what he commanded us of good was that we should not wail. A woman said, 'O Messenger of God, the family of so-and-so helped me (in mourning), so I will not give you allegiance until I help them.' She said, 'So I helped them, then I gave him allegiance.' She said, 'No woman among us fulfilled it except me and Umm Sulaym.'"],[21584,"From Umm 'Atiyyah regarding His saying {and they will not disobey you in what is right}, she said: Part of it is wailing. I said to the Prophet ﷺ when we gave allegiance to him that we would not disobey him in what is right: 'O Messenger of God, except the family of so-and-so.'"],[21585,"That we should mourn for a deceased person beyond three days, not applying perfume, not applying kohl, and not wearing a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb (a Yemeni cloth). She said: He permitted them when they bathe after purification to use qust and azfar (types of incense)."],[21586,"\"The deceased wife does not mourn except for her husband, she does not put on henna, perfume, or wear colored clothing except for a garment made of cotton.\" Hisham narrates from Hafsah, from Umm Atiyyah, from the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ something similar to this."],[21587,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No one should mourn for a deceased person beyond three days except a woman, for she mourns for her husband four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a garment of 'asb, nor apply kohl, nor apply perfume except at the time of her purification, when she may apply qust and azfar.'"],[21589,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A woman should not mourn beyond three days except for her husband, for she mourns four months and ten days. She should not wear a dyed garment except a washed garment, nor apply kohl, nor dye with henna, nor touch perfume except when she has purified from her menstruation, after that with qust or azfar.'"],[21590,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21591,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21592,"About following funeral processions, and it was not made obligatory upon us."],[21595,"About following funeral processions, and he did not make it obligatory upon us."],[21596,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon 'A'ishah and said, 'Do you have anything?' She said, 'No, except something that Nusaybah, who is Umm 'Atiyyah, sent to us from the sheep that was sent to her as sadaqah (charity).' He said, 'It has reached its proper place.'"],[21597,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿĀʾishah: “Do you have anything to feed me?” She said: “No, except from the sheep that Nusaybah sent to me from the zakāh.” He said: “Bring it, for it has reached its destination.”"],[21598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me a sheep from the zakāh, and ʿĀʾishah sent me some of it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to ʿĀʾishah, he said: “Do you have anything?” She said: “No, except that Nusaybah sent us from the sheep that I sent to her.” He said: “It has reached its destination.”"],[21599,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah, who had pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ, she said: “We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge after the ritual bath as anything.”"],[21600,"“We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge after purification as anything.”"],[21601,"“We used not to consider the yellowish or brownish discharge as anything.”"],[21602,"One of the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ came to us and said: “Wash her with lote leaves, and wash her an odd number of times — three, or five, or more than that if you see fit — and put camphor in the last washing. When you finish, inform me.” She said: “When we finished, we informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: ‘Shroud her in it.’” She said: “We braided her hair into three braids, her forelock and two side braids, then we placed them behind her.”"],[21603,"From Umm ʿAṭiyyah al-Anṣāriyyah: One of the daughters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Wash her with water and lote leaves, and wash her an odd number of times, three or five or more if you see fit, and put camphor or some camphor in the last washing. When you finish, inform me.” We informed him, and he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: “Shroud her in it.” She said: “So we braided her hair into three braids, her forelock and two side braids, and placed them behind her.”"],[21606,"“We washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ and parted her hair into three braids.”"],[21607,"I heard Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn say: Umm ʿAṭiyyah told us that they made the hair of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ into three braids. I said: “Did she undo it, wash it, and then make it into three braids?” She said: “Yes.”"],[21608,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding washing his daughter: “Begin with her right side and the places of ablution from her.”"],[21609,"From Umm al-Hudhayl, who is Ḥafṣah bint Sīrīn, from Umm ʿAṭiyyah, she said: “When we washed the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, he said to us while we were washing her: ‘Begin with her right side and the places of ablution.’”"],[21610,"Umm ʿAṭiyyah told us: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us not to withhold the māʿūn.” I said: “What is the māʿūn?” She said: “What people lend to one another.”"],[21611,"I heard Umm ʿAṭiyyah say: \"We used to go out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to treat the wounded and bury the slain.\""],[21612,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to instruct us to guard our private parts and our tongues, and he said: \"They bring you in [to ruin] and do not bring you out.\""],[21613,"When the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"Wash her an odd number of times, three or five, and put camphor in the last [wash], or something of camphor. When you have washed her, inform me.\" So we informed him. She said: He threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: \"Wrap her with it.\""],[21614,"A daughter of the Prophet ﷺ died. The Prophet ﷺ entered and said: \"Wash her an odd number of times, three or five, or as you see fit, and make it odd.\" So we washed her. Then he entered and threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: \"Wrap her with it beneath her shroud, and put camphor in the last [wash].\""],[21615,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from wearing gold and from silver-plating vessels. The women spoke to him about wearing gold, but he refused us, and he permitted us to silver-plate vessels."],[21616,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAlī on a military expedition. I saw him raising his hands and saying: \"O Allah, do not cause me to die until You show me ʿAlī.\""],[21617,"I was among the women who escorted one of the Prophet's ﷺ daughters to her husband. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: \"When she performs ghusl, pour water over her head three times.\" Yaḥyā said: I said to Sharīk: \"From janābah?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[21618,"He said to her: \"Who was this person with you?\" She said: \"There was no one with me, and I did not wake up until you woke me.\" He said: \"Join your family.\" People talked about her. Her father said to her: \"My little daughter, people have spoken a lot about you. So tell me your story. If the man has spoken truthfully against you, you sent someone to kill him, so the slander would be cut off from you. But if he was lying, you would have taken him to one of the soothsayers of Yemen for judgment.\" She swore to him by what they used to swear by that he was indeed lying against her. Then he said to al-Fākih: \"O man, you have accused my daughter of a grave matter. So take me to one of the soothsayers of Yemen for judgment.\" So ʿUtbah went out with a group from Banū ʿAbd Manāf, and al-Fākih went out with a group from Banū Makhzūm, and Hind went out with them along with some women. When they approached the land, and they said: \"We will go to the soothsayer,\" Hind's condition changed and her face changed. Her father said to her: \"I see what is upon you of changed condition, and that is only because of something hateful to you. Would that this had been before people witnessed our journey!\" She said: \"No, by Allah, my father, it is not because of something hateful. But I know that you are coming to a human being who errs and is right, and I do not feel safe that he will name me with a mark that will be a disgrace upon me among the Arabs.\" He said: \"I will test him before he looks into your affair.\" He whistled to his horse until it lowered [its head], then he took a grain of wheat and inserted it into its urethra and tied a strap over it. When they arrived in the morning, [the soothsayer] honored them and slaughtered for them. When they sat down, ʿUtbah said to him: \"We have come to you about a matter, and I have hidden something for you to test you with. So look at what it is.\" He said: \"A she-camel in a ...?\" He said: \"I want something clearer than this.\" He said: \"A grain of wheat in the urethra of a horse.\" He said: \"You are right. Look into the affair of these women.\" He began to approach one of them, strike her shoulder, and say: \"Rise,\" until he approached Hind, struck her shoulder, and said: \"Rise, you are neither unchaste nor an adulteress, and you will give birth to a boy who will be called Muʿāwiyah.\" Then al-Fākih rose to her and took her hand, but she pulled her hand away from his and said: \"Away with you! By Allah, I will be keen for that [child] to be from other than you.\" Then Abū Sufyān married her, and she gave birth to Muʿāwiyah."],[21619,"Hind came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, there was no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be humiliated by Allah than your household, and today there is no household on the face of the earth more beloved to me to be honored by Allah than your household.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"And also, by the One in Whose hand is my soul.\" Maʿmar said: meaning they will surely increase. Then she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abū Sufyān is a stingy man. Is there any sin upon me if I take from his wealth to support his dependents without his permission?\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"There is no harm upon you to spend on them with what is reasonable.\""],[21620,"ʿAbdullāh b. Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Hishām b. ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, who said: Hind, the mother of Muʿāwiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"Abū Sufyān is a miserly man and he does not give me what suffices me and my child except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any sin upon me in that?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take what suffices you and your children, with what is reasonable.\""],[21621,"Hind, the mother of Muʿāwiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Abū Sufyān is a miserly man and he does not give my children except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there anything upon me in that?\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Take what suffices you and your children, with what is reasonable.\""],[21622,"'Hind came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man and he does not give me enough for me and my child, except for what I take from his wealth without him realizing.' He said: Take what is sufficient for you and your child, on a reasonable basis.' \" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2293)"],[21623,"Hind, the mother of Mu'awiyah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a stingy man, and he does not give me and my children enough except what I take from him without his knowledge. Is there any blame on me in that?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Take what suffices you and your children in a reasonable manner.\""],[21624,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man. Should we feed our slaves from his wealth?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[21625,"Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? She said, \"Yes, I heard him say, 'The first thing to be weighed in the Balance is good character.'\""],[21626,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband's house or her mothers' houses except that she has torn every veil between her and the Most Merciful ﷻ.\""],[21627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"O Muslim women, you should adhere to glorification (tasbih), declaring God's oneness (tahlil), and sanctification (taqdis). Count them on your fingertips, for they will be made to speak and will be questioned, and they will not be heedless, lest you forget the mercy.\" Abu Kurayb attributed Hani b. 'Uthman, saying: al-Juhani."],[21628,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding women to attend to glorification, declaring God's oneness, and sanctification, and to count them on their fingertips, saying, \"They will be questioned and made to speak.\" Ibn Dawud said, \"It has reached me that al-Thawri asked Hani about this hadith.\""],[21629,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Muslim, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated to us, from his uncle Ibn Shihab, from Humayd b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" (Qul huwa Allahu ahad), and he said, \"It is a third of the Quran or equal to it.\""],[21630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21631,"From his mother Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah, one of the first emigrant women, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, saying, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people.\""],[21633,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good.\""],[21634,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He is not a liar who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying good.\""],[21635,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying it.\""],[21636,"He informed him that his mother, Umm Kulthūm bt. ʿUqbah, who was among the female companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ and among the first female emigrants who gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and conveys good or says good.”"],[21637,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “A liar is not the one who says something to reconcile between people.”"],[21638,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people, who says good or conveys good.”"],[21639,"They gave allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ. She informed him that she heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21640,"I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ permit lying in anything except in three cases. The Messenger of God ﷺ would not count it as lying: a man who reconciles between people, adding to the speech while intending reconciliation; a man who speaks in war; and a man who talks to his wife, and a woman who talks to her husband.”"],[21641,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ permit lying except in three cases. The Messenger of God ﷺ would say, “I do not count it as lying: a man who reconciles between people, a man who speaks in war, and a man who talks to his wife and a woman who talks to her husband.”"],[21642,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21643,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21644,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21645,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “He is not a liar who says good or conveys good.”"],[21646,"That she heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"He who makes peace between the people by inventing good information or saying good things, is not a liar.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2692)"],[21648,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “He is not a liar who reconciles between people and conveys good or says good.”"],[21649,"She heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, “He is not a liar who reconciles between two people.”"],[21650,"From Umm Kulthum bt. ʿUqba b. Abī Muʿayṭ, and she was the wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf, and she had prayed in the direction of both qiblas with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He is not a liar who makes peace between people and says good or conveys good.”"],[21651,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “The best charity is that given to a hostile relative.”"],[21658,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: Which deeds are best? He said: “Faith in Allah, then prayer at the beginning of its time.”"],[21684,"“I did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye his hair until he died.”"],[21685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Umm Habibah bt. al-‘Abbas as she toddled in front of him, and he said ﷺ: “If this one reaches [maturity] while I am alive, I will marry her.” He was taken before she reached [maturity], so al-Aswad b. ‘Abd al-Asad married her, and she bore him Rizq b. al-Aswad and Lubabah bt. al-Aswad, whom she named after her mother, Umm al-Fadl."],[21701,"From Umm 'Uthman bt. Sufyan, the mother of Shaybah's child, who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ called Shaybah, and he opened the House. When he entered, he bowed and placed his sides."],[21705,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was ʿAli, who was convalescing. She said: We had hanging clusters of grapes. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up to eat, and ʿAli stood up to eat. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Gently, for you are convalescing.” She said: So ʿAli sat down, and the Prophet ﷺ ate from them. Then I served them chard and barley. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Eat from this.”"],[21713,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ in the house of Hafsah, and he was saying, “No man who was present at Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah will enter the Fire.” Hafsah said, “O Messenger of God, God says: {And there is none of you but will come to it; this is, upon your Lord, a decree that must be accomplished.}” He said, “Then what?” She said, {Then We will save those who feared God and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees.}"],[21718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you about the best of people, a man?” They said, “Yes indeed.” He pointed with his hand toward the east and said: “A man holding the reins of his horse in the path of Allah, waiting to raid or be raided upon. Shall I not tell you about the best of people after him, a man?” They said, “Yes indeed.” He pointed with his hand toward the Hijaz and said: “A man among his sheep, who establishes the prayer, gives the zakah, knows what is due to Allah from his wealth, and has withdrawn from people.”"],[21737,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take a midday nap at my place. I would spread a leather mat for him, and he would nap on it and sweat. I would mix musk with his sweat. Muhammad b. Sirin said, 'I asked Umm Sulaym for some of that musk, and she gave me some. When Muhammad died, he was embalmed with that musk, and Muhammad liked to embalm the deceased with musk.'"],[21738,"Umm Sulaym was with Abu Talha al-Ansari on the day of Hunayn, and she had a dagger. Abu Talha said to her, 'What is this with you, O Umm Sulaym?' She said, 'A dagger I have taken; if any of the polytheists comes near me, I will rip his belly with it.' Abu Talha said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umm Sulaym says? She says such and such.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, some of the freed captives who came after us fled with you, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Umm Sulaym, Allah has sufficed and done well.'"],[21761,"She said to Safiyyah, \"Are you the one who will cause us to fail? Indeed, you are holding us back.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What is that?\" 'A'ishah said, \"Safiyyah has menstruated.\" He said, \"It was said that she has already performed the Ifadah.\" He said, \"Then no, in that case.\" He said, \"So they returned to Ibn 'Abbas and said, 'We found the hadith as she narrated it to us.'\""],[21774,"When the Prophet ﷺ went on the expedition to Badr, I said, “O Messenger of God, permit me to go on a raid with you to treat your wounded and nurse your sick, so that perhaps God may grant me martyrdom.” He said, “Stay in your house, for God will grant you martyrdom.” She was called “the martyr,” and she had recited the Qur’an. She asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to make a place in her house to pray, and he permitted her."],[21775,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “O Abū Ayyūb, the divorce of Umm Ayyūb is a sin.”"],[21776,"That the Prophet ﷺ stopped at her place. She said, “We made him food containing some of these herbs.” Sufyān said, “Leeks and other things.” He disliked it and said to his companions, “Eat, for I am not like one of you; I fear I would offend my companion [the angel].”"],[21777,"That she asked the Prophet ﷺ, “Will we visit each other when we die, and will we see one another?” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The soul will be a bird that hangs on the trees, until on the Day of Resurrection every soul enters its body.”"],[21778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No zakah is due on newly acquired wealth until a year passes over it.”"],[21779,"She went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, as the sixth of six women. News of that reached the Prophet ﷺ, so he sent for her and said, “With whose permission did you women set out?” I saw anger in him. We said, “O Messenger of Allah, we set out with medicine to treat the wounded, we hand arrows, serve sawiq, spin hair, and help in the cause of Allah.” He said to us, “Stay put.” When Allah granted him victory over Khaybar, he allotted us a share just as he allotted the men. I asked, “What was that?” She said, “Dates.”"],[21797,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Saʿd b. ʿUbāda, greeted him, but he did not respond and remained silent. She said: Saʿd regretted it and said to me: Go to the Messenger of God ﷺ and tell him that we remained silent hoping that he would give us more. She said: Then he came and greeted at the door; I heard his voice but did not see him. She said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'What are you?' She said: 'I am Umm Mildam.' He said: 'You? Then no welcome to you and no greetings.'"],[21798,"She brought a small skin of ghee to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered Bilāl, who squeezed it and then returned it to her. She went back and found it full, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: Has something been revealed concerning me, O Messenger of God? He said: 'And what is that, O Umm Mālik?' She said: Why did you return my gift to me? He called Bilāl and asked him about that. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I squeezed it until I felt embarrassed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Congratulations to you, O Umm Mālik; this is a blessing whose reward God has hastened.' Then he taught her to say after every prayer: 'Glory be to God' ten times, 'Praise be to God' ten times, and 'God is greatest' ten times."],[21801,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do not soak dates and raisins together; soak each of them separately."],[21802,"I witnessed Aminah when she gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When labor struck her, I looked at the stars as they hung low until I said: They will surely fall upon me. When she gave birth, a light came out of her that illuminated the house we were in and the dwelling, so that there was nothing I looked at except light."],[21803,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, our husbands prevent us from praying with you, and we love to pray with you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your prayer in your houses is better than your prayer in your rooms, and your prayer in your rooms is better than your prayer in your courtyards, and your prayer in your courtyards is better than your prayer in congregation.'"],[21809,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned a tribulation and said: 'The best of you in it, and the best of people in it, is a man who withdraws with his wealth, worships Allah, and gives His due, and a man who takes hold of his horse's head, frightening the enemy and they frighten him.'"],[21836,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was stoning Jamrat al-‘Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice from the bottom of the valley, and he was saying: “O people, do not kill one another. Stone with pebbles like those used for khazf.” He threw seven [pebbles], then left without stopping. Behind him was a man shielding him from the people. I said: “Who is this?” They said: “Al-Fadl b. ‘Abbas.”"],[21837,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the meat of domestic donkeys. He said: “Does it not graze on pasture and eat trees?” The man said: “Yes.” He said: “Then eat of its meat.”"],[21842,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “Hasten the iftar and delay the suhur.”"],[21843,"I brought a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet’s wives refused to accept it, saying, “We do not accept gifts.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, “Take the gift of Umm Sunbula, for she is from our desert people and we are from her settled people.” And he gave her the valley of such-and-such. Then Abdullah b. Hasan b. Hasan b. Ali b. Abi Talib bought it from her. He said: He gave her a small herd. Amr b. Qayzi said: I saw some of them. Abu Kurayb said: I said to Zayd b. al-Hubab, “Who gave it to her?” He replied, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[21855,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a young boy who wet himself, so he commanded to clean him up. Then, a young girl was brought to him who had menstruated, so he commanded to wash her.\""],[21856,"“Perhaps I used to contend with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over ablution water from a single vessel.”"],[21857,"Abd al-Munim Abu Said al-Harrani al-Iswari narrated to us, from al-Salt b. Dinar, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from a woman among them called Umm Afif, who said: “We gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he took allegiance from the women, and he enjoined upon them that they should not converse with a man except a mahram, and he commanded us to recite the Fatiha of the Book over our dead.”"],[21858,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a large bowl of tharid was brought. The Messenger of God ﷺ ate, and I ate with him, and Dhul-Yadayn ate with us. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ took a bone with meat on it and handed it to me. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" I said, \"I was fasting, then I forgot.\" Dhul-Yadayn said, \"Now, after you have eaten your fill?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"No harm upon you. It is only a provision that God has brought to you, so complete your fast.\""],[21859,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he ordered for me some barley porridge and clothed me with a cloak."],[21865,"The naqir is the hollowed-out base of palm trunks, that which the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade."],[21867,"Her father took her to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped his hand over her and blessed her. She said, \"She became a devout, righteous woman.\""],[21868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked out one evening and said, \"O people, are you not ashamed?\" They said, \"Of what, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"You gather what you do not eat, build what you do not inhabit, and hope for what you do not attain. Are you not ashamed of that?\""],[21869,"She went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him to provide them with a servant. The Messenger of God ﷺ had just arrived from a journey and had acquired some slaves. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"The orphans of the people of Badr have preceded you.\""],[21870,"I saw Budayl b. Warqa' on a camel following the people and proclaiming, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ orders you not to fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.\""],[21871,"From her mother, Umm Sinan al-Aslamiyyah, one of the women who gave the pledge, she said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of God, I have come to you with shyness, and I did not come to you until I was compelled by need.” He said, “If you were self-sufficient, it would be better for you.”"],[21872,"“O Prophet of God, what equals Hajj with you?” He said, “An ‘Umrah in Ramadan.”"],[21873,"“Umar ؓ allocated for the women of the emigrants in thousand thousand; among them was Umm ‘Abd.”"],[21874,"“He waited for Umm ‘Abd until she prayed over ‘Utbah.”"],[21875,"She sent to the Messenger of God ﷺ a bowl of milk at the time of his breaking the fast while he was fasting, and that was during the length of the day and intense heat. The Messenger of God ﷺ sent back to her: “How did you get this milk?” She said, “From a sheep of mine.” He sent back to her messenger: “How did you get this sheep?” She said, “I bought it with my own money.” So he took it from her. When it was the next day, Umm ‘Abd Allah came to him and said, “O Messenger of God, I sent you the milk as a gift for you because of the length of the day and intense heat, and you sent the messenger back about it.” He said to her, “With that the messengers were commanded: that we eat only what is pure and do only what is righteous.”"],[21876,"When Abu Musa became gravely ill, his wife cried out. He said, “Do you not know what the Messenger of God ﷺ said?” She said, “Yes,” then fell silent. It was said to her afterwards, “What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say?” She said, “The Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘God has cursed whoever shaves, tears, or wails.’”"],[21877,"I entered upon Abu Musa while he was in his final illness. His wife was about to weep or intended to, so Abu Musa said to her, “Have you not heard what the Messenger of God ﷺ said?” She said, “Yes,” and fell silent. When Abu Musa died, Yazid said: I met his wife and said to her, “Abu Musa’s saying: ‘Have you not heard what the Messenger of God ﷺ said,’ then you fell silent.” She said, “Yes, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: ‘He is not one of us who shaves, wails, or tears.’”"],[21878,"Umm Kabshah, a woman from ‘Udhrah of Quda‘ah, said: “O Messenger of God, permit me to go out with such-and-such an army.” He said, “No.” I said, “O Messenger of God, I do not intend to fight; I only intend to treat the wounded and the sick, or give water to the sick.” He said, “Were it not that it would become a sunnah and it would be said, ‘So-and-so went out,’ I would have permitted you. But sit.”"],[21879,"\"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding mixing two things, so I asked, 'And what are they?' He said, 'Dates and raisins.' And she was the mother of Mugheeth ibn Abi Abdur Rahman, and she had prayed towards both Qiblas during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' \""],[21880,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Every intoxicant is forbidden.”"],[21881,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ grew old and put on weight, he leaned on her."],[21882,"Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, who was one of the first emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ, informed me that she brought her son to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who had not reached the age of eating food, and she had pressed his uvula because of a throat ailment. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Why do you press your children’s throats with these? Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, one of which is pleurisy.” ‘Ubayd Allah said: Umm Qays informed me that her son urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, but did not wash it."],[21883,"Umm Qays bt. Mihsan entered with a son of hers who had not yet eaten food, and he urinated on the Messenger of God ﷺ, so he called for water and sprinkled it on him."],[21884,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik (h) and Bakr b. Sahl narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Yusuf narrated to us: Malik informed us (h) and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Utbah, from Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, that she brought a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she seated him in his lap, and he urinated on his garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it, and did not wash it."],[21885,"That she came to the Prophet ﷺ with a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it on it, and did not wash it."],[21886,"That she brought a small son of hers who had not yet eaten food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seated him in his lap, and he urinated on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it, and did not wash it."],[21887,"That she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a small son of hers upon whom she had hung amulets for 'udhrah (throat inflammation). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Why do you treat your children with these amulets? Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, among them pleurisy.\" 'Ubayd Allah said: And Umm Qays informed me that her son urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and poured it over the urine, and did not wash it."],[21888,"\"We entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with me was a son of mine who had not yet eaten food. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap, and he urinated on his garment. He called for water and sprinkled it on it, and did not wash it.\""],[21889,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Use this Indian wood—meaning costus—for it contains seven cures, among them pleurisy.\""],[21890,"\"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a son of mine who had not yet eaten food. He placed him in his lap, and he urinated on the garment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He called for water and sprinkled it on his garment, and did not wash it.\""],[21891,"From Umm Qays bt. Mihsan—and she was among the first of the emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she was the sister of 'Ukkashah bt. Mihsan—that she brought a son of hers who had not reached the age of eating food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for water and sprinkled it over the urine, and did not wash it."],[21892,"Um Qais said to me, \"If you could see me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding hands in a path from the streets of Madinah, where there is no house, until we reached the graveyard of Gharkad. He said to me, 'O Um Qais!' I said, 'Here I am, at your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'You will see this graveyard from which Allah will resurrect seventy thousand people on the Day of Resurrection, resembling the full moon on a night of the full moon. They will enter Paradise without any reckoning.' Ukashah stood up and said, 'Am I included in them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, you are.' Then another man stood up and said, 'Am I included in them, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Ukashah has beaten you to it.'\""],[21893,"From Abu al-Hasan, the mawla of Umm Qays bt. Mihsan, from Umm Qays, that she said: My son died, and I grieved over him. I said to the one washing him, \"Do not wash my son with cold water, lest you kill him.\" 'Ukkashah b. Mihsan went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him of her words. He smiled and said, \"What she said—may her life be long.\" We do not know of any woman who lived as long as she did."],[21894,"That she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about menstrual blood that gets on a garment. He said, \"Wash it with water and sidr (lote-tree leaves), and scrub it with a rib (of a palm leaf).\""],[21895,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from Bushayr b. Yasar, that Husayn b. Mihsan informed him that his paternal aunt entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day, and he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Look to how you are toward him, for he is your paradise and your hell.\""],[21896,"That she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a need, and he fulfilled her need. Then he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Look to how you are toward him, for he is your paradise and your hell.\""],[21897,"She came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"Do you have a husband?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"How are you toward him?\" She said, \"I do not fall short except what I am unable to do.\" He said, \"Know that he is your Paradise and your Hell.\""],[21898,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Al-Hajjaj b. Safwan narrated to us from Usayd b. Abi Usayd al-Barrad, from a woman among those who gave the pledge. She said: Among what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took upon us was: \"That we not disobey him in what is right, that we not scratch a face, not let down hair, not tear a collar, and not call for woe.\""],[21899,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have paths to the mosque that are foul.\" He said, \"Are there not beyond them paths cleaner than them?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then this for this.\""],[21900,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have a path that is bad during rain.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is there not besides it a good path?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then that for that.\""],[21901,"From Zaynab bt. Nubayt b. Jabir, from her mother or her maternal aunt, daughters of Abu Umamah. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted to me his daughters—meaning Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah. They said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adorned us with gold earrings.\""],[21902,"she said, the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ recited the Āyah of Stoning to us: \"al-shaykhu wa-al-shaykhah idhā zanayā fārjumūhumā al-battata bimā qaḍayā min al-ladhhah (The [married] man and a woman, if they commit adultery, then absolutely stone them for what they spent in [seeking] pleasure.)\" (Using translation from Ḥākim 8070)"],[21903,"I was one day with Zaynab, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while we were dyeing clothes with red ochre. While we were doing that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared before us. When he saw the red ochre, he turned back. When Zaynab saw that, she knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what she had done. So she took water and washed her clothes and hid all redness. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, looked, saw nothing, and entered."],[21904,"I witnessed Aminah when she gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When labor struck her, I looked at the stars descending until I said, \"They will surely fall upon me.\" When she gave birth to him, a light came out from her that illuminated the house we were in and the dwelling. There was nothing I looked at except light."],[21905,"From an orphan woman who was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Thaqif, that she narrated to Safiyyah bt. Abi 'Ubayd that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for whoever dies there, I will be a witness or intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[21906,"When Muhammad b. Talhah was born, I brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"What did they name him?\" We said, \"Muhammad.\" He said, \"This is my name and his kunyah is Abu al-Qasim.\""],[21907,"My father went out on a military expedition during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to look after us and milk a goat of ours. He would milk it into a large bowl and it would fill up. When Khabbab returned, he milked it, and its milking returned to its former amount."]]);
